"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/401\",\n            \"id\": 3955708570,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7EgozR\",\n            \"number\": 401,\n            \"title\": \"skip version check for dev builds\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"id\": 881031,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-02-18T03:24:43Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-02T00:59:38Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-03-02T00:59:37Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/401\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/401\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/401.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/401.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-03-02T00:59:37Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\n- Dev builds now use `{tag}-dev-{commit}` version format (e.g. `v0.4.5-dev-755fbfde`)\\n- Version check skips versions containing `-dev` in the prerelease suffix\\n- Normal prereleases like `-rc1` still trigger the update notification\\n- Removed `mise build:all` task — cross-arch builds are handled by the release GitHub Action, so a local build:all serves no purpose\\n\\nThis gives us a simple way to mark dev builds and skip version checks on them, without affecting real prerelease versions.\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/401/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/401/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/472\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/472/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/472/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/472/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/472\",\n            \"id\": 3981403385,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7F0Azo\",\n            \"number\": 472,\n            \"title\": \"Detect and warn on #456 git config corruption (user.name = literal us…\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 3,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T04:13:04Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-26T03:37:47Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-02-26T03:37:47Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/472\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/472\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/472.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/472.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"…er.email)\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/472/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/472/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/181\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/181/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/181/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/181/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/181\",\n            \"id\": 3914504184,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7CYnBo\",\n            \"number\": 181,\n            \"title\": \"Fix duplicate session IDs in checkpoint storage (ENT-252)\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"id\": 881031,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-02-09T05:18:09Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-10T00:47:14Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-02-10T00:47:13Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/181\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/181\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/181.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/181.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-02-10T00:47:12Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"  When Claude Code is running and the user makes git commits, two hooks fire sequentially: PrepareCommitMsg and PostCommit. Each independently decides whether the session has produced new content by calling filterSessionsWithNewContent().\\r\\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \\r\\n  The bug is a race condition between these two hooks:                         \\r\\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \\r\\n  1. Commit 1 — both hooks agree there's new content. A new checkpoint_id XYZ is generated, the session is condensed, and session folder /0/ is created with session_id=A.                                                                                                                                            \\r\\n  2. Commit 2 — PrepareCommitMsg runs first and sees no new content since commit 1. It reuses LastCheckpointID=XYZ (instead of generating a fresh one) and writes the checkpoint trailer to the commit message.                                                                                                         \\r\\n  3. Between the two hooks — Claude is still running and writes new transcript lines to disk.                                                                                                                                                                                                                         \\r\\n  4. PostCommit runs and calls filterSessionsWithNewContent() again. This time it finds new content (the lines Claude wrote in the gap). It condenses the session into checkpoint XYZ — which already has /0/. The write layer blindly appends, creating /1/ with the same session_id=A.\\r\\n\\r\\n  The root cause is that PrepareCommitMsg chose to reuse an existing checkpoint_id (because it saw no new content), but PostCommit saw new content (because the session kept writing) and triggered a condensation into that same checkpoint. The write layer (writeStandardCheckpointEntries) had no deduplication — it\\r\\n   always appended a new session folder regardless of whether that session_id already existed.\\r\\n\\r\\n  The fix (already applied to committed.go) makes the write layer defensive: before creating a new session folder, findSessionIndex checks if the session_id already exists in the checkpoint. If it does, it overwrites that slot in place instead of appending a duplicate.\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches core committed-checkpoint write and aggregation logic; mistakes could corrupt stored checkpoint summaries or session content ordering, though coverage is strengthened with new regression tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Fixes ENT-252 by making `WriteCommitted` reuse an existing session slot when the same `SessionID` is written again, instead of always appending a new numbered subdirectory.\\n> \\n> Overwriting a session now clears any prior files under that session path to avoid stale `prompt.txt`/`context.md`, and root `metadata.json` aggregation (`CheckpointsCount`, `FilesTouched`, `TokenUsage`) is recomputed from all session metadata entries rather than incrementally appended.\\n> \\n> Adds a focused test suite covering in-place updates, index reuse (no `/2/` creation), stale-file cleanup, and correct re-aggregation after overwrites.\\n> \\n> <sup>Written by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot) for commit f6242e26622c70dfe20de780c905322f951cdc89. This will update automatically on new commits. Configure [here](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/181/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/181/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/104\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/104/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/104/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/104/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/104\",\n            \"id\": 3856723363,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M6_Z6A3\",\n            \"number\": 104,\n            \"title\": \"Fix a bug that caused session conflicts\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T16:38:32Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-01-27T00:36:28Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-01-27T00:36:27Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/104\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/104\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/104.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/104.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-01-27T00:36:27Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"This was reported by @dipree but also @georg might have seen variations of it. After digging through the `entire/sessions` logs and what data we had (and trying different theories) this is where we landed: \\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\n  The Bug Scenario\\r\\n\\r\\n  1. Session A (914e68cc) starts\\r\\n    - InitializeSession creates state with CheckpointCount: 0\\r\\n  2. User runs a Task (subagent) in Session A\\r\\n    - PreToolUse[Task] fires → createStartingAgentCheckpoint → SaveTaskCheckpoint\\r\\n    - This creates a commit on the shadow branch (even with no file changes!)\\r\\n    - CheckpointCount stays at 0\\r\\n  3. User closes Claude without main agent making file changes\\r\\n    - Stop hook fires but commitWithMetadata returns early (\\\"No files were modified\\\")\\r\\n    - Session A state: CheckpointCount: 0, shadow branch has commits\\r\\n  4. Session B (f9b37e51) tries to start\\r\\n    - InitializeSession checks: state == nil || state.CheckpointCount == 0 → TRUE\\r\\n    - Sees shadow branch with commits tagged 914e68cc\\r\\n    - Loads Session A's state file (exists with CheckpointCount: 0)\\r\\n    - Returns SessionIDConflictError\\r\\n  5. User sees the error message about \\\"orphaning existing work\\\"\\r\\n    - But working tree is clean (task changes were undone, committed, or never existed)\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is probably the important aspect: \\r\\n\\r\\n> - This creates a commit on the shadow branch (even with no file changes!)\\r\\n\\r\\nSince that commit caused then the other session to fail to start since there was a commit in the shadow branch but no local changes, so it gave the wrong instructions.\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> Eliminates creation of \\\"starting\\\" subagent checkpoints and empty marker commits to prevent session conflicts and reduce noise.\\n> \\n> - `PreToolUse[Task]`: now only captures pre-task state; no checkpoint/commit is created\\n> - `AutoCommitStrategy.commitTaskCodeToActive`: skips commit when no file changes; removes TaskStart handling\\n> - Removes `IncrementalTypeTaskStart`, `FormatSubagentStartMessage`, and related tests; simplifies `FormatIncrementalSubject`\\n> - Updates integration/unit tests to expect a single completed checkpoint (no start checkpoint)\\n> - Docs updated to reflect new hook behavior and when checkpoints are created\\n> \\n> <sup>Written by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot) for commit 49bda7279bb7c82d15f88ed58f1f81654daa27a5. This will update automatically on new commits. Configure [here](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/104/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/104/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/280\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/280/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/280/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/280/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/280\",\n            \"id\": 3929294464,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7DJfK9\",\n            \"number\": 280,\n            \"title\": \"Layered secret detection using gitleaks patterns and entropy\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-02-12T00:42:44Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-12T06:22:23Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-02-12T06:22:20Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/280\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/280\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/280.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/280.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-02-12T06:22:20Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": null,\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/280/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/280/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/169\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/169/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/169/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/169/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/169\",\n            \"id\": 3908907693,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7CG4Sv\",\n            \"number\": 169,\n            \"title\": \"Consolidate session state types and simplify transcript tracking (ENT-221)\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"khaong\",\n              \"id\": 351934,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTkzNA==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/351934?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/khaong\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-02-07T00:12:12Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-09T04:56:42Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-02-09T04:50:28Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/169\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/169\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/169.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/169.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-02-09T04:50:28Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\n- Replace duplicate `SessionState`/`PromptAttribution` structs with type aliases to `session.State`/`session.PromptAttribution`, eliminating ~140 lines of converter boilerplate\\n- Simplify transcript offset tracking: 3 overlapping fields → 2 clean ones (`CheckpointTranscriptStart`, `StepTranscriptStart`) with backward-compatible migration\\n- Add `CheckpointTranscriptStart` to committed metadata with deprecated fallback, deduplicate `sessionStateDirName` constant\\n- Add `Phase`, `PendingCheckpointID`, `LastInteractionTime` fields to `session.State` for upcoming state machine wiring\\n\\n## Details\\n\\n**Type consolidation (Task 2):**\\n- `strategy.SessionState` → `type SessionState = session.State` (type alias)\\n- `strategy.PromptAttribution` → `type PromptAttribution = session.PromptAttribution`\\n- Removed `sessionStateToStrategy()`/`sessionStateFromStrategy()` converters\\n- Renamed `CheckpointCount` → `StepCount` (JSON tag preserved for backward compat)\\n\\n**Transcript simplification (Task 3):**\\n- `CondensedTranscriptLines` + `TranscriptLinesAtStart` → `CheckpointTranscriptStart` (session state)\\n- `LastTranscriptLineCount` → `StepTranscriptStart` (ephemeral pre-prompt state)\\n- `NormalizeAfterLoad()` migrates old state files transparently\\n- `CommittedMetadata.GetTranscriptStart()` helper prefers new field, falls back to old\\n\\n## Test plan\\n- [x] JSON round-trip migration tests for `NormalizeAfterLoad`\\n- [x] All existing unit + integration tests pass\\n- [x] `mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci` — 0 issues, all pass\\n- [x] 30 files changed, net +12 lines\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n## PR Stack (ENT-221)\\n> **2 of 5 (1B)** ← you are here\\n> 1. #168 — Pure session phase state machine\\n> 2. #169 — Consolidate session state types + transcript simplification\\n> 3. #170 — Wire state machine into hooks\\n> 4. #172 — Phase-aware PostCommit + PrepareCommitMsg amend fix\\n> 5. #174 — Cleanup: session helpers, transition logging, Gemini parity\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches hook execution paths and checkpoint metadata/state persistence, so regressions could affect transcript scoping, condensation timing, and session cleanup across agents; backward-compat migrations reduce but don’t eliminate risk for existing session files.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Unifies session state handling by aliasing `strategy.SessionState`/`PromptAttribution` to `session.State`/`session.PromptAttribution`, renaming `CheckpointCount`→`StepCount`, and adding/migrating new lifecycle fields (`Phase`, `LastInteractionTime`, `PendingCheckpointID`) with backward-compatible normalization.\\n> \\n> Simplifies transcript scoping by replacing multiple overlapping counters with `CheckpointTranscriptStart` (persisted per session + written into committed checkpoint metadata) and `StepTranscriptStart` (per-turn pre-prompt state), including fallbacks for older metadata/state and updating explain/summarize logic to use `CommittedMetadata.GetTranscriptStart()`.\\n> \\n> Hooks and tooling are updated to rely on session state files (not `.entire/current_session`), wire phase transitions on session start/turn end/session stop (including deferred condensation dispatch), add Claude transcript flush polling on stop, and introduce `entire sessions fix` plus enhanced `entire reset` (`--session` + guard against resetting active sessions).\\n> \\n> <sup>Written by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot) for commit 35b780e7d654b3c923f501502948c53d1289d2d7. This will update automatically on new commits. Configure [here](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/169/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/169/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/101\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/101/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/101/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/101/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/101\",\n            \"id\": 3848098536,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M6-90ov\",\n            \"number\": 101,\n            \"title\": \"add codeline agent attribution for manual commits\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T16:05:26Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-01-28T00:03:04Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-01-28T00:03:02Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/101\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/101\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/101.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/101.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-01-28T00:03:02Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"This adds new fields to the `metadata.json`:\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\n    \\\"initial_attribution\\\": {\\r\\n      \\\"calculated_at\\\": \\\"2026-01-23T14:30:00Z\\\",\\r\\n      \\\"agent_lines\\\": 142,\\r\\n      \\\"human_added\\\": 12,\\r\\n      \\\"human_modified\\\": 6,\\r\\n      \\\"human_removed\\\": 3,\\r\\n      \\\"total_committed\\\": 154,\\r\\n      \\\"agent_percentage\\\": 92.2\\r\\n    }\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is done by comparing the shadow branch against the commit that was made. Any change not in the shadow branch was made by the user. Based on that we calculate a percentage.\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> Introduces commit-time attribution metrics and prompt-time tracking to quantify agent vs. human contributions in manual-commit flow.\\n> \\n> - Adds `initial_attribution` to `metadata.json` with fields like `agent_lines`, `human_added`, `human_modified`, `human_removed`, `total_committed`, and `agent_percentage`; timestamps UTC\\n> - Implements attribution calculation by diffing `base → shadow` (agent work) and `shadow → head` (post-checkpoint user edits), excluding binary files; retains attribution across multi-session merges\\n> - Captures per-prompt user edits via new session state (`PromptAttributions`, `PendingPromptAttribution`) computed at prompt start from the worktree; stored on checkpoint save and cleared after condensation\\n> - Extends manual-commit strategy to compute and persist attribution during condensation; logs debug info; converts session state to/from strategy types\\n> - Adds comprehensive unit/integration tests (including deletion-only, no double-counting, staging vs worktree) and architecture docs; updates go.mod with `go-diff` dependency\\n> \\n> <sup>Written by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot) for commit 6faf3631cd9afb93b7cb174b9b0f245097c30925. This will update automatically on new commits. Configure [here](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/101/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/101/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          }\n        ],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      },\n      \"issues\": {\n        \"total_count\": 2,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1807\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1807/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1807/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1807/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/1807\",\n            \"id\": 4928515413,\n            \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABJcMtVQ\",\n            \"number\": 1807,\n            \"title\": \"Proposal: remove the subagent-checkpoint machinery (pre-task/post-task/post-todo) — likely unneeded\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"id\": 881031,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-07-20T11:33:25Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-21T21:50:52Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": null,\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n              \"total\": 0,\n              \"completed\": 0,\n              \"percent_completed\": 0\n            },\n            \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n              \"blocked_by\": 0,\n              \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n              \"blocking\": 0,\n              \"total_blocking\": 0\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Proposal\\n\\nEvaluate removing the **subagent / task-checkpoint** subsystem — the `pre-task`, `post-task`, and `post-todo` hooks and everything they feed. Investigation suggests it produces data that nothing consumes.\\n\\nRaised as the deferred follow-up from #1806 (which repaired the Claude Code matchers so these hooks fire again). This issue is the \\\"do we even want this granularity?\\\" decision.\\n\\n## What this subsystem is\\n\\n- **`pre-task`** — snapshots untracked files before a subagent runs (baseline helper)\\n- **`post-task`** — on subagent finish, writes a *task checkpoint* to the shadow branch bundling the subagent's file diff + its own transcript (`agent-<id>.jsonl`) + attribution (`subagent_type`, `task_description`, `agent_id`, `tool_use_id`)\\n- **`post-todo`** — cuts *incremental* checkpoints during a long subagent run\\n\\nBacked by shared machinery: `handleLifecycleSubagentStart/End` (`cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go`), `SaveTaskStep` / `TaskStepContext` (`cmd/entire/cli/strategy/`), task-checkpoint write paths (`cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/ephemeral.go`, `persistent.go`), and `pre-task` state (`cmd/entire/cli/state.go`).\\n\\n## Why it looks unneeded\\n\\n**The product consumes session-level data only** (checked in `entire.io`):\\n- Ingestion reads `full.jsonl` / `transcript.jsonl` for session index 0 (`api/src/lib/checkpoint-payload-hydrator.ts`). Subagent transcripts (`agent-*.jsonl`) are **never read**.\\n- `is_task` / `tool_use_id` are parsed into `SessionInfo` once (`api/src/lib/github.ts:660-661`) then never queried or displayed.\\n- `subagent_type`, `task_description`, `is_incremental`, `incremental_sequence`, `agent_id`, `is_task_checkpoint` → **0 matches** anywhere in the product. No UI renders subagents.\\n\\n**Local consumers are dead or cosmetic:**\\n- `rewind` (the one feature using subagent-boundary checkpoints) is deprecated and slated for removal.\\n- Remaining use is `[Task]` labels in `checkpoint list` / `explain` — navigational garnish.\\n\\n**Cross-agent:** the machinery is shared by **Claude Code, Cursor, Factory AI Droid, and Copilot CLI**. On Claude Code it was dead (the #1806 matcher bug); on the other three it fires today but produces the same inert task checkpoints.\\n\\n## What we'd lose: nothing consumed\\n\\n- Code the subagent writes is still captured by the `Stop` / turn checkpoint (whole-worktree). No code loss in the common single-worktree flow.\\n- Subagent transcript, per-subagent rewind points, attribution, per-subagent tokens — none are read by the product or any live command.\\n\\n**One honest caveat:** subagents in an **isolated worktree** aren't covered by `Stop`, and `post-task` was the only thing that would capture them. But that protection doesn't effectively exist today (hooks were broken/unconsumed), so removal doesn't regress vs current reality. If isolated-worktree subagent capture ever becomes a real requirement, it's a fresh, correctly-scoped feature.\\n\\n## Removal scope (if approved)\\n\\n- Hook install + lifecycle parse across the 4 agents (`subagent-start/stop`, `pre-tool-use/post-tool-use`, Claude matchers)\\n- Shared dispatch cases (`SubagentStart`/`SubagentEnd` in `lifecycle.go`; subagent classification in `hook_registry.go`)\\n- Strategy: `SaveTaskStep`, `TaskStepContext`, task-checkpoint write paths in `checkpoint/ephemeral.go` + `persistent.go`\\n- `pre-task` state (`state.go`), `post-todo` handler\\n- The deprecated `rewind` task-checkpoint branch (already going away)\\n- Tests + docs across all four agents\\n\\n## Decision needed\\n\\nKeep (bet on a future subagent-level product feature — the dead `isTask` parse suggests it was once intended) **or** remove (delete unconsumed cross-agent complexity).\\n\\nIf we're not going to surface subagent-level data in the product in the foreseeable future, the recommendation is **remove**.\\n\\n/cc — deferred from #1806\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1807/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1807/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"pinned_comment\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2980\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2980/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2980/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2980/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2980\",\n            \"id\": 6110766677,\n            \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABbDrmVQ\",\n            \"number\": 2980,\n            \"title\": \"Post-push session attach publishes linked_commits but checkpoint remains absent from activity and Dispatch\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"lcv-leo\",\n              \"id\": 268063598,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD_pTbg\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/268063598?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/lcv-leo\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 7,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-30T00:14:37Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-05T17:58:31Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-11-05T17:58:31Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n              \"total\": 0,\n              \"completed\": 0,\n              \"percent_completed\": 0\n            },\n            \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n              \"blocked_by\": 0,\n              \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n              \"blocking\": 0,\n              \"total_blocking\": 0\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Context and impact\\n\\nWe use Entire alongside GitHub for real changes to a private web application. We reached this problem while trying to generate the team's Dispatch after a squash merge, not while constructing a synthetic checkpoint test. This report was prepared with Codex assistance at the repository operator's request; the observations below come from the official CLI and API responses.\\n\\nThe original checkpoint is available remotely, but has no branch membership after the feature branch is deleted. We understand why a squash commit without an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer needs repair. The problem reported here is that the documented post-push `session attach` repair reports success and publishes `linked_commits`, yet the activity API still cannot find the new checkpoint or link it to that commit. As a result, a Dispatch for the recent release says there are no checkpoints. A wider-window Dispatch succeeds but omits the recent release.\\n\\n## Environment\\n\\n- Windows, PowerShell; GitHub private repository `LCV-Ideas-Software/astrologo-app`.\\n- Installed CLI: `0.12.2-lcv.windows-console.1+idle-fallback.2`, based on v0.12.2. These are the locally authorized Windows-console and stale sibling-session patches tracked in #2926 / #2972 and #2979. **I have not reproduced this with an unmodified binary**, and am not claiming otherwise. No further binary, Git identity, signing, or hook configuration change was made for this investigation.\\n- Git-ref checkpoint storage, mirror placements ready in BR and US. The repository view resolves the activity API to `aws-us-east-2.api.entire.io` and repo ID `01M5Z457WFR60E17SC5GNHDRH5`.\\n- The affected captured session is about 3.3 MB, not the multi-GB session from #2933. It was captured during actual work on PR #540.\\n\\n## What led us here\\n\\n1. PR #540's signed feature commit was `6405cf2a09b158721a63bcbcdac933067ee188a2`, checkpoint `01M64TPXT3N02BC8RX20YX4XQB`, session `01a1896c-8d01-77d2-afeb-82b5439fbfcc`.\\n2. The published squash commit is `0b227a331c1ea32b594c8916336ac8a42d9a3660`. Its message mentions the checkpoint in prose but does **not** contain an `Entire-Checkpoint:` trailer. The feature branch was deleted after publication.\\n3. `entire checkpoint explain 01M64TPXT3N02BC8RX20YX4XQB --repo gh/LCV-Ideas-Software/astrologo-app --json` succeeds. The activity checkpoint-resolution response reports `branches: []`, `default_branch: null`, and `suggested_branch: null` for that checkpoint.\\n4. The activity API's checkpoint-status response counts 12 checkpoints and reports access allowed. The main-branch list contains only one older checkpoint from PR #528 and reports `history_status: \\\"complete\\\"`. Thus this is not a missing login or an empty repository.\\n5. I queued the native mirror resync. It returned `status: \\\"queued\\\"`; the main list still contained only the older checkpoint.\\n6. I checked the official `session attach` help and preview. It explicitly said the published commit would remain unchanged and a new checkpoint would carry the exact commit link. There were no unrelated outgoing checkpoint refs. The configured Git email equals the target commit author's email.\\n7. I ran:\\n\\n   ```text\\n   entire session attach 01a1896c-8d01-77d2-afeb-82b5439fbfcc --agent codex --commit 0b227a331c1ea32b594c8916336ac8a42d9a3660 --force\\n   ```\\n\\n   The command warned that there were no new turns since the original checkpoint, then returned exit 0:\\n\\n   ```text\\n   Created checkpoint 01M6524YWT7N18SBAWPA444AK6\\n   Linked to commit 0b227a331c1e in the checkpoint; the commit is unchanged (already pushed)\\n   [entire] Pushing 1 checkpoint ref(s) to origin..... done\\n   Pushed checkpoint metadata to origin\\n   ```\\n\\n8. The new checkpoint's `metadata.json` contains:\\n\\n   ```json\\n   \\\"linked_commits\\\": [{\\n     \\\"sha\\\": \\\"0b227a331c1ea32b594c8916336ac8a42d9a3660\\\",\\n     \\\"repo\\\": \\\"gh/LCV-Ideas-Software/astrologo-app\\\"\\n   }]\\n   ```\\n\\n   It also has `files_touched: null` and an empty session prompt. I am not claiming it represents new work; this was a repair of the link to an already captured real session.\\n\\n9. `git ls-remote origin refs/entire/checkpoints/K6/01M6524YWT7N18SBAWPA444AK6` confirms the published ref at `d58987752d72ca61358bbf1103f101c5cb4e308d`. The main commit is unchanged. I queued a second resync **after this new ref was published**.\\n10. Following that resync, the main list still has only the old checkpoint. At 00:12:27 UTC on 30 October 2026 (21:12:27 in Brazil on 29 October), the API still returned HTTP 404 `{\\\"error\\\":\\\"checkpoint not found\\\"}` for the newly attached checkpoint. This observation is bounded to the few minutes after the repair; it is not a claim that ingestion can never complete. The commit-checkpoint endpoint also returned an empty list with complete history.\\n11. A Dispatch covering 25–29 October successfully completed with **one** checkpoint, from PR #528. This is a useful control: generation works for the existing indexed membership. It does not demonstrate coverage of PR #540 or validate the new attachment.\\n\\n## Expected behavior / requested guidance\\n\\nWhat is the supported way to attach an **already captured session with no new turns** to an already-pushed squash commit, without rewriting shared Git history or fabricating another code change?\\n\\nIf `session attach` is that repair, please check whether the empty incremental attachment or `linked_commits` ingestion is preventing the association from becoming visible. If asynchronous indexing needs a different official trigger, please document that trigger and an observable completion status. The CLI success message alone currently does not let us verify the repaired association.\\n\\nI read #321 (closed) and #1889 (regional Dispatch routing). This report concerns the present post-push attachment result and missing activity membership, rather than assuming a new instance of the older routing issue. Full private evidence is retained for the operator; this report intentionally excludes source code, transcripts, prompts, credentials, and personal data.\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2980/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2980/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n            \"pinned_comment\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          }\n        ],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e15\",\n      \"query\": \"repo:entireio/cli checkpoint assets extract\",\n      \"prs\": {\n        \"total_count\": 103,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2844\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2844/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2844/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2844/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2844\",\n            \"id\": 5955368891,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABJuEOZQ\",\n            \"number\": 2844,\n            \"title\": \"Link an agent's own commit in another repository\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-21T06:13:38Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-10T15:54:08Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": null,\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2844\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2844\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2844.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2844.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2375/changes/cli/1636\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nFixes #1439 (narrowed to the agent's own commits).\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nSession state lives per git common dir. A session homed in repo A whose agent commits in another Entire-enabled repo B gets no `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer: B's hooks only see B's sessions, and nothing records where the session lives.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\n- **Session-home index.** Turn start records the session's worktree and owner process in a per-user cache (`session-homes/<id>.json` under `userdirs.CacheRoot`). It's only a pointer: B asks git for the worktree's common dir (with `GIT_DIR`/`GIT_INDEX_FILE` scrubbed) and loads the state read-only from A's store. Records older than the active-session window are ignored, and older than 7 days are deleted.\\n- **prepare-commit-msg in B.** Only when B's own sessions link nothing, with no TTY (or `commit_linking: always`), never for `--amend` without a new message, merges, commits inheriting checkpoint trailers, or sequence operations (`--amend -m` and trailer-less squashes link as new commits, like the local fast path). The committer must be identified (`IsCaller()`, tracked) by `resolveCallerIdentity` over B's sessions plus the indexed foreign ones, so a nearer B-homed agent wins over a passed-through variable. Stamps a fresh checkpoint ID and leaves a marker for post-commit.\\n- **Opt-in, off by default.** Linking puts A's session transcript into B's checkpoints, which B pushes. It runs only after a developer turns it on for A with `entire configure --cross-repo-commits on`. It needs a person at an interactive terminal, outside a detected agent session, with no override (agent detection is best-effort, so the terminal check is the second signal); `off` works anywhere. The choice lives in A's git common dir (`entire/cross-repo-commits`), where a cloned repository can't put it, and is checked again under A's lock in post-commit. The help text says plainly that the same owner is not the same audience: a private A and a public B under one org both pass the checks below.\\n- **Destination check.** Every push URL of the remote B's checkpoints go to, plus B's `checkpoint_remote` when one is in effect, must resolve to the same forge and owner as A's `origin`. Any error, missing origin, unknown forge or mismatch refuses. The check runs at commit time; a remote added before the push isn't re-checked.\\n- **Redaction coverage.** Linking is refused unless B's redaction covers A's: the same scanner engines, PII categories and patterns, and every custom rule (inline or in `.entire/redactors` packs, compared by regex). Redaction is configured once per process, so A's settings aren't merged in mid-hook.\\n- **No summary.** A's transcript isn't sent to B's summary provider.\\n- Each refusal leaves git's output a one-line notice with no paths or commands (printed from commit-msg, since the installed prepare-commit-msg hook discards stderr).\\n- **post-commit in B.** Takes A's state lock (30s bound) through the shared session-state mutate helper, condenses the session's transcript since its last checkpoint into B's store with B's settings, and saves A's state the way a guest-linked commit does: the transcript window advances, while A's base, files, turn checkpoints and `LastCheckpointID` stay put. `files_touched` is the committed files the transcript wrote under B, or the whole commit when it wrote none of them (shell edits).\\n\\n## Known limits\\n\\n- B's checkpoint isn't finalized at turn end; the rest of the turn lands in A's next checkpoint.\\n- B's checkpoint carries A's session transcript up to the commit, including earlier turns that only touched A (as every checkpoint stores the full transcript). This is documented in the opt-in help and docs; A's next checkpoint window starts after it.\\n- If post-commit can't condense (A's lock busy past 30s, session no longer eligible), B's commit keeps a trailer with no checkpoint; this is logged at Warn.\\n- Telemetry for these commits follows B's consent setting.\\n- `entire session current` run in B still reports no state for the session.\\n- A relative transcript path whose name collides with a committed file in B could be listed in B's `files_touched`.\\n\\nSupersedes the approach of #1777 / #1959 for this case.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- Security: opt-in on/off/missing/garbage, `on` refused without a terminal and from an agent session, push URL or `checkpoint_remote` of another owner, no remote, unknown forge, redaction coverage (missing rule, PII category, packs, unreadable settings), opt-in re-checked under the lock, summary skipped, squash inheriting a trailer gets no foreign stamp, a content-less B session beside the foreign link.\\n\\n- Unit: index record/list/prune/symlink refusal, `LoadReadOnly`, the scrubbed common-dir lookup, resolver (env claim, ancestry, refused states, own-repo record, nested local agent wins, hook repo selectors), commit hooks (stamping, TTY, amend, pre-stamped, condensation, hand-typed trailer, held lock, home amend keeps its ID).\\n- Integration (real git hooks in B): agent commit in B links, then A's own commit and turn end; two foreign sessions in different agents each link only their own commit; a B session with content takes the commit over a foreign one.\\n- Two sessions of one agent process (e.g. after `/clear`) resolve to the most recent, as the existing ranking does locally (unit; the integration harness can't separate owners by ancestry).\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2844/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2844/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2069\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2069/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2069/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2069/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2069\",\n            \"id\": 5195556437,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABAUQlLA\",\n            \"number\": 2069,\n            \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): externalize images in subagent transcripts before size cap\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"id\": 257360244,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T17:48:48Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-26T23:46:45Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": null,\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2069\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2069\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2069.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2069.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"**Trail:** https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1100\\n\\n**What:** Run image externalization on subagent transcripts (when enabled) before the 50MB size check, and store returned assets under `tasks/<id>/assets/`.\\n\\n**Why / how it helps:** Subagent path only sanitized then size-checked/redacted, so image-heavy transcripts were dropped whole and Codex `input_image` base64 reached redaction intact (corruption risk).\\n\\n**How:** `prepareSubagentTranscript`: sanitize → optional `imageextract` → size-check externalized bytes; wire assets into persistent + ephemeral task writers.\\n\\n**Testing:**\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/ -count=1` (375 passed)\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/transcript/imageextract/`\\n- `go build ./...` clean\\n\\nFixes #2063\\n\\nRelated: #2060 (redact skip for `input_image`), #2058 (durable subagent storage still open)\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2069/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2069/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": {\n              \"id\": 2626939,\n              \"client_id\": \"Iv23lieFG10uOnChW4TN\",\n              \"slug\": \"entire\",\n              \"node_id\": \"A_kwHOAfprLM4AKBV7\",\n              \"owner\": {\n                \"login\": \"entireio\",\n                \"id\": 33188652,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjMzMTg4NjUy\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33188652?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"Organization\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"name\": \"Entire\",\n              \"description\": \"\",\n              \"external_url\": \"https://entire.com\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/entire\",\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-01-09T21:20:56Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-23T08:32:31Z\",\n              \"permissions\": {\n                \"administration\": \"read\",\n                \"checks\": \"write\",\n                \"contents\": \"write\",\n                \"emails\": \"read\",\n                \"members\": \"read\",\n                \"metadata\": \"read\",\n                \"pull_requests\": \"write\",\n                \"statuses\": \"read\",\n                \"workflows\": \"write\"\n              },\n              \"events\": [\n                \"check_suite\",\n                \"create\",\n                \"delete\",\n                \"fork\",\n                \"member\",\n                \"membership\",\n                \"organization\",\n                \"pull_request\",\n                \"push\",\n                \"repository\",\n                \"star\",\n                \"team\"\n              ]\n            },\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3045\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3045/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3045/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3045/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3045\",\n            \"id\": 6250176154,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABNZmFPQ\",\n            \"number\": 3045,\n            \"title\": \"codex: offer to install hooks where Codex reads them in linked worktrees\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-11-06T20:32:10Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-09T03:17:33Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": null,\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3045\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3045\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3045.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3045.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Problem\\n\\nIn a linked worktree, `entire enable --agent codex` (and `entire agent add codex`) writes `<worktree>/.codex/hooks.json`, but Codex loads the **primary checkout's** `.codex/hooks.json` (the `.bare` layout root for `.bare` worktrees; pinned by the `codex app-server` `hooks/list` tests). With no hooks file there, Codex runs no Entire hooks and nothing is captured. `enable` warned (\\\"Hooks in the current-worktree file will not run here\\\") and `entire status` showed \\\"Codex hooks are not active in this worktree\\\", but nothing fixed it, so people who only work in worktrees got no checkpoints.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nAfter installing in the current worktree, when Codex reads a different hooks file that is absent, has only user hooks, or has outdated Entire hooks, setup asks (default **No**):\\n\\n> Codex reads hooks from `<primary>/.codex/hooks.json`, not from this worktree. Install Entire's Codex hooks there too? This leaves an uncommitted change in `<primary>`.\\n\\n- **Yes:** merges Entire's hooks into that file (never clobbers user hooks) and says: \\\"This is an uncommitted change in that checkout. Open /hooks in Codex to approve them.\\\" (Codex trust records are keyed to that path, so status moves to \\\"N Codex hook(s) need approval\\\".)\\n- **Consent is read from the terminal itself** (`interactive.OpenPromptTTY`), so piped stdin can't answer it; agent sessions (`review.DetectAgentSession`) are never asked.\\n- **No, `--yes`, no terminal, agents/CI:** writes nothing and prints the remedy: re-run `entire agent add codex` in this worktree from a terminal and answer yes. (It does not suggest running enable in the primary, which would enable Entire there.) `.bare` layouts keep the \\\"apply the generated hooks.json at `<root>`\\\" guidance.\\n- **Optional by design:** an aborted prompt or a failed write warns and prints the remedy and setup still completes; only a cancelled command stops setup.\\n\\n### Safety\\n- The write target is the root `ResolveHookDiscovery` derived from Git metadata, carried as a trusted field on `DiscoveredHooksPath` (never recovered from the path with `filepath.Dir`).\\n- Discovery is re-resolved right before the write and must match exactly what the user was shown.\\n- Writes go through `agent.OpenHookConfig(root, \\\".codex/hooks.json\\\")`: anchored root, `MkdirAllNoSymlink`, atomic write, symlinked `.codex`/`hooks.json` refused. Malformed or unreadable files, unresolved discovery, submodules, and a separate Git directory's storage parent (which can hold other repositories' storage; it gets its own remedy) are never offered.\\n- Merging keeps every field of existing user hooks (e.g. `async`, `timeoutSec`, `statusMessage`, extra group keys); this also fixes that loss for the current-worktree install. Duplicate Entire entries are collapsed, and a `null` hooks file no longer panics.\\n- `entire doctor` (including `--force`) never writes; it and `entire status` name the remedy, and only suggest \\\"answer yes\\\" when setup would actually offer the write. Removal stays current-checkout only (documented).\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/AGENT.md` documents the consent exception to \\\"never write another checkout\\\"; `filesystem-safety.md` notes the discovered Codex root under `HookConfigFile`.\\n\\n`InstallHooks` now shares `installHooksInto` with the discovered-root install; the Codex + skill steps after agent setup moved into `finishAgentSetup` (kept `runEnableInteractive` under the complexity limit).\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- Unit (`agent/codex`): create/merge/update the discovered file, `.bare` root, refusal for malformed, symlinked `.codex`/leaf, changed/unresolved discovery; candidate table; normal checkouts, submodules and separate-git-dir worktrees never offered.\\n- CLI: yes writes then no re-prompt; no / cannot-prompt write nothing and print the remedy; cancelled prompt and a symlink appearing after the offer both warn and keep setup going; outdated primary prompts, current doesn't; `--yes` with a TTY never prompts; doctor never writes.\\n- Integration (`codex app-server` `hooks/list`): after answering yes in a linked worktree and in a `.bare` worktree, `hooks/list` from the worktree returns Entire's hooks sourced from the primary / layout-root file; declining writes nothing.\\n- Live with the branch binary: piped (no TTY) → remedy, no write; TTY + `n` → prompt, remedy, no write; TTY + `y` → `main/.codex/hooks.json` with Entire's 7 hooks (untracked in main), and `entire status` in the worktree changes from \\\"not active\\\" to \\\"7 Codex hook(s) need approval · open /hooks\\\".\\n- **Baseline on current main** (real Codex turn in a linked worktree, main binary on PATH): enable wrote only the worktree file, status said \\\"not active\\\", the turn ran but only the user's own `~/.codex` hooks fired, `entire session list` showed no sessions, and the commit got no `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer (0 checkpoints).\\n- **Real Codex sessions** (Codex 0.166, branch binary on PATH) in linked worktrees, on the final build as well: before approval, Codex skipped Entire's project hooks and nothing was recorded (matches the new \\\"open /hooks to approve\\\" message); after approving in `/hooks`, the next `codex exec` turn fired SessionStart, UserPromptSubmit, PostToolUse and Stop, Entire recorded the session, and committing produced an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer and a checkpoint with the prompt. Re-run after the review fixes in a second linked worktree: same result. Live: an existing user hook with `async`/`timeoutSec`/`statusMessage`/extra key in the primary kept all fields; with `AI_AGENT`/`CLAUDECODE` set, no prompt and the remedy printed.\\n- `mise run check`: everything this PR touches passes (cli, agent/codex, integration_test); lint 0 issues; complexity gate clean. Unrelated local failures: `TestProbeConfigDir_AsksClaude` / `TestResolveClaudeConfigDir_PrefersClaudesAnswer` (5s timeouts under load, pass alone) and `TestHandlePush_RealSendPack_ShallowRepoAmendsAgent` (fails on main locally).\\n\\n## Follow-ups (not in this PR)\\n- CI's `test-codex-hooks` job installs the latest Codex rather than the pinned 0.149.0 that AGENT.md describes.\\n- `warnCodexHooksAfterRemoval` says \\\".codex/hooks.json is tracked\\\" even for `.bare` roots.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3045/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3045/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2891\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2891/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2891/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2891/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2891\",\n            \"id\": 6027894516,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABKnj7pQ\",\n            \"number\": 2891,\n            \"title\": \"Pi: externalize images and keep image-only user turns\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-25T18:37:01Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-25T20:40:53Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-25T20:40:50Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2891\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2891\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2891.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2891.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-25T20:40:50Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2549/changes/cli/1682\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nStacked on #2862 (base `alex/ent-3403-pi-converter`). Follow-up to the image pass-through that was reverted on #2862 (37f2a58c59) until Pi had an image codec.\\n\\n## What\\n\\n- **Pi image codec** (`cmd/entire/cli/transcript/imageextract`). Pi writes images as `{\\\"type\\\":\\\"image\\\",\\\"data\\\":<base64>,\\\"mimeType\\\":…}` items in user message and tool result content. With `redaction.externalize_images` on, Claude Code and Codex images moved to `assets/`, but Pi's stayed inline. `piCodec` externalizes them with the shared engine, so the byte-exact round trip, media type detection from the bytes, size limits and dedupe are the same as for the other codecs.\\n- **Image-only Pi user turns are kept** (reapplies 04be3751ed). The Pi converter dropped image items, so a user message holding only an image produced no line and the turn boundary was lost. Image items now pass through verbatim in source order, as Claude Code's do. With externalization on, `transcript.jsonl` is built from the externalized transcript, so it carries the placeholder rather than the base64.\\n- **Security doc**: Pi gets its own row in the pasted-images table. By default Pi images are stored inline and unredacted (Pi's `type: image` items match the redaction skip rule, like Claude Code's); with externalization on they move to `assets/`.\\n\\n## Note on size\\n\\nWith externalization off (the default), images are inline in both `full.jsonl` and `transcript.jsonl` for Claude Code and Codex already; Pi now matches them. With it on, all three store each image once under `assets/`.\\n\\n## Check\\n\\n`mise run check`: fmt and lint clean; all tests pass except `e2e/agents` `TestOpenCodeSeedRepoPlantsDeps`, which also fails on `main` locally (it cannot parse a local OpenCode 2 version). New tests in `imageextract/pi_test.go`: byte-exact round trip for user and tool-result images, media type from bytes, non-Pi image shapes left alone, and an end-to-end extract → `Convert` check that `transcript.jsonl` keeps the placeholder (it fails without the pass-through commit).\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes how Pi screenshots are stored in checkpoints (inline vs `assets/`) and extends the shared image-externalization path; behavior matches existing Claude/Codex semantics but still stores pasted images unredacted when enabled.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Pi joins Claude Code and Codex for optional image externalization**, and **the Pi compact converter keeps user image blocks** so image-only turns are not dropped.\\n> \\n> With `redaction.externalize_images` enabled, a new **`piCodec`** in `imageextract` finds Pi’s `{\\\"type\\\":\\\"image\\\",\\\"data\\\":…,\\\"mimeType\\\":…}` items (user content and tool results), swaps base64 for `entire-asset:assets/…` placeholders via the shared extract/reinject engine, and is registered on `AgentTypePi`. Tests cover byte-exact round trip, media-type-from-bytes, ignoring non-Pi shapes, and extract → `Convert` keeping placeholders in `transcript.jsonl`.\\n> \\n> **`piEmitUserContent`** now emits text blocks and passes image items through as raw JSON in source order (including image-only messages). **`docs/security-and-privacy.md`** documents Pi’s inline vs `assets/` behavior; **`transcript/README.md`** notes the pass-through shape.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit ca2b14e63668f350b2d0cd626df3ec534c96c4da. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2891/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2891/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2892\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2892/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2892/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2892/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2892\",\n            \"id\": 6028262930,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABKn2S9g\",\n            \"number\": 2892,\n            \"title\": \"Condense an IDLE session prepare-commit-msg linked by its live transcript\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-25T19:15:52Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-26T11:05:58Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-26T11:05:55Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2892\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2892\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2892.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2892.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-26T11:05:55Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2556/changes/cli/1683\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nFixes [ENT-3537](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/ENT-3537/cli-writes-checkpoint-trailer-but-skips-condensing-when-an-agent).\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nAn IDLE session whose new work since its last checkpoint exists only in its live transcript (no turn-end step since then, or one that left no files and no stored transcript) gets an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer from prepare-commit-msg: `sessionHasNewContent` extracts the transcript's edits and overlaps them with the staged files. Post-commit then declined the same session:\\n\\n- `hasNew`: post-commit ran the same live-transcript check with no staged files, so the overlap could never match (without task records the session had \\\"no new content\\\").\\n- Overlap: for IDLE sessions `filesTouchedBefore` came only from persisted `FilesTouched`, which is empty here, so `shouldCondenseWithOverlapCheck` returned false.\\n\\nThe commit kept a trailer pointing at a checkpoint that was never written, and the session's usage went to its next checkpoint, possibly on another branch.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n- `liveTranscriptCheckApplies` is the one condition both hooks use for \\\"judge this session by its live transcript\\\"; `sessionHasNewContent` now calls it instead of two separate branches.\\n- The live-transcript check overlaps with the commit's files: staged in prepare-commit-msg, committed in post-commit (`contentCheckOpts.committedFiles`).\\n- Post-commit takes such an IDLE session's overlap from its transcript's uncheckpointed edits (`filesTouchedWithLiveTranscript`). ENDED sessions are unchanged: with no persisted files they take the discard action.\\n- `hasMidTurnClaimant` → `hasLiveTranscriptClaimant`: it also counts these IDLE writers, so a file-less ACTIVE reader is held off the commit by the read-only gate instead of condensing into the writer's checkpoint (this predated the change). An IDLE writer counts only if its transcript grew since its last checkpoint, so a Claude subagent's already-checkpointed edits can't claim the commit.\\n- Only IDLE sessions get the committed files in post-commit. An ENDED one would otherwise count its transcript edits as new content, take the discard action anyway, and never be marked fully condensed.\\n- Transcript edits are made relative to the session's home, so a non-ACTIVE session is judged by them only for commits at its home (`transcriptEditsApplyHere`), in both hooks and the claimant check. In stacked worktrees that touch the same files, a sibling's commit otherwise got the session's trailer and guest-condensed it, consuming the work the home's later commit needed.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n`idle_live_transcript_condense_test.go`, through the real prepare-commit-msg → commit → post-commit hooks:\\n\\n- Trailer resolves for no turn-end step, completed task records, and a turn-end step without a record (all red before the fix).\\n- The session stays out of a commit its transcript didn't edit.\\n- An ACTIVE reader is not condensed into the IDLE writer's checkpoint.\\n- Sibling worktree: with a record of the sibling the trailer resolves; with only transcript evidence nothing is linked, with or without files pending at home. Either way the home's and a third worktree's pending files survive.\\n- Stacked worktrees: a sibling commits its own `feature.go` before the home commits the transcript's `feature.go`; the sibling gets no trailer and the home's trailer resolves.\\n- An ENDED session with transcript-only edits is marked fully condensed after a commit.\\n- An IDLE session whose only matching edits are an already-checkpointed subagent's doesn't hold an ACTIVE reader off the commit.\\n\\nEach half of the fix and the claimant change were mutation-checked against these tests. `TestPostCommit_IdleSession_NoTranscriptFallbackForCarryForward` still passes: its session has a stored transcript, so the helper leaves it alone.\\n\\n## Not covered\\n\\n- An ENDED session with no persisted files can still be stamped by prepare-commit-msg and discarded by post-commit. Fixing it means deciding whether to condense such a session or not stamp it.\\n- The ticket's exact incident state is unconfirmed. The stacked-worktree case (1652 stacked on 1651, touching the same files) fits it: on main both commits got trailers that resolve to nothing. The `files_touched_before` field of the incident's `post-commit: carry-forward prep` log line would settle it.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes post-commit condensation and read-only gate logic for IDLE/transcript-only sessions; mistakes could mis-attribute checkpoints or skip condensation, but behavior is heavily covered by new hook tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Fixes **ENT-3537**: when **prepare-commit-msg** links an **IDLE** session using only its **live transcript** (no turn-end step, or a step that left no `FilesTouched` / stored transcript), **post-commit** now **condenses** into that trailer instead of leaving a checkpoint ID that was never written.\\n> \\n> **prepare-commit-msg** and **post-commit** now share **`liveTranscriptCheckApplies`** for “judge this session by the live transcript.” The live-transcript overlap check uses **`contentCheckOpts.commitFiles()`**—staged files before commit, **committed files** after—so both hooks agree. Post-commit passes **`committedFiles`** into **`sessionHasNewContent`**, derives overlap for those IDLE sessions via **`filesTouchedWithLiveTranscript`**, and **`hasMidTurnClaimant`** is renamed to **`hasLiveTranscriptClaimant`** so transcript-only IDLE writers block file-less ACTIVE readers on the read-only gate.\\n> \\n> New hook integration tests in **`idle_live_transcript_condense_test.go`** cover trailer resolution, unrelated commits, reader vs writer, and sibling worktrees; **`mid_turn_commit_test.go`** updates for the **`commitFiles` set** API on **`sessionHasNewContentFromLiveTranscript`**.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 27884f98d29a8e33957f1b7ea611d0e7a9d7bfbf. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2892/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2892/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2782\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2782/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2782/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2782/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2782\",\n            \"id\": 5858177451,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABIhLC9A\",\n            \"number\": 2782,\n            \"title\": \"Count session and checkpoint tokens from each agent's running total\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-15T00:58:17Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-10T08:21:03Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-11-10T08:21:00Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2782\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2782\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2782.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2782.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-11-10T08:21:00Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2250/changes/cli/1579\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nMakes token accounting correct by construction. Today `entire` works out each checkpoint's tokens by slicing transcripts at offsets, and every double count and undercount we've found comes from those slices starting or ending in the wrong place: turns without file changes went missing (Claude Code `entire status` showed 64k against 285k actually spent), a repeated Stop on a turn that changed files counts the turn twice, a message whose lines straddle an agent's mid-turn commit counts twice, and Copilot counts cache twice.\\n\\nThis PR has each session keep the agent's own running total (the **token ledger**), and each checkpoint store what that total grew by since the session's previous checkpoint.\\n\\n## 1. One shared reader for every agent\\n`agent.ReadCumulativeUsage` reads a session's running total for any agent. It owns the files:\\n- it reads only the bytes appended since the last reading (a no-op reading costs under 1ms), and waits for a line's end;\\n- it detects a rewritten transcript (the 512 bytes before its last offset no longer match) and reads it again, reporting `Restarted`;\\n- it reads a small or rewritten file (OpenCode's export, Droid's `settings.json`, a Claude Code subagent) whole, only when its size or last bytes changed, and never reports that as a restart;\\n- it never follows a symlink or opens a FIFO beside the transcript, and reads `.entire` through its confined reader.\\n\\nEach agent supplies a `UsageCounter` (50–150 lines) built from shared parts in `agent/usage_counting.go`:\\n- `KeyedUsage` counts per-call records once per key, with the agent's rule for a repeated record (`KeepFirst` for replays, `KeepLast` for records re-written, `KeepMostOutput` for streamed messages), a window of open records per file, and per-child sums;\\n- `RunningTotal` sums running totals across a counter restart; `KeyedUsage.CoveredBy` combines records with a running total where an agent writes both.\\n\\n| Agent | What it counts |\\n|---|---|\\n| Claude Code | Assistant messages by `message.id`, most output winning; subagents (and their subagents, Workflow agents) as children |\\n| Codex | `token_usage_record` by `response_id` (replays keep the first copy), combined with segment-summed `token_count` totals; children from the session's subagent inventory |\\n| Copilot CLI | `session.usage_record` by `apiCallId` (cache split out of input), combined with `session.shutdown` totals, which include subagents, so their records are subtracted |\\n| OpenCode | The export's assistant messages, reasoning counted once |\\n| Pi | Per-message usage on every branch |\\n| Factory Droid | `settings.json`'s `tokenUsage`, one call per assistant message |\\n| Antigravity | `PLANNER_RESPONSE` step usage by step index |\\n\\nChild sessions (Droid Workers, OpenCode child sessions) are not read here: #2824's child-session credit counts them once, and ledger checkpoints add it as the per-turn path does.\\n\\n## 2. The token ledger\\n- `SessionState.TokenLedger` (`session/token_ledger.go`, `strategy/token_ledger.go`) holds the running total, read **under the session lock** at turn start, every Stop and every condensation. `TokenUsage` is its total; a checkpoint stores its pending growth; a successful checkpoint write (or attach) marks it checkpointed, and that mark never moves back.\\n  - A repeated or concurrent Stop reads the same total, so it adds nothing — including on a turn that changed files.\\n  - A commit in the middle of a turn stores everything up to the commit; the rest lands in the next checkpoint. A message straddling that commit counts once.\\n- **Which sessions:** sessions this CLI starts at a turn start, for the seven agents above. Legacy states, states created at Stop or by attach, Cursor, Vogon and external agents keep today's per-turn path unchanged.\\n- **Takes over at the first reading with usage**; what the per-turn accounting already checkpointed counts as checkpointed.\\n- **Rewritten transcripts:** a lower reading is ignored (a stale copy), unless the transcript restarted: then the difference moves to `Base` and the total carries on.\\n- **Stop** skips the per-turn token calculation for ledger sessions (for Claude Code it read every subagent transcript only to be discarded).\\n- **Session end** takes a last reading, so usage an agent writes after its final Stop (Copilot's shutdown totals) is counted.\\n- **A new transcript path** for the session is read as a restart, so history the new file repeats is not counted twice.\\n- **Attach** reads the transcript being attached, updates session state under the session lock, and marks as checkpointed exactly what its checkpoint stored.\\n- **Checkpoint metadata** adds `session_token_usage`, the session's running total at that checkpoint, next to `token_usage`.\\n\\n## Checked\\n- **Real sessions, old vs new:** 726 local sessions across six agents on the final code (154 Copilot, 302 Codex, 149 Claude Code, 39 Antigravity, 37 Pi, 45 Droid), plus 36 OpenCode exports on an earlier revision: the shared reader gives exactly the totals of the per-agent code it replaces, and reading each file in nine pieces gives the same totals as one read. The only difference is intended: Droid Workers are no longer the ledger's children (13 sessions), because #2824's child-session credit counts them. Worst incremental step 126ms; largest cursor 38KB (a Claude session with 190 subagents: 123KB).\\n- **Live sessions** (`e2e/tests/token_ledger_test.go`): turns that changed files, one that changed nothing, and an agent commit mid-turn; for every session, checkpoints plus pending equal the session total, which equals a fresh read of the agent's files. Passes for all seven agents: Claude Code, Codex, Copilot, OpenCode, Pi, Droid and Antigravity.\\n\\n## Tests\\n- `TestUsageCounters_Conformance`: every agent with a counter needs a fixture in `testdata/usage/<agent>/`, read whole, in pieces cut at and around every line end, and after a rewrite.\\n- Reader tests: partial lines, rewrites, whole files, symlinked files beside the transcript, files that fail to read and return, moved files, the per-file window, merge policies.\\n- Ledger unit and strategy tests: repeated readings, growth, stale reads, rewrites, child high-water marks, handover from the per-turn accounting, attach under the lock, adopt's copy.\\n- Integration through the real hooks: Claude Code (repeated Stop on a file-changing turn, no-change turns between commits, mid-turn agent commit, a message straddling it, a subagent finishing in a later turn, a rewritten transcript), Codex (repeated Stop, mid-turn commit), Droid (Worker plus the parent's second Stop). With the ledger off, the repeated Stop and the straddling message fail.\\n\\n`mise run lint`: 0 issues. Unit and integration suites pass.\\n\\nSize: +3016/-56 in total.\\n\\n## Not in this PR / known limits\\n- External agents keep the per-turn accounting (the protocol has no incremental token call).\\n- A session's first reading reads its files whole (1.3s on an 82MB Claude transcript with 190 subagents); every later reading reads what was appended. Codex children are read through the inventory again only when a child file changed.\\n- Only an appended transcript can report a rewrite; for an OpenCode undo, or a Droid rewrite, a lower total is ignored until the total passes the old one — an undercount, not a double count.\\n- A crash between a checkpoint write and the state save can store the same growth twice (true of main's accounting too).\\n- A session whose state was lost counts from its next turn start; seeding from the latest checkpoint's `session_token_usage` is a follow-up. Deleting the per-turn path once legacy states age out, and server use of `session_token_usage`, are follow-ups.\\n- Overlaps #2856 (mid-turn double count): for ledger sessions it is superseded; whichever lands second reconciles.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2782/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2782/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2692\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2692/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2692/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2692/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2692\",\n            \"id\": 5747531142,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABHJnjMg\",\n            \"number\": 2692,\n            \"title\": \"Remove shadow branches and line attribution\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-07T15:30:41Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-08T20:34:41Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-08T20:34:37Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2692\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2692\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2692.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2692.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-08T20:34:37Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1509\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAgent turns no longer write anything to git. Older versions committed a full working-tree snapshot to a per-worktree shadow branch (`entire/<commit>-<worktree>`) at every turn end. That was the source of runaway local storage, and cleaning those branches up at the wrong moment made uncondensed work unreachable. Turn ends now record pending work in session state only: the step count, the files the agent touched, and each touched file's git blob hash. A checkpoint is written only when you commit.\\n\\nLine attribution is removed entirely, including the AI/Human/Mixed labels in `entire blame`, which now reports whether each line's commit is linked to a checkpoint. Checkpoint metadata no longer carries `initial_attribution` or `combined_attribution`; entire.io derives the experts counts from those and must be told they stop arriving.\\n\\nCommits link to a session by file name: any committed path the session touched links it, except a new file at a path the agent deleted. Carry-forward after a partial commit compares the recorded hashes with the commit and the worktree, so a `git add -p` remainder, a pending deletion, or a session upgraded from the old state format keeps its uncommitted work. Gitignored files, submodule pointers, and paths inside a submodule or beneath a symlinked directory never enter the tracked files, so they can no longer keep a session pending forever; edits inside a submodule belong to the nested repository's own session. Whether a committed file still has uncommitted agent changes is asked of `git status`, so repositories with `text=auto` or `core.autocrlf` no longer keep fully committed files pending.\\n\\nLifecycle decisions (condensation, the zombie sweep, orphan cleanup, doctor) key on one predicate over session state instead of whether a shadow ref exists. Pending step rows, explain of temporary checkpoints, incremental task checkpoints and the Claude Code post-todo hook install are gone. `checkpoint list --pending` now previews what the next commit's checkpoint will contain.\\n\\nClaude Code gains a transcript prompt extractor, so its prompts no longer depend on `prompt.txt` alone.\\n\\nAddresses #2663, #2378, #2350, #1730, #1807 and #2653. Supersedes trail 1486 (`soph/fix-shadow-after-midturn-commit`), which patches code this PR deletes.\\n\\n## Migrations\\n\\nTurn ends no longer write shadow branches (entire/<commit>-<worktree>): pending work is tracked in session state and checkpoints are written only when you commit. Branches left by older versions are not removed automatically. `entire doctor` and `entire status` report them, and `entire doctor --force` or `entire disable --uninstall` deletes the `entire/<commit>-<worktree>` form without touching session state. The oldest bare `entire/<commit>` form is only ever listed, since a branch of your own named after a short SHA looks the same; `entire clean --all` removes it behind a confirmation. Do not use plain `entire clean` for this: it also clears pending session state. They hold full snapshots of your working tree, so run it once after upgrading. Deleting the branches frees no space by itself: a later `git gc` reclaims it once their objects are two weeks old. `git gc --prune=now` frees it immediately, but it drops every unreachable object in the repository (recently dropped stashes included) and must only run when no other git process is active.\\n\\n`entire blame --json` reports a per-line `status` (`checkpoint`, `commit`, `uncommitted`) instead of `authorship` and `tag`. Its summary reports checkpoint-linked, commit and uncommitted line counts instead of AI/Human/Mixed counts.\\n\\nNew checkpoints no longer include `initial_attribution`, `combined_attribution` or `prompt_attributions`; checkpoints written by older versions keep theirs, and rewrites (explain `--generate`, attach) carry them through unchanged. Session state files written by older versions still load; their attribution and `last_checkpoint_commit_hash` keys are dropped on the next save.\\n\\nThe Claude Code post-todo hook is no longer installed, and any `entire enable` prunes it and says so. Its subcommand stays so older hook configs keep working. An older CLI run against the same tracked `.claude/settings.json` reports the hooks as out of date and re-adds it; this CLI removes it again on the next `entire enable`.\\n\\nCommit pending agent work before downgrading to a previous release: the previous CLI deletes ended but uncondensed session state when its shadow branch is missing, and this release never writes one.\\n\\n`entire session info --json` and `entire session current --json` report the number of turns not yet condensed into a checkpoint as `pending_turns`. The old `checkpoints` field is still emitted with the same value for this release only and will be removed in the next one; switch scripts to `pending_turns`. `entire status --json` adds `legacy_shadow_branches`.\\n\\n## Follow-ups, not in this PR\\n\\nDowngrade safety: the previous CLI deletes ended but uncondensed session state when its shadow branch is missing, and this release never writes one, so rolling back after pending work discards it. The migration note covers it; a patch on the previous release line whose orphan check also requires no pending work, named as the minimum safe downgrade target, is a release-management follow-up (trail finding 01M4DD0R83YC).\\n\\nWorktree scoping, deferred to the #2531 work: scoping the zombie sweep and doctor to the current worktree, retiring the stored transcript copy with the growth check moving to the live transcript position, prompts and transcript for guest-linked commits, and capture following the event's cwd. #2531 itself must be reworked after this lands, since it pins sessions through shadow-branch steps; #2486 is expected to close in its favour.\\n\\nTracked on the priority list for go-git (#DM2KFD6): its worktree hashing lacks gitattributes, filter, and index-aware CRLF handling, which is why this PR asks `git status` instead of hashing; porting that logic into go-git would let the CLI drop the subprocess.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n`mise run check` (fmt, lint, unit, integration, Vogon canary) and `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` on the final tree, with a cold lint cache, after merging main at `375819df95`. Every commit builds and vets on its own. A focused security review of the cross-worktree stored-transcript read (a path taken from on-disk session state, gated by `git worktree list` registration and the `.entire` anchor) found no findings. The only local failures are the known OpenCode seed-cache guard and the Claude config-probe timeout, which passes alone.\\n\\nNew unit, integration and command tests cover: recorded-hash carry-forward (partial commits, pending, committed and re-created deletions, upgraded sessions, an unreadable worktree); name-based linking; gitignored and submodule paths on every capture route; the doctor legacy-branch check; the `--pending` preview in text and JSON without a TTY; and the Claude prompt extractor against the real transcript fixture.\\n\\nReal-agent E2E passed on `44ebccb136` for every leg (claude-code, codex, cursor-cli, copilot-cli, factoryai-droid, opencode, antigravity, roger-roger, and Windows): https://github.com/entireio/cli/actions/runs/37655720329. One changed expectation is `TestInteractiveNewFileLinksAfterUserRewrite`, which now expects a trailer after a user rewrites an agent-created file.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **High Risk**\\n> This rewrites core session-to-checkpoint lifecycle, persistent metadata contracts, and labs blame JSON—high blast radius for upgrades, downstream consumers (e.g. entire.io attribution fields), and real-agent E2E behavior.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Turn-end work stays out of git.** Agent stops no longer commit working-tree snapshots to `entire/<commit>-<worktree>` shadow branches; **SaveStep** only updates local session state (step count, files touched, content hashes, transcript copy). Permanent checkpoints are written at **`git commit`** onto metadata refs, matching the updated README/CLAUDE contract.\\n> \\n> **Checkpoint storage and metadata slim down.** The ephemeral/shadow-branch store (`EphemeralStore`, `WriteTemporary`, task step writes, related benchmarks and tests) is removed. **`CheckpointAttribution`** and all **`Attribution`** fields (`initial_attribution`, `combined_attribution`, `prompt_attributions`, `EphemeralBranch`) drop out of `api/checkpoint` and git/fs backends.\\n> \\n> **`entire blame` / `why` semantics change.** Per-line **AI/Human/Mixed** authorship is gone; JSON uses **`status`** (`checkpoint`, `commit`, `uncommitted`) and summaries count checkpoint-linked vs other commits. Help text states Entire does not attribute lines to AI vs humans—only whether the blame commit carries an **Entire-Checkpoint** trailer.\\n> \\n> **Claude Code hooks and prompts.** The **post-todo** (`TaskCreate|TaskUpdate`) hook is no longer installed; **`entire enable`** prunes stale installs while keeping the subcommand registered. New **`prompts.go`** implements **`PromptExtractor`** / **`TranscriptPromptExtractor`** so user prompts come from transcript bytes with injected/meta lines filtered.\\n> \\n> **Operator/docs touchpoints.** `checkpoint list --pending` documents **`is_next_checkpoint`** preview semantics; legacy shadow branches are called out for **`entire doctor`** / **`entire clean`**. E2E/debug skills swap “attribution” for **file tracking** language.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 19b37c48aedde9efe68606e4a9ca48b42ae13064. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2692/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2692/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2779\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2779/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2779/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2779/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2779\",\n            \"id\": 5855508859,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABIfDJFA\",\n            \"number\": 2779,\n            \"title\": \"Count a turn's step and tokens once when its Stop repeats\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-14T20:55:03Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-16T06:03:47Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-16T06:03:47Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2779\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2779\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2779.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2779.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1576\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Bug\\n\\nA Stop for a file-changing turn can reach Entire more than once: a retried hook, a duplicate delivery, or two hook processes racing. Each repeat runs SaveStep again. It adds the turn's tokens to `TokenUsage` and `CheckpointTokenUsage` again, and increments `StepCount` again.\\n\\nMeasured with the real hooks before this fix:\\n\\n| Agent | Session total | Pending window | `StepCount` | Committed checkpoint |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Claude Code (turn 100/10) | 200/20 | 200/20 | 2 | 100/10 (correct) |\\n| Cursor (turn 200/50) | 400/100 | 400/100 | 2 | 400/100 |\\n\\n- **Claude Code:** the committed checkpoint is right because condensation recounts it from the transcript. The session total stays doubled.\\n- **Cursor:** the hook tokens double end to end, including the committed checkpoint.\\n- **Git:** no extra commit is written, because SaveStep writes no git objects.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nSaveStep records which turn its last step came from, in the same locked mutation that adds the tokens and the step:\\n\\n- **A repeat** is a Stop that read a transcript of the same byte size as the recorded step. A new turn grows the transcript. This covers a repeat whose pre-prompt state an earlier Stop already removed, and a turn that never had a TurnStart.\\n- **A Stop whose pre-prompt nonce** (`PrePromptState.TurnNonce`) **differs from the recorded one** is always a new turn.\\n  - TurnStart writes the nonce before it takes any session lock, so a TurnStart that times out on the lock still gets a fresh one. Such a TurnStart never rotates `TurnID`, which is why this is not keyed on `TurnID`.\\n  - A matching nonce alone is not enough: a Stop that ran late can read the next turn's nonce from the per-session pre-prompt file.\\n- **A repeat** still merges its files, but adds no tokens and no step.\\n  - Exception: if a commit condensed the window in between, the repeat counts one step, because its files are new pending work.\\n\\n## Legitimate paths preserved\\n\\n- **Normal Stop after TurnStart:** counts once.\\n- **First Stop after a mid-session enable, and turns with no TurnStart** (Droid exec mode, a turn the agent starts on its own): each grows the transcript, so each still counts.\\n- **A TurnStart that hit the session-lock timeout:** gets a new nonce, so its turn counts.\\n- **Antigravity's suppressed mid-turn TurnStart, mid-turn commits, and Ctrl-C recovery:** unchanged.\\n- **Compaction, Droid Workers and attach:** do not go through SaveStep.\\n\\n## Overlap with #2722\\n\\n#2722 applies a turn's tokens at the turn-end transition when the turn changes no files, gated on the ACTIVE phase. This PR covers the file-changing path, so the two do not overlap in behaviour. They do conflict textually: this PR wraps SaveStep's token block, which #2722 extracts into `applyTurnTokenUsage`. Whichever merges second resolves that.\\n\\nFollow-up after both land: #2722's no-change path should record the same marker. Otherwise a no-change Stop followed by a file-changing repeat counts the turn twice.\\n\\nRemaining gaps, unchanged from main:\\n- A Stop-hook continuation in the same turn still counts its tokens from transcript line 0.\\n- A late duplicate that reads the next turn's pre-prompt state is not caught.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- **Integration, with real hooks:**\\n  - Claude Code: a repeated Stop, concurrent Stops, a next turn after the repeat, Stops without TurnStart (plus a repeat of one), and an unprompted turn after a prompted one.\\n  - Cursor: a repeated Stop and concurrent Stops, both checked through to the committed checkpoint.\\n- **Unit (SaveStep):**\\n  - a repeated nonce;\\n  - a matching nonce over a grown transcript (a late Stop holding the next turn's nonce) still counts;\\n  - a new nonce while `TurnID` stays unrotated;\\n  - matching on transcript size when there is no nonce;\\n  - turn identity unknown;\\n  - a repeat after condensation counts a step but no tokens, and keeps `TranscriptIdentifierAtStart`.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2779/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2779/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2897\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2897/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2897/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2897/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2897\",\n            \"id\": 6030328285,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABKpeQ3Q\",\n            \"number\": 2897,\n            \"title\": \"transcript: one Codex item mapping for stored rollouts and live streams\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-25T22:56:14Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-30T04:15:13Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-30T04:15:09Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2897\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2897\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2897.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2897.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-30T04:15:09Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2565/changes/cli/1686\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nCurrent Codex rollouts record every item (commands, file changes, MCP calls, web searches, messages) as `item_completed` events, and Codex's app-server daemon sends the same items live as `item/started` / `item/completed` notifications. This PR maps both through one Codex item model, so a stored checkpoint and a live stream of the same session show the same lines.\\n\\n- `internal/transcript/codexitem` (stdlib-only, internal like Pi's parser): decodes an item from either encoding into one `Item`. A table writes every item kind in both encodings and checks they decode equal (small inline test data, no fixture files).\\n- `Convert` takes an item path for rollouts whose first turn records user or agent message items; older rollouts keep the `response_item` path unchanged. The choice is made on the whole rollout, so `Convert` and `ConvertWithBoundary` agree (every StartLine is tested).\\n  - Commands are `Bash` tool uses with the script from `<shell> -lc/-c` (shell quoting, including `$'…'`, decoded) and their output; file changes are `FileChange` with each file's diff; MCP calls `server.tool`; web searches, image views and sub-agent spawns map to tool uses with results.\\n  - Usage per model call as on main (`codexUsageTracker` over `total_token_usage` snapshots), on the call's last assistant line; a reasoning-only call gets a usage-only line.\\n  - Items without an ID or of unmapped kinds (reasoning, plans, compaction) are skipped.\\n- `transcript.CodexNotificationRecords(method, params, CodexLive)`: the public entry for a live stream, mapping one daemon item notification with the same mapping (plus text/output so far for running items). Tested equal to `Convert`'s records for every kind in that table.\\n\\nThe live consumer is `entire stream codex` in entireio/entire-stream (in progress).\\n\\n`mise run check` passes (the claudecode config-probe 5 s timeouts seen under load pass alone).\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Rxmv1Yre5x8Re4F6G9FrUm\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes Codex transcript shape and conversion routing for newer rollouts; behavior is heavily tested against fixtures but wrong path detection or item mapping would affect checkpoints and live streams.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **`internal/transcript/codexitem`**, a stdlib-only parser that turns Codex **`item_completed`** rollout lines and app-server **`item/started` / `item/completed`** params into one normalized **`Item`** (messages, commands, file changes, MCP, web search, spawns, etc.), including shell script extraction from `<shell> -lc/-c` argv and daemon command strings.\\n> \\n> **`Convert`** now picks an **item path** when the rollout’s first turn has user/agent message items (`hasCodexItems` on the full file); older rollouts still use the **`response_item`** path. The item path emits **one transcript line per item** (e.g. `Bash`, `FileChange`, `server.tool`), attaches **per-model-call usage** on the call’s last assistant line (same `token_count` delta rules as before), and skips unmapped kinds (reasoning, compaction). **`CodexNotificationRecords`** exposes the same mapping for live daemon notifications, with **`CodexLive`** for partial agent text, command output, and interrupted turns.\\n> \\n> Docs in **`transcript/README.md`** describe the item vs `response_item` behavior; guards allow **`codexitem`** as an internal parser dependency and whitelist the file-change **`diff`** JSON tag in git diff scanning.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 2f4372adea7427dd891527cabdedf9fd4fa43ebe. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2897/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2897/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2861\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2861/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2861/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2861/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2861\",\n            \"id\": 5973409843,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABJ8ghhA\",\n            \"number\": 2861,\n            \"title\": \"Add an ip category to PII redaction\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-22T05:04:47Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-23T08:09:21Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-23T08:09:19Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2861\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2861\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2861.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2861.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-23T08:09:19Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1654\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nPII redaction covers email, phone and US street addresses. With it fully on, internal network addresses (`ssh deploy@10.24.3.17`, `db at 192.168.1.40:5432`, `fd12::1`) are stored in checkpoints as written.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nNew `ip` category, token `[REDACTED_IP]`, **on by default when `redaction.pii.enabled` is true** (like email and phone; `\\\"ip\\\": false` turns it off).\\n\\nA dotted quad is ambiguous in coding transcripts: version numbers (`1.17.2.3`) and user agents (`Chrome/154.0.0.0`) share the shape. So, like Presidio and Cloud DLP, a match is redacted only when it looks like an address in use:\\n\\n- private, link-local, or CGNAT (`10/8`, `172.16/12`, `192.168/16`, `169.254/16`, `100.64/10`, `fc00::/7`, `fe80::/10`), or\\n- network syntax around it: `://`, `@`, `:port`, `/cidr`, `->`, or\\n- a network word on the same line (`ip`, `host`, `server`, `ssh`, `tcp`, `dns`, `connect`, ...), or a JSON key that names an address (`host`, `remote_addr`, `HOST_IP`, `clientIP`).\\n\\nNever redacted: loopback, unspecified, `0.0.0.0/8`, `255.255.255.255`, `N.0.0.0`, documentation addresses (`192.0.2.0/24`, `198.51.100.0/24`, `203.0.113.0/24`, `2001:db8::/32`, `3fff::/20`), the first address of each private block (`10.0.0.0/8` in code), the value of a version label (`Version=10.0.0.0`, `AssemblyVersion(\\\"10.1.2.3\\\")`), and anything continuing a longer token (`v1.2.3.4`, `go1.2.3.4`, `1.2.3.4-rc1`, OIDs, `u64::from`, `a[1::2]`). Ports stay visible (`[REDACTED_IP]:443`).\\n\\nKnown limits (documented, and tagged `limit:` in the table below): a public address with no context (a plain list, an access-log client address, `\\\"PublicIpAddress\\\": \\\"...\\\"` in AWS CLI output) is not redacted, nor is an address in a path field such as cwd or file_path, which no layer scans; a version number next to a network word on the same line, or in a private range without a version label, can be.\\n\\n## Behavior changes to call out in the release notes\\n\\n- Repos that already have `pii.enabled: true` start redacting IPs on upgrade.\\n- Older CLIs reject unknown `pii` keys, so a committed `\\\"ip\\\": false` breaks teammates on older versions; the docs say to set it only after upgrading.\\n- A value under a credential key (password, client_secret, api_key) that also contains an email, phone number or IP address is now replaced whole; before, only the PII was redacted and the secret beside it was kept.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n- `redact/testdata/ip_lines.txt`: 72 lines shaped like tool output from .NET, JVM, Python, Node, Go, Kubernetes, Docker, AWS/Terraform, Linux networking, SSH/Git and logs, with the addresses that must be redacted marked. `go test ./redact -run TestIPLines -v` logs **93% precision and 78% recall**. The lines lean toward hard cases, so read these as a regression gauge, not a population rate.\\n- No existing library fit: goredact and betterleaks have no IP detector; incognigo's `IPAddress()` has no context, so in coding transcripts it flags version numbers, `c::d`-style code and loopback.\\n- `BenchmarkRedactJSONLBytes_PII`: about +4% time with ip on; byte-scan prefilters keep the IP regexes off most strings.\\n- End to end with the branch binary in a test repo, run before the latest commit (whose changes do not affect these inputs): the committed checkpoint has `[REDACTED_IP]` for the private, public-with-port and IPv6 addresses, and leaves `1.17.2.3`, `Chrome/154.0.0.0`, `v1.2.3.4`, `127.0.0.1:8080`, `u64::from` and `a[1::2]` untouched.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- `redact/pii_ip_test.go`: 57 redacted and 49 not-redacted cases, the category toggle, `String` and `JSONLContent` integration, network-key detection, and `TestIPLines` over the table.\\n- Settings strict decode and local merge of `pii.ip`; category defaults via the extracted `piiConfigFromSettings`.\\n- `mise run check` passes (two timing tests in unrelated packages failed under heavy machine load and pass on rerun).\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes what gets stored in checkpoints when PII is enabled (new default-on IP redaction) and adds heuristic detection that may miss bare public IPs or occasionally redact version-like strings near network context.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds an **`ip` PII redaction category** (`[REDACTED_IP]`) that is **on by default** when `redaction.pii.enabled` is true, with optional `\\\"ip\\\": false` in settings (decode/merge + docs on older CLI compatibility).\\n> \\n> Detection is **context-aware** for IPv4/IPv6: private/link-local/CGNAT, URL/port/CIDR/arrow syntax, or nearby network words trigger redaction; loopback, version strings, bare public IPs without context, and similar false positives are skipped. Implementation lives in new `redact/pii_ip.go`, wired through `PIIIP` in the PII layer with byte-scan prefilters.\\n> \\n> PII settings → runtime mapping is centralized in **`piiConfigFromSettings`** (replacing inline wiring in `EnsureRedactionConfigured`). Security docs describe behavior and limits; tests cover settings merge, category defaults, redaction cases, and a PII+IP benchmark.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit a3f43fbb329f0b36524762b63fc3d48ded074522. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2861/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2861/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2334\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2334/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2334/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2334/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2334\",\n            \"id\": 5400957958,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABC2XDtw\",\n            \"number\": 2334,\n            \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): count subagents in live condensation\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-09-09T14:43:15Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-10T20:12:46Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-10T20:12:44Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2334\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2334\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2334.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2334.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-10T20:12:44Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1275\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nA mid-turn commit that condenses when no shadow branch resolves may have no `CheckpointTokenUsage` to draw the subagent total from, so the committed checkpoint recorded `\\\"subagent_tokens\\\": null` even though the subagent transcripts were still sitting on disk. This closes that documented gap.\\n\\n- `extractSessionDataFromLiveTranscript` now resolves the session's subagents directory (`paths.SubagentsDir`, the same layout `lifecycle.go`, `review/manifest.go`, and `agentimport` use) and passes it to `agent.CalculateTokenUsage`, so the live path counts subagents instead of always yielding nil.\\n- That extractor returns a cumulative-since-session-start total, so `calculateLiveTranscriptTokenUsage` rescopes it against `SubagentTokensBaseline` before it becomes checkpoint metadata — the same subtraction `SaveStep` already does, so later checkpoints report their own share rather than re-reporting the session total.\\n- The fresh cumulative snapshot is kept on `state.TokenUsage`, because that is what `resetCheckpointWindow` snapshots as the *next* window's baseline. `applyBackfilledSessionTokenUsage` uses the explicitly directional `replaceSubagentTokensFrom`; leaving the scoped window delta on session state would make the next baseline regress to that delta.\\n- The full scan runs only when no checkpoint-scoped subagent total already exists, the agent supports subagent extraction, the session ID is non-empty, and a real non-symlinked subagent directory exists. Re-reading every subagent transcript costs roughly 29x the main-transcript-only call, so each gate preserves the cheap path where possible.\\n- Shadow-branch condensation is deliberately unchanged: it still fills from the already-rescoped `state.CheckpointTokenUsage` through `fillMissingSubagentTokensFrom`.\\n- `CLAUDE.md`'s token-usage-scoping paragraph now describes both paths instead of only the shadow one.\\n\\nThis supersedes #1394. The broader loss during normal condensation was already fixed by `a5cf26df8`; this closes the remaining live pre-`SaveStep` case.\\n\\n## Credit\\n\\nThis work originated in #1394 by Bryan Wade (@stale2000), who identified the missing subagent totals and contributed the original tests and fix. Thank you for the investigation and original contribution.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- `TestCalculateLiveTranscriptTokenUsage_RescopesSubagentCumulativeTotal` — drives two logical checkpoints over a real Claude Code transcript plus a subagent transcript: the first records the full 200, and after `RebaselineSubagentTokens` the second records only the 60 the subagent grew by, while session state advances to the 260 cumulative. It also asserts the backfill does not overwrite that cumulative with the checkpoint delta.\\n- `TestLiveSubagentsDir_OnlyEnablesNeededSupportedDirectoryScan` — pins the cost/capability/session-ID gates and rejects regular files and symlinked session directories.\\n- `TestExtractSessionDataFromLiveTranscript_IncludesScopedSubagentTokens` — exercises the production live entry point across two windows, including a nonzero transcript start and baseline subtraction.\\n- The pre-existing `TestCondenseSessionByID_CapturesSubagentBaselineViaRealResetPath` and the `SaveStep` rescoping tests continue to cover the shadow-branch path end to end.\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes checkpoint token metadata for a specific condensation timing (live pre-SaveStep); incorrect baseline math could misreport subagent usage in checkpoints, but the pattern matches existing rescoping and is covered by new tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Live mid-turn condensation** (before `SaveStep` has filled `CheckpointTokenUsage`) now records **subagent token usage** in checkpoint metadata instead of omitting it.\\n> \\n> The live transcript path calls new `calculateLiveTranscriptTokenUsage`, which resolves the subagent directory via `paths.SubagentsDir`, runs the same cumulative extractor as other live reads, then **subtracts `SubagentTokensBaseline`** so each checkpoint stores a delta rather than re-reporting prior subagent usage. Shadow-branch condensation still uses the cheaper `withSubagentTokensFrom` / `CheckpointTokenUsage` path.\\n> \\n> Docs in `CLAUDE.md` describe this branch of token scoping; the old “known gap” comment on `withSubagentTokensFrom` is removed. Tests cover cumulative rescoping across two logical checkpoints.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 159c668df17299d5eb50ec60beb732d0acfaad18. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\\n\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2334/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2334/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2777\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2777/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2777/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2777/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2777\",\n            \"id\": 5854945725,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABIemuhw\",\n            \"number\": 2777,\n            \"title\": \"Count Claude subagents named only in the structured tool result\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-14T20:16:12Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-16T20:53:55Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-16T20:53:52Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2777\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2777\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2777.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2777.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-16T20:53:52Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1574\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nForeground Explore and Plan subagents in Claude Code are missing from checkpoints. Their tokens never reach `subagent_tokens`, and their transcripts are never searched for modified files.\\n\\n`spawnedAgentIDs` finds subagents from the `agentId: <id>` line in an Agent tool result's text. Foreground Explore and Plan results are a hand-back report with no such line. This is verified on Claude Code 2.1.289, 2.1.294, 2.1.296 and 2.1.300. So `subagents/agent-<id>.jsonl` is never read. In one run that was about 52k tokens, roughly 40% of the session.\\n\\nThe SubagentStop hook doesn't make up for it: a foreground agent that changed no files gets no task record.\\n\\nForeground general-purpose results and background (`async_launched`) results still print the line, so they were counted correctly.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nEvery Agent result line names its agent in the structured `toolUseResult.agentId`, whatever its status. The forked-skill scan already read that field for `status: \\\"forked\\\"`.\\n\\n- **Every status:** the scan now reads `toolUseResult.agentId` for every status. Empty or path-unsafe IDs are ignored.\\n- **The structured ID wins:** if a tool result names an agent there, that result's `agentId:` text is never read, because the text can quote other agents' IDs.\\n- **Text as the fallback:** results with no structured ID, as in older transcripts, still fall back to the text. The fallback now reads the last `agentId:`, which is the trailer Claude Code appends, instead of the first.\\n\\nBoth callers, `CalculateTotalTokenUsage` and `ExtractAllModifiedFiles`, go through `spawnedAgentIDs`, so they are unchanged. Subagent transcripts are keyed by agent ID, so an agent found both ways is still read once. The parent's own usage counts only assistant lines, so it can't absorb a subagent's.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- **`TestStructuredAgentCountsTowardSession`:** a table with a forked-skill case and a foreground-agent case. Each goes through both tokens and modified files. The foreground case fails on main.\\n- **`TestToolResultAgentIDs`:** covers every status, follow-ups, inline skills, empty and unsafe IDs, and assistant lines.\\n- **`TestSpawnedAgentIDs_StructuredIDWinsOverText`:** checks that a quoted ID never wins, including in a follow-up, and that results with no structured ID, or with a non-object `toolUseResult`, fall back to the text.\\n- **`TestExtractAgentIDFromText`:** a new row where the report quotes another ID before the trailer.\\n\\n## Recorded transcripts\\n\\n`CalculateTotalTokenUsage` was run on six recorded sessions. Values are input / cache creation / cache read / output / API calls, with ground truth taken from the subagent transcripts after deduplicating by message id:\\n\\n| Case | Main | This branch (equals ground truth) |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Foreground Explore, 2.1.296 | none | 6 / 18243 / 33410 / 785 / 3 |\\n| Foreground Explore, 2.1.294 | none | 6 / 14725 / 26348 / 810 / 3 |\\n| Foreground Explore, 2.1.289 | none | 26 / 15504 / 28614 / 553 / 3 |\\n| Foreground Plan, 2.1.296 | none | 4 / 11254 / 22435 / 729 / 2 |\\n| Background, 2.1.296 | same | 6 / 16544 / 29990 / 856 / 3 |\\n| Foreground general-purpose, 2.1.296 | same | 6 / 18651 / 33969 / 379 / 3 |\\n\\n## Live check (Claude Code 2.1.300, Codex 0.156.1)\\n\\nEach run went through the whole path in a fresh scratch repo: `entire enable`, then the agent prompt with real hooks, then `git commit`, then reading the checkpoint metadata. Each agent ran once with a binary built from main and once with this branch. Live numbers vary from run to run, so each run is compared with its own ground truth.\\n\\n| Agent | Binary | Parent `token_usage` | `subagent_tokens` | Ground truth (subagent) |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Claude, foreground Explore | main | 8 / 22714 / 107234 / 770 / 4 (exact) | **missing** | 4 / 19786 / 17502 / 446 / 2 |\\n| Claude, foreground Explore | this branch | 8 / 22224 / 108230 / 911 / 4 (exact) | 4 / 19899 / 17600 / 513 / 2 | 4 / 19899 / 17600 / 513 / 2 |\\n| Codex, `spawn_agent` child | main | 11471 / 0 / 50176 / 310 / 4 (exact) | 10112 / 0 / 98816 / 719 / 6 | exact |\\n| Codex, `spawn_agent` child | this branch | 10990 / 0 / 50176 / 292 / 4 (exact) | 13805 / 0 / 48128 / 461 / 4 | exact |\\n\\nCodex counts child threads through its SubagentStart/SubagentStop ledger, which this change doesn't touch. It behaves the same on both binaries: exact subagent tokens, the child's task record, and `docs/red.md` attributed.\\n\\n## Follow-up\\n\\nFactory Droid has its own text-only `ExtractSpawnedAgentIDs` (`factoryaidroid/transcript.go`). It hasn't been checked for the same gap.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes how spawned subagent transcripts are resolved for token usage and modified-file extraction; incorrect parsing could mis-attribute session metadata, but scope is limited to Claude Code transcript parsing with extensive new tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Fixes missing **foreground Explore/Plan** (and other) Claude subagents in checkpoints by discovering agent IDs from structured `toolUseResult.agentId` on tool results, not only from `agentId:` text or forked-skill `status: \\\"forked\\\"`.\\n> \\n> **`forkedSkillAgentIDs`** is replaced by **`toolResultAgentIDs`**, which scans any user tool result with `toolUseResult.agentId` (completed, async_launched, forked, etc.), tracks which `tool_use_id`s were named structurally, and keeps the first launcher per agent ID. **`spawnedAgentIDs`** merges those IDs first, then falls back to text parsing only for results that did not name an agent structurally (older transcripts).\\n> \\n> **`extractAgentIDFromText`** now takes the **last** `agentId:` in the result text so quoted IDs in the report body do not win over Claude’s trailer line.\\n> \\n> Tests cover structured-vs-text precedence, follow-ups, foreground agents in token/file aggregation, and the last-`agentId:` behavior.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 1cbb38f8f3a27a1304b2c7dd8f11a17d6555c33a. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2777/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2777/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2687\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2687/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2687/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2687/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2687\",\n            \"id\": 5735711304,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABHAKT8w\",\n            \"number\": 2687,\n            \"title\": \"Record agents spawned by Claude Code's Workflow tool and forked skills\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-06T21:33:39Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-08T17:48:18Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-08T17:48:15Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2687\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2687\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2687.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2687.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-08T17:48:15Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1505\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAgents that Claude Code's `Workflow` tool launches, and agents that skills with `context: fork` run in, left no trace in the checkpoint: no `tasks/` entry, no stored transcript, no subagent tokens. Entire's launch hooks (`PreToolUse`/`PostToolUse`) match only the `Agent` tool, so neither kind of agent got an in-flight record, and each of its `SubagentStop` events was skipped as \\\"no live in-flight marker\\\".\\n\\n### Workflow agents\\n\\nClaude Code fires `SubagentStart` for every workflow agent with `agent_id` and `agent_type: \\\"workflow-subagent\\\"`. This PR:\\n\\n- installs Claude Code's `SubagentStart` hook with matcher `workflow-subagent`, so direct `Agent` launches never invoke it (the parser also ignores any other agent type);\\n- records a live task record per workflow agent, keyed by its `agent_id` (a Workflow call's `tool_use_id` is shared by all its agents); a repeated start cannot reset a record still in session state;\\n- lets the existing `SubagentStop` correlation by `agent_id` complete it from `agent_transcript_path` under `subagents/workflows/<run>/`;\\n- makes the transcript fallbacks (a commit while an agent is still running, the SessionEnd sweep) also look in the run directory, through one shared resolver in `paths` that replaces two duplicates;\\n- counts workflow agents in the session's `subagent_tokens`, for the runs the parent transcript launched (the launch's structured `toolUseResult.runId`, with the result's `Run ID: wf_…` text as a fallback), so `entire import` puts their tokens on the launching turn; an agent found in more than one run counts once, from its newest transcript;\\n- logs `agent_id`/`agent_type` when a `SubagentStop` is skipped.\\n\\n### Forked skills\\n\\nA skill with `context: fork` runs in an agent of its own. Claude Code names that agent only in the `Skill` call's result (`status: \\\"forked\\\"`, `agentId`, `background`); its `SubagentStart` reports an ordinary type such as `general-purpose`, so no `SubagentStart` matcher can single it out. This PR:\\n\\n- installs `PostToolUse[Skill]` → the existing `post-task` command. A forked result records the launch under the Skill call's `tool_use_id` with the agent's ID, and the agent's `SubagentStop` completes it. Inline skills produce no event; the hook exits after a JSON parse for them;\\n- treats a missing `background` flag as still running; a fork reported finished (`background: false`) completes at once with files from its transcript only, since no `PreToolUse` baseline exists for a Skill call (otherwise every uncommitted worktree change would be credited to it);\\n- reads the agent from the parent transcript's structured `toolUseResult`, so its tokens count in the session's `subagent_tokens` and its edits in turn-end file attribution;\\n- logs a re-woken agent's repeated `SubagentStop` at debug instead of warn: a background agent stops again each time a child it launched wakes it (this also applies to background `Agent` subagents with background children).\\n\\nExisting installs get the new hooks with `entire enable`; until then `entire status` and `entire doctor` report the Claude hook config as outdated.\\n\\nPart of #2685 (and the forked-skill case of #2215): this PR gives each workflow agent and each forked skill's agent a task record and counts them in the session's subagent tokens. Each record's own `token_usage` is still undercounted (see below), which is being fixed in a separate PR; #2685 should close once both are in.\\n\\n## Verified\\n\\n- Live, Claude Code 2.1.291, binary from this branch: a Workflow running three parallel agents (each writing its own file) produced `tasks/<agent_id>/` ×3 with `task.json`, the agent transcript and the right file; `checkpoint explain --json` lists 3 tasks. Session `subagent_tokens` equals the summed `message.usage` of the three agent transcripts before and after the commit, with no double counting in a later checkpoint. A direct `Agent` subagent in the same session still gets exactly one `toolu_…`-keyed record, and Entire's `subagent-start` did not run for it. No warnings in `entire.log`.\\n- Same reproduction on `main`: no `tasks/`, `\\\"tasks\\\": []`, no `subagent_tokens`, three skipped `SubagentStop`s.\\n- Live, forked skill (binary from this branch): one session running an inline fan-out skill, a `context: fork` skill whose agent launches two background `Agent` subagents, and two `run_in_background` `Agent` calls produced 7 task records with the right files and no duplicates, including `tasks/<skill tool_use_id>/` for the forked agent (`task_description` `/fanout-fork`, full transcript). Session `subagent_tokens` went from 8 API calls on `main` to 12, now including the forked agent's own calls. On `main` the forked agent had no record.\\n- `mise run check` passes. New tests (hook install/upgrade/uninstall/health, parse filter, repeated start, resolver layout, token discovery and dedup, import turn split, forked-skill parse/launch modes, integration tests including a commit while an agent is still running and a finished fork beside unrelated worktree changes) fail on `main`.\\n\\n## Not in this PR\\n\\n- Per-task `token_usage` undercounts: it is computed at `SubagentStop`, before Claude Code has written the agent's final message to its transcript, so a task record misses its last API call(s) while the stored transcript has them (live: `task.json` 1 call, stored transcript 2). The same race exists on `main` for direct `Agent` subagents. Session `subagent_tokens` is computed later and is correct. Fix in a separate PR off `main` (recompute each task's tokens from the transcript stored at checkpoint time).\\n- A forked skill's agent stops once per wake; the first stop completes its record, so the record's `files` and `token_usage` stop there (live: 2 of 4 calls). The stored transcript is complete, the parent's next turn end still attributes later edits, and the per-task token PR recomputes tokens from it.\\n- Agents launched inside a forked skill get task records but are not in the session's `subagent_tokens` (their IDs are in the forked agent's transcript, not the parent's), the same limit as other nested subagents. To be handled with the token PR.\\n- A task record's `files` come from the agent's transcript, so files an agent changes through Bash (`echo >>`) are not listed on its record; they still appear in the session's `files_touched`. Same as direct `Agent` subagents.\\n- #2685 also reports a fourth, late `SubagentStop` for three agents; two live runs here produced exactly three. The skip log now includes `agent_id` and `agent_type`, so a repeat can be identified.\\n- Line attribution of subagent edits to the human: #2653.\\n- `session adopt` does not yet accept a workflow agent's transcript path.\\n- The web task view still needs checking with task ids that are agent ids rather than parent `tool_use_id`s.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2687/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2687/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2795\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2795/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2795/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2795/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2795\",\n            \"id\": 5883720481,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABI1kCbQ\",\n            \"number\": 2795,\n            \"title\": \"Add a release mirror with a GitHub fallback\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-16T11:56:03Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-20T08:01:53Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-20T08:01:52Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2795\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2795\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2795.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2795.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-20T08:01:52Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1591\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nEvery install and update path resolved a version and fetched bytes from GitHub alone, so a GitHub outage made an **already-published** release unobtainable — not just unreleasable. This publishes the same artifacts to a second origin we own and reads ours first, with GitHub as the fallback.\\n\\nReading ours first is deliberate: a fallback that only runs during an incident is a fallback nobody has tested. This way every install exercises the path.\\n\\n## What reads what\\n\\n`versioncheck.versionOrigins` is an ordered chain (`install.entire.com`, then `api.github.com`) walked by `fetchLatestForChannel`. `scripts/install.sh` walks the same two origins for archives and checksums. `httpTimeout` (2s) bounds the **whole chain**, and each candidate gets an equal share of what is left — so a primary that hangs cannot swallow the budget and starve the fallback, which would leave update checks worse off than before the second origin existed.\\n\\nTwo rules, both borrowed from `checkpoint/remote/checkpoint_ref.go`:\\n\\n1. **Fail open.** Every origin failing is reported as one error, never as \\\"you are up to date\\\" or \\\"there is nothing to install\\\".\\n2. **A definite bad answer aborts; an unreachable one advances.** A checksum *mismatch* exits rather than falling through — bytes that disagree with their own origin's checksums mean that origin is corrupt, and retrying elsewhere would hide it. Bad *metadata* goes the other way and advances: while discovering a version another origin may simply know better.\\n\\nPublishing inverts rule 1 on purpose. `publish-channel-manifest.sh` fails **closed** — if it cannot read the current pointer it refuses to publish, because its only question is \\\"can I prove this move is forward\\\". The write is conditional on the object the guard inspected (`--if-match`), so a concurrent publisher cannot leave the pointer at the older version.\\n\\n## What gets published\\n\\n| Key | Contents |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `v<version>/` | archives and `checksums.txt`, immutable |\\n| `channels/{stable,nightly}.json` | the channel pointer, `max-age=60` |\\n| `installers/install.{sh,ps1}` | the install scripts, `max-age=300`, stable only |\\n| `scoop/entire.json` | the Scoop manifest with URLs repointed at this origin, stable only |\\n\\nOrder inside `release.yml` is load-bearing: artifacts, then the macOS Developer ID check, then the pointer, then the shared keys. The shared keys come **after** the pointer — which looks backwards — because they are not versioned, so publishing them first means a release the pointer refuses leaves them rolled back with nothing advanced.\\n\\n`mod_timestamp` is pinned to the commit so rebuilding a tag is byte-identical. Without it a retried release would re-upload different bytes and a different `checksums.txt` to URLs cached immutable for a year, and a mixed edge cache is a hard install failure under rule 2.\\n\\n## Windows\\n\\n`scoop install https://install.entire.com/scoop/entire.json` installs with no bucket and therefore no git, and `scoop update` re-fetches that URL and upgrades in place. Both verified against Scoop v0.6.0 on a Windows VM. The bucket manifest keeps its GitHub URLs, so the ordinary `scoop install entire` path is unchanged — this is an additional route, not a replacement that puts every Scoop install behind one origin.\\n\\n`install.ps1` itself is **not** covered: it is mirrored so it can be fetched, but it still resolves versions through `api.github.com` and downloads archives from GitHub releases. That is the remaining Windows gap and it is recorded in the design doc.\\n\\n## Turning it on\\n\\nThe publishing side is inert until `ENTIRE_RELEASE_BUCKET` is set; deleting it and rerunning restores exactly the old behaviour. The variables are now set and `install.entire.com` is serving, so the next stable release is the first that mirrors. After it, check that `channels/stable.json` names the new version, `v<version>/checksums.txt` returns 200 with an immutable cache-control, and `installers/install.sh` and `scoop/entire.json` return 200.\\n\\nThe gate tests the variable for **non-emptiness**, not presence: `release.yml` always exports it, an unset Actions variable exports as empty, and `isEnvSet` alone would have enabled the pipe with an empty bucket and no credentials — failing every release instead of staying inert.\\n\\nThe Homebrew cask and the bucket's Scoop manifest still point at GitHub on purpose. Repointing the cask is the highest-value follow-up once this is proven, since the sha256 stays pinned in the manifest.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n`scripts/test-release-origins.sh` (`mise run test:release-origins`, and a CI job) runs both scripts against local fake origins — version discovery, download and verification from our origin, fallback to GitHub for both, a checksum mismatch aborting rather than falling through, a hung origin still failing over, `--version` pinning, unusable manifest metadata advancing, the pointer's routing, monotonicity, fail-closed read and conditional write, and the installer and Scoop manifest publishing. 86 assertions, hermetic, and it refuses to run an installer still aimed at a public origin.\\n\\nVerified locally: `mise run check` green (93 packages, both canary legs), `go vet` for darwin/linux/windows. The Windows installer checks run in CI.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2795/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2795/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2646\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2646/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2646/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2646/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2646\",\n            \"id\": 5693360804,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABGecw7A\",\n            \"number\": 2646,\n            \"title\": \"Credit background subagent edits to the agent, not the user\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-03T20:43:08Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-05T15:13:23Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-05T15:13:23Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2646\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2646\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2646.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2646.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1471\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nA Claude Code subagent's lines are recorded as human lines. In agent-scenarios run `single-subagent/claude-code/2.1.288-2` (checkpoint `01M41NGSZKGXKNP8586A7ECP5Y`), a subagent wrote 37 lines and the checkpoint recorded `agent_lines: 0` with `user_lines_added: 37`. Codex records the same scenario correctly.\\n\\n## Cause\\n\\nThe subagent's own transcript is read correctly; the problem is timing. All Claude Code 2.1.288 Agent launches run in the background:\\n\\n1. The parent's turn ends while the subagent is still running, so the shadow snapshot lacks its edits.\\n2. The subagent finishes. Task completion records its files but writes no snapshot.\\n3. The task-notification fires `UserPromptSubmit` in the same millisecond as `SubagentStop`. Turn-start prompt attribution diffs the worktree against the stale snapshot and counts every line as user work (`manual_commit_attribution.go`, `CalculatePromptAttribution`).\\n4. The notification turn's Stop doesn't snapshot the file either: it was already in the worktree when that turn started, and the parent transcript's reference to the subagent is in an earlier turn.\\n\\nAt commit, agent lines are base→shadow minus the user lines on agent files, which comes out to 0. Codex is unaffected because its parent waits for the child inside the same turn.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nThe session state gets `PendingSubagentFiles`: files a subagent wrote that no shadow snapshot holds yet, each mapped to a git blob of the file's content when the subagent's edit was observed.\\n\\n- When a subagent completes, `CompleteTaskRecord` records the edits it made since its last scan, in the same state update that completes the record.\\n- Turn start does the same for still-running subagents before attribution runs. This covers the notification turn winning the race with `SubagentStop`.\\n- Turn-start prompt attribution measures user edits to a pending file from its observed content, not from the stale snapshot.\\n- A commit before the next snapshot does the same: the observed content stands in for the snapshot.\\n- Each task record keeps how far its subagent transcript has been scanned (`ScannedTranscriptLines`). Turn start and completion resume there, and turn end advances still-running subagents past what it snapshotted, so an edit already snapshotted isn't marked pending again.\\n- Turn end snapshots pending files, and `SaveStep` removes the ones it wrote. That includes a skipped step whose tree already holds them; that path keeps the pending prompt attribution for the next real step. Condensation drops the committed ones.\\n- Turn end also snapshots agent files whose user edits the turn's prompt attribution counted. Without this, an untracked agent file the turn didn't touch stays stale in the snapshot, and the commit counts the same user lines twice.\\n- If a baseline blob can't be read, the file's current content is used, which credits it all to the subagent rather than to the user.\\n\\n**Shell-written files.** The transcript analyzer sees only edit tool calls, and agent-scenarios found Bash-only subagents recorded with no files and their lines credited to the user. In local transcripts, 99% of subagents use Bash and 13% use edit tools. Claude Code now reports the time window of each Bash and edit call (`ToolCallWindowExtractor`, `agent/claudecode/tool_call_window.go`). A changed file the analyzer didn't name is the subagent's when its modification time falls inside one of the subagent's write-looking shell calls and inside no other agent's write-capable call in the session (`matchShellWrittenFiles`, `subagent_shell_files.go`). When calls overlap, the side whose calls name the file wins; otherwise the file is ambiguous: it counts as agent work for attribution but isn't listed on the task record. A file modified outside every agent tool call stays the user's. A prototype over 339 known subagent edits in local transcripts attributed none to the wrong agent; 88% matched one agent and 12% were ambiguous.\\n\\nRemaining imprecision: a user edit made between the subagent writing a file and Entire observing it (at completion, or at the next turn start for a still-running subagent) is credited to the subagent.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nEach test was written first and failed before its fix.\\n\\n`TestSubagentCheckpoints_BackgroundSubagentEdit_AttributedToAgent` covers:\\n\\n- `SubagentStop` before the notification turn, and after it.\\n- A commit before any later turn ends.\\n- Each of those both without and with an earlier parent snapshot. Without one, the stray lines fall into the pre-session baseline: `agent_lines: 0`, `human_added: 0`. With one, they show as human: `agent_lines: 1`, `human_added: 3`, matching the report.\\n\\nDisabling the turn-start transcript scan makes the \\\"notification turn first\\\" variants fail again, so both halves of the fix are covered. `TestSubagentCheckpoints_UserEditToSubagentFile_StaysHuman` covers the two review findings: user edits to a subagent's file after it finished (commit before the next turn, and after the notification turn), and while it's still running after its edit was snapshotted. Before the fix, all three credited the user's 2 lines to the agent. Ablations confirm the coverage: scanning from line 0 again fails the still-running variant, and using committed content again fails the commit-before-next-turn variant.\\n\\n`TestSubagentCheckpoints_BackgroundSubagentShellEdit_AttributedToAgent` covers a subagent that writes only through `printf … >`, plus a human file written while it runs, outside any agent call. It runs the subagent-stop-first, notification-turn-first and commit-before-the-next-turn variants. Before the matcher, all three recorded `agent_lines=1 human_added=5` and an empty `task.json` file list; disabling the matcher fails them again. Unit tests cover the extractor, the write heuristic and the matcher's overlap and tie-break rules.\\n\\nA unit test covers clearing pending files on a skipped `SaveStep`.\\n\\n`mise run lint` is clean. `mise run test:ci` passes except `TestOpenCodeSeedRepoPlantsDeps`, which fails the same way on `main` locally (it needs the e2e OpenCode bootstrap).\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2646/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2646/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1881\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1881/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1881/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1881/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1881\",\n            \"id\": 5028749237,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M74960h\",\n            \"number\": 1881,\n            \"title\": \"ci: add daily checkpoint-availability audit job\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"id\": 881031,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-07-31T10:29:09Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-10T13:11:15Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-27T09:22:50Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1881\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1881\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1881.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1881.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/959\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\n`entire trail resume 955` failed with **\\\"checkpoint not found\\\"**: checkpoint `01KYSGR4W1ZATZRW47J510EZGJ` was referenced by a commit trailer on `feat/repo-mirror-use` (reached `origin`), but its git-refs ref `refs/entire/checkpoints/GJ/01KYSGR4W1…` was **never pushed** to the checkpoint remote `entireio/cli-checkpoints`. The git-refs backend enqueues checkpoint refs for a best-effort pre-push drain; when that drain never runs or fails silently, the branch commit and the checkpoint ref diverge — and the gap is invisible until someone tries to resume.\\n\\nThis adds an **active** daily audit so orphaned checkpoints surface within 24h instead of at resume time.\\n\\n## What\\n\\n- **`scripts/checkpoint-audit.sh`** — walks every branch commit in a window (`--branches --remotes --since`), extracts `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers using git's own `%(trailers:…)` formatting (handles squash-merge multi-trailers), and diffs them against one `git ls-remote refs/entire/checkpoints/*`. The checkpoint ID is the ref leaf, so membership is a plain string-set lookup (works for ULID + legacy hex, no shard math).\\n  - Exit `0` all present · `1` missing (prints a context table) · `2` remote/setup error, so a broken remote never reads as \\\"0 missing\\\".\\n  - The checkpoint remote is public, so the audit needs **no credentials**. The script still honors `ENTIRE_CHECKPOINT_TOKEN` (RFC 7617 basic-header auth, matching the CLI) if the remote ever goes private.\\n- **`.github/workflows/checkpoint-audit.yml`** — daily 07:00 UTC cron + `workflow_dispatch`. Fails the job on missing checkpoints; reports via `GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY`, an uploaded artifact (`.md` + `.json`), and Slack. No App token / secrets needed (default `GITHUB_TOKEN` checkout + anonymous public fetch).\\n- **`mise.toml`** — `checkpoint:audit` task for local runs.\\n\\n## Report shape\\n\\n| Checkpoint | Commit | Author | Branch(es) | Date | Subject |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| `01KYSGR4W1ZATZRW47J510EZGJ` | `4e229c05` | Matthias Wenz | feat/repo-mirror-use | 2026-07-30T14:42:18+02:00 | feat(repo): add `entire repo mirror use`… |\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- **Positive**: 7-day window → exit 1, flagged the known-missing `01KYSGR4W1…` (and caught a second real orphan). Valid table + JSON. ~3s.\\n- **Remote-error**: bogus token → exit 2 (not 0).\\n- Anonymous `git ls-remote` against `cli-checkpoints` confirmed working with no credentials (repo is public).\\n- shellcheck / `mise run lint:shellcheck` / gofmt / gomod / YAML valid / all `uses:` SHA-pinned. No Go files touched.\\n\\n## Note\\n\\nSlack reuses the existing `E2E_SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` secret. Nothing else to provision.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1881/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1881/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1915\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1915/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1915/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1915/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1915\",\n            \"id\": 5087094993,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M774S6k\",\n            \"number\": 1915,\n            \"title\": \"Add cross-repo checkpoint explain via --repo (ENT-1523)\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"evisdren\",\n              \"id\": 256443556,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD0kEpA\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256443556?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/evisdren\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-08-07T05:11:46Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-10T21:48:09Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-10T21:48:09Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1915\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1915\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1915.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1915.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/986\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n`entire search --repo '*'` returns checkpoint hits from any accessible repo, but `entire checkpoint explain <id>` only resolved against the cwd repo — foreign checkpoints always failed with `no checkpoint or commit found`, and agents burned turns retrying (observed live in the search-bench skill arm).\\n\\nThis adds `--repo <owner/name | gh/owner/name | repo-ULID>` (plus `--cluster`) to `checkpoint explain`:\\n\\n- **Targeted single-ref fetch**: fetches only `refs/entire/checkpoints/<shard>/<id>` from the target repo's Entire mirror (`entire://<cluster-host>/gh/<owner>/<repo>`, resolved via the same pull-gated placements authority `repo clone` uses) into the cwd repo's object store. Never fetches a whole branch.\\n- **Unchanged render path**: the pre-fetch runs before output-mode routing, so prose, `--json`, `--transcript`, and `--full` all work on the fetched checkpoint.\\n- **Same-repo no-op**: `--repo` naming the cwd repo (per the origin remote) behaves identically to no flag.\\n- **Reuses existing resolution**: `looksLikeULID` + `GetRepo` (same as `repo get <ulid>`), `parseMirrorCloneRef` charset validation, `gitremote.ResolveRemoteRepo`, and a `listPullablePlacements` helper extracted from `repo clone`.\\n- **Guardrails**: `--repo` requires a full checkpoint ID (a prefix cannot name a ref) and a checkpoint target; mutually exclusive with `--commit`/`--session`/`--generate`; `--cluster` requires `--repo`. Server-provided cluster hosts pass the same `validateClusterHost` anti-token-leak guard as clone.\\n\\nNew fetch primitive: `remote.FetchCheckpointRefFrom(ctx, url, ref)` — explicit URL treated as authoritative, so an empty ls-remote wraps `plumbing.ErrReferenceNotFound` (absence) while transport failures stay distinguishable.\\n\\n## Known gaps (flagging for team discussion)\\n\\n1. **Legacy branch-only repos & external `checkpoint_remote`**: a mirror that doesn't hold per-checkpoint refs can't serve this path. It fails with a specific error naming the repo (never the generic \\\"no checkpoint or commit found\\\"). Candidate server work: a checkpoint-content endpoint on entire-api, or core exposing a repo's checkpoint remote — neither exists today.\\n2. **Read-routing corner**: a fetched cross-repo *legacy 12-hex* checkpoint in a cwd repo with branch-primary config lists but content-reads route only to the branch store. ULIDs (all new checkpoints) are unaffected — `readOrder` always routes them to the refs store.\\n\\n## Follow-ups (out of scope)\\n\\n- Packaged `search` skill update (entireio/skills, follow-up to skills#39) to pass `--repo` from search results' `org`/`repo` fields.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] Unit: flag parsing, ULID→owner/name via httptest core (`GET /repos/{id}`), same-repo detection across ssh/https/entire:// origins, flag-combination validation, full-ID requirement\\n- [x] Fetch primitive: present ref fetches, missing ref ⇒ `ErrReferenceNotFound`, unreachable remote ⇒ NOT absence\\n- [x] End-to-end: fetch a real git-refs checkpoint from a foreign repo via explicit path URL, then `runExplain` renders it\\n- [x] `mise run check` (fmt + lint + test:ci incl. canary 59/59 + 4/4) green\\n- [ ] Manual smoke (needs login): from a checkout ≠ entire.io, `entire checkpoint explain 01KYVBXNF3ZRG9CZ5YGNXYJCZ4 --repo entireio/entire.io --full --no-pager`\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Read-only feature but adds control-plane calls, mirror selection, and git fetch into the local object store; incorrect absence classification could mislead users, though contracts and tests mirror existing `FetchCheckpointRef` behavior.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Cross-repo `checkpoint explain`** adds `--repo` (owner/name, `gh/…`, or repo ULID) and optional `--cluster` so a checkpoint from another repo can be explained from the current worktree—e.g. after `entire search --repo`.\\n> \\n> Before output routing, the command resolves the target repo (control-plane lookup for ULIDs, same-repo no-op via `origin`), picks a pullable Entire mirror like `repo clone`, and **single-ref fetches** `refs/entire/checkpoints/<shard>/<id>` into the cwd object store. Prose, `--json`, `--transcript`, and `--full` then run unchanged. Guardrails: full checkpoint ID only, `--repo` incompatible with `--commit` / `--session` / `--generate`, and a specific error when the mirror lacks per-checkpoint refs.\\n> \\n> **Checkpoint remote** refactors probe+fetch into `probeAndFetchCheckpointRef` and adds `FetchCheckpointRefFrom` for explicit URLs (authoritative absence vs transport errors).\\n> \\n> **`listPullablePlacements`** is extracted from `repo clone` for shared mirror placement resolution. Flag validation moves to `validateExplainFlags`.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 7e12aa92b43010b7b92e53d1566b119be96db033. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1915/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1915/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2119\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2119/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2119/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2119/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2119\",\n            \"id\": 5238395396,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABA17OSA\",\n            \"number\": 2119,\n            \"title\": \"fix(strategy): log a commit trailer no session condensed into\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-08-24T19:01:03Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-01T08:33:52Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-01T08:33:49Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2119\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2119\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2119.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2119.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-01T08:33:49Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1138\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nExtracted from #2034 at review request — the warning it added fired on ordinary git usage, so it came out of that PR and lands here with the guards it needed.\\n\\n## The gap\\n\\n`PrepareCommitMsg` stamps an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer on a session it judges eligible. `PostCommit` then decides independently whether to condense that session. When the two disagree, the commit ships a trailer naming a checkpoint nobody wrote, and `entire explain` on it resolves to nothing.\\n\\nEach half looks like a routine skip on its own — \\\"session not eligible\\\", \\\"nothing new to condense\\\" — so the divergence is invisible today. There's a known live instance of this shape (IDLE session with empty `FilesTouched`), which is what motivated the warning.\\n\\n## Why DEBUG, not WARN\\n\\nReview found two more false-positive classes beyond the two guarded below, and the second is not cheaply fixable: `git merge --squash` and `git commit -C` copy an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer out of an existing commit message without being sequencer operations, and `PrepareCommitMsg` deliberately never stamps a squash — so no local session owns the inherited ID and `isGitSequenceOperation` does not see it.\\n\\nThe exact discriminator is \\\"did Entire mint this trailer for this commit\\\", but `PrepareCommitMsg` writes no session state at all today, so recording that adds a lock-taking write to a read-only hook on the latency-critical path. Not worth it for a diagnostic. So this logs at DEBUG, where a false positive costs nothing; an authoritative check belongs in `entire doctor`, which can afford to ask the store whether the ID resolves. That is the natural follow-up and is not in this PR.\\n\\n## The signal\\n\\nTwo inputs, because neither alone is sufficient:\\n\\n- **This invocation** — `postCommitProcessSessionLocked` now reports whether the session condensed. This has to be read from the call rather than inferred from state afterwards: carry-forward on a partial commit clears `LastCheckpointID` that `condenseAndUpdateState` had just set (`TestPostCommit_ActiveSession_CarryForward_PartialCommit` pins that clearing as intended), so a successful partial condensation is indistinguishable from never having condensed. Caught in review; regression test added.\\n- **A previous commit** — ownership seeded from `LastCheckpointID` across the pre-loop snapshot, which is the amend case and also covers an amend whose owning session has since ended and is skipped by the loop.\\n\\n## The two exclusions\\n\\nThese matter even at DEBUG: without them the line says nothing useful to whoever greps for it.\\n\\n- **Amend.** `handleAmendCommitMsg` preserves or restores the trailer, and a message-only amend has nothing new to condense. Covered by seeding ownership from the pre-loop snapshot, which also catches the case where the owning session has since ended and the loop skips it.\\n- **Cherry-pick, revert, rebase replay.** The trailer rides along from a source commit whose session may not exist in this worktree at all, so ownership can't be established locally. Covered by the `isRebase` guard (`isGitSequenceOperation` already detects all three).\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nFive subtests in `TestPostCommit_UnclaimedCheckpointTrailer` — the shape the line is for, plus amend, amend-after-session-ended, sequence operation, and a session that does condense — and `TestPostCommit_PartialCommit_TrailerIsClaimed` for the carry-forward case.\\n\\nEvery guard has a test that fails when that guard alone is removed, verified by mutation. That kept catching things: the first version passed every case while the pre-loop seed was dead code, because the amend case as written was caught by the in-loop check instead. The seed only matters for an amend after the session ended, so that case was added.\\n\\n## Also\\n\\nCorrects `filterSessionsWithNewContent`'s doc comment. It claimed a withheld stale task record is rescued by \\\"PostCommit … through `sessionHasNewContent`\\\", but withholding the trailer means PostCommit returns at its no-trailer early exit before reaching any session. The rescue is `endSessionNow` or a later trailered commit.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n`mise run fmt`, `mise run lint` (0 issues), `mise run test:ci` (unit + integration + canary) all clean.\\n\\nRebased onto #2013, which added a second `LastCheckpointID` assignment for guest condensation and moved PostCommit onto `findSessionsForCommitLinking` — the same resolver PrepareCommitMsg uses. Had those diverged, every identity-linked guest commit would have false-positived.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2119/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2119/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1942\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1942/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1942/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1942/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1942\",\n            \"id\": 5114005437,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M79Mu-V\",\n            \"number\": 1942,\n            \"title\": \"feat(explain): cross-repo checkpoint explain via the entire-api cell (ENT-1523)\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-08-10T20:18:10Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-10T21:43:41Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-10T21:43:40Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1942\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1942\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1942.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1942.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-10T21:43:40Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1003\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n`entire checkpoint explain <id> --repo owner/name` explains a checkpoint owned by another repository, reading it from that repo's entire-api cell over HTTP.\\n\\nThis is an alternative to #— the `--repo` implementation on `surf-lightning` (trail 986), which fetches the checkpoint's git ref into the local repo. Same user-facing feature, different data path. Opening it as a separate PR so the two approaches can be compared directly.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\n`entire search` is cross-repo; `explain` was not. Search hands you an identifier the natural next command cannot resolve:\\n\\n```\\n$ entire checkpoint explain b754d1dae6b8      # a checkpoint in entirehq/entiredb\\nno checkpoint or commit found matching \\\"b754d1dae6b8\\\"\\n```\\n\\nThe compact-search work (trail 982) makes this sharper: its per-hit shape is deliberately too thin to answer anything alone, and its skill template has to tell agents to *give up* on cross-repo hits (\\\"summarize from the compact fields alone; `explain` cannot read them\\\").\\n\\n## Approach\\n\\nThe cell already serves everything explain renders — it's how the web app shows you any repo's checkpoint without cloning it:\\n\\n| Endpoint | Serves |\\n|---|---|\\n| `GET /repos/{repo_id}/checkpoints/{id}` | commit, `filesTouched`, sessions + prompts, per-session and aggregate tokens |\\n| `GET /repos/{repo_id}/checkpoints/{id}/transcript/raw` | the stored transcript bytes |\\n\\n`apiCheckpointReader` implements the two checkpoint reader tiers (`CheckpointReader` + `SessionReader`) plus the optional `AuthorReader`. That's the whole surface the render path consumes, so **every output mode reuses the existing renderers verbatim** — prose, `--short`, `--full`, `--json`, `--transcript`/`--raw-transcript`. No second output implementation.\\n\\nIt deliberately does **not** implement `Writer`. A foreign checkpoint is read-only from here, and leaving `Write` off the type makes that structural instead of a convention the flag layer has to remember (there's a test pinning it).\\n\\n## What this buys over fetching git refs\\n\\n**Nothing is written to the local repository.** Verified from a scratch repo against production, after explaining a real foreign checkpoint:\\n\\n| | git-ref fetch | this PR |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `refs/entire/*` left behind | 1 | **0** |\\n| `.git` size | 3.5 MB | **108 K** |\\n| `entire tokens profile` | 1 checkpoint, 72.4M tokens (another repo's) | **0 checkpoints** |\\n| cleanup path | none (`entire clean --all` doesn't touch checkpoint refs) | nothing to clean |\\n\\n**No `--cluster` flag.** Cell routing is automatic via `resolveRepoCellTarget`. The ref-fetch path resolves mirror placements instead and dead-ends without it:\\n\\n```\\n# git-ref fetch\\n$ entire checkpoint explain <id> --repo entireio/cli\\nrepo is mirrored on 4 clusters; pass --cluster to choose one of: ...\\n\\n# this PR\\n$ entire checkpoint explain <id> --repo entireio/cli\\n● Checkpoint 01KXGTTNGCEACC83QZEJ5YAF0D\\n  ...\\n```\\n\\n**Wider coverage.** Same checkpoint ID, same repo, both binaries:\\n\\n```\\n# git-ref fetch\\ncheckpoint 01KZP3V62DKQBG9ZKS6T2ADR00 not found in the mirror for entireio/cli;\\nrepos using the legacy branch-based checkpoint store ... are not supported cross-repo yet\\n\\n# this PR\\n● Checkpoint 01KZP3V62DKQBG9ZKS6T2ADR00\\n  session  a78beaef-a2ab-4cad-9900-f4d3c3b51959\\n```\\n\\nThe cell resolves the storage layout itself (`checkpointlayout.RefAndFolder(id, data.RefBacked)`), so branch-backed and ref-backed repos both work — the ref-fetch path is ref-layout-only by construction.\\n\\n## Fidelity decisions (both tested)\\n\\n- **`Branch` is left empty**, not filled from the envelope. The cell reports branches *containing* the commit; the local field means the branch the checkpoint was *created* on. A checkpoint made on a feature branch and since merged reports `main`, so putting that behind the same JSON key would mislead every `--json` consumer.\\n- **Transcript bytes come from `.../transcript/raw`**, never the parsed message-tree endpoint. `explain` documents `--transcript` as the same bytes as `--raw-transcript`; sourcing them from a derived shape would quietly break that.\\n- **A missing `checkpointTranscriptStart` reads as 0** (unscoped) rather than an invented offset — identical to how a local checkpoint written before that field existed behaves.\\n- **Oversize transcripts error** instead of truncating into the renderer.\\n\\n## Flag rules\\n\\n`--repo` needs a full checkpoint ID (a prefix would require listing the foreign repo's checkpoints — that's `search`'s job) and is mutually exclusive with `--commit`, `--session`, `--search-all`, and `--generate`. Naming the current repo is a no-op that falls through to the local path, which is faster and can also read unpushed checkpoints.\\n\\nA bare repo ID is not accepted, only `owner/name` / `gh/owner/name` — the control plane and the search index expose different identifiers for a repository, and guessing which space an opaque ID belongs to would key the lookup off the wrong one. `owner/name` is what search's `repo` field gives you.\\n\\n## Error messages\\n\\nA 404 leads with the cause that actually dominates:\\n\\n```\\ncheckpoint 01KV... is not available for entireio/cli yet: it may not have been\\npushed, or Entire may not have finished ingesting it. Checkpoints you have not\\npushed are only readable in the repo that created them\\n```\\n\\n## Drive-bys\\n\\n- Extracted `validateExplainFlagCombinations` out of `newExplainCmd` (it was over the `maintidx` limit with the new flag).\\n- Renamed `resolveCurrentRepoID` → `resolveRepoIDFromMirror`; it takes explicit coordinates and now serves a foreign repo too.\\n- Stopped rendering an empty `<>` when an author has a name but no email.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n`mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci` all green (lint: 0 issues). 25 new tests: envelope mapping, the raw-vs-parsed endpoint assertion, envelope caching (one fetch across all read tiers), 404/403/empty/no-session paths, oversize transcript, `List` unsupported, not-a-`Writer`, flag validation, and all four render modes against a stub reader.\\n\\nManually verified end-to-end against production for prose, `--json`, `--full` (3,273 lines), and `--transcript` (3.1 MB), plus clean stdout JSON with the spinner on stderr.\\n\\n## Known gap\\n\\nThe availability precondition is *pushed and ingested*, so a just-pushed checkpoint may briefly 404. The message above says so; if that lag turns out to be user-visible in practice, a retry hint would be the follow-up.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> New authenticated HTTP read path and flag surface on a heavily used command; risk is moderated by read-only semantics (no local git writes), strict flag mutual exclusion, and extensive tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **`entire checkpoint explain <id> --repo owner/name`** so cross-repo `search` hits can be drilled down without pulling foreign git objects into the local repo.\\n> \\n> **`apiCheckpointReader`** loads checkpoint metadata and raw transcript bytes from the repo’s entire-api cell (`GET .../checkpoints/{id}` and `.../transcript/raw`), maps them into the existing checkpoint reader types, and **does not implement `Writer`**. Prose, `--json`, `--full`, and transcript modes reuse the same renderers as local explain.\\n> \\n> **`runCrossRepoExplain`** resolves mirror `repo_id`, dials the owning cell via `NewAuthenticatedEntireAPICellClient`, and rejects incompatible flags (`--commit`, `--session`, `--search-all`, `--generate`). `--repo` on the current checkout is a no-op to the local path. Cross-repo requires a **full** checkpoint ID.\\n> \\n> Notable fidelity choices: **`Branch` stays empty** (cell “containing branches” ≠ creation branch), transcripts always from **raw** endpoint, oversize transcripts **error** instead of truncating, and 404 messaging calls out unpushed/not-yet-ingested checkpoints.\\n> \\n> Also extracts **`validateExplainFlagCombinations`**, renames **`resolveCurrentRepoID` → `resolveRepoIDFromMirror`** for foreign-repo use, fixes author lines when email is missing, and documents the feature in **CLAUDE.md**. Broad unit test coverage for the API reader and cross-repo explain paths.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 346b7fb5b53078c1a8f46fdce807151a081e4dcd. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1942/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1942/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2180\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2180/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2180/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2180/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2180\",\n            \"id\": 5294323027,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBhzniQ\",\n            \"number\": 2180,\n            \"title\": \"Confine Entire's filesystem use to `os.Root` anchors\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"pjbgf\",\n              \"id\": 5452977,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NTI5Nzc=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5452977?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pjbgf\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-08-30T20:54:52Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-01T13:15:42Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-01T13:15:40Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2180\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2180\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2180.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2180.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-01T13:15:40Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1184\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\nEstablish os.Root anchors for the seven trees Entire reads and writes using names it does not control, including agent session IDs, tool-use IDs, investigation run IDs, git status output, and checkpoint tree entries fetched from a remote. Each tree has one owning abstraction, and operations beneath an anchor reject symlinks instead of merely relying on os.Root\\r\\n  containment.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ### Anchors\\r\\n\\r\\n  One owning abstraction per tree: entiredir, gitdir, worktreedir, agent.SessionStore, agent.HookConfigFile, userdirs, and pluginRoot.\\r\\n\\r\\n  Long-lived anchors are memoized through a single osroot.Shared registry. agent.SessionStore is intentionally opened per operation because transcript fallback search may probe hundreds of candidate directories; retaining those roots in the non-evicting registry would consume one file descriptor per candidate.\\r\\n\\r\\n  Resolver-derived files must use the anchor for their owning tree. They must not create an anchor from filepath.Dir of the target being opened, because that places the caller-resolved components above the root and leaves them unenforced. Explicit caller-named settings and token-store paths are documented exceptions because the parent directory is itself part of the caller’s selection.\\r\\n\\r\\n  TestRootBasesAreTrusted fails the build when a new root-opening site is not on the allowlist, or when an allowlisted site no longer opens a root.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ### Refusals\\r\\n\\r\\n  - .entire must be a real directory, and every direct entry must be a regular file or directory. Four distinct failure conditions are matched positively so the reported remedy fits the  fault.\\r\\n\\r\\n  - Symlinks are refused, not followed or silently skipped, in trees Entire owns, including at a walk root and in every component beneath an anchor.\\r\\n\\r\\n    fs.WalkDir obtains its root DirEntry using fs.Stat, which follows symlinks, while only entries below the root come from ReadDir. The previous callback guards inspected d.Type(), so\\r\\n    they did not protect the walk root. A symlinked .entire/metadata/<session> could therefore be traversed and have its target committed and pushed. This protection had previously existed\\r\\n    with filepath.Walk, which uses Lstat, and was lost during conversion.\\r\\n\\r\\n  - Filesystem operations pin path components instead of checking and resolving them again. Parent directories are opened one component at a time, with symlinks rejected at every level.\\r\\n    Reads, writes, directory creation, removal, enumeration, and walks then operate relative to those pinned descriptors. This closes the check/use gap where an attacker could replace a\\r\\n    verified directory before the subsequent operation.\\r\\n\\r\\n  - Worktree content read or modified by Entire also rejects symlink components where following them would redirect the operation. This includes agent hook configuration, managed agent\\r\\n    scaffold files, .gitignore, .worktreeinclude, agent session files, and files read for trail-review selected text.\\r\\n\\r\\n  - Settings resolved by Entire are never read through a link, enforced in the settings reader itself because eighteen call sites invoke settings.Load without passing through the pre-run\\r\\n    guard. Explicit caller-selected settings paths trust the caller-selected parent as their root but still refuse a symlink at the target file.\\r\\n\\r\\n  - “We could not find out” is not “there is nothing here.” WorktreeRoot falls back to the current directory only after Git positively reports that the directory is not in a repository. It\\r\\n    does not fall back when Git is absent from $PATH, repository ownership is dubious, the context is cancelled, or repository discovery otherwise fails.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ### Interrupted atomic writes\\r\\n\\r\\n  jsonutil.WriteFileAtomicIn creates a temporary file named <base>.<16 hex>.tmp beside its target. Because .entire/metadata/<session> is copied wholesale into checkpoint trees, a hook\\r\\n  killed during an atomic write could leave an orphan that was committed in every later checkpoint.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ParseChunkIndex also previously used fmt.Sscanf(\\\"%03d\\\"), which stops successfully at the first non-digit. A temporary file whose random suffix began with digits could therefore be\\r\\n  interpreted as a transcript chunk.\\r\\n\\r\\n  Checkpoint walks now recognize and ignore only the complete temporary-file naming pattern, while ParseChunkIndex accepts only an entirely numeric suffix.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ### Repository opening\\r\\n  gitrepo.OpenCurrent no longer falls back to OpenPath(\\\".\\\") when the worktree root cannot be established.\\r\\n\\r\\n  The single caller that intentionally wants best-effort cwd behavior uses OpenCurrentOrCwd explicitly. It is dispatched from main.go after Cobra processing, reads only a policy ref, and\\r\\n  discards every error.\\r\\n\\r\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n> [!NOTE]\\r\\n> **High Risk**\\r\\n> Broad security and correctness changes to path containment, symlink handling, repository resolution, and checkpoint metadata walks; misconfiguration could break enable/hooks, transcript restore, or open the wrong repo in edge cases.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> **Overview**\\r\\n> Routes Entire’s sensitive filesystem work through **trusted `os.Root` anchors** (`.entire`, git common dir, worktree, hook configs, session stores, etc.) instead of assembling absolute paths and calling plain `os.*`. **CLAUDE.md** documents the seven trees, symlink refusal, atomic-write temp handling, and when rooting is deliberately skipped.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> **Agent hook configs** now go through shared **`agent.HookConfigFile`** / `OpenHookConfig` on the worktree root (all built-in agents), so `entire enable` cannot create or write through a checked-in symlinked `.claude` / `.cursor` / `.codex` / etc. **Session transcript writes** are centralized in **`agent.SessionStore`** and **`WriteSessionFile`**, rejecting session IDs that escape the agent’s session directory. **`.entire` transcript caches** (OpenCode export, Pi hook cache, Factory fallback state) use **`entiredir`** + **`ReadTranscriptFile`** / **`StatTranscriptFile`** for reads under `.entire`.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> **Checkpoint safety:** `ParseChunkIndex` only accepts an all-digit suffix (no more `fmt.Sscanf` mis-reading `full.jsonl.<hex>.tmp` as a chunk); walks are documented to skip `jsonutil` temp names. **`gitrepo.OpenCurrent`** no longer falls back to `OpenPath(\\\".\\\")` when the worktree cannot be resolved; **`OpenCurrentOrCwd`** is reserved for the one advisory caller. External-agent discovery tests inject worktree root via **`settings.WithWorktreeRoot`** instead of relying on removed cwd-relative settings fallbacks.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 1d863f6ed67cbd5f95b1a45a26f75a2c386b3143. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\r\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2180/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2180/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1618\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1618/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1618/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1618/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1618\",\n            \"id\": 4798503612,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7tVLEm\",\n            \"number\": 1618,\n            \"title\": \"feat(onboarding): guided setup ladder — enable walks login/mirror/import, status shows the checklist, re-enable resumes\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 2,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-07-02T22:06:28Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-19T21:15:34Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-19T21:15:34Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1618\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1618\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1618.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1618.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## What\\n\\n`entire enable` currently ends at \\\"hooks installed\\\" and calls it success, leaving users with local checkpoints, an empty web UI, and no signal that login + mirroring even exist as steps. This PR turns onboarding into a **converging setup ladder**:\\n\\n- **`entire enable`** finishes with a single consent prompt — *\\\"Finish setup?\\\"* (set up everything / choose step by step / skip for now) — that walks login → mirror → history import for whatever is missing, then prints a checklist:\\n\\n  ```\\n  Setup 1/3 complete\\n    ✓ Agent hooks    Claude Code\\n    ✗ Logged in\\n    ✗ Repo mirrored  needs login\\n  → Run `entire enable` to finish setup (2 steps left)\\n    run later: entire auth login\\n  ```\\n\\n- **`entire status`** renders the same checklist from the same source (plus a `setup` object in `--json`), collapsing to one quiet `Connected: <handle> · mirrored to <slug>` line once done.\\n- **Re-running `entire enable` is the resume path**: rung state is recomputed from ground truth (hooks on disk, stored login, control-plane mirror list, local transcript discovery), so an interrupted setup — or a rung completed out-of-band — is picked up exactly where it left off, with no progress state to corrupt. The previous hard short-circuit at \\\"Entire is already enabled.\\\" now re-offers only the missing rungs.\\n\\n## Design decisions\\n\\n- **One consent prompt, not a wizard**: the happy path is one keypress + one browser tab. Step-by-step is opt-in for cautious users.\\n- **Best-effort offers**: a failed login or mirror create prints a notice and a retry hint; enable never fails because of a connect rung.\\n- **Blocked ≠ missing**: mirror without login renders as \\\"needs login\\\" instead of offering a command that would 401; run-later hints are deduped so the fix-command appears once.\\n- **Skipping isn't a mode**: the skip option reads \\\"Skip for now — finish anytime with `entire enable`\\\". Tracking continues either way; on an already-mirrored repo a skipper's sessions still reach the UI on their next push.\\n- **Non-interactive contract** (`--yes` / no TTY): never prompts, never creates a mirror implicitly; the checklist hints carry the follow-up commands.\\n- **Mirror probe is bounded** (5s) and degrades to \\\"unknown\\\" offline; the auth check is deliberately offline (stored context, not token refresh). A mirror created this pass renders as \\\"created — sync in progress\\\" while the server-side clone finishes, instead of a false ✗.\\n\\n## Relationship to #1595\\n\\nThe import rung ships with a **minimal inline offer** (same flow as `entire import <agent>`: checkpoint policy honored, redaction config loaded, `agentimport.Run` per discoverable agent) — live testing showed that a ladder which dead-ends at 3/4 with a run-later hint undercuts the whole flow. When #1595 lands, its richer enable-time offer (per-agent selection, first-run gating) **replaces the internals of this rung** — the rung interface doesn't change, and the remaining overlap is a small `setup.go` conflict for whichever merges second.\\n\\n## Tests & verification\\n\\n- TDD throughout: unit tests for the ladder model, each rung, the renderer, the offer runner (mode/decline/best-effort/dedupe/sync-lag/import), status wiring, and the re-enable resume paths.\\n- `mise run lint` clean; `mise run test:ci` fully green (unit + integration + e2e canary).\\n- Live smoke-tested end-to-end, including: real browser OAuth through the consent prompt, a real mirror created via the flow (`entirehq/tmp-onboarding-smoke` on aws-us-east-2), interrupted-setup resume, out-of-band `entire import` reflected automatically, step-by-step declines honored, and the full one-pass ladder ending at `Connected`. The walkthrough caught and this PR fixes: the dead resume path on already-enabled repos, the false `✗ Repo mirrored` right after a successful create, and the misleading skip-option copy.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n## Walkthrough of the changes\\n\\n### What happens when you run `entire enable` now\\n\\nThe existing flow (agent select → hooks → strategy) is untouched. At the end, instead of printing `Ready.` and stopping, enable calls `runEnableOnboarding` (`setup.go`), which:\\n\\n1. **Clears cached probe failures** (`mirrorProbeCache.clearUnreachable`) — an explicit enable means the user consents to re-paying a probe that recently failed.\\n2. **Runs the ladder** (`onboardingLadder(...).Checks`): four rungs — hooks, auth, mirror, import — each recomputing its state from ground truth, concurrently:\\n   - **hooks** → done if any agent hooks are installed (local FS).\\n   - **auth** → done if the active context has a stored token (keyring, deliberately offline — no token refresh). Keyring *failure* is `unknown` (+ `entire auth status` hint), not \\\"not logged in\\\".\\n   - **mirror** → parses `origin`; non-GitHub → `not_applicable`; not logged in → `blocked`; otherwise asks the control plane (both the active-context core *and* the default cluster core, deduped — a mirror on either counts), behind a 15-min cache. Probe failure → `unknown`, cached 5 min so offline terminals don't hang every run.\\n   - **import** → discovers transcripts for agents with hooks installed, dry-runs them against the checkpoint store to count unimported turns (memoized behind a fingerprint of file mtimes/sizes + the metadata-branch tip — exact invalidation, no TTL). Policy-restricted repo → `not_applicable`.\\n3. **Shows one consent prompt** if anything actionable is missing (`promptOnboardingSetupMode`):\\n   ```\\n   Finish setup? Logs in to entire.io and mirrors this repo so your work shows up in the web UI.\\n   › Yes, set up everything (recommended)\\n     Choose step by step\\n     Skip for now — finish anytime with `entire enable`\\n   ```\\n   Blocked rungs are only listed if the thing blocking them is also being offered (login unblocks mirror in the same pass). Ctrl-C = skip.\\n4. **Runs the offers** for whatever the user accepted (`runOffers`, re-checking each rung immediately before acting — a rung completed out-of-band is never re-run):\\n   - **login** → the exact `entire login` browser flow (`runLoginAuto`).\\n   - **mirror** → `createAndAwaitMirror` with `--no-wait` (placement registered, clone continues server-side; suspended placements are reported and *not* treated as success).\\n   - **import** → #1595's machinery (`sessionImportDiscover/Prompt/Run`): policy-gated, redaction-configured, per-agent. In \\\"everything\\\" mode it imports all eligible; in step-by-step it shows #1595's picker (Import/Skip for one agent, multi-select for several) *as* the confirmation.\\n   Offers are best-effort: a failure prints one line and enable still succeeds.\\n5. **Prints the closing checklist** — per-rung ✓/✗/? rows with exact `run later:` commands for anything skipped or failed:\\n   ```\\n   Setup 2/4 complete\\n     ✓ Agent hooks    Claude Code\\n     ✓ Logged in      peyton\\n     ✗ Repo mirrored  commits won't appear in the web UI\\n     ✗ History        12 claude-code sessions found, not imported\\n   → Run `entire enable` to finish setup (2 steps left)\\n     run later: entire repo mirror create github.com/acme/api\\n   ```\\n\\n### Resume: re-running `entire enable` is the recovery path\\n\\nThere is no setup-progress state anywhere. Every enable recomputes the rungs from ground truth, so an interrupted setup (Ctrl-C mid-login, declined mirror, closed terminal) resumes by just running enable again — it offers only what's still missing, and a fully-connected repo prints one quiet `Connected:` line and exits. The previously-dead \\\"Entire is already enabled.\\\" path now runs the ladder too, and so does the bootstrap (`--init-repo`) path.\\n\\n### `--yes` and `--agent` semantics (exact contracts)\\n\\n| Invocation | Prompts? | Auto-imports? | Login/mirror implicit? |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `enable` (TTY) | consent prompt | via consent | via consent |\\n| `enable --yes`, first run | never | **yes** (matches #1595's merged contract + its integration tests) | **never** |\\n| `enable --yes`, later runs | never | no — \\\"unimported history exists\\\" can't distinguish new history from history the user declined | never |\\n| `enable --agent X` | never (flag is documented non-interactive) | no | never |\\n| `enable --agent X --yes`, first run | never | yes, **scoped to agent X only** | never |\\n| no TTY, no `--yes` | never | no — checklist hints only | never |\\n\\n### What `entire status` now shows\\n\\nThe same ladder renders below the existing output: the checklist while setup is incomplete (with a `→ Run 'entire enable'` pointer), collapsing to `Connected: <handle> · mirrored to <slug>` once done. `status --json` gains `\\\"setup\\\": {\\\"hooks\\\": \\\"done\\\", \\\"auth\\\": \\\"missing\\\", \\\"mirror\\\": \\\"blocked\\\", \\\"import\\\": \\\"not_applicable\\\"}`. This makes status networked (bounded: 5s timeout, 15-min cache, failures cached 5 min) — a deliberate trade so the checklist is discoverable where confused users already look.\\n\\n### Changes to existing code\\n\\n- `setup.go` (+34): the ladder call at the end of all three enable paths, `firstRun` capture, and **removal of #1595's `maybeOfferSessionImport` call sites** (the ladder is the single offer surface — previously both fired back-to-back).\\n- `setup_import.go` (−64): #1595's orchestrator + first-run gate deleted; its discovery/prompt/import helpers survive unchanged and are what the import rung's offer calls. Its four `TestEnableOffersImport_*` integration tests pass with identical observable behavior.\\n- `repo_mirror.go` (+8): `createAndAwaitMirror` write-throughs the probe cache on successful placement — so the checklist's own hinted command heals the cache, not just the offer path.\\n- `status.go` (+15): rendering + JSON wiring, behind a stubbable seam.\\n\\n### Suggested reading order\\n\\n`onboarding/onboarding.go` (the model, pure) → `onboarding_rungs.go` (ground truth; the most decision-dense file) → `onboarding_offer.go` (consent enforcement) → `onboarding_offer_actions.go` (thin compositions) → `onboarding_render.go` + caches (mechanical) → the four integration edits. 55% of the diff is tests; four prior review rounds' findings are fixed in the commits from `577523c5c` onward, readable as a changelog.\\n\\n**Fastest hands-on check:** scratch repo with a GitHub origin → `entire enable` → \\\"Yes, set up everything\\\" → `entire status` → `entire enable` again (idempotent, exits quietly when connected).\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Entire trail:** https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/742/feat-onboarding-guided-setup-ladder-enable-walks-login\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1618/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1618/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1287\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1287/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1287/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1287/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1287\",\n            \"id\": 4539142975,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7gKoTh\",\n            \"number\": 1287,\n            \"title\": \"feat(agent): add Antigravity (agy) CLI agent\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 2,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-05-28T09:06:05Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-24T13:44:21Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-24T13:44:17Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1287\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1287\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1287.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1287.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-24T13:44:17Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/444\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n> **Status: Preview.** The integration ships with `IsPreview() == true` — users see a \\\"(Preview)\\\" label in the agent selector, `entire agent list`, and the hook-install message. Known limitations are listed below and in `docs/architecture/agent-guide.md` (\\\"Antigravity status: Preview\\\").\\n\\nFirst-class support for **Antigravity CLI** (`agy`), Google's successor to Gemini CLI, as a new Entire agent — the complete integration: lifecycle hooks, transcript decoding, native token counts, review-skill discovery, resume tracking, docs, and E2E wiring. Consolidates the previously stacked PRs #1356 (tokens) and #1381 (transcript decode) plus the gap-fix and review-fix rounds into this single parent.\\n\\n**Scope map** (~7.2k insertions; ~60% tests):\\n\\n| Area | What |\\n|---|---|\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/` | agent package: 3 lifecycle hooks (`pre-tool-use`, `pre-invocation`, `stop`), transcript analyzers (prompts, positions, modified files), async-transcript handling, token tee (`statusline.go`/`title_install.go`), review-skill discovery |\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go`, `state.go`, `event.go` | conditional TurnStart (resume tracking), out-of-band token baseline/delta, committed-state filtering for mid-turn commits |\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/` | empty-transcript degrade (agy-scoped), late-flush prompt recovery, checkpoint-scoped token resolution, agy summary/count cases |\\n| `agent/skilldiscovery/` | shared SKILL.md scanner (claude-code rewired onto it) |\\n| e2e + CI | agy runner with three auth modes (ADC → `GEMINI_API_KEY` → OAuth), trusted-workspace seeding, fatal-vs-transient classification, agy-log + hook-probe artifact capture; **dispatch-only** in workflows (see limitations) |\\n| docs | CLAUDE/AGENTS, architecture guide quirks section, checklist, e2e README |\\n\\n## Real-agy quirks (all hardened in code + tests)\\n\\n- **`invocationNum` is 0-indexed**; PreInvocation fires per *model invocation*. `invocationNum > 0` emits a conditional TurnStart (`Event.SuppressIfSessionActive`) the dispatcher drops only when a turn is genuinely mid-flight — so resumes (`agy --conversation`) are tracked and follow-up invocations don't clobber the pre-prompt baseline.\\n- **agy writes its transcript AFTER `Stop`.** `PrepareTranscript` briefly waits then materializes a placeholder; condensation degrades to a files/prompt-only checkpoint (agy-scoped) and prompts are re-extracted late (`resolvePromptsFromLateFlushedTranscript`).\\n- **Tokens have exactly one surface** — the title/statusline JSON. The global `title` slot is claimed by `entire hooks antigravity title-tee` (wrap-preserving, doctor-checked); TurnStart snapshots a baseline, TurnEnd computes the delta (`OutOfBandTokenSource`).\\n- **Tool args are double-encoded**; `decodeAgyString`/`decodeAgyBool` tolerate both shapes. macOS `/tmp` symlinks resolved.\\n- **No SessionStart hook surface** → silent tracking (same as Cursor/OpenCode/Copilot/Pi). agy's PostToolUse/PostInvocation hooks are deliberately **not installed** — no lifecycle mapping, and they'd spawn a no-op subprocess per tool call.\\n\\n## Review & verification\\n\\n- Three-dimension agent review (correctness / over-engineering / hooks-and-docs-vs-agy-1.0.15) followed by a 28-agent adversarially-verified full-implementation review; **all 10 verified findings fixed** (token double-counting, tokens lost on fully-committed turns, deletion-filter regression, cross-worktree title-tee uninstall, e2e retry masking, degrade scoping, hook-prefix matching, + 3 cleanups).\\n- Hook contract verified byte-for-byte against agy's official docs (1.0.15 changed no hook behavior).\\n- Analyzer methods validated against **385 real captured agy transcripts: 0 errors, 0 offset mismatches**; full-pipeline replay of a real transcript reproduces prompts/files/checkpoint contents.\\n- Live smoke on this tip: `entire agent add antigravity` → real hook wiring → mid-turn commit with unwritten transcript → checkpoint + trailer + scoped tokens + `entire status` all correct. Real `agy` fired PreInvocation live (session state created); the model call itself is quota-gated (below).\\n- **2026-07-13 review round (3-reviewer pass + live testing on real agy)**: `TestSingleSessionManualCommit` passed live with real token counts; fresh-repo smoke verified install → live turn → commit → condensation → resume (`agy --conversation`) → token scoping across two commits. agy auto-updated 1.0.16→1.1.1 mid-session; hook wire contract re-verified unchanged, but agy 1.1 moved the skill-discovery directories — fixed, along with the ADC-mode quota-log peek, a doctor false-positive for non-agy teammates, an explicit Stop-hook timeout, and an `agent remove` warning about the global title-tee. Deferred minors are tracked as findings on trail 444.\\n\\n> **Behavior note (all agents):** the ghost-session fix intentionally changes shadow-branch preservation — a read-only ACTIVE session (no tracked files) no longer keeps its shadow branch alive on commit (`phase_postcommit_test.go` updated accordingly). Both checkpoint writers skip zero-file writes, so nothing such a session wrote can be stranded.\\n\\n## Known limitations (preview)\\n\\n- **Live agy E2E runs in the default matrix in agy's Gemini API-key mode** (no account session; the shared `GEMINI_API_KEY` secret). agy ≤ 1.1.24 loaded `.agents/hooks.json` on that route but never executed the hooks (google-antigravity/antigravity-cli#893, still open upstream); bisecting the release binaries with a probe hook shows **agy ≥ 1.1.25 executes them**, and CI installs `releases/latest` (1.2.7 as of 2026-09-21). The optional `ANTIGRAVITY_GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS_JSON` secret still switches the leg to ADC; the `cloudcode-pa` backend remains entitlement-gated (subject 110002). Fail-fast classification covers quota/entitlement walls plus `GEMINI_API_KEY … not set` / `API_KEY_INVALID`. Details in `e2e/README.md`.\\n- **Transcript-derived file lists can be incomplete** when agy persists a step with `truncated_fields` and drops `TargetFile` (reported by @ecgang, ~0.8% of `replace_file_content` calls in their corpus). Now logged as a WARN per dropped call instead of a silent skip; live PreToolUse stdin is never truncated so only the late-flush / first-turn fallbacks are affected. Awaiting a real fixture.\\n- Mid-turn-commit checkpoints record zero tokens (the turn's delta lands on the next condensation — totals stay correct; documented at the fallback).\\n- No in-agy banner (no SessionStart hook surface) — tracking is silent inside the agy UI; `entire status` is the visibility surface.\\n- First-turn mid-turn commits can produce a files/prompt-only checkpoint (agy's transcript lands after Stop); prompts recover on the next condensation.\\n- Token capture depends on `entire hooks antigravity title-tee` owning/wrapping agy's global `title` slot (doctor-checked, setup-repaired).\\n- Wire format captured on agy 1.0.14/1.0.15, re-verified unchanged on agy 1.1.1 (2026-07-13) and 1.1.22 (2026-08-27: still exactly 5 hook types; statusline/title payload unchanged). agy is fast-moving — 1.1 moved the skill directories (handled), 1.1.10 fixed hook ordering so `Stop`/`PostInvocation` fire reliably, 1.1.12 answers `-p \\\"/hooks\\\"` locally (used by `entire doctor` to verify the workspace hooks actually load, zero quota).\\n\\n## 2026-08-27/28 update\\n\\n- Merged `origin/main` (was 3 months behind): ported to local-dev removal, `IsManagedHookCommand(cmd)`, `AreHooksInstalled → (bool, error)`, 4-value `RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI`, main's `skilldiscovery` extraction.\\n- Fixed the CI install step: the agy release tarball ships the binary as `antigravity`, so the leg had never started in CI.\\n- Added `GEMINI_API_KEY` e2e mode, optional ADC, trusted-workspace seeding, agy-log + hook-probe artifacts (agy emits no log line for hook execution — the probe is how #893 was found).\\n- `entire doctor`: \\\"Antigravity hooks: LOADED/NOT LOADED by agy\\\" via `agy -p /hooks --add-dir <root> --output-format json` (version-gated ≥ 1.1.12), plus the untrusted-workspace trap from the test report.\\n- `truncated_fields` degrade path (above). Docs refreshed for 1.1.22.\\n\\n## 2026-09-22 update (trail-444 review rounds after real Windows/macOS testing)\\n\\n- **Windows (confirmed on Windows 11 ARM64, agy 1.2.7):** agy hands hook commands to cmd.exe, so the sh wrapper failed silently and nothing was tracked. Antigravity now installs the bare direct-shell wrapper (`agent.WrapWindowsProductionSilentHookCommandDirect`) when `HookHostIsWindows()`. The status store's root-relative names were backslash-joined on Windows and never created; they are slash-separated now and `osroot.MkdirAllNoSymlink` refuses backslash names.\\n- **`entire doctor`:** the `agy -p /hooks` probe was observed to run a full model turn on Windows and only proved agy parsed hooks.json, so it is opt-in (`ENTIRE_ANTIGRAVITY_DOCTOR_PROBE=1`). By default doctor now checks, at zero cost, that the installed hook entry is the shape this host needs (`HooksEntryMatchesHost`) and says how to reinstall. An unparseable agy version no longer produces \\\"run `agy update`\\\".\\n- **Prompt loss on later-turn manual commits (user-reported, three checkpoints):** the last rung of the condensation prompt ladder now extracts from the transcript bytes being stored (`agent.TranscriptPromptExtractor`) instead of re-reading the live path, and condensation logs which rung supplied the prompts. A new integration test runs two turns in agy's real order and commits each manually.\\n- Smaller: uninstall leaves a hooks.json with no Entire entry untouched; readers no longer leave orphan lock files; prune pairs a snapshot file with its lock; `--add-dir` must be absolute (documented, and the probe refuses a relative root); the merge-gating `e2e.yml` pins agy to 1.2.7 while nightly keeps `latest`.\\n- **Re-test on the fixed head (2026-09-22):** live two-turn agy conversation with a manual commit after each turn on `entireio/entire-sandbox` — both checkpoints carry the right prompt (the later turn at transcript offset 4), tokens recorded, status store under `~/.cache/entire/antigravity/status` with no orphan locks, doctor clean without the probe. Full antigravity e2e suite: 48 pass / 3 skipped both locally and in CI; the 5 `TestInteractive*` failures were the harness, not the CLI — interactive agy in a never-run HOME shows a color-scheme chooser and a Terms consent before the prompt. The isolated HOME now seeds `cache/onboarding.json` as complete (established by walking onboarding in a scratch HOME and diffing), and the runner clicks through both screens as a fallback.\\n- **Command smoke matrix (2026-09-22, sandbox, agy session present):** `agent list/add/remove`, `status` (+`--json`), `session list/current/info/tokens/stop`, `checkpoint list/explain/tokens/search`, `search`, `recap --static`, `activity`, `agent-help`, `doctor` (default and with the probe opt-in), `configure --summarize-provider antigravity`, `checkpoint explain --generate`, `dispatch --local --agent antigravity`, `clean --dry-run`, `disable`/`enable`. Two real bugs found and fixed: agy 1.2.x ignores stdin in print mode, so `GenerateText` now passes the prompt in argv (`dispatch --local` had handed agy an empty prompt); and the summarizer had no condenser for agy's step JSONL, so `explain --generate` reported an empty transcript — `antigravity.CondenseTranscript` now feeds it. Both re-verified live.\\n- **Shadow-branch pinning (review finding on the smoke-matrix head):** the ghost-session fix had narrowed \\\"active session with uncondensed content\\\" to \\\"active session with tracked files\\\", which would let a sibling's condensation delete the only checkpoint of a session whose first step captured a transcript before any edit. The gate now uses the same test condensation uses (`sessionHasShadowContent`: files, written steps, or task checkpoints); the ghost still has none of those. Table test covers files-only and steps-only.\\n- Merged `origin/main` a third time (session-store tests; no code conflicts).\\n- **Windows, on a real Windows host (2026-09-22 evening):** the antigravity leg is now dispatchable in `e2e-windows.yml` (agy 1.2.7 from `agy_cli_windows_x64.zip`, API-key mode; the harness redirects `USERPROFILE` with `HOME` so agy and the `entire` hooks it spawns agree on the isolated home). `TestSingleSessionManualCommit` passed on `windows-latest` ([run 35803986610](https://github.com/entireio/cli/actions/runs/35803986610)): the cmd.exe wrapper fired PreInvocation/PreToolUse/Stop, agy wrote the file through a PreToolUse hook, the Stop hook saved the shadow checkpoint, and the commit carries its `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer. The first run failed only on the harness's `sh -c` probe hook, which cmd.exe cannot run and which made agy refuse the tool call; the probe now skips itself on Windows. Runner is x64; ARM64 remains the reviewer's manual evidence. Follow-up: add antigravity to the nightly Windows leg.\\n- **2026-09-23:** Victor's Windows and review-round fixes landed directly on the branch. On top of them: the title-tee idempotency test stands up an agy on PATH (the tee is now only claimed where agy exists); the summary prompt's `[Files Modified]` list is bounded like the transcript; the e2e harness removes Antigravity's isolated home with the repo; the commit fast path treats only a missing or store-refused transcript as \\\"no content\\\" (any other stat error fails toward condensing); and **the title-tee now preserves a pre-existing user title command on Windows** — `--wrap-b64 <base64url>` where agy runs the slot through cmd.exe, re-run through cmd.exe by the tee, with uninstall restoring either form byte for byte. Previously that case failed on every model call on Windows (no tokens, user title gone); an older finding had deferred it with \\\"revisit if agy ships on Windows\\\". Review round on that head: a TTY mid-turn commit before agy's first Stop lost its trailer because the slow path required transcript growth before looking at hook-captured files (fixed: files carry the decision, growth is the fallback); the summary-prompt bounds had leaked into `explain --full` (display formatter is unbounded again, LLM callers use `FormatCondensedTranscriptForPrompt`); the Antigravity install hint used backticks the picker mangles.\\n- **Merged main again** for #2554: `agent.IsPreview` is gone, so Antigravity's preview status is documentation only (AGENT.md, agent-guide.md); this branch's own selector/list preview labels were reverted before that.\\n\\n## 2026-09-21 update\\n\\n- Merged `origin/main` again (~905 commits; 14 conflicts). Main deleted `e2e-isolated.yml` / `e2e-checkpoints-v2.yml` and gave `e2e.yml` a `test` regex input, so the antigravity CI wiring now lives only in `e2e.yml`. Adapted to main's checks: `StepContext.MetadataDirAbs` removal, the `writeTestFile` helper removal, `goconst` on the hook type literal, the transcript-read ratchet (`transcript_read_guard_test.go`; antigravity registers one read like every other agent), the e2e prompt-timeout chain (`boundPrompt`), the `userdirs` consumer audit (the statusline tee now resolves through `userdirs.CacheDirChecked`), and the summary-capable provider pin (antigravity has `GenerateText`, so it joins the list and the README).\\n- **#893 verified fixed upstream in agy 1.1.25** by bisecting real release binaries in an isolated HOME with `modelProvider: gemini` and a probe `hooks.json`: 1.1.22/1.1.23/1.1.24 fire nothing, 1.1.25/1.2.0/1.2.7 fire PreInvocation + Stop. The release notes never mention it. The antigravity leg is back in the default `e2e.yml` matrix and the dispatch-only caveats are rewritten (`AGENT.md`, `agent-guide.md`, `e2e/README.md`).\\n- **Nightly install smoke** (`nightly-e2e.yml`) gains an antigravity leg on Linux and macOS (agy from the latest release tarball, API-key mode, 25-minute step cap for the 2.5x multiplier). It can only go green once this PR is in a published nightly, since that workflow checks out the nightly tag.\\n- **Model bump:** agy 1.2.x dropped `gemini-3.5-flash-low` from `agy models` (both auth modes) and rejects it with `invalid model selection`; the harness default is now `gemini-3.8-flash-low`.\\n- CI run [35650998214](https://github.com/entireio/cli/actions/runs/35650998214) then passed `TestSingleSessionManualCommit` for antigravity in API-key mode (no ADC secret present, agy from `releases/latest`): the org `GEMINI_API_KEY` is valid and the full hook set, PreToolUse included, executes on that route.\\n\\n- **Live smoke on entire.io (2026-09-21):** `entire` built from this branch drove real agy 1.2.7 sessions in API-key mode against `entireio/entire-sandbox` on both checkpoint backends — [git-branch session](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-sandbox/session/8dfd5617-4bd3-4dab-aff5-42cc697bb429) (checkpoint `593b557e273d`) and [git-refs session](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-sandbox/session/74e375f5-45f0-47f8-9b0e-e152bdfcb0e9) (checkpoint `01M33B0YNF2RDS4ANXE7H8PZ2E`). Hooks, title-tee, trailer, condensation, push and ingestion all worked; the three trail-444 findings (dedup/append race, bare `os.Remove` in prune, `os.Stat` on the transcript path) are fixed in `9f688a8763` by anchoring the status store on `userdirs.CacheRoot` and locking the dedup-append.\\n\\n## Follow-ups (deliberately out of scope)\\n\\n- Record the model: agy's PreInvocation payload carries `modelName`, but checkpoint metadata leaves `model` empty today.\\n- entire.io's activity view labels these sessions \\\"Unknown\\\" while the search index says `Antigravity` — a web-side display mapping, not this repo.\\n- `entire doctor` could warn when agy < 1.1.25 runs in API-key mode (hooks load but never execute there).\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] `mise run check` green locally (fmt, lint 0 issues, unit + integration + canary) — re-run 2026-09-21 on the merged tree\\n- [ ] CI green on the merged tip\\n- [x] `e2e.yml` antigravity leg green in API-key mode on agy latest, no ADC secret — [run 35650998214](https://github.com/entireio/cli/actions/runs/35650998214) (`TestSingleSessionManualCommit`, 2026-09-21)\\n- [x] Analyzer validation against 385 real transcripts + real-transcript pipeline replay\\n- [x] Live smoke of install → hooks → commit → checkpoint → status on this tip\\n- [x] `mise run test:e2e --agent antigravity TestSingleSessionManualCommit` — passed live 2026-07-13 (real agy, real tokens in the condensed checkpoint)\\n- [x] Live fresh-repo smoke 2026-07-13: enable → live agy turn → commit/trailer/condensation → resume via `agy --conversation` → checkpoint-scoped token deltas across two commits\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> New agent code paths affect session lifecycle, hook-installed repo files, and checkpoint condensation; risk is mitigated by extensive tests but behavior depends on undocumented agy wire formats.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **preview** first-class support for **Antigravity CLI** (`agy`): a new `antigravity` agent package that registers with Entire, installs five workspace hooks into `.agents/hooks.json` (`entire` entry → `entire hooks antigravity <verb>`), and maps hook stdin to lifecycle events (`TurnStart`, `ToolUse`, `TurnEnd`).\\n> \\n> Lifecycle behavior is tailored to real `agy` quirks: **`TurnStart` only when `invocationNum == 0`** (follow-up pre-invocations are ignored so baselines aren’t reset); **`Stop` with `fullyIdle` → `TurnEnd`** (so `SaveStep`/checkpoints run); **post-invocation is a no-op** because transcripts aren’t ready yet; **`PrepareTranscript`** creates an empty placeholder when the transcript file is still missing after stop. **Pre-tool-use** records touched files from mutating tools, including double-encoded args and parent-dir symlink normalization (macOS `/tmp`).\\n> \\n> Also wires **non-interactive `GenerateText`** via `agy -p`, JSONL transcript chunk/reassemble (passthrough v1), registry/hooks CLI imports, integration tests over subprocess hooks, and optional **E2E** registration when `agy` is on `PATH`.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit f141838ceac0e3ae2d7cfea32e5762eaecb2ef72. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1287/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1287/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1611\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1611/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1611/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1611/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1611\",\n            \"id\": 4797333096,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7tRWnm\",\n            \"number\": 1611,\n            \"title\": \"Add `entire doctor migrate-checkpoints` (git-branch → git-refs)\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-07-02T18:45:24Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-09T11:13:01Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-09T11:12:59Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1611\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1611\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1611.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1611.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-09T11:12:59Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/735\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nAdds a migration that converts checkpoints on the `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch into per-checkpoint refs under `refs/entire/checkpoints/<shard>/<id>` — the layout the git-refs store uses — so a repo on the git-branch store can move to git-refs.\\n\\n## How it works\\n`checkpoint.MigrateBranchToRefs(ctx, repo, dryRun)` walks the v1 branch tip and, for each checkpoint:\\n- Takes the checkpoint's **current subtree object** and wraps it in a **fresh commit** (existing branch commits are *not* remapped), then points the ref at it.\\n- Because the git-refs ref tree is the branch's `<shard>/<id>` subtree **byte-for-byte**, a migrated checkpoint reads identically under either backend.\\n\\n**Idempotent:** a checkpoint whose ref already carries the same tree is skipped; a *changed* checkpoint re-migrates by **fast-forward** (the new commit parents on the existing ref, so nothing is lost from history). Safe to re-run after more branch activity.\\n\\n## The command\\n`entire doctor migrate-checkpoints` — reports `migrated / already-up-to-date / total`.\\n\\nPush behavior (as requested): the function only enqueues; the command decides whether to push:\\n- **Interactive** → prompts \\\"Push N migrated checkpoint ref(s) now?\\\"\\n- **Non-interactive** → never pushes; refs stay queued and flush on the next `git push` once git-refs is the primary store.\\n- `--dry-run` reports what would migrate without writing refs.\\n\\n## Push reuse\\nThe git-refs pre-push queue-flush is extracted into `strategy.flushCheckpointRefsQueue`, shared by the fail-soft pre-push path and the new error-surfacing `strategy.PushMigratedCheckpointRefs`. So \\\"push now\\\" goes through the exact same fast-forward + fetch/replay recovery logic (no force). No behavior change to pre-push.\\n\\n## Testing\\n- New `migrate_test.go`: basic migration + byte-identical ref trees + read-back via the git-refs store; idempotent re-run (all skipped, refs unmoved); advance-on-branch-change (fast-forward parenting); dry-run writes nothing; no-branch no-op.\\n- Build clean, lint 0 issues (the flush extraction keeps `dupl` quiet). Checkpoint + strategy unit suites pass; integration **392**; git-refs canary **58/58 +1 skip**, roger 4/4.\\n\\n## Not included (follow-ups)\\n- ULID emission, and pushing a `git-branch` mirror for downgrade safety — unchanged from the git-refs store's existing scope.\\n\\nRefs: #1471\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Migration rewrites local git refs and checkpoint data layout; push behavior differs between interactive opt-in and fail-soft pre-push, though logic is shared and tested.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **`entire doctor migrate-checkpoints`** so repos on the git-branch checkpoint store can move to the git-refs layout (`refs/entire/checkpoints/<shard>/<id>`).\\n> \\n> **`checkpoint.MigrateBranchToRefs`** walks checkpoints on `entire/checkpoints/v1`, wraps each checkpoint’s **current subtree** in a new commit, and points the per-checkpoint ref at it (enqueueing push like normal git-refs writes). It is **idempotent** (same tree → skip; changed tree → fast-forward parent) and supports **`--dry-run`**. Unmappable IDs are skipped with a warning.\\n> \\n> The doctor subcommand reports migrated / skipped / total counts. **Interactive** runs can opt into an immediate push; **non-interactive** runs leave refs queued for the next `git push`.\\n> \\n> **`strategy.flushCheckpointRefsQueue`** extracts the git-refs push-queue drain logic from pre-push; pre-push still **fail-soft** on errors, while **`PushMigratedCheckpointRefs`** surfaces errors for the migration “push now” path. **`migrate_test.go`** covers migration fidelity, idempotency, branch updates, dry-run, and no-branch no-op.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 856c7ca4901267f64d64d99860d4fa4edeff40ab. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1611/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1611/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1566\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1566/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1566/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1566/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1566\",\n            \"id\": 4770827542,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7r6vi2\",\n            \"number\": 1566,\n            \"title\": \"Per-checkpoint git-ref checkpoint store (git-refs backend)\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-06-29T18:59:25Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-02T11:36:20Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-02T11:36:17Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1566\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1566\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1566.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1566.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-02T11:36:17Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/693\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nImplements the **per-checkpoint git-ref checkpoint store** (#1471): each checkpoint is stored under its own ref `refs/entire/checkpoints/<shard>/<id>` (pointing at a commit whose tree root is that checkpoint's contents) instead of the single append-only `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch. Selectable via config, **off by default** — the git-branch store remains the default and is unchanged.\\n\\n> Targets `main`. **#1576** (path.Join cleanup) is stacked on top of this branch.\\n\\n## What's in it\\n1. **Ref resolver** — `CheckpointID.ShardFor` shards on the **last two characters for both formats** (legacy 12-hex and ULID): one positional rule, no format detection, so the shard can't be computed inconsistently between callers, and the random suffix spreads evenly while IDs stay sortable. `RefName` builds the ref and **rejects invalid/`KindUnknown` IDs** (returns an error rather than a malformed ref); `ParseRef` is the inverse. This is the git-refs namespace only — the v1 branch tree keeps its independent first-two `Path()` layout.\\n2. **git-refs store** — `gitRefsStore` implementing the full `api/checkpoint` contract over per-checkpoint refs, sharing the `treeWriter` core (so `dupl` stays quiet); registered as a git-backed `git-refs` backend. Orphan-then-parented per-checkpoint history; stamps `checkpoint_version = refs-v1`. Plus the flock-protected JSONL **push-discovery queue**. Read paths distinguish a genuinely-absent checkpoint (→ not-found) from real IO/fetch errors, which now propagate instead of being masked as \\\"not found.\\\"\\n3. **Config-aware pre-push** — when the primary is `git-refs`, `PrePush` drains the queue and pushes the per-checkpoint refs **fast-forward-only (never force)**. There is no server-side ref protection, so a force push could let a buggy/racing client clobber good remote history; instead a diverged ref is recovered by **fetch + replay** of the local-only commit onto the remote tip, then retried. It also **honors the checkpoint policy** (skips the push on a diverged/unsupported-format policy, leaving refs queued) exactly like the v1 path.\\n4. **On-demand ref fetch** — a missing checkpoint ref is fetched on read (resume/explain/attribution/tokens), so checkpoints written on another machine resolve after clone.\\n5. **`refs-v1` read/write policy** + explain-on-clone fetches the specific ref by full ID.\\n6. **e2e/CI** — backend-aware test harness, `E2E_CHECKPOINT_STORE` knob → `ENTIRE_CHECKPOINTS_PRIMARY` env override, the git-refs leg added to the PR-CI canary matrix, and an `e2e-checkpoint-store` workflow to run the full suite against either backend.\\n\\n## Rollout\\nSelected via the `checkpoints.{primary, mirrors}` taxonomy (or the `ENTIRE_CHECKPOINTS_PRIMARY` env override). `primary: git-refs` + `mirror: git-branch` is the parallel-rollout shape (refs authoritative; v1 still written locally). ID **generation** stays 12-hex for now — emitting ULIDs is a separate, deliberately deferred change; the store shards/reads **both** formats today.\\n\\n## Explicitly out of scope (follow-ups)\\n- ULID **emission** (generation switch).\\n- **Backfill/migration** of existing v1 checkpoints into per-checkpoint refs.\\n- v1-**mirror push** for full downgrade safety (mirrors are write-only locally for now).\\n- **OPF** for the git-refs push path.\\n\\n## Testing\\n`mise run lint` 0 issues (dupl quiet — `treeWriter` core is shared); full unit suite passes; `mise run test:integration` 379 pass; `go vet -tags e2e ./e2e/...` clean. Canary green in **both** modes: git-branch 59/59 + roger 4/4 (unchanged), and `E2E_CHECKPOINT_STORE=git-refs` 58/59 + roger 4/4 (the one skip is `TestAlternates`, a v1-branch-specific object-alternate rebase-sync test with no analog for the git-refs store's independent per-checkpoint refs).\\n\\nRefs: #1471\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **High Risk**\\n> Large change to checkpoint persistence, git push/sync, and remote fetch paths; wrong behavior could lose or fail to sync checkpoint metadata across machines, though git-branch remains the default.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds an optional **`git-refs`** checkpoint backend: each checkpoint lives on its own ref `refs/entire/checkpoints/<shard>/<id>` (commit tree = checkpoint contents) instead of only the shared `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch. Default remains **git-branch**; selection is via `checkpoints.primary` or **`ENTIRE_CHECKPOINTS_PRIMARY`** / **`ENTIRE_CHECKPOINTS_MIRRORS`**.\\n> \\n> The new **`gitRefsStore`** implements the same read/write contract as the branch store (shared tree helpers), stamps **`refs-v1`**, and enqueues touched refs in a flock-protected JSONL **push queue**. **Pre-push** drains that queue and **batch force-pushes** those refs when the primary is git-refs (no v1 OPF path yet). **On-demand ref fetch** (`RefFetcher` / `FetchCheckpointRef`) lets resume, explain, attribution, and tokens resolve checkpoints written on another machine after clone.\\n> \\n> **`refs-v1`** is now read/write-supported in checkpoint policy; tests that mocked “unsupported refs” move to **`refs-v2`**. E2E gains backend-aware helpers, `E2E_CHECKPOINT_STORE`, and a **`e2e-checkpoint-store`** workflow to run the suite against either backend.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 220c6b1e59e4e83f7636a014f6ea14ea262ed6a0. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1566/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1566/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1589\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1589/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1589/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1589/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1589\",\n            \"id\": 4786414979,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7st3oe\",\n            \"number\": 1589,\n            \"title\": \"feat(transcript): externalize images (Claude Code, Codex) + capture Cursor sidecar images\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"id\": 257360244,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-07-01T14:21:11Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-10T20:40:38Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-10T20:40:37Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1589\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1589\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1589.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1589.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-10T20:40:37Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"**Trail:** https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/716\\n\\n**What:** Opt-in externalization/capture of images from checkpoint sessions, for **Claude Code, Codex, and Cursor**. Each captured image is stored in a per-session `assets/` folder (raw blob + `assets/manifest.json`). Every other agent flows through unchanged (no codec, no sidecar → no-op).\\n\\nTwo mechanisms, one storage layout:\\n\\n- **Claude Code & Codex — transcript codec (lossless round trip).** Inline base64 images are lifted out of the transcript and replaced with a compact, path-bearing placeholder (`entire-asset:assets/img-<id>.<ext>`); on restore the exact bytes are re-injected in place. Contract: `ReinjectImages(ExtractImages(x)) == x`, byte-for-byte.\\n- **Cursor — sidecar store capture (preserve/view-only).** Cursor keeps pasted/generated images in a per-session SQLite blob store (`~/.cursor/chats/<workspace>/<session>/store.db`), not the JSONL transcript Entire condenses — so the transcript codec can't reach them. A new `SidecarImageProvider` capability locates that store, shells out to `sqlite3` to read image blobs (filtered by magic bytes), and stores them as checkpoint assets. There is no transcript placeholder and no reinject: Cursor reads its own store on restore, so the checkpoint assets are for preservation/viewing.\\n\\n**Why / how it helps:** Agents inline images as huge base64 in the transcript, which bloats `full.jsonl`, makes it expensive to read/summarize, and pushes large blobs to the platform. Externalizing shrinks transcripts, lets git content-address and dedupe identical images across checkpoints, and keeps restore lossless. Codex is an especially big win: real sessions carry 100+ MB of inline image base64 (OpenAI's own issue [#22603](https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/22603)); one real session in testing saved ~119 MB. Cursor's images never reached the checkpoint at all before — now they're preserved with the session.\\n\\n**How:**\\n- New `transcript/imageextract` package: a shared extraction engine + reinject routine that take a per-agent *collector*, so codecs differ only in how they find images. **Claude Code codec:** `{\\\"type\\\":\\\"image\\\",\\\"source\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"base64\\\",…}}` blocks. **Codex codec:** the `data:image/…;base64,…` data-URI marker (input, generated, and tool-output images). Byte-exact via swapping only the bare base64 *value* in place (never re-marshalling JSON), refusing any image whose bytes don't re-encode to the exact original, longest-first ordering, and a no-orphan guard.\\n- New `agent.SidecarImageProvider` optional capability + `agent.AsSidecarImageProvider` helper; the strategy layer calls it during condensation and finalize. The Cursor agent implements it via a best-effort `sqlite3` shell-out (copies the store to a temp path first so a live session can't lock/mutate it and any WAL is applied). Asset names are content-hashed (`img-<sha256>.<ext>`), so identical images dedupe.\\n- Extraction runs **before** redaction in both write paths (condensation and stop-hook finalize): base64 is high-entropy and would otherwise be flagged; the low-entropy placeholder survives redaction.\\n- Media type is detected from the decoded magic bytes (declared type as fallback) — real Codex data-URIs mislabel some PNGs as `image/jpeg`. Metadata only; the transcript's declared type is untouched, so the round trip stays byte-exact.\\n- Storage: assets written as raw blobs + manifest in the same atomic checkpoint commit; backfill/finalize replaces (never accumulates) so there are no orphaned blobs; the pre-push OPF rewrite preserves the `assets/` subtree verbatim.\\n- Opt-in via `redaction.externalize_images` (project or local settings) or `ENTIRE_EXTERNALIZE_IMAGES=1`. Off by default. Reinject is gated on placeholder presence, not the flag.\\n\\n**Agents intentionally NOT supported (verified against real sessions):**\\n- **Copilot CLI** — transcripts carry no image data at all (`attachments` always empty). No-op.\\n- **Antigravity** — not a supported Entire agent (no registry entry). Out of scope.\\n- **Gemini CLI** — no real Gemini image existed on disk to confirm the wire format live; not shipped rather than shipped on a spec guess. Stays a no-op.\\n\\n**Testing:**\\n- `mise run lint` — 0 issues; `mise run test:ci` — unit + integration + Vogon canary green on the committed tree.\\n- Codec units (Claude/Codex): byte-exact round trip; dedup; substring-safe; tiny/non-base64 left inline; compact vs spaced serialization; media-type detection; ordering.\\n- Cursor sidecar units: image blobs captured with correct media type + byte-exact data; mixed PNG/JPEG; identical images deduped; text-only store yields nothing; missing store / missing sqlite3 / empty session ref are graceful no-ops; magic-byte detection.\\n- Checkpoint integration: store→`ReadSessionContent` byte-exact (Claude/Codex); finalize/backfill re-externalizes and replaces assets; identical-transcript backfill keeps assets; OPF preserves `assets/`.\\n- **Real data:** Claude — a real 17MB session log round-trips byte-exact; Codex — 176 images across 12 real rollouts, valid magic on every asset, up to ~119 MB saved; Cursor — a real 48KB JPEG from an actual `store.db` extracted and verified.\\n- **End-to-end through the real hook binary:** Claude & Codex — inline image → condensation → finalize → real `entire/checkpoints/v1` placeholder + asset + manifest → restore reinjects byte-exact. Cursor — real hook flow with an image in `store.db` → condensation captures it as a checkpoint asset (blob + manifest, byte-exact) while the transcript stays untouched.\\n\\n**Risk / rollback:** Off by default; no behavior change unless enabled; reinject is a no-op without placeholders; Cursor capture is best-effort (silent no-op if `sqlite3`/store absent). Revert by reverting the commits on this branch.\\n\\n**Follow-ups:** live-confirm Gemini post-migration; platform-side web rendering of the stored assets (the CLI stores them; the entire.io session viewer would need to fetch/render `assets/` by placeholder id or manifest).\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1589/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1589/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1630\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1630/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1630/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1630/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1630\",\n            \"id\": 4809673932,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7t44-b\",\n            \"number\": 1630,\n            \"title\": \"Route checkpoint reads by ID kind across git backends\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-07-04T16:05:16Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-04T16:49:44Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-04T16:49:42Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1630\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1630\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1630.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1630.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-04T16:49:41Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## What\\n\\nFollow-up **#1** from the ULID-emission review (#1629). Reads previously resolved only against the *configured primary* store, so after a git-branch⇄git-refs flip — or while running the two side by side — a checkpoint stored in the other backend was reported missing (and attach could even suggest an unfixable fetch). This adds **id-kind read routing** so the CLI resolves a checkpoint by its format, wherever it lives.\\n\\n## Routing rules (per Stefan's spec)\\n\\n- **ULID** → git-refs store only; **never** the branch (regardless of active backend).\\n- **hex + git-branch primary** → branch only.\\n- **hex + git-refs primary** → refs first, then git-branch fallback (a hex checkpoint may still sit on the pre-migration v1 branch, or have been migrated into refs).\\n- `List` unions both backends; `GetCheckpointAuthor` routes the same way (`AuthorReader` preserved).\\n- **Writes are not kind-routed** — they stay on the configured primary (+ mirrors); the minted ID already matches the primary's format.\\n\\n## How\\n\\n`checkpoint.Open` now returns a `kindRoutingStore` wrapping the write fanout plus the two git read stores (reusing the primary for its kind, building the sibling). Every general read path — resume, explain, attribution, blame, tokens, attach — inherits routing for free. No config knob; it's automatic.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n`routing_store_test.go` covers: ULID→refs (incl. *\\\"a ULID never reads from the branch\\\"*), hex→branch, hex-fallback and migrated-hex-in-refs under a refs primary, `List` union, session-read routing, author routing. `open_config_test.go` updated to the new \\\"`Persistent` is always the routing store\\\" invariant.\\n\\nVerified: unit + integration (390) + E2E canary on **both** backends (git-branch 4/4, git-refs 58/59 +1 known skip).\\n\\n## Not in scope (separate follow-up #2)\\n\\nThe write-boundary guard for the ULID⇒refs invariant (warn/reject when a ULID would be condensed onto a git-branch primary). Left deliberately — it needs topology-role awareness (a git-branch *mirror* of a git-refs primary legitimately receives ULIDs).\\n\\n## Review updates (commit `80c7a4e`)\\n\\nAddressed the Cursor Bugbot findings and a `/simplify` reuse cleanup:\\n\\n- **Fetch errors no longer block the branch fallback** (Cursor, medium): `firstResolved` now falls through to the next store on a non-final store's **error** as well as on \\\"absent\\\". Under a git-refs primary, a hex read whose refs lookup fails on an on-demand ref fetch (network) still resolves from the git-branch store. The final store's result (hit/absent/error) is returned verbatim, and single-store orders are unchanged.\\n- **`List` dedups by checkpoint ID** (Cursor, low): a checkpoint present in both backends (a mirrored ULID, or a hex on the branch also migrated into refs) now appears once (most-recent kept).\\n- **Shared sort helper** (`/simplify` reuse): extracted `sortCheckpointInfosByRecency`, now used by the git-branch, git-refs, and routing `List` implementations.\\n- New tests: refs-fetch-error-falls-back-to-branch, and List-dedup across backends.\\n\\nThe rest of `/simplify` was judged already-clean: `firstResolved`/`readOrder` stay centralized (the fallback fix depends on it), and \\\"routing-as-a-backend / backends-declare-their-id-kind\\\" was deemed over-engineering for two backends. `List` querying both backends is intentional (union completeness) — a bounded per-command cost, not a hot path.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches the central `checkpoint.Open` read path for resume, explain, attach, and list; behavior changes are intentional for migration but any routing bug could surface as missing checkpoints.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Checkpoint reads no longer depend on whichever git backend is configured as primary.** `checkpoint.Open` always exposes a `kindRoutingStore` around the write fanout (primary + mirrors) plus dedicated git-branch and git-refs read stores, built via `buildKindReadStores` (reusing the primary where it matches).\\n> \\n> **Routing behavior:** ULID IDs are read only from git-refs; legacy hex IDs follow the active primary (branch-only under git-branch, refs then branch fallback under git-refs). `List` merges both backends; session reads and `GetCheckpointAuthor` use the same order; **writes** still go only through the configured primary and mirrors.\\n> \\n> Adds `routing_store.go` with `firstResolved` fallback semantics, unit tests for migration/coexistence cases, updates `open_config_test.go` expectations, and documents read routing in `sessions-and-checkpoints.md`.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 4a1f5fa174a74af3abde658cc6431d6dc653291b. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1630/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1630/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1533\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1533/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1533/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1533/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1533\",\n            \"id\": 4750646997,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7q5-5t\",\n            \"number\": 1533,\n            \"title\": \"Phase 2: pluggable checkpoint stores (registry + topology)\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-06-26T08:46:48Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-29T13:07:58Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-06-29T13:07:55Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1533\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1533\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1533.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1533.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-06-29T13:07:55Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/672\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nImplements **Phase 2 — topology + registry** of the pluggable checkpoint stores refactor (#1433). Phases 0–1 (the seam + `api/checkpoint` contract) already merged; this adds the factory, settings-driven backend selection, and independent-backend mirror fan-out.\\n\\nDefault config (no `checkpoints` block → the `git-branch` backend, no mirrors) is byte-identical to today.\\n\\n## How it works\\n\\n- **Backend registry** (`cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/registry.go`): maps a backend type to a factory + capabilities. The built-in **`git-branch`** backend (stores the committed record on the `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch) is registered by default. Other backends register via `Register`; in practice only test-only backends do (through `RegisterForTesting`), so a production binary can't select them.\\n- **Settings** (`settings.LoadCheckpointsConfig`): a `checkpoints.{primary, mirrors}` block using a discriminated `{type, config}` shape, read through a **fail-soft** loader — a missing, unreadable, whole-file-malformed, or unrelated-broken settings file quietly falls back to the default backend; it errors only on an invalid `checkpoints` block. Local settings override base wholesale.\\n- **`checkpoint.Open`** builds the primary and mirrors through the registry. When mirrors are configured, the persistent store is a **fan-out wrapper**: all reads come from the primary; writes hit the primary first, then each mirror best-effort (failures logged, never surfaced). With no mirrors it returns the primary unwrapped, preserving its concrete type and optional `AuthorReader`.\\n\\n## Two topology rules (the constraints, after review)\\n\\n- **The primary must be a git-backed backend.** `gitBacked` is a declared capability: a backend whose committed record lives in this repo's git object store. The checkpoint lifecycle (resume bootstrap, doctor reconcile, explain tree-read, push, cleanup, pre-push OPF) drives the primary through the repo and its refs, so a non-git-backed primary is rejected rather than silently half-supported. (This relaxes once Phase 3 moves the lifecycle behind the store.)\\n- **At most one backend of each type** across primary + mirrors. Two backends of the same type share the same refs/storage today, so a `git-branch` mirror under a `git-branch` primary would double-write v1 — rejected. This deliberately *permits* a different git-backed backend (e.g. a future **`git-refs`**) to mirror alongside a `git-branch` primary, i.e. the branch↔refs **parallel-rollout** topology. A future per-mirror config (same type, distinct repo/refs) could relax it further.\\n\\n## Reference backend (test-only)\\n\\n`cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/fsstore` — a filesystem/JSON implementation of the full `api/checkpoint` contract, registered only via `RegisterForTesting`. A seam integration test drives a `git-branch` primary + `fs` mirror through `Open` and asserts all four `WriteRequest` variants land in both backends while reads resolve from the primary. Serves as a worked example for a real backend.\\n\\n## Supporting changes\\n- Route `tokens profile` through `checkpoint.Open` (was the one production path still constructing a store directly).\\n- Export `checkpoint.RedactedJoinedPrompts` / `RedactSummary` so alternate backends redact prompts and summaries identically to the git store.\\n- Extract shared settings-path helpers (`settingsAbsPaths`/`worktreeSettingsPaths`).\\n- benchutil keeps its direct constructor (documented bench fixture).\\n\\n## Review\\nReviewed by Codex twice (with a `/simplify` pass between) and by the PR bots; findings addressed — local-override loader bug (Cursor Bugbot), atomic-write reuse of `jsonutil.WriteFileAtomic` (Copilot), fail-soft settings reads, fsstore fidelity (CreatedAt/metadata/summary redaction), and the taxonomy reframe above.\\n\\n## Out of scope (later phases)\\n- **Phase 3** — relocate push/fetch sync into the store; cleanup-delete + pre-push OPF fan-out to mirrors (mirrors are currently best-effort write-only and never a read/sync source without reconciliation); doctor mirror repair. This is also what unlocks a non-git-backed primary.\\n- de-gitting the `api/checkpoint` `plumbing.Hash` DTOs (needed by a real S3/gmeta backend).\\n\\n## Testing\\n`mise run check` green: fmt, lint (0 issues), and the full CI suite (unit + integration + e2e canary).\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1533/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1533/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2075\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2075/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2075/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2075/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2075\",\n            \"id\": 5197481010,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABAV0V2g\",\n            \"number\": 2075,\n            \"title\": \"feat(agent): add Goose coding agent integration\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Ar9av\",\n              \"id\": 29639685,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NjM5Njg1\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29639685?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Ar9av\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Ar9av\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Ar9av/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Ar9av/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Ar9av/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Ar9av/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Ar9av/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Ar9av/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Ar9av/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Ar9av/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Ar9av/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T21:54:18Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-19T22:03:13Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-19T22:03:13Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2075\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2075\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2075.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2075.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"Adds Goose as a built-in agent. Goose is the Agentic AI Foundation's Apache-2.0 coding agent ([goose-docs.ai](https://goose-docs.ai/)).\\n\\n```\\nentire enable --agent goose\\n```\\n\\n![enable](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ar9av/cli/assets-goose/goose/01-enable.png)\\n\\n## Why this agent\\n\\nI scored the Agentic Tools Almanac's catalogue against the four things Entire needs from an agent: a turn-start hook, a turn-end hook, a native transcript on disk, and resume by session id. No tool in that catalogue documents all four.\\n\\nGoose came closest. The Almanac's own `_shared/source-audit.md` rates it `official-only` and records a live-verified hook run on v1.44.0. It fires all four lifecycle events, puts `session_id` on hook stdin, and ships export, import and resume as first-class verbs. The Linux Foundation governs it, so the rug-pull risk is lower than the proprietary options.\\n\\nTwo runners-up and why they lost:\\n\\n- **Qwen Code** hands hooks both `session_id` and `transcript_path`, the best payload in the survey, but the audit rates it `mixed` and no resume-by-id invocation is documented.\\n- **OpenHands** only supports hooks at project scope (`.openhands/hooks.json`), which breaks enable-once-per-machine.\\n\\nI ruled out Amazon Q (AWS marks it unmaintained), Continue CLI (the Almanac live-tested it and hooks never fire in headless mode; the repo is read-only after the Cursor acquisition), Amp (no subprocess hooks at all), Cline (turn-end is documented as \\\"coming soon\\\"), Kiro (no session-end event), and Auggie (no turn-start event).\\n\\n## Existing workflows stay untouched\\n\\nEvery Go change in this PR adds lines. `git show HEAD -- '*.go' | grep '^-'` returns nothing, so no existing branch, switch case, or function body changed behaviour. Outside the new package the diff is 40 added lines across 7 files:\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `agent/registry.go` | 2 name/type constants |\\n| `hooks_cmd.go` | 1 blank import |\\n| `agent/resume_command.go` | 1 new `case` |\\n| `summarize/summarize.go` | 1 new `case` plus a builder function |\\n| `explain.go` | 2 new `case` arms |\\n| `strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go` | 1 new `case` |\\n| `activity_cmd.go` | 1 map entry |\\n\\nNothing routes through Goose unless a user runs `entire enable --agent goose`. The four `AgentType` switches I touched are the ones with no compile-time exhaustiveness check, where a missing case degrades to `Unknown` in silence, so I wired all four rather than leaving a latent gap.\\n\\n## Design: Goose keeps sessions in SQLite\\n\\n`goose info` reports the store at `~/.local/share/goose/sessions/sessions.db`. The binary carries in-place `ALTER TABLE` migrations for at least four columns, so reading that schema would couple us to something the vendor rewrites under us.\\n\\nThe integration follows the OpenCode pattern instead. It reads through `goose session export --format json` and restores through `goose session import`, and never opens the database. `--format json` is not optional: export defaults to markdown, which is lossy and cannot be imported back.\\n\\n![hooks](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ar9av/cli/assets-goose/goose/04-hooks.png)\\n\\n## What the docs got wrong\\n\\nI installed goose v1.46.0 and round-tripped a transcript through an isolated `XDG_DATA_HOME` to capture the export schema. Three findings that guessing would have missed:\\n\\n1. **The message array is `conversation`, not `messages`.** OpenCode's analogous export uses `messages`. Copying that shape yields an empty transcript with no error.\\n2. **Cache token fields disagree between layers.** The export spells them `cache_read_input_tokens` and `cache_write_input_tokens`; the SQLite columns behind them are `cache_read_tokens` and `cache_write_tokens`.\\n3. **Tool names arrive in more than one spelling.** Goose namespaces tools as `<extension>__<tool>` at runtime, but the Almanac records a live-verified case where a hook received the bare name, so a matcher on the documented spelling never fires. File extraction matches on suffix and accepts the bare, namespaced, and import-inherited spellings.\\n\\n`AGENT.md` in the new package records the protocol with per-claim provenance, tagging each fact `[verified]` (observed from the binary) or `[documented]` (read from docs, not executed).\\n\\nChunking and reassembly operate on a raw field map rather than the modelled struct, so top-level keys the package does not describe survive a round trip instead of vanishing on every checkpoint. A test asserts this against the real export.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n`gofmt`, `golangci-lint` 2.11.3, `go test -race ./cmd/...`, the integration suite, and the Vogon E2E canary all pass.\\n\\nBeyond that I ran the agent end to end against a built binary. Firing `session-start`, `turn-start` and `turn-end` produced a checkpoint carrying the right commit trailer, the extracted file list, and a transcript that reads back out through `checkpoint explain`. Token totals match the export exactly: input 124.6k, cache read 112.8k, cache write 11.8k, output 394.\\n\\n![status](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ar9av/cli/assets-goose/goose/02-status.png)\\n\\n![explain](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ar9av/cli/assets-goose/goose/03-explain.png)\\n\\nThe 40+ unit tests include a genuine v1.46.0 export committed as `testdata/real_export_v1_46_0.json`, which guards the field names above. `security_contract_test.go` pins the path-component guard on `ResolveSessionFile` and on both session-id entry points.\\n\\n## Three things to push back on\\n\\n1. **`CalculateTokenUsage` ignores its `fromOffset` argument.** Goose reports usage as session-level totals with no per-message block to scope by, so the method returns the session total whatever offset it gets. The method comment says so and a test pins it, but it deviates from the interface contract and a reviewer may want a different shape.\\n2. **The hook payload is `[documented]`, not `[verified]`.** Firing a hook needs a configured model provider (`goose doctor` reports none), so I could not execute one here. The payload shape and native tool names come from docs plus the Almanac's live test on v1.44.0. No `e2e/` harness ships for the same reason.\\n3. **I set `IsPreview() = true` and left `agent-help` classification alone.** CLAUDE.md calls those product judgments, so I took the safe default and am flagging both rather than deciding them.\\n\\n## Screenshots branch\\n\\nThe images above live on the `assets-goose` branch of my fork, kept out of this diff on purpose.\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2075/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2075/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1381\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1381/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1381/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1381/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1381\",\n            \"id\": 4599855183,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7jQCNy\",\n            \"number\": 1381,\n            \"title\": \"feat(antigravity): populate checkpoint prompt field via condensation-time transcript decoding\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-06-05T20:18:36Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-01T15:31:30Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-01T15:31:28Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1381\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1381\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1381.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1381.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-01T15:31:28Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/531\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nFills the previously-empty committed checkpoint `\\\"prompt\\\"` field for the **Antigravity (agy)** agent.\\n\\n**Root cause:** agy writes its transcript file *after* its `Stop` hook returns, so the framework's TurnEnd prompt backfill (`lifecycle.go`) sees an empty transcript and `prompt.txt` stays empty. Condensation (`git commit`) re-reads the now-populated live transcript but only read prompts from `prompt.txt` — it never re-extracted from the transcript. So agy checkpoints landed with an empty prompt.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n- **`agent/antigravity/transcript.go`** — implement `PromptExtractor.ExtractPrompts` (parse `USER_INPUT` steps, strip the `<USER_REQUEST>` wrapper) and `TranscriptAnalyzer` (`GetTranscriptPosition` + `ExtractModifiedFilesFromOffset`, reusing the existing `decodeAgyString`/`resolveAgySymlinks` helpers). Mirrors the codex template; one shared `agyStep` schema, one offset convention.\\n- **`strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`** — a general `resolvePromptsFromLateFlushedTranscript` fallback called from **both** prompt-resolution sites (`extractSessionData`, `extractSessionDataFromLiveTranscript`) when prompts are empty, re-extracting from the populated live transcript at condensation. General to any `PromptExtractor`; a safe no-op for agents that already capture prompts at TurnStart (guarded by `len(data.Prompts) == 0`).\\n\\n## Notable\\n\\n- **Behavior note:** implementing `TranscriptAnalyzer` also opts agy into transcript-based modified-file extraction + mid-turn detection (`hasNewTranscriptWork`), which previously short-circuited. It degrades gracefully (empty transcript → position 0 → no spurious work), and transcript-derived paths match `parsePreToolUse` (absolute, symlink-resolved) so they dedupe cleanly with the hook-derived set.\\n- **Out of scope:** token counting (handled by the `OutOfBandTokenSource` title-tee, #1356). **No UI changes** — the merged entire.io `AntigravityParser` already renders prompts from the transcript.\\n- **Attribution was investigated and is already correct** — `initial_attribution.agent_lines` reflects agent work (verified 3 lines / 100% on a real agy checkpoint). The `prompt_attributions[].agent_lines_added` diagnostic is `0` at checkpoint 1 *by design* (a base→last-checkpoint snapshot with no prior checkpoint); it is not the result field. **No attribution code changed.**\\n- **Minor follow-up:** the mutating-tool-name list (`write_to_file`/`replace_file_content`/`multi_replace_file_content`) is duplicated between `transcript.go` and `lifecycle.go:parsePreToolUse` — could be unified into one shared set.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] `mise run check` green — gofmt, golangci-lint (0 issues), `test:ci` (unit + integration + Vogon canary, `-race`)\\n- [x] **Verified end-to-end against real agy 1.0.5**: the committed `prompt.txt` on `entire/checkpoints/v1` equals the user's prompt (empty before this fix)\\n- [x] Integration test `TestAntigravity_PromptInCheckpointMetadata` with a **verified negative control** (empty-transcript-through-commit → test fails), proving the condensation-time path is load-bearing\\n- [x] Offset off-by-one and absolute-path convention each pinned by a focused test\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches commit-time condensation and checkpoint metadata for all agents that use the empty-prompt fallback, but the path is guarded and only runs when prompts are missing; Antigravity also gains transcript-based file tracking, which could affect mid-turn detection.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Antigravity checkpoints no longer ship with an empty **prompt** when the agent flushes its JSONL transcript **after** `Stop` (TurnEnd backfill saw an empty file). The Antigravity agent now implements **`PromptExtractor`** and **`TranscriptAnalyzer`**: user text from `USER_INPUT` steps (stripping `<USER_REQUEST>`), non-blank line offsets, and deduped paths from mutating tool calls via existing `decodeAgyString` / `resolveAgySymlinks`.\\n> \\n> Manual-commit **condensation** adds `resolvePromptsFromLateFlushedTranscript`, invoked from both shadow-branch and live-transcript extraction when `prompt.txt` is still empty—only for agents that implement `PromptExtractor`, so other agents are unchanged.\\n> \\n> Coverage includes unit tests for extraction/offsets/paths, a strategy test for the fallback helper, and integration **`TestAntigravity_PromptInCheckpointMetadata`** (empty transcript through Stop, late populate, then commit asserts `prompt.txt`).\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit a53079147fdfb0f581d2b7d053fc8272cf4b3c87. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1381/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1381/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1995\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1995/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1995/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1995/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1995\",\n            \"id\": 5151833785,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7_GruZ\",\n            \"number\": 1995,\n            \"title\": \"fix(trail): send the pre-image anchor with --patch suggested changes\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-08-14T13:01:13Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-17T07:30:35Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-17T07:30:33Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1995\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1995\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1995.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1995.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-17T07:30:33Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1048\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\n`entire trail finding add --patch/--patch-file` has **never once succeeded**. The CLI built the suggested change from `change_type` + `patch` + `instruction` and nothing else, but the API requires a full pre-image anchor for any non-`manual_instruction` change:\\n\\n```go\\n// entire-api internal/store/suggested_changes.go (and the identical BFF check)\\npatch → expected_file_path → expected_file_hash\\n      → expected_start_line → expected_end_line → expected_lines\\n```\\n\\n`expected_file_path` was just the first check to fail; filling only that field would have moved the error to `expected_file_hash`. Every call came back with `invalid_request: unified_diff change requires expected_file_path`, so only `--instruction` ever got through — which is why CLI-created findings carry prose instead of diffs, and why `entire trail finding apply` had no CLI-created patches to apply.\\n\\n## Since when\\n\\nBroken since the flags shipped.\\n\\n| When | What |\\n|---|---|\\n| 2026-05-18 | Server-side requirement lands in entire.io |\\n| 2026-06-05 | `43067b86d` adds `--patch`/`--patch-file`, sending only `change_type` + `patch` |\\n| 2026-06-11 | `38e470409` fixes the endpoint and surfaces per-item errors — the failure becomes visible |\\n\\nNo version of `trail_review_cmd.go` has ever assigned `ExpectedFilePath` (verified across all 29 commits touching the file).\\n\\n**Measured impact.** Scanning every agent transcript on one machine (954 files, 142k records): 92 real `trail finding add` invocations, 68 successful — all `-m`/`--instruction` only. 10 used `--patch`; 9 failed with this exact error across 6 review sessions on 3 separate days, and the 1 success is the verification call for this branch. Six times an agent reached for a machine-applicable fix and silently fell back to prose.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\nDerive the anchor from the patch plus the worktree:\\n\\n- **path + line span** — parsed from the diff headers and the old-side `@@` ranges, spanning min-start to max-end across hunks\\n- **`expected_lines`** — the byte-exact pre-image slice, line endings intact (deliberately *not* CRLF-normalized like `selected_text`)\\n- **`expected_file_hash`** — the git blob OID, so it matches `git hash-object <file>`, read through the repository's object format so a sha256 repo isn't handed a sha1 value\\n\\nCases the API would reject now fail locally with an actionable message instead of a server error: multi-file patches, file-creation patches (`--- /dev/null` has no pre-image to anchor to → use `--instruction`), hunks past EOF, missing files. Patch paths run through the same whole-patch safety check the apply path already used, so a patch is held to one standard whether it's being written or applied.\\n\\n## Behavior changes\\n\\nTwo, both deliberate:\\n\\n- **A `--patch` with no `--file` now gets a location.** It previously produced a locationless `whole_change` finding even though the patch named the file and lines exactly. It now lands on the patch's file and full hunk span (`Location: .gitignore:3-5`). An explicit `--file`/`--line` still wins — the anchor only fills a gap.\\n- **A `--file` naming a different file than the patch modifies is rejected**, rather than storing a finding whose location and fix point at different places. The API forces single-file patches, so there's no sensible reading of that state.\\n\\nA line-range disagreement (`--line 45` with hunks at 10–20) is deliberately **not** checked: pointing at where a problem manifests while fixing elsewhere in the same file is legitimate.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- Posted real findings with `--patch-file` to a trail: accepted, `unified_diff` with the right file, location derived correctly. Mismatch guard rejects as expected. Test findings dismissed.\\n- `mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci` all clean.\\n- New unit tests cover the full anchor payload (via `reflect.DeepEqual` on the whole request, which caught that the stored patch is trimmed), the location defaulting and precedence, the mismatch rejection, and six parser rejection cases.\\n\\n## Open questions for review\\n\\n- **`expected_file_hash` has no consumer** anywhere — CLI, cell, or frontend — and no documented algorithm. I picked the git blob OID because it's repo-native and hand-verifiable, and documented the convention on the API type. Worth pinning down while there's still only one producer: a later consumer computing it differently would read every CLI-created suggestion as stale.\\n- **Hash source is the worktree, not the review head blob.** The worktree is consistent with the patch (both written against the same tree); the head blob would be reproducible by the server. Reasonable people differ — flagging rather than deciding unilaterally.\\n\\n## Follow-ups not taken\\n\\n- `gitBlobHash` is now the third \\\"git blob hash of content\\\" in the tree (`strategy/content_overlap.go:534`, `checkpoint/migrate.go:234`); extracting into `gitrepo` is a clean mechanical follow-up.\\n- The anchor parser and the apply path's `validateUnifiedDiffPatchPaths` still scan the patch separately; unifying them means touching the apply path, which deserves its own diff.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> <sup>[Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) is generating a summary for commit ea829fbb1c8e77b835d86071aedd4f92123de489. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1995/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1995/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1560\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1560/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1560/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1560/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1560\",\n            \"id\": 4770320551,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7r5DhN\",\n            \"number\": 1560,\n            \"title\": \"explain: enrich JSON summary and surface list truncation\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"computermode\",\n              \"id\": 2917645,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTc2NDU=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2917645?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/computermode\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-06-29T17:37:50Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-29T20:43:53Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-06-29T20:43:52Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1560\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1560\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1560.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1560.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-06-29T20:43:52Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/692\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What\\n\\nEnriches `entire explain` output across four small, related gaps:\\n\\n1. **Full summary in `--json`** — the JSON export previously dropped everything except `intent`/`outcome`, even though the prose view already renders friction, open items, and learnings. `--json` now exposes the full persisted `Summary` (`friction`, `open_items`, and categorized `learnings` → `repo`/`code`/`workflow`).\\n2. **List truncation visibility** — the prose branch list silently capped at 100 checkpoints. It now prints a stderr note when checkpoints are hidden, pointing at `--json --limit <N>`.\\n3. **Fast-fail `--generate` on imported checkpoints** — the read-only rejection now happens on metadata alone, before fetching transcript blobs.\\n4. **Clearer no-trailer message** — distinguishes a commit that exists but wasn't created during an Entire session from a commit that wasn't found.\\n\\n## How\\n\\n- `explain_export.go`: extended `checkpointSessionSummary` with `learnings`/`friction`/`open_items` (all `omitempty`); new `summaryToExportJSON` helper reuses the existing `hasAnyLearning` so empty learnings stay `nil` (no `{}` noise). Redaction is already applied upstream at persist time, so no new privacy surface.\\n- `explain.go`: branch list probes `branchCheckpointsLimit+1` and slices to the cap via the extracted, unit-tested `capBranchCheckpoints`; threaded `errW` through the call chain. Added a metadata-only `ReadCheckpoint` guard before the content load for imported `--generate`. Reworded the no-trailer hint.\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- The `--limit` flag help still reads \\\"Only meaningful with --json\\\" — accurate, since the prose path keeps the fixed 100 cap and points users at `--json --limit` rather than honoring `--limit` itself.\\n- Truncation wording is deliberately vague (\\\"more exist\\\") — the `limit+1` probe only proves ≥1 more exists, never an exact count.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n`mise run check` passes: fmt clean, lint 0 issues, all unit + integration + e2e canary tests green. New tests: `TestSessionMetadataToJSON_FullSummary`, `TestSessionMetadataToJSON_EmptySummaryStaysClean`, `TestCapBranchCheckpoints`, plus a `--generate`-on-imported rejection assertion in `TestImportClaudeCode_EndToEnd`.\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> CLI output and JSON export parity only; no auth, persistence, or security surface changes beyond exposing summary fields already stored and shown in prose.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **`entire checkpoint explain --json`** now includes the full persisted session summary—`friction`, `open_items`, and categorized `learnings`—via `summaryToExportJSON`, matching what the prose view already shows. Empty categories stay omitted (`omitempty`).\\n> \\n> **Branch / list views** (`checkpoint list`, default explain) fetch `limit+1` checkpoints, cap at 100 with `capBranchCheckpoints`, and print a **stderr** note when more exist (pointing at `--json --limit <N>`). `errW` is threaded through the branch explain call chain so truncation never pollutes piped stdout.\\n> \\n> **`--generate`** on imported checkpoints is rejected after a metadata-only `ReadCheckpoint` check, avoiding prefetch and transcript loads for a guaranteed read-only failure.\\n> \\n> The **no Entire-Checkpoint trailer** hint now states the commit exists but was not created in an Entire session (or the trailer was removed).\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit cdd32fa9502414035a774a59b97a3d615ed87bdc. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1560/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1560/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1568\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1568/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1568/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1568/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1568\",\n            \"id\": 4771529547,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7r9EIU\",\n            \"number\": 1568,\n            \"title\": \"feat(attach): warn on empty transcript, capture footer, amend-fail note\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"computermode\",\n              \"id\": 2917645,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTc2NDU=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2917645?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/computermode\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-06-29T20:55:20Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-01T22:07:09Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-01T22:07:07Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1568\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1568\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1568.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1568.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-01T22:07:07Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/699\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What\\n\\nImproves `entire attach` diagnosability and feedback across four small, related changes — no behavioral regressions, attach still always writes the checkpoint.\\n\\n1. **Warn on a transcript that parses to nothing** (highest value). When `extractTranscriptMetadata` yields no first prompt and zero turns, attach previously produced a contentless checkpoint silently. It now emits a warning to **stderr** and continues. It stays a *warning, not a hard error*: agents whose user-content shape isn't matched by the generic JSONL/Gemini parser (codex/copilot/pi/factory) can legitimately yield empty metadata from a valid transcript, and token usage is still computed agent-specifically. Under `--review` the warning additionally calls out that the review prompt will be empty.\\n\\n2. **Post-attach summary footer.** A real attach now prints `Captured: <turns> · <model> · <tokens>` from data already in scope, reusing the existing `totalTokens`/`formatTokenCount` helpers. Each segment is omitted when its value is absent (turns 0, empty model, nil token usage).\\n\\n3. **Surface the amend-failure reason.** When `--amend` fails, the reason is now printed to stderr (`Could not amend the commit automatically (...)`) in addition to the existing debug log, so the user knows the best-effort amend was attempted before the manual-paste trailer fallback. Polish, not a correctness fix — the recovery path already worked.\\n\\n4. **Help-text accuracy.** `--force` help notes the amend is best-effort; Long help documents transcript-based agent auto-detection.\\n\\n## How\\n\\n- Threads an `errW io.Writer` through `runAttach` (the cobra caller passes `cmd.ErrOrStderr()`) so warnings/notes land on stderr, never interleaved with stdout success lines.\\n- Extracts three small helpers — `warnEmptyTranscriptMetadata`, `printAttachFooter`/`attachSummaryLine`, and `amendOrPrintTrailer` (the last de-duplicates the two amend call sites and keeps `runAttach` under the `maintidx` linter threshold).\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nAdded `TestAttach_WarnsOnEmptyTranscriptMetadata` (+ `_Review` variant), `TestAttachSummaryLine` (footer builder incl. nil-token and empty cases), and `TestAttach_NonInteractivePrintsTrailerForManualPaste`. Existing `runAttach` call sites updated for the new signature.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n`mise run check` passed: lint 0 issues, unit + integration (59 vogon) + e2e canary (4) all green.\\n\\n## Reviewer notes\\n\\n- The amend *hard-fail* path isn't cleanly stubbable without injecting the git command, so it remains untested; the non-interactive trailer branch is covered instead.\\n- The empty-transcript warning reports the `--agent` flag value verbatim (per spec), which may be the `claude-code` default even when auto-detection later resolves a different agent.\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> CLI-only UX and messaging around attach; checkpoint write semantics are unchanged and failures remain non-fatal where documented.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **`entire attach`** gets clearer CLI feedback without changing the core rule that a checkpoint is still written.\\n> \\n> When transcript parsing yields **no user prompts and zero turns**, attach now **warns on stderr** (and continues). With **`--review`**, the warning also notes an **empty review prompt**. A new stdout line **`Captured: <turns> · <model> · <tokens>`** summarizes what was stored; segments are omitted when unknown.\\n> \\n> **Commit amend** behavior is centralized in **`amendOrPrintTrailer`**: failures log and print **`Could not amend the commit automatically (...)`** on stderr, then still show the manual **`Entire-Checkpoint`** trailer. **`runAttach`** takes a separate **`errW`** writer so diagnostics stay off stdout. Help text documents **best-effort `--force` amend** and **agent auto-detection** when `--agent` misses the transcript.\\n> \\n> Tests cover empty-metadata warnings, the footer builder, and non-interactive trailer fallback; existing **`runAttach`** call sites pass the new stderr argument.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit ae3a8aac32c85344d1dc8eb7c4417304b41daa6b. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1568/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1568/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1007\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1007/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1007/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1007/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1007\",\n            \"id\": 4309508151,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7UpZi4\",\n            \"number\": 1007,\n            \"title\": \"Cursor: agent-lifecycle export/import via CheckpointContributor + CheckpointRestorer\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"id\": 881031,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 7,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-04-22T13:57:33Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-14T08:15:52Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-14T08:15:51Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": true,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1007\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1007\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1007.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1007.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nExport and import of Cursor Agent sessions are wired through the agent lifecycle via `CheckpointContributor` and `CheckpointRestorer`. No standalone Cursor commands are needed.\\n\\nThis update also makes the post-restore hint metadata-aware:\\n\\n- Cursor Agent checkpoints print `agent --resume <id>`.\\n- Cursor IDE checkpoints keep the existing `Open this project in Cursor.` message.\\n- Legacy checkpoints fall back to the recorded model so older restored sessions still get the best available hint.\\n\\n## User Flow\\n\\n1. Cursor Agent or Cursor IDE runs with Entire hooks installed.\\n2. On checkpoint save, Cursor contributes its session archive into the checkpoint metadata.\\n3. `entire rewind` restores the worktree and asks Cursor to restore contributed files.\\n4. `entire resume` restores logs from committed checkpoints and prints the correct resume hint for the original Cursor client.\\n\\n## Implementation Notes\\n\\n- Added agent-level resume formatting context with checkpoint metadata.\\n- Cursor hooks now persist whether the checkpoint came from Cursor Agent or Cursor IDE.\\n- Session and checkpoint metadata carry agent-specific key/value data through condensation and restore.\\n- Cursor restore still rebuilds the native chat/transcript state from checkpointed files.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/...`\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor`\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint`\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy`\\n- [x] `mise run lint`\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1007/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1007/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1591\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1591/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1591/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1591/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1591\",\n            \"id\": 4787371117,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7sxCJw\",\n            \"number\": 1591,\n            \"title\": \"feat(transcript): externalize images from Codex transcripts\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"id\": 257360244,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-07-01T16:24:52Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-01T16:28:33Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-01T16:27:53Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1591\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1591\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1591.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1591.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-01T16:27:53Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/717\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n**Stacked on #1589** (base branch `feat-image-externalize`) — this PR is only the Codex delta.\\n\\n**What:** Extend image externalization to Codex. Codex rollout JSONL embeds images as base64 data-URIs (`data:image/…;base64,…`) — in `input_image` image_url values, user messages, and `function_call_output` — and inlines multi-MB generated images the same way. This lifts them into per-session checkpoint `assets/` blobs with a placeholder, and reinjects byte-exactly on restore, exactly like the Claude Code codec.\\n\\n**Why / how it helps:** Codex is a bigger win than Claude here. Real sessions on disk carry 100+ MB of inline image base64; OpenAI's own issue [#22603](https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/22603) reports image-heavy rollouts taking minutes to open. Externalizing shrinks `full.jsonl`, cuts what's pushed to the platform, dedupes identical images, and keeps restore lossless. Also: without externalization, an inline Codex `input_image` base64 (which redaction does *not* skip, since the enclosing type is `input_image`, not `image`) can be mangled by the high-entropy redaction pass — extracting before redaction preserves it.\\n\\n**How:**\\n- Refactor the codec into a shared extraction engine + reinject routine that take a per-agent *collector*; codecs now differ only in how they find images.\\n- New `codexCodec` keyed on the `data:image/…;base64,…` marker (not a specific field), so input, generated, and tool-output images are covered uniformly. The bare base64 value is swapped (the tiny `data:…;base64,` prefix stays inline), so the swap is format-agnostic and byte-exact — the same value-swap contract as Claude.\\n- Detect the media type from the decoded magic bytes (declared type as fallback): real Codex data-URIs mislabel some PNGs as `image/jpeg`, so the asset filename/manifest should reflect the actual content. Metadata only — the transcript's declared type is untouched, so the round trip stays byte-exact.\\n- Register `agent.AgentTypeCodex` in the codec map. No changes to condensation/persistence/finalize/settings — that plumbing is agent-agnostic; reuses the same opt-in `redaction.externalize_images` flag.\\n\\nCodex's `SanitizePortableTranscript` (which runs before `full.jsonl` is chunked) only drops `compaction` lines and strips `reasoning.encrypted_content`; image-bearing message and tool-output lines pass through, so the placeholder survives and the byte-exact contract holds against the stored bytes.\\n\\n**Testing:**\\n- `mise run lint` — 0 issues; `mise run test:ci` — unit + integration + Vogon canary green on the committed tree.\\n- Codec units: data-URI round trip; `function_call_output` embedded data-URI; multiple images in one message (the real Codex case); dedup; text-only no-op; tiny data-URI left inline; media-type detection (jpeg vs png); extract-before-redact ordering (secret redacted, image reinjects). Claude codec unchanged and still passing.\\n- **Real-data:** ran the codec over real Codex rollouts — 176 images across 12 sessions, every asset valid PNG/JPEG magic, extract→reinject byte-exact, up to ~119 MB saved in one session.\\n- **Integration (real hook flow):** a Codex session (rollout with a data-URI image) → post-commit condensation → stop finalize → assert the real `entire/checkpoints/v1` `full.jsonl` carries the placeholder (base64 gone), the asset blob + `manifest.json` are written, and `ReadSessionContent` reinjects byte-exact.\\n\\n**Risk / rollback:** Off by default (opt-in flag), no-op for agents without a codec, reinject is a no-op without placeholders. Revert by reverting the two commits on this branch. Incidental large data-URIs embedded in fetched tool output are also externalized — harmless (still bloat, still lossless).\\n\\n**Follow-ups:** Cursor/Copilot/others; platform-side web rendering of the stored asset (shared with #1589).\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1591/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1591/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1616\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1616/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1616/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1616/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1616\",\n            \"id\": 4798051681,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7tTsv6\",\n            \"number\": 1616,\n            \"title\": \"cli: add code search with multi-region fan-out and TUI tab (ENT-990)\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"evisdren\",\n              \"id\": 256443556,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD0kEpA\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256443556?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/evisdren\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 10,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-07-02T20:43:34Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-07T19:30:45Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-07T19:30:44Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1616\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1616\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1616.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1616.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-07T19:30:44Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\n- Adds `cmd/entire/cli/codesearch/` — client package for peregrine's `/search/api/search` endpoint\\n- Wires `--code` and `--case-sensitive` flags into `entire search`, gated behind `ENTIRE_CODE_SEARCH=1`\\n- Multi-region fan-out using the shared cell-routing foundation (`cell_fanout.go`): list repos → group by cell → parallel search with per-cell timeouts → merge results\\n- Adds a **Code tab** (key `4`) to the interactive search TUI, showing code search results alongside checkpoints, sessions, and commits\\n- Code search runs in parallel with checkpoint search when the TUI launches\\n- Detail pane shows file location, score, and context lines (before/after) for the selected match\\n\\n## How it works\\n\\n| Scenario | Auth path | Behavior |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `--code query` (no filter) | `ListRepos` → group by cell → `fanOutCells` | Fan-out across all cells |\\n| `--code --repo owner/name query` | Single cell via repo filter resolution | Single cell (repo's owner) |\\n| `--code repo:owner/name query` | Same (inline filter parsed) | Single cell |\\n| `--code --all-repos query` | Fan-out (same as no filter) | Fan-out across all cells |\\n| TUI Code tab | Async `performCodeSearch` tea.Cmd | Parallel with checkpoint search |\\n\\n## TUI Code Tab\\n\\n- Hidden behind `ENTIRE_CODE_SEARCH=1` feature flag (tab only appears when enabled)\\n- Results show `repo:path:line` as the title with the matching context line below\\n- Detail pane shows full context (before/after lines), repo, path, line, column, and score\\n- Full-screen detail view via Enter key, same as other tabs\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/codesearch/codesearch.go` — client types and `Search()` function\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/codesearch/codesearch_test.go` — client tests\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search_cmd.go` — command wiring, fan-out via shared `fanOutCells`, output formatters\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search_cmd_test.go` — command tests (merge, output, flags)\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search_tui.go` — Code tab: result rendering, detail pane, async fetch, key bindings\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search_tui_test.go` — updated for new `newSearchModel` signature\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/codesearch/...` passes\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/ -run TestSearch` passes\\n- [x] `mise run lint` clean\\n- [x] Manual testing with `ENTIRE_CODE_SEARCH=1 entire search auth`\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> New authenticated multi-cell fan-out and repo-index resolution can return incomplete results on truncation or partial failures; behavior is gated but touches core search UX and shared cell routing.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Introduces **code search** for `entire search`, behind **`ENTIRE_CODE_SEARCH=1`**, calling peregrine via a new **`codesearch`** package (`GET /api/v1/search/api/search` through the cell API gateway).\\n> \\n> **CLI:** New **`--code`** and **`--case-sensitive`** flags; checkpoint-only flags (`--author`, `--date`, `--branch`, `--page`) are rejected with `--code`. Repo scoping uses **`--repo`**, **`--all-repos`**, or inline **`repo:`** only—**`author:` / `date:` / `branch:`** stay in the query as literal text. Default scope is the current repo via **`currentRepoSlugWithForge`** (forge-prefixed slugs for index matching). Output is grep-style text or JSON, including **`failed_jurisdictions`** on partial multi-region failures.\\n> \\n> **Routing:** **`searchAllCells`** lists repos from the control plane, resolves filters to ULIDs (**`resolveRepoFilters`**, BFF-aligned), groups by cell, and uses shared **`fanOutCells`** with per-cell timeouts; **`mergeSearchResults`** ranks by score, dedupes, caps **`--limit`**, and tolerates partial cell errors.\\n> \\n> **TUI:** When the flag is on, search gains a **Code** tab (key **4**), async code search alongside checkpoint search, list/detail UI for matches, and generation-guarded stale result handling.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 66a9c67767467f64c0db19841cb1b6b94f9f5faf. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1616/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1616/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1315\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1315/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1315/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1315/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1315\",\n            \"id\": 4566355568,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7hhytS\",\n            \"number\": 1315,\n            \"title\": \"Mirror v1.1 checkpoint writes\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"pfleidi\",\n              \"id\": 118549,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjExODU0OQ==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118549?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pfleidi\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 2,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-06-01T20:55:16Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-02T01:48:39Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-06-01T22:06:31Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1315\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1315\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1315.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1315.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-06-01T22:06:30Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/469\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Goal\\n\\nMake the deferred user-facing checkpoint write paths compatible with `strategy_options.checkpoints_version: \\\"1.1\\\"` without generalizing the checkpoint writer yet.\\n\\nWhen the option is exactly the JSON string `\\\"1.1\\\"`, `session attach` and `checkpoint explain --generate` continue writing existing v1 metadata first, then mirror the resulting `entire/checkpoints/v1` tip to `refs/entire/checkpoints/v1.1`.\\n\\n## Scope and decisions\\n\\n- Keeps the change narrowly scoped to `session attach` and `checkpoint explain --generate`.\\n- Leaves `checkpoint.GitStore` as-is; mirroring is not moved into the generic writer in this step.\\n- Uses the existing settings semantics: only exact string `\\\"1.1\\\"` enables the v1.1 mirror.\\n- Treats foreground command paths differently from hooks: mirror failures return an error instead of being log-only.\\n- Leaves successful v1 writes in place when v1.1 mirroring fails, with wrapped errors that name both refs.\\n- Runs the strict mirror before later success-side effects: before attach session-state save / commit amendment, and before the explain success block.\\n\\n## Implementation\\n\\n- Adds a CLI strict mirror helper gated by `settings.MirrorsToV1CustomRef(ctx)`.\\n- Reads the current `paths.MetadataBranchName` tip and sets `paths.MetadataRefName` to that exact hash.\\n- Calls the helper immediately after `store.WriteCommitted(...)` in attach and after `store.UpdateSummary(...)` in explain summary generation.\\n- Keeps hook-side mirroring behavior separate, preserving its log-only failure policy.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- Covers opt-in mirroring, disabled no-op behavior, missing v1 metadata branch handling, advancing an existing custom ref, and replacing a locally-ahead custom ref with the exact v1 tip.\\n- Covers `session attach` mirroring through unit coverage and the real integration-test CLI path.\\n- Covers `checkpoint explain --generate` mirroring with a deterministic summary-provider stub.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `mise run build`\\n- `mise run lint`\\n- `mise run test:ci`\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes when and how checkpoint metadata refs are updated on user-facing attach and summary-generation paths; failures can abort the command after a successful v1 write.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> When `strategy_options.checkpoints_version` is exactly **`\\\"1.1\\\"`**, deferred CLI writes still land on **`entire/checkpoints/v1`**, then a new strict helper **`mirrorToV1CustomRef`** points **`refs/entire/checkpoints/v1.1`** at that branch tip (force-overwrite local mirror; v1 stays canonical).\\n> \\n> **`session attach`** calls the mirror right after **`WriteCommitted`**; **`entire explain --generate`** calls it after **`UpdateSummary`**. Mirror failures **return an error** (unlike hook-side mirroring, which only logs), run **before** later success steps (attach session state / commit amend, explain success output), and leave the v1 write in place with a message naming both refs.\\n> \\n> Unit, attach/explain, and integration tests cover opt-in mirroring, disabled no-op, missing v1 branch, advancing the custom ref, and resetting a locally-ahead custom ref to the v1 tip.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 2e3b5d8245899bc1947b894d9fa4a0932ecd94f2. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1315/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1315/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1540\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1540/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1540/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1540/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1540\",\n            \"id\": 4754428342,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7rGZyi\",\n            \"number\": 1540,\n            \"title\": \"import: support cursor, pi, factory, codex, copilot, gemini\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"computermode\",\n              \"id\": 2917645,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTc2NDU=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2917645?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/computermode\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-06-26T18:59:14Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-29T20:32:33Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-06-29T20:32:31Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1540\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1540\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1540.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1540.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-06-29T20:32:31Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/676\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\n## What\\r\\n\\r\\nExtends `entire import` (PR #1527, Claude Code only) to the other supported agents: **Cursor, Pi, Factory AI Droid, Codex, Copilot CLI, and Gemini CLI**. Each `entire import <agent>` subcommand now surfaces automatically. Supports https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/1336.\\r\\n\\r\\nOpenCode is intentionally **out of scope**: it has no on-disk transcript Entire can read (transcripts only materialize via `opencode export`), and its sessions aren't repo-attributable.\\r\\n\\r\\n## How\\r\\n\\r\\nPR #1527 built the agent-agnostic orchestration (discovery loop, idempotent per-turn IDs, redaction, checkpoint write) behind an `Importer` seam. This adds one self-contained `Importer` per agent and registers them in the `importers` slice — no command wiring, since `import_cmd.go` iterates `agentimport.All()`.\\r\\n\\r\\nEach importer reuses its agent's **existing** transcript methods rather than re-encoding parsing:\\r\\n\\r\\n| Agent | Granularity | Tokens / Model |\\r\\n|---|---|---|\\r\\n| cursor | per-turn | none (nil tokens, empty model — records neither) |\\r\\n| pi | per-turn | `CalculateTokenUsage` + `ExtractModel` (branch-aware) |\\r\\n| factoryai-droid | per-turn | subagent-aware `CalculateTotalTokenUsage`; model from adjacent `.settings.json` |\\r\\n| codex | per-turn | cumulative-usage delta; **global store**, filtered by `session_meta.cwd` |\\r\\n| copilot-cli | per-turn | `CalculateTokenUsage`; **flat store**, filtered by `session.start` cwd/gitRoot |\\r\\n| gemini | per-session | single JSON doc, message-index offsets → one checkpoint/session |\\r\\n\\r\\nCodex and Copilot share a `repoMatches` helper (equal-or-descendant, symlink-normalized) so their global/flat stores only import the current repo's sessions.\\r\\n\\r\\nImported checkpoints keep the merged Claude behavior: commit-less, `Kind:\\\"imported\\\"`, `[imported]` label, not rewindable, idempotent per `sha256(sessionID + \\\"/\\\" + turnUUID)`.\\r\\n\\r\\nNo changes to `claude.go`, `Run`, the `Importer` interface, or `Turn`.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Testing\\r\\n\\r\\n- Per-agent unit tests: `Discover` (lookback / `--session` filter / repo-match) and `SplitTurns` (turn boundaries, prompt/model/tokens; Gemini single-turn).\\r\\n- Registry test asserts all seven importers register with distinct names.\\r\\n- End-to-end `Run` test through the Cursor importer (nil tokens / empty model) confirms the generic pipeline + idempotency.\\r\\n- `mise run lint` (0 issues) and the import/agentimport test suites pass locally. Verified against sample fixtures: cursor 3 turns / pi 2 / factory 2 / codex 2 / copilot 2 / gemini 1.\\r\\n\\r\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\r\\n\\r\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n> [!NOTE]\\r\\n> **Medium Risk**\\r\\n> Imports local transcripts into persistent checkpoints with format-specific parsing and repo attribution; mistakes could mis-attribute sessions or miscount tokens, but scope is additive with strong test coverage and no auth/data-path changes.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> **Overview**\\r\\n> Extends **`entire import`** beyond Claude Code by registering six new **`Importer`** implementations (Cursor, Pi, Factory AI Droid, Codex, Copilot CLI, Gemini CLI) in the static `importers` slice—existing command wiring via `agentimport.All()` picks them up automatically.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> Each agent gets its own **`Discover`** (30-day lookback, optional session filter, agent-specific paths) and **`SplitTurns`** logic, mostly delegating tokens/model to existing agent helpers. **Codex** and **Copilot** filter global/flat session stores with shared **`repoMatches`** (cwd/gitRoot under repo, symlink-normalized). **Gemini** differs: one checkpoint per session with message-index offsets, not per user turn. **Cursor** imports with nil tokens and empty model.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> Adds per-agent unit tests, a registry test for all seven names, shared test fixtures, and a **`Run`** end-to-end test through the Cursor importer for idempotency and checkpoint writes without token/model data.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 2045376ffaa20acbe3cde17f741851dc37e9680e. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\r\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1540/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1540/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1350\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1350/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1350/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1350/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1350\",\n            \"id\": 4582485789,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7iWrrE\",\n            \"number\": 1350,\n            \"title\": \"doctor: check and repair the v1.1 committed-read mirror\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"computermode\",\n              \"id\": 2917645,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTc2NDU=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2917645?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/computermode\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-06-03T18:13:22Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-04T23:45:30Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-06-04T23:45:27Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1350\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1350\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1350.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1350.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-06-04T23:45:27Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/501\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What\\n\\nFollow-up to #1335. That PR established the v1.1 committed-ref contract: reads resolve `refs/entire/checkpoints/v1.1` **as-is** — read paths no longer create, repair, or advance the mirror. That leaves no repair path when the mirror drifts (pre-#1335 state, a raw `git fetch` of v1 outside entire, a crash between v1 write and mirror update, external ref meddling). A drifted mirror silently makes v1.1 reads miss checkpoints.\\n\\nThis PR makes `entire doctor` the repair tool:\\n\\n- **`strategy.DiagnoseCommittedMetadataMirror`** — read-only classifier of the mirror against the local v1 tip: `NOT CONFIGURED | OK | NO METADATA | MISSING | STALE (behind) | DIVERGED | V1 BRANCH MISSING`. Returns the resolved `CommittedRefs` so callers repair via the existing `MirrorCommittedMetadataRef`.\\n- **`entire doctor` check #2** (right after the disconnected-metadata check, which rewrites v1 and re-mirrors — this catches residual drift):\\n  - silent in v1 mode; `✓ OK` when healthy (including fresh repos with no metadata yet)\\n  - `MISSING` / `STALE` / `DIVERGED` → explain, confirm (auto with `--force`), point the mirror at the v1 tip; the diverged copy explicitly says the discarded commits aren't on v1\\n  - mirror-outlives-v1 anomaly → warn-only with a pasteable `git fetch` suggestion (never auto-\\\"fixed\\\", even under `--force`)\\n  - check errors accumulate like the existing checks without aborting the rest of doctor\\n- **`entire doctor bundle`** — new `entire-refs.txt`: `for-each-ref` over entire's ref namespaces (v1 branch, v1.1 mirror, shadow/trails branches, origin tracking) plus a `mirror status: STALE (mirror abc1234, v1 def5678)` diagnosis line. Best-effort and goes through the standard redaction path.\\n\\n## Design notes\\n\\n- Status labels have one source: doctor headlines and the bundle line both render `MirrorStatus.String()`, so the two surfaces can't drift.\\n- Messages and the fetch suggestion render `diag.Refs.Primary` rather than hardcoding `entire/checkpoints/v1`, so doctor's guidance survives a future topology flip.\\n- Diagnosis deliberately does **not** reuse `strategy.IsAncestorOf`: that helper is a depth-capped (1000), error-swallowing log walk, and a long-lived v1 branch grows one commit per condensation — a merely-stale mirror past the cap would misclassify as DIVERGED with misleading messaging. The diagnosis uses go-git's exact ancestry and surfaces errors.\\n- The confirm prompt is extracted to `confirmDoctorFix`, now shared with `checkDisconnectedMetadata`.\\n- Restoring a deleted v1 branch is out of scope (warn-only); so are mirror-ref deletion in `entire clean` and the v1.1 remote-fetch story for `entire resume` (separate follow-ups).\\n\\n## Coverage\\n\\n- `strategy`: table-driven `TestDiagnoseCommittedMetadataMirror` — all seven states, plus the read-only invariant (diagnosis never creates/moves/deletes the ref).\\n- `cli`: table-driven `TestCheckCommittedMetadataMirror` — per-state output, `--force` repairs actually move the ref to the v1 tip, warn-only state stays untouched; `TestRunSessionsFix_IncludesMirrorCheck` proves the wiring into the main doctor flow.\\n- `cli`: `TestWriteDoctorBundle_CapturesEntireRefs` — bundle contains `entire-refs.txt` with the refs and the diagnosis line.\\n- Docs: `sessions-and-checkpoints.md` v1.1 section now names doctor as the repair path.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- mise run fmt\\n- mise run lint\\n- mise run test:ci (incl. Vogon canary), re-run after merging main\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Repairs rewrite the local mirror ref to match v1 (diverged case discards mirror-only commits after user confirmation), which directly affects checkpoint read visibility but does not change v1 writes or remote sync.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds a **checkpoints v1.1 read-mirror** repair path to `entire doctor`, following the contract that read paths use `refs/entire/checkpoints/v1.1` as-is.\\n> \\n> **Strategy:** Introduces `DiagnoseCommittedMetadataMirror` and `MirrorStatus` labels (`MISSING`, `STALE`, `DIVERGED`, etc.) to compare the local mirror to the `entire/checkpoints/v1` tip using go-git ancestry (not the depth-capped helper). Repair still uses `MirrorCommittedMetadataRef`.\\n> \\n> **Doctor:** New check #2 runs after disconnected-metadata reconciliation; it is silent in v1-only mode, can auto-repair missing/stale/diverged mirrors with `--force` or after confirm via shared `confirmDoctorFix`, and stays **warn-only** when the mirror exists but v1 is gone (suggested `git fetch`). Mirror check failures accumulate like other doctor errors.\\n> \\n> **Bundle:** `entire doctor bundle` adds `entire-refs.txt` listing entire-related refs plus a `mirror status:` line using the same status strings.\\n> \\n> Tests cover diagnosis, doctor wiring, and bundle capture; architecture docs name doctor as the mirror repair tool.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 39b2bbc44fd114875813f19a6d8de11448f5de61. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1350/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1350/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1209\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1209/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1209/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1209/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1209\",\n            \"id\": 4442349243,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7bV4wS\",\n            \"number\": 1209,\n            \"title\": \"Checkpoints v2 push speedup: simplify v2 migration hint check\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"computermode\",\n              \"id\": 2917645,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTc2NDU=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2917645?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/computermode\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-05-14T01:31:12Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-14T21:14:20Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-05-14T21:14:19Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1209\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1209\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1209.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1209.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-05-14T21:14:19Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/375\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\n## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nThis PR improves the performance of the pre-push hook for v2-enabled repos with 100+ checkpoints down from ~60s (!) to 20s. Tested with the `entiredb` repo. Observed push times went down from close to a minute to about 20 seconds (still unacceptable but much better while the refs fixes are being addressed). Double-checked and ensured checkpoints were pushed up correctly.\\r\\n\\r\\n- Replace the v1 <> v2 missing checkpoints check for the migration hint message with a single \\\"does v2 /main exist?\\\" ref probe. The hint now only fires when migration was never run; partial migrations are no longer flagged (a little drift is acceptable post-migration since we fall back to v1 in the UI when we display transcripts for now anyway).\\r\\n- Drops the per-push cost of listing the full v1 and v2 committed-checkpoint sets just to decide whether to print one line\\r\\n\\r\\nExtracted from #1208 — the rotation/blob-fetch perf fixes from that PR are left in place there.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Test plan\\r\\n\\r\\n- [x] `mise run fmt && mise run lint` clean\\r\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/ -run TestPrintCheckpointsV2MigrationHint` passes\\r\\n- [ ] Manual: pre-push on a v2-enabled repo no longer prints the hint once `v2/main` exists, even with v1 checkpoints that were never mirrored\\r\\n\\r\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\r\\n\\r\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n> [!NOTE]\\r\\n> **Low Risk**\\r\\n> Low risk: changes are limited to advisory stderr hint logic during pushes and corresponding tests, with no impact on checkpoint data writes or syncing behavior.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> **Overview**\\r\\n> `printCheckpointsV2MigrationHint` now decides whether to warn solely by probing for `refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/main` (via `v2MainRefExists`) when `checkpoints_version: 2` is committed, rather than listing and cross-checking v1/v2 checkpoint inventories.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> Tests were updated accordingly by removing v1-mirroring fixtures and deleting the `hasUnmigratedV1Checkpoints` test suite, and by asserting the hint is suppressed once v2 `/main` exists and printed otherwise.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit f7a4cb480a58ced1c951428b9d92668ec4e604dc. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\r\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1209/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1209/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1310\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1310/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1310/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1310/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1310\",\n            \"id\": 4565122217,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7hduAQ\",\n            \"number\": 1310,\n            \"title\": \"Capture generic slash skill prompts\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"dipree\",\n              \"id\": 3369400,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNjk0MDA=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3369400?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/dipree\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-06-01T17:37:53Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-02T20:31:26Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-06-02T20:31:26Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": true,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1310\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1310\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1310.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1310.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\n- add a generic `/skill:<name>` prompt parser for agents whose turn-start hook exposes the raw prompt\\n- append prompt skill events in the lifecycle dispatcher while letting native adapter events win\\n- persist generic events with explicit provenance, command-only native metadata, and user-message collapse hints\\n\\n## Scope: user-invoked prompt skills only\\n\\nThis change captures **user-invoked** skill calls of the form `/skill:<name>` typed\\ninto the prompt. It does **not** add generic detection of skill **tool calls**.\\n\\n| Event | event_type | source.signal | collapse.target | Where it is produced |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| User prompt `/skill:<name>` | `prompt_invocation` | `prompt_slash_command` | `user_message` | generic, this PR (lifecycle TurnStart) |\\n| Pi `/skill:<name>` (pre-expansion) | `prompt_invocation` | `input_slash_command` | `user_message` | Pi extension (native) |\\n| Claude `Skill` tool use | `tool_invocation` | `skill_tool_use` | `tool_pair` | Claude transcript extractor (native) |\\n\\nTool-call skill detection stays **agent-specific** (currently Claude Code's `Skill`\\ntool) because tool formats and skill semantics vary per agent and generic tool-call\\nheuristics would be unreliable.\\n\\n## Slash-command format validation\\n\\nValidated against installed agent binaries (Claude Code 2.1.x, Codex, OpenCode, Pi):\\n\\n| Agent | User skill prompt syntax | Uses `/skill:<name>`? | Covered |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Pi | `/skill:<name>` | yes | natively, pre-expansion (Pi `input` event). At framework TurnStart Pi's prompt is already the expanded `<skill ...>` block, so the generic parser does not re-match it; the native event wins. |\\n| Claude Code | `/<skill-name>` + `Skill` tool | no | tool calls → `tool_invocation`; `/<skill-name>` is the skill's own name, not `/skill:` |\\n| Codex | none (skills injected/tool) | no | n/a |\\n| OpenCode | none | no | n/a |\\n| Gemini CLI | none | no | n/a |\\n| Cursor | none | no | n/a |\\n| Factory Droid | none | no | n/a |\\n| Copilot CLI | none | no | n/a |\\n\\n**Conclusion:** among shipped agents the literal `/skill:<name>` syntax is **Pi-only**,\\nand Pi is already covered natively before expansion. The generic TurnStart parser is a\\nforward-looking, low-risk fallback for any agent whose turn-start hook surfaces a raw\\n`/skill:<name>` prompt. It is intentionally strict (only `/skill:`, never every\\n`/<word>`) to avoid misclassifying ordinary slash commands as skills, and it only\\nfires when the firing TurnStart agent matches the owning agent so forwarded hooks\\n(e.g. Cursor IDE → Claude) do not duplicate events.\\n\\n## Testing\\n- `mise exec -- go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent ./cmd/entire/cli`\\n- `mise exec -- go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/pi ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy ./cmd/entire/cli`\\n- `env -u GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT -u PI_CODING_AGENT mise exec -- go test ./...`\\n- Manual E2E: simulated Codex `user-prompt-submit` with `/skill:trigger-analysis`, committed with trailer, and verified `skill_events` in checkpoint metadata.\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Adds optional checkpoint metadata parsing and lifecycle append logic with deduplication; no auth, payments, or core commit path changes.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds a **generic fallback** so turn-start hooks that expose the raw user prompt can record explicit **`/skill:<name>`** invocations in checkpoint metadata, even when the agent has no native skill adapter.\\n> \\n> A new parser recognizes a leading slash command (after whitespace), emits a **`prompt_invocation`** skill event with signal **`prompt_slash_command`**, and stores only the command in **`native`** (not the rest of the prompt). **`handleLifecycleTurnStart`** appends these events before session init; **native adapter events** (e.g. Pi’s pre-expansion input event) **win** and duplicates are skipped.\\n> \\n> Collapse hints target the user message and default to collapsed, matching other explicit skill signals.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 9cc75f0f28ef5e320b5860d6b7b9a01d088c77d6. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1310/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1310/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1180\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1180/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1180/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1180/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1180\",\n            \"id\": 4424978517,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7adcQt\",\n            \"number\": 1180,\n            \"title\": \"Fix failed commit bug during checkpoints v2 migrations \",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"computermode\",\n              \"id\": 2917645,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTc2NDU=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2917645?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/computermode\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-05-11T23:20:20Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-11T23:53:13Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-05-11T23:53:10Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1180\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1180\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1180.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1180.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-05-11T23:53:10Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/354\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n ## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\n  `entire migrate --checkpoints v2` was failing partway through on partial-clone repos because go-git's pack-index cache occasionally loses track of objects that live in promisor packs. Native\\r\\n   `git` resolves the same hashes fine. This branch adds CLI fallbacks at the two call sites that produced the failures.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ### Errors fixed\\r\\n\\r\\n  Migrate would crash with one of these (the specific symptom shifts with go-git's pack-cache state between runs):\\r\\n\\r\\n  failed to write batched v2 /main entries: failed to get commit for ref refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/main: object not found\\r\\n\\r\\n  failed to write batched v2 /main entries: failed to apply batched /main checkpoint trees: failed to apply changes in 3b: failed to read tree: packfile not found\\r\\n\\r\\n  failed to write batched v2 /main entries: failed to get commit for ref refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/main: packfile not found\\r\\n\\r\\n  ### Fix\\r\\n\\r\\n  - **`checkpoint/parse_tree.go`** — in `ApplyTreeChanges`, if `repo.TreeObject(rootTreeHash)` fails, fall back to `git ls-tree <hash>` via a new `readTreeEntriesViaCLI` helper that parses\\r\\n  each line into `[]object.TreeEntry`.\\r\\n  - **`checkpoint/v2_store.go`** — in `GetRefState`, if `repo.CommitObject(ref.Hash())` fails, fall back to `git rev-parse <hash>^{tree}` via a new `commitTreeHashViaCLI` helper to recover\\r\\n  just the tree hash (all the caller needs).\\r\\n\\r\\n  Both fallbacks emit a single `logging.Warn` so we can see in `entire doctor logs` how often the path fires, and `errors.Join` both errors when even the CLI can't resolve the object so the\\r\\n  original go-git error is preserved. Same pattern as the blob-side workaround in `FetchingTree.blobOnDisk` / `readFileViaGit`.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ## Test plan\\r\\n\\r\\n  - [x] `mise run check` (fmt + lint + unit + integration + e2e canary) — all 58 + 4 tests pass.\\r\\n  - [x] `./entire migrate --checkpoints v2` against the local repo where the bug originally reproduced — migration completes, `/main` advances, no shard left unwritten.\\r\\n  - [ ] Verify the warn lines appear in `.entire/logs/entire.log` next time go-git's pack cache wedges (couldn't force the trigger; the path is wired into the exact failure sites, but didn't\\r\\n  fire during the validation run because go-git's state self-corrected).\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Introduces new fallback paths that shell out to `git` when go-git cannot read commit/tree objects, which changes behavior in object resolution and adds reliance on external command execution during migrations.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Fixes v2 checkpoint migration failures in partial-clone repos by adding **CLI fallbacks when go-git can’t load objects**.\\n> \\n> `ApplyTreeChanges` now falls back to `git ls-tree` to read tree entries, and `V2GitStore.GetRefState` falls back to `git rev-parse <commit>^{tree}` to recover the tree hash; both paths emit a `logging.Warn` and join errors when the fallback also fails.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 2123cb3aab088b9ff230284d636b0fb258bab968. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1180/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1180/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1230\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1230/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1230/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1230/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1230\",\n            \"id\": 4481635403,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7dSJl4\",\n            \"number\": 1230,\n            \"title\": \"feat(agent): stream-driven summaries with provider-aware errors\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-05-19T22:47:37Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-21T19:50:22Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-21T19:50:22Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1230\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1230\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1230.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1230.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/398\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nExtends PR #964's streaming summary UI from Claude to the other four built-in summary providers — **Codex**, **Gemini**, **Cursor**, and **Copilot**. Each agent now implements `agent.StreamingTextGenerator`, sharing a new `agent.StreamingGeneratorTemplate` that owns subprocess lifecycle (mirrors the `review/types/template.ReviewerTemplate` pattern from PR #1192).\\n\\n**Base branch:** `feat/explain-stream-progress` (PR #964). When that merges to `main`, this rebases cleanly.\\n\\n## Architecture\\n\\n- `agent.StreamingGeneratorTemplate` — shared spawn → pipe → parse → drain → wait. Per-agent code provides only `BuildCmd` (argv) and `Parser` (stdout → events). 5 unit tests cover the template; agents use it via composition.\\n- `agent.testutil.FakeStreamCmd` — extracted from `claudecode/generate_streaming_test.go` so all 5 streaming agents share one subprocess fake.\\n- `summaryProgressWriter.handle` — `PhaseFirstToken` rendering now gracefully degrades when `TTFTms`/`CachedInputTokens` are zero (Gemini, Cursor, Copilot have neither; Codex has cached but no TTFT).\\n- `claudecode` keeps its own `generate_streaming.go` — no migration. Per user decision: don't refactor the established Claude path.\\n\\n## Per-agent observations\\n\\nEach agent's stream protocol is different. The unified UX hides this:\\n\\n| Agent | TTFT | Cached tokens | Tokens during stream | Final duration |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| **Codex** | no | yes (`turn.completed.usage`) | no — single chunk arrival | locally measured (`time.Since(turn.started)`) |\\n| **Gemini** | no | no | yes — per assistant delta | real (`result.stats.duration_ms`) |\\n| **Cursor** | no | captured but not yet shown on Done line | yes — per assistant w/ timestamp_ms | real (`result.duration_ms`) |\\n| **Copilot** | no | no | yes — per `assistant.message_delta` (estimated from char length) | real (sum of per-turn `assistant.message.outputTokens`) |\\n\\nCursor's stream includes `thinking` events (internal reasoning) which are intentionally ignored — Connecting phase persists during the thinking window.\\n\\n## Test approach\\n\\n- **Per-agent unit tests** — parser + integration tests using synthetic NDJSON fixtures (`testdata/stream_{success,error}.jsonl`) that mirror the real CLI shape captured during implementation.\\n- **Real-CLI smoke tests** — every agent was end-to-end verified against checkpoint \\\\`d86ffe2e995d\\\\` (734k-token transcript). UI sequence verified for each: phase ordering, parens-with-cached-tokens for Codex, no-parens for the others, running token counter ticking, real numbers in the final line.\\n- **Two-stage review** — every chunk got both spec-compliance and code-quality review subagents. All ✅ APPROVED with deferred nits.\\n\\n## Commits\\n\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`\\nf0caf4962 feat(cursor):     implement StreamingTextGenerator\\n2960d6236 fix(copilotcli):  tick output-token counter during streaming\\n74dc1470f feat(copilotcli): implement StreamingTextGenerator\\n1e0e93f18 feat(geminicli):  implement StreamingTextGenerator\\n47583e9c2 fix(codex):       redact raw error envelopes + surface skipped malformed lines\\n3d0a38c01 feat(codex):      implement StreamingTextGenerator\\n00b841b0d feat(agent):      add StreamingGeneratorTemplate + progress-writer field degradation\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`\\n\\nBoth fix commits are responses to bugbot/code-quality review on the immediately-preceding chunk. Each chunk + fix is independently buildable and testable.\\n\\n## Known gaps / follow-ups\\n\\n- **`looksLikeUnrecognizedFlag` helper duplication** (4 near-identical predicates across codex/geminicli/copilotcli/cursor). Each has a `//nolint:dupl` annotation pointing at a planned post-merge consolidation. `dupl` never actually fired at threshold 75 — the annotations are prophylactic.\\n- **Privacy-decode pattern duplication** (3× across codex/geminicli/copilotcli error branches; cursor's is simpler since its error envelope only carries `result.result`). A shared \\\\`agent.SafeErrorMessage\\\\` helper was flagged but deferred to keep the surface clean while patterns settle.\\n- **Cursor's `cacheReadTokens`** is parsed into `done.CachedInputTokens` but the progress writer's PhaseDone line doesn't currently display cached tokens. Future-proofing — UI can pick it up later without a parser change.\\n- **Cursor authentication required.** The `agent` CLI exits with `Authentication required` without an interactive `agent login` or `CURSOR_API_KEY`. The streaming path inherits this — without auth, the template surfaces a generic `TextGenerationError` (same as the non-streaming path always has).\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] Unit tests pass: \\\\`mise run test:ci\\\\` (58 unit + 4 canary E2E)\\n- [x] Lint clean: \\\\`mise run lint\\\\` (0 issues)\\n- [x] Real-CLI smoke: Codex, Gemini, Cursor, Copilot — all verified UI sequence end-to-end on \\\\`d86ffe2e995d\\\\`\\n- [x] Timeout diagnostic: \\\\`--summary-timeout-seconds 3\\\\` exercised on each agent — phase-attribution diagnostic from PR #964 carries through the new template\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Adds new subprocess-driven streaming generation paths for multiple providers plus a shared lifecycle wrapper; failures could surface as incorrect progress reporting or fallback/error handling regressions.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds streaming summary support for **Codex**, **Gemini CLI**, **Cursor agent**, and **Copilot CLI** by introducing a shared `agent.StreamingGeneratorTemplate` that owns subprocess setup, stdout parsing/draining, stderr capture, and a standardized fallback signal (`ErrUnrecognizedStreamingFlag`).\\n> \\n> Each agent now has a streaming parser for its NDJSON protocol that emits `PhaseConnecting`/`PhaseFirstToken`/`PhaseGenerating`/`PhaseDone` (including token/duration data when available) and falls back to non-streaming `GenerateText` when the CLI rejects streaming flags.\\n> \\n> Test infrastructure is expanded with a shared `agent/testutil.FakeStreamCmd` (replacing an inline Claude helper), new per-agent NDJSON fixtures + unit tests, and the summary UI is tweaked so `PhaseFirstToken` renders optional TTFT/cached-token clauses only when present (no empty parens).\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit f0caf496203750cf17ebaf085059c69e3a6d2722. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1230/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1230/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1313\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1313/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1313/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1313/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1313\",\n            \"id\": 4565772693,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7hf17H\",\n            \"number\": 1313,\n            \"title\": \"Add Pi review-runner adapter\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"dipree\",\n              \"id\": 3369400,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNjk0MDA=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3369400?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/dipree\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-06-01T19:26:48Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-02T14:23:42Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-02T14:23:39Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1313\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1313\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1313.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1313.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-02T14:23:39Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/467\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAdds **Pi** as a first-class `entire review` worker by implementing its `AgentReviewer` adapter. This is the concrete proof that the previous \\\"only claude-code/codex/gemini\\\" limit was just missing adapters, not a launch-capability wall.\\n\\nStacked on #1312 (review profiles). Review/merge that first.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n- **`cmd/entire/cli/agent/pi/reviewer.go`** — `NewReviewer()` returning a `ReviewerTemplate`:\\n  - `BuildCmd`: `pi --mode json --print [--model <model>] <prompt>` with `ENTIRE_REVIEW_*` env via `AppendReviewEnv`\\n  - `Parser`: maps Pi's `--mode json` `AgentSessionEvent` stream (`message_update` text deltas, `tool_execution_start`, `message_end`/`turn_end` usage, `agent_end`) into Entire's review `Event` stream. Falls back to `message_end` content text when no deltas streamed; uses `stopReason` for success.\\n- **`cmd/entire/cli/agent/pi/generate.go`** — `GenerateText` so Pi can also serve as a master / summary provider.\\n- **Wiring**: `launchableReviewerFor` returns `pi.NewReviewer()`; Pi added to summary provider binaries, default-profile agents, master-preference order, and config/help text.\\n- **Session matching**: Pi runs are matched to their lifecycle sessions by model too (same-agent/different-model workers resolve correctly); `agent_end` backfills the model via `ExtractModel`.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- `reviewer_test.go`: name, argv/env shape with `--model`, JSON event-stream parsing, message-end fallback text\\n- manifest test for same-agent/different-model disambiguation\\n- `go vet ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/pi/...`\\n- `env -u PI_CODING_AGENT go test ./cmd/entire/cli/...`\\n- targeted review integration tests\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches review orchestration, manifest session matching, and summary provider selection; behavior is well covered by unit tests but depends on Pi CLI JSON event stability.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Pi** is wired into `entire review` as a first-class worker alongside Claude Code, Codex, and Gemini, using the shared `ReviewerTemplate` pattern instead of marker fallback.\\n> \\n> A new **`pi` review adapter** runs `pi --mode json --print [--model …] <prompt>` with `ENTIRE_REVIEW_*` env, and maps Pi’s NDJSON session stream (text deltas, tools, usage, `stopReason`, `agent_end`) into Entire review events, including fallback text from `message_end` when no deltas streamed. **`GenerateText`** (`pi --print --no-tools --no-session`) lets Pi act as a review master and checkpoint summary provider.\\n> \\n> **Integration:** `launchableReviewerFor` returns `pi.NewReviewer()`; Pi is added to summary-provider binaries, default profile agents (prompt-driven like Gemini), master preference order, and user-facing configure/help text. On **`agent_end`**, `TurnEnd` now sets **`Model`** from the captured session transcript via `ExtractModel`.\\n> \\n> **Manifest matching** uses tighter model ID normalization (strip provider prefix / tier suffix) so multiple Pi workers with different models map to the correct lifecycle sessions; tests cover argv/env, JSON parsing, and same-agent/model disambiguation.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 27f6781a799e96a7c4612f9b6ef00dd94867c87c. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1313/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1313/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1231\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1231/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1231/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1231/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1231\",\n            \"id\": 4481780661,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7dSn95\",\n            \"number\": 1231,\n            \"title\": \"labs: entire investigate — multi-agent investigation loop\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"alishakawaguchi\",\n              \"id\": 6415609,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTU2MDk=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6415609?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/alishakawaguchi\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [\n              {\n                \"login\": \"alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"id\": 6415609,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTU2MDk=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6415609?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              }\n            ],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-05-19T23:16:32Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-27T23:04:50Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-05-27T23:04:47Z\",\n            \"assignee\": {\n              \"login\": \"alishakawaguchi\",\n              \"id\": 6415609,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTU2MDk=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6415609?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/alishakawaguchi\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1231\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1231\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1231.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1231.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-05-27T23:04:47Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/397\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/19c1d75f-b70a-4d2d-b745-a4405e2fca81\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\n- Adds `entire investigate` (labs / hidden) — a round-robin multi-agent investigation loop that drives claude-code, codex, and gemini-cli through turns appending findings/evidence/stances to a shared findings doc until quorum / stalled / paused / cancelled.\\r\\n- Subcommands: `fix [run-id]`, `show [run-id]`, `clean [run-id|--all]`.\\r\\n- Inputs: `[seed-doc]` positional, `--issue-link <url>` (gh-resolved with userinfo redaction + untrusted-content envelope), or — when the spawn-time picker fires — an in-picker \\\"Investigation prompt\\\".\\r\\n- Lifecycle: per-turn `pending_turn` state.json contract, env-var provenance handshake (ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_*) adopted by `UserPromptSubmit` hook, condense into checkpoint metadata on commit, `HasInvestigation` umbrella flag on the checkpoint summary surfaced via `entire status` and the soft-warn guard.\\r\\n- Resume: `--continue <run-id>` reloads `RunState`, rewrites the manifest with the new terminal outcome (no longer leaves stale \\\"paused\\\" records).\\r\\n\\r\\n### Supporting refactors (review/investigate boundary)\\r\\n\\r\\n- New leaf packages, each consumed by both commands so the duplication is gone:\\r\\n  - \\\\`cmd/entire/cli/tuiutil/\\\\` — width-aware text helpers + \\\\`FormatDuration\\\\`\\r\\n  - \\\\`cmd/entire/cli/gitexec/\\\\` — \\\\`git\\\\` CLI runner (separates stdout from stderr-as-error-context)\\r\\n  - \\\\`cmd/entire/cli/uiform/\\\\` — accessible huh form constructor + \\\\`PromptYN\\\\`\\r\\n  - \\\\`cmd/entire/cli/provenance/\\\\` — single source of truth for ENTIRE_REVIEW_* / ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_* env contract\\r\\n- \\\\`lifecycle.go\\\\`: \\\\`adoptReviewEnv\\\\` + \\\\`adoptInvestigateEnv\\\\` share \\\\`tryAdoptEnv(spec)\\\\`.\\r\\n- \\\\`investigate/show.go\\\\` and \\\\`clean.go\\\\` share \\\\`ResolveByRunID\\\\` for exact-then-prefix resolution.\\r\\n- \\\\`investigate\\\\` uses \\\\`jsonutil.WriteFileAtomic\\\\` / \\\\`checkpoint/id.Generate\\\\` / agent name constants instead of re-implementing.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Security hardening (from adversarial review)\\r\\n\\r\\n- \\\\`runGhExec\\\\` redacts URL userinfo (\\\\`https://user:TOKEN@github.com/...\\\\`) before any arg reaches an error string — earlier credential-redaction only covered the seed-doc / log paths.\\r\\n- \\\\`--issue-link\\\\` now requires an interactive y/N before launching agents with permission/sandbox bypass; non-interactive callers see the warning on stderr and proceed (CI / scripted use is not hard-blocked).\\r\\n- Issue body + comments are wrapped in a \\\\`<untrusted source=\\\\\\\"...\\\\\\\">\\\\` envelope and any literal \\\\`</untrusted>\\\\` inside the body is defanged with a zero-width space.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Test plan\\r\\n\\r\\n- [x] \\\\`mise run fmt && mise run lint\\\\` clean\\r\\n- [x] \\\\`go test ./cmd/entire/cli/...\\\\` all green\\r\\n- [x] Manual smoke: \\\\`entire investigate <seed.md>\\\\` (single agent, multi-agent picker)\\r\\n- [x] Manual smoke: \\\\`entire investigate --issue-link <github-url>\\\\` (accept + decline branches)\\r\\n- [x] Manual smoke: pause (Ctrl+C) → \\\\`entire investigate --continue <id>\\\\` → reaches quorum → manifest rewritten with new outcome\\r\\n- [x] Manual smoke: \\\\`entire investigate fix <id>\\\\`, \\\\`show <id>\\\\`, \\\\`clean <id>\\\\` / \\\\`clean --all\\\\`\\r\\n\\r\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\r\\n\\r\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n> [!NOTE]\\r\\n> **High Risk**\\r\\n> High risk due to introducing a new command that spawns external agent processes with sandbox/permission-bypass flags, adds deletion functionality (`investigate clean`), and extends checkpoint metadata/wire formats (`HasInvestigation` + investigate fields) that affect on-disk persisted data.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> **Overview**\\r\\n> Adds a hidden labs `entire investigate` command that runs a round-robin multi-agent loop (with resume via `--continue`), bootstraps a per-run findings doc (from seed doc, issue link, or picker prompt), persists run state/manifests, and provides `fix`, `show`, and `clean` subcommands (including confirmed deletion of saved investigation artifacts).\\r\\n> \\r\\n> Introduces a shared `spawn.Spawner` interface plus concrete spawners for `claude-code`, `codex`, and `gemini-cli` (using non-interactive invocation and permission/sandbox-bypass flags), and adds `agentlaunch.LaunchFixAgent` to start follow-up “fix” sessions while stripping review/investigate provenance env.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> Extends checkpoint/session metadata to record investigation provenance (`investigate_*` fields) and a `HasInvestigation` umbrella flag, propagates it through v2 checkpoint summary merge logic and `entire explain --json` export, and adds tests (unit + integration) pinning the new on-disk/JSON wire formats and adoption via `ENTIRE_INVESTIGATE_*` env vars.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit f8edb812a0f5158f7c91f01c67db40dfe00e6d82. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\r\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1231/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1231/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1212\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1212/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1212/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1212/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1212\",\n            \"id\": 4446761431,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7bjrzf\",\n            \"number\": 1212,\n            \"title\": \"Improve support for sub-agents on same branch\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"pjbgf\",\n              \"id\": 5452977,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NTI5Nzc=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5452977?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pjbgf\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-05-14T14:34:07Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-14T17:41:48Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-05-14T17:41:46Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1212\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1212\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1212.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1212.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-05-14T17:41:46Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/376\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\nMultiple sessions sharing a shadow branch (same base commit + worktree) raced on the final SetReference at the end of WriteTemporary, and the race was silently lost to last-writer-wins. A stress test driving 8 concurrent sessions × 4 checkpoints each saw 75-94% of checkpoints orphaned per run.\\r\\n\\r\\nWrap WriteTemporary and WriteTemporaryTask in a per-shadow-branch flock under <git-common-dir>/entire-shadow-locks/ and replace the bare SetReference with `git update-ref <ref> <new> <old>` (CAS) plus a small retry budget. The flock serializes our own writers across goroutines and processes; the CAS catches external `git update-ref` callers as defense in depth.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter: 30/30 race iterations land all 32 checkpoints with no losses.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Before vs after\\r\\n| Test scenario | Before | After |\\r\\n|---|---:|---:|\\r\\n| 20 race iterations, 8 sessions × 4 checkpoints | 75–94% commits lost | 0 commits lost |\\r\\n| 30 race iterations (final) | n/a | 0 commits lost |\\r\\n\\r\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n> [!NOTE]\\r\\n> **Medium Risk**\\r\\n> Changes shadow-branch ref update semantics and introduces cross-process locking plus a CAS retry loop, which can affect checkpoint correctness and potentially block/hang if locking/backoff misbehaves. Scope is limited to checkpoint write paths and is covered by a new concurrency regression test.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> **Overview**\\r\\n> **Prevents concurrent checkpoint writers from clobbering shadow branches.** Temporary checkpoint writes (`WriteTemporary` and `WriteTemporaryTask`) are now wrapped in a per-shadow-branch filesystem lock and update the branch ref using `git update-ref` compare-and-swap with bounded retries and jittered backoff.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> Adds platform-specific flock implementations (Unix/Windows), stores lockfiles under `<git-common-dir>/entire-shadow-locks/`, and introduces a stress test that runs many concurrent `SaveStep` calls against the same shadow branch and validates the resulting commit chain/tree consistency.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 7350c3f9d841b68351215e2bf00e7dd9d6a9cd34. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\r\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1212/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1212/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1078\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1078/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1078/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1078/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1078\",\n            \"id\": 4350735925,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7WuPSB\",\n            \"number\": 1078,\n            \"title\": \"Format entire explain generated summary \",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 3,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-04-29T13:02:27Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-04-30T15:54:45Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-04-30T15:54:43Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1078\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1078\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1078.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1078.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-04-30T15:54:43Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/265\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\n## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\n  - Reuse the shared Entire markdown styling helpers so `entire explain` can render generated\\r\\n  checkpoint summaries with the same branded terminal markdown treatment as dispatch output.\\r\\n  - Replace the summary-present `entire explain` body with structured markdown sections for intent,\\r\\n  outcome, learnings, friction, open items, and verbose/full files while preserving plain markdown for\\r\\n  piped and `NO_COLOR` output.\\r\\n  - Add a compact checkpoint metadata header with session, created time, author, tokens, and\\r\\n  associated commits, then tighten the summary spacing so `## Intent` starts directly under the header\\r\\n  rule.\\r\\n  - Refactor pager command construction so default `less` receives `LESS=-R` only when the user has\\r\\n  not set `PAGER` or `LESS`.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ## Test Plan\\r\\n\\r\\n  - `mise run check`\\r\\n  - `mise run test:ci`\\r\\n  - Pseudo-terminal smoke check: `script -q /tmp/entire-explain-tty.out ./entire explain --checkpoint\\r\\n  <checkpointID> --no-pager`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches user-facing CLI output formatting and paging behavior; low functional risk but moderate compatibility risk for scripts/tests that parse explain output or rely on previous pager environment defaults.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Updates `entire explain` to emit a compact, styled checkpoint header (session/created/author/tokens/commits) and to render AI checkpoint summaries as structured markdown sections (Intent/Outcome/Learnings/Friction/Open Items, plus Files in verbose/full), using the shared terminal markdown renderer and respecting `NO_COLOR`/piped output.\\n> \\n> Refactors transcript display to use section rules and tighter spacing, adjusts output strings across unit/integration/e2e tests and docs, and extracts pager command construction so the default `less` pager gets `LESS=-R` only when the user hasn’t set `PAGER`/`LESS` (with new tests around env behavior).\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit e008cc705f3bcd5bffc236eb064a0ab2f90cc6f4. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1078/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1078/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1146\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1146/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1146/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1146/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1146\",\n            \"id\": 4402484321,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7ZVO9I\",\n            \"number\": 1146,\n            \"title\": \"Add experimental `entire learn` command with embedded markdown + release-time regen\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"alishakawaguchi\",\n              \"id\": 6415609,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTU2MDk=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6415609?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/alishakawaguchi\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [\n              {\n                \"login\": \"alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"id\": 6415609,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTU2MDk=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6415609?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              }\n            ],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 5,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-05-07T22:50:26Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-11T05:02:44Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-05-15T16:23:59Z\",\n            \"assignee\": {\n              \"login\": \"alishakawaguchi\",\n              \"id\": 6415609,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTU2MDk=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6415609?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/alishakawaguchi\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1146\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1146\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1146.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1146.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/323\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\nMade `entire learn` so I can stop teaching agents how to use the CLI. Tired of pasting instructions in every prompt and watching them `-h` their way through every subcommand, or having to update my agent.md file all the time. Now I can just point at `entire learn`.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nAdds `entire learn`, an experimental Hidden top-level command (advertised under `entire labs`) that renders a state-aware tour of the CLI. Two rendering modes:\\r\\n\\r\\n1. **Default `entire learn`** — reads pre-rendered markdown from `cmd/entire/cli/learn/embedded/learn.md`, passes it through glamour, prints. ~50ms file-read + render.\\r\\n2. **`entire learn --regenerate`** (hidden, maintainer-only) — runs a TextGenerator agent against the live cobra tree to refresh `embedded/learn.md` before each release. Output is raw markdown to stdout; the command refuses to run unless stdout is redirected.\\r\\n\\r\\nRelease CI integration in `.github/workflows/release.yml` runs `mise run learn:regenerate` (atomic write + validation: ≥4 `## ` headers, presence of the `docs.entire.io/cli` footer) before GoReleaser. The regen step is `continue-on-error: true` so a flaky agent or missing `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` doesn't block the release; a dedicated Slack notification fires on regen failure separately from the existing release-failure alert.\\r\\n\\r\\nState-aware rendering: when Entire isn't enabled in the current repo, prints a short setup prompt; when enabled but no agent hooks are installed, prints an agent-install prompt; once a first commit has been captured, falls through to the full embedded tour (with a one-paragraph tail explaining that search/resume/rewind will gain real data after the next commit).\\r\\n\\r\\nMirrors `entire review`'s shape: top-level `Hidden: true`, advertised in `experimentalCommands` for `entire labs`.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Demos**\\r\\nhttps://cleanshot.com/share/35CFYwL1\\r\\n\\r\\n## Test plan\\r\\n\\r\\n- [x] `mise run learn:regenerate` locally with `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` set produces a valid `embedded/learn.md` (≥4 `## ` headers, includes `docs.entire.io/cli` footer)\\r\\n- [x] `entire learn` from a fresh checkout shows the embedded tour, rendered through glamour\\r\\n- [x] `entire learn --regenerate > /tmp/learn.md` produces sanitized markdown (control sequences stripped); refuses to run if stdout is a TTY\\r\\n- [x] `entire learn --help` shows correct help text\\r\\n- [x] `entire labs` lists `entire learn`\\r\\n- [x] State-aware fallbacks: setup prompt when disabled, agent-install prompt when enabled-without-agent, first-capture tail before any commit\\r\\n- [x] Existing tests: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/learn/...` passes (tests parallelized and hardened against host environment)\\r\\n- [x] Release workflow triggered on a `-rc.test` tag exercises the regen path end-to-end\\r\\n\\r\\n## Notes\\r\\n\\r\\nThe branch went through several code review passes (Claude-driven parallel agent reviews + codex adversarial review). Major findings addressed:\\r\\n- NBSP-mid-tagname Unicode bypass in tag escape\\r\\n- Terminal-injection sanitization on agent output before persistence\\r\\n- Atomic-write mise task with stronger CI validation\\r\\n- External-agent discovery in `ResolveTextGenerator` (mirrors `resolveCheckpointSummaryProvider`)\\r\\n- Settings double-load avoided via cached closure\\r\\n- Per-command descriptions required in capability sections of the regenerated markdown\\r\\n- `t.Parallel()` added to all learn-package tests; tests hardened against host environment (no reliance on real \\\\$HOME, real git config, or ambient `ENTIRE_*` env)\\r\\n\\r\\nThe earlier `--latest` blog-digest mode (RSS fetch + summarize most recent `entire.io` post) was removed during the rename back to `learn`: it added a network-dependent path that didn't fit the \\\\\\\"teach the CLI surface\\\\\\\" framing. The embedded-markdown + maintainer-regenerate flow is the whole feature now.\\r\\n\\r\\nDeferred to follow-up PRs: spinner/TUI dedup with `dispatch_tui.go`, `checkpoint.HasCommitted` short-circuit, dispatch's `sanitizeDispatchPromptString` consolidation with the new `stripInvisibles`.\\r\\n\\r\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\r\\n\\r\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n> [!NOTE]\\r\\n> **Medium Risk**\\r\\n> Adds a new top-level CLI command plus agent-driven generation paths and modifies the release workflow; failures are best-effort but could affect shipped tour content and release-time automation.\\r\\n>\\r\\n> **Overview**\\r\\n> Adds an experimental hidden `entire learn` command (advertised via `entire labs`) that renders a state-aware CLI tour from an embedded `learn.md` by default, with `--regenerate` (hidden) producing the embedded markdown via an agent.\\r\\n>\\r\\n> Introduces a new `cmd/entire/cli/learn` package to discover the cobra command surface, resolve repo stage (setup/agent install/first capture/workflow), build hardened agent prompts (tag-escape + control-sequence stripping), and select an available TextGenerator (including external `entire-agent-*`). Adds a small TUI spinner while agent work runs and extends `mdrender` to allow per-command style overrides.\\r\\n>\\r\\n> Updates the release GitHub Action to *best-effort* regenerate the embedded tour (installs pinned Claude CLI, runs `mise run learn:regenerate` with validation/atomic write), annotate failures, and send a dedicated Slack warning when regeneration fails without failing the release.\\r\\n>\\r\\n> <sup>Originally reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for an earlier commit when the command was named `tour`. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\r\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1146/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1146/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1170\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1170/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1170/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1170/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1170\",\n            \"id\": 4413295731,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7Z4guS\",\n            \"number\": 1170,\n            \"title\": \"feat(agent): add pi coding agent integration in-tree\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"dipree\",\n              \"id\": 3369400,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNjk0MDA=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3369400?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/dipree\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-05-09T17:39:53Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-11T14:10:51Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-05-11T14:10:49Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1170\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1170\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1170.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1170.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-05-11T14:10:49Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"Adds a built-in [Pi](https://github.com/earendil-works/pi-mono) integration. Ports the external [`entire-agent-pi`](https://github.com/entireio/external-agents/tree/main/agents/entire-agent-pi) plugin in-tree so Pi ships in every Entire CLI binary.\\r\\n\\r\\n## What it does\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter `entire enable --agent pi`:\\r\\n\\r\\n| Capability | How |\\r\\n|---|---|\\r\\n| Lifecycle hooks | Embedded TS extension at `.pi/extensions/entire/index.ts` forwards `session_start` / `before_agent_start` / `agent_end` / `session_shutdown` to `entire hooks pi <event>` |\\r\\n| Checkpoints | One per `before_agent_start` → `agent_end` pair |\\r\\n| Transcript capture | Pi's native JSONL is read live during the turn and copied to `<repo>/.entire/tmp/pi/<id>.json` at `agent_end` |\\r\\n| Files touched | `TranscriptAnalyzer` extracts paths from `write` / `edit` `toolCall` arguments |\\r\\n| Token attribution | `TokenCalculator` sums per-message `usage` (input / output / cacheRead / cacheWrite / api_call_count) |\\r\\n| v2 compact transcript | Branch-aware `compactPi` dispatched via `isPiFormat` sniffer; output is byte-compatible with the external plugin |\\r\\n| Resume | `pi --session <id>` (specific) or `pi --continue` (empty) |\\r\\n\\r\\n## Why it's not just a copy of the external plugin\\r\\n\\r\\n| Property | External | This PR |\\r\\n|---|---|---|\\r\\n| `DetectPresence` | `which pi` | repo-local `.pi/` only (matches Claude/Gemini/OpenCode convention) |\\r\\n| `FormatResumeCommand` | hard-coded `pi --continue` | honours session ID |\\r\\n| Session staging dir | `.entire/tmp` | `.entire/tmp/pi/` (avoids `AgentForTranscriptPath` collision with other agents) |\\r\\n| `session_shutdown` recovery | clears cache without reading | reads cache first so `SessionEnd` carries the right ID |\\r\\n| NPM type import | `@mariozechner/pi-coding-agent` (stale) | `@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent` |\\r\\n| Tree-aware parsing | per-agent (private) | shared `cmd/entire/cli/agent/pi/pijsonl/` so agent + compactor stay in sync |\\r\\n\\r\\n## Tests\\r\\n\\r\\n40+ unit tests + integration suite + Vogon E2E canary. `mise run check` green.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Out of scope\\r\\n\\r\\n`TextGenerator`, `SkillDiscoverer`/`AgentReviewer`, Vogon canary, `ExtractSummary`. Easy follow-ups; not required for the core \\\"track sessions, checkpoint, attribute tokens, compact\\\" loop.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Commits\\r\\n\\r\\n1. **`feat(agent): add pi coding agent integration in-tree`** — initial port\\r\\n2. **`fix(agent/pi): address review feedback`** — critical compactor bug (active-branch resolution on truncated data → abandoned-branch leak), `pijsonl` extraction, scanner buffer 1 MB → 10 MB, foreign-file rejection in `InstallHooks`, `GetSessionDir` repo-root resolution, doc fixes\\r\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1170/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1170/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/765\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/765/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/765/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/765/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/765\",\n            \"id\": 4131604897,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7NLeYg\",\n            \"number\": 765,\n            \"title\": \"feat: Agent Improvement Engine (insights, improve, evolve)\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"alishakawaguchi\",\n              \"id\": 6415609,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTU2MDk=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6415609?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/alishakawaguchi\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-03-25T00:44:27Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-08T21:05:31Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-05-08T21:05:31Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": true,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/765\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/765\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/765.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/765.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nAdds three new features to help users improve their AI coding sessions based on collected session data:\\n\\n- **`entire insights`** — Session quality scoring, cross-session trends, and agent comparisons. SQLite-cached, <1s response time.\\n- **`entire improve`** — Two-phase friction analysis (SQLite index → transcript deep-read → Claude CLI) that generates context file improvement suggestions (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, .cursorrules, .gemini) with evidence and unified diffs.\\n- **Evolution loop** — Auto-triggers improvement suggestions after N sessions (configurable, opt-in).\\n\\n### Architecture\\n\\n- **SQLite cache** (`.entire/insights.db`) — local analytics cache using `modernc.org/sqlite` (pure Go, CGO_ENABLED=0 compatible). Populated from `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch with staleness detection.\\n- **Commit-time scoring** — Session quality scores computed during condensation (pure math, <1ms, no AI call). Written to `insights/scores/` on the checkpoint branch for future frontend consumption.\\n- **Shared `llmcli` package** — Common Claude CLI execution extracted from `summarize/claude.go`. Both summarize and improve use it with different prompts.\\n- **`termstyle` package** — Shared terminal styling extracted from `status_style.go` to avoid duplication across renderers.\\n\\n### New packages\\n\\n| Package | Purpose |\\n|---------|---------|\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/termstyle/` | Shared terminal styling |\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/llmcli/` | Shared Claude CLI execution |\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/insightsdb/` | SQLite cache layer |\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/insights/` | Scoring algorithm + trend analysis |\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/improve/` | Context file detection, friction analyzer, suggestion generator |\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/evolve/` | Evolution loop trigger + suggestion tracker |\\n\\n### Key decisions\\n\\n- Requires summarization enabled — insights/improve gate on `IsSummarizeEnabled()`\\n- Improve uses two-phase analysis: SQLite finds recurring friction themes, then reads transcript excerpts from git for evidence before generating suggestions\\n- Evolution loop is opt-in (`evolve.enabled: false` by default)\\n- Binary size: +~8MB from `modernc.org/sqlite` (32MB → 40MB)\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [ ] Run `mise run test:ci` — all unit + integration tests pass\\n- [ ] Verify `entire insights` renders scores, trends, and agent comparisons\\n- [ ] Verify `entire improve --dry-run` shows friction patterns without AI call\\n- [ ] Verify `entire improve` generates context file suggestions\\n- [ ] Verify `.entire/insights.db` is created and populated on first run\\n- [ ] Verify scoring happens at commit time (check `CondenseResult.SessionScore`)\\n- [ ] Verify pre-existing tests still pass (strategy, summarize, settings)\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Adds new CLI commands plus a new SQLite cache and hooks into session condensation to compute/store quality scores, which could impact core session/metadata workflows and local disk state. Also introduces Claude CLI execution via a shared runner and transcript reads, increasing integration surface with external tooling.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Introduces a new analytics and improvement workflow: `entire insights` computes per-session quality scores, trend metrics, and agent comparisons from a local SQLite cache, with both terminal and `--json` output.\\n> \\n> Adds `entire improve` to analyze recent sessions for recurring friction (SQLite index + optional transcript deep-read) and then call the Claude CLI to generate context-file suggestions (with evidence and unified diffs), including a `--dry-run` mode that skips AI/transcript reads.\\n> \\n> Adds an opt-in evolution loop (`settings.evolve`) to track sessions since the last improvement run and print a tip prompting users to run `entire improve` after a configurable threshold; also refactors shared infrastructure by extracting `llmcli` (Claude CLI runner + git isolation) and `termstyle` (shared lipgloss styling), and adds the `modernc.org/sqlite` dependency for the new cache.\\n> \\n> <sup>Written by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot) for commit 78163861a9d55e259d57a04274ccf521e30edd96. Configure [here](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/765/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/765/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/958\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/958/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/958/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/958/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/958\",\n            \"id\": 4265562142,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7SeyqE\",\n            \"number\": 958,\n            \"title\": \"fix: skip empty sessions and prevent phantom checkpoint paths\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"pfleidi\",\n              \"id\": 118549,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjExODU0OQ==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118549?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pfleidi\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 2,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-04-15T00:45:28Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-04-15T23:47:53Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-04-15T23:47:51Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/958\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/958\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/958.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/958.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-04-15T23:47:51Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Problem\\n\\nWhen an agent session has no file changes and no transcript (e.g., Codex running inside Claude Code via the [codex-plugin-cc](https://github.com/openai/codex-plugin-cc)), the condensation logic writes metadata-only checkpoint stubs. This creates noise in checkpoint history and records phantom file paths pointing to non-existent transcript files.\\n\\n### How Codex companion creates empty sessions\\n\\nThe codex-plugin-cc runs Codex via an app-server protocol inside Claude Code. It does not call Entire hooks directly — but `entire enable` installs `.codex/hooks.json` and enables the `codex_hooks` feature flag in `.codex/config.toml`. Codex itself reads these hooks and fires `SessionStart`, `UserPromptSubmit`, and `Stop` via `entire hooks codex *`, creating a separate SessionState in `.git/entire-sessions/` alongside Claude Code's session.\\n\\nThe Codex hook payloads have a nullable `transcript_path` field that is often null, and the app-server does not write rollout files to `~/.codex/sessions/` (it uses a SQLite database instead). This means:\\n\\n- No `SaveStep` is called → no transcript on the shadow branch\\n- `TranscriptPath` is empty → no live transcript to read\\n- No rollout file on disk → no way to resolve the transcript after the fact\\n- `CondenseSession` proceeds anyway → metadata-only stub with phantom paths\\n\\nValidated via logs for checkpoint `5b6978164aea`: the Codex session fired `SessionStart` and `TurnStart` hooks with `session_ref: \\\"\\\"`, was condensed into 4 consecutive commits with `transcript_bytes: 0`, and never fired a `Stop` hook.\\n\\n### Prior behavior\\n\\n1. `CondenseSession` returned an error when there was no shadow branch and no `TranscriptPath` — but for sessions that had a shadow branch (from another session's commits on the same branch), it silently proceeded with empty transcript data\\n2. `writeSessionToSubdirectory` unconditionally recorded `Transcript` and `ContentHash` paths in the checkpoint summary even when `writeTranscript` wrote nothing, creating phantom paths to non-existent files\\n3. `tryAgentCommitFastPath` added `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers for any ACTIVE session, even empty ones — creating dangling trailers pointing to nothing on the metadata branch\\n4. `CondenseSessionByID` (used by `entire doctor`) would retry empty sessions indefinitely, never marking them as resolved\\n\\n## Solution\\n\\nSkip condensation for sessions with no meaningful content, and prevent phantom artifacts at every layer.\\n\\n### Skip gate in `CondenseSession`\\n\\nAfter extraction and file filtering, if both `sessionData.Transcript` and `sessionData.FilesTouched` are empty, return `CondenseResult{Skipped: true}` instead of writing a metadata-only stub. All three callers handle `Skipped`:\\n\\n- **`condenseAndUpdateState`** (PostCommit) — returns false, preserves shadow branches\\n- **`CondenseSessionByID`** (doctor) — marks `FullyCondensed=true` so doctor doesn't retry\\n- **`CondenseAndMarkFullyCondensed`** (eager condense) — marks `FullyCondensed=true`\\n\\n### Extraction refactor\\n\\nExtracted `extractOrCreateSessionData` from `CondenseSession` to handle three cases cleanly: shadow branch extraction, live transcript extraction, and a new default case that returns empty session data (letting the skip gate handle it) instead of erroring.\\n\\n### Phantom path fix in `writeSessionToSubdirectory`\\n\\n`writeTranscript` now returns `(bool, error)`. The caller only records `Transcript` and `ContentHash` paths in `SessionFilePaths` when files were actually written.\\n\\n### Dangling trailer prevention in `tryAgentCommitFastPath`\\n\\nThe prepare-commit-msg fast path now skips ACTIVE sessions with no `TranscriptPath`, no `FilesTouched`, and `StepCount == 0`. This prevents adding `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers that would point to nothing on the metadata branch.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] `TestCondenseSession_SkipsWhenNoTranscriptAndNoFiles` — empty session → `Skipped == true`\\n- [x] `TestCondenseSession_DoesNotSkipWhenFilesTouchedButNoTranscript` — files but no transcript → condensed normally\\n- [x] `TestCondenseSessionByID_SkippedPreservesState` — doctor path marks `FullyCondensed`\\n- [x] `TestCondenseAndMarkFullyCondensed_SkippedMarksFullyCondensed` — eager path marks `FullyCondensed`\\n- [x] `TestTryAgentCommitFastPath_SkipsEmptySession` — no trailer for empty session\\n- [x] `TestTryAgentCommitFastPath_AcceptsSessionWithContent` — trailer for session with content\\n- [x] `TestTryAgentCommitFastPath_SkipsEmptyButAcceptsContentSession` — multi-session: skips empty Codex, uses Claude Code\\n- [x] `TestWriteCommitted_EmptyTranscript_NoPhantomPaths` — no phantom paths for empty transcript\\n- [x] `TestWriteCommitted_WithTranscript_PathsPopulated` — paths set when transcript exists\\n- [x] `TestShadowStrategy_AgentCommit_GetsTrailerWhenSessionHasContent` — integration test for fast path with content\\n- [x] Full CI suite passes (`mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci`)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches core checkpoint condensation and commit-hook trailer logic; while behavior is guarded by tests, it can change when/which sessions get linked to commits and marked condensed.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Prevents **empty/companion agent sessions** (no transcript and no files touched) from being condensed into checkpoints, avoiding metadata-only stubs and dangling `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers.\\n> \\n> `CondenseSession` now returns a `CondenseResult.Skipped` early via a new skip gate (and a small extraction refactor), and all callers handle skips by not updating state/cleaning up branches or by marking sessions `FullyCondensed` to stop `entire doctor` retry loops. The commit-message fast path (`tryAgentCommitFastPath`) now ignores ACTIVE sessions with no condensable content.\\n> \\n> Fixes **phantom checkpoint paths** by having `writeTranscript` return whether it actually wrote files, and only populating `SessionFilePaths.Transcript`/`ContentHash` when present; adds targeted unit and integration regression coverage for these scenarios.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 5a5167508a040a260736f3e889bdac177f3a67fb. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/958/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/958/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/821\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/821/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/821/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/821/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/821\",\n            \"id\": 4182739702,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7PFR7D\",\n            \"number\": 821,\n            \"title\": \"feat: push logic for checkpoints v2 refs\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"pfleidi\",\n              \"id\": 118549,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjExODU0OQ==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118549?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pfleidi\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-03-31T22:23:45Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-04-06T20:57:35Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-04-06T20:57:32Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/821\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/821\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/821.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/821.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-04-06T20:57:32Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nImplements push logic for checkpoints v2 refs under `refs/entire/`. This is task A7 from the [checkpoints v2 design spec](docs/superpowers/specs/2026-03-19-checkpoints-v2-design.md).\\n\\nWhen both `checkpoints_v2` and `push_v2_refs` are enabled in strategy options, the pre-push hook pushes v2 refs alongside the existing v1 branch using explicit refspecs:\\n\\n```\\nrefs/entire/checkpoints/v2/main:refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/main\\nrefs/entire/checkpoints/v2/full/current:refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/full/current\\nrefs/entire/checkpoints/v2/full/0000000000001:refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/full/0000000000001\\n```\\n\\n### How it works\\n\\n**Push gating:** Both settings must be true:\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"strategy_options\\\": {\\n    \\\"checkpoints_v2\\\": true,\\n    \\\"push_v2_refs\\\": true\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**What gets pushed:** `/main`, `/full/current`, and the latest archived generation (older archives are immutable and were pushed when created).\\n\\n**Merge recovery for `/main` and `/full/current`:** When a push fails (non-fast-forward), the CLI fetches the remote ref, flattens both trees, combines entries, and creates a merge commit — same strategy as v1. This works conflict-free because both refs contain only sharded checkpoint directories (`<id[:2]>/<id[2:]>/`) with no root-level files.\\n\\n**Rotation conflict recovery:** When `/full/current` push fails and the remote has an archived generation we don't have locally, another machine rotated. Instead of merging two divergent `/full/current` refs (which would duplicate data across generations), the CLI merges local data into the latest archived generation:\\n\\n```\\nStarting state (synced): /full/current has 95 checkpoints\\n\\nUser A: adds 7 → 102 → rotation triggers\\n  /full/0000000000001: 102 checkpoints (95 shared + 7 from A)\\n  /full/current: fresh orphan\\n  Pushed to remote.\\n\\nUser B: adds 3 → 98 locally, pushes /full/current → non-fast-forward\\n  Recovery:\\n    1. ls-remote → discovers /full/0000000000001 (not local)\\n    2. Fetch /full/0000000000001\\n    3. Tree-merge local /full/current into /full/0000000000001\\n       → 95 shared deduplicated by git content-addressing, result: 105\\n    4. Update generation.json timestamps, push /full/0000000000001\\n    5. Adopt remote /full/current as local\\n\\nFinal state:\\n  /full/0000000000001: 105 checkpoints (no duplication)\\n  /full/current: fresh orphan\\n```\\n\\nThis preserves the key GC property: each checkpoint's raw transcript exists in exactly one generation, so deleting a generation ref makes its unique blobs unreachable.\\n\\n### generation.json changes\\n\\n`generation.json` is no longer written to `/full/current` on every checkpoint write. It's written only at archive time (during rotation), containing just timestamps:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"oldest_checkpoint_at\\\": \\\"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\\\",\\n  \\\"newest_checkpoint_at\\\": \\\"2026-02-15T00:00:00Z\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThe `checkpoints` list field has been removed. Checkpoint count for rotation is determined by walking shard directories in the tree. This keeps `/full/current` free of root-level files, making all tree merges conflict-free.\\n\\n### Fetch-on-demand\\n\\n- **Checkpoint remote:** When `push_v2_refs` is enabled and a checkpoint remote is configured, the v2 `/main` ref is fetched from the checkpoint remote URL on first push (same one-time pattern as v1).\\n- **`entire resume`:** When a transcript isn't found locally, `readTranscriptFromFullRefs` discovers and fetches remote `/full/*` refs before giving up. Respects `checkpoint_remote` configuration.\\n- All `V2GitStore` instances receive the resolved fetch remote at construction time — no hardcoded `\\\"origin\\\"`.\\n\\n### Other improvements\\n\\n- Extracted `WalkCheckpointShards` helper for reusable two-level shard iteration (used by `CountCheckpointsInTree` and `ListCommitted`)\\n- Exported `GenerationRefPattern`, `GetRefState`, `ListArchivedGenerations`, `AddGenerationJSONToTree` for cross-package use\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] Unit tests for all push/merge/rotation functions (`push_v2_test.go`)\\n- [x] Integration tests for full push cycle and disabled-push gating (`v2_push_test.go`)\\n- [x] Updated generation tests for archive-time-only `generation.json`\\n- [x] `mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci` passes\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Adds new git push/fetch/merge paths for custom v2 refs (including rotation-conflict handling) and changes generation rotation metadata, which could impact checkpoint durability and resume/restore behavior if edge cases are missed.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Enables **optional pushing of v2 checkpoint refs** (under `refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/*`) from the pre-push hook when both `checkpoints_v2` and `push_v2_refs` are set, including fetch+tree-merge recovery on non-fast-forward and special handling when `/full/current` was rotated remotely.\\n> \\n> Changes v2 generation management so `/full/current` no longer writes `generation.json` on each write; rotation now **counts checkpoints by walking shard dirs**, writes `generation.json` only when archiving, and resets `/full/current` to an empty orphan commit.\\n> \\n> Adds v2 read/fetch plumbing: `V2GitStore` can read committed metadata and raw transcripts across `/full/current` + archived generations (with on-demand remote fetch), `resume`/`RestoreLogsOnly` prefer v2 when enabled with v1 fallback, and checkpoint-remote setup can fetch the v2 `/main` ref when v2 pushing is enabled.\\n> \\n> <sup>Written by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot) for commit edca0a90161e18f5b1e86877c4041e6185b66735. Configure [here](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/821/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/821/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1015\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1015/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1015/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1015/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1015\",\n            \"id\": 4317777414,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7VEV_f\",\n            \"number\": 1015,\n            \"title\": \"feat: entire recap command\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-04-23T17:44:53Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-05T16:06:39Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-05-05T16:06:35Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1015\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1015\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1015.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1015.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-05-05T16:06:35Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/bd45a590a611\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n- Redesigns the `entire recap` terminal output per spec at `docs/2026-04-22-entire-recap-visual-redesign-design.md`\\n- Three-panel layout (summary → activity strip → agents), per-agent cards with comparison bars\\n- Wires CLI to the new `/api/v1/me/recap` endpoint (pairs with entirehq/entire.io#1604)\\n- New TUI `v` keybinding cycles view mode (me/team/both)\\n- Drops `--30` flag (redundant with `--month`), drops the worktrees/labels/repos bottom panel\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- **Server client** — `cmd/entire/cli/recap/me_recap.go` (new) fetches `/api/v1/me/recap`; `recap.go` prefers it with fallback to the old three-endpoint stack.\\n- **Bar primitive** — `cmd/entire/cli/recap/render_bar.go` (new) renders comparison bars with 9 TDD unit tests.\\n- **Summary panel** — `render_summary.go` (new): `you` / `team` metric rows + reflowing `top` line + context line. Empty signals omit instead of placeholder.\\n- **Activity strip** — `render_activity.go` (new): every cell rendered (including zero days), axis anchored to today, `most active` annotation.\\n- **Agents card** — rewritten around three field groups: bars → team qualitative → your qualitative. Empty rows drop entirely.\\n- **View toggle** — `--view me|contributors|both` + TUI `v` key. Prefixes only in both mode.\\n- **Cleanup** — removes `Range30d`, removes bottom panel, adds JSON tags to `LabelCount`.\\n\\n## Pairs with\\n\\n- Server endpoint: entirehq/entire.io#1604 (draft)\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] 9 `renderComparisonBar` unit tests (TDD, all pass)\\n- [x] Summary / activity / agents card renderer tests updated\\n- [x] `mise run check` — full CI gate green (90s)\\n- [x] Live smoke vs. local wrangler dev: renders the spec output with real me + team data\\n\\n## Out of scope / follow-ups\\n\\n- Rename `recap` → `activity` per `docs/2026-04-21-entire-activity-replan.md`\\n- Server-side `aggregateByAgent` unit tests (against entire.io)\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Adds a new `entire recap` command that combines local session data with authenticated server endpoints and a new on-disk cache, plus an optional TUI mode; regressions would primarily impact CLI output and network interactions. Risk is moderated by extensive unit tests and best-effort fallbacks when auth/API data is unavailable.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Introduces a new `entire recap` command that summarizes recent checkpoint activity with a redesigned 3-panel terminal layout (summary, activity strip, per-agent cards) and optional TUI rendering.\\n> \\n> The recap pipeline now loads local session/checkpoint state, links checkpoints to commits via `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers, and optionally enriches checkpoints from the API (labels/skills/tool profile) using a safe, version-aware disk cache that avoids caching “empty/pending” analyses.\\n> \\n> Adds team/contributor comparisons by fetching aggregated data from the new `/api/v1/me/recap` endpoint (with fallback to legacy repo-overview endpoints + batch analyses), plus new flags for time range, agent filtering, view mode (`me|contributors|both`), refresh-cache, and allowing insecure HTTP for local dev.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 32c0f746ecf677adb620da4700c68a864e2ae9dd. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1015/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1015/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1009\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1009/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1009/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1009/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1009\",\n            \"id\": 4310263184,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7Ur4da\",\n            \"number\": 1009,\n            \"title\": \"one more pass on top of feat/entire-review\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-04-22T16:00:42Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-04-23T06:54:36Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-04-23T06:43:41Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1009\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1009\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1009.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1009.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-04-23T06:43:41Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/3eaecdfe2315\\n\\nA few review / bug fixes.\\r\\n\\r\\n- removed `--track-only` replaced it with `entire review attach` instead - I think `--track-only` is to complicated and easy to forget (both to do it before, but also to remove it after)\\r\\n- allow specifying a \\\"prompt\\\" instead of just using skills (is not great yet, the page after the skill pick asks you for a prompt)\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\n  {\\r\\n    \\\"review\\\": {\\r\\n      \\\"claude-code\\\": {\\r\\n        \\\"skills\\\": [\\\"/pr-review-toolkit:review-pr\\\", \\\"/test-auditor\\\"],\\r\\n        \\\"prompt\\\": \\\"Focus on security regressions this week, then run the skills above.\\\"\\r\\n      }\\r\\n    }\\r\\n  }\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n- `--agent <name>` flag (`47c40ada2`) — select a specific configured agent when more than one is in `review:`; unknown value surfaces a concrete error listing the configured alternatives.\\r\\n\\r\\n- Hooks-installed gate(`d420e6671`) — aborts with a clear `entire configure --agent <name>` pointer when the selected agent's hooks aren't installed (silent failure shape: marker would otherwise be written with no hook to adopt it).\\r\\n\\r\\n- `ReviewPrompt` field (`7d9aadb91`) — records the ground-truth text of the review request alongside the structured `ReviewSkills` list. Composed prompt for spawn; first user prompt from the transcript for attach.\\r\\n\\r\\n- Review-attach surfaces (`2505c5fd2`) — two equivalent ways to tag an existing session as a review:\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\nentire attach <session-id> --review [--skills \\\"/a,/b\\\"]\\r\\nentire review attach <session-id> [--skills \\\"/a,/b\\\"]\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nBoth funnel into `runAttach` via an `attachOptions` struct. Skills resolve after agent detection (`d81953ed5`) so a Gemini session attached without `--agent` correctly auto-detects. External agents work on both surfaces (`76535a29d`).\\r\\n\\r\\nThis also adds the first prompt from the log as review_prompt\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### UX polish\\r\\n\\r\\n**First-run banner** (`7f2fdb06b`) — running `entire review` with no config used to silently drop into the picker. Now prints an explicit \\\"first-run setup\\\" banner, gates the picker on a huh confirmation, and signposts \\\"Setup complete — running review now.\\\" when transitioning to the actual review.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Helpful error text** in the empty-installed-agents case.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Internal cleanups\\r\\n\\r\\n- `runAttach` grew an `attachOptions` struct to avoid a 6th positional param.\\r\\n- Extracted `runAttachSurfaceReviewErrors` so review-mode errors reach stderr under root's `SilenceErrors=true`.\\r\\n- `review_test.go` got a shared `setupReviewTestRepoWithCommit` helper, test constants for repeated agent/skill names, and a `reflect.DeepEqual` merge-result assertion fixing a bug where multi-element skill slices weren't compared element-wise.\\r\\n- `slices.Contains` replaces a throwaway map build in the hooks gate; direct map lookup replaces a linear scan in `selectReviewAgent`'s override path.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Test coverage\\r\\n\\r\\n- Regression tests for every correctness fix (marker agent/SHA binding, picker wipes, fallback marker survival, existing-checkpoint review refusal).\\r\\n- End-to-end integration tests for both attach surfaces, including Gemini auto-detection without `--agent`.\\r\\n- Pinned behavior tests for the data model: `ReviewPrompt` roundtrip, marker location, `Kind.IsReview` umbrella, config-doesn't-leak-into-attach.\\r\\n\\r\\nAll unit + integration + canary E2E tests green. No API calls consumed — Vogon canary + external-agent canary cover the checkpointing paths.\\r\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes the persisted review configuration schema and checkpoint/session metadata (adds `review_prompt`), plus modifies review marker adoption logic; this can affect backward compatibility and how reviews are tagged/recorded across agents and repos.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **review-mode attach** support via `entire attach --review` (plus new `entire review attach` alias), recording review metadata (`kind=agent_review`, optional `review_skills`, and new **`review_prompt`** captured from the transcript’s first user prompt) into session state and committed checkpoint metadata.\\n> \\n> Upgrades `entire review` configuration from `review: {agent: [skills...]}` to `review: {agent: {skills, prompt}}`, adds first-run setup confirmation UX, supports `--agent` selection when multiple agents are configured, and prevents silent failure by aborting when the chosen agent’s hooks are not installed.\\n> \\n> Hardens pending-review marker adoption by scoping to **worktree + agent name** and discarding stale markers when HEAD SHA has moved; also fixes non-launchable-agent behavior to preserve the marker and instruct users to start the agent manually instead of relying on the removed `--track-only` path. Extensive new unit/integration tests cover these regressions and end-to-end flows.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 4ffaef2c56e365974deb8a429df4da0a2c0c0043. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1009/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 1,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 1\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1009/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/921\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/921/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/921/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/921/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/921\",\n            \"id\": 4241455718,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7RjnP4\",\n            \"number\": 921,\n            \"title\": \"fix: support Claude JSON array responses for summaries\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-04-10T19:58:48Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-04-11T11:32:09Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-04-11T11:32:08Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/921\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/921\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/921.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/921.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-04-11T11:32:08Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\nSupports both Claude CLI `--output-format json` response shapes when generating summaries:\\n- legacy single-object output like `{ \\\"result\\\": ... }`\\n- newer array output containing a `type: \\\"result\\\"` item\\n\\nThis fixes summary generation for Claude Code environments that emit array-shaped JSON while preserving compatibility with installs that still return the legacy object shape.\\n\\n## Changes\\n- add a shared Claude CLI result extractor in the `agent` package\\n- reuse that extractor in `summarize/claude.go` and `agent/claudecode/generate.go`\\n- add regression coverage for array-shaped Claude responses in summary generation\\n- add Claude Code `GenerateText` coverage for array-shaped responses\\n\\n## Verification\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/summarize ./cmd/entire/cli/agent ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode`\\n- manual end-to-end verification with local Claude shims for both object and array response shapes against `entire explain --checkpoint <id> --generate --force`\\n\\nCloses #750\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Low risk, localized change to Claude CLI response parsing with added test coverage; primary risk is unforeseen response variants causing summary/text generation to fail to parse.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds a shared `agent.ExtractClaudeCLIResult` helper that can pull the `result` payload from both legacy single-object Claude CLI JSON and newer array-shaped responses.\\n> \\n> Updates Claude-based summary generation (`summarize/claude.go`) and Claude Code `GenerateText` to use this extractor, and injects a `CommandRunner` into `ClaudeCodeAgent` to make the behavior testable. New tests cover array responses (and the missing-`result` error path) for both summarization and text generation.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit d9ddd3190ffadcd0d7fa33c24fc0bf88a05b23e1. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/921/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/921/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/417\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/417/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/417/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/417/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/417\",\n            \"id\": 3960808061,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7ExQnV\",\n            \"number\": 417,\n            \"title\": \"Add Copilot agent support\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"id\": 881031,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T03:28:38Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-04-17T16:07:46Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-03-05T23:07:05Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": true,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/417\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/417\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/417.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/417.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"Entire-Checkpoint: c74816392558\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/417/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 2,\n              \"+1\": 1,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 1,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/417/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/922\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/922/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/922/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/922/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/922\",\n            \"id\": 4241596835,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7RkClN\",\n            \"number\": 922,\n            \"title\": \"Clean up condensation logic: type-enforced redaction boundaries\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"pfleidi\",\n              \"id\": 118549,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjExODU0OQ==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118549?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pfleidi\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 3,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-04-10T20:32:53Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-04-11T00:24:18Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-04-11T00:24:17Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/922\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/922\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/922.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/922.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-04-11T00:24:17Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Problem\\n\\nThe condensation path in `CondenseSession()` had three issues:\\n\\n1. **Redundant redaction** — The same transcript was redacted up to 3 times during a v2 condensation: once in `CondenseSession` for the compact transcript input, once in `GitStore.writeTranscript` for v1, and once in `V2GitStore.writeTranscriptBlobs` for v2 full transcript.\\n\\n2. **Scattered v2 checks** — `settings.IsCheckpointsV2Enabled(ctx)` was checked in `CondenseSession`, again redundantly inside `compactTranscriptForV2`, and in `writeCommittedV2IfEnabled`.\\n\\n3. **Implicit redaction contracts** — The `compact` package and checkpoint stores accepted raw `[]byte` transcripts with no indication of whether redaction had been applied. The expectation that data should be redacted was implicit and undocumented.\\n\\n## Solution\\n\\nIntroduce `redact.RedactedBytes` — an opaque struct type (unexported `data` field) that can only be produced by `redact.JSONLBytes()` or the escape-hatch `redact.AlreadyRedacted()` for trusted sources. This establishes compile-time contracts at package boundaries:\\n\\n- **`compact.Compact`** accepts `RedactedBytes`, enforcing that only redacted transcripts are compacted\\n- **`WriteCommittedOptions.Transcript`** and **`UpdateCommittedOptions.Transcript`** use `RedactedBytes`, documenting the store contract\\n- **`replaceTranscript`** and **`writeTranscriptBlobs`** accept `RedactedBytes` at the function parameter level, preventing unredacted writes to permanent storage\\n\\n### Key changes\\n\\n- **`CondenseSession`** redacts the transcript once early, then passes the single `RedactedBytes` result to both the compact path and the checkpoint stores — eliminating 2 redundant redaction passes\\n- **Store write paths** (`writeTranscript`, `writeTranscriptBlobs`, `replaceTranscript`, `UpdateCommitted`) no longer redact internally for in-memory data. The `TranscriptPath` file-read fallback retains its own redaction since data from disk is untrusted\\n- **`attach.go`** now explicitly redacts before calling `WriteCommitted` (previously relied on store-internal redaction)\\n- **`compactTranscriptForV2`** accepts `RedactedBytes` and drops the redundant `IsCheckpointsV2Enabled` guard (both callers already check)\\n- **Hooks finalize path** propagates `RedactedBytes` end-to-end instead of stripping to `[]byte` and re-wrapping\\n\\n### Safety\\n\\nIf transcript redaction fails in `CondenseSession`, the transcript is dropped rather than persisting potentially sensitive content. The checkpoint metadata (files touched, attributions, etc.) is still written — only the transcript is omitted.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] `mise run fmt && mise run lint` — zero issues\\n- [x] `mise run test:ci` — all unit + integration tests pass\\n- [x] `mise run test:e2e:canary` — Vogon E2E tests pass\\n- [ ] Verify `redact.JSONLBytes` calls in store write paths exist only in `TranscriptPath` fallback blocks\\n- [ ] Verify `IsCheckpointsV2Enabled` no longer appears in `compactTranscriptForV2`\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Medium risk because it changes core checkpoint persistence APIs (transcript types and redaction responsibilities) and could affect what transcript data is stored if any call site fails to redact or mishandles the new contract.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Enforces explicit redaction boundaries for checkpoint transcripts** by introducing `redact.RedactedBytes` and requiring callers to pass *pre-redacted* transcript data into checkpoint write/update flows.\\n> \\n> Redaction is moved out of store internals for in-memory transcripts: `WriteCommittedOptions.Transcript`/`UpdateCommittedOptions.Transcript`, transcript replacement, and v2 full-transcript blob writing now operate on `RedactedBytes` as-is, while file-based fallbacks (`TranscriptPath`, subagent transcripts) still redact on read because disk content is treated as untrusted.\\n> \\n> Condensation/finalization paths now redact once (with perf spans) and reuse the result for v1 storage, v2 compact transcript generation, and AI summarization; on redaction failure they **drop the transcript but still write metadata**. Tests/benchmarks/migration/explain/summarize/compact are updated to wrap trusted fixtures and persisted transcripts via `redact.AlreadyRedacted` and to validate the new “store preserves redacted transcript” behavior.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 09c40402e7b32a326913f190e206e6378527c6d9. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/922/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/922/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/923\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/923/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/923/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/923/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/923\",\n            \"id\": 4241811938,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7Rks6t\",\n            \"number\": 923,\n            \"title\": \"Fix flaky Cursor/OpenCode E2E behavior and transcript prep timing\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"pfleidi\",\n              \"id\": 118549,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjExODU0OQ==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118549?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pfleidi\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-04-10T21:26:48Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-04-11T07:06:00Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-04-11T07:05:59Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/923\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/923\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/923.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/923.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-04-11T07:05:59Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\n- Re-resolve Cursor transcript paths before waiting and increase transcript preparation wait time to avoid missing nested session file writes.\\n- Reduce Cursor interactive test flakiness by broadening ready-state prompt matching and slightly increasing startup/trust-dialog wait windows.\\n- Make OpenCode honor per-prompt timeout overrides and raise `TestMultiSessionSequential` prompt timeouts to reduce timeout-bound failures.\\n- Harden a checkpoint path-normalization test on macOS by resolving temp dir symlinks before repo initialization.\\n\\n## Validation\\n- go build ./...\\n- go vet ./...\\n- go test -c -tags e2e ./e2e/tests\\n- mise run test:e2e:canary\\n- mise run test:e2e --agent cursor-cli \\\"TestInteractive(AttributionMultiCommitSameSession|AttributionOnAgentCommit|ContentOverlapRevertNewFile|MultiStep|ShadowBranchCleanedAfterAgentCommit)$\\\"\\n- mise run test:e2e --agent opencode TestMultiSessionSequential\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Low risk: changes are limited to transcript polling behavior and test/e2e timeouts/prompt matching, with minimal impact on core business logic. Main risk is masking genuine failures by increasing waits or broadening readiness regexes.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Hardens Cursor transcript preparation** by extending the wait window and making polling respect `ctx` deadlines/cancellation using a timer-based sleep.\\n> \\n> **Stabilizes E2E agent runs** by broadening Cursor CLI ready-state prompt matching, increasing startup/trust-dialog wait timeouts, and making OpenCode honor `WithPromptTimeout` over the `E2E_TIMEOUT` env var.\\n> \\n> **Reduces test flakiness across platforms** by resolving macOS temp-dir symlinks in a checkpoint path-normalization test, and by raising timeouts in `TestMultiSessionSequential` via per-prompt overrides.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 957579f47695861bbcc28d1e8aca82e7fa13b9ca. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/923/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/923/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/230\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/230/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/230/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/230/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/230\",\n            \"id\": 3923981674,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7C3z2L\",\n            \"number\": 230,\n            \"title\": \"feat: add export mode with showcase redaction to explain command\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"sunnypatneedi\",\n              \"id\": 5299693,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTk2OTM=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5299693?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/sunnypatneedi\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/sunnypatneedi\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/sunnypatneedi/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/sunnypatneedi/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/sunnypatneedi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/sunnypatneedi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/sunnypatneedi/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/sunnypatneedi/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/sunnypatneedi/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/sunnypatneedi/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/sunnypatneedi/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [\n              {\n                \"id\": 10224940200,\n                \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACYXQ0qA\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/needs-issue\",\n                \"name\": \"needs-issue\",\n                \"color\": \"e99695\",\n                \"default\": false,\n                \"description\": \"PR submitted without a corresponding issue\",\n                \"archived_at\": null,\n                \"archived_by\": null\n              }\n            ],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 4,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-02-10T23:17:17Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-04-07T15:39:55Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-04-07T15:39:55Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/230\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/230\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/230.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/230.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nCompanies are starting to[ ask for sessions](https://x.com/garrytan/status/2018976030644748341?s=20) for proof-of-work to evaluate orchestration mastery. This allows to export the session in a safe and secure way that showcases the judgement and skills of the individual building with agents.\\n\\nAdds structured export functionality to the `explain` command for creating portfolio-ready showcases of AI sessions with privacy-safe redaction.\\n\\nCloses #374\\n\\n## Key Changes\\n\\n- **Export flags**: `--export`, `--showcase`, `--format` (json/markdown), `-o`/`--output`\\n- **Showcase redaction**: Aggressive privacy filters for public sharing\\n  - Pattern-based: URLs, IPs, DB strings, emails, JWTs, PEM keys, ARNs\\n  - Structural: project-relative paths, project name normalization\\n  - Blocklist: user-defined terms (company names, codenames)\\n  - Entropy-based: existing secret detection\\n- **Settings integration**: showcase config in `strategy_options`\\n- **Formatters**: JSON and Markdown output formats\\n- **Integration tests**: full export workflow coverage\\n\\n## Usage\\n\\n```bash\\n# Export with showcase redaction (privacy-safe)\\nentire explain -c <checkpoint-id> --export --showcase --format=json -o showcase.json\\n\\n# Export as markdown for README\\nentire explain -c <checkpoint-id> --export --showcase --format=markdown -o SHOWCASE.md\\n```\\n\\n## Configuration\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"strategy_options\\\": {\\n    \\\"showcase\\\": {\\n      \\\"redact_paths\\\": true,\\n      \\\"redact_usernames\\\": true,\\n      \\\"redact_project_info\\\": true,\\n      \\\"allowed_paths\\\": [\\\"src/\\\", \\\"lib/\\\"],\\n      \\\"custom_blocklist\\\": [\\\"company-name\\\"]\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Security Note\\n\\nAlways review output before publishing - redaction is best-effort and cannot guarantee 100% removal of all sensitive data.\\n\\n## Test Plan\\n\\n- [x] Unit tests for showcase redaction (`redact/showcase_test.go`)\\n- [x] Unit tests for settings helpers (`settings/settings_test.go`)\\n- [x] Unit tests for formatters (`cli/explain_formatters_test.go`)\\n- [x] Integration tests for export workflow (`integration_test/explain_export_test.go`)\\n- [x] Documentation updated in CLAUDE.md\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches user-facing CLI output and introduces new redaction logic; incorrect patterns or config parsing could leak sensitive data or over-redact shared content, though the feature is opt-in and well-tested.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds a new `entire explain --export` mode (checkpoint-only) that outputs a structured export in `json` or `markdown`, optionally writing to a file via `-o/--output`, and enforces clear flag validation/mutual exclusivity with existing transcript/verbosity/generation modes.\\n> \\n> Introduces *showcase redaction* (`--showcase`) layered on top of existing entropy-based secret redaction, adding pattern/blocklist/structural redaction (e.g., internal URLs, private IPs, DB strings, emails/JWT/PEM, git remote URLs, user paths) and a new settings-backed config parser under `strategy_options.showcase`.\\n> \\n> Adds new formatter helpers plus unit and integration test coverage for export formats, settings parsing, and end-to-end redaction behavior, and documents the feature in `CLAUDE.md`.\\n> \\n> <sup>Written by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot) for commit 0ac238dae99b1d934b6763978586dbe7ff1c9d87. This will update automatically on new commits. Configure [here](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/230/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/230/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/875\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/875/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/875/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/875/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/875\",\n            \"id\": 4226802988,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7Q5n5-\",\n            \"number\": 875,\n            \"title\": \"Add Codex support for explain --generate\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-04-08T18:37:39Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-04-10T08:50:17Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-04-10T08:50:14Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/875\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/875\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/875.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/875.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-04-10T08:50:14Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"Adds support to generate summary from codex session with `entire explain -c <checkpointID> --generate`\\r\\n\\r\\nAvoids error `failed to generate summary: transcript has no content to summarize`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\r\\n> [!NOTE]\\r\\n> **Medium Risk**\\r\\n> Adds a new parsing/scoping path for Codex transcripts used by `explain --generate`, which could affect checkpoint transcript slicing and summary accuracy for Codex sessions but is localized to transcript processing.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> **Overview**\\r\\n> `explain --generate` and transcript rendering now support Codex sessions by scoping checkpoint transcripts using Codex `response_item` offsets (via new `codex.SliceFromResponseItem`) instead of generic line slicing.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> `summarize.BuildCondensedTranscriptFromBytes` gains a Codex path that compacts Codex rollout JSONL into the shared condensed transcript format (including tool calls), and `compact` Codex format detection is broadened to recognize additional Codex line types. New tests cover Codex scoping and condensed-transcript extraction, and tool-detail extraction is hardened against nil inputs.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 71897706a984a94e6e51c0f2f300e77e83c0494a. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\r\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/875/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/875/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/812\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/812/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/812/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/812/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/812\",\n            \"id\": 4175106432,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7OzUeE\",\n            \"number\": 812,\n            \"title\": \"Fix attribution inflation from intermediate commits\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-03-31T01:48:48Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-04-08T14:19:07Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-04-07T14:40:08Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/812\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/812\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/812.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/812.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-04-07T14:40:08Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nFixes attribution inflation that caused agent percentages to be incorrectly deflated, and adds holistic combined attribution for multi-session checkpoints. Supersedes #813.\\n\\n## Problems Fixed\\n\\n### 1. Intermediate commit inflation\\nWhen calculating non-agent file contributions, the code used `attributionBaseCommit → headCommitHash` (session start → current commit). In multi-commit sessions, this counted ALL user edits since session start instead of just this commit's changes.\\n\\n**Fix:** Use `parentCommitHash → headCommitHash` (first parent → current commit) so only this commit's non-agent file changes are counted.\\n\\n### 2. Pre-session worktree dirt\\nPA1 (first PromptAttribution) captures the worktree state at session start, which includes files already dirty before the session (CLI config from `entire enable`, leftover changes). These were incorrectly added to human contribution counts.\\n\\n**Fix:** Split prompt attributions into baseline (PA1, `CheckpointNumber <= 1`) and session (PA2+). PA1 is used for agent line correction but excluded from human counts.\\n\\n### 3. Multi-session cross-contamination\\nIn multi-session commits (e.g., 3 `claude -p` calls then commit), each session's attribution counted files from OTHER agent sessions as human work. Session A creating `blue.md` would see Session B's `red.md` as human-added.\\n\\n**Fix:** Thread `allAgentFiles` (union of all sessions' `FilesTouched`) through the attribution pipeline. Files touched by any agent session are excluded from human counts in all sessions.\\n\\n### 4. Commit session claiming `.entire/` config files\\nWhen a session with no `FilesTouched` (e.g., a commit-only session) falls back to using all committed files, `.entire/` config files from `entire enable` were included as agent work.\\n\\n**Fix:** Filter `.entire/` paths from the fallback in `committedFilesExcludingMetadata()`.\\n\\n### 5. PA1 using shared shadow branch for new sessions\\nNew sessions incorrectly used the shadow branch (which may contain other sessions' checkpoint data) as the PA1 reference. This caused pre-session worktree dirt to be missed because it already existed in the shared shadow tree.\\n\\n**Fix:** New sessions (`StepCount == 0`) always diff against the base commit tree for PA1, not the shadow branch.\\n\\n### 6. Combined attribution (replaces #813)\\nAdded holistic `combined_attribution` field on `CheckpointSummary` for multi-session checkpoints. Instead of naively summing per-session values (which double-counts), this diffs `parent → HEAD` once and classifies files as agent vs human based on the union of sessions with real checkpoints (`CheckpointsCount > 0`). Filters `.entire/` and `.claude/` config paths.\\n\\n## Test Results\\n\\n| Scenario | Per-session | Combined |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 3 agent sessions (create blue, create red, commit) | Each file session: 100% | 100% |\\n| Agent file + human file + commit | Agent session: 25% (1 of 4 lines) | 25% |\\n| Single session create + commit | 100% | n/a |\\n| Two agent sessions + human commit | Both: 100% | 100% |\\n| Agent modifies existing file | 100% | n/a |\\n\\n## Files Changed\\n\\n- `manual_commit_attribution.go` — `AllAgentFiles` on `AttributionParams`, `isAgentOrMetadataFile()` helper, `classifyBaselineEdits()` for PA1 split\\n- `manual_commit_condensation.go` — Thread `allAgentFiles` through opts, `committedFilesExcludingMetadata()` for `.entire/` filtering\\n- `manual_commit_hooks.go` — Compute `allAgentFiles` union in PostCommit, PA1 shadow branch guard (`StepCount > 0`), holistic `updateCombinedAttributionForCheckpoint()`\\n- `checkpoint/committed.go` — `ReadSessionMetadata()`, `UpdateCheckpointSummary()`\\n- `checkpoint/checkpoint.go` — `CombinedAttribution` field on `CheckpointSummary`\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/812/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/812/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/534\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/534/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/534/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/534/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/534\",\n            \"id\": 3998221616,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7GrnTM\",\n            \"number\": 534,\n            \"title\": \"Support resuming from squash merge commits with multiple checkpoints\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"pfleidi\",\n              \"id\": 118549,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjExODU0OQ==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118549?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pfleidi\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 3,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T23:11:13Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-04T00:17:36Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-03-04T00:17:34Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/534\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/534\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/534.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/534.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-03-04T00:17:34Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\n- Support `entire resume` on squash merge commits that contain multiple `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers\\r\\n- Fix checkpoint ordering bug where git CLI squash merges list trailers newest-first, causing the oldest transcript to overwrite the newest on disk\\r\\n- Deduplicate sessions by `SessionID` across checkpoints, keeping the most recent transcript\\r\\n\\r\\n## Problem\\r\\n\\r\\nWhen a feature branch with multiple commits (each with its own `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer) is squash-merged, all trailers end up in a single commit message. `entire resume` previously only parsed the first trailer, losing all other sessions.\\r\\n\\r\\nAdditionally, GitHub squash merges list trailers chronologically (oldest first), but git CLI squash merges list them in reverse order (newest first). Since `RestoreLogsOnly` writes session files eagerly, the last checkpoint processed wins on disk — meaning reverse-ordered trailers caused the oldest transcript to overwrite the newest.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Changes\\r\\n\\r\\n**`cmd/entire/cli/trailers/trailers.go`** — Add `ParseAllCheckpoints()` to extract all `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers from a commit message (not just the first).\\r\\n\\r\\n**`cmd/entire/cli/resume.go`** — \\r\\n- Switch from `ParseCheckpoint` (single) to `ParseAllCheckpoints` (multi) throughout `findBranchCheckpoint` and `findCheckpointInHistory`\\r\\n- Change `branchCheckpointResult.checkpointID` → `checkpointIDs []CheckpointID`\\r\\n- Add `resumeMultipleCheckpoints`: reads metadata for all checkpoint IDs, sorts by `CreatedAt` ascending, then restores in order so the newest checkpoint always writes last\\r\\n- Add `deduplicateSessions`: merges sessions across checkpoints, keeping the one with the latest `CreatedAt` when a `SessionID` appears in multiple checkpoints\\r\\n- Extract `displayRestoredSessions` to share session display logic between single and multi-checkpoint paths\\r\\n\\r\\n**`cmd/entire/cli/resume_test.go`** — Add unit tests for `deduplicateSessions` (including three-occurrence staleness edge case), `findCheckpointInHistory` with multiple trailers, `findBranchCheckpoint` with squash merge, and checkpoint timestamp sorting.\\r\\n\\r\\n**`cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/resume_test.go`** — Add integration test simulating a full squash merge workflow: two sessions on a feature branch, squash merge to main, then `entire resume` restoring both sessions.\\r\\n\\r\\n**`cmd/entire/cli/trailers/trailers_test.go`** — Add tests for `ParseAllCheckpoints`.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Caveat: Optimization\\r\\n\\r\\nI thought about optimizing this process by only restoring the very latest checkpoint, but realized that this wouldn't work as expected:\\r\\n\\r\\nA committed checkpoint only contains the sessions that were condensed at that specific commit. When a feature branch is squash merged, Git/GitHub preserves all Entire-Checkpoint trailers from the original commits in the squash commit body. Each trailer points to a different checkpoint on entire/checkpoints/v1, and different checkpoints may contain different sessions.\\r\\n\\r\\nSince there is no single checkpoint that aggregates all sessions from the branch, the resume command must iterate over every checkpoint ID found in the squash commit and restore each one. Sessions are de-duplicated by ID, keeping the entry with the latest CreatedAt.\\r\\n\\r\\nOptimizing by only restoring the latest checkpoint would silently drop any session whose last activity was on an earlier commit.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Test plan\\r\\n\\r\\n- [x] `mise run test:ci` passes (unit + integration)\\r\\n- [x] Integration test `TestResume_SquashMergeMultipleCheckpoints` covers the end-to-end squash merge flow\\r\\n- [x] Unit test `TestResumeMultipleCheckpoints_SortsByCreatedAt` verifies reverse-ordered checkpoints are sorted correctly\\r\\n- [x] Unit tests for `deduplicateSessions` cover no-duplicates, newer-wins, older-loses, three-occurrence, and mixed scenarios\\r\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/534/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/534/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/783\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/783/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/783/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/783/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/783\",\n            \"id\": 4143813730,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7Nt3_5\",\n            \"number\": 783,\n            \"title\": \"Add authenticated API client for trail commands\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"matthiaswenz\",\n              \"id\": 898121,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg5ODEyMQ==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/898121?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/matthiaswenz\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/matthiaswenz\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/matthiaswenz/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/matthiaswenz/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/matthiaswenz/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/matthiaswenz/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/matthiaswenz/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/matthiaswenz/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/matthiaswenz/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/matthiaswenz/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/matthiaswenz/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-03-26T13:14:16Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-26T18:52:09Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-03-26T18:52:07Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/783\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/783\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/783.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/783.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-03-26T18:52:07Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\r\\n- Adds a bearer-token HTTP client (`api/client.go`) that injects the CLI login token into all outgoing API requests via a custom `http.RoundTripper` (currently only used for `/api/trails` routes)\\r\\n- Adds support for private trails API with typed request/response structs for it (`api/trail_types.go`)\\r\\n- Migrates all four trail commands (`list`, `create`, `show`, `update`) from local git storage (`trail.Store`) to the remote trails API at `/api/v1/trails/:host/:owner/:repo`\\r\\n- Exports `strategy.ResolveRemoteRepo()` to extract host/owner/repo from git remotes to figure out the proper parameters for use with the trails API\\r\\n- Removes git-based trail storage from hooks and push:\\r\\n  - Removes checkpoint-trail linking from post-commit hook (API links implicitly by branch name)\\r\\n  - Removes trails branch push from `PrePush` and `PushTrailsBranch()`\\r\\n  - Keeps `TrailsBranchName` constant and `IsShadowBranch` exclusion as safety net for existing repos\\r\\n\\r\\n## Test plan\\r\\n- [ ] Run `entire login` then `entire trail list` against local dev server\\r\\n- [ ] Verify trail CRUD operations work via API (`create`, `update`, show by branch)\\r\\n- [ ] Verify `git push` no longer attempts to push `entire/trails/v1`\\r\\n- [ ] Run `mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci` (passing locally)\\r\\n\\r\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/783/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/783/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/155\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/155/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/155/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/155/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/155\",\n            \"id\": 3900601507,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7BrTdp\",\n            \"number\": 155,\n            \"title\": \"refactor: call a checkpoint a checkpoint\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"khaong\",\n              \"id\": 351934,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTkzNA==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/351934?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/khaong\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-02-05T09:35:35Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-05T09:47:22Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-02-05T09:47:20Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/155\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/155\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/155.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/155.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-02-05T09:47:20Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"while we're here - let's rename the branch to what it actually contains\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Branch-name changes affect where checkpoint metadata is written/read, so existing repos expecting `entire/sessions/v1` may need migration or compatibility handling.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Renames the metadata orphan branch used to store committed checkpoint metadata from `entire/sessions/v1` to **`entire/checkpoints/v1`** by updating `paths.MetadataBranchName`.\\n> \\n> Updates cleanup/shadow-branch logic, CLI tests, and helper scripts (test harness, attribution E2E, and `migrate-sessions.sh`) to reference the new branch name and ensure it remains excluded from shadow-branch cleanup.\\n> \\n> <sup>Written by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot) for commit 4f326978a24a0be124011ad97b30f4208088f61e. This will update automatically on new commits. Configure [here](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/155/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/155/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/572\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/572/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/572/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/572/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/572\",\n            \"id\": 4009199994,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7HOefO\",\n            \"number\": 572,\n            \"title\": \"Remove context.md and scope prompt.txt to checkpoint-only prompts\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"id\": 881031,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-03-02T04:23:42Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-04T22:56:47Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-03-04T22:56:45Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/572\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/572\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/572.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/572.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-03-04T22:56:45Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"Closes #571\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n- **Remove `context.md` entirely** — it was dead code (written during checkpointing but never consumed by any reader). Removes generation, writing, reading, and all test/doc references across 19 files.\\n- **Scope `prompt.txt` to checkpoint-only prompts** — previously stored all session prompts joined by `---`, but every consumer only used the first or last. Now stores only prompts from the current checkpoint portion of the transcript.\\n- Net deletion of **542 lines** of unnecessary code and complexity.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n**context.md removal:**\\n- `generateContextFromPrompts()` function and all callers\\n- `Context` fields from `WriteCommittedOptions`, `UpdateCommittedOptions`, `SessionContent`, `SessionFilePaths`\\n- context.md blob creation/reading in `committed.go`\\n- `createContextFile()` from `lifecycle.go`\\n- `GetSessionContext()` and `getCheckpointsForSession()` (dead code)\\n- context.md fallback in `getSessionDescriptionFromTree()`\\n- `ContextFileName` constant from `paths.go`\\n\\n**prompt.txt scoping:**\\n- Added `extractCheckpointPrompts()` that scopes transcript by agent type (JSONL/Gemini/OpenCode) before extracting prompts\\n- Updated `extractSessionData()` and `extractSessionDataFromLiveTranscript()` to use it\\n- Filesystem path in `lifecycle.go` was already checkpoint-scoped — no change needed\\n\\n**Backward compatibility:**\\n- Old `context.md` files on `entire/checkpoints/v1` are simply ignored (no reader)\\n- Old `prompt.txt` with all-session prompts still works with `ExtractFirstPrompt()`/`extractLastPrompt()`\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] `go build ./...` compiles cleanly\\n- [x] `mise run fmt` — no formatting changes\\n- [x] `mise run test:ci` — all unit + integration tests pass\\n- [x] Manual: `entire explain` on a repo with existing checkpoints (backward compat)\\n- [x] Manual: Create new session, commit, verify no `context.md` on committed branch\\n- [x] Manual: `entire rewind` to verify session labels display correctly\\n\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/572/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/572/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/576\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/576/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/576/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/576/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/576\",\n            \"id\": 4010796990,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7HTqQm\",\n            \"number\": 576,\n            \"title\": \"Add post-file-edit hook for real-time file tracking\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"khaong\",\n              \"id\": 351934,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTkzNA==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/351934?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/khaong\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-03-02T11:37:15Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-02T11:48:43Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-03-02T11:48:43Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": true,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/576\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/576\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/576.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/576.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\n- Add `post-file-edit` hook that fires on every Write/Edit tool call in Claude Code, fixing the orphaned checkpoint bug where `FilesTouched` was only updated at turn boundaries\\n- Track detailed file edit records (path, action, lines added/removed) in append-only JSONL logs per session\\n- Include file edits in checkpoint metadata at condensation time for attribution and analytics\\n- Update session state `FilesTouched` in real-time so PostCommit's overlap check works for mid-turn commits\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n**New types** (`agent/types.go`): `FileEdit` struct, `FileEditAction` type, `CountLines()` helper\\n\\n**JSONL storage** (`session/file_edits.go`): `AppendFileEdit()`, `ReadFileEdits()`, `ClearFileEdits()` on `StateStore`\\n\\n**Hook installation** (`agent/claudecode/hooks.go`): `HookNamePostFileEdit` constant, Write/Edit matchers in `InstallHooks()`\\n\\n**Input parsing** (`hooks_file_edit.go`): `parseFileEditHookInput()` extracts file path and computes line counts from PostToolUse payloads\\n\\n**Handler** (`hooks_claudecode_handlers.go`): `handleClaudeCodePostFileEdit()` normalizes path, appends to JSONL log, merges into `FilesTouched`\\n\\n**Condensation** (`strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`): Loads file edits, passes to `WriteCommitted()`, clears after successful condensation\\n\\n**Checkpoint metadata** (`checkpoint/committed.go`): Writes `file_edits.jsonl` blob to checkpoint tree\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] Unit tests for `CountLines()` and `FileEdit` struct (`agent/types_test.go`)\\n- [x] Unit tests for JSONL append/read/clear operations (`session/file_edits_test.go`)\\n- [x] Unit tests for input parsing of Write and Edit payloads (`hooks_file_edit_test.go`)\\n- [x] Integration test: Write hook updates `FilesTouched` in session state\\n- [x] Integration test: Edit hook creates JSONL log with correct fields\\n- [x] Integration test: Same file edited twice only appears once in `FilesTouched`\\n- [x] All existing tests pass (`mise run test:ci`)\\n- [x] Linter clean (only pre-existing `ireturn` warnings remain)\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/576/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/576/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/595\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/595/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/595/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/595/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/595\",\n            \"id\": 4019872831,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7HxQHe\",\n            \"number\": 595,\n            \"title\": \"Add model tracking for Claude Code and Gemini CLI agents\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"khaong\",\n              \"id\": 351934,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTkzNA==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/351934?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/khaong\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 2,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-03-04T03:51:22Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-05T15:57:35Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-03-05T15:57:34Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/595\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/595\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/595.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/595.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-03-05T15:57:34Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\n- Add `ModelUpdate` event type and cross-process model hint persistence (`.git/entire-sessions/{session_id}.model`) for agents that report the LLM model before SessionState exists\\r\\n- Capture model from Claude Code's `SessionStart` hook payload (`model` field)\\r\\n- Capture model from Gemini CLI's `BeforeModel` hook payload (`llm_request.model` field) via `ModelUpdate` event\\r\\n- **Wire model name through to checkpoint metadata** — `state.ModelName` was captured in SessionState by PR #581 but never flowed through to `CommittedMetadata` / `metadata.json`. This was a gap in the original PR that affected all agents, not just the ones added here.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Design\\r\\n\\r\\n### Model hint file\\r\\n\\r\\nSessionState requires `BaseCommit` (used for shadow branch naming, checkpoint writing, doctor classification) and is only created during `TurnStart`. Claude Code reports the model on `SessionStart` which fires as a separate CLI process before `TurnStart`. A lightweight `.model` hint file bridges this gap — it's written early, read once during `TurnStart` to populate `state.ModelName`, then sits unused until session cleanup.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Checkpoint metadata gap (fix for #581)\\r\\n\\r\\nPR #581 added `ModelName` to `SessionState` and `session.State` but never added a `Model` field to `WriteCommittedOptions` or `CommittedMetadata`. This meant model information was captured per-session but silently dropped during condensation to `entire/checkpoints/v1`. This PR adds the missing `Model` field to the checkpoint pipeline so it appears in `metadata.json`.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Verification\\r\\n\\r\\n**Confirmed model delivery** (Claude Code v2.1.66):\\r\\n- Interactive mode: `\\\"model\\\":\\\"claude-sonnet-4-6\\\"` present in SessionStart payload ✅\\r\\n- Print mode (`-p`): `\\\"model\\\":\\\"\\\"` — Claude Code omits model in non-interactive mode ❌ \\r\\n- E2E interactive test (`TestInteractiveMultiStep`): `\\\"model\\\":\\\"claude-sonnet-4-6\\\"` in logs ✅\\r\\n\\r\\n**Confirmed end-to-end in Gemini CLI E2E** (build `d1ce5026`):\\r\\n- `\\\"model\\\": \\\"gemini-2.5-flash\\\"` in committed `metadata.json` ✅\\r\\n\\r\\n## Test plan\\r\\n\\r\\n- [x] Unit tests pass (`mise run test:ci`)\\r\\n- [x] Gemini CLI E2E: model appears in checkpoint metadata\\r\\n- [x] Claude Code E2E (interactive): model received on SessionStart and persisted to checkpoint metadata\\r\\n\\r\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/595/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/595/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/679\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/679/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/679/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/679/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/679\",\n            \"id\": 4053915555,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7JfgMe\",\n            \"number\": 679,\n            \"title\": \"Add `entire search` command\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"evisdren\",\n              \"id\": 256443556,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD0kEpA\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256443556?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/evisdren\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 5,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-03-10T19:55:22Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-04-02T18:35:48Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-04-02T18:35:47Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/679\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/679\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/679.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/679.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-04-02T18:35:47Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\r\\n- New `entire search` command with hybrid semantic + keyword checkpoint search\\r\\n- Interactive Bubble Tea TUI with alt-screen, pagination, detail cards, and inline search bar\\r\\n- Calls the Entire search service via thin HTTP client (no direct Turbopuffer/OpenAI keys needed)\\r\\n- Auth via `entire login` device flow token, sent as `Bearer` header\\r\\n- Supports `--author`, `--date`, `--branch` flags and inline filter syntax (`author:name date:week branch:main`)\\r\\n- Accessible mode (`ACCESSIBLE=1`) renders static table instead of TUI\\r\\n- JSON output (`--json`) for scripting/agent consumption\\r\\n- Client-side pagination with lazy-fetch fallback for server-side pagination\\r\\n\\r\\n## Features\\r\\n- **Interactive TUI**: Alt-screen with search bar (`/`), j/k navigation, n/p pagination, detail card for selected result\\r\\n- **Filter syntax**: `author:<name>`, `date:<week|month>`, `branch:<name>` — works in CLI args and TUI search bar\\r\\n- **Pagination**: Requests up to 200 results for TUI, paginates client-side at 25/page, with lazy-fetch for additional pages\\r\\n- **Accessible mode**: `ACCESSIBLE=1` requires a query and renders a plain text table\\r\\n- **Multiple output modes**: Interactive TUI (default), static table (accessible), JSON (scripted)\\r\\n\\r\\n## Files\\r\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search/` — search client package (`github.go` for remote parsing, `search.go` for API client + filter parsing)\\r\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search_cmd.go` — Cobra command with flag/inline filter merging\\r\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search_tui.go` — Bubble Tea TUI (model, update, view, pagination, detail cards)\\r\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search_cmd_test.go` — Command-level tests (accessible mode)\\r\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search_tui_test.go` — TUI unit tests (navigation, pagination, fetch-more, filter clearing, view states)\\r\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search/search_test.go` — API client tests (URL construction, params, errors, parsing)\\r\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/root.go` — command registration\\r\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/status_style.go` — shared `isTerminalWriter` helper\\r\\n\\r\\n## Companion PR\\r\\n- Search service: entirehq/entire.io#981\\r\\n\\r\\n## Test plan\\r\\n- [x] `mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci` — all pass\\r\\n- [ ] `entire search \\\"test query\\\"` — returns results in TUI\\r\\n- [ ] `entire search \\\"test\\\" --json` — returns JSON array\\r\\n- [ ] `entire search \\\"test\\\" --author alice --date week --branch main` — filters applied\\r\\n- [ ] `entire search \\\"test author:alice branch:main\\\"` — inline filters extracted from args\\r\\n- [ ] `entire search` — opens TUI with search bar focused\\r\\n- [ ] `ACCESSIBLE=1 entire search \\\"test\\\"` — renders static table\\r\\n- [ ] `ACCESSIBLE=1 entire search` — returns error requiring a query\\r\\n- [ ] TUI: `/` opens search bar, enter searches, esc cancels, n/p pages, q quits\\r\\n- [ ] TUI: new search clears previous filters\\r\\n- [ ] `entire search \\\"test\\\" --json | jq .` — piped output works\\r\\n\\r\\n🤖 Generated with [C\\r\\n<img width=\\\"903\\\" height=\\\"817\\\" alt=\\\"Screenshot 2026-03-31 at 2 54 16 PM\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/725cd424-0728-4db3-ae6e-cc25957c4126\\\" />\\r\\nlaude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\r\\n\\r\\n<img width=\\\"899\\\" height=\\\"571\\\" alt=\\\"Screenshot 2026-03-31 at 2 54 27 PM\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f551cbdb-d83f-4d62-bfc0-aa6a8f4f00eb\\\" />\\r\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Adds a new CLI surface area that makes authenticated HTTP requests using the user’s GitHub token and introduces a sizeable Bubble Tea TUI; failures could impact CLI UX and pagination/filter correctness but are isolated to the new command path.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Introduces a new (currently *hidden*) `entire search` command that queries the Entire search service for checkpoint results, supporting interactive TUI browsing, accessible-mode static output, and `--json` output with client-side pagination.\\n> \\n> Adds a small `search` package for parsing GitHub `origin` remotes, parsing inline filters (`author:`, `date:`, `branch:`, `repo:` including `repo:*`), validating repo scoping semantics, and performing the authenticated `GET /search/v1/search` request.\\n> \\n> Refactors terminal detection in `status_style.go` via a shared `isTerminalWriter` helper, registers the new command in `root.go`, and updates `go.mod` to make Bubble Tea/Bubbles direct dependencies with comprehensive unit tests covering URL construction, error handling, filter parsing, and TUI behavior.\\n> \\n> <sup>Written by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot) for commit 6947c67bc51e0d23d4c6988988eb76422c38e7a2. Configure [here](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/679/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/679/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/772\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/772/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/772/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/772/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/772\",\n            \"id\": 4136224103,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7NYuwZ\",\n            \"number\": 772,\n            \"title\": \"feat: add Codex CLI agent integration\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-03-25T15:16:27Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-27T16:41:15Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-03-27T16:41:13Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/772\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/772\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/772.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/772.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-03-27T16:41:13Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nAdds agent integration for [OpenAI Codex CLI](https://github.com/openai/codex), supporting lifecycle hooks, transcript analysis, token tracking, and prompt extraction.\\n\\n### What's implemented\\n\\n- **Agent package** (`cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/`) with all core + optional interfaces:\\n  - `Agent`, `HookSupport`, `HookResponseWriter` — lifecycle hooks via `.codex/hooks.json`\\n  - `TranscriptAnalyzer` — extracts modified files from `apply_patch` tool calls in rollout JSONL\\n  - `TokenCalculator` — reads cumulative token usage from `event_msg.token_count` entries\\n  - `PromptExtractor` — extracts user prompts from `response_item` messages with `role: \\\"user\\\"`\\n- **Hook events**: SessionStart → `SessionStart`, UserPromptSubmit → `TurnStart`, Stop → `TurnEnd`, PreToolUse → pass-through (no lifecycle action)\\n- **Config setup** (`entire enable --agent codex`):\\n  - `.codex/hooks.json` — per-repo lifecycle hooks\\n  - `.codex/config.toml` — per-repo `features.codex_hooks = true` (feature is still under development in Codex)\\n  - `~/.codex/config.toml` — project trust entry (required for Codex to load project-level config)\\n- **E2E runner** (`e2e/agents/codex.go`) with isolated `CODEX_HOME`, auth symlink, model pinning, startup dialog dismissal\\n- **43 unit tests** across 4 test files\\n- **Research one-pager** at `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/AGENT.md`\\n\\n### What's missing (blocked on Codex side)\\n\\n| Gap | Reason | Impact |\\n|-----|--------|--------|\\n| **No SessionEnd hook** | Codex doesn't fire a hook when a session terminates, only at end-of-turn (Stop) | Framework handles gracefully — session cleanup is less precise but functional |\\n| **PostToolUse** | PR still in review on Codex side | Can't track tool outputs; no SubagentAwareExtractor possible yet |\\n| **No subagent hooks** | No PreTask/PostTask equivalent | Can't track spawned subagents |\\n| **`codex_hooks` feature flag** | Default off (stage: UnderDevelopment) | `entire enable` writes it to project config + trusts the project, but if the feature graduates to stable this config becomes unnecessary |\\n| **PreToolUse is shell-only** | Only fires for Bash tool, not MCP/other tools | File modification detection relies on transcript parsing (apply_patch), not hooks |\\n| **TranscriptPreparer** | Not needed — Codex materializes rollout before firing hooks | Confirmed by reading `hook_transcript_path()` → `ensure_rollout_materialized()` in Codex source |\\n| **TextGenerator** | No `codex --print` equivalent | Can't generate AI-powered metadata (trail titles, summaries) |\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [ ] `mise run test` — all unit tests pass (43 new tests)\\n- [ ] `mise run lint` — clean (only pre-existing ireturn issues in capabilities.go)\\n- [ ] `mise run test:e2e --agent codex TestSingleSessionManualCommit` — hooks fire, checkpoint created\\n- [ ] `mise run test:e2e --agent codex TestInteractiveMultiStep` — interactive session with prompt pattern `›`\\n- [ ] `mise run test:e2e:canary` — Vogon canary unaffected\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Adds a new built-in agent integration that installs hooks and writes Codex config/trust entries (including in `~/.codex/config.toml`), which could affect local developer environments if the install/uninstall logic is wrong.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds a new built-in `codex` agent integration with lifecycle hook handling, transcript parsing, token usage calculation, and prompt extraction based on Codex JSONL rollout files.\\n> \\n> Implements hook installation/uninstallation for `.codex/hooks.json`, plus automatic enabling of Codex’s `codex_hooks` feature in project `.codex/config.toml` and adding a per-repo trust entry to the user’s `~/.codex/config.toml`. Registers the new agent in the registry/CLI imports, adds Codex-specific E2E harness support, and includes a Codex integration one-pager and unit tests covering hooks, lifecycle parsing, and transcript analysis.\\n> \\n> <sup>Written by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot) for commit 81d10dc5f65433be75199a5c2833c418125540f2. Configure [here](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/772/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/772/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/162\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/162/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/162/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/162/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/162\",\n            \"id\": 3904681441,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7B46Eg\",\n            \"number\": 162,\n            \"title\": \"Skip checkpoint on /quit\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T03:31:36Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-10T06:11:58Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-02-10T06:11:57Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/162\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/162\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/162.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/162.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-02-10T06:11:57Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Behavior change is narrowly scoped to the Gemini `session-end` hook and mainly removes side-effectful git/metadata operations, reducing the chance of unexpected commits at exit.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Gemini CLI’s `session-end` hook is simplified to *stop creating a fallback checkpoint/commit* on explicit exit; it now only parses the session-end input and calls `markSessionEnded(sessionID)`.\\n> \\n> This removes the default-branch skip gate and the prior best-effort flow that created session metadata and attempted `commitGeminiSession`, shifting condensation/checkpoint triggering to subsequent git hooks for ended sessions.\\n> \\n> <sup>Written by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot) for commit 5f5f045c8e9e8f5217cbc001126469a89d6c7b70. This will update automatically on new commits. Configure [here](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/162/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/162/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/634\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/634/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/634/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/634/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/634\",\n            \"id\": 4032435528,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7IaQbt\",\n            \"number\": 634,\n            \"title\": \"feat: add TokenCalculator for Copilot CLI agent\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-03-06T06:05:51Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-06T13:21:10Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-03-06T13:21:07Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/634\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/634\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/634.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/634.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-03-06T13:21:07Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": null,\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/634/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/634/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/323\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/323/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/323/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/323/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/323\",\n            \"id\": 3936999349,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7DjCvw\",\n            \"number\": 323,\n            \"title\": \"fix: subagent file modifications invisible to checkpoint detection (ENT-297)\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"khaong\",\n              \"id\": 351934,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTkzNA==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/351934?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/khaong\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 2,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-02-13T12:42:10Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-16T01:38:19Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-02-16T01:38:17Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/323\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/323\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/323.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/323.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-02-16T01:38:17Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nFixes subagent file modifications being invisible to checkpoint detection. When Claude Code delegates work to subagents via the Task tool, file changes made by those subagents were not tracked, causing:\\n- Missing checkpoints at Stop (subagent-only changes → `totalChanges=0`)\\n- Missing checkpoint trailers on mid-session commits\\n- Incomplete file lists in condensed checkpoint metadata\\n- Failed PostCommit condensation for mid-subagent commits (transcript data unavailable)\\n\\n### Changes\\n\\n- **`ExtractAllModifiedFiles()`** — new function that scans both main and subagent transcripts (`agent-<id>.jsonl`) for Write/Edit/NotebookEdit tool calls\\n- **Stop hook** — uses `ExtractAllModifiedFiles` so checkpoints aren't skipped when only subagents modify files\\n- **`sessionHasNewContentFromLiveTranscript`** — augmented with subagent transcript scanning for mid-session commit detection\\n- **Shared helper `extractModifiedFilesFromLiveTranscript`** — consolidates 3 duplicated code blocks (main transcript extraction + subagent augmentation + path normalization)\\n- **`extractSessionDataFromLiveTranscript`** — uses shared helper so condensed checkpoints include subagent files\\n- **PostCommit ACTIVE sessions** — trusts PrepareCommitMsg's trailer validation instead of re-analyzing transcripts (unreliable when subagents are still running at commit time)\\n- **Removed `sessionHasNewContentInCommittedFiles`** — now unused after the PostCommit simplification\\n\\n### Key insight\\n\\nAt PostCommit time during a mid-subagent commit, subagent transcript data is unavailable: the main transcript has no `tool_result` with `agentId:` yet, and subagent files may still be in-flight. Since PrepareCommitMsg already validates the trailer (unconditionally for no-TTY/agent commits, via content detection for TTY/human commits), PostCommit trusts that decision for ACTIVE sessions rather than re-validating.\\n\\nFixes [ENT-297](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/ENT-297)\\n\\n## Test plan\\n- [x] Unit tests for `ExtractAllModifiedFiles` (4 cases: includes subagent files, deduplicates, no subagents, subagent-only changes)\\n- [x] Unit test for `sessionHasNewContentFromLiveTranscript` with subagent-only modifications\\n- [x] Unit test for PostCommit ACTIVE session always condensing\\n- [x] Integration test `TestHookRunner_SimulateStop_SubagentOnlyChanges` (both strategies)\\n- [x] Manual test: subagent commit → trailer added → checkpoint created\\n- [x] Full CI suite passes (`mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci`)\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/323/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/323/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/705\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/705/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/705/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/705/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/705\",\n            \"id\": 4083943897,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7K_yRL\",\n            \"number\": 705,\n            \"title\": \"Fallback to script parsing if prompt wasn't available through hooks\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-03-16T17:55:43Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-17T10:55:52Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-03-17T10:55:50Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/705\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/705\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/705.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/705.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-03-17T10:55:50Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"The E2E tests are currently failing for Factory AI Droid because the tests assumes an extracted prompt but using `droid exec` will not trigger `UserPromptSubmit` which means we got no prompt. This meant so far an empty prompt was stored. \\r\\n\\r\\nIf we now have no prompt.txt at the end of the turn we fallback to session transcript parsing to extract the prompt.\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/705/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/705/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/654\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/654/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/654/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/654/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/654\",\n            \"id\": 4036844274,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7Iov3D\",\n            \"number\": 654,\n            \"title\": \"Fix cursor-cli E2E flakiness\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"alishakawaguchi\",\n              \"id\": 6415609,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTU2MDk=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6415609?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/alishakawaguchi\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/foll