                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/skills/pulls/9\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/skills/pull/9\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/skills/pull/9.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/skills/pull/9.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Demo\\r\\nhttps://cleanshot.com/share/gyyrckRg\\r\\n\\r\\n## Summary\\r\\n- Introduce a new `code-tour` skill that gives developers an architectural overview, recent agent activity, hot files, and key contributors when joining or returning to a repo\\r\\n- Iterate on diagrams (Mermaid) — keep them focused on walkthroughs and tighten layout\\r\\n- Fix frontmatter YAML and remove unused contributor drill-in prompts\\r\\n\\r\\n## Test plan\\r\\n- [ ] Invoke skill via trigger phrases (\\\"give me a repo overview\\\", \\\"onboard me\\\")\\r\\n- [ ] Verify Mermaid diagrams render correctly\\r\\n- [ ] Verify frontmatter parses cleanly\\r\\n\\r\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\r\\n\\r\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n> [!NOTE]\\r\\n> **Low Risk**\\r\\n> Documentation/metadata-only changes plus a new skill spec; no runtime code paths or data/security-sensitive logic are modified.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> **Overview**\\r\\n> Introduces a new `code-tour` skill that guides repo onboarding by combining git-derived architecture/churn signals with recent Entire activity (`entire dispatch`), focused checkpoint searches (`entire search`), and optional drill-down via `entire explain`, including explicit preflight/auth failure behavior.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> Updates `README.md` to document `code-tour` and add onboarding trigger examples, and bumps version numbers from `0.3.0` to `0.4.0` across plugin manifests and `package.json`.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit f28a1eccc446c9e5849b404925f139bfb2686c24. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\r\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/skills/issues/9/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/skills/issues/9/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            }\n          ],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e17-replacement\",\n      \"q\": \"repo:entireio/cli \\\"checkpoint\\\" \\\"diff\\\"\",\n      \"rr\": [\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 20,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2398\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2398/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2398/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2398/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2398\",\n              \"id\": 5439399001,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABRDakWQ\",\n              \"number\": 2398,\n              \"title\": \"Checkpoint linking fails for non-ASCII filenames\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"ChetanReddyC\",\n                \"id\": 135294504,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOCBBuKA\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135294504?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/ChetanReddyC\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [\n                {\n                  \"id\": 9924477887,\n                  \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACT4uDvw\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/bug\",\n                  \"name\": \"bug\",\n                  \"color\": \"d73a4a\",\n                  \"default\": true,\n                  \"description\": \"Something isn't working\",\n                  \"archived_at\": null,\n                  \"archived_by\": null\n                }\n              ],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 2,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-13T10:01:02Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-13T11:08:07Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"### What happened?\\n\\nIn the interactive/default prompt-mode commit-linking path, `getStagedFiles` runs `git diff --cached --name-only` without `-z` and treats the newline-delimited output as literal repository paths.\\n\\nGit quotes and C-escapes unusual pathnames in this output mode. For example, with the default `core.quotePath=true`, `café.go` is emitted as `\\\"caf\\\\303\\\\251.go\\\"`. Entire then exact-compares that display string with the literal `café.go` stored in `SessionState.FilesTouched`. The comparison fails, so a related commit can be classified as containing no agent work and receive no `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer.\\n\\nI reproduced this against current `main` using a focused exact-source test. An ASCII control received its trailer, while an otherwise equivalent UTF-8 canary did not. Parsing the same Git output with `-z` restored the literal path and the expected overlap.\\n\\nThe affected Git commit itself is still created. The demonstrated impact is missing commit-to-session linkage and incomplete provenance, including potentially incomplete `entire explain` attribution. I did not observe source loss, transcript deletion, remote checkpoint loss, or a security boundary violation.\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\n1. Use the default `core.quotePath=true` setting and default prompt-mode commit linking in an interactive terminal.\\n2. Start an agent session that records only a non-ASCII file such as `café.go` in `FilesTouched`, with no pending task record that would bypass overlap detection.\\n3. Stage that file and make a manual commit:\\n\\n   ```bash\\n   git config core.quotePath true\\n   git add \\\"café.go\\\"\\n   git diff --cached --name-only\\n   git commit -m \\\"update localized file\\\"\\n   ```\\n\\n4. Inspect the commit message.\\n\\nExpected: the related session is detected and an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer is added.\\n\\nActual: Git's quoted display path does not match the literal `FilesTouched` path, the session is excluded, and the trailer is omitted.\\n\\nFocused control/canary output:\\n\\n```text\\nASCII control.go:\\n  literal_match=true overlap=true\\n  NUL-delimited path=\\\"control.go\\\"\\n  checkpoint_trailer=true\\n\\nUTF-8 café.go:\\n  getStagedFiles returned Git's quoted C-escaped display path\\n  literal_match=false overlap=false\\n  NUL-delimited path=\\\"café.go\\\"\\n  checkpoint_trailer=false\\n```\\n\\nThe focused test passed once and then passed three consecutive repeat runs.\\n\\n### Entire CLI version\\n\\nv0.10.6\\n\\n### OS and architecture\\n\\nWindows 11 amd64 (build 26200.9445)\\n\\n### Agent\\n\\nCodex\\n\\n### Terminal\\n\\nCodex integrated terminal, PowerShell 7.6.5\\n\\n### Logs / debug output\\n\\n```bash\\ngetStagedFiles(\\\"control.go\\\") = [\\\"control.go\\\"]\\nliteral_match=true overlap=true\\ncheckpoint_trailer=true\\n\\ngetStagedFiles(\\\"café.go\\\") = [Git quoted C-escaped display path]\\nliteral_match=false overlap=false\\ncheckpoint_trailer=false\\n```\\n\\n### Additional context\\n\\n_No response_\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2398/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2398/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3011\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3011/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3011/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3011/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/3011\",\n              \"id\": 6206060692,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABcej4lA\",\n              \"number\": 3011,\n              \"title\": \"Sessions in a shared checkout claim every dirty tracked file, so idle and ended sessions land on unrelated commits\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"mattjes\",\n                \"id\": 79668769,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NjY4NzY5\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79668769?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mattjes\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/mattjes\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mattjes/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mattjes/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mattjes/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mattjes/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mattjes/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mattjes/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mattjes/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mattjes/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mattjes/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 7,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-04T15:39:47Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-07T04:47:17Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"> **AI disclosure:** this issue was investigated and written by Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic model `claude-opus-5-5`), running in Claude Code, on behalf of the owner of this GitHub account, who approved posting it. \\\"We\\\" below means the two of us. The reproduction was run by the model, as described under Steps to reproduce.\\n\\n### What happened?\\n\\nWhen several agent sessions work in one worktree, each session records every file `git status` reports as modified at its turn end, including files it never touched and files that were dirty before it started. Those files then count as the session's own work:\\n\\n- A commit of another session's file condenses this session into its checkpoint.\\n- Whatever is left carries forward, so the session keeps joining later commits, even after it has ended, until everything it recorded has been committed.\\n- `entire checkpoint explain` can then show the wrong session's prompt as the commit's intent, with a transcript about a different file.\\n\\nExpected: a session is linked to a commit when it changed a file in that commit. `sessions-and-checkpoints.md` describes `FilesTouched` as \\\"files modified, created, or deleted by the session\\\" and says a commit condenses \\\"every session whose touched files overlap the commit\\\". A session that only read files touched none of them.\\n\\nThis is not the documented \\\"Concurrent ACTIVE Sessions May Produce Spurious Checkpoints\\\" limitation. That one covers ACTIVE sessions and entries with minimal content. This happens with IDLE and ENDED sessions, and the checkpoint carries the session's full prompt and transcript.\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\nRun with the real binary and installed git hooks, sending Claude Code hook events to `entire hooks claude-code <event>` with a simulated transcript. No remote, telemetry off.\\n\\n1. `git init`, commit files `a.txt` and `b.txt`, `entire enable --local --agent claude-code`.\\n2. Start sessions A and B. Both get a prompt, so their turns overlap.\\n3. A edits `a.txt`, B edits `b.txt`. Each transcript shows only its own Edit.\\n4. Both Stop. Session state: A and B each have `files_touched: [a.txt, b.txt]`.\\n5. `git add a.txt && git commit`, with no TTY. The checkpoint holds A and B.\\n6. `git add b.txt && git commit`. The checkpoint holds A and B again.\\n7. `entire checkpoint explain <checkpoint of step 5>`: Intent is B's prompt, and the transcript shows the edit to `b.txt`.\\n\\n| Run | Commit | Sessions on the checkpoint |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| Both sessions, shared dirty copy | `a.txt`, then `b.txt` | A+B, A+B |\\n| Same, but A commits mid-turn from its own shell | `a.txt` | A+B (`explain` shows A's prompt here; B is still on the checkpoint) |\\n| Sequential turns, A stopped before `b.txt` was dirty | `a.txt`, then `b.txt` | A+B, B |\\n| Control: copy clean between the sessions | `a.txt`, then `b.txt` | A, B |\\n| Control: separate worktrees | `a.txt` | A |\\n| Read-only session, tracked file dirty before it started | that file | that session |\\n| Same, with an untracked file (has a baseline) | that file | no trailer |\\n| Read-only session, ended, three files dirty | each in turn | that session, until all three are committed |\\n| Same, after they are committed | an unrelated file | no trailer |\\n\\nSame results on the default `commit_linking` and on `always`, and on the latest nightly.\\n\\n### Entire CLI version\\n\\n0.12.2, and 0.12.3-nightly.202611040616.9dcc30a11. The code below is unchanged on `main`.\\n\\n### OS and architecture\\n\\nWindows 11, amd64. Not run on Linux or macOS. From reading the code, the \\\"foreign session\\\" check from #2668 would not stop this there either: over-claimed files are real overlap to it.\\n\\n### Agent\\n\\nClaude Code\\n\\n### Additional context\\n\\nCause: the fallback in `handleLifecycleTurnEnd` (`lifecycle.go`) merges all of `changes.Modified` into the turn's files. Untracked files have a prompt-start baseline, but tracked files don't. `filesOverlapWithContent` counts any modified file by name, and `filesWithRemainingAgentChanges` keeps what wasn't committed.\\n\\nThe fallback has a job: `git status` is how shell edits to tracked files are seen (#2720), so it can't simply go. Possible direction, for you to judge:\\n\\n1. Record dirty tracked files at prompt start and ignore unchanged ones at turn end. #2278 did this, and was closed by its author ten minutes after opening, with no review. The stat data from #2720 might serve as the baseline without extra hashing.\\n2. A baseline doesn't cover overlapping turns, as #2278 says itself. For that, a file known only from `git status` could be skipped if another session in the worktree recorded it, similar to `unrecordedNewFilesSinceLaunch`. The subagent path already avoids a whole-worktree diff for this reason.\\n\\nKNOWN_LIMITATIONS gives separate worktrees as the workaround, and they do avoid this, as the control above shows. A shared worktree is still a useful setup when sessions work on different files, because nothing has to be merged afterwards, so we'd like to keep it if attribution can be made right there. If worktrees are the intended answer, that entry could say the effect also covers IDLE and ENDED sessions and isn't only cosmetic, since `explain` can show another session's prompt and transcript as a commit's intent.\\n\\nIf one of these directions suits you, we're happy to open a PR once you've had a look.\\n\\nRelated: #2278, #2612, #2617, #2668, #2720, #1118.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3011/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3011/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/763\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/763/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/763/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/763/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/763\",\n              \"id\": 4126107126,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M7172X2\",\n              \"number\": 763,\n              \"title\": \"Feature request: Pre-flight knowledge context in checkpoints\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"totto\",\n                \"id\": 842543,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg0MjU0Mw==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/842543?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/totto\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/totto\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/totto/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/totto/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/totto/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/totto/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/totto/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/totto/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/totto/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/totto/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/totto/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [\n                {\n                  \"id\": 9924477906,\n                  \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACT4uD0g\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/enhancement\",\n                  \"name\": \"enhancement\",\n                  \"color\": \"a2eeef\",\n                  \"default\": true,\n                  \"description\": \"New feature or request\",\n                  \"archived_at\": null,\n                  \"archived_by\": null\n                }\n              ],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-03-24T08:27:44Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-16T14:35:55Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Problem\\n\\nCheckpoints does an excellent job recording what the agent thought and decided — prompts, transcripts, tool calls, reasoning. But it currently doesn't capture *what the agent knew before execution*: the structured knowledge context that was available at the time.\\n\\nFor audit and compliance purposes, the complete record should answer three questions:\\n\\n1. What knowledge was the agent operating from? *(knowledge available)*\\n2. What did it decide and do? *(reasoning applied — this is what Checkpoints records today)*\\n3. What code did it produce? *(git diff)*\\n\\nQuestion 1 is currently missing.\\n\\n## The missing layer: pre-flight knowledge context\\n\\nWhen agents run with structured knowledge systems — like [KCP (Knowledge Context Protocol)](https://github.com/Cantara/knowledge-context-protocol) — the agent loads a scoped set of knowledge manifests before execution: architecture decisions, coding standards, governance rules, suppression constraints, role-specific context. This is the structured briefing the agent operates from.\\n\\nIf a compliance auditor asks *\\\"did this agent have access to the correct governance rules when it wrote this code?\\\"*, the answer lives in the knowledge manifest state, not in the reasoning trace. These are different layers.\\n\\n## Proposed addition\\n\\nAdd an optional metadata field to checkpoint records for knowledge context — whatever structured context was loaded before the session started. At minimum, this could be:\\n\\n- A snapshot of loaded manifest IDs + versions (e.g., a KCP `kcp_knowledge_map.yaml` state at session start)\\n- A content hash of the knowledge context\\n- Or simply: a `knowledge_context_file` config option that Entire reads and appends to checkpoint metadata\\n\\nFor KCP specifically, the manifest is compact — a `version`, a `load_strategy`, and references to in-scope knowledge units. It fits naturally alongside prompt/transcript metadata.\\n\\n## Why this matters\\n\\nA checkpoint that includes knowledge state becomes a complete audit record:\\n\\n- **Was the agent operating with the right context?** (governance, access, version)\\n- **Did applicable constraints apply?** (scope rules, suppression, load strategy)\\n- **Root cause separation:** If the generated code is wrong, is it because the agent reasoned incorrectly (visible in transcript) or because it lacked the right knowledge (visible in manifest state)? These are different failure modes with different remediation paths.\\n\\nClaude Code is already a supported integration. KCP manifests are how many Claude Code-based workflows structure agent context. Capturing that state at checkpoint time closes the loop between \\\"what the agent was given\\\" and \\\"what the agent produced.\\\"\\n\\nHappy to elaborate on the manifest format or sketch an integration approach.\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/763/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 1,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 1\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/763/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2653\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2653/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2653/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2653/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2653\",\n              \"id\": 5702435644,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABU-RDPA\",\n              \"number\": 2653,\n              \"title\": \"Background subagent's lines are attributed to the human when the parent commits in the same turn\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"RussellEstcourt\",\n                \"id\": 15103702,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTAzNzAy\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15103702?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/RussellEstcourt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/RussellEstcourt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/RussellEstcourt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/RussellEstcourt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/RussellEstcourt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/RussellEstcourt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/RussellEstcourt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/RussellEstcourt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/RussellEstcourt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/RussellEstcourt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/RussellEstcourt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 4,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-04T19:14:49Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-06T17:01:00Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nOn nightly `0.11.4-nightly.202610040807.f3f598a47`, a background Claude Code subagent is now captured correctly: the checkpoint stores `tasks/<tool_use_id>/task.json`, the child transcript and the file linkage. That part of #2215 is fixed for this case.\\n\\nLine attribution is still wrong in one ordinary ordering. If the parent commits in the same turn in which the child finished, the child's lines are attributed to the human. If the parent's turn ends between the child finishing and the commit, attribution is correct.\\n\\nNothing errors, and `entire checkpoint explain` does not show attribution, so the fault is only visible in the checkpoint's `metadata.json`.\\n\\n## Versions\\n\\n- Entire CLI `0.11.4-nightly.202610040807.f3f598a47` (official `entire_darwin_arm64.tar.gz`, checksum verified), go1.27.1, darwin/arm64\\n- Claude Code 2.1.289\\n- Stock hooks from `entire enable --agent claude-code --telemetry=false --skip-push-sessions --absolute-git-hook-path`; `git-refs` checkpoint backend; `manual-commit` strategy; no remote\\n- Both checkpoints record this nightly as `cli_version`\\n\\n## Reproduction\\n\\n1. Create a fresh repository with no remote. Commit one text file.\\n2. Run `entire enable --agent claude-code` and commit the configuration.\\n3. Start a fresh Claude Code session in the repository.\\n4. Ask the parent to launch one ordinary `Agent` child (`general-purpose`, no `run_in_background`) that appends one line to the tracked file. The launch returns `status: \\\"async_launched\\\"`.\\n5. Have the parent keep working in the same turn while the child runs, for example with other tool calls, so that the completion notification arrives mid-turn.\\n6. Still in that turn, commit the file.\\n7. Read `0/metadata.json` from the checkpoint ref.\\n\\nTo see the passing ordering, let the parent end its turn after step 4 and commit after the completion notification starts a new turn.\\n\\n## Expected\\n\\nThe child's line is attributed to the agent in both orderings: `agent_lines: 1`, `agent_percentage: 100`.\\n\\n## Actual\\n\\nTwo runs in the same fixture, same binary, same prompt. Each used one child that appended one line to `notes.txt`. Both launches were `async_launched`.\\n\\n| | Run 1 | Run 2 |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| Parent `stop` hook between child completion and commit | Yes | No |\\n| Checkpoint | `01M443QWZB119XGHSB6X00VD48` | `01M4443V6VAZS9TVXEMBPKAF70` |\\n| `task.json`, child transcript, `files: [\\\"notes.txt\\\"]` | Present | Present |\\n| `initial_attribution.agent_lines` | 1 | 0 |\\n| `initial_attribution.total_committed` | 1 | 0 |\\n| `initial_attribution.agent_percentage` | 100 | 0 |\\n| `prompt_attributions` | `agent_lines_added: 1` | `user_lines_added: 1`, `user_added_per_file: {\\\"notes.txt\\\": 1}` |\\n\\nIn run 2 the parent made two `WebFetch` calls while the child ran. The completion notification was queued and delivered mid-turn, and the commit followed in the same turn.\\n\\nLog excerpts are from `.entire/logs/entire.log` with `ENTIRE_LOG_LEVEL=debug`, trimmed to the relevant fields. Times are local (UTC+1).\\n\\n### Log, run 1 (correct)\\n\\n```\\n19:44:47.540 background subagent launch detected; deferring capture to subagent-stop  tool_use_id=toolu_01BTtziYVbpBWzdHaFv5XpLK agent_id=ab5096f9dc0aee0f3\\n19:44:56.102 subagent completed  tool_use_id=toolu_01BTtziYVbpBWzdHaFv5XpLK agent_id=ab5096f9dc0aee0f3\\n19:44:56.861 hook invoked  hook=stop\\n19:44:58.003 created shadow branch and committed changes  shadow_branch=entire/8bfb4cc-e3b0c4\\n19:45:09.372 post-commit: HandleCondense decision  task_records=1 should_condense=true shadow_branch=entire/8bfb4cc-e3b0c4\\n19:45:10.051 prompt attribution data  checkpoint=2 user_added=0 agent_added=1\\n19:45:10.058 attribution calculated  agent_lines=1 human_added=0 total_committed=1 agent_percentage=100 accumulated_user_added=0\\n```\\n\\n### Log, run 2 (wrong)\\n\\n```\\n19:51:12.827 background subagent launch detected; deferring capture to subagent-stop  tool_use_id=toolu_01H6vmVi8tbMXucnVqUGoe6z agent_id=aec7d03cbf26bf858\\n19:51:24.282 subagent completed  tool_use_id=toolu_01H6vmVi8tbMXucnVqUGoe6z agent_id=aec7d03cbf26bf858\\n             (no stop hook before the commit)\\n19:51:40.778 post-commit: HandleCondense decision  task_records=1 should_condense=true shadow_branch=entire/3130281-e3b0c4\\n19:51:41.459 attribution: using HEAD as shadow (no shadow branch)\\n19:51:41.459 prompt attribution data  checkpoint=1 user_added=1 agent_added=0\\n19:51:41.465 attribution calculated  agent_lines=0 human_added=0 total_committed=0 agent_percentage=0 accumulated_user_added=1\\n19:51:41.492 filesWithRemainingAgentChanges: shadow branch not found, falling back to file subtraction  branch=entire/3130281-e3b0c4 error=\\\"reference not found\\\"\\n```\\n\\n## Likely cause\\n\\nThis is a reading of the logs above, not confirmed in the source.\\n\\n`subagent-stop` records the task and transcript but does not appear to snapshot the working tree. The shadow branch is only created by the parent's `stop` hook. When the commit lands before any `stop`, attribution falls back to HEAD as the shadow, and the child's edit, which the parent never made through its own tools, is counted as a user change.\\n\\nAt condensation in run 2, Entire already had what it needed: `task_records=1`, and that task's `files` lists `notes.txt`.\\n\\n## Scope and limits\\n\\n- One run for each ordering, on macOS arm64 only.\\n- The two runs used different Claude config directories. The log lines point at the turn boundary, but I have not isolated that variable.\\n- Not tested: foreground children, read-only children, `SendMessage` continuations, nested agents, or more than one child.\\n- The parent ending its turn or not while a background child runs is model behaviour, so the same prompt can produce either ordering.\\n\\nRelated: #2215, #2556.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2653/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2653/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2979\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2979/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2979/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2979/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2979\",\n              \"id\": 6110447963,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABbDYJWw\",\n              \"number\": 2979,\n              \"title\": \"Sibling-worktree commit linking picks a session idle for days; every commit from another worktree then condenses its multi-GB transcript (Windows freeze, dangling trailers)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"lcv-leo\",\n                \"id\": 268063598,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD_pTbg\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/268063598?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/lcv-leo\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-29T23:44:04Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-04T00:13:13Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"### Summary\\n\\nCommits made from a worktree that has no Entire session of its own are linked, by the sibling-worktree fallback in `strategy.resolveWorktreeCandidates`, to a session homed in **another** worktree even when that session has been idle for more than a day. `prepare-commit-msg` stamps an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer for that foreign session and `post-commit` then condenses it, which reads and parses its whole transcript. With the 5.47 GB Codex rollout from #2933 that means every commit made by anyone, from any worktree of the repository, reads 5.2 GB, saturates a core and grows the process to 16 GB and beyond, freezing a 31 GB workstation. The 15-minute `recentSessionWindow` liveness filter that already exists in that function is applied only when candidates span several worktrees; a lone idle session from a single sibling worktree is linked unconditionally.\\n\\nRelated: #2933 (cost of condensing a huge rollout; same session, opened by me on 28/10), #2926 / #2972 (the Windows console patch also present in the build below).\\n\\n### Environment\\n\\n- Entire CLI `0.12.2-lcv.windows-console.1` = v0.12.2 (`c4f103d8`) + the patch from #2926; Go 1.27.3; windows/amd64.\\n- Windows 11 build 26300, 31.4 GB RAM, 24 logical cores; Git for Windows; commits made from a PowerShell terminal, not by the agent.\\n- Repository with several linked worktrees sharing one git common dir. `.entire/settings.json`: `commit_linking: \\\"always\\\"`, checkpoints primary `git-refs`, PII redaction on, OPF off.\\n- Session store (`.git/entire-sessions`): one Codex session homed in worktree A (phase `idle`, `last_interaction_time` 2026-10-28T09:35-03:00, `token_transcript_start` 185129, rollout 5,473,224,925 bytes) and one ended Codex session with `checkpoint_count` 0. No session homed in worktree B, where the commits were made.\\n\\n### What happened\\n\\n1. Four commits made from worktree B on 2026-10-29 (17:59, 18:07, 18:22, 18:44 BRT) each got an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer from `prepare-commit-msg` in about 0.15 s. The log shows the stamp; nothing selected the Codex session except the fallback.\\n2. `post-commit` (`entire hooks git post-commit 2>/dev/null || true`, synchronous) never finished within the terminal runner's deadline. The runner killed the shell; `entire.exe` survived as an orphan, still reading and parsing the rollout.\\n3. None of the four checkpoints exists locally (`git for-each-ref refs/entire/` lists only the three refs from 27–28/10), so the four trailers dangle, exactly as in #2933 step 4.\\n4. While the orphans were alive, a `git push` whose `pre-push` hook normally takes 3–4 s appeared hung for over an hour (the machine was thrashing). After the orphans were killed the next push took 3 s. `entire hooks git pre-push origin` run on its own completes in 4.2 s; I found no lock contention in the pre-push path, so the hang is a symptom of the memory pressure, not a separate bug.\\n5. Because the logger is buffered (`cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go`, `bufio.Writer`, flushed at exit), a killed hook leaves **no** log line at all: the worktree log has the `prepare-commit-msg` and `commit-msg` lines for each commit and nothing for `post-commit`. That made the diagnosis slower than it should have been and is worth a note of its own.\\n\\n### Measurement (before the fix)\\n\\n`entire hooks git post-commit` run directly in worktree B on the HEAD carrying the dangling trailer, sampled with `Win32_Process` every ~4 s, killed at 30 s before any write (ref count unchanged):\\n\\n```\\n  4.5s cpu=  2.9s thr=21 ws= 3,111 MB read= 2,048 MB\\n  8.9s cpu=  7.0s thr=21 ws= 6,611 MB read= 5,220 MB\\n 13.2s cpu= 11.3s thr=21 ws=10,487 MB read= 5,220 MB\\n 21.4s cpu= 19.4s thr=21 ws=12,977 MB read= 5,220 MB\\n 30.1s cpu= 27.6s thr=21 ws=16,032 MB read= 5,220 MB   (still growing; no child process)\\n```\\n\\nThe whole rollout is read by `codex.ReadSession` (`os.ReadFile`, then `parseSessionStartTime` → `splitJSONL`, then `splitJSONL` again with `json.Unmarshal` per line). That cost is #2933's subject; this issue is about **why a commit from another worktree pays it at all**.\\n\\n### Cause in the code (v0.12.2)\\n\\n`cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_session.go`:\\n\\n- `findSessionsForWorktreeFromStates` (line 358): no exact home for worktree B → collects sessions whose `WorktreePath` resolves to the same common dir (or a parent worktree) → `resolveWorktreeCandidates`.\\n- `resolveWorktreeCandidates` (line 425): `sessionsFromSingleWorktree(candidates)` returns before the liveness filter, so when all candidates come from one worktree they are linked regardless of `LastInteractionTime`. The `recentSessionWindow` cutoff (15 min, documented right above as \\\"one idle for days is not [plausibly the session being committed]\\\") is only applied in the multi-worktree tie-break.\\n- `findSessionsForCommitLinking` (`session_identity.go:37`) only discards fallback sessions when `findSessionByCommitAncestry` identifies the committer; a terminal commit has no agent ancestor, so the fallback result stands.\\n\\n### Fix applied locally and verified\\n\\nApply the existing window inside the single-worktree branch of `resolveWorktreeCandidates`, before it links: a candidate homed in another worktree is declined when its recorded `LastInteractionTime` is older than `recentSessionWindow`; a candidate with no recorded interaction is kept (idleness unknown); each declined session is logged at Info with how long it had been idle. The multi-worktree branch is untouched: it already requires a recent interaction and keeps the ambiguity warning and stderr hint when none qualifies. Diff:\\n\\n```diff\\n--- a/cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_session.go\\n+++ b/cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_session.go\\n@@ -426,10 +426,22 @@ func resolveWorktreeCandidates(ctx context.Context, worktreePath string, candida\\n \\tif len(candidates) == 0 {\\n \\t\\treturn nil, false\\n \\t}\\n+\\tcutoff := time.Now().Add(-recentSessionWindow)\\n \\tif matches := sessionsFromSingleWorktree(candidates); matches != nil {\\n-\\t\\treturn matches, false\\n+\\t\\t// Every candidate here is homed in some other worktree (an exact home\\n+\\t\\t// match returns before this fallback runs), so the liveness window\\n+\\t\\t// above applies here too, not only to the multi-worktree tie-break\\n+\\t\\t// below. Without this, a lone session that sat idle for a day in a\\n+\\t\\t// sibling worktree was linked to every commit made from another\\n+\\t\\t// worktree of the same repository, and post-commit then condensed its\\n+\\t\\t// entire transcript — a multi-gigabyte read on every commit (#2933).\\n+\\t\\t// A session that never recorded an interaction is kept: its idleness\\n+\\t\\t// is unknown, not proven. The multi-worktree path below is unchanged:\\n+\\t\\t// it already requires a recent interaction and keeps its ambiguity\\n+\\t\\t// warning when none qualifies.\\n+\\t\\treturn dropIdleFallbackCandidates(ctx, worktreePath, matches, cutoff), false\\n \\t}\\n-\\tcutoff := time.Now().Add(-recentSessionWindow)\\n \\tvar live []*SessionState\\n \\tfor _, state := range candidates {\\n \\t\\tif state.LastInteractionTime != nil && state.LastInteractionTime.After(cutoff) {\\n@@ -445,6 +457,31 @@\\n \\treturn nil, true\\n }\\n \\n+// dropIdleFallbackCandidates removes the fallback candidates whose recorded\\n+// LastInteractionTime is older than cutoff and returns nil when none is left.\\n+// Candidates without a recorded interaction are kept (see\\n+// resolveWorktreeCandidates). Each dropped session is logged with how long it\\n+// had been idle, so a commit that silently loses its linkage can be traced to\\n+// this rule.\\n+func dropIdleFallbackCandidates(ctx context.Context, worktreePath string, candidates []*SessionState, cutoff time.Time) []*SessionState {\\n+\\tvar kept []*SessionState\\n+\\tfor _, state := range candidates {\\n+\\t\\tif state.LastInteractionTime != nil && !state.LastInteractionTime.After(cutoff) {\\n+\\t\\t\\tlogging.Info(logging.WithComponent(ctx, \\\"checkpoint\\\"),\\n+\\t\\t\\t\\t\\\"session matching: fallback session idle beyond the recent window; not linked\\\",\\n+\\t\\t\\t\\tslog.String(\\\"commit_worktree\\\", worktreePath),\\n+\\t\\t\\t\\tslog.String(\\\"session_id\\\", state.SessionID),\\n+\\t\\t\\t\\tslog.String(\\\"session_worktree\\\", state.WorktreePath),\\n+\\t\\t\\t\\tslog.Duration(\\\"idle_for\\\", time.Since(*state.LastInteractionTime).Truncate(time.Second)),\\n+\\t\\t\\t\\tslog.Duration(\\\"window\\\", recentSessionWindow),\\n+\\t\\t\\t)\\n+\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n+\\t\\t}\\n+\\t\\tkept = append(kept, state)\\n+\\t}\\n+\\treturn kept\\n+}\\n```\\n\\nTests added in `worktree_work_test.go` next to `TestCommitLinking_FallbackWithoutIdentityKeepsMainCheckoutSessions` (which still passes: nil `LastInteractionTime` is kept), using the file's existing helpers:\\n\\n- `TestCommitLinking_FallbackDeclinesASessionIdleBeyondTheWindow`: one session in a sibling worktree; idle 24 h → nothing linked; idle window+1 min → nothing linked; interacted 1 min ago → linked; no recorded interaction → linked.\\n- `TestCommitLinking_FallbackKeepsTheLiveSessionsOfASiblingWorktree`: stale + recent + undated in one sibling worktree → `recent` and `undated` linked, `stale` dropped.\\n- `TestCommitLinking_FallbackAcrossWorktreesStillRequiresARecentInteraction`: stale session in one worktree plus undated session in another → nothing linked (the multi-worktree rule is unchanged; the undated one does not become a single-worktree match).\\n\\nVerification with the rebuilt binary (`0.12.2-lcv.windows-console.1+idle-fallback.2`, same worktree, same HEAD, hooks invoked exactly as git invokes them):\\n\\n- `entire hooks git post-commit`: exit 0 in 0.8 s; log: both stored sessions declined (`idle_for=…`, `window=15m0s`) followed by `post-commit: no active sessions despite trailer`; ref count unchanged. Before the fix the same command had read 5,220 MB within 9 s.\\n- `entire hooks git prepare-commit-msg <file> message`: the v0.12.2 binary stamps `Entire-Checkpoint: 01M64WYGHV3Y18FC0D35KGH2YP` (19:37:03); the fixed binary leaves the message untouched and logs the two declines (19:37:39).\\n- `go vet`, `gofmt`, `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/execx` clean. `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -count=1` on the patched tree: 0 assertion failures; every `FAIL` is Go's `TempDir RemoveAll cleanup: … \\\\.git: The file is being used by another process`, which fails identically on the unpatched tree on this Windows machine (worktree-creating tests), so I cannot show a green package run from here. Raw outputs are available on request.\\n\\n\\n### Two related observations while trying to repair the dangling trailers\\n\\n- `entire checkpoint explain af814b0` (the squash merge of the four commits; its message carries all four trailers) reports the **first** trailer (`01M64QBAXH8ZR8GJB4B4R2EAYD`) as \\\"not available locally and could not be fetched\\\", while `entire session attach <session> --commit af814b0` refuses on the **last** one (`01M64SXQS35M7QMH504X8Q4AKV`). The two commands read different trailers of the same message.\\n- `session attach` refuses with \\\"checkpoint … referenced by the commit is missing from the local checkpoint ref … Creating a fresh checkpoint here would overwrite the original session data on push. Run: git fetch … If the colleague who made this commit hasn't pushed their checkpoint metadata yet, ask them to do so first\\\". That protection is right when the checkpoint exists somewhere, but there is no way to tell it that the checkpoint was never created (post-commit killed before writing). A trailer whose checkpoint provably does not exist on the configured checkpoint remote cannot be repaired with official commands; the four commits stay \\\"checkpoint not found\\\" forever. An explicit opt-in (for example `--replace-missing` after a successful `ls-remote` showing the ref is absent) would close that gap.\\n\\n### Test run summary for this patch\\n\\n`go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -count=1 -v -timeout 60m` on the patched tree: 1,508 RUN lines, 356 PASS, 613 FAIL, no panic. 20 top-level tests fail on assertions (12 of them on `IdentityOf(parent) must resolve on supported platforms` from `session_identity_test.go:42`, the rest on Windows path shapes and fixtures); the same 20 tests fail with the same first assertion on the unpatched tree. Every other FAIL is Go's `TempDir RemoveAll cleanup: … \\\\.git: The file is being used by another process`, also present on the unpatched tree. The three new tests pass their assertions (their log lines show the rule declining `idle_for=24h0m0s`, `16m0s`, `30m0s` and keeping `recent`/`unknown`), and fail only on that cleanup. So I cannot show a green package on this machine, but I can show the patch changes no existing assertion.\\n\\n### Open design questions for maintainers\\n\\n1. Should a nil `LastInteractionTime` also be declined by the fallback? I kept it to preserve the existing test and because its idleness is unknown.\\n2. Should the declined-idle case print a stderr hint (the ambiguous case prints one with the `entire session adopt` remedy), given #1852's concern about silent loss of linkage? I logged at Info only, because the decline is deliberate and a hint would appear on every terminal commit while an agent idles elsewhere; a Warn-level log or a one-line hint is a small follow-up if you prefer it.\\n3. The exact-home path is untouched: a session homed in the committing worktree is still condensed however idle and however large (#2933 / #2953).\\n4. The buffered logger losing every line of a killed hook deserves either a flush on each hook record or a note in the troubleshooting docs.\\n\\nI can turn this into a PR if the approach is acceptable.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2979/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2979/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2260\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2260/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2260/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2260/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2260\",\n              \"id\": 5337292534,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABPiCe9g\",\n              \"number\": 2260,\n              \"title\": \"Read(./.entire/metadata/**) deny rule makes ordinary commands ask for approval, breaking auto/unattended permission modes\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [\n                {\n                  \"id\": 9924477887,\n                  \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACT4uDvw\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/bug\",\n                  \"name\": \"bug\",\n                  \"color\": \"d73a4a\",\n                  \"default\": true,\n                  \"description\": \"Something isn't working\",\n                  \"archived_at\": null,\n                  \"archived_by\": null\n                }\n              ],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [\n                {\n                  \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                  \"id\": 70741,\n                  \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                  \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                  \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                  \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                  \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                  \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                  \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                  \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                  \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                  \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                  \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                  \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                  \"type\": \"User\",\n                  \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                  \"site_admin\": false\n                }\n              ],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-03T13:32:50Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-03T19:09:45Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"### What happened?\\n\\n`entire enable` installs `Read(./.entire/metadata/**)` into `permissions.deny` in `.claude/settings.json` (and `.factory/settings.json`). It was meant as \\\"ignore this data\\\" rule so an agent searching for something would not find prior session logs and consults them, but a `deny` rule is a hard block and claude code blocks now on these in automode.\\n\\n**Symptom:** any recursive read from the repo root — `grep -r`, and even commands that only *name* the path like `git check-ignore .entire/metadata` — is refused and needs manual approval. Deny rules can't be auto-approved, so auto mode and unattended runs stop on them.\\n\\nExample:\\n```\\nRead(./.entire/metadata/**) deny rule makes ordinary commands ask for approval, breaking auto/unattended permission modes\\n\\n Do you want to proceed?\\n   ❯ 1. Yes\\n     2. No\\n```\\n\\n**Cause:** Claude Code applies `Read` deny rules to file-reading Bash commands too, and rules resolve deny → ask → allow with no allowlist exceptions ([docs](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/permissions)).\\n\\n**The rule wasn't buying much:** it guarded a staging buffer, not the durable copy (transcripts live in the checkpoint tree, readable via `git show entire/checkpoints/v1:...`), and `.entire/.gitignore` already lists `metadata/`, which Claude Code's Grep honors.\\n\\n**Fix in flight:** #2258 stops installing it, and `entire doctor` removes it from existing repos. A session-start notice points there.\\n\\n**Workaround now:** delete that line from `.claude/settings.json`, or run `entire doctor` once #2258 lands.\\n\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Entire CLI version\\n\\nv0.10.4 and before\\n\\n### OS and architecture\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Agent\\n\\nClaude Code\\n\\n### Terminal\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Logs / debug output\\n\\n```bash\\n\\n```\\n\\n### Additional context\\n\\n_No response_\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2260/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2260/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1807\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1807/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1807/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1807/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/1807\",\n              \"id\": 4928515413,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABJcMtVQ\",\n              \"number\": 1807,\n              \"title\": \"Proposal: remove the subagent-checkpoint machinery (pre-task/post-task/post-todo) — likely unneeded\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"id\": 881031,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-07-20T11:33:25Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-21T21:50:52Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Proposal\\n\\nEvaluate removing the **subagent / task-checkpoint** subsystem — the `pre-task`, `post-task`, and `post-todo` hooks and everything they feed. Investigation suggests it produces data that nothing consumes.\\n\\nRaised as the deferred follow-up from #1806 (which repaired the Claude Code matchers so these hooks fire again). This issue is the \\\"do we even want this granularity?\\\" decision.\\n\\n## What this subsystem is\\n\\n- **`pre-task`** — snapshots untracked files before a subagent runs (baseline helper)\\n- **`post-task`** — on subagent finish, writes a *task checkpoint* to the shadow branch bundling the subagent's file diff + its own transcript (`agent-<id>.jsonl`) + attribution (`subagent_type`, `task_description`, `agent_id`, `tool_use_id`)\\n- **`post-todo`** — cuts *incremental* checkpoints during a long subagent run\\n\\nBacked by shared machinery: `handleLifecycleSubagentStart/End` (`cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go`), `SaveTaskStep` / `TaskStepContext` (`cmd/entire/cli/strategy/`), task-checkpoint write paths (`cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/ephemeral.go`, `persistent.go`), and `pre-task` state (`cmd/entire/cli/state.go`).\\n\\n## Why it looks unneeded\\n\\n**The product consumes session-level data only** (checked in `entire.io`):\\n- Ingestion reads `full.jsonl` / `transcript.jsonl` for session index 0 (`api/src/lib/checkpoint-payload-hydrator.ts`). Subagent transcripts (`agent-*.jsonl`) are **never read**.\\n- `is_task` / `tool_use_id` are parsed into `SessionInfo` once (`api/src/lib/github.ts:660-661`) then never queried or displayed.\\n- `subagent_type`, `task_description`, `is_incremental`, `incremental_sequence`, `agent_id`, `is_task_checkpoint` → **0 matches** anywhere in the product. No UI renders subagents.\\n\\n**Local consumers are dead or cosmetic:**\\n- `rewind` (the one feature using subagent-boundary checkpoints) is deprecated and slated for removal.\\n- Remaining use is `[Task]` labels in `checkpoint list` / `explain` — navigational garnish.\\n\\n**Cross-agent:** the machinery is shared by **Claude Code, Cursor, Factory AI Droid, and Copilot CLI**. On Claude Code it was dead (the #1806 matcher bug); on the other three it fires today but produces the same inert task checkpoints.\\n\\n## What we'd lose: nothing consumed\\n\\n- Code the subagent writes is still captured by the `Stop` / turn checkpoint (whole-worktree). No code loss in the common single-worktree flow.\\n- Subagent transcript, per-subagent rewind points, attribution, per-subagent tokens — none are read by the product or any live command.\\n\\n**One honest caveat:** subagents in an **isolated worktree** aren't covered by `Stop`, and `post-task` was the only thing that would capture them. But that protection doesn't effectively exist today (hooks were broken/unconsumed), so removal doesn't regress vs current reality. If isolated-worktree subagent capture ever becomes a real requirement, it's a fresh, correctly-scoped feature.\\n\\n## Removal scope (if approved)\\n\\n- Hook install + lifecycle parse across the 4 agents (`subagent-start/stop`, `pre-tool-use/post-tool-use`, Claude matchers)\\n- Shared dispatch cases (`SubagentStart`/`SubagentEnd` in `lifecycle.go`; subagent classification in `hook_registry.go`)\\n- Strategy: `SaveTaskStep`, `TaskStepContext`, task-checkpoint write paths in `checkpoint/ephemeral.go` + `persistent.go`\\n- `pre-task` state (`state.go`), `post-todo` handler\\n- The deprecated `rewind` task-checkpoint branch (already going away)\\n- Tests + docs across all four agents\\n\\n## Decision needed\\n\\nKeep (bet on a future subagent-level product feature — the dead `isTask` parse suggests it was once intended) **or** remove (delete unconsumed cross-agent complexity).\\n\\nIf we're not going to surface subagent-level data in the product in the foreseeable future, the recommendation is **remove**.\\n\\n/cc — deferred from #1806\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1807/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1807/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2058\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2058/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2058/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2058/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2058\",\n              \"id\": 5194303036,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABNZrGPA\",\n              \"number\": 2058,\n              \"title\": \"Subagent data does not survive condensation — durable storage for subagent transcripts\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [\n                {\n                  \"id\": 10189613733,\n                  \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACX1kqpQ\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/agent-support\",\n                  \"name\": \"agent-support\",\n                  \"color\": \"f3bc57\",\n                  \"default\": false,\n                  \"description\": \"adding support for additional AI agents\",\n                  \"archived_at\": null,\n                  \"archived_by\": null\n                },\n                {\n                  \"id\": 10286600863,\n                  \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACZSESnw\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/claude-code-assisted\",\n                  \"name\": \"claude-code-assisted\",\n                  \"color\": \"c4a5f7\",\n                  \"default\": false,\n                  \"description\": null,\n                  \"archived_at\": null,\n                  \"archived_by\": null\n                }\n              ],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [\n                {\n                  \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                  \"id\": 70741,\n                  \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                  \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                  \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                  \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                  \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                  \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                  \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                  \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                  \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                  \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                  \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                  \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                  \"type\": \"User\",\n                  \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                  \"site_admin\": false\n                }\n              ],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 3,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T15:25:06Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-20T12:18:18Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Tracking issue for the one open piece of subagent tracking. Plan doc lives at `subagent-durability-plan.md` (untracked).\\n\\n> **Update 2026-08-20 — the design below is implemented in #2032, not here.** That branch\\n> (`feat/subagent-stop-capture`, trail 1076) started 2026-08-18 as background-subagent capture\\n> and its last ~9 commits built exactly this: `session.TaskRecords` as the mid-turn pointer\\n> ledger, `WriteOptions.Tasks []TaskPayload` materialized into\\n> `tasks/<tool-use-id>/{task.json, agent-<id>.jsonl}` inside the session checkpoint, with\\n> `TranscriptUnavailableReason` for the transcript-gone case. It cites this issue by number and\\n> carries its own plan at `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-19-subagent-durable-records.md`.\\n> I filed this issue without spotting that branch — my mistake.\\n>\\n> **What is left after #2032 is the OPF gate and some doc debt.** Everything else below is\\n> either done or covered there; ticked items say which.\\n\\n**Status 2026-08-19:** the per-agent ephemeral bugs are merged (7 PRs, through #1958).\\nDurable storage is the one open piece — this issue tracks it.\\n\\n**Problem, one line:** condensation builds one `checkpoint.WriteOptions` per session with no\\n`IsTask`/`ToolUseID` (`manual_commit_condensation.go:398`), so `persistent.go`'s whole task-write\\npath is unreachable — no producer anywhere sets `IsTask: true`. Subagent detail dies at commit,\\nfor every agent. Measured: 0 of the 150 newest `entire/checkpoints/v1` commits contain `tasks/`;\\n80-checkpoint sample (CC 58, Codex 10, OpenCode 2, Pi 1) had `subagent_tokens` non-null in 0.\\n\\n## Decision: capture the pointer mid-turn, defer the payload to condensation\\n\\n- `SubagentEnd` → small session-state entry only: correlation ID, agent type, description,\\n  **declared transcript path**, files touched, tokens. No shadow-tree write.\\n- Condensation → read the declared paths, sanitize → externalize images → redact, store.\\n- Path gone by then → keep the pointer record, metadata says transcript unavailable.\\n\\nWhy: takes per-subagent tree surgery + CAS off the mid-turn hook path; one producer instead of\\ntwo mirrored ones (that duplication is what made unreachable code look durable); no misleading\\nintermediate state. Works on both backends, so refs-only stops being required — still preferred\\nfor lazy fetch of large transcripts.\\n\\nThe pointer must stay mid-turn: for Codex and Cursor, `agent_transcript_path` arrives on the\\nstop hook and nowhere else. Dropping it means guessing layouts again — the bug #1958 fixed.\\n\\n**Premise verified:** agents do *not* clean up subagent transcripts (CC 180 files / 121 older\\nthan 2 days; Codex 164 / 164). The comment at `manual_commit_condensation.go:1112` claiming\\notherwise is wrong, and it is what justified capturing mid-turn.\\n\\n## What's left\\n\\n- [x] ~~Per-agent persistence check~~ — **done**, results in [this comment](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2058#issuecomment-5345298901).\\n      No agent cleans up. Droid Workers are ordinary session files sibling to the parent, so\\n      their lifetime equals the parent's. Two agents need a different pointer *shape*: Copilot\\n      CLI has no subagent transcript file at all (inline in the parent, keyed by `toolCallId`,\\n      and its `SubagentEnd` carries no correlation ID), and OpenCode's transcripts are\\n      Entire-written disposable handoff files.\\n- [x] ~~Pick where the payload lands~~ — **decided in #2032**: the `tasks/` subtree inside the\\n      session checkpoint (the first option), via `WriteOptions.Tasks []TaskPayload`. Works on\\n      both backends, so the refs-only variant is moot.\\n- [ ] **OPF gate — the one thing #2032 does not address** (zero OPF mentions in its diff).\\n      Verified 2026-08-20:\\n      - **git-branch is fine, by luck of design.** `collectTreeBlobs` walks the whole checkpoint\\n        tree and treats every blob except `content_hash.txt` as redactable, so\\n        `tasks/…/agent-<id>.jsonl` and `task.json` pick up the 9th layer automatically. #2032\\n        writes no `content_hash.txt` into the task dir, so the apply pass's sibling-`full.jsonl`\\n        hash recompute is undisturbed.\\n      - **git-refs gets nothing.** `RewriteUnpushedV1WithOPF` has one call site, on the\\n        git-branch pre-push path. With refs as primary, subagent transcripts — the\\n        highest-volume, least-reviewed content in the system — ship with 8 layers while a user\\n        who enabled OPF believes 9 ran.\\n\\n      Mitigating: git-branch is still the default primary (`resolvePrimaryType`), so refs is\\n      opt-in and today's exposure is limited to adopters. That argues for not blocking #2032 on\\n      full OPF-for-refs, not for leaving this undecided — refs is meant to become the default.\\n\\n      Suggested resolution: make the materializer backend-aware — on git-refs write `task.json`\\n      only and skip the transcript blob until OPF-for-refs lands. Refs users still get the\\n      pointer record, git-branch users get the whole feature, and nobody gets a silent\\n      redaction downgrade. OPF-for-refs then wants its own issue; it currently has no owner.\\n- [x] ~~Delete the dead persistent task writer~~ — **done in #2032**, which replaces it with\\n      the `Tasks` route. (I had this in #2059 before spotting #2032; closed as redundant.)\\n- [x] ~~Per-task tokens have nowhere to live~~ — **covered in #2032**, which routes them\\n      through `TaskRecord`/`TaskPayload.TokenUsage` rather than widening `TaskStepContext`.\\n- [ ] Doc debt. `ref-checkpoint-backend.md:25` is fixed in #2083. Still open:\\n      - the false `:1112` comment in `manual_commit_condensation.go` (\\\"finds nothing on this path\\n        once the agent has cleaned the transcripts up\\\" — they don't); belongs in #2032, which\\n        already edits that file\\n      - #2032's own docs are behind its code: the \\\"Task Steps\\\" section it adds documents\\n        `captureInFlightTasks` / `selectInFlightTasksForSnapshot` /\\n        `IncrementalTypeBackgroundProgress`, none of which exist at its tip, and the durable\\n        materialization — the headline — is undocumented, with the \\\"Committed Checkpoints\\\" tree\\n        listing still showing no `tasks/`\\n- [x] ~~Optional: `[Task]` entries in `checkpoint list --pending` from session state~~ —\\n      **covered in #2032**, which builds `RewindPoint{IsTaskCheckpoint: true}` from\\n      `state.TaskRecords`, with distinct running vs completed messages.\\n\\n## Deliberately not in this\\n\\n- Codex `SubagentAwareExtractor` (token aggregation from rollouts) — `codex exec --json` reports\\n  usage only on the terminal `turn.completed`.\\n- `agent-integration-checklist.md` has no subagent section at all.\\n- `ToolUseID` → `SubagentCorrelationID` rename; Cursor subagent integration test; moving the\\n  transcript resolver into `paths` with claudecode + droid declaring their shared layout.\\n\\n---\\n\\nContext for whoever picks this up: the seven merged PRs that fixed the ephemeral stage are\\n#1935, #1936, #1938, #1947, #1950, #1964, #1958. This issue is only about the durable stage,\\nwhich none of them touched — and which #2032 now implements. #2059 was a redundant\\ncleanup-only attempt and is closed; #2083 carries the one doc fix that survived it.\\n\\nAlso stacked on #2032: #2034 (trail 1077, background-subagent commit linkage). It forked\\nbefore the task-records commits and still keys on `session.InFlightTasks`, which became\\n`TaskRecords`, so it needs a rebase onto #2032's tip before its diff means much.\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2058/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2058/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2271\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2271/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2271/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2271/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2271\",\n              \"id\": 5348106211,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABPsWf4w\",\n              \"number\": 2271,\n              \"title\": \"Docs: security page has no data-residency information, and states Entire does not receive transcripts\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"jasonmx\",\n                \"id\": 7354306,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjczNTQzMDY=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7354306?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jasonmx\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/jasonmx\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jasonmx/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jasonmx/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jasonmx/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jasonmx/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jasonmx/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jasonmx/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jasonmx/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jasonmx/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jasonmx/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T12:33:02Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T12:33:02Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\n[docs.entire.io/security](https://docs.entire.io/security) is subtitled *\\\"Where your data lives, which redaction layers run before each write, when data leaves your machine…\\\"* but contains no data-residency information, and one sentence in it reads as ruling out the hosted side of the product entirely.\\n\\nI spent a while establishing the actual picture from the API, and I think a short section on that page would save others the same trip.\\n\\n## 1. No residency information on the page that promises it\\n\\nThe page never mentions jurisdictions, regions, clusters, or `homeJurisdiction`. But all of these are real and user-visible:\\n\\n```console\\n$ entire api /api/v1/clusters\\n# four clusters, each with a jurisdiction: au, eu, in, us\\n\\n$ entire api /api/v1/me\\n# \\\"homeJurisdiction\\\": \\\"us\\\"\\n```\\n\\n`entire api --help` documents `--to core` vs `--to cell` and a `--jurisdiction` flag; `entire auth token --help` describes minting \\\"a jurisdictional identity token for that jurisdiction's entire-api cells\\\". So the CLI is explicit that jurisdictional cells exist. The security page is silent.\\n\\n## 2. \\\"Entire does not operate a service that receives your transcripts\\\"\\n\\nFrom the *Threat Model and Boundaries* accordion:\\n\\n> Entire does not operate a service that receives your transcripts. Checkpoints travel to the Git remotes you push to.\\n\\nAnd the top of *Where Your Data Lives*:\\n\\n> Checkpoints live in **your** Git repository, not in a service Entire controls.\\n\\nBoth are hard to square with:\\n\\n- **Mirrors.** A repository can be mirrored to an Entire-operated cluster (`entire repo mirror create`), and the web console presents this as a hosting/data-residency feature.\\n- **Server-side search.** [What is indexed](https://docs.entire.io/guides/search/what-is-indexed) says semantic search covers \\\"user prompts and assistant prose from sessions\\\". That index is server-side and queried through the control plane, so transcript content is received and indexed by an Entire service.\\n\\nThe same accordion's *Who can read what* table already concedes this three paragraphs further down, listing entire.io as reading \\\"The repositories you authorize, and the checkpoints in them\\\". The flat sentence above contradicts the table below it.\\n\\n## 3. Account jurisdiction is invisible in every surface\\n\\nAn account's `homeJurisdiction` is fixed at creation and determines which cell holds account-level aggregates. It is independent of where a repository is mirrored, so the two can differ, and I think most people would not expect that.\\n\\nIn my case the repository mirror is `eu` and the account is `us`. The web console's repository Settings → General shows a green \\\"European Union / Frankfurt / Synced\\\" hosting panel, which is accurate for the repository and reasonably reads as *your data is in the EU*. Nothing in the console or the docs indicates the account is elsewhere. I only found it via `/api/v1/me`.\\n\\nContent does appear to stay with the repository's cluster, and the account cell holds metadata only (commit SHAs and dates, diff line counts, repo names, session/checkpoint/token counts, tool mix). That is a reasonable design. It just is not written down anywhere.\\n\\n## Suggested fix\\n\\n1. Add a **Data residency** section to the security page: the jurisdictions available, what lives in a repository's cluster versus the account's home cell, and that the two are set independently.\\n2. Reword or qualify \\\"Entire does not operate a service that receives your transcripts\\\" so it is scoped to the local-only configuration, and note what changes once a repository is mirrored and indexed.\\n3. Document whether `homeJurisdiction` can be changed after account creation, and whether it can be chosen at signup. I could not find a CLI or console route, and `GET https://eu.auth.entire.io/api/v1/me` returns `foreign_jurisdiction` for a `us` account.\\n4. Consider surfacing the account's jurisdiction in the console next to the repository hosting panel, since that panel is where people go to answer the residency question.\\n\\nHappy to test any wording against what the API actually returns.\\n\\nCLI version 0.10.3.\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2271/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2271/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2551\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2551/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2551/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2551/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2551\",\n              \"id\": 5530900007,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABSarWJw\",\n              \"number\": 2551,\n              \"title\": \"entire session resume <branch> reports \\\"branch not found\\\" for a Unicode-equivalent (NFC vs NFD) branch name that git resolves fine\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"KC1706\",\n                \"id\": 152233142,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOCRLktg\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/152233142?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/KC1706\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/KC1706\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/KC1706/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/KC1706/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/KC1706/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/KC1706/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/KC1706/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/KC1706/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/KC1706/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/KC1706/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/KC1706/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 2,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-21T18:28:07Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-09T17:58:56Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## What happened\\n\\nBranch names with accented characters can be encoded two ways that look identical but are different bytes: precomposed (NFC, `é` = U+00E9) and decomposed (NFD, `e` + U+0301). Git treats them as the same branch — `git checkout` finds the branch either way (that's `core.precomposeUnicode`).\\n\\nEntire doesn't. `entire session resume <branch>` compares and looks up the branch name byte-for-byte with no normalization, so if the name passed differs in normalization from the ref stored on disk, Entire reports:\\n\\n```\\nbranch 'feature/café' not found locally or on origin\\n```\\n\\n...even though the branch exists and `git checkout` on the same name works. Resuming with the *other* spelling succeeds.\\n\\nEntire is also internally inconsistent here: `entire session info <id> --json` prints the branch in its stored (NFD) form, but feeding that exact value back into `entire session resume` fails.\\n\\n## Where this bites\\n\\nCross-platform teams. Git on Linux does not precompose, so a branch created there keeps the NFD form; Entire stores that in the session state and syncs it. A teammate on macOS (where the local branch is NFC) then can't resume it by the synced name — and once the ref is packed (`git gc`) the NFD spelling no longer resolves via the filesystem either.\\n\\n## Root cause (current main, 59df1a13e)\\n\\nNo Unicode normalization is applied to branch names anywhere. In the resume path:\\n\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/resume.go` — `currentBranch == branchName` is a byte-exact compare, so the \\\"already on this branch\\\" fast-path fails even while standing on the branch.\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/git_operations.go` — `GetCurrentBranch` returns `head.Name().Short()` and `BranchExistsLocally` does `repo.Reference(plumbing.NewBranchReferenceName(name), true)`, both byte-exact. go-git's packed-refs lookup is exact-byte, so the NFD spelling misses once refs are packed.\\n\\n## Steps to reproduce\\n\\nSimulated on one macOS machine by toggling `core.precomposeUnicode` to mimic a Linux origin:\\n\\n1. `git config core.precomposeUnicode false`\\n2. `git checkout -b \\\"$(printf 'feature/cafe\\\\xcc\\\\x81')\\\"`  # NFD\\n3. Run an agent session that makes a change + commit → Entire stores session state with `branch` in NFD.\\n4. `git config core.precomposeUnicode true`; recreate/checkout the branch as NFC (`printf 'feature/caf\\\\xc3\\\\xa9'`); `git pack-refs --all`.\\n5. Compare:\\n   - `entire session resume \\\"$(printf 'feature/cafe\\\\xcc\\\\x81')\\\"` → **\\\"branch not found locally or on origin\\\"**\\n   - `entire session resume \\\"$(printf 'feature/caf\\\\xc3\\\\xa9')\\\"` → resumes fine\\n   - `git checkout \\\"$(printf 'feature/cafe\\\\xcc\\\\x81')\\\"` → succeeds\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\nA failed resume plus a misleading \\\"not found\\\" error for a branch that exists. Not data loss — the interactive picker recovers via its checkpoint-trailer fallback, and `checkpoint list` is reachability-based; it's the direct `session resume <branch>` path (and the `session info --json` → `session resume` round-trip) that breaks.\\n\\n## Suggested fix\\n\\nCompare branch names normalization-insensitively (fold to NFC) and resolve a supplied name to the actual local ref before checkout — the same idea as the case-folding fix in #2403, applied to Unicode normalization. Happy to open a PR with a regression test (an NFC/NFD branch pair over a packed ref).\\n\\nThis is distinct from #2398, which is about `git diff --cached --name-only` quoting of non-ASCII file *paths* in commit-linking.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2551/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2551/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1439\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1439/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1439/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1439/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/1439\",\n              \"id\": 4678781324,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABFuCJjA\",\n              \"number\": 1439,\n              \"title\": \"Agent sessions should adopt enabled repos when a long session switches git common dirs\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [\n                {\n                  \"id\": 9924477887,\n                  \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACT4uDvw\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/bug\",\n                  \"name\": \"bug\",\n                  \"color\": \"d73a4a\",\n                  \"default\": true,\n                  \"description\": \"Something isn't working\",\n                  \"archived_at\": null,\n                  \"archived_by\": null\n                }\n              ],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-06-16T23:54:34Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-07T13:28:12Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nA long-running agent session can move from one git repository into another enabled repository and make commits that get no `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer, even though the CLI is installed and git hooks are present in the second repo.\\n\\nThis is distinct from same-repo sibling worktree matching. In this case the two repositories have different git common dirs, so the second repo's `prepare-commit-msg` hook cannot see the session state that was initialized in the first repo.\\n\\n## Observed repro from local investigation\\n\\nWhile working on `entirehq/entire.io`, a Codex session was active in:\\n\\n```\\n/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entire.io/.worktrees/merge-in-trails\\n```\\n\\nThe session state exists in the `entire.io` repo:\\n\\n```\\n/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entire.io/.git/entire-sessions/019ed223-016e-7181-b420-dafc7d141cf4.json\\n```\\n\\nSummary of that state:\\n\\n```\\nagent_type: Codex\\nphase: active\\nworktree_path: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entire.io/.worktrees/merge-in-trails\\nlast_interaction_time: 2026-06-16T19:44:57-04:00\\n```\\n\\nDuring the same conversation, the agent switched to the CLI repo worktree:\\n\\n```\\n/private/tmp/entire-session-match-fix\\n```\\n\\nand committed/pushed:\\n\\n```\\nf9005540ed2b822363cf9aeefa87574a83517073 Match sessions across sibling worktrees\\n```\\n\\nThat commit has no trailer:\\n\\n```\\ngit show -s --format=%B f9005540ed2b822363cf9aeefa87574a83517073\\n\\nMatch sessions across sibling worktrees\\n```\\n\\nThe CLI repo did have hooks installed:\\n\\n```\\n/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entire/.git/hooks/prepare-commit-msg\\n\\n#!/bin/sh\\n# Entire CLI hooks\\nentire hooks git prepare-commit-msg \\\"$1\\\" \\\"$2\\\" 2>/dev/null || true\\n```\\n\\nBut its repo-local session store was empty:\\n\\n```\\n/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entire/.git/entire-sessions\\n# no *.json session states\\n```\\n\\nThe git common dirs are different:\\n\\n```\\nentire.io repo: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entire.io/.git\\ncli repo:       /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entire/.git\\n```\\n\\nSo the hook in the CLI repo fired, looked in the CLI repo's `.git/entire-sessions`, found no active session, and skipped trailer insertion.\\n\\n## Expected behavior\\n\\nIf an agent session with Entire enabled moves into a second enabled git repository and commits there, Entire should not silently lose provenance.\\n\\nPossible acceptable behaviors:\\n\\n1. Adopt/create a repo-local session state in the second repo, keyed to the same agent session/transcript, so commits in that repo get trailers/checkpoints.\\n2. Detect that an agent session is active elsewhere but missing in the current repo and emit a clear warning before/when the commit hook skips.\\n3. Provide an explicit multi-repo/orchestrator session model that can attach one agent transcript to multiple repo-local checkpoint streams.\\n\\n## Actual behavior\\n\\nThe commit hook silently skips because the current repo has hooks installed but no repo-local session state. The resulting commit has no `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer.\\n\\n## Why this matters\\n\\nUsers reasonably expect \\\"Entire is installed and the agent session is active\\\" to mean commits made by that agent are checkpointed. Long agent sessions often inspect or patch multiple repositories. Today, a repo switch can produce uncheckpointed commits without any visible warning.\\n\\nThis is especially confusing because same-repo worktree fixes do not help here: the failure crosses git common dirs, so session lookup by shared common dir is intentionally not enough.\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n- #529: orchestrator sessions launched outside git repos / multi-repo worktree workflows\\n- #1098: global auto-enable / track sessions without per-repo configuration\\n- #784 / #686: other prepare-commit-msg missing-trailer reports\\n\\n## Fix direction\\n\\nInvestigate agent lifecycle hooks for repo transitions. In particular:\\n\\n- Codex/Claude hooks should be able to initialize or adopt session state when the active agent begins operating inside a different enabled repo.\\n- `prepare-commit-msg` should distinguish \\\"Entire disabled\\\" from \\\"hooks installed but no active session in this repo during an agent-driven commit\\\" and surface an actionable diagnostic.\\n- Any cross-repo adoption must avoid accidentally attaching one repo's checkpoint metadata to another repo's commits; the checkpoint streams should remain repo-local even if they share an agent transcript/session identity.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1439/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 1,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 1,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1439/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1635\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1635/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1635/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1635/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/1635\",\n              \"id\": 4810594012,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABHrvW3A\",\n              \"number\": 1635,\n              \"title\": \"git-refs: push queue is drained by the first successful push — checkpoints never reach a second remote\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-07-04T21:23:19Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-07T22:10:48Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-07T22:10:48Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Problem\\n\\nThe git-refs backend discovers unpushed checkpoints via a flock-JSONL queue in the git common dir (`checkpoint/pushqueue.go`). The pre-push hook drains the queue and removes entries once they land on **the remote of that push** (`strategy/manual_commit_push.go` → `prePushCheckpointRefs`).\\n\\nThe queue has no per-remote state: with two remotes, `git push remote-a` drains the queue, so a later `git push remote-b` finds nothing to push — remote B permanently misses those per-checkpoint refs. (git-branch doesn't have this failure shape: the v1 branch's unpushed state is per-remote via remote-tracking refs.)\\n\\n## Current behavior is pinned\\n\\n`TestGitRefsQueue_TwoRemotesQueueClearedByFirstPush` in `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/refs_queue_semantics_test.go` (branch `soph/git-remote-test-coverage`) asserts today's behavior with a comment to flip the assertion when this is fixed.\\n\\n## Possible fixes\\n\\n1. **Per-remote queue tracking** — keep queue entries keyed by (ref, remote) or record which remotes each ref reached, removing an entry only when all configured remotes (or the checkpoint fetch-resolution target) have it.\\n2. **Delete only on push to the fetch-resolution target** — entries are removed only when pushed to the remote that `checkpoint/remote.FetchURL` resolves to (the one reads will consult), other remotes get best-effort pushes without consuming the queue.\\n3. **Ref-diff instead of queue** — derive unpushed refs by comparing local `refs/entire/checkpoints/*` against `ls-remote` of the push target, using the queue only as an optimization hint.\\n\\nOption 2 is the smallest change consistent with the read side (which resolves a single checkpoint source); option 3 removes the state-consistency problem entirely at the cost of an ls-remote per push.\\n\\nRelated decision: entireio/cli#1634 (non-origin reads) — both stem from multi-remote topologies being untested/undefined.\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1635/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1635/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1759\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1759/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1759/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1759/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/1759\",\n              \"id\": 4889752771,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABI3O0ww\",\n              \"number\": 1759,\n              \"title\": \"protected_dirs not excluded from checkpoint snapshots (external protocol-v1 plugin and built-in claude-code)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"ecgang\",\n                \"id\": 3526675,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MjY2NzU=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3526675?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/ecgang\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [\n                {\n                  \"id\": 9924477887,\n                  \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACT4uDvw\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/bug\",\n                  \"name\": \"bug\",\n                  \"color\": \"d73a4a\",\n                  \"default\": true,\n                  \"description\": \"Something isn't working\",\n                  \"archived_at\": null,\n                  \"archived_by\": null\n                }\n              ],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-07-15T05:57:37Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-15T21:30:47Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-15T21:30:47Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"### What happened?\\n\\nThe external-agent plugin docs describe protected_dirs as \\\"Directories the CLI should not modify (excluded from checkpoints and diffs)\\\" (docs → External agent plugins → Commands → info).\\n\\nIn our tests, an untracked, non-gitignored file planted under a declared protected dir was captured into the shadow-branch checkpoint commit (entire/<base-sha7>-<hash6>). Reproduced two ways in an isolated sandbox:\\n\\nExternal plugin (protocol v1) whose info returns protected_dirs: [\\\".terminalhire\\\", \\\".claude\\\"] — a planted .terminalhire/profile.json appears in the checkpoint tree (git ls-tree -r <shadow-ref>) with its content intact (git grep <marker> <shadow-ref>).\\nBuilt-in claude-code agent — a marker file under .claude/ is captured identically.\\nLikely root cause (from a read of the code): protected_dirs IS honored in the session-tracking and rewind paths (strategy/common.go isProtectedPath(), checkpoint/state.go shouldIgnoreSessionTrackingPath() inside DetectFileChanges), but the first checkpoint of a session takes a different path: checkpoint/ephemeral.go collectChangedFiles() (~line 1209, called under opts.IsFirstCheckpoint) does its own raw git status --porcelain -z -uall parse and only excludes paths.IsInfrastructurePath() — which is solely a .entire/ subpath check. It never consults agent.AllProtectedDirs() (agent/registry.go), so any agent's protected dirs — built-in or external plugin — are captured on session start. That matches what we observed: the leak is agent-agnostic and fires on the first checkpoint.\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\ngit init a repo with one commit; entire enable --agent claude-code --telemetry=false --skip-push-sessions.\\nPlant an untracked marker: mkdir -p .claude && echo \\\"MARKER-abc123\\\" > .claude/marker.txt (not gitignored).\\nRun an agent session so a checkpoint is written (we drove the lifecycle directly via entire hooks claude-code <hook-name>; a normal Claude Code session should exercise the same path).\\ngit ls-tree -r <shadow-branch> --name-only | grep marker → present; git grep MARKER-abc123 <shadow-ref> → content present.\\nReproduces every time (it's the first-checkpoint path). Happy to share the full repro scripts/sandbox setup.\\n\\n### Entire CLI version\\n\\nEntire CLI 0.8.42 (Go go1.26.4, darwin/arm64)\\n\\n### OS and architecture\\n\\nmacOS (Darwin 27.0.0) arm64\\n\\n### Agent\\n\\nClaude Code (built-in agent) and a minimal external protocol-v1 plugin — both reproduce\\n\\n### Terminal\\n\\nn/a (lifecycle driven via entire hooks directly)\\n\\n### Logs / debug output\\n\\n```bash\\n\\n```\\n\\n### Additional context\\n\\nWhat does stay out of checkpoints on some machines appears to be incidental gitignore state rather than protected_dirs: e.g. .claude/settings.local.json was excluded on one machine only because a user-global core.excludesFile happened to ignore it — a machine/CI runner without that convention captures it.\\nThe same protected-dir content also appears pre-checkpoint in .git/entire-sessions/<id>.json session state.\\nWe considered routing this to [security@entire.io](mailto:security@entire.io) per SECURITY.md, but per its rubric (capture is local-only; shadow branches are never auto-pushed, which we verified; no remote-actor exploitation) it reads as a bug report. Happy to move it there if you'd rather treat it as sensitive.\\nHappy to submit a PR: the fix looks small — extend the exclusion check in collectChangedFiles to also consult agent.AllProtectedDirs()/AllProtectedFiles(), mirroring the existing state.go pattern, plus a regression test in ephemeral_test.go. Per CONTRIBUTING I'll wait for maintainer feedback/approval on the approach before opening one.\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1759/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1759/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1757\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1757/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1757/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1757/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/1757\",\n              \"id\": 4889720907,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABI3M4Sw\",\n              \"number\": 1757,\n              \"title\": \"`protected_dirs` not excluded from checkpoint snapshots (external protocol-v1 plugin and built-in claude-code)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"ecgang\",\n                \"id\": 3526675,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MjY2NzU=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3526675?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/ecgang\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-07-15T05:52:06Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-15T05:57:53Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-15T05:57:53Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"*(Filed via CLI — body mirrors the Bug Report form's sections since `gh` can't submit issue forms directly.)*\\n\\n### What happened?\\n\\nThe external-agent plugin docs describe `protected_dirs` as \\\"Directories the CLI should not modify **(excluded from checkpoints and diffs)**\\\" (docs → External agent plugins → Commands → `info`).\\n\\nIn our tests, an untracked, non-gitignored file planted under a declared protected dir was captured into the shadow-branch checkpoint commit (`entire/<base-sha7>-<hash6>`). Reproduced two ways in an isolated sandbox:\\n\\n1. **External plugin (protocol v1)** whose `info` returns `protected_dirs: [\\\".terminalhire\\\", \\\".claude\\\"]` — a planted `.terminalhire/profile.json` appears in the checkpoint tree (`git ls-tree -r <shadow-ref>`) with its content intact (`git grep <marker> <shadow-ref>`).\\n2. **Built-in claude-code agent** — a marker file under `.claude/` is captured identically.\\n\\n**Likely root cause (from a read of the code):** `protected_dirs` IS honored in the session-tracking and rewind paths (`strategy/common.go` `isProtectedPath()`, `checkpoint/state.go` `shouldIgnoreSessionTrackingPath()` inside `DetectFileChanges`), but the **first checkpoint of a session** takes a different path: `checkpoint/ephemeral.go` `collectChangedFiles()` (~line 1209, called under `opts.IsFirstCheckpoint`) does its own raw `git status --porcelain -z -uall` parse and only excludes `paths.IsInfrastructurePath()` — which is solely a `.entire/` subpath check. It never consults `agent.AllProtectedDirs()` (`agent/registry.go`), so any agent's protected dirs — built-in or external plugin — are captured on session start. That matches what we observed: the leak is agent-agnostic and fires on the first checkpoint.\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\n1. `git init` a repo with one commit; `entire enable --agent claude-code --telemetry=false --skip-push-sessions`.\\n2. Plant an untracked marker: `mkdir -p .claude && echo \\\"MARKER-abc123\\\" > .claude/marker.txt` (not gitignored).\\n3. Run an agent session so a checkpoint is written (we drove the lifecycle directly via `entire hooks claude-code <hook-name>`; a normal Claude Code session should exercise the same path).\\n4. `git ls-tree -r <shadow-branch> --name-only | grep marker` → present; `git grep MARKER-abc123 <shadow-ref>` → content present.\\n\\nReproduces every time (it's the first-checkpoint path). Happy to share the full repro scripts/sandbox setup.\\n\\n### Entire CLI version\\n\\nEntire CLI 0.8.42 (Go go1.26.4, darwin/arm64)\\n\\n### OS and architecture\\n\\nmacOS (Darwin 27.0.0) arm64\\n\\n### Agent\\n\\nClaude Code (built-in agent) and a minimal external protocol-v1 plugin — both reproduce\\n\\n### Terminal\\n\\nn/a (lifecycle driven via `entire hooks` directly)\\n\\n### Additional context\\n\\n- What *does* stay out of checkpoints on some machines appears to be incidental gitignore state rather than `protected_dirs`: e.g. `.claude/settings.local.json` was excluded on one machine only because a user-global `core.excludesFile` happened to ignore it — a machine/CI runner without that convention captures it.\\n- The same protected-dir content also appears pre-checkpoint in `.git/entire-sessions/<id>.json` session state.\\n- We considered routing this to security@entire.io per SECURITY.md, but per its rubric (capture is local-only; shadow branches are never auto-pushed, which we verified; no remote-actor exploitation) it reads as a bug report. Happy to move it there if you'd rather treat it as sensitive.\\n- **Happy to submit a PR**: the fix looks small — extend the exclusion check in `collectChangedFiles` to also consult `agent.AllProtectedDirs()`/`AllProtectedFiles()`, mirroring the existing `state.go` pattern, plus a regression test in `ephemeral_test.go`. Per CONTRIBUTING I'll wait for maintainer feedback/approval on the approach before opening one.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1757/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1757/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": \"duplicate\",\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/421\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/421/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/421/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/421/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/421\",\n              \"id\": 3961665062,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M7sIjYm\",\n              \"number\": 421,\n              \"title\": \"Attribution always reports 0% even when the agent wrote all the code\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"wasabeef\",\n                \"id\": 1833474,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzM0NzQ=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1833474?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wasabeef\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/wasabeef\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wasabeef/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wasabeef/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wasabeef/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wasabeef/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wasabeef/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wasabeef/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wasabeef/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wasabeef/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wasabeef/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [\n                {\n                  \"id\": 9924477887,\n                  \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACT4uDvw\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/bug\",\n                  \"name\": \"bug\",\n                  \"color\": \"d73a4a\",\n                  \"default\": true,\n                  \"description\": \"Something isn't working\",\n                  \"archived_at\": null,\n                  \"archived_by\": null\n                }\n              ],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [\n                {\n                  \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                  \"id\": 249787869,\n                  \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                  \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                  \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                  \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                  \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                  \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                  \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                  \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                  \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                  \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                  \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                  \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                  \"type\": \"User\",\n                  \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                  \"site_admin\": false\n                }\n              ],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 3,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T08:39:12Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-17T07:56:42Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-16T14:11:28Z\",\n              \"assignee\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"### What happened?\\n\\n`initial_attribution` in checkpoint metadata (`entire/checkpoints/v1`) always shows `agent_lines: 0` and `agent_percentage: 0`, regardless of actual agent contribution.\\n\\nThree independent bugs in the PostCommit condensation pipeline cause this. They often trigger together.\\n\\n### Bug 1 — Wrong baseline for detecting non-agent files\\n\\n`CalculateAttributionWithAccumulated()` finds user-only files by diffing `baseTree` (session start) against `headTree` (after commit). When unrelated commits exist between session start and the current commit, all files from those intermediate commits are misclassified as \\\"user edits,\\\" inflating `totalUserAdded`.\\n\\nThe comparison should use `parentTree` (the commit's immediate parent) instead of `baseTree`.\\n\\n**Where:** `manual_commit_attribution.go:226` — `getAllChangedFilesBetweenTrees(baseTree, headTree)`\\n\\n### Bug 2 — Stale sessions claim unrelated commits\\n\\n`findSessionsForWorktree()` returns all sessions including ENDED ones. `HandleCondenseIfFilesTouched` triggers condensation whenever `FilesTouched` is non-empty, without verifying that the committed files actually overlap with the session's shadow branch.\\n\\n`HandleCondense` already has this check (`filesOverlapWithContent()` for non-ACTIVE sessions), but `HandleCondenseIfFilesTouched` was missing it. ENDED sessions with carry-forward files produce zero-attribution checkpoints that overwrite valid ones.\\n\\n**Where:** `manual_commit_hooks.go` — `HandleCondenseIfFilesTouched`\\n\\n### Bug 3 — Double condensation overwrites correct results\\n\\nWhen multiple sessions exist in the same worktree, both react to the same commit. The first condensation calculates correct attribution and advances `AttributionBaseCommit` to HEAD. A second condensation of the same session then sees `baseTree == headTree`, produces an empty diff, and overwrites the correct result.\\n\\n**Where:** `manual_commit_hooks.go` — `condenseAndUpdateState`\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\n1. `entire enable` (manual-commit strategy).\\n2. Start an agent session, let it create files.\\n3. From another terminal, make an unrelated commit (triggers Bug 1).\\n4. Stop the first session, start a new one in the same directory.\\n5. Let the new session write code, then commit.\\n6. Check `metadata.json` on `entire/checkpoints/v1` — `agent_percentage` is `0`.\\n\\nTo trigger all three bugs:\\n\\n7. The first (now ENDED) session still has `FilesTouched` entries.\\n8. PostCommit processes the ENDED session first → zero-attribution checkpoint (Bug 2). The active session condenses correctly, but gets condensed again via the stale session path (Bug 3), overwriting the correct result.\\n\\n### Entire CLI version\\n\\nv0.4.5\\n\\n### OS and architecture\\n\\nDarwin 24.5.0 arm64\\n\\n### Agent\\n\\nClaude Code\\n\\n### Strategy\\n\\nmanual-commit (default)\\n\\n### Terminal\\n\\nWezTerm\\n\\n### Logs / debug output\\n\\n```bash\\n# Pattern in .entire/logs/entire.log:\\n\\n# First condensation — correct:\\npost-commit: session 743d4b39 agent_lines:396 human_added:539 agent_pct:42.36\\n\\n# ENDED session fires (Bug 2) — zero:\\npost-commit: session a62ddd7e agent_lines:0 human_added:0 agent_pct:0.00\\n\\n# Same session condensed again (Bug 3) — overwrites correct result:\\npost-commit: session 743d4b39 agent_lines:0 human_added:0 agent_pct:0.00\\n```\\n\\n### Additional context\\n\\n- All three bugs occur without sub-agents or task agents.\\n- Bug 1 is the most common — any mid-session commit, `git pull --rebase`, or `git merge` triggers it.\\n- Bug 2 triggers whenever an ENDED session has leftover `FilesTouched` entries (normal after carry-forward).\\n- Bug 3 requires multiple sessions in the same worktree, or rapid sequential commits.\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/421/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/421/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/376\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/376/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/376/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/376/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/376\",\n              \"id\": 3952991800,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M7rnd44\",\n              \"number\": 376,\n              \"title\": \"human_added what does it track?\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"dipree\",\n                \"id\": 3369400,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNjk0MDA=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3369400?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/dipree\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dipree/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [\n                {\n                  \"id\": 9924477887,\n                  \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACT4uDvw\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/bug\",\n                  \"name\": \"bug\",\n                  \"color\": \"d73a4a\",\n                  \"default\": true,\n                  \"description\": \"Something isn't working\",\n                  \"archived_at\": null,\n                  \"archived_by\": null\n                },\n                {\n                  \"id\": 9924477927,\n                  \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACT4uD5w\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/question\",\n                  \"name\": \"question\",\n                  \"color\": \"d876e3\",\n                  \"default\": true,\n                  \"description\": \"Further information is requested\",\n                  \"archived_at\": null,\n                  \"archived_by\": null\n                },\n                {\n                  \"id\": 10228506727,\n                  \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACYaqgZw\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/migrated-from-discussion\",\n                  \"name\": \"migrated-from-discussion\",\n                  \"color\": \"bfccd0\",\n                  \"default\": false,\n                  \"description\": \"\",\n                  \"archived_at\": null,\n                  \"archived_by\": null\n                }\n              ],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 2,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-02-17T14:17:00Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-16T03:37:01Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-16T03:37:01Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"> Originally posted by @gdiab on Feb 17, 2026 in [Discussion #365](https://github.com/entireio/cli/discussions/365) (Q&A)\\n\\nhad two commits.  A 1-line fix and a 357-line feature and the human_added value was the same for both?\\r\\n\\r\\nThis suggests it's measuring something structural rather than actual human keystrokes. What is it measuring?\\n\\n---\\n*Migrated from GitHub Discussions*\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/376/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/376/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1061\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1061/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1061/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1061/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/1061\",\n              \"id\": 4342725070,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABAti5zg\",\n              \"number\": 1061,\n              \"title\": \"PRD: Restructure CLI commands into noun groups (session/checkpoint/agent/doctor)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"id\": 881031,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [\n                {\n                  \"id\": 9924477906,\n                  \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACT4uD0g\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/enhancement\",\n                  \"name\": \"enhancement\",\n                  \"color\": \"a2eeef\",\n                  \"default\": true,\n                  \"description\": \"New feature or request\",\n                  \"archived_at\": null,\n                  \"archived_by\": null\n                }\n              ],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-04-28T11:22:37Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-04-29T16:56:37Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-04-29T16:56:37Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Problem Statement\\n\\nThe Entire CLI has accumulated 17 visible top-level commands plus a handful of hidden ones. Users hit several problems:\\n\\n- `entire --help` reads as a wall of verbs with no grouping. Discoverability suffers — useful commands like `attach`, `resume`, `rewind`, `explain`, and `trace` sit at the same depth as repo lifecycle commands like `enable`/`disable`/`status`.\\n- The naming verb-first instead of noun-verb diverges from the conventions users already know (`git`, `kubectl`, `gh`, `docker`). When a user thinks \\\"I want to inspect a checkpoint\\\", they look for a `checkpoint` noun and find none.\\n- `entire configure` is a vague catch-all that mixes interactive setup with agent CRUD via flags (`--agent`, `--remove`). The agent-management surface is buried in flag descriptions instead of being a first-class set of subcommands.\\n- `entire reset` overlaps with `entire clean` and is confusingly hidden.\\n- `entire search` is implemented but hidden, leaving useful checkpoint search undiscoverable.\\n- Several commonly needed troubleshooting capabilities are missing: there is no way to show the active session for the current directory, no direct viewer for a checkpoint by ID (it requires `explain --checkpoint <id>`), no way to diff two checkpoints, no way to tail the operational logs, and no way to produce a self-contained diagnostic bundle for bug reports.\\n- The existing `explain` command does three different jobs (list checkpoints on a branch, show a single checkpoint, show a session) routed through flags, which makes its own `--help` hard to scan and reason about.\\n\\n## Solution\\n\\nReorganize the command surface around four noun groups — `session`, `checkpoint`, `agent`, `doctor` — promote the troubleshooting capabilities to first-class subcommands, and fold overlapping verbs together. Keep the most common top-level verbs (`rewind`, `resume`, `attach`, `explain`, `trace`, `search`) as silent permanent aliases so existing muscle memory and documentation continue to work.\\n\\nThe change is rolled out in three phases. Phase 1 (this PRD) introduces the new structure entirely additively: every existing invocation continues to work unchanged, and the deprecated aliases (`configure`, `reset`) print a one-time stderr warning. Phase 2 (a later release) adds deprecation warnings to additional renamed top-levels if needed. Phase 3 (a future major release) hides the deprecated aliases.\\n\\nThe final shape:\\n\\n```\\nentire\\n├── enable\\n├── disable\\n├── status\\n├── login / logout\\n├── activity\\n├── dispatch\\n├── agent                             # was: configure\\n│   ├── list\\n│   ├── add <name>\\n│   └── remove <name>\\n├── session                           # alias: sessions\\n│   ├── list\\n│   ├── info <id> [--json]\\n│   ├── stop [id]\\n│   ├── attach <id>\\n│   ├── resume <branch>\\n│   └── current                       # NEW\\n├── checkpoint                        # aliases: cp, checkpoints\\n│   ├── list                          # NEW (was: explain default)\\n│   ├── show <id> [--short|--full|--raw|--generate]\\n│   ├── rewind [--to|--list|--logs-only|--reset]\\n│   ├── search [query]                # unhidden\\n│   └── diff <a> <b>                  # NEW\\n├── doctor                            # default: scan + fix\\n│   ├── trace\\n│   ├── logs [--tail|--follow]        # NEW\\n│   └── bundle                        # NEW\\n├── clean [--shadow]                  # absorbs `reset`\\n├── help / version\\n└── hidden: hooks, migrate, trail, configure (warn), reset (warn), …\\n```\\n\\nPermanent silent top-level aliases:\\n\\n| Alias | Resolves to |\\n|-------|-------------|\\n| `entire rewind` | `entire checkpoint rewind` |\\n| `entire resume` | `entire session resume` |\\n| `entire attach` | `entire session attach` |\\n| `entire explain` | `entire checkpoint show` (smart-route between checkpoint-id, commit-sha, session-id) |\\n| `entire trace` | `entire doctor trace` |\\n| `entire search` | `entire checkpoint search` (hidden alias) |\\n| `entire sessions` | `entire session` (Cobra alias) |\\n\\nDeprecated aliases with one-time stderr warning:\\n\\n| Alias | Resolves to |\\n|-------|-------------|\\n| `entire configure` | `entire agent` (interactive picker) |\\n| `entire configure --agent <x>` | `entire agent add <x>` |\\n| `entire configure --remove <x>` | `entire agent remove <x>` |\\n| `entire reset` | `entire clean --shadow` |\\n\\n## User Stories\\n\\n1. As a CLI user new to Entire, I want `entire --help` to fit in a screen and clearly group commands by domain, so that I can discover commands without scrolling.\\n2. As a CLI user familiar with `git`/`kubectl`/`gh`, I want a noun-verb structure so the CLI feels predictable and matches my muscle memory.\\n3. As a developer who frequently uses `entire rewind`, I want my existing one-word invocation to keep working forever, so that I do not have to retrain my muscle memory.\\n4. As a developer using `entire resume <branch>` and `entire attach <id>`, I want those one-word forms preserved as silent aliases of the new `session` subcommands, so that scripts and personal docs do not break.\\n5. As a developer who uses `entire explain <commit-sha>`, I want the smart-routing behavior preserved so a sha resolves to the underlying checkpoint and an id resolves to a checkpoint show.\\n6. As a CLI user managing AI agent integrations, I want to run `entire agent list` to see which agents are integrated in this repo, so that I do not have to read settings JSON.\\n7. As a CLI user adding an agent, I want `entire agent add claude-code` to be the canonical command, so that the action is self-documenting.\\n8. As a CLI user removing an agent, I want `entire agent remove claude-code` instead of `entire configure --remove claude-code`, so that the verb matches the intent.\\n9. As a CLI user running `entire configure` out of habit, I want the command to keep working with a single deprecation warning pointing me to `entire agent`, so that I have time to update my habits.\\n10. As a CLI user, I want `entire enable` to remain a focused on/off switch and not also handle agent CRUD, so that the lifecycle of the integration is easy to reason about.\\n11. As a developer debugging a session issue, I want `entire session current` to tell me which session is writing checkpoints in this directory right now, so that I do not have to guess from `sessions list`.\\n12. As a developer reviewing a checkpoint by ID, I want `entire checkpoint show <id>` to be a direct command instead of `entire explain --checkpoint <id>`, so that I do not have to remember a flag.\\n13. As a developer reviewing the recent activity on a branch, I want `entire checkpoint list` (the new default) to give me the previous `entire explain` no-arg behavior, so the most common view stays available.\\n14. As a developer comparing two points in a session, I want `entire checkpoint diff <a> <b>` so I can see the delta in files-touched, tokens, and transcripts between two checkpoints.\\n15. As a developer searching for a past checkpoint, I want `entire checkpoint search \\\"fix login\\\"` to be discoverable in `--help` instead of hidden, because the underlying capability is already implemented.\\n16. As a developer with a stale shadow branch, I want a single `entire clean --shadow` that does what `entire reset` used to do, so that there is one canonical \\\"clean up state\\\" command.\\n17. As a developer who learned `entire reset`, I want it to keep working with a deprecation warning, so I can migrate at my own pace.\\n18. As a developer triaging a hook failure, I want `entire doctor logs` to tail `.entire/logs/` instead of having to remember the path, so that I can see operational output quickly.\\n19. As a developer who needs to keep watching the logs while reproducing an issue, I want `entire doctor logs --follow` to behave like `tail -f`, so I can iterate without restarting the command.\\n20. As a developer reporting a bug, I want `entire doctor bundle` to produce a single zip of logs + settings + git snapshot, so that I can attach it to an issue without manual copy-pasting.\\n21. As a maintainer reviewing bug reports, I want users to be able to attach a deterministic diagnostic bundle, so that I have consistent context across reports.\\n22. As a developer, I want `entire doctor` (no args) to remain the existing scan-and-fix command, so that the most common usage stays unchanged.\\n23. As a developer, I want `entire doctor trace` to be the new home for the existing `entire trace` command, while the top-level `entire trace` keeps working silently.\\n24. As a developer, I want `entire sessions` (plural) to be a Cobra alias of `entire session`, so that I can use whichever form feels natural.\\n25. As a CLI maintainer, I want every Phase 1 change to be additive so that no user-visible invocation breaks at release time.\\n26. As a CLI maintainer, I want deprecation warnings to print only once per process so that scripts running many subcommands do not spam stderr.\\n27. As a CLI maintainer, I want the new noun groups to be wired through small, testable modules (agent CRUD, checkpoint view, checkpoint diff, alias factory, deprecation warner) so that group commands are thin Cobra wrappers around tested cores.\\n28. As a CLI maintainer, I want the `agent` package to be Cobra-free so that its CRUD logic is reusable and testable in isolation.\\n29. As a CLI maintainer, I want `checkpointview` to be Cobra-free so that the formatting logic for `checkpoint list`, `checkpoint show`, and the `explain` alias is shared and golden-tested.\\n30. As a CLI maintainer, I want one alias factory used by all seven silent aliases and both deprecated aliases, so that alias behavior is consistent and rare bugs are fixed in one place.\\n31. As a developer reading `CLAUDE.md`, I want the Key Directories section updated to reflect the new noun groups, so that contributors understand the layout.\\n32. As a CLI user using accessibility mode, I want every new interactive picker (e.g. the `agent` no-arg picker) to honor `ACCESSIBLE=1`, so that the new structure does not regress accessibility.\\n\\n## Implementation Decisions\\n\\n### Modules to build\\n\\n- **`agent` package (new)** — Cobra-free CRUD over agent integrations: `Add(ctx, name)`, `Remove(ctx, name)`, `List(ctx)`. Lifts logic out of the existing `setup.go` flows. Becomes the core powering `entire agent add|remove|list`, the deprecated `configure` alias, and the existing `enable` first-run bootstrap.\\n- **`checkpointview` package (new)** — Cobra-free list/show formatters with selectable verbosity (short, full, raw, default-detailed) and intent/summary generation. Lifted from `explain.go`. Backs `checkpoint list`, `checkpoint show`, and the `explain` top-level alias.\\n- **`checkpointdiff` package (new)** — Cobra-free diff over two checkpoint identifiers. Reads checkpoint trees via the existing `checkpoint.GitStore`. Returns a structured diff (file-touched delta, token delta, transcript delta) plus a renderer.\\n- **`doctorlogs` module (new)** — Reads `.entire/logs/`, supports `--tail N` (default last N lines) and `--follow` (polling, no fsnotify dependency).\\n- **`doctorbundle` module (new)** — Produces a zip containing the logs directory, current settings (project + local), `git status` / `git log -n 50` / `git remote -v` snapshot, CLI version, and Go runtime info. Returns the path to the produced archive.\\n- **`alias` helper (new, single file)** — `aliasOf(child *cobra.Command, opts ...AliasOption) *cobra.Command` produces a thin top-level Cobra command that delegates to the child's `RunE` while preserving args, flags, and exit codes. Optional `WithDeprecation(replacement string)` triggers a once-per-process stderr warning.\\n- **`deprecation` helper (new)** — `WarnOnce(cmd, replacement)` emits a single stderr line per process (guarded by a `sync.Once`).\\n\\n### Modules to modify\\n\\n- **`cmd/entire/cli/root.go`** — Stops registering the now-grouped commands at the root. Adds four new group roots (`session`, `checkpoint`, `agent`, `doctor`). Registers all silent aliases via the `alias` helper. Registers `configure` and `reset` as deprecated aliases.\\n- **`cmd/entire/cli/setup.go`** — Carves agent CRUD out into the new `agent` package. `enable` / `disable` stay; their bodies become thinner, focused on state toggle and first-run bootstrap.\\n- **`cmd/entire/cli/clean.go`** — Adds `--shadow` flag whose handler calls into the existing `manual_commit_reset` logic from the strategy package, replacing the hidden `reset` command.\\n- **`cmd/entire/cli/explain.go`** — Decomposed into `checkpoint_list.go`, `checkpoint_show.go`, and a slim alias wrapper that preserves the smart-routing between checkpoint id, commit sha, and session id. Shared formatting moves into the `checkpointview` package.\\n- **`cmd/entire/cli/sessions.go`** — Renamed/restructured to register children under a `session` parent. Adds `attach`, `resume`, and `current` as session subcommands. The plural `sessions` form remains as a Cobra alias on the parent.\\n- **`cmd/entire/cli/trace_cmd.go`** — Becomes a child of the `doctor` group; the existing top-level form remains as a silent alias.\\n- **`cmd/entire/cli/search_cmd.go`** — Becomes a child of the `checkpoint` group; the top-level form stays registered but hidden as an alias.\\n\\n### Architectural decisions\\n\\n- **Silent aliases** are produced by the `alias` helper to avoid duplicating Cobra command construction; they reuse the child's `RunE` directly, so behavior cannot drift.\\n- **Deprecated aliases** print exactly one warning per process, regardless of how many times the alias is invoked or recursed into.\\n- **No settings/feature flag** gates the rollout — Phase 1 is purely additive, so a runtime gate would add complexity without value.\\n- **`doctor` is both a runnable command and a parent**: bare `entire doctor` runs the existing scan-and-fix flow, while `entire doctor trace|logs|bundle` are subcommands.\\n- **Accessibility**: any new interactive picker (the `agent` group's no-arg flow) uses `NewAccessibleForm` per the existing convention.\\n- **Hidden infrastructure commands** (`hooks`, `git-hook`, `migrate`, `__send_analytics`, `curl-bash-post-install`, `trail`) are unchanged.\\n- **CLAUDE.md** is updated to document the new groups and the `agent`, `checkpointview`, and `checkpointdiff` packages under \\\"Key Directories\\\". The \\\"Code Patterns\\\" section gains a brief note describing the alias and deprecation helpers.\\n\\n### API contracts\\n\\n- The deprecation warning format is fixed: `Warning: 'entire <old>' is deprecated; use 'entire <new>' instead.` printed to stderr, exit code unchanged.\\n- `entire doctor bundle` writes its archive to a deterministic path under the OS temp directory and prints that path to stdout (so it is shell-pipeable).\\n- `entire doctor logs --follow` exits cleanly on SIGINT.\\n- `entire checkpoint diff <a> <b>` accepts checkpoint IDs (12-hex prefix accepted) and returns a non-zero exit code only on lookup failure, not on a non-empty diff.\\n\\n### Out-of-band changes\\n\\n- Update getting-started docs and `gettingStarted` constant in `root.go` to reference `entire enable` (already canonical) and remove any lingering `entire configure` references where appropriate, while keeping the deprecation alias functional.\\n\\n## Testing Decisions\\n\\nA good test exercises external behavior: command-line invocation, output, exit code, and observable state changes (files written, settings updated, archives produced). Tests should not assert on Cobra internals or pin specific log strings unless those strings are part of the user contract. Tests prefer `testutil.InitRepo` over raw `git.PlainInit` per CLAUDE.md, and every test calls `t.Parallel()` unless it modifies process-global state.\\n\\n### Tested modules\\n\\n- **`agent` package** — Add (new agent + idempotent re-add), Remove (existing + missing), List (empty + populated). Verifies hooks installation/uninstallation side effects on a temp repo.\\n- **`checkpointview` package** — Golden tests for short / full / raw renderings against fixture transcripts. Asserts intent/summary fallbacks when no AI summary is present.\\n- **`checkpointdiff` package** — Diff between two synthetic checkpoints (file-touched delta, token delta), empty diff for identical inputs, error path for missing checkpoint.\\n- **`alias` helper** — Top-level alias forwards args, flags, and exit codes to child. Deprecated alias prints exactly one stderr line per process even when invoked twice in the same process.\\n- **`clean --shadow`** — Removes shadow branch and session state files for current HEAD; behaves identically to the old `reset` command on equivalent fixtures.\\n- **`doctor logs`** — Returns last N lines from a fixture log directory; `--follow` exits on context cancellation.\\n- **`doctor bundle`** — Produced zip exists at the printed path and contains the expected entries (logs, settings.json, git snapshot file, version info).\\n\\n### Skipped (or only smoke-tested)\\n\\n- Cobra wiring in `root.go` is not unit-tested; coverage comes from the alias and group children's tests.\\n- Existing tests for `rewind`, `resume`, `attach`, `explain`, `trace`, `search`, `sessions`, `configure`, and `reset` continue to pass against the alias surface; no new tests are added there in Phase 1.\\n\\n### Prior art\\n\\n- Integration tests in `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/` cover hook-driven flows using `testutil.InitRepo` and `execx.NonInteractive` — the new bundle/logs tests follow the same pattern.\\n- Existing `explain_test.go`, `sessions_test.go`, and `clean_test.go` are the closest reference for command-level test shape.\\n- Strategy package tests demonstrate fixture-based shadow-branch setup that the `clean --shadow` test reuses.\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n\\n- Phase 2 (additional deprecation warnings) and Phase 3 (hiding deprecated aliases). Scheduled for later releases once Phase 1 lands.\\n- Renaming or restructuring the hidden infrastructure commands (`hooks`, `git-hook`, `migrate`, `trail`, `__send_analytics`, `curl-bash-post-install`).\\n- Any changes to checkpoint storage, session state machine, or strategy semantics. The new `checkpoint`/`session` groups are reorganizations of existing capabilities, not new behavior.\\n- Adding `checkpoint replay`, `update` (self-update), `feedback`/`report`, or any other commands floated during exploration but not selected.\\n- Changes to telemetry events. The `__send_analytics` subprocess is unchanged.\\n- Any refactor of `activity` or `dispatch`.\\n\\n## Further Notes\\n\\n- Phase 1 is intentionally additive so that `mise run test:ci` should remain green throughout. The integration test suite already invokes the existing top-level commands, which continue to work via aliases.\\n- The Vogon canary suite must run after the changes (`mise run test:e2e:canary`) to verify the new structure does not regress hook-driven flows; no Vogon changes are anticipated since prompt wording does not change.\\n- Documentation updates land in the same PR: `CLAUDE.md` Key Directories section, getting-started snippet in `root.go`, and any inline references in `--help` output that still mention the old names should be reviewed for accuracy.\\n- Future work to consider after Phase 1 lands: `checkpoint replay <id>` (re-run a captured prompt against current HEAD), `update` (CLI self-update partner to the existing `curl-bash-post-install`), and `report`/`feedback` (one-shot bug submission using `doctor bundle`).\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1061/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1061/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/930\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/930/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/930/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/930/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/930\",\n              \"id\": 4248015777,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M79M5Oh\",\n              \"number\": 930,\n              \"title\": \"DROD CLI : failed to capture pre-task state: tool_use_id is required\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"SvenMeyer\",\n                \"id\": 25609,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjA5\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25609?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/SvenMeyer\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/SvenMeyer\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/SvenMeyer/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/SvenMeyer/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/SvenMeyer/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/SvenMeyer/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/SvenMeyer/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/SvenMeyer/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/SvenMeyer/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/SvenMeyer/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/SvenMeyer/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [\n                {\n                  \"id\": 9924477887,\n                  \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACT4uDvw\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/bug\",\n                  \"name\": \"bug\",\n                  \"color\": \"d73a4a\",\n                  \"default\": true,\n                  \"description\": \"Something isn't working\",\n                  \"archived_at\": null,\n                  \"archived_by\": null\n                }\n              ],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 2,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-04-12T12:34:25Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-16T14:01:18Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-16T14:01:18Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"### What happened?\\n\\nI am getting quite some error with factory.ai DROID CLI now.\\n```\\n$ entire --version\\nEntire CLI 0.5.4 (746a74cd)\\nGo version: go1.26.2\\nOS/Arch: linux/amd64\\n```\\n\\n\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Entire CLI version\\n\\n0.5.4\\n\\n### OS and architecture\\n\\nArchLinux / Manjaro KDE\\n\\n### Agent\\n\\nDOID CLI\\n\\n### Terminal\\n\\nKDE Konsole\\n\\n### Logs / debug output\\n\\n```bash\\nHOOKS  PreToolUse → Task\\n └─ Script: entire hooks factoryai-droid pre-tool-use\\n └─ Result : Exit code: 1\\n   stderr:\\n   failed to capture pre-task state: tool_use_id is required\\n\\n HOOKS  PreToolUse → Task\\n └─ Script: entire hooks factoryai-droid pre-tool-use\\n └─ Result : Exit code: 1\\n   stderr:\\n   failed to capture pre-task state: tool_use_id is required\\n\\n   can you write the plan to `docs-dev/tasks/v0.2.2-openfort-implementation-with-onboarding.md` and    \\n   mark `docs-dev/tasks/v0.2.1-openfort-implementation-part-2.md` as superseeded                       \\n                                                                                                       \\n   then commit and push it all                                                                         \\n\\n HOOKS  PostToolUse → Task\\n └─ Script: entire hooks factoryai-droid post-tool-use\\n └─ Result : Exit code: 1\\n   stderr:\\n   failed to parse hook event: failed to parse hook input: json: cannot unmarshal string into Go struct\\n    field postToolHookInputRaw.tool_response of type struct { AgentID string \\\"json:\\\\\\\"agentId\\\\\\\"\\\" }\\n```\\n\\n### Additional context\\n\\nI had no problems with v0.5.3 afaik\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/930/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/930/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": \"duplicate\",\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/363\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/363/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/363/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/363/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/363\",\n              \"id\": 3949743876,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M7rbE8E\",\n              \"number\": 363,\n              \"title\": \"Scrub sensitive data (PII & secrets) from LLM context and checkpoints\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"ishaan812\",\n                \"id\": 70190533,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMTkwNTMz\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70190533?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ishaan812\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/ishaan812\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ishaan812/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ishaan812/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ishaan812/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ishaan812/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ishaan812/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ishaan812/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ishaan812/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ishaan812/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ishaan812/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [\n                {\n                  \"id\": 9924477906,\n                  \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACT4uD0g\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/enhancement\",\n                  \"name\": \"enhancement\",\n                  \"color\": \"a2eeef\",\n                  \"default\": true,\n                  \"description\": \"New feature or request\",\n                  \"archived_at\": null,\n                  \"archived_by\": null\n                }\n              ],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 2,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-02-16T22:03:12Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-18T17:50:59Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-03-18T17:50:59Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Problem\\n\\nWhen using Entire with agents, sensitive data can end up in session transcripts, checkpoints, and persisted metadata. Agents often pull from tools that contain PII or secrets:\\n\\n- **Issue trackers** (Linear, Jira) — ticket descriptions, assignee emails, customer-facing content, internal IDs\\n- **Git history** — commit messages, branch names, diff context that reference users or sensitive work\\n- **Team chat** (Slack, Discord) — when agents read channels or threads with user data, meeting links, or credentials\\n- **Internal APIs / databases** — query results, API responses that return user records\\n- **Config and env** — `.env` values, API keys, tokens that surface in tool outputs or error logs\\n\\nExamples of what can leak: emails, names, phone numbers, addresses, meeting links, API keys, access tokens, internal IDs, Slack tokens, OAuth credentials.\\n\\nFor teams rolling out Entire, this creates friction — especially when sessions touch production-ish data or shared tooling. Developers need stronger guarantees that PII and secrets get redacted before anything is stored or synced.\\n\\n**Note:** The CLI already redacts many secret patterns (API keys, tokens) before writing checkpoints. This request is about extending that to PII and making it configurable.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Desired Behavior\\n\\n1. **Before any trajectory or context is persisted** (locally or remotely), pass it through a PII + secrets filter.\\n\\n2. **The filter should:**\\n   - Redact common PII (emails, phone numbers, addresses, etc.)\\n   - Redact known secrets (API keys, tokens) — partially exists today\\n   - Allow users to add custom patterns for their stack (e.g. Linear ticket IDs, Jira keys, internal identifiers)\\n\\n3. **Redaction should be clearly marked** — e.g. `[REDACTED_EMAIL]`, `[REDACTED_SECRET]` — so checkpoints remain useful for debugging without leaking raw data.\\n\\n4. **Configurable** — Users should be able to toggle categories (PII vs secrets) and add custom rules, ideally via settings.\\n\\n5. **Run early** — Scrubbing should happen as close to the “edge” as possible so sensitive content never leaves the local environment unfiltered.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Proposed Approach\\n\\n- Extend the existing redaction layer to support PII patterns (emails, phones, addresses)\\n- Add typed replacement tokens instead of a generic string\\n- Add a config section (e.g. in `settings.json`) to toggle categories and define custom patterns\\n- Consider a Go PII library as a starting point and extend for common SaaS identifiers\\n\\nA built-in, configurable scrubbing layer would make it safer for teams to adopt Entire when sessions touch sensitive tooling or data. Happy to iterate and work on this with maintainers. An initial PR could focus on a minimal pass for secrets + common PII, then expand to configurable patterns.\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/363/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 1,\n                \"+1\": 1,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/363/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/983\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/983/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/983/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/983/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/983\",\n              \"id\": 4289017592,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M7_pTb4\",\n              \"number\": 983,\n              \"title\": \"Bug: External Agent $PATH auto-discovery fails for non-built-in and passive agents (v0.5.5)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"braverock\",\n                \"id\": 1668391,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NjgzOTE=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1668391?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/braverock\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/braverock\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/braverock/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/braverock/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/braverock/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/braverock/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/braverock/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/braverock/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/braverock/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/braverock/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/braverock/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [\n                {\n                  \"id\": 9924477887,\n                  \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACT4uDvw\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/bug\",\n                  \"name\": \"bug\",\n                  \"color\": \"d73a4a\",\n                  \"default\": true,\n                  \"description\": \"Something isn't working\",\n                  \"archived_at\": null,\n                  \"archived_by\": null\n                }\n              ],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [\n                {\n                  \"login\": \"ashtom\",\n                  \"id\": 70720,\n                  \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzIw\",\n                  \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70720?v=4\",\n                  \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom\",\n                  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/ashtom\",\n                  \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/followers\",\n                  \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/following{/other_user}\",\n                  \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                  \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                  \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/subscriptions\",\n                  \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/orgs\",\n                  \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/repos\",\n                  \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/events{/privacy}\",\n                  \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/received_events\",\n                  \"type\": \"User\",\n                  \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                  \"site_admin\": false\n                },\n                {\n                  \"login\": \"blackgirlbytes\",\n                  \"id\": 22990146,\n                  \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTkwMTQ2\",\n                  \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22990146?v=4\",\n                  \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/blackgirlbytes\",\n                  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/blackgirlbytes\",\n                  \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/blackgirlbytes/followers\",\n                  \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/blackgirlbytes/following{/other_user}\",\n                  \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/blackgirlbytes/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                  \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/blackgirlbytes/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                  \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/blackgirlbytes/subscriptions\",\n                  \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/blackgirlbytes/orgs\",\n                  \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/blackgirlbytes/repos\",\n                  \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/blackgirlbytes/events{/privacy}\",\n                  \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/blackgirlbytes/received_events\",\n                  \"type\": \"User\",\n                  \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                  \"site_admin\": false\n                }\n              ],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 3,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-04-18T19:51:27Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-12T19:03:17Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-05-12T19:03:17Z\",\n              \"assignee\": {\n                \"login\": \"ashtom\",\n                \"id\": 70720,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzIw\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70720?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/ashtom\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"# Bug: External Agent `$PATH` auto-discovery fails for non-built-in and passive agents (v0.5.5)\\n\\n## Description\\nWhile building an external agent for the Zed Editor (`entire-agent-zed`), we discovered several logic gaps in `entire` v0.5.5 that prevent external agents on the `$PATH` from being correctly discovered, configured, and attached. \\n\\nThe protocol documentation states that placing a valid `entire-agent-<name>` binary on the `$PATH` is sufficient for auto-discovery, but several CLI commands currently bypass or prematurely filter out these discoveries.\\n\\n## Issues Identified\\n\\n1. **`entire attach` fails instantly**: \\n   `cmd/entire/cli/attach.go` does not call `external.DiscoverAndRegisterAlways()`. When passing `--agent zed`, the CLI validates against the hardcoded registry and fails with `unknown agent: zed` before `$PATH` discovery is ever attempted.\\n\\n2. **`entire status` hides external agents**: \\n   `cmd/entire/cli/status.go` does not invoke `$PATH` discovery before iterating the registry. External agents correctly enabled in `.entire/settings.json` will not appear in the status output.\\n\\n3. **`entire configure` gatekeeping**: \\n   In `cmd/entire/cli/setup.go`, the interactive menu explicitly filters out any discovered agents where `AsHookSupport(ag)` is false. This prevents \\\"passive\\\" GUI agents (agents that act as database tailers and rely on standard git hooks rather than their own start/stop hooks) from being enabled via the UI.\\n\\n4. **Context-less Discovery Silently Fails**: \\n   In `cmd/entire/cli/agent/external/discovery.go`, `DiscoverAndRegister` checks `settings.IsExternalAgentsEnabled(ctx)`. If the command is triggered in a context where the local `.entire` settings file path isn't perfectly resolved, it defaults to `false` and skips `$PATH` scanning entirely.\\n\\n## Steps to Reproduce\\n1. Place a valid external agent binary (e.g., `entire-agent-mock`) on your `$PATH` that returns valid `info` JSON.\\n2. Run `entire attach <session-id> --agent mock` -> Fails with `unknown agent`.\\n3. Run `entire status` -> Agent is not listed.\\n\\n## Proposed Solution\\nWe have successfully patched these issues locally and verified them against the test suite. The minimal fixes involve:\\n- Adding `external.DiscoverAndRegisterAlways(cmd.Context())` to the `RunE` setup in `attach.go`.\\n- Adding `external.DiscoverAndRegisterAlways(ctx)` to `runStatus` in `status.go`.\\n- Removing the `AsHookSupport` exclusion block in `setup.go`'s `detectOrSelectAgent` flow so passive agents can be selected.\\n- Adjusting the strict `settings.json` check in `discovery.go` so hooks can reliably find external binaries.\\n\\nI have attached a `.patch` file containing these fixes to this issue.\\n\\n### Patch File\\n```diff\\nFrom 8dc6e70a2398982ce90daf980b4c1000446f6f55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001\\nFrom: \\\"Brian G. Peterson\\\" <brian@braverock.com>\\nDate: Sat, 18 Apr 2026 13:31:06 -0500\\nSubject: [PATCH] fix: external agent auto-discovery logic for passive binaries\\n\\n- Call DiscoverAndRegisterAlways in attach.go so it can find external agents\\n- Call DiscoverAndRegisterAlways in status.go so external agents appear in the status menu\\n- Remove AsHookSupport gatekeeper in setup.go to allow configuring passive GUI external agents\\n- Bypass settings.json check in discovery.go so external agents can be found during global hooks\\n---\\n cmd/entire/cli/agent/external/discovery.go | 5 -----\\n cmd/entire/cli/attach.go                   | 4 ++++\\n cmd/entire/cli/status.go                   | 3 +++\\n 3 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)\\n\\ndiff --git a/cmd/entire/cli/agent/external/discovery.go b/cmd/entire/cli/agent/external/discovery.go\\nindex 2f5f944b..f48af391 100644\\n--- a/cmd/entire/cli/agent/external/discovery.go\\n+++ b/cmd/entire/cli/agent/external/discovery.go\\n@@ -12,7 +12,6 @@ import (\\n \\t\\\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\\\"\\n \\t\\\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/types\\\"\\n \\t\\\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/logging\\\"\\n-\\t\\\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/settings\\\"\\n )\\n \\n const (\\n@@ -29,10 +28,6 @@ const discoveryTimeout = 10 * time.Second\\n // Errors during discovery are logged but do not prevent other agents from loading.\\n // Discovery is skipped when the external_agents setting is not enabled.\\n func DiscoverAndRegister(ctx context.Context) {\\n-\\tif !settings.IsExternalAgentsEnabled(ctx) {\\n-\\t\\tlogging.Debug(ctx, \\\"external agent discovery disabled (external_agents not enabled in settings)\\\")\\n-\\t\\treturn\\n-\\t}\\n \\tdiscoverAndRegister(ctx)\\n }\\n \\ndiff --git a/cmd/entire/cli/attach.go b/cmd/entire/cli/attach.go\\nindex e75a01f1..42c243a6 100644\\n--- a/cmd/entire/cli/attach.go\\n+++ b/cmd/entire/cli/attach.go\\n@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@ import (\\n \\t\\\"time\\\"\\n \\n \\t\\\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\\\"\\n+\\t\\\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/external\\\"\\n \\t\\\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli\\\"\\n \\t\\\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/types\\\"\\n \\tcpkg \\\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint\\\"\\n@@ -57,6 +58,9 @@ Supported agents: claude-code, gemini, opencode, codex, cursor, copilot-cli, fac\\n \\t\\t\\tif checkDisabledGuard(cmd.Context(), cmd.OutOrStdout()) {\\n \\t\\t\\t\\treturn nil\\n \\t\\t\\t}\\n+\\n+\\t\\t\\texternal.DiscoverAndRegisterAlways(cmd.Context())\\n+\\n \\t\\t\\tagentName := types.AgentName(agentFlag)\\n \\t\\t\\treturn runAttach(cmd.Context(), cmd.OutOrStdout(), args[0], agentName, force)\\n \\t\\t},\\ndiff --git a/cmd/entire/cli/status.go b/cmd/entire/cli/status.go\\nindex 991a2dcb..a83c3dd0 100644\\n--- a/cmd/entire/cli/status.go\\n+++ b/cmd/entire/cli/status.go\\n@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@ import (\\n \\t\\\"strings\\\"\\n \\t\\\"time\\\"\\n \\n+\\t\\\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/external\\\"\\n \\t\\\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/paths\\\"\\n \\t\\\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/session\\\"\\n \\t\\\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/settings\\\"\\n@@ -51,6 +52,8 @@ func newStatusCmd() *cobra.Command {\\n }\\n \\n func runStatus(ctx context.Context, w io.Writer, detailed, jsonOutput bool) error {\\n+\\texternal.DiscoverAndRegisterAlways(ctx)\\n+\\n \\tif jsonOutput {\\n \\t\\treturn runStatusJSON(ctx, w)\\n \\t}\\n-- \\n2.51.0\\n\\n```\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/983/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/983/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            }\n          ],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 235,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2715\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2715/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2715/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2715/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2715\",\n              \"id\": 5769418051,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABHbK90w\",\n              \"number\": 2715,\n              \"title\": \"feat(checkpoint): upload checkpoints in the background after the user's push\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-08T21:52:00Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-06T19:52:33Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2715\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2715\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2715.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2715.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1530\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n> **Scope:** the main change here is the background checkpoint upload (section 2). Section 1, the bounded chunked push, is also split out on its own as #3018 (fixes #2986, the Windows command-line limit). Once #3018 merges, merging main into this branch drops it from this diff.\\n\\n## Problem\\nThe pre-push hook pushed every queued checkpoint ref in one `git push` with no deadline. #2522 bounded only the per-ref retry fallback. A large backlog, a slow uplink or an unreachable SSH host could hold the user's own `git push` for minutes or indefinitely, which pushes users toward `--no-verify` and leaves checkpoints untracked.\\n\\nThe hook's push also got the user's own push **rejected**. GitHub rejects a push whose pack arrives within about a second of another push to the same repository finishing (`(failed)`, `missing necessary objects`, `fatal error in commit_refs`), and it rejects the later one. The hook's checkpoint push finished milliseconds before git sent the user's pack: 7 of 16 user pushes were rejected against a real GitHub repository, and 3 of 6 for `git push && git push <tag>`.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n### 1. Bounded, chunked batch (`fix(checkpoint): bound the git-refs pre-push batch push`)\\n- **Chunked push:** queued refs are pushed in chunks of up to `checkpointRefPushChunkSize` (200), and each chunk leaves the queue as soon as it lands. A backlog drains across pushes instead of being cut at the same point every time.\\n- **Adaptive chunk size:** a chunk cut by the budget quarters the next chunk size, down to one ref, and a push that lands everything doubles it back (`PushQueue.ChunkSizeHint`). A link too slow to land a full chunk within the budget would otherwise cut the same chunk on every push and never make progress. A budget cut ends the flush (\\\"Stopped pushing\\\") rather than running the per-ref fallback on a spent budget, and moves the cut chunk to the back of the queue.\\n- **One budget:** in the pre-push path, the batch and the per-ref fallback share one `checkpointFlushBudget` (2m). Worst case was unbounded + 2m; it is now 2m.\\n- **Failed chunks:** a failed chunk doesn't stop later chunks; only its refs go to the per-ref fallback.\\n- **Stopping early:** batching stops after 2 consecutive failed chunks, an SSH auth failure, the budget, or an interrupt. The first chunk is always attempted.\\n- **Partial delivery:** if a later chunk fails after earlier ones landed, the pre-push still commits the captured sync remote and shows its warnings, based on how many refs actually landed.\\n- **Migration push:** the explicit migration push (`PushQueuedCheckpointRefs`) keeps the batch unbounded, and its per-ref fallback gets a fresh budget after the batch.\\n- **Unreachable remote:** if git couldn't connect on the first chunk the remote saw (nothing landed or was rejected before it), the flush stops after that one attempt. It prints that line and leaves the queue in order.\\n  - \\\"Couldn't connect\\\" means a connect-phase failure from ssh or curl: unresolvable host, or a failed connect.\\n  - The printed line has credentials redacted, control bytes stripped, and is capped.\\n  - The match is deliberately narrow. It skips localized strerror text, mid-transfer timeouts and `remote:` lines; a miss falls back to the bounded fallback.\\n- **SSH connect timeout:** OpenSSH gets `-o ConnectTimeout=60` under the hook unless the command sets one. A value in `~/.ssh/config` is overridden; 60s leaves room for slow-starting proxies.\\n- **Redaction helper:** the free-text credential redaction helper moves to `gitremote` so the push path and the plugin path share it.\\n\\n### 2. Background upload, after the user's push\\nThe pre-push hook no longer pushes checkpoint refs. The upload runs in one detached `entire __checkpoint_upload` worker per repository, after the user's push.\\n- **Hand-off:** the hook records its `git push`, hands the queue to the worker, prints \\\"Uploading checkpoints in the background\\\", and returns. This replaces the earlier 10s inline window.\\n  - A push with nothing queued is recorded too, so a worker still uploading waits for it.\\n  - The recorded PID is the hook's nearest `git` ancestor, found by walking up at most 6 processes, which leaves room for `sh` and hook managers.\\n  - On macOS and Linux the git process is found and fingerprinted through `proclive` (`CurrentAncestry`, `Check`), the same package session liveness uses. `proclive` cannot introspect Windows, so there a Toolhelp snapshot and the process creation time stand in, and the wait uses the process handle.\\n- **Wait, then upload:** before each pass the worker waits for every recorded push to exit (`waitForUserPushes`).\\n  - It then settles for 1.5s and checks again, so a chained push (`git push && git push --tags`) gets recorded and waited for too.\\n  - A push whose git process wasn't found gets a fixed 3s delay. A reused PID (its start time changed) or an unreaped zombie counts as exited.\\n  - Each recorded push is waited for until it exits, up to 10m; after 2m no new rounds are taken.\\n  - The worker checks again between chunks, so a push made during a long upload is waited for too. That wait counts against the pass budget.\\n- **Retry for the race:** if GitHub still rejects the worker's own push with that error, `batchPushCheckpointRefs` retries it twice, after 1s and 2s. The match is on git's `--porcelain` `[remote rejected] (failed|missing necessary objects)` lines (and the human-readable form); every other failure takes the existing path. No measured run needed it.\\n- **Checkpoints land about 1–4s after `git push` returns.** Push-triggered server work (runners, monitors, trail review) doesn't read checkpoint data, so it doesn't depend on the order.\\n- **One flush at a time:** every flush serialises on an upload lock in the git common dir. A push that finds the lock held leaves a request; whoever releases the lock starts a worker for it. The migration push waits, bounded, and says so.\\n- **Decisions stay with the hook:**\\n  - The hook resolves the OPF decision before taking the lock, where it can still prompt. The worker carries it as run/skip/unset and never re-resolves it.\\n  - The worker uploads nothing if settings or redaction can't be loaded, or if a required OPF run can't happen in its process.\\n  - The sync-remote capture is committed only after the worker's own delivery lands.\\n- **Visible:** the worker records its last run. The next push prints a failure or announcement once — with the remote's rejection reason (e.g. a push-protection unblock URL) or the SSH hint, not only \\\"checkpoint ref push failed\\\" — and `entire status` shows \\\"uploading in the background\\\" or the last stop reason.\\n- **Bounded:** each worker pass has a 10m budget, which bounds the batch too, and the run has 30m. Each chunk has a 75s stall timeout; a stalled chunk moves to the back of the queue and quarters the chunks after it in the same pass (down to 2), except a single ref, which gets the pass budget.\\n- **Nothing left waiting:** a worker that ends with a request still pending (out of passes or time) starts another for it.\\n- **Stays inline (never a background process)** in CI, with `strategy_options.background_checkpoint_upload: false`, and under `ENTIRE_CHECKPOINT_UPLOAD_FOREGROUND=1` (test harnesses).\\n  - A flush that pushed refs then waits 1.2s before the hook returns, so git's pack doesn't land right behind it.\\n  - The harness env skips that wait, because its remotes are local paths, which never reject back-to-back pushes.\\n- **`trail create` uploads after its own push:** it runs `git push` with `ENTIRE_CHECKPOINT_UPLOAD_AFTER_PUSH=1`.\\n  - The hook records the request (remote, OPF decision, pending capture) without starting a worker.\\n  - The push is recorded as a user push, so the in-process upload settles after it and a running worker waits for it.\\n  - After the push returns, the command runs that pass in-process (`strategy.UploadRequestedCheckpoints`). \\\"Pushed branch\\\" still means the checkpoints went too.\\n  - If the push fails, the request it recorded is dropped; the refs stay queued for the next push.\\n- **`execx.SpawnDetached`:**\\n  - Children get the null device instead of a pipe (ported from the OPF scan worker branch).\\n  - Inherited descriptors are marked close-on-exec before the spawn. Without that, the worker inherited the write end of `git-remote-entire`'s stdin, and `git push` to an `entire://` remote couldn't exit until the worker did.\\n\\n### 3. plink fix (`fix(checkpoint): give plink -batch instead of OpenSSH -o options`)\\nThis bug is separate from the hang, but it lives in the same function.\\n\\nThe hook appended `-o BatchMode=yes` to any ssh command, so plink rejected it and every hook checkpoint push failed for PuTTY users. The variant is now resolved the way git does it (`GIT_SSH_VARIANT`, `ssh.variant`, then the program name parsed like `split_cmdline`):\\n\\n| Client | Options added |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| OpenSSH | `BatchMode` and `ConnectTimeout`, unchanged |\\n| plink / putty | `-batch` |\\n| TortoisePlink, `simple` | none; env unchanged |\\n| Unrecognized wrappers | `BatchMode` only, as before (#1523) |\\n\\nA `GIT_SSH` path is shell-quoted when rewritten into `GIT_SSH_COMMAND`, so a path with spaces stays one word. `auto` defers to name detection, as in git. If the git config naming the ssh command can't be read, the environment is left unchanged.\\n\\n## Measured\\n\\n### Live test (current head)\\n**Live test: PR head `8e12a9e363` vs main `ed3124066b`**, with the real `entire` pre-push hook. The checkpoints are synthetic.\\n\\n**Large backlog to GitHub over SSH.** 200 checkpoints × 500KB (about 100MB). The remote already holds about 4,000 checkpoint refs.\\n\\n| | `git push` returned | all checkpoints on GitHub |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| main, run 1 | 26.4s | 28.0s |\\n| main, run 2 | 33.7s | 35.0s |\\n| this PR, run 1 | 2.2s | 27.6s |\\n| this PR, run 2 | 2.5s | 33.4s |\\n\\nThe user gets their terminal back about 10× sooner. Delivery time is unchanged; the upload runs after the push instead of inside it.\\n\\n**Hang.** A local remote stalls for 5 minutes on any push carrying checkpoint refs, standing in for a hung SSH connection or a very slow link. 50 × 100KB.\\n\\n| | `git push` returned |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| main | 300.6s (blocked for the whole stall) |\\n| this PR | 0.4s |\\n\\nOn this PR the background upload gave up on the stalled chunk after its 75s limit and left the refs queued. The next push delivered them.\\n\\n**Small backlog.** 5 × 100KB to GitHub. `git push` takes 3.2s on this PR and 6.3s on main. The checkpoints land about 2s later than on main (at about 10s instead of about 8s), because the worker waits for git to exit and then settles for 1.5s.\\n\\n**User push rejected** on GitHub (fresh checkpoint queued per push):\\n\\n| | before (`e4be83da22`) | this PR |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| single push | 7/16 | 0/37 |\\n| `git push && git push <tag>` | 3/6 | 0/10 |\\n\\n### Earlier measurements\\nBoth remotes were real throwaway repos. Each run uploaded 200 checkpoints of about 100KB each (roughly 20MB) through the pre-push hook.\\n\\n| Remote | v0.10.6 | this PR, chunks of 25 (earlier head) | this PR, chunks up to 200 |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| GitHub (ssh) | 7s | 20s | 7s |\\n| Entire | 4s | 11s | 4s |\\n\\nOn a simulated slow link (1s per push plus 0.75s per ref), v0.10.6 blocked `git push` for 152s. This PR caps the wait at the 2m budget and leaves the rest queued for the next push.\\n\\nBackground upload at the earlier 10s-inline head, 200 queued checkpoints. `git push` blocked / when all checkpoints were on the remote:\\n\\n| Scenario | main | earlier head (10s inline) |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| GitHub, 5 checkpoints | 6s | 5–6s, delivered inline |\\n| Entire, 5 checkpoints | 2–4s | 2–3s, delivered inline |\\n| GitHub, 200 × 100KB | 12s | 9s, delivered inline |\\n| Entire, 200 × 100KB | 11s | 9s, delivered inline |\\n| GitHub, 200 × 500KB | 28s | 13s, all landed at 57s |\\n| Entire, 200 × 500KB | 41s | 13s, all landed at 57s |\\n| Simulated slow link | 151s | 10s, all landed at 165s |\\n\\n## Known limitations\\n- With background upload off (CI, the setting), a very slow uplink still waits up to the 2m budget, and a backlog drains over several pushes.\\n- Checkpoints upload even when the user's own push is rejected (a non-fast-forward, say), as they did when the hook pushed them.\\n- A push started by hand while the worker's own push is in flight can still race it. The worker's retry covers its own push, but not the user's.\\n- The split and per-ref retries after a failed chunk don't wait for user pushes between their pushes.\\n- The same race likely exists on the git-branch (`entire/checkpoints/v1`) backend. That's out of scope here.\\n- `execx_unix.go` doesn't build on FreeBSD (`rlimit` field types). FreeBSD isn't a release target.\\n- The worker resolves settings from, and runs in, the worktree that spawned it. The queue is shared across worktrees, as before. On Windows, the worker's cwd blocks `git worktree remove` until the run ends.\\n- Chunks are capped by ref count, not bytes. Entire's remote helper buffers the whole pack in memory, so very large checkpoints could hit size limits; v0.10.6 sent the entire backlog in one push.\\n- Unrecognized ssh wrappers that reject `-o` still get `BatchMode`; that behavior is unchanged.\\n\\n## Testing\\n- **New strategy tests:**\\n  - a backlog uploads in chunks;\\n  - the budget keeps landed chunks (fails without the fix);\\n  - a rejected chunk doesn't stop later chunks;\\n  - the batch stops after 2 consecutive failed chunks;\\n  - the migration batch has no budget;\\n  - an unreachable remote stops at once, using a fake ssh client: one attempt, cause printed, queue unchanged.\\n- **New remote tests:**\\n  - unreachable-remote detection, including false-positive cases;\\n  - ssh variant resolution (plink, quoted paths, `GIT_SSH_VARIANT`, `ssh.variant`);\\n  - `split_cmdline`-style parsing.\\n- **After-push tests:**\\n  - the hook hands off without pushing and records the user push, even with an empty queue;\\n  - the walk from a git alias, the way git runs a hook, finds git's PID;\\n  - the wait covers git exiting, a push recorded mid-wait, and the unknown-PID delay;\\n  - the retry matcher is tested against captured outputs, and the retry happens only on the race;\\n  - inline uploads settle;\\n  - `trail create`'s recorded upload runs in-process;\\n  - the integration test asserts the user's branch reaches the remote before the checkpoint refs.\\n- `mise run fmt && mise run lint` is clean, and the Windows and Linux builds vet clean.\\n- `mise run test:ci` fails locally only in tests that fail the same way on the unmodified head and pass in its CI (`TestPreviewNextCheckpoint`, `TestCheckpointListPending_Preview*`, a `TestDetectOrSelectAgent` flake).\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2715/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2715/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2550\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2550/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2550/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2550/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2550\",\n              \"id\": 5530524042,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABEdpDoA\",\n              \"number\": 2550,\n              \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): preserve newer same-ref queue updates\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Vishal202-rgb\",\n                \"id\": 188738250,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOCz_qyg\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/188738250?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Vishal202-rgb\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Vishal202-rgb\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Vishal202-rgb/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Vishal202-rgb/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Vishal202-rgb/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Vishal202-rgb/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Vishal202-rgb/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Vishal202-rgb/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Vishal202-rgb/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Vishal202-rgb/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Vishal202-rgb/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-21T17:49:08Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-21T17:52:28Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2550\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2550\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2550.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2550.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nFixes #2008.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Preserve a newer same-ref queue entry added while a checkpoint push is in flight.\\r\\n* Keep `readLocked` de-duplication behavior for `Drain` and `Peek`.\\r\\n* Add a regression test covering the same-ref enqueue race.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Testing\\r\\n\\r\\n* `git diff --check`\\r\\n* Added `TestPushQueue_RemovePreservesNewerSameRefEntry`\\r\\n\\r\\nNote: The Go test suite was not run locally because Go is not installed in the environment.\\r\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2550/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2550/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3113\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3113/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3113/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3113/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3113\",\n              \"id\": 6325872395,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABOVvD5Q\",\n              \"number\": 3113,\n              \"title\": \"fix(strategy): give a reserved checkpoint ID to one commit only\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n                \"id\": 26940511,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI2OTQwNTEx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Beehtrix\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 2,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-11T09:49:10Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-14T09:16:13Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3113\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3113\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3113.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3113.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes #3069.\\n\\nStacked on #3068, which is stacked on #3034 and #3005. The fix needs #3068's per-commit take: without it, the first commit's post-commit takes every stamp, including the fresh one the next commit now gets, and that commit would keep a trailer for a checkpoint that is never written (#3030). So this branch is built on #3068's head (e8250a77), and until those merge the diff here also shows their commits. This PR's own changes are the seven commits on top of e8250a77. After them, main is merged in (ae1c9ec3) to clear a conflict in `docs/development/checkpoint-implementation.md`: #3108 rewrote the session-state bullet right next to the commit-linking bullet that #3034 and #3068 change, and the merge keeps both. #3068's head is merged in after that as it moves, most recently 62a06a0d (7988c573), which brings main at ce16562b through #3034.\\n\\nThis is the shared reservation I raised in #3069, found while working on #3068. It changes when a reservation is handed out, and makes a post-commit wait briefly for an earlier one, so I'd value a review of the approach.\\n\\n## The bug (on main as well)\\n\\n`checkpointIDForSessions` gives a session's reserved checkpoint ID (`PendingCondensationID`) to every prepare-commit-msg until a post-commit condenses into it. git lets the next commit start once one is made, before its post-commit runs. So with a session holding reservation R:\\n\\n1. Commit A's prepare stamps R, and A lands.\\n2. Commit B's prepare runs before A's post-commit has condensed the session. The session still holds R, so B carries R too.\\n3. A's post-commit condenses the session into R and clears the reservation. R is now the session's `LastCheckpointID`.\\n4. B's post-commit targets R, which exists. `stampedByAnotherCommit` lets the session write there because R is its `LastCheckpointID`, so it condenses again and replaces the session's slot in R with the range since A.\\n\\nSo B names A's checkpoint, and A's checkpoint ends up holding B's work instead of its own. The first test below checks R's stored range: on #3068's head it starts at line 2 (B's range), not 0. That is a bit worse than I described in #3069, where I said B's work stays pending.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\n- **Prepare passes over a stamp another commit carries** (`stampCarriedInFlight`). It skips a reservation when prepare recorded stamping it, no post-commit has released that entry, and either:\\n  - a post-commit took the stamp and is still running. A post-commit only takes a stamp its commit carries, so this holds wherever HEAD has gone since, as when that commit was amended away;\\n  - or no post-commit has taken it yet, and a commit on HEAD's first parents, made since the HEAD it was stamped on, carries it (at most `maxCommitsInFlight` back).\\n\\n  The commit then gets the next session's reservation, or a fresh ID (`freeReservation`). After the check, prepare reads the session's reservation again, since A's post-commit may have condensed the session and released its entry since prepare loaded it.\\n- **A message that already names that stamp doesn't make it this commit's.** A message saved from A (`commit -F`, or `-C` of A) names R. Until A's post-commit took the stamp, prepare counted R as its own and added no trailer. `stampedTrailer` now passes over a stamp a commit made since carries, so B gets a trailer of its own.\\n- **Post-commit keeps the sessions entries of the stamps it takes until it returns** (`releaseStampedSessions`, deferred in `PostCommit`), marked with its process and the time (`stampTaker`). The take still removes the stamps at once. A later post-commit's take keeps such an entry while that process is alive, or for a minute where `proclive` can't tell (Windows, until #3071), and drops it once the process has stopped. `takeStampsIn` now returns entries only for the stamps it takes. It also leaves a stamp its commit carries when a commit before it, made since the stamp, carries it too (`carriedBefore`). That is a message saved from the earlier commit, so the stamp is that commit's, and its post-commit still finds it.\\n- **The later post-commit waits for the earlier one** (`awaitEarlierCondensations`, run from `PostCommit` through `settledSessions` together with the `beforeCondense` hook). B's post-commit can reach the session while it still reserves R and A's post-commit is still running. It used to skip the session then (\\\"preserving interrupted condensation with a different checkpoint ID\\\"), and with no other session condensing into B's ID, B's trailer named a checkpoint that is never written. It now waits for A's post-commit to condense the session, polling every 50 ms for at most 10 seconds, then reads the sessions again. It waits only for a post-commit that took its stamps before its own take. Each take marks the entries it takes with one time (`stampRecords.takenAt`), so of two post-commits, only the one that took later can wait for the other, and the two never wait for each other. This goes by take order rather than by how the commits relate, so it also covers an amend of A, and a commit made on top of that amend.\\n\\nWhat stays the same:\\n\\n- A commit retried on the same HEAD after an aborted attempt keeps the reservation. Its stamp was recorded on HEAD, so no commit made since carries it.\\n- Once the earlier post-commit is done, or has stopped, a session still holding the reservation wasn't condensed into it, and the next commit takes it, as on main.\\n\\n## Not covered\\n\\n- **A post-commit that hasn't taken its records yet.** The wait covers an earlier post-commit that has taken its stamp. If B's post-commit runs before A's has taken anything, that is the reordering #3068 lists under \\\"Post-commit finds its commit by reading HEAD\\\".\\n- **A wait that reaches its bound.** If A's post-commit takes more than 10 seconds to get to the session, B's goes on and skips the session, as before.\\n- **An earlier post-commit that skips the session.** A's post-commit can leave a session it was stamped for uncondensed, as the read-only gate does when another session claims A's files. The session then still reserves R, and B's post-commit skips it as a session reserving a different ID. If no other session condenses into B's ID, B's trailer names a checkpoint that is never written. B would have shared R before this change. Closing it means condensing a session into another ID while it still holds a reservation, which the guard that keeps an interrupted condensation from being written twice rules out.\\n- **A later commit whose session an earlier post-commit consumes.** If A's post-commit condenses all of an idle session's pending work before B's post-commit runs, B finds no overlap left and condenses nothing, so B's trailer names a checkpoint that is never written. That already happens on main whenever the session holds no reservation, since A and B then get fresh IDs of their own (#3120). A session holding a reservation used to give B the same ID as A, so B named A's checkpoint. Now B gets its own ID in that case too, and behaves the same way. Writing B's checkpoint from what prepare saw is a design call, so it's left to that issue.\\n- **Mixed binaries.** An older binary's prepare doesn't check, and its post-commit doesn't mark or keep the entries.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- `TestCommitHooks_NextCommitPreparedBeforePostCommitDoesNotShareTheReservation` drives the race through the hooks. On #3068's head (e8250a77) it fails twice: the second commit carries the reservation, and the first commit's checkpoint ends up with the second commit's range.\\n- `TestCommitHooks_LaterPostCommitWaitsForTheEarlierCondensation` drives the other ordering. A's post-commit is held after its take while B lands and B's post-commit runs. Without the wait, B's checkpoint is never written.\\n- `TestPrepareCommitMsg_SavedMessageNamingAnInFlightStampGetsItsOwn` prepares B with A's prepared message. Without the check, B gets no trailer of its own.\\n- `TestPrepareCommitMsg_RetryAfterAbortedAttemptKeepsTheReservation` guards the retry.\\n- `TestCheckpointIDForSessions_ReadsTheReservationAgain` covers prepare's second read, and `TestCheckpointIDForSessions_SkipsAReservationCarriedInFlight` covers the choice between sessions.\\n- Five tests cover when a stamp counts as carried: `TestStampCarriedInFlight_UntilItsPostCommitIsDone`, `TestStampCarriedInFlight_NotForAnAbandonedStamp`, `TestStampCarriedInFlight_ForACommitAmendedAway`, `TestTakeStampRecords_KeepsAnEntryWhileItsTakerRuns` and `TestTakeStampRecords_DropsAnEntryWhoseTakerStopped`.\\n- `TestAwaitEarlierCondensations_UntilTheSessionIsCondensed`, `_NotWhenNothingIsComing`, `_NotForALaterCommitsReservation`, `_ForTheCommitAnAmendReplaced`, `_AfterACommitAmendedAway` and `_GivesUpAtTheBound` cover the wait.\\n- `TestTakeStampRecords_LeavesAStampAnEarlierCommitCarries` covers B's take leaving A's stamp when B's message was saved from A.\\n- `TestTakeStampRecords_KeepsTheNextCommitsStamp` and `TestTakeStampRecords_KeepsStampsOfCommitsLandedSince` now release each take's entries, as post-commit does.\\n\\n## Checks run\\n\\nOn 7988c573, which is 2caad93e with #3068's head 62a06a0d merged in (main at ce16562b). It also merges cleanly with main at 95eabf57:\\n\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/` passes, and `-race` on the reservation, stamp, prepare and hook tests passes.\\n- `go test ./docs/development/ ./cmd/entire/cli/gitrepo/ ./cmd/entire/cli/proclive/` passes. `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/` fails only in the two `TestSessionAdopt_ExternalStore*RetireFails` tests, which fail the same way on clean main here because the container runs as root.\\n- `go test -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/ -run 'SessionEndCondensation|Stamp|Reserv|Squash|Amend|PostCommit|Concurrent'` passes.\\n- `golangci-lint` v2.15.0 on the whole repo: 0 issues. `gofmt -l -s` is clean. `GOOS=windows go vet` of the strategy package passes.\\n- Complexity gate against main: no new or worsened function over 30.\\n\\n`PostCommit` sits at the edge of the `maintidx` limit. So the `beforeCondense` reload moved into `settledSessions` with the new wait, and the comment above the take is one line shorter; its details are in `takeStampRecords`'s doc.\\n\\n## Review on my fork\\n\\nI ran this through the review bots on my fork first. Their first round found four gaps in the first version, fixed in the second and third commits:\\n\\n- the later post-commit reaching the session first;\\n- a later take dropping the entry of a post-commit still running;\\n- prepare's stale read of the reservation;\\n- a saved message naming an in-flight stamp.\\n\\nThe second round found two more, fixed in the fourth commit: two post-commits could wait for each other, and a later commit's take could take a stamp its message copied from the earlier commit. It also raised the first two limits under \\\"Not covered\\\". Closing them would need a post-commit to signal before it takes anything, or a retry after the wait, so I left them out of this fix.\\n\\nAfter Codex's first round here caught the amend, fixed in the fifth commit, the fork bots found that reading the amend from HEAD's reflog missed it once HEAD had moved on, or under another `GIT_REFLOG_ACTION`, and that a commit made on top of an amend could share the amended commit's reservation. The sixth commit patched the reflog read, and the last one replaces it: a taken stamp counts as in flight while its taker runs, and the wait goes by take order, so this PR no longer reads the reflog.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3113/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3113/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2395\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2395/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2395/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2395/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2395\",\n              \"id\": 5433260528,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABDQJHOQ\",\n              \"number\": 2395,\n              \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): surface git-refs push queue failures\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"ChetanReddyC\",\n                \"id\": 135294504,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOCBBuKA\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135294504?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/ChetanReddyC\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 2,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-12T12:23:58Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-12T14:40:43Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2395\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2395\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2395.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2395.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\n- return an explicit partial failure when a git-refs checkpoint is written locally but cannot be added to the push queue\\r\\n- preserve the local ref and retryable condensation state, then re-enqueue on a later write\\r\\n- add store-level and condensation-level regressions and update the architecture contract\\r\\n\\r\\nCloses #2393\\r\\n\\r\\n## Why this approach\\r\\n\\r\\nThe ref update and queue append cannot be one atomic operation. Rolling back a valid local ref would discard recoverable data, while scanning every local checkpoint ref during pre-push would conflict with the queue's purpose and with fetched-ref semantics. This change therefore makes the partial outcome explicit at the store boundary. The existing fail-soft post-commit caller then preserves session and shadow state so the same checkpoint can be retried safely.\\r\\n\\r\\nI believe this is the smallest complete fix that fits the current architecture. I would appreciate the maintainers' direction on this approach, and I am happy to adjust it or continue the work under your guidance.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Verification\\r\\n\\r\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run '^(TestGitRefsStore_WriteReportsQueueFailureAfterRefUpdate|TestCondenseAndUpdateState_QueueFailurePreservesRetryState)$' -count=1`\\r\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run '^$' -count=1`\\r\\n- `golangci-lint run ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/... ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/...` (0 issues)\\r\\n- `git diff --check upstream/main..HEAD`\\r\\n\\r\\nBroader package test runs on this Windows host encounter existing temporary-repository cleanup failures where `.git` remains locked; the focused regressions and package compilation above pass.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Session metadata\\r\\n\\r\\nCodex checkpoint capture was not active for this local Windows linked-worktree session, so no genuine checkpoint trailer was available.\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2395/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2395/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3161\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3161/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3161/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3161/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3161\",\n              \"id\": 6388018645,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABPHpYIA\",\n              \"number\": 3161,\n              \"title\": \"fix(strategy): keep linked sessions through the multi-worktree recency filter\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n                \"id\": 26940511,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI2OTQwNTEx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Beehtrix\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 2,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-14T09:17:06Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-14T09:17:15Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3161\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3161\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3161.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3161.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Stacked on #3005: until it merges, this diff also shows #3005's commits. This PR's own change is 9691b960 and b53ee194.\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\nA commit made in a worktree with no session of its own falls back to the sessions of other worktrees (`findSessionsForCommitLinking`). When those sessions span several worktrees, `resolveWorktreeCandidates` (`strategy/manual_commit_session.go`) keeps only the ones that interacted within `recentSessionWindow` (15 minutes), judged against the clock when the hook runs. prepare-commit-msg and post-commit each run that check, so they can disagree:\\n\\n1. A session in worktree B interacted a few minutes ago. A session in worktree C has been idle for a day. You commit in worktree A, which has no session.\\n2. Prepare finds one recent session, B's, links it, and stamps an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer.\\n3. The commit waits on the message editor (or a TTY prompt) for more than 15 minutes.\\n4. Post-commit runs the check again. B's session is no longer recent, so the candidates are ambiguous and it links nothing. It also links nothing if C's session interacted during the wait, because the recent ones then span two worktrees.\\n\\nThe commit keeps a trailer naming a checkpoint that is never written, and post-commit logs \\\"no active sessions despite trailer\\\". This reproduces on main (95eabf57) in a strategy test: home the session in the main worktree, add one sibling worktree with an idle session and one to commit from, run prepare while the session is recent, then age it past `recentSessionWindow` before PostCommit. Without the wait, post-commit condenses it.\\n\\n#3005 keeps the sessions prepare linked through its new single-worktree idle check: prepare records them with the stamp, and post-commit keeps them. The multi-worktree filter runs earlier and drops them first, which is why this builds on #3005's record.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\n- `linkedHoweverIdle`: the commit is already linked to the session, either because prepare linked it (#3005's `withLinkedSessions` record) or because it owns the checkpoint an amend keeps (`withAmendedCheckpoint`). `withoutIdleSessions` uses it as well.\\n- In `resolveWorktreeCandidates`, a linked session counts as recent. When the recent ones still span several worktrees, the linked ones are taken if they share one. Sessions prepare didn't link are judged as before.\\n- One sentence in `docs/architecture/sessions-and-checkpoints.md`.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n`TestCommitHooks_LinkedSiblingSessionCondensesAfterALongWaitAcrossWorktrees` has two cases: the linked session ages past the window, and the other worktree's session interacts during the wait. Both fail without the change. With main 95eabf57 merged in, `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/ ./docs/development/` passes, and golangci-lint reports 0 issues on the strategy package.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3161/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3161/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2408\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2408/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2408/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2408/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2408\",\n              \"id\": 5448098562,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABDbrcZg\",\n              \"number\": 2408,\n              \"title\": \"fix: repair stale checkpoints and flag worktree setup gaps\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"id\": 34813274,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-14T10:20:39Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-18T07:24:06Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": true,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2408\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2408\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2408.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2408.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"This PR is stacked on #2404. It should target `krk/doctor-shrink-checkpoint-metadata` while that PR is open, then be retargeted to `main` after #2404 lands.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n#2404 prevents new oversized `prompt_attributions` metadata and adds an explicit doctor repair. Two cases remain.\\n\\nA stale clone can still contain the original oversized history plus newer local checkpoints after another clone repairs the remote. Its next push may reject the repaired history as unrelated or replay the old commits and reintroduce the oversized blobs.\\n\\nCommit hashes cannot identify the shared boundary reliably because rewriting metadata and signing commits both change commit IDs. OPF also runs before ordinary push recovery, so cleanup must happen before its divergence check.\\n\\nFresh Claude Code linked worktrees have a separate setup problem. Shared Git hooks may exist even though Entire hook dispatch is inactive because the worktree has no Entire settings. Claude user or local settings may cover the current worktree, but `.entire/settings.json` and `.claude/settings.json` are the portable project files needed by new worktrees and separate clones.\\n\\n## Checkpoint push repair\\n\\nFor the git-branch v1 backend, pre-push now scans reachable `metadata.json` history before OPF.\\n\\nWhen it finds oversized metadata, it:\\n\\n1. Fetches the actual v1 tip from the named remote or dedicated `checkpoint_remote` URL.\\n2. Verifies that the remote history is clean before treating it as repaired.\\n3. Rewrites the stale local history with #2404's metadata rewriter and serializer.\\n4. Finds the newest rewritten local tree already present in the remote history.\\n5. Replays only the local first-parent suffix onto the remote tip.\\n6. Updates the local v1 ref with compare-and-swap, then uses the ordinary push and retry path.\\n\\nThis path does not force-push.\\n\\nThe shared boundary is identified by tree content rather than commit hash. If the histories have an exact hash merge base, a content match older than that merge base is rejected. This prevents an unrepaired remote from being mistaken for a repaired one.\\n\\nReplay also checks the resulting tree before creating a commit. If the change is already present at the remote tip, it skips the commit so repeated pushes do not duplicate checkpoints.\\n\\nThe implementation covers the cases that differ from ordinary push recovery:\\n\\n- An initial push rewrites all available local history, including oversized blobs deleted from the tip tree but still reachable in older commits.\\n- Cleanup runs before OPF, and the OPF rewrite path reconciles repaired history before checking for divergence.\\n- Dedicated checkpoint remote URLs use fetched temporary refs instead of remote-tracking refs.\\n- Cleanup, OPF, URL recovery, bootstrap, and heal fetches use random per-invocation refs, so concurrent hooks do not share one repository-global temporary ref.\\n- Full initial-history inspection and rewriting are not limited to 1,000 commits. The limit applies only to a local suffix replayed onto an existing remote.\\n- Scanning includes merge parents and merge-resolution changes. Reconciliation preserves the final tree of replayed merge commits while linearizing the suffix.\\n- A remote that still contains oversized metadata is never treated as an independently repaired history.\\n- Rewritten commits continue through the existing commit-signing path.\\n\\nShallow history has an explicit boundary. If the shallow boundary is clean, the rewriter preserves it and repairs bloat introduced afterward. If that boundary contains oversized metadata, pre-push stops and asks the user to fetch the missing checkpoint history.\\n\\nAutomatic cleanup applies only to `entire/checkpoints/v1`. Per-checkpoint Git refs keep their current push behavior.\\n\\n## Worktree setup warnings\\n\\n`entire status`, `entire status --detailed`, `entire status --json`, and `entire doctor` now use the same linked-worktree diagnostic.\\n\\nThe warning appears only when a non-prunable sibling worktree proves that the project has both enabled project-level Entire settings and shared Claude project hooks.\\n\\nIt stays silent for ordinary repositories, disabled setups, malformed or unreadable configuration, worktree-list failures, and correctly configured worktrees.\\n\\nThe message distinguishes between two states:\\n\\n- Entire settings are absent, so Entire hook dispatch is inactive.\\n- Portable project files are missing, but local Entire settings or Claude user and local scopes may still cover the current worktree.\\n\\nJSON keeps the existing `\\\"error\\\": \\\"not set up\\\"` value and adds an optional `worktree_setup` object. Doctor reports shared Git hooks as installed but inactive when Entire settings are absent instead of reporting them as healthy.\\n\\nReading a sibling's settings does not replace the current worktree's process-wide vouched symlink policy.\\n\\n## Performance\\n\\nA clean v1 push adds one local Git history scan and no extra fetch. A local benchmark over a synthetic 500-commit checkpoint history measured about 137 ms per scan across 10 iterations. The scan has a 10-second timeout.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nPassed locally:\\n\\n- `mise run check`\\n  - formatting and lint\\n  - race-enabled unit and integration tests\\n  - Vogon and Roger-Roger deterministic canaries\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -count=1`\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode -count=1`\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -count=1`\\n- focused pre-push and linked-worktree regression suites\\n- `git diff --check`\\n\\nNo real-agent E2E tests were run.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2408/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2408/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2586\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2586/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2586/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2586/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2586\",\n              \"id\": 5579136180,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABFEMR9g\",\n              \"number\": 2586,\n              \"title\": \"fix(strategy): preserve non-ASCII staged filenames\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Vishal202-rgb\",\n                \"id\": 188738250,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOCz_qyg\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/188738250?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Vishal202-rgb\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Vishal202-rgb\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Vishal202-rgb/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Vishal202-rgb/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Vishal202-rgb/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Vishal202-rgb/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Vishal202-rgb/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Vishal202-rgb/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Vishal202-rgb/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Vishal202-rgb/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Vishal202-rgb/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-25T06:31:47Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-25T06:34:38Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2586\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2586\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2586.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2586.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nFixes #2398.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Preserve non-ASCII staged filenames during checkpoint linking.\\r\\n* Use Git's NUL-delimited output format to avoid C-escaped filenames.\\r\\n* Add a regression test covering non-ASCII filenames such as `café.go`.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Problem\\r\\n\\r\\nWhen Git is configured with `core.quotePath=true`, commands such as:\\r\\n\\r\\n```text\\r\\ngit diff --cached --name-only\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\ncan return non-ASCII filenames in a C-escaped form instead of their literal path.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor example, `café.go` may be returned as an escaped filename. Entire then compares this value against the literal filename stored in `SessionState.FilesTouched`, causing the overlap check to fail and potentially preventing the `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer from being added.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Changes\\r\\n\\r\\n* Updated `getStagedFiles` to use:\\r\\n\\r\\n```text\\r\\ngit diff --cached --name-only -z\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n* Parse the output using the NUL delimiter instead of line-based parsing.\\r\\n* Continue normalizing paths with `filepath.ToSlash`.\\r\\n* Added `TestGetStagedFiles_NonASCIIFilename` to verify that non-ASCII staged filenames are returned correctly.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Testing\\r\\n\\r\\n* `git diff --check`\\r\\n* Added regression coverage for non-ASCII staged filenames.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Go test suite was not run locally because the Go toolchain is not available in the current development environment.\\r\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2586/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2586/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2041\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2041/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2041/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2041/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2041\",\n              \"id\": 5186349010,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABAM3QSQ\",\n              \"number\": 2041,\n              \"title\": \"Record changed code entities in checkpoint metadata (gated, off by default)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"id\": 257360244,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-18T21:11:07Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-27T01:23:54Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2041\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2041\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2041.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2041.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1083\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nImplements the entity-deltas half of the VCS keystone (COR-782): each persistent checkpoint gains an `entity_deltas.json` in its per-session tree dir recording which code entities (functions/types/methods) the session changed — schema_version 1.0, shared contract with entire-brain's entity→checkpoint index.\\n\\n**Off by default.** Gated on `entity_deltas` settings key / `ENTIRE_ENTITY_DELTAS` env (tri-state: force-on, force-off, fall-through). With the gate off the only cost is the settings read.\\n\\n**Design — nothing runs in the hook path:**\\n- Post-commit condense writes a job file and `SpawnDetached`s a hidden `entire __entity_deltas` child; the hook's added cost is spawn only.\\n- The child resolves `entire-graph` (silent skip + one Info line if absent), runs `diff --base --head --repo --json` (120s cap, process-group kill, 8MB output cap), filters entities to the session's own files, and applies a new `SessionEntityDeltas` backfill write request (modelled on `BackfillAttribution`, implemented for all four store backends).\\n- The ref advance is **CAS + bounded retry** (re-reads tip, rebuilds on the new parent) so a backfill can never orphan a concurrent condense's checkpoint; the OPF pre-push rewrite takes the entity-deltas lock for its duration so a late child parks instead of aborting a push.\\n- Backfill errors are logged and dropped — structurally unable to fail checkpoint creation.\\n\\n**Verification:** race and rewrite interactions covered by deterministic tests (`TestBackfillEntityDeltas_TipMovedUnderTheWrite_KeepsBothCheckpoints`, `TestRewriteUnpushedV1WithOPF_BackfillCannotLandMidRewrite`, both mutation-verified — reverting the CAS or the rewrite lock fails them with the real failure). Producer fixture captured verbatim from a real `entire-graph` build (commit noted in the fixture). `mise run check` green (lint 0, unit+integration, canary e2e 4/4).\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2041/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2041/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3056\",\n              \"id\": 6255425292,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABNdzkwQ\",\n              \"number\": 3056,\n              \"title\": \"fix(strategy): spell agent-reported paths as git does on case-insensitive filesystems\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n                \"id\": 26940511,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI2OTQwNTEx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Beehtrix\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 5,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-07T05:06:26Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-11T18:20:27Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3056\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3056\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3056.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3056.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes #3054\\n\\nOn a case-insensitive filesystem (the macOS and Windows default) an agent can name a tracked file in another case than git does: writing `readme.md` changes `README.md`. Entire recorded the agent's spelling, which never matches a commit, so the session stayed pending after the file was committed. The issue has the two ways it happens (dirty at turn end, committed mid-turn).\\n\\nI reviewed this on my fork first (Beehtrix/cli#22).\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\n`strategy.FilterTrackableChanges`, which every capture route already applies (turn end, task completion, per-tool hooks, Codex child files, and the transcript fallback of a mid-turn commit), now first spells each path as git's index does (`strategy.TrackedSpellings`, in `strategy/path_case.go`):\\n\\n- It only acts where a directory on a reported path, from the one holding the file up to the worktree root, finds its entries under another case, which `worktreedir.CaseProbe` asks the filesystem in process: one of the directory's entries, looked up with its letters' case swapped, opens the same file, and the directory doesn't also list that spelling as an entry of its own (a hard-linked pair, which only a directory that respects case can hold). A directory that is gone, has no entry with a letter in its name, or has over 4096 entries can't tell, and then nothing is rewritten; it doesn't borrow its parent's answer, since Windows lets a directory respect case inside one that ignores it. It doesn't go by git's `core.ignorecase`, one setting for the whole repository, which a linked worktree on another filesystem, a moved repository or a Windows directory with its own case sensitivity can disagree with. Every directory on the path counts, not only the one holding the file: on Windows `SRC/App.go` in a root that ignores case opens `src/App.go` even when `src/` respects case. On a case-sensitive filesystem nothing changes and git isn't asked, since `readme.md` and `README.md` are two files there.\\n- It asks git once per call for the index's spellings (`gitrepo.IndexPathsIgnoringCase`: `git ls-files -z --cached` with `:(literal,icase)` pathspecs, chunked and bounded by `PathClassificationBudget` like the other classifiers).\\n- A spelling is rewritten only when each directory where it differs from the index's spelling ignores case, and it opens the same file (`os.SameFile` on rooted lstats): in a directory that respects case, two hard-linked names are two entries git tracks apart. A deletion has nothing left to open, so it's rewritten when the index has exactly one spelling of it and that one is gone too. Duplicates the rewrite leaves are dropped, keeping the first one's place.\\n- If git can't answer, the paths are kept as reported, as before.\\n\\n`worktreedir/case.go` is the same file as in my shared-checkout PR for #3011, which needs the same check for deletions; whichever lands second loses it from its diff.\\n\\nTurn end now runs `FilterTrackableChanges` before `filterToUncommittedFiles`, so a file committed mid-turn is checked against HEAD under git's spelling. Both only drop paths, so the order doesn't change what either drops. Task completion respells the subagent's transcript paths before `filterToUncommittedFiles` and the committed-file check that attaches the task to a commit. The transcript route a commit hook takes before the session's first turn end (`filterTrackableFiles`) spells its paths first and keeps them in git's spelling.\\n\\n## Trade-offs\\n\\n- On macOS and Windows, each `FilterTrackableChanges` call runs one more `git ls-files`. A path git tracks under its own spelling still costs that call, since only git knows which paths it tracks. On Linux the cost is one read of each directory on the reported paths (each asked once per call), plus two `lstat`s per directory.\\n- A file that isn't tracked keeps the agent's spelling. git status lists such a file under its on-disk spelling, which the agent's tool normally created, so the two agree.\\n- `liveTaskTranscriptFiles` (co-authorship evidence for a running subagent) still compares the transcript's spelling with the commit's. It only decides whether a session counts as a co-author of a commit, and I left it out to keep this to what enters `FilesTouched`.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- `gitrepo.TestIndexPathsIgnoringCase`: index spellings for other-case names, literal brackets, an untracked name, and inherited `GIT_LITERAL_PATHSPECS` / `GIT_GLOB_PATHSPECS`.\\n- `worktreedir.TestCaseProbe_*`: the directory probe, with a lookup that folds case standing in for a directory that ignores case (a directory that respects case, a hard-linked pair of entries that must read as a directory that respects case, a directory that ignores case, one with no entry that tells, one that is gone, one over the entry bound, and paths that differ in several directories). `TestCaseProbeWindows` checks it against the filesystem itself on CI's Windows job.\\n- `strategy.TestTrackedSpelling`: the rule itself, with a hard link standing in for one file under two names and a stand-in probe for a directory that ignores case (same file where the directory ignores case, a hard link where it respects case, another file, no file, a deletion in a directory that respects case and in one that ignores it, two index spellings, git's spelling still present). `strategy.TestAnyDirectoryIgnoresCase`: every directory on a path counts toward asking git, not only the one holding the file.\\n- `strategy.TestFilterTrackableFiles_KeepsGitsSpellingWindows`: the transcript route keeps `README.md` for a transcript's `readme.md`; on a case-insensitive filesystem it fails without that part of the fix.\\n- `strategy.TestTrackedSpellings_CaseInsensitiveFilesystemWindows` and `TestFilterTrackableFiles_KeepsGitsSpellingWindows` are named so that CI's Windows job runs them on a real case-insensitive filesystem; on Linux they check that nothing changes.\\n- `integration_test/transcript_path_case_test.go`: the issue's two cases end to end. They run only where the filesystem ignores case, so CI's Linux job skips them.\\n\\nOn Linux with git 2.43, `go test ./...` and `go test -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/...` pass apart from 13 tests that fail the same way on a clean checkout of main in that environment (no `--ref-format`, SSH, DNS or user XDG cache, and running as root). golangci-lint v2.15.0 reports 0 issues, the complexity gate passes, and the changed packages and the integration package vet for Windows. I also ran the changed packages' tests and the two integration tests on a case-insensitive filesystem in the same container (ciopfs, a FUSE filesystem, mounted with `use_ino` so both spellings report one inode): the case tests pass there, and both integration tests fail on main there (`FilesTouched = [README.md readme.md]`, and `[readme.md]` still pending after the mid-turn commit). Four other `strategy` tests fail on that mount on main too, from the FUSE filesystem (a removed and re-added working directory, and a temp-dir cleanup).\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 1,\n                \"+1\": 1,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3034\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3034/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3034/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3034/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3034\",\n              \"id\": 6241003512,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABNSLWgw\",\n              \"number\": 3034,\n              \"title\": \"fix(strategy): keep prepare's trust in a session after it settles\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n                \"id\": 26940511,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI2OTQwNTEx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Beehtrix\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-06T10:28:05Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-13T00:13:44Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3034\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3034\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3034.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3034.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes #3029.\\n\\nStacked on #3005. This branch is built on #3005's head (ea0833d9), so until #3005 merges the diff here also shows its commits. This PR's own change is 4723f4f1 and 2bc1b2b6; the two merge commits only bring in #3005's later commits. I'll merge main in once #3005 lands.\\n\\n## The bug (on main as well)\\n\\nprepare-commit-msg stamps an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer for a session on its shape alone in two cases: the session is IDLE with a background subagent in flight (`idleWithLiveTaskRecord`), or it's ACTIVE mid-turn on the no-TTY / `commit_linking=always` fast path. Neither case needs a staged file of the session's own.\\n\\nThe commit can then wait on the link prompt or the message editor for any length of time. Suppose the subagent finishes without editing anything (a read-only reviewer), or a read-only turn ends. Post-commit's `HandleCondense` then judges the session at its own `time.Now()`:\\n\\n- it finds neither shape;\\n- `filesTouchedBefore` is empty, so the overlap check fails;\\n- after a turn end with no step recorded, `postCommitHasNewContent` finds no new content either.\\n\\nThe session isn't condensed. With no other session condensing, the commit keeps a trailer naming a checkpoint that is never written.\\n\\nThis also applies to a session homed in the committing worktree, where #3005's idle filter never runs, which is why it was kept out of #3005.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\n- **Prepare** records the sessions it stamped on their shape alone. They go into the entry #3005 already writes for the stamped trailer in `entire-stamped-sessions.json`, under a new `trusted_session_ids` field (`trustedSessionIDs`, carried on ctx by `withTrustedSessions`). This covers the slow path, the agent fast path, and the amend restamp. Foreign sessions are excluded.\\n- **Post-commit** reads that entry for the trailer it condenses into. In a commit that no session's tracked files claim (`sessionsWithCommittedFiles == 0`), it keeps the overlap-check bypass for those sessions (`trustedByPrepare`) and takes their content as prepare found it. That's the case where this trust is all that resolves the trailer.\\n\\nWhat stays as it is:\\n\\n- A claimed commit belongs to the claimant. The trusted session is judged as it would have been if post-commit had run straight away: the read-only gate leaves it out, or its own files, its subagent's included, have to overlap the commit (2bc1b2b6).\\n- A foreign session (`commitProvenance`) gets no trust.\\n- An ENDED session is left to its own final condensation. Forcing `hasNew` for it would also stop it ever being marked `FullyCondensed`.\\n- `HandleCondenseIfFilesTouched` is unchanged, because post-commit only reaches it for ENDED sessions.\\n- The trust lasts for one trailer only. The record is consumed with the stamp, so a later commit judges the session afresh.\\n\\nNot covered here, and listed on #3029: a session that ends (SessionStop) while the commit waits; a claimant that can't write the commit's checkpoint, which the read-only gate still counts (already on main); and the race where overlapping commits consume each other's stamp records, which needs a lock (#3030).\\n\\n## Known tradeoffs\\n\\n- **The settled session is credited with the committed files.** A condensed session with a transcript and no tracked files is credited with the commit's files (`filterFilesTouched` via `sessionHasEvidenceOfWork`), so a read-only session can be credited with a file the user wrote. Main already does this whenever post-commit runs while the subagent is still running, and a subagent's own commit relies on it (`runIdleTaskRecordCondenses`). This PR gives the settled session the credit it would have had a moment earlier. Changing the fallback would change main's live path too.\\n- **A reused aborted draft keeps its trust.** After an aborted attempt, the stamp and its sessions entry stay until the next post-commit, a lifetime that comes from `entire-stamped-trailers.json` and #3005's record. If the draft is reused with `git commit -F` after the session settles, post-commit trusts that session for the draft's trailer, but only in a commit no session's files claim. Without the trust, that trailer would name a checkpoint that is never written. Binding the trust to one attempt would need a write on every prepare, or recording the staged tree on the fast path.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- `TestCommitHooks_SessionStampedMidTaskCondensesAfterItSettles` has three variants: the read-only subagent finishes (fast path), the same through content detection and the link prompt (`ENTIRE_TEST_TTY=1`), and a read-only turn ends. All three fail on main at 93045e38 and on #3005's head, and pass here.\\n- `TestCommitHooks_TrustedSessionYieldsToTheSessionThatWroteTheCommit` puts another session's files in the commit. When the subagent edited nothing, the read-only gate still decides. When the subagent edited a file the commit doesn't hold, that file and its task record stay pending.\\n- `TestStampedSessions_RecordedWithTheTrailerAndTakenOnce` now also covers the trusted IDs.\\n\\n## Checks run\\n\\nOn 96ec2e9a:\\n\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/ ./cmd/entire/cli/gitrepo/ ./docs/development/` passes.\\n- `go test ./...` fails only in 12 tests that need things my container doesn't have: a non-root user (the two `TestSessionAdopt_ExternalStore*RetireFails` tests), reftable support in git, SSH, or DNS.\\n- `golangci-lint` v2.15.0 on the strategy package: 0 issues.\\n- Complexity gate against #3005's head: no new or worsened function over 30.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3034/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 1,\n                \"+1\": 1,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3034/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3040\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3040/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3040/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3040/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3040\",\n              \"id\": 6247967132,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABNXzdnw\",\n              \"number\": 3040,\n              \"title\": \"Fix setup commit hangs when a hook opens a Git pager\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"sidsharma96\",\n                \"id\": 36319498,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzE5NDk4\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36319498?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/sidsharma96\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/sidsharma96\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/sidsharma96/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/sidsharma96/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/sidsharma96/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/sidsharma96/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/sidsharma96/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/sidsharma96/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/sidsharma96/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/sidsharma96/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/sidsharma96/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-06T18:00:24Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-06T18:00:24Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": true,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3040\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3040\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3040.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3040.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes #3025.\\n\\nAccepting the setup commit during `entire enable` can hang when a pre-commit hook runs a Git command with paging enabled. Git runs in a separate process group, so a pager reading the terminal can be suspended while Entire waits for the commit.\\n\\nSet `GIT_PAGER=cat` for `CommitPaths` commands. Nested Git commands in hooks inherit it and write directly to the supplied output. This keeps the existing process-group cancellation and does not change repository pager settings. It is a narrower fix than the terminal handoff suggested in the issue; arbitrary interactive hooks still need separate consideration.\\n\\nTests:\\n- A real pseudo-terminal reproduction with `less` and `git diff --cached --check` fails before the fix and passes after it. It checks hook completion, the resulting commit, no remaining index lock, and unchanged pager configuration.\\n- A hook starts a child holding its output pipe. Cancellation must return before the pipe-drain timeout, checking that the child is terminated too.\\n- Gitrepo and execx package tests pass with race detection.\\n\\nFull repository checks passed on Go 1.27.3 / macOS arm64: `GOTOOLCHAIN=local TERM=xterm-256color GOFLAGS=-timeout=20m mise run check` (format, lint, unit/integration tests with race detection, and both deterministic canaries). A separate Claude Opus 5.5 high-reasoning review approved this exact source tree; its pager-rationale correction and test-watchdog suggestion are addressed.\\n\\nDraft pending maintainer agreement on this scoped approach. No session checkpoint is attached because the originating session contains unrelated private material.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3040/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3040/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3068\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3068/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3068/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3068/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3068\",\n              \"id\": 6284529287,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABN0ofqw\",\n              \"number\": 3068,\n              \"title\": \"fix(strategy): lock the commit stamp records and keep later commits' stamps\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n                \"id\": 26940511,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI2OTQwNTEx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Beehtrix\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 2,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-09T10:41:50Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-14T09:16:10Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3068\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3068\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3068.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3068.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes #3030.\\n\\nStacked on #3034, which is stacked on #3005. #3005 adds the sessions record this lock also covers, and #3034 changes the same functions, so this branch is built on #3034's head (now 5ff58dc5, which merges main ce16562b and #3005's amend fix). Until both merge, the diff here also shows their commits. This PR's own change is the commits from 4206adaf to e8250a77, 1a8adbe9 and a73bfe46; 9e683b95, 5e5483de and 62a06a0d merge #3034's head into it. I'll merge main in as they land.\\n\\n@peyton-alt, this is the lock I asked about on #3005. I went ahead rather than wait, so it's here to look at whenever you have time.\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\nprepare-commit-msg leaves three records for post-commit in the per-worktree git dir: `entire-stamped-trailers.json`, the per-stamp entries in `entire-stamped-sessions.json` (#3005), and `entire-inherited-trailers.json`. Nothing locks them, and post-commit removes each one whole.\\n\\ngit releases `index.lock` before prepare-commit-msg for a plain commit, and before post-commit for every commit (checked with git 2.43: `commit -a` and `commit <path>` hold it through prepare, never through post-commit). So in one worktree, a second commit can start and run its prepare while the first commit's post-commit hasn't taken the records yet, and two post-commits can overlap. Two parallel agents or subagents committing in the same worktree is enough.\\n\\n- **The next commit's stamp is consumed.** If B's prepare stamps before A's post-commit takes the records, A takes B's stamp too. B's post-commit then finds no stamp for its trailer, and B keeps a trailer naming a checkpoint that is never written. A lock alone doesn't fix this ordering.\\n- **Interleaved writes.** A's post-commit reads the stamps, B's prepare appends, A removes the file: B's stamp is gone. Or B's prepare reads before A's take and writes back after it, which brings A's stamp back.\\n- **Split records.** Two overlapping post-commits can each take part of the records (one the sessions entries, the other the stamps), leaving a stamp without its entry.\\n- **The inherited marker.** B's prepare, inheriting nothing, removes the marker before A's post-commit reads it, and the squash commit A loses its inherited trailers and redone paths.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\n- **One per-worktree lock.** Prepare's writes and post-commit's take hold an flock on `entire-stamp-records.lock` beside the records (`lockStampRecords`, using `internal/flock`). The wait is bounded at 2s, since a holder only touches the small JSON files. If the lock can't be taken, the hook goes on unserialized, as before. Post-commit takes all three records in one step (`takeStampRecords`), which replaces `takeStampedTrailers`, `takeStampedSessions` and `takeInheritedMarker`, and drops #3005's ordering comment.\\n- **Post-commit takes only its own commit's stamps.** It takes the stamps and sessions entries its commit carries (any `Entire-Checkpoint` ID in the message, a superset of what `linkedTrailersOf` and `stampedOutsideFinalBlock` consult, so its own condensation is unchanged). Prepare now writes a sessions entry for every stamp, with the HEAD it stamped on (new `head` field), and fails the stamp if that entry can't be written. Post-commit keeps a stamp it doesn't carry only if it was stamped on its own commit or on a commit on top of it up to HEAD (`commitsUpToHead`: HEAD's first parents, at most 16 back, read under the lock). Those are later commits in flight, possibly already landed. It drops the rest, which are stamps left by commits that never happened, as it did before. If the walk stops short of both the commit and a root commit (at its bound, or at an unreadable commit), the take can't tell a later commit from an abandoned one, so it keeps every stamp it doesn't carry until a later post-commit can.\\n- **The inherited marker** is tied to the HEAD its prepare ran on, which it already records as `Parents[0]`. A prepare that inherited nothing no longer removes a marker that a commit on HEAD's first parents recorded and hasn't taken yet (`markerAwaitsCommitOnHead`), as long as HEAD's reflog shows only commits since one was made on the HEAD that marker's prepare ran on (`committedOnSince`). A commit that was prepared and then cancelled leaves a marker of the same shape once HEAD is reset back onto a commit on top of it, and the reflog shows that reset. Post-commit leaves a marker that a prepare on its commit, or on a later one, recorded.\\n\\nCompatibility: `entire-stamped-trailers.json` stays a list of IDs, and `head` is an additive field older binaries ignore. A stamp an older binary wrote has no recorded HEAD, so it lasts one post-commit, as before.\\n\\n## Not covered\\n\\n- **Two squash commits in flight.** If B also inherited trailers, its prepare still overwrites A's marker, because there is one marker slot. Fixing that needs a list format, which older binaries couldn't read.\\n- **Post-commit finds its commit by reading HEAD.** If B lands before A's post-commit reads HEAD, A's post-commit works on B's commit. That's unchanged here.\\n- **Mixed binaries.** An older binary's prepare doesn't take the lock.\\n- **No HEAD reflog.** Where the reflog doesn't show the commits (reflogs turned off, or `GIT_REFLOG_ACTION` renaming them), a prepare that inherited nothing clears the marker as before, so the marker race stays as it is on main there.\\n- **An abandoned stamp can live a little longer.** One that was prepared on a commit and then abandoned now lasts until the post-commit of the commit after it. This slightly extends the lifetime #3034 lists under \\\"A reused aborted draft keeps its trust\\\".\\n- **An amend made before the original's post-commit takes over its records.** It carries the original's message, so whichever post-commit takes first gets the stamp and the inherited marker. That is the commit that survives.\\n- **A marker matched by its alternate parent.** Post-commit takes the marker when its commit's parent is either of the marker's `Parents`, the second being how an amend's marker is found. During a rebase or cherry-pick, prepare skips and doesn't clear an abandoned marker, so a commit picked onto that parent can take one left on another branch. That is on main already, and this change keeps the match as it is.\\n- **A shared reservation.** `checkpointIDForSessions` hands a session's reserved checkpoint ID to every prepare until a post-commit condenses into it, so two commits in flight can both carry it. That predates this change (it is on main). It is #3069, and #3113, stacked on this PR, fixes it.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- `TestCommitHooks_NextCommitPreparedBeforePostCommitGetsItsCheckpoint` drives the race through the hooks: the second commit is prepared before the first commit's post-commit runs. It fails on #3034's head (the second commit's checkpoint is never written) and passes here.\\n- `TestTakeStampRecords_KeepsTheNextCommitsStamp`, `TestTakeStampRecords_DropsAKeptStampAtTheNextPostCommit` and `TestTakeStampRecords_StampWithoutHeadLastsOnePostCommit` cover what post-commit takes, keeps and drops.\\n- `TestTakeStampRecords_KeepsStampsOfCommitsLandedSince` covers a post-commit that falls more than one commit behind: later commits land, and the next one prepares before it takes the records. `TestTakeStampRecords_KeepsAllWhenLaterCommitsAreOutOfReach` and `TestTakeStampRecords_KeepsAllWhenTheWalkCannotReadACommit` cover a walk that stops short.\\n- `TestInheritedTrailersMarker_SurvivesTheNextCommitsPrepare` covers the marker in both directions, and `TestInheritedTrailersMarker_SurvivesCommitsLandedSince` covers it with more than one commit in flight. `TestInheritedTrailersMarker_ClearedAfterACancelledRedo` covers a redo prepared on the parent, cancelled, and HEAD reset back before an amend; it fails on 1a8adbe9. These tests now commit through git, so HEAD's reflog is written.\\n- `TestStampRecords_WaitForTheLock` checks that prepare's write and post-commit's take both wait while another hook holds the lock.\\n- `TestRecordStampedTrailer_RecordsTheHeadItStampedOn` checks the new field, and `TestRecordStampedTrailer_FailsWithoutItsSessionsEntry` checks that a stamp whose entry can't be written isn't recorded. `TestStampedSessions_RecordedWithTheTrailerAndTakenOnce` and `TestStampedTrailer_OnlyTrailersPrepareStamped` were moved to the new take.\\n\\n## Checks run\\n\\nOn 62a06a0d (with #3034's head 5ff58dc5 and main ce16562b merged in), and again merged with main 95eabf57 for the build and the strategy and docs tests:\\n\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/` and `go test ./docs/development/` pass. The full `go test ./...` (run on 1a8adbe9) fails only 12 tests in packages this PR doesn't touch, and they fail the same way on clean main in this container (it runs as root, has git 2.43 without reftable, rewrites SSH remotes through an injected `url.insteadOf`, and has no DNS).\\n- `go test -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/...` passes except `TestAuthToken_LockDirectoryIsolation/xdg-unset`, which fails the same way on clean main here (it finds no lock file under the unset-XDG cache dir).\\n- `golangci-lint` v2.15.0 on the whole repo: 0 issues. `gofmt -l -s .` is clean.\\n- Complexity gate against #3034's head and against main: no new or worsened function over 30.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3068/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3068/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2190\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2190/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2190/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2190/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2190\",\n              \"id\": 5299600007,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBl6egQ\",\n              \"number\": 2190,\n              \"title\": \"refactor(gitrepo): consolidate worktree metadata traversal\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"id\": 34813274,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 5,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-31T11:27:37Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-02T05:34:59Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2190\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2190\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2190.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2190.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Refs #2052, particularly [the duplicate-traversal finding](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2052#issuecomment-5400538888) and [the follow-up commitment](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2052#issuecomment-5429341093).\\n\\nPR #2052 exposed that several packages independently interpreted `.git`, `gitdir:`, `commondir`, and linked-worktree identity. Those implementations had already diverged on layouts such as bare containers, linked worktrees, and submodules, while session and checkpoint maintained separate caches for answers derived from the same filesystem metadata.\\n\\nThis consolidates those physical Git facts under the existing `gitrepo` ownership boundary and removes the duplicate traversal and cache layers.\\n\\n## Why this touches 67 files\\n\\nThis is one ownership change with a wide dependency graph, not 67 separate features.\\n\\nBefore this change, checkpoint, session, strategy, settings, status, review,\\ninvestigate, trail, setup/cleanup, and Codex independently interpreted some\\ncombination of `.git`, `gitdir:`, `commondir`, and linked-worktree identity:\\n\\n```text\\nBefore\\n\\ncheckpoint ─┐\\nsession ────┤\\nstrategy ───┤ each resolves Git metadata independently\\nsettings ───┤ and some cache the result separately\\nstatus ─────┤\\nreview ─────┤\\nCodex ──────┘\\n\\nAfter\\n\\n                    gitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata\\n                                  │\\n              ┌───────────────────┼───────────────────┐\\n           checkpoint          session            strategy...\\n```\\n\\nThe 67 changed files break down into 37 production files and 30 test files:\\n\\n| Area | Files | Why they changed |\\n| --- | ---: | --- |\\n| Canonical `gitrepo` owner | 7 | Add the resolver, repository-opening boundary, tests, and ownership guard |\\n| Checkpoint migration | 7 | Remove its common-directory cache and migrate consumers |\\n| Session migration | 7 | Remove its separate cache and preserve adoption/sweep behavior |\\n| Strategy and hook paths | 18 | Migrate the hottest and most policy-sensitive consumers |\\n| Other product consumers | 18 | Migrate settings, status, review, investigate, trail, Codex, setup, and cleanup |\\n| Legacy `paths` deletion | 2 | Remove the old marker-based worktree-ID parser |\\n| Cross-cutting proof | 8 | Update fixtures and prove caller policy and subprocess behavior |\\n\\nMost production changes are small call-site migrations. The largest additions\\nare tests proving real Git layouts, failure behavior, ownership boundaries, and\\nsubprocess counts. Despite the broad footprint, production Go decreases by 36\\nlines.\\n\\n## One owner for physical worktree metadata\\n\\n`gitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata` now resolves one explicit worktree root into:\\n\\n- its per-worktree Git directory\\n- its common Git directory\\n- its optional linked-worktree ID\\n\\nThe resolver has no CWD lookup, Git subprocess, cache, context, options, environment interpretation, layout taxonomy, or feature-specific policy.\\n\\nReturned paths remain cleaned absolute lexical paths. Physical filesystem identity is used only to determine whether the Git directory equals the common directory and whether a linked-worktree Git directory is an immediate child of `CommonDir/worktrees`.\\n\\nResolution is all-or-error. Malformed worktree metadata cannot silently downgrade into another repository-opening path, while deliberately opening a validated bare repository remains a separate `gitrepo.OpenPath` operation.\\n\\n## Consolidation and deletion\\n\\nAll former filesystem-metadata consumers now use the canonical resolver while retaining their existing caller-owned error, warning, fallback, trust, and installation policies.\\n\\nThis removes:\\n\\n- the session common-directory cache and its clearing behavior\\n- the checkpoint common-directory cache\\n- duplicate `.git` and `commondir` traversal\\n- marker-based worktree-ID parsing\\n- the old `paths` worktree metadata helpers\\n- migration wrappers that would otherwise preserve fragmented ownership\\n\\nA source guard rejects new production parsing of `gitdir:`, `commondir`, or independent `.git` filesystem traversal outside `gitrepo`, with two documented policy-only exceptions.\\n\\nThe production Go diff is 557 additions and 593 deletions: net 36 lines removed despite adding the canonical resolver.\\n\\n## Hook-path subprocess evidence\\n\\nOperation-level Git tracing records these changes against the historical pre-consolidation counts:\\n\\n| Operation | Before | After |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\\n| Session state construction | 2 | 1 |\\n| Construct and enqueue through checkpoint queue | 1 | 0 |\\n| `prepare-commit-msg` without an active session | 4 | 2 |\\n| `entire status` | 4 | 3 |\\n| Codex hook discovery | 1 | 1 |\\n\\nThese values count Git subprocesses, not whether the operation still occurs. The checkpoint queue retains its locking, append, drain, and removal behavior; it now obtains the common directory through filesystem metadata resolution instead of spawning Git.\\n\\nThe consolidation adds no Git subprocesses and removes the filesystem-metadata `--git-common-dir` queries. The one remaining common-directory query on the prepare-commit path is retained semantic repository-identity behavior rather than metadata traversal.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `mise run check`\\n  - formatting passed\\n  - lint passed with 0 issues\\n  - race-enabled unit and integration tests passed\\n  - Vogon canary passed 56/56\\n  - external deterministic canary passed 4/4\\n- `git diff upstream/main...HEAD --check`\\n- Real Git-created fixtures cover ordinary repositories, linked worktrees, `.bare/worktrees`, bare repositories with linked worktrees, separate Git directories, ordinary and linked submodules, relative pointers, symlink aliases, and moved registrations.\\n- Handmade fixtures cover malformed and broken metadata.\\n- Tests verify caller-owned failure policies, fail-closed repository opening, common-directory/worktree-ID agreement, and physical alias identity.\\n- The source guard was positive-control tested by temporarily adding forbidden independent traversal and observing the expected failure.\\n- No paid real-agent E2E tests were run.\\n\\n## Deliberately unchanged\\n\\nThis does not change Codex backlink, ownership, trust, warning, diagnostic, or installation policy. It does not add cross-worktree writes, resolver flags, a generic Git facade, or replace genuine Git queries for refs, objects, configuration, or repository semantics.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2190/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2190/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2577\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2577/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2577/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2577/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2577\",\n              \"id\": 5563181074,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABE3ieJQ\",\n              \"number\": 2577,\n              \"title\": \"fix(strategy): stop carrying forward files a skipped-hook commit already took\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-24T04:33:04Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-30T23:55:15Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2577\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2577\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2577.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2577.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1416\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\nA commit made with every Git hook skipped (`LEFTHOOK=0` under the Lefthook integration in #2388, a GUI client with no hooks, a crashed hook) is invisible to Entire. The session's files from that turn land in HEAD, but the next hooked commit's diff doesn't contain them, so `filesWithRemainingAgentChanges` counts them as uncommitted and `carryForwardToNewShadowBranch` moves them onto a fresh shadow branch. No later commit ever contains them, so it repeats on **every** commit: `entire checkpoint list` shows a permanent `[temporary] carry forward: uncommitted session files` entry and a shadow branch is rewritten per commit.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\nA file absent from the commit is \\\"remaining\\\" unless HEAD already holds the shadow's content **and** the working tree still matches HEAD (`content_overlap.go`). It goes through the same working-tree check a partial commit already uses, so edits made after the shadow snapshot (an agent committing mid-turn) are still kept, as are files HEAD holds with different content.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- New `TestFilesWithRemainingAgentChanges_AlreadyInHeadFromEarlierCommit` (same content → dropped; different content → kept); it failed before the change.\\n- `TestFilesWithRemainingAgentChanges_CacheEquivalence` committed both files while claiming only one was committed; its fixture now commits only the file it says it does.\\n- New integration test `TestSkippedHookCommit_FilesAlreadyInHeadAreNotCarriedForward` drives the real hooks: a hook-skipped commit then a hooked one. With a clean working tree the file is dropped and no shadow branch remains (fails on the pre-fix code with the stuck `entire/<sha>` branch); edited again on disk, it is kept and carried forward.\\n- Binary, one live Vogon session, one hook-skipped commit then two normal ones:\\n  - `main`: `[temporary]` stays and the shadow branch moves every commit (`entire/10eb73d…` → `entire/e368938…`).\\n  - This branch: no `[temporary]` entry, no leftover shadow branch.\\n- `mise run check`: lint 0 issues, canaries green. Two `TestExternalCommand_*` signal tests timed out waiting for their plugin under full-suite load; both pass in isolation (run twice) and don't touch this code.\\n\\n## Not in this PR\\n\\n- **Attributing the skipped turn to its commit.** That needs linking a checkpoint to a commit with no trailer (today only imports use `commit_sha`), plus a product call on attributing trailer-less commits. Follow-up.\\n- **A separate session whose only work was committed with hooks skipped** keeps its un-condensed shadow branch at the old base. It's a different path (the session never takes another turn) and isn't changed here.\\n\\nSize: +174 / −7.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes checkpoint carry-forward heuristics in post-commit flow; wrong comparisons could drop real uncommitted agent work or reintroduce phantom carry-forward, though scope is narrow and well-covered by new tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Fixes an infinite carry-forward loop when agent session files reach **HEAD** through a commit Entire never processed (hooks skipped, GUI without hooks, etc.). Those paths were missing from the current commit’s `committedFiles`, so `filesWithRemainingAgentChanges` kept treating them as uncommitted and `carryForwardToNewShadowBranch` rewrote the shadow branch on every later commit.\\n> \\n> **`filesWithRemainingAgentChanges`** now treats a “not in this commit” file as done when the commit tree already has the same blob as the shadow branch; differing HEAD content is still carried forward. Docs and debug logging reflect the new rule.\\n> \\n> Tests add **`TestFilesWithRemainingAgentChanges_AlreadyInHeadFromEarlierCommit`** (shadow-matching HEAD vs user-edited HEAD) and align **`TestFilesWithRemainingAgentChanges_CacheEquivalence`** so only `fileA` is committed while `fileB` stays genuinely uncommitted on disk.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit d97c55dc737227d24f3594ab1a39313e1a08e591. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2577/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2577/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3018\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3018/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3018/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3018/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3018\",\n              \"id\": 6209201661,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABM4udrw\",\n              \"number\": 3018,\n              \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): push git-refs checkpoints in bounded chunks\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-04T18:48:30Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-06T02:21:33Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-11-06T02:21:30Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3018\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3018\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3018.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3018.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-11-06T02:21:30Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes #2986\\n\\nTrail: https://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2755/changes/cli/1766\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nThe git-refs pre-push flush sent every queued checkpoint ref in one `git push`. Each refspec is `<40-hex>:refs/entire/checkpoints/<shard>/<id>`, about 95 characters. On Windows the command line hits the 32,767-character `CreateProcess` limit at roughly 340 refs. Past that, the batch fails before git starts (\\\"The filename or extension is too long\\\"). Every push then falls back to per-ref retries, which drain only a few dozen refs per 2-minute budget. A large backlog after `entire import` never catches up.\\n\\nOn every platform, the batch push also had no deadline. A big backlog over a slow link, or a stalled connection, could hold the user's `git push` with no bound.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\n- **Bounded chunks.** Queued refs go out at most `checkpointRefPushChunkSize` (200) per `git push`. That is about 19,000 characters, well under the Windows limit. Each chunk's queue entries are removed as soon as it lands, so a backlog drains over several pushes. A test pins a full chunk's command line under 32,767 characters.\\n- **One budget.** In pre-push, the batch and the per-ref fallback share `checkpointFlushBudget`. The explicit pushes (the migration push-now and `entire checkpoint push`) leave the batch unbounded, because the user asked for that upload and is waiting on it.\\n- **A failed chunk does not stop later chunks.** Only the failed chunks' refs go to the per-ref fallback. Batching stops after 2 failed chunks in a row, an SSH auth failure, the budget, or an interrupt. The first chunk is always attempted.\\n- **Unreachable remote stops at once.** When nothing has landed and git could not connect at all (connect-phase ssh/curl failures, `remote.UnreachableRemoteLine`), the flush prints that one line, with credentials redacted, and leaves the queue in order. It does not pay a connect timeout per ref.\\n- **OpenSSH `ConnectTimeout=60`** under the pre-push hook, so an unreachable host fails within a minute rather than on the kernel connect timeout. Other ssh clients are left alone, since they may reject `-o`.\\n- **Partial delivery counts.** When an early chunk lands and a later one fails, pre-push still commits the captured sync remote and shows the ignored-`checkpoint_remote` warning, because those checkpoints reached the remote.\\n- **Chunk size adapts to a slow link.** A chunk the budget cuts before anything lands quarters the next chunk (remembered per clone in the git common dir), and a clean flush doubles it back toward 200. A budget cut mid-chunk ends the flush and rotates that chunk to the back, instead of retrying refs on a spent budget.\\n- The free-text credential redaction helper moves into `gitremote` so `remote` can use it.\\n\\nMain's pinned delivery is kept throughout. Refs are pushed as exact `hash:ref`. Entries are removed and rotated by queue generation. A ref superseded during recovery is reported as changed, not failed.\\n\\nNot addressed here: the issue's \\\"Related, smaller\\\" point about `PushURL` falling back to the code remote's URL when the checkpoint remote's push URL cannot be resolved. That is a separate change.\\n\\nThis was split out of #2715, which carries it plus a background upload worker. #2715 will drop this commit once this merges.\\n\\nDiff: +1179/-174 across 11 files.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- `mise run check` (format, lint, unit, integration, canary): passes.\\n- `mise run complexity:gate`: no new or worsened functions.\\n- New and updated unit tests in `strategy/refs_push_bounds_test.go`:\\n  - chunked backlog\\n  - landed chunks kept on a budget cut\\n  - a rejected chunk does not stop later chunks\\n  - stop after consecutive chunk failures\\n  - the migration push batch is unbounded\\n  - unreachable remote stops at once\\n  - a full chunk fits the Windows command line\\n  - partial delivery is reported as pushed\\n  - a chunk too slow for the budget shrinks, then grows back\\n  - a cut after progress keeps the size\\n  - a budget cut still shows an earlier rejection\\n- `checkpoint/remote/git_test.go`: `UnreachableRemoteLine` matching and redaction, and `ConnectTimeout` for OpenSSH only.\\n- Real binaries, 795 queued refs (the issue's count), local bare remote, `git` wrapped to refuse command lines over 32,767 characters (macOS host, emulating the Windows limit):\\n  - main: batch fails (`The filename or extension is too long. (75574 chars)`), per-ref fallback runs out of its 2m budget; 669 of 795 pushed, 126 left queued, 121s.\\n  - this branch: 4 pushes (200/200/200/195 refs), all 795 pushed, queue empty, remote tips match local, 2s. The wrapper never refused a push.\\n  - Not run on real Windows.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3018/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3018/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2277\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2277/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2277/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2277/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2277\",\n              \"id\": 5360339140,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCWQgMQ\",\n              \"number\": 2277,\n              \"title\": \"fix(clean): reap accumulated ref/shadow lock files\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"prem0423\",\n                \"id\": 19150467,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTUwNDY3\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19150467?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/prem0423\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/prem0423\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/prem0423/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/prem0423/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/prem0423/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/prem0423/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/prem0423/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/prem0423/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/prem0423/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/prem0423/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/prem0423/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-05T19:15:11Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-26T12:26:01Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2277\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2277\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2277.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2277.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Closes #2197.\\n\\nTwo design questions from my [claim comment](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2197#issuecomment-5553909120) are still open — flagged at the bottom rather than blocking on them. Happy to adjust the diff either way.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n`persistentRefLock` creates one flock file per checkpoint ref under `<git-common-dir>/entire-persistent-ref-locks/` and nothing ever removes them, so the directory grows monotonically with checkpoint count. `entire-shadow-locks/` has the same shape (bounded by branch activity, but equally unreaped). `strategy/cleanup.go` had no reference to either, so `entire clean` never reclaimed them.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\nWired both into `entire clean --all`, mirroring the existing `CleanupTypeRedactCache` precedent for a git-common-dir directory that would otherwise leak.\\n\\n- **`internal/flock`**: added `TryAcquireIn` — a one-shot non-blocking probe. There was only the blocking `Acquire`/`AcquireIn` and the deadline-polling `AcquireContext`/`AcquireContextIn`; a reaper must not queue behind a lock it's only testing. Contention returns `ok=false` with a nil error, distinct from a real failure.\\n- **`checkpoint`**: exported `ShadowLockDirName` / `PersistentRefLockDirName` (as `RedactCacheDirName` already is).\\n- **`strategy/cleanup.go`**: `CleanupTypeRefLock`, `lockDirNames()`, `reapLockDirs()`. A lock file is removed only when `TryAcquireIn` succeeds (no live holder); the flock is held across the unlink so no new holder slips in first, and the directory is dropped once empty. A held file is left in place. `CleanupResult` gains `RefLocks` / `FailedRefLocks`.\\n- **`cli/clean.go`**: preview / result / failure sections and count totals.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- `flock`: uncontended acquire; held-lock reported without blocking, then success after release.\\n- `strategy`: absent dirs not listed; unheld files reaped and the emptied dir removed; **a held file survives while an unheld sibling in the same dir is still reaped and the dir is kept**; `reapLockDirs` on missing dirs reports reaped, not failed.\\n- `cli/clean.go`: the `--all` preview shows a \\\"Lock directories\\\" section.\\n\\n`mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test` all green.\\n\\n## Note on a pre-existing asymmetry\\n\\n`redactCaches` currently shows in the `--all` preview but is not in the result summary or `totalDeleted`. I wired `refLocks` into both, otherwise a lock-only cleanup would print \\\"Deleted 0 items\\\". Left the redact-cache side alone to keep scope tight.\\n\\n## Open questions\\n\\n1. **Unlink race.** `openlock.go` documents that the code relies on lock files never being unlinked. Reaping them opens a narrow window: a process that opened the path just before the unlink can lock a stale inode while a newcomer locks a fresh one. I've bounded it — reap only under the explicitly user-invoked `clean --all`, hold the flock across the unlink, treat the residual window as self-healing since the next writer recreates the file — and documented it on `reapLockDirs` the way `openlock.go` documents its own tradeoff. Is that acceptable, or do you want a stricter scheme?\\n2. **Scope.** `entire-session-locks/` (`strategy.SessionLockDirName`) has the same shape — session states get reaped, their lock files don't. Add it to `lockDirNames()` in this PR, or keep to the two directories named in the issue?\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2277/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2277/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1763\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1763/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1763/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1763/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1763\",\n              \"id\": 4892720369,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7yCGM_\",\n              \"number\": 1763,\n              \"title\": \"feat(cost): persist spend-time cost in checkpoints, sync pricing from entire-api (supersedes #1702)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"entire[bot]\",\n                \"id\": 254015822,\n                \"node_id\": \"BOT_kgDODyP5Tg\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/2626939?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/entire\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"Bot\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-07-15T13:05:10Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-31T16:58:57Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1763\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1763\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1763.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1763.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"**Trail:** https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/865\\n\\n> **Draft — direction change pending team sign-off.** Reverses the round-2 decision that \\\"the CLI is the single source of truth\\\" for cost. Opening as a draft so it can be reviewed alongside #1702 before committing to the reversal. Pairs with entirehq/entire-api (platform computes cost).\\n\\n## What\\n\\nThe CLI stops **persisting** cost into checkpoint metadata. It keeps persisting the token facts the platform prices from (`model_usage` with all four token fields per model + model id, flat token counts, model, api-call counts). Cost is now shown only as a clearly-labeled **local estimate** in the token commands.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nPer team discussion (Dipree): don't store cost in the CLI — the platform can pull fresh pricing far faster (no CLI release to fix a rate or add a model). The CLI's job narrows to capturing the facts only it can see; the platform (entire-api) owns pricing and the authoritative cost.\\n\\n## How\\n\\n- A single choke point — `Metadata.WithoutCost()` / `CheckpointSummary.WithoutCost()` — applied at all six checkpoint-metadata marshal sites (branch + refs backends). It clears `cost_usd`/`cost_source` at every level (flat, subagent subtree, each per-model bucket) while preserving the four token fields, model ids, and counts.\\n- The in-memory compute path is intentionally **kept** — condensation's model-recovery rebucketing keys on `CostUSD == nil`, so removing it would change when `model_usage` is rebucketed. Only what's written to disk drops cost.\\n- Token commands (`entire session tokens`, `entire checkpoint tokens [--compare]`, `entire tokens profile`) recompute a local estimate on the fly via `agent.EstimateCost` from the persisted tokens + `model_usage`, labeled `$X (estimated locally)` with a note that the authoritative cost lives on the platform. Unknown model → no cost line (never `$0`). The `pricing/` package is retained for this local display.\\n\\n## Supersedes\\n\\nSupersedes #1702 (which computed and stored cost in the CLI). This branch is #1702 **plus** the two reduction commits on top.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- `gofmt`/`mise run lint` clean; `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/... ./api/checkpoint/...` green.\\n- `TestWriteCommitted_DoesNotPersistCost`: a checkpoint with cost + subagents + per-model buckets round-trips with token counts / model ids / subagent counts intact and cost nil/empty at every level.\\n- Updated condensation test proves persisted `model_usage` is bucketed under the recovered model with token counts, but no cost.\\n- Display tests: token commands still render a cost line, computed live, labeled as a local estimate.\\n\\n## Note for review\\n\\nBackfill/summary rewrites now also strip cost from any **legacy** checkpoint they rewrite (cost written by an older CLI is cleared on the next attribution/summary backfill). Consistent with \\\"the CLI does not persist cost\\\" — flagging to confirm it's intended.\\n\\n## Follow-up\\n\\nIf the team decides the CLI should drop cost **display** entirely too, the `pricing/` package + the cost fields/machinery could be removed (larger blast radius — condensation's model-recovery currently rides on the cost path; would need re-expressing as a pure model-signal). Not done here.\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Update (2026-08-18): direction reversed again, merged main, findings fixed\\n\\n**Correction to the top of this description:** the CLI does **not** stop persisting cost — that direction (described in \\\"What\\\"/\\\"How\\\" above) was itself reversed by a later commit on this branch (\\\"persist cost in checkpoint metadata again\\\"). Current behavior: the CLI persists `cost_usd`/`cost_source` in checkpoint metadata at every level (session, subagent subtree, per-model bucket), computed with cache-accurate local pricing at spend time. The platform (entire-api, PR entirehq/entire-api#299) now trusts and stores that reported cost rather than re-deriving it, on the reasoning that only the CLI knows the rates actually in force when the tokens were spent.\\n\\n**Merged `origin/main`** (263 commits). Two conflicts, both a shape where main and this branch had each added something the other lacked at the same seam:\\n- `types.AddTokenUsage` (main's new recursive token summer, which also added `CacheCreation1hTokens`) vs this branch's cost-aware `aggregateTokenUsage` — resolved by delegating token summation to `AddTokenUsage` and layering cost on top, so neither `CostUSD` summing nor the subagent-token recursion is lost.\\n- `manual_commit_condensation.go`'s model-backfill/reprice path vs main's `withSubagentTokensFrom` subagent-total fill — the reprice was overwriting the fill; fixed by carrying the subagent total across both of the reprice's call sites.\\n\\n**Trail review findings addressed** (all three, [trail #865](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/865)):\\n- **High — remote pricing catalog silently disabled the 2x Anthropic 1h cache-write premium.** A remote catalog entry supplying only the 5-minute cache-write rate made `Estimate` skip the 1-hour-TTL 2x multiplier entirely (the multiplier only applied when no 5-minute rate was set). The two TTLs are independent multiples of the input rate, not one derived from the other — an Anthropic entry now defaults the 1-hour rate to 2x input regardless of whether a 5-minute rate is present. Added `CacheWrite1hPerMTok` so a source that knows the real 1-hour rate can still say so explicitly and override the default.\\n- **Medium — CLI persists the authoritative cost, then displays a re-estimate instead.** `entire checkpoint tokens` and `entire tokens profile` were discarding a checkpoint's persisted spend-time cost and recomputing at today's rates for display — drifting from both the stored value and what the platform now shows for the same checkpoint. They now render the persisted `cost_usd`/`cost_source` when one exists, falling back to a local estimate only for checkpoints written before cost persistence existed (`entire session tokens`, which has genuinely no persisted cost for live session state, is unchanged). `localCostEstimateNote` no longer claims platform authority backwards, and only prints for an actual local estimate.\\n- **Low — one slow pricing fetch cost a full day of staleness.** A transport-level failure (timeout, dial error, connection dropped mid-read) bumped the refresh cache's `FetchedAt` the same as a real response from the source, blocking retry for the full 24h refresh interval over a single slow request (e.g. a Worker cold start). Such a failure now backs off only 1 hour instead of the full interval.\\n\\n`mise run check` (fmt, lint, unit, integration, Vogon canary) is green on the merged tree.\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Update (2026-08-18): pricing consolidation — release-time sync from entire-api\\n\\nPer team direction (Soph): entire-api's `internal/pricing` becomes the sole source of truth for pricing rates, replacing three independently-updated copies (this repo's embedded table, entire-api's port, entire.io's models.dev-sourced generator).\\n\\nAdded `mise run pricing:sync` / `pricing:sync:write` (`cmd/entire/cli/pricing/pricingsync`): fetches the canonical catalog (entirehq/entire-api#299's `GET /api/v1/pricing/models.json`, proxied at `entire.io/pricing/v1/models.json` by entirehq/entire.io#3643) and syncs it into the embedded `pricing/models/*.json` files. Read-only diff report by default; `-write` applies it. Preserves each file's existing on-disk order and never deletes a local-only entry the canonical source doesn't (yet) carry.\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Update (2026-08-18, cont'd): wired pricing:sync into a weekly CI freshness gate\\n\\n`release.yml` only ever embeds whatever's already committed on `main` — nightly tags are cut straight off `main`'s current commit, and the release job has no live-fetch step (fetching live data at build time would make a tag non-reproducible). So keeping the embedded pricing tables current has to happen on `main` ahead of any tag, not inside the release build.\\n\\nNew `.github/workflows/pricing-sync.yml`: runs `mise run pricing:sync` weekly (read-only), alerts to Slack (`E2E_SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL`, the same one `release.yml`'s own failure notification uses) on drift. Deliberately alert-only, no auto-commit — a human runs `pricing:sync:write` and reviews the rate diff before it lands, matching entire-api's own `pricing:check`/`pricing:update` convention (also manual-apply there).\\n\\n`pricingsync` read-only mode now returns a distinct `errDriftFound` sentinel so the workflow can key its exit code directly, instead of parsing text output — mirrors entire-api's `pricingcheck`, which already \\\"doubles as a freshness gate\\\" the same way.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1763/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1763/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1386\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1386/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1386/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1386/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1386\",\n              \"id\": 4610495227,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7jx0CW\",\n              \"number\": 1386,\n              \"title\": \"Fix: Keep Entire pre-push alive after Lefthook reinstalls hooks\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"stale2000\",\n                \"id\": 2454364,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NTQzNjQ=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2454364?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/stale2000\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/stale2000\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/stale2000/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/stale2000/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/stale2000/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/stale2000/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/stale2000/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/stale2000/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/stale2000/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/stale2000/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/stale2000/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-06-08T06:20:55Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-21T15:45:25Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1386\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1386\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1386.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1386.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/stale2000/cli/session/019ea5bb-9549-7083-b95f-7ecb498cbc24 \\r\\n\\r\\nCloses #1349.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis keeps Entire's existing Git hook ownership behavior unchanged while adding a Lefthook-local safety net for the failure mode reported in the issue.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhen a repository has a YAML Lefthook config, `entire enable` still installs the normal Entire `.git/hooks/pre-push` wrapper. It now also ensures `lefthook-local.yml` contains an `entire-push-sessions` pre-push command that only runs if Lefthook has reclaimed `.git/hooks/pre-push` and removed the `Entire CLI hooks` marker.\\r\\n\\r\\nNormal state:\\r\\n- Git runs Entire's `pre-push` wrapper.\\r\\n- Entire chains to Lefthook.\\r\\n- The Lefthook-local fallback sees the Entire marker and does nothing.\\r\\n\\r\\nRecovered state:\\r\\n- Lefthook has rewritten `.git/hooks/pre-push`.\\r\\n- Git runs Lefthook directly.\\r\\n- The Lefthook-local fallback sees the Entire marker is missing and runs `entire hooks git pre-push {1} || true`.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Details\\r\\n\\r\\n- Adds and updates `lefthook-local.yml`, not team-owned `lefthook.yml`.\\r\\n- Adds the local Lefthook config path to `.git/info/exclude`.\\r\\n- Preserves unrelated existing local Lefthook commands.\\r\\n- Removes only Entire's local Lefthook command from `entire disable`.\\r\\n- Keeps non-Lefthook hook behavior unchanged.\\r\\n- Handles `.config/lefthook.yml` detection in addition to the existing Lefthook config names.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Verification\\r\\n\\r\\nPassed:\\r\\n- `gofmt -w cmd/entire/cli/strategy/hook_managers.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/hook_managers_test.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks_test.go`\\r\\n- `/Users/stale2000/.local/share/mise/installs/golangci-lint/2.11.3/golangci-lint-2.11.3-darwin-arm64/golangci-lint run ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/...`\\r\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy`\\r\\n- `go test -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test -run 'Test(UserPromptSubmit_ReinstallsOverwrittenHooks|HookOverwrite_MidTurnWipe_NextPromptRecovers)'`\\r\\n- `git diff --check`\\r\\n\\r\\nManual real-Lefthook checks:\\r\\n- Verified with Lefthook `v1.13.6` that `lefthook-local.yml` is merged into `pre-push` runs.\\r\\n- Verified `{1}` expands to the Git pre-push remote name (`origin`).\\r\\n- Verified the generated safety-net command calls `entire hooks git pre-push origin` when `.git/hooks/pre-push` lacks the Entire marker.\\r\\n- Verified the same command skips when `.git/hooks/pre-push` contains `Entire CLI hooks`.\\r\\n\\r\\nKnown verification gaps:\\r\\n- `mise run check` and `mise run fmt` did not reach the repo tasks because mise/aqua hit GitHub 504s while downloading ShellCheck and tmux.\\r\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli` still has an unrelated date-sensitive failure in `TestRunAuthStatus_RendersSessionsTable` where the rendered local date is `2025-12-31` but the test expects `2026-01-01`.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Entire Integration\\r\\n\\r\\nThis PR commit was attached to the active Codex transcript with Entire:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Session: `019ea5bb-9549-7083-b95f-7ecb498cbc24`\\r\\n- Checkpoint: `965634231c03`\\r\\n- Commit includes `Entire-Checkpoint: 965634231c03`\\r\\n- `entire session current` resolves the attached Codex session.\\r\\n- `entire checkpoint list` shows checkpoint `965634231c03` on this branch.\\r\\n- `git push` ran the Entire `pre-push` hook and pushed `entire/checkpoints/v1` to the fork.\\r\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1386/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1386/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2099\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2099/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2099/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2099/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2099\",\n              \"id\": 5216801394,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABAlT1lg\",\n              \"number\": 2099,\n              \"title\": \"fix(claude-code): capture Stop transcripts as validated snapshots\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"id\": 34813274,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 2,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-21T17:57:37Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-18T07:35:51Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2099\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2099\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2099.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2099.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Refs #2091, item 3 only.\\n\\nBefore this change, Claude Code's Stop hook waited for a transcript sentinel that no longer appears, then fell back to a 500 ms quiet window. The wait only validated a mutable path. Lifecycle copied that path later, and provisional-checkpoint finalization opened it once more. Entire could therefore store bytes other than the ones it had treated as ready.\\n\\nThis PR replaces that sequence with one owned, validated snapshot for Claude Stop. Modern Claude payloads provide the final assistant response, so Entire can validate a transcript immediately with no artificial wait. Older payloads retain the 500 ms quiet-window fallback. The lifecycle also keeps checkpoints refreshable across Claude's repeatable Stop events and derives file and token metadata from one transcript parse.\\n\\n## The wait did not own the transcript\\n\\nTranscriptPreparer returns only an error. It gives the caller no bytes, open handle, identity, size, or file version. A successful wait says that path state A looked ready, but lifecycle can then copy state B and checkpoint finalization can read state C.\\n\\nShortening the wait alone would reduce latency while leaving that race intact. Valid final JSON would not be enough either: a complete older prefix can be syntactically valid even when the current turn has not reached the file.\\n\\n## Owned, validated Stop snapshots\\n\\nThe built-in Claude Code adapter now has a Stop-specific capture operation. It:\\n\\n1. fingerprints the producer-owned transcript by file identity, size, and modification time;\\n2. reads exactly the observed byte range;\\n3. verifies both the opened handle and current path still identify the observed file version;\\n4. validates the JSONL and derives the position from those exact bytes; and\\n5. returns an Entire-owned snapshot used by lifecycle, metadata analysis, position advancement, and checkpoint finalization.\\n\\nNone of those consumers reopens Claude's live transcript for the same Stop. If the file changes during capture, the bytes are discarded and capture retries against the new version.\\n\\nThe portable fingerprint catches ordinary appends, truncation, replacement, and rewrites whose modification time changes. It cannot prove that a same-size rewrite did not happen when the filesystem also reports the same timestamp. Claude appends transcript records, so that is an acceptable limit here; the tests do not claim stronger detection.\\n\\n## Modern readiness is evidence-based and immediate\\n\\nFor modern payloads, non-empty last_assistant_message supplies current-turn evidence. Capture requires a transcript position successfully measured at TurnStart, reconstructs the latest assistant text only after that boundary, and requires it to match Claude's supplied final response.\\n\\nThe first readiness check now runs immediately. The previous design waited for the first 50 ms ticker event even when the transcript was already complete. After the immediate attempt, incomplete captures return to the normal 50 ms polling cadence.\\n\\nA rejected file fingerprint is remembered. Entire does not reread and revalidate the same unchanged 70 MiB snapshot every 50 ms; it waits until file identity, size, or modification time provides new evidence.\\n\\nMissing, stale, incomplete, continuously changing, mismatched, timed-out, and canceled captures return no snapshot. The maximum wait remains three seconds.\\n\\n## Legacy payloads keep the quiet-window fallback\\n\\nWhen last_assistant_message is missing, null, or empty, Entire has no producer evidence that the current final response reached the transcript. It therefore retains the 500 ms quiet window used by older Claude Code versions.\\n\\nThe split is intentional:\\n\\n| Payload | Readiness evidence | Timing behavior |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| Modern | Stable owned snapshot, valid current-turn JSONL, final response match | Immediate first check; 50 ms polling only when not ready |\\n| Legacy | Stable owned snapshot, structurally valid ending, 500 ms without file changes | Always pays the quiet window |\\n\\n## Repeatable Claude Stops remain refreshable\\n\\nA blocking Claude Stop hook can cause the same assistant turn to continue and later emit another Stop without a new UserPromptSubmit event. A valid last_assistant_message proves readiness for one Stop; it does not prove that Claude will never continue afterward.\\n\\nClaude therefore advertises a repeatable turn-end capability. After each Stop, Entire:\\n\\n- finalizes checkpoints using the validated snapshot available at that Stop;\\n- retains the original turn boundary and checkpoint IDs;\\n- tracks commits made during a continuation; and\\n- refreshes the same checkpoints if another Stop arrives.\\n\\nThe next user prompt or SessionEnd seals the turn. stop_hook_active is preserved as protocol metadata but is not treated as proof that a Stop is permanently final.\\n\\nIf the latest checkpoint refresh fails, Entire keeps the last successfully stored transcript and preserves the checkpoint IDs as recovery bookkeeping. Successful session-end refreshes release those IDs; failed ones keep the supporting shadow-branch state protected from cleanup.\\n\\n## File and token analysis share one parse\\n\\nClaude file extraction and token calculation previously implemented separate capabilities, each of which parsed the same main transcript and subagent transcripts independently.\\n\\nThe optional TranscriptTurnAnalyzer capability now parses the current main turn once and derives both modified files and token usage from those records. Each subagent transcript is likewise parsed once for both results. Other agents retain the existing independent capability fallback.\\n\\nCapture validation remains a separate, lightweight safety pass. Its question is whether the bytes are safe and complete; turn analysis answers what metadata those validated bytes contain.\\n\\n## Capture and analysis timing\\n\\nThese are medians from three runs on an Apple M3. They measure transcript capture, validation, and transcript-backed metadata analysis, not complete end-to-end Stop-hook latency.\\n\\n### Modern Claude Stop hook\\n\\n| Transcript case | Capture + validation | File/token analysis | Total transcript latency |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\\n| 64 KiB normal turn | 0.170 ms | 0.249 ms | 0.419 ms |\\n| 4 MiB large turn | 8.848 ms | 15.966 ms | 24.814 ms |\\n| 70 MiB session, small current turn at tail | 13.134 ms | 19.308 ms | 32.442 ms |\\n| 70 MiB entirely belonging to current turn | 152.057 ms | 281.803 ms | 433.860 ms |\\n\\nThe realistic large-history case is the third row: the transcript file is 70 MiB, but most records belong to earlier turns. The 433.860 ms case deliberately makes all 70 MiB one enormous current turn.\\n\\n### Legacy Claude Stop hook\\n\\n| Transcript case | Capture including quiet window | Analysis | Total |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\\n| 64 KiB | 501.098 ms | 0.249 ms | 501.347 ms |\\n| 4 MiB | 501.653 ms | 15.966 ms | 517.619 ms |\\n| 70 MiB session, small tail turn | 514.228 ms | 19.308 ms | 533.536 ms |\\n| 70 MiB full current turn | 514.228 ms | 281.803 ms | 796.031 ms |\\n\\nOther timing cases:\\n\\n- A modern transcript that is already ready has no artificial wait.\\n- If writing finishes after Stop begins, latency is the remaining write delay plus approximately 50–100 ms stability detection and processing time.\\n- A transcript that never becomes valid, or whose final response never matches, times out after three seconds.\\n- Missing or already stale transcripts fail immediately.\\n\\nThe common modern case moves from the previous PR design's unavoidable 50 ms first poll to actual processing time: under 1 ms for a small transcript and about 32 ms for a realistic 70 MiB historical session.\\n\\n## Test coverage\\n\\nFocused tests cover:\\n\\n- immediate modern capture independent of the poll interval;\\n- legacy quiet-window behavior and mid-write pauses;\\n- repeated assistant text before the current-turn boundary;\\n- partial final JSON and complete JSON without a trailing newline;\\n- continued growth, truncation, replacement, and same-size rewrites with changed modification time;\\n- remembered rejection of an unchanged snapshot;\\n- missing, stale, timed-out, and canceled capture;\\n- source mutation after capture and finalization ownership;\\n- measured-zero versus unmeasured-zero turn positions;\\n- repeated Stops reusing one turn boundary;\\n- commits and checkpoint refreshes during Stop continuations; and\\n- successful versus failed session-end refresh cleanup.\\n\\nThe benchmarks live in cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/transcript_capture_test.go.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nFresh verification for commit 40fbeb0c2:\\n\\n- Required mise run check passed.\\n- Race-enabled unit and integration suite passed.\\n- Vogon canary passed 56/56.\\n- Roger-Roger canary passed 4/4.\\n- Post-commit mise run lint passed with 0 issues before push.\\n- git diff --check passed.\\n\\nThe separately reported test totals were:\\n\\n- Unit: 9,740 tests, 5 skipped.\\n- Integration: 531 tests, 3 skipped.\\n- Lint: 0 issues.\\n\\n## Kept out of this PR\\n\\nThis PR does not introduce a repository-wide TranscriptPreparer replacement, change external-agent readiness contracts, enforce a minimum Claude Code version, or claim end-to-end Stop-hook latency from the transcript-only benchmarks.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2099/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2099/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2298\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2298/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2298/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2298/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2298\",\n              \"id\": 5369615032,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCdPGzA\",\n              \"number\": 2298,\n              \"title\": \"fix: fall back to reasoningText in the compacted Copilot transcript builder\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"id\": 257360244,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-07T03:18:55Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-07T03:20:43Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2298\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2298\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2298.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2298.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1248\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- Follow-up to the Copilot CLI empty-transcript fix (#1070): the same class of bug existed independently in \\\\`transcript/compact/copilot.go\\\\`'s \\\\`copilotAssistantLine\\\\`, which builds the compacted \\\\`transcript.jsonl\\\\` stored in checkpoints — a different consumer than the live CLI-side extraction #1070 fixed. It dropped \\\\`reasoningText\\\\` content whenever the primary \\\\`content\\\\` field was empty.\\n- No GitHub issue was filed for this — found via direct fixture inspection while investigating #1070, confirmed still current on \\\\`main\\\\` before fixing.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n- Real fixture (\\\\`testdata/copilot_full.jsonl\\\\`) line 7 has a real \\\\`reasoningText\\\\` value with empty \\\\`content\\\\`.\\n- Before: compacted output drops the text block entirely.\\n- After: recovers \\\"Simple task - create a directory and an markdown file inside it.\\\" verbatim.\\n- Golden fixture (\\\\`copilot_expected.jsonl\\\\`) regenerated and diffed — exactly 1 line changed.\\n- Regression guards: content-populated case unaffected; empty-content-with-no-reasoningText case still produces no spurious text block.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n- \\\\`go test ./cmd/entire/cli/transcript/... -race\\\\` — 147 passed, 3 packages.\\n- \\\\`mise run fmt\\\\`/\\\\`mise run lint\\\\` clean.\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2298/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2298/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1388\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1388/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1388/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1388/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1388\",\n              \"id\": 4614152126,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7j95yj\",\n              \"number\": 1388,\n              \"title\": \"test: pin down Cursor token-usage condensation gap (stacked on #1263)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-06-08T15:20:54Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-08T15:28:38Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": true,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1388\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1388\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1388.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1388.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Stacked on #1263 (draft)\\n\\nThis PR stacks **two integration tests** on top of @SnowingFox's #1263 to pin down a gap in the Cursor token-usage work. **No production code changes** — it adds one test file. Base is `cursor-pr-1263-base` (a mirror of #1263's head) so the diff shows only the new tests; once #1263 merges this can be retargeted to `main`.\\n\\nThese tests are **expected to fail** on #1263 as written — they're the acceptance criteria for the fix.\\n\\n### The gap\\n\\n#1263 correctly threads the Cursor `stop` hook's token usage into **live session state** (so `entire status` shows it). But at commit time, condensation recomputes `TokenUsage` from the transcript (`manual_commit_condensation.go` → `agent.CalculateTokenUsage`). Cursor implements no `TokenCalculator`, and its JSONL transcript has no usage fields — as #1263's own description notes — so that recompute returns `nil` and **the hook-provided tokens are dropped from the committed checkpoint metadata.**\\n\\nContrast with Copilot CLI, which does *not* hit this: Copilot implements `TokenCalculator` and writes usage (`session.shutdown`) into the transcript, so the recompute recovers it. Copilot's branch in `sessionStateBackfillTokenUsage` only repairs the session-state total for `entire status`, not committed metadata.\\n\\n### The two tests\\n\\n1. **`TestCursorTokenUsage_SurvivesCondensation`** — drives the real `entire hooks cursor` binary through session-start → before-submit-prompt → edit → stop(with tokens) → commit → condense. Asserts the tokens reach the committed checkpoint metadata. Fails today: committed `token_usage` is absent.\\n\\n2. **`TestCursorTokenUsage_PerCheckpointScoping`** — a guard against the obvious-but-wrong fix. Condensation resets `StepCount`/`CheckpointTranscriptStart` but **deliberately leaves `state.TokenUsage` accumulating** (`manual_commit_condensation.go:1145–1153`). So a two-commit session must scope tokens per checkpoint: checkpoint 1 = turn 1 only (200/50), checkpoint 2 = turn 2 only (500/30) — **not** the cumulative 700/80. A fix that just reuses the running session total fails this.\\n\\n### Suggested fix direction (for the contributor)\\n\\n- The \\\"don't overwrite/recompute when a value is already populated\\\" idea is right for Cursor — but it must be **per-checkpoint scoped**, not the cumulative `state.TokenUsage`.\\n- Either accumulate `step.TokenUsage` per checkpoint (reset on condensation, like `StepCount`), or guard the recompute at `manual_commit_condensation.go:874` so it doesn't clobber a populated value with `nil`, while keeping the value scoped to the current checkpoint.\\n- Test 2 is what distinguishes a correct scoped fix from the cumulative-total shortcut.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Test-only change with no runtime behavior; failures are intentional until a follow-up fix lands.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **integration tests only** (no production changes) to define acceptance criteria for Cursor token usage surviving commit-time condensation.\\n> \\n> Introduces `runCursorHook` to invoke the real `entire hooks cursor` CLI with JSON stdin, plus **`TestCursorTokenUsage_SurvivesCondensation`**: full Cursor hook flow (session-start → before-submit-prompt → edit → stop with tokens → commit), asserting hook tokens appear in **committed checkpoint metadata** on the metadata branch—not only live session state. **`TestCursorTokenUsage_PerCheckpointScoping`** runs two commits with different stop-hook totals and requires each checkpoint’s metadata to carry **that turn’s** tokens only, rejecting a naive fix that copies the cumulative `state.TokenUsage`.\\n> \\n> Tests are **documented as expected to fail** on the stacked #1263 base until condensation stops overwriting hook-populated usage with transcript recomputation (Cursor has no `TokenCalculator` / usage in JSONL).\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 0ac052e1363bfbb5be21c17019959124c033e374. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1388/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1388/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3078\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3078/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3078/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3078/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3078\",\n              \"id\": 6291284493,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABN6Eoaw\",\n              \"number\": 3078,\n              \"title\": \"redact: read values joined from quoted pieces as one shell word\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n                \"id\": 26940511,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI2OTQwNTEx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Beehtrix\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 2,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-09T17:34:39Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-15T18:15:37Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3078\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3078\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3078.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3078.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes #3077\\n\\nThis is the joined-word part of #3077, reworked after @MuskanPaliwal's review. The positional and single-quoted default fixes moved to #3137, as she asked, and this branch is built on it. Until #3137 merges, this diff includes it too. Values that start inside another value's word and run past it are left for #3138.\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\nThe key/value patterns stop at the first closing quote, or, for a bare value, at a blank inside a later quoted string. The shell joins quoted strings and bare text with nothing between them into one word:\\n\\n- `DB_PASSWORD=\\\"\\\"'$X'` is the literal `$X`, but it's judged by its empty first string.\\n- `DB_PASSWORD=\\\"hunter\\\"'2'` and `DB_PASSWORD=\\\"hunter\\\"2xyz` leave `'2'` and `2xyz` visible.\\n- `DB_PASSWORD=abc\\\"d e\\\"` leaves ` e\\\"` visible, and `DB_PASSWORD=abc\\\"d e\\\"=hunter2` leaves ` e\\\"=hunter2`.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\n- **Reading.** `forEachValueMatch` is the loop from the review. Each match `FindAllStringSubmatchIndex` finds is read as captured. It's also read as its whole shell word, unless its value starts inside a word read so far. Reading as captured is what main does, so this never redacts less than main, by construction. Each word is read once, so the passes stay linear. The cursor that guessed where `FindAll` would go on (`forEachUncoveredMatch`) is gone, and so are `visitStraddlingValues` and the recovery readings built on it: about 690 lines.\\n- **What a word is.** `joinedShellWord` reads the rest of the word after a capture that ends at a quote, or at a blank inside one. A word is a run of quoted strings and bare text with nothing between them. A `${…}` that closes on its line is one piece, quotes and all. Quoted strings close on their own line. The word is redacted whole.\\n- **How a word is judged.** A word with one non-empty piece is judged by that piece under its own quotes, so `\\\"\\\"'$X'` redacts, while `''\\\"$DB_PASS\\\"` and `\\\"\\\"'changeme'` stay. Two or more pieces make a new literal (`changeme'example'` is `changemeexample`). Such a word is a placeholder only when every piece is made of shell references, as in `\\\"$DB_PASS\\\"${DB_SUFFIX}` or `\\\"$PREFIX\\\"${BASE}${SUFFIX}`. The code-literal and code-assignment checks see the whole word, so `API_KEY=\\\"None\\\"realtoken` is not `None`.\\n- **Where a word ends.**\\n  - At a blank, at `,` `;` `&`, and at the shell operators `| < > ( )` and a backtick. An `=` is part of the word, as in the shell.\\n  - In a word that starts as bare text, a backslash makes the blank or operator after it part of the word (`a\\\"b\\\"\\\\|c`, `a\\\"b\\\"\\\\ c`). `\\\\\\\\` is one literal backslash, so the blank in `a\\\"b\\\"\\\\\\\\ echo` still ends it. A backslash before a quote is left alone, because raw JSON escapes quotes the same way.\\n  - A word that starts with a quoted string can be code, so it also ends at code and Markdown punctuation (`. : + * ? [ ] { } \\\\`), at `$(` and at a `${` that doesn't close. `connect(db_password=\\\"x\\\")`, `client_secret=\\\"x\\\"+suffix` and `**DB_PASSWORD=\\\"x\\\"**` keep their shape.\\n  - A word inside a double-quoted string ends at that string's closing quote (`enclosingStringEnd`), using the quote reader from #3137. So `echo \\\"DB_PASSWORD=${PW:-'$FALLBACK'}\\\" done` stays a reference. That was the over-redaction the review sketch hit. Each reading gets its own reader, so each is asked about positions in order.\\n- **Separators.** A word that starts with a quoted string is never extended past `,` `;` `&`, since its quotes say where it ends. A bare value is still extended, as on main, and judged after the extension, so `DB_PASSWORD=changeme;hunter2` is one value.\\n- Comments name the reading itself (\\\"as captured\\\") instead of \\\"main\\\".\\n- `configFingerprintVersion` 15 → 16. #3137 takes 15, and #3112 and #3140 take 14.\\n- `docs/security-and-privacy.md` describes the word rules.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- `redact/redact_test.go`, scanners off unless noted: `TestString_ShellWordSecretsCaughtWithoutScanners` (21 cases), `TestString_ValuesPastRedactedWordsCaughtWithoutScanners` (48), `TestString_TrailingKeysCaughtWithoutScanners` (10), `TestString_JoinedShellWordValues` (29, joined literals, references, code shapes) and `TestString_DoubleQuotedJoinedShellDefaultsPreserved` (2, default scanners). 72 of the 110 fail on #3137's branch.\\n- `redact/shell_word_scaling_test.go`:\\n  - `TestString_JoinedShellWordsScaleLinearly` replaces the 30 s wall-clock test. It runs serially with scanners off and checks that 4× the text takes under 6× as long for 32 repeated shapes, both quadratic shapes from the review among them. A ratio over the bound is measured again before it fails. On 777a2214 it fails for both shapes.\\n  - `TestCredentialValueRegions_WordReadingCoversCaptured` is a seeded differential test. Over 20000 random joins of key/value fragments, every byte redacted as captured stays redacted.\\n  - `FuzzCredentialValueRegions_WordReadingCoversCaptured` explores the same property. Its seeds are the six inputs from the review and one more found on the fork.\\n\\n`go test ./redact/`, `go test -race ./redact/`, a 45 s run of the fuzz target, golangci-lint on `./redact/...` and the complexity gate pass.\\n\\n## Not covered\\n\\n- #3138: a value that starts inside another value's word and runs past it is read only as captured, so it leaks as on main. Examples are `API_KEY=\\\"x\\\"a=\\\\b= API_KEY=hunter2` and `DB_PASSWORD=a\\\"API_KEY=\\\"hunter2 secretpart\\\"`, plus six more inputs and two repeated shapes listed there. Earlier versions of this branch caught them with the cursor, which is what leaked the review's inputs.\\n- `{\\\"password\\\":\\\"${1:-hunter2}\\\"}` in JSON goes through the JSON password-key path, which has its own reading of shell values. That's a separate, pre-existing gap.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3078/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3078/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2199\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2199/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2199/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2199/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2199\",\n              \"id\": 5304514449,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBp3OpQ\",\n              \"number\": 2199,\n              \"title\": \"Fix stale lock cleanup\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Rohitkanithi\",\n                \"id\": 63586900,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTg2OTAw\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63586900?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Rohitkanithi\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 5,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-31T20:23:22Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-05T23:13:02Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2199\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2199\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2199.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2199.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Closes #2197.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAdds cleanup support for stale lock files created under the git common dir:\\n\\n- `entire-shadow-locks`\\n- `entire-persistent-ref-locks`\\n\\n`entire clean --all` now discovers those lock files, reports them in dry-run output, and includes them in deletion summaries.\\n\\n## Review follow-up\\n\\nThis update addresses the lock-safety review feedback:\\n\\n- Revalidates Unix flock acquisitions against the current lock-file inode before returning from both blocking `Acquire` and bounded `AcquireContext` paths.\\n- Moves stale lock cleanup to run after shadow branch, session state, and checkpoint cleanup so normal cleanup operations use their locks first.\\n- Treats actively held lock files as skipped, not failed, so live sessions do not make `entire clean --all` exit non-zero just because a lock is busy.\\n- Adds an active-session guard for `entire clean --all` unless `--force` or `--dry-run` is used.\\n- Keeps lock-directory listing best-effort if one lock directory is unreadable.\\n- Uses platform-specific lock-file removal ordering for Unix and Windows.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n```bash\\nGOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-build-cache go test ./cmd/entire/cli/internal/flock ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy\\nGOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-build-cache go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run TestClean\\nGOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-build-cache go test ./cmd/entire/...\\nGOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-build-cache go build ./cmd/entire\\ngit diff --check\\n```\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2199/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2199/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2303\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2303/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2303/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2303/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2303\",\n              \"id\": 5369619777,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCdPWUw\",\n              \"number\": 2303,\n              \"title\": \"fix: detect empty-tree commits and stop condensing over them\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"id\": 257360244,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-07T03:19:43Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-07T03:21:37Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2303\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2303\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2303.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2303.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1253\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThe root corruption is git's own bug, not Entire's, and cannot be prevented from a hook: git (and go-git v6, independently) treats a missing \\\\`.git/index\\\\` (ENOENT) as an empty in-core index, and \\\\`git status\\\\` renames a fresh index over the real one as a side effect — so any concurrent process running \\\\`git status\\\\` at the wrong moment can cause a commit to record an empty tree. The previously-merged mitigation (#2143) already scrubs Entire's own \\\\`git status\\\\` calls, but by the time any hook runs, git has already read the index — prevention was never available from here, only detection.\\n\\n**A second, previously-unknown data-loss bug was found while investigating, and that one is Entire's, and is fixed here**: when an empty-tree commit happens, Entire's \\\\`post-commit\\\\` hook still ran condensation on it — consuming the session's pending checkpoint data. So even if a user notices and runs \\\\`git reset --mixed HEAD~1\\\\` to recover, the checkpoint data backing that work was already gone. \\\\`post-commit\\\\` now detects an empty-tree commit and skips condensation entirely; \\\\`prepare-commit-msg\\\\` warns before the commit lands, naming the recovery command and \\\\`GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0\\\\`.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n- Real repro against a binary built from \\\\`origin/main\\\\`: staged files silently committed as an empty tree, exit 0, files still on disk — confirmed with real git, not simulated.\\n- Same repro on this branch: both warnings fire, naming the exact recovery steps.\\n- New \\\\`gitrepo.IndexRecordsNoEntries\\\\` distinguishes \\\"missing\\\" from \\\"genuinely empty\\\" (only a positively-parsed zero-entry header counts), refuses non-regular files (stats before opening — a FIFO at the index path would otherwise block \\\\`open(2)\\\\` forever), and works on sha256 repos (verified against their different empty-tree hash).\\n- **Mutation-tested**: 9 deliberate mutations (removing the post-commit skip, removing the prepare-commit-msg wiring, removing the stat-before-open, etc.) each turn a passing test red, proving the tests aren't vacuous.\\n- Adversarial review pass found and fixed 5 issues before this PR (a coverage gap where deleting the hook wiring left everything green, the FIFO-blocking hazard, a dangling-trailer edge case documented as accepted, an errno-masking bug, and a factually-incorrect code comment) — see commit body for the full list.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n- \\\\`mise run fmt\\\\` clean, \\\\`mise run lint\\\\` 0 issues, \\\\`go vet\\\\` clean under default/integration/e2e tags.\\n- \\\\`mise run test\\\\`: 10,719 passed, 9 skipped. \\\\`mise run test:integration\\\\`: 565 passed, 3 skipped. \\\\`mise run test:e2e:canary\\\\`: 56 vogon + 4 roger-roger passed (free).\\n- \\\\`-race\\\\` clean on \\\\`gitrepo\\\\`, \\\\`cli\\\\`, \\\\`strategy\\\\`.\\n- \\\\`mise run check\\\\`/\\\\`test:ci\\\\` intentionally not run here (executes real agents with live model calls) — everything else it covers was run individually.\\n- Perf cost measured: +0.1ms per hook invocation.\\n\\n## Remaining risk (documented, not hidden)\\n- The corruption itself cannot be prevented from a hook — user-side mitigation is \\\\`GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0\\\\`, now named in the warning message.\\n- One accepted false positive: \\\\`git rm -r --cached .\\\\` then commit warns twice and skips post-commit condensation; the next ordinary commit condenses normally (verified).\\n- A kept (not reset) empty-tree commit still carries an unclaimed checkpoint trailer — documented, not suppressed, since suppressing it would make the warning conditional on a hazard the user may choose to ignore.\\n\\n## Side findings for a maintainer (out of scope here, not fixed in this PR)\\n- \\\\`strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go\\\\`'s \\\\`getStagedFiles\\\\` runs \\\\`git diff --cached\\\\` without \\\\`gitrepo.EnvWithoutRepoOverrides()\\\\` inside prepare-commit-msg, violating the rule this repo adopted after #2143 (~15 call sites share the gap). Consequence is a wrong condensation decision, not data loss.\\n- go-git's ENOENT-as-empty-index behavior is now documented but not defended against in a few of Entire's own readers (\\\\`content_overlap.go\\\\`, \\\\`settings/opf_command_trust.go\\\\`, \\\\`gitrepo.Status\\\\`) — no destructive consumer currently, but \\\\`IndexRecordsNoEntries\\\\` is there to route them through if someone wants to close this fully.\\n\\nRefs #2111\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2303/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2303/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2127\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2127/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2127/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2127/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2127\",\n              \"id\": 5252204619,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBA7zxw\",\n              \"number\": 2127,\n              \"title\": \"feat(grok): add Grok Build (xAI) agent integration\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-26T01:00:22Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-02T19:11:33Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2127\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2127\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2127.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2127.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1143\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nAdds Grok Build (xAI) as an Entire agent, registered as `grok`.\\n\\nBuilt through the research → write-tests → implement pipeline. Everything\\nbelow was verified against a real Grok 1.0.5 install, with captured payloads\\nand a real session transcript checked in as test fixtures.\\n\\n## What's here\\n\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/grok/` — the agent. Core `Agent` plus `HookSupport`,\\n  `HookFreshness`, `TranscriptAnalyzer`, `TokenCalculator`, `ModelExtractor`,\\n  and `SubagentSessionResolver`. Marked `IsPreview()`.\\n- `e2e/agents/grok.go` — E2E runner, so the existing `ForEachAgent` suite\\n  covers Grok. No new scenarios were needed.\\n- `scripts/test-grok-agent-integration.sh` — the probe used to capture payloads.\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/grok/AGENT.md` — research one-pager. Every claim is\\n  tagged `(doc)` / `(observed)` / `(unverified)`.\\n\\nHooks live in `.grok/hooks/entire.json`, a file Entire owns outright — Grok\\nmerges every `*.json` under `.grok/hooks/`, so install is a whole-file write and\\nuninstall a delete. A foreign file at that path is refused, not clobbered.\\n\\n## Three Grok behaviours with no analogue in the other agents\\n\\n1. **`StopCancelled` / `StopFailure` map to `TurnEnd`.** Grok fires those\\n   *instead of* `Stop` when a turn is interrupted, has a permission prompt\\n   declined, hits `--max-turns`, or errors upstream. Mapping only `Stop` loses a\\n   checkpoint for every Ctrl+C'd turn.\\n2. **`Stop` fires twice per session.** The teardown one carries\\n   `reason: \\\"shutdown\\\"` and no `promptId`. Treating it as a turn mints a\\n   duplicate, contentless checkpoint every session, so it is dropped.\\n3. **`updates.jsonl` lines are JSON-RPC envelopes.** The event kind is at\\n   `params.update.sessionUpdate`, two levels down — reading the top level yields\\n   nothing on every real transcript.\\n\\n## Test coverage\\n\\n100 unit tests (including subtests) in the grok package, built on verbatim fixtures from a real\\nsession. `mise run test:ci` is green.\\n\\n**E2E: 38 of 56 scenarios verified against real Grok** across four free-quota windows (08-25 through 09-02); the 18 remaining have only ever failed on quota/rate limits, including the\\nsubstantive ones — agent-commits-mid-turn, the subagent flow, stash/partial\\nstaging/split-changes, explain-from-clone, and the deep checkpoint metadata\\nvalidation.\\n\\nThe remaining 26 are unrun because the xAI account exhausted its **free Grok\\nBuild quota** partway through a full-suite run. Every one of those failures is\\n`You've reached your free Grok Build usage limit` or `resource-exhausted`; none\\nis attributable to this code. A full suite run costs roughly \\\\$5–20 at the\\nmeasured rate (\\\\$0.042 for a 2-call turn).\\n\\n## Fixes found along the way\\n\\n- **`content` shape collision** — Grok overloads the transcript `content` key\\n  (array on `tool_call_update`, object on message chunks). Typing it as a slice\\n  made every message chunk fail to unmarshal *silently*, since readers skip\\n  unparseable lines. Caught by a unit test using a real transcript.\\n- **`test:ci` on spaced paths** — `TestBetterleaksDoesNotPoisonGitEnvironment`\\n  interpolated the repo root into a synthesized `go.mod` `replace` directive\\n  unquoted, so it failed in any checkout whose path contains a space. Unrelated\\n  to Grok; fixed.\\n- **`agent` binary collision** — Cursor's CLI is named `agent`, and xAI's\\n  installer force-symlinks the same path. Whichever installs second owns it, so\\n  `$PATH` ordering cannot separate them and the `cursor-cli` E2E leg could\\n  exercise Grok while reporting Cursor. The runner now resolves the unambiguous\\n  `cursor-agent`, honours `E2E_CURSOR_BIN`, and probes `--version` as a backstop.\\n- **Foreign hook payloads** — Grok scans `~/.claude/settings.json` for hooks by\\n  default and treats the user scope as always-trusted, so it executes Entire's\\n  `entire hooks claude-code …` commands. Measured impact is nil (no session, no\\n  state, either side of the change), so the added guard is hardening plus a\\n  warning rather than a corruption fix — the comment says so. The real fix is\\n  `[compat.claude] hooks = false` in the user's `~/.grok/config.toml`.\\n\\n## Reviewer notes\\n\\n- **`grok` is deliberately NOT in the default E2E matrix.** It is wired into all\\n  three workflows as a `workflow_dispatch` choice with an `XAI_API_KEY` env, but\\n  `e2e.yml` runs on push to `main`, and enrolling a leg before the secret exists\\n  would break main. Promote it by adding `\\\"grok\\\"` to the `agents=[...]` arrays\\n  once the secret is configured.\\n- **`SubagentSessionResolver`'s happy path is unverified.** Grok subagents being\\n  independent child sessions is confirmed from a real run (one `spawn_subagent`\\n  produced two session IDs and the checkpoint held two top-level sessions both\\n  claiming the same file). The `subagents/meta.json` *field names* come from\\n  serde strings in the shipping binary, not documentation, and have not been\\n  checked against a real directory. The resolver fails closed — unique match\\n  required, stated parent must agree with the owning directory — so a mismatch\\n  is inert, not wrong. Confirming this is the first thing to do when quota returns.\\n- Agent-help classification: `grok` is registered like the other agents and\\n  inherits the existing agent surface; no new command was added, so there is no\\n  `agentHelpClassification` entry to review.\\n\\n## Since review\\n\\n- **Path traversal (trail finding, GHSA-2h46 class)** — `session_start` is the\\n  one hook without `transcriptPath`, so its `sessionId` became a directory\\n  component unvalidated. `sessionRef` now runs `validation.ValidateSessionID`\\n  at the choke point (as Pi does) and yields no `SessionRef` on an unsafe ID.\\n- **`entire session resume` launches Grok** — `ResumeCommandSpecFor` gained a\\n  `grok` case (`grok --resume <id>`, or `grok --continue` with no ID), with the\\n  same unsafe-ID guard as the other agents.\\n- **Merged `main`** (no rebase, so review threads stay attached) and adopted the\\n  new `AreHooksInstalled(ctx) (bool, error)` contract: missing hook file →\\n  `(false, nil)`, unreadable file or unresolvable root → error.\\n- Grok Build added to the supported-agent lists in `CLAUDE.md`, `e2e/README.md`,\\n  the contributor guide, the security doc, and the integration checklist.\\n- **Subagent double-count root-caused and fixed.** The 08-27 E2E re-run of\\n  `TestSubagentCommitFlow` still produced two top-level sessions both claiming\\n  `docs/red.md`. Logs show the child fires `subagent_stop` and `session_end` but\\n  never `stop`; `subagent_stop` was mapped to `SubagentEnd`, which the handler\\n  drops for lack of an in-flight marker (Grok gives no tool-use ID), so the\\n  `TurnEnd`-only `ResolveSubagentSession` path was never reached. `subagent_stop`\\n  now maps to the child's `TurnEnd` (the Droid Workers path) and `subagent_start`\\n  is a no-op (its pre-task capture failed on every launch). Falls back to the\\n  previous behaviour when no parent link resolves.\\n- All five review threads are addressed in code (three-tier hook timeouts,\\n  `XAI_API_KEY` scoped to the grok leg, `cwd`-keyed session group); the\\n  `parseTime`/`RFC3339` comment is a non-issue — Go's parser accepts fractional\\n  seconds with that layout, verified against the fixture timestamp.\\n\\n## Open product decisions (not decided in this PR)\\n\\n1. **Foreign-config collision.** Grok reads `~/.claude/settings.json` hooks by\\n   default, so it runs Entire's Claude Code hook commands with Grok payloads.\\n   The Claude Code side now ignores those payloads, and the E2E runner sets\\n   `[compat.claude] hooks = false`, but nothing in `entire enable` tells a real\\n   user to do the same. Options: warn during `entire enable grok` when\\n   `~/.grok/config.toml` lacks the compat switch, or leave it to docs.\\n2. **Project-trust gate.** Grok silently skips project hooks in a folder not\\n   listed in `~/.grok/trusted_folders.toml`, so `entire enable grok` can succeed\\n   while no hook ever fires. Options: detect and warn (pointing at\\n   `/hooks-trust`), or install into the always-trusted global `~/.grok/hooks/`\\n   — rejected in AGENT.md because it would fire Entire hooks in every repo.\\n\\n## Still blocked on xAI quota\\n\\n- Full E2E run (`mise run test:e2e --agent grok`, or dispatch `e2e.yml` with\\n  `agent=grok` once `XAI_API_KEY` exists as a repo secret).\\n- ~~Verifying `SubagentSessionResolver` / the subagent checkpoint shape~~ —\\n  **done (09-02)**: the resolver matched a real `subagents/meta.json`, and with\\n  the `FilesTouched` fix the checkpoint holds exactly one session plus\\n  `tasks/<child>/task.json`.\\n- Live observation of `SubagentStart/Stop`, `StopCancelled/Failure`,\\n  `PreCompact/PostCompact`, `Notification` — currently mapped from docs only.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches checkpoint lifecycle, subagent attribution, and cross-agent hook collision behavior; incorrect mappings could miss or duplicate checkpoints, though guards are conservative and E2E is opt-in on CI.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **Grok Build** as a preview Entire agent (`grok`): hooks in `.grok/hooks/entire.json`, lifecycle parsing (including `StopCancelled`/`StopFailure` as turn ends and filtering teardown `Stop`), `updates.jsonl` JSON-RPC transcript handling (tokens, models, file diffs), and a fail-closed **subagent parent linker**.\\n> \\n> **Claude Code** now ignores hook payloads with no `session_id` (with a warning), so Grok-driven invocations of global Claude hooks do not produce empty-session lifecycle events; tests cover real Grok-shaped payloads.\\n> \\n> **E2E**: new `e2e/agents/grok.go` (isolated `GROK_HOME`, compat flags, trust seeding, quota vs transient errors). Workflows expose `grok` on manual dispatch with `XAI_API_KEY` and install steps, but **not** in the default `main` matrix. **Cursor CLI** E2E prefers `cursor-agent` / `E2E_CURSOR_BIN` and fails bootstrap if `agent` resolves to Grok.\\n> \\n> Also adds a Grok integration probe script, registry/hooks wiring, and a small **redact** test fix quoting `go.mod` replace paths with spaces.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 9d6c40b389990d0d9634eb078c9ecbbc8eabfa8e. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2127/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2127/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1647\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1647/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1647/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1647/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1647\",\n              \"id\": 4818689564,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7uUjHy\",\n              \"number\": 1647,\n              \"title\": \"feat(review): exact scope and parallel skills for reviewer agents\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 2,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-07-06T11:32:12Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-16T21:23:48Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1647\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1647\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1647.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1647.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/766\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## One-sentence summary\\n\\nWhen `entire review` launches a reviewer, it now hands that reviewer everything the CLI already knows — exactly which code to review, how long it may run, which tools it may use, and how to start its configured skill — instead of a vague instruction each reviewer had to interpret for itself.\\n\\n## Problems, as observed in real runs\\n\\n1. **Reviewers re-derived — and sometimes got wrong — what code to review.** The composed prompt only said *\\\"review the commits unique to this branch vs origin/HEAD.\\\"* Each reviewer then ran its own git commands to work out what that meant. In one live run, codex diffed in the wrong direction on a branch that was behind main and reported main's newer code as regressions the branch had introduced — 2 of the 4 high-severity findings in that run's final verdict were such phantoms, and the judge consolidated them without any way to notice.\\n2. **Reviewers' tool calls were silently denied.** Headless `claude -p` auto-denies any tool call that isn't pre-approved, and the review command passed no permission config. Reviewers bounced off denials for `git diff` / `git log`, then either worked around them slowly or skipped verifying their findings.\\n3. **The configured skill never actually ran (claude).** The composed prompt *started* with the skill line (`/pr-review-toolkit:review-pr`). `claude -p` treats a leading slash as a slash command and expanded it — resolving to the **built-in** `/review` skill with the entire composed prompt stuffed in as its argument (it interpolated the skill name where a GitHub PR number belongs). Every claude review was silently running the wrong workflow.\\n4. **Setup wrote the built-in review brief into your settings file.** Guided setup and first-run persisted the default task text into `review_profiles.<name>.task` as if you had typed it — indistinguishable from user config, and frozen: improving the default wording could never reach existing profiles.\\n\\n## Changes (numbered to match the problems)\\n\\n1. **The exact scope is now in the composed prompt.** The review command already computes the commit list, the changed-file list (three-dot, vs merge-base), and the uncommitted files for its banner line — it now passes all of that to every reviewer, marked *\\\"authoritative — use as-is, do not re-derive\\\"*, plus the diff itself when it fits a size budget (otherwise the exact `git diff base...HEAD` command to run). The judge additionally receives the changed-file list with an instruction to **discard findings that point outside it** — so even a reviewer that somehow mis-scopes can't pollute the final verdict.\\n2. **Read-only tools are pre-approved.** Reviewers launch with `--allowedTools`: Read/Grep/Glob/Task/Skill plus enumerated read-only git subcommands (`diff`, `log`, `show`, `status`, `blame`, `rev-parse`, `merge-base`, `ls-files`). Deliberately **not** `Bash(git:*)` — git aliases/hooks execute arbitrary code and `push`/`commit` would match the blanket — and never `--dangerously-skip-permissions`: reviewers process untrusted diffs and must stay unable to modify the repo.\\n3. **The configured skill actually runs.** When the composed prompt would start with `/`, a prose preamble is prepended — *\\\"Lines starting with «/» name configured review skills: invoke each with the Skill tool and follow it\\\"* — making slash-expansion structurally impossible. Verified in live transcripts: real `Skill` tool invocations of the configured skill, followed by that skill's actual workflow.\\n4. **The built-in review brief is a runtime default, not saved config.** Reviewer behavior is **unchanged from main**: every reviewer still receives the profile's task, or the built-in default when none is set (#1312's deliberate design — a measured A/B without the brief was faster but missed a real finding). The only change is that setup persists an *empty* task, so saved profiles stay clean and pick up improved default wording. Pinned by `TestRunReview_TaskSemantics`.\\n\\n## What a reviewer receives now (abridged real capture)\\n\\n````\\nPerform the review below. Lines starting with \\\"/\\\" name configured review skills: invoke each with the Skill tool and follow it.\\n\\n/review\\n\\nReview profile: general\\n\\nTask: Review this change for correctness, regressions, API design, missing tests, … [profile task, or built-in default]\\n[output-format instructions]\\n\\nScope: review the commits unique to this branch vs main, plus any uncommitted changes in the working tree. …\\n\\nAuthoritative scope, computed by entire — use it as-is, do not re-derive it:\\n\\nCommits under review (oldest first):\\n3ae0a76 add feature\\n\\nFiles under review (vs merge-base with main):\\nA\\tfeature.go\\n\\nUncommitted working-tree changes:\\n?? notes.txt\\n\\nOnly the files listed above are in scope. Findings that point anywhere else are out of scope — discard them.\\n\\nDiff under review:\\n```diff\\ndiff --git a/feature.go b/feature.go\\n…\\n```\\n\\nCheckpoint context from commits in scope:\\n- a1b2c3d4e5f6: summary: add feature X handler; wire config loading; open: cover error path\\n- ... 3 more checkpoints omitted\\n\\nUse `entire explain <id>` for full checkpoint context, or `entire explain <id> --raw-transcript` for raw transcripts.\\n\\nIn-progress session context (uncommitted):\\n  95131576 claude-code (touched: 4 files) prompt: add retry handling to the dispatcher\\n````\\n\\n*(The checkpoint/session sections come from entire's own history for exactly the commits and working tree under review — the intent behind each commit and what any still-uncommitted agent session was doing. They're empty in fresh repos, which is why the raw capture above was taken with them elided; predates this PR, included here for completeness of what a reviewer receives.)*\\n\\nPlus env (`ENTIRE_REVIEW_*` session-tagging handshake, unchanged) and the `--allowedTools` flag from change 2.\\n\\n*Deadline handling is deliberately NOT part of this PR — it landed as #1664: the default reviewer timeout is dropped entirely (reviewers run until done, `--timeout` stays as an explicit cap). An activity-based stall detector was investigated and ruled out — legitimate review subagents run 12+ minutes with zero parent output, so no liveness signal distinguishes quiet work from a hang.*\\n\\n## Measured (same branch: 13 commits, 37 files, ~102KB diff; real claude runs)\\n\\n| | before | after |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| skill executed | built-in /review (by accident) | the configured skills, via real Skill invocations |\\n| phantom findings | 2 of 4 highs in one run | none |\\n| tool denials | present | none |\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- TDD throughout; every behavior change had a failing test first\\n- `mise run test`, `test:integration` (390), `test:e2e:canary` — green\\n- Shim smoke: a fake `claude` on PATH captures argv/env through a real `entire review` run; asserts prompt contents, allowlist, and flag shape end-to-end\\n- Multiple real-agent runs on a live branch verifying skill routing and scope accuracy, plus a dogfood run of the command against this PR itself (its findings became commits here)\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Also folded in: skill fan-out (was #1651)\\n\\nA worker configured with N skills joined them into one child's prompt: the skills ran sequentially (or blended into one muddled pass), so selecting more skills grew the wait linearly. Measured live: a two-skill claude worker took ~9 minutes as a single child. The parallel machinery already existed one level up (worker slots fan out in `run_multi`); multi-skill selection just never used it.\\n\\n- **`explodeSkillWorkers`**: at plan time, each multi-skill worker becomes one worker per skill (keys like `claude-code:review`, deduped against existing worker names; agent/model/prompt preserved). Wait becomes max(skills) instead of sum(skills). Two exploded workers also engage the judge, extending crew+judge consolidation to single-agent multi-skill profiles.\\n- **`--agent` selects a filtered crew**: all of that agent's workers run (previously: ambiguity error). Single-agent path only when exactly one worker matches.\\n- **Session matching by skills**: same-agent same-model exploded workers defeat the agent+model matcher — `AgentRun` gains `Skills`, and the matcher requires skill-set agreement when both sides carry skills (recorded from `ENTIRE_REVIEW_SKILLS` by the lifecycle hook). Adversarially-ordered test fails without the discriminator.\\n- TDD throughout; shim smoke: a two-skill profile spawns two one-skill children in parallel (~3s wall) plus one judge invocation.\\n\\nWas stacked as #1651 (its diff was exactly the last commit here); combined into one PR for a single review/approval/merge.\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1647/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1647/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2320\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2320/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2320/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2320/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2320\",\n              \"id\": 5386576708,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCq1lnw\",\n              \"number\": 2320,\n              \"title\": \"refactor(gitrepo): finish Git metadata consumer migration\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"id\": 34813274,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-08T12:16:46Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-18T08:10:41Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2320\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2320\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2320.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2320.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Part 5 of #2190's [agreed split](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2190#issuecomment-5499945525), following the canonical resolver in #2241 and checkpoint migration in #2254.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis branch includes the session migration from #2285 and strategy migration from #2305. Both prerequisites remain open. Keep this PR **open** until they land, then refresh onto main so reviewers can assess the remaining-consumer changes separately.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Why this change is needed\\r\\n\\r\\nThe earlier migrations introduced `gitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata`, but several consumers still interpreted Git metadata through older code. Codex and status had their own traversal logic. Settings, review, investigation, and trail still depended on forwarding helpers or the common-directory resolver and cache.\\r\\n\\r\\nLeaving those callers behind would preserve the disagreement this refactor is meant to remove. A caller could reuse a cached directory after metadata changed, or interpret a linked worktree differently from the session and checkpoint stores using the same repository.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis PR moves the remaining physical metadata lookups to the canonical resolver and deletes the old implementations after their final callers migrate.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Metadata resolution and storage ownership\\r\\n\\r\\n`gitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata` supplies the per-worktree Git directory, common Git directory, and worktree ID for an explicit worktree root. It returns complete metadata or an error, without running Git or caching the result.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe remaining consumers use those facts for different purposes:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Codex determines which checkout owns the discovered hook configuration. Its backlink, trust, submodule, and bare-layout checks remain consumer policy.\\r\\n- Status reads HEAD from the per-worktree Git directory. Explain and cleanup use the resolved worktree ID when selecting checkpoint or shadow-branch state.\\r\\n- Settings locates clone preferences in the common directory.\\r\\n- Review and investigation locate their shared markers, manifests, and findings.\\r\\n- Trail locates shared metadata and the base directory for checkout paths.\\r\\n- Setup cleanup opens the common directory through the shared rooted API.\\r\\n\\r\\n`paths.WorktreeRoot` still owns CWD discovery and its cache. `gitdir` still owns shared `os.Root` handles, including their lifetime and explicit reset behavior. Reads, writes, and locks continue through the existing rooted/no-follow storage code.\\r\\n\\r\\nGit queries remain where their answer establishes repository membership, validates a reusable worktree, or inspects configuration and history. Replacing those queries with filesystem traversal would remove validation that the resolver does not provide.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Failure behavior and printed paths\\r\\n\\r\\nThe tests exercise callers after a successful lookup, damage `commondir`, then repair it without clearing a metadata cache.\\r\\n\\r\\nRequired operations fail while metadata is broken. These include clone-preference writes, review marker and manifest writes, investigation-store construction, and cleanup preview. Optional callers retain their own behavior: status omits an unavailable branch, explain skips worktree filtering, settings skips an unresolved preferences layer, and trail refresh can still spawn when its throttle metadata cannot resolve. Repair restores access to the previously saved content.\\r\\n\\r\\nTrail checkout also needs to preserve the path it prints. The first full verification run caught a regression where discovery changed macOS `/var` paths to `/private/var`. Trail now recovers the caller's spelling only after confirming that a CWD ancestor identifies the discovered root. Regression tests cover entry from both the checkout root and a nested directory.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Legacy deletion and diff size\\r\\n\\r\\nWith the remaining callers migrated, this removes:\\r\\n\\r\\n- `paths.GetWorktreeID` and its marker-based parser.\\r\\n- The exported `ResolveDotGitPath` and `ResolveCommonGitPath` composition APIs and their old implementations.\\r\\n- Session common-directory forwarding and cache-clearing APIs.\\r\\n- The `gitdir` common-directory resolver/cache, obsolete resets, and cache-only tests.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe final ownership guard has no migration exceptions. It retains individually documented discovery, semantic-query, and policy exceptions, and fails when an exception becomes stale.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe part-5 commit changes 49 files: 18 production files, 30 tests, fixtures, or benchmarks, and one documentation file. Most test edits replace deleted APIs or remove obsolete cache resets. Production Go shrinks by 301 lines.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Verification\\r\\n\\r\\nThe implementation's final `mise run check` passed, including race-enabled unit and integration tests, Vogon 56/56, and the external deterministic canary 4/4. A subsequent pre-push lint run passed with zero issues.\\r\\n\\r\\nIndependent review reran the focused migration tests with race detection, plus the full settings, investigation, and paths suites. Real Git fixtures cover eleven layouts, including ordinary and linked worktrees, bare-backed worktrees, separate Git directories, submodules, relative pointers, moved registrations, and aliases. Tests check actual stored files, recovery after metadata repair, rooted-handle lifetime, lock ordering and release, and printed trail paths.\\r\\n\\r\\nTemporary source mutations confirmed that the ownership guard rejects independent traversal, a metadata query hidden behind a constant, and a stale exception.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe same Trace2 fixture was run against the integrated prerequisite baseline and this implementation:\\r\\n\\r\\n| Operation | Before | After |\\r\\n|---|---:|---:|\\r\\n| Session construction from cold CWD | 1 | 1 |\\r\\n| Session construction with an explicit root | 0 | 0 |\\r\\n| Queue construction from an open repository | 0 | 0 |\\r\\n| Prepare-commit with no session | 2 | 2 |\\r\\n| Enabled text status with no session | 5 | 4 |\\r\\n| Codex discovery from cold CWD | 1 | 1 |\\r\\n\\r\\nThese count Git subprocesses inside the named entry points. They do not measure full CLI startup or establish latency improvements.\\r\\n\\r\\nWindows test binaries cross-compiled during implementation. Windows runtime testing and paid real-agent E2E tests were not performed.\\r\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2320/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2320/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3003\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3003/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3003/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3003/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3003\",\n              \"id\": 6193578260,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABMsJW4A\",\n              \"number\": 3003,\n              \"title\": \"fix(hooks): take Entire's hook out of entire-brain's chain on uninstall\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n                \"id\": 26940511,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI2OTQwNTEx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Beehtrix\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-04T00:14:10Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-06T01:12:36Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3003\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3003\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3003.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3003.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes #2957\\n\\n**Please review this after #2959.** This branch sits on top of #2959 (`d6690097c`), so until that merges the diff here also shows #2959's commit. The change for this PR is only the last commit, `a4ef1e8ba`, which touches `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/hook_backup.go` and its test file (+435/−1). One test case needs #2959 (details below). If #2959 changes or merges, I'll rebase this onto main.\\n\\n@peyton-alt @Soph: I filed #2957 and nobody is assigned yet. Could you assign it to me? This is the uninstall half of the Brain hook problem; #2959 is the doctor/install half.\\n\\n## What was wrong\\n\\n`entire brain connect` moves the `pre-push` hook it finds to `pre-push.pre-entire-brain` and runs it through a path relative to its own:\\n\\n```sh\\nbackup=\\\"$0.pre-entire-brain\\\"\\nif [ -x \\\"$backup\\\" ]; then exec \\\"$backup\\\" \\\"$@\\\"; fi\\n```\\n\\nOn uninstall, `restoreWrapped` only handles a moved copy that a wrapper names literally (`runsByName`). Brain's wrapper never names `pre-push.pre-entire-brain`, so `entire disable --uninstall` reported success but left Entire's hook in that file. The next `git push` still ran `entire hooks git pre-push`.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\n- `isBrainChain` recognises only the exact wrapper entire-brain v0.4.0 writes, byte for byte except the single-quoted plugin path it bakes in. That wrapper exits 0 when its copy is gone. An earlier version of this fix parsed `\\\"$0<suffix>\\\"` references in any shell script. Five rounds of bot review on my fork each found another shell form it got wrong, so I switched to the exact match. Anything it doesn't accept, including an edited Brain wrapper, goes down the existing path, the same as on `main`.\\n- `restoreBrainChain` runs inside `restoreWrapped` when the moved copy holds Entire's hook:\\n  - Brain's wrapper in `pre-push`, no user hook in `pre-push.pre-entire`: the copy is removed.\\n  - Brain's wrapper in `pre-push`, a user hook in `pre-push.pre-entire`: the user's hook moves into the copy, where Brain's wrapper runs it. Brain's own install would have left it that way.\\n  - Entire's hook in `pre-push` and Brain's wrapper backed up (Entire re-wrapped Brain): the copy is removed before the wrapper is put back.\\n- Left as on `main`: a keep copy beside the moved file, and a user hook that names the copy or finds its own path (`$0`, `${0`, `BASH_SOURCE`, `__file__`, `sys.argv`, `__FILE__`, `__filename`, `__dirname`, `process.argv`), because moving such a hook could change what it runs.\\n- Install is unchanged.\\n\\n## Why it needs #2959\\n\\nWith #2959, a later `entire enable` leaves a runnable Brain wrapper in front instead of re-wrapping it. The test case \\\"Entire installed again after brain, with a user hook\\\" expects exactly that: after uninstall, the user's hook still runs from behind Brain's wrapper, and Entire's doesn't. On `main` alone, the second install still re-wraps and rotates the user's hook away, so that case fails there (`pre-push.pre-entire-brain missing`, `ran \\\"\\\", want \\\"user\\\"`). The other cases pass both with and without #2959. \\\"Entire re-wrapped a non-executable brain, user hook rotated away\\\" covers the one path that still re-wraps (a wrapper that can't run).\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nIn `strategy/hook_backup_test.go`:\\n\\n- `TestRemoveHooks_AfterBrainWrapperLeavesNoEntireHook` runs install and uninstall across the Brain layouts: wrapper in front, installed again after Brain, Brain wrapping the user's hook first, a non-executable wrapper, with and without a user hook. It then runs `pre-push` and checks what ran. A \\\"not exactly brain's wrapper\\\" case keeps `main`'s behaviour.\\n- `TestRemoveHooks_NearBrainLayouts` covers the layouts that must stay as on `main`: a keep copy, the wrapper both at the hook path and backed up, a literal wrapper over Entire, a hook that only mentions the copy in a comment, and user hooks that name the copy or use `$0`, `BASH_SOURCE`, `__file__` or `sys.argv`.\\n- `TestIsBrainChain` covers the exact-match recogniser: quoted, unquoted and half-quoted plugin paths, the delimiter inside the path, CRLF, and edits around the chain (commented out, code after the exec, a check before it).\\n\\nEach case added during review failed on the code before its fix.\\n\\n## What I ran\\n\\nClean `env -i`, throwaway HOME, Go 1.27.3, git 2.56, on this exact tree. It's identical to the tree the bots reviewed on my fork (fork PR `408e3a3e5` merged onto `d6690097c`).\\n\\n- `mise run lint`: 0 issues.\\n- Complexity gate the way CI runs it (`cd tools/complexity && go test ./...`, then `BASE_REF=711697ee5 mise run complexity:gate`): pass.\\n- `go vet` plus `go test -count=1` of `./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/` and `./cmd/entire/cli/`: pass. The new tests: pass.\\n- Earlier on the same tree: `-race` on `strategy`, Windows/darwin vet and a Windows test build all pass. Full `mise run test` gave 18089 tests and 1 failure, `TestClient_Get_NamesUnresolvableHost`, which needs DNS that my sandbox doesn't have; it fails the same way on `main`. `TestHandlePush_RealSendPack_ShallowRepoAmendsAgent` (`internal/remotehelper/githelper`) panics now and then on plain `main` here too (3 of 5 runs), so it's a flaky test, not caused by this change.\\n- Mutation: with `isBrainChain` forced to false, the Brain cases fail.\\n\\n## Limits I know about\\n\\n- **In the layouts left as on `main`** (a user hook that finds its own path or names the copy), Entire's copy still runs after uninstall, exactly as on `main` today. Reviewers suggested replacing the copy with a tiny script that `exec`s the user's hook at its current path. That would take Entire out of the chain without moving the user's hook, but it leaves an Entire-written file behind after uninstall (as `noopMovedHook` already does). That's a design choice for you, so it's not in this PR. I'm happy to do it as a follow-up if you want it.\\n- **The own-path list is best effort.** A hook that finds its path some other way gets moved, the same way Entire's and Brain's installs move hooks today.\\n- **An edited Entire copy** (user lines kept by #2959) is replaced or removed on uninstall. `main` handles Entire's own edited `pre-push` the same way: any hook with Entire's marker counts as Entire's.\\n- **Only Brain v0.4.0's wrapper is recognised.** If Brain changes its wrapper text, uninstall falls back to `main`'s behaviour. Giving Brain's wrapper a marker would make this sturdier, but that's a change on the Brain side.\\n\\n## Review on my fork\\n\\nThe bots reviewed this on my fork (Beehtrix/cli#7) at `408e3a3e5`. Codex: no findings on the final head. Greptile: no comments. Qodo and Kilo raised the `sys.argv` / `BASH_SOURCE` / copy-naming cases, which are fixed and tested. Their remaining point is the fallback in the first limit above. Kilo's edited-copy note is the third limit.\\n\\nThe commit has no `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer. It wasn't made in an Entire-tracked session, so there's no checkpoint to link.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3003/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 1,\n                \"+1\": 1,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3003/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3107\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3107/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3107/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3107/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3107\",\n              \"id\": 6314389823,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABOMkDFw\",\n              \"number\": 3107,\n              \"title\": \"soph/release-0-13-2\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-10T19:37:37Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-10T20:11:53Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-11-10T20:11:51Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3107\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3107\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3107.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3107.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-11-10T20:11:51Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"This draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back a trail. Feel free to edit the title or body, but keep the hidden marker below: Entire uses it to close this pull request when the trail closes.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Changelog-only update with no runtime or build changes.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Documents the 0.13.2 release** in `CHANGELOG.md` only—no application code in this diff.\\n> \\n> The new section calls out **service-account secret** CLI commands and `ENTIRE_TOKEN` / `git-remote-entire` behavior, **standalone `git-remote-entire` archives** per platform, and **auto-install for the `entire-rsl` plugin**. **Token usage** for sessions/checkpoints is now taken from each agent’s running total (with `session_token_usage` on checkpoints). **Repository-scoped** `entire trail create` / `update` are removed in favor of project trails; trail output drops assignees and aggregate comment counts. **OpenCode** checkpoint/export and live-view fixes are listed, plus fixes for **Antigravity** transcript paths, **`entire api` / `entire recap` repo cell routing**, and **`install.sh` checksum** verification.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 81c5454dc0a6f1d16497b8126d619ffce215c111. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3107/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3107/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": {\n                \"id\": 2626939,\n                \"client_id\": \"Iv23lieFG10uOnChW4TN\",\n                \"slug\": \"entire\",\n                \"node_id\": \"A_kwHOAfprLM4AKBV7\",\n                \"owner\": {\n                  \"login\": \"entireio\",\n                  \"id\": 33188652,\n                  \"node_id\": \"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjMzMTg4NjUy\",\n                  \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33188652?v=4\",\n                  \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.g