entireio/cli/pull/2774\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2774.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2774.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-14T17:52:28Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1571\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Documentation-only change to CHANGELOG.md; no runtime or CLI behavior is modified in this diff.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds a **0.11.5 (2026-10-14)** section to `CHANGELOG.md`, documenting the release that shipped in other PRs.\\n> \\n> **Breaking / migrations** called out include dropping shadow branches for pending agent work (session state + commit-time checkpoints), removing line-level AI/Human attribution from `entire blame` and checkpoint metadata, and narrowing `entire repo delete` to `/et/...` paths only.\\n> \\n> **Notable additions** in the notes: `entire checkpoint delete`, `entire trail merge`, opt-in project-scoped trails, create wizards, mirror detach, cascade repo delete, cross-repo `checkpoint explain`, agent-home session lookup, and Workflow/fork subagent capture.\\n> \\n> **Other sections** summarize behavior changes (session attach, review trust model, BFF removal for activity/dispatch), security fixes (HTTPS downgrade, proxy env, sandboxed summary generation), and housekeeping.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 77dba51dba0510efe9564c25a80fb2cc7be3f34a. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2774/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2774/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2582\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2582/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2582/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2582/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2582\",\n              \"id\": 5570810040,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABE9iZZw\",\n              \"number\": 2582,\n              \"title\": \"Redone commits keep their checkpoint trailers\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-24T15:40:47Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-01T18:53:35Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-01T18:53:32Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2582\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2582\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2582.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2582.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-01T18:53:32Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1420\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Redone commits keep their checkpoint trailers\\n\\nBuilds on #2574 (squash, merged), which added the post-commit fix both rely on: condense only into the trailer that has no checkpoint yet. This diff is the redo work only.\\n\\n**Symptom.** An agent commits several times during a session, then the work is redone as logical commits with `git reset` and new commits. The new commits have no `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer, so the session disappears from the trail.\\n\\n**Cause.** A reset leaves no message to copy trailers from.\\n\\n**Fix, in prepare-commit-msg (agent-agnostic):**\\n- **Where the dropped work starts:** it's read from HEAD's reflog, not `ORIG_HEAD`, so unstaging or a stash doesn't lose it. Resets that didn't move HEAD are skipped, and the tip the last real reset left is where the dropped work starts.\\n- **What counts as dropped:** only commits that tip alone reaches. Commits still on HEAD, a remote or another branch are never inherited, so merged-in main history and a teammate's commit that an undone rebase brought in stay out. A backup branch pointing at the tip itself doesn't count.\\n- **When a trailer is inherited:** a dropped commit's trailers are copied only when *every* staged file it changed is byte-identical to its dropped version. One matching lockfile, empty file or deletion among rewritten files is not a redo.\\n- **When the redo ends:** commits made since the reset keep it open only if each of them redid dropped work. A checkout, merge, rebase or pull ends it.\\n- **Amend folds too:** `git reset --soft HEAD~1 && git commit --amend` inherits the folded commit's trailer.\\n- **Inherited trailers are links:** they're recorded as inherited, so post-commit never condenses into one. That covers the editor flow, where the inherited trailer lands after the stamped one.\\n\\n**Adversarial review (Stefan).** Stefan's red tests for reset are here, split from 4a5df627d0. All 8 failures are fixed: a coincidental lockfile, a convergent deletion, an old reset window, merged-in main, an undone rebase, editor-flow ordering, unstaging after `reset --soft`, and an amend fold. His 4 guards still pass.\\n\\n**Measured with real hooks.** One session made two linked commits, then they were redone:\\n\\n| Redo | Nightly | This branch |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `reset --soft` + one `commit -m` | 0 trailers | 2 |\\n| `reset` + two commits, one per file | 0, 0 | 1, 1 |\\n\\n**Follow-ups.** Matching is per file; it could be tightened to hunks if commit-level precision matters.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes prepare-commit-msg and inherited-trailer bookkeeping that drive which checkpoint receives condensed session data; mistakes could mis-link sessions or write metadata under the wrong ID, though coverage is heavy on edge cases.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Redone commits keep their `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers** when work is replayed after `git reset`, so agent sessions stay on the trail after squash-style redos.\\n> \\n> `prepare-commit-msg` now calls **`withRedoneTrailers`**, which finds commits dropped by the latest real reset via **HEAD reflog** (not `ORIG_HEAD`), limits inheritance to commits only the old tip still reaches, and copies trailers only when staged content **byte-matches** the dropped commit’s files. **Amend-after-soft-reset** folds dropped trailers through **`prepareAmendCommitMsg`**; inherited IDs are recorded like squash links so post-commit does not condense into them. **`recordInheritedTrailersOnAmend`** and shared **`writeInheritedTrailers`** adjust parent-hash handling for amends.\\n> \\n> Adds **`manual_commit_redo.go`**, unit/adversarial redo tests, integration adversarial post-commit tests, and architecture docs for the redo rules.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 03b59cc8cd3a9ec54229abee77611495ccf7fd83. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2582/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2582/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2842\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2842/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2842/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2842/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2842\",\n              \"id\": 5949416645,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABJpVxlQ\",\n              \"number\": 2842,\n              \"title\": \"Changelog 0.11.6\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n         