ew**\\n> **Publishes the [0.11.6] release notes (2026-10-20)** by replacing the empty `[Unreleased]` heading with a dated section and recording what shipped in this version.\\n> \\n> The new entry calls out **breaking/migration** items: removal of `entire trail request-changes` and deprecation of `entire trail resume --repo`. It also summarizes **Added** work (per-reviewer review configs, trail merge branch controls, worktree session linking, release-mirror installs, etc.), **Changed** behavior (project trails for repo writers, stdin-based prompts for privacy, search 429 backoff), a large **Fixed** set centered on redaction, token counts, checkpoints on redo commits, and remote-helper quoting, plus **Housekeeping** (transcript package refactor, Go 1.27.3, govulncheck).\\n> \\n> This PR only edits `CHANGELOG.md`; it does not implement the listed features.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit ac59f3091e6635a218b7f4a176fd47775b9ab37e. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2842/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2842/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2305\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2305/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2305/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2305/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2305\",\n              \"id\": 5371939122,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCfGZcQ\",\n              \"number\": 2305,\n              \"title\": \"refactor(strategy): use canonical git metadata resolution (split part 4)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"id\": 34813274,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-07T08:15:33Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-16T03:45:51Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2305\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2305\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2305.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2305.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Strategy and hook paths still resolve Git metadata through separate helpers and subprocesses. This moves their physical directory and worktree-ID lookups to `gitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata`, using explicit worktree roots while preserving rooted storage access and caller-owned failure policy.\\n\\nPart 4 of #2190’s [agreed split](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2190#issuecomment-5499945525), following #2241 and #2254. **Depends on #2285 (part 3).** Keep this PR **open** until part 3 lands; then rebase onto refreshed main and rerun checks before requesting review.\\n\\n## Before requesting review\\n\\n- Move `session.NewStateStore` in this PR together with the session lock. This PR moves `stateLockForSession` to `paths.WorktreeRoot` + `gitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata`, but the CWD store stays on `gitdir.CommonDir` until #2320. With an exported `GIT_DIR`, state files and their lock would land in different repositories.\\n- Move the sweep throttle with the store, so the zombie list and the throttle marker use one resolver. Prefer taking the marker location from the store that listed the zombies.\\n- Decide how split `GIT_DIR`/`GIT_WORK_TREE` layouts behave. The canonical resolver reads `.git` inside the work tree, so once the store, lock, and sweep move, session state fails when the work tree has no `.git`. Either add a CWD entry point that honors exported `GIT_DIR`/`GIT_COMMON_DIR`, or reject the layout with a clear error and document it.\\n- Rebase onto `main` after #2285 lands; the branch currently conflicts.\\n\\n## Metadata resolution and storage\\n\\nThe canonical resolver supplies the common Git directory, per-worktree Git directory, and worktree ID for strategy storage, hook sequence detection, reset, cleanup, reconciliation, checkpoint-sync capture, and session routing. Shared session state and captured sync settings remain in the common directory; rebase and cherry-pick markers remain per-worktree.\\n\\nThe resolver stays context-free, option-free, cache-free, subprocess-free, and all-or-error. Strategy retains discovery and error policy. Reads, writes, and locks continue through the existing rooted/no-follow storage primitives. Git queries that validate repository membership or inspect configuration/history remain; explicitly targeted queries use the existing `EnvWithoutRepoOverrides` helper.\\n\\n## Consistent locking across aliases\\n\\nMulti-store session operations resolve every directory identity before creating or acquiring locks. They deduplicate and order repositories by filesystem identity: device/inode on Unix and volume/file index on Windows, matching the identifiers used by `os.SameFile`.\\n\\nPath sorting alone is insufficient on a case-insensitive filesystem. For example, callers using `alpha` and `Alpha` can order the same repository differently relative to `Beta`, then each block on the other caller’s first lock. Identity ordering makes both callers choose the same physical order. Rooted lock acquisition, cancellation behavior, and reverse-order release are preserved.\\n\\n## Scope of deletion\\n\\n`strategy.GetGitCommonDir` is removed after migrating its callers. Shared session/gitdir resolver and cache APIs, `paths.GetWorktreeID`, and the old gitrepo composition APIs remain for the remaining consumers and final cleanup. Settings, status, Codex, trail, and unrelated consumers are outside this slice.\\n\\nThe shared migration ledger entries remain unchanged. Retired query entries now log diagnostics so the intermediate migration passes; unlisted queries and independent traversal still fail the guard. Final strict ledger cleanup belongs to part 5.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `mise run check`: passed in 279.46 seconds, including formatting, zero-issue lint, race-enabled unit/integration tests, Vogon 56/56, and the external deterministic canary 4/4.\\n- A subsequent pre-push `mise run lint` passed.\\n- `mise run dup`: completed with 908 repository-wide advisory findings; none involve the four files in the lock-ordering fix.\\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\\n- Windows amd64 strategy tests cross-compiled successfully; Windows runtime testing was not performed.\\n- The case-alias ordering regression failed before the fix and passes afterward on macOS. The original temporary reproduction also passes. Other focused tests assert real lock contention and release, invalid identities before lock creation, lexical path preservation, shared-worktree storage, metadata damage/repair, linked-worktree reset, supported conflicting Git selectors, and no-follow refusal.\\n- No paid real-agent E2E tests ran.\\n\\nIndependent Trace2 runs against parent `3dbdf8b83` and the migration measured complete strategy methods with fresh strategy instances and cleared discovery caches:\\n\\n| Operation | Parent | After |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\\n| PrepareCommitMsg, no session | 4 | 3 |\\n| PrepareCommitMsg, active session | 3 | 2 |\\n| PostCommit, no session | 2 | 2 |\\n| PostCommit, active condensation | 13 | 12 |\\n\\nThese count Git subprocesses within the strategy methods, not full Cobra startup, and do not establish latency improvements.\\n\\n## Findings while working on this PR\\n\\nWhile testing repository isolation, I found that `gitrepo.EnvWithoutRepoOverrides()` removes `GIT_DIR`, `GIT_WORK_TREE`, and `GIT_INDEX_FILE`, but leaves `GIT_COMMON_DIR`.\\n\\nI reproduced the failure with two isolated repositories, each with a different `core.hooksPath`. With `GIT_COMMON_DIR` pointing to repository B, a Git subprocess targeting repository A and using the helper returned B's hooks path. The command succeeded without reporting an error.\\n\\nAdding `GIT_COMMON_DIR` to the filter makes the same query return A's hooks path. A local follow-up fix includes tests for variable removal and the real Git query.\\n\\nThis omission already exists on `main` and is excluded from this refactor. The reproduction deliberately supplied the environment variable; I have not confirmed an incident during normal use.\\n\\n## Separate existing limitations\\n\\nMulti-store lock acquisition retains its existing unbounded wait behavior; cancellation while blocked is not newly made interruptible here.\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2305/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2305/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2959\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2959/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2959/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2959/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2959\",\n              \"id\": 6096267049,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABLed7OQ\",\n              \"number\": 2959,\n              \"title\": \"fix(doctor): count Brain's pre-push wrapper as installed hooks\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n                \"id\": 26940511,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI2OTQwNTEx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Beehtrix\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 6,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-29T08:55:07Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-07T01:11:25Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2959\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2959\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2959.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2959.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes #2949\\nRelated to #2960\\n\\n@peyton-alt @Soph: I asked on the issue to be assigned (https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2949#issuecomment-6486951877) and haven't had a reply yet. I'm opening this so it can be reviewed. If you'd rather fix it on the Brain side instead (giving Brain's wrapper a marker `doctor` recognizes), tell me and I'll close this.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\n`entire brain connect` installs its own `pre-push` hook. It moves the hook it finds (Entire's) to `pre-push.pre-entire-brain`, and its own hook ends with:\\n\\n```sh\\nbackup=\\\"$0.pre-entire-brain\\\"\\nif [ -x \\\"$backup\\\" ]; then exec \\\"$backup\\\" \\\"$@\\\"; fi\\n```\\n\\nSo Entire's hook still runs, with git's stdin and arguments. But the new `pre-push` doesn't have the `# Entire CLI hooks` marker, so `hookStateIn` treats it as foreign and reports the whole set as `GitHooksAbsent`. I checked what happens next with the real plugin (brain v0.4.0, and v0.5.0 since its release today, see Verification):\\n\\n- `entire doctor` shows `Git hooks: NOT INSTALLED` / \\\"Commits in this repository are not captured as checkpoints\\\" on a setup that works, and suggests `--force` to fix it.\\n- `EnsureSetup` runs on every agent turn and reinstalls whenever `IsGitHookInstalled` is false. On the first turn after `brain connect`, it backs Brain's hook up to `pre-push.pre-entire`, puts Entire's hook in front, and prints `[entire] Your pre-push hook still runs, after Entire's (moved to .git/hooks/pre-push.pre-entire).` into the agent's hook output. After that, doctor says OK again.\\n\\nPushes keep working after that re-wrap. Entire's new `pre-push` runs Entire, then Brain's hook from `pre-push.pre-entire`. Brain's `$0`-relative chain then looks for `pre-push.pre-entire.pre-entire-brain`, which doesn't exist, so it stops there (Brain's source says that's deliberate, so the host's hook doesn't run twice). The old Entire copy in `pre-push.pre-entire-brain` is left behind and nothing runs it. So the bug users see is doctor's false report (and its `--force` advice) between `brain connect` and the next agent turn, plus a re-wrap that isn't needed. Commits and pushes were always captured.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\nThe changes are in `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks.go`, a `skip` parameter on `refreshMovedEntireHooks` in `hook_backup.go`, and a small per-OS execute check (`hook_exec_unix.go`, `hook_exec_windows.go`).\\n\\n`hookStateIn`: if `pre-push` doesn't have Entire's marker but is Brain's wrapper, it classifies the copy the wrapper runs (`pre-push.pre-entire-brain`) the same way it classifies `pre-push` today:\\n\\n- Entire's current hook there → `GitHooksCurrent`, and doctor says OK.\\n- Entire's hook from before the ref list → `GitHooksOutdated`, and it gets reinstalled (see below).\\n- Anything else → `GitHooksAbsent`, as before.\\n\\n\\\"Brain's wrapper\\\" means exactly the hook entire-brain writes (`pushHookContent` in entire-brain), with only the plugin path left open. The path has to be the same in both places, quoted the way Brain's `shellSingleQuote` quotes it. Any edit to the wrapper reads as another tool's hook and takes the existing re-wrap path. That includes an early `exit`, the chain inside a condition, a second `backup=`, or even a harmless extra command. Earlier versions of this PR matched the marker, `backup=` and `exec` lines one by one. Automated review found several edits that kept those lines but never ran the chain, so I switched to the exact match. It fails safe: anything it doesn't accept gets the behavior `main` has today.\\n\\nBoth files must be regular files (read NoFollow), and the kernel must let this process execute them. The check calls `faccessat(X_OK)` on the hook's name, relative to the hooks directory's own descriptor (opened from the existing `os.Root`), with the real ids. That's what git's `access(X_OK)` and Brain's `[ -x ]` guard ask, so ownership, the permission class that applies, POSIX ACLs and root all count the same way, and no path is resolved outside the root. A check that accepts any execute bit is wrong in both directions:\\n\\n- A copy at mode `0655` owned by the user reads as runnable, but git and `[ -x ]` skip it.\\n- A named-user ACL can deny execute even when the mode allows it, or grant it when the mode doesn't.\\n\\nWindows has no execute bit, so there both files only have to be regular files.\\n\\n`installHooks` (the Brain branch lives in `installBehindBrainWrapper` and `updateEditedBrainCopy`): when `pre-push` is Brain's wrapper and the copy it runs is Entire's (same check), it writes Entire's hook into that copy and leaves the wrapper alone, instead of backing the wrapper up to `pre-push.pre-entire`.\\n\\n- If Entire had already backed up the user's own `pre-push` to `pre-push.pre-entire` before Brain was installed, the copy gets the chained hook, the same content Entire would write at the hook path. Its `$(dirname \\\"$0\\\")`-relative chain still finds the user's hook from there.\\n- Before writing that copy, it refreshes any other moved copies of Entire's hook to the hook that never chains, the same way the normal install path does. Without that, a manager's wrapper in `pre-push.pre-entire` that runs an older Entire copy could chain back to `pre-push.pre-entire` forever.\\n- Right before each write it re-reads the copy. If another tool replaced it after install read it, install stops with `errHookChangedDuringInstall`, as the hook path already does.\\n- The copy is only rewritten whole when it reads Outdated or is exactly a pre-push hook Entire writes (chained or not, for the prefix its own line runs).\\n\\nIf the user added lines to the copy, it still reads Current, so doctor says OK and agent turns leave it alone. That's the same rule `TestCheckGitHookState_UserAdditionsAreNotDrift` and #2878 set for Entire's own hook. Before this change, both re-wrapped Brain's hook.\\n\\nAn explicit install (`entire enable`, `entire configure --force` or `--absolute-git-hook-path`) over such an edited copy replaces only the one line that runs Entire's pre-push handler, keeps the user's lines, and prints `[entire] Updated the line that runs Entire in .git/hooks/pre-push.pre-entire-brain; the lines you added there are kept.` That line has to be exactly one Entire wrote: today's line for any prefix, or a line from before the ref list. Without this, an edited copy with an old line that ignores Entire's exit status (`entire hooks git pre-push \\\"$1\\\" || true`) kept letting a push through after Entire's pre-push check failed, while `configure --force` reported `✓ Reinstalled git hook`, and `--absolute-git-hook-path` left the line bare. (`main` rewrites the whole copy on these commands and drops the user's lines.) The updated copy keeps its permission bits (with owner `rwx`), so a private `0700` copy holding the user's lines doesn't become readable by everyone. Review of an earlier version caught that it was rewritten at `0755`.\\n\\nInstall leaves the copy as it is and prints a warning that the hook in it wasn't updated when the copy has:\\n\\n- no such line, or more than one;\\n- that line continued from or onto another line with `\\\\`;\\n- another uncommented line that runs Entire's handler, such as the user's own `if [ -n \\\"$CI\\\" ]; then entire hooks git pre-push \\\"$1\\\"; fi`.\\n\\nReplacing the line in those cases would change what the user wrote, or break the shell syntax.\\n\\nIn every Absent case above, install still takes the old re-wrap path, which puts Entire's hook in front where it runs.\\n\\nI also updated the `ReinstallGitHooks` doc comment, which said a wrapper without the marker always reads Absent.\\n\\n`main` moved while this was open and now has the complexity gate (`mise run complexity:gate`). With the Brain branch inline, `installHooks` went from 37 to 92, so I split it: the Brain branch is now `installBehindBrainWrapper` and `updateEditedBrainCopy`, and the existing reclaim-from-pre-commit/hook-manager block moved unchanged into `reclaimHookFromOtherTools`, so `installHooks` doesn't end up more complex than on `main`. Behavior didn't change: the same tests and the same manual runs below give the same results as before the split.\\n\\nThe diff is 4 production files (+346/-25) and 2 test files (+486), squashed into one commit on `main` @ 711697e.\\n\\nOverlap: #2640, #2643 and #2388 (still open) touch the same functions in `strategy/hooks.go`. None of them covers the Brain layout. I re-ran `git merge-tree` today against their current heads (84a2d47, b5651f9, fc5d778). Each already conflicts with `main` @ 711697e, and against this head each has the same conflicting files and the same number of conflict hunks (3, 6 and 4) as against `main`.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- `strategy/hooks_test.go` `TestCheckGitHookState_BrainPrePushWrapper` (table, parallel, filesystem-only):\\n  - Brain's wrapper plus Entire's current hook reads Current, and so does a plugin path containing a quote or the word `exit`.\\n  - Brain's wrapper plus Entire's hook from before the ref list reads Outdated.\\n  - These read Absent:\\n    - a hook that isn't Entire's;\\n    - no moved copy;\\n    - a non-Brain wrapper next to Entire's moved copy;\\n    - the `exec` line commented out;\\n    - an `exit 0`, a `[ -n \\\"$SKIP\\\" ] && exit 0` or a `case ... exit` before the chain;\\n    - the chain inside `if false`;\\n    - a second `backup=`;\\n    - a command after the chain, or an `echo` before it;\\n    - two different plugin paths.\\n  - Execute permission (skipped on Windows): no execute bit on the moved copy or on the wrapper reads Absent, and so does an execute bit for group and other only at `0655` (skipped as root). Owner-only `0700` reads Current.\\n- `TestCheckGitHookState_BrainWrapperOnlyCountsForPrePush`: Brain's wrapper in `post-commit`'s place reads Absent.\\n- `TestInstallGitHooks_BrainPrePushWrapperRefreshesOtherMovedCopies`: Brain's layout, plus a manager wrapper in `pre-push.pre-entire` that runs `pre-push.old`, an Entire hook from before the chain guard that chains straight back. After `InstallGitHook`, `pre-push.old` is the hook that never chains, the copy Brain runs is chained, and both wrappers are unchanged.\\n- `TestInstallGitHooks_KeepsBrainPrePushWrapper`: real `InstallGitHook`, with and without the user's own `pre-push` there first, then Brain's layout with a stale moved copy.\\n  - Both `ReinstallGitHooks` (agent turn) and `InstallGitHook` (enable) leave the wrapper byte-for-byte.\\n  - They rewrite the copy to the current hook, chained when the user's hook is in `pre-push.pre-entire`.\\n  - They leave the user's hook where it was, or create no `pre-push.pre-entire` when there wasn't one.\\n  - Afterwards the set reads Current.\\n- `TestInstallGitHooks_BrainCopyKeepsUserAdditions`: an agent turn leaves an edited copy byte-for-byte. `enable` keeps the user's line and replaces only an Entire line that isn't today's. A copy that is exactly Entire's hook is still rewritten.\\n- `TestInstallGitHooks_BrainCopyWithUserLineKeepsItsMode` (skipped on Windows): `enable` updates Entire's line in an edited copy at `0700`, `0750` and `0755`, and the copy keeps its mode.\\n- `TestInstallGitHooks_BrainCopyWithUserLineGetsTheAbsolutePath`: `--absolute-git-hook-path` writes the absolute path into the copy's Entire line, and the user's line stays.\\n- `TestInstallGitHooks_BrainCopyWithoutOneEntireLineIsReported`: two Entire lines, Entire's line inside the user's condition, a commented-out Entire line, and an Entire line continued from or onto another line. Each is left byte-for-byte with the warning.\\n- `TestInstallGitHooks_BrainCopyReplacedDuringInstallIsKept` (not parallel; it swaps `afterHookBackup`): the copy is replaced between read and write, for a stale copy and for one with a user line. The result is `errHookChangedDuringInstall`, and the replacement stays.\\n- `TestInstallGitHooks_BrainCopyWithUserLineStillRefreshesOtherMovedCopies`: the copy has a user line, and `pre-push.old` is still refreshed, so it can't chain back.\\n- `doctor_test.go` `TestCheckGitHooks_BrainPrePushWrapper`: the wrapper Brain writes, then `checkGitHooks` with and without `--force`. Both print `✓ Git hooks: OK` and leave the wrapper byte-for-byte.\\n\\nThe wrapper text in the tests is what `pushHookContent` in entire-brain writes, except for the plugin path. I checked it against entire-brain's source and against real installs: v0.4.0 earlier, v0.5.0 today. `pushHookContent` and `shellSingleQuote` are unchanged between v0.4.0 and v0.5.0.\\n\\n### Failing without the fix\\n\\nI reverted `hooks.go` and `hook_backup.go` to `main` @ 711697e and removed `hook_exec_*.go`, keeping the tests from the branch head, then ran `go test -count=1 -run Brain ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/ ./cmd/entire/cli/`:\\n\\n- Every case that expects Current, Outdated, an unchanged wrapper, a kept user line, a warning or `errHookChangedDuringInstall` fails. That's ten of the eleven tests above, the doctor test included. The tenth, `TestCheckGitHookState_BrainWrapperOnlyCountsForPrePush`, only expects Absent.\\n- The Absent cases pass on `main` too, because `main` reads every Brain layout as Absent. They're there to keep the new check from accepting a layout that doesn't run Entire's hook.\\n\\nEach new check also has a case that failed at the commit before it was added (run when each was added, not re-run on this head):\\n\\n- the `0655` cases, on a check that accepts any execute bit;\\n- the condition, comment and continuation cases, on a substring match for Entire's line;\\n- `exit`/`if false`/`case`/second `backup=`, on the line-by-line wrapper match;\\n- the quoted path;\\n- the mode test (run today);\\n- the replaced-copy test.\\n\\nEverything passes at the branch head.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nLinux amd64 (kernel 6.12), git 2.56.0, go 1.27.3, golangci-lint 2.15.0, mise. Clean environment: `env -i` with only HOME/PATH/Go cache variables, and no agent, plugin or telemetry variables. Throwaway HOME, config dir and cache for the real-plugin runs.\\n\\nRun today on this tree (head d669009, on `main` @ 711697e; the runs used fork commit 73167d6, which has the identical tree):\\n\\n- `mise run lint`: `0 issues`, and gofmt, gomod, shellcheck, secretpatterns and mise all passed. `mise run fmt`: no changes (`git status --short` empty afterwards).\\n- The complexity gate as CI runs it (`cd tools/complexity && go test ./...`, then `BASE_REF=711697e mise run complexity:gate`): `no new or worsened function over cognitive complexity 30`.\\n- `go vet` and `go test` for `./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/` and `./cmd/entire/cli/`: ok. `go test -race ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/`: ok. `GOOS=windows` and `GOOS=darwin` `go vet`, and `go test -c` of strategy: ok.\\n- `mise run test`: 18054 tests, 22 skipped, 1 failure. The failure is `TestClient_Get_NamesUnresolvableHost` in `cmd/entire/cli/api`, a DNS test that fails the same way on `main` @ 711697e in this environment (17991 tests, same single failure).\\n- Real Brain v0.5.0 (`entire plugin install brain`, then `entire enable`, then `entire brain connect` with no account):\\n  - Doctor on `main` @ 711697e: `Git hooks: NOT INSTALLED`. With this PR: `✓ Git hooks: OK`.\\n  - A push through Brain's wrapper runs Entire's `hooks git pre-push origin` (stub `entire` that logs its calls).\\n  - An agent turn (`entire hooks claude-code user-prompt-submit`) leaves Brain's wrapper and the copy in place.\\n- The copy Brain runs set to a v0.5-era hook with a user line, plus a stub `entire` that fails `hooks git pre-push`. Doctor says OK and the push goes through. Then `entire configure --force`, or `entire enable` in a separate run:\\n  - On the previous head of this PR (81db09a, run Nov 2, not re-run today), both reported success and left the copy byte-for-byte, and the next push still went through.\\n  - On this head, only that line is replaced (the user's line stays), and the next push is rejected.\\n  - On `main`, both re-wrap Brain's hook, rewrite the copy from the template and drop the user's line, and the push is rejected.\\n- A bare-`entire` copy with a user line, then `configure --absolute-git-hook-path`. On 81db09a (Nov 2) the copy stayed bare. On this head it has the absolute path, and the user's line stays. On `main` the user's line is dropped.\\n- `chmod 0655` on the copy or on Brain's wrapper (owned by me, so the owner has no execute bit):\\n  - On this head, doctor says `NOT INSTALLED`, the agent turn re-wraps, and the next push runs Entire's hook, as on `main`.\\n  - On the version before the kernel check (Nov 2), doctor said OK, and git skipped the wrapper (`hint: The '.git/hooks/pre-push' hook was ignored…`) or Brain's `[ -x ]` skipped the copy, so Entire's hook never ran.\\n- ACLs, using `sudo` to make the copy root-owned:\\n  - Mode `0755` with `u:<me>:r--` (readable, no execute for me): doctor says `NOT INSTALLED`, then re-wrap, then Entire runs. Before the kernel check (Nov 2), doctor said OK and nothing ran Entire.\\n  - Mode `0750` with `u:<me>:rwx`: doctor says OK, and the push runs Entire through Brain's wrapper.\\n\\nRun on 5e67636/0544a12 (Oct 29), not re-run on this head. The code they exercise hasn't changed since, except for the wrapper match and the execute check, which the tests above cover:\\n\\n- A user line in the copy survives `entire enable`, an agent turn and `entire doctor --force`, and a push runs Entire once and then the user's line.\\n- A stale copy, then an agent turn: doctor says `OUT OF DATE`, the turn rewrites the copy, and Brain's wrapper stays.\\n- `chmod -x` on either file, or Brain's `exec` commented out: `NOT INSTALLED`, then re-wrap, as on `main`.\\n- The user's own `pre-push`, then `enable`, then `brain connect`, then `enable` again: a push runs Entire's hook and then the user's, before and after the second enable. On `main`, the second enable rotates the user's hook away (#2960).\\n- A manager wrapper in `pre-push.pre-entire` running an Entire copy from before the chain guard: the next push finishes, with Entire called twice.\\n- `mise run test:e2e:canary`: passed.\\n\\nWhat I didn't run:\\n\\n- Windows and macOS themselves. They're covered only by cross-compiling (`go vet`, `go test -c`). The Windows CI job only runs tests matching `Windows|MSYS`.\\n- A Linux kernel or filesystem where `faccessat` relative to a directory descriptor behaves differently.\\n- A hosted Brain sync, which needs an account and doesn't touch hooks.\\n- The Entire side of a real push with a real login. I used a stub `entire` to count calls.\\n- CI on this exact head before pushing it. CI ran on my fork on earlier heads.\\n\\n## Known limits / open questions\\n\\n- This takes the CLI-side option from the issue. The other option is for Brain's wrapper to carry a marker `doctor` understands. I asked on the issue which you prefer and haven't heard back yet.\\n- Brain's wrapper is matched exactly. If Brain changes its wrapper, or the user edits it in any way (a harmless added command included), the CLI goes back to reading Absent and re-wrapping, which is today's behavior. That fails safe: pushes still run Entire's hook. It also brings back what happens on `main` after a re-wrap, including #2960 when the user's hook is in `pre-push.pre-entire`.\\n- `entire disable --uninstall` leaves Entire's hook running behind Brain's wrapper, on this branch and on `main` after its re-wrap. `restoreWrapped` matches wrappers by literal file name, and Brain uses `$0`. That bug was already there before this PR and is filed separately as #2957. The fix for it has to adjust one test case to this PR's layout (see the note below).\\n- Agent turns don't touch a copy the user added lines to, because it reads Current. If that copy still has an old fail-open line (`|| true`), doctor says OK and pushes ignore Entire's exit status until an explicit `entire enable` / `configure --force` updates the line. That's the same rule `main` applies to Entire's own edited `pre-push`: I ran the same edited hook at `.git/hooks/pre-push` without Brain on `main`, and doctor says OK and the push goes through there too.\\n- If the user's own hook is in `pre-push.pre-entire` but the edited copy Brain runs has no chain to it, an explicit install replaces only Entire's line and doesn't add the chain, so the user's hook doesn't run. Adding the chain would mean rewriting their file. On `main`, the re-wrap rotates the user's hook away instead (#2960).\\n- A copy the user edited whose Entire line runs the removed local-dev launcher (`./scripts/entire-dev`, `go run ...`) reads Outdated. Agent turns and `enable` rewrite it whole, dropping the user's lines, as `main` does for this copy and for Entire's own `pre-push`. The historical local-dev line forms vary too much to match safely.\\n- Other moved copies, such as a hook manager's `pre-push.old`, are still refreshed from the template, as on `main`.\\n- Without Brain, Entire's own `pre-push` at mode `0655` (owner has no execute bit) still reads OK on `main` and on this branch, while git skips it. I ran that on both. It's an existing gap in how Entire checks its own hook, outside this PR.\\n- An agent turn doesn't repair a loop further down the chain. Example: the copy Brain runs chains to `pre-push.pre-entire`, that is a hook manager's wrapper running `pre-push.old`, and `pre-push.old` is an Entire hook from before the chain guard that chains straight back to `pre-push.pre-entire`. The copy reads Current, so the turn skips it, and pushes loop until an explicit `entire enable`, which refreshes `pre-push.old` (`TestInstallGitHooks_BrainPrePushWrapperRefreshesOtherMovedCopies`). I ran the same layout without Brain on `main`: it also reads Current and loops. On `main` with Brain, the turn's re-wrap happens to refresh `pre-push.old`, but it also moves the manager's wrapper to a dated copy that no longer runs.\\n- When install updates Entire's line in an edited copy, the file is replaced through a temp file and rename. Its mode is kept, but POSIX ACL entries are not: the new file gets the directory's default ACL, if any. Every hook write on `main` does the same, and `main` also drops the user's lines there.\\n- Brain's wrapper isn't recognised when the plugin path contains a newline. The match requires each quoted path to sit on one line. I checked it: such a layout reads Absent and gets `main`'s re-wrap.\\n- If the hooks directory is searchable but not readable, the directory descriptor can't be opened, and the layout reads Absent (main's re-wrap path). Install would need write access there anyway.\\n\\n## Missing Entire-Checkpoint trailers\\n\\nNone of these commits has an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer. CONTRIBUTING asks for them, but this work wasn't done in an Entire-captured session that produced one, and I won't make one up. If you need checkpoint linkage, I can redo the commits inside a captured session.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2959/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 1,\n                \"+1\": 1,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2959/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2574\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2574/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2574/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2574/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2574\",\n              \"id\": 5557027647,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABEyuw_A\",\n              \"number\": 2574,\n              \"title\": \"Squashed commits keep their checkpoint trailers\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-23T17:26:53Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-25T17:11:44Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-25T17:11:40Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2574\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2574\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2574.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2574.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-25T17:11:40Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1414\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Squashed commits keep their checkpoint trailers\\n\\n**Symptom.** An agent commits several times during a session, then the commits are squashed locally with `git merge --squash` and your own message. The new commit has no `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer, so the session disappears from the trail. GitHub squash merges were already fine: they keep the trailers.\\n\\n**Cause.** The hooks stepped aside for squashes and relied on git's default message to carry the old trailers. Any message you write yourself dropped them.\\n\\n**Fixes, in the git hooks (agent-agnostic):**\\n\\n1. **Squash inherits.** When `SQUASH_MSG` is present, prepare-commit-msg copies its trailers into the message whatever source git reports (`-m` reports `message`, not `squash`). It does this only when a staged path is one the recorded commits changed, so touching up a squashed file before committing still counts. An abandoned squash's leftover message inherits nothing, and its seeded trailers are removed.\\n2. **Inherited trailers are links, never targets.** Matching still runs, so work the session still holds gets a fresh trailer after the inherited ones. prepare-commit-msg records which trailers it inherited, in the per-worktree git dir, tied to the commit's parent. Post-commit never condenses into one, even when its checkpoint just isn't in this clone's store, for example on a teammate's squashed branch.\\n3. **Post-commit writes to the right checkpoint.** Among the stamped trailers it condenses only into the one with no checkpoint yet, and rechecks that target just before writing. Condensation refuses to write into a checkpoint the session didn't stamp and isn't amending. Before this, post-commit took the first trailer and wrote pending work into an older checkpoint, a bug that was latent on `main` for default-message squashes.\\n\\n**Adversarial review (Stefan).** Stefan's red tests for squash are here, split from 4a5df627d0; the reset half is in the stacked PR. Both failures are fixed:\\n- Declining the link on a `-m` squash of a teammate's branch no longer writes the session's work under the teammate's checkpoint ID.\\n- Squashing with an edited file keeps the trailer git seeded. This was a regression from main.\\n\\n**Measured with real hooks.** One session made two linked commits (trailers T1 and T2), then they were squashed:\\n\\n| Squash | Nightly | This branch |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `rebase -i` squash, default message | 2 trailers | 2 |\\n| `rebase -i` fixup | 1 | 1 (git discards the folded message; known gap) |\\n| `merge --squash` + `commit -m` | 0 | 2 |\\n| `merge --squash` with pending session work | fresh trailer only, links lost | T1, T2 inherited plus a fresh T3; T2's checkpoint untouched |\\n\\nSeveral trailers on one commit is the shape GitHub squash merges already produce, and the server, web app and `resume` already read it.\\n\\nResets (`git reset` then recommitting) are handled in the stacked follow-up PR, which builds on the post-commit fix here.\\n\\n**Follow-ups.** `rebase -i` fixup drops the folded commit's trailers by git's design.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2574/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2574/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2785\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2785/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2785/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2785/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2785\",\n              \"id\": 5865644792,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABInHbWw\",\n              \"number\": 2785,\n              \"title\": \"Redone commits don't mint a fresh checkpoint for inherited work\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-15T11:57:15Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-16T15:18:00Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-16T15:17:57Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2785\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2785\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2785.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2785.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-16T15:17:57Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1582\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nE2E run [38724857355](https://github.com/entireio/cli/actions/runs/38724857355/job/116388096213) failed `TestExplainCheckpoint` (claude-code). Haiku committed `docs/feature.md` itself, then ran `git reset HEAD~1`, and the test's own commit came out with two checkpoint trailers: the inherited `3afa00e9bfa6` (correct, via the redo inheritance from 6170bc1612) and a fresh `93418f0f011f`.\\n\\nThe fresh one was wrong. The reset put the file back in the worktree, the next turn end recorded it as touched again, and session matching saw transcript growth plus an overlapping staged file. The new checkpoint's transcript slice held only the agent's commit and reset, which the turn-end finalize had already folded into `3afa00e9bfa6`.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n- The redo step (`inheritReplacedCommitsTrailers`) now also reports which staged paths the inherited checkpoints already hold. A path counts only when the newest dropped commit that changed it carries a checkpoint that is not deleted and exists in this clone's store (`capturedCheckpoints`), and the staged content and mode both match what that commit left. Inheriting the trailer stays permissive: a trailer whose capture failed still links, but holds nothing, so the session's work gets a fresh checkpoint. Content, mode and deletions come from one rename-free read of the commit index git is preparing (`parseStagedRaw` now also keeps the staged mode, building on #2330), so `git commit -a` and path-limited commits compare what they commit.\\n- `PrepareCommitMsg` returns right after inheriting when every staged path is held, so a pure redo gets no fresh trailer, whatever the session phase.\\n- Otherwise the staged-files overlap check in `filterSessionsWithNewContent` sees only the redo's other staged paths, from the same rename-free view, so only other session work earns a fresh checkpoint. (A rename-detecting list would hide a staged deletion paired with a held file.)\\n- Prepare records the held paths in the inherited-trailers marker. After a redo that stamps no fresh trailer (pure, or partial with no session's other work), which condenses nothing, post-commit (`reconcileRedoneFiles`) drops them from this worktree's sessions' touched files when the commit holds the recorded content, as carry-forward would. Only held files go through that check; other touched files, steps and transcript growth stay pending untouched.\\n- `openRepositoryTimed` is extracted to keep `PrepareCommitMsg` under the `maintidx` limit; the `open_repository` span no longer includes the redo lookup.\\n- The deleted-checkpoint list is loaded once per commit, each dropped commit's diff is computed once, and store lookups are memoized.\\n- Documented in `docs/architecture/sessions-and-checkpoints.md` and `docs/development/checkpoint-implementation.md`.\\n\\n## Deliberately not changed\\n\\nWhenever a fresh trailer is stamped, a redundant checkpoint is preferred to a lost or dangling link:\\n\\n- On a partial redo (redone files staged together with other files), the mid-turn agent fast path still stamps a fresh trailer. Transcripts miss edits made through shell commands (`sed -i`, formatters, codegen), so it cannot rule out new work.\\n- Post-commit judges overlap without the redo, so a session that only redid work may fold into another session's fresh checkpoint. An earlier commit on this branch excluded redone paths there, but that left a fresh trailer with no checkpoint behind it when a stale ACTIVE session tracked only redone files, or when a read-only ACTIVE session was gated out by a redo-only claimant.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nRegression tests in `manual_commit_redo_test.go`. The fixture writes real checkpoints for its trailers through the hooks' own store. Each test fails without its fix (mutation-checked), except the aborted-commit one, which two independent guards cover. Every test that expects a fresh trailer runs prepare, the commit and post-commit, and asserts the trailer resolves in the checkpoint store:\\n\\n- a pure redo, with an ended or an active session, gets only the inherited trailers;\\n- after a pure redo, only the redone file leaves the session's touched files, and a later human edit to it doesn't link back to the session;\\n- a redo plus new session work gets the inherited trailer and a fresh one;\\n- a redo plus a file the session never touched gets only the inherited trailer;\\n- a mode change after the reset gets a fresh trailer;\\n- a later dropped commit without a checkpoint that changed the same file leaves it uncovered;\\n- a partial redo by an active session keeps its fast-path trailer;\\n- a stale ACTIVE session tracking only redone files, a read-only ACTIVE session beside a redo-only claimant, and two ended sessions all leave the fresh trailer resolvable;\\n- a dropped commit whose checkpoint is missing or deleted keeps the session's fresh capture;\\n- a staged deletion git pairs with a held file as a rename stamps no fresh trailer;\\n- content and mode are read from the temporary commit index, not `.git/index`;\\n- an aborted commit's marker never settles files a later commit didn't contain;\\n- the cleanup never prunes touched files the redo doesn't hold.\\n\\n`mise run check` passes.\\n\\n## Follow-ups\\n\\n- The amend fold (`git reset --soft HEAD~1 && git commit --amend`) goes through `stampFreshCheckpointForAmend` and may have the same issue; not checked.\\n- The e2e helpers (`GetCheckpointTrailer` / `AssertHasCheckpointTrailer`) assume a single trailer per commit, though squash and multi-commit redos legitimately produce several.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes prepare-commit-msg trailer stamping and session content matching on reset/redo paths; incorrect logic could omit needed trailers or over-link commits, though behavior is covered by new tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Fixes **prepare-commit-msg** so a pure **redo** after `git reset` inherits dropped commits’ `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers but does **not** mint a new checkpoint when staged files are only recommitted work.\\n> \\n> Redo detection now returns a **`redo`** value (inherited IDs, matched staged paths, and whether every staged path is redone). When all staged paths are redone, the hook exits after inheriting trailers; otherwise **`filterSessionsWithNewContent`** ignores redone paths when deciding if a session has new work, so reset/turn-end “touched again” files are not treated as fresh session content. **`recommitsFilesOf`** returns the matched paths per dropped commit, and only commits that still carry live checkpoints contribute paths.\\n> \\n> Adds regression tests (pure redo, redo plus new session work, redo plus unrelated files) and documents the behavior in **sessions-and-checkpoints**.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit b05ce0e53e1ae0bf30114e863ad6c5acdc87d167. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2785/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2785/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": {\n                \"id\": 2626939,\n                \"client_id\": \"Iv23lieFG10uOnChW4TN\",\n                \"slug\": \"entire\",\n                \"node_id\": \"A_kwHOAfprLM4AKBV7\",\n                \"owner\": {\n                  \"login\": \"entireio\",\n                  \"id\": 33188652,\n                  \"node_id\": \"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjMzMTg4NjUy\",\n                  \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33188652?v=4\",\n                  \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio\",\n                  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio\",\n                  \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/followers\",\n                  \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/following{/other_user}\",\n                  \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                  \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                  \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/subscriptions\",\n                  \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/orgs\",\n                  \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/repos\",\n                  \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/events{/privacy}\",\n                  \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/received_events\",\n                  \"type\": \"Organization\",\n                  \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                  \"site_admin\": false\n                },\n                \"name\": \"Entire\",\n                \"description\": \"\",\n                \"external_url\": \"https://entire.com\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/entire\",\n                \"created_at\": \"2026-01-09T21:20:56Z\",\n                \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-23T08:32:31Z\",\n                \"permissions\": {\n                  \"administration\": \"read\",\n                  \"checks\": \"write\",\n                  \"contents\": \"write\",\n                  \"emails\": \"read\",\n                  \"members\": \"read\",\n                  \"metadata\": \"read\",\n                  \"pull_requests\": \"write\",\n                  \"statuses\": \"read\",\n                  \"workflows\": \"write\"\n                },\n                \"events\": [\n                  \"check_suite\",\n                  \"create\",\n                  \"delete\",\n                  \"fork\",\n                  \"member\",\n                  \"membership\",\n                  \"organization\",\n                  \"pull_request\",\n                  \"push\",\n                  \"repository\",\n                  \"star\",\n                  \"team\"\n                ]\n              },\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2905\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2905/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2905/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2905/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2905\",\n              \"id\": 6038574497,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABKwGa1A\",\n              \"number\": 2905,\n              \"title\": \"changelog 0.12.2\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-26T11:15:42Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-26T11:26:39Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-26T11:26:37Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2905\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2905\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2905.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2905.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-26T11:26:37Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2590/changes/cli/1690\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Documentation-only changelog update; no runtime or behavioral changes in this diff.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds a **0.12.2** (2026-10-26) section to `CHANGELOG.md`, documenting the release without code changes in this PR.\\n> \\n> The new notes cover **enable/setup** (post-`entire enable` commit guidance for `.entire` and agent hook files), **transcripts** (per-call token usage on assistant lines; Pi image externalization), **agent UX** (first-turn injected context for all sessions; trail comment writes blocked from agents; Trails help grouping), a **checkpoint trailer** fix for idle live-transcript sessions, and **housekeeping** (internal Pi JSONL parser move).\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 2bdc610939d59d9843c55ae6b95bf0ffc07365db. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2905/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2905/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3110\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3110/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3110/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3110/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3110\",\n              \"id\": 6322041797,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABOStpww\",\n              \"number\": 3110,\n              \"title\": \"fix(hooks): identify a chained Trunk launcher without grep\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n                \"id\": 26940511,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI2OTQwNTEx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Beehtrix\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-11T05:01:46Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-16T03:31:03Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3110\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3110\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3110.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3110.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Review after entireio/cli#3051 merges. Until then this PR also contains that PR's commits. It now includes #3051's current head (`b6335784`), so only these commits are new here:\\n\\n- `0177d8e9a` fix(hooks): identify a chained Trunk launcher without grep\\n- `43eb8416c` fix(hooks): bound the no-grep Trunk launcher scan\\n- `3be66e57f` Merge #3051's head into trunk-chain-no-grep\\n- `b46370d3a` test(hooks): check the 64KiB scan cap instead of a 2s wall clock\\n- `807b2a206` test(hooks): share the Trunk chain test helpers\\n- `e32a8f2f5` fix(hooks): keep the user's lines when upgrading a Trunk chain\\n- `1b84203c1` refactor(hooks): choose the installed hook's content in one helper\\n- `2b158373b` fix(hooks): recheck an outdated Trunk chain under the hooks lock\\n- `663435fac` Merge #3051's head into trunk-chain-no-grep\\n\\n@Soph this is a small follow-up to #3051, in the Trunk hook chain you already reviewed. Please take a look after that pull request (or I can rebase this onto main once it merges).\\n\\n#3051 sources Trunk's launcher under the hook's own name when the backup contains Trunk's callback line, identified with `grep -qxF`. If `grep` is not on PATH, that check fails and the chain runs the launcher as `<hook>.pre-entire`, which Trunk refuses with exit 2. That fallback predates #3051.\\n\\nThis change replaces that `grep` with a whole-line comparison in `/bin/bash --norc`, so a missing `grep` can no longer misroute Trunk. The scan reads at most 64KiB (Trunk's launcher is under 2KiB), so a compiled or otherwise large backup is not read to EOF before it runs. As on #3051, the chain only probes or runs a regular executable, so an executable FIFO backup cannot hang the hook.\\n\\nExisting installs whose hook still holds #3051's generated grep chain over a Trunk backup now read Outdated, so `ReinstallGitHooks` upgrades them without running `entire enable` again. It replaces only the old chain block, for this chain and for the pre-#3051 chain that #3051 migrates, so commands the user added to Entire's hook before or after the chain are kept. Whether to upgrade is decided again under the hooks lock, so when two setups both found the old chain, the second finds the hook already upgraded and leaves it alone instead of regenerating it. The block has to match whole, exactly as generated and exactly once, so a chain edited by hand inside the block stays Current. A hook that is stale for another reason, and `entire enable`, still regenerate it. Like #3051's check, this one reads only a regular-file backup, through the hooks directory's `os.Root` and without following links, so a symlinked backup is left for `entire enable`. A non-Trunk backup stays Current.\\n\\nThe commits do not have Entire-Checkpoint trailers.\\n\\n## Tests (Go 1.27.3, git 2.43.0)\\n\\n- `TestInstallHooks_ChainedTrunkLauncherNeedsNoGrepOnPath` failed before the change (`Unknown git-hooks callback 'pre-push.pre-entire'`, exit 2) and passes after.\\n- `TestReinstallGitHooks_GrepTrunkChainIsOutdated` plants the old grep-based chain, asserts Outdated, reinstalls, and checks that `pre-push` reaches Trunk as `pre-push` with no `grep` on PATH.\\n- `TestReinstallGitHooks_OutdatedTrunkChainKeepsUserLines` adds a line before and after each old chain, then checks that both survive the reinstall and run along with Trunk as `pre-push`. It fails on `807b2a206` and passes now.\\n- `TestInstallHooks_QueuedTrunkUpgradeKeepsAnEarlierUpgrade` classifies the hooks once and installs twice, as two setups queued on the hooks lock would, then checks that the user's lines are still there and run. It fails on `1b84203c1` and passes now.\\n- `TestCheckGitHookState_TrunkChainOutdatedIsSpecific` covers the grep chain over a Trunk backup (Outdated), the same chain edited by hand, and the grep chain over an ordinary backup (both Current).\\n- The `symlinked Trunk launcher is not followed` case and `TestInstallGitHook_Pre3051TrunkChainToSymlinkedLauncher` fail on `43eb8416c` and pass now. `TestChainedHook_FIFOBackupDoesNotHang` hangs on `43eb8416c` and returns at once now.\\n- `TestInstallHooks_ChainedBackupScanStopsAt64KiB` puts Trunk's callback line after 1MiB of padding and checks that the backup still runs as its own program. It fails when the 64KiB cap is removed. It replaces a test that gave the whole chain 2s.\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/` passes in full, and the hook tests (`-run 'Hook|Trunk|GitHook|Reinstall|Chain|FIFO'`) also pass with `-race`.\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/ -run 'Hook|Doctor'` passes.\\n- `go test -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/ -run 'Hook|Chain|Overwrite|LocalDev'` passes.\\n- `golangci-lint run ./...` (v2.15.0) reports 0 issues, and `gofmt -l -s` of the changed files is clean.\\n- The complexity gate against main reports no new or worsened function over 30.\\n- Windows `go vet` and `go test -c` of the `strategy` package succeed.\\n- `git merge-tree` into current main (`76f1b512`) is clean. This branch is behind main by the same commits as #3051, and none of them touch the files changed here.\\n\\n## Bot review\\n\\nFork PR https://github.com/Beehtrix/cli/pull/33 is the exact head, base `fix-trunk-hook-name-2673` (#3051's head), so the diff is only this follow-up.\\n\\n- Kilo and Codex (run, verified): the first version identified the launcher by reading the backup to EOF, which was slow on compiled hooks. I measured 3.5s for a 17MB binary (Codex measured 7.3s on a 14.9MB Go executable) versus 16ms with `grep` and 2ms with a 64KiB `/bin/bash` read. That is fixed in `43eb8416c`.\\n- Codex on `43eb8416c` (run, verified): the Outdated check followed a symlinked backup out of the hooks directory, and an executable FIFO backup could hang the hook in the scan. Both were already fixed on #3051, so `3be66e57f` merges #3051's head into this branch. Codex re-reviewed `3be66e57f` and had no findings.\\n- Kilo (read-only, verified, fixed): a hand-edited Entire hook whose backup is still Trunk would have been rewritten and lost those edits. Since `3be66e57f` the check matches only the exact generated chain, so that hook stays Current. Baz marked it addressed.\\n- Kilo (read-only, verified false): Kilo warned that `%%` in the Go template would drop everything from the first newline, losing a callback already inside the 64KiB cap. That `%%` is only `fmt.Sprintf` escaping. The generated hook uses bash `%` (shortest suffix), which keeps complete lines through the last newline. I checked this in bash: `line1\\\\nline2\\\\npartial` becomes `line1\\\\nline2`.\\n- Greptile on `3be66e57f` (read-only, verified, fixed): the large-backup test gave the whole hook chain 2s, which a busy runner under `-race` can miss on a correct build. `b46370d3a` checks the 64KiB cap directly instead, and the run is bounded only by the shared `hookRunTimeout`, like the other chained-hook tests.\\n- SonarCloud on `b46370d3a` (read-only, verified, fixed): the loop that restricts the hooks' PATH appeared three times in the tests, and the subtests of `TestCheckGitHookState_TrunkChainOutdatedIsSpecific` reached cognitive complexity 30. `807b2a206` moves the repeated code into shared test helpers. The planted chains are byte-for-byte what they were before, and `dupl` at threshold 50 reports nothing in the file.\\n- Codex on `807b2a206` (run, verified, fixed): an old chain with steps the user added outside it still matched, and `ReinstallGitHooks` rewrote the whole hook, dropping those steps. #3051 had the same gap, and now has the same fix in `eed2dcd8c`. `e32a8f2f5` replaces only the old chain block and keeps the rest of the file, and `1b84203c1` keeps `installHooks` under the complexity gate. The generated hooks are byte-for-byte unchanged.\\n- Codex on `1b84203c1` (run, verified, fixed), and Kilo and Greptile on the fork (read-only, verified, fixed): `ReinstallGitHooks` classifies the hooks before it takes the hooks lock, so two setups could both find the old chain. The second then no longer found the block, fell back to a freshly generated hook and dropped the lines the first had kept. `2b158373b` checks the hook again under the lock, as described above. #3051's fix gets the same recheck in `b63357841`, and `663435fac` merges both into this branch without changing its tree.\\n- SonarCloud on `1b84203c1` (read-only, verified, fixed): `TestReinstallGitHooks_OutdatedTrunkChainKeepsUserLines` reached cognitive complexity 18 (limit 15). `2b158373b` moves its setup and checks into two helpers, which the new queued-upgrade test shares.\\n- Gitar is on the free plan and did not post findings. CodeRabbit skipped the fork (non-default base). Qodo's trial has ended. Copilot had no quota.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3110/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 1,\n                \"+1\": 1,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3110/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2897\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2897/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2897/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2897/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2897\",\n              \"id\": 6030328285,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABKpeQ3Q\",\n              \"number\": 2897,\n              \"title\": \"transcript: one Codex item mapping for stored rollouts and live streams\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-25T22:56:14Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-30T04:15:13Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-30T04:15:09Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2897\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2897\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2897.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2897.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-30T04:15:09Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2565/changes/cli/1686\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nCurrent Codex rollouts record every item (commands, file changes, MCP calls, web searches, messages) as `item_completed` events, and Codex's app-server daemon sends the same items live as `item/started` / `item/completed` notifications. This PR maps both through one Codex item model, so a stored checkpoint and a live stream of the same session show the same lines.\\n\\n- `internal/transcript/codexitem` (stdlib-only, internal like Pi's parser): decodes an item from either encoding into one `Item`. A table writes every item kind in both encodings and checks they decode equal (small inline test data, no fixture files).\\n- `Convert` takes an item path for rollouts whose first turn records user or agent message items; older rollouts keep the `response_item` path unchanged. The choice is made on the whole rollout, so `Convert` and `ConvertWithBoundary` agree (every StartLine is tested).\\n  - Commands are `Bash` tool uses with the script from `<shell> -lc/-c` (shell quoting, including `$'…'`, decoded) and their output; file changes are `FileChange` with each file's diff; MCP calls `server.tool`; web searches, image views and sub-agent spawns map to tool uses with results.\\n  - Usage per model call as on main (`codexUsageTracker` over `total_token_usage` snapshots), on the call's last assistant line; a reasoning-only call gets a usage-only line.\\n  - Items without an ID or of unmapped kinds (reasoning, plans, compaction) are skipped.\\n- `transcript.CodexNotificationRecords(method, params, CodexLive)`: the public entry for a live stream, mapping one daemon item notification with the same mapping (plus text/output so far for running items). Tested equal to `Convert`'s records for every kind in that table.\\n\\nThe live consumer is `entire stream codex` in entireio/entire-stream (in progress).\\n\\n`mise run check` passes (the claudecode config-probe 5 s timeouts seen under load pass alone).\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Rxmv1Yre5x8Re4F6G9FrUm\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes Codex transcript shape and conversion routing for newer rollouts; behavior is heavily tested against fixtures but wrong path detection or item mapping would affect checkpoints and live streams.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **`internal/transcript/codexitem`**, a stdlib-only parser that turns Codex **`item_completed`** rollout lines and app-server **`item/started` / `item/completed`** params into one normalized **`Item`** (messages, commands, file changes, MCP, web search, spawns, etc.), including shell script extraction from `<shell> -lc/-c` argv and daemon command strings.\\n> \\n> **`Convert`** now picks an **item path** when the rollout’s first turn has user/agent message items (`hasCodexItems` on the full file); older rollouts still use the **`response_item`** path. The item path emits **one transcript line per item** (e.g. `Bash`, `FileChange`, `server.tool`), attaches **per-model-call usage** on the call’s last assistant line (same `token_count` delta rules as before), and skips unmapped kinds (reasoning, compaction). **`CodexNotificationRecords`** exposes the same mapping for live daemon notifications, with **`CodexLive`** for partial agent text, command output, and interrupted turns.\\n> \\n> Docs in **`transcript/README.md`** describe the item vs `response_item` behavior; guards allow **`codexitem`** as an internal parser dependency and whitelist the file-change **`diff`** JSON tag in git diff scanning.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 2f4372adea7427dd891527cabdedf9fd4fa43ebe. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2897/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2897/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2508\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2508/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2508/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2508/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2508\",\n              \"id\": 5480952799,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABD2H0nA\",\n              \"number\": 2508,\n              \"title\": \"Remove the checkpoint policy feature\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"pfleidi\",\n                \"id\": 118549,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjExODU0OQ==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118549?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pfleidi\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-16T23:23:59Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-17T10:54:11Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-17T10:54:08Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2508\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2508\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2508.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2508.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-17T10:54:08Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1355\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nThe hidden `entire checkpoint policy` command wrote a client-side ref, `refs/entire/policies/checkpoint`, and pushed it to the checkpoint sync remote. That namespace is reserved on the Entire side for server-managed policy data, and Entire's git mirroring rejects a push that carries a client-written ref under it. One rejected ref fails the whole push, so a repository whose upstream carried the policy ref could no longer be mirrored at all: every sync failed and retried, and none of its branches or tags landed until the ref was removed.\\n\\nThe policy never earned that cost. The CLI was the only writer of the ref, so every hook, condensation pass, and explicit checkpoint writer was reading a ref that only ever held the default policy, and the feature carried its own package, telemetry event, and a dedicated repository-open fallback. Removing the feature removes the writer.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\nThe checkpoint policy feature is removed end to end: the `checkpointpolicy` package, the hidden `entire checkpoint policy` command, the post-run upgrade warning, the `checkpoint_policy_blocked` telemetry event, and every gate that read the ref (git hooks, agent hooks, condensation, the Stop finalize pass, all three pre-push paths, and the `attach` / `import` / `explain --generate` write guards). `gitrepo.OpenCurrentOrCwd` goes with it, since the warning was its only caller, as does `versioncheck.UpdateCommandShell`, whose only two callers were the policy command and the policy warning. Net change is 136 insertions against 4034 deletions across 63 files.\\n\\nThe branch is split into self-contained commits, each compiling on its own, in dependency order: agent hooks, git hooks plus telemetry, the strategy, the checkpoint writers, the command and warning, the package itself with its docs, and then the seams the removal left — stale references (lint config, complexity feature map, test plan), the dead `UpdateCommandShell` API, the agent-help classification, and two things the removal exposed rather than caused (see below).\\n\\n## Decisions made during development\\n\\n- **`checkpoint explain` is classified task-driven, and the checkpoint group stays task-driven.** `policy` was the group's only task-driven child, so deleting it left `agentHelpAudienceNote` rendering the group's own audience over four read-only children — a listing that said \\\"task-driven\\\" above a drill-down that said \\\"read-only\\\" four times. Classifying `explain` is the fail-safe way to answer that: `--generate` writes a summary onto the checkpoint and spends tokens with the summary provider, the audience axis has no flag granularity, and this table's stated direction is an agent declining to run something it could have rather than running something it should not have. The group therefore renders `read-only except: explain` — the same shape it had before, with a different command named. **This is a product judgment call and a reviewer should feel free to move it.**\\n- **What that classification costs is repaid on the agent channel, not hidden.** Demoting `explain` tells an agent to avoid the drill-down that `checkpoint list` and `checkpoint search` exist to feed, over a flag it was never going to pass. `agentHelpGuidance` now carries the distinction for agents (\\\"reading is free; `--generate` is the exception\\\"), and `explain`'s cobra `Long` carries the half a human wants too — which is where CLAUDE.md says each kind of text belongs.\\n- **A group whose audience contradicts its children now fails the build.** `agentHelpAudienceNote` falls back to the group's own audience whenever its classified children agree *with each other*, which its comment described as their agreeing with the *group*. Those are not the same thing, and the gap is exactly how the checkpoint group came to need a decision at all. The fallback itself is correct — the group's audience also covers hidden children the note never counts, and `checkpoint resume` switches branches — so `TestAgentHelpClassification_GroupAudienceMatchesUnanimousChildren` catches the disagreement instead and leaves the call to a human. Verified non-vacuous: flipping `explain` back to read-only fails it by name.\\n- **The v1 pre-push opens the repository only when OPF needs it, in its own span.** The repository handle was shared between the policy sync and the OPF rewrite; with the sync gone, the open moves inside the `OPFRun` branch so the common no-OPF path no longer opens the repo at all. It gets its own `open_repository` span rather than sitting inside `opf_pre_push_rewrite`, so that span keeps measuring what it measured in every trace recorded before — the open is not free on a reftable repo, where `gitrepo` routes reference reads back through the git CLI.\\n- **`OpenCurrentOrCwd` is deleted rather than kept for future use.** Its doc comment and the CLAUDE.md guidance both said the cwd fallback was acceptable only for a read-only advisory; no such caller remains, and keeping a footgun with no user contradicts the \\\"OpenCurrent fails rather than guessing\\\" rule.\\n- **The refs-migration doc now names what the removal makes silent.** `checkpoint_min_version` was the mechanism that turned \\\"an old CLI cannot read refs checkpoints\\\" into an explicit upgrade nudge, and `ref-checkpoint-backend.md` still justified skipping a dual-write on the grounds that the case \\\"is a feature, not something to paper over\\\". With the nudge gone it is a silent feature — an old CLI sees a partial history and is told nothing — so the doc says that rather than arguing from a mechanism that no longer exists.\\n- **Existing checkpoint refs on remotes are untouched.** Nothing deletes `refs/entire/policies/checkpoint` where it already exists; the CLI simply stops reading or advancing it.\\n\\n## Reviewer notes\\n\\n- No repository is known to carry a non-default policy ref, and no CLI command clears one any more. If one turns up, `git update-ref -d refs/entire/policies/checkpoint` locally plus `git push <remote> :refs/entire/policies/checkpoint` removes it, and deleting it from the upstream is what restores mirroring for a repository that hit the sync failure above.\\n- The CHANGELOG entries that introduced the feature (#1508, #1509) are left as historical record; no changelog entry is added here, because the command was hidden and experimental and nothing depended on it.\\n- `TestExecuteAgentHookPostTodoFailsWhenPolicyUnsupported` was the only unit test driving `executeAgentHook` with `HookNamePostTodo`, and this branch rewrites that dispatch condition. It is deleted rather than adapted: without the policy assertion there is nothing left to assert, since a bare \\\"returns no error\\\" would pass even if the condition broke. Restoring real coverage means observing the PostTodo side effect, which is a separate piece of work; the integration suite covers the path today.\\n- Merging main brought two conflicts, both resolved in `852757b5c4` with the reasoning in its message. `checkpointpolicy/remote.go` was a modify/delete — `7693ebb5ca` fixed `checkpointpolicy.Push`'s error formatting, entirely inside the package this branch deletes, so the deletion stands and nothing needs porting. `CLAUDE.md` was the larger one: `d16dce053f` slimmed it from 2143 lines to 199 and moved the detail into `docs/development/`, so this branch's three CLAUDE.md edits are re-applied at their new homes (`cli-conventions.md`, `git-safety.md`, `checkpoint-implementation.md`) rather than lost by taking main's file wholesale.\\n- Two integration tests in `external_command_signal_unix_test.go` failed once under `-race` during the full suite with \\\"plugin never reached ready state\\\", then passed in isolation and on a full rerun of the package. They are unrelated to this change.\\n\\n## Rendered Markdown\\n\\n- [docs/architecture/sessions-and-checkpoints.md](https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/remove-checkpoint-policy/docs/architecture/sessions-and-checkpoints.md)\\n- [docs/architecture/ref-checkpoint-backend.md](https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/remove-checkpoint-policy/docs/architecture/ref-checkpoint-backend.md)\\n- [docs/testing/git-remote-test-plan.md](https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/remove-checkpoint-policy/docs/testing/git-remote-test-plan.md)\\n- [docs/development/cli-conventions.md](https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/remove-checkpoint-policy/docs/development/cli-conventions.md)\\n- [docs/development/git-safety.md](https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/remove-checkpoint-policy/docs/development/git-safety.md)\\n- [docs/development/checkpoint-implementation.md](https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/remove-checkpoint-policy/docs/development/checkpoint-implementation.md)\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2508/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2508/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3065\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3065/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3065/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3065/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3065\",\n              \"id\": 6282993511,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABNzZHBg\",\n              \"number\": 3065,\n              \"title\": \"redact: redact international phone numbers in pii.phone\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n                \"id\": 26940511,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI2OTQwNTEx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Beehtrix\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-09T08:56:06Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-11T20:28:41Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3065\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3065\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3065.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3065.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes #2976\\n\\n@rennf93 proposed this on the issue and planned to send it once a maintainer agreed. No maintainer has replied since Oct 29, so I'm opening it to give you something concrete to look at. It follows the issue's design, a fourth E.164 branch with their per-country test table. If you'd rather @rennf93 send their own PR, say so and I'll close this one. cc @MuskanPaliwal\\n\\nI reviewed this on my fork first (Beehtrix/cli#17).\\n\\n## What was wrong\\n\\nWith `pii.phone` on, `phoneRegex` in `redact/pii.go` only matches North American numbers, so a number in international format outside `+1` stayed in the transcript:\\n\\n```\\n+44 20 7946 0958       unchanged\\n+54 9 11 0000-0001     unchanged\\n+39 347 000 0001       +39 [REDACTED_PHONE]   (the national part happens to be NANP-shaped)\\n```\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\n`intlPhoneRegex` (`redact/pii_phone.go`) matches a `+`, a country code other than `1`, and the national number, separated by spaces (one or more, tabs and no-break spaces included), dashes, dots, one slash, or one parenthesized group (a trunk zero or an area code). Like the IP rules, the regex only finds the shape, and `redactableIntlPhone` decides. A match is redacted when:\\n\\n- it has 9 to 15 digits in all, country code included (E.164 allows at most 15). A space also joins a number to the text after it, so groups after a space that take it past 15 digits are left out (`+44 20 7946 0958 2026` becomes `[REDACTED_PHONE] 2026`), along with all the spaces before them, so aligned text keeps its spacing. A dash or dot is never cut, so a long signed decimal stays out;\\n- the `+` doesn't continue a word, a version or a path (`1.2.3+20241029`, `x+23456789012`, `ab/+2345678901`). A slash that ends a URI scheme is fine (`tel://+442079460958`), and so is a dot (`Tel.+44 20 7946 0958`). A letter after a backslash counts as an escape, so `\\\\n+44 20 7946 0958` is still redacted, using the IP code's `followsEscape`;\\n- the number doesn't run on into a word. If its last group starts a word after a space, the number ends before that space (`+44 20 7946 0958 9am` becomes `[REDACTED_PHONE] 9am`). An attached extension stays visible, as with North American numbers (`[REDACTED_PHONE]x123`, `[REDACTED_PHONE]ext123`, `[REDACTED_PHONE]ext 123`);\\n- the first group is the country code, 1 to 3 digits. A longer first group is allowed only before a space (`+447700 900123`, a national number with its 0 swapped for `+44`), so a date that starts with the year (`+2026-11-06 19:24`) doesn't pass;\\n- there is at most one slash, which separates an area code (`+49 30/23125678`). Two make a date (`+31/12/2024 23:59`), unless the second is in a group after a space (see the next point);\\n- with dots, dots are the only separator apart from spaces after the country code and the parenthesized group, there are at least two, and the digits don't form an IPv4 address. So `+33.1.99.00.12.34`, `+33 1.99.00.12.34`, `+33 (0)1.99.00.12.34`, `+33 (0) 1.99.00.12.34`, `(+33) 1.99.00.12.34` and `+34.912.345.678` are numbers, while a decimal (`+48.8566140`), `+233.252.18.110` and `+31.12.2024 23:59` are not. When only groups after a space break these rules or the slash rule, the number before them decides, and the groups stay in the match as they do without dots, since one may belong to the number (`+49 30123456 78.90`, `+33 1.99.00.12.34 2026` and `+44 20 7946 0958 1/2/3` become `[REDACTED_PHONE]`);\\n- a `(+39)` country code is redacted with its parentheses, and the `(` counts as the boundary whatever comes before it (`Tel.(+44) 20 7946 0958` becomes `Tel.[REDACTED_PHONE]`). A `)` or a slash after a longer first group ends the number instead (`(+442079460958)` becomes `([REDACTED_PHONE])`, `+442079460958/123` becomes `[REDACTED_PHONE]/123`).\\n\\nNumbers written without separators (`+442079460958`) are redacted too, the way `+15551234567` already is. National numbers without the `+` stay out of scope, as the issue says.\\n\\nSome text that isn't a phone number has the same shape and is redacted: digits written one by one (`+2 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1`), a date with dashes followed by a time (`+29-10-2024 12:30:00`), a signed integer of 9 to 15 digits (`+2147483647`), and numbers in aligned columns (`+4        3  0123456789`). The docs say so. In the tests, these and the rows that are compromises (`+33 1.99.00.12.34 2026` and `+44 20 7946 0958 1/2/3` go whole) are named `known limit: ...`, so a later fix doesn't read as a regression.\\n\\nTwo smaller changes:\\n\\n- The North American rule also matches the national part of `+39 347 000 0001`. The merged placeholder was already right, but the counts saw two phone numbers. `dropNestedIPRegions` in `redact/pii_ip.go` becomes `dropNestedPIIRegions` in `redact/pii.go`, and drops a region nested inside an earlier one with the same label, so the number counts once, even when a region of another label (a custom pattern matching the `39`) sorts between them. IP regions keep main's rule and are compared only with the region kept just before them: the version-key rule removes built-in IP matches afterwards, and dropping more custom `ip` matches inside them would expose their text. `TestPIIIntegration_CustomIPInsideVersionValueAfterOtherRegion` covers that. The leak main already has in that spot (a custom `ip` match inside a version value with nothing sorting between) is fixed separately in #3127.\\n- The IP and international phone validators go through one `validateCandidate` call in `detectPII`. That keeps `detectPII` under the complexity gate (it would have gone from 28 to 35).\\n\\n`configFingerprintVersion` goes from 13 to 14, since the new pattern alters output that the hashed config can't see (main took 13 for image data URIs in #2963).\\n\\n`docs/security-and-privacy.md` now describes the international shapes and what isn't matched, and the \\\"US-centric\\\" limitation is narrowed to national formats.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n`TestDetectPII_InternationalPhones` is the table from the issue. Numbers from IT, AR, UK, DE, FR and ES must redact, plus RU, BR, JP and IN, in the separator styles above. So must numbers in JSON, after an escape or a dot, in parentheses, in `tel://` and `sms://` URIs, with tabs, no-break spaces, repeated spaces or a slash, with an extension, followed by other numbers or words, and two in a row. Versions, IPs, timestamps and offsets, dates (with slashes too), ULIDs, long IDs, base64, decimals, exponents, short signed numbers, glued suffixes and national formats must not. All 65 cases with an international number fail on main, and so do the four known false positives. `TestDetectPII_InternationalPhoneCountsOnce` covers the nested region and fails on main too, and `..._CountsOnceAcrossLabels` covers a custom pattern sorting between the two matches.\\n\\n`go test ./redact` passes, and so do `golangci-lint` v2.15.0, the duplication check, the secret-pattern lint and the complexity gate.\\n\\n## False positives\\n\\nThe issue asked about IDs and timestamps, so I ran the new rule over the same corpora used for the IP and address rules:\\n\\n| Corpus | Text scanned | Intl matches |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| The 33 `full.jsonl` transcripts on this repo's public `refs/entire/checkpoints/*` refs (string values, path fields skipped like the JSONL redactor does) | 84 MB | 0 |\\n| Seven repos: cli, entire-brain, entire-graph, skills, external-agents, git-sync, homebrew-tap | 327 MB | 0 |\\n| The Go module cache after building cli and installing golangci-lint | 537 MB | 12 (16 now, see below) |\\n\\nOf the 12, 3 are in other projects' PII-sanitizer test data (two phone numbers, and a test card number written after a `+`). The other 9 are signed integer literals: protobuf's timestamp code (`maxTimestamp = +253402300799`, `Seconds: +9876543210`) and a Go compiler test (`(+9876654310)`, once per toolchain in the cache, which is where the 13th comes from). Since then the cache picked up a newer posthog-go with the same sanitizer test data (2 more), and allowing several spaces between groups added one: a comment table in segmentio/asm's base64 code (`+4        3  0123456789`). An unbroken number with a `+` and nothing else around it is the shape this rule can't tell from a phone number. I kept unbroken numbers in because that's how E.164 numbers usually appear in code, config and logs. For comparison, the existing North American rule matches 987 times on the same module cache, including lists such as `998\\\\n999\\\\n1000`.\\n\\nAlmost all of the roughly 68,000 `+<digit>` candidates in these corpora have fewer than 9 digits (diff hunk headers, offsets, exponents). None of the text is a phone directory, so this measures the false positives on code and English prose, not recall. The tests cover recall.\\n\\n## Performance\\n\\nThe regex starts with a literal `+`, so Go's regexp skips to each `+` instead of trying every position. `BenchmarkRedactJSONLBytes_PII/email-phone`, run three times each on main and on this branch, interleaved, gave 594/605/646 ms on main (f4327183) against 584/599/624 ms on this branch, and `email-phone-ip` gave 612/633/626 ms against 599/680/620 ms. That's within noise. Allowing several spaces between groups didn't slow it down either: 672/682 ms with it against 733/748 ms without it.\\n\\n## Overlap\\n\\nMy PR for #2977 (European addresses, also @rennf93's issue) edits the same docs table row and US-centric bullet in `docs/security-and-privacy.md`. That PR, #3048 (command-line passwords) and #3127 also bump `configFingerprintVersion`; this one goes to 14 because main took 13. #3127 also changes the IP rule this PR moves into `dropNestedPIIRegions`. The PRs are independent of each other against `main`: whichever lands later needs a small merge and the next fingerprint number, and I'll push that once the earlier one merges.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3065/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 1,\n                \"+1\": 1,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3065/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2821\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2821/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2821/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2821/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2821\",\n              \"id\": 5931887826,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABJbacmw\",\n              \"number\": 2821,\n              \"title\": \"Keep other worktrees' sessions off an identified committer's commit\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-19T21:30:30Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-22T19:38:51Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-22T19:38:48Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2821\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2821\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2821.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2821.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-22T19:38:48Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1613\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nFixes ENT-2463.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nAn agent that starts in the main checkout and moves into a linked worktree (Claude Code's `EnterWorktree`, which creates `.claude/worktrees/…`) stays homed in the main checkout. When it commits from the linked worktree, no session is homed there, so worktree matching falls back to every session of the main checkout. The shortcuts that skip content checks then condense every one of those sessions that is mid-turn into the agent's commit. These shortcuts are the no-TTY fast path, content detection by transcript growth, and post-commit ACTIVE condensation. The result is one checkpoint that holds the committer's session plus unrelated sessions from the main checkout, and the trail shows all of them.\\n\\nReproduced on the 0.10.7 release and on current main. #2668 hides the unrelated session only while that session's agent is still running.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nIn `findSessionsForCommitLinking`: when process ancestry identifies the committer and no session is homed in the committing worktree, the fallback's matches are dropped.\\n- A session from another worktree joins only through its record of this worktree (`hasWorktreeEntry`, from #2531), and is held to those edits (`LinkedByWorktreeEntry`).\\n- Sessions homed in the committing worktree still join alongside the identified committer, as before.\\n- A commit with no identified committer (Windows, no recorded owner) keeps the fallback unchanged.\\n\\n`findSessionsForWorktreeFromStates` now reports whether its result came from the fallback. Amend restore and post-rewrite (`findSessionsForWorktree`) are unchanged.\\n\\nDiff: +201/−13 across 6 files.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nEach new test fails without the fix:\\n- An identified committer in a sibling worktree, and in a worktree nested under the main checkout, links only itself plus a main-checkout session that recorded edits there. That session is flagged `LinkedByWorktreeEntry`.\\n- An identified committer homed in a third worktree, where the fallback would otherwise pick the main checkout's recent session.\\n- Through `PrepareCommitMsg` + `PostCommit`: the committer is stamped and condensed, and a mid-turn main-checkout session with pending work is not condensed into the checkpoint.\\n\\nGuards that also pass without the fix:\\n- With no identified committer, the fallback still links the main checkout's sessions.\\n- Sessions homed in the committing worktree stay linked next to an identified committer.\\n\\nLive, with real agents (headless). An unrelated Codex session in the main checkout edits README.md and stays mid-turn in `sleep`; the agent under test creates a linked worktree, edits there and commits. Entire's hooks are pinned to the build under test.\\n\\n| Committer | main | this branch |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Claude Code (`EnterWorktree` into `.claude/worktrees/`) | Codex session stamped and condensed into the commit | committer only |\\n| Codex | Codex bystander condensed into the commit (older nightly; main build rate-limited) | committer only |\\n| Pi | bystander condensed | committer only |\\n| Copilot CLI | bystander condensed | committer only |\\n| OpenCode | bystander condensed | bystander not condensed (OpenCode's own checkpoint not written, see below) |\\n| Antigravity | — | committer only |\\n| Cursor CLI | bystander condensed | bystander condensed (see below) |\\n\\nAlso checked against real binaries with a scripted repro: an unrelated mid-turn session in the main checkout, with its agent alive or gone. Built from this branch, that session is never linked when the committer is identified; the committer always is.\\n\\nRe-run after merging main (`ed9977c8a2`), with a Codex session mid-turn in the main checkout: Codex committing from a worktree, and Claude Code committing after `EnterWorktree` (local build with #2855). Both checkpoints held only the committer, and the mid-turn session kept its pending work.\\n\\n## Not in this PR\\n\\n- Checkpoints already written with extra sessions stay as they are. Cleaning those up would be a separate server-side change.\\n- A commit with no identified committer while an unrelated session is mid-turn still links it (unchanged from main; #2668 covers the case where that agent is running).\\n- A committer Entire cannot identify by process ancestry still gets the fallback. Headless `cursor-agent -p` ran no Entire hooks at all, so no session was recorded and the bystander was condensed on both builds; in the IDE, Cursor's recorded owner is the extension host, which is not an ancestor of its commands.\\n- A first-turn commit made after Claude Code's `EnterWorktree` got a trailer but no checkpoint (\\\"live transcript is empty or unreadable\\\"); fixed separately in #2855. OpenCode's transcript was likewise unreadable mid-turn; that is not covered by #2855.\\n- If #2668 merges first, this PR needs a small merge in the same function, or the other way round.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2821/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2821/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2012\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2012/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2012/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2012/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2012\",\n              \"id\": 5171903112,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABABQ4bw\",\n              \"number\": 2012,\n              \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): preserve newer same-ref queue entries\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"mikemikimike\",\n                \"id\": 186855910,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOCyMx5g\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186855910?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mikemikimike\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/mikemikimike\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mikemikimike/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mikemikimike/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mikemikimike/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mikemikimike/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mikemikimike/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mikemikimike/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mikemikimike/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mikemikimike/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mikemikimike/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 2,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-17T12:33:06Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-21T02:43:19Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-21T02:43:19Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2012\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2012\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2012.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2012.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Related issue\\n\\nFixes #2008: https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2008\\n\\n## Background\\n\\nThe checkpoint push queue is shared through Git's common directory. A push can\\npublish a ref's older tip while another process or linked worktree advances the\\nsame ref and enqueues it again. Removing queue entries by ref name alone can\\nthen discard an update that was not published. Duplicate enqueues from migration\\nmust also continue to collapse to one pending ref.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- Snapshot local ref hashes before pushing and remove queued entries only when\\n  the ref still matches the published snapshot.\\n- Treat a missing ref as a zero-hash snapshot and prune it only if it remains\\n  missing; retain an entry if that ref is recreated.\\n- Preserve refs advanced during an in-flight push, including updates made from\\n  a linked worktree and acknowledgments from concurrent flushes.\\n- Add queue, migration, and linked-worktree regressions for these cases.\\n\\nThis keeps the queue's existing de-duplicated ref semantics and does not change\\nthe checkpoint ref format or push protocol. If a ref advances during a push, its\\nentry remains queued for the next flush.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run \\\"TestPushQueue_RemoveIfUnchanged|TestMigrateBranchToRefs_ReenqueuesAlreadyImportedRef|TestFlushCheckpointRefsQueuePreservesLinkedWorktreeAdvance\\\" -count=1` - passed.\\n- `GOMAXPROCS=2 GO_TEST_PARALLEL=2 mise run test:ci:core` - passed with race detection across the core package set.\\n- `GOMAXPROCS=2 GOMEMLIMIT=2200MiB GOGC=75 mise run lint` - passed.\\n- `git diff --check` - passed.\\n\\nNot run: `mise run test:ci`, which includes the integration test package and E2E canary suite.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2012/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2012/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2660\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2660/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2660/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2660/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2660\",\n              \"id\": 5715837495,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABGwNtlw\",\n              \"number\": 2660,\n              \"title\": \"Revert \\\"Fix background-subagent attribution with busy-window tracking and full snapshots\\\"\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"id\": 881031,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-05T16:49:01Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-05T18:51:27Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-05T18:51:24Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2660\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2660\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2660.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2660.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-05T18:51:24Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1484\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nReverts entireio/cli#2651 -> in case this is related with e2e failures https://github.com/entireio/cli/actions/runs/37338554197\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **High Risk**\\n> Reverts checkpoint capture and attribution semantics for subagents, shell edits, and concurrent sessions—likely restoring prior mis-attribution but addressing e2e failures tied to #2651.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Reverts** the background-subagent attribution work from #2651: full dirty-worktree shadow snapshots, stop-time snapshots, and per-session “claims since” / busy-worktree prompt boundaries.\\n> \\n> Ephemeral checkpoints go back to **first checkpoint = whole changed worktree via `git status`**, later checkpoints = **caller-supplied modified/new/deleted paths** (with gitignore filtering), with skip only when the **tree hash** matches the previous shadow tip—not when the whole worktree is unchanged vs. transcript detection. `WriteEphemeralResult.ChangedFiles`, `SkipWhenUnchanged`, and `ClaimsSince` are removed, along with revert-to-base and `changedSince` tree logic.\\n> \\n> **Lifecycle** again **skips `SaveStep` when turn-end file detection is empty** (still runs token/cleanup bookkeeping), drops **subagent-stop worktree snapshots** and **`snapshotAgentStop`**, and no longer treats “no detected changes” as a conditional snapshot path or handles `ErrNothingToSnapshot`. **`RefreshSessionOwner` on session start** is removed.\\n> \\n> **Attribution / session state** drops `ClaimsSince*`, prompt **`Incomplete` / worktree-busy** skipping, `recordClaimsStart`, cross-session file claiming from snapshot diffs, and `ExistingSessionOnly` saves; `FilesTouched` is driven by transcript-reported paths again. Related unit/integration tests and **attribution.md** busy-window docs are removed or updated; path-normalization tests expect invalid paths to **skip** updates again.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 5f1714a7dedc3e45abcba8fd8d259ead4de9307c. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2660/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2660/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2329\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2329/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2329/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2329/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2329\",\n              \"id\": 5395169111,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCxsWMQ\",\n              \"number\": 2329,\n              \"title\": \"fix(doctor): respect explicit checkpoint remote selection\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-09T04:58:35Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-11T19:21:41Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-11T19:21:38Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2329\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2329\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2329.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2329.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-11T19:21:38Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1272\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n- Stop the shared doctor/enable destination note from asking users to choose among remotes after a valid strategy_options.checkpoint_push_remote selection.\\n- Reuse ResolveCheckpointSyncRemote and require a successful config-source result; absent or invalid selections still receive the existing choice warning.\\n- Preserve multiple-push-URL warnings, including when the selected remote has multiple push URLs.\\n\\n## Reproduction\\n\\nWith origin and fork configured and checkpoint_push_remote set to fork, status correctly reported fork (source=config), while doctor still printed Checkpoint destination: REVIEW and asked the user to choose a remote. Running the before/after binaries against the same isolated repository confirms that this patch removes the incorrect note without changing the selected destination.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- Regression demonstrated failing before the fix and passing afterward.\\n- Four cases: explicit fork, absent selection, nonexistent selection, and explicit fork with multiple push URLs.\\n- Related status/checkpoint-sync and doctor metadata tests passed.\\n- mise run check passed on an identical patch in a temporary space-free checkout: unit/integration tests with race detection, lint, and deterministic Vogon/roger-roger canaries.\\n- mise run lint passed again on the original formatted tree; git diff --check passed.\\n\\nThe original checkout path contains spaces, exposing an existing unquoted go.mod replace path in TestBetterleaksDoesNotPoisonGitEnvironment. The temporary clone was given a normal repository origin URL for an existing trail test that reads checkout identity. Neither harness issue required code changes in this PR.\\n\\n## Scope and related work\\n\\nDiagnostic output only: no election, push, read, migration, or dedicated-storage behavior changes. User configuration changes are excluded.\\n\\nRelated to #2327, which changes wording and automatic Entire-remote election in the same area. This patch handles explicit source=config selection independently; integration should preserve both conditions and the revised wording.\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Diagnostic-only changes to enable/doctor messaging; checkpoint sync election and push paths are untouched.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Fixes doctor/enable checkpoint destination notes** when the user has already pinned a remote via `strategy_options.checkpoint_push_remote`.\\n> \\n> Remote topology inspection now calls `strategy.ResolveCheckpointSyncRemote` and treats a **config-sourced** election as `explicitlySelected`. The shared “choose among remotes” / `Checkpoint destination: REVIEW` messaging is skipped when that applies; absent or invalid settings still show the existing multi-remote warning.\\n> \\n> **Multiple push URLs** on the selected remote still trigger fan-out warnings. Election, push, and sync behavior are unchanged—this is advisory CLI output only.\\n> \\n> Adds `TestCheckpointDestinationNote_ExplicitSelection` covering explicit selection, default, missing remote, and multi-URL on an explicit remote.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 7a15f32532e0ec32661fdcf0650c1cc40dec8c20. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2329/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2329/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2406\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2406/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2406/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2406/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2406\",\n              \"id\": 5446905666,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABDat1rQ\",\n              \"number\": 2406,\n              \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): compare the git-refs shard case-insensitively\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"wangzhengzhuo05\",\n                \"id\": 175673456,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOCniQcA\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175673456?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wangzhengzhuo05\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/wangzhengzhuo05\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wangzhengzhuo05/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wangzhengzhuo05/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wangzhengzhuo05/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wangzhengzhuo05/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wangzhengzhuo05/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wangzhengzhuo05/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wangzhengzhuo05/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wangzhengzhuo05/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wangzhengzhuo05/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-14T08:15:53Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-18T03:43:50Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-18T03:43:50Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2406\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2406\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2406.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2406.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## What\\n\\n`ParseRef` now compares the git-refs shard **case-insensitively**, so a checkpoint ref written under a differently-cased shard directory is still readable.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\n`CheckpointID.ShardFor()` shards by the last two characters of the ID, case preserved. ULID IDs are canonically uppercase Crockford base32, legacy hex IDs are lowercase. On a case-insensitive filesystem (macOS APFS default, Windows NTFS default), a new ULID checkpoint whose shard is `6B` is written into a pre-existing legacy `6b` directory — git resolves both to the same physical directory. `ParseRef` then required an exact case-sensitive match against the ref's directory component, rejected the ref as malformed, and the checkpoint became **permanently invisible** to `checkpoint list` / `checkpoint explain` even though its git object was intact and uncorrupted.\\n\\nThe reporter's verification against this source:\\n\\n```\\nParseRef(\\\"refs/entire/checkpoints/6b/01M2DCHJCHTR9T9MZTSB7WV76B\\\")\\n// -> id=\\\"\\\", ok=false                         <- the failure\\nParseRef(\\\"refs/entire/checkpoints/6B/01M2DCHJCHTR9T9MZTSB7WV76B\\\")\\n// -> id=\\\"01M2DCHJCHTR9T9MZTSB7WV76B\\\", ok=true  <- only the directory case differs\\n```\\n\\nThis is the read-side fix named first in the issue. It is also a prerequisite for any write-side change: correcting the spelling at write time still has to read the refs already on disk with the older spelling.\\n\\n## How\\n\\n* `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/refs_naming.go` — `cid.ShardFor() != shard` becomes `!strings.EqualFold(cid.ShardFor(), shard)`, with a comment explaining the collision and the doc comment on `ParseRef` updated to say the match is case-insensitive. `ShardFor` is deliberately unchanged: changing the canonical spelling would make every existing uppercase-shard ref on case-sensitive filesystems unreadable.\\n\\nThe guard keeps its original purpose: folding only the case still rejects a ref that points at a genuinely different bucket (`f6` vs `a1`), and shards are ASCII hex or Crockford base32, so folding is unambiguous.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nNew `TestParseRef_CaseInsensitiveShard` in `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/refs_naming_test.go` covers:\\n\\n1. the exact reported case — ULID whose canonical shard is `6B`, stored under `6b` — now parses back to its ID;\\n2. the mirror case — a lowercase legacy ID under an uppercase `F6` directory;\\n3. the guard is not weakened — a genuinely different bucket (`a1`) is still rejected.\\n\\nIt is a separate test function rather than a table case in `TestParseRef` because that table asserts a byte-identical `RefName` round-trip, and `RefName` rebuilds the canonical spelling, which a case-different input can never reproduce.\\n\\n```\\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/ -count=1 -run 'TestRefName|TestParseRef'\\nok  \\tgithub.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint\\t0.032s\\n```\\n\\n### Mutation check\\n\\nReverting only the production line (`!strings.EqualFold(...)` back to `cid.ShardFor() != shard`) makes the new test fail on both must-parse assertions — `expected \\\"01M2DCHJCHTR9T9MZTSB7WV76B\\\", actual \\\"\\\"` — while the third (guard) case still passes. Restoring the fix returns the package to green. The new test therefore pins exactly this regression.\\n\\n## AI-generated code disclosure\\n\\nThe change was implemented with AI assistance (OpenCode + muse-spark 1.3, from the task file in the diff) and reviewed and verified by hand: the focused test suite was re-run locally, and the mutation check above was performed on the real production file.\\n\\nFixes #2401\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2406/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2406/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2830\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2830/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2830/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2830/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2830\",\n              \"id\": 5939111155,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABJhEIvw\",\n              \"number\": 2830,\n              \"title\": \"build: bump Go to 1.27.2 and golangci-lint to 2.15.0\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-20T09:13:46Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:37:02Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:36:58Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2830\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2830\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2830.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2830.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:36:58Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1622\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nBumps the pinned Go toolchain to 1.27.2 (`mise.toml`, `go.mod`, and the minimum version in CONTRIBUTING/README/WINDOWS) and golangci-lint to 2.15.0. CI's lint step reads the golangci-lint version from `mise.toml`, so no workflow edit is needed.\\n\\ngolangci-lint 2.15's errcheck now flags error values received from a channel and discarded. It found five sites, all in tests: the two antigravity lock tests now print the received error when they fail, the two group-kill cancel tests signal on a `chan struct{}` and discard the expected `cmd.Wait()` error with a `//nolint` like the rest of the repo, and the plugin confirm test reports what the stuck prompt returned on timeout.\\n\\nVerified locally: golangci-lint 2.15.0 reports 0 issues across the repo, `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` is clean, and `mise run test:ci` passes on go1.27.2.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Toolchain and linter version bumps with documentation and test-only changes; no production runtime behavior is modified in this diff.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Bumps the **minimum Go toolchain** from **1.27.1** to **1.27.2** in `go.mod`, `mise.toml`, and contributor docs (`CONTRIBUTING.md`, `README.md`, `WINDOWS.md`), and upgrades **golangci-lint** from **2.13.2** to **2.15.0** in `mise.toml`.\\n> \\n> Several tests are tightened for cancellation and locking: Unix process-group cancel tests signal completion with a `struct{}` channel and treat post-cancel `Wait()` errors as expected; Antigravity lock-serialization tests include the goroutine error in failure messages; the accessible plugin confirmation timeout path reports the prompt result when the input is closed.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 6efc2a7979942ed0ac74cbaba9efe11f8384a637. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2830/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2830/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": {\n                \"id\": 2626939,\n                \"client_id\": \"Iv23lieFG10uOnChW4TN\",\n                \"slug\": \"entire\",\n                \"node_id\": \"A_kwHOAfprLM4AKBV7\",\n                \"owner\": {\n                  \"login\": \"entireio\",\n                  \"id\": 33188652,\n                  \"node_id\": \"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjMzMTg4NjUy\",\n                  \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33188652?v=4\",\n                  \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio\",\n                  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio\",\n                  \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/followers\",\n                  \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/following{/other_user}\",\n                  \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                  \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                  \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/subscriptions\",\n                  \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/orgs\",\n                  \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/repos\",\n                  \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/events{/privacy}\",\n                  \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/received_events\",\n                  \"type\": \"Organization\",\n                  \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                  \"site_admin\": false\n                },\n                \"name\": \"Entire\",\n                \"description\": \"\",\n                \"external_url\": \"https://entire.com\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/entire\",\n                \"created_at\": \"2026-01-09T21:20:56Z\",\n                \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-23T08:32:31Z\",\n                \"permissions\": {\n                  \"administration\": \"read\",\n                  \"checks\": \"write\",\n                  \"contents\": \"write\",\n                  \"emails\": \"read\",\n                  \"members\": \"read\",\n                  \"metadata\": \"read\",\n                  \"pull_requests\": \"write\",\n                  \"statuses\": \"read\",\n                  \"workflows\": \"write\"\n                },\n                \"events\": [\n                  \"check_suite\",\n                  \"create\",\n                  \"delete\",\n                  \"fork\",\n                  \"member\",\n                  \"membership\",\n                  \"organization\",\n                  \"pull_request\",\n                  \"push\",\n                  \"repository\",\n                  \"star\",\n                  \"team\"\n                ]\n              },\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2651\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2651/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2651/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2651/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2651\",\n              \"id\": 5699233056,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABGi_28Q\",\n              \"number\": 2651,\n              \"title\": \"Fix background-subagent attribution with busy-window tracking and full snapshots\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-04T12:22:14Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-05T16:08:58Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-05T16:08:54Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2651\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2651\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2651.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2651.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-05T16:08:54Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1476\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nFix background-subagent and shell-written changes being incorrectly credited to the user.\\n\\nThis changes the attribution heuristic: a prompt is treated as a human-edit boundary only when the worktree is idle. While another session or a live background subagent is working, prompt-start attribution records no human diff.\\n\\n**Intentional trade-off:** human edits made during an agent-busy window can be credited to the agent. This is timing-based attribution, not exact authorship.\\n\\nSupersedes #2646 and #2650.\\n\\n## Why attribution was wrong\\n\\nTwo gaps caused agent work to look like human work:\\n\\n1. A background subagent could write after its parent's turn ended without producing another snapshot. Its changes then appeared in the next prompt's “user edits since the last snapshot” diff. Claude Code's completion notification can start that prompt before the subagent-stop hook finishes.\\n2. Later snapshots could miss shell-written changes, particularly edits to pre-existing untracked files that neither transcript parsing nor turn-end change detection identified.\\n\\n## New behavior\\n\\n| Boundary | Behavior |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Prompt while idle | Record human changes since the previous snapshot, retaining the existing first-prompt baseline rule. |\\n| Prompt while busy | Do not record a human diff. |\\n| Turn end | Snapshot the dirty worktree, including changes not named in the transcript. |\\n| Background subagent's final stop | Snapshot before completing its task record. |\\n| Commit | Keep the existing attribution calculation, using the more complete snapshots and accumulated human-edit records. |\\n\\n“Busy” means another qualifying session is mid-turn, or this or another session has a live background subagent in the same worktree. Ended sessions and sessions with a confirmed-dead owner do not count; stale active turns are excluded, and unknown liveness uses the existing recency fallback.\\n\\nAn owner exiting does not itself end the session. SessionStart refreshes owner identity so resumed sessions can count as busy again.\\n\\n## Implementation and safeguards\\n\\n- Every shadow snapshot captures the dirty worktree via `git status`, rather than relying on transcript-reported file lists. Ignore and protected-path exclusions still apply, including ignore rules matching tracked files.\\n- Files reverted since the previous snapshot return to their base content. Snapshots report which files changed since the previous snapshot.\\n- A background subagent's final stop uses `snapshotAgentStop` before completing its task record. Turn ends with no detected files use the normal save/accounting path so newly captured changes retain their token usage.\\n- Fallback snapshots skip writes when no worktree content changed. Missing or ended sessions are checked under the save lock, so late fallback stops cannot recreate them or write new snapshots for them.\\n- Snapshot-derived file ownership excludes files attributed to human edits or already claimed by another live session. Unknown human attribution does not automatically claim snapshot files. These exclusions apply to snapshot-derived additions, not the existing transcript/detected-file lists.\\n- Snapshot code files remain raw local shadow data; this PR does not add source-code redaction or change checkpoint push behavior.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\nIntegration coverage includes:\\n\\n- Both notification-before-stop and stop-before-notification ordering.\\n- Commits before the next parent turn, with and without an earlier parent snapshot.\\n- Background subagent writes through edit tools and Bash.\\n- Long-running subagents spanning multiple parent prompts.\\n- Human edits after completion remaining human-attributed.\\n- Shell edits to pre-existing untracked files.\\n\\nUnit coverage includes busy/liveness rules, owner refresh, full snapshots, reverted files, token preservation, late stops, cross-session file ownership, and tracked-file ignore policy.\\n\\nCI at `79ee6f97c7fd954df1ccb6744b8fd7dd3a4eab16` passes lint, core tests, all three integration shards, Codex-hook tests, Windows tests, and deterministic canaries for both checkpoint backends. CodeQL, license, binary-size, and control-plane checks also pass. The Entire approval gate still requires a reviewer approval; passing CI is not approval to merge.\\n\\n## Follow-ups\\n\\n- Simplifying the existing per-prompt attribution machinery (`prompt_attributions`, turn-end file lists, and the first-prompt baseline rule).\\n- Recognizing Codex `turn_aborted` as completion so aborted child turns do not remain classified as busy.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2651/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2651/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3071\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3071/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3071/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3071/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3071\",\n              \"id\": 6284536208,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABN0o3EQ\",\n              \"number\": 3071,\n              \"title\": \"feat(proclive): track agent process liveness on Windows\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n                \"id\": 26940511,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI2OTQwNTEx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Beehtrix\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 7,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-09T10:42:18Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-14T09:06:41Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3071\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3071\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3071.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3071.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes #3053: `proclive` has no Windows implementation, so no Windows session records an owner.\\n\\n## What changes on Windows\\n\\n`proclive` returned \\\"unsupported\\\" on Windows (#1488 left it out of scope). So until now:\\n\\n- **Liveness** of a mid-turn session was always unknown. `entire status`, `entire doctor`, attach and the exited-owner sweep fell back to `IsStuckActive`, which counts a turn over an hour as stuck even while its agent still runs.\\n- **Commit provenance** never marked a session foreign. With no TTY, `prepare-commit-msg`'s fast path stamped any mid-turn session, so a script's commit during another session's turn went to that session.\\n\\nWith this PR, a Windows session records its agent's process as owner at turn start, `Check` reports it alive or dead, and a commit hook's ancestry walk can show that a live owner is not its ancestor, as on Linux and macOS. That should make @mattjes's Windows baseline (https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/3053#issuecomment-6706927443) come out as it does on Linux, where the first row gives no trailer instead of A.\\n\\n## How\\n\\nA `proc_windows.go` behind the existing seam:\\n\\n- `procStat` opens the process with `PROCESS_QUERY_LIMITED_INFORMATION`. It reads the parent PID (`NtQueryInformationProcess`), the creation time (`GetProcessTimes`) and the image name (`QueryFullProcessImageName`). The creation time is the start fingerprint. It's absolute, like darwin's, so `bootID` returns no guard.\\n- An exited process that some handle still holds counts as gone: its handle is signaled, or its exit code is no longer `STILL_ACTIVE`. The handle check also catches a process that exited with 259 as its code. It needs `SYNCHRONIZE`. Where a process's DACL denies that, a process whose exit code still reads `STILL_ACTIVE` is reported as unknown, not alive.\\n- **Where a walk ends.** Windows keeps a process's parent PID after the parent exits, and the PID can then be reused, so no walk reaches an init. `procStat` therefore checks the parent too. If the parent has exited, or its PID now names a process created after the child, `procStat` reports PID 1, where `walkAncestry` already ends a complete chain. Windows never assigns PID 1. The chain up to the first process without a living parent holds every living ancestor, which is what `Ancestry.Complete` needs to mean on Windows. It is also what Linux and macOS give when a parent exits mid-chain: the child is reparented to init, and the walk reaches PID 1 without the processes above it. Creation order comes from the process sequence number, which the kernel counts per boot, so a clock change can't reorder it. Where the system doesn't report one (older Windows versions, Wine), the creation time stands in.\\n- A parent it can't open (another user's process, so access denied) is reported unverified. The walk then stops there incomplete, and `Excludes` proves nothing, as after any failed lookup.\\n- **Windows and WSL.** They can share a hostname and a checkout, so each can read the owners the other recorded, but their PIDs name different process tables. Every owner now records the OS of the binary that recorded it (`Identity.OS`). `Check`, `Depth` and `Excludes` treat an owner recorded for another OS as one they can't judge, so WSL's sweep can't end a live Windows session, and a Windows commit hook can't mark a WSL session foreign. Owners recorded before this carry no OS and are judged as before. Every turn start records a new owner, so only a turn that was already running at upgrade lacks one.\\n- `isTransient` ignores a `.exe` suffix and adds `cmd`, `powershell`, `pwsh` and `conhost`, so the owner is the agent, not the shell that ran the hook.\\n\\n`doctor_classify_live_test.go` and `owner_wiring_test.go` now build on Windows too: they need nothing Unix-only. The two doctor tests now carry `Windows` in their names, so the `test-windows` job runs them. `TestInitializeSession_CapturesOwner` keeps its name for now, because no strategy test that builds a git repo runs on that job yet; it's in the test list below. The docs that said Windows can't introspect are updated.\\n\\n## The risk\\n\\nA wrong owner. If the first non-shell ancestor of a turn-start hook is a short-lived intermediary rather than the agent, the owner reads as dead while the agent still runs. `entire doctor` and the sweep would then end that session, and `entire status` would show it as exited. The same rule already holds on Linux and macOS. What's new is each agent's Windows hook chain, which I can't see from Linux. It needs a run with real agents on Windows before it merges.\\n\\n@mattjes, you offered on #3053 to test with real Claude Code sessions. Thank you, that's exactly what this needs. The branch is `fix-windows-proclive-3053`. What would help most:\\n\\n1. `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/proclive/`, plus `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/ -run TestInitializeSession_CapturesOwner`. The new proclive tests have `Windows` in their names.\\n2. In a real Claude Code session, once a turn has started: the session's state file under `.git/entire-sessions/` should have an `owner` whose `name` is the agent's process (`claude.exe`, or `node.exe` for an npm install), not `bash.exe` or `cmd.exe`. `entire status` should show the session as active while the agent runs.\\n3. Close the agent mid-turn without ending the session. `entire status` should then show it as exited, and `entire doctor` should end it.\\n4. Your two #3011 scenarios again on this branch. Both rows should now come out as they do on Linux: row 1 should no longer go to A, because the commit hook can now tell that A's live agent isn't its ancestor.\\n\\nCodex, Cursor, Copilot CLI or Droid would be worth a look too if you have any of them installed, since each starts its hooks differently.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n`proc_windows_test.go`. Every test has `Windows` in its name, so the `test-windows` job runs them. They start real processes by re-executing the test binary:\\n\\n- `procStat` on itself and on a child: the parent PID, an `.exe` name, a creation-time fingerprint.\\n- A process whose parent has exited reports PID 1, and a walk from it is complete.\\n- `Check` reads a live child as alive and the same child as dead once it exits. That includes while Go still holds its handle, which keeps an exited process and its PID in the table.\\n- A start mismatch reads as dead. `CurrentAncestry` puts the parent at depth 0 and excludes a child exactly when the walk is complete. `ResolveOwner` never returns a shell.\\n- `TestProcessCreatedAfterWindows`: creation order by sequence number, including a clock set back between parent and child, and the creation-time fallback.\\n- `TestCheck_OtherOSIsUnknown`, `TestAncestryDepth_RejectsAnotherOS` and two new `TestAncestryExcludes` cases, in `proclive_test.go`: an owner recorded for another OS is unknown to `Check`, and never matches or excludes. They don't depend on the platform, so the regular test job runs them. They pass under Wine too.\\n\\nI don't have a Windows machine. Under Wine 9.0 on Linux, every proclive test passes, three runs in a row. I also ran them under a stand-in `agent.exe` that starts the test binary through `cmd.exe`, as an agent would start a hook. `ResolveOwner` skipped `cmd.exe` and returned `agent.exe`, and the ancestry walk was complete. The two renamed doctor tests pass the same way. Wine doesn't report sequence numbers, so those runs use the creation-time fallback. Wine isn't Windows, so mattjes's run and the `test-windows` job are the real checks.\\n\\nOn Linux, the proclive and session tests pass, and so do the strategy and cli tests for owners, provenance, identity, caller resolution and doctor. golangci-lint v2.15.0 is clean for `./...` and for proclive and strategy with `GOOS=windows`.\\n\\n@Soph, `proclive` and its seam are yours from #1488. This follows the shape in #3053.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3071/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3071/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2289\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2289/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2289/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2289/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2289\",\n              \"id\": 5364820409,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCZmK3Q\",\n              \"number\": 2289,\n              \"title\": \"feat(recall): `entire recall` — checkpoint history as trust-ranked associative memory\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"voxmastery\",\n                \"id\": 118175632,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOBws3kA\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118175632?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/voxmastery\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/voxmastery\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/voxmastery/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/voxmastery/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/voxmastery/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/voxmastery/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/voxmastery/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/voxmastery/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/voxmastery/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/voxmastery/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/voxmastery/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-06T12:02:30Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-21T11:20:56Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-21T11:20:56Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2289\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2289\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2289.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2289.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nAdds an experimental `entire recall` command: checkpoint history as trust-ranked associative memory. A developer, or a fresh agent session whose context window has closed, asks *\\\"what did we decide and why\\\"* and gets ranked hits, each carrying a **tier** (LEDGER commit record / INTENT user prompt / chat assistant claim), a **verdict** of the claim against the commit it sits on, and the backing commit — instead of a transcript dump.\\n\\nGit records what changed; checkpoints preserve why. But preserved context is an archive, not a memory: search returns transcripts, and a statement like \\\"this change is isolated to one package\\\" sits there looking as authoritative as everything else even when the diff reaches three others. `recall` ranks checkpoint context by how much it can be trusted, not by keyword match.\\n\\nBuilt on Track 1 of the BTW Buildathon 2026 (Bengaluru) with Entire's own checkpoints, trailers and Graph as the input corpus. This PR is the feature only; the event write-up, benchmark provenance and demo live on the fork's `main`.\\n\\n## What is in the PR\\n\\n**Go shim** — `cmd/entire/cli/recall_cmd.go`, `recall_collect.go` (+ tests). `entire recall ingest` walks trailered commits on the current branch, reads each checkpoint's transcript and diff through the persistent store, and pipes JSON to the `recall` binary. `entire recall <question>` renders the ranked hits (`--json` for machines). No ranking logic lives in Go.\\n\\n**Rust crate** — `recall/` on [FluctlightDB](https://github.com/voxmastery/FluctlightDB) (embedded, local, MIT/Apache-2.0). `ingest` maps prompts (`UserExplicit`), assistant turns (`ChatAssertion`), commit records (`LedgerVerified`) and touched files to engrams. `activate` never sorts on raw activation: provenance → `SourceKind`; `agreement()` runs six ordered checks of a claim against its commit — graph-reach scope, named file, action polarity, identifier anchor, lexical, 4-gram cosine — and the result adds or removes evidence before a noisy-OR confidence sets the score.\\n\\n**Entire Graph** supplies the reach the scope check uses: one `entire graph symbols` stream, then `impact` on the first two code symbols each touched file defines, capped at 40 queries per ingest. No graph → no edges; nothing is fabricated.\\n\\n**Wiring** follows the existing conventions: `experimental.Register` (hidden in stable builds, shown in developer/nightly), an `agentHelpClassification` entry (`recall` and `recall ingest` are **task-driven, unlisted** — `ingest` rebuilds derived state under `.entire/recall`, so the group cannot claim read-only), a row in `entire labs`, and a CLAUDE.md paragraph. The binary is located via `$ENTIRE_RECALL_BIN`, then `recall` on `$PATH`, then `recall/target/{release,debug}/recall`; the Go side builds and tests without Rust installed.\\n\\n## Privacy boundary: sensitive repositories\\n\\n- **Nothing leaves the machine.** The brain is an embedded database under `.entire/recall/` (gitignored). The only network on the ingest path is git fetching the repo's own checkpoint refs. `recall/scripts/verify-offline.sh` runs ingest and activate under `strace -f -e trace=network` and fails on a single socket call — measured, not asserted, because FluctlightDB's dependency tree does include `hyper`/`tokio` (behind an unused feature and an uncalled server module).\\n- **A checkpoint whose transcript cannot be read is never dropped.** Its commit record is ingested with the missing fields declared in `unavailable`. On this repository that is the difference between 3 and 125 checkpoints, because most checkpoint refs live on an upstream remote a fork cannot read.\\n- **Fourth verdict `unverifiable`, distinct from `neutral`.** Neutral means \\\"checked, found nothing\\\". Unverifiable means \\\"could not check: the field this check needed was redacted or unavailable\\\". Unavailability is *declared* by the shim, never inferred from an empty field, so complete checkpoints take a byte-identical path.\\n- **The interface never presents partial context as complete.** Every answer opens with a coverage line; `--json` returns `{\\\"coverage\\\": ..., \\\"hits\\\": [...]}`. `complete` is printed only when every checkpoint was indexed whole, the commit walk was not cut short, and the graph was consulted. Hits from partial context carry `partial: [...]` and their confidence is capped at 0.50, below any corroborated hit.\\n- `entire recall ingest --no-transcripts` never opens a transcript.\\n\\n## Evaluation\\n\\n`cargo run --release --example bench` runs `agreement()` over 840 labelled claim/commit pairs generated from this repository's own public history under four of the CodeFuse-CommitEval mutation rules (operation type, file path, function name, component):\\n\\n| metric | value |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Precision | 0.869 |\\n| Recall | 0.270 |\\n| Specificity | 0.927 |\\n| Latency | ~145 µs per verdict |\\n\\nPrecision-biased on purpose: when it flags a claim as contradicted it is right 87% of the time, and it stays silent otherwise. Recall is the documented limitation. The thresholded checks are calibrated to this repo's commit style; the structural identifier-anchor check is the part that transfers.\\n\\n**Note on `recall/bench/bench_840.json` (3.7 MB):** it contains real diffs from this repository's history, including the AWS Access Key ID fixture your secret-redaction tests use. GitHub secret scanning flags it on the fork; it is your own test fixture, already present across many upstream commits, not a live credential. Happy to move the file to Git LFS or an external download if you would rather not carry it in-tree.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/...` — all packages pass except `TestPathIsVersioned_ReftableRepo`, which needs git ≥ 2.45 and fails identically on `main` here (git 2.43)\\n- [x] `gofmt -s`, `go vet`, `golangci-lint run ./cmd/entire/cli/...` — no new issues (one pre-existing gosec finding in `utils.go`, untouched)\\n- [x] `go mod tidy` — no changes; dupl at threshold 75 — no hits in the new files\\n- [x] `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets` (0 warnings), `cargo test` (27 passed)\\n- [x] `cargo run --release --example bench` — P 0.869 / R 0.270 / Spec 0.927\\n- [x] `recall/scripts/verify-offline.sh` — 0 network syscalls\\n- [x] Live: `entire recall ingest` on this repo → 125 checkpoints, coverage line `PARTIAL · 5 of 125 checkpoints complete · 120 without transcript · …`; queries return the expected commits as LEDGER hits with `◌ partial context: transcript unavailable` where the transcript was unreadable\\n- [ ] `mise run check` end to end (mise is not installed on this machine; the individual steps above were run directly)\\n- [ ] Reviewer call on `listed`/audience for `recall` in `agentHelpClassification` — I took the safe default (unlisted, task-driven) per CLAUDE.md\\n\\n## Known limitations / follow-ups\\n\\n- Recall 0.270: a high-precision screen, not a comprehensive detector.\\n- Thresholds need per-repository calibration outside this repo.\\n- Engrams carry no embedding vectors, so paraphrase reads as neutral rather than corroborated; populating `semantic_vector` with a local embedder is the highest-value next step.\\n- Prose with a slash in it (`definition/search`, `owner/repo`) can still trip the file check on long pasted prompts; per-sentence claims rather than per-turn is the fix.\\n- The graph index is per-HEAD; `entire graph index` before ingest avoids a ~90 s re-index.\\n\\n🧙 Built with [WOZCODE](https://wozcode.com)\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2289/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2289/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2211\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2211/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2211/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2211/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2211\",\n              \"id\": 5308899549,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBtW1lw\",\n              \"number\": 2211,\n              \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): serialize OPF ref updates\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"id\": 34813274,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 15,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-01T07:12:39Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-06T16:30:08Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-06T16:30:08Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2211\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2211\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2211.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2211.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-06T16:30:08Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes #2204\\n\\nA native Git checkpoint writer and an OPF rewrite could both read the same ref value and then both report a successful update. The OPF paths used go-git's compare-and-swap, which does not participate in native Git's reference-locking protocol. A native transaction could therefore commit after the OPF rewrite and silently discard it.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\nIntroduce `gitrepo.CompareAndSwapRef`, a shared direct-ref compare-and-swap built on a native `git update-ref --stdin` transaction. The transaction prepares the update first, acquiring Git's ref lock, verifies that the ref is not symbolic while that lock is held, and then commits.\\n\\nThe native helper now backs:\\n\\n- shadow-branch updates\\n- all persistent-ref writers using `updatePersistentRef`, including the Stop hook\\n- both OPF rewrite paths: the shared v1 ref and per-checkpoint refs\\n\\nThe OPF scan remains outside the ref transaction. Its final CAS uses the value observed before the scan, so a concurrent update is rejected instead of overwritten.\\n\\n`CASPersistentRef` deliberately does not acquire Entire's persistent-writer flock. Its expected value predates the call, and native Git is the correctness boundary. Avoiding the flock also prevents deadline-free pre-push operations from waiting indefinitely. Transient native lock contention is retried with a bounded budget; a genuine stale-value conflict is terminal.\\n\\n## Transaction and failure behavior\\n\\nThe separate `git symbolic-ref` invocation is deliberate. Git does not allow `symref-verify` and an update of the same ref in one transaction because it treats them as multiple updates to that ref. Preparing the native update first keeps the ref locked while the symbolic-ref probe runs, closing the conversion race.\\n\\nCAS error classification recognizes only Git's exact stale-value diagnostics. Corrupt refs, unreadable refs, namespace conflicts, and other permanent failures retain their underlying diagnosis rather than being mislabeled and retried. The v1 rewrite reports `V1RefMovedError` only after a successful reread confirms that the ref actually changed.\\n\\nCancellation closes the transaction's stdin so Git can abort cleanly. A three-second `WaitDelay` bounds shutdown if a hook or inherited pipe prevents the process from exiting.\\n\\n## Performance\\n\\nRouting the shared write path through the transaction increases a measured ref update from 13.4 ms to 22.0 ms—an 8.6 ms cost per update. That is under 1% of the roughly 3-second p50 Stop-hook latency.\\n\\nThe extra symbolic-ref process is required for the direct-ref guarantee described above; it is not an accidental round trip.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nRegression tests use real native Git transactions and cover both files and reftable repositories. They exercise:\\n\\n- both OPF lost-update races\\n- symbolic-ref rejection and concurrent symbolic conversion\\n- native lock contention and bounded retry behavior\\n- cancellation and lock release\\n- malformed, corrupt, unreadable, and namespace-conflicting refs\\n- preservation of the original failure when a v1 ref cannot be reread\\n\\nThe focused race tests passed ten consecutive runs.\\n\\n`mise run check` passed after the review fixes, including formatting, lint, race-enabled unit and integration tests, and the Vogon and Roger-Roger canary suites.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2211/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2211/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2572\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2572/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2572/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2572/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2572\",\n              \"id\": 5554897614,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABExBMNA\",\n              \"number\": 2572,\n              \"title\": \"test: characterize Git CLI behavior before go-git migration\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-23T14:28:54Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-24T10:42:16Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-24T10:42:12Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2572\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2572\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2572.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2572.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-24T10:42:12Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1412\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nEstablish the native Git CLI behavior before replacing selected subprocesses with go-git. This is a standalone characterization-test PR; production Git operations remain unchanged.\\n\\n- Cover branch validation, HEAD/checkpoint reads, commit-ref peeling, tracking-ref enumeration, shallow detection, remote config scopes, and tree diffs.\\n- Exercise SHA-1/SHA-256, files/reftable refs, packed refs, linked worktrees, shared-clone alternates, cancellation, errors, and index preservation.\\n- Add a reusable test environment helper that isolates Git config and repository/object-store selectors, with restoration coverage.\\n- Document the shell-out inventory, replacement candidates, and compatibility constraints in `docs/development/git-cli-audit.md`.\\n\\n## Compatibility findings\\n\\nThe tests intentionally pin existing behavior, including behavior that a direct library substitution could change:\\n\\n- Branch validation expands `@{-1}` using checkout history.\\n- HEAD reads honor exported Git repository selectors, even with an explicit directory.\\n- An existing empty shallow file counts as shallow.\\n- `diff-tree --root` on a non-root commit still compares against its parent.\\n- Remote enumeration includes included config and worktree-local remotes.\\n- The native branch-display fallback reports unborn HEAD as detached.\\n\\nFollow-up implementation PRs should preserve these contracts or explicitly propose a behavior change, rather than silently adjusting the tests during migration.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- [x] `mise run check` — formatting, lint, unit/integration tests with race detection, deterministic canaries\\n- [x] Vogon: 56 scenarios passed\\n- [x] Roger Roger: 4 scenarios passed\\n- [x] `mise run lint` again after the final formatting pass and before push\\n\\nNo paid real-agent E2E tests were run.\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Test-only and documentation changes; no production Git operations or runtime behavior modified.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **native-Git characterization tests** and a **go-git migration audit** without changing production Git subprocess behavior.\\n> \\n> New parity tests compare CLI helpers to `git` across branch validation, `HeadSHA`, tree diffs, shallow detection, HEAD checkpoint reads, ref/remote reads, and tracking refs—covering SHA-1/SHA-256, reftable, packed refs, linked worktrees, cancellation, and error vs empty results. **`gitenv.IsolateRepository`** extends test isolation by clearing `GIT_DIR` / worktree / object-store env vars (with a restore test). **`docs/development/git-cli-audit.md`** inventories shell-out call sites, migration candidates, and six behaviors the tests intentionally pin (e.g. `@{-1}` expansion, empty shallow file, `GIT_DIR` overriding explicit paths).\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit aa231a1b8ef57cc5d28622589363293870d5e849. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2572/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2572/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2187\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2187/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2187/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2187/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2187\",\n              \"id\": 5298206561,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBkzgvQ\",\n              \"number\": 2187,\n              \"title\": \"Rename the rewind-point vocabulary to pending checkpoints\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-31T08:40:41Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-31T10:17:16Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-31T10:17:13Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2187\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2187\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2187.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2187.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-31T10:17:13Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1188\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n#2178 removed the rewind restore path, but the listing machinery that survived it kept the name — and what `checkpoint list --pending` returns is a pending checkpoint: one not yet condensed onto `entire/checkpoints/v1`. The rename is safe to do now precisely because the machine-readable surface was already clean: no JSON key, flag, or command path has ever contained \\\"rewind\\\", so this touches only Go identifiers, comments, and human-readable text.\\n\\n> Was stacked on #2186; that merged, and this PR now targets `main` with just the two rename commits.\\n\\n## Mapping\\n\\n| Old | New | Uses |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `RewindPoint` | `PendingCheckpoint` | 63 |\\n| `ResolveAgentForRewind` | `ResolveAgentForResume` | 19 |\\n| `GetRewindPoints` | `ListPendingCheckpoints` | 15 |\\n| `pendingRewindPointJSON` | `pendingCheckpointJSON` | 7 |\\n| `rewindPointLabel` | `pendingCheckpointLabel` | 4 |\\n| `pendingRewindPointsLimit` | `pendingCheckpointsLimit` | 4 |\\n| `GetLogsOnlyRewindPoints` | `ListLogsOnlyPendingCheckpoints` | 3 |\\n| `getImportedRewindPoints` | `getImportedPendingCheckpoints` | 3 |\\n| `RewindPoints` | `PendingCheckpoints` | 1 |\\n\\n119 uses across 20 files. `Get-` became `List-` because these return a slice and take a limit; `ResolveAgentForRewind` became `ForResume` because all three callers are resume commands (`newResumeCmd`, `newCheckpointResumeCmd`, `newTrailResumeCmd`).\\n\\nKept as-is per the brief: `RestoreLogsOnly`, `RestoredSession`, `SessionRestoreStatus`, `ClassifyTimestamps`, `ResolveLatestCheckpointFromMap`.\\n\\n**File moves** (`git mv`): `strategy/manual_commit_rewind.go` → `manual_commit_pending.go`, and `strategy/rewind_test.go` → `strategy/restore_logs_test.go`. The second is deliberately not `manual_commit_pending_test.go`: every test left in that file exercises the log-restore/resume half (`RestoreLogsOnly`, prompt preview, `FirstDisplayPrompt`, `ResolveAgentForResume`), while the listing half is tested in `manual_commit_test.go`.\\n\\nNo gopls on this machine, so renames went through word-boundary regex applied longest-name-first — so `GetRewindPoints` and `GetLogsOnlyRewindPoints` could not be shredded by the `RewindPoint` pass — with `go build ./...` gating every step. Word boundaries also skip test function names (`TestResolveAgentForRewind` has no boundary before `Resolve`), so those were renamed separately, along with the file-local `writeCommittedRewindCheckpoint` helper (now `writeCommittedCheckpoint` — it writes a *committed* checkpoint, not a pending one) and two test-agent fixture strings.\\n\\n## Explicitly unchanged\\n\\n- **The `--pending` flag**, every command path, and every alias. The diff's only flag line is its help *text*; no `Use:` or `Aliases:` line moved.\\n- **The JSON shape.** `grep '^[+-].*json:\\\"'` over the entire diff returns **nothing** — every field in `pendingCheckpointJSON` carries an explicit tag, so renaming the Go type cannot move a key. `checkpoint list --pending --json` stays byte-identical, and `TestPendingCheckpointJSON_MatchesRewindListContract` (which keeps its historical suffix) still passes.\\n- **CHANGELOG.md** — untouched.\\n- **`internal/remotehelper/transport/proxy.go`** — its \\\"rewind\\\" is HTTP request-body rewinding.\\n- **Every \\\"rewind\\\" that means moving a git ref backwards**: `fetch_rewind_protection_test.go` (filename included), `safely_advance_local_ref_test.go`, `checkpoint_remote_test.go`, the explain fetch tests.\\n- **Historical references**, which explain why the current shape is what it is: the `rewind --list` mentions in `checkpoint_list.go` / `checkpoint_group.go` (that bridge is *why* the JSON is frozen), the \\\"former interactive rewind picker\\\" whose format `pendingCheckpointLabel` inherited, and `deprecated_strings_test.go`'s never-advertise entry for `entire rewind`.\\n\\n## Strings and comments\\n\\n`checkpoint list --pending` no longer says \\\"No pending rewind points found.\\\" or \\\"Pending rewind points are created automatically…\\\"; the flag help, `Long` text, and two error paths follow. The first-turn context injection listed \\\"(enable, disable, clean, rewind, auth)\\\" as destructive commands — `entire rewind` has not existed since #1747, so a third of that warning pointed at nothing.\\n\\nThree comments were wrong about *mechanisms*, not just names, and were checked against the code rather than reworded:\\n\\n- `gitrepo/status.go` named \\\"review, rewind\\\" as the paths keeping the unbounded `Status` walk. The real two are `review_target.go` and `detectFileChangesUnbounded` (`session adopt`); both are now named.\\n- `manual_commit_session.go` attributed `FindSessionsForCommit` **and** `ClearSessionState` to \\\"the rewind reset command\\\". They belong to *different* commands — `entire clean` (clean.go:177) and `entire doctor` (doctor.go:406).\\n- `common.go`'s `DeleteBranchCLI` cited `HardResetWithProtection` as its sibling go-git v5 workaround. That function exists nowhere in the tree; the real one is `CheckoutBranch` in `git_operations.go`. (This was the follow-up flagged in #2178 and #2186.)\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `mise run fmt && mise run lint` — 0 issues, per commit.\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/...` — pass, per commit.\\n- `bash -n` on both edited shell scripts — clean.\\n- Full `mise run test:ci` — **exit 0**: unit + integration (`-race`) + canary 56/56 vogon and 4/4 roger-roger. The `TestCodexAppServerHooksList_*` failure known to hit macOS with codex installed did **not** fire.\\n\\n**String assertions updated** (the only ones that pin text this PR changes): `checkpoint_list_test.go` pinned \\\"No pending rewind points found.\\\" twice. Both are exact-match `require.Contains` calls, so nothing else could have drifted silently. `trail_injection_text_test.go` asserts only the prefix \\\"Leave setup and destructive commands\\\", so the context-injection edit leaves it passing. No canary test greps CLI output for \\\"rewind points\\\", and no E2E prompt wording changed.\\n\\n## Left for a follow-up, not done here\\n\\nComments in the **agent implementations** still describe rewind as live: `claudecode/claude.go:188`, `codex/codex.go:91`, `opencode/opencode.go:225-239`, and the two `security_contract_test.go` files. The brief enumerated the comment sites it had verified and these were not among them, so rather than guess at agent-side session-import mechanics I left them. One is a real finding worth its own PR: `claudecode.FindCheckpointUUID` carries a comment saying it \\\"served task checkpoint rewind… no production caller remains… should be removed\\\", i.e. dead exported API — a deletion, not a rename.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Rename-only refactor with preserved JSON contract and no behavior changes to checkpoint listing, resume, or restore-logs paths.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> After removing the `rewind` restore path, this PR renames the surviving listing vocabulary so it matches what **`checkpoint list --pending`** actually returns: checkpoints not yet condensed onto `entire/checkpoints/v1`.\\n> \\n> **API and types:** `RewindPoint` → `PendingCheckpoint`, `GetRewindPoints` → `ListPendingCheckpoints`, `GetLogsOnlyRewindPoints` → `ListLogsOnlyPendingCheckpoints`, and `ResolveAgentForRewind` → `ResolveAgentForResume` (resume/trail resume callers only). Strategy code moves from `manual_commit_rewind.go` to **`manual_commit_pending.go`**; log-restore tests move to **`restore_logs_test.go`**.\\n> \\n> **User-visible surface:** Help text and empty-state messages say “pending checkpoints” instead of “pending rewind points”; the test harness step is **`list-pending-checkpoints`**. **`--pending`**, command paths, and **`checkpoint list --pending --json`** field names are unchanged so scripts that parsed deprecated `rewind --list` keep working.\\n> \\n> **Docs and comments:** CLAUDE.md, architecture docs, and scattered comments now describe list/resume/log-restore instead of file rewind; a few stale references are corrected (e.g. agent context injection no longer lists `rewind`, `ProtectedDirs` describes checkpoint capture, and wrong command names for session cleanup helpers).\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit fcd4e868c5f0119f8511bd43dc44d7b75fb00bd4. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2187/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2187/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2590\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2590/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2590/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2590/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2590\",\n              \"id\": 5580210737,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABFFDyBg\",\n              \"number\": 2590,\n              \"title\": \"Use go-git for local commit and reference reads\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-25T08:17:43Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-25T21:12:10Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-25T21:12:08Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2590\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2590\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2590.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2590.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-25T21:12:08Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1424\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nFollow-up to the characterization tests in #2572 and literal branch validation in #2579. Move four local read paths to go-git on files-backed worktrees without explicit Git store selectors:\\n\\n- Read HEAD checkpoint trailers from the commit message, reusing the repository subsequently used for checkpoint lookup.\\n- Resolve metadata tracking refs and peel nested annotated tags to commits; ref existence alone is insufficient.\\n- Reuse `ResetSession`'s repository when checking whether a shadow branch survived native deletion. The pinned go-git version rereads packed refs on lookup; no reopen or upstream cache fix is needed.\\n- Iterate tracking refs using the exact `refs/remotes/<remote>/` prefix, skipping dangling symbolic refs and verifying target objects.\\n\\n## Compatibility boundaries\\n\\nThis is a normal-path migration, not wholesale subprocess removal. Retain native reads for explicit Git repository/object-store selectors and bare repositories; retain native commit reads for replacement objects and missing objects that Git can backfill. Repository discovery stays native. Detect reftable before opening its CLI-backed adapter and retain a single native command for each of these reads, avoiding adapter subprocess multiplication. Linked-worktree hooks export `GIT_DIR`, so they retain native reads too. The current storer has no prefix iterator; files-backed tracking-ref detection still enumerates all refs, an accepted cost for repositories with many loose checkpoint refs. Branch deletion and its native pre-check, arbitrary revision expressions, history counts, doctor reports, config, and tree diffs are unchanged. No user-visible behavior change is intended.\\n\\nDocument the boundaries in the Git safety reference and record migration progress in the audit. Extend shared fixture isolation to clear namespace and replacement-ref-base overrides consumed by the new compatibility gate.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- Existing native-Git characterization tests remain the oracle.\\n- Git Trace2 regression tests assert exactly one subprocess per migrated reftable read after root discovery, covering main and linked worktrees and nested metadata tags.\\n- Added local reads with Git removed from PATH after root resolution; index bytes and dirty working files remain unchanged.\\n- Added same-handle visibility of native packed-ref deletion, warmed-root-cache selector overrides, bare repositories, replacement commits, and missing-object regressions.\\n- Added commit-reader coverage for packed refs, linked worktrees, shared-clone alternates, nested tags, wrong object types, missing refs, cancellation, and SHA-1/SHA-256 reftable repositories.\\n- `mise run check` passed: formatting, lint, unit/integration tests, 56 Vogon scenarios, and 4 Roger Roger scenarios. No paid real-agent E2E tests run.\\n- Final pre-push `mise run lint` passed.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2590/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2590/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2668\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2668/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2668/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2668/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2668\",\n              \"id\": 5721530776,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABG0ypRA\",\n              \"number\": 2668,\n              \"title\": \"Keep a running agent's session off commits it did not make\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-06T01:37:55Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-20T20:56:03Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-20T20:56:01Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2668\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2668\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2668.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2668.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-20T20:56:00Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1490\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nWith no TTY (or `commit_linking=always`), `prepare-commit-msg` stamps the first ACTIVE session without checking what the commit contains, and `post-commit` condenses ACTIVE and live-task sessions without an overlap check. Both shortcuts assume the commit is the agent's own.\\n\\nA commit from outside that agent breaks the assumption: a hookless agent, a script or queue job, or a GUI client committing an unrelated file while Claude Code is mid-turn in the same worktree. That commit gets Claude's `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer and Claude's transcript. Reproduced on `main` with the real binary and installed git hooks:\\n\\n| Commit | `main` | this PR |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Detached, no-TTY commit of an unrelated file while an agent is mid-turn | linked ✗ | not linked ✓ |\\n| The agent's own no-TTY commit of a shell edit | linked ✓ | linked ✓ |\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nA session is **foreign** to a commit only on positive evidence:\\n- its recorded owner (`SessionState.Owner`, captured at turn start) is **alive**,\\n- it is **absent** from the commit hook's process ancestry, walked all the way to init (`Ancestry.Excludes`), and\\n- no agent's caller-session variable (`CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`, `CURSOR_CONVERSATION_ID`, …) names it.\\n\\nA foreign session skips the fast path, links only on staged-file overlap (task records and transcript growth don't count), and condenses only on committed-file overlap. For an IDLE session, a running subagent whose transcript names a staged or committed file counts as that overlap, on both the trailer and the condensation side. For an ACTIVE session, the overlap also counts the live transcript's edits since the last condensation, so the current turn's files link from the second turn on (FilesTouched holds only earlier turn ends' files for an agent without file-edit hooks). A commit that does contain the session's files still links, and so does a commit containing a file the session's still-running subagent wrote (its transcript names the file before it reaches the parent's tracked files).\\n\\nEverything else keeps today's behaviour: no owner, a dead or unverifiable owner, a truncated walk, Windows. The ancestry snapshot now walks up to 64 levels (owner capture stays at 12) so deep hook chains (hook managers, pre-commit, shims) can still be judged.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- `proclive`: walk completeness (init, limit, stat failure, PID-namespace cut-off) and `Excludes` guards (host, boot, start fingerprint, truncated walk).\\n- `strategy`: provenance verdicts for a live non-ancestor, an ancestor, no owner, dead owner, empty host, and a caller-session claim; each commit hook walks the ancestry once and every identity decision shares it.\\n- Integration (14): unrelated file not linked; session's file still linked; in-flight task record doesn't link; `commit_linking=always` at a terminal; caller-session claim keeps the fast path; the agent's own no-TTY commit still links; post-commit doesn't condense a foreign session into another agent's commit; a foreign parent whose running subagent wrote a committed file is still condensed, and gets the trailer when it is the only session; a running subagent does not link a file it did not write; a second turn's mid-turn edit links (no-TTY and `commit_linking=always` at a terminal) and its checkpoint holds the session, while an unrelated file still doesn't; an edit already in an earlier checkpoint (carry-forward after a partial commit) doesn't link a later commit of the same path.\\n- `mise run check` passes.\\n\\nDiff: +782/−78 across 12 files.\\n\\n## Risk\\n\\nChecked against real IDE-hosted agents on macOS, with this branch's binary in a scratch repo:\\n\\n| Agent | Hooks run under | Agent's commands run under | Agent's own no-TTY commit |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Claude Code in VS Code | the extension's `claude` process | the same `claude` process | linked (owner is an ancestor; `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` also set) |\\n| Cursor agent | the extension host | a separate, sandboxed process (owner not found in the commit's ancestry) | linked through `CURSOR_CONVERSATION_ID`, which Cursor sets on the agent's commands |\\n| Antigravity `agy` 1.4.3 (`-p`) | `agy` | a shell under the same `agy` process | linked (owner is an ancestor; no caller-session variable needed) |\\n| Factory Droid 0.243.0 (`droid exec`) | `droid` | a shell under the same `droid` process | linked (owner is an ancestor; no caller-session variable needed) |\\n\\nGemini CLI support has been removed. External agents were not probed: one that runs its commands outside its hook process and sets no caller-session variable falls back to content detection for its own mid-turn commits. The Antigravity row covers headless `agy -p`; an agent run from the Antigravity editor was not probed.\\n\\nCommits typed into either IDE's integrated terminal carry neither, so they count as foreign to a live session there, which is the intended behaviour. An IDE agent that runs commands outside its hook process *and* sets no caller-session variable would lose the fast path for its own commits and fall back to content detection. On Windows the ancestry check doesn't run, so behaviour matches `main`.\\n\\n`commit_linking=always`: a person's terminal commit while an agent is mid-turn used to take the fast path; it now links only on overlap with the session's files (tracked files plus the live transcript's edits), so a file the agent changed only through a shell command (`sed -i`, a codegen script) doesn't link when a person commits it mid-turn.\\n\\nDetached commits: a commit from a command the agent detached (`nohup`, `setsid`, a background job whose shell exited) is reparented, so its own session looks foreign. Agents that export a caller-session variable (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Copilot CLI, Pi) still link through it; the others fall back to content detection. Rare, and it errs toward not linking.\\n\\n## Follow-ups\\n\\n- An ACTIVE foreign OpenCode parent's running subagent edit doesn't count yet: #2807 adds `hasFreshLiveTaskRecord` (any phase but ENDED); whichever of the two merges second should use it in this PR's two foreign checks. Claude is unaffected (an ACTIVE Claude parent's live transcript already includes its running subagents' edits).\\n- A process started from an agent's shell inherits that agent's caller-session variable, so a long-running worker launched from it still counts as the agent.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes commit-linking and condensation heuristics on a security-sensitive attribution path; conservative fallbacks preserve legacy behavior when ancestry cannot be proven, but IDE-hosted agents with mismatched owner vs hook ancestry may lose the fast path without caller-session env vars.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Stops mid-turn agent sessions from attaching to **commits the agent did not make** (hookless tools, scripts, GUI clients in the same worktree). The no-TTY / `commit_linking=always` fast path and post-commit ACTIVE/live-task shortcuts no longer treat every active session as the committer.\\n> \\n> **`commitProvenance`** marks a session **foreign** only with positive evidence: recorded `Owner` is alive, absent from the hook process ancestry all the way to init (`proclive.Ancestry.Excludes`), and not named by a caller-session env var (`CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`, etc.). Foreign sessions are dropped from the fast path, must show **staged-file overlap** to get a trailer (task records / transcript growth ignored), and post-commit condensation requires **committed-file overlap** instead of recency alone. Commits that actually include the session’s files still link; caller-session claims and ancestor owners keep today’s behavior.\\n> \\n> **`proclive`** adds a deeper ancestry walk (`maxAncestryDepth` 64), `walkAncestry` completeness, and `Excludes`/`Complete()` so “not an ancestor” is only asserted on a full walk. Docs and seven integration tests cover the matrix (unrelated file, session file, in-flight task, `always`, caller claim, own agent, post-commit isolation).\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 082d844f57b45130da96d53fb73e9d57adc22993. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2668/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2668/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2662\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2662/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2662/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2662/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2662\",\n              \"id\": 5716136527,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABGwdBGg\",\n              \"number\": 2662,\n              \"title\": \"Fix E2E regressions from busy-window attribution (#2651)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-05T17:12:46Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-09T08:50:30Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-09T08:50:30Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2662\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2662\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2662.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2662.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1486\\r\\n\\r\\nFixes the E2E failures on main after #2651:\\r\\n\\r\\n- `TestDirtyWorkingTree` and `TestMidTurnCommit_DifferentFilesThanPreviousTurn` (opencode, factoryai-droid, antigravity, cursor-cli) fail because a shadow branch is left behind after the commit.\\r\\n- `TestFactoryCommittedCheckpointExcludesPreExistingUntrackedFiles` (factoryai-droid): the commit gets no checkpoint.\\r\\n\\r\\n## 1. Fallback snapshot with no human baseline\\r\\n\\r\\n#2651 takes a fallback snapshot at turn end when the agent reported no file change (`SkipWhenUnchanged`). When the agent commits mid-turn, condensation deletes the shadow branch and clears the step count and the pending prompt diff. The turn-end snapshot then has no human diff for its window, so it can claim nothing as agent work. But pre-existing human dirt still differs from HEAD, so the snapshot was written and recreated a shadow branch that holds only human changes.\\r\\n\\r\\n`SaveStep` now skips a `SkipWhenUnchanged` snapshot when the session has no human baseline for the window (`humanDiffUnknown`: first step, no pending prompt diff). A snapshot that does have a pending prompt diff is still written, so a human edit made before a notification turn stays in the snapshot and is not counted twice at commit.\\r\\n\\r\\n## 2. Droid Worker stop takes no snapshot\\r\\n\\r\\nDroid runs a Worker as a session of its own. At the Worker's turn end, Entire records a completed task record on the parent session, with no snapshot. Since #2651, the parent's turn end can snapshot first (the test's untracked human file differs from HEAD), which creates a shadow branch without the Worker's file. At commit, the content overlap check requires a new file's content in the shadow tree, finds the Worker's file missing, and nothing condenses into the commit. Before #2651, there was no shadow branch at that point, so the check fell back to matching file names.\\r\\n\\r\\n`saveSubagentSessionTaskStep` now snapshots the parent's worktree before completing the record, as every other subagent stop does.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Tests\\r\\n\\r\\n- `TestSnapshot_MidTurnCommitWithHumanDirt_LeavesNoShadowBranch`: fails on main with `found [entire/a40814f-e3b0c4]`.\\r\\n- `TestFactoryDroidWorkerFileCommittedAfterParentSnapshot`: fails on main (the commit gets no trailer).\\r\\n- `TestFactoryDroidWorkerSessionBecomesTaskCheckpoint` asserted that no shadow branch exists after a Worker's turn. Its stated concern is shadow data written under the Worker's own session, so it now checks that no shadow branch carries the Worker's session metadata. Pointing the snapshot at the Worker's session makes it fail.\\r\\n- `mise run check`: lint is clean and integration tests pass. The only local failure is `TestOpenCodeSeedRepoPlantsDeps`, which needs the opencode deps bootstrap.\\r\\n- E2E on this branch before the droid fix (run 37348437798): everything passed except the droid test above.\\r\\n\\r\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\r\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2662/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2662/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2254\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2254/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2254/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2254/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2254\",\n              \"id\": 5335119781,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCCSMhQ\",\n              \"number\": 2254,\n              \"title\": \"refactor(checkpoint): use canonical Git metadata resolution (split part 2)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"id\": 34813274,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-03T09:59:53Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T15:15:20Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-04T15:15:20Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2254\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2254\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2254.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2254.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-04T15:15:20Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"> **Dependency:** This PR is built on #2241 and must not merge before it. Until #2241 lands, the Files changed view includes both #2241 and this checkpoint refactor. After #2241 merges, this branch will be rebased onto `main` and force-pushed so the PR contains only the checkpoint changes.\\n\\nFor the checkpoint-only change before that rebase, see the [comparison against the prerequisite branch](https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal/cli/compare/refactor-git-metadata-owner...refactor-checkpoint-metadata-resolution).\\n\\nRefs #2052 and #2190.\\n\\nPR #2190 established the broader direction: physical Git worktree metadata should have one canonical owner instead of being rediscovered independently across the CLI. PR #2241 introduces that owner in `gitrepo` and migrates repository opening. This PR follows it by moving the checkpoint subsystem onto the canonical metadata boundary and deleting checkpoint's duplicate traversal and caching implementation.\\n\\nThis is intended as an ownership refactor rather than a checkpoint behavior change. Queue placement, redaction caching, persistent refs, shadow refs, locking, and caller-specific failure policies remain intact.\\n\\n## Broader refactor\\n\\nCheckpoint operations need to know both the current worktree root and the repository's common Git directory. The common directory determines where repository-wide state such as the push queue and redaction cache belongs, particularly when a command runs from a linked worktree.\\n\\nBefore this change, checkpoint resolved that metadata itself:\\n\\n```text\\nCheckpoint operation\\n        │\\n        ▼\\ncheckpoint.resolveGitCommonDir\\n        │\\n        ├── git rev-parse --git-common-dir\\n        ├── package-level mutex\\n        └── per-worktree cache\\n```\\n\\nThat made checkpoint a second owner of the same physical Git facts already being consolidated under `gitrepo`. It also gave checkpoint its own cache lifecycle, cancellation-dependent behavior, and subprocess cost.\\n\\nAfter this change, checkpoint starts from the already-open repository and delegates physical metadata resolution to the canonical owner:\\n\\n```text\\nCheckpoint operation\\n        │\\n        ▼\\ncheckpoint.repositoryDirs\\n        │\\n        ▼\\ngitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata\\n        │\\n        ├── Worktree root\\n        ├── Per-worktree Git directory\\n        └── Common Git directory\\n```\\n\\nThe checkpoint package retains a small adapter because checkpoint callers commonly need the worktree root and common directory together. Interpretation of `.git`, `gitdir:`, `commondir`, and linked-worktree layout remains owned exclusively by `gitrepo`.\\n\\n## Why remove the checkpoint cache\\n\\nThe deleted cache was compensating for a Git subprocess rather than caching an expensive domain object. Once metadata resolution becomes rooted filesystem inspection, the cache no longer provides a useful ownership boundary.\\n\\nRemoving it has three useful consequences:\\n\\n- An already-open repository no longer launches `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` when constructing checkpoint state.\\n- Repairs to `.git` or `commondir` metadata are observed by the next operation instead of remaining hidden behind a stale cached result.\\n- Checkpoint no longer owns a mutex, cache-clearing API, or cancellation-dependent cache semantics for facts owned by `gitrepo`.\\n\\nThis also removes the checkpoint-specific resolver and its cache-only tests.\\n\\n## Checkpoint consumers moved to the canonical boundary\\n\\nThe migration covers the checkpoint paths that depend on repository metadata:\\n\\n- rooted push-queue construction\\n- redaction-cache placement\\n- persistent ref updates\\n- ref-store construction\\n- ephemeral checkpoint storage\\n- shadow-ref operations\\n- file-lock placement\\n\\nThese consumers now receive metadata from the same resolver used when opening the repository, without introducing a generic Git facade or moving checkpoint-specific policy into `gitrepo`.\\n\\n## Caller policy remains local\\n\\nThe canonical resolver reports metadata facts and errors; it does not decide whether an individual checkpoint feature is required or optional.\\n\\nThat distinction remains deliberate:\\n\\n- Push-queue construction fails closed because enqueueing against the wrong repository directory could lose or misdirect required work.\\n- Redaction caching fails open because caching is an optimization and transcript redaction can continue without it.\\n- Persistent ref updates retain their existing locking, compare-and-swap conflict handling, retry, and cancellation behavior.\\n- Linked worktrees continue sharing repository-wide state through the common Git directory.\\n- Shadow refs and ephemeral checkpoint data retain their existing worktree-specific placement.\\n\\n## Observable effect\\n\\nNo user-facing command or checkpoint format changes.\\n\\nThe operational effect is narrower:\\n\\n- checkpoint metadata lookup no longer launches a Git subprocess for an already-open repository\\n- checkpoint metadata is no longer memoized independently from the filesystem\\n- malformed metadata continues to follow each caller's existing required or optional failure policy\\n- ordinary repositories and linked worktrees retain their existing storage locations\\n\\nThe checkpoint-only layer relative to #2241 contains 16 files, with 139 additions and 211 deletions. Most additions are focused behavioral tests; the production change primarily removes duplicate traversal and cache machinery.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `mise run check`\\n  - formatting passed\\n  - lint passed with 0 issues\\n  - race-enabled unit and integration tests passed\\n  - Vogon canary passed 56/56\\n  - external deterministic canary passed 4/4\\n- Pre-PR `mise run lint` passed with 0 issues.\\n- `git diff upstream/main...HEAD --check` passed.\\n- A real linked-worktree fixture proves that its queue is stored in the main repository's common Git directory.\\n- A repair test proves that corrected metadata is observed immediately without clearing a cache.\\n- A Git Trace2 test proves that constructing a checkpoint queue from an already-open repository launches no metadata Git subprocess.\\n- The Trace2 positive control runs `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` and confirms that the subprocess detector records it.\\n- Tests preserve the required queue fail-closed and optional redaction-cache fail-open policies.\\n- The repository ownership guard no longer needs an exception for checkpoint metadata traversal.\\n- Source-built `entire status` passed.\\n- Source-built `entire doctor` reported metadata branches and hooks as healthy; it also found two pre-existing ended sessions awaiting condensation, unrelated to this diff.\\n\\nNo paid real-agent E2E tests were run.\\n\\n## Deliberately not included\\n\\nThis PR does not migrate session, strategy, hook, or other product consumers. Those areas have separate migrations so their error handling, fallback behavior, and performance-sensitive paths can be reviewed independently.\\n\\nIt also does not redesign checkpoint persistence, change ref formats, alter queue semantics, add cross-worktree writes, or replace genuine Git queries for refs, objects, configuration, and repository semantics.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2254/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2254/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1881\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1881/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1881/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1881/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1881\",\n              \"id\": 5028749237,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M74960h\",\n              \"number\": 1881,\n              \"title\": \"ci: add daily checkpoint-availability audit job\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"id\": 881031,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-07-31T10:29:09Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-10T13:11:15Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-27T09:22:50Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1881\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1881\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1881.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1881.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/959\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\n`entire trail resume 955` failed with **\\\"checkpoint not found\\\"**: checkpoint `01KYSGR4W1ZATZRW47J510EZGJ` was referenced by a commit trailer on `feat/repo-mirror-use` (reached `origin`), but its git-refs ref `refs/entire/checkpoints/GJ/01KYSGR4W1…` was **never pushed** to the checkpoint remote `entireio/cli-checkpoints`. The git-refs backend enqueues checkpoint refs for a best-effort pre-push drain; when that drain never runs or fails silently, the branch commit and the checkpoint ref diverge — and the gap is invisible until someone tries to resume.\\n\\nThis adds an **active** daily audit so orphaned checkpoints surface within 24h instead of at resume time.\\n\\n## What\\n\\n- **`scripts/checkpoint-audit.sh`** — walks every branch commit in a window (`--branches --remotes --since`), extracts `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers using git's own `%(trailers:…)` formatting (handles squash-merge multi-trailers), and diffs them against one `git ls-remote refs/entire/checkpoints/*`. The checkpoint ID is the ref leaf, so membership is a plain string-set lookup (works for ULID + legacy hex, no shard math).\\n  - Exit `0` all present · `1` missing (prints a context table) · `2` remote/setup error, so a broken remote never reads as \\\"0 missing\\\".\\n  - The checkpoint remote is public, so the audit needs **no credentials**. The script still honors `ENTIRE_CHECKPOINT_TOKEN` (RFC 7617 basic-header auth, matching the CLI) if the remote ever goes private.\\n- **`.github/workflows/checkpoint-audit.yml`** — daily 07:00 UTC cron + `workflow_dispatch`. Fails the job on missing checkpoints; reports via `GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY`, an uploaded artifact (`.md` + `.json`), and Slack. No App token / secrets needed (default `GITHUB_TOKEN` checkout + anonymous public fetch).\\n- **`mise.toml`** — `checkpoint:audit` task for local runs.\\n\\n## Report shape\\n\\n| Checkpoint | Commit | Author | Branch(es) | Date | Subject |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| `01KYSGR4W1ZATZRW47J510EZGJ` | `4e229c05` | Matthias Wenz | feat/repo-mirror-use | 2026-07-30T14:42:18+02:00 | feat(repo): add `entire repo mirror use`… |\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- **Positive**: 7-day window → exit 1, flagged the known-missing `01KYSGR4W1…` (and caught a second real orphan). Valid table + JSON. ~3s.\\n- **Remote-error**: bogus token → exit 2 (not 0).\\n- Anonymous `git ls-remote` against `cli-checkpoints` confirmed working with no credentials (repo is public).\\n- shellcheck / `mise run lint:shellcheck` / gofmt / gomod / YAML valid / all `uses:` SHA-pinned. No Go files touched.\\n\\n## Note\\n\\nSlack reuses the existing `E2E_SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` secret. Nothing else to provision.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1881/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1881/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2330\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2330/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2330/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2330/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2330\",\n              \"id\": 5396685764,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCy5pJA\",\n              \"number\": 2330,\n              \"title\": \"fix(strategy): compare redo content in the commit index\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"id\": 34813274,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-09T07:57:34Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-16T10:26:59Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-16T09:48:13Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2330\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2330\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2330.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2330.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-16T09:48:13Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"`git commit -a` and path-limited commits prepare the commit in a temporary `GIT_INDEX_FILE`. Redo detection (`inheritReplacedCommitsTrailers`) read staged paths from that index but blob IDs from go-git's ordinary index, so it compared the dropped commit with content that was not being committed. It also let git's rename detection hide staged deletions. The inherited `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer was wrong in both directions.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nAfter `git reset HEAD~1`:\\n\\n- Recommitting the dropped commit's exact content with `git commit -a`, `git commit -- <path>` or `git commit --amend -a` loses its trailer.\\n- Staging that content, rewriting a file, then committing with `-a` or `-- <path>` inherits the trailer for work the commit no longer contains.\\n- Deleting a file the dropped commit changed, while adding a similar file, also inherits the trailer, even with a plain `git add` and `git commit`. Git reports the pair as a rename, so the deletion is never compared.\\n\\nA plain `git add` followed by `git commit` was otherwise correct, because both indexes agree.\\n\\n## Cause\\n\\n`stagedBlobs` (`manual_commit_redo.go`, added in 6170bc161) listed paths with `getStagedFiles`, which runs `git diff --cached` and so honors `GIT_INDEX_FILE`. It then looked up each blob in `repo.Storer.Index()`, which reads `.git/index`. During `-a`, path-limited and `--amend -a` commits, those are different indexes.\\n\\n`git diff --cached` also detects renames, following the user's `diff.renames` (on by default). A rename's raw record carries only its destination path, so the source's staged deletion never reached the comparison.\\n\\nThe existing redo tests call `PrepareCommitMsg` directly, where no temporary index exists, so they could not see the difference.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n`getStagedChanges` reads paths and full blob IDs in one `git diff --cached --raw -z --no-abbrev` query, through the existing `parseStagedRaw` (which already skips submodule gitlinks and reports rename destinations). `getStagedFiles` and `stagedBlobs` both build on it, and the second index read is removed. The query deliberately keeps the hook environment: `GIT_INDEX_FILE` identifies the commit Git is preparing.\\n\\n`stagedBlobs` adds `--no-renames`, so a rename's source is compared as the staged deletion it is. `getStagedFiles` keeps reporting a rename's new path, so its squash and session-overlap callers do not change.\\n\\n`git-safety.md` moves the hook-environment rules into their own section and adds the `--no-renames` rule. `CLAUDE.md` now also covers hook queries of the hook's own refs, which the redo path runs.\\n\\n## How this PR changed\\n\\nThis PR originally fixed the same mismatch in session linking (`stagedFilesOverlapWithContent`). Upstream 389e855b6 then made new-file linking match by name, and prepare-commit-msg stopped reading the index there, so that change no longer applies and was dropped while syncing with `main`. The same mismatch had meanwhile appeared in redo detection, which this PR now fixes.\\n\\nI started this from the side finding in #2303 about `getStagedFiles`, which suggests stripping the hook environment. Doing that would read both paths and blob IDs from `.git/index`. They'd agree with each other and still miss what `git commit -a` or a path-limited commit records. This fix keeps `GIT_INDEX_FILE`, so the comparison reads the index Git is committing from.\\n\\nRelated: #2111. This does not fix its empty-tree corruption.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n`TestRedo_ComparesTheCommitIndex` runs real `git commit` through Entire's hooks, with the arguments the installed hooks pass. The dropped commit edits `a.txt` and `b.txt` and deletes `d.txt`.\\n\\nVerified RED against `main`:\\n\\n```text\\n--- FAIL: TestRedo_ComparesTheCommitIndex/all                []string(nil) does not contain \\\"a1b2c3d4e5f6\\\"\\n--- FAIL: TestRedo_ComparesTheCommitIndex/partial            []string(nil) does not contain \\\"a1b2c3d4e5f6\\\"\\n--- FAIL: TestRedo_ComparesTheCommitIndex/amend-all          []string(nil) does not contain \\\"a1b2c3d4e5f6\\\"\\n--- FAIL: TestRedo_ComparesTheCommitIndex/all-rewritten      []string{\\\"a1b2c3d4e5f6\\\"} should not contain \\\"a1b2c3d4e5f6\\\"\\n--- FAIL: TestRedo_ComparesTheCommitIndex/partial-rewritten  []string{\\\"a1b2c3d4e5f6\\\"} should not contain \\\"a1b2c3d4e5f6\\\"\\n--- FAIL: TestRedo_ComparesTheCommitIndex/renamed-deletion   []string{\\\"a1b2c3d4e5f6\\\"} should not contain \\\"a1b2c3d4e5f6\\\"\\n```\\n\\nWith the commit-index change alone, only `renamed-deletion` still fails; `--no-renames` fixes it. The `staged` case passes throughout, as a control. All seven pass with the fix. `TestParseStagedRaw` also asserts each path's blob ID and deletions.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] `TestRedo_ComparesTheCommitIndex` (7 cases), plus the existing redo and adversarial redo tests\\n- [x] `mise run lint`: 0 issues\\n- [x] `mise run check`: passes except `TestExternalCommand_SigintReachesPlugin`, which failed once under `-race` load (its plugin never reached the ready state) and passes 3/3 when run alone\\n- [ ] Paid real-agent E2E tests not run\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2330/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2330/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2771\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2771/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2771/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2771/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2771\",\n              \"id\": 5848810407,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABIZpYrg\",\n              \"number\": 2771,\n              \"title\": \"fix(runners): make trail-review report every issue in one pass\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"hiddeco\",\n                \"id\": 10063039,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDYzMDM5\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10063039?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hiddeco\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/hiddeco\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hiddeco/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hiddeco/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hiddeco/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hiddeco/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hiddeco/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hiddeco/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hiddeco/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hiddeco/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hiddeco/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-14T13:36:07Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-14T15:38:29Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-14T15:38:26Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2771\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2771\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2771.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2771.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-14T15:38:26Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1568\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\n## Why\\r\\n\\r\\nThe trail-review runner drip-feeds findings. Across the last 80 trails, 147 of 172 runs that produced findings produced exactly one. On five sampled trails, 66% of findings raised from round 2 onward flagged code that an earlier round had already reviewed. Each held-back finding costs a fix-and-push round, and fixes shaped around a partial list get reworked. One trail discarded its whole validation design after five fix commits.\\r\\n\\r\\nEntire does not cap, filter or dedup review comments, so the template is what holds findings back:\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Anti-padding rules.** Three of them (\\\"do not invent\\\", \\\"an empty result is correct and expected\\\", \\\"do not pad with borderline findings\\\"), plus \\\"if you cannot honestly assign a severity, do not raise it\\\". This is despite `confidence` already existing to carry uncertainty.\\r\\n- **\\\"Alternative designs\\\" are excluded.** A defect whose fix is structural can only be reported as one symptom.\\r\\n- **Previous findings are mislabelled.** `{{previous_findings}}` is called \\\"open findings\\\", but the server sends open, resolved and dismissed findings, each reduced to a keyword fingerprint. Combined with \\\"do not repeat … even if anchored on a nearby line\\\", this suppresses distinct issues that share vocabulary with an earlier one.\\r\\n- **No room for other sites.** \\\"Prefer a single changed line\\\" and \\\"1–3 short sentences\\\" leave nowhere to name the other sites of a defect.\\r\\n\\r\\n## What changes in the prompt\\r\\n\\r\\n- It states that the review runs on every push and the author fixes everything it reports, so each run reports every qualifying issue in one pass.\\r\\n- One test replaces the exclusion list and anti-padding rules: an issue qualifies when you can name a concrete input, state or sequence that makes the code behave wrongly. Structural causes, and unchanged code the branch now relies on, are in scope. Style, naming, docs, test coverage and cleanups that change no behaviour are not.\\r\\n- New review steps:\\r\\n  - Read the whole diff before commenting.\\r\\n  - Try to get past each guard the branch adds.\\r\\n  - Check what each write path does to existing data it wasn't asked to change.\\r\\n  - Find every site of each root cause.\\r\\n- One comment per root cause, listing its other sites. Defects that need different fixes get separate comments, and interacting fixes are called out.\\r\\n- Uncertainty goes in `confidence`, not into whether to report.\\r\\n- Previous findings are described as the server actually sends them:\\r\\n  - Open and dismissed findings are not raised again.\\r\\n  - An incomplete fix of a resolved finding is raised.\\r\\n  - A different defect on a nearby line is new.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe output contract is unchanged. In the high-risk surface list, two stale entries now match the current code. Shadow branches (removed in #2692), rewind/file restore and `reset --hard` are gone. Destructive git ops now lists checkout, forced checkout over a worktree, branch and ref deletion, and `entire clean`; the checkpoint entry names checkpoint refs and metadata.\\r\\n\\r\\nRelated changes:\\r\\n\\r\\n- `runnerdefaults/runners/trail-review.json` gets the same contract in condensed form.\\r\\n- The tune prompt (`buildTunePrompt`) now tells the tuner to keep this contract, so `entire runner tune` can't strip it back out. A test asserts the guideline is present.\\n- trail-review's `timeout_ms` goes from 15 to 25 minutes and `auto_stop_minutes` from 20 to 30, in both files. The server allows up to 30 minutes. Over three weeks of production runs, trail-review's median was 128s, p99 626s and the slowest success 882s, and two runs timed out (a timed-out run publishes nothing). In replays the one-pass template ran 1.4–3× longer than the old one, which would push that tail past 15 minutes.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Evidence\\r\\n\\r\\nI replayed early review heads of five trails (two authors' code) with Sonnet, the runner's model. Each template ran 4–5 times per head, and four of the trails were scored blind against the issues later rounds raised.\\r\\n\\r\\n| Per pass, revised vs current | Result |\\r\\n|---|---|\\r\\n| Later-round issues found | about 2× |\\r\\n| Other verified defects found | about 4× |\\r\\n| Previous findings repeated | none |\\r\\n| Wrong or speculative comments | 4 of 14 → 8 of 35: twice as many, but a smaller share of everything reported |\\r\\n\\r\\nMost later-round issues were found by neither template in a single pass. Expect fewer rounds, not one-round reviews.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Review follow-up\\n\\nEach review point was tested rather than adopted on trust. The checks: 16 more replay runs of a variant with the suggested prompt edits, re-scored blind against the existing runs; an 8-run test of the dismissed-finding clause; 6 runs of the real tune prompt; and production timings for 802 runs.\\n\\n| Suggestion | Result | Action |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Stale high-risk entries | Confirmed, and wider: rewind and `reset --hard` are gone too | Fixed |\\n| Time budget | Confirmed by production timings | Timeout raised |\\n| Say \\\"fixing or dismissing\\\" instead of \\\"fixes everything\\\" | No less noise (7 → 9 wrong comments) and fewer real findings (20 → 14) | Not changed |\\n| Re-raise a dismissal whose reason no longer holds | No effect: 0 of 4 runs re-raised a dismissal the code contradicts, with or without the clause | Not added |\\n| Check tuned templates after tuning | All 6 tune runs kept the full contract, with or without the guideline | Not added |\\n\\nThe review now reports more per pass, including more wrong comments (about 1 in 4 in replays). Many authors here are agents that will act on every finding, so the fix loop should show `confidence` and treat low-confidence findings as candidates to verify. That is a product change outside this prompt.\\n\\n## Notes\\r\\n\\r\\n- Runner configs are read from the default branch, so this takes effect after merge. Reviews on this PR still run with the old template.\\r\\n- `mise run check` fails on four date-pinned checkpoint preview tests (`TestCheckpointListPending_Preview*`, `TestPreviewNextCheckpoint`). They fail identically on `main` and are unrelated to this change.\\r\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2771/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2771/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2559\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2559/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2559/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2559/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2559\",\n              \"id\": 5542637979,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABEnXENg\",\n              \"number\": 2559,\n              \"title\": \"changelog 0.11.0\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-22T16:57:30Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-22T17:22:46Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-22T17:22:43Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2559\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2559\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2559.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2559.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-22T17:22:43Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1399\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Documentation-only changelog update; no runtime or build behavior changes in this diff.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds the **0.11.0** (2026-09-22) section to `CHANGELOG.md`, documenting the release in Keep a Changelog form rather than changing product code.\\n> \\n> The new entry summarizes **breaking changes** (control-plane command renames, broader `logout`, local-only `enable`, async mirrors only, `investigate` as a plugin), **features** (native `/et/` repo refs, mirror/clone/cluster UX, branch protection, auth and checkpoint-remote options, OpenCode summaries, provisioning waits, CI/E2E coverage), plus **behavior changes**, **bugfixes**, **security** fixes, **housekeeping**, and a contributor **Thanks** line—with PR links for each item.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 88ff02c74011a7a43d7a8b2bcaa93c695943b53b. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2559/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2559/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1926\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1926/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1926/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1926/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1926\",\n              \"id\": 5094168054,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M78PChT\",\n              \"number\": 1926,\n              \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): preserve concurrent persistent ref updates\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"ChetanReddyC\",\n                \"id\": 135294504,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOCBBuKA\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135294504?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/ChetanReddyC\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ChetanReddyC/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 3,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-07T21:40:35Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-31T19:09:13Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-31T19:09:13Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1926\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1926\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1926.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1926.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-31T19:09:12Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nFixes entireio/cli#1917.\\r\\n\\r\\nConcurrent checkpoint writers could read the same persistent ref tip, build<br>independent commits, and successfully update the ref without preserving both<br>mutations. The later update made the earlier completed data unreachable.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis follows the reproduction and guidance from entireio/cli#1920.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Changes\\r\\n\\r\\n* Add a cross-process lock scoped to each persistent ref.\\r\\n* Replace unconditional ref updates with native Git CAS using:<br>`git update-ref <ref> <new> <old>`.\\r\\n* Retry from a freshly read parent after CAS conflicts.\\r\\n* Rebuild the tree and commit on every retry.\\r\\n* Apply the same protection to:\\r\\n  * `git-branch` writes\\r\\n  * `git-refs` writes\\r\\n  * persistent-ref initialization\\r\\n  * git-branch to git-refs migration\\r\\n* Add focused CAS retry and cleanup tests.\\r\\n* Add the concurrent two-Stop-hook integration regression for both backends.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Testing\\r\\n\\r\\n* Soph's sequential/concurrent integration test passed for both<br>`git-branch` and `git-refs`.\\r\\n* Five-repeat stress run passed all 20 integration scenarios.\\r\\n* Focused checkpoint, migration, dispatch, and enqueue tests passed.\\r\\n* `go vet ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint` passed.\\r\\n* `gofmt -s` and `git diff --check` passed.\\r\\n* Rebased and verified against current `main`.\\r\\n* Added coverage proving that cancellation before CAS prevents the ref write.\\r\\n* Added coverage proving that successful CAS followed by cancellation still\\r\\n  enqueues the ref for push.\\r\\n* The sequential and concurrent #1920 scenarios pass for both `git-branch`\\r\\n  and `git-refs`, with both session updates preserved.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe full checkpoint package was also run. Seven existing Windows tests are<br>environment-sensitive because they access the real Git configuration or<br>AppData paths; the remaining package tests passed.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Notes\\r\\n\\r\\nThe implementation uses the same lock/CAS/retry pattern already used by the<br>shadow-branch store. The retry rebuilds from the new tip rather than reusing a<br>commit built from the stale parent.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Behavior and scope\\r\\n\\r\\n`casUpdateRef` uses `exec.CommandContext`, so cancellation before the CAS\\r\\nprevents `git update-ref` from running and the checkpoint ref is not written.\\r\\nThis is intentional: no partial checkpoint is stranded, `FullyCondensed`\\r\\nremains false, and PostCommit can retry the work later.\\r\\n\\r\\nCancellation after a successful CAS does not prevent push discovery. Enqueueing\\r\\nis context-free, so a ref that was successfully written is still recorded in\\r\\nthe push queue.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe lock-plus-CAS guarantee in this PR covers writers in the `checkpoint`\\r\\npackage. Pre-existing unconditional writes to the same refs from `strategy`\\r\\nremain follow-up scope.\\r\\n\\r\\nLock granularity differs by backend:\\r\\n\\r\\n* `git-refs` locks each checkpoint ref independently.\\r\\n* `git-branch` locks the shared v1 branch, so all checkpoint writes in a\\r\\n  repository are serialized.\\r\\n\\r\\nNote: This commit does not include an Entire-Checkpoint trailer because the implementation session was not captured by Entire.\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1926/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1926/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1905\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1905/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1905/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1905/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1905\",\n              \"id\": 5072597495,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M77JvUh\",\n              \"number\": 1905,\n              \"title\": \"feat(checkpoint): push checkpoint refs to one destination, and say where\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-05T15:36:51Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-07T10:36:55Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-07T10:36:52Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1905\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1905\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1905.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1905.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-07T10:36:52Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/979\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n> **Stacked on #1897** (base branch is `soph/multi-pushurl-tests`) — it carries the test helpers this builds on. Merge #1897 first; the diff here is then just the behavior change.\\n\\n## Why refs need one destination\\n\\nThe push-discovery queue records only a ref — `{\\\"ref\\\": …}`, no per-destination state — so *\\\"this ref is pushed\\\"* has to mean one place. git's fan-out across a remote's several push URLs can't provide that, in two distinct ways:\\n\\n1. **One failing URL fails the whole invocation**, so no ref unqueues even though other URLs took it. A dead mirror wedges the queue indefinitely, retried on every push.\\n2. **git's iteration isn't uniform.** A ref *rejection* returns and git carries on to later URLs; a *transport* failure (missing repo, auth, bad host) `die()`s. Verified:\\n\\n| First URL fails with… | Later URLs | Exit |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| non-fast-forward rejection | ✅ still pushed | 1 |\\n| unreachable / transport | ❌ **skipped entirely** | 128 |\\n\\nSo an unreachable mirror in *first* position meant nothing was pushed anywhere, while the same mirror last was harmless. Position silently decided the outcome.\\n\\n## What changes\\n\\nWhen a remote carries **more than one push URL**, checkpoint refs target its **first push URL** directly and the rest are skipped. The recovery fetch uses the same target, which also fixes a real mismatch: fan-out reconciled the remote's *fetch* url while pushing to its pushurls, so with a `pushurl` configured we were reconciling a repository nothing had been pushed to.\\n\\n**A single push URL keeps the remote NAME as the target**, so the overwhelmingly common topology is byte-identical to before — remote-tracking refs still update, output still says `origin`, no URL-keyed promisor config appears. Only multi-URL remotes are affected.\\n\\n**git-branch deliberately keeps fan-out.** Its v1 branch is a single shared ref with no queue to keep coherent, and mirroring it to every push URL is what people configure those remotes for (guarded by `..._Branch_RepeatedPushesKeepBothURLsInSync` in #1897). The backends therefore differ on multi-URL remotes; that's documented at the decision point in `refs_push_destination.go` rather than left to be discovered.\\n\\n### Trade, accepted deliberately\\n\\n- Checkpoint refs live in **exactly one repository**. Clone that repository and reads resolve (its url becomes the clone's fetch URL); clone a different mirror of the same code and they don't. `checkpoint_remote` remains the way to name a checkpoint repository explicitly.\\n- A first push URL that **rejects** a ref no longer lets later URLs receive it. git would have carried on; we stop. That's the price of a destination the queue can reason about.\\n\\n## Saying where — three surfaces\\n\\nSince the choice is otherwise invisible:\\n\\n- **pre-push** warns on stderr, naming the chosen URL and how many were skipped;\\n- **`entire enable`** notes it (both the first-time setup path and re-enable);\\n- **`entire doctor`** reports it under `Checkpoint destination: REVIEW`.\\n\\nAll three also cover the *other* ambiguous topology — **several remotes**, where checkpoints follow whichever remote you push to while `resume`/`explain` always read via `origin`, so checkpoints pushed elsewhere aren't found again. All are silent on an ordinary repo and whenever `checkpoint_remote` already pins a destination.\\n\\n## Two message fixes on the way past\\n\\n- The batch-rejection retry claimed **\\\"Some checkpoint refs diverged\\\"** for *every* failure, including an unreachable destination — pointing users at the wrong problem. It now says the push was rejected without asserting why.\\n- `printCheckpointRemoteHint` (\\\"a checkpoint remote is configured in Entire settings\\\") fired for any URL target, and would now fire for a URL we picked ourselves. Gated on an actual `checkpoint_remote`.\\n- `RedactURL` renders a plain filesystem path as `:///path/to/repo`; display now passes paths through and only redacts URL-shaped values.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nRefs tests from #1897 change meaning, so the diff shows the behavior flip:\\n\\n- `..._Refs_FanOutToBothPushURLs` → **`..._Refs_GoesToFirstPushURLOnly`**: first URL receives them, second does **not**, and they unqueue — the property the whole rule exists to enable.\\n- `..._Refs_UnreachableSecondPushURL_RefsStayQueued` → **`..._IsIgnored`**: a broken *later* mirror is now irrelevant; refs land and unqueue. Previously this topology wedged the queue forever.\\n- **New** `..._Refs_UnreachableFirstPushURL_ReachesNothing`: the `die()` case, previously uncovered.\\n- **New** `..._DestinationNoteSurfaces`: doctor reports both ambiguous topologies and stays silent on an ordinary repo.\\n\\n`mise run check` green (lint 0 issues, canary 59 + 4).\\n\\n## Note for reviewers\\n\\n`gitremote.GetPushURLs` is also added by #1898. Whichever lands first, the other rebases and the duplicate drops out — trivial either way.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes pre-push checkpoint sync for multi-push-URL remotes (git-refs only); wrong first URL or user expecting mirrors could miss checkpoints until they set checkpoint_remote.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Git-refs** checkpoint ref pushes no longer rely on git’s multi-URL fan-out. When a remote has **more than one push URL**, refs go to the **first push URL only** (single-URL remotes still push by remote name, unchanged). Recovery fetch uses the same target so push and reconcile stay aligned.\\n> \\n> Adds **`gitremote.GetPushURLs`** / **`remote.GetPushURLs`**, **`resolveRefsPushDestination`**, and **`remote_topology`** so **`entire doctor`** and **`entire enable`** explain ambiguous setups (multi-push-URL remotes and multiple remotes vs **origin** for reads). Pre-push stderr warns when extra push URLs are skipped; **`checkpoint_remote`** still pins an explicit repo and suppresses those notes.\\n> \\n> Also fixes misleading **“refs diverged”** retry messaging and limits **`printCheckpointRemoteHint`** to configured **`checkpoint_remote`**.\\n> \\n> Integration tests flip from fan-out expectations to first-URL-only behavior and add doctor coverage.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 7b9968b40463f86924571a36045906aaa8c0bb31. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1905/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1905/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2259\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2259/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2259/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2259/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2259\",\n              \"id\": 5337003121,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCD0DNQ\",\n              \"number\": 2259,\n              \"title\": \"fix(trailers): align the trailer writer with the final-block grammar\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"id\": 34813274,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-03T13:04:43Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-19T12:00:20Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-19T12:00:20Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2259\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2259\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2259.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2259.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes #2256. Stacked on #2253. Merge #2253 first, then this one.\\n\\n`AppendCheckpointTrailer` could write a trailer that neither `git interpret-trailers --parse` nor our own strict readers accept. `entire checkpoint attach` then printed a successful amend for linkage that did not exist.\\n\\n## The mismatch\\n\\nThe writer and the readers disagreed about one character, leading whitespace.\\n\\n`finalTrailerBlock` classifies raw lines on purpose. Git treats an indented line after a trailer as a continuation of that trailer's value, never as a new trailer. `appendTrailerLine` ran `strings.TrimSpace` before calling `IsTrailerLine`, so an indented `  Foo: bar` looked like a trailer to the writer and like body text to every reader.\\n\\nA message whose final paragraph is an indented pseudo-trailer got the new trailer joined onto that paragraph with no blank line above it. The result is one paragraph that is not a trailer block, and three things follow from it:\\n\\n- `attach` reported `Amended commit ... with Entire-Checkpoint: B`.\\n- `PostCommit` re-read the commit, found no trailer, and skipped linkage.\\n- `attach`'s own dedup check could not see the trailer either, so a second run appended another copy.\\n\\nThe commit ends up carrying trailer text that no consumer recognises, and the user is told the opposite.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\nI pulled `finalTrailerBlock`'s classification loop into a shared `isTrailerBlock(lines []string) bool`, and the writer now classifies the final non-comment paragraph with it, on raw lines. One grammar, two callers. A paragraph the writer will join has to be one the readers accept.\\n\\nJoining also requires a blank line between that paragraph and the content above it. That guard keeps a trailer-shaped subject line such as `fix: bug`, which `IsTrailerLine` matches for good reason, from having the trailer glued onto it. Sharing the grammar without the guard would fix the indented case and break the far more common one.\\n\\n`finalTrailerBlock` behaves exactly as before. `isTrailerBlock` returns false for an empty slice, which covers the old `start == end` guard, and the old loop could only reach its final return with `seenTrailer` already true, since a non-trailer first line always hit the `default` arm.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nWhole-message occurrences stay discovery candidates, so squash resume keeps working. Only final-block placement authorizes mutation, which is the boundary #2253 sets. `ParseCheckpoint` and `ParseAllCheckpoints` are untouched.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nI proved the red state by restoring the pre-fix `trailers.go` under the new tests. Five subtests fail, and all five pass with the fix:\\n\\n```\\n--- FAIL: TestAppendCheckpointTrailerRecognizedByFinalBlockParser/indented_pseudo-trailer_paragraph\\n--- FAIL: TestAppendCheckpointTrailerRecognizedByFinalBlockParser/tab-indented_pseudo-trailer_paragraph\\n--- FAIL: TestAppendCheckpointTrailer/indented_pseudo-trailer_paragraph_starts_a_new_block\\n--- FAIL: TestAppendCheckpointTrailer/tab-indented_pseudo-trailer_paragraph_starts_a_new_block\\n--- FAIL: TestAppendCheckpointTrailer/trailer_block_ending_in_a_continuation_line_is_joined\\n```\\n\\n`TestAppendCheckpointTrailerRecognizedByFinalBlockParser` is a writer to reader roundtrip. It asserts that every message the writer produces is one `finalTrailerBlock` reads the trailer back out of, which is the invariant that was missing rather than a restatement of the writer's own logic.\\n\\n| Check | Result |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `mise run fmt && mise run lint` | 0 issues across go, gofmt, mise, gomod, shellcheck; fmt rewrote nothing |\\n| `mise run test` | 10387 tests, 8 skipped, 0 failures |\\n| `mise run test:integration` | 562 tests, 3 skipped, 0 failures |\\n| `mise run test:e2e:canary` | vogon 56/56, roger-roger 4/4 |\\n\\nI did not run `mise run test:e2e`, which calls real agents and costs money.\\n\\n## Reading this diff before #2253 merges\\n\\nThe base branch lives on my fork, so GitHub cannot use it as this PR's base. Until #2253 merges, this PR shows all three commits and its diff includes #2253's changes. Review only the last commit, `fix(trailers): align the trailer writer with the final-block grammar`. Once #2253 lands, the diff collapses to that commit on its own.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2259/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2259/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2123\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2123/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2123/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2123/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2123\",\n              \"id\": 5246382154,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABA8QPQg\",\n              \"number\": 2123,\n              \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): avoid false empty result after truncated session scan\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"SparshM8\",\n                \"id\": 188700067,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOCz9Vow\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/188700067?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/SparshM8\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/SparshM8\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/SparshM8/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/SparshM8/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/SparshM8/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/SparshM8/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/SparshM8/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/SparshM8/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/SparshM8/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/SparshM8/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/SparshM8/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-25T13:25:04Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-25T15:45:53Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-25T15:45:52Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2123\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2123\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2123.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2123.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nFixes #2089.\\r\\n\\r\\n`checkpoint explain --session <id>` can report `checkpoints 0` and `No checkpoints found on this branch.` when the underlying checkpoint scan reaches its limit and the requested session is not present in the returned window. That output is a false negative: older checkpoints may exist but were not examined.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Root cause\\r\\n\\r\\n`getBranchCheckpoints` already returns a truncation signal, but the branch-view path discarded that state before applying the session filter. When filtering removed every checkpoint from the bounded result, the formatter could not distinguish “the branch has no checkpoints” from “no matching checkpoint was found in an incomplete scan.”\\r\\n\\r\\n## Changes\\r\\n\\r\\n* Preserve the scan-truncation state through the branch formatter.\\r\\n* Report that no matching checkpoint was found **in the scanned results** when a session-filtered scan is truncated.\\r\\n* Keep the existing empty-history message unchanged for genuinely non-truncated empty results.\\r\\n* Add a native regression test covering the truncated, zero-match-after-filter case.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis change does not alter checkpoint collection limits, JSON output, or the behavior of an unfiltered empty branch.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Validation\\r\\n\\r\\n* `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestFormatBranchCheckpoints|TestGetBranchCheckpoints_TruncationSignal|TestRunExplainBranchWithFilter'`\\r\\n* `go test ./cmd/entire/cli`\\r\\n* `git diff --check`\\r\\n\\r\\nBoth targeted and complete `cmd/entire/cli` package tests pass locally.\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2123/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2123/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2950\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2950/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2950/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2950/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2950\",\n              \"id\": 6083778009,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABLUZssQ\",\n              \"number\": 2950,\n              \"title\": \"fix(pi): keep forwarding lifecycle after /reload, /new and /resume; handle stdin EPIPE\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n                \"id\": 26940511,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI2OTQwNTEx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Beehtrix\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 4,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T17:08:38Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-11T08:04:34Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-11-10T22:41:38Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2950\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2950\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2950.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2950.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-11-10T22:41:38Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes #2930. Assigned to me; the approach follows Soph's comment on the issue.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nTwo bugs in the Pi extension template (`cmd/entire/cli/agent/pi/entire_extension.ts`, installed as `.pi/extensions/entire/index.ts`):\\n\\n1. **Lifecycle stops after `/reload`, `/new` and `/resume`.** The extension set `process.env.ENTIRE_PI_NESTED = \\\"1\\\"` on its own process. Pi builds a replacement extension instance in the same process on those commands. The replacement saw its predecessor's marker, treated itself as a nested subagent and returned before registering the lifecycle handlers. Entire stopped capturing the session until Pi restarted.\\n2. **An EPIPE on the hook's stdin can crash Pi.** `child.stdin?.end(...)` had no `error` listener. If `entire` is missing or exits before reading the payload, Node emits EPIPE asynchronously as a stream `error`, which neither the `try/catch` nor the `execFile` callback sees.\\n\\n## What\\n\\n- **Nested marker:** the marker now holds the PID of the top-level Pi that set it. An instance is nested only when the marker is set and names a different process. A nested Pi does not overwrite the marker. Entire's own hook subprocesses still inherit it, and the Go side still never reads it.\\n- Setting the marker only on spawned children isn't possible here: subagents are spawned by Pi's separate subagent extension (see #1936), which this extension can't hook.\\n- **stdin:** `child.stdin?.on(\\\"error\\\", () => {})` before `end()`.\\n- Regenerated the committed copy `.pi/extensions/entire/index.ts` so `TestCommittedHookConfigsAreCurrent` and `TestCommittedDogfoodExtensionIsCurrent` stay green. Updated the `piNestedEnvVar` comment in `hooks.go` and the Pi section of `docs/architecture/agent-guide.md`.\\n\\n## Known limitation\\n\\nA `\\\"1\\\"` written by an older version of the extension still counts as nested. If someone runs the old extension, upgrades Entire, then does `/reload`, the old code has already set `\\\"1\\\"` in that Pi process, so that one session is not captured until Pi restarts. The new code can't tell that leftover `\\\"1\\\"` from one inherited from an older parent Pi, because the old extension sets no other flag. It isn't a regression: with the old code every `/reload` stopped capture. It's documented in a code comment next to the check.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nNew `cmd/entire/cli/agent/pi/extension_runtime_test.go`, following the pattern of `opencode/plugin_tasks_test.go`. It loads the rendered extension under Node with a minimal stand-in for Pi's extension API and a fake `entire` on `PATH`, and skips if `node` is missing.\\n\\n- `TestExtension_ReplacementInstanceKeepsForwarding`: a second instance in the same process still forwards lifecycle hooks. Fails before the fix.\\n- `TestExtension_HookStdinErrorDoesNotCrash`: a fake `entire` that exits without reading a 4 MiB prompt doesn't crash the process. Failed 30 of 30 runs before the fix and passed 30 of 30 after.\\n- `TestExtension_NestedProcessSkipsLifecycle` and `TestExtension_MarkerFromOlderExtensionStillNests`: guard behavior #1936 already had. They pass before and after.\\n\\nThe tests also pass when the temp directory path contains a space.\\n\\n## Not verified\\n\\n- I did not run Pi itself. The tests assume Pi re-runs the extension factory in the same process on `/reload`, `/new` and `/resume`, as the issue describes, and that subagents inherit `process.env`.\\n- Pi 1.4.0's interactive mode (read, not run) catches uncaught exceptions, treats EPIPE as a dead terminal and exits with code 129, so an unhandled EPIPE still kills Pi. I did not run it.\\n- Type-checked both extension copies with `tsc --strict` against pi-coding-agent 1.4.0's types. The only error is already on main (`event.prompt` on `BeforeAgentStartEvent`); this change adds none.\\n- With mise: `mise run lint` passes; `mise run test` passes except two tests that also fail on unmodified main in my sandbox (TERM=dumb; DNS that resolves `.invalid`). `test:ci:core` (-race, integration), the integration package under -race, `test:e2e:canary`, `lint:licenses` and `test:release-origins` pass. Not run: Windows jobs, Codex app-server hook test.\\n- No `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers: Entire wasn't capturing the session this was written in.\\n- I ran this on a fork PR first (Greptile, Qodo, Kilo, Gitar, Codex). One real finding, a test path with spaces, was fixed. The remaining bot comments there are about upstream files carried in by an earlier stale diff.\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2950/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 1,\n                \"+1\": 1,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2950/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2288\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2288/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2288/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2288/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2288\",\n              \"id\": 5364326027,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCZPEog\",\n              \"number\": 2288,\n              \"title\": \"Audit UI\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"shadow2022-coder\",\n                \"id\": 124486930,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOB2uFEg\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124486930?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/shadow2022-coder\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/shadow2022-coder\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/shadow2022-coder/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/shadow2022-coder/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/shadow2022-coder/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/shadow2022-coder/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/shadow2022-coder/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/shadow2022-coder/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/shadow2022-coder/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/shadow2022-coder/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/shadow2022-coder/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 3,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-06T10:10:12Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-21T11:18:50Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-21T11:18:49Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2288\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2288\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2288.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2288.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": null,\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2288/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2288/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2646\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2646/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2646/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2646/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2646\",\n              \"id\": 5693360804,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABGecw7A\",\n              \"number\": 2646,\n              \"title\": \"Credit background subagent edits to the agent, not the user\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-03T20:43:08Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-05T15:13:23Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-05T15:13:23Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2646\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2646\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2646.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2646.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1471\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nA Claude Code subagent's lines are recorded as human lines. In agent-scenarios run `single-subagent/claude-code/2.1.288-2` (checkpoint `01M41NGSZKGXKNP8586A7ECP5Y`), a subagent wrote 37 lines and the checkpoint recorded `agent_lines: 0` with `user_lines_added: 37`. Codex records the same scenario correctly.\\n\\n## Cause\\n\\nThe subagent's own transcript is read correctly; the problem is timing. All Claude Code 2.1.288 Agent launches run in the background:\\n\\n1. The parent's turn ends while the subagent is still running, so the shadow snapshot lacks its edits.\\n2. The subagent finishes. Task completion records its files but writes no snapshot.\\n3. The task-notification fires `UserPromptSubmit` in the same millisecond as `SubagentStop`. Turn-start prompt attribution diffs the worktree against the stale snapshot and counts every line as user work (`manual_commit_attribution.go`, `CalculatePromptAttribution`).\\n4. The notification turn's Stop doesn't snapshot the file either: it was already in the worktree when that turn started, and the parent transcript's reference to the subagent is in an earlier turn.\\n\\nAt commit, agent lines are base→shadow minus the user lines on agent files, which comes out to 0. Codex is unaffected because its parent waits for the child inside the same turn.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nThe session state gets `PendingSubagentFiles`: files a subagent wrote that no shadow snapshot holds yet, each mapped to a git blob of the file's content when the subagent's edit was observed.\\n\\n- When a subagent completes, `CompleteTaskRecord` records the edits it made since its last scan, in the same state update that completes the record.\\n- Turn start does the same for still-running subagents before attribution runs. This covers the notification turn winning the race with `SubagentStop`.\\n- Turn-start prompt attribution measures user edits to a pending file from its observed content, not from the stale snapshot.\\n- A commit before the next snapshot does the same: the observed content stands in for the snapshot.\\n- Each task record keeps how far its subagent transcript has been scanned (`ScannedTranscriptLines`). Turn start and completion resume there, and turn end advances still-running subagents past what it snapshotted, so an edit already snapshotted isn't marked pending again.\\n- Turn end snapshots pending files, and `SaveStep` removes the ones it wrote. That includes a skipped step whose tree already holds them; that path keeps the pending prompt attribution for the next real step. Condensation drops the committed ones.\\n- Turn end also snapshots agent files whose user edits the turn's prompt attribution counted. Without this, an untracked agent file the turn didn't touch stays stale in the snapshot, and the commit counts the same user lines twice.\\n- If a baseline blob can't be read, the file's current content is used, which credits it all to the subagent rather than to the user.\\n\\n**Shell-written files.** The transcript analyzer sees only edit tool calls, and agent-scenarios found Bash-only subagents recorded with no files and their lines credited to the user. In local transcripts, 99% of subagents use Bash and 13% use edit tools. Claude Code now reports the time window of each Bash and edit call (`ToolCallWindowExtractor`, `agent/claudecode/tool_call_window.go`). A changed file the analyzer didn't name is the subagent's when its modification time falls inside one of the subagent's write-looking shell calls and inside no other agent's write-capable call in the session (`matchShellWrittenFiles`, `subagent_shell_files.go`). When calls overlap, the side whose calls name the file wins; otherwise the file is ambiguous: it counts as agent work for attribution but isn't listed on the task record. A file modified outside every agent tool call stays the user's. A prototype over 339 known subagent edits in local transcripts attributed none to the wrong agent; 88% matched one agent and 12% were ambiguous.\\n\\nRemaining imprecision: a user edit made between the subagent writing a file and Entire observing it (at completion, or at the next turn start for a still-running subagent) is credited to the subagent.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nEach test was written first and failed before its fix.\\n\\n`TestSubagentCheckpoints_BackgroundSubagentEdit_AttributedToAgent` covers:\\n\\n- `SubagentStop` before the notification turn, and after it.\\n- A commit before any later turn ends.\\n- Each of those both without and with an earlier parent snapshot. Without one, the stray lines fall into the pre-session baseline: `agent_lines: 0`, `human_added: 0`. With one, they show as human: `agent_lines: 1`, `human_added: 3`, matching the report.\\n\\nDisabling the turn-start transcript scan makes the \\\"notification turn first\\\" variants fail again, so both halves of the fix are covered. `TestSubagentCheckpoints_UserEditToSubagentFile_StaysHuman` covers the two review findings: user edits to a subagent's file after it finished (commit before the next turn, and after the notification turn), and while it's still running after its edit was snapshotted. Before the fix, all three credited the user's 2 lines to the agent. Ablations confirm the coverage: scanning from line 0 again fails the still-running variant, and using committed content again fails the commit-before-next-turn variant.\\n\\n`TestSubagentCheckpoints_BackgroundSubagentShellEdit_AttributedToAgent` covers a subagent that writes only through `printf … >`, plus a human file written while it runs, outside any agent call. It runs the subagent-stop-first, notification-turn-first and commit-before-the-next-turn variants. Before the matcher, all three recorded `agent_lines=1 human_added=5` and an empty `task.json` file list; disabling the matcher fails them again. Unit tests cover the extractor, the write heuristic and the matcher's overlap and tie-break rules.\\n\\nA unit test covers clearing pending files on a skipped `SaveStep`.\\n\\n`mise run lint` is clean. `mise run test:ci` passes except `TestOpenCodeSeedRepoPlantsDeps`, which fails the same way on `main` locally (it needs the e2e OpenCode bootstrap).\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2646/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2646/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2024\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2024/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2024/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2024/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2024\",\n              \"id\": 5175161073,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABAD3d8A\",\n              \"number\": 2024,\n              \"title\": \"feat(telemetry): missed-opportunity signal at checkpoint condensation\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"jdx\",\n                \"id\": 216188,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjE4OA==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216188?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jdx\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/jdx\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 8,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-17T20:29:29Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-24T21:53:31Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-24T21:53:30Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2024\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2024\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2024.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2024.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-24T21:53:30Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1071\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nRaw search-command counts can't say whether adoption is low — most sessions have nothing worth searching for. The denominator that makes the rate meaningful is **commits that landed files already carrying AI checkpoint history without the session ever consulting search**. Entire is the only tool that can compute it, and nothing emitted it.\\n\\nOn each successful post-commit condensation, emit `cli_commit_condensed`.\\n\\n## Properties\\n\\n| Property | Meaning |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `used_search` | Did the session invoke `entire search`? **Omitted** when not measurable — see below. |\\n| `used_search_source` | How `used_search` was determined: `command`, `subagent`, `none`, or `unsupported`. Always present. |\\n| `prior_ai_history` | Did any committed file appear in a recent commit carrying an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer? |\\n| `files_committed` | Count only. |\\n\\nThe event is named for the **commit**, not the checkpoint, because every property is commit-scoped: `files_committed` counts that commit's files, and `prior_ai_history` asks whether commits *before* this one touched them — which is what the probe's `--skip=1` is for. The commit-less condensation paths (doctor repair, session-end leftovers) deliberately emit nothing; rows without a commit would be indistinguishable from genuine misses and would inflate the denominator rather than complete it. Covering them would need a `trigger` discriminator plus nullable commit-scoped fields — a change to what the metric means, not a bug fix. The rationale is recorded at both call sites and on `newCommitCondensedSignal`.\\n\\n## Measuring `used_search`\\n\\nThe first version was a `bytes.Contains` probe. Review measured it at **18 false positives to 1 true positive** across 328 real transcripts, and the false positives are structural — Entire installs the artifacts that trip its own probe (`setup_search_skill.go` embeds `entire search --json` in the search skill's body; `investigate/prompt.go` injects it into every investigate prompt). The direction is what made it unusable: inflating `used_search` deflates the missed-opportunity rate, so the metric reads \\\"adoption is fine\\\" for the wrong reason.\\n\\nIt now matches a recorded tool invocation through a new built-in-only `ToolInvocationScanner` capability whose dispatcher returns `(found, supported)`:\\n\\n- **`command`** — a shell tool ran the command, matched in *command position* (start of command or after a shell separator, tolerating env assignments and a path prefix), so `cd sub && entire search x` matches while `grep -rn \\\"entire search\\\" cmd/` does not.\\n- **`subagent`** — the `entire-search` subagent was dispatched. This is the primary path, not a nicety: `setup_search_skill.go` installs search as a subagent, so the intended usage records an `Agent`/`Task` `tool_use` and runs the actual command in a *separate* subagent transcript that condensation never reads. A shell-only matcher would report \\\"did not search\\\" for exactly the sessions that adopted the feature.\\n- **`unsupported`** — no walker exists for this agent's transcript shape. `used_search` is then **omitted from the payload rather than sent as false**, so a consumer filtering `used_search = false` excludes unknowns instead of absorbing them; a missing PostHog property is not `false`. Claude Code is the only implementer today.\\n\\nConsumers should compute the rate over the measurable population:\\n\\n```sql\\nSELECT countIf(properties.prior_ai_history AND NOT properties.used_search) / count()\\nFROM events\\nWHERE event = 'cli_commit_condensed'\\n  AND properties.used_search_source != 'unsupported'\\n```\\n\\n## Privacy and cost\\n\\nContent-free by construction: booleans, a count, and the agent registry key — never file paths, prompts, or transcript content. Gated on `ENTIRE_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT` and then the opt-in telemetry setting **before any probe work**, so an opted-out user never pays for the git-log subprocess. The PostHog call is the existing detached-child path and never blocks the hook.\\n\\nBoth commit-scoped costs are memoized once per commit rather than per session: the settings load and the single `git log`, whose 13.8ms is almost entirely process spawn (8.7ms for `git --version` alone, and flat across a 60x range of output size). Both resolve on first use, so a commit where no session condenses pays nothing.\\n\\nThe `git log` record framing is NUL-anchored (`--format=%x00%H%n%B`). A commit message cannot contain NUL, so the record marker rests on nothing about message content — the previous `%x1e`/`%x1f` framing took its delimiters from the raw body, and a body containing either control character split a record early and dropped a real trailer, making `prior_ai_history` read false and suppressing a genuine miss.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nRegression coverage for each documented false-positive class (grep, commit message, tool output, assistant prose, the scaffolded skill body being written, the injected investigate prompt); unprobeable agents required to report `unsupported` when fed a transcript that *does* contain a real invocation; the hint/matcher case-sensitivity relationship pinned in both directions; the zero-value probe required not to present itself as a measurement; a commit body containing literal `\\\\x1e`/`\\\\x1f` still attributed; empty-message and merge commits pinned; and the probe and settings load asserted to run once across several sessions.\\n\\nVerified green: `mise run lint` 0 issues, all 64 packages, plus both canary suites (56 Vogon, 4 roger-roger).\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2024/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2024/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2244\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2244/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2244/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2244/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2244\",\n              \"id\": 5328198691,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABB8xkGA\",\n              \"number\": 2244,\n              \"title\": \"changelog 0.10.4\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-02T19:19:11Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-02T19:49:51Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-02T19:49:49Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2244\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2244\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2244.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2244.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-02T19:49:49Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1223\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Documentation-only changelog entry; no runtime or build behavior changes in this PR.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds the **0.10.4** (2026-09-02) section to `CHANGELOG.md`, documenting the release that landed across many prior PRs—not new product code in this diff.\\n> \\n> **Added** covers Entire-native `repo clone` shorthand, dispatch jurisdiction scoping (and cloud dispatch fix), real `--search-skill` installs, trail JSON `original_branch`, and opt-in async mirror creation.\\n> \\n> **Security** is a large block: `.entire` path hardening, `os.Root` filesystem containment, OAuth redirect handling, plugin PATH resolution, shadow-branch cleanup suffix rules, investigate fix path resolution, unsandboxed investigate notices, and `~/.config/entire` permissions.\\n> \\n> **Fixed** highlights concurrent checkpoint ref locking/CAS, review judge hangs on cancel, and checkpoint trailer debug logging.\\n> \\n> **Housekeeping** notes test isolation, removal of the dead rewind restore path (~1.8k lines), doc corrections, shellcheck on `scripts/`, E2E fixes, `tools/complexity`, and dependency bumps.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 8f4f1f8e196a72187bd1fca89eda722867cd0b5d. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2244/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2244/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2178\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2178/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2178/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2178/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2178\",\n              \"id\": 5292096909,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBgLHpw\",\n              \"number\": 2178,\n              \"title\": \"Remove the dead rewind restore path from the manual-commit strategy\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-30T12:37:09Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-31T07:07:56Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-31T07:07:53Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2178\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2178\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2178.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2178.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-31T07:07:53Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1183\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThe `rewind` commands were removed a while ago and nothing replaced them, so\\nthe code that writes checkpoint contents back over the worktree has had no\\ncaller outside its own tests ever since. CLAUDE.md has been describing it as\\n\\\"machinery pending removal\\\" in so many words. This is the removal.\\n\\n## What was removed\\n\\n| File | Declarations | LOC |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_rewind.go` | `Rewind`, `resetShadowBranchToCheckpoint`, `CanRewind`, `PreviewRewind` | 338 |\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/common.go` | `checkCanRewindWithWarning`, `countLines`, `computeDiffStats` | 191 |\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/strategy.go` | `RewindPreview` | 16 |\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/rewind_test.go` | 2 `PreviewRewind` tests, 3 `Rewind` execution tests | 563 |\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_test.go` | 3 `CanRewind` tests | 118 |\\n\\n1,226 lines deleted, no behaviour change: none of these were reachable from a\\ncommand.\\n\\n`countLines` and `computeDiffStats` had no caller but `checkCanRewindWithWarning`,\\nand they are in the same commit as it rather than a follow-up because leaving\\nthem for one commit fails the `unused` linter. `splitLines` next to them stays —\\n`content_overlap.go` uses it. The `countLines` in `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go` is\\na different function and is untouched.\\n\\nThere is no `Strategy` Go interface to update — CLAUDE.md describes one, but the\\nstrategy is a concrete `*ManualCommitStrategy`, so removing the methods was\\nenough.\\n\\n## What stays, and why\\n\\nEverything that reads a checkpoint without touching working files:\\n\\n- `GetRewindPoints` / `GetLogsOnlyRewindPoints` — feed `entire checkpoint list\\n  --pending` (`cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint_list.go:52,88`).\\n- `RestoreLogsOnly` and its helpers (`restoredPromptPreview`,\\n  `FirstDisplayPrompt`, `extractPromptsFromTranscriptBytes`,\\n  `ResolveAgentForRewind`, `readSessionPrompt`, `classifySessionsForRestore`,\\n  `ClassifyTimestamps`, `ResolveLatestCheckpointFromMap`) — feed `entire resume`\\n  and `entire trail resume`. It writes session logs into the agent's session\\n  directory, never worktree files, so it is not part of the restore path.\\n- The `RewindPoint`, `RestoredSession` and `SessionRestoreStatus` types and the\\n  \\\"rewind point\\\" vocabulary. Nothing was renamed.\\n\\n## How it was verified\\n\\nA whole-program VTA call graph over all 100 packages, rooted at every cobra\\ncommand constructor (155), every package initializer and every `main`, reports\\nzero reachable owners for `Rewind`, `PreviewRewind`, `CanRewind` and\\n`checkCanRewindWithWarning`, and real owners for everything in the keep list.\\nRe-running it after the removal shows the dead entries gone and the live ones\\nstill reachable:\\n\\n```\\nGetRewindPoints         -> 1 owners: newCheckpointListCmd\\nGetLogsOnlyRewindPoints -> 1 owners: newCheckpointListCmd\\nResolveAgentForRewind   -> 3 owners: newCheckpointResumeCmd, newResumeCmd, newTrailResumeCmd\\n```\\n\\nA repo-wide grep for the removed names now matches only the two doc paragraphs\\nthat say they are gone.\\n\\n## Docs\\n\\n`CLAUDE.md`: rewrote the \\\"`Rewind()` has no CLI surface\\\" paragraph to describe\\nthe current state rather than a pending decision, and fixed three places the\\nremoval made wrong — the `Strategy` bullet list, the `common.go` /\\n`manual_commit*.go` key-file descriptions, and the unbounded-`gitrepo.Status`\\nsentence, which listed rewind alongside review and `session adopt`.\\n`checkCanRewindWithWarning` was that third caller; review and `session adopt`\\nare now the only two. `AGENTS.md` is a symlink and is unchanged.\\n\\n`docs/architecture/sessions-and-checkpoints.md`: the storage table sold both\\ncheckpoint types on rewind, and the concurrent-sessions list referred to a\\n\\\"rewind UI\\\". `checkpoint-scenarios.md` needed nothing — it never mentions\\nrestoring.\\n\\n## Follow-ups noted, not done\\n\\n- `agent.Agent.ProtectedDirs()` is **not** orphaned by this — it still has 9\\n  reachable owners through `agent.AllProtectedDirs`, reached from\\n  `strategy.protectedDirs`, `checkpoint.isProtectedCheckpointPath` and\\n  `shouldIgnoreSessionTrackingPath`. No action needed.\\n- `HardResetWithProtection` no longer exists anywhere in the tree; the only\\n  trace is a stale cross-reference in the `DeleteBranchCLI` doc comment\\n  (`cmd/entire/cli/strategy/common.go`). Left alone to keep this PR to the\\n  strategy's restore path.\\n\\n## Test results\\n\\n| Command | Result |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `mise run fmt && mise run lint` | clean, 0 issues (run after fmt, on the formatted tree) |\\n| `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/... ./cmd/entire/cli/` | ok — strategy 62.1s, cli 88.4s |\\n| `mise run test:ci` (unit + integration `-race` + Vogon canary) | exit 0 — canary 56/56 vogon, 4/4 roger-roger |\\n\\nThe `TestCodexAppServerHooksList_*` failure that is known to hit macOS machines\\nwith codex installed did **not** occur on this run; both tests pass here\\n(`--- PASS` on each, run directly to confirm they were not silently skipped).\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Dead-code removal with no CLI entry points left; retained paths are read-only checkpoint listing and log restore only.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Removes the manual-commit strategy machinery that wrote checkpoint trees back onto the worktree after the `rewind` CLI commands were dropped. **`Rewind`**, **`PreviewRewind`**, **`CanRewind`**, shadow-branch reset on restore, and **`checkCanRewindWithWarning`** (plus its diff-stat helpers) are deleted from `manual_commit_rewind.go` and `common.go`; the **`RewindPreview`** type goes away from `strategy.go`, along with the associated tests (~1.2k lines).\\n> \\n> **Checkpoint listing and log-only resume are unchanged.** `GetRewindPoints` / `GetLogsOnlyRewindPoints` still power `checkpoint list --pending`; `RestoreLogsOnly` still copies transcripts into the agent session dir for `entire resume` / trail resume without touching tracked or untracked files.\\n> \\n> Docs now state explicitly that a “rewind point” is list/resume vocabulary, not file restore: `CLAUDE.md` (strategy interface, key files, unbounded `git status` call sites—rewind removed, review and `session adopt` remain) and `docs/architecture/sessions-and-checkpoints.md` (storage table and concurrent-session wording).\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 83d70c5c91618ae0f66b19a19345cf42fc395ea1. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2178/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2178/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1898\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1898/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1898/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1898/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1898\",\n              \"id\": 5064200820,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M76us78\",\n              \"number\": 1898,\n              \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): base checkpoint_remote ownership on origin, not the push target\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-04T19:35:29Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-07T11:22:57Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-07T11:22:54Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1898\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1898\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1898.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1898.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-07T11:22:54Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/971\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n> **Rebased onto `main` after #1905 merged.** Both PRs added `gitremote.GetPushURLs`; this one now consumes the merged copy, so `gitremote.go` drops out of the diff entirely (7 files → 6) and `remote.GetPushURL` delegates to the `remote.GetPushURLs` wrapper that came with #1905 rather than reaching past it to `gitremote` and re-wrapping the error. No behavior change from the rebase.\\n\\n## Background: what the fork check was for\\n\\n`checkpoint_remote` is normally committed in `.entire/settings.json`, so anyone who forks a project inherits it. `e8b589835` added \\\"fork detection\\\" to stop a contributor's session data being pushed into the upstream project's checkpoint repo — one they typically can't write to and shouldn't be writing to. Sound guard.\\n\\nIt was implemented by comparing **the push remote's** owner to the checkpoint repo's owner.\\n\\n## The problem\\n\\nThat conflates two different questions: *\\\"is this `checkpoint_remote` mine?\\\"* and *\\\"where is this particular push going?\\\"* Two consequences:\\n\\n- **Pushing to any differently-owned remote disables your own `checkpoint_remote`** — and the fallback then sends the checkpoints *to that remote*. A backup remote in another org, or a colleague's fork, receives your session transcripts instead of your configured checkpoint repo. Exactly the opposite of what the explicit setting asked for.\\n- **It has no single answer for a remote with several push URLs.** git allows `remote.<name>.pushurl` to repeat and pushes to all of them, so one boolean verdict has to cover a set of destinations that may have different owners. #1905 has since removed the ambiguity on the **git-refs** backend by sending checkpoint refs to the first push URL only; **git-branch** still fans out to every one of them, so the problem is real there.\\n\\nNothing in the suite pinned the intended reading: 16 of 18 `TestPushURL` cases use `pushRemote: \\\"origin\\\"`, and the two `\\\"upstream\\\"` cases exercise a *missing* remote rather than a differently-owned one. \\\"Push remote owner\\\" and \\\"origin owner\\\" were indistinguishable everywhere.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\nAsk the ownership question directly, from two local signals — no network, so the pre-push path stays free of SSH passphrase/security-key prompts:\\n\\n1. A `checkpoint_remote` in `.entire/settings.local.json` is gitignored and per-clone, so it **cannot** have been inherited by cloning or forking. Always ours.\\n2. Otherwise compare the checkpoint repo's owner against **origin's** owner: *\\\"am I working in a repo owned by whoever owns the checkpoint repo?\\\"* A fork clone has origin `<fork>/app` against an upstream-owned checkpoint repo, and mismatches.\\n\\nThe push destination no longer enters the decision, which is what gives the multi-push-URL case a single answer.\\n\\n**Both existing fork tests pass unchanged** — they were written with `originURL` set to the fork (`https://github.com/fork/app.git`, `entire://.../gh/fork/app`), which is good evidence this is the reading that was intended all along.\\n\\nSignal 1 doubles as the escape hatch for a checkpoint repo legitimately owned by a different account or org than origin — a config the previous check had no way to express.\\n\\n3. If there is **no origin at all**, the push remote's URL is the only identity the repo has, so it is used instead — which is what the predecessor effectively did. A repo whose only remote is e.g. `upstream` must not lose its configured checkpoint remote just because nothing is named `origin`. In that topology there is no origin-vs-push-remote divergence to worry about: the repo has exactly one identity. (Added in the second commit, from an Entire trail finding — see below.)\\n\\n### What gets compared, case by case\\n\\n| Scenario | Identity used | `checkpoint_remote` | Verdict |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Normal repo | origin `acme/app` | `acme/checkpoints` | owners match → **honored** |\\n| Fork contributor, inherited committed setting | origin `fork/app` | `acme/checkpoints` | mismatch → **ignored**; checkpoints go to their own fork |\\n| Cross-org, set in `settings.local.json` | — (provenance short-circuit) | `myorg/checkpoints` | local-only → **honored** |\\n| Cross-org, committed in `settings.json` | origin `me/app` | `myorg/checkpoints` | mismatch → **ignored** — known limitation, use `settings.local.json` |\\n| Pushing to a `backup` remote in another org | origin `acme/app` | `acme/checkpoints` | origin decides → **honored** ← the misroute this PR fixes |\\n| No origin; only `upstream` = `acme/app` | push remote `acme/app` | `acme/checkpoints` | match → **honored** ← the trail-finding fix |\\n| Local-path origin `/tmp/repo` | unparseable | `acme/checkpoints` | owner undeterminable → **ignored** (prior behavior preserved) |\\n\\nThe property that matters: the last three rows no longer depend on *where this particular push is headed*, so the verdict is well-defined however many push URLs the remote carries.\\n\\n## Also in here\\n\\n- **Read the push remote's URL with `git remote get-url --push`** when deriving transport. A remote's push destination is `remote.<name>.pushurl` when set, so the plain `url` can name a different repository than the one being pushed to. Latent until now because `url == pushurl` in the common case. On a multi-URL remote this takes the **first** push URL — which post-#1905 is not an arbitrary tiebreak but the URL checkpoint refs actually land in, so transport and (origin-less) ownership are now derived from the destination itself.\\n- **The inherited case logs at Warn instead of Debug**, with the `settings.local.json` hint, so a user whose `checkpoint_remote` is being ignored can find out why.\\n\\n## Behavior changes\\n\\n| Scenario | Before | After |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Fork clone, inherited committed setting | ignored, checkpoints → your remote | unchanged |\\n| Own repo, push to a differently-owned remote | **ignored, checkpoints → that remote** | honored, checkpoints → checkpoint repo |\\n| `checkpoint_remote` in `settings.local.json`, origin owner differs | ignored | honored |\\n| Remote with a `pushurl` in another repo | transport from the fetch url | transport from the push url |\\n| Origin absent, same-owner push remote | honored (push-remote owner) | honored (push-remote owner) |\\n| Non-forge URL, e.g. a local path (owner undeterminable) | fallback | unchanged |\\n\\n## Second commit: Entire trail finding (trail 971, medium)\\n\\nThe review agent caught that the first commit regressed one topology: keying ownership on origin made a **missing** origin read as \\\"inherited\\\", so a repo whose only remote is `upstream` — with an owner matching the checkpoint repo — silently lost checkpoint-remote routing, where the predecessor would have used it. Origin still decides when it exists; only its complete absence falls back to the push remote as identity. The check moved after the push-remote read (needed for transport anyway) to have that URL available, and the reason strings now name which remote was consulted.\\n\\nFinding resolved on the trail with the fixing commit.\\n\\n## Known interaction with #1893\\n\\n#1893 adds a precedence tier that elects **the current branch's push destination** as the checkpoint sync remote, specifically to support the *clone-upstream, add-your-fork* topology (origin is a base repo you can't push; the branch tracks your fork). This PR's ownership rule assumes the opposite — that origin is *yours*.\\n\\nWhere they meet, the fork guard stops firing:\\n\\n| | origin | `checkpoint_remote` (committed) | verdict |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Fork clone (assumed here) | `fork/app` | `acme/checkpoints` | mismatch → ignored ✅ |\\n| Clone upstream + add fork (#1893's case) | `acme/app` | `acme/checkpoints` | **match → honored** ⚠️ |\\n\\nIn the second row a contributor's transcripts target the upstream project's checkpoint repo. The usual outcome is an auth failure and checkpoints never leaving the machine; where they do have write access, the session data lands upstream — the thing `e8b589835` exists to prevent.\\n\\nThis is the same class as the trail finding fixed in the second commit (*keying on origin assumes origin is yours*), and it only becomes reachable when #1893's tracking tier lands. Flagging it here; the resolution belongs to #1893, which is the PR that makes that topology first-class.\\n\\n## Not in scope\\n\\nDivergence recovery across multiple push URLs. #1905 settled it for **git-refs** by picking one destination; on **git-branch** the original constraint stands (fast-forward-only push plus one local ref cannot satisfy N independently diverged remotes with cherry-pick reconciliation), and the executable specs merged with #1897 document the behavior. It needs its own design.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- Three new `TestPushURL` cases, each verified to fail against the previous implementation: differently-owned push remote with matching origin; `settings.local.json` provenance; transport derived from the push URL. Reverting just the `GetPushURL` call makes the last one fail with `https://…` where `git@…` is expected.\\n- Two further `TestPushURL` cases for the no-origin fallback, also verified against the previous logic (the first reported exactly `enabled = false, want true`): no origin + same-owner push remote → honored; no origin + differently-owned push remote → still inherited.\\n- All pre-existing `TestPushURL` cases pass unchanged.\\n- After the rebase onto #1905: `mise run test:ci` green end to end (unit + integration `-race` + canary 4/4), `mise run lint` 0 issues. The multi-push-URL integration matrix #1905 brought in passes unchanged, which is the check that matters here — `remote.GetPushURL` and `resolveRefsPushDestination` now read the same first push URL.\\n- README and `docs/testing/git-remote-test-plan.md` (row B5) updated to describe ownership by origin, including the two cases that must *not* fall back.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1898/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1898/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2149\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2149/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2149/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2149/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2149\",\n              \"id\": 5270181674,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBPMRcg\",\n              \"number\": 2149,\n              \"title\": \"Changelog 0.10.3\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-27T17:09:46Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-27T17:15:55Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-27T17:15:54Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2149\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2149\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2149.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2149.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-27T17:15:54Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1161\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Documentation-only changelog update with no runtime or build changes in this diff.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds the **0.10.3** section to `CHANGELOG.md`, documenting the release rather than changing product code.\\n> \\n> The entry groups shipped work across **Added** (durable subagent data in committed checkpoints, process-identity commit linking, zombie-session sweep, configurable redaction engines, `entire doctor trace` aggregation, trail body `If-Match`, and opt-in telemetry), **Changed** (continuous search TUI, CLI/web search parity, clearer cluster login hints), **Security** (redacted `task_description`, betterleaks 1.8.x), and a long **Fixed** list—highlights include `--no-optional-locks` on internal `git status`, incremental transcript redaction for Stop-hook performance, bounded hook walks, condensation checkpoint-ID durability, `entire disable --uninstall` honesty, Cursor transcript attribution, partial-clone checkpoint reads, and `entire-cli/<version>` User-Agent on control-plane traffic. **Housekeeping** covers CI, lint behavior, dependency bumps, and dropping automatic gemini-cli E2E from main.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 803b2811ba43c4c9c100ea11af6d73394c0d6819. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2149/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2149/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2165\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2165/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2165/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2165/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2165\",\n              \"id\": 5283521121,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBZyazQ\",\n              \"number\": 2165,\n              \"title\": \"feat(tokens): breakdown-first token reports (B1)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T00:44:00Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-01T03:29:42Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-01T03:29:42Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2165\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2165\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2165.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2165.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1173\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n> **Stacked on #2155 (`tokens`).** The diff shows only this branch's commits; GitHub retargets to `main` when #2155 merges. Depends on #2155 for the `thinking_tokens` / `cache_creation_1h_tokens` / subagent `model` fields and the `token_transcript_start` window.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nRebuilds `entire session tokens`, `entire checkpoint tokens`, and `entire tokens profile` so every report leads with **where the tokens went** — tools (with a drill-down to the command, file or host), skills, subagents, context replay, assistant text — weighted by the provider's list-price ratios per call and per model, honest about legacy checkpoints, and closed by at most two recommendations written as plain sentences whose every figure appears in a table above them. Attribution is recomputed from the agent's own transcript for Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Gemini CLI and Pi; Cursor, Copilot CLI and Factory AI Droid stay totals-only and say so. Reference: `docs/architecture/token-reports.md` (written for the web team to mirror).\\n\\n## What landed\\n\\n- **`cmd/entire/cli/tokenreport`** — pure leaf package: price ratios per model family (verified 2026-08-28, dated in the code), per-call long-context tiers, known-TTL vs metadata pricing; attribution rules with a randomised conservation test; six calibrated recommendation causes (gates per agent from the 2026-08-28 grounding run); agent capability profiles; legacy-scope classification and dedupe; formatting.\\n- **`agent.TokenAttributor`** implemented by Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Gemini CLI and Pi; shared `types.TimeSpan`, `transcript.ToolDetail`/`ToolInputFromMap`/`ToolInputFromJSON`. Every attributor carries a window-independence test — which caught a real slice-boundary loss in the first two implementations before any report shipped.\\n- **`SessionReader.ReadTaskRecords`** across all six store implementers, so subagent rows get their type, usage and timing from the committed `tasks/<id>/task.json` records.\\n- **Commands** rebuilt as load → `tokenreport` → render on one shared renderer: `checkpoint tokens` (slices at `token_transcript_start`, never `checkpoint_transcript_start`; legacy checkpoints labelled and priced honestly; `--compare` gains per-class cost shares), `session tokens` (live transcript incl. subagent transcripts; `Duration: … so far`), `tokens profile` (metadata only, grouped by agent, legacy rows deduped, no recommendations in this version), bare `entire tokens` (= current session), `entire labs` row and agent-help guidance.\\n- **Condensation** derives `session_metrics.duration_ms` from the session's timestamps for agents that report none.\\n- **Fixes found on the way:** Codex counted duplicate `token_count` events as API calls (~2×) and dropped `cache_write_input_tokens`; `addCheckpointTokenUsage` silently dropped thinking and 1h cache-write tokens when flattening subagent chains (now everything sums through `types.AddTokenUsage`, saturating).\\n\\n## Heads-ups for downstream consumers (entire-api / web)\\n\\n- `session_metrics.duration_ms` is now present (derived) on most new checkpoints, including imported sessions.\\n- `checkpoint tokens --json` is additive — `context{…}` kept, `id`/`message` kept on recommendations — except `severity`/`signals` are dropped and each `contributors[]` element is now `{kind,label,skill,model,usage,cost_share,source,details[]}` (was `{tokens,percent,confidence,signals}`). New keys: `source`, `duration_seconds`, `effort`, `cost`, `legacy`, `agent_reported_cost`, `recommendations[].kind/text/cause/cited`, `comparison.cost_share`.\\n- `session tokens --json`: same contributor/recommendation changes; `recommendations[].id` values are now the six causes (`no-token-data`, `context-replay-hotspot`, … are gone); `contributors` is always present; a session with no recorded usage prints \\\"Token usage: not recorded\\\" instead of a recommendation.\\n- `tokens profile --json` drops `usage_scope`, `missing_token_data`, the old `tokens` object, `signals`, `recommendations`; adds `collapsed`, `excluded_test_agents`, `agents[]`, `total_tokens`.\\n- Codex `api_calls` now counts distinct cumulative totals; `cache_write_input_tokens` → `cache_creation_tokens`.\\n\\n## Not in this PR (Plan B2)\\n\\nCross-session patterns and the `remember:` / `## Token habits` flow; `Pattern:` lines in `--agent-brief`; `Memory`/`Seen`/`Of` on recommendations stay empty. `session tokens` stays `listed: false` in agent-help until §8.7 is decided.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `mise run fmt` + `mise run lint` (0 issues) + `mise run test` (10,664 tests, 6 skipped) + `mise run test:integration` (558 tests, 3 skipped) at `bfc459d17` — all green; the e2e canary was not run locally (CLAUDE.md: E2E only on request), CI runs the canaries on every push.\\n- Real-checkpoint harness (20 committed checkpoints across five agents, `checkpoint tokens --json`): provider identity exact for all 8 Gemini/OpenCode reports; legacy transcript-derived subsets match 19/19; conservation Σ contributors == `tokens.*` exact (all seven classes + total) on six `token_usage_version: 2` checkpoints written by this branch's own writer into a temp repo (Claude Code ×2 with a subagent record, Pi, OpenCode, Gemini CLI, and a two-session Claude+Pi checkpoint). No checkpoint in the repo's history carries version 2 yet, so the legacy leg exercises the labelled-legacy path instead.\\n- Every task was implemented test-first and reviewed twice (spec compliance, then code quality) before landing.\\n\\n## Changelog (for release notes)\\n\\n### Changed\\n- `entire session tokens`, `entire checkpoint tokens` and `entire tokens profile` now lead with where the tokens went — tools, skills, subagents, context replay and assistant text, with drill-down details and estimated cost shares from the provider's list-price ratios — instead of five totals and boilerplate advice. Attribution is recomputed per API call from the agent's own transcript for Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Gemini CLI and Pi (Cursor, Copilot CLI and Factory AI Droid stay totals-only and say so); recommendations are at most two sentences whose every figure is visible in the tables above; legacy checkpoints are labelled and deduped rather than summed; and `session_metrics.duration_ms` is derived at condensation for agents that report none ([#2165](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2165))\\n\\n### Fixed\\n- Codex API-call counts no longer double-count duplicate `token_count` events, and `cache_write_input_tokens` is recorded ([#2165](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2165))\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2165/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2165/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2022\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2022/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2022/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2022/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2022\",\n              \"id\": 5175138360,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABAD2Tkg\",\n              \"number\": 2022,\n              \"title\": \"fix(search): drop the Checkpoints tab from the search TUI (ENT-1595)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"id\": 6415609,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTU2MDk=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6415609?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [\n                {\n                  \"login\": \"alishakawaguchi\",\n                  \"id\": 6415609,\n                  \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTU2MDk=\",\n                  \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6415609?v=4\",\n                  \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi\",\n                  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/alishakawaguchi\",\n                  \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/followers\",\n                  \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/following{/other_user}\",\n                  \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                  \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                  \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/subscriptions\",\n                  \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/orgs\",\n                  \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/repos\",\n                  \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/events{/privacy}\",\n                  \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/received_events\",\n                  \"type\": \"User\",\n                  \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                  \"site_admin\": false\n                }\n              ],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 3,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-17T20:26:15Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-18T17:50:42Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-18T17:50:40Z\",\n              \"assignee\": {\n                \"login\": \"alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"id\": 6415609,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTU2MDk=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6415609?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2022\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2022\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2022.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2022.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-18T17:50:40Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## What the checkpoint tab looked like before\\n\\nThe `entire search` / `entire checkpoint search` TUI had four type tabs — **Checkpoints, Sessions, Commits, Code** — with **Checkpoints as the default** selected tab. The CLI never sends a type filter to the search service; the backend returns all types and the TUI filtered the results client-side by `type == checkpoint` for that tab.\\n\\n## Why it's now stale\\n\\nENT-1595 made the search service **fold checkpoint hits into their owning sessions server-side** — a checkpoint now surfaces as its session, and the general search path no longer returns standalone checkpoint rows (they come back as `session` rows carrying a `matchedCheckpointId`). So the CLI's Checkpoints tab — the default — now always shows **zero results**.\\n\\nThe entire.io web frontend already dropped its Checkpoints tab (entire.io #3690); web search now shows sessions, commits, PRs, and repos.\\n\\n## What I changed\\n\\n- Removed the **Checkpoints** tab from the search TUI.\\n- Made **Sessions** the default results tab.\\n- Renumbered the type keys: `1` Sessions, `2` Commits, `3` Code (help hint updated `1-4` → `1-3`).\\n- Updated the affected TUI tests.\\n\\nKept scoped to the tab: the internal `typeFilterCheckpoints` value and the generic type-filter/pagination machinery remain (still used to classify any stray rows and exercised by tests). No changes to the search request, the non-interactive/accessible output, or the search service.\\n\\n## Product decision\\n\\n**Remove the tab entirely, matching the web (#3690) and the fold model** — rather than keeping it as an opt-in `filter_type=checkpoints` view. Rationale: the CLI has no code path that requests raw checkpoints (it never sends a type filter), and the web made the same call. Raw checkpoints stay reachable **by ID** via `entire checkpoint explain <id>`, which folded session rows already route to, so removing the browse tab strands nothing.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n`mise run fmt && mise run lint` clean; `mise run test` green (9158 tests). E2E not run locally (per repo guidance; CI runs it on isolated runners).\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> UI-only tab/default/key changes in the search TUI with matching test updates; no search API or auth changes.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Removes the **Checkpoints** type tab from the interactive `entire search` TUI and aligns it with server-side folding (ENT-1595) and the web UI: checkpoint hits show up as **Sessions**, so the old default tab was always empty.\\n> \\n> **Sessions** is now the default tab. Type shortcuts are **1** Sessions, **2** Commits, **3** Code (footer help **1-3**). Tab counts ignore checkpoints; the search placeholder mentions sessions/commits/code instead of checkpoints.\\n> \\n> Tests assert the Checkpoints label is gone, key bindings match the new layout, and still use `typeFilterCheckpoints` internally where they exercise generic list/pagination behavior.\\n> \\n> The diff also downgrades `@opencode-ai/plugin` in `.opencode/package-lock.json` (1.4.7 → 1.4.3), which looks unrelated to the search UI change.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit c44d1b23539baa76afe117080a2c18294444ff13. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2022/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2022/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2184\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2184/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2184/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2184/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2184\",\n              \"id\": 5295528031,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBitXRg\",\n              \"number\": 2184,\n              \"title\": \"Isolate test git invocations from host git config\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"toothbrush\",\n                \"id\": 423357,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMzM1Nw==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/423357?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/toothbrush\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 2,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-31T01:37:14Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-01T01:08:06Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-01T01:08:03Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2184\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2184\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2184.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2184.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-01T01:08:03Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1185\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\n## Why\\r\\n\\r\\n`TestGitStatusCallSitesPassNoOptionalLocks` failed on any machine with `color.ui = always` (ANSI escapes broke its output parse), and an audit found 54 more test call sites running git with the host's real config — hooks, colors, `init.defaultBranch`, gpgsign all leak into test repos.\\r\\n\\r\\nI went and tried to remove as many as possible of our hand-rolled Git env isolation instances.  Hopefully the next person's agent will copy the shared helper pattern.\\r\\n\\r\\n## What\\r\\n\\r\\n- New `cmd/entire/cli/testutil/gitenv` package: the single git-isolation implementation (`Isolated`, `IsolateProcess`, `IsolateMain`, `Run`, `EnvHermetic`). Dependency-free, so internal tests of packages testutil imports (gitrepo) can use it too.\\r\\n- Call sites keep the existing `testutil.GitIsolatedEnv` / `testutil.RunGit` / `testutil.IsolateGitConfigEnv` spelling — testutil delegates to gitenv, so the diff touches only the previously un-isolated call sites, not every caller.\\r\\n- Every bare `exec.Command(\\\"git\\\", …)` in test code now goes through `testutil.RunGit` or sets an isolated env (biggest win: `strategy/hooks_test.go`, −200 lines of exec boilerplate).\\r\\n- e2e's `TestMain` uses `gitenv.IsolateMain()`, gaining system-config and `GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS` isolation it previously lacked.\\r\\n- `gitrepo/reftable_test.go` drops its three hand-rolled env blocks; being an internal test of a package testutil imports, it calls `gitenv` directly.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Verification\\r\\n\\r\\nFull `mise run check` green (86 packages + vogon canary), on a machine with `color.ui = always` where the guard previously failed. Details in PR comment.\\r\\n\\r\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2184/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2184/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1991\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1991/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1991/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1991/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1991\",\n              \"id\": 5147518743,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7-44iQ\",\n              \"number\": 1991,\n              \"title\": \"feat(strategy): capture the checkpoint sync remote from tracked pushes\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-14T02:09:44Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-18T11:44:18Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-18T11:44:16Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1991\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1991\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1991.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1991.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-18T11:44:16Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1046\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nThe single-remote election (ENT-1451, v0.10.0) guesses the checkpoint sync destination from config at rest: `checkpoint_push_remote` -> `origin` -> sole -> first in `.git/config`. A user whose branches push a non-origin remote loses that election to a dormant origin, so every push is gated and checkpoints strand locally until they discover and hand-configure `checkpoint_push_remote`. The first user report landed the day after release (\\\"I have a bunch of repos where the git remote I push to isn't called origin. It looks like this means I no longer push checkpoints.\\\").\\n\\n#1893 fixed \\\"checkpoints sync where they shouldn't\\\" (transcript fan-out) but left \\\"checkpoints don't sync where they should\\\" as an opt-in config remedy. This PR is the second half.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\n**Capture**: during pre-push, a push whose target agrees with the branch's declared push destination (`branch.<name>.pushRemote` -> `remote.pushDefault` -> `branch.<name>.remote` — the config a bare `git push` resolves through) and differs from the current election persists that remote as the **captured election**, announces it on stderr, and the same push carries the checkpoints:\\n\\n```\\n[entire] Checkpoints now sync to \\\"fork\\\" — the remote your branch pushes to. Override with strategy_options.checkpoint_push_remote in .entire/settings.local.json.\\n```\\n\\nNew election precedence: explicit setting (fail-closed, unchanged) -> **captured** (fail-soft: a renamed/removed captured remote falls through instead of disabling sync) -> origin -> sole -> first.\\n\\n**Neither signal elects alone.** Declaration without a push is the config-at-rest bug that got the static tracking tier dropped pre-merge in #1893 (`74e239a9`: a `clone -o base` stranded every origin push — pinned by `TestCheckpointSyncRemote_TrackingAloneDoesNotReroute`); a push without declaration is the pre-#1893 transcript leak (a one-off `git push upstream` for a PR must never publish transcripts). Capture acts only on their intersection.\\n\\n**Phase-1 rules** (multi-remote set is the follow-up):\\n- At most one captured remote; **first capture sticks** — a mixed-habit repo whose branches push two remotes cannot flip the election per push.\\n- State is list-shaped from day one (`.git/entire-checkpoint-sync-remotes.json`, `{\\\"remotes\\\":[...]}`) so lifting the cap needs no migration.\\n- Explicit `checkpoint_push_remote` outranks and disables capture; dedicated `checkpoint_remote` URL mode and `push_sessions: false` never reach it.\\n- `entire status` renders the source: `fork (captured from your pushes)`; `--json` reports `checkpoint_sync_remote_source: \\\"captured\\\"`.\\n\\n## Test changes worth reviewer attention\\n\\nThe existing single-remote integration tests set up their gated remote with `push -u`, which under capture is a *declared* destination — pushing it now legitimately re-elects. Their setups reset tracking (`setBranchTrackingRemote`) so they keep pinning the undeclared-one-off shape, and `TestCheckpointSyncRemote_BranchTrackingDoesNotReroute` is split into its two surviving truths:\\n\\n- `TrackingAloneDoesNotReroute`: a tracked-but-never-pushed remote still never receives data and captures nothing (the `74e239a9` regression pin).\\n- `TrackedPushCapturesElection`: the fork topology end to end — capture fires, the same push delivers, origin is gated thereafter, status reports `captured`.\\n\\nUnit: captured-tier precedence table, capture predicate table (declaration precedence, already-elected no-op, first-capture-sticks, config disable, raw-URL), corrupt/missing state fail-soft.\\n\\n## Sequencing\\n\\n**Merge after #1956 -> #1951.** Reads still resolve through origin until that stack lands; merging capture first would route checkpoints to a remote other clones cannot read from. Nothing in this diff depends on the stack's code — the read chain picks up the captured election automatically once both exist.\\n\\nNot done here, deliberately: multi-remote set (needs per-remote push-queue state — ENT-1494's rescope), capture from pushed refspecs rather than HEAD's branch (hook doesn't plumb stdin refspecs; a miss is conservative), `entire clean` leaving the state file (parity with the push-queue file).\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n`mise run fmt` clean, `mise run lint` 0 issues, full unit suite (8,846), full integration suite (475), Vogon canary — all green.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> <sup>[Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) is generating a summary for commit c1cda853176388acbcc93681a17c0583617e536f. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1991/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1991/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2107\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2107/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2107/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2107/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2107\",\n              \"id\": 5232715480,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABAxXT3g\",\n              \"number\": 2107,\n              \"title\": \"perf: reuse redaction prefixes at condensation and Stop finalize\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-24T08:34:21Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-24T12:37:18Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-24T12:37:16Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2107\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2107\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2107.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2107.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-24T12:37:16Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1129\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nCloses the scope limit #2002 shipped with: prefix reuse covered only the shadow write, while post-commit condensation and the Stop finalize rewrite still re-redacted the whole session transcript on every checkpoint.\\n\\n## Why now\\n\\nA coworker hit **Codex's 30s Stop-hook timeout** on a 65MB rollout. The hook copied the transcript, then reread, sanitized, redacted and rewrote the whole thing — 30.203s, killed, leaving the checkpoint's final full-transcript rewrite incomplete. That is user-visible breakage rather than latency, so it jumped the queue ahead of the other items in #2091.\\n\\nHis numbers also say he already *has* #2002: 28.6s on ~65MB versus the 66.7s/70MB I measured pre-fix is roughly what the sharding buys, with none of the reuse — exactly the uncovered path.\\n\\nCondensation is the same shape, and after #2002 it is the largest remaining non-network cost in slow hook traces (**29.6%** of slow-trace time; `push_checkpoint_refs` is 69.7% but is network I/O).\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\nBoth paths now go through a new `checkpoint.RedactTranscriptIncremental`. Two design points are about correctness, not speed:\\n\\n**The redactor is a parameter, used for both the appended suffix and the whole-content fallback.** Previously the suffix was hardcoded to `RedactBlobBytes` while each caller picked its own fallback, so the two could diverge and splice a prefix produced by one pipeline onto a suffix produced by another. One parameter for both makes that unrepresentable.\\n\\n**Entries are namespaced by `TranscriptScope`**, because these paths do not redact the same bytes — the shadow write stores a *sanitized* transcript, condensation and finalize a *sanitized and image-externalized* one. Sharing one key would have been safe (the prefix hash rejects a mismatch) but would have missed on every checkpoint: a silently useless cache rather than a wrong one. The key also carries the session ID so concurrent sessions in one worktree never share an entry.\\n\\nThe per-subagent transcript opts out with a nil repo — written once per task, not appended across checkpoints.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nThe one that matters is byte-identity: incremental output equals a whole-transcript pass, across five appends. On its own that test would pass just as happily with the cache doing nothing, so there is a second test that counts the bytes handed to the redactor and asserts it sees **only the appended suffix**.\\n\\nAlso covered: scope isolation, session isolation, error propagation on both the full and the suffix path (a degraded scanner must fail the write, never ship a reused prefix alone), and that a single-JSON-value transcript (OpenCode's shape) is never cached for splicing.\\n\\n## One note on the diff\\n\\n`redactFinalizedTranscript` is extracted rather than inlined because eight added lines pushed `finalizeAllTurnCheckpoints` past the `maintidx` threshold. Extracting was the honest fix; a `nolint` would not have been.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `mise run lint` — 0 issues\\n- `mise run test:ci` — green, including `checkpoint` (328s) and `strategy` (111s), 56 vogon + 4 roger-roger canary\\n- Rebased onto main after #2106 unbroke the build\\n\\nRefs #2091.\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> <sup>[Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) is generating a summary for commit 95a7587984f33d13d42a8fdf06d67dbd423e84de. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2107/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2107/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2291\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2291/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2291/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2291/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2291\",\n              \"id\": 5368984828,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCcvasw\",\n              \"number\": 2291,\n              \"title\": \"perf: reduce transcript and repeated-secret scan allocations\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"id\": 257360244,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-07T01:34:35Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-08T10:32:20Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-08T10:32:18Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2291\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2291\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2291.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2291.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-08T10:32:18Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1241\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n- Search each distinct betterleaks finding value once per `String` call, avoiding duplicate whole-input searches and duplicate regions. For valid JSONL, this benefit is within one string field, such as a large tool result containing repeated request-log entries; equal values in separate fields or lines are not deduplicated together.\\n- Read transcript blobs directly into a size-reserved byte buffer instead of copying through `File.Contents()` strings; preallocate the chunk slice as well. The size hint covers both normal chunks and current unchunked shadow transcripts, up to a 1 GiB sanity ceiling. Above that, reads retain incremental growth. This ceiling is an allocation hint limit, not a read-size limit.\\n- Preserve transcript bytes, fallback behavior, and redaction output. Each duplicate finding previously generated the same unlabeled regions; eliminating duplicate work does not change output, so no `configFingerprintVersion` bump is needed. No API or configuration changes.\\n- Keep characterization coverage for base, legacy, present-empty, absent, and numerically ordered chunked transcripts. The present-empty result must remain non-nil because ephemeral reads use nil to select the legacy fallback. Use filename constants consistently.\\n\\n## Benchmarks\\n\\nOriginal before/after medians from five runs with `-benchtime=500ms -benchmem`, Go 1.26.6 on darwin/arm64 (Apple M5 Pro):\\n\\n| Workload | Time before → after | Allocated bytes before → after |\\n|---|---:|---:|\\n| 1,000 repeated credentials in one String call | 175.428 → 116.936 ms | 292.007 → 119.687 MB |\\n| 1 MiB transcript read | 380.988 → 69.679 µs | 6,291,204 → 1,057,024 |\\n| 8 MiB transcript read | 1,233.019 → 414.637 µs | 50,331,431 → 8,397,057 |\\n\\nThe existing ClaudeFull2 fixture was effectively unchanged (167.462 → 163.730 ms).\\n\\nSoph's review identified that the original 50 MB hint ceiling excluded current unchunked shadow transcripts. The new 64 MiB benchmark exercises that case. Fresh A/B medians comparing the previous PR implementation (`caf73c69b`) with the amendment, using the same new benchmark, Go 1.26.6, Apple M5 Pro, `GOMAXPROCS=4`, `-benchtime=20x -count=3 -benchmem`:\\n\\n| 64 MiB transcript | Previous PR | Amendment |\\n|---|---:|---:|\\n| Time | 6.299 ms | 2.952 ms |\\n| Allocated bytes | 268,435,280 | 67,117,320 |\\n| Allocations | 24 | 6 |\\n\\nThat is approximately 75% fewer allocated bytes. The 1 MiB and 8 MiB allocation counts remain unchanged. These benchmarks use real in-memory Git objects to isolate read/allocation costs; they are not end-to-end CLI speedup, peak-RSS, or production-frequency claims. The frequency of transcripts above 50 MB has not been measured here.\\n\\nBenchmark output assertions check correctness. Performance comparisons are manual against a base ref; CI does not enforce an allocation or timing baseline.\\n\\n```sh\\ngo test ./redact -run '^$' -bench '^BenchmarkRedactStringRepeatedSecret$/Occurrences1000$' -benchtime=500ms -count=5 -benchmem\\nGOMAXPROCS=4 go test ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint -run '^TestReadTranscriptFromTreeFormats$' -bench '^BenchmarkReadTranscriptFromTree$' -benchtime=20x -count=3 -benchmem\\n```\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n`agent.ReassembleJSONL` pre-sizing, image-asset reads, and direct legacy fallback reads remain separate follow-ups, as requested in review.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- [x] Same-benchmark A/B for 1 MiB, 8 MiB, and 64 MiB; three runs per side.\\n- [x] `TestReadTranscriptFromTreeFormats` and focused redaction checks.\\n- [x] `mise run check`: formatting, lint (0 issues), race-enabled unit/integration suite, and deterministic Vogon/Roger-Roger canaries; exit 0 in 241.96 seconds.\\n- [x] `golangci-lint config verify` separately passed. Its online schema fetch was blocked inside the otherwise network-restricted full-check run; the actual lint analysis passed there.\\n- [x] Independent read-only review and `git diff --check`.\\n\\nVogon reports 56/56 and Roger-Roger 4/4; raw Vogon output includes four expected agent-specific skips. Reassembly and image-read follow-ups were not implemented.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2291/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2291/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1951\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1951/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1951/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1951/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1951\",\n              \"id\": 5122202288,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M79nLIV\",\n              \"number\": 1951,\n              \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): reads follow the elected sync remote (ENCLI-255)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-11T16:12:07Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-18T08:28:05Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-18T08:28:02Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1951\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1951\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1951.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1951.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-18T08:28:02Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"> [!NOTE]\\n> **Rescoped 2026-08-11:** the git-refs discovery fix (a [#1771](<https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/1771>)-era gap independent of this PR's election work) was carved out into [#1956](<https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/1956>) and this PR is now **stacked on it** (base = `fix/checkpoint-refs-discovery`; merges after it, GitHub retargets to main automatically). This diff is now the read-chain work only. Its remaining scope — reads for elected≠origin setups (`checkpoint_push_remote` users, `git clone -o`, origin-less repos) — has no known users yet; if the team prefers, entireio/cli#1634's alternative resolution (document origin-only reads and warn) remains on the table.\\n\\n[https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1010](<https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1010>)\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nPR entireio/cli#1893 made checkpoint **writes** sync to one elected remote (`checkpoint_push_remote` → origin → sole → first). Every **read** path still hardcoded `origin`:\\n\\n* A user with `checkpoint_push_remote: \\\"upstream\\\"` (the supported answer for fork setups) writes checkpoints to upstream — then `resume`/`explain` fetch from origin and report them missing. This is the \\\"checkpoints that cannot be read back\\\" gap named in `74e239a9d`'s own doc comment.\\n* Repos with no `origin` at all failed every read.\\n* git-refs cross-machine discovery did nothing without a dedicated `checkpoint_remote` — a second machine never discovered refs-native checkpoints in the default setup.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\n**Writes confine; reads search.** Reads consult an ordered candidate chain — the elected sync remote first, then `origin` as a **read-only legacy tier** (pre-entireio/cli#1893 checkpoints live there) — via `strategy.CheckpointReadRemotes` / `CheckpointReadRemotesWithElection`:\\n\\n* **Fail-open for reads** (deliberate asymmetry): an election error yields `[origin]`. Write fail-closed prevents leaking; failing reads closed would only prevent *finding* data.\\n* **Per-operation semantics** everywhere (fetch targets, tracking-ref readers, blob hydration, checkpoint-policy reads): try candidates in order, not-found and transport errors both advance, if every candidate fails, transport uncertainty outranks absence: the first non-absence error is surfaced, and only all-positive misses report checkpoint not found.\\n* **Local-ref writers stay elected-remote-only**: `EnsurePrimaryRef`, the metadata-fetch advance, `promoteRemoteTrackingPrimary`, and the local policy-ref update never act on the legacy tier — a stale origin feeding `SafelyAdvanceLocalRef` (which replays commits on divergence) is the entireio/cli#1374-class hazard. Keyed on the explicit election result, never the chain's first entry (which can be the fail-open origin). Pinned by `TestPromoteRemoteTrackingPrimary_FailOpenChainNeverPromotes`, `TestEnsurePrimaryRef_StaleOriginTracking*`, and an end-to-end confinement scenario; reviewers mutation-tested these pins.\\n* **git-refs discovery without a dedicated store**: `checkpoint list`/branch explain now ls-remote every read candidate for `refs/entire/*` and merge the listings (union — pre-entireio/cli#1893 refs landed on whichever remote the hook fired for, so disjoint legacy refs are realistic and first-non-empty would shadow one side). Best-effort: per-candidate failures don't block the rest.\\n* The remoteless \\\"checkpoint absent\\\" classification keeps its positive-evidence requirements (successful empty remote listing, live ctx, readable settings without a `checkpoint_remote` key).\\n* Non-goals preserved: dedicated `checkpoint_remote` URL derivation unchanged; repo-identity and code-branch origin uses untouched; hook-context ref fetchers deliberately single-target (write-side).\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n* Unit: resolver chain table (incl. fail-open, tracking-independence pin per `74e239a9d`'s contract), per-site candidate iteration, four-condition absence guard, confinement pins (mutation-verified in review).\\n* Integration: 6 scenarios on both backends — configured read-back, legacy-origin fallback (union + no local-primary recreation), upstream-only repo, cross-machine discovery on a pristine clone, remoteless absence, end-to-end confinement with an unreachable elected remote.\\n* Full `mise run check` green (fmt, lint, unit, integration `-race`, Vogon canary).\\n\\n## Notes for reviewers\\n\\n* **Known cosmetic residual:** `attach`'s pasteable fetch hint can name origin while the data lives on the elected remote (the fetch itself iterates the chain and works); documented in-code, candidate for a follow-up.\\n* **This removes the read-back objection recorded in** `74e239a9d` (which dropped the zero-config tracking election tier). The remaining objection there — silent no-op on pushes to other remotes — still stands; whether to revisit the tracking tier is a product call, now unblocked from the read side.\\n* Unblocks the B1–B7 multi-remote tests of `docs/testing/git-remote-test-plan.md` (decision D-1 fully resolved: writes confine to the elected remote, reads search elected-then-origin).\\n\\nCloses entireio/cli#1634 (entireio/cli#1634).\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](<https://claude.com/claude-code>)\\n\\n## Added after review (Stefan)\\n\\nTwo commits landed on this branch after the original review round. Flagging them\\nexplicitly so the diff's extra ~17 files are accounted for.\\n\\n### `perf(checkpoint): bound the read chain and stop re-electing per call`\\n\\nFixes two costs the read-candidate chain above introduced, both measured against\\n`origin/main` with a PATH-shimmed `git` counting subprocesses.\\n\\n**Unbounded worst case.** Per-candidate budgets replaced single shared ones — a\\nreal fix, since one shared budget let a hung leader starve the legacy origin tier\\n— but nothing bounded the total, and these read paths have no outer deadline\\n(`entire resume` sets none; `main()` uses `context.WithCancel`, not\\n`WithTimeout`). `fetchBlobsByHash` lost the most: it used to sit inside one\\n2-minute budget that also covered its fallbacks, and per-target budgets left\\nthose on the caller's uncapped context.\\n\\n`ReadChainBudget` now wraps all three chains — ref hydration, the metadata branch\\nchain, and blob hydration including its fallbacks — with per-candidate budgets\\nnested inside. It is an absolute 3 minutes rather than `n tiers × one window`:\\nsized as a multiple it equals the loop's own worst case, so it cannot bind and\\nbuys nothing. `ReadChainLoopBudget` holds back a sixth so the fallbacks are\\nfunded rather than merely inside it, and `ReadFetchTimeout` is exported so the\\ncli-side paths stop carrying their own 2-minute literals.\\n\\n**Election cost.** The election re-runs per call by design and each run shells out\\nto git twice over `.git/config`. One command elects several times — `entire\\ncheckpoint list` resolves the chain four times — spending **15** git subprocesses\\nwhere main spent **9**. `WithGitRemoteCache` memoizes only those two reads,\\nper invocation. The election result, settings, and #1991's captured-election file\\nstay uncached, so a write followed by a re-resolve still sees the new value —\\ncaching the election result would have silently broken capture. `entire mcp`\\nserves a whole agent session from one context, so it installs a fresh cache per\\nrequest. After: **9**, matching main exactly.\\n\\n`WarnIfMetadataDisconnected` now takes the caller's context instead of building\\n`context.Background()`; the detached context ignored both interrupt cancellation\\nand the cache.\\n\\n### `Merge branch 'main'` — composed with #1994\\n\\n#1994 and this branch both rewrote `getSessionsBranchTree` to fix the same\\nsymptom (a committed checkpoint reading as \\\"not found\\\" while the data exists\\nelsewhere) from opposite ends: #1994 added a **network tier** (fetch v1 from a\\ndedicated `checkpoint_remote`), this branch added **candidate breadth**. Four\\nfiles were unions of orthogonal additions; `persistent.go` needed composing:\\n\\n1. **Local-then-network.** All candidates resolve locally first; only when none\\n   holds checkpoint data does `tryFetchMetadataBranch` run.\\n2. **#1994's trigger generalized** to the chain via `anyTreeHasCheckpointData`,\\n   keeping the reason it is \\\"no data\\\" and not \\\"no ref\\\" — a local orphan makes a\\n   ref resolve and would mask the miss. The once-per-store latch is untouched and\\n   matters more now, since each entry resolves N candidates.\\n3. **Three superseded helpers deleted**, all at zero callers: `getFetchingTree`,\\n   `resolveSessionsBranchTree`, `resolveSessionsBranchRef`. That removed the last\\n   `ReadBootstrappableFromOrigin` use, completing this branch's rename.\\n4. **Both error contracts survive** — error only when no tree resolved; trees\\n   returned with a nil error when they resolved but hold no data, so `List` still\\n   reads as empty offline instead of hard-failing on a transport error.\\n\\nDecisions 1–4 are judgment calls across two authors' designs and deserve a second\\npair of eyes, particularly 2 and 4. Both sides' pinning tests pass on the merged\\ntree: `TestEnable_GitRefsPrimaryDoesNotPullCheckpointBranch` and\\n`persistent_metadata_branch_fetch_test.go` for #1994's recovery, the\\nread-candidate and read-confinement suites for this branch's chain.\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**<br>Touches core checkpoint/resume/metadata sync across many call sites; incorrect local-ref promotion or candidate ordering could hide or mis-merge remote checkpoint data, though confinement and integration tests target the entireio/cli#1374 hazard.\\n>\\n> **Overview**<br>Fixes the mismatch where checkpoint **writes** followed the elected sync remote but **reads** still assumed `origin`, so fork/`checkpoint_push_remote` setups could push to upstream and fail on `resume`/`explain`.\\n>\\n> Introduces `strategy.CheckpointReadRemotes` / `CheckpointReadRemotesWithElection`: elected remote first, then read-only `origin` for pre-single-remote data; election errors **fail open** to `[origin]` when present. `OpenOptions.ReadRemotes` flows into the git-branch store (tracking-ref bootstrap) and `FetchCheckpointRefFrom` (per-ref fetch with shared try-next semantics).\\n>\\n> **Fetch and discovery paths** iterate candidates: metadata branch fetch (`fetchMetadataFromReadRemotes`, advance local primary only for elected), blob hydration, `ListCheckpointRefsOnRemote` (union of ls-remote across candidates when no dedicated `checkpoint_remote`), checkpoint policy `SyncFrom` with `SkipLocalUpdate` on the legacy tier.\\n>\\n> **Local-ref writers** stay **elected-only**: `EnsurePrimaryRef`, `promoteRemoteTrackingPrimary`, doctor metadata repair, and policy push targets use the explicit election—not the chain’s first entry—so stale origin cannot drive `SafelyAdvanceLocalRef` (entireio/cli#1374). Legacy data is served via tracking refs and `GetRemotePrimaryTree` without recreating local `entire/checkpoints/v1`.\\n>\\n> CLI surfaces (`resume`, `explain`, `attribution`, `doctor`, hooks, etc.) pass `ReadRemotes` into `checkpoint.Open`; docs updated. Dedicated `checkpoint_remote` and hook single-target ref fetchers are unchanged.\\n>\\n> Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](<https://cursor.com/bugbot>) for commit 01f91215d1de5840a0ce46bc84f6727f3fe15cb4. Configure [here](<https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot>).\\n\\n\\n## Findings pass (2026-08-17, review artifact ed17f4e4)\\n\\nAll 15 findings from the high-effort review are resolved: 5 pre-fixed in `20289d23a`, 9 fixed in `11773e1e3` + the reconciliation merge `eaea08613`, and the structural hand-threading finding fixed at the enforcement level in `0889b2e5c` — an AST invariant test fails CI naming the exact file:line when any production `OpenOptions` literal omits the `ReadRemotes` key (self-derivation inside `checkpoint.Open` stays blocked on a strategy-into-checkpoint import cycle; documented in the test). The trail's finding board is at zero open.\\n\\n**Two fixes reverse previously reviewed pins — please bless explicitly:**\\n\\n1. **Failed election now seeds a MISSING local primary from origin** (was: fresh orphan; the old pin was mutation-tested). Rationale: checkpoint pushes are already fail-closed while the election is broken, so the orphan bought no safety — and it guaranteed a disjoint history (permanent non-fast-forward) the moment the user fixed `checkpoint_push_remote`. Seeding a missing ref is not the #1374 replay-on-divergence hazard; the elected-exists confinement pin is unchanged. `TestEnsurePrimaryRef_FailedElectionSeedsMissingPrimaryFromOrigin`.\\n\\n2. **Checkpoint-ref hydration aborts on transport failure instead of advancing to the legacy tier** (was: \\\"transport errors advance\\\", recorded as a deliberate semantic difference). Rationale: this one path INSTALLS the canonical local ref (+ref:ref), checkpoint refs advance via backfills, and hydration only runs when the ref is absent — so a legacy install under elected-remote uncertainty permanently plants a stale tip. Scope: git-refs hydration only; git-branch tree reads still serve through outages (integration matrix split per backend). `TestFetchCheckpointRefFrom_ElectedTransportFailureRefusesLegacyInstall`.\\n\\nAlso fixed: attach's local-presence gates are local-only again via `PersistentRefs.PrimaryAsLocalRead` (the chain's per-checkpoint fall-through defeated them — the session-clobber finding); attach/import get the read chain; `GetCheckpointAuthor` iterates the chain; policy `SyncFrom` reports the enforced local policy when a read-only baseline cannot advance the ref; resume's metadata fetch is bootstrap-only for legacy tiers; `List` skips ancestor trees.\\n\\nNote for the stacked PR: #2003 needs its base merged forward past `eaea08613`.\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1951/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1951/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2262\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2262/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2262/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2262/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2262\",\n              \"id\": 5339714515,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCGAvyA\",\n              \"number\": 2262,\n              \"title\": \"changelog 0.10.5\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-03T17:48:52Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-03T18:29:14Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-03T18:29:12Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2262\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2262\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2262.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2262.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-03T18:29:12Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1232\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Documentation-only changelog update; no runtime or security behavior changes ship in this diff.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds the **0.10.5** (2026-09-03) section to `CHANGELOG.md`, documenting the release without any product code changes in this PR.\\n> \\n> **Changed** covers dropping the Claude Code / Droid `Read(./.entire/metadata/**)` deny rule (with `enable` / `doctor` cleanup) and clearer `entire experts --repo` errors from placement lookup.\\n> \\n> **Fixed** includes releasing `full.jsonl` after condensation, cross-federation `git clone entire://…` when one login can auth the cluster, and `entire doctor` messaging while waiting on session locks.\\n> \\n> **Security** entries span cluster well-known login URL restrictions, `checkpoint explain --repo` response verification, locked session state clears, and pasted-image handling in `docs/security-and-privacy.md`.\\n> \\n> **Housekeeping** notes moving cross-jurisdiction HTTP transport to `entireio/auth-go`'s `crossjuris` package.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 7d6e7e4007ab50cb42856380f4642b424ee8d69a. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2262/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2262/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2322\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2322/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2322/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2322/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2322\",\n              \"id\": 5387667311,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCrtpZw\",\n              \"number\": 2322,\n              \"title\": \"session: resolve the session running the command, not the one that moved last\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-08T13:58:47Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-09T13:52:29Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-09T13:52:26Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2322\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2322\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2322.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2322.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-09T13:52:26Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1266\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n`entire session current` could silently return another worktree’s most recently active session as the caller’s. Agents using that ID with `session adopt` could move an unrelated live session and reset its checkpoint bookkeeping.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- Resolve the caller using agent-published session IDs and process ancestry together, accounting for nested agents. Report uncertain matches as `caller-ambiguous` rather than claiming they identify the caller.\\n- Keep worktree and cross-worktree recency fallbacks, but distinguish them from caller identification. `session current --json` includes `resolution`; cross-worktree and ambiguous results warn on stderr. Untracked callers receive a diagnostic instead of an unrelated session.\\n- Use the resolver for `session current`, bare `session tokens`, and git-hook log attribution. `session tokens --current` remains worktree-only.\\n- Validate environment IDs centrally and clear all supported caller-session variables in integration/E2E harnesses, including agents the harness does not import.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\nFocused caller-resolution and command tests pass, covering nesting, ambiguous and untracked claims, ancestry, unsafe IDs, and cross-worktree fallbacks. `git diff --check` passes.\\n\\n## Follow-up\\n\\n`IsCaller()` distinguishes identification from a guess, but does not yet guard `session adopt`. Preventing adoption of another caller’s session remains separate work.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2322/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2322/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2310\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2310/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2310/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2310/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2310\",\n              \"id\": 5374915673,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABChiM-A\",\n              \"number\": 2310,\n              \"title\": \"fix(gitrepo): strip inherited `GIT_COMMON_DIR`\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"id\": 34813274,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-07T12:50:35Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-23T12:51:52Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-23T12:51:52Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2310\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2310\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2310.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2310.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-23T12:51:52Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Follow-up to the [findings recorded in split-four PR #2305](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2305#user-content-findings-while-working-on-this-pr), where this existing helper limitation was left out of the refactor.\\n\\n`gitrepo.EnvWithoutRepoOverrides()` removes `GIT_DIR`, `GIT_WORK_TREE`, and `GIT_INDEX_FILE`, but leaves `GIT_COMMON_DIR`. A Git command explicitly targeting repository A can therefore read shared Git data from repository B. Setting `cmd.Dir` or passing `git -C` does not clear the inherited override.\\n\\nA regression test reproduces this with two isolated repositories, each with a different `core.hooksPath`. It points the repository environment variables at B, then runs `git rev-parse --git-path hooks` in A using the helper. Before the fix, the command succeeds but returns B's hooks path. After the fix, it returns A's path.\\n\\nThis adds `GIT_COMMON_DIR` to the existing filter. It affects only commands already using the helper. The helper's comments also clarify that commands inspecting the commit being prepared must retain Git's temporary index.\\n\\nThe reproduction deliberately supplies the environment variable. No incident during normal use has been confirmed.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- The exact regression command failed before the fix and passes afterward: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/gitrepo -run TestEnvWithoutRepoOverrides -count=1`.\\n- Full `gitrepo`, `checkpoint`, and `strategy` package tests passed with `-count=1`.\\n- `mise run check` passed on the full rerun, including race-enabled unit/integration tests, 56 Vogon canaries, and 4 external deterministic canaries.\\n- A separate `mise run lint` after formatting passed with zero issues. `git diff --check` passed.\\n\\nThe first full check failed `TestHooksGitCmd_DiscoverExternalAgents_WhenEnabled` and `TestExternalCommand_SigintReachesPlugin`. Both passed on a focused rerun and in the subsequent full check, without code changes. No paid real-agent E2E tests ran.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2310/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2310/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/779\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/779/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/779/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/779/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/779\",\n              \"id\": 4138249272,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7NeeVV\",\n              \"number\": 779,\n              \"title\": \"Fix: Normalize FilesTouched paths to prevent missing checkpoint trail…\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Adityakk9031\",\n                \"id\": 143548997,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOCI5iRQ\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/143548997?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Adityakk9031\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Adityakk9031\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Adityakk9031/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Adityakk9031/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Adityakk9031/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Adityakk9031/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Adityakk9031/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Adityakk9031/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Adityakk9031/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Adityakk9031/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Adityakk9031/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-03-25T20:17:44Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-08T18:53:44Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-08T18:53:44Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/779\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/779\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/779.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/779.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Issue\\r\\nCommits never receive Entire-Checkpoint trailers despite hooks running correctly. The prepare-commit-msg hook finds sessions but logs \\\"no content to link\\\" for all of them.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe root cause is a path format mismatch in \\r\\nstagedFilesOverlapWithContent\\r\\n. \\r\\ngetStagedFiles()\\r\\n returns repo-relative paths (e.g., src/screens/SessionDetail.tsx) from git diff --cached --name-only, but state.FilesTouched stores the exact paths the agent provides — often absolute (e.g., /Users/alex/project/src/screens/SessionDetail.tsx). The touchedSet[stagedPath] lookup silently fails, so no file ever reaches the content comparison logic.\\r\\n\\r\\nA contributing factor is that opencode export returns invalid JSON, which prevents the active session's live transcript fallback from detecting content.\\r\\n\\r\\nSolution\\r\\nNormalize at write time: \\r\\nmergeFilesTouched\\r\\n now accepts a worktreePath parameter and normalizes all incoming paths to repo-relative form via a new \\r\\nnormalizeToRepoRelative\\r\\n helper before storing them in state.FilesTouched.\\r\\nBasename fallback at read time: \\r\\nstagedFilesOverlapWithContent\\r\\n now builds a secondary touchedByBase map keyed by filepath.Base(). When the exact path lookup fails, it falls back to basename matching to handle stale sessions from older CLI versions.\\r\\nDebug logging: A new log line (\\\"path format mismatch, matched by basename\\\") makes this class of silent failure visible in future.\\r\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/779/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/779/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1387\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1387/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1387/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1387/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1387\",\n              \"id\": 4613287131,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7j7DBz\",\n              \"number\": 1387,\n              \"title\": \"Sign checkpoints at push time\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"pjbgf\",\n                \"id\": 5452977,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NTI5Nzc=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5452977?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pjbgf\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-06-08T13:26:50Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-05T12:01:28Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-05T12:01:27Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1387\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1387\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1387.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1387.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/537\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n ## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\n  Defer GPG/SSH signing of checkpoint commits from creation time to push time. During an agent session, checkpoint commits accumulate\\r\\n  unsigned on the local `entire/checkpoints/v1` ref — no GPG agent calls per step. At pre-push, every local-only commit is cherry-picked\\r\\n  onto the remote tip with strict signing, with a visible per-commit progress line and an interactive retry/skip/abort prompt on failure.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ## Why\\r\\n\\r\\n  - **Performance:** active sessions create many checkpoint commits; the per-step `SignCommitBestEffort` round-trip to the GPG/SSH agent\\r\\n  dominated commit latency.\\r\\n  - **Visibility:** signing was silent — users couldn't tell when the agent was being invoked or which commit it was signing.\\r\\n  - **Correctness:** local-only checkpoints don't need signatures; only what leaves the machine.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ## What changes\\r\\n\\r\\n  - `CreateCommit` and the orphan metadata-branch init no longer sign.\\r\\n  - `createCherryPickCommit` is split into `buildCherryPickCommit` + `persistCherryPickCommit` so a new push-time loop can sign each\\r\\n  cherry-picked clone between build and persist.\\r\\n  - New strict `SignCommit(ctx, commit) error` alongside the existing `SignCommitBestEffort` (now a logging wrapper). `ErrSigningDisabled`\\r\\n  sentinel.\\r\\n  - `PrePush` fetches the remote tip into the appropriate ref (temp ref for URL targets), runs the sign-loop over local-only commits,\\r\\n  advances the local ref to the new signed tip, then pushes. On any abort the local ref stays untouched.\\r\\n  - Cross-clone safety: empty-tree orphans are filtered out, and tree construction uses diff-based application (mirroring `cherryPickOnto`)\\r\\n   so per-clone files accumulate onto the remote tip rather than overwriting it.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ## UX\\r\\n\\r\\n  [entire] Fetching latest from remote...\\r\\n  [entire] Signing commits:\\r\\n          10/10: Finalize transcript for Checkpoint: 17d941007e3b\\r\\n  [entire] Pushing entire/checkpoints/v1 to checkpoint remote... done\\r\\n\\r\\n  - TTY: a static header and a single status line that rewrites in place — no scrollback noise.\\r\\n  - Non-TTY (CI): one line per commit, preserved for the audit trail.\\r\\n  - Signing failure: `Retry, skip, or abort? [r/s/a]:`. Non-TTY defaults to skip (with a `logging.Warn`).\\r\\n  - Setting: `sign_checkpoint_commits` (default `true`) gates the whole loop.\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **High Risk**\\n> Changes when and how metadata refs are rewritten before push (cherry-pick, ref advance, cross-clone filtering); signing failures can block push or leave unsigned commits on the chain.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Checkpoint commit signing moves from per-step creation to pre-push**, so local `entire/checkpoints/v1` history stays unsigned during sessions and only commits that will leave the machine are signed.\\n> \\n> `CreateCommit` and orphan metadata ref init **no longer call the signer**. Signing is centralized in a new strict `SignCommit` (returns `ErrSigningDisabled` and propagates signer errors); `SignCommitBestEffort` is a thin logging wrapper. Cherry-pick helpers split into **`buildCherryPickCommit` / `persistCherryPickCommit`** so push can sign between build and store.\\n> \\n> **`PrePush`** runs **`signLocalCommitsForPush`** before each checkpoint ref push: fetch remote tip, collect local-only commits (`collectCommitsSince` now supports `exclude == ZeroHash`), optionally drop empty-tree orphan dupes on cross-clone pushes, then **`signAndPersistCommits`** (diff-based cherry-pick + per-commit signing, TTY progress, retry/skip/abort on failure). Abort leaves the local ref unchanged; signing off via `sign_checkpoint_commits` skips the loop. Metadata reconcile still uses best-effort signing on its cherry-pick path.\\n> \\n> Tests cover unsigned `CreateCommit`, strict `SignCommit`, and end-to-end pre-push signing behavior.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit b2d3e845e6aaaaade398400d047b9de0ba655d38. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1387/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1387/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2506\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2506/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2506/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2506/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2506\",\n              \"id\": 5480150945,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABD1e0Cw\",\n              \"number\": 2506,\n              \"title\": \"docs: slim repository instructions into task-specific references\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-16T21:30:35Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-17T08:46:14Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-17T08:46:11Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2506\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2506\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2506.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2506.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-17T08:46:11Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1353\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- Reduce CLAUDE.md from 152,872 to 12,730 bytes (~92%), retaining repository-wide safety rules and a task-specific reading map.\\n- Preserve detailed implementation contracts and incident rationale in seven docs/development references; retain the AGENTS.md symlink.\\n- Correct stale accessibility/keyring guidance, including Copilot instructions, and redirect inbound documentation and Go comment/error references.\\n- Add a scoped unit-test guard for the 20 KiB root budget and local inline Markdown links/heading anchors in CLAUDE.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, and docs/development/*.md. External URLs, prose pointers, and other documentation outbound links remain outside its scope.\\n\\n## Validation\\n- mise run check (formatting, lint, race-enabled unit/integration tests, deterministic canaries)\\n- mise run lint again after the final formatting pass\\n- mise run test:integration (600 tests, 3 skipped)\\n- Documentation guard and affected source guard tests\\n- git diff --cached --check\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Documentation, link targets, and comment-only changes with no production code behavior changes.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Reorganizes agent/contributor documentation** so `CLAUDE.md` / `AGENTS.md` stay a short entry point (~92% smaller) with repo-wide safety rules, verification commands, and a **“read when relevant”** table into `docs/development/*` and existing architecture docs.\\n> \\n> **Moves** the former monolithic instruction content (API routing, caller-session resolution, testing, filesystem/git safety, checkpoint contracts, etc.) into **task-specific references** under `docs/development/`, and **redirects** `CONTRIBUTING.md`, Copilot instructions, and several Go comment/error strings from `CLAUDE.md` to those paths.\\n> \\n> **Adds** `go test ./docs/development` guards for the **20 KiB** `CLAUDE.md` budget and valid local Markdown links/anchors in the instruction doc set.\\n> \\n> **Updates** Copilot accessibility guidance to recommend **`uiform.New`** (and `NewAccessibleForm` in `cli`) instead of per-call-site `isAccessibleMode` / `WithAccessible` wiring in `strategy`.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit d16dce053f82321a0bf77f3c943938af0cf2d44f. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2506/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2506/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2354\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2354/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2354/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2354/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2354\",\n              \"id\": 5413221479,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABDAPXNw\",\n              \"number\": 2354,\n              \"title\": \"fix: address open code-scanning alerts\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-10T14:06:42Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-10T14:20:31Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-10T14:20:29Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2354\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2354\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2354.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2354.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-10T14:20:29Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1293\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nCodeQL default setup was enabled on this repo this morning (`actions`, `go`, `js/ts`, `python`; threat model `remote`), and its first scan opened 16 alerts. This closes all of them.\\n\\n## `actions/missing-workflow-permissions` × 13\\n\\nSix workflows ran with GitHub's default `GITHUB_TOKEN` scopes because neither the workflow nor the job declared a `permissions` block. Every job now has an explicit least-privilege set, derived from what the job actually does rather than from a blanket default:\\n\\n| Workflow | Choice | Why |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `ci.yml` | workflow `contents: read`; `test` job `{}` | Five jobs only check out; no job in the file touches the token. The `test` gate job reads only `needs.*.result`. |\\n| `e2e-isolated.yml` | workflow `contents: read` | Single job, checkout only. Its agent API keys are repository secrets, not token scopes. |\\n| `license-check.yml` | workflow `contents: read` | The reusable workflow checks this repo out and hands the token to mise-action. |\\n| `e2e-windows.yml` | workflow `contents: read` | Checkout only. |\\n| `e2e.yml` | workflow `{}`; per-job grants | `matrix-setup` only writes `$GITHUB_OUTPUT`. `notify-slack` gets `actions: read`. The `e2e-windows` caller gets `contents: read`. `e2e-tests` keeps its existing block. |\\n| `e2e-checkpoint-store.yml` | workflow `{}` | `matrix-setup` needs nothing; the other job already declared its scopes. |\\n\\nTwo of these deserve a second look from a reviewer:\\n\\n- **`e2e.yml` `notify-slack` → `actions: read` only.** It calls `gh api repos/{repo}/actions/runs/{id}/jobs`, which is documented as needing just the Actions read permission; Slack is reached through an incoming webhook, so it needs no repository read. The same-named job in `nightly-e2e.yml` only posts to the webhook and correctly sits at `{}` today, which is what confirmed the two jobs genuinely differ. If this turns out to need `contents: read` too, the failure mode is silent loss of e2e failure notifications on `main`, so it is worth a sanity check on the first `main` push.\\n- **`e2e-windows.yml` is reached via `workflow_call` from `e2e.yml`.** A reusable workflow can never hold more than its caller, so the calling job grants `contents: read` to match what the called workflow now declares. Without that pairing the Windows leg would fail at checkout.\\n\\nVerified by parsing all 15 workflows and printing each job's effective permissions — every file is valid YAML and no job is left implicit. The untouched workflows (`e2e-checkpoints-v2.yml`, `nightly-e2e.yml`) already declared theirs per-job, which is why they were never flagged.\\n\\n## `go/allocation-size-overflow` × 3\\n\\nAll three are unreachable, but they split two ways.\\n\\n**Fixed in code** — `redact/redact.go` sized a map from `len(seenSlice)+1` on the one branch where `len(seenSlice) == duplicateKeySliceThreshold`, so the value is always 17. It now sizes from the constant, which is what the code meant; the alert goes away as a side effect of saying it plainly.\\n\\n**Dismissed as false positives** — the two transcript compactors use `make([]T, 0, 1+len(slice))` as a capacity hint. That can only overflow at `len == math.MaxInt`, which for these element types (`geminiToolCall` 96B, `copilotToolRequest` 56B, both measured) would need ~10²⁰ bytes of backing array — far past Go's `maxAlloc`, so `json.Unmarshal` cannot produce it. Dropping the `+1` would clear the alert but costs a realloc per assistant line carrying text, and every other reformulation keeps the same flagged arithmetic. So the reason is recorded at each call site, so nobody \\\"fixes\\\" the hint away later, and alerts #30/#31 are dismissed with that reasoning.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `mise run fmt && mise run lint` — clean (0 issues)\\n- `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` — clean (`test:ci` compiles host-only, so this is the cross-OS guard)\\n- `mise run test:ci` — green: 91 packages plus both canary legs (56 and 4 tests)\\n\\nNo behaviour changes: the Go diff is one constant substitution plus three comments.\\n\\nThe 13 Actions alerts stay open until CodeQL re-scans `main`; `codeql-actions.yml` runs on this PR since it touches `.github/workflows/**`, so the analysis result is visible here first.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> CI permission tightening could break checkout or Slack failure classification if scopes are wrong; Go changes are comments plus one equivalent map capacity constant.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Closes **16 CodeQL alerts** from new default scanning—mostly **explicit least-privilege `permissions`** on six GitHub Actions workflows, plus small Go tweaks for **`go/allocation-size-overflow`**.\\n> \\n> **Actions:** Workflows that relied on the default `GITHUB_TOKEN` scopes now declare what each job actually needs—e.g. **`ci.yml`** uses workflow **`contents: read`** and the aggregate **`test`** gate job uses **`permissions: {}`**; **`e2e.yml`** defaults to deny-all at workflow level and grants **`contents: read`** on the **`e2e-windows`** reusable call and **`actions: read`** on **`notify-slack`** (for `gh api` job listing); checkout-only flows get **`contents: read`** or **`{}`** where no token is used.\\n> \\n> **Go:** In **`redact/redact.go`**, duplicate-key detection sizes the spill-over map with **`duplicateKeySliceThreshold+1`** instead of **`len(seenSlice)+1`** on the threshold branch (same effective size, satisfies CodeQL). **`copilot.go`** and **`gemini.go`** keep the `1+len(tools)` slice capacity hint and add comments that overflow is unreachable so future “fixes” do not drop the hint.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 3e15fbc7c924188bf207b6b4c84b837475c5e355. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2354/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2354/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2219\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2219/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2219/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2219/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2219\",\n              \"id\": 5313856906,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBxVvyw\",\n              \"number\": 2219,\n              \"title\": \"Fix stale lock cleanup\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Rohitkanithi\",\n                \"id\": 63586900,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTg2OTAw\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63586900?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Rohitkanithi\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 2,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-01T15:42:47Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T15:56:22Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-04T15:56:22Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2219\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2219\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2219.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2219.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Closes #2197.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAdds cleanup support for stale lock files created under the git common dir:\\n\\n- `entire-shadow-locks`\\n- `entire-persistent-ref-locks`\\n\\n`entire clean --all` now discovers those lock files, reports them in dry-run output, and includes them in deletion summaries.\\n\\n## Review follow-up\\n\\nThis update addresses the lock-safety review feedback:\\n\\n- Revalidates Unix flock acquisitions against the current lock-file inode before returning from both blocking `Acquire` and bounded `AcquireContext` paths.\\n- Moves stale lock cleanup to run after shadow branch, session state, and checkpoint cleanup so normal cleanup operations use their locks first.\\n- Treats actively held lock files as skipped, not failed, so live sessions do not make `entire clean --all` exit non-zero just because a lock is busy.\\n- Adds an active-session guard for `entire clean --all` unless `--force` or `--dry-run` is used.\\n- Keeps lock-directory listing best-effort if one lock directory is unreadable.\\n- Uses platform-specific lock-file removal ordering for Unix and Windows.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n```bash\\nGOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-build-cache go test ./cmd/entire/cli/internal/flock ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy\\nGOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-build-cache go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run TestClean\\nGOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-build-cache go test ./cmd/entire/...\\nGOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-build-cache go build ./cmd/entire\\ngit diff --check\\n```\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2219/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2219/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2241\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2241/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2241/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2241/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2241\",\n              \"id\": 5323086804,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABB4qmmA\",\n              \"number\": 2241,\n              \"title\": \"refactor(gitrepo): centralize metadata resolution (split part 1)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"id\": 34813274,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 5,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-02T11:06:38Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-03T20:21:55Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-03T20:21:55Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2241\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2241\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2241.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2241.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-03T20:21:55Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Refs #2190.\\r\\n\\r\\nPR #2190 moved every Git metadata consumer at once. The review exposed two separate jobs: define one owner for the metadata, then migrate its callers.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is split part 1. It adds the resolver and changes only repository opening. Checkpoint, session, strategy, hooks, and other consumers stay unchanged here.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Files and ownership\\r\\n\\r\\nThree production files and four test files change. All paths below are relative to `cmd/entire/cli/gitrepo/`.\\r\\n\\r\\n| File | Before | After |\\r\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\r\\n| `metadata.go` | No file | Resolves the three metadata facts |\\r\\n| `repository.go` | Opening rediscovered paths | Resolves and passes metadata |\\r\\n| `reftable.go` | Errors looked like absence | Returns inspection errors |\\r\\n| `metadata_guard_test.go` | No guard | Blocks new duplicate traversal |\\r\\n| `metadata_test.go` | No resolver tests | Covers real and broken layouts |\\r\\n| `repository_test.go` | Tested the old path | Covers fallback and failures |\\r\\n| `reftable_test.go` | Tested boolean detection | Covers inspection errors |\\r\\n\\r\\nThe call path changes like this:\\r\\n\\r\\n```text\\r\\nBefore\\r\\n\\r\\nOpenPath\\r\\n  ├── resolve .git and commondir while opening\\r\\n  ├── resolve them again while checking alternates\\r\\n  └── fall back without one validated metadata result\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter\\r\\n\\r\\nOpenPath\\r\\n  └── ResolveWorktreeMetadata\\r\\n        ├── GitDir\\r\\n        ├── CommonDir\\r\\n        └── WorktreeID\\r\\n              │\\r\\n              ├── repository storage\\r\\n              ├── alternates inspection\\r\\n              └── reftable inspection\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n## One resolver for three facts\\r\\n\\r\\n`gitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata` resolves an explicit worktree root into:\\r\\n\\r\\n- `GitDir`\\r\\n- `CommonDir`\\r\\n- `WorktreeID`\\r\\n\\r\\nThe resolver takes a worktree root. It does not discover one from CWD, read Git environment variables, run Git, cache results, or choose a caller's policy.\\r\\n\\r\\nResolution is all-or-error. Malformed or unreadable metadata stops the open.\\r\\n\\r\\n`gitrepo.OpenPath` now resolves metadata once and passes those facts into repository opening, object-alternates detection, and reftable inspection.\\r\\n\\r\\nA bare-repository open is tried only when worktree metadata does not exist.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Symlinks and `..` keep their filesystem meaning\\r\\n\\r\\nLexically cleaning a path through a symlink can change where `..` leads. The resolver checks filesystem identity before it returns a cleaned path.\\r\\n\\r\\nLinked-worktree registrations may use physical aliases. They must still resolve to an immediate child of `CommonDir/worktrees`.\\r\\n\\r\\nInspection errors now reach the caller. They no longer mean \\\"feature absent.\\\" This applies to reftable inspection and malformed `.git` layouts.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Fixes a hang that is already released\\r\\n\\r\\n`OpenPath` on `main` identifies a `.git` entry by reading it: `os.Stat`, then `os.ReadFile`. That works for a directory or a regular file. For three other entry types the read never finishes.\\r\\n\\r\\n| `.git` is | `main` | This PR |\\r\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\r\\n| A FIFO with no writer | Blocks until a writer opens it | Refused on type |\\r\\n| A symlink to such a FIFO | Blocks until a writer opens it | Refused on type |\\r\\n| A symlink to `/dev/zero` | Reads forever, memory grows | Refused on type |\\r\\n\\r\\nThe resolver checks the type first. It opens only a directory or a regular file, and refuses anything else by name.\\r\\n\\r\\nNone of these arrive by clone. Git refuses a `.git` path component in a tree at any depth, so each one needs local write access to the worktree. This is a robustness fix, not a vulnerability.\\r\\n\\r\\n## `gitdir:` strictness now matches Git\\r\\n\\r\\nThe legacy parser accepted pointer files that Git rejects. It cut the prefix at `gitdir:` instead of `gitdir: `, then trimmed whitespace from the remainder. That let `gitdir:target`, ` gitdir: target`, and `gitdir:\\\\ttarget` all resolve. Git requires the single space and trims nothing.\\r\\nThe fixture covers seven `.git` pointer spellings. The new resolver agrees with Git on all seven. The legacy parser agreed on three.\\r\\nThis changes behavior. A `.git` file that worked only because Entire was more permissive than Git now fails, and every other Git tool was already failing it.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Stop new duplicate traversal\\r\\n\\r\\nA source guard scans production Go across the repository. It rejects new `.git`, `gitdir:`, and `commondir` traversal outside `gitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata`.\\r\\nThe guard lists the existing callers that later PRs must migrate:\\r\\n\\r\\n- checkpoint metadata\\r\\n- session metadata\\r\\n- strategy and hooks\\r\\n- remaining product consumers\\r\\n\\r\\nThe exception list records each function and the one `git rev-parse` flag it may use. If that function starts using another metadata flag, the guard fails. The test also fails when a listed exception no longer exists.\\r\\n\\r\\nA temporary multi-file repository test runs the complete scanner. It proves that the scanner follows a package constant into another file, scans production code under `internal/`, and ignores a parameter named `gitDir`.\\r\\n\\r\\nPositive controls cover rooted filesystem APIs, package constants, `Readlink`, aliased imports, and legacy resolver calls.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Verification\\r\\n\\r\\n- `mise run check`\\r\\n  - formatting passed\\r\\n  - lint passed with 0 issues\\r\\n  - race-enabled unit and integration tests passed\\r\\n  - Vogon canary passed 56/56\\r\\n  - external deterministic canary passed 4/4\\r\\n- `git diff main --check`\\r\\n- Real Git fixtures cover ordinary, linked, bare, separate-Git-dir, submodule, symlink-alias, moved-registration, alternates, and reftable layouts.\\r\\n- On the seven `.git` pointer spellings in the fixture, the new resolver matches Git on 7/7. The legacy parser matched 3/7.\\r\\n- Broken fixtures verify fail-closed repository opening and typed absence.\\r\\n\\r\\nNo paid real-agent E2E tests were run.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Deliberately not included\\r\\n\\r\\nCheckpoint, session, strategy, hooks, and other product consumers still use their existing paths. Separate PRs will migrate them without mixing their error and fallback policies into this resolver change. The last migration will remove the legacy resolvers.\\r\\n\\r\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2241/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2241/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1886\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1886/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1886/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1886/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1886\",\n              \"id\": 5032611616,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M75Kd0n\",\n              \"number\": 1886,\n              \"title\": \"remote: classify a remoteless repo as checkpoint-ref absence, not outage\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-07-31T19:09:13Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-03T11:10:50Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-03T11:10:48Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1886\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1886\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1886.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1886.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-03T11:10:48Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/963\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nMain is currently red: `TestRunExplainAuto_GeneratePersistsHexOnBranchUnderRefsPrimary` fails on the tip (see #1885's test-core run — that PR only touches `trail show`, and the failure reproduces on pristine main with its diff stashed).\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\nA semantic conflict between the last two merges — each green alone:\\n\\n- #1811 routes backfill writes (e.g. `explain --generate` summary persistence) through the git-refs store.\\n- #1824's on-demand fetch probes the remote when the local ref is missing, with the (correct) contract that transport failure is never mapped to absence.\\n\\nIn a **fully local repository** — no origin remote, no checkpoint_remote — the probe's origin-name fallback runs `git ls-remote origin`, gets exit 128 (`'origin' does not appear to be a git repository`), and the contract turns \\\"this repo has no remotes\\\" into a hard error. Backfill routing then fails instead of falling through to the branch store.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nBefore probing: if the fetch target is the non-authoritative origin fallback, no checkpoint_remote is configured, and origin has no URL, return the ref's absence (`plumbing.ErrReferenceNotFound`) — a repo with no remotes has no remote that could host checkpoint refs. Deliberately narrow:\\n\\n- checkpoint_remote configured but unresolvable → unchanged (fallback emptiness still refuses to classify as absence)\\n- genuine transport failures → unchanged (still never absence)\\n\\nNew regression test `TestFetchCheckpointRef_NoRemoteAtAllIsAbsence` alongside the existing probe-contract tests, all green; the failing explain test passes with this fix.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Small, scoped change to checkpoint ref fetch error classification with a regression test; does not relax transport-vs-absence rules for configured or reachable remotes.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Fixes **backfill / `explain --generate` routing** in fully local repos where on-demand checkpoint ref probing would hit the non-authoritative `origin` fallback and surface `git ls-remote` exit 128 as a transport error instead of “ref not found.”\\n> \\n> **`FetchCheckpointRef`** adds a narrow pre-probe guard: when the target is the `origin` fallback, `checkpoint_remote` is not configured, and `origin` has no URL, it returns **`plumbing.ErrReferenceNotFound`** (wrapped) without calling `ls-remote`. Behavior is unchanged when `checkpoint_remote` is set (including unresolvable) or when a real remote exists but is unreachable.\\n> \\n> Adds regression test **`TestFetchCheckpointRef_NoRemoteAtAllIsAbsence`** for a repo with no remotes.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 66c06c5b561dd982012268c675bea67ecc5a1a4a. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1886/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1886/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2399\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2399/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2399/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2399/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2399\",\n              \"id\": 5439470451,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABDU6wrQ\",\n              \"number\": 2399,\n              \"title\": \"fix(strategy): keep non-ASCII staged paths literal so commit linking matches\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"wangzhengzhuo05\",\n                \"id\": 175673456,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOCniQcA\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175673456?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wangzhengzhuo05\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/wangzhengzhuo05\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wangzhengzhuo05/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wangzhengzhuo05/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wangzhengzhuo05/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wangzhengzhuo05/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wangzhengzhuo05/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wangzhengzhuo05/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wangzhengzhuo05/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wangzhengzhuo05/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/wangzhengzhuo05/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-13T10:18:28Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-18T03:43:47Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-18T03:43:47Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2399\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2399\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2399.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2399.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"**What**\\n\\n`getStagedFiles` in `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go` now parses `git diff --cached --name-only -z` and splits the output on NUL, so staged paths are returned literally instead of as git's quoted/C-escaped display form.\\n\\n**Why**\\n\\nWith git's default `core.quotePath=true`, the newline-delimited `--name-only` output quotes and C-escapes unusual pathnames — `café.go` comes back as the display string `\\\"caf\\\\303\\\\251.go\\\"`. That string was exact-compared against the literal path stored in `SessionState.FilesTouched`, so a session that touched only a non-ASCII file was classified as contributing no content to the commit: the commit was still created, but it received no `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer and its provenance (`entire explain` attribution) was incomplete. Reported with a focused control/canary reproduction in #2398: an ASCII control file got its trailer, an otherwise equivalent UTF-8 canary did not.\\n\\n**How**\\n\\n- Pass `-z` to the git invocation and iterate the NUL-delimited fields, keeping `filepath.ToSlash` on every entry.\\n- Drop the `\\\\r\\\\n` → `\\\\n` normalization: it only existed to unwrap the newline framing, and `-z` emits NUL-terminated, unquoted names.\\n- The function's contract is unchanged: `(non-nil empty slice, nil)` when nothing is staged, `(nil, err)` only when git itself fails, and the same error wrapping.\\n- This follows the precedent already in the same package: `priorAICommitFiles` in `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/telemetry_signals.go` uses `-z` for the same reason, so paths match their `FilesTouched` form.\\n\\n**Tests**\\n\\nNew `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/staged_files_quoting_test.go`, `TestGetStagedFiles_PreservesNonASCIIPaths`: sets `core.quotePath true` explicitly, stages a literal `café.go` plus an ASCII `control.go`, and asserts both come back literal and that no returned entry is git-quoted or C-escaped.\\n\\n```\\n$ gofmt -l cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/staged_files_quoting_test.go\\n(no output)\\n$ go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/ -count=1\\nok  \\tgithub.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/strategy\\t25.187s\\n$ go build ./...\\n(exit 0)\\n```\\n\\n**Mutation check**\\n\\nReverting only the fix (removing `-z`, i.e. the previous behaviour) makes the new test fail with exactly the string from the report — the assertion output is the single staged entry `\\\"\\\\\\\"caf\\\\\\\\303\\\\\\\\251.go\\\\\\\"\\\\ncontrol.go\\\\n\\\"`, which contains neither literal filename. Restoring `-z` returns the package suite to green, so the test guards the defect rather than the implementation.\\n\\nFixes #2398.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2399/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2399/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2195\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2195/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2195/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2195/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2195\",\n              \"id\": 5303757762,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBpQP3A\",\n              \"number\": 2195,\n              \"title\": \"feat(search): report result selections from the CLI search TUI (ENT-2073)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"id\": 6415609,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTU2MDk=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6415609?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [\n                {\n                  \"login\": \"alishakawaguchi\",\n                  \"id\": 6415609,\n                  \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTU2MDk=\",\n                  \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6415609?v=4\",\n                  \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi\",\n                  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/alishakawaguchi\",\n                  \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/followers\",\n                  \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/following{/other_user}\",\n                  \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                  \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                  \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/subscriptions\",\n                  \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/orgs\",\n                  \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/repos\",\n                  \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/events{/privacy}\",\n                  \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/received_events\",\n                  \"type\": \"User\",\n                  \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                  \"site_admin\": false\n                }\n              ],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 2,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-31T18:55:35Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-02T20:39:03Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-02T20:39:02Z\",\n              \"assignee\": {\n                \"login\": \"alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"id\": 6415609,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTU2MDk=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6415609?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2195\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2195\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2195.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2195.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1192\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What was missing\\n\\nWe couldn't tell whether CLI search is any *good* — only that it was alive.\\n\\nAn important correction to the ticket first: **the CLI is not uninstrumented.** An existing search event already reports that a search ran, how long it took, how many results came back, and how it failed. It shipped a few days ago and is landing normally — 64 events from 7 users. It just lands in a **separate PostHog project for CLI telemetry**, not the web app's project, which is where the audit looked. There's no ingestion bug to chase, and four of the five things the ticket asked for already existed.\\n\\nThe real gap was the fifth: whether the user opened any of the results.\\n\\n## Why it matters\\n\\nCounts and timings measure liveness, not relevance. A search returning 80 results in three seconds looks equally healthy whether the user found what they wanted in the first row or gave up after the twentieth. The web app has tracked result clicks all along; the CLI had no equivalent, so the click-through half of \\\"is search any good?\\\" was invisible.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\nOne new event, emitted when the user opens a result's detail view in the search TUI.\\n\\n1. Instrumented at the single key handler both the checkpoint tabs and the code tab open through, so both surfaces are covered without per-tab wiring.\\n2. Reports the result's kind, its position in the list, the size of that list, and which surface. **Position is the point** — a healthy ranking gets picked from the top row far more often than the twentieth, and that isn't derivable from counts.\\n3. Deduped per position within a result set, so opening and closing the same row repeatedly counts once. Opening several *different* rows still counts each, because having to dig is itself the signal.\\n4. The result-kind value is clamped to a known list. The search decoder passes unrecognized kinds straight through from the server, so without clamping an arbitrary server-supplied string could have been forwarded into analytics.\\n\\nNo query text, result titles, repo names, or file paths are sent — enums, counts, and one position only. A test asserts on the payload's key set, so a field added later fails rather than quietly leaking. Opt-out gating is identical to the existing search event's, so anyone opted out of one is opted out of both.\\n\\n## Naming, for the parallel MCP work\\n\\nScheme is surface prefix plus what happened, so the MCP surface should emit its own completed/selected pair reusing these property names. Note that cross-surface dashboards need **both** PostHog projects — CLI events don't go to the web app's.\\n\\n## Verified\\n\\nAll unit tests and lint pass clean. Main merged in with no conflicts. Reviewed the branch diff for regressions and dead code — none found.\\n\\nTrail review caught one real bug during review, now fixed in a follow-up commit: the dedupe was keyed on the reported surface rather than the active tab, and since two tabs report the same surface, opening the top row of the second tab you visited was silently swallowed. Keyed on the tab instead; the added regression test fails against the old key.\\n\\nNo changelog entry: this repo writes the changelog in one batch per release, not per PR.\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Telemetry-only changes with opt-in gating and no search or auth behavior changes; main risk is miscounted analytics if dedupe logic regresses, which the new tests target.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **click-through telemetry** for the interactive `entire search` TUI via a new `cli_search_result_selected` event, emitted when the user confirms a row and opens the detail view (checkpoint tabs and Code tab share the same Confirm handler).\\n> \\n> Payloads stay **content-free**: command path, search mode, clamped result type, rank, and result count—gated the same way as existing search outcome telemetry (settings + env opt-out), with emit deferred as a `tea.Cmd` so settings load and detached analytics do not block the Update loop.\\n> \\n> **Deduping** uses separate semantic and code ledgers keyed by `tab:rank`, reset only when that result set refreshes (not on pagination), fixing undercount when Commits/Sessions share mode `checkpoint` and double-report when parallel semantic/code responses land at different times. Unknown API result types map to `other` before analytics.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit c3e7e3e5a6928f11acb1b3c04f0c6323b4666afc. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2195/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2195/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1504\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1504/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1504/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1504/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1504\",\n              \"id\": 4723776942,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7piaVt\",\n              \"number\": 1504,\n              \"title\": \"checkpoint: extract persistent contract to api/checkpoint\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-06-23T07:55:54Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-24T14:15:32Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-06-24T14:15:30Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1504\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1504\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1504.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1504.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-06-24T14:15:30Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/647\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n> **Stacked on #1495** (the persistent/ephemeral split + scope-based read/write API). Review/merge that first; this diff is against that branch. Carries the same latest-`main` merge as #1495.\\n\\n## What\\n\\nThe final step of the #1433 reorder: extract the **persistent-checkpoint contract** into a new `github.com/entireio/cli/api/checkpoint` package — born with the persistent vocabulary and scope-based names (the whole reason we did the rename before relocating).\\n\\n**Moved to `api/checkpoint`:**\\n- Persisted document types: `Metadata`, `CheckpointSummary`, `Summary`/`LearningsSummary`/`CodeLearning`, `Attribution`, `SessionFilePaths`, `SessionMetrics`, `CheckpointInfo`, `SessionContent`.\\n- Option types: `WriteOptions`, `UpdateOptions`, `PrecomputedTranscriptBlobs`.\\n- Contract surface:\\n  - read tiers `CheckpointReader` (`Read`, `List`) + `SessionReader` (the four session reads), composed into `PersistentStore`;\\n  - `Writer` + the sealed `WriteRequest` union (`Session` / `SessionTranscript` / `SessionSummary` / `CheckpointAttribution`);\\n  - the reader helpers (`ReadCheckpoint`, `ReadLatestSessionContent`, `ReadRawSessionLogForCheckpoint`), the sentinel errors, and `CheckpointVersionBranchV1`.\\n\\nThe contract depends only on **leaf** packages (`agent/types`, `checkpoint/id`, `redact`, go-git `plumbing`) — a backend can implement it without the CLI's agent/TUI/git machinery.\\n\\n**Stays in `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint`:** `GitStore` + methods, `Open`, the `Stores` facade, `PersistentRefs`, `AuthorReader`, `normalizeCheckpointSummary`, and the entire git-only ephemeral surface.\\n\\n## Zero call-site churn\\n\\n`cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint` imports the contract and re-exports every moved symbol via aliases (`aliases.go`):\\n\\n```go\\ntype CheckpointSummary = apicheckpoint.CheckpointSummary\\nvar  ErrCheckpointNotFound = apicheckpoint.ErrCheckpointNotFound\\nfunc ReadCheckpoint(...) (...) { return apicheckpoint.ReadCheckpoint(...) }\\n```\\n\\nAll existing importers compile unchanged; the backend imports `api/checkpoint` directly. (Helpers are thin wrapper funcs, not mutable vars — addressing the earlier review note.)\\n\\n## Cleanup (post-review `/simplify` pass)\\n- Extracted a shared `getSessionTree` helper: the four `SessionReader` methods each repeated the same context-check → fetching-tree → checkpoint-tree → session-subtree navigation (with identical `ErrCheckpointNotFound` wrapping) before reading their files. Behavior unchanged.\\n\\n## Notes\\n- `PrecomputedTranscriptBlobs.isUsable` → exported `IsUsable` (its one caller is now across the package boundary).\\n- The `Write` union is sealed to `api/checkpoint`, so the impl-package unknown-request test was dropped (no longer expressible); per-request dispatch coverage remains.\\n- Doc-comment terminology aligned to \\\"persistent\\\" (was \\\"committed\\\") on the moved option types.\\n\\n## Verification\\n`go build ./...`, full `go test ./...`, and `mise run lint` (0 issues) green; validated with `codex exec review` (which confirmed `errors.Is` still works across the alias boundary) and a 4-agent `/simplify` review (reuse / simplification / efficiency / altitude).\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1504/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1504/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2273\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2273/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2273/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2273/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2273\",\n              \"id\": 5350167315,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCOVPDw\",\n              \"number\": 2273,\n              \"title\": \"flock: revalidate lock file inode after acquire\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Rohitkanithi\",\n                \"id\": 63586900,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTg2OTAw\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63586900?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Rohitkanithi\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 2,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T15:49:54Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-05T20:17:09Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-05T20:17:09Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2273\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2273\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2273.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2273.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-05T20:17:09Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nAdds inode revalidation to the Unix flock implementation after a lock is acquired. If the locked file descriptor no longer matches the current lock-file name, the lock is released and acquisition retries against the current file.\\n\\nThis covers:\\n\\n- `Acquire`\\n- `AcquireContext`\\n- `AcquireIn`\\n- `AcquireContextIn`\\n- blocking `LOCK_EX`\\n- polling `LOCK_NB`\\n\\nThe path-based open error is wrapped so wrapcheck is satisfied.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n```bash\\nGOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-build-cache go test ./cmd/entire/cli/internal/flock\\nGOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-build-cache go build ./cmd/entire\\ngit diff --check\\n```\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2273/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2273/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            }\n          ],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e18-narrow\",\n      \"q\": \"org:entireio \\\"review tour\\\"\",\n      \"rr\": [\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 0,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 1,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1146\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1146/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1146/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1146/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1146\",\n              \"id\": 4402484321,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7ZVO9I\",\n              \"number\": 1146,\n              \"title\": \"Add experimental `entire learn` command with embedded markdown + release-time regen\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"id\": 6415609,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTU2MDk=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6415609?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [\n                {\n                  \"login\": \"alishakawaguchi\",\n                  \"id\": 6415609,\n                  \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTU2MDk=\",\n                  \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6415609?v=4\",\n                  \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi\",\n                  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/alishakawaguchi\",\n                  \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/followers\",\n                  \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/following{/other_user}\",\n                  \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                  \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                  \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/subscriptions\",\n                  \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/orgs\",\n                  \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/repos\",\n                  \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/events{/privacy}\",\n                  \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/received_events\",\n                  \"type\": \"User\",\n                  \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                  \"site_admin\": false\n                }\n              ],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 5,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-05-07T22:50:26Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-11T05:02:44Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-05-15T16:23:59Z\",\n              \"assignee\": {\n                \"login\": \"alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"id\": 6415609,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTU2MDk=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6415609?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1146\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1146\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1146.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1146.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/323\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\nMade `entire learn` so I can stop teaching agents how to use the CLI. Tired of pasting instructions in every prompt and watching them `-h` their way through every subcommand, or having to update my agent.md file all the time. Now I can just point at `entire learn`.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nAdds `entire learn`, an experimental Hidden top-level command (advertised under `entire labs`) that renders a state-aware tour of the CLI. Two rendering modes:\\r\\n\\r\\n1. **Default `entire learn`** — reads pre-rendered markdown from `cmd/entire/cli/learn/embedded/learn.md`, passes it through glamour, prints. ~50ms file-read + render.\\r\\n2. **`entire learn --regenerate`** (hidden, maintainer-only) — runs a TextGenerator agent against the live cobra tree to refresh `embedded/learn.md` before each release. Output is raw markdown to stdout; the command refuses to run unless stdout is redirected.\\r\\n\\r\\nRelease CI integration in `.github/workflows/release.yml` runs `mise run learn:regenerate` (atomic write + validation: ≥4 `## ` headers, presence of the `docs.entire.io/cli` footer) before GoReleaser. The regen step is `continue-on-error: true` so a flaky agent or missing `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` doesn't block the release; a dedicated Slack notification fires on regen failure separately from the existing release-failure alert.\\r\\n\\r\\nState-aware rendering: when Entire isn't enabled in the current repo, prints a short setup prompt; when enabled but no agent hooks are installed, prints an agent-install prompt; once a first commit has been captured, falls through to the full embedded tour (with a one-paragraph tail explaining that search/resume/rewind will gain real data after the next commit).\\r\\n\\r\\nMirrors `entire review`'s shape: top-level `Hidden: true`, advertised in `experimentalCommands` for `entire labs`.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Demos**\\r\\nhttps://cleanshot.com/share/35CFYwL1\\r\\n\\r\\n## Test plan\\r\\n\\r\\n- [x] `mise run learn:regenerate` locally with `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` set produces a valid `embedded/learn.md` (≥4 `## ` headers, includes `docs.entire.io/cli` footer)\\r\\n- [x] `entire learn` from a fresh checkout shows the embedded tour, rendered through glamour\\r\\n- [x] `entire learn --regenerate > /tmp/learn.md` produces sanitized markdown (control sequences stripped); refuses to run if stdout is a TTY\\r\\n- [x] `entire learn --help` shows correct help text\\r\\n- [x] `entire labs` lists `entire learn`\\r\\n- [x] State-aware fallbacks: setup prompt when disabled, agent-install prompt when enabled-without-agent, first-capture tail before any commit\\r\\n- [x] Existing tests: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/learn/...` passes (tests parallelized and hardened against host environment)\\r\\n- [x] Release workflow triggered on a `-rc.test` tag exercises the regen path end-to-end\\r\\n\\r\\n## Notes\\r\\n\\r\\nThe branch went through several code review passes (Claude-driven parallel agent reviews + codex adversarial review). Major findings addressed:\\r\\n- NBSP-mid-tagname Unicode bypass in tag escape\\r\\n- Terminal-injection sanitization on agent output before persistence\\r\\n- Atomic-write mise task with stronger CI validation\\r\\n- External-agent discovery in `ResolveTextGenerator` (mirrors `resolveCheckpointSummaryProvider`)\\r\\n- Settings double-load avoided via cached closure\\r\\n- Per-command descriptions required in capability sections of the regenerated markdown\\r\\n- `t.Parallel()` added to all learn-package tests; tests hardened against host environment (no reliance on real \\\\$HOME, real git config, or ambient `ENTIRE_*` env)\\r\\n\\r\\nThe earlier `--latest` blog-digest mode (RSS fetch + summarize most recent `entire.io` post) was removed during the rename back to `learn`: it added a network-dependent path that didn't fit the \\\\\\\"teach the CLI surface\\\\\\\" framing. The embedded-markdown + maintainer-regenerate flow is the whole feature now.\\r\\n\\r\\nDeferred to follow-up PRs: spinner/TUI dedup with `dispatch_tui.go`, `checkpoint.HasCommitted` short-circuit, dispatch's `sanitizeDispatchPromptString` consolidation with the new `stripInvisibles`.\\r\\n\\r\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\r\\n\\r\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n> [!NOTE]\\r\\n> **Medium Risk**\\r\\n> Adds a new top-level CLI command plus agent-driven generation paths and modifies the release workflow; failures are best-effort but could affect shipped tour content and release-time automation.\\r\\n>\\r\\n> **Overview**\\r\\n> Adds an experimental hidden `entire learn` command (advertised via `entire labs`) that renders a state-aware CLI tour from an embedded `learn.md` by default, with `--regenerate` (hidden) producing the embedded markdown via an agent.\\r\\n>\\r\\n> Introduces a new `cmd/entire/cli/learn` package to discover the cobra command surface, resolve repo stage (setup/agent install/first capture/workflow), build hardened agent prompts (tag-escape + control-sequence stripping), and select an available TextGenerator (including external `entire-agent-*`). Adds a small TUI spinner while agent work runs and extends `mdrender` to allow per-command style overrides.\\r\\n>\\r\\n> Updates the release GitHub Action to *best-effort* regenerate the embedded tour (installs pinned Claude CLI, runs `mise run learn:regenerate` with validation/atomic write), annotate failures, and send a dedicated Slack warning when regeneration fails without failing the release.\\r\\n>\\r\\n> <sup>Originally reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for an earlier commit when the command was named `tour`. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\r\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1146/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1146/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            }\n          ],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e19-narrow\",\n      \"q\": \"repo:entireio/forgemark \\\"histograms\\\"\",\n      \"rr\": [\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 0,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 0,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e16-narrow\",\n      \"q\": \"repo:entireio/entire-brain \\\"ranking\\\" \\\"explanation\\\"\",\n      \"rr\": [\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 0,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 3,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/6\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/6/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/6/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/6/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/6\",\n              \"id\": 4605215351,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSm5-5c7jhViP\",\n              \"number\": 6,\n              \"title\": \"Agent-UX improvements: tokenized search, overview, recency, blind-spots, impact/id fixes\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"ashtom\",\n                \"id\": 70720,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzIw\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70720?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/ashtom\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-06-06T21:45:56Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-07T00:30:42Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-06-07T00:30:42Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/pulls/6\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/6\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/6.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/6.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-06-07T00:30:42Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Stacked on `claude/semantic-warning-path-fix`. Improves the agent-facing brain surface, driven by actually consuming the brain on a real project (`gh/ashtom/podcasts`) and iterating with a Sonnet evaluator across three rounds.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n**Search that works for natural language**\\n- Route all `inspect` specialist text kinds (decisions/validation/tool-paths) through the tokenized ranker instead of whole-phrase substring matching. A natural-language question now matches on overlapping terms instead of returning nothing unless the exact phrase appears verbatim. (On podcasts, `inspect decisions \\\"why did we choose supabase over convex for the queue\\\"` went from **0 results** to the actual dated decision.)\\n- Semantic symbol `search` gains a token-overlap fallback for multi-word queries (`search \\\"feed refresh worker\\\"`: 0 → 20 results) and resolves a record `id` (from `search`/`overview`) for `context`/`impact`.\\n- Drop common question/filler words (why, did, over, instead, …) from tokenization so high-specificity terms aren't diluted.\\n\\n**Explainability & consistency**\\n- Every text match carries `score`, `matched_terms`, and a `timestamp`; the report carries `query_terms` so a thin/empty result is debuggable. Semantic search results also carry a `score`.\\n- Opt-in `--relax` (and MCP `relax` arg) for best-effort partial matches, flagged `partial`.\\n- Equally-scored history records ordered by recency (parsed from the session path) so \\\"current state of X\\\" surfaces the latest decision first.\\n- Empty result arrays emit `[]` instead of `null` across search/context/impact/boundaries/inspect/tests for one uniform shape.\\n\\n**New capabilities**\\n- `entire brain overview` — a single-call project map: stack stats, route/tool/workflow counts, build/test commands, entrypoints, key documents, and recent decisions.\\n- `entire brain stale --blind-spots` (and MCP `blind_spots` arg) — lists the files the semantic provider couldn't fully index. On podcasts this revealed all 125 \\\"partial failures\\\" are `.sql` migrations, i.e. TypeScript coverage is fully trustworthy.\\n\\n**Correctness fixes**\\n- `inspect impact` no longer returns an empty impacted set when a file resolves to many roots (raised the shared budget); roots: 24 → 200 total symbols (176 impacted) on `feed-refresh.ts`.\\n- Path-like queries skip the token fallback, so a nonexistent path no longer matches half the index on the token \\\"file\\\" and reports a bogus blast radius.\\n- `brief`'s semantic context now populates for natural-language task strings (was always empty).\\n\\n## Validation\\n- `mise run lint`, `go test -race ./...`, and the deterministic Phase 1 suite all pass.\\n- Each change verified against the live `gh/ashtom/podcasts` brain (refreshed with `entire brain refresh`).\\n- One existing test updated where tokenized matching legitimately surfaces a relevant decision the old substring matcher missed.\\n\\n## Deliberately out of scope (provider-side, in `entire-sem`)\\nSQL files unparsed by the bundled tree-sitter grammar; route boundaries lacking `file_path`; low-confidence/spurious CALLS relations. These need provider changes, not plugin changes.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/6/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/6/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/44\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/44/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/44/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/44/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/44\",\n              \"id\": 4678283783,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSm5-5c7nN1W7\",\n              \"number\": 44,\n              \"title\": \"patterns v2: rebuildable SQLite pattern corpus (stacked on #43)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"ashtom\",\n                \"id\": 70720,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzIw\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70720?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/ashtom\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-06-16T22:09:31Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-18T07:51:28Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-06-18T07:51:25Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/pulls/44\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/44\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/44.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/44.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-06-18T07:51:25Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Implements `docs/pattern_v2.md` end-to-end: a clean-room, Entire-Brain-native pattern **corpus** (`patterns/corpus.sqlite`) that improves the *whole* brain — refresh, patterns, brief, overview, query/get, review, handoff, MCP, and workspaces — with skill formation as one downstream consumer. Stacked on #43; reuses that branch's deterministic, token-free extraction + redaction. **No new model calls on the refresh/watch path.**\\n\\n## What's new (the 8-priority completion)\\n\\n**P1 — `patterns` reads the V2 corpus.** The public listing (+`--json`, `--type task|procedure|risk|practice|theme`, `--scope`) reads `patterns`/`pattern_evidence`/`dossiers`: type, scope, strength, support, dossier/verifier state, top anchor, id. Rejected dossiers suppressed; legacy JSON is fallback only.\\n\\n**P2 — workspaces are first-class V2.** `buildWorkspacePatternCorpus` aggregates member-repo corpora (not merged JSON) into a workspace corpus: `scope='workspace'`, `n_repos>=2`, per-repo breakdown (`workspace_pattern_repos`), member anchors, stable ids. Only redacted anchor pointers cross into the workspace store. `workspace patterns <name>`, `workspace refresh`, and `workspace get <ws> <repo-key>/pattern:<id>` all wired.\\n\\n**P3 — the missing tables, implemented.** `episode_symbols` (semantic graph), `episode_commits` (local `[branch hash]` only, no network), `synapses` (explanation edges: pattern→evidence→fact/file/symbol/commit, workspace→repo), `themes` table, and a run-history surface (`patterns/runs.ndjson`, shown in `patterns status`). Docs/schema match; empty-by-design tables are marked, not claimed done.\\n\\n**P4 — deep dossiers + full-span verifier.** `patterns verify --deep` audits each pattern against its COMPLETE evidence set (every backing episode by `episode_key`, corrected/failed first, with parameters and failure→recovery pairs), fingerprinted over the full set, cached in `deep_dossiers`. Explicit, egress-gated, never from refresh.\\n\\n**P5 — themes / latent practices.** Deterministic episode-shape classifier (conversation/read-only/shell/write → `episode_shapes`); recurring read-only/conversational clusters become theme candidates; `patterns verify --themes` promotes them. Verified themes appear in `patterns`, `get`, brief, overview (task-gated; rejected never surface).\\n\\n**P6 — wired into the rest of the brain.** `brief --handoff` carries current/stale consolidations; `review --patterns` attaches risk/practice/task context (opt-in, omitempty — the versioned review contract stays byte-stable by default); MCP `brain_patterns`/`brain_patterns_status`/`brain_get` are corpus-backed (pattern:/theme: ids); `query`/`search --patterns` adds capped `related_patterns` pointers **without touching facts/history/docs ranking** (default output byte-identical → no regression by construction).\\n\\n**P7 — skill lifecycle on V2 ids.** Skill formation sources promotable, non-rejected (shallow AND deep) task patterns by corpus id; skill-memory current/update/declined/reconsider lines up with the V2 listing; dedupe (overwrite refusal + declined-unchanged suppression), hand-edit (file SHA) and missing-file drift all work.\\n\\n**P8 — docs + this description match the code**, with an as-built status table in `docs/pattern_v2.md`.\\n\\n## The pipeline, end to end (live evidence)\\n`refresh` → `patterns` list → `get pattern:<id>` → `brief` (1 consolidation + 1 theme for a matching task) → `workspace patterns` (`commit:push` across entire-brain + cli) → `verify --deep` blocked under `ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS`, cached (4/4) when enabled. The deterministic gate promotes; the agent verifier is the final arbiter (it **rejected** generic `commit:push` deep, so `patterns skills` correctly returns 0).\\n\\n## Multi-repo workspace evidence (`entire-brain` + `entire-cli`)\\n| corpus | sessions | episodes | commands | fact links | symbol links | commits | patterns | dossiers | themes | synapses |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| entire-brain | 131 | 674 | 9,804 | 3,315 | 848 | 79 | 1,047 | 4 | 7 | 5,572 |\\n| entire-cli | 2,110 | 22,928 | 101,020 | 96,100 | 5,884 | 3,226 | 8,317 | 26 | 464 | 65,408 |\\n| workspace | — | — | — | — | — | — | **539** (cross-repo) | — | — | — |\\n\\nVerifier examples: entire-brain themes accepted 1 / rejected 6; deep dossiers rejected 3/4 (incl. generic `commit:push`), 1 needs_split. **Redaction leak count = 0** real tokens and 0 real home usernames across both corpora and the workspace store (the boundary rule preserves API `/users/<login>` paths).\\n\\n## Constraints upheld\\nrefresh/watch deterministic + token-free; no hidden commands (all public, documented, tested); single build path (`refresh` and `patterns refresh` keep every layer current; workspace likewise); user decisions kept outside the rebuildable corpus; redaction at every CLI/JSON/MCP/agent/cache egress; `ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS`/local-only blocks every agent path; existing workspace + skill-memory behavior preserved.\\n\\n## Validation\\n`gofmt -l -s .` empty · `go vet ./...` clean · `go test ./...` green · release-evidence audits pass (radar-tool manifest refreshed for the surface edits).\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/44/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/44/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/55\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/55/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/55/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/55/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/55\",\n              \"id\": 4796582498,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSm5-5c7tO3U2\",\n              \"number\": 55,\n              \"title\": \"feat(viz): local, no-egress visual interface for the brain\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"id\": 257360244,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-07-02T17:00:36Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-02T21:02:32Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-02T21:02:32Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/pulls/55\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/55\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/55.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/55.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-02T21:02:32Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"**What**\\n- Adds `entire brain viz [path]` (in the `explore` group): a local, loopback-only, no-egress web interface that renders the brain as an explorable, force-directed graph. The semantic code graph, facts, sessions, history, and docs each render as their own graph, with search, a ⌘K palette, a node inspector, a node-count slider, and session replay.\\n- Self-contained: a hand-authored, zero-build SPA embedded via `go:embed` — no CDN, no JS toolchain — so the pure-Go single-binary build is preserved.\\n\\n**Why / how it helps**\\n- The brain was only explorable via the CLI and the terminal dashboard. This adds a visual way to navigate a repo's brain in the browser, fully offline.\\n\\n**How**\\n- New `internal/cli/viz.go`: a cobra command + `http.ServeMux` + read-only JSON handlers, each wrapping an existing brain loader. Binds `127.0.0.1` only; a CSP header (`default-src 'self'` …) makes the no-egress guarantee machine-checkable.\\n- New module-root `webui.go` embeds `webui/dist` (mirrors `templates.go`/`embedmodel.go`). Frontend: `graph.js` (Canvas2D Barnes-Hut force sim + renderer), `app.js` (router/fetch/wiring), `index.html`, `style.css`.\\n- One-line command registration in `root.go`.\\n- Scale: the node-count slider reaches each feature's true total, bounded by a 300k safety ceiling; the semantic edge budget scales with node count (~4/node, capped at 90k). The relations query is chunked so a large graph can't exceed SQLite's bound-variable limit.\\n\\n**Testing / verification**\\n- `go build ./...`, `gofmt -l`, and `go vet ./internal/cli/` clean.\\n- `go test ./internal/cli/` — full package green, including the new tests. Confirmed on the committed tree (`git show HEAD`).\\n- New tests: chunked relations query at 20k symbols (the old single query bound 40001 params and errored with \\\"too many SQL variables\\\"); all six feature endpoints degrade to 200 + valid JSON on an unbuilt brain; loopback-only bind asserts `127.0.0.1`; CSP/nosniff applied through the real mux; a huge `?limit` clamps without panic; node/edge JSON field mappings.\\n- Manual: rendered the semantic graph at full scale (11,211 nodes / 44,844 edges) and full history (172,432 nodes) with no collapse or tab crash; exercised session replay, search, and the empty/unbuilt-brain states.\\n- An adversarial audit (7 dimensions, each finding independently verified) surfaced 8 issues; all are fixed in this branch: SQLite IN-clause variable-limit → chunked; `?limit=0` history ceiling bypass → clamped; search/palette stale-response race → sequence guard; plus the test-coverage gaps above.\\n\\n**No-egress**\\n- Loopback bind, embedded assets, disk-only reads, and a CSP enforced on every response. No outbound network of any kind.\\n\\n**Risk / rollback**\\n- Additive: a new command (~2.6k lines) and a one-line `root.go` change. The single shared change is chunking `findSemanticRelationsForSymbolsInSQLite` — behavior is identical for small symbol sets (one batch) and correct for large sets where it previously errored; the full package suite is green. Rollback: drop the branch.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/55/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/55/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            }\n          ],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"bounded-list\",\n      \"q\": \"repo:entireio/cli \\\"checkpoint list\\\" \\\"limit\\\"\",\n      \"rr\": [\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 6,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2718\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2718/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2718/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2718/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2718\",\n              \"id\": 5781708988,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABWJ3gvA\",\n              \"number\": 2718,\n              \"title\": \"Feature request: --author and --branch filters for entire checkpoint list\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"PhilipeGatis\",\n                \"id\": 4982462,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5ODI0NjI=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4982462?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipeGatis\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/PhilipeGatis\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipeGatis/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipeGatis/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipeGatis/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipeGatis/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipeGatis/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipeGatis/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipeGatis/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipeGatis/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipeGatis/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 4,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-09T16:56:53Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-12T12:14:35Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"### Problem or use case\\n\\nOn a team where several people use Entire in the same repo, teammates' pushed checkpoints already show up in `entire checkpoint list`, but there is no local way to narrow the list to one person, or to look at another branch without checking it out. Questions like \\\"what did Alice's sessions do on this feature?\\\" or \\\"what happened on `feat/x` while I'm on `main`?\\\" need either scrolling the full list or server-side `entire search`, which requires login and network access.\\n\\n### Desired behavior\\n\\n```shell\\n$ entire checkpoint list --author alice\\n$ entire checkpoint list --branch feat/login-timeout\\n$ entire checkpoint list --branch feat/login-timeout --author alice@example.com --json\\n```\\n\\n### Proposed solution\\n\\nTwo local-only filters on `entire checkpoint list` (human and `--json` views):\\n\\n- `--author <name|email>`: case-insensitive substring match on the commit author (like `git log --author`, without regex). Applied during the commit walk, **before** the list limit, so a teammate's older checkpoints aren't evicted by newer ones from others. Imported (commit-less) checkpoints have no author and are left out when the filter is set. `--json` gains `author_name` / `author_email`.\\n- `--branch <name>`: list checkpoints as if HEAD were that branch. Resolves `refs/heads/<name>`, then `refs/remotes/origin/<name>`. The default branch keeps the full DAG walk; other branches keep the first-parent walk that stops at the default branch, i.e. today's rules derived from the named ref instead of HEAD. Unknown branches return an error (merged-and-deleted branches are out of scope).\\n\\nBoth are rejected with `--pending` and combine with `--session`.\\n\\nI have a working prototype with tests (`mise run check` passes), stacked as two commits on my fork:\\n- `--author`: https://github.com/PhilipeGatis/cli/compare/main...feat/checkpoint-list-author-filter\\n- `--branch` on top: https://github.com/PhilipeGatis/cli/compare/feat/checkpoint-list-author-filter...feat/checkpoint-list-branch-filter\\n\\nQuestions before opening a PR:\\n1. One PR or two (author first, branch stacked)?\\n2. Should imported checkpoints appear with `--branch`? (They do in the current-branch view today.)\\n3. Remote fallback: only `origin`, or any remote / accept `origin/foo`?\\n4. `cli/git_operations.go` keeps its own `IsOnDefaultBranch` (ENT-129). The prototype adds `strategy.IsDefaultBranchName` and leaves that copy alone. OK?\\n\\n### Alternatives or workarounds\\n\\n- `entire search --author/--branch`: server-side only, needs an account.\\n- `git log --author=... --grep=Entire-Checkpoint`: works, but loses the checkpoint view, session info and `--json` shape.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2718/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2718/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1195\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1195/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1195/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1195/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/1195\",\n              \"id\": 4432837757,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCDe8fQ\",\n              \"number\": 1195,\n              \"title\": \"Search returns 0 results for Claude Code checkpoints despite successful capture (CLI 0.6.1 + 0.6.2-nightly)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"WrangleMeThis\",\n                \"id\": 283154621,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOEOCYvQ\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/283154621?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/WrangleMeThis\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/WrangleMeThis\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/WrangleMeThis/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/WrangleMeThis/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/WrangleMeThis/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/WrangleMeThis/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/WrangleMeThis/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/WrangleMeThis/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/WrangleMeThis/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/WrangleMeThis/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/WrangleMeThis/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 3,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-05-12T21:43:07Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-07T13:18:46Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"### Summary\\n\\nIn a real production monorepo with Entire installed via Path B (Entire wrapping Lefthook), capture works end-to-end for Claude Code sessions — trailers are attached, checkpoints land in `entire/checkpoints/v1`, the branch pushes to a separate private checkpoint remote, `entire activity` / `entire dispatch` / `entire checkpoint explain` all see the data — but `entire search` **and** `entire checkpoint search` **return 0 results for every query**, including queries that match exact content from the captured transcripts.\\n\\nThis is the Claude Code variant of [#1171](<https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/1171>) (Codex variant, same author, brand-new repo repro). Filing separately because:\\n\\n* Different agent (Claude Code, not Codex)\\n* Different repo profile (real multi-package monorepo, not a clean canary)\\n* Same end-state regardless: search is empty while every other surface sees the data\\n\\n### Environment\\n\\n* Entire CLI: pre-flight done on `0.6.2-nightly.202605090651.30e58ea3`, production rollout on stable `0.6.1`\\n* macOS arm64\\n* Agent: Claude Code ([claude.ai](<http://claude.ai>) / Claude Code CLI)\\n* Lefthook 1.13.6 (project) / 2.1.6 (system PATH)\\n* Hook architecture: Path B — Entire wraps Lefthook via `entire configure --force` in `prepare` script in `package.json`\\n* Separate private checkpoint remote: `agiterra/tankloop-checkpoints-private`\\n* GitHub App: Entire installed on `agiterra` org with `repository_selection=all`\\n\\n### What works\\n\\n* `entire status` — Enabled, Claude Code + Codex agents active\\n* Capture: every commit gets an `Entire-Checkpoint: <id>` trailer\\n* Push: `entire/checkpoints/v1` syncs to the checkpoint remote on every `git push`\\n* `entire checkpoint list` — shows local checkpoints (2 on `main`)\\n* `entire checkpoint explain <id>` — shows the full transcript, prompts, file list, tokens\\n* `entire activity` — shows 11 checkpoints across 3 repos, including all of today's `agiterra/tankloop` work, with proper agent attribution (Claude Code 64% / Codex 36%)\\n* `entire dispatch` — generates digests citing real repo activity\\n* PII redaction working in captured transcripts (verified: real emails replaced with `REDACTED_EMAIL`)\\n\\n### What fails\\n\\nAll search variants return empty:\\n\\n```\\n$ entire search \\\"lefthook\\\" --json\\n{ \\\"results\\\": [], \\\"total\\\": 0, \\\"page\\\": 1, \\\"total_pages\\\": 1, \\\"limit\\\": 25 }\\n\\n$ entire search \\\"redaction\\\" --json\\n{ \\\"results\\\": [], \\\"total\\\": 0, \\\"page\\\": 1, \\\"total_pages\\\": 1, \\\"limit\\\": 25 }\\n\\n$ entire search \\\"Path B\\\" --json\\n{ \\\"results\\\": [], \\\"total\\\": 0, \\\"page\\\": 1, \\\"total_pages\\\": 1, \\\"limit\\\": 25 }\\n\\n$ entire checkpoint search \\\"lefthook\\\" --json\\n{ \\\"results\\\": [], \\\"total\\\": 0, \\\"page\\\": 1, \\\"total_pages\\\": 1, \\\"limit\\\": 25 }\\n\\n$ entire checkpoint search \\\"\\\" --branch main --json\\n{ \\\"results\\\": [], \\\"total\\\": 0, \\\"page\\\": 1, \\\"total_pages\\\": 1, \\\"limit\\\": 25 }\\n```\\n\\nThese tokens are all in the captured transcripts and commit messages — verified via `entire checkpoint explain <id>` which prints them inline.\\n\\n### Sample checkpoints (real)\\n\\nFrom `entire checkpoint list` on `agiterra/tankloop` `main`:\\n\\n* `632b58b88c75` — commit `9f71259` (\\\"chore(agents): notify on pull when entire CLI is missing\\\")\\n* `b5bbb47b6e39` — commit `5465328` (\\\"feat(agents): adopt entire for session provenance ([#25](<https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/25>))\\\")\\n\\nBoth contain extensive Claude Code transcripts; neither is discoverable via search.\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\nOnce a checkpoint is visible in `entire activity` and `entire checkpoint explain` returns the transcript, an exact-token search from the captured prompts or transcript should be discoverable via `entire search` / `entire checkpoint search` after indexing completes.\\n\\n### Actual behavior\\n\\nSearch service returns empty for every query, no matter how recent or how stale the checkpoint, no matter which `--repo`, `--branch`, or `--author` filter is applied.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n`search` is a load-bearing skill for cross-agent context recall. Without it, `what-happened`, `search`, and the Entire skills wrapping these commands are effectively non-functional for our team. The marketing value of \\\"find prior work before changing X\\\" disappears.\\n\\n### Related\\n\\n* entireio/cli#1171 — Codex variant, clean repro, also from us (`agiterra` / `WrangleMeThis`). Same symptom, different agent.\\n\\n🤖 Peace , B.Sweet\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1195/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1195/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2089\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2089/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2089/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2089/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2089\",\n              \"id\": 5208592370,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABNnTP8g\",\n              \"number\": 2089,\n              \"title\": \"checkpoint explain --session reports \\\"No checkpoints found\\\" when the scan limit truncates (false negative; misleads the shipped search skill)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"marcioferreira-debug\",\n                \"id\": 265178343,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD85M5w\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/265178343?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/marcioferreira-debug\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/marcioferreira-debug\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/marcioferreira-debug/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/marcioferreira-debug/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/marcioferreira-debug/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/marcioferreira-debug/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/marcioferreira-debug/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/marcioferreira-debug/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/marcioferreira-debug/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/marcioferreira-debug/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/marcioferreira-debug/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-20T22:51:13Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-22T12:21:33Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"### Summary\\n\\n`entire checkpoint explain --session <id>` applies a default scan limit, but when that limit truncates the scan it reports **zero checkpoints in definitive language** rather than reporting truncation. The output simultaneously claims the history is empty and admits it may be hidden:\\n\\n```\\n  branch       <branch>\\n  session      <session-id>\\n  checkpoints  0\\n\\nNo checkpoints found on this branch.\\nCheckpoints will appear here after you save changes during an agent session.\\nnote: checkpoint list reached its scan limit; older checkpoints may be hidden. Run 'entire checkpoint explain --json --limit <N>' to see more.\\n```\\n\\nThe same command with an explicit limit returns the checkpoints immediately:\\n\\n```\\nentire checkpoint explain --session <id> --json --limit 2000\\n→ [ { \\\"checkpoint_id\\\": \\\"…\\\", \\\"session_id\\\": \\\"…\\\", \\\"agent\\\": \\\"Claude Code\\\", … }, … ]\\n```\\n\\nSo the data is present and reachable. Only the default-limit path misreports it.\\n\\n### Why this matters more than a cosmetic wording issue\\n\\nThe headline (`checkpoints 0` + `No checkpoints found`) and the footnote (`older checkpoints may be hidden`) contradict each other, and the wrong half is the prominent one. A human may read down to the note. **An agent generally does not.**\\n\\nThis bites the search skill that Entire itself installs (`--search-skill`, `ENTIRE-MANAGED SEARCH SKILL v1`). Observed live: a subagent following the shipped v1 prompt concluded\\n\\n> \\\"the accessible session transcripts in Entire don't contain the diagnostic discussion … the decision-making appears to have been done post-hoc in commit messages rather than during an interactive session transcript that Entire captured.\\\"\\n\\nThat was false. The session file held **306** matches for the search term, and `--limit 2000` returned the checkpoints at once. The agent reported absence of history as a finding, with no signal to the user that the lookup had been truncated.\\n\\nStep 5 of the shipped v1 prompt compounds it:\\n\\n> \\\"If nothing looks right, rerun a narrower `entire search --json --compact` instead of explaining many hits or switching tools.\\\"\\n\\nWhen the cause of \\\"nothing looks like it exists\\\" is a silent truncation, *narrowing* is exactly the wrong recovery — it makes the false negative more confident. The prompt has no instruction to raise the limit before concluding absence.\\n\\n### Environment\\n\\n* Entire CLI **0.10.2** (go1.26.6, darwin/arm64)\\n* Checkpoint backend: `git-refs`\\n* Agents: Claude Code + Codex\\n* ~900 checkpoints in the repo, created by the history import that `entire enable` offers (`Imported 921 turn(s) from 29 session(s)`)\\n* Private GitHub repo; all checkpoint refs confirmed pushed to origin\\n\\nPossibly relevant: the imported checkpoints carry `\\\"is_logs_only\\\": true`, and some `message` fields are terminal scrollback rather than prompts. I did not test whether the same truncation reports zero on natively-captured (non-imported) checkpoints.\\n\\n### Reproduction\\n\\n1. Enable Entire on a repo with substantial agent history, accepting the history import at `enable` (enough to exceed the default scan limit — ~900 checkpoints here).\\n2. Pick a session id known to contain matching content.\\n3. `entire checkpoint explain --session <id>` → `checkpoints 0`, `No checkpoints found on this branch.`\\n4. `entire checkpoint explain --session <id> --json --limit 2000` → checkpoints returned.\\n\\n### Suggested fixes\\n\\nAny one of these would remove the false negative; the first two seem most valuable:\\n\\n1. **Do not print `No checkpoints found` when the scan was truncated.** If the limit was hit and zero matched, that is an *inconclusive* result, not an empty one. Say so in the headline — e.g. `checkpoints 0 of ≥N scanned (scan limit reached — pass --limit to widen)`.\\n2. **Make the `--json` shape carry it.** A `\\\"truncated\\\": true` / `\\\"scan_limit_reached\\\": true` field would let agents detect this programmatically instead of relying on prose in a note they don't read.\\n3. **Auto-widen once** when a `--session`-scoped lookup returns zero and the limit was hit, since a session-scoped query has a naturally bounded result set.\\n4. **Update the shipped search skill** to require an explicit high-limit lookup before an agent may state that history has no match. (Patched locally, but it is an `ENTIRE-MANAGED` file, so a `--force` reinstall or a v2 skill will silently overwrite the fix.)\\n\\n### Related\\n\\nAdjacent but distinct from #1195 — there, `entire search` returns 0 while `checkpoint explain` sees the data. Here it is `checkpoint explain` itself under-reporting. I also saw search return only `type: \\\"commit\\\"` hits while matching transcripts existed, which may be the same surface as #1195.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2089/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2089/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1171\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1171/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1171/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1171/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/1171\",\n              \"id\": 4413408976,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBw9G0A\",\n              \"number\": 1171,\n              \"title\": \"Search stays empty after successful Codex & Claude checkpoint capture in clean repo repro\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"WrangleMeThis\",\n                \"id\": 283154621,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOEOCYvQ\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/283154621?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/WrangleMeThis\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/WrangleMeThis\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/WrangleMeThis/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/WrangleMeThis/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/WrangleMeThis/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/WrangleMeThis/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/WrangleMeThis/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/WrangleMeThis/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/WrangleMeThis/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/WrangleMeThis/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/WrangleMeThis/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 3,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-05-09T18:10:22Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-07T13:18:47Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"### Summary\\n\\nIn a brand-new clean GitHub repo, Entire successfully captures a Codex checkpoint, injects an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer, pushes `entire/checkpoints/v1`, and shows the checkpoint in both `entire activity` and `entire dispatch`, but `entire search` / `entire checkpoint search` still return 0 results for an exact unique token from the committed file.\\n\\nThis repro was done after normalizing git identity and using a strict order of operations to avoid mixed authors, preexisting branches, or GitHub-generated starter commits.\\n\\n### Clean repro\\n\\nEnvironment:\\n- Entire CLI 0.6.1\\n- macOS arm64\\n- Agent: Codex CLI\\n\\nOrder of operations:\\n1. Set git identity to `Brian Sweet <brian@agiterra.io>`.\\n2. Create a brand-new local repo with `git init -b main`.\\n3. Make the initial commit locally: `chore: initial empty repo`.\\n4. Create the GitHub repo from that local history and push it.\\n5. Run `entire enable --agent codex --force --telemetry=false`.\\n6. Start Codex inside the repo.\\n7. Have Codex create a plain text file with a unique token, commit it, keep the hook-added trailer, push, and exit cleanly.\\n\\nControlled repo:\\n- `BrianSweet/entire-orderops-local-canary-20260509-130023`\\n\\nControlled canary commit:\\n- commit: `df6c7e091ac2493aea605da737cc6780ffca6173`\\n- trailer: `Entire-Checkpoint: bee65c2cc740`\\n- committed token: `zz-entire-orderops-local-canary-20260509-f6`\\n\\n### What works\\n\\n- `git show -s --format=%B HEAD` shows the trailer\\n- `git ls-remote --heads origin main entire/checkpoints/v1` shows both branches on origin\\n- `entire checkpoint list` shows checkpoint `bee65c2cc740`\\n- `entire checkpoint explain --commit df6c7e091ac2493aea605da737cc6780ffca6173 --short --no-pager` succeeds\\n- `entire dispatch --since 1d --repos BrianSweet/entire-orderops-local-canary-20260509-130023` sees the canary test\\n- `entire activity` shows the repo and the Codex checkpoint/commit\\n\\n### What fails\\n\\nBoth of these return 0 results for the exact token from the committed file:\\n\\n```bash\\nentire search \\\"zz-entire-orderops-local-canary-20260509-f6\\\" --json\\n\\nentire checkpoint search \\\"zz-entire-orderops-local-canary-20260509-f6\\\" \\\\\\n  --json --repo BrianSweet/entire-orderops-local-canary-20260509-130023\\n```\\n\\nObserved result from both:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"results\\\": [],\\n  \\\"total\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"page\\\": 1,\\n  \\\"total_pages\\\": 1,\\n  \\\"limit\\\": 25\\n}\\n```\\n\\nI rechecked again at **2026-05-09 13:04:24 EDT** and search was still empty while `entire activity` continued to show the checkpointed commit.\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\nOnce a checkpointed commit is visible in `entire activity` and `entire dispatch`, an exact-token search from the committed file should be discoverable via `entire search` / `entire checkpoint search` after indexing completes.\\n\\n### Actual behavior\\n\\nCheckpoint capture, local explain, branch push, dispatch, and activity all work, but search remains empty.\\n\\n### Why this repro should be high-signal\\n\\nThis was intentionally reduced to:\\n- one brand-new repo\\n- one consistent git author identity\\n- one local initial commit (not GitHub-generated)\\n- one plain text canary file\\n- one Codex session started inside the repo\\n- one successful trailer-linked commit\\n\\nSo this looks like a search/indexing-specific failure rather than a hook/install/repo-history problem.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1171/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1171/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1965\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1965/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1965/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1965/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/1965\",\n              \"id\": 5127778171,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABMaOvew\",\n              \"number\": 1965,\n              \"title\": \"warn when a coding agent commits in an enabled repo but no session is being recorded\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"id\": 34813274,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-12T06:08:26Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-14T09:35:47Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"### Problem or use case\\n\\nan enabled repo can silently accept agent-driven commits while recording nothing. entire's git hooks run on every commit, in the right repo, with settings loaded, and when they find no session they log a debug line (`manual_commit_hooks.go:414`) and move on. the user finds out much later, when they go looking for a session that was never recorded. i'd like to propose that this combination becomes a warning instead.\\n\\nhow i got here: i ran a long claude code session against this repo. it created a worktree, wrote a fix, committed twice, opened a pr. days later i wanted to look back at the session:\\n\\n```\\n~/W/o/e/c/fix-checkpoint-metadata-bloat> entire checkpoint list\\n  branch       fix-checkpoint-metadata-bloat\\n  checkpoints  0\\n```\\n\\nnothing on the branch and nothing in the web ui. the mistake was mine: i use a bare-clone worktree layout (a parent folder holding `.bare/` plus one directory per worktree) and i started the agent in the parent folder instead of inside a worktree. agents read their repo-level config from the directory the session starts in, and that's where entire's hooks live (`.claude/settings.json` in my case, and the equivalent checked-in files for the other integrations). the parent folder has none, so no agent hook ever fired. the folder doesn't feel wrong either: its `.git` file points at the bare gitdir, so git commands work, branches resolve, commits succeed.\\n\\nbut the specific mistake matters less than the shape of it. \\\"agent committing, nothing recorded\\\" is reachable many ways:\\n\\n- the agent session started outside the worktree (my case, and possible with any integrated agent, and from any directory above a normal repo)\\n- the hooks are registered but the binary they invoke fails at startup (i also had a second, older `entire` on my path that can't parse this repo's current settings schema; every hook invocation through it would die silently)\\n- the hooks were removed or drifted out of the agent's settings file\\n- session state was wiped mid-conversation with `entire clean`\\n\\nno one warning can name the cause, and it doesn't need to. the commit is the anchor: at that moment the git hook already has everything needed to notice. entire is enabled in the worktree. the commit is agent-driven (claude code sets `CLAUDECODE=1` in the environment of every command it runs, verified, and it also sets `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`, so the warning could even name the unrecorded session; the `interactive` package already reads `GEMINI_CLI`, `COPILOT_CLI` and `PI_CODING_AGENT` as agent markers for tty detection; markers for the remaining integrations would need to be verified per agent). and no session anywhere in the repo has seen recent activity.\\n\\n### Desired behavior\\n\\n```\\n$ git commit -m \\\"fix: ...\\\"\\n[entire] a coding agent is committing but no session is being recorded.\\ndid the agent session start outside this worktree? run 'entire doctor' to check.\\n\\n$ entire doctor          # run from the layout root\\n  ✗ you're at the root of a bare-clone worktree layout, not inside a worktree.\\n    entire is enabled in 3 worktrees below this directory:\\n      main/  fix-a/  fix-b/\\n    agent sessions started here are not recorded. start them inside a worktree.\\n```\\n\\na nice property of the git-hook route: hook stderr goes to whatever process ran `git commit`, which is the agent itself, so the warning lands in the agent's transcript and the agent can pass it on to the user immediately.\\n\\n### Proposed solution\\n\\n**warn when:** settings are enabled, an agent env marker is present, and no session anywhere in the repo shows recent activity (session state carries `LastInteractionTime`, so \\\"recent\\\" is a cheap check against a live window rather than a guess). cause-agnostic on purpose: it catches every path into \\\"nothing recorded\\\" without having to detect any of them specifically. rate-limited the way `warnStaleEndedSessions` already does it (sentinel file mtime in the session-state dir, fail-open), once per worktree until a live session appears.\\n\\na note on why the condition is \\\"no recently active session\\\" rather than the more obvious \\\"no session state files at all\\\": ended sessions deliberately leave their state files behind (they're kept for amend-trailer restoration), and stray files accumulate in long-lived repos. i checked my own repo while writing this: `.git/entire-sessions/` contains leftover state from months ago, so a zero-files condition would never fire anywhere a session has ever run. recency is the version of the signal that keeps working after the first week.\\n\\n**stay quiet when:** a session is recently active somewhere in the repo, even if not in this worktree. that shape is usually deliberate (task fan-out into fresh worktrees, review in isolated worktrees, an agent cd-ing between checkouts), the driving session is alive and recording in its own worktree, and `entire session adopt` already covers moving it. warning here would mostly nag power users.\\n\\n**supporting pieces:**\\n\\n- the env markers could live in the agent registry, next to the per-agent facts each integration already declares (protected dirs, transcript layout). the hook checks the union over registered agents instead of a hardcoded list, each integration verifies its own agent's marker, and new integrations get detection for free.\\n- `entire doctor` could learn to diagnose the most common cause. detection: cwd `.git` is a file pointing at a bare gitdir, registered worktrees are children of cwd, and at least one of them has entire enabled while cwd has none. output: the message shown above, listing the enabled worktrees by name so the fix is a visible `cd`. no auto-fix on purpose: writing agent config at the layout root would be wrong (there's nothing to record against) and would teach the wrong habit. doctor's existing wiring checks (`checkClaudeCodeHookDrift`) already help with the hook-drift causes.\\n- these two land together or not at all: the warning's \\\"run `entire doctor`\\\" hint is only honest once doctor can actually recognize the situation. today doctor reports a healthy worktree (correctly, the worktree's wiring is fine) and has no concept of the layout root.\\n\\n**edge cases i thought about:**\\n\\n- human commits with no agent env never warn.\\n- a human committing from a shell that inherited an agent marker gets misread once, then the rate limit caps it.\\n- someone deliberately running an untracked agent in an enabled repo eats one line, and a settings switch (`warnings.unrecorded_agent_commit: false` or similar) turns it off for good.\\n- agents without a verified marker are missed, which is the status quo; registry-driven detection makes each fix a one-liner in the integration.\\n- there's no race with the first commit of a healthy session: session state is written at session start (`lifecycle.go` initializes it on the session-start event), before the agent can run anything, so if hooks fired at all a recently-active session exists. its absence is exactly the signal.\\n- a human committing by hand while no agent has run recently, in a repo with an agent marker leaked into the shell: the worst-case false positive, one line, once, suppressible.\\n\\nhappy to take this if the shape sounds right, and equally happy if you'd rather solve it differently.\\n\\n### Alternatives or workarounds\\n\\n- discipline: always `cd` into a worktree before starting the agent. works until it doesn't, which is how i got here.\\n- running `entire doctor` proactively from inside a worktree confirms the wiring, though it reports healthy in this scenario, and in practice you only run doctor once you already suspect something.\\n- `entire import` (experimental) can backfill the lost session from the agent's own transcript after the fact, which recovers the data but not the moment the warning was needed.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1965/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1965/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2980\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2980/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2980/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2980/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2980\",\n              \"id\": 6110766677,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABbDrmVQ\",\n              \"number\": 2980,\n              \"title\": \"Post-push session attach publishes linked_commits but checkpoint remains absent from activity and Dispatch\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"lcv-leo\",\n                \"id\": 268063598,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD_pTbg\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/268063598?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/lcv-leo\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 7,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-30T00:14:37Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-05T17:58:31Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-11-05T17:58:31Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Context and impact\\n\\nWe use Entire alongside GitHub for real changes to a private web application. We reached this problem while trying to generate the team's Dispatch after a squash merge, not while constructing a synthetic checkpoint test. This report was prepared with Codex assistance at the repository operator's request; the observations below come from the official CLI and API responses.\\n\\nThe original checkpoint is available remotely, but has no branch membership after the feature branch is deleted. We understand why a squash commit without an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer needs repair. The problem reported here is that the documented post-push `session attach` repair reports success and publishes `linked_commits`, yet the activity API still cannot find the new checkpoint or link it to that commit. As a result, a Dispatch for the recent release says there are no checkpoints. A wider-window Dispatch succeeds but omits the recent release.\\n\\n## Environment\\n\\n- Windows, PowerShell; GitHub private repository `LCV-Ideas-Software/astrologo-app`.\\n- Installed CLI: `0.12.2-lcv.windows-console.1+idle-fallback.2`, based on v0.12.2. These are the locally authorized Windows-console and stale sibling-session patches tracked in #2926 / #2972 and #2979. **I have not reproduced this with an unmodified binary**, and am not claiming otherwise. No further binary, Git identity, signing, or hook configuration change was made for this investigation.\\n- Git-ref checkpoint storage, mirror placements ready in BR and US. The repository view resolves the activity API to `aws-us-east-2.api.entire.io` and repo ID `01M5Z457WFR60E17SC5GNHDRH5`.\\n- The affected captured session is about 3.3 MB, not the multi-GB session from #2933. It was captured during actual work on PR #540.\\n\\n## What led us here\\n\\n1. PR #540's signed feature commit was `6405cf2a09b158721a63bcbcdac933067ee188a2`, checkpoint `01M64TPXT3N02BC8RX20YX4XQB`, session `01a1896c-8d01-77d2-afeb-82b5439fbfcc`.\\n2. The published squash commit is `0b227a331c1ea32b594c8916336ac8a42d9a3660`. Its message mentions the checkpoint in prose but does **not** contain an `Entire-Checkpoint:` trailer. The feature branch was deleted after publication.\\n3. `entire checkpoint explain 01M64TPXT3N02BC8RX20YX4XQB --repo gh/LCV-Ideas-Software/astrologo-app --json` succeeds. The activity checkpoint-resolution response reports `branches: []`, `default_branch: null`, and `suggested_branch: null` for that checkpoint.\\n4. The activity API's checkpoint-status response counts 12 checkpoints and reports access allowed. The main-branch list contains only one older checkpoint from PR #528 and reports `history_status: \\\"complete\\\"`. Thus this is not a missing login or an empty repository.\\n5. I queued the native mirror resync. It returned `status: \\\"queued\\\"`; the main list still contained only the older checkpoint.\\n6. I checked the official `session attach` help and preview. It explicitly said the published commit would remain unchanged and a new checkpoint would carry the exact commit link. There were no unrelated outgoing checkpoint refs. The configured Git email equals the target commit author's email.\\n7. I ran:\\n\\n   ```text\\n   entire session attach 01a1896c-8d01-77d2-afeb-82b5439fbfcc --agent codex --commit 0b227a331c1ea32b594c8916336ac8a42d9a3660 --force\\n   ```\\n\\n   The command warned that there were no new turns since the original checkpoint, then returned exit 0:\\n\\n   ```text\\n   Created checkpoint 01M6524YWT7N18SBAWPA444AK6\\n   Linked to commit 0b227a331c1e in the checkpoint; the commit is unchanged (already pushed)\\n   [entire] Pushing 1 checkpoint ref(s) to origin..... done\\n   Pushed checkpoint metadata to origin\\n   ```\\n\\n8. The new checkpoint's `metadata.json` contains:\\n\\n   ```json\\n   \\\"linked_commits\\\": [{\\n     \\\"sha\\\": \\\"0b227a331c1ea32b594c8916336ac8a42d9a3660\\\",\\n     \\\"repo\\\": \\\"gh/LCV-Ideas-Software/astrologo-app\\\"\\n   }]\\n   ```\\n\\n   It also has `files_touched: null` and an empty session prompt. I am not claiming it represents new work; this was a repair of the link to an already captured real session.\\n\\n9. `git ls-remote origin refs/entire/checkpoints/K6/01M6524YWT7N18SBAWPA444AK6` confirms the published ref at `d58987752d72ca61358bbf1103f101c5cb4e308d`. The main commit is unchanged. I queued a second resync **after this new ref was published**.\\n10. Following that resync, the main list still has only the old checkpoint. At 00:12:27 UTC on 30 October 2026 (21:12:27 in Brazil on 29 October), the API still returned HTTP 404 `{\\\"error\\\":\\\"checkpoint not found\\\"}` for the newly attached checkpoint. This observation is bounded to the few minutes after the repair; it is not a claim that ingestion can never complete. The commit-checkpoint endpoint also returned an empty list with complete history.\\n11. A Dispatch covering 25–29 October successfully completed with **one** checkpoint, from PR #528. This is a useful control: generation works for the existing indexed membership. It does not demonstrate coverage of PR #540 or validate the new attachment.\\n\\n## Expected behavior / requested guidance\\n\\nWhat is the supported way to attach an **already captured session with no new turns** to an already-pushed squash commit, without rewriting shared Git history or fabricating another code change?\\n\\nIf `session attach` is that repair, please check whether the empty incremental attachment or `linked_commits` ingestion is preventing the association from becoming visible. If asynchronous indexing needs a different official trigger, please document that trigger and an observable completion status. The CLI success message alone currently does not let us verify the repaired association.\\n\\nI read #321 (closed) and #1889 (regional Dispatch routing). This report concerns the present post-push attachment result and missing activity membership, rather than assuming a new instance of the older routing issue. Full private evidence is retained for the operator; this report intentionally excludes source code, transcripts, prompts, credentials, and personal data.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2980/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2980/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            }\n          ],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 30,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2605\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2605/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2605/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2605/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2605\",\n              \"id\": 5614343491,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABFfcnFA\",\n              \"number\": 2605,\n              \"title\": \"List remote-only imported checkpoints in fresh git-refs clones\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"nodo\",\n                \"id\": 829178,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjgyOTE3OA==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/829178?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/nodo\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-28T12:13:59Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-28T12:37:21Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2605\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2605\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2605.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2605.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1438\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\n## Problem\\r\\n\\r\\n`entire checkpoint list` shows 0 checkpoints in a fresh clone of a git-refs repo whose checkpoints are all imported, although `git ls-remote origin 'refs/entire/checkpoints/*'` shows them.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Root cause\\r\\n\\r\\nNot the remote selection: `ListCheckpointRefsOnRemote` already queries origin when no `checkpoint_remote` is set (the #1771 description is outdated there).\\r\\n\\r\\nImported checkpoints carry no commit trailer, so they only surface through `getImportedPendingCheckpoints`. That function opened a second store and listed **local refs only**. Remote-discovered stubs would have been dropped anyway: `Imported` is unknown until the ref is read.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Fix\\r\\n\\r\\n- Reuse the discovery-enabled List from `getBranchCheckpoints` and hydrate remote-only stubs that could be imported: legacy-hex IDs not linked by a commit trailer. Imports always get hex IDs (`agentimport.DeriveCheckpointID`); ULIDs are native git-refs checkpoints and are skipped.\\r\\n- Each candidate is fetched lazily, one ref at a time. No bulk `git fetch refs/entire/checkpoints/*` (keeps #1770's constraint).\\r\\n- Hydration recovers `CreatedAt`, so legacy hex IDs (no ULID timestamp) sort correctly.\\r\\n- On feature branches, main's trailers also mark checkpoints as linked, so they aren't fetched just to learn they're not imported.\\r\\n- Both hydration passes share one `ListHydrationPassTimeout` budget (was two back-to-back 30s passes). Stubs skipped or failed are counted in a stderr warning.\\r\\n- Imported prompts are read only for entries that survive `--limit`.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Known trade-off\\r\\n\\r\\nA fresh clone with many unlinked legacy-hex checkpoints still fetches them one per ref, bounded by the 30s budget, converging across runs as refs become local. Making importedness visible names-only (ref namespace or index ref) would remove this; left as a follow-up since it's a storage-format change.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Testing\\r\\n\\r\\n- `TestGetBranchCheckpoints_ListsRemoteOnlyImportedCheckpoints`: no `checkpoint_remote`, two remote-only imported legacy-hex checkpoints listed newest-first by `CreatedAt`; an unlinked ULID stub is not fetched.\\r\\n- `TestGetBranchCheckpoints_FeatureBranchSkipsMainLinkedStubs`: main-linked stub is not fetched on a feature branch.\\r\\n- Both fail without the respective change.\\r\\n- Manually: fresh `entire repo clone /et/nodo/ent-1` now shows `checkpoints 2` (was 0).\\r\\n- `mise run check` passes.\\r\\n\\r\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\r\\n\\r\\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01XcFpdubBsdwHLGfZyZHWPg\\r\\n\\r\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes checkpoint list enumeration and remote ref hydration timing/budgets; wrong linked/imported filtering could hide checkpoints or cause extra fetches, but behavior is bounded by existing timeouts and covered by new integration tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Fixes **empty checkpoint lists on fresh clones** when checkpoints are **imported** (no commit trailers) but only exist as **remote git-refs**.\\n> \\n> `getBranchCheckpoints` now reuses the discovery-enabled store list and runs an **imported pass** that **lazy-hydrates** remote **legacy-hex** stubs (not commit-trailer **linked**, not native ULIDs) to read `Imported` and `CreatedAt` for sorting. **Trailer-linked** IDs are tracked during the commit walk; on **feature branches**, `markTrailerLinked` also scans shared/main history (including merge side branches) so main-linked stubs are not fetched just to exclude them.\\n> \\n> **List hydration** and the imported pass share one **`ListHydrationPassTimeout`** budget via `hydrateListedWithin`; imported **prompts** load only after the display **limit** is applied. Stderr **warnings** cover budget/fetch failures.\\n> \\n> Integration tests cover remote-only imported listing (CreatedAt order, no ULID fetch), feature-branch skip of main-linked stubs, and shared remote-discovery test helpers.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 2eae3f976cbd218b17a5a6233a21277ecced2c73. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2605/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2605/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2875\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2875/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2875/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2875/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2875\",\n              \"id\": 5996926699,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABKPPHAg\",\n              \"number\": 2875,\n              \"title\": \"Make the checkpoint list remote timeout configurable\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"entire[bot]\",\n                \"id\": 254015822,\n                \"node_id\": \"BOT_kgDODyP5Tg\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/2626939?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/entire\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"Bot\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-23T11:28:32Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-23T12:30:49Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-23T12:30:47Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2875\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2875\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2875.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2875.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-23T12:30:47Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1667\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n`entire checkpoint list` gives each remote 5 seconds to list `refs/entire/checkpoints/*`. When a remote takes longer, checkpoints pushed from another machine drop out of the list. This adds `strategy_options.checkpoint_ref_list_timeout_seconds` to change that budget.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n`checkpointRefListTimeout` in `git_operations.go` bounds each `git ls-remote` that remote checkpoint discovery runs. When it expires, that remote's checkpoints drop out of the list. With one remote the CLI warns on stderr; when the elected remote times out but `origin` answers, nothing warns. Remotes with many refs take longer to answer: `ls-remote` sends no `ref-prefix` for the `refs/entire/checkpoints/*` pattern, so the remote advertises every ref and git filters them locally.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n`settings.CheckpointRefListTimeoutValue` reads `strategy_options.checkpoint_ref_list_timeout_seconds`, and `listCheckpointRefsOnRemote` uses it on both the dedicated `checkpoint_remote` path and the read-candidate path. The option works in `settings.json` or per machine in `settings.local.json`. The accessor ignores values that aren't positive numbers and caps values above 120 at 2 minutes, one full checkpoint read fetch (`remote.ReadFetchTimeout`), since the value usually comes from a committed `settings.json`. The key lives under `strategy_options` because the strict settings loader rejects unknown top-level keys, which would make a committed `settings.json` unloadable for older CLIs. README and `docs/architecture/ref-checkpoint-backend.md` document the option.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- Unit tests cover the accessor, including the cap and a value that would overflow `time.Duration`, and a `settings.local.json` override read through the real loader.\\n- Two listing tests run against an HTTP remote that never answers, one per path. With the override disabled, both fail at 60 s instead of finishing under their 20 s bound.\\n- A rebuilt binary against a remote whose `ls-remote` takes 7 s lists the missing checkpoint once the setting is 10, including the multi-remote case that dropped it without a warning.\\n- `mise run lint`: 0 issues. The Vogon canary passes. `mise run check` fails locally on two tests outside this change: `TestAttachCommit_FetchesBeforeDecidingAHeadIsUnpushed`, whose setup assumes a push by URL leaves `origin/main` alone (git 2.56 updates it), and `TestDialLatencies`, a flake that passes 10 of 10 runs on its own and failed once under load when another test bound the port it had closed.\\n\\nNot in scope: the silent drop when one of several remotes times out.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01N29n9Hg5en5sFgsbZUkyqo\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2875/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2875/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2229\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2229/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2229/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2229/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2229\",\n              \"id\": 5318936348,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABB1YGrg\",\n              \"number\": 2229,\n              \"title\": \"fix: cap local git-blob reads on checkpoint trees\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"id\": 257360244,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-02T02:18:57Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-02T11:18:53Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2229\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2229\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2229.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2229.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1211\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- `readSummaryFromCheckpointTree` and sibling readers pulled checkpoint metadata/prompt/transcript content via go-git's `file.Contents()` with no size cap. Checkpoint trees are not always locally authored — they can be fetched from a shared/pushed remote (`entire/checkpoints/v1`, or a per-checkpoint ref), which any collaborator with checkpoint-push access, or a compromised/malicious remote, controls the bytes of. An oversized blob was read into memory in full — a memory-exhaustion DoS reachable via routine commands (`entire checkpoint explain`, `checkpoint list`, `entire status`).\\n- The HTTP checkpoint reader already caps the equivalent read (`checkpoint_api_reader.go`'s `maxAPITranscriptBytes`, `LimitReader+1`); the local git-blob path had no equivalent.\\n- Adds `readBlobContents` (`fetching_tree.go`), capped at `agent.MaxChunkSize` (50MB) — the same limit the store already writes transcripts under, so anything this store wrote stays readable, and anything larger signals tampering/corruption. Callers that would otherwise treat a content-read failure as \\\"field absent, keep going\\\" now check for `ErrCheckpointBlobTooLarge` and fail loudly instead of silently degrading to a truncated/empty result.\\n\\n## Known follow-up (not yet covered here, same fix pattern applies)\\n- `ephemeral.go`'s two shadow-branch-tree transcript reads\\n- `migrate.go`'s metadata read\\n- `persistent.go`'s remaining ~5 sites (session metadata at `readCommittedInfoFromCheckpointTree`, asset reinjection, chunk reassembly, and the two legacy-filename fallback reads at the end of `readTranscriptFromTree`)\\n\\nFlagging these explicitly rather than silently leaving them — will follow up with the same `readBlobContents` helper.\\n\\n## Verification\\n- `go build ./cmd/entire/...` passes.\\n- Existing checkpoint-package test suite (`TestReadSessionContent*`, `TestUpdatePersistentRef*`, etc.) passes unchanged with the fix in place.\\n- A dedicated oversized-blob (50MB+) reproduction test is deferred — writing/committing a 50MB fixture is exactly the kind of CPU-heavy operation worth avoiding in this pass; will add before merge or in the follow-up.\\n- Full `mise run check` deferred to a follow-up pass to keep local CI load down.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n- [x] `go build` passes\\n- [x] Existing test suite green with the fix\\n- [ ] Dedicated oversized-blob reproduction test (deferred)\\n- [ ] Remaining call sites (ephemeral.go, migrate.go, persistent.go x5) — follow-up\\n- [ ] Full `mise run check` (deferred, will run before merge)\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2229/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2229/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1727\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1727/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1727/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1727/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1727\",\n              \"id\": 4864903377,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7wpwwG\",\n              \"number\": 1727,\n              \"title\": \"fix(explain): find checkpoints merged into non-default target branches\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"entire[bot]\",\n                \"id\": 254015822,\n                \"node_id\": \"BOT_kgDODyP5Tg\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/2626939?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/entire\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"Bot\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-07-12T01:19:03Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-13T12:54:55Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1727\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1727\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1727.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1727.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Trail: https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/834\\n\\nFixes #931.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nMerging a feature branch into a target branch dropped every session reference — checkpoint links and agent labels — from the target branch whenever the merge produced a merge commit and the target was not the repository's default branch. `entire checkpoint list` and `entire checkpoint explain` showed nothing for the merged work on that branch.\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\n`getBranchCheckpoints` and `getAssociatedCommits` scan history for `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers. On every branch that is not the repository default, they used a **first-parent-only** walk. Checkpoints brought in by a merge live on the merge commit's **second** parent, which a first-parent walk never visits — so the references vanished from the target branch.\\n\\nA prior fix restored a full DAG walk, but only for the repository default branch (`isOnDefault`). Every other merge target stayed broken:\\n\\n- a non-default target such as a `release` branch, or\\n- `main` itself, when git resolves the default branch elsewhere (e.g. `origin/HEAD` still points at `master`).\\n\\nTrue fast-forward merges were already fine — the moved commits and their trailers become the target's linear (first-parent) history — which is why the symptom tracked \\\"merge commit into a non-default target\\\" rather than literally fast-forward.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nReplace the first-parent walk on non-default branches with `walkBranchOwnCommits`: a DAG walk that follows **every parent not reachable from the default branch**, pruning (never descending into) commits shared with the default branch.\\n\\n- Discovers checkpoints merged in via second parents (the #931 fix).\\n- Still excludes the default branch's own history at the merge base — the exact property that motivated first-parent traversal — so \\\"main merged into a feature branch\\\" continues to exclude main's checkpoints, and the walk never explodes into main's full history.\\n- Bounded by the existing `commitScanLimit`; zero new cost on write/commit/push paths.\\n\\n### One adjacent read-path gap closed alongside it\\n\\n- **Deep-history leak in the reachable-from-default set.** `computeReachableFromMain` marked only the most recent `MaxCommitTraversalDepth` (1000) commits of main's first-parent chain. A branch that merged main in long ago — with main since advanced past that bound — left the merged-in former-main-tip outside the set, so the walk descended into main's older history and surfaced main's checkpoints on the branch (the leak invariant, in reverse). The scan stays **bounded** (`mainSpineScanLimit`, ~60ms regardless of main length — an unbounded scan was multiple seconds on a repo with tens of thousands of commits and runs on every read); when it stops before main's root it falls back to a **commit-date frontier** — any commit at or before the oldest scanned main commit is treated as main's history. This is the same commit-date boundary git's own `rev-list` uses for `main..HEAD`: it keeps the deep-history leak closed (a former main tip merged in beyond the window is older than the frontier, so still pruned) while erring toward exclusion (past the bound it may hide a branch-unique commit older than the frontier rather than risk a leak). First-parent-only semantics are preserved, so merged-in feature commits are still shown, and the scan runs once per command.\\n\\n### Out of scope: the ephemeral (shadow-branch) counterpart\\n\\nThe same \\\"first-parent misses a merge's second parent\\\" shape exists in the **temporary / in-progress** (shadow-branch) read path (`isShadowBranchReachable`). Making it merge-aware trades one harm for another — a full-DAG walk leaks a default-branch session's in-progress checkpoints onto a branch that merged the default branch in, while pruning shared-with-main hides the active session on a brand-new branch (`checkout -b` then start coding, before the first commit). The two are the same topological case and irreducible without persisting the session's origin branch, a feature-sized write-path change. This PR therefore leaves the shadow path at its **pre-existing first-parent-only behavior** (`isShadowBranchReachable` is byte-identical to `main`) and tracks the fix as follow-up #1730. #931 itself is a committed-checkpoint read-path bug.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n`go test ./cmd/entire/cli/... ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/...` green; `gofmt -s` and `golangci-lint` (0 issues) clean; affected tests also pass under `-race`.\\n\\nTraversal scoping is locked down in **both** directions — merged-in discovery and default-branch exclusion — and every case below is mutation-verified: removing the reachable-from-default prune fails every exclusion assertion; reverting to a first-parent-only walk fails every discovery assertion; restoring the depth limit fails the deep-history leak test.\\n\\n- `TestGetBranchCheckpoints_NonDefaultTargetFindsMergedCheckpoints` — the merged checkpoint is found on a non-default target, and a default-only checkpoint does not leak. The target is anchored at the default branch's tip so that default-only checkpoint is a genuine first-parent ancestor (previously it branched from the base commit, which made the \\\"must not leak\\\" assertion vacuous — it passed even with the prune removed).\\n- `TestGetBranchCheckpoints_MainMergedIntoFeatureExcludesMainCheckpoint` — merging the default branch INTO a feature branch does not surface the default branch's checkpoints (they arrive on the merge's second parent).\\n- `TestGetBranchCheckpoints_OctopusMergeIntoNonDefaultTarget` — an octopus merge (three feature parents) surfaces every merged checkpoint; default-branch checkpoints stay excluded.\\n- `TestGetBranchCheckpoints_NestedMergeIntoNonDefaultTarget` — a transitively merged sub-feature checkpoint (sub-feature → feature A → release) is discovered.\\n- `TestGetBranchCheckpoints_DeepHistoryDoesNotLeakMainCheckpoint` — with main advanced past the scan bound, an old main checkpoint merged in via a former-main-tip does not leak onto the branch (the commit-date frontier fail-safe prunes it). Fails without the fail-safe.\\n- `TestComputeReachableFromMain_ScanIsBounded` — the main first-parent scan visits at most `mainSpineScanLimit` commits regardless of main length (no O(main) read-path blowup). Fails with an unbounded scan.\\n- `TestGetBranchCheckpoints_ComputesReachabilityOncePerCall` — the scan runs once per `getBranchCheckpoints` call, not once per checkpoint.\\n\\n### Live before/after — same repo, non-default target `release`, feature merged via `--no-ff`\\n\\nVerified end-to-end via the deterministic `vogon` hook-replay agent (real session hooks → shadow branch → condensed checkpoint on `entire/checkpoints/v1`), running a pre-fix binary and the fixed binary against the same repo.\\n\\nCommitted checkpoint (baseline pre-fix → fixed):\\n\\n```\\n>>> entire checkpoint list        (pre-fix)          (fixed)\\n  branch       release            release            release\\n  checkpoints  0                  1  ● b7d5fa68…  \\\"create a markdown file …\\\"\\n```\\n\\nInvariant re-checked live: on a feature branch with the default branch merged in (`--no-ff`), both the branch-point and the merged-in default-branch checkpoints stay excluded — the fixed and pre-fix binaries agree, confirming no leakage was introduced. The shadow (in-progress) path is unchanged from `main`, so the fresh-branch \\\"`checkout -b` then start coding\\\" session still shows exactly as before.\\n\\n### Edge matrix (live, isolated scratch repos)\\n\\n| Scenario | Result |\\n|---|---|\\n| Non-default target, `--no-ff` merge commit (the bug) | fixed — checkpoint visible |\\n| Non-default target, true `--ff-only` | still works |\\n| Default branch (`main`), `--no-ff` and divergent merge | still works (unchanged) |\\n| Multiple sessions on feature → ff-merge into main | all 3 visible |\\n| Target branch has its own checkpoint + merged-in feature | both visible |\\n| ff-merge performed from a linked worktree | visible (list + explain) |\\n| Octopus merge (3+ parents) into non-default target | all merged checkpoints visible |\\n| Nested merge (sub-feature → feature → release) | transitive checkpoint visible |\\n| Deep history: main advanced >1000 commits past an old merge-main-in | main's old checkpoints excluded (no leak) |\\n| Invariant: main merged INTO a feature branch | main's checkpoints still excluded |\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1727/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1727/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3056\",\n              \"id\": 6255425292,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABNdzkwQ\",\n              \"number\": 3056,\n              \"title\": \"fix(strategy): spell agent-reported paths as git does on case-insensitive filesystems\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n                \"id\": 26940511,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI2OTQwNTEx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Beehtrix\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 5,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-07T05:06:26Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-11T18:20:27Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3056\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3056\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3056.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3056.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes #3054\\n\\nOn a case-insensitive filesystem (the macOS and Windows default) an agent can name a tracked file in another case than git does: writing `readme.md` changes `README.md`. Entire recorded the agent's spelling, which never matches a commit, so the session stayed pending after the file was committed. The issue has the two ways it happens (dirty at turn end, committed mid-turn).\\n\\nI reviewed this on my fork first (Beehtrix/cli#22).\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\n`strategy.FilterTrackableChanges`, which every capture route already applies (turn end, task completion, per-tool hooks, Codex child files, and the transcript fallback of a mid-turn commit), now first spells each path as git's index does (`strategy.TrackedSpellings`, in `strategy/path_case.go`):\\n\\n- It only acts where a directory on a reported path, from the one holding the file up to the worktree root, finds its entries under another case, which `worktreedir.CaseProbe` asks the filesystem in process: one of the directory's entries, looked up with its letters' case swapped, opens the same file, and the directory doesn't also list that spelling as an entry of its own (a hard-linked pair, which only a directory that respects case can hold). A directory that is gone, has no entry with a letter in its name, or has over 4096 entries can't tell, and then nothing is rewritten; it doesn't borrow its parent's answer, since Windows lets a directory respect case inside one that ignores it. It doesn't go by git's `core.ignorecase`, one setting for the whole repository, which a linked worktree on another filesystem, a moved repository or a Windows directory with its own case sensitivity can disagree with. Every directory on the path counts, not only the one holding the file: on Windows `SRC/App.go` in a root that ignores case opens `src/App.go` even when `src/` respects case. On a case-sensitive filesystem nothing changes and git isn't asked, since `readme.md` and `README.md` are two files there.\\n- It asks git once per call for the index's spellings (`gitrepo.IndexPathsIgnoringCase`: `git ls-files -z --cached` with `:(literal,icase)` pathspecs, chunked and bounded by `PathClassificationBudget` like the other classifiers).\\n- A spelling is rewritten only when each directory where it differs from the index's spelling ignores case, and it opens the same file (`os.SameFile` on rooted lstats): in a directory that respects case, two hard-linked names are two entries git tracks apart. A deletion has nothing left to open, so it's rewritten when the index has exactly one spelling of it and that one is gone too. Duplicates the rewrite leaves are dropped, keeping the first one's place.\\n- If git can't answer, the paths are kept as reported, as before.\\n\\n`worktreedir/case.go` is the same file as in my shared-checkout PR for #3011, which needs the same check for deletions; whichever lands second loses it from its diff.\\n\\nTurn end now runs `FilterTrackableChanges` before `filterToUncommittedFiles`, so a file committed mid-turn is checked against HEAD under git's spelling. Both only drop paths, so the order doesn't change what either drops. Task completion respells the subagent's transcript paths before `filterToUncommittedFiles` and the committed-file check that attaches the task to a commit. The transcript route a commit hook takes before the session's first turn end (`filterTrackableFiles`) spells its paths first and keeps them in git's spelling.\\n\\n## Trade-offs\\n\\n- On macOS and Windows, each `FilterTrackableChanges` call runs one more `git ls-files`. A path git tracks under its own spelling still costs that call, since only git knows which paths it tracks. On Linux the cost is one read of each directory on the reported paths (each asked once per call), plus two `lstat`s per directory.\\n- A file that isn't tracked keeps the agent's spelling. git status lists such a file under its on-disk spelling, which the agent's tool normally created, so the two agree.\\n- `liveTaskTranscriptFiles` (co-authorship evidence for a running subagent) still compares the transcript's spelling with the commit's. It only decides whether a session counts as a co-author of a commit, and I left it out to keep this to what enters `FilesTouched`.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- `gitrepo.TestIndexPathsIgnoringCase`: index spellings for other-case names, literal brackets, an untracked name, and inherited `GIT_LITERAL_PATHSPECS` / `GIT_GLOB_PATHSPECS`.\\n- `worktreedir.TestCaseProbe_*`: the directory probe, with a lookup that folds case standing in for a directory that ignores case (a directory that respects case, a hard-linked pair of entries that must read as a directory that respects case, a directory that ignores case, one with no entry that tells, one that is gone, one over the entry bound, and paths that differ in several directories). `TestCaseProbeWindows` checks it against the filesystem itself on CI's Windows job.\\n- `strategy.TestTrackedSpelling`: the rule itself, with a hard link standing in for one file under two names and a stand-in probe for a directory that ignores case (same file where the directory ignores case, a hard link where it respects case, another file, no file, a deletion in a directory that respects case and in one that ignores it, two index spellings, git's spelling still present). `strategy.TestAnyDirectoryIgnoresCase`: every directory on a path counts toward asking git, not only the one holding the file.\\n- `strategy.TestFilterTrackableFiles_KeepsGitsSpellingWindows`: the transcript route keeps `README.md` for a transcript's `readme.md`; on a case-insensitive filesystem it fails without that part of the fix.\\n- `strategy.TestTrackedSpellings_CaseInsensitiveFilesystemWindows` and `TestFilterTrackableFiles_KeepsGitsSpellingWindows` are named so that CI's Windows job runs them on a real case-insensitive filesystem; on Linux they check that nothing changes.\\n- `integration_test/transcript_path_case_test.go`: the issue's two cases end to end. They run only where the filesystem ignores case, so CI's Linux job skips them.\\n\\nOn Linux with git 2.43, `go test ./...` and `go test -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/...` pass apart from 13 tests that fail the same way on a clean checkout of main in that environment (no `--ref-format`, SSH, DNS or user XDG cache, and running as root). golangci-lint v2.15.0 reports 0 issues, the complexity gate passes, and the changed packages and the integration package vet for Windows. I also ran the changed packages' tests and the two integration tests on a case-insensitive filesystem in the same container (ciopfs, a FUSE filesystem, mounted with `use_ino` so both spellings report one inode): the case tests pass there, and both integration tests fail on main there (`FilesTouched = [README.md readme.md]`, and `[readme.md]` still pending after the mid-turn commit). Four other `strategy` tests fail on that mount on main too, from the FUSE filesystem (a removed and re-added working directory, and a temp-dir cleanup).\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 1,\n                \"+1\": 1,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2921\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2921/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2921/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2921/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2921\",\n              \"id\": 6061482275,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABLCkECQ\",\n              \"number\": 2921,\n              \"title\": \"feat(checkpoint): add a manual push policy and entire checkpoint push\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"id\": 34813274,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-27T14:43:17Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-29T17:39:56Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-29T17:39:52Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2921\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2921\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2921.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2921.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-29T17:39:52Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2630/changes/cli/1704\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nPart of ENT-3141\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2921/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2921/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": {\n                \"id\": 2626939,\n                \"client_id\": \"Iv23lieFG10uOnChW4TN\",\n                \"slug\": \"entire\",\n                \"node_id\": \"A_kwHOAfprLM4AKBV7\",\n                \"owner\": {\n                  \"login\": \"entireio\",\n                  \"id\": 33188652,\n                  \"node_id\": \"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjMzMTg4NjUy\",\n                  \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33188652?v=4\",\n                  \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio\",\n                  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio\",\n                  \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/followers\",\n                  \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/following{/other_user}\",\n                  \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                  \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                  \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/subscriptions\",\n                  \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/orgs\",\n                  \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/repos\",\n                  \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/events{/privacy}\",\n                  \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/received_events\",\n                  \"type\": \"Organization\",\n                  \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                  \"site_admin\": false\n                },\n                \"name\": \"Entire\",\n                \"description\": \"\",\n                \"external_url\": \"https://entire.com\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/entire\",\n                \"created_at\": \"2026-01-09T21:20:56Z\",\n                \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-23T08:32:31Z\",\n                \"permissions\": {\n                  \"administration\": \"read\",\n                  \"checks\": \"write\",\n                  \"contents\": \"write\",\n                  \"emails\": \"read\",\n                  \"members\": \"read\",\n                  \"metadata\": \"read\",\n                  \"pull_requests\": \"write\",\n                  \"statuses\": \"read\",\n                  \"workflows\": \"write\"\n                },\n                \"events\": [\n                  \"check_suite\",\n                  \"create\",\n                  \"delete\",\n                  \"fork\",\n                  \"member\",\n                  \"membership\",\n                  \"organization\",\n                  \"pull_request\",\n                  \"push\",\n                  \"repository\",\n                  \"star\",\n                  \"team\"\n                ]\n              },\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2187\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2187/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2187/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2187/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2187\",\n              \"id\": 5298206561,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBkzgvQ\",\n              \"number\": 2187,\n              \"title\": \"Rename the rewind-point vocabulary to pending checkpoints\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-31T08:40:41Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-31T10:17:16Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-31T10:17:13Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2187\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2187\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2187.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2187.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-31T10:17:13Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1188\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n#2178 removed the rewind restore path, but the listing machinery that survived it kept the name — and what `checkpoint list --pending` returns is a pending checkpoint: one not yet condensed onto `entire/checkpoints/v1`. The rename is safe to do now precisely because the machine-readable surface was already clean: no JSON key, flag, or command path has ever contained \\\"rewind\\\", so this touches only Go identifiers, comments, and human-readable text.\\n\\n> Was stacked on #2186; that merged, and this PR now targets `main` with just the two rename commits.\\n\\n## Mapping\\n\\n| Old | New | Uses |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `RewindPoint` | `PendingCheckpoint` | 63 |\\n| `ResolveAgentForRewind` | `ResolveAgentForResume` | 19 |\\n| `GetRewindPoints` | `ListPendingCheckpoints` | 15 |\\n| `pendingRewindPointJSON` | `pendingCheckpointJSON` | 7 |\\n| `rewindPointLabel` | `pendingCheckpointLabel` | 4 |\\n| `pendingRewindPointsLimit` | `pendingCheckpointsLimit` | 4 |\\n| `GetLogsOnlyRewindPoints` | `ListLogsOnlyPendingCheckpoints` | 3 |\\n| `getImportedRewindPoints` | `getImportedPendingCheckpoints` | 3 |\\n| `RewindPoints` | `PendingCheckpoints` | 1 |\\n\\n119 uses across 20 files. `Get-` became `List-` because these return a slice and take a limit; `ResolveAgentForRewind` became `ForResume` because all three callers are resume commands (`newResumeCmd`, `newCheckpointResumeCmd`, `newTrailResumeCmd`).\\n\\nKept as-is per the brief: `RestoreLogsOnly`, `RestoredSession`, `SessionRestoreStatus`, `ClassifyTimestamps`, `ResolveLatestCheckpointFromMap`.\\n\\n**File moves** (`git mv`): `strategy/manual_commit_rewind.go` → `manual_commit_pending.go`, and `strategy/rewind_test.go` → `strategy/restore_logs_test.go`. The second is deliberately not `manual_commit_pending_test.go`: every test left in that file exercises the log-restore/resume half (`RestoreLogsOnly`, prompt preview, `FirstDisplayPrompt`, `ResolveAgentForResume`), while the listing half is tested in `manual_commit_test.go`.\\n\\nNo gopls on this machine, so renames went through word-boundary regex applied longest-name-first — so `GetRewindPoints` and `GetLogsOnlyRewindPoints` could not be shredded by the `RewindPoint` pass — with `go build ./...` gating every step. Word boundaries also skip test function names (`TestResolveAgentForRewind` has no boundary before `Resolve`), so those were renamed separately, along with the file-local `writeCommittedRewindCheckpoint` helper (now `writeCommittedCheckpoint` — it writes a *committed* checkpoint, not a pending one) and two test-agent fixture strings.\\n\\n## Explicitly unchanged\\n\\n- **The `--pending` flag**, every command path, and every alias. The diff's only flag line is its help *text*; no `Use:` or `Aliases:` line moved.\\n- **The JSON shape.** `grep '^[+-].*json:\\\"'` over the entire diff returns **nothing** — every field in `pendingCheckpointJSON` carries an explicit tag, so renaming the Go type cannot move a key. `checkpoint list --pending --json` stays byte-identical, and `TestPendingCheckpointJSON_MatchesRewindListContract` (which keeps its historical suffix) still passes.\\n- **CHANGELOG.md** — untouched.\\n- **`internal/remotehelper/transport/proxy.go`** — its \\\"rewind\\\" is HTTP request-body rewinding.\\n- **Every \\\"rewind\\\" that means moving a git ref backwards**: `fetch_rewind_protection_test.go` (filename included), `safely_advance_local_ref_test.go`, `checkpoint_remote_test.go`, the explain fetch tests.\\n- **Historical references**, which explain why the current shape is what it is: the `rewind --list` mentions in `checkpoint_list.go` / `checkpoint_group.go` (that bridge is *why* the JSON is frozen), the \\\"former interactive rewind picker\\\" whose format `pendingCheckpointLabel` inherited, and `deprecated_strings_test.go`'s never-advertise entry for `entire rewind`.\\n\\n## Strings and comments\\n\\n`checkpoint list --pending` no longer says \\\"No pending rewind points found.\\\" or \\\"Pending rewind points are created automatically…\\\"; the flag help, `Long` text, and two error paths follow. The first-turn context injection listed \\\"(enable, disable, clean, rewind, auth)\\\" as destructive commands — `entire rewind` has not existed since #1747, so a third of that warning pointed at nothing.\\n\\nThree comments were wrong about *mechanisms*, not just names, and were checked against the code rather than reworded:\\n\\n- `gitrepo/status.go` named \\\"review, rewind\\\" as the paths keeping the unbounded `Status` walk. The real two are `review_target.go` and `detectFileChangesUnbounded` (`session adopt`); both are now named.\\n- `manual_commit_session.go` attributed `FindSessionsForCommit` **and** `ClearSessionState` to \\\"the rewind reset command\\\". They belong to *different* commands — `entire clean` (clean.go:177) and `entire doctor` (doctor.go:406).\\n- `common.go`'s `DeleteBranchCLI` cited `HardResetWithProtection` as its sibling go-git v5 workaround. That function exists nowhere in the tree; the real one is `CheckoutBranch` in `git_operations.go`. (This was the follow-up flagged in #2178 and #2186.)\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `mise run fmt && mise run lint` — 0 issues, per commit.\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/...` — pass, per commit.\\n- `bash -n` on both edited shell scripts — clean.\\n- Full `mise run test:ci` — **exit 0**: unit + integration (`-race`) + canary 56/56 vogon and 4/4 roger-roger. The `TestCodexAppServerHooksList_*` failure known to hit macOS with codex installed did **not** fire.\\n\\n**String assertions updated** (the only ones that pin text this PR changes): `checkpoint_list_test.go` pinned \\\"No pending rewind points found.\\\" twice. Both are exact-match `require.Contains` calls, so nothing else could have drifted silently. `trail_injection_text_test.go` asserts only the prefix \\\"Leave setup and destructive commands\\\", so the context-injection edit leaves it passing. No canary test greps CLI output for \\\"rewind points\\\", and no E2E prompt wording changed.\\n\\n## Left for a follow-up, not done here\\n\\nComments in the **agent implementations** still describe rewind as live: `claudecode/claude.go:188`, `codex/codex.go:91`, `opencode/opencode.go:225-239`, and the two `security_contract_test.go` files. The brief enumerated the comment sites it had verified and these were not among them, so rather than guess at agent-side session-import mechanics I left them. One is a real finding worth its own PR: `claudecode.FindCheckpointUUID` carries a comment saying it \\\"served task checkpoint rewind… no production caller remains… should be removed\\\", i.e. dead exported API — a deletion, not a rename.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Rename-only refactor with preserved JSON contract and no behavior changes to checkpoint listing, resume, or restore-logs paths.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> After removing the `rewind` restore path, this PR renames the surviving listing vocabulary so it matches what **`checkpoint list --pending`** actually returns: checkpoints not yet condensed onto `entire/checkpoints/v1`.\\n> \\n> **API and types:** `RewindPoint` → `PendingCheckpoint`, `GetRewindPoints` → `ListPendingCheckpoints`, `GetLogsOnlyRewindPoints` → `ListLogsOnlyPendingCheckpoints`, and `ResolveAgentForRewind` → `ResolveAgentForResume` (resume/trail resume callers only). Strategy code moves from `manual_commit_rewind.go` to **`manual_commit_pending.go`**; log-restore tests move to **`restore_logs_test.go`**.\\n> \\n> **User-visible surface:** Help text and empty-state messages say “pending checkpoints” instead of “pending rewind points”; the test harness step is **`list-pending-checkpoints`**. **`--pending`**, command paths, and **`checkpoint list --pending --json`** field names are unchanged so scripts that parsed deprecated `rewind --list` keep working.\\n> \\n> **Docs and comments:** CLAUDE.md, architecture docs, and scattered comments now describe list/resume/log-restore instead of file rewind; a few stale references are corrected (e.g. agent context injection no longer lists `rewind`, `ProtectedDirs` describes checkpoint capture, and wrong command names for session cleanup helpers).\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit fcd4e868c5f0119f8511bd43dc44d7b75fb00bd4. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2187/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2187/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3107\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3107/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3107/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3107/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3107\",\n              \"id\": 6314389823,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABOMkDFw\",\n              \"number\": 3107,\n              \"title\": \"soph/release-0-13-2\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-10T19:37:37Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-10T20:11:53Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-11-10T20:11:51Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3107\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3107\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3107.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3107.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-11-10T20:11:51Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"This draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back a trail. Feel free to edit the title or body, but keep the hidden marker below: Entire uses it to close this pull request when the trail closes.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Changelog-only update with no runtime or build changes.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Documents the 0.13.2 release** in `CHANGELOG.md` only—no application code in this diff.\\n> \\n> The new section calls out **service-account secret** CLI commands and `ENTIRE_TOKEN` / `git-remote-entire` behavior, **standalone `git-remote-entire` archives** per platform, and **auto-install for the `entire-rsl` plugin**. **Token usage** for sessions/checkpoints is now taken from each agent’s running total (with `session_token_usage` on checkpoints). **Repository-scoped** `entire trail create` / `update` are removed in favor of project trails; trail output drops assignees and aggregate comment counts. **OpenCode** checkpoint/export and live-view fixes are listed, plus fixes for **Antigravity** transcript paths, **`entire api` / `entire recap` repo cell routing**, and **`install.sh` checksum** verification.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 81c5454dc0a6f1d16497b8126d619ffce215c111. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3107/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3107/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": {\n                \"id\": 2626939,\n                \"client_id\": \"Iv23lieFG10uOnChW4TN\",\n                \"slug\": \"entire\",\n                \"node_id\": \"A_kwHOAfprLM4AKBV7\",\n                \"owner\": {\n                  \"login\": \"entireio\",\n                  \"id\": 33188652,\n                  \"node_id\": \"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjMzMTg4NjUy\",\n                  \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33188652?v=4\",\n                  \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio\",\n                  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio\",\n                  \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/followers\",\n                  \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/following{/other_user}\",\n                  \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                  \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                  \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/subscriptions\",\n                  \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/orgs\",\n                  \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/repos\",\n                  \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/events{/privacy}\",\n                  \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/received_events\",\n                  \"type\": \"Organization\",\n                  \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                  \"site_admin\": false\n                },\n                \"name\": \"Entire\",\n                \"description\": \"\",\n                \"external_url\": \"https://entire.com\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/entire\",\n                \"created_at\": \"2026-01-09T21:20:56Z\",\n                \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-23T08:32:31Z\",\n                \"permissions\": {\n                  \"administration\": \"read\",\n                  \"checks\": \"write\",\n                  \"contents\": \"write\",\n                  \"emails\": \"read\",\n                  \"members\": \"read\",\n                  \"metadata\": \"read\",\n                  \"pull_requests\": \"write\",\n                  \"statuses\": \"read\",\n                  \"workflows\": \"write\"\n                },\n                \"events\": [\n                  \"check_suite\",\n                  \"create\",\n                  \"delete\",\n                  \"fork\",\n                  \"member\",\n                  \"membership\",\n                  \"organization\",\n                  \"pull_request\",\n                  \"push\",\n                  \"repository\",\n                  \"star\",\n                  \"team\"\n                ]\n              },\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2785\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2785/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2785/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2785/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2785\",\n              \"id\": 5865644792,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABInHbWw\",\n              \"number\": 2785,\n              \"title\": \"Redone commits don't mint a fresh checkpoint for inherited work\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-15T11:57:15Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-16T15:18:00Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-16T15:17:57Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2785\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2785\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2785.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2785.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-16T15:17:57Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1582\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nE2E run [38724857355](https://github.com/entireio/cli/actions/runs/38724857355/job/116388096213) failed `TestExplainCheckpoint` (claude-code). Haiku committed `docs/feature.md` itself, then ran `git reset HEAD~1`, and the test's own commit came out with two checkpoint trailers: the inherited `3afa00e9bfa6` (correct, via the redo inheritance from 6170bc1612) and a fresh `93418f0f011f`.\\n\\nThe fresh one was wrong. The reset put the file back in the worktree, the next turn end recorded it as touched again, and session matching saw transcript growth plus an overlapping staged file. The new checkpoint's transcript slice held only the agent's commit and reset, which the turn-end finalize had already folded into `3afa00e9bfa6`.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n- The redo step (`inheritReplacedCommitsTrailers`) now also reports which staged paths the inherited checkpoints already hold. A path counts only when the newest dropped commit that changed it carries a checkpoint that is not deleted and exists in this clone's store (`capturedCheckpoints`), and the staged content and mode both match what that commit left. Inheriting the trailer stays permissive: a trailer whose capture failed still links, but holds nothing, so the session's work gets a fresh checkpoint. Content, mode and deletions come from one rename-free read of the commit index git is preparing (`parseStagedRaw` now also keeps the staged mode, building on #2330), so `git commit -a` and path-limited commits compare what they commit.\\n- `PrepareCommitMsg` returns right after inheriting when every staged path is held, so a pure redo gets no fresh trailer, whatever the session phase.\\n- Otherwise the staged-files overlap check in `filterSessionsWithNewContent` sees only the redo's other staged paths, from the same rename-free view, so only other session work earns a fresh checkpoint. (A rename-detecting list would hide a staged deletion paired with a held file.)\\n- Prepare records the held paths in the inherited-trailers marker. After a redo that stamps no fresh trailer (pure, or partial with no session's other work), which condenses nothing, post-commit (`reconcileRedoneFiles`) drops them from this worktree's sessions' touched files when the commit holds the recorded content, as carry-forward would. Only held files go through that check; other touched files, steps and transcript growth stay pending untouched.\\n- `openRepositoryTimed` is extracted to keep `PrepareCommitMsg` under the `maintidx` limit; the `open_repository` span no longer includes the redo lookup.\\n- The deleted-checkpoint list is loaded once per commit, each dropped commit's diff is computed once, and store lookups are memoized.\\n- Documented in `docs/architecture/sessions-and-checkpoints.md` and `docs/development/checkpoint-implementation.md`.\\n\\n## Deliberately not changed\\n\\nWhenever a fresh trailer is stamped, a redundant checkpoint is preferred to a lost or dangling link:\\n\\n- On a partial redo (redone files staged together with other files), the mid-turn agent fast path still stamps a fresh trailer. Transcripts miss edits made through shell commands (`sed -i`, formatters, codegen), so it cannot rule out new work.\\n- Post-commit judges overlap without the redo, so a session that only redid work may fold into another session's fresh checkpoint. An earlier commit on this branch excluded redone paths there, but that left a fresh trailer with no checkpoint behind it when a stale ACTIVE session tracked only redone files, or when a read-only ACTIVE session was gated out by a redo-only claimant.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nRegression tests in `manual_commit_redo_test.go`. The fixture writes real checkpoints for its trailers through the hooks' own store. Each test fails without its fix (mutation-checked), except the aborted-commit one, which two independent guards cover. Every test that expects a fresh trailer runs prepare, the commit and post-commit, and asserts the trailer resolves in the checkpoint store:\\n\\n- a pure redo, with an ended or an active session, gets only the inherited trailers;\\n- after a pure redo, only the redone file leaves the session's touched files, and a later human edit to it doesn't link back to the session;\\n- a redo plus new session work gets the inherited trailer and a fresh one;\\n- a redo plus a file the session never touched gets only the inherited trailer;\\n- a mode change after the reset gets a fresh trailer;\\n- a later dropped commit without a checkpoint that changed the same file leaves it uncovered;\\n- a partial redo by an active session keeps its fast-path trailer;\\n- a stale ACTIVE session tracking only redone files, a read-only ACTIVE session beside a redo-only claimant, and two ended sessions all leave the fresh trailer resolvable;\\n- a dropped commit whose checkpoint is missing or deleted keeps the session's fresh capture;\\n- a staged deletion git pairs with a held file as a rename stamps no fresh trailer;\\n- content and mode are read from the temporary commit index, not `.git/index`;\\n- an aborted commit's marker never settles files a later commit didn't contain;\\n- the cleanup never prunes touched files the redo doesn't hold.\\n\\n`mise run check` passes.\\n\\n## Follow-ups\\n\\n- The amend fold (`git reset --soft HEAD~1 && git commit --amend`) goes through `stampFreshCheckpointForAmend` and may have the same issue; not checked.\\n- The e2e helpers (`GetCheckpointTrailer` / `AssertHasCheckpointTrailer`) assume a single trailer per commit, though squash and multi-commit redos legitimately produce several.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes prepare-commit-msg trailer stamping and session content matching on reset/redo paths; incorrect logic could omit needed trailers or over-link commits, though behavior is covered by new tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Fixes **prepare-commit-msg** so a pure **redo** after `git reset` inherits dropped commits’ `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers but does **not** mint a new checkpoint when staged files are only recommitted work.\\n> \\n> Redo detection now returns a **`redo`** value (inherited IDs, matched staged paths, and whether every staged path is redone). When all staged paths are redone, the hook exits after inheriting trailers; otherwise **`filterSessionsWithNewContent`** ignores redone paths when deciding if a session has new work, so reset/turn-end “touched again” files are not treated as fresh session content. **`recommitsFilesOf`** returns the matched paths per dropped commit, and only commits that still carry live checkpoints contribute paths.\\n> \\n> Adds regression tests (pure redo, redo plus new session work, redo plus unrelated files) and documents the behavior in **sessions-and-checkpoints**.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit b05ce0e53e1ae0bf30114e863ad6c5acdc87d167. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2785/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2785/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": {\n                \"id\": 2626939,\n                \"client_id\": \"Iv23lieFG10uOnChW4TN\",\n                \"slug\": \"entire\",\n                \"node_id\": \"A_kwHOAfprLM4AKBV7\",\n                \"owner\": {\n                  \"login\": \"entireio\",\n                  \"id\": 33188652,\n                  \"node_id\": \"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjMzMTg4NjUy\",\n                  \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33188652?v=4\",\n                  \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio\",\n                  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio\",\n                  \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/followers\",\n                  \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/following{/other_user}\",\n                  \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                  \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                  \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/subscriptions\",\n                  \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/orgs\",\n                  \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/repos\",\n                  \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/events{/privacy}\",\n                  \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/received_events\",\n                  \"type\": \"Organization\",\n                  \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                  \"site_admin\": false\n                },\n                \"name\": \"Entire\",\n                \"description\": \"\",\n                \"external_url\": \"https://entire.com\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/entire\",\n                \"created_at\": \"2026-01-09T21:20:56Z\",\n                \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-23T08:32:31Z\",\n                \"permissions\": {\n                  \"administration\": \"read\",\n                  \"checks\": \"write\",\n                  \"contents\": \"write\",\n                  \"emails\": \"read\",\n                  \"members\": \"read\",\n                  \"metadata\": \"read\",\n                  \"pull_requests\": \"write\",\n                  \"statuses\": \"read\",\n                  \"workflows\": \"write\"\n                },\n                \"events\": [\n                  \"check_suite\",\n                  \"create\",\n                  \"delete\",\n                  \"fork\",\n                  \"member\",\n                  \"membership\",\n                  \"organization\",\n                  \"pull_request\",\n                  \"push\",\n                  \"repository\",\n                  \"star\",\n                  \"team\"\n                ]\n              },\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1768\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1768/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1768/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1768/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1768\",\n              \"id\": 4895934048,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7yMkxO\",\n              \"number\": 1768,\n              \"title\": \"feat(checkpoint): add checkpoint list --json (machine-readable listing; migrate off rewind --list)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"id\": 257360244,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-07-15T20:04:43Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-15T22:29:52Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-15T22:29:50Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1768\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1768\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1768.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1768.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-15T22:29:50Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"**Trail:** https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/869\\n\\n**What:** Adds `--json` and `--pending` to `entire checkpoint list`, giving a machine-readable checkpoint listing on a non-deprecated command, and migrates every consumer off the deprecated `rewind --list`.\\n\\n**Why:** `rewind --list` was the only machine-readable checkpoint listing, which blocked the announced removal of the deprecated `rewind` command. Addresses #1767.\\n\\n**How:**\\n- `checkpoint list --json` → condensed checkpoints (`entire/checkpoints/v1`) as JSON.\\n- `checkpoint list --pending [--json]` → the live shadow-branch rewind points; `--pending --json` is a **byte-for-byte drop-in for `rewind --list`** (same keys, `omitempty`, RFC3339 date, trailing newline, cap-20), so consumers migrate transparently.\\n- Repointed the `GetRewindPoints` / `RewindList` helpers (`testenv.go`, `e2e/entire.go`, `setup_cmd_test.go`, `testutil.go`) — the ~48 downstream call sites are untouched because the parsed shape is identical.\\n- Removed the `rewind --list` listing surface + now-dead code from `rewind.go` (unused imports, `runRewindList`); extracted the shared label logic. Kept the `checkpoint rewind --to/--logs-only` **action** command and its ~20 regression tests.\\n- Updated docs + dev harness scripts (`WINDOWS.md`, `.claude/skills/test-repo/SKILL.md`, `test-harness.sh`, `scripts/test-attribution-e2e.sh`).\\n\\n**Scope note:** This completes the issue's listing + migration goal. Full removal of the `checkpoint rewind` / top-level `rewind` **command** (the action flow + its ~20 regression tests) is the separate follow-up #1767 itself defers (\\\"whether the interactive rewind flow survives elsewhere is part of that removal decision, not this issue\\\") — not bundled here, so that test coverage isn't silently dropped.\\n\\n**Testing:**\\n- `gofmt` clean; `mise run lint` 0 issues; `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/...` green; `go vet -tags integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/` clean.\\n- New `checkpoint_list_test.go` (5 tests), mutation-verified; the drop-in JSON contract is pinned field-by-field against the old `rewind --list`.\\n- Canary `TestSubmoduleWorktree_SessionCreatesCheckpoint` (drives the migrated `GetRewindPoints`) PASSes end-to-end.\\n- Independent adversarial audit: CONFIRMED-CLEAN (caught + fixed two dev-harness scripts still invoking `rewind --list`).\\n\\n**Known minor follow-up:** the condensed `--json` truncation note suggests re-running with `--limit`, which `checkpoint list` does not yet expose (stderr-only, fires only past the default cap).\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1768/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1768/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2696\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2696/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2696/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2696/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2696\",\n              \"id\": 5752526656,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABHNox6Q\",\n              \"number\": 2696,\n              \"title\": \"Add entire checkpoint delete\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-07T22:03:33Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-08T17:19:20Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-08T17:19:18Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2696\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2696\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2696.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2696.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-08T17:19:18Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1513\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nAdds `entire checkpoint delete <id>`: removes one checkpoint locally and from every checkpoint remote that holds it, on both backends.\\n\\n```\\nentire checkpoint delete <id> [--dry-run] [-f|--force] [--local-only] [--remote <name>]... [--json]\\n```\\n\\n## Behavior\\n\\n- **Plan first.** Lists the local ref / v1 copy, every remote (status per target, URLs redacted), the session(s) and their tokens, session states it will clear, and the session's other local checkpoints. `--dry-run` prints this and changes nothing.\\n- **Confirmation.** Prompts (multi-select of remotes, then confirm). Without a TTY, or with `--json`, it refuses unless `--force`. Active sessions are refused unless `--force`. Exact ids only.\\n- **Order.** Session-state links cleared (never token offsets/usage) → local ref CAS-deleted → push-queue entry removed → remote deletes → one re-check per remote, so a concurrent pre-push can't re-land it.\\n- **Refs backend.** Remote deletes use `--force-with-lease` on the oid seen by ls-remote. A stale lease on an already-absent ref counts as deleted (e.g. one repo reached through two URL spellings).\\n- **v1 branch.** Per target: fetch that remote's v1 tip, commit the subtree removal on it, push with a lease; unrelated local v1 commits are never pushed. When the two removal commits are the only difference, local v1 is rebuilt on the pushed one so the next push (including the OPF rewrite) sees no divergence; any other divergence is left alone for pre-push / OPF to handle as today. History keeps the content; the output says so.\\n- **No resurrection.** The id goes on a local deleted list in the git common dir. `prepare-commit-msg` strips its `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer (amend, `-m`, `-F`, squash, cherry-pick `-x` notes), and the hooks never condense new work into a listed id or restore one on amend; new agent work gets a fresh id. `doctor migrate` skips listed ids. `explain` says the checkpoint was deleted.\\n- **Safety refusals.** On a git-branch primary, a delete that excludes a v1 push destination (`--local-only`, `--remote`, deselection) is refused, because the local removal would reach that remote on the next push anyway.\\n- **Agent help.** User-owned; agents are told never to run it unless the user asks, and never to pass `--force` themselves.\\n\\n## Known limits\\n\\n- `--force` both skips the prompt and overrides the active-session refusal (deliberate: one flag for \\\"I know\\\").\\n- On a git-branch primary, only the first push URL's v1 copy is adopted locally; a capture-elected push remote isn't seen by the refusal check (documented).\\n\\n## Not in this PR\\n\\n- entire.io still shows the checkpoint until the API handles ref deletes (phase 2).\\n- Other clones that still hold it can push it back (tombstones, later).\\n- Deleting a session's other checkpoints too vs rewriting them: undecided; this only lists them.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- Unit + integration (both backends): dry run, refusal matrix, remote rejection + retry, pushurl ≠ fetch URL, same repo under two URLs, `checkpoint_remote` + legacy origin, `--local-only` + next push, `push_sessions=false`, v1 remote ahead, next push after a v1 delete (with unpushed local checkpoints), OPF rewrite after delete, trailer stripping variants, deleted-list record/unrecord.\\n- Real repos: a private GitHub repo (refs) and an Entire-native repo (v1 branch), real Claude Code sessions; deleted on GitHub/Entire, mirror pruned on next sync, fresh clone doesn't get it, push/amend don't bring it back. entire.io still served it (phase 2).\\n- Manual end-to-end with the built binary, real git hooks and a bare remote, both backends: 24/24 checks (dry run, no-TTY refusal, prefix refusal, delete local + remote + queue + session state, sibling untouched, explain, push after delete, amend, re-delete).\\n- `mise run check` and `mise run lint` pass.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2696/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2696/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2127\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2127/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2127/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2127/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2127\",\n              \"id\": 5252204619,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBA7zxw\",\n              \"number\": 2127,\n              \"title\": \"feat(grok): add Grok Build (xAI) agent integration\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-26T01:00:22Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-02T19:11:33Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2127\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2127\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2127.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2127.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1143\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nAdds Grok Build (xAI) as an Entire agent, registered as `grok`.\\n\\nBuilt through the research → write-tests → implement pipeline. Everything\\nbelow was verified against a real Grok 1.0.5 install, with captured payloads\\nand a real session transcript checked in as test fixtures.\\n\\n## What's here\\n\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/grok/` — the agent. Core `Agent` plus `HookSupport`,\\n  `HookFreshness`, `TranscriptAnalyzer`, `TokenCalculator`, `ModelExtractor`,\\n  and `SubagentSessionResolver`. Marked `IsPreview()`.\\n- `e2e/agents/grok.go` — E2E runner, so the existing `ForEachAgent` suite\\n  covers Grok. No new scenarios were needed.\\n- `scripts/test-grok-agent-integration.sh` — the probe used to capture payloads.\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/grok/AGENT.md` — research one-pager. Every claim is\\n  tagged `(doc)` / `(observed)` / `(unverified)`.\\n\\nHooks live in `.grok/hooks/entire.json`, a file Entire owns outright — Grok\\nmerges every `*.json` under `.grok/hooks/`, so install is a whole-file write and\\nuninstall a delete. A foreign file at that path is refused, not clobbered.\\n\\n## Three Grok behaviours with no analogue in the other agents\\n\\n1. **`StopCancelled` / `StopFailure` map to `TurnEnd`.** Grok fires those\\n   *instead of* `Stop` when a turn is interrupted, has a permission prompt\\n   declined, hits `--max-turns`, or errors upstream. Mapping only `Stop` loses a\\n   checkpoint for every Ctrl+C'd turn.\\n2. **`Stop` fires twice per session.** The teardown one carries\\n   `reason: \\\"shutdown\\\"` and no `promptId`. Treating it as a turn mints a\\n   duplicate, contentless checkpoint every session, so it is dropped.\\n3. **`updates.jsonl` lines are JSON-RPC envelopes.** The event kind is at\\n   `params.update.sessionUpdate`, two levels down — reading the top level yields\\n   nothing on every real transcript.\\n\\n## Test coverage\\n\\n100 unit tests (including subtests) in the grok package, built on verbatim fixtures from a real\\nsession. `mise run test:ci` is green.\\n\\n**E2E: 38 of 56 scenarios verified against real Grok** across four free-quota windows (08-25 through 09-02); the 18 remaining have only ever failed on quota/rate limits, including the\\nsubstantive ones — agent-commits-mid-turn, the subagent flow, stash/partial\\nstaging/split-changes, explain-from-clone, and the deep checkpoint metadata\\nvalidation.\\n\\nThe remaining 26 are unrun because the xAI account exhausted its **free Grok\\nBuild quota** partway through a full-suite run. Every one of those failures is\\n`You've reached your free Grok Build usage limit` or `resource-exhausted`; none\\nis attributable to this code. A full suite run costs roughly \\\\$5–20 at the\\nmeasured rate (\\\\$0.042 for a 2-call turn).\\n\\n## Fixes found along the way\\n\\n- **`content` shape collision** — Grok overloads the transcript `content` key\\n  (array on `tool_call_update`, object on message chunks). Typing it as a slice\\n  made every message chunk fail to unmarshal *silently*, since readers skip\\n  unparseable lines. Caught by a unit test using a real transcript.\\n- **`test:ci` on spaced paths** — `TestBetterleaksDoesNotPoisonGitEnvironment`\\n  interpolated the repo root into a synthesized `go.mod` `replace` directive\\n  unquoted, so it failed in any checkout whose path contains a space. Unrelated\\n  to Grok; fixed.\\n- **`agent` binary collision** — Cursor's CLI is named `agent`, and xAI's\\n  installer force-symlinks the same path. Whichever installs second owns it, so\\n  `$PATH` ordering cannot separate them and the `cursor-cli` E2E leg could\\n  exercise Grok while reporting Cursor. The runner now resolves the unambiguous\\n  `cursor-agent`, honours `E2E_CURSOR_BIN`, and probes `--version` as a backstop.\\n- **Foreign hook payloads** — Grok scans `~/.claude/settings.json` for hooks by\\n  default and treats the user scope as always-trusted, so it executes Entire's\\n  `entire hooks claude-code …` commands. Measured impact is nil (no session, no\\n  state, either side of the change), so the added guard is hardening plus a\\n  warning rather than a corruption fix — the comment says so. The real fix is\\n  `[compat.claude] hooks = false` in the user's `~/.grok/config.toml`.\\n\\n## Reviewer notes\\n\\n- **`grok` is deliberately NOT in the default E2E matrix.** It is wired into all\\n  three workflows as a `workflow_dispatch` choice with an `XAI_API_KEY` env, but\\n  `e2e.yml` runs on push to `main`, and enrolling a leg before the secret exists\\n  would break main. Promote it by adding `\\\"grok\\\"` to the `agents=[...]` arrays\\n  once the secret is configured.\\n- **`SubagentSessionResolver`'s happy path is unverified.** Grok subagents being\\n  independent child sessions is confirmed from a real run (one `spawn_subagent`\\n  produced two session IDs and the checkpoint held two top-level sessions both\\n  claiming the same file). The `subagents/meta.json` *field names* come from\\n  serde strings in the shipping binary, not documentation, and have not been\\n  checked against a real directory. The resolver fails closed — unique match\\n  required, stated parent must agree with the owning directory — so a mismatch\\n  is inert, not wrong. Confirming this is the first thing to do when quota returns.\\n- Agent-help classification: `grok` is registered like the other agents and\\n  inherits the existing agent surface; no new command was added, so there is no\\n  `agentHelpClassification` entry to review.\\n\\n## Since review\\n\\n- **Path traversal (trail finding, GHSA-2h46 class)** — `session_start` is the\\n  one hook without `transcriptPath`, so its `sessionId` became a directory\\n  component unvalidated. `sessionRef` now runs `validation.ValidateSessionID`\\n  at the choke point (as Pi does) and yields no `SessionRef` on an unsafe ID.\\n- **`entire session resume` launches Grok** — `ResumeCommandSpecFor` gained a\\n  `grok` case (`grok --resume <id>`, or `grok --continue` with no ID), with the\\n  same unsafe-ID guard as the other agents.\\n- **Merged `main`** (no rebase, so review threads stay attached) and adopted the\\n  new `AreHooksInstalled(ctx) (bool, error)` contract: missing hook file →\\n  `(false, nil)`, unreadable file or unresolvable root → error.\\n- Grok Build added to the supported-agent lists in `CLAUDE.md`, `e2e/README.md`,\\n  the contributor guide, the security doc, and the integration checklist.\\n- **Subagent double-count root-caused and fixed.** The 08-27 E2E re-run of\\n  `TestSubagentCommitFlow` still produced two top-level sessions both claiming\\n  `docs/red.md`. Logs show the child fires `subagent_stop` and `session_end` but\\n  never `stop`; `subagent_stop` was mapped to `SubagentEnd`, which the handler\\n  drops for lack of an in-flight marker (Grok gives no tool-use ID), so the\\n  `TurnEnd`-only `ResolveSubagentSession` path was never reached. `subagent_stop`\\n  now maps to the child's `TurnEnd` (the Droid Workers path) and `subagent_start`\\n  is a no-op (its pre-task capture failed on every launch). Falls back to the\\n  previous behaviour when no parent link resolves.\\n- All five review threads are addressed in code (three-tier hook timeouts,\\n  `XAI_API_KEY` scoped to the grok leg, `cwd`-keyed session group); the\\n  `parseTime`/`RFC3339` comment is a non-issue — Go's parser accepts fractional\\n  seconds with that layout, verified against the fixture timestamp.\\n\\n## Open product decisions (not decided in this PR)\\n\\n1. **Foreign-config collision.** Grok reads `~/.claude/settings.json` hooks by\\n   default, so it runs Entire's Claude Code hook commands with Grok payloads.\\n   The Claude Code side now ignores those payloads, and the E2E runner sets\\n   `[compat.claude] hooks = false`, but nothing in `entire enable` tells a real\\n   user to do the same. Options: warn during `entire enable grok` when\\n   `~/.grok/config.toml` lacks the compat switch, or leave it to docs.\\n2. **Project-trust gate.** Grok silently skips project hooks in a folder not\\n   listed in `~/.grok/trusted_folders.toml`, so `entire enable grok` can succeed\\n   while no hook ever fires. Options: detect and warn (pointing at\\n   `/hooks-trust`), or install into the always-trusted global `~/.grok/hooks/`\\n   — rejected in AGENT.md because it would fire Entire hooks in every repo.\\n\\n## Still blocked on xAI quota\\n\\n- Full E2E run (`mise run test:e2e --agent grok`, or dispatch `e2e.yml` with\\n  `agent=grok` once `XAI_API_KEY` exists as a repo secret).\\n- ~~Verifying `SubagentSessionResolver` / the subagent checkpoint shape~~ —\\n  **done (09-02)**: the resolver matched a real `subagents/meta.json`, and with\\n  the `FilesTouched` fix the checkpoint holds exactly one session plus\\n  `tasks/<child>/task.json`.\\n- Live observation of `SubagentStart/Stop`, `StopCancelled/Failure`,\\n  `PreCompact/PostCompact`, `Notification` — currently mapped from docs only.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches checkpoint lifecycle, subagent attribution, and cross-agent hook collision behavior; incorrect mappings could miss or duplicate checkpoints, though guards are conservative and E2E is opt-in on CI.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **Grok Build** as a preview Entire agent (`grok`): hooks in `.grok/hooks/entire.json`, lifecycle parsing (including `StopCancelled`/`StopFailure` as turn ends and filtering teardown `Stop`), `updates.jsonl` JSON-RPC transcript handling (tokens, models, file diffs), and a fail-closed **subagent parent linker**.\\n> \\n> **Claude Code** now ignores hook payloads with no `session_id` (with a warning), so Grok-driven invocations of global Claude hooks do not produce empty-session lifecycle events; tests cover real Grok-shaped payloads.\\n> \\n> **E2E**: new `e2e/agents/grok.go` (isolated `GROK_HOME`, compat flags, trust seeding, quota vs transient errors). Workflows expose `grok` on manual dispatch with `XAI_API_KEY` and install steps, but **not** in the default `main` matrix. **Cursor CLI** E2E prefers `cursor-agent` / `E2E_CURSOR_BIN` and fails bootstrap if `agent` resolves to Grok.\\n> \\n> Also adds a Grok integration probe script, registry/hooks wiring, and a small **redact** test fix quoting `go.mod` replace paths with spaces.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 9d6c40b389990d0d9634eb078c9ecbbc8eabfa8e. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2127/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2127/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2327\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2327/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2327/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2327/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2327\",\n              \"id\": 5391178766,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCuhTvw\",\n              \"number\": 2327,\n              \"title\": \"feat(checkpoint): add `entire checkpoint migrate`\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"toby\",\n                \"id\": 83556,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTU2\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83556?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toby\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/toby\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toby/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toby/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toby/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toby/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toby/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toby/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toby/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toby/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toby/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-08T19:45:32Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-15T18:35:00Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2327\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2327\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2327.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2327.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1271\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n> **Stacked on #2335** (`feat(checkpoint): elect the Entire remote for checkpoint sync`). Review that first; this PR's base is its branch and will be retargeted to `main` once it merges. Best reviewed **commit by commit**: the four commits are layered so each builds and is reviewable on its own.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nOnce an Entire remote is elected (#2335), new checkpoints flow there, but the ones already pushed to GitHub stay behind. This PR brings that backlog over, verifies it, and cleans up the old remote with consent, then rewards the user with what they have accumulated.\\n\\n## Commits\\n\\n1. **`feat(strategy): checkpoint artifact migration engine`** — inventory, hydrate into a tmp namespace and promote via `SafelyAdvanceLocalRef`, requeue, verify at the local hash, chunked delete. Removal addresses the old remote by its single push URL so the dedicated-`checkpoint_remote` rewrite can never apply, and refuses fan-out remotes. `batchPushRefs` chunks refspecs (a backlog publish overran ARG_MAX); `PushQueue.EnqueueAll`; `remote.DeleteRefs` (trail cleanup reuses it); the ls-remote parser moves into the `checkpoint` package. **Review question:** can anything be deleted that was not verified? Never force-pushed?\\n2. **`feat(checkpoint): migration planner, copy and value summary`** — the pure planner over the repo's state (no remotes, dedicated store, fail-closed setting, choice among remotes, pinned elsewhere, already home, publish only, migrate, convert first) and every user-facing string in one file; the local value block; `formatTokenCount` gains `M`. **Review question:** are the states and the copy right?\\n3. **`feat(checkpoint): add entire checkpoint migrate`** — the command. Two planning passes (local facts, then ls-remote inventories), pickers whose first option is always no-change, `--to` recorded in `.entire/settings.local.json` only when the election would not already pick it, git-branch repos converted to refs and flipped, publish through the OPF- and policy-gated queue flush, verify, then delete only verified refs and only with consent (`--remove` when non-interactive; `--yes` never implies it). Bare non-interactive runs report and change nothing. Classified user-owned and unlisted in agent-help. **Review question:** is the non-interactive contract safe for agents?\\n4. **`feat(status): surface the checkpoint migration in status, doctor, enable and docs`** — the network-free status nudge and `checkpoint_sync_migration` JSON field, doctor's destination check, the re-enable pointer, the command name restored in the announcement, hint and topology advice, and the docs.\\n\\n## Decisions for reviewers\\n\\n- `checkpoint migrate` is **user-owned and unlisted** in agent-help: it pushes transcripts, deletes remote refs and writes settings.\\n- The backend flip writes the **project** `.entire/settings.json` (a repo-wide format decision) and prints a commit hint; it is skipped under `ENTIRE_CHECKPOINTS_PRIMARY`.\\n- The ledger records `done` once data is verified on the destination, and `declined` when cleanup is refused; both silence the status nudge.\\n- No prompt inside `git push`; the hook announces and points at the command. Offering the migration from `repo mirror use`, which creates the remote, is a natural follow-up.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- `mise run lint`: 0 issues. Full unit and integration suites (both backends) and the Vogon canary pass on the stack.\\n- New: 14 engine tests over two local bares, 30-row planner table, executor tests against a fake engine (verify-missing stops before remove, remove failure keeps the ledger honest, decline records declined, `--yes` never removes, `--dry-run` only lists), status rendering tests, and seven end-to-end `checkpoint migrate` scenarios on both backends.\\n- Copilot's earlier comment that `for i := range count` does not compile is incorrect (Go 1.22+; this module is Go 1.26) and its suggested patch would not compile; the test passes.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2327/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2327/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2180\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2180/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2180/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2180/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2180\",\n              \"id\": 5294323027,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBhzniQ\",\n              \"number\": 2180,\n              \"title\": \"Confine Entire's filesystem use to `os.Root` anchors\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"pjbgf\",\n                \"id\": 5452977,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NTI5Nzc=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5452977?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pjbgf\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-30T20:54:52Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-01T13:15:42Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-01T13:15:40Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2180\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2180\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2180.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2180.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-01T13:15:40Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1184\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\nEstablish os.Root anchors for the seven trees Entire reads and writes using names it does not control, including agent session IDs, tool-use IDs, investigation run IDs, git status output, and checkpoint tree entries fetched from a remote. Each tree has one owning abstraction, and operations beneath an anchor reject symlinks instead of merely relying on os.Root\\r\\n  containment.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ### Anchors\\r\\n\\r\\n  One owning abstraction per tree: entiredir, gitdir, worktreedir, agent.SessionStore, agent.HookConfigFile, userdirs, and pluginRoot.\\r\\n\\r\\n  Long-lived anchors are memoized through a single osroot.Shared registry. agent.SessionStore is intentionally opened per operation because transcript fallback search may probe hundreds of candidate directories; retaining those roots in the non-evicting registry would consume one file descriptor per candidate.\\r\\n\\r\\n  Resolver-derived files must use the anchor for their owning tree. They must not create an anchor from filepath.Dir of the target being opened, because that places the caller-resolved components above the root and leaves them unenforced. Explicit caller-named settings and token-store paths are documented exceptions because the parent directory is itself part of the caller’s selection.\\r\\n\\r\\n  TestRootBasesAreTrusted fails the build when a new root-opening site is not on the allowlist, or when an allowlisted site no longer opens a root.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ### Refusals\\r\\n\\r\\n  - .entire must be a real directory, and every direct entry must be a regular file or directory. Four distinct failure conditions are matched positively so the reported remedy fits the  fault.\\r\\n\\r\\n  - Symlinks are refused, not followed or silently skipped, in trees Entire owns, including at a walk root and in every component beneath an anchor.\\r\\n\\r\\n    fs.WalkDir obtains its root DirEntry using fs.Stat, which follows symlinks, while only entries below the root come from ReadDir. The previous callback guards inspected d.Type(), so\\r\\n    they did not protect the walk root. A symlinked .entire/metadata/<session> could therefore be traversed and have its target committed and pushed. This protection had previously existed\\r\\n    with filepath.Walk, which uses Lstat, and was lost during conversion.\\r\\n\\r\\n  - Filesystem operations pin path components instead of checking and resolving them again. Parent directories are opened one component at a time, with symlinks rejected at every level.\\r\\n    Reads, writes, directory creation, removal, enumeration, and walks then operate relative to those pinned descriptors. This closes the check/use gap where an attacker could replace a\\r\\n    verified directory before the subsequent operation.\\r\\n\\r\\n  - Worktree content read or modified by Entire also rejects symlink components where following them would redirect the operation. This includes agent hook configuration, managed agent\\r\\n    scaffold files, .gitignore, .worktreeinclude, agent session files, and files read for trail-review selected text.\\r\\n\\r\\n  - Settings resolved by Entire are never read through a link, enforced in the settings reader itself because eighteen call sites invoke settings.Load without passing through the pre-run\\r\\n    guard. Explicit caller-selected settings paths trust the caller-selected parent as their root but still refuse a symlink at the target file.\\r\\n\\r\\n  - “We could not find out” is not “there is nothing here.” WorktreeRoot falls back to the current directory only after Git positively reports that the directory is not in a repository. It\\r\\n    does not fall back when Git is absent from $PATH, repository ownership is dubious, the context is cancelled, or repository discovery otherwise fails.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ### Interrupted atomic writes\\r\\n\\r\\n  jsonutil.WriteFileAtomicIn creates a temporary file named <base>.<16 hex>.tmp beside its target. Because .entire/metadata/<session> is copied wholesale into checkpoint trees, a hook\\r\\n  killed during an atomic write could leave an orphan that was committed in every later checkpoint.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ParseChunkIndex also previously used fmt.Sscanf(\\\"%03d\\\"), which stops successfully at the first non-digit. A temporary file whose random suffix began with digits could therefore be\\r\\n  interpreted as a transcript chunk.\\r\\n\\r\\n  Checkpoint walks now recognize and ignore only the complete temporary-file naming pattern, while ParseChunkIndex accepts only an entirely numeric suffix.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ### Repository opening\\r\\n  gitrepo.OpenCurrent no longer falls back to OpenPath(\\\".\\\") when the worktree root cannot be established.\\r\\n\\r\\n  The single caller that intentionally wants best-effort cwd behavior uses OpenCurrentOrCwd explicitly. It is dispatched from main.go after Cobra processing, reads only a policy ref, and\\r\\n  discards every error.\\r\\n\\r\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n> [!NOTE]\\r\\n> **High Risk**\\r\\n> Broad security and correctness changes to path containment, symlink handling, repository resolution, and checkpoint metadata walks; misconfiguration could break enable/hooks, transcript restore, or open the wrong repo in edge cases.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> **Overview**\\r\\n> Routes Entire’s sensitive filesystem work through **trusted `os.Root` anchors** (`.entire`, git common dir, worktree, hook configs, session stores, etc.) instead of assembling absolute paths and calling plain `os.*`. **CLAUDE.md** documents the seven trees, symlink refusal, atomic-write temp handling, and when rooting is deliberately skipped.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> **Agent hook configs** now go through shared **`agent.HookConfigFile`** / `OpenHookConfig` on the worktree root (all built-in agents), so `entire enable` cannot create or write through a checked-in symlinked `.claude` / `.cursor` / `.codex` / etc. **Session transcript writes** are centralized in **`agent.SessionStore`** and **`WriteSessionFile`**, rejecting session IDs that escape the agent’s session directory. **`.entire` transcript caches** (OpenCode export, Pi hook cache, Factory fallback state) use **`entiredir`** + **`ReadTranscriptFile`** / **`StatTranscriptFile`** for reads under `.entire`.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> **Checkpoint safety:** `ParseChunkIndex` only accepts an all-digit suffix (no more `fmt.Sscanf` mis-reading `full.jsonl.<hex>.tmp` as a chunk); walks are documented to skip `jsonutil` temp names. **`gitrepo.OpenCurrent`** no longer falls back to `OpenPath(\\\".\\\")` when the worktree cannot be resolved; **`OpenCurrentOrCwd`** is reserved for the one advisory caller. External-agent discovery tests inject worktree root via **`settings.WithWorktreeRoot`** instead of relying on removed cwd-relative settings fallbacks.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 1d863f6ed67cbd5f95b1a45a26f75a2c386b3143. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\r\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2180/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2180/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2188\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2188/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2188/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2188/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2188\",\n              \"id\": 5298216312,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBk0ABA\",\n              \"number\": 2188,\n              \"title\": \"fix(strategy): bound turn checkpoint finalization\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"id\": 34813274,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-31T08:41:55Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-16T08:29:55Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-16T08:29:55Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2188\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2188\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2188.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2188.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-16T08:29:55Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Closes #2148\\n\\nAt turn end, finalize rewrites every checkpoint the turn created with the full transcript. Each rewrite can fetch refs and blobs from the remote. Every fetch has its own limit, and the dead-network memos keep a remote that is down from costing that limit once per checkpoint. Nothing limited the pass as a whole, though. A slow remote that still answers finishes each fetch just under its limit, trips neither memo, and the total outlasts the host's hook timeout. The host kills the hook before Entire saves session state. The checkpoints keep their provisional transcripts, and the only trace is a few warning logs.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\nThe network phase of `finalizeAllTurnCheckpoints`, meaning the checkpoint store open and the write loop, now runs under a deadline. The deadline comes from the real limit the agent's host puts on the turn-end hook.\\n\\n**Finalize checks the deadline at entry and in the network phase, never in the middle of local work.** If the deadline has already passed at entry, finalize doesn't start. Nothing it prepared could be written by then, and the hook needs that time to save state. Reading, sanitizing, externalizing and redacting the transcript is local work that never looks at the context, so nothing cuts it off halfway. Its time still counts against the budget. If it runs long, finalize stops at the first network step instead of starting fetches it can't finish. Finalize checks again after the store opens, so precompute doesn't hash the transcript for writes that will never start. A write that fails as the deadline passes logs its error, and finalize then counts it as an interruption.\\n\\n**The deadline is `processStart` plus a per-agent budget**, the same pattern `sessionEndCondenseDeadline` uses. The host starts its clock when it spawns the hook, so Entire starts its clock at process start too. The budget comes from the agent running the hook, not from `state.AgentType`, which can be empty.\\n\\n**Each agent declares its host's turn-end hook timeout** through a new `agent.TurnEndHookTimeouter` capability. Entire derives the budget from it in one place, so changing the timeout changes the budget too. #1237 just changed Claude Code's. `agent.TurnEndBudgetWithin` keeps a fifth of the timeout, between 2s and 10s, for saving state after finalize. A timeout of zero or less falls back to the default.\\n\\n| Agent | Turn-end hook limit | Source | Budget |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Claude Code | 120s | `checkpointHookTimeoutSec` | 110s |\\n| Antigravity | 300s | `stopHookTimeoutSeconds` | 290s |\\n| Factory AI Droid | 60s | Host default ([docs](https://docs.factory.com/reference/hooks-reference)) | 50s |\\n| Codex | 30s | `defaultHookTimeoutSec` | 24s |\\n| Copilot CLI | 30s | Host default ([docs](https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/reference/hooks-configuration)) | 24s |\\n| Pi | 10s | The extension's `execFile` timeout, pinned by a test | 8s |\\n| Cursor, OpenCode, Vogon, external agents | Unknown or none | `defaultTurnEndHookTimeout` (30s) | 24s |\\n\\n`TestTurnEndHookTimeoutLedger` makes every built-in agent either declare a timeout or appear in `turnEndHookTimeoutFallbacks` with a reason, and it fails on a stale entry. A new agent can't pick up the default by accident. External agents always get the default, because the protocol has no field for a hook timeout.\\n\\n## When finalize is cut short\\n\\n- Checkpoints finalize already rewrote keep the full transcript. The rest keep their provisional one.\\n- The unfinalized IDs stay in `TurnCheckpointIDs`, as they already do for the late-transcript and degraded-scanner exits. A second Stop in the same turn retries them with a fresh budget. Otherwise the next turn start clears them and the provisional transcripts stay for good. I expect the retry to be rare. Claude Code, Codex, Copilot CLI and most other hosts fire Stop once per turn, so for them a cut-off checkpoint keeps its provisional transcript. That's the price of finishing inside the host's limit, and I think it's the right trade.\\n- Finalize sets `CaptureDegradedAt`, so `entire status` reports the problem. This now covers the host cancelling the hook too (SIGTERM ends the root context), which used to leave no trace.\\n- Finalize records the interruption where it sees it rather than guessing afterwards. An ordinary write error doesn't count as degradation. One older path also keeps the IDs; see \\\"Not included\\\".\\n- A cut-off checkpoint shows up once, as capture degradation, and not again as a finalize error.\\n\\n## Older Antigravity installs\\n\\nThe Antigravity budget assumes the 300s Stop timeout Entire installs. Installs from before bd1e2ff72 have no timeout, so agy's 30s default applies and kills the hook long before the 290s budget runs out. `AntigravityAgent.RepairHookTimeouts` lets `entire doctor` add the missing timeout without asking, the same repair Claude Code already has. It edits the raw JSON, so keys Entire doesn't model survive. It only touches Entire's own Stop handler, which it finds by command. It keeps a timeout that's already set under any key case, skips null entries, and leaves a disabled entry alone. The doctor message now covers an agent default that's too short as well as one that's too long.\\n\\nDoctor only helps people who run it. So Antigravity now also reports a missing Stop timeout through `CheckHookConfig`, and `entire status` shows \\\"Antigravity hooks out of date · run 'entire doctor'\\\". `--json` lists the agent under `hooks_outdated`. The check and the repair share one function, so status flags an install exactly when doctor has a timeout to add. Running doctor always clears the warning. A user's own handlers, a timeout they set, or a disabled entry never trigger it.\\n\\n## Decision for reviewers\\n\\n**The 30s fallback** is a judgment call. Cursor documents only a \\\"platform default\\\". OpenCode has no limit at all. Entire's plugin runs the hook through `spawnSync`, which blocks OpenCode's UI until `entire` exits, so the fallback is the only limit OpenCode gets. 30s matches what Codex and Copilot enforce. It's one constant in `lifecycle.go`.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nFinalize deadline tests:\\n\\n- With no deadline, a future deadline, or slow fetches and no deadline, every checkpoint finalizes.\\n- A deadline that passed before the network phase, a deadline that expires mid-loop while the parent context lives, a context that ends mid-loop, and a parent cancelled before start each leave the right checkpoints provisional. Each records degradation and counts no error.\\n- An expired deadline at entry skips preparation, keeps the IDs and records degradation.\\n- A deadline that passes while finalize prepares the transcript stops it before any fetch or precompute and keeps the IDs.\\n- When the host cancels the hook during preparation, the repository open fails. Finalize counts that as an interruption, not an error, and keeps the IDs.\\n- A second pass over kept IDs finalizes them and clears the list.\\n- An invalid checkpoint ID, or a write that fails while the context is alive, counts as an error and not as degradation.\\n- The degraded-scanner and late-transcript exits keep their IDs under an expired deadline.\\n- The logs give the deadline as its own cause, so a host cancellation never looks like the budget running out.\\n\\nAgent and budget tests:\\n\\n- Every agent that declares a timeout gets a budget above zero and below that timeout.\\n- Pi's Go constant matches the `.ts` extension.\\n- The ledger test above.\\n\\nAntigravity tests:\\n\\n- The repair adds a missing Stop timeout. It keeps an existing timeout, including `\\\"Timeout\\\"` in another case, and keeps unmodeled keys, foreign entries, a user's handler in the Stop list, `null` entries and a disabled entry. It leaves the file alone when there's nothing to add.\\n- The status check reports absent with no Entire entry, and current for a fresh install, an existing timeout in either case, a user's handler, or a disabled entry. It reports outdated only for Entire's Stop handler with no timeout.\\n\\nHow the timing tests stay deterministic:\\n\\n- In the parent-cancel mid-loop case, the fake fetcher ends the context itself.\\n- In the deadline mid-loop case, the second fetch blocks until the deadline fires. A 10s fallback makes a regression fail instead of hang. The deadline is 3s because it also covers transcript preparation and the store open, which leaves a slow runner time to reach the first fetch.\\n- The two preparation tests block the transcript read on a FIFO, so the deadline or the cancellation lands while preparation runs. Each test also fails if finalize exits before it reaches the read, so neither can pass on the entry check. They run on Unix only, since they need a FIFO.\\n\\nI checked each new test against a planted regression, and each one failed. The regressions were the deadline check moved to the top, the checks around the store open removed, the repository-open interruption check removed, writes ignoring the deadline, cancellation not flagged, a write error flagged as degradation, interrupted IDs cleared or kept off by one, Pi's constant drifting, and a missing or stale ledger entry.\\n\\nI also ran it end to end with a built binary. An Antigravity install with the Stop timeout removed shows the `entire status` warning. `entire doctor` adds the 300s timeout and the warning goes away. A fresh install shows no warning.\\n\\nOn the final commit, format, lint (0 issues), and the unit, integration and canary tests all pass.\\n\\n## Not included\\n\\n- No durable retry queue for cut-off checkpoints.\\n- No change to the per-fetch budgets, and no batching of missing-blob fetches.\\n- Entire doesn't read a hook timeout the user lowered themselves in Claude Code, Codex, Antigravity or Copilot CLI. The budget comes from the timeout Entire installs or the host default.\\n- Entire doesn't write an explicit timeout into Cursor's hook config. That would swap the fallback for a known limit. But existing installs only get a hook config change through a doctor repair, so it belongs in its own PR.\\n- Local turn-end work counts against the budget, because the clock starts at process start like the host's. For an agent with no host limit, such as OpenCode, finalize can now give up on checkpoints that used to finish when local work runs long. A longer default for agents we know have no limit would fix that. Follow-up.\\n- Local preparation has no time limit once it starts. Finalize checks the deadline before and after it, so a long preparation never starts fetches, but preparation itself can eat into the headroom. Cursor's sidecar image read can take up to `sqlite3Timeout` (30s) against the assumed 30s hook limit. Pi has 2s of headroom to redact what may be a large transcript. The cheap fix is to cap the sidecar read at whatever deadline is left. Follow-up.\\n- If a turn start is missed because its hook failed or was killed, the kept IDs carry into the next turn. That turn's Stop then rewrites the older checkpoints with the newer turn's transcript and prompts, and skips the prompt backfill. The late-transcript and degraded-scanner exits could already do this. A slow remote makes it more likely. Follow-up.\\n- If the checkpoint store fails to open for any reason other than the deadline, finalize still returns with `TurnCheckpointIDs` set and doesn't record capture degradation. That predates this PR. Follow-up.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2188/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2188/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1211\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1211/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1211/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1211/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1211\",\n              \"id\": 4443057024,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7bX4-E\",\n              \"number\": 1211,\n              \"title\": \"feat: entire prompts search - searchable prompt history from checkpoints\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"AasheeshLikePanner\",\n                \"id\": 126905285,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOB5BrxQ\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/126905285?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/AasheeshLikePanner\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/AasheeshLikePanner\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/AasheeshLikePanner/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/AasheeshLikePanner/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/AasheeshLikePanner/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/AasheeshLikePanner/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/AasheeshLikePanner/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/AasheeshLikePanner/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/AasheeshLikePanner/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/AasheeshLikePanner/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/AasheeshLikePanner/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 6,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-05-14T04:04:24Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:29:05Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:29:05Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": true,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1211\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1211\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1211.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1211.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary:\\r\\n\\r\\nImplements `entire prompts` — a local, offline-first command for searching the prompts behind your checkpoint history. This is the \\\"search\\\" feature from the roadmap: surfacing the *why* behind commits, not just the *what*.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## What's in this PR\\r\\n\\r\\nFour commands:\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\nentire prompts search \\\"cache decision\\\"     # full-text search with filters\\r\\nentire prompts list                         # recent prompts, newest first\\r\\nentire prompts show <checkpoint-id>        # full prompt text for a checkpoint\\r\\nentire prompts index --rebuild / --status  # manage the local index\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nFilters on search: `--agent`, `--branch`, `--kind`, `--after`, `--files`, `--limit`, `--json`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## How it works \\r\\n\\r\\nOn every commit, the PostCommit hook appends a new entry to `.entire/prompts/index.ndjson` — a gitignored, appendable newline-delimited JSON file that lives next to your repo. No external service, no database, works offline.\\r\\n\\r\\nOn search, the index loads into memory and each entry gets scored:\\r\\n- Exact phrase match → +10\\r\\n- All query tokens found → +5  \\r\\n- Any token found → +1\\r\\n- Term density bonus → up to +2\\r\\n\\r\\nTokenization runs NFC unicode normalization → lowercase → word boundary split → stopword filter → Porter stemmer. So `\\\"caching\\\"` matches prompts containing `\\\"cache\\\"`, `\\\"cached\\\"`, `\\\"caches\\\"`.\\r\\n\\r\\nQueries are sanitised before tokenizing — regex metacharacters stripped, minimum 2-char guard, quoted phrases extracted for exact matching.\\r\\n\\r\\nFile locking on writes: `O_CREATE|O_EXCL` for atomic acquisition, 3 retries with 50ms backoff for concurrent PostCommit hooks, stale lock detection (>30s) to survive crashes.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## Architecture decisions\\r\\n\\r\\n- **NDJSON over SQLite** — appendable without full rewrites, no CGO, human-readable, portable\\r\\n- **Porter stemmer** (`github.com/kljensen/snowball`) — one new pure-Go dependency, zero CGO\\r\\n- **Local index, not cloud** — prompts are personal context, should stay local and work offline\\r\\n- **PostCommit hook integration** — index updates happen transparently, no user action needed\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## Tests\\r\\n\\r\\n19 tests across `rank_test.go` and `store_test.go`:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Tokenizer: stemming, stopwords, unicode normalization, special chars\\r\\n- Query parser: basic, phrase extraction, regex stripping, min length\\r\\n- Scorer: exact phrase, all tokens, term density\\r\\n- Search: ranking, empty query, filter application\\r\\n- Store: concurrent writes, single entry, empty slice, lock contention\\r\\n\\r\\nBenchmarks:\\r\\n- Tokenize: ~0.1ms\\r\\n- Search 1K entries: 5.6ms (target <100ms)\\r\\n- Index load 1K entries: 2.8ms (target <50ms)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Tested live** against 4 real checkpoints, 94 prompts, 98KB index. Search, list, show all working end-to-end.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## Known gaps \\r\\n\\r\\nThree things are stubbed or incomplete — none affect the core feature working:\\r\\n\\r\\n- `ReviewPrompt` for `agent_review` kind not yet wired — entries with `kind: agent_review` fall back to empty prompt text. Will fix in follow-up.\\r\\n- `TokenCount`, `ParentCheckpointID`, `SubagentDepth` fields exist in the schema but aren't populated from metadata yet.\\r\\n- `entire prompts index --verify` flag exists but is a no-op placeholder.\\r\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1211/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1211/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1560\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1560/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1560/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1560/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1560\",\n              \"id\": 4770320551,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7r5DhN\",\n              \"number\": 1560,\n              \"title\": \"explain: enrich JSON summary and surface list truncation\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"computermode\",\n                \"id\": 2917645,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTc2NDU=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2917645?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/computermode\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-06-29T17:37:50Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-29T20:43:53Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-06-29T20:43:52Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1560\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1560\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1560.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1560.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-06-29T20:43:52Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/692\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What\\n\\nEnriches `entire explain` output across four small, related gaps:\\n\\n1. **Full summary in `--json`** — the JSON export previously dropped everything except `intent`/`outcome`, even though the prose view already renders friction, open items, and learnings. `--json` now exposes the full persisted `Summary` (`friction`, `open_items`, and categorized `learnings` → `repo`/`code`/`workflow`).\\n2. **List truncation visibility** — the prose branch list silently capped at 100 checkpoints. It now prints a stderr note when checkpoints are hidden, pointing at `--json --limit <N>`.\\n3. **Fast-fail `--generate` on imported checkpoints** — the read-only rejection now happens on metadata alone, before fetching transcript blobs.\\n4. **Clearer no-trailer message** — distinguishes a commit that exists but wasn't created during an Entire session from a commit that wasn't found.\\n\\n## How\\n\\n- `explain_export.go`: extended `checkpointSessionSummary` with `learnings`/`friction`/`open_items` (all `omitempty`); new `summaryToExportJSON` helper reuses the existing `hasAnyLearning` so empty learnings stay `nil` (no `{}` noise). Redaction is already applied upstream at persist time, so no new privacy surface.\\n- `explain.go`: branch list probes `branchCheckpointsLimit+1` and slices to the cap via the extracted, unit-tested `capBranchCheckpoints`; threaded `errW` through the call chain. Added a metadata-only `ReadCheckpoint` guard before the content load for imported `--generate`. Reworded the no-trailer hint.\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- The `--limit` flag help still reads \\\"Only meaningful with --json\\\" — accurate, since the prose path keeps the fixed 100 cap and points users at `--json --limit` rather than honoring `--limit` itself.\\n- Truncation wording is deliberately vague (\\\"more exist\\\") — the `limit+1` probe only proves ≥1 more exists, never an exact count.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n`mise run check` passes: fmt clean, lint 0 issues, all unit + integration + e2e canary tests green. New tests: `TestSessionMetadataToJSON_FullSummary`, `TestSessionMetadataToJSON_EmptySummaryStaysClean`, `TestCapBranchCheckpoints`, plus a `--generate`-on-imported rejection assertion in `TestImportClaudeCode_EndToEnd`.\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> CLI output and JSON export parity only; no auth, persistence, or security surface changes beyond exposing summary fields already stored and shown in prose.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **`entire checkpoint explain --json`** now includes the full persisted session summary—`friction`, `open_items`, and categorized `learnings`—via `summaryToExportJSON`, matching what the prose view already shows. Empty categories stay omitted (`omitempty`).\\n> \\n> **Branch / list views** (`checkpoint list`, default explain) fetch `limit+1` checkpoints, cap at 100 with `capBranchCheckpoints`, and print a **stderr** note when more exist (pointing at `--json --limit <N>`). `errW` is threaded through the branch explain call chain so truncation never pollutes piped stdout.\\n> \\n> **`--generate`** on imported checkpoints is rejected after a metadata-only `ReadCheckpoint` check, avoiding prefetch and transcript loads for a guaranteed read-only failure.\\n> \\n> The **no Entire-Checkpoint trailer** hint now states the commit exists but was not created in an Entire session (or the trailer was removed).\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit cdd32fa9502414035a774a59b97a3d615ed87bdc. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1560/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1560/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1527\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1527/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1527/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1527/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1527\",\n              \"id\": 4747651055,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7qwUr-\",\n              \"number\": 1527,\n              \"title\": \"Add import tool for sessions prior to enabling Entire\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"computermode\",\n                \"id\": 2917645,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTc2NDU=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2917645?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/computermode\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-06-25T21:52:39Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-26T19:52:05Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-06-26T00:53:21Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1527\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1527\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1527.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1527.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-06-26T00:53:21Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/668\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\n## What\\r\\n\\r\\nAdds the ability to import a coding agent's pre-existing local transcripts into Entire as read-only checkpoints, so a repo adopting Entire isn't starting from zero (`checkpoint list`/`explain`, `search`, `tokens`, and server-side recap/UI work on day-one history). Supports #1336 (enable doesn't prompt to import yet - requires manual kickoff for validation first). Claude Code is the only agent implemented; the package is structured so others can be added.\\r\\n\\r\\nSurface: a hidden command, discoverable via `entire labs`:\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\nentire import claude-code [--path DIR] [--dry-run] [--session ID]...\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nThere is intentionally **no** enable-time prompt this pass — importing is an explicit, opt-in command.\\r\\n\\r\\n## How\\r\\n\\r\\n- New `cmd/entire/cli/agentimport/` package. The orchestration (discovery loop, idempotent per-turn IDs, redaction, checkpoint write) is agent-agnostic; each agent plugs in an `Importer` (`Discover` + `SplitTurns`). A static list of supported importers backs `entire import <agent>` — adding an agent is a new `Importer`, no command wiring.\\r\\n- Discovers `~/.claude/projects/<sanitized-repo-path>/*.jsonl` (fixed **one-month** lookback), splits each session into **per-user-prompt turns**, and writes one checkpoint per turn — reusing existing transcript parsing, per-turn token accounting (incl. subagent rollups), and redaction (`redact.JSONLBytes`).\\r\\n- Imported checkpoints are stored on the normal `entire/checkpoints/v1` metadata branch, tagged `Kind:\\\"imported\\\"` with provenance (source, session/turn UUIDs, line range, content hash, import version). They're **commit-less** (no `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer) and surface in `list`/`explain` via an `Imported` flag, labeled `[imported]`.\\r\\n- **Idempotent**: per-turn checkpoint IDs are `sha256(sessionID + \\\"/\\\" + turnUUID)`, so re-running skips already-imported turns.\\r\\n- **Not rewindable**: `checkpoint rewind` refuses imported checkpoints with a clear read-only message.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Tradeoffs / known limitations (do later)\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Import is manual.** It is not offered during `entire enable` (an earlier iteration prompted at enable time; removed for now). Users run `entire import claude-code` when they want it.\\r\\n- **Imported history is pushed** to the backend like normal checkpoints (it's what lights up server-side search/recap/UI). **Privacy note:** up to a month of old conversations (and provenance such as `transcript_path`) sync on the next push, unless checkpoint pushing is disabled. (An earlier iteration kept imports local-only on a separate `entire/imports/v1` ref; reverted — it caused explain-by-id and `[temporary]`-duplication bugs and was a cross-cutting overhaul. Single-ref is simpler; a local-only/opt-in-to-push mode could be revisited.)\\r\\n- **Read-only** by design: imported checkpoints have no working-tree snapshot, so they are not rewindable.\\r\\n- **Claude Code only** this pass (the package and `entire import <agent>` surface leave room for others).\\r\\n\\r\\n## Reviewer notes\\r\\n\\r\\n- `Kind:\\\"imported\\\"` + `Provenance` + an `Imported` umbrella flag were added to the checkpoint metadata contract (`api/checkpoint`).\\r\\n- Verified locally: `mise run lint` (0 issues) and `mise run test:ci` (unit + integration + e2e canary) green; an end-to-end integration test covers dry-run, import, `[imported]` labeling (no `[temporary]` duplication), explain-by-id, idempotency, and rewind refusal.\\r\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1527/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1527/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1616\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1616/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1616/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1616/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1616\",\n              \"id\": 4798051681,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7tTsv6\",\n              \"number\": 1616,\n              \"title\": \"cli: add code search with multi-region fan-out and TUI tab (ENT-990)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"evisdren\",\n                \"id\": 256443556,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD0kEpA\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256443556?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/evisdren\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 10,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-07-02T20:43:34Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-07T19:30:45Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-07T19:30:44Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1616\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1616\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1616.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1616.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-07T19:30:44Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\n- Adds `cmd/entire/cli/codesearch/` — client package for peregrine's `/search/api/search` endpoint\\n- Wires `--code` and `--case-sensitive` flags into `entire search`, gated behind `ENTIRE_CODE_SEARCH=1`\\n- Multi-region fan-out using the shared cell-routing foundation (`cell_fanout.go`): list repos → group by cell → parallel search with per-cell timeouts → merge results\\n- Adds a **Code tab** (key `4`) to the interactive search TUI, showing code search results alongside checkpoints, sessions, and commits\\n- Code search runs in parallel with checkpoint search when the TUI launches\\n- Detail pane shows file location, score, and context lines (before/after) for the selected match\\n\\n## How it works\\n\\n| Scenario | Auth path | Behavior |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `--code query` (no filter) | `ListRepos` → group by cell → `fanOutCells` | Fan-out across all cells |\\n| `--code --repo owner/name query` | Single cell via repo filter resolution | Single cell (repo's owner) |\\n| `--code repo:owner/name query` | Same (inline filter parsed) | Single cell |\\n| `--code --all-repos query` | Fan-out (same as no filter) | Fan-out across all cells |\\n| TUI Code tab | Async `performCodeSearch` tea.Cmd | Parallel with checkpoint search |\\n\\n## TUI Code Tab\\n\\n- Hidden behind `ENTIRE_CODE_SEARCH=1` feature flag (tab only appears when enabled)\\n- Results show `repo:path:line` as the title with the matching context line below\\n- Detail pane shows full context (before/after lines), repo, path, line, column, and score\\n- Full-screen detail view via Enter key, same as other tabs\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/codesearch/codesearch.go` — client types and `Search()` function\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/codesearch/codesearch_test.go` — client tests\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search_cmd.go` — command wiring, fan-out via shared `fanOutCells`, output formatters\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search_cmd_test.go` — command tests (merge, output, flags)\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search_tui.go` — Code tab: result rendering, detail pane, async fetch, key bindings\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search_tui_test.go` — updated for new `newSearchModel` signature\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/codesearch/...` passes\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/ -run TestSearch` passes\\n- [x] `mise run lint` clean\\n- [x] Manual testing with `ENTIRE_CODE_SEARCH=1 entire search auth`\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> New authenticated multi-cell fan-out and repo-index resolution can return incomplete results on truncation or partial failures; behavior is gated but touches core search UX and shared cell routing.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Introduces **code search** for `entire search`, behind **`ENTIRE_CODE_SEARCH=1`**, calling peregrine via a new **`codesearch`** package (`GET /api/v1/search/api/search` through the cell API gateway).\\n> \\n> **CLI:** New **`--code`** and **`--case-sensitive`** flags; checkpoint-only flags (`--author`, `--date`, `--branch`, `--page`) are rejected with `--code`. Repo scoping uses **`--repo`**, **`--all-repos`**, or inline **`repo:`** only—**`author:` / `date:` / `branch:`** stay in the query as literal text. Default scope is the current repo via **`currentRepoSlugWithForge`** (forge-prefixed slugs for index matching). Output is grep-style text or JSON, including **`failed_jurisdictions`** on partial multi-region failures.\\n> \\n> **Routing:** **`searchAllCells`** lists repos from the control plane, resolves filters to ULIDs (**`resolveRepoFilters`**, BFF-aligned), groups by cell, and uses shared **`fanOutCells`** with per-cell timeouts; **`mergeSearchResults`** ranks by score, dedupes, caps **`--limit`**, and tolerates partial cell errors.\\n> \\n> **TUI:** When the flag is on, search gains a **Code** tab (key **4**), async code search alongside checkpoint search, list/detail UI for matches, and generation-guarded stale result handling.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 66a9c67767467f64c0db19841cb1b6b94f9f5faf. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1616/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1616/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1650\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1650/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1650/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1650/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1650\",\n              \"id\": 4819808169,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7uYOwS\",\n              \"number\": 1650,\n              \"title\": \"cli: show recent sessions (not commits) in `entire activity`\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-07-06T13:54:16Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-06T18:24:24Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-06T18:24:22Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1650\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1650\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1650.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1650.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-06T18:24:22Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/769\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nThe entire.io Overview page renders a recent-**sessions** feed from `GET /api/v1/me/sessions`, but `entire activity` rendered a recent-**commits** feed from `/me/commits`. The two surfaces listed different things, so a session with no resulting commit never showed in the CLI, and a commit bundling several sessions showed as one row — the lists never lined up.\\n\\n## What\\n\\nMake sessions the default recent-list in `entire activity`, matching the web exactly. The stat cards, contribution heatmap, and repo chart (all from `/me/activity`) are unchanged; only the bottom list changes.\\n\\n- **Sessions feed** — fetch `/me/sessions` at `limit=50` (mirroring the web's `USER_OVERVIEW_RECENT_SESSIONS_LIMIT`), group by the local day of `lastActivityAt` (newest first, unknown last), and render one row per session with the same fields the web row shows: display name (capped at 120), repo, a `public` tag when `isPublic`, agent badge, friendly model label, and checkpoint count.\\n- **Commits stay available** behind `entire activity --commits`.\\n- **`formatModel` ported** from `entire.io/frontend/src/lib/model.ts` to Go so labels read identically (`claude-opus-4-6` → \\\"Opus 4.6\\\", `gpt-4o` → \\\"GPT-4o\\\", `gemini-2.0-flash` → \\\"Gemini 2.0 Flash\\\", legacy date suffixes stripped). Same test cases as the web's `model.test.ts`.\\n- **Routing** — reuses the existing `runAuthenticatedActivityAPI`, so `/me/sessions` goes to the caller's home entire-api cell with the data-API fallback (the routing landed in #1641).\\n- **Dedup** — extracts `fetchActivityWith` (activity aggregate + chosen list, fetched concurrently) and a generic `groupItemsByDay`, so the session and commit paths don't duplicate the plumbing.\\n\\n`entire agent-help activity` picks up the new `--commits` flag automatically (it renders live from the cobra tree).\\n\\n### Endpoint note\\n\\n`/me/sessions` reports `isPublic: false` unconditionally today (entire-api has no GitHub-login-on-session source), so the `public` tag is implemented for correctness but will rarely render from the cell — matching the repo sessions surface.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- New unit tests: `formatModel` (mirrors the web's `model.test.ts`), `groupSessionsByDay` (ordering + unknown-date handling), `fetchSessions` (path/window/envelope parsing via httptest), and session-row rendering (fields, singular/plural, untitled fallback).\\n- `mise run fmt` clean, `mise run lint` 0 issues, `mise run test:ci` green (unit + integration + Vogon canary).\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> User-facing CLI display and read-only API calls only; commits remain available via `--commits`, with solid unit test coverage.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **`entire activity` now defaults to a recent-sessions list** aligned with the entire.io Overview: it calls `GET /api/v1/me/sessions` with `limit=50`, groups by local day of `lastActivityAt`, and renders rows (title, repo, optional `public`, agent, formatted model, checkpoint count). Stat cards, heatmap, and repo chart from `/me/activity` are unchanged.\\n> \\n> **`entire activity --commits`** restores the previous recent-commits behavior. Static and TUI paths both branch on that flag; the header vs list rendering is split (`renderActivityHeader` + session or commit list).\\n> \\n> **Plumbing:** generic `fetchActivityWith` loads activity and the chosen list concurrently; `groupItemsByDay` / `localDayOf` dedupe day grouping for commits and sessions. **`formatModel`** is added in Go to mirror the web’s friendly model labels.\\n> \\n> Tests cover sessions fetch/render/grouping and `formatModel`; existing `runActivity` tests pass the new `showCommits` argument.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 887f764057293d18909e23374921e993d9606a6c. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1650/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1650/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1270\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1270/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1270/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1270/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1270\",\n              \"id\": 4528085420,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7fmu12\",\n              \"number\": 1270,\n              \"title\": \"Add Go v2 checkpoint migration tool\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"pfleidi\",\n                \"id\": 118549,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjExODU0OQ==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118549?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pfleidi\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 3,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-05-26T23:02:23Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-03T00:25:12Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-03T00:25:12Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": true,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1270\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1270\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1270.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1270.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## What\\nAdds a Go-based migration binary under `cmd/migrate-v2-checkpoints` to restore useful v2-only checkpoint data into v1 storage. It reuses the existing checkpoint stores instead of line-for-line porting the shell script.\\n\\n## How\\n- Adds optional commit timestamp support to committed checkpoint writes.\\n- Discovers checkpoint trailers in branch history after a selected base commit.\\n- Reads v2 metadata and raw transcript content through the v2 store.\\n- Writes restored v1 checkpoints through the production v1 `GitStore` path.\\n- Supports list, dry-run, and apply modes with skipped-data reporting.\\n- Adds focused tests for timestamp preservation, discovery, migration, dry-run, existing v1 data, and incomplete v2 data.\\n\\n## Notes\\nThe migration intentionally skips transcript data that lacks usable v2 metadata, since that data is not useful for v1 restoration by itself.\\n\\n## Verification\\n- `mise run lint`\\n- `go build -ldflags \\\"-X github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/versioninfo.Version=v0.0.0-dev-9df43932c -X github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/versioninfo.Commit=9df43932c\\\" -o /private/tmp/entire-pr-check ./cmd/entire`\\n- `go build -o /private/tmp/migrate-v2-checkpoints-pr-check ./cmd/migrate-v2-checkpoints`\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint ./cmd/migrate-v2-checkpoints -count=1`\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Apply mode rewrites the v1 metadata branch from discovered v2 data; mistakes could affect checkpoint history, though dry-run and skip-existing-session behavior limit exposure.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds a **`migrate-v2-checkpoints`** CLI that discovers checkpoints from **`Entire-Checkpoint`** trailers in normal branch history (with **`--since`**, **`--head`**, list / dry-run / apply) and restores eligible v2 sessions into v1 via the existing **`GitStore`** / **`V2GitStore`** paths, skipping sessions already on v1 and reporting missing v2 metadata or raw transcripts.\\n> \\n> Committed checkpoint writes gain optional **`CommitTime`** so metadata-branch commits can keep historical author/committer times during migration (zero still means “now”; **`CreatedAt`** is not reused as the git timestamp). Checkpoint pushes now use an explicit **`refs/heads/…:refs/heads/…`** refspec so stale **`refs/entire/checkpoints/v1`** refs cannot make the source branch ambiguous.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit f5ef3cab98abe5087b17f8834d8229ecc6cb2036. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1270/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1270/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1330\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1330/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1330/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1330/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1330\",\n              \"id\": 4573853188,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7h6TS3\",\n              \"number\": 1330,\n              \"title\": \"Read session resume checkpoints from v1.1 ref\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"pfleidi\",\n                \"id\": 118549,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjExODU0OQ==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118549?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pfleidi\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-06-02T18:06:09Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-02T20:15:03Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-06-02T20:15:00Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1330\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1330\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1330.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1330.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-06-02T20:15:00Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/483\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What\\n\\nPort `entire session resume <branch>` to read committed checkpoint metadata and transcripts from the configured committed checkpoint read store. When checkpoints v1.1 is enabled, resume now reads from the local custom ref instead of the v1 metadata branch.\\n\\n## How\\n\\n- Use `checkpoint.NewCommittedReadStore(ctx, repo)` in the resume metadata and transcript paths.\\n- Keep v1 remote metadata fetch behavior limited to v1 reads; v1.1 missing metadata is reported against the custom ref instead of falling back to v1.\\n- Update logs-only transcript restoration through `ManualCommitStrategy.RestoreLogsOnly` to use the same committed read store.\\n- Add focused v1 and v1.1 resume tests for metadata selection, squash/latest resolution, missing v1.1 metadata, and transcript restoration.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- [x] `mise run fmt`\\n- [x] `mise run lint`\\n- [x] `mise run build`\\n- [x] `mise run test`\\n\\n## Reviewer Notes\\n\\nThis PR intentionally avoids migrating general `checkpoint rewind` listing/interactive behavior. The shared `RestoreLogsOnly` path is updated because `session resume` uses it for transcript restoration.\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes how resume resolves metadata and transcripts across v1 vs v1.1 refs; wrong ref selection could block resume or restore stale logs, though behavior is covered by new tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **`entire session resume`** now loads committed checkpoint metadata and transcripts through **`checkpoint.NewCommittedReadStore`**, so checkpoints **v1.1** read from the configured local custom ref instead of falling back to **`entire/checkpoints/v1`**.\\n> \\n> The resume path drops direct metadata-branch tree reads and routes remote recovery through the same store/ref. **v1** remote fetch/promotion stays on the v1 branch only; when the active read ref is the v1.1 custom ref, missing metadata is reported as local-only (e.g. **`entire explain`**) rather than seeding from stale v1. Squash commits still pick the latest checkpoint by metadata timestamp. **`ManualCommitStrategy.RestoreLogsOnly`** uses the same committed read store for transcript restore (used by resume).\\n> \\n> Tests cover v1.1-only reads, no stale v1 fallback, squash latest selection, and v1.1 transcript restoration.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 6d37d3dfa447b8c52bbedb91236f9614f05ecd18. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1330/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1330/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1506\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1506/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1506/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1506/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1506\",\n              \"id\": 4728954081,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7pzhtw\",\n              \"number\": 1506,\n              \"title\": \"feat(runner): add `entire runner setup` to scaffold and tailor trail runners\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-06-23T19:32:34Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-01T13:58:31Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-01T13:58:30Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1506\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1506\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1506.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1506.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-01T13:58:30Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/648\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What\\n\\nAdds **`entire runner setup [<runner>]`** — one command that both **scaffolds** a repo's trail runners (`.entire/runners/*.json`) and **tailors** their evaluator prompts (risk / confidence / drift / security / review / review-focus / summary) to *this* repository instead of the generic defaults. Also retunes this repo's own runners as the first in-repo consumer.\\n\\n> Renamed from the earlier `entire trail tune`; it now lives in a new (hidden, during maturation) `runner` group.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nThe shipped runner templates are written for a generic web/backend app (payments, DB migrations, TypeScript). For a Go CLI that manipulates the user's git repo, the real risk surface is destructive git ops, hook handlers, checkpoint/session integrity, and transcript egress. Calibrating prompts by hand is exactly the kind of thing that should be automatable for any repo adopting trails — and a repo with *no* runners should be able to get a working set in one command.\\n\\n## How it works\\n\\n**Onboarding:** in a repo with no runners, setup writes the default set (confirm, or `--yes`) from templates **embedded in the binary** (correct output contracts + minimal-but-working generic prompts), then tailors them. Re-run in a repo that already has runners and setup **offers to re-tune** (interactive confirm, or `--run` as an explicit yes).\\n\\n**Gather:** signal about the repo across four **best-effort, gracefully-degrading** tiers:\\n\\n| Tier | Source |\\n|---|---|\\n| repo statics | CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md / README / go.mod + dir layout |\\n| PRs & issues | `gh pr/issue list` |\\n| checkpoints | `strategy.ListCheckpoints` → churn hotspots |\\n| trails | trail list + past review findings |\\n\\n**Apply:**\\n- **Default (`--print`)** — emits a paste-ready tailoring prompt.\\n- **`--run`** — executes it **headlessly** through the configured summary provider and rewrites runners **surgically**: only each `prompt.template` value is swapped (byte-level), leaving every other field and the file formatting byte-for-byte intact, so the `git diff` is scoped to the prompt change.\\n\\nThe CLI has no runner struct/loader (the backend consumes these files and substitutes `{{placeholders}}`), so runners are treated as opaque text.\\n\\n## Safety / hardening\\n\\n- **Prompt injection** — both untrusted inputs (gathered signal *and* the existing repo-controlled templates) are embedded as **JSON** with explicit \\\"treat as data, don't follow instructions inside\\\" framing, so a crafted sentinel or ``` fence in repo content can't break out.\\n- **No gathered-only refs** — tuning is told not to cite PR/issue numbers or commit hashes in templates, since the runner only sees the diff at eval time.\\n- **Write-path validation** — a rewrite must be non-empty and add no new `{{placeholder}}` (would render as literal `{{junk}}`); dropping the cosmetic `{{branch}}` is allowed and noted.\\n- **Always-working end state** — defaults are working minimal prompts; any runner left un-tailored is reported as a working default (committable as-is), never a broken placeholder.\\n- **No-op vs failure** — an empty `{}` proposal is a clean no-op; proposals all rejected/out-of-scope return an error.\\n\\n## UX & debugging\\n\\n- **Spinner** on the two long waits (gather, headless agent run); degrades to `✓ <step>` when not a TTY.\\n- **`--debug-dir <dir>`** writes `prompt.txt` (assembled prompt incl. gathered signal) and, on `--run`, `response.txt` (raw model output) — so a skipped/odd rewrite is inspectable.\\n- `--insecure-http-auth` threaded through to the trails API client.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nUnit tests cover output parsing (fenced / prose-wrapped / `{}`), surgical template replacement (special-char preservation), placeholder validation (add rejected, drop allowed), runner loading/filtering, source-flag parsing, prompt assembly, injection-breakout, embedded-defaults validity + working-contract, onboarding create/no-op, and the debug dump. Build + lint clean.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> `--run` can rewrite committed `.entire/runners` JSON from model output (mitigated by placeholder checks and surgical edits), and the updated eval prompts change how future trails score branches.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **`entire trail tune [<runner>]`**, which collects repo-specific signal (docs/layout, `gh` PRs/issues, checkpoint churn, trail review findings) and either prints a paste-ready rewrite prompt or, with **`--run`**, drives the configured summary provider to update **only** each runner’s `prompt.template` via byte-level JSON replacement (other fields and formatting unchanged).\\n> \\n> **`--sources`** and **`--limit`** control which signal tiers are included; tiers degrade gracefully when `gh`, checkpoints, or trails are unavailable. Before writes, rewritten templates must keep the original **`{{placeholder}}`** set; gathered signal and existing templates are embedded as **JSON** with explicit untrusted-data framing to reduce prompt injection.\\n> \\n> Shipped **risk**, **confidence**, and **review-focus** runner prompts in `.entire/runners/` are retuned for this Go CLI (destructive git ops, hooks, checkpoints, transcript egress) as the first in-repo consumer. Unit tests cover parsing, surgical replacement, validation, loading/filtering, and injection-breakout behavior.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 77524874aef721ac302a59f740e54d5eb5dea2c4. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1506/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1506/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1144\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1144/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1144/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1144/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1144\",\n              \"id\": 4401406800,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7ZR2D4\",\n              \"number\": 1144,\n              \"title\": \"feat: machine-readable export surface for sessions and checkpoints\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"id\": 6415609,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTU2MDk=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6415609?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 3,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-05-07T19:23:03Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-07T22:38:06Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-05-07T22:38:04Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1144\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1144\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1144.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1144.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-05-07T22:38:04Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/320\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAdds a thin, additive CLI surface that exposes session and checkpoint data\\nas a stable contract for external consumers (Baton, eval pipelines, the\\n`session-handoff` skill). Closes #1125.\\n\\nNo new top-level commands, no schema invention. JSON envelopes are\\nmetadata-only; transcript bytes always stream to stdout from a flag.\\n\\n**New flags:**\\n- `entire session info <id> --transcript` / `entire session current --transcript`\\n  — stream the live raw agent transcript to stdout (snapshot semantics:\\n  trailing partial JSONL line is trimmed; `<-ctx.Done()` cancels the read).\\n- `entire session list --json` — same per-entry envelope as\\n  `session info --json`, emitted as an array (`[]` for empty).\\n- `entire checkpoint explain --json` — metadata-only envelope. List view\\n  if no target, single-checkpoint object if a target is given. Per-session\\n  read failures surface an explicit `error` field (no silent stub entries);\\n  list-view non-context errors propagate (no swallowed `[]`).\\n- `entire checkpoint explain <id> --transcript` — stream the normalized\\n  compact transcript (V2 `transcript.jsonl` on `/main`).\\n- `entire checkpoint explain <id> --raw-transcript --session-index N` —\\n  pick a specific session in a multi-session checkpoint (default: latest).\\n  `--session-index` also works with `--transcript`.\\n\\n**Internal:**\\n- Shared `matchCheckpointPrefixWithRemoteFallback` helper used by both the\\n  prose `runExplainCheckpointWithLookup` and the new export resolver.\\n- New `sessionOutputMode` enum replaces `(jsonOutput, transcriptOutput bool)`\\n  so the trichotomy is total in code.\\n- New exported `strategy.ResolveTranscriptPath` for live-transcript callers\\n  outside the strategy package.\\n- New `errCheckpointHasNoSessions` sentinel — distinguishes empty vs\\n  missing checkpoints for callers using `errors.Is`.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] Unit + integration tests pass (`mise run test:ci`)\\n- [x] Lint clean (`mise run lint`)\\n- [x] Manual smoke test against a real repo with v1 + v2 checkpoints\\n- [x] `--json` envelope verified to never embed transcript bytes\\n  (`TestRunExplainExport_JSONNeverEmbedsTranscript`)\\n- [x] `--session-index` distinct content per session verified end-to-end\\n  (264KB session 0 vs 1.4MB session 1, distinct sessionIds)\\n- [x] Positional commit-SHA fallback verified end-to-end\\n- [x] `<-ctx.Done()` cancellation contract verified via close-on-done pattern\\n- [x] Partial trailing line trimmed\\n  (`TestInfoCmd_TranscriptTrimsPartialTrailingLine`)\\n- [x] Missing transcript path surfaces cause to stderr (not silent SilentError)\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Adds new machine-readable CLI output modes that stream transcript bytes and emit JSON envelopes, which could affect scripting/automation and output/exit-code behavior if edge cases are missed.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds a **machine-readable export surface** to existing CLI commands.\\n> \\n> `entire checkpoint explain` gains `--json` (metadata-only list or single-checkpoint envelope with `partial` + per-session `error` reporting), `--transcript` (stream v2 compact transcript), `--session-index` (select session in multi-session checkpoints), and `--limit` (cap JSON list output with truncation note). Export resolution now retries missing checkpoint prefixes via a shared remote-metadata fetch helper, and supports positional fallback to commit-trailer resolution.\\n> \\n> `entire session info` and `entire session current` gain `--transcript` to stream the live on-disk agent transcript with snapshot/cancellation semantics and agent-aware shaping (JSONL line streaming vs whole-JSON validation), while `entire session list` gains `--json` to emit the same per-session JSON envelopes as `session info --json`. Also exports `strategy.ResolveTranscriptPath` for non-strategy callers and adds comprehensive tests for the new flags and edge cases.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 8eedeadd791f4f9456bdcabfb9034d33cf502d2d. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1144/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1144/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1942\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1942/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1942/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1942/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1942\",\n              \"id\": 5114005437,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M79Mu-V\",\n              \"number\": 1942,\n              \"title\": \"feat(explain): cross-repo checkpoint explain via the entire-api cell (ENT-1523)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-10T20:18:10Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-10T21:43:41Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-10T21:43:40Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1942\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1942\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1942.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1942.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-10T21:43:40Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1003\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n`entire checkpoint explain <id> --repo owner/name` explains a checkpoint owned by another repository, reading it from that repo's entire-api cell over HTTP.\\n\\nThis is an alternative to #— the `--repo` implementation on `surf-lightning` (trail 986), which fetches the checkpoint's git ref into the local repo. Same user-facing feature, different data path. Opening it as a separate PR so the two approaches can be compared directly.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\n`entire search` is cross-repo; `explain` was not. Search hands you an identifier the natural next command cannot resolve:\\n\\n```\\n$ entire checkpoint explain b754d1dae6b8      # a checkpoint in entirehq/entiredb\\nno checkpoint or commit found matching \\\"b754d1dae6b8\\\"\\n```\\n\\nThe compact-search work (trail 982) makes this sharper: its per-hit shape is deliberately too thin to answer anything alone, and its skill template has to tell agents to *give up* on cross-repo hits (\\\"summarize from the compact fields alone; `explain` cannot read them\\\").\\n\\n## Approach\\n\\nThe cell already serves everything explain renders — it's how the web app shows you any repo's checkpoint without cloning it:\\n\\n| Endpoint | Serves |\\n|---|---|\\n| `GET /repos/{repo_id}/checkpoints/{id}` | commit, `filesTouched`, sessions + prompts, per-session and aggregate tokens |\\n| `GET /repos/{repo_id}/checkpoints/{id}/transcript/raw` | the stored transcript bytes |\\n\\n`apiCheckpointReader` implements the two checkpoint reader tiers (`CheckpointReader` + `SessionReader`) plus the optional `AuthorReader`. That's the whole surface the render path consumes, so **every output mode reuses the existing renderers verbatim** — prose, `--short`, `--full`, `--json`, `--transcript`/`--raw-transcript`. No second output implementation.\\n\\nIt deliberately does **not** implement `Writer`. A foreign checkpoint is read-only from here, and leaving `Write` off the type makes that structural instead of a convention the flag layer has to remember (there's a test pinning it).\\n\\n## What this buys over fetching git refs\\n\\n**Nothing is written to the local repository.** Verified from a scratch repo against production, after explaining a real foreign checkpoint:\\n\\n| | git-ref fetch | this PR |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `refs/entire/*` left behind | 1 | **0** |\\n| `.git` size | 3.5 MB | **108 K** |\\n| `entire tokens profile` | 1 checkpoint, 72.4M tokens (another repo's) | **0 checkpoints** |\\n| cleanup path | none (`entire clean --all` doesn't touch checkpoint refs) | nothing to clean |\\n\\n**No `--cluster` flag.** Cell routing is automatic via `resolveRepoCellTarget`. The ref-fetch path resolves mirror placements instead and dead-ends without it:\\n\\n```\\n# git-ref fetch\\n$ entire checkpoint explain <id> --repo entireio/cli\\nrepo is mirrored on 4 clusters; pass --cluster to choose one of: ...\\n\\n# this PR\\n$ entire checkpoint explain <id> --repo entireio/cli\\n● Checkpoint 01KXGTTNGCEACC83QZEJ5YAF0D\\n  ...\\n```\\n\\n**Wider coverage.** Same checkpoint ID, same repo, both binaries:\\n\\n```\\n# git-ref fetch\\ncheckpoint 01KZP3V62DKQBG9ZKS6T2ADR00 not found in the mirror for entireio/cli;\\nrepos using the legacy branch-based checkpoint store ... are not supported cross-repo yet\\n\\n# this PR\\n● Checkpoint 01KZP3V62DKQBG9ZKS6T2ADR00\\n  session  a78beaef-a2ab-4cad-9900-f4d3c3b51959\\n```\\n\\nThe cell resolves the storage layout itself (`checkpointlayout.RefAndFolder(id, data.RefBacked)`), so branch-backed and ref-backed repos both work — the ref-fetch path is ref-layout-only by construction.\\n\\n## Fidelity decisions (both tested)\\n\\n- **`Branch` is left empty**, not filled from the envelope. The cell reports branches *containing* the commit; the local field means the branch the checkpoint was *created* on. A checkpoint made on a feature branch and since merged reports `main`, so putting that behind the same JSON key would mislead every `--json` consumer.\\n- **Transcript bytes come from `.../transcript/raw`**, never the parsed message-tree endpoint. `explain` documents `--transcript` as the same bytes as `--raw-transcript`; sourcing them from a derived shape would quietly break that.\\n- **A missing `checkpointTranscriptStart` reads as 0** (unscoped) rather than an invented offset — identical to how a local checkpoint written before that field existed behaves.\\n- **Oversize transcripts error** instead of truncating into the renderer.\\n\\n## Flag rules\\n\\n`--repo` needs a full checkpoint ID (a prefix would require listing the foreign repo's checkpoints — that's `search`'s job) and is mutually exclusive with `--commit`, `--session`, `--search-all`, and `--generate`. Naming the current repo is a no-op that falls through to the local path, which is faster and can also read unpushed checkpoints.\\n\\nA bare repo ID is not accepted, only `owner/name` / `gh/owner/name` — the control plane and the search index expose different identifiers for a repository, and guessing which space an opaque ID belongs to would key the lookup off the wrong one. `owner/name` is what search's `repo` field gives you.\\n\\n## Error messages\\n\\nA 404 leads with the cause that actually dominates:\\n\\n```\\ncheckpoint 01KV... is not available for entireio/cli yet: it may not have been\\npushed, or Entire may not have finished ingesting it. Checkpoints you have not\\npushed are only readable in the repo that created them\\n```\\n\\n## Drive-bys\\n\\n- Extracted `validateExplainFlagCombinations` out of `newExplainCmd` (it was over the `maintidx` limit with the new flag).\\n- Renamed `resolveCurrentRepoID` → `resolveRepoIDFromMirror`; it takes explicit coordinates and now serves a foreign repo too.\\n- Stopped rendering an empty `<>` when an author has a name but no email.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n`mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci` all green (lint: 0 issues). 25 new tests: envelope mapping, the raw-vs-parsed endpoint assertion, envelope caching (one fetch across all read tiers), 404/403/empty/no-session paths, oversize transcript, `List` unsupported, not-a-`Writer`, flag validation, and all four render modes against a stub reader.\\n\\nManually verified end-to-end against production for prose, `--json`, `--full` (3,273 lines), and `--transcript` (3.1 MB), plus clean stdout JSON with the spinner on stderr.\\n\\n## Known gap\\n\\nThe availability precondition is *pushed and ingested*, so a just-pushed checkpoint may briefly 404. The message above says so; if that lag turns out to be user-visible in practice, a retry hint would be the follow-up.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> New authenticated HTTP read path and flag surface on a heavily used command; risk is moderated by read-only semantics (no local git writes), strict flag mutual exclusion, and extensive tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **`entire checkpoint explain <id> --repo owner/name`** so cross-repo `search` hits can be drilled down without pulling foreign git objects into the local repo.\\n> \\n> **`apiCheckpointReader`** loads checkpoint metadata and raw transcript bytes from the repo’s entire-api cell (`GET .../checkpoints/{id}` and `.../transcript/raw`), maps them into the existing checkpoint reader types, and **does not implement `Writer`**. Prose, `--json`, `--full`, and transcript modes reuse the same renderers as local explain.\\n> \\n> **`runCrossRepoExplain`** resolves mirror `repo_id`, dials the owning cell via `NewAuthenticatedEntireAPICellClient`, and rejects incompatible flags (`--commit`, `--session`, `--search-all`, `--generate`). `--repo` on the current checkout is a no-op to the local path. Cross-repo requires a **full** checkpoint ID.\\n> \\n> Notable fidelity choices: **`Branch` stays empty** (cell “containing branches” ≠ creation branch), transcripts always from **raw** endpoint, oversize transcripts **error** instead of truncating, and 404 messaging calls out unpushed/not-yet-ingested checkpoints.\\n> \\n> Also extracts **`validateExplainFlagCombinations`**, renames **`resolveCurrentRepoID` → `resolveRepoIDFromMirror`** for foreign-repo use, fixes author lines when email is missing, and documents the feature in **CLAUDE.md**. Broad unit test coverage for the API reader and cross-repo explain paths.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 346b7fb5b53078c1a8f46fdce807151a081e4dcd. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1942/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1942/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/954\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/954/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/954/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/954/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/954\",\n              \"id\": 4264173496,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7SaQxJ\",\n              \"number\": 954,\n              \"title\": \"Add summary TUI for browsing checkpoints\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"id\": 6415609,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTU2MDk=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6415609?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-04-14T19:03:59Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-08T21:05:38Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-05-08T21:05:38Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": true,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/954\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/954\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/954.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/954.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\n- Adds `entire summary` command with an interactive Bubble Tea TUI for browsing checkpoints\\n- Reads session data directly from the checkpoint store (no SQLite/insightsdb dependency)\\n- Users can filter by time (24h/7d/30d/all) and branch (current/repo), and press `g` to generate AI summaries persisted to the checkpoint branch\\n- Includes `summarytui` package (model/update/view, detail rendering, styles, keybindings), `termstyle` shared styling package, and comprehensive tests\\n\\n## Test plan\\n- [ ] Run `mise run check` (fmt + lint + tests)\\n- [ ] Run `entire summary` in a repo with existing checkpoints — verify list loads, detail pane renders\\n- [ ] Press `g` on a checkpoint without a summary — verify generation works and persists\\n- [ ] Test time filter cycling with `1` key and branch filter with `2` key\\n- [ ] Test `entire summary --json` outputs valid JSON\\n- [ ] Test accessible mode with `ACCESSIBLE=1 entire summary`\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Adds a new interactive command that reads and updates checkpoint metadata (including persisting AI-generated summaries) across v1/v2 stores; main risk is regressions in checkpoint I/O and UX edge cases rather than security-critical behavior.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds a new `entire summary` command that loads recent committed checkpoints and lets users browse session metadata and cached AI summaries via an interactive Bubble Tea split-pane TUI, with filters for time range and branch scope and optional `--json` output.\\n> \\n> Supports on-demand summary generation (`g`) that reuses existing transcript-scoping + AI summarization helpers and persists the generated `Summary` back to the checkpoint store (v1 and v2 when available), with an accessible-mode text fallback.\\n> \\n> Introduces the new `summarytui` UI package (rendering, keybindings, pagination, filtering) and a shared `termstyle` utility for terminal color/width-aware formatting, plus comprehensive unit tests and a settings toggle under `strategy_options.summarize.enabled`.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit a456873fdb97b475c349354199776b39388f447c. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/954/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/954/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/144\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/144/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/144/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/144/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/144\",\n              \"id\": 3894737830,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7BX5TX\",\n              \"number\": 144,\n              \"title\": \"feat(explain): improve explain command with author, commits, and filtering\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"khaong\",\n                \"id\": 351934,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTkzNA==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/351934?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/khaong\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-02-04T05:26:30Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-04T07:13:52Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-02-04T07:13:50Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/144\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/144\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/144.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/144.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-02-04T07:13:50Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nImplements ENT-212: Improve `entire explain` command with better checkpoint detail views and filtering.\\n\\n- **`--commit <sha>` now shows checkpoint details**: Extracts `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer from commit and delegates to checkpoint detail view\\n- **`--session` filters list view**: Instead of showing session details, now filters the checkpoint list by session ID (prefix match supported)\\n- **Checkpoint detail shows author**: Retrieves author from `entire/sessions` commit history\\n- **Checkpoint detail shows associated commits**: Lists git commits that reference the checkpoint via trailer\\n- **`--search-all` flag**: Removes branch/depth limits when searching commits (documented as \\\"may be slow\\\")\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] Unit tests for all new functions (`TestGetAssociatedCommits`, `TestGetCheckpointAuthor`, etc.)\\n- [x] Integration tests for new flag behavior (`TestExplain_SessionFilter`, `TestExplain_CommitWithCheckpointTrailer`, etc.)\\n- [x] `mise run test:ci` passes (unit + integration + race detection)\\n- [x] `mise run lint` clean\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Medium risk due to behavior changes in `entire explain` routing/output and new git-history scanning logic that could impact performance or completeness of results, though changes are mostly read-only and guarded with best-effort error handling.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Improves `entire explain` by making `--session` a *list-view filter* (prefix supported) rather than a separate session-detail mode, while keeping `--commit`/`--checkpoint` mutually exclusive.\\n> \\n> Checkpoint detail output now includes **checkpoint author** (derived from the `entire/sessions` history) and a **list of associated git commits** that reference the checkpoint via the `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer; a new `--search-all` flag removes scan limits for this association lookup.\\n> \\n> `--commit` behavior changes to *resolve the `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer and delegate to checkpoint detail view*; commits without the trailer now print a “no associated checkpoint” message instead of showing generic commit info. Adds `trailers.FormatCheckpoint` helper and extensive unit/integration tests covering new routing, filtering, author lookup, and association logic.\\n> \\n> <sup>Written by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot) for commit 3dbf613b1ab881e3d12d4e9daf22a48a60067a20. This will update automatically on new commits. Configure [here](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/144/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/144/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1007\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1007/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1007/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1007/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1007\",\n              \"id\": 4309508151,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7UpZi4\",\n              \"number\": 1007,\n              \"title\": \"Cursor: agent-lifecycle export/import via CheckpointContributor + CheckpointRestorer\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"id\": 881031,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 7,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-04-22T13:57:33Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-14T08:15:52Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-14T08:15:51Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": true,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1007\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1007\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1007.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1007.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nExport and import of Cursor Agent sessions are wired through the agent lifecycle via `CheckpointContributor` and `CheckpointRestorer`. No standalone Cursor commands are needed.\\n\\nThis update also makes the post-restore hint metadata-aware:\\n\\n- Cursor Agent checkpoints print `agent --resume <id>`.\\n- Cursor IDE checkpoints keep the existing `Open this project in Cursor.` message.\\n- Legacy checkpoints fall back to the recorded model so older restored sessions still get the best available hint.\\n\\n## User Flow\\n\\n1. Cursor Agent or Cursor IDE runs with Entire hooks installed.\\n2. On checkpoint save, Cursor contributes its session archive into the checkpoint metadata.\\n3. `entire rewind` restores the worktree and asks Cursor to restore contributed files.\\n4. `entire resume` restores logs from committed checkpoints and prints the correct resume hint for the original Cursor client.\\n\\n## Implementation Notes\\n\\n- Added agent-level resume formatting context with checkpoint metadata.\\n- Cursor hooks now persist whether the checkpoint came from Cursor Agent or Cursor IDE.\\n- Session and checkpoint metadata carry agent-specific key/value data through condensation and restore.\\n- Cursor restore still rebuilds the native chat/transcript state from checkpointed files.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/...`\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor`\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint`\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy`\\n- [x] `mise run lint`\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1007/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1007/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/112\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/112/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/112/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/112/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/112\",\n              \"id\": 3863305991,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M6_vu9l\",\n              \"number\": 112,\n              \"title\": \"Adds checkpoint-focused explanations and a branch-aware default view to entire explain\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"id\": 881031,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-01-28T02:57:54Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-01-29T04:41:24Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-01-29T04:41:22Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/112\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/112\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/112.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/112.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-01-29T04:41:22Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes `explain`’s default behavior and adds new checkpoint lookup paths that traverse git history and shadow branches, which could affect performance and edge-case correctness on unusual repos. No auth/security-sensitive logic is touched.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> `entire explain` now defaults to a **branch checkpoints view** instead of requiring an active session, listing committed and reachable temporary (shadow) checkpoints grouped by checkpoint/session and filtered against the repo’s default branch.\\n> \\n> Adds `--checkpoint/-c` to explain a single checkpoint by ID or prefix, with `--short` and `--full` verbosity (including transcript output), and improves commit explain to recognize `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers and backfill session IDs via checkpoint metadata.\\n> \\n> Refactors default-branch/ancestry detection into shared strategy helpers (`GetDefaultBranchName`, `IsOnDefaultBranch`, `IsAncestorOf`) and extends the checkpoint store with `ListAllTemporaryCheckpoints`; updates and expands unit/integration tests accordingly.\\n> \\n> <sup>Written by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot) for commit 387eacf47f655c2315edc72a0a627a13bea1511f. This will update automatically on new commits. Configure [here](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/112/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/112/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/533\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/533/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/533/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/533/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/533\",\n              \"id\": 3998146752,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7GrXj-\",\n              \"number\": 533,\n              \"title\": \"fix: detect and repair disconnected metadata branches at read/write time\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"dvydra\",\n                \"id\": 62726,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNzI2\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62726?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dvydra\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/dvydra\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dvydra/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dvydra/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dvydra/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dvydra/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dvydra/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dvydra/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dvydra/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dvydra/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dvydra/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 6,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T22:50:14Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-06T01:13:13Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-03-06T01:13:11Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/533\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/533\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/533.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/533.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-03-06T01:13:11Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nDetects and repairs disconnected `entire/checkpoints/v1` metadata branches — a state caused by the empty-orphan bug (fixed going forward by #511). Users who hit that bug and continued working have local checkpoint data on a completely disconnected history from remote (no common ancestor).\\n\\n**Key distinction:** *Diverged* (shared ancestor, unique commits on each side) is normal multi-dev flow handled by the push path's tree merge. *Disconnected* (no common ancestor) is the bug state that this PR repairs.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n### New: cherry-pick reconciliation (`strategy/metadata_reconcile.go`)\\n\\nWhen local and remote share no common ancestor, local commits are cherry-picked onto the remote tip:\\n\\n1. Detect via `git merge-base` (exit 0 = shared ancestry, exit 1 = disconnected)\\n2. Walk local branch tip→root, collect commits oldest-first\\n3. Skip empty-tree commits (the orphan bug artifact)\\n4. For each commit: compute full delta from parent (adds + modifies + deletes), apply onto current tip\\n5. Update local branch ref\\n\\nCheckpoint shards use unique paths (`<id[:2]>/<id[2:]>/`), so cherry-picks always apply cleanly. All data is preserved with linear history.\\n\\n### Reconciliation runs at read/write time, not `enable` time\\n\\nRuns once per process (via `sync.Once`) when commands actually access the metadata branch — explain, rewind, resume, clean, condensation. Three call sites:\\n\\n- `ManualCommitStrategy.getCheckpointStore()` — covers strategy-mediated reads/writes\\n- `getBranchCheckpoints()` in `explain.go` — bypasses strategy, creates own GitStore\\n- `ListCheckpoints()` in `strategy/common.go` — opens own repo, reads branch directly\\n\\nThis is the right place because `enable` may run before the user has fetched remote data.\\n\\n### Simplified `EnsureMetadataBranch` (runs during `enable`)\\n\\nNow only handles:\\n- Create local from remote when local doesn't exist\\n- Replace empty orphan with remote\\n- Create empty orphan when neither exists\\n\\nRemoved `syncMetadataBranch` and `isAncestorCLI` — disconnected repair is now handled by `EnsureMetadataReconciled`.\\n\\n### User-facing output\\n\\n```\\n[entire] Detected disconnected session metadata (local and remote share no common ancestor)\\n[entire] Cherry-picking 3 local checkpoint(s) onto remote...\\n[entire] Done — all local and remote checkpoints preserved\\n```\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `strategy/metadata_reconcile.go` | **New** — detection + cherry-pick repair |\\n| `strategy/metadata_reconcile_test.go` | **New** — 7 tests covering no-ops, disconnected repair, multi-commit, modifications |\\n| `strategy/common.go` | `EnsureMetadataReconciled()` gate; simplified `EnsureMetadataBranch`; removed `syncMetadataBranch`/`isAncestorCLI` |\\n| `strategy/manual_commit.go` | Reconciliation call in `getCheckpointStore()` |\\n| `strategy/common_test.go` | Updated existing tests for new behavior |\\n| `cli/explain.go` | Reconciliation call in `getBranchCheckpoints()` |\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] `mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci`\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/ -run TestReconcileDisconnected -v` — all 7 tests pass\\n- [x] Manual: clone repo with remote checkpoints, create disconnected local orphan, run `entire explain`, verify reconciliation and explain succeeds\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/533/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/533/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            }\n          ],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rate-limit\",\n      \"q\": \"repo:entireio/git-sync \\\"rate limit\\\"\",\n      \"rr\": [\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 0,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 0,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"page-graph\",\n      \"q\": \"repo:entireio/entire-graph \\\"pagination\\\"\",\n      \"rr\": [\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 0,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 1,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/144\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/144/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/144/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/144/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/144\",\n              \"id\": 5198708977,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSqVa0c8AAAABAWyxYw\",\n              \"number\": 144,\n              \"title\": \"Publish re-audited letta and supermemory LoCoMo numbers\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"id\": 257360244,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-20T01:30:04Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-20T02:10:02Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-20T02:10:01Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/144\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/144\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/144.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/144.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-20T02:10:01Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/104\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nBoth the letta and supermemory rows in the 8-system LoCoMo comparison were flagged **suspect, not\\nyet re-audited** in `FAIR-CONFIG.md`, and supermemory additionally had a confirmed extraction-model\\ndefect (documented in the existing `‡` footnote). This PR rebuilds both arms on fresh\\ninfrastructure, re-runs the full 1,540-question suite under the identical fairness spine every\\nother row uses (`FAIR_MODE=1`, same answerer/judge `gpt-5.6-sol`, same extraction model\\n`azure_ai/gpt-5.6-terra`, `top_k=200`), and publishes the results.\\n\\n- **letta: 80.58 → 84.68** (`field_letta_loco_v3`, 1304/1540). Re-audited clean — zero dropped\\n  questions, zero empty-context retrievals, zero errors across all 1,540 questions. No defect was\\n  found in the original number; the original infrastructure was deleted before it could be\\n  re-audited directly, so this is a clean re-measurement superseding a suspect number, not a bug\\n  fix.\\n- **supermemory: 77.60 → 82.08** (`field_sm_loco_v3`, 1264/1540). Two real, independent defects\\n  found and fixed:\\n  1. supermemory's self-hosted server silently selects the wrong AI SDK provider whenever pointed\\n     at a non-default endpoint (mandatory for our Azure deployment), degrading every\\n     structured-output extraction call to a schema-less response the deployment rejects. Fixed\\n     with a 2-byte binary patch (sha256-verified against the official release manifest) plus a\\n     wire-level parameter adapter.\\n  2. supermemory deduplicates documents by content, so any retry after a transient failure\\n     resubmits identical text — which its own dedup then rejects, guaranteed. Fixed with a stable\\n     content-derived `custom_id`.\\n  \\n  One limitation is disclosed rather than worked around: supermemory's search API hard-caps\\n  `limit` at 100 with no pagination, so it answers from an effective top-100 budget while every\\n  other arm gets the full top-200 — recorded per-question (`requested_top_k`/`limit_used`/\\n  `clamped`) for auditability. 114/1,540 questions (7.4%) returned an empty context; checked\\n  individually (not asserted): zero errors, normal search latency, spread across 9 of 10\\n  conversations (not clustered), consistent with a genuine retrieval-miss characteristic rather\\n  than the original defect.\\n\\n## Files changed\\n\\n- `README.md` — table numbers\\n- `bench/memory/RUN-INDEX.md` — new `field_letta_loco_v3` / `field_sm_loco_v3` rows; old rows\\n  marked superseded\\n- `bench/memory/LOCOMO-COMPARISON.md` — table (rows 10/11), headline numbers, the zero-empty-context\\n  claim (now correctly scoped), the `‡` footnote (full rewrite — defect resolved, new disclosure),\\n  §8's bug-fix list (four competitors now, not three), §10's gate wording\\n- `bench/memory/FAIR-CONFIG.md` — §7 verdicts flipped from suspect to resolved, with outcomes\\n- `bench/memory/RUNNING-LOCOMO.md` — summary table numbers\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- Both final result files' `metadata.run_id`/`total_questions` confirmed directly (1540/1540 each)\\n- Scores extracted from each run's own `metrics_by_cutoff.top_200.overall`, not hand-tallied\\n- Zero `search_dropped` confirmed across all 1,540 questions in both arms, by direct file\\n  inspection\\n- supermemory's extraction calls confirmed landing on `gpt-5.6-terra-2026-07-09` via the token\\n  meter (not asserted)\\n- supermemory's 114 empty-context questions individually inspected: `search_dropped: false`, no\\n  error field, normal latency, spread across 9/10 conversations — ruled out as a repeat of the\\n  original defect\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/144/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/144/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            }\n          ],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"perfetto\",\n      \"q\": \"repo:entireio/cli perfetto\",\n      \"rr\": [\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 0,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 0,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"repo:entireio/git-sync \\\"same repository\\\"\",\n      \"q\": \"repo:entireio/git-sync \\\"same repository\\\"\",\n      \"rr\": [\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 0,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 1,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/18\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/18/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/18/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/18/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/18\",\n              \"id\": 4353589412,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOR9SkY87W3rmJ\",\n              \"number\": 18,\n              \"title\": \"Expand on integration tests\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"pjbgf\",\n                \"id\": 5452977,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NTI5Nzc=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5452977?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pjbgf\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-04-29T20:50:39Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-04-30T08:25:27Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-04-30T08:25:24Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/pulls/18\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/18\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/18.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/18.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-04-30T08:25:24Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \" ## Summary\\r\\nExtends integration coverage in `internal/syncer/integration_test.go` in two areas: **sync-mode prune semantics** and **incremental relay push failure handling**.\\r\\n  ### Sync-mode `--prune`\\r\\n  - **`TestRun_IntegrationSyncPruneDeletesOrphanedBranch`** — With no ref filter, `Run` with `--prune` removes a target-only branch absent from the source; checks `Deleted` and that the managed branch still matches the source.\\r\\n  - **`TestRun_IntegrationSyncPrunePreservesTargetTagWithoutIncludeTags`** — With `--prune` but without `--tags`, a target-only tag must survive so branch-only prune does not drop release-style markers.\\r\\n  - **`TestRun_IntegrationPrunePreservesUnrelatedTargetBranchUnderFilter`** — Table-driven cases for `--branch` and `--map`: unrelated branches on the target stay present and their hashes unchanged under filtered prune.\\r\\n  These clarify **prune scope** and guard against deleting refs users expect to keep while still enforcing orphan branch cleanup in sync mode.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ### Incremental push failure and retry\\r\\n  - **`TestRun_IntegrationIncrementalPushFailureRecoversOnRetry`** — Injects a **one-shot `ng`** from the target receive-pack on the **incremental relay** path (after a fast-forward plan). Asserts the first `Run` **errors**, the **target ref is unchanged** (only ok’d commands commit), and a **retry** completes incremental relay with **`RelayMode` incremental**, **two receive-pack attempts**, and the target at the new source head.\\r\\n  This pins the **failure-and-retry contract** for incremental sync and complements bootstrap-focused push tests; it does not replace mid-stream cancel/drop coverage (still mainly on `Bootstrap` via `receivePackRaw`).\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Mostly test-only, but adds a new public-config validation that rejects identical source/target URLs and could break existing workflows that relied on that configuration.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Expands test coverage** for sync/replicate planning and end-to-end `Run` behavior, focusing on `--prune` scoping rules (preserve out-of-scope target-only branches when `--branch`/`--map` is used; delete orphan branches when unfiltered) and tag-prune boundaries (don’t prune tags unless `--tags`, prune target-local tags when `--tags --prune`, and preserve tags created mid-sync).\\n> \\n> Adds an **incremental relay failure/retry integration test** that injects a one-shot `receive-pack` rejection, asserting the first run errors without advancing the target and the retry completes via incremental relay.\\n> \\n> Introduces `validation.ValidateEndpoints` and wires it into `newSession` (only when a target is required) to **reject identical source/target URLs** across `Run`/`Bootstrap`/`Probe`, with unit tests. Integration tests now register an empty go-git config loader in `TestMain` to avoid environment-dependent git config affecting runs.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit c3089e94b311b4cc2d08035b4dcde64491dd33f8. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/18/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/18/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            }\n          ],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"repo:entireio/git-sync \\\"identical\\\" \\\"endpoint\\\"\",\n      \"q\": \"repo:entireio/git-sync \\\"identical\\\" \\\"endpoint\\\"\",\n      \"rr\": [\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 0,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 3,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/122\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/122/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/122/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/122/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/122\",\n              \"id\": 5562237117,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOR9SkY88AAAABE21FdA\",\n              \"number\": 122,\n              \"title\": \"fix: refuse POST redirects in guardRedirects unless FollowInfoRefsRedirect is set\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"jaysomani\",\n                \"id\": 69755312,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NzU1MzEy\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69755312?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jaysomani\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/jaysomani\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jaysomani/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jaysomani/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jaysomani/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jaysomani/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jaysomani/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jaysomani/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jaysomani/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jaysomani/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jaysomani/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 5,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-24T02:43:06Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-13T15:35:34Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/pulls/122\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/122\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/122.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/122.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"\\r\\nguardRedirects's CheckRedirect closure now returns http.ErrUseLastResponse for POST redirects unless conn.FollowInfoRefsRedirect is set, matching vanilla git's http.followRedirects=initial default where only the /info/refs GET auto-follows. GET redirect behaviour is unchanged.\\r\\n\\r\\nRequired restructuring NewHTTPConnWithClient so guardRedirects closes over the *HTTPConn directly (reading FollowInfoRefsRedirect live at redirect time) rather than running before the struct exists.\\r\\n\\r\\nAlso corrects TestGuardRedirectsAnchorsOnTheIssuedRequest which modelled a post-adoption cross-site redirect but never set FollowInfoRefsRedirect, making the scenario unreachable under the corrected logic.\\r\\n\\r\\nOn a cross-host POST redirect without the flag, the failure mode changes from a delayed opaque 401 (Authorization stripped mid-flight by the existing sameSite guard) to an immediate clear http 307 error — the intended improvement from the issue.\\r\\n\\r\\nFixes #67\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/122/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/122/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/124\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/124/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/124/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/124/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124\",\n              \"id\": 5926912911,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOR9SkY88AAAABJXbk9w\",\n              \"number\": 124,\n              \"title\": \"fix: authenticate the GitHub repo-size preflight and log its outcome\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"nodo\",\n                \"id\": 829178,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjgyOTE3OA==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/829178?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/nodo\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 8,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-19T15:39:13Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-21T15:59:16Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-21T15:59:13Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/pulls/124\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-21T15:59:13Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Problem\\n\\nWhen bootstrapping from a `github.com` source without `--target-max-pack-bytes`, git-sync asks the GitHub REST API (`GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}`) for the repository size. It switches to 512 MiB batches when the size is 1.5 GiB or more. That lookup sent no credentials. For a private repository GitHub answers 404 to an anonymous caller, so every private repository bootstrapped as a single pack, whatever its size.\\n\\nNothing reported this:\\n- Every failure (non-200, transport error, parse error) returned silently.\\n- The \\\"selected batched mode\\\" message only showed with verbose logging.\\n\\nPublic repositories were exposed too: anonymous calls share GitHub's 60 requests/hour limit per egress IP.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n**Authenticated lookup**\\n- The size request now carries the source connection's credentials (basic or bearer): an explicit token, a `user:token@` in the source URL, or credentials the git credential helper supplied when the git server asked for them. A public repository never asks, so with only a helper its lookup stays anonymous. A URL username without a password is not sent: it may be an account name.\\n- If the API refuses the token with 401 or 403 (for example an SSO-unauthorized PAT), the lookup retries once anonymously. A public repository is never worse off than before. If the retry fails too, the refusal is reported rather than hidden behind the retry's 404.\\n- The new `HTTPConn.CredentialsFor(dest)` decides which credentials may go to the API, checking the real destination. Each credential is measured from the URL it is bound to (the endpoint for explicit and URL credentials, the looked-up host for helper ones), the destination must be same-site with it, and with TLS verification off nothing crosses to another host. So helper credentials looked up for a redirect host stay with that host, and an API base on another site gets nothing.\\n- `GitHubOwnerRepo` now treats `github.com` as GitHub only on its scheme's default port. The connection's redirect guard still strips credentials from any hop that leaves the API's site, and the logged `authenticated` reflects the request that actually produced the answer.\\n\\n**Visible outcome**\\n- Every lookup that is attempted is logged through `Options.BootstrapLogger`. This does not need verbose mode.\\n- Fields: `repository`, `authenticated`, `http_status`, `refused_auth_status`, `refused_auth_error`, `size_kb` or `error`, `threshold_kb`, `mode`, `target_max_pack_bytes`.\\n- A failed lookup logs at WARN and also prints a notice that the bootstrap starts with a single pack, so CLI users see it without `-v` (it can still switch to batches if the target rejects the pack). The notice names the token refusal when there was one. Under `-v` the failure is printed once, and the verbose log and `BootstrapLogger` use the same record name.\\n\\n**Hardening**\\n- A reported size of 0 counts as unknown, like a missing or negative size: bootstrap only runs with source refs, so 0 means GitHub has not sized the repo yet. It warns and prints the notice.\\n- A cancelled run reports nothing. Every error text (transport errors included) is cleaned before it is logged or printed.\\n- A 401/403 counts as a refused token only when the request still carried it, so a redirect that stripped the credentials is neither retried nor blamed on the token.\\n- Wiki sources (`owner/repo.wiki`) get no lookup: the API has nothing to size.\\n- Each lookup request has its own 30s timeout, so a slow refusal does not starve the anonymous retry.\\n- GitHub's error message is cleaned (control characters including C1, bidi formatting) and truncated before it is logged.\\n\\n**Docs**\\n- `docs/usage.md` documents the lookup and its credential scope.\\n- Updated the `BootstrapLogger` doc comments and `CHANGELOG.md`.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nNew file `internal/strategy/bootstrap/github_preflight_test.go`, written test-first. It covers:\\n- a private repo: 404 without auth, 200 with auth, so batched (also end-to-end through `Execute`);\\n- a bearer token, `user:token@` URL credentials, and a bare URL username not being sent;\\n- no credentials with TLS verification off, or to an API base on another site;\\n- lookup failure: one-shot, a WARN record and a notice;\\n- the anonymous retry on 401/403, the refusal reported when the retry fails too, and no retry on other failures;\\n- a transport error, and unusable bodies (not JSON, no size, negative size);\\n- sanitizing GitHub's error message;\\n- a small repo staying one-shot without a warning, and one reporting size 0 warning as unknown;\\n- a cancelled run, unclean transport errors, an unauthenticated 403 after a redirect, and the per-attempt timeout;\\n- skipped lookups (caller already batching, non-default port, non-GitHub host);\\n- a redirect that leaves the API's site dropping credentials (asserting the target was reached, and logged as unauthenticated);\\n- `CredentialsFor` in `internal/gitproto/smarthttp_test.go`: explicit, helper and URL credentials, helper credentials bound to a redirect host, and TLS verification off.\\n\\nThe preflight tests reach a local TLS server as `https://api.github.com`, so the destination check runs as in production.\\n\\nThe new tests fail against the previous implementation. `go test ./...`, `go test -race` on the affected packages and `golangci-lint run` (v2.11.4) all pass.\\n\\n---\\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FUdEhv4HALJ9DCRUP7GzTw)_\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches credential scoping for cross-host API calls and bootstrap batching decisions; mistakes could leak tokens or mis-size packs, but changes are heavily tested and fail closed on redirects/TLS-off.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Fixes batched bootstrap for large private GitHub repos** by sending source credentials on the `GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}` size preflight (scoped to `api.github.com` via new `HTTPConn.CredentialsFor`), with same-site/TLS rules aligned to redirect handling and helper creds bound to `authOrigin`.\\n> \\n> The preflight moves into `github_preflight.go` with structured **`BootstrapLogger` / `PushLogger`** records, CLI **notices** on lookup failure, **401/403 → one anonymous retry**, stricter **`GitHubOwnerRepo`** parsing, and **`sanitize.Line`** for API/error text in logs. Docs and changelog describe the behavior.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit d0e7b7873bb287a3c90f5ed779923b16b26d5b15. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/124/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/124/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": {\n                \"id\": 1236702,\n                \"client_id\": \"Iv23liqTIFEtdIu6Vn1r\",\n                \"slug\": \"claude\",\n                \"node_id\": \"A_kwHOBIuudM4AEt7e\",\n                \"owner\": {\n                  \"login\": \"anthropics\",\n                  \"id\": 76263028,\n                  \"node_id\": \"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjc2MjYzMDI4\",\n                  \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76263028?v=4\",\n                  \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics\",\n                  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/anthropics\",\n                  \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/followers\",\n                  \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/following{/other_user}\",\n                  \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                  \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                  \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/subscriptions\",\n                  \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/orgs\",\n                  \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/repos\",\n                  \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/events{/privacy}\",\n                  \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/received_events\",\n                  \"type\": \"Organization\",\n                  \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                  \"site_admin\": false\n                },\n                \"name\": \"Claude\",\n                \"description\": \"Run Claude Code from your GitHub Pull Requests and Issues to respond to reviewer feedback, fix CI errors, or modify code, turning it into a virtual teammate that works alongside your development pipelines.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is built on the publicly available Claude Code SDK.\",\n                \"external_url\": \"https://anthropic.com/claude-code\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/claude\",\n                \"created_at\": \"2025-04-30T17:54:24Z\",\n                \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-12T22:28:30Z\",\n                \"permissions\": {\n                  \"actions\": \"write\",\n                  \"administration\": \"read\",\n                  \"checks\": \"write\",\n                  \"contents\": \"write\",\n                  \"discussions\": \"write\",\n                  \"issues\": \"write\",\n                  \"members\": \"read\",\n                  \"merge_queues\": \"read\",\n                  \"metadata\": \"read\",\n                  \"pull_requests\": \"write\",\n                  \"repository_creation\": \"write\",\n                  \"repository_hooks\": \"write\",\n                  \"statuses\": \"read\",\n                  \"vulnerability_alerts\": \"read\",\n                  \"workflows\": \"write\"\n                },\n                \"events\": [\n                  \"branch_protection_rule\",\n                  \"check_run\",\n                  \"check_suite\",\n                  \"commit_comment\",\n                  \"discussion\",\n                  \"discussion_comment\",\n                  \"issues\",\n                  \"issue_comment\",\n                  \"merge_group\",\n                  \"merge_queue_entry\",\n                  \"pull_request\",\n                  \"pull_request_review\",\n                  \"pull_request_review_comment\",\n                  \"pull_request_review_thread\",\n                  \"push\",\n                  \"release\",\n                  \"repository_ruleset\",\n                  \"status\",\n                  \"sub_issues\"\n                ]\n              },\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/108\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/108/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/108/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/108/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/108\",\n              \"id\": 5192976034,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOR9SkY88AAAABASLszQ\",\n              \"number\": 108,\n              \"title\": \"Bind explicit credentials to the host they were configured for\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T13:09:08Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-20T15:36:34Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-20T15:36:30Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/pulls/108\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/108\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/108.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/108.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-20T15:36:30Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes the highest-severity item left from the security review. **Stacked on #107** so the `smarthttp.go` changes don't conflict — the base is that branch, so this diff shows only its own changes. I'll rebase onto `main` once #107 merges.\\n\\n## The problem\\n\\nWith `--source-follow-info-refs-redirect` / `--target-follow-info-refs-redirect`, git-sync adopts the host `/info/refs` redirected to and addresses it directly for follow-up RPCs — re-attaching the configured token to requests aimed at that host, *after* Go's `http.Client` had deliberately stripped `Authorization` on the cross-host hop.\\n\\nReproduced with two local servers, where the endpoint 307s to an unrelated host:\\n\\n```\\n[LEGIT] GET  Authorization=\\\"Basic Z2l0OlNVUEVSX1NFQ1JFVF9QQVRfMTIzNDU=\\\"\\n[EVIL]  GET  Authorization=\\\"\\\"                    ← stdlib stripped it\\n[EVIL]  POST Authorization=\\\"Basic Z2l0OlNVUEVS…\\\" ← git-sync re-sent it\\n```\\n\\nAny redirect an attacker can cause is enough: an open redirect on the real host, a hostile mirror, or a MITM on a plain-`http` source. On the target side the token usually carries write access.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\nAn explicitly supplied credential — token flags, bearer flags, or userinfo in the URL — now goes only to the host named on the command line and its subdomains, on the same scheme and port. Anything else gets nothing, plus a warning naming the withheld host, and the credential helper is consulted for that host instead:\\n\\n```\\nsource: withholding the configured credentials from http://localhost:64772/repo.git:\\n/info/refs redirected outside 127.0.0.1. Consulting the git credential helper for that host instead.\\n```\\n\\nCredentials resolved *from* the helper are untouched — they're looked up keyed on the host being challenged, so they were already bound to their destination. The subdomain allowance keeps the case the flag exists for working: `example.com` → `replica.example.com` still authenticates.\\n\\n## Why redirect policy moved into git-sync\\n\\nThe same-site rule is stricter than the stdlib's on purpose. Go compares hostnames only, ignoring scheme and port, so it forwards `Authorization` from `host:443` to `host:9999` — a different service, potentially a different tenant. My first version of the end-to-end test caught exactly this: both `httptest` servers are on `127.0.0.1`, so the stdlib happily carried the token across the port boundary and the test failed.\\n\\nThat hop isn't visible from the request-building code, because the redirect is followed *inside* a single `http.Client.Do`. So policy now lives in a per-connection `CheckRedirect` that strips the header on any hop leaving the endpoint's site, layered over whatever policy the caller set (theirs still runs and can still veto). Setting `CheckRedirect` replaces the stdlib's ten-redirect default, so that cap is reimposed explicitly — otherwise this fix would have introduced a redirect-loop hang.\\n\\nThe client is shallow-copied per connection, sharing the caller's `Transport`, so nothing the caller passed in is mutated or reconfigured.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- `sameSite` in isolation, including the near-misses: suffix without a dot boundary (`notgithub.com` vs `github.com`), attacker-controlled prefix domain (`github.com.evil.example`), scheme downgrade, port change, and IP addresses having no subdomains.\\n- End to end against `httptest`: the cross-site POST must carry no credentials, and a same-site redirect must still carry them.\\n- By hand: the original two-server reproduction now logs an empty `Authorization` on both requests to the redirect target.\\n\\n`gofmt`, `go vet`, `golangci-lint` (0 issues), `go test ./...` 17/17, `-race` on `gitproto` and `syncer`.\\n\\n## Behavior change to be aware of\\n\\nIf a deployment today relies on the redirect target receiving the configured token and that target is **not** same-site with the endpoint, it will start getting 401s. The fix is to store those credentials in the git credential helper against the redirect host — git-sync will find them there, and the helper is now installed alongside an explicit token so that path actually works.\\n\\nWhat counts as same-site, precisely:\\n\\n| redirect | credentials |\\n|---|---|\\n| same host, any path | kept |\\n| subdomain of the endpoint host | kept |\\n| `http` → `https`, same host | kept (upgrade) |\\n| `https` → `http` | **withheld** (downgrade) |\\n| different host | **withheld** |\\n| different port (default ports normalized) | **withheld** |\\n\\n`docs/usage.md` gains a \\\"Credentials and redirects\\\" section explaining this; the flags were previously documented only in their flag help text.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **High Risk**\\n> Changes authentication and credential routing on HTTP redirects—a security-critical path—with behavior change for deployments that relied on sending configured tokens to non-same-site redirect hosts.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Fixes a **credential leak** when `--source-follow-info-refs-redirect` / `--target-follow-info-refs-redirect` is enabled: after `/info/refs` redirects, follow-up RPCs hit the redirect host directly and git-sync was re-attaching CLI/URL tokens that Go’s client had already stripped on the cross-host hop.\\n> \\n> **Explicit credentials** (tokens, bearer flags, URL userinfo) are now sent only to the configured host’s **same site** — matching host or subdomain, **same scheme and port** — via new `sameSite` logic and `outgoingAuth` on `HTTPConn`. Off-site redirect targets get no token, a one-time stderr warning, and the git credential helper on 401. Helper-resolved creds are unchanged.\\n> \\n> Redirect handling adds **`guardRedirects`**: a shallow `http.Client` copy with `CheckRedirect` that drops `Authorization` on hops leaving the endpoint site (tighter than stdlib hostname-only rules) and re-applies the 10-redirect cap. Info/refs and RPC paths use `outgoingAuth` instead of raw `c.Auth`; helper attach paths mark `authIsExplicit = false`.\\n> \\n> Docs add **Credentials and redirects** in `usage.md`; CHANGELOG documents the security fix. Tests cover `sameSite` edge cases and end-to-end cross-site vs same-site redirect behavior.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit b0e0f88541d3bbbe472233a7ce0bbe63124c4115. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/108/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/108/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            }\n          ],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"diff-specific\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"sparse-specific\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"tour-specific\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assets-specific\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\nTWENTY_PUBLIC_EVIDENCE_7D9A"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"mkdir -p '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public'\ncat > '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/searches.json' <<'TWENTY_PUBLIC_EVIDENCE_7D9A'\n{\n  \"queries\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b24\",\n      \"query\": \"repo:entireio/cli review manifest corrupt\",\n      \"prs\": {\n        \"total_count\": 7,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2332\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2332/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2332/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2332/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2332\",\n            \"id\": 5400614060,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABC2FnDQ\",\n            \"number\": 2332,\n            \"title\": \"session adopt: refuse a session that is not this command's caller\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-09-09T14:14:29Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-02T14:09:27Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": null,\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2332\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2332\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2332.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2332.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1273\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\n`session adopt` moves a live session into the current worktree and resets its checkpoint bookkeeping (`StepCount`, `CheckpointTranscriptStart`, `LastCheckpointID`, and `FilesTouched`). Selecting the wrong session can therefore mutate another agent's running session and detach its next commit from its work.\\n\\nThat happened when an agent read a foreign session ID from `entire session current` and passed it to `session adopt`. #2322 made caller resolution explicit through `SessionResolution` and `IsCaller()`; this PR applies that ownership boundary to the command that mutates a session.\\n\\nThe existing checks were insufficient:\\n\\n- `sessionBelongsToSourceWorktree` only proves the session ID and source worktree agree with each other.\\n- `isAdoptableSourceSession` only proves the session is still live.\\n\\nNeither proves that the selected session belongs to the process invoking the command.\\n\\n## Behavior\\n\\n| Case | Outcome |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| The selected session is identified as the caller's own | Adopt silently |\\n| A different session is identified as the caller | Require terminal confirmation; refuse without a terminal |\\n| Caller ownership is ambiguous, unavailable, or based on an incomplete candidate set | Require terminal confirmation; refuse without a terminal |\\n| `--allow-foreign-session` is passed | Proceed deliberately |\\n\\nAuto-selection uses the same guard, so `entire session adopt --from <path>` cannot bypass ownership checks by omitting the session ID. The ownership decision is repeated against the locked source state immediately before mutation.\\n\\nNon-interactive refusal prints an actionable `--allow-foreign-session` remedy. Prompt cancellation follows the shared form-cancellation path and cannot proceed with the mutation.\\n\\n## Combined caller resolution\\n\\nCross-repository adoption cannot rely on the ordinary resolver alone: `ResolveCallerSession` reads the current repository's session store, while the relevant owner may exist only in the source store. This matters for Gemini CLI and OpenCode, which publish no caller-session environment variable and can only be identified through process ancestry.\\n\\n`IdentifyCallerSession` therefore runs the identification tier over the combined target and source candidate set. Source states are first-class candidates rather than a fallback, and supplied source state wins an ID collision with a stale target copy. The shared resolver remains the single ownership policy:\\n\\n- nearest owner in process ancestry wins;\\n- equal ancestry depth is broken by most recent interaction;\\n- inherited environment claims do not outrank a nearer recorded owner;\\n- the existing depth-zero rule applies when an unplaceable claim cannot be nearer;\\n- imported and already-adopted states do not compete;\\n- ambiguity does not authorize mutation.\\n\\n## Incomplete candidate sets\\n\\nA store listing normally skips an individual state file it cannot read so one corrupt file does not hide every healthy session. That is appropriate for display, but unsafe for ownership: a missing candidate may be the nearer owner whose absence changes the winner.\\n\\n`StateStore.ListWithSkipped` reports those omissions and `ResolvedSession.Incomplete` carries them through caller resolution. Adoption fails closed when either source or target candidates are incomplete, while `session list`, `session current`, and both `session tokens` selection paths warn on stderr and keep structured stdout valid.\\n\\nThe detailed invariants and rejected alternatives are documented in [`docs/architecture/session-caller-resolution.md`](docs/architecture/session-caller-resolution.md).\\n\\n## Why the override is separate\\n\\n`--allow-foreign-session` is intentionally distinct from `--force` and `--yes`. Those flags already control replacement and same-store confirmation, and agents commonly retry failures with `--force`. Waiving ownership requires a flag that states that intent explicitly.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nComprehensive unit and real-binary integration coverage includes:\\n\\n- foreign, unidentified, and ambiguous callers;\\n- successful adoption of the caller's own session;\\n- cross-repository agents without a session-ID environment variable;\\n- nested owners, inherited environment claims, and equal-depth recency;\\n- source/target ID collisions and source-state precedence;\\n- locked ownership revalidation;\\n- incomplete source and target stores;\\n- `--force` / `--yes` not granting the waiver;\\n- `--allow-foreign-session` registration and behavior;\\n- non-interactive refusal output and preservation of source state;\\n- completeness warnings for session list/current/tokens without corrupting JSON output.\\n\\nExisting adoption tests identify their fixture through `adoptAsCaller`, so they exercise the supported path rather than the escape hatch and remain isolated from caller-session variables inherited from a developer's agent.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- `mise run lint`\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/ ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/`\\n- `go test -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test -run 'TestSessionAdoptGuard_' -count=1`\\n- `GOOS=windows go vet ./cmd/...`\\n\\n### Existing macOS-only failures\\n\\nFour unrelated tests fail on clean `origin/main` because macOS resolves `/var/...` to `/private/var/...` while their expected strings use the unresolved `t.TempDir()` path:\\n\\n- `TestCheckAgentDirSymlinks_ScansBeneathAVouchedLink`\\n- `TestCheckAgentDirSymlinks_VouchedLinkWithCleanTargetReportsOnlyTheLink`\\n- `TestSymlinkedHooksDirError_UsesTheQuotedCommand`\\n- `TestSymlinkedHooksDirError_RemedyIsPasteable`\\n\\nThey are unchanged by this PR.\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2332/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2332/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2795\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2795/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2795/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2795/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2795\",\n            \"id\": 5883720481,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABI1kCbQ\",\n            \"number\": 2795,\n            \"title\": \"Add a release mirror with a GitHub fallback\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-16T11:56:03Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-20T08:01:53Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-20T08:01:52Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2795\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2795\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2795.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2795.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-20T08:01:52Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1591\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nEvery install and update path resolved a version and fetched bytes from GitHub alone, so a GitHub outage made an **already-published** release unobtainable — not just unreleasable. This publishes the same artifacts to a second origin we own and reads ours first, with GitHub as the fallback.\\n\\nReading ours first is deliberate: a fallback that only runs during an incident is a fallback nobody has tested. This way every install exercises the path.\\n\\n## What reads what\\n\\n`versioncheck.versionOrigins` is an ordered chain (`install.entire.com`, then `api.github.com`) walked by `fetchLatestForChannel`. `scripts/install.sh` walks the same two origins for archives and checksums. `httpTimeout` (2s) bounds the **whole chain**, and each candidate gets an equal share of what is left — so a primary that hangs cannot swallow the budget and starve the fallback, which would leave update checks worse off than before the second origin existed.\\n\\nTwo rules, both borrowed from `checkpoint/remote/checkpoint_ref.go`:\\n\\n1. **Fail open.** Every origin failing is reported as one error, never as \\\"you are up to date\\\" or \\\"there is nothing to install\\\".\\n2. **A definite bad answer aborts; an unreachable one advances.** A checksum *mismatch* exits rather than falling through — bytes that disagree with their own origin's checksums mean that origin is corrupt, and retrying elsewhere would hide it. Bad *metadata* goes the other way and advances: while discovering a version another origin may simply know better.\\n\\nPublishing inverts rule 1 on purpose. `publish-channel-manifest.sh` fails **closed** — if it cannot read the current pointer it refuses to publish, because its only question is \\\"can I prove this move is forward\\\". The write is conditional on the object the guard inspected (`--if-match`), so a concurrent publisher cannot leave the pointer at the older version.\\n\\n## What gets published\\n\\n| Key | Contents |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `v<version>/` | archives and `checksums.txt`, immutable |\\n| `channels/{stable,nightly}.json` | the channel pointer, `max-age=60` |\\n| `installers/install.{sh,ps1}` | the install scripts, `max-age=300`, stable only |\\n| `scoop/entire.json` | the Scoop manifest with URLs repointed at this origin, stable only |\\n\\nOrder inside `release.yml` is load-bearing: artifacts, then the macOS Developer ID check, then the pointer, then the shared keys. The shared keys come **after** the pointer — which looks backwards — because they are not versioned, so publishing them first means a release the pointer refuses leaves them rolled back with nothing advanced.\\n\\n`mod_timestamp` is pinned to the commit so rebuilding a tag is byte-identical. Without it a retried release would re-upload different bytes and a different `checksums.txt` to URLs cached immutable for a year, and a mixed edge cache is a hard install failure under rule 2.\\n\\n## Windows\\n\\n`scoop install https://install.entire.com/scoop/entire.json` installs with no bucket and therefore no git, and `scoop update` re-fetches that URL and upgrades in place. Both verified against Scoop v0.6.0 on a Windows VM. The bucket manifest keeps its GitHub URLs, so the ordinary `scoop install entire` path is unchanged — this is an additional route, not a replacement that puts every Scoop install behind one origin.\\n\\n`install.ps1` itself is **not** covered: it is mirrored so it can be fetched, but it still resolves versions through `api.github.com` and downloads archives from GitHub releases. That is the remaining Windows gap and it is recorded in the design doc.\\n\\n## Turning it on\\n\\nThe publishing side is inert until `ENTIRE_RELEASE_BUCKET` is set; deleting it and rerunning restores exactly the old behaviour. The variables are now set and `install.entire.com` is serving, so the next stable release is the first that mirrors. After it, check that `channels/stable.json` names the new version, `v<version>/checksums.txt` returns 200 with an immutable cache-control, and `installers/install.sh` and `scoop/entire.json` return 200.\\n\\nThe gate tests the variable for **non-emptiness**, not presence: `release.yml` always exports it, an unset Actions variable exports as empty, and `isEnvSet` alone would have enabled the pipe with an empty bucket and no credentials — failing every release instead of staying inert.\\n\\nThe Homebrew cask and the bucket's Scoop manifest still point at GitHub on purpose. Repointing the cask is the highest-value follow-up once this is proven, since the sha256 stays pinned in the manifest.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n`scripts/test-release-origins.sh` (`mise run test:release-origins`, and a CI job) runs both scripts against local fake origins — version discovery, download and verification from our origin, fallback to GitHub for both, a checksum mismatch aborting rather than falling through, a hung origin still failing over, `--version` pinning, unusable manifest metadata advancing, the pointer's routing, monotonicity, fail-closed read and conditional write, and the installer and Scoop manifest publishing. 86 assertions, hermetic, and it refuses to run an installer still aimed at a public origin.\\n\\nVerified locally: `mise run check` green (93 packages, both canary legs), `go vet` for darwin/linux/windows. The Windows installer checks run in CI.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2795/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2795/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1116\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1116/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1116/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1116/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1116\",\n            \"id\": 4383114221,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7YV7VU\",\n            \"number\": 1116,\n            \"title\": \"WIP: Add gh-style plugin system (skeleton + dispatch + local install)\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"ashtom\",\n              \"id\": 70720,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzIw\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70720?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/ashtom\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-05-05T09:49:15Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-05T15:36:46Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-05-05T15:36:45Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": true,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1116\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1116\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1116.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1116.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/298\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n- New `cmd/entire/cli/plugin` package with manager/classification (binary/script/local), YAML manifest, dispatcher (Unix direct exec, Windows `sh.exe` for scripts), local symlink install, and remove.\\n- `entire plugin {install,list,remove,exec}` subcommands wired into root.\\n- `main.go` now calls `plugin.Dispatch` before the unknown-command suggestion path; cobra resolves built-ins first, so plugins can never shadow built-ins. `plugin exec` is the escape hatch.\\n\\nFoundational milestones from `docs/plugin-system-plan.md`. Network-dependent paths (GitHub release binary install, git-clone script install, upgrade, create scaffolds, search/browse/pin, update notifier, docs page) are deferred.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] `mise run lint` passes (0 issues)\\n- [x] `mise run test` passes\\n- [x] `mise run test:integration` passes\\n- [x] `mise run test:e2e:canary` passes\\n- [x] Manual end-to-end: install → list → dispatch → exec\\n- [x] Built-in shadowing: `entire status` resolves to built-in even when `entire-status` plugin is installed; `entire plugin exec status` invokes the plugin\\n- [x] Conflict check: `entire plugin install` refuses a directory whose name matches a built-in\\n- [x] Exit code propagation: child exits 42 → parent exits 42\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Adds a new plugin execution path for unknown commands and introduces filesystem-based install/remove/list behavior, which can affect CLI command resolution and process exit codes. Main risk is dispatch/exec edge cases across platforms (Windows `sh.exe` routing) and potential regressions in unknown-command handling.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds an initial gh-style plugin system: a new `plugin` package can discover installed plugins (binary/script/local), parse/write `manifest.yml`, track pins via `.pin-*`, and execute plugins with stdio inheritance, `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR` injection, and exit-code propagation (including Windows `sh.exe` routing for script plugins).\\n> \\n> Wires new `entire plugin {install,list,remove,exec}` commands into the CLI and updates `main.go` to attempt `plugin.Dispatch` on unknown commands/flags before showing suggestions, while ensuring built-in Cobra commands/aliases always take precedence. Includes unit tests covering classification, local install via symlink, remove semantics, dispatch precedence, argv handling, env injection, and exit-code propagation, plus adds `gopkg.in/yaml.v3` dependency.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 7376f07db54b7a2d0cbe664f311696be12f39529. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1116/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1116/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/508\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/508/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/508/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/508/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/508\",\n            \"id\": 3992854972,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7GZ5DT\",\n            \"number\": 508,\n            \"title\": \"fix: harden E2E test isolation and reliability\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"khaong\",\n              \"id\": 351934,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTkzNA==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/351934?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/khaong\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 2,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T02:14:46Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-27T04:01:10Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-02-27T04:01:08Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/508\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/508\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/508.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/508.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-02-27T04:01:08Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\n- **Isolate E2E from user settings**: Replace `isolatedConfigDir()` (which symlinked most of `~/.claude/`) with `cleanConfigDir()` that creates an empty temp dir. `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` is now always set, preventing leakage of CLAUDE.md, skills, projects, and plugins into test runs.\\n- **Skip Claude onboarding**: Write minimal `hasCompletedOnboarding` config locally so Claude Code doesn't show the first-run theme/login flow that the test harness can't navigate.\\n- **Fix WaitFor race condition**: `Send()` now snapshots terminal content *after* the echo renders, so `WaitFor(\\\"❯\\\")` won't false-match on the prompt character in echoed input.\\n- **Ensure hooks use test binary**: Prepend the test binary's directory to `PATH` in `TestMain` so git hooks and agent hooks resolve to the same `entire` binary the harness uses.\\n- **Preflight info in artifacts**: Write binary path and version to `entire-version.txt`, printed after the test report for easy diagnosis.\\n- **Extract shared E2E runner**: Deduplicate the 4 nearly-identical mise e2e tasks into `mise-tasks/test-e2e`.\\n- **Configurable concurrency gate**: `RegisterGate` now respects `E2E_CONCURRENT_TEST_LIMIT` env var to override the default per-agent gate size. Gemini default changed from 3 to 2.\\n- **Scenario-level restart on transient errors**: Replace prompt-level retry (which left stale CLI session state that poisoned checkpoint flow) with full scenario restart via panic/recover. On transient API errors (e.g. OpenCode \\\"Token refresh failed\\\"), the entire test scenario restarts with a fresh repo — up to 2 restarts before failing.\\n- **Bump AssertNewCommits timeout**: Increased from 10s to 20s to handle slower interactive agent responses (e.g. OpenCode taking 13s to commit).\\n- **Test report success/failure banner**: Add a colorized footer banner to the E2E test report — red `💥 FAILED (x/y passed) 💥` or green `🎉 ALL N TESTS PASSED 🎉` — for quick visual pass/fail identification.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] Run `mise run test:e2e:claude` locally — verify no onboarding flow, no user CLAUDE.md leakage\\n- [x] Verify `entire-version.txt` in artifacts shows binary path and version\\n- [x] Run interactive tests (TestAttributionOnAgentCommit, etc.) — verify WaitFor no longer returns prematurely\\n- [x] Verify `mise run test:e2e:gemini` respects gate size (default 2, overridable via `E2E_CONCURRENT_TEST_LIMIT`)\\n- [x] Verify `mise run test:e2e` / `test:e2e:claude` / `test:e2e:opencode` all delegate to shared runner\\n- [x] Run `mise run test:e2e:opencode` — verify scenario restart triggers on transient API errors instead of corrupted retries\\n- [x] Verify test report shows colored banner at the end of output\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/508/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/508/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/673\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/673/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/673/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/673/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/673\",\n            \"id\": 4050344309,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7JUJ9b\",\n            \"number\": 673,\n            \"title\": \"feat: windows build (fixes #370)\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"talaikis\",\n              \"id\": 7689499,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjc2ODk0OTk=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7689499?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/talaikis\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/talaikis\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/talaikis/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/talaikis/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/talaikis/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/talaikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/talaikis/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/talaikis/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/talaikis/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/talaikis/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/talaikis/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-03-10T08:52:22Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-04-08T12:59:59Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-04-08T12:59:59Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/673\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/673\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/673.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/673.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"Adds native Windows install (using Golang build) script.\\r\\n\\r\\nUsage:\\r\\n\\r\\n```bash\\r\\n# locally\\r\\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\\\\install.ps1\\r\\n\\r\\n# remotely\\r\\nSet-ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned -Scope Process; iwr https://entire.io/install.ps1 | iex\\r\\n```\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/673/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/673/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/679\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/679/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/679/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/679/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/679\",\n            \"id\": 4053915555,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7JfgMe\",\n            \"number\": 679,\n            \"title\": \"Add `entire search` command\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"evisdren\",\n              \"id\": 256443556,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD0kEpA\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256443556?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/evisdren\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 5,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-03-10T19:55:22Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-04-02T18:35:48Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-04-02T18:35:47Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/679\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/679\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/679.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/679.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-04-02T18:35:47Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\r\\n- New `entire search` command with hybrid semantic + keyword checkpoint search\\r\\n- Interactive Bubble Tea TUI with alt-screen, pagination, detail cards, and inline search bar\\r\\n- Calls the Entire search service via thin HTTP client (no direct Turbopuffer/OpenAI keys needed)\\r\\n- Auth via `entire login` device flow token, sent as `Bearer` header\\r\\n- Supports `--author`, `--date`, `--branch` flags and inline filter syntax (`author:name date:week branch:main`)\\r\\n- Accessible mode (`ACCESSIBLE=1`) renders static table instead of TUI\\r\\n- JSON output (`--json`) for scripting/agent consumption\\r\\n- Client-side pagination with lazy-fetch fallback for server-side pagination\\r\\n\\r\\n## Features\\r\\n- **Interactive TUI**: Alt-screen with search bar (`/`), j/k navigation, n/p pagination, detail card for selected result\\r\\n- **Filter syntax**: `author:<name>`, `date:<week|month>`, `branch:<name>` — works in CLI args and TUI search bar\\r\\n- **Pagination**: Requests up to 200 results for TUI, paginates client-side at 25/page, with lazy-fetch for additional pages\\r\\n- **Accessible mode**: `ACCESSIBLE=1` requires a query and renders a plain text table\\r\\n- **Multiple output modes**: Interactive TUI (default), static table (accessible), JSON (scripted)\\r\\n\\r\\n## Files\\r\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search/` — search client package (`github.go` for remote parsing, `search.go` for API client + filter parsing)\\r\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search_cmd.go` — Cobra command with flag/inline filter merging\\r\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search_tui.go` — Bubble Tea TUI (model, update, view, pagination, detail cards)\\r\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search_cmd_test.go` — Command-level tests (accessible mode)\\r\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search_tui_test.go` — TUI unit tests (navigation, pagination, fetch-more, filter clearing, view states)\\r\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search/search_test.go` — API client tests (URL construction, params, errors, parsing)\\r\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/root.go` — command registration\\r\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/status_style.go` — shared `isTerminalWriter` helper\\r\\n\\r\\n## Companion PR\\r\\n- Search service: entirehq/entire.io#981\\r\\n\\r\\n## Test plan\\r\\n- [x] `mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci` — all pass\\r\\n- [ ] `entire search \\\"test query\\\"` — returns results in TUI\\r\\n- [ ] `entire search \\\"test\\\" --json` — returns JSON array\\r\\n- [ ] `entire search \\\"test\\\" --author alice --date week --branch main` — filters applied\\r\\n- [ ] `entire search \\\"test author:alice branch:main\\\"` — inline filters extracted from args\\r\\n- [ ] `entire search` — opens TUI with search bar focused\\r\\n- [ ] `ACCESSIBLE=1 entire search \\\"test\\\"` — renders static table\\r\\n- [ ] `ACCESSIBLE=1 entire search` — returns error requiring a query\\r\\n- [ ] TUI: `/` opens search bar, enter searches, esc cancels, n/p pages, q quits\\r\\n- [ ] TUI: new search clears previous filters\\r\\n- [ ] `entire search \\\"test\\\" --json | jq .` — piped output works\\r\\n\\r\\n🤖 Generated with [C\\r\\n<img width=\\\"903\\\" height=\\\"817\\\" alt=\\\"Screenshot 2026-03-31 at 2 54 16 PM\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/725cd424-0728-4db3-ae6e-cc25957c4126\\\" />\\r\\nlaude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\r\\n\\r\\n<img width=\\\"899\\\" height=\\\"571\\\" alt=\\\"Screenshot 2026-03-31 at 2 54 27 PM\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f551cbdb-d83f-4d62-bfc0-aa6a8f4f00eb\\\" />\\r\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Adds a new CLI surface area that makes authenticated HTTP requests using the user’s GitHub token and introduces a sizeable Bubble Tea TUI; failures could impact CLI UX and pagination/filter correctness but are isolated to the new command path.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Introduces a new (currently *hidden*) `entire search` command that queries the Entire search service for checkpoint results, supporting interactive TUI browsing, accessible-mode static output, and `--json` output with client-side pagination.\\n> \\n> Adds a small `search` package for parsing GitHub `origin` remotes, parsing inline filters (`author:`, `date:`, `branch:`, `repo:` including `repo:*`), validating repo scoping semantics, and performing the authenticated `GET /search/v1/search` request.\\n> \\n> Refactors terminal detection in `status_style.go` via a shared `isTerminalWriter` helper, registers the new command in `root.go`, and updates `go.mod` to make Bubble Tea/Bubbles direct dependencies with comprehensive unit tests covering URL construction, error handling, filter parsing, and TUI behavior.\\n> \\n> <sup>Written by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot) for commit 6947c67bc51e0d23d4c6988988eb76422c38e7a2. Configure [here](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/679/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/679/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/445\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/445/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/445/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/445/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/445\",\n            \"id\": 3968606208,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7FKz7e\",\n            \"number\": 445,\n            \"title\": \"OpenCode transcript refactor\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 2,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-02-20T13:38:51Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-23T16:20:50Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-02-23T16:20:45Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/445\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/445\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/445.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/445.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-02-23T16:20:45Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"This refactor changes how OpenCode transcript handling works. Previously, the TypeScript plugin wrote JSON/JSONL transcripts to temp files and passed the file paths to hooks. \\r\\n\\r\\nNow, the plugin only sends the session ID, and the Go hook handler calls `opencode export` directly to get the native JSON format. This eliminates race conditions between plugin shutdown and the hook reading the transcript, and ensures full data fidelity by using OpenCode's own export format.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis means we are not creating an artificial JSONL that is not compatible to our rendering for Claude Code JSONL anyway, and we are not generating our own OpenCode style JSON file with the risk of breaking imports in the future. \\r\\n\\r\\nAlso the old approach had an issue that we want the full log on each checkpoint, so if you resume/rewind we can restore the context before the last prompt too. The initial implementation only capture the log from the start of the last prompt.\\r\\n\\r\\nMain things: \\r\\n\\r\\n- using `opencode export` to get the full logs so we can store them\\r\\n- removed the export.json logic completely and only use the logs from ☝️ \\r\\n- there was a bug with `file_path` being used and not `filePath` that broken checkpointing when only existing files were edited by tooling. New files worked (need to look at e2e test later if we need to make sure we have that...)\\r\\n\\r\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/445/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/445/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          }\n        ],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      },\n      \"issues\": {\n        \"total_count\": 0,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b25\",\n      \"query\": \"repo:entireio/entire-brain hosted feed corrupt cursor\",\n      \"prs\": {\n        \"total_count\": 2,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/452\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/452/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/452/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/452/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/452\",\n            \"id\": 5992004366,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSm5-5c8AAAABKLTXnQ\",\n            \"number\": 452,\n            \"title\": \"One memory-sync path: per-fact wire everywhere (COR-2233: COR-2234 + COR-2235 + COR-2236)\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"evisdren\",\n              \"id\": 256443556,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD0kEpA\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256443556?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/evisdren\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-23T04:41:13Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-23T06:03:10Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-23T06:03:08Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/pulls/452\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/452\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/452.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/452.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-23T06:03:08Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/363\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nOne hosted memory-sync wire must remain before the stable CLI release (COR-2233): manual `memories sync --memories-backend=http` drove the branch-head CAS wire while connected background sync drove the per-fact wire, and local-gitmeta was a third mechanism with different (CAS) semantics. Decisions recorded in Linear/brain: the per-fact wire (COR-2126) is the only long-term path; connect is the consent moment (ADR-P1-A reconciliation); gitmeta is removed rather than kept as an opt-in (evis, 2026-10-23).\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n**COR-2234 — connected default**\\n- Plain `memories sync` on a connected repo syncs over the hosted per-fact wire (batch upsert + delta feed), with honest output and exit codes: a failed push or pull fails the command and names the failed half (COR-2202 precedent). The pull still runs after a failed push so the team's memories land.\\n- Under `ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS`/`LOCAL_ONLY`, a connected repo's plain sync is skipped loudly (exit 0, JSON shape under `--json`). It must not fall back to a local gitmeta merge: the local head is stale on connected repos, and a keep-both merge against it re-raises every deferred per-fact conflict into the local review queue (observed: 1365 spurious proposals on this repo).\\n\\n**COR-2235 — CAS wire retired**\\n- `--memories-backend=http` drives the same per-fact exchange.\\n- Deleted: `HTTPServer.Current/CurrentWithAuthors/Advance`, the hosted proposals-queue client, the `memories proposals` command (incl. `repair` and `docs/proposal-queue-repair.md`), the shared-proposal ledger, sync-time proposal publish/reconcile, and the `memories review` interlock that deferred shared proposals to the hosted queue (local review settles everything now).\\n- Transport-security tests (body limits, token redaction, https floor, repo-id segment rule, dial retry, timeouts, error-body surfacing, wire fuzz) were retargeted from the CAS methods to the per-fact methods, not dropped.\\n\\n**COR-2236 — gitmeta removed; sync is hosted-only**\\n- Plain `memories sync` on an unconnected repo fails gracefully with the connect remedy; memories stay local until the repo connects.\\n- `--memories-backend`/`ENTIRE_BRAIN_FACTS_BACKEND` value `local-gitmeta` (incl. the legacy `--facts-backend` alias) fails with a clear removed-value message; any other non-`http` value names the one supported backend. Every refusal is egress-free.\\n- Deleted: factgitmeta's fact-set head `Backend` and factsync's read-merge-CAS loop (`Sync`, the `Server` seam) plus the `--member` flag and sync-raised-proposal persistence. The factgitmeta package stays — its `MetaStore` and gitmeta engine back the entity index in the same `gitmeta.git` store (exercised by the entityindex suite).\\n- Already-synced gitmeta fact heads become orphaned bytes nothing reads; the privacy purge caveat says exactly that (the store can't be deleted wholesale — it also holds the entity index).\\n\\n**Server-side impact check:** current entire-api routes only `/repos/{id}/brain/facts` (upsert + feed) through the gateway to brainstore; the `advance`/`proposals` endpoints no longer exist server-side (verified in the entire monorepo at 90dfe547f). This client was their last consumer — no deprecation window needed.\\n\\n## Compat\\n\\n- `http` keeps its meaning (hosted, now per-fact). `local-gitmeta` fails with a clear message per the COR-2233 compat rule for removed values.\\n- Breaking (pre-stable): `memories sync --json` reports upsert counts + feed totals (or `{skipped, reason}` under the kill switch); `memories proposals` and `memories sync --member` are gone; unconnected plain sync now errors instead of silently syncing a local store.\\n\\n## Bugbot\\n\\nBoth findings on d2a89cd are fixed in 0e353c1: the NO_EGRESS skip answers in JSON under `--json`, and a corrupt hosted binding fails the sync with a rebind remedy instead of warning and merging against the stale local head.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- `go test ./...` green (on an isolated GOCACHE — the shared build cache was being mutated by a concurrent session, which produced two phantom failures first).\\n- Manual runs with the dev binary:\\n  - connected repo, plain sync → `synced … via hosted (https://aws-us-east-2.api.entire.io): pushed added=2 …; feed facts=2278 kept=1548`, exit 0\\n  - unconnected repo, plain sync → \\\"not connected … run 'entire brain connect'\\\", exit 1, zero egress\\n  - `--memories-backend=local-gitmeta` → removed-value error, exit 1, zero egress\\n  - unreachable hosted target → named pull failure, exit 1\\n  - connected + `ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS=1` → skip message (JSON under `--json`), exit 0, zero egress\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/452/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/452/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/403\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/403/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/403/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/403/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/403\",\n            \"id\": 5905922006,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSm5-5c8AAAABJG6eAg\",\n            \"number\": 403,\n            \"title\": \"Per-fact push + reachability-filtered pull (COR-2126)\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"evisdren\",\n              \"id\": 256443556,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD0kEpA\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256443556?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/evisdren\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-18T03:55:49Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-19T03:06:44Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-19T03:06:42Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/pulls/403\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/403\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/403.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/403.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-19T03:06:42Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/316\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nCOR-2110 v3: branch-named fact heads break on rename, delete, and recycle, and merged trails' facts never reached teammates without a promote step. This PR replaces the branch-head CAS sync client with per-fact sync against brainstore's new endpoints (COR-2123), closing COR-2126. The previously planned `lineage.json` rename/recycle detection is cancelled — the rebuild covers both.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n- **Push**: `hostedFactsSyncAndPull` batch-upserts the branch store to `POST /api/v1/repos/{id}/brain/facts:upsert` (NDJSON, 1000/chunk, sanitized + identity-verified first). Idempotent, so every trigger fires it without coordination.\\n- **Pull**: fetches the repo-wide delta feed (`GET /api/v1/repos/{id}/brain/facts`, keyset cursor persisted in a repo-level cache under the plugin cache tree), then rebuilds the branch store locally: keep a fact when its trail merged (`trailId`), any anchor commit is reachable from HEAD, it belongs to this member (token sub), or it has no session/commit anchors (repo pool) — plus this machine's own facts the feed has not seen. Removal pass stands down without member identity and spares records with local transcript anchors (proof they were distilled here).\\n- **Kept discipline**: unchanged gate ladder, never-fails stderr contract, pull-only degradation when push is denied (synced marker withheld so the blind-spot note keeps firing), one-way status lifecycle. Sync no longer raises keep-both proposals — per-fact storage keeps conflicting facts side by side; resolution stays deferred to the async pipeline.\\n- The old `factsync` head client remains only for the manual `facts sync` command until its own deprecation; single-store collapse of branch directories is a declared later stage.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- Full suite + `-race` green; new coverage: wire client, feed cache, filter rules, cursor resume/reset, pull-only, retirement one-way, recycle decontamination, own-fact survival.\\n- Live against aws-us-east-2 (`gh/entireio/entire-brain`): first sync pushed 958 facts; a fresh clone with an empty brain pulled all 958 with server-stamped authors, synced marker, and cursor; `recall` ranked the sentinel fact first; re-sync was idempotent (`unchanged=958`) and resumed from the cursor; a retraction in one checkout reached the clone as `retracted`, and the clone's stale active push did not revive it.\\n- Single-account env cannot exercise the foreign-member drop live; `TestHostedSyncFilterDropsUnreachable` and `TestKeepHostedFact` pin it.\\n\\n## Risks / follow-ups\\n\\n- A forged repo-pool feed record blocks every pull fail-closed until purged server-side (deliberate, same discipline as the old head verify).\\n- Re-binding a repo to a different hosted target pushes the old target's pulled facts to the new one — pre-existing behavior, worth its own ticket.\\n- Feed-cache loader skips corrupt lines but a single >4 MiB line would wedge it (`bufio.Scanner` cap); no realistic fact approaches that size.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Large change to hosted memory sync (push/pull, local rebuild, and data visibility rules); behavior is heavily tested but mistakes could mis-share or drop facts across teammates.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Hosted sync (COR-2126)** drops branch-head CAS, proposals, and `lineage.json`-style merge in favor of per-fact brainstore APIs: NDJSON batch upsert on push and a repo-wide delta feed on pull.\\n> \\n> **Push** sanitizes and identity-checks the branch store, chunks to `facts:upsert`, and skips HTTP when empty. **Pull** pages the feed into a repo-level cache (cursor + records under the plugin cache), filters the full cache with `keepHostedFact` (trail id, JWT `sub`, git reachability, repo pool), then rebuilds the branch store—dropping feed-known facts that fail the filter while keeping unsynced locals and transcript-anchored distillations. Invalid page tokens reset cache and cursor once; push failure still pulls but withholds the per-branch synced marker.\\n> \\n> Adds `internal/factsync` upsert/feed client, feed cache helpers, and broad tests; connect/hook tests use the new fake wire. Manual `facts sync` still uses the legacy head client.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 781685cfa63f4e8dadac90e87962e365e423db6d. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/403/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/403/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          }\n        ],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      },\n      \"issues\": {\n        \"total_count\": 0,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b26\",\n      \"query\": \"repo:entireio/git-sync endpoint fragment\",\n      \"prs\": {\n        \"total_count\": 0,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      },\n      \"issues\": {\n        \"total_count\": 0,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b27\",\n      \"query\": \"repo:entireio/git-sync include prefix invalid\",\n      \"prs\": {\n        \"total_count\": 1,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/121\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/121/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/121/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/121/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/121\",\n            \"id\": 5426089854,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOR9SkY88AAAABDKhbqQ\",\n            \"number\": 121,\n            \"title\": \"COR-1642: include-prefix ref scope and empty in-scope prune (T1)\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"nodo\",\n              \"id\": 829178,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjgyOTE3OA==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/829178?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/nodo\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 2,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-09-11T15:29:59Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-11T20:17:42Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-11T20:17:40Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/pulls/121\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/121\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/121.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/121.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-11T20:17:40Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"Trail T1 of the COR-1566 namespace-replication plan. Dormant on its own: nothing sets either field until the mirror-pipeline worker (T2) does.\\n\\n## What this adds\\n\\n**`RefScope.IncludeRefPrefixes []string`** narrows a request to one or more namespaces. With any prefix set, a ref outside all of them is neither pushed nor pruned, in every kind. One `inScope` predicate in `internal/planner` answers that question at all four sites that previously asked only about exclusions — the desired-set branch pass, the tag/other-kind pass under `AllRefs`, `TargetScope.Manages`, and `PruneTarget` — so push scope and prune scope cannot disagree: a ref the run would not push is one it must not delete. Exclusions still apply within an included prefix (`inScope` = include, then the existing exclusions), and explicit `Mappings` bypass both exactly as they bypass exclusions today.\\n\\nThe ls-refs prefix is deliberately **not** narrowed: `RefPrefixes` stays `refs/` under `AllRefs`, because the rule below needs to see whether the source advertised anything at all.\\n\\n**`SyncPolicy.AllowEmptyScope bool`** lets an empty in-scope desired set prune instead of failing. Without it, a replicate whose scope matched no source ref fails with the historical \\\"no source refs matched\\\", so a caller replicating a namespace can never propagate the deletion of its last ref — and the mirror worker classifies that failure as a benign no-op and reports ready, leaving every replica stale. With it, a source that advertised at least one ref proceeds with an empty desired set and the target's in-scope refs prune.\\n\\nA source that advertised **nothing at all** still fails: that observation is indistinguishable from a withheld or hidden listing, and pruning a namespace on the strength of a silence would delete the replica's refs. It now reports `ErrSourceEmptyUnverified` rather than the historical message, so a scoped caller can tell \\\"your namespace is empty\\\" from \\\"we were shown nothing\\\".\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\nThree rules, each rejected rather than silently discarded:\\n\\n- **`AllowEmptyScope` is replicate-only.** Only replicate's empty-set branch consults the policy; elsewhere the run returns the historical error and keeps the refs the caller meant to prune.\\n- **`AllowEmptyScope` requires `IncludeRefPrefixes`** — without a scope to be empty, the policy is inert.\\n- **`AllowEmptySource` is mutually exclusive with `IncludeRefPrefixes`** — that policy is a claim about the repository, and only the unscoped listing can back it.\\n\\nPlus a shape check: every `IncludeRefPrefixes` entry must start with `refs/`. A blank or `refs/`-less prefix scopes a request to nothing, and nothing is a legal scope — the run plans zero refs and succeeds, so under `AllowEmptyScope` and prune the typo reports a healthy no-op forever.\\n\\nEach is enforced at both edges on purpose, matching how the existing `AllowEmptySource` + `AllRefs` rule is handled: at the request edge, where `SyncRequest.Validate()` is a public contract callers can invoke without running a sync, and at the syncer edge — the one point every entry shares, which is what covers `unstable` and the CLI.\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- **Target scope is not quite request scope.** `InTargetScope` exempts git-sync's own `refs/gitsync/` scaffolding from the include half: prune is the only cleaner a stale bootstrap marker has (`isLiveBootstrapMarker` spares the live ones), so without the exemption a prefix-scoped mirror accumulates markers forever and the ENT-2054 resume route never fires. A bootstrap marker is the exception to the exception: ownership comes from the branch it checkpoints rather than from its own name, so **a run manages exactly the markers of the branches it manages, minus any it excludes by name** — an exclusion naming the marker is the caller's own carve-out and still wins. `isLiveBootstrapMarker` can only speak for one run's desired set, so without that two syncs with different scopes sharing a target (a github-kind mirror and a namespace-kind one on one placement) read each other's live resume state as abandoned scaffolding and delete it — reachable from either direction, a narrowing include or a carving exclusion. Nothing is stranded by this: a branch a run does not manage was never bootstrapped by it, so its marker belongs to whoever does. Source-side discovery skips the namespace already. Callers whose target refuses writes outside the included prefixes must exclude `refs/gitsync/` explicitly; the markers of branches a run manages stay prunable.\\n- `replicateBootstrapRoute` now stands down on an empty desired set. It was unreachable with one before; bootstrap has nothing to import from an empty set, so the run belongs on the replicate path where prune does the work.\\n- The new field is threaded through `client.go` **and** all three `unstable` config builders — the field-threading guards in both packages cover this, and `unstable` is the API the worker (T2) uses.\\n- **No CLI flags.** `AllowEmptyScope` has no natural flag (neither does `AllowEmptySource`), and a lone `--include-ref-prefix` would hand CLI users a scope they cannot prune with.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- `internal/planner/include_test.go`: fetch set across all three kinds, prune set (one in-scope deletion, out-of-scope branch/tag/note untouched), an exclusion inside an included prefix, a mapping outside the prefix staying exempt, and a blank prefix failing closed to an empty scope rather than a full one.\\n- `internal/syncer/empty_scope_test.go`: end-to-end against two in-memory repos over the smart-HTTP test server — a populated source with nothing in scope and a target holding both an in-scope and an out-of-scope ref prunes exactly the in-scope one; a source that advertised no refs still fails with `ErrSourceEmptyUnverified` and the target keeps its ref; plus the two validation rules at the syncer edge. Both integration tests were confirmed to fail without the policy.\\n- `client_test.go`: the two rules at the request edge, and the permitted combination still validating.\\n\\n`go build`, `go vet`, `mise run lint` and `go test ./...` are clean.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01XKc1v3szE19sjrjWAzo7cz\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes replicate planning, prune scope, and bootstrap resume routing; wrong scope could prune or spare the wrong refs, though validation and tests target the failure modes.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **prefix-scoped replication** and a policy so an empty in-scope namespace can **prune** instead of failing.\\n> \\n> **`RefScope.IncludeRefPrefixes`** limits push and prune to refs under the given `refs/…` prefixes (all ref kinds). Discovery, `TargetScope.Manages`, and prune planning share **`InScope` / `InTargetScope`** so push and prune cannot disagree; exclusions still apply inside the prefix, and explicit mappings bypass the filter. Invalid prefixes are rejected at validation. **`refs/gitsync/`** bootstrap markers stay prunable on the target with special rules so resume state is not stranded or deleted across writers with different scopes. Source **ls-refs** stays unscoped under `AllRefs` so “empty namespace” stays distinct from “source showed nothing.”\\n> \\n> **`SyncPolicy.AllowEmptyScope`** (replicate + `Prune` + `AllRefs` + include prefixes) treats an empty in-scope desired set as work: prune in-scope target refs when the source advertised at least one ref. If the source advertised nothing, the run fails with **`ErrSourceEmptyUnverified`** instead of pruning blindly. **`AllowEmptySource`** and include prefixes are mutually exclusive; misconfigured combinations are rejected at the client and syncer edges, not silently ignored.\\n> \\n> Fields are threaded through stable and **unstable** clients; **CHANGELOG** documents the behavior.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 98ad974a5f6ae1c30d1949d3efc0c0def8209321. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/121/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/121/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          }\n        ],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      },\n      \"issues\": {\n        \"total_count\": 0,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b28\",\n      \"query\": \"repo:entireio/entire-graph stats cache mtime\",\n      \"prs\": {\n        \"total_count\": 3,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/213\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/213/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/213/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/213/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/213\",\n            \"id\": 5353727491,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSqVa0c8AAAABCRM4TQ\",\n            \"number\": 213,\n            \"title\": \"perf(stats): one-line answer, and stop burning the machine to get it\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"id\": 257360244,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T22:29:40Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-05T12:29:23Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-05T12:29:22Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/213\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/213\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/213.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/213.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-05T12:29:22Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/165\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n`entire graph stats` was reported as (a) pegging the machine and (b) printing a report when the\\nuser wants one number. Both are fixed, and the fix for the weak part of the estimate turned out\\nto be the same change as half the performance fix.\\n\\n## Before / after, on the reported directory\\n\\nThe machine that reported this has **1.9 GB across 3,323 `*.jsonl`** under one project\\n(`~/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv`). Wall clock and peak RSS from `/usr/bin/time -l`,\\ntwo to three runs per cell:\\n\\n| `--since` | before | after, cold (`--no-cache`) | after, warm memo |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `30d` (the default) | **60.1–70.0 s**, 99–101 MB | 14.9–15.4 s, 108 MB | **0.34–0.64 s**, 191–259 MB |\\n| `all` | 49.6–61.6 s, 99–101 MB | 13.5–13.8 s, 110–112 MB | 0.64–1.00 s, 259–264 MB |\\n| `1d` | 39.3 s, 101 MB | 3.1–4.1 s, 45–46 MB | 0.28–0.65 s, 153–233 MB |\\n\\nThe default run is **~180x faster warm and ~4x faster cold**. Peak RSS is the honest cost: the\\nwarm path holds the memo (6.6 MB gzipped on disk) in memory, so peak rises from ~100 MB to\\n~190–264 MB. `--no-cache` keeps it at ~110 MB.\\n\\nWhere the time went, and why it is gone:\\n\\n* **Half of it was system time, not parsing.** The old estimator priced its counterfactual by\\n  resolving the top-hit file of every credited graph call, which ran two regexes over the whole\\n  tool result and then an `os.OpenRoot` plus a per-component `Lstat` for up to 72 path candidates.\\n  Baseline runs spent **16–35 s in `sys`**; the new ones spend **0.7–1.0 s**. Replacing the model\\n  deleted that work outright.\\n* **`--since` was applied after the scan.** `--since 1d` JSON-parsed all 1.9 GB and then threw it\\n  away in the per-session filter. Candidates are now pruned by file mtime first: `1d` parses 683\\n  of 3,323 files, `7d` 2,325, `30d` 3,322, `all` 3,323. (Pruning is per *session*, so a project\\n  with a handful of long-lived sessions — this one has ten — prunes little at 30d and a lot at 1d.\\n  The memo is what makes the wide windows fast.)\\n* **Nothing was cached across runs.** Transcripts are append-mostly, so a per-file summary memo\\n  makes repeat runs near-instant.\\n\\n## What is measured and what is estimated\\n\\n**Estimated — and it stays labelled as such.** The counterfactual cannot be observed. The `~` is\\nin the default line for that reason, and the full model text is printed under `--verbose` and\\ncarried verbatim in `savings_model` in the JSON.\\n\\n**What changed is that both of the model's prices are now measured**, per session, from the\\nsession's own transcript:\\n\\n```\\ngraph cost/call         = locate result bytes      / locate results observed\\nexploration cost/call   = exploration result bytes / exploration results observed\\nsaving per substitution = max(0, exploration cost/call - graph cost/call)\\ntokens saved            = credited locate calls x saving per substitution / 4\\n```\\n\\nThe only assumption left is the 1:1 substitution ratio, and it is not invented: a paired A/B\\nbenchmark of this tool measured **0.980 exploration calls displaced per graph call**. It is\\ncarried as 1:1, which understates. The old model guessed *both* inputs — the counterfactual was\\n\\\"one whole file\\\", sized by whatever file the result happened to name, falling back to the repo's\\nmedian tracked-file size — and on this directory that produced **82.9 M tokens** where the\\nmeasured-input model produces **46 k**. The estimator no longer touches the repository's\\nfilesystem at all.\\n\\n**Consistency check against our own benchmark.** This repo's paired A/B puts the effect at\\nCOST +2.49 %, CI [−6.83, +11.18], median negative, with graph output *larger* per call than the\\nbaseline's. The new model on ten real sessions:\\n\\n| sessions | per-call delta (exploration − graph, bytes) |\\n|---|---|\\n| 4 positive | +665, +1131, +1177, +1411 |\\n| 4 negative | −118, −525, −3641, −4095 |\\n| 2 | no locate calls at all |\\n\\nMean per-call delta is **negative** (−424 B/call); 4 of 8 sessions with locate calls saved\\nnothing. Aggregate: 45,963 tokens against 33.5 B billed. That sits inside a CI that straddles\\nzero and reproduces the \\\"graph output is often larger per call\\\" finding rather than contradicting\\nit — the model reports **0 for a session where the graph cost more than it displaced, and that is\\nnot floored away at the total**, which is a sum of per-session results.\\n\\n## New default output\\n\\n```\\n$ entire graph stats --repo .\\n[entire-graph] ~45,963 tokens saved\\n```\\n\\nOne line. Green on a terminal; plain text under `NO_COLOR`, a pipe or a redirect, via the same\\n`shouldUseColor` rules the rest of the binary uses. The two degenerate cases stay one line too\\n(\\\"no coding-agent session transcripts for this repo yet…\\\", \\\"no sessions in this window…\\\").\\n\\n**`--verbose` restores the full report** — repo/sessions/window lines, the graph-calls-vs-\\nexploration line, both tables, billed tokens, the new measured per-call costs, and the wrapped\\nmodel text.\\n\\n**`--format json` is unchanged in shape.** `scripts/entire-graph-statusline.sh` reads\\n`estimated_savings_est_tokens` and `estimated_savings_pct_of_session_tokens` on every prompt\\nrender, so keys are only ever added: `transcripts_considered`, `transcripts_from_cache`,\\n`graph_locate_calls`, `graph_locate_returned_bytes`, `graph_bytes_per_locate_call`,\\n`exploration_bytes_per_call`, `sessions_with_positive_savings`, `substitution_ratio`.\\n`median_tracked_file_bytes` is retired but stays in the contract, always 0.\\n`TestStatsJSONContractKeepsEveryPublishedKey` asserts the 29 previously published keys against a\\ngolden list, and `--verbose` is asserted not to change the JSON.\\n\\n## Accuracy audit (independent of the model)\\n\\n* **Cross-transcript double counting — real, and measured.** Across the 3,316 real transcripts,\\n  **215 `tool_use` ids and 168 usage-bearing `message.id`s appear in more than one transcript of\\n  the same session** (Claude Code replays a forked subagent's history into the new file; zero\\n  collisions cross session boundaries). The old code billed each of those twice, in both call\\n  counts and bytes. Sessions are now assembled from per-call and per-message identities, so one\\n  API call counts once however many transcripts carry it.\\n* **Tool-result pairing is strictly file-local** — 0 of 155,343 results pair with a `tool_use` in\\n  a different file — which is what makes a per-file summary a faithful unit and the memo sound.\\n* **Per-call prices divide by results observed, never calls issued**, so a call whose result never\\n  reached the transcript cannot deflate a price.\\n* **`mulDiv`** replaces `a*b/c`. The product already reaches ~10^13 on real volumes and would\\n  silently wrap int64; it is now exact via `bits.Mul64`/`bits.Div64`, saturating instead of\\n  wrapping, with the `hi >= c` boundary pinned (`bits.Div64` *panics* at `hi == c`).\\n* **`roundTo`** uses `math.Round` instead of an int64 truncation that rounded negatives toward\\n  zero and was undefined outside int64 range.\\n* **Determinism**: two runs over an unchanged directory are byte-identical, asserted for the\\n  default text, `--verbose` and JSON.\\n* The memo's key is file *identity* (path + size + mtime) salted with the summary schema, the CLI\\n  version and the running executable's own size and mtime — a rebuilt binary misses rather than\\n  trusting a summary written by different parsing code. A missing, truncated, corrupt or\\n  foreign-schema memo is treated as empty and recomputed, never served. Entries for transcripts\\n  no longer on disk are dropped each run, driven by the full candidate list so a narrow `--since`\\n  does not evict what a later `--since all` wants.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n19 new tests; every behaviour change has one that fails on a compile-clean revert (14 reverts\\napplied, built, and run: mtime prune, session-scoped prune, cross-transcript tool_use dedup,\\ncross-transcript usage dedup, terse default, locate-only pricing, `roundTo`, `mulDiv`, colour\\ngating, JSON contract, memo lookup, memo key, memo salt, memo pruning). 20 mutants applied to the\\nnew decision helpers in both directions; 15 killed, 5 survived and were adjudicated — one was a\\ngenuine escape (`hi >= c` → `hi > c`, a `bits.Div64` panic path) and is now killed by\\n`mulDiv(1<<32, 1<<32, 1)`; the other four are equivalent mutants with proofs in the review notes\\n(`a <= 0`→`a < 0` and `displaced <= x`→`<` differ only where both branches return 0;\\n`||`→`&&` in the savings precondition is unreachable because `mulDiv` is total; dropping\\n`cutoff.IsZero()` is equivalent because no `time.Time` is `Before` the zero time).\\n\\nTests changed rather than deleted where they encoded the old shape:\\n`TestStatsTextOutputCarriesRatioAndCaveat` now drives `--verbose` (that is where the report went)\\nand additionally asserts the new measured-per-call line; the missing-dir and empty-dir tests were\\nupdated to the new one-line wording; `TestStatsSavingsModelMath` and\\n`TestStatsSavingsFlooredAtZeroWhenGraphCostsMore` were rewritten around the new arithmetic; the\\nstatus-line fixture's exploration results were enlarged, because the badge exists to show a\\nsession where exploration cost more per call than the graph did.\\n\\nDeleted with the code they covered: `TestStatsMedianFallbackWhenTopHitUnresolvable`,\\n`TestStatsFileSizeStaysInsideTheSelectedRepository` and `stats_mount_windows_test.go` (both\\njunction tests) all exercised the repository-filesystem probing that no longer exists — `stats`\\nnow never opens a file in the scanned repository, which removes that traversal surface entirely.\\n\\n`go build ./...`, `go vet ./...` (also `GOOS=windows` and `GOOS=linux`), `gofmt -l -s .` clean;\\n`go test ./... -count=1` and `go test -race ./... -count=1` green (4,951 tests);\\n`scripts/entire-graph-statusline_test.sh` 151/151.\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/213/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/213/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/240\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/240/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/240/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/240/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/240\",\n            \"id\": 5375459288,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSqVa0c8AAAABCh95sw\",\n            \"number\": 240,\n            \"title\": \"fix(statusline): render the savings figure alone by default\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"id\": 257360244,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-09-07T13:43:17Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-07T14:19:56Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-07T14:19:55Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/240\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/240\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/240.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/240.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-07T14:19:55Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/170\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What the badge renders today\\n\\nNine segments: the savings figure, a three-verb split, exploration calls, exploration tokens, a graph-first tick, a share of locates, and a share of session tokens. On this machine:\\n\\n```\\n[GRAPH] ↗ 49.4K saved · 154 search · 24 impact · 14 nbrs · 94 other\\n        · vs 109.7K explore · 64.8M explore tok · graph-first 0% · <1% of locates\\n```\\n\\nThat is a report, not a status line, and it sits next to everything else a host already puts there.\\n\\n## Why cut it rather than reorder it\\n\\n**\\\"Is the graph being used\\\" is `entire graph stats`' question.** It answers on demand, with room to explain itself. A status line renders on every keystroke and has no room to qualify anything.\\n\\n**`explore tok` reads as a savings claim it is not.** It puts a multi-million token figure on a line whose headline number is five orders of magnitude smaller. It is the exploration corpus, not a saving — but adjacency invites reading it as one, and the paired benchmark does not support a number that size. A number that large next to `saved` is a claim we would have to defend.\\n\\n## The change\\n\\nDefault is the savings figure alone:\\n\\n```\\n[GRAPH] ↗ 6.6K saved\\n```\\n\\nEverything else is unchanged and opt-in behind `ENTIRE_GRAPH_STATUSLINE_DETAIL=1`. Nothing is deleted — the full rendering is one env var away, and the header comment documents both forms.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\nThe suite's 23 existing segment tests exercise the detailed rendering, so it keeps its coverage: `run_json`/`run` now pass `DETAIL=1`, and because `env` applies assignments in order a caller passing `DETAIL=0` still overrides it. `clean_env` unsets the new variable so tests stay hermetic.\\n\\nA new test pins the default — the same fixture that renders the full line must print one segment and none of the other seven:\\n\\n```\\nassert_eq 'default line is the savings figure alone' '[GRAPH] ↗ 2.1M saved'\\n```\\n\\nIt fails on a compile-clean revert of the gate with `FAIL default line is the savings figure alone`.\\n\\n**159 passed, 0 failed.**\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nThe badge had also been switched off locally since 2026-08-07 on the belief that its render cache was content-keyed and recomputed `stats` every render (measured then at 127% CPU). Reading and timing the current script, that is not what it does — the cache filename is session id plus a digest of the transcript *path*, freshness is a separate size+mtime stamp, a miss serves the previous line and refreshes in the background under a lock, and three consecutive renders measured 0.05s / 0.05s / 0.04s. So the badge is cheap; it was just saying too much.\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/240/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/240/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/372\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/372/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/372/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/372/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/372\",\n            \"id\": 6016924278,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSqVa0c8AAAABKfB9SQ\",\n            \"number\": 372,\n            \"title\": \"fix(sem): index partial clones offline when Git honours GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"id\": 257360244,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-24T19:49:36Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-25T18:06:56Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-25T18:06:55Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/372\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/372\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/372.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/372.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-25T18:06:55Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2510/changes/entire-graph/285\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n`entire graph index --head` failed on any partial clone:\\n\\n```\\nresolve committed HEAD for preindex: refuse Git subprocesses for unsafe or unreadable repository\\nmetadata under \\\".../entiredb\\\": its Git config declares a promisor remote (a partial clone), so Git\\ncommands here can fetch objects over the network; indexing falls back to a filesystem walk to stay offline\\n```\\n\\nThe fallback that message promises exists only on query paths (`prepareSource`'s `E_NO_GIT_HEAD`\\nwalk, and the uncached build in `loadOrBuildSearchSnapshotPersisting`), so `index --head` simply\\nreturned, and every query on such a repository rebuilt an uncached working-tree snapshot (N2).\\nThe `entiredb` and `cli` checkouts both hit this: the Entire CLI fetches checkpoints from a\\n`blob:none` promisor remote named by its URL, not `origin`.\\n\\n**Why it matters most: Brain gets no code context on partial clones.** On the machine where this\\nwas found, Brain's Graph-owned store builds `semantic` sources from `graph index --head`. Of the\\nfive Brain repositories there, the two partial clones (`cli`, `entiredb`) have **no `semantic`\\nsource**, because Graph refused them with the promisor message. `entire-graph` and `entire-brain`\\nhave one. (`entire.io` has none either, but it is not a partial clone, so that is unrelated.) With\\nthis PR, `index --head` succeeds on both partial clones, so Brain can index them at all.\\n\\nThis PR:\\n\\n- **Admits a partial clone only when the Git that runs in it is proven to honour\\n  `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH`**: Git **2.45.1** or newer, or on an older release line 2.39.4+, 2.40.2+,\\n  2.41.1+, 2.42.2+, 2.43.4+ or 2.44.1+. **2.45.0 is refused** (see below). So are its `.windows.N` and `.rcN` forms,\\n  `2.45.GIT` dev builds, and any unknown or unparseable version.\\n- **Probes `git version` in exactly the directory string the provider's Git commands use**: the\\n  `--repo` path as given, with the same logical `PWD`, never its symlink target. A per-directory\\n  version manager (asdf or mise `.tool-versions`, which walks up from `PWD`) is therefore asked\\n  about the Git it will really run. The result is cached per (that directory string, binary path,\\n  size, mtime). The key is deliberately not symlink-resolved: two spellings of one directory can sit\\n  under different `.tool-versions` files, so a canonical key would let an answer for `real/repo` be\\n  reused for `link/repo`. Failures are cached too, so the refusal and its diagnosis always share one\\n  answer.\\n- **Keeps the refusal otherwise, with true text.** The new message claims only what is known:\\n  `its Git config declares a promisor remote (a partial clone), and lazy fetching cannot be proven\\n  disabled for the Git on PATH (2.45.0), so a Git command here could contact the promisor remote to\\n  fetch a missing object; Git subprocesses are refused for this repository. GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH stops\\n  every lazy fetch in Git 2.45.1 or newer (or, on an older release line, 2.39.4+, 2.40.2+, 2.41.1+,\\n  2.42.2+, 2.43.4+ or 2.44.1+)`. For an unknown version it says the version could not be determined, and\\n  claims nothing else about it.\\n- **`HeadCommitAndTree` uses `git -c i18n.logOutputEncoding=UTF-8 log -1 --no-walk`** instead of\\n  `git show -s`. `show -s` still diffs HEAD against its parent, and rename detection then reads the\\n  parent's blobs, so on a real `blob:none` clone it died with `unable to read <oid>` on any HEAD\\n  that renames and edits a file. The encoding pin fixes a pre-existing failure: a repository with\\n  `i18n.logOutputEncoding=UTF-16` broke every committed-tree command with \\\"malformed HEAD\\n  commit/tree metadata\\\".\\n- **The same encoding pin is applied** to the co-change (`FileCochanges`) and checkpoint-lookup\\n  (`FindCommitWithCheckpoint`) `git log` reads, which a UTF-16 setting silently emptied.\\n- **Static launch scan.** It resolves packages by import path, sees package-level initializers and\\n  function values, and rejects dot imports, so an `import ex \\\"os/exec\\\"` alias can no longer slip\\n  past. It also rejects:\\n  - `exec.Cmd` used as a value type (a zero value or an embedded field); only `*exec.Cmd` is allowed;\\n  - raw process-creating system calls (`SYS_EXECVE`, `SYS_FORK`, `SYS_CLONE`, ...);\\n  - process-creating C functions reached through cgo: `C.system`, a cgo preamble, or any\\n    `.c/.h/.cc` file in the module. The vendored grammar C was checked: it contains none.\\n  It now walks `bin/` and `node_modules/` too, since the go tool compiles an imported package there.\\n- **CI checks the version table against real boundary Gits.** A path-filtered workflow\\n  (`lazy-fetch-git-matrix.yml`) builds Git 2.45.0 and the 2.44.1 backport from checksummed kernel.org\\n  tarballs and runs the two oracle tests against them. The runners' own Git (2.55/2.56) is always\\n  past the boundary.\\n- Updates `docs/trust-and-security.md`, `docs/semantic-provider-requirements.md`, the `gitutil`\\n  comments and the changelog.\\n\\n### Why offline is still guaranteed, and which guard does the work\\n\\n**`GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1` does the work: with a qualifying Git, no fetch is ever attempted.** Git\\nstarts a lazy fetch in only one place, `promisor-remote.c` `fetch_objects()`. Every caller reaches\\nit through `promisor_remote_get_direct()`, including the blob prefetch that rename detection does\\nin `log`, `diff` and `show`. git/git@7b70e9efb18c (\\\"upload-pack: disable lazy-fetching by default\\\")\\nmade `fetch_objects()` return before it spawns `git fetch` when `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` is true. That\\ncommit shipped in the April 2024 security releases (2.39.4, 2.40.2, 2.41.1, 2.42.2, 2.43.4, 2.44.1,\\n2.45.1) and in every release from 2.46.0. The table in `lazy_fetch_guard.go` was checked against\\n`promisor-remote.c` at each listed tag and at the tag before it; only the listed tags have the\\ncheck.\\n\\n**2.45.0 is not one of them.** Its `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` (from `git --no-lazy-fetch`) only clears\\n`fetch_if_missing`, which the rename prefetch ignores. An earlier revision of this PR used a 2.45.0\\nfloor. Its citation (`2c206fc`) does not resolve, and an adversarial review reproduced the hole:\\nwith Git 2.45.0 on `PATH`, `FileCochanges` (`log --name-only`) and `ChangedFiles`\\n(`diff --find-renames`) spawned `git fetch origin ... --filter=blob:none --stdin`, stopped only by\\n`GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL`. On Git for Windows, `transport.c` `is_file(url)` stats a UNC promisor URL\\nbefore that allowlist check, which is SMB egress.\\n\\n`GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=` stays as an independent second layer. This PR does not rest on it.\\n\\n**Empirical check across real Git builds** (`2.44.0`, `2.45.0`, `2.44.1`, `2.45.1` are source\\nbuilds). The fixture is a partial clone whose HEAD renames and edits a file; the parent blob is\\nwithheld and the `file://` source is still reachable. `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1` and\\n`GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=` are set, and a spy `git` in `GIT_EXEC_PATH` counts child `git fetch` processes:\\n\\n| Git | guard says | `log --name-only` | `diff --find-renames` | `cat-file -p <missing>` |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 2.44.0 | refuse | **fetch** | **fetch** | **fetch** |\\n| 2.45.0 | refuse | **fetch** | **fetch** | none |\\n| 2.44.1 (backport) | admit | none | none | none |\\n| 2.45.1 | admit | none | none | none |\\n| 2.50.1 (Apple Git-155) | admit | none | none | none |\\n| 2.54.0 | admit | none | none | none |\\n\\nThis is `TestLazyFetchGuardMatchesObservedGitBehaviour`, which fails if any Git the guard admits\\nstarts a fetch. It always checks the Git on `PATH` (2.55/2.56 in CI), and `ENTIRE_GRAPH_TEST_GITS`\\nadds more.\\n\\n**Per-directory Git selection.** The reviewer's asdf-style shim walks up from `PWD` and runs Git\\n2.44.0 under any `.tool-versions` that pins it. Their cases, re-run on this branch:\\n\\n| case | previous revision (36c0cc41) | this branch |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| a: `.tool-versions` at the repo root | probe 2.44.0, refused, 0 fetches | probe 2.44.0, refused, 0 fetches |\\n| b: `.tool-versions` in a subdirectory, `--repo` subdir | refused, 0 fetches | probe 2.44.0, refused, 0 fetches |\\n| c, c2: same, cwd in the subdirectory, no `--repo` | 0 fetches | commands run at the root with 2.54.0, 0 fetches |\\n| **d: `--repo evil/link`, `link -> real/clone`, `evil/.tool-versions` pins 2.44.0** | **probe 2.54.0 at `real/clone`, 16 commands with 2.44.0 at `evil/link`, 1 lazy-fetch child** (stopped only by `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL`) | **probe 2.44.0 at `evil/link`, refused, 0 commands, 0 fetches** |\\n\\n**One guard at a time, raw Git 2.54.0**, on the deterministic fixture. That fixture is\\n`git clone --no-local file://$SRC`, repacked without one blob, then\\n`remote.origin.promisor=true` and `partialclonefilter=blob:none`. Verified: in-pack 3, `missing=1`.\\nIt is copied fresh per probe, and exit codes are captured before any pipe:\\n\\n| env | `cat-file -e` exit | `cat-file -p` exit | missing after | stderr |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1` only | 1 | 128 | 1 | none / `Not a valid object name`: **no fetch attempted** |\\n| no guards | 0 | 0 | **0** | `filtering not recognized by server`: the fetch ran, so the fixture is live |\\n| `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=` only | 1 | 128 | 1 | **`fatal: transport 'file' not allowed`**: attempted, blocked at transport |\\n| both (production) | 1 | 128 | 1 | as the first row |\\n\\nAt the product level, removing `noLazyFetchEnv` from `gitSubprocessEnvironment` makes `index --head`\\nspawn `git fetch origin --filter=blob:none --stdin` on Git 2.54, 2.45.1 and the 2.44.1 backport.\\nRemoving only `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL` changes nothing.\\n\\n### Every Git subprocess site\\n\\nAll production Git processes are built by the two constructors in `internal/gitutil/git.go`. Both\\napply `gitSubprocessEnvironment`, the single place `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1` and `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=`\\nare set:\\n\\n- `newCmd` (applies the Git environment when the program is `\\\"git\\\"`; every call passes the\\n  literal): `IndexNonRegularPaths` (`ls-files -s`), `ListIndexFiles`, `ListWorktreeFiles`,\\n  `ListIgnoredWorktreeFiles` (`ls-files`), `OversizeBlobAtRev` (`cat-file blob`),\\n  `NewBatchFileReader` (`cat-file --batch-command`), `treeEntryMetadataBatch` (`ls-tree -l`). In\\n  `worktree_paths.go`: `treeBlobMembersBatch`, `VisitWorktreePaths`,\\n  `VisitWorktreeDirectoryEntries`, `firstNestedIgnorePaths`, `boundedNestedIgnorePaths`,\\n  `listLiteralWorktreePathBatch`, `IndexHasFilesUnder`.\\n- `runWithStderr` (via `newCmd`): `ShowFile` (`show <object>`), `readBlobAtRev` (`cat-file blob`),\\n  `run`.\\n- `run` (via `runWithStderr`): `RepoRoot`, `RepoPrefix`, `RevParse`, `HeadCommitAndTree` (`log`),\\n  `FirstParent`, `FindCommitWithCheckpoint` (`log --grep`), `ListRegularFiles`, `ListFiles`\\n  (`ls-tree -r`), `ChangedFiles` (`diff --raw --find-renames`), `FileCochanges`\\n  (`log --name-only`), `RemoteURLs` (`config --get-regexp`), and `LazyFetchGuard` (`git version`).\\n- `newGitCmdWithCallerLocale`: `grepPatternLines`, `grepTreePaths`, `runGrepFixedStringMatches`\\n  (`git grep`).\\n\\nFound with `entire graph neighbors --direction in` on `newCmd`, `run`, `runWithStderr` and\\n`newGitCmdWithCallerLocale`, plus `git grep 'exec\\\\.Command'` over all non-test Go files.\\n\\nOther process launches, reviewed and allowlisted by the static scan:\\n- `internal/gitutil/process_job_windows.go` `newPathOutputCreationParent`: `syscall.CreateProcess`\\n  of a suspended surrogate of this executable, which executes nothing.\\n- `internal/cli/verify.go` `runVerifyShell`: runs the user's own test command.\\n- `internal/bench/worker.go` and `cmd/graph-bench/main.go`: benchmark harnesses.\\n\\n## Measurements\\n\\nThis is a correctness fix; the speed effect is N2. Method:\\n- `query --head` wall time on the two partial clones (main checkouts, read-only).\\n- base = `origin/main` (`d4a0c186`), new = this branch.\\n- Fresh `--cache-dir` per binary, one untimed warm-up for new, then 3 interleaved reps under the\\n  shared measurement lock.\\n- load1 3.9 to 5.8.\\n\\n| repo | query | base median (reps) | new median (reps) | new cache hit |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| `cli` | \\\"condense session transcript into checkpoint\\\" | **34.26 s** (33.72, 34.26, 34.70) | **2.51 s** (2.67, 2.51, 2.42) | 3/3 |\\n| `entiredb` | \\\"repair under-replicated providers quorum write\\\" | **6.61 s** (7.02, 6.61, 6.55) | **2.03 s** (2.22, 1.99, 2.03) | 3/3 |\\n\\n**Output identity.** Only provenance changes. Comparing base and new JSON, the full ordered result\\nlist (`file_path#symbol_name`) is **identical** for both queries. New adds `commit`/`tree` and drops\\nthe working-tree fallback warnings (`W_GIT_WORKTREE_FALLBACK`, `E_NO_GIT_HEAD`,\\n`W_REPO_IGNORED_SOURCE`, plus `W_GITDIR_SWEEP_BUDGET` on `cli`).\\n\\n**Caveat, not caused here.** A query containing an abbreviation-table word (\\\"repository\\\",\\n\\\"configuration\\\", ...) on a committed-tree cache hit takes the alias preselect route (review item\\n#1), which is slow on large trees. On `entiredb` that was 15.6 s new vs 8.8 s base, because base\\nnever reached that route on a partial clone. Every non-partial repository pays it today.\\n\\n**Live** (Git 2.54.0, fresh cache, read-only):\\n- `entiredb` (`8f93cd6a6e`): base exits 1 with the refusal. New exits 0: 2542 files, 36068 symbols,\\n  198448 relations, completeness `ok`, 15 partial failures (14 `E_PARSE_ERROR`, 1 `E_MINIFIED`;\\n  none from missing blobs).\\n- `cli` (`3d1b73ff2`): base exits 1. New exits 0: 1427 files, 28619 symbols, 160320 relations,\\n  1 `E_MINIFIED`.\\n- A `GIT_TRACE` build indexing `cli --head` made 19 Git invocations and **zero** `git fetch`.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\nEvery test was weakened to red and restored, and each restore was checked with `git diff`.\\n\\n| test | pins | weakened to | red line |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `TestParseLazyFetchGuardStatus` (gitutil) | 2.45.1/2.46/2.54/Apple admitted; **2.45.0, `2.45.0.windows.1`, `2.45.0.rc0/rc2`, `2.45.GIT`** refused; each backport and the patch before it | floor back to 2.45.0; 2.44.1 backport dropped | `\\\"git version 2.45.0\\\" = {Effective:true} ... want effective false` (also `.windows.1`, `.rc0`, `.rc2`) |\\n| `TestLazyFetchGuardMatchesObservedGitBehaviour` (gitutil) | no Git the guard admits starts a lazy fetch (table above) | floor back to 2.45.0 | `Git 2.45.0 is trusted to honour GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH, but git log --name-only ... started a lazy fetch` |\\n| `TestNoProviderCommandStartsALazyFetchWhicheverGitIsOnPath` (cli) | product level: `index`, `query`, `diff`, `commit` on a rename partial clone start no child Git, whatever Git is on PATH (incl. the 2.45.0 build) | floor back to 2.45.0; `noLazyFetchEnv` dropped | `with Git \\\"2.45.0\\\" on PATH ... started Git child commands: -c fetch.negotiationAlgorithm=noop fetch origin ... --filter=blob:none --stdin` |\\n| `TestLazyFetchGuardProbesInTheRepositoryDirectory` (gitutil) | a cwd-sensitive fake Git (`.tool-versions` → 2.44.0) is probed where it runs | probe in `os.TempDir()` | `probe in a directory that pins Git 2.44.0 = {Version:2.54.0 Effective:true}` |\\n| `TestLazyFetchGuardProbesTheLogicalPathNotTheSymlinkTarget` (gitutil) | asdf-style fake Git walking up from `PWD`: `evil/link -> real/repo` with `evil/.tool-versions` pinning 2.44.0 is probed as 2.44.0, and the two spellings keep separate cache entries | probe cwd symlink-resolved again (`filepath.EvalSymlinks`) | `probe for .../evil/link (a symlink under a directory pinning Git 2.44.0) = {Version:2.54.0 Effective:true}; it asked about the symlink target` |\\n| `TestPartialCloneThroughASymlinkIsProbedWhereItsCommandsRun` (cli) | product level, case d: the shim's \\\"old Git\\\" (reports 2.44.0, runs Git with `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` removed) is refused through `--repo evil/link`; no lazy fetch | probe cwd symlink-resolved again | `the pinned old Git started a lazy fetch through .../link; the probe vouched for a different Git` |\\n| `TestGitMetadataGuardProbesTheGivenPathOfASymlinkedRepository` (sem) | the predicate probes the given `--repo` string, not its resolved path | probe `resolver.baseResolved` | `the guard probed Git in \\\"/private/var/...\\\", want exactly the given path \\\"/var/...\\\"` |\\n| `TestPartialCloneWithAURLNamedCheckpointPromisor` (cli) | the real Entire shape: `origin` ordinary, promisor on `remote.https://github.com/entireio/cli-checkpoints.git` (dots, slashes, colon): refused on 2.45.0, admitted offline with no fetch on a proven Git | detection limited to the `\\\"origin\\\"` remote | `index --head with a URL-named promisor on Git 2.45.0 = <nil>, want the promisor refusal`; sem: `remote named by its own URL: admitted on Git 2.45.0` |\\n| `TestGitMetadataGuardProbesGitOnlyForPartialClones` (sem) | ordinary repos never probe; the predicate probes the repository directory | predicate probes `os.TempDir()` | `the guard probed Git in \\\"/var/folders/.../T/\\\", want the repository` |\\n| `TestLazyFetchGuardCachesAFailedProbe` (gitutil), `TestPartialCloneRefusalAndDiagnosisShareOneProbe` (sem) | a failed first probe refuses, and the diagnosis explains that instead of re-probing | cache successes only; diagnosis probes on its own | `probes after one failure = {} then {2.54.0 true}`; `diagnosis ... = \\\"\\\"; it re-probed` |\\n| `TestPartialCloneRefusalNamesTheGitVersionAndPromisesNoFallback` (sem) | \\\"cannot be proven disabled\\\", never \\\"predates/older than\\\"; unknown version says so | message says the Git \\\"predates the fix\\\" | `calls the Git old; it is only unproven` |\\n| `TestEveryGitSubprocessIsBuiltByTheGuardedConstructors` + `TestProcessLaunchScanCatchesAliasedAndValueUses` (gitutil) | launches matched by import path, incl. package-level values and dot imports; wrappers used as values; `exec.Cmd` value types (`var c exec.Cmd`, embedding); `syscall.Syscall(SYS_EXECVE, ...)`; `C.system`, a cgo preamble calling `system`, and a `.c` file calling `posix_spawn`, all inside a `bin/` package | added `evasion.go` (`import ex \\\"os/exec\\\"; var launch = ex.CommandContext; ex.Command(\\\"git\\\",\\\"fetch\\\")`); scanner reverted to name-based matching; each new rule disabled in turn; `bin/` skipped again | `evasion.go:5:14: package-level declaration references os/exec.CommandContext ...`; `scan missed \\\"package-level declaration uses exec.Cmd as a value type\\\"`, `\\\"... syscall.SYS_EXECVE\\\"`, `\\\"shell calls the process-creating C function system through cgo\\\"`, `\\\"bin/helper/spawn.c is C source ...\\\"` |\\n| `TestFindProcessCFunctionCallMatchesWholeCallsOnly` (gitutil) | `system(`/`popen\\\\t(` match; `subsystem(`, `my_fork(`, `systematic(` and the string `\\\"system\\\"` do not | identifier-boundary check removed | `findProcessCFunctionCall(\\\"subsystem(x); my_fork(); a.b\\\") = \\\"system\\\", want \\\"\\\"` |\\n| `TestHistoryReadsIgnoreRepositoryLogOutputEncoding` (gitutil) | co-change pairs and checkpoint lookup survive a UTF-16 `i18n.logOutputEncoding` | each pin removed | `FileCochanges ... = []gitutil.FileCochange{}, want the a.go/b.go pair`; `FindCommitWithCheckpoint ... = \\\"\\\", checkpoint abc123def456 has no associated commit` |\\n| `TestHeadCommitAndTreeIgnoresRepositoryLogOutputEncoding` (gitutil) | UTF-16 `i18n.logOutputEncoding` repo still resolves HEAD | encoding pin removed | `git log returned malformed HEAD commit/tree metadata` |\\n| (a) `TestIndexHeadIndexesAPartialCloneOffline` (cli) | remote deleted: `--head` indexes all 3 files, no failures | guard reverted; `show -s` restored | `refuse Git subprocesses ...`; `git show -s ...: unable to read` |\\n| (b) `TestPartialCloneMissingBlobIsAnErrorNotALazyFetch` (cli) | missing HEAD blob: `E_FILE_READ`, no child Git (spy with control) | `noLazyFetchEnv` dropped | `indexing started Git child commands (a lazy fetch) for the missing blob` |\\n| (c) `TestIndexHeadRefusesPartialCloneOnUnprovenGit` (cli) | a stand-in Git **2.45.0** is refused, with the corrected text | floor back to 2.45.0 | `index --head admitted a partial clone on Git 2.45.0` |\\n| (d) `TestQueryHeadReusesTheCacheOnAPartialClone` (cli) | N2: second `query --head` is a cache hit | guard reverted | `query fell back to the working tree` |\\n| `TestEveryGitInvocationCarriesTheNoEgressGuards` (cli) | a logging `git` on PATH across 11 commands plus `git grep`: both guards on every call | either var dropped; only the grep constructor unguarded | `git grep ... ran with GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=\\\"<unset>\\\"` |\\n| sem gate and detection tests, Windows UNC tests | the same config is refused on 2.45.0 or unknown and admitted on 2.45.1; detection pinned with a stand-in Git | admit always | `admitted on Git 2.45.0, which does not honour GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH for every lazy fetch` |\\n\\nTwo cache-revalidation tests used a promisor remote as their \\\"metadata became unsafe\\\" trigger. They\\nnow use an `include`, which is refused on every Git version; a harmless config key turns them red.\\n\\nLocal (Git 2.54.0):\\n- `go test -p 1` of whole packages under the measurement lock: `./internal/gitutil`, `./internal/sem`,\\n  and (in the first revision) `./internal/cli`.\\n- All focused tests above also pass under `-race`.\\n- The Git-matrix tests were run with `ENTIRE_GRAPH_TEST_GITS` pointing at the 2.44.0, 2.45.0,\\n  2.44.1 and 2.45.1 source builds. The new workflow's check step was run locally against the\\n  2.45.0 and 2.44.1 builds; its build step runs only in CI.\\n- The reviewer's shim cases a, b, c, c2 and d were re-run against this branch (table above).\\n- CI runners have Git 2.55.0 (ubuntu) and 2.56.0 (macOS), so the \\\"admitted\\\" tests run there rather\\n  than skip.\\n\\n### What works on a partial clone now, and what does not\\n\\nThese read the committed tree and reuse its cache: `index --head`, `query --head`, `impact`,\\n`neighbors`, `def`, `context`, `store`, `health`, `snapshot`. All were checked exit 0 on a rename\\npartial clone, with no blob fetched.\\n\\nAnything that needs a blob the clone lacks fails or degrades instead of fetching it:\\n- A missing HEAD file is reported as `E_FILE_READ`.\\n- `diff` and `commit` exit 1 when rename detection needs a missing blob (for example `commit HEAD`\\n  on a commit that renames and edits a file).\\n- Co-change (`FILE_CHANGES_WITH`) relations are omitted when history needs one; #378 adds a warning\\n  for that.\\n\\nNeither `entiredb` nor `cli` is affected by these limits, since their history blobs are local.\\n\\n### Follow-ups, not in this PR\\n\\n- The static launch scan is a guard against accidents and easy evasions, not a proof. It still\\n  cannot see: `reflect.New(reflect.TypeOf((*exec.Cmd)(nil)).Elem())`, `plugin.Open`, assembly\\n  (`.s`) or `syscall.Syscall` with a computed number, and launches inside third-party module\\n  dependencies. Enumerating packages with `go list -deps` and adding a vet-style analyzer would\\n  close those.\\n- Co-change on a partial clone with missing history blobs still drops `FILE_CHANGES_WITH`; #378\\n  makes that visible as a warning.\\n\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/372/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/372/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          }\n        ],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      },\n      \"issues\": {\n        \"total_count\": 0,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b29\",\n      \"query\": \"repo:entireio/entire-brain workspaceGraphGeneration\",\n      \"prs\": {\n        \"total_count\": 1,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/294\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/294/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/294/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/294/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/294\",\n            \"id\": 5518782854,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSm5-5c8AAAABEUV7KA\",\n            \"number\": 294,\n            \"title\": \"Correct entity history joins and bound workspace graph caching and selection\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"ashtom\",\n              \"id\": 70720,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzIw\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70720?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/ashtom\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-09-20T15:40:33Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-20T23:43:53Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-20T17:38:53Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/pulls/294\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/294\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/294.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/294.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-20T17:38:53Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/214\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nFix F18, F19, F55–F57, F74 and F75. Entity aliases resolve complete rename cycles deterministically; batch ingestion caches list timestamps while preserving ordering. Warm entity views refresh checkpoint/session joins and explicit unknown branches return errors. Workspace graph caches bind to membership and source generations, and cross-repository edge selection retains only the bounded best results.\\n\\nValidation: full Go suite, focused race tests, vet and formatting pass. Regressions cover long alias chains/cycles, warm joins, removed members, stale/late graph writers, and selected-edge equivalence to an exhaustive reference. Local microbenchmarks reduce 20k list pushes from 242ms to 4.4ms; 250k workspace pairs with limit one allocate about 123KB instead of 472MB. Pair enumeration is still quadratic; retained result memory is bounded.\\n<details>\\n<summary>Recorded reproduction and verification evidence</summary>\\n\\nActual excerpts from retained worker logs; omitted lines are not new output. Red means the recorded pre-fix behavior (or explicitly reverted behavior), not a compilation failure. Green is the executed corrected test/package result. Filenames identify retained evidence beside this group’s result report.\\n\\n**Alias cycles/chains (F18)** — red `f18-red.log`, green `f18-f19-final.log`.\\n\\n```text\\nRED\\n--- FAIL: TestThreeNameRenameCycle (0.29s)\\n--- FAIL: TestResolveLongAliasChainAndCycleEntry (0.00s)\\nGREEN\\nok  \\tgithub.com/entireio/entire-brain/internal/entityindex\\t29.697s\\n```\\n\\n**Warm joins and explicit branches (F55–F57)** — red `f55-f57-red.log`, green `f55-f57-green.log`.\\n\\n```text\\nRED\\n--- FAIL: TestEntityWarmCacheHonorsPrivacyFailure (0.07s)\\n--- FAIL: TestEntityCacheIncludesNewSessionJoin (0.05s)\\n--- FAIL: TestEntityUnknownBranchCannotUnfilter (0.04s)\\nGREEN\\nok  \\tgithub.com/entireio/entire-brain/internal/cli\\t4.579s\\n```\\n\\n**Workspace membership cache (F74)** — red `f74-red.log`, green `f74-compatibility.log`.\\n\\n```text\\nRED\\n--- FAIL: TestRemovedMemberCannotRemainInGraph (0.12s)\\nGREEN\\nok  \\tgithub.com/entireio/entire-brain/internal/cli\\t2.337s\\n```\\n\\n**Measured performance (F19/F75), not synthetic failure assertions.** Same-host microbenchmark excerpts; list mutation and retained-edge allocation only, not end-to-end indexing. Pair enumeration remains quadratic.\\n\\n```text\\nBEFORE f19-before.log\\nBenchmarkBatchOneEntity/20000-8        \\t       3\\t 241972986 ns/op\\t 2279480 B/op\\t      22 allocs/op\\nAFTER f19-after.log\\nBenchmarkBatchOneEntity/20000-8        \\t       3\\t   4364806 ns/op\\t 2281253 B/op\\t      24 allocs/op\\nBEFORE f75-before.log\\nBenchmarkWorkspaceCrossEdgesBounded/500-8         \\t       1\\t 116365167 ns/op\\t472566688 B/op\\t      44 allocs/op\\nAFTER f75-after.log\\nBenchmarkWorkspaceCrossEdgesBounded/500-8         \\t       1\\t  15553375 ns/op\\t  123456 B/op\\t       6 allocs/op\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/294/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/294/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": {\n              \"id\": 2626939,\n              \"client_id\": \"Iv23lieFG10uOnChW4TN\",\n              \"slug\": \"entire\",\n              \"node_id\": \"A_kwHOAfprLM4AKBV7\",\n              \"owner\": {\n                \"login\": \"entireio\",\n                \"id\": 33188652,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjMzMTg4NjUy\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33188652?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"Organization\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"name\": \"Entire\",\n              \"description\": \"\",\n              \"external_url\": \"https://entire.com\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/entire\",\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-01-09T21:20:56Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-23T08:32:31Z\",\n              \"permissions\": {\n                \"administration\": \"read\",\n                \"checks\": \"write\",\n                \"contents\": \"write\",\n                \"emails\": \"read\",\n                \"members\": \"read\",\n                \"metadata\": \"read\",\n                \"pull_requests\": \"write\",\n                \"statuses\": \"read\",\n                \"workflows\": \"write\"\n              },\n              \"events\": [\n                \"check_suite\",\n                \"create\",\n                \"delete\",\n                \"fork\",\n                \"member\",\n                \"membership\",\n                \"organization\",\n                \"pull_request\",\n                \"push\",\n                \"repository\",\n                \"star\",\n                \"team\"\n              ]\n            },\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          }\n        ],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      },\n      \"issues\": {\n        \"total_count\": 0,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b30\",\n      \"query\": \"repo:entireio/forgemark SSE deadline\",\n      \"prs\": {\n        \"total_count\": 0,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      },\n      \"issues\": {\n        \"total_count\": 0,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b31\",\n      \"query\": \"repo:entireio/forgemark runs memory\",\n      \"prs\": {\n        \"total_count\": 1,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/forgemark/issues/22\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/forgemark\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/forgemark/issues/22/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/forgemark/issues/22/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/forgemark/issues/22/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/22\",\n            \"id\": 5944389131,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOTKIlTs8AAAABJlRkvA\",\n            \"number\": 22,\n            \"title\": \"Housekeeping for the HTTP client and the serve history view\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"pjbgf\",\n              \"id\": 5452977,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NTI5Nzc=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5452977?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pjbgf\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 2,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-20T15:21:59Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-20T15:40:11Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-20T15:40:08Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/forgemark/pulls/22\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/22\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/22.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/22.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-20T15:40:08Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/forgemark/trails/11\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\nRedirects\\r\\n- All forge requests (pushes, clones, the ref sweep and the push-options\\r\\n  probe) now share one redirect policy instead of per-call handling. Like\\r\\n  git's default for the initial info/refs request, a redirect within the\\r\\n  configured origin (same scheme, host and port) is followed. One that\\r\\n  leaves it stops the run with a clear error.\\r\\n- -push-options now works with forges that redirect within their own\\r\\n  origin, such as GitLab's repo to repo.git.\\r\\n\\r\\nHistory\\r\\n- The history listing decodes only what a summary needs (run fields,\\r\\n  target names and levels) and skips the per-second series, so listing\\r\\n  stays about one read per file as runs get longer. Legacy docs are\\r\\n  summarized exactly as before.\\r\\n- Docs whose levels can't be loaded are skipped from the listing, as\\r\\n  before, so everything listed can be opened. A doc damaged only in its\\r\\n  series still lists, and opening it reports the error.\\r\\n- At most two history reads run at once, which keeps server memory\\r\\n  predictable.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes credential-bearing HTTP redirect handling and history API behavior; mistakes could leak auth or change which runs appear in history, but behavior is covered by new tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Unifies forge HTTP behavior around a **same-origin redirect policy** on the shared client: redirects that keep scheme, hostname, and port are followed (matching git for cases like GitLab `repo` → `repo.git`); anything that would leave the configured origin is refused so Basic auth is not forwarded to another host, port, or subdomain. The push-options probe drops its ad-hoc “no redirect” check and uses that client, so `-push-options` works on same-origin redirects while startup and ref cleanup still fail closed on cross-origin redirects.\\n> \\n> **History listing and server reads** are tightened for large result files: `List` decodes only summary fields via `readSummary` (skipping per-second `Series`), with the same legacy normalization and exclusion of docs whose `levels` would fail `Load`. History routes are wrapped with a **two-slot concurrency limit** so exposed binds cannot spike memory on parallel full-doc reads.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 953134003cb5ccea59987c6d8a0aef84964737e4. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/forgemark/issues/22/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/forgemark/issues/22/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          }\n        ],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      },\n      \"issues\": {\n        \"total_count\": 0,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b32\",\n      \"query\": \"repo:entireio/cli attachment read limit\",\n      \"prs\": {\n        \"total_count\": 8,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3002\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3002/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3002/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3002/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3002\",\n            \"id\": 6187458536,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABMnNZQA\",\n            \"number\": 3002,\n            \"title\": \"Add trail attachment add, list, and remove\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"entire[bot]\",\n              \"id\": 254015822,\n              \"node_id\": \"BOT_kgDODyP5Tg\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/2626939?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/entire\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"Bot\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-11-03T17:07:47Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-05T19:08:30Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-11-05T19:08:27Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3002\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3002\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3002.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3002.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-11-05T19:08:27Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2688/changes/cli/1737\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nPart of trail #2688 (closing CLI trail command gaps), change cli/1737.\\n\\n## What\\n\\n`entire trail attachment` manages the images a project trail's description shows, through `/{host}/{project}/trails/{trail}/attachments`:\\n\\n- `entire trail attachment add <file>` uploads an image and prints the line that shows it in the description: `![image](attachment:<id>)`. It registers the upload with an `Idempotency-Key`, PUTs the bytes to the presigned URL, and completes it. If anything after registering fails (the server's size limit, a refused PUT, a failed completion), it deletes the attachment it registered, so a failed upload leaves nothing behind. `--json` prints the attachment and the line.\\n- `entire trail attachment list` lists the trail's attachments, including uploads that never completed, with the reference for each ready image.\\n- `entire trail attachment remove <id> --force` deletes one.\\n\\nThe trail is selected like `trail comment`: `--trail <number|ULID|repo/number>`, `--branch`, or the current branch's parent, with `--project`.\\n\\n## Why it works now\\n\\nentire-api change entire-api/734 (et/entirehq trail 1492) gave attachment images a Markdown form: a line holding only `![alt](attachment:<ULID>)` becomes an image when a project trail body is written as Markdown, and a body read back renders each image as `![image](attachment:<ULID>)`. Before it, `trail update --body` replaced any image added in the web editor with the text `[image]`. The CLI prints the reference in exactly the form the server renders back, so a description read with `trail show --json`, edited, and written back keeps its images.\\n\\n## Decisions to review\\n\\n- **Type from the bytes.** `add` detects the type from the file's contents and accepts only PNG, JPEG, GIF, and WebP up to 10 MiB, before any request. The cell trusts the declared type, and only those four render inline; any other reference stays literal text. Width and height are sent for PNG, JPEG, and GIF (the standard library has no WebP decoder; they are optional).\\n- **The presigned PUT never gets the caller's token.** It uses its own client from `httpclient.New` (so it keeps the shared HTTPS-downgrade redirect policy), sends the declared `Content-Type`, and refuses a non-HTTPS URL except on loopback (tests).\\n- **`remove` requires `--force`**, like deleting a project trail comment message, since it cannot be undone and the image disappears from any description that references it.\\n- **Classification:** `trail attachment` is `task-driven`, unlisted, like `trail update`, whose description it feeds. Agent guidance says to keep existing `attachment:` lines when writing a body back, and never to run `remove` or pass `--force` unless the user asks for that attachment to be deleted.\\n- **Not included:** inserting the reference into the description automatically, and downloading an attachment. Both are easy to add if wanted.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- Tests cover the full upload (intent body with type and dimensions, Idempotency-Key, the exact bytes and Content-Type at the storage URL with no Authorization header, completion), `--json`, files refused before any request (SVG named `.png`, empty, over 10 MiB, a directory, missing), a plaintext upload URL, `list` with and without a reference, `remove` requiring `--force` and an attachment ID, a refused PUT removing the registered attachment, and the URL's expiry left to storage (a local clock running ahead must not refuse a valid URL). `list`, `add`, and `remove` are classified separately: `list` read-only, the others task-driven.\\n- Live, read-only, against production: `trail attachment list --trail 2688 --project gh/entireio` reaches the route and returns the empty list. I did not upload to a real trail.\\n- `mise run fmt`, `mise run lint`, the complexity gate, and `GOOS=windows go vet` are clean; `go test ./internal/... ./cmd/entire/cli/ ./docs/...` passes.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3002/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3002/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3056\",\n            \"id\": 6255425292,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABNdzkwQ\",\n            \"number\": 3056,\n            \"title\": \"fix(strategy): spell agent-reported paths as git does on case-insensitive filesystems\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n              \"id\": 26940511,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI2OTQwNTEx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Beehtrix\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 5,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-11-07T05:06:26Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-11T18:20:27Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": null,\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3056\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3056\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3056.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3056.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"Fixes #3054\\n\\nOn a case-insensitive filesystem (the macOS and Windows default) an agent can name a tracked file in another case than git does: writing `readme.md` changes `README.md`. Entire recorded the agent's spelling, which never matches a commit, so the session stayed pending after the file was committed. The issue has the two ways it happens (dirty at turn end, committed mid-turn).\\n\\nI reviewed this on my fork first (Beehtrix/cli#22).\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\n`strategy.FilterTrackableChanges`, which every capture route already applies (turn end, task completion, per-tool hooks, Codex child files, and the transcript fallback of a mid-turn commit), now first spells each path as git's index does (`strategy.TrackedSpellings`, in `strategy/path_case.go`):\\n\\n- It only acts where a directory on a reported path, from the one holding the file up to the worktree root, finds its entries under another case, which `worktreedir.CaseProbe` asks the filesystem in process: one of the directory's entries, looked up with its letters' case swapped, opens the same file, and the directory doesn't also list that spelling as an entry of its own (a hard-linked pair, which only a directory that respects case can hold). A directory that is gone, has no entry with a letter in its name, or has over 4096 entries can't tell, and then nothing is rewritten; it doesn't borrow its parent's answer, since Windows lets a directory respect case inside one that ignores it. It doesn't go by git's `core.ignorecase`, one setting for the whole repository, which a linked worktree on another filesystem, a moved repository or a Windows directory with its own case sensitivity can disagree with. Every directory on the path counts, not only the one holding the file: on Windows `SRC/App.go` in a root that ignores case opens `src/App.go` even when `src/` respects case. On a case-sensitive filesystem nothing changes and git isn't asked, since `readme.md` and `README.md` are two files there.\\n- It asks git once per call for the index's spellings (`gitrepo.IndexPathsIgnoringCase`: `git ls-files -z --cached` with `:(literal,icase)` pathspecs, chunked and bounded by `PathClassificationBudget` like the other classifiers).\\n- A spelling is rewritten only when each directory where it differs from the index's spelling ignores case, and it opens the same file (`os.SameFile` on rooted lstats): in a directory that respects case, two hard-linked names are two entries git tracks apart. A deletion has nothing left to open, so it's rewritten when the index has exactly one spelling of it and that one is gone too. Duplicates the rewrite leaves are dropped, keeping the first one's place.\\n- If git can't answer, the paths are kept as reported, as before.\\n\\n`worktreedir/case.go` is the same file as in my shared-checkout PR for #3011, which needs the same check for deletions; whichever lands second loses it from its diff.\\n\\nTurn end now runs `FilterTrackableChanges` before `filterToUncommittedFiles`, so a file committed mid-turn is checked against HEAD under git's spelling. Both only drop paths, so the order doesn't change what either drops. Task completion respells the subagent's transcript paths before `filterToUncommittedFiles` and the committed-file check that attaches the task to a commit. The transcript route a commit hook takes before the session's first turn end (`filterTrackableFiles`) spells its paths first and keeps them in git's spelling.\\n\\n## Trade-offs\\n\\n- On macOS and Windows, each `FilterTrackableChanges` call runs one more `git ls-files`. A path git tracks under its own spelling still costs that call, since only git knows which paths it tracks. On Linux the cost is one read of each directory on the reported paths (each asked once per call), plus two `lstat`s per directory.\\n- A file that isn't tracked keeps the agent's spelling. git status lists such a file under its on-disk spelling, which the agent's tool normally created, so the two agree.\\n- `liveTaskTranscriptFiles` (co-authorship evidence for a running subagent) still compares the transcript's spelling with the commit's. It only decides whether a session counts as a co-author of a commit, and I left it out to keep this to what enters `FilesTouched`.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- `gitrepo.TestIndexPathsIgnoringCase`: index spellings for other-case names, literal brackets, an untracked name, and inherited `GIT_LITERAL_PATHSPECS` / `GIT_GLOB_PATHSPECS`.\\n- `worktreedir.TestCaseProbe_*`: the directory probe, with a lookup that folds case standing in for a directory that ignores case (a directory that respects case, a hard-linked pair of entries that must read as a directory that respects case, a directory that ignores case, one with no entry that tells, one that is gone, one over the entry bound, and paths that differ in several directories). `TestCaseProbeWindows` checks it against the filesystem itself on CI's Windows job.\\n- `strategy.TestTrackedSpelling`: the rule itself, with a hard link standing in for one file under two names and a stand-in probe for a directory that ignores case (same file where the directory ignores case, a hard link where it respects case, another file, no file, a deletion in a directory that respects case and in one that ignores it, two index spellings, git's spelling still present). `strategy.TestAnyDirectoryIgnoresCase`: every directory on a path counts toward asking git, not only the one holding the file.\\n- `strategy.TestFilterTrackableFiles_KeepsGitsSpellingWindows`: the transcript route keeps `README.md` for a transcript's `readme.md`; on a case-insensitive filesystem it fails without that part of the fix.\\n- `strategy.TestTrackedSpellings_CaseInsensitiveFilesystemWindows` and `TestFilterTrackableFiles_KeepsGitsSpellingWindows` are named so that CI's Windows job runs them on a real case-insensitive filesystem; on Linux they check that nothing changes.\\n- `integration_test/transcript_path_case_test.go`: the issue's two cases end to end. They run only where the filesystem ignores case, so CI's Linux job skips them.\\n\\nOn Linux with git 2.43, `go test ./...` and `go test -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/...` pass apart from 13 tests that fail the same way on a clean checkout of main in that environment (no `--ref-format`, SSH, DNS or user XDG cache, and running as root). golangci-lint v2.15.0 reports 0 issues, the complexity gate passes, and the changed packages and the integration package vet for Windows. I also ran the changed packages' tests and the two integration tests on a case-insensitive filesystem in the same container (ciopfs, a FUSE filesystem, mounted with `use_ino` so both spellings report one inode): the case tests pass there, and both integration tests fail on main there (`FilesTouched = [README.md readme.md]`, and `[readme.md]` still pending after the mid-turn commit). Four other `strategy` tests fail on that mount on main too, from the FUSE filesystem (a removed and re-added working directory, and a temp-dir cleanup).\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 1,\n              \"+1\": 1,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2919\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2919/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2919/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2919/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2919\",\n            \"id\": 6055335424,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABK9lnzg\",\n            \"number\": 2919,\n            \"title\": \"fix(subagent): store a foreground subagent's task when it commits its own work\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n              \"id\": 34813274,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-27T08:09:30Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-27T14:51:32Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-27T14:51:30Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2919\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2919\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2919.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2919.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-27T14:51:30Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2629/changes/cli/1702\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nWhen a Claude Code foreground subagent commits its own work, the checkpoint linked to that commit has no `tasks/` entry, and the subagent's transcript is never stored (#2903).\\n\\nA foreground subagent's task record is created only at post-task, when it finishes. Its own commit happens earlier, so that commit's condensation has no record to store. Post-task then drops the already-committed files (`filterToUncommittedFiles`), finds nothing left, and logs \\\"no file changes detected, skipping task record\\\". No later step adds it, because the turn-end rewrite of mid-turn checkpoints carries no tasks.\\n\\nThe skip was added in 1ceb9c357e to stop an orphaned shadow branch. Shadow branches have since been removed, but the skip remained.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n- **Pre-task** records the turn's checkpoint IDs (`PreTaskState.TurnCheckpointIDs`; nil means unknown).\\n- **Post-task**: when files the subagent's transcript names are now in HEAD, it takes the checkpoints condensed during the run (the entries `TurnCheckpointIDs` gained past the snapshot, by position, so an amend's repeated ID counts) and writes the completed record into the newest one whose `files_touched` include one of those files (`strategy.AttachTaskToCheckpoint`). Files the subagent left uncommitted still complete a normal record for the commit that later carries them; when it committed everything, nothing is left pending. Otherwise behavior is unchanged.\\n- **Write failures** are kept in `PendingTaskAttachments` and retried into the same checkpoint at each turn end, up to three times. Post-task fires once per Task call, so it cannot retry itself. Pending attachments are not pending work, so they never condense into another commit's checkpoint, and adopt clears them with the other checkpoint references.\\n- **Store:** a new `Tasks` write request adds task records to an existing checkpoint without touching its sessions and never creates one. It is implemented for the branch, refs and fs backends and routed like the other backfills.\\n- Task payload building moves out of `materializeTaskRecords` unchanged, so condensation and post-task share it.\\n\\n## Limits\\n\\n- A subagent that creates files only through shell commands (no Write or Edit in its transcript) is not attached, and falls back to today's skip.\\n- A read-only subagent running alongside the one that committed is not attached. This is intentional and tested.\\n- A subagent that commits only part of its work has its task stored twice: in its own commit's checkpoint and in the checkpoint of the commit that later carries the rest. A running background task is already stored at every condensation the same way.\\n- If the store or a candidate checkpoint cannot be read when choosing, the record goes to the newest candidate rather than being dropped, and a warning is logged.\\n- A write that still fails after three turn ends is dropped with a warning.\\n- This path stores images inline in the task transcript instead of externalizing them, since turn-end replaces the session's stored assets. Externalization is opt-in and off by default.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- Integration: the existing mid-run commit test now also checks that the subagent commit's checkpoint stores the task transcript and that it survives Stop. New tests cover:\\n  - an earlier parent checkpoint in the turn and a parallel read-only subagent, which are not attached;\\n  - two overlapping subagents that each commit, each stored in its own checkpoint;\\n  - a subagent amending the parent's commit;\\n  - a subagent committing only part of its work, stored in both commits' checkpoints;\\n  - a failed write retried at turn end, and given up on after three failed turn ends.\\n- Store: the `Tasks` write lands in each backend, a missing checkpoint returns not-found, and routing falls back to the branch store for a hex ID under a refs primary.\\n- Mutation checks: removing the routing case, the files guard, the files-based choice, or the position-based selection, lifting the retry cap, or attaching only when everything is committed each fails the matching test.\\n- Real binary: a repro script drives `entire enable`, real git hooks and Claude Code hook payloads. Before the fix the subagent's commit checkpoint had no `tasks/`; after it, it has the full transcript and `task.json`.\\n- `mise run check` passes: lint clean, all test packages OK.\\n- Not run: a live `claude -p` repro (paid API calls).\\n\\nFixes #2903\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2919/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2919/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": {\n              \"id\": 2626939,\n              \"client_id\": \"Iv23lieFG10uOnChW4TN\",\n              \"slug\": \"entire\",\n              \"node_id\": \"A_kwHOAfprLM4AKBV7\",\n              \"owner\": {\n                \"login\": \"entireio\",\n                \"id\": 33188652,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjMzMTg4NjUy\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33188652?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"Organization\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"name\": \"Entire\",\n              \"description\": \"\",\n              \"external_url\": \"https://entire.com\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/entire\",\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-01-09T21:20:56Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-23T08:32:31Z\",\n              \"permissions\": {\n                \"administration\": \"read\",\n                \"checks\": \"write\",\n                \"contents\": \"write\",\n                \"emails\": \"read\",\n                \"members\": \"read\",\n                \"metadata\": \"read\",\n                \"pull_requests\": \"write\",\n                \"statuses\": \"read\",\n                \"workflows\": \"write\"\n              },\n              \"events\": [\n                \"check_suite\",\n                \"create\",\n                \"delete\",\n                \"fork\",\n                \"member\",\n                \"membership\",\n                \"organization\",\n                \"pull_request\",\n                \"push\",\n                \"repository\",\n                \"star\",\n                \"team\"\n              ]\n            },\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2859\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2859/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2859/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2859/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2859\",\n            \"id\": 5972806310,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABJ8CBvw\",\n            \"number\": 2859,\n            \"title\": \"feat(transcript): emit one Codex assistant line per model call with per-call usage\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"khaong\",\n              \"id\": 351934,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTkzNA==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/351934?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/khaong\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 3,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-22T04:01:16Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-25T20:38:12Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-25T20:38:09Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2859\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2859\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2859.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2859.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-25T20:38:09Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2357/changes/cli/1652\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nSlice 2b of ENT-3337: the Codex converter now writes one assistant line per model call, with pricing-grade per-call usage.\\n\\n**Stacked.** Base is `alex/ent-3337-transcript-converters` (slice 2a, Claude converter, PR #2858), which is itself stacked on slice 1 (`alex/ent-3337-transcript-format-fields`). Merge order: slice 1, then 2a, then this PR (rebase its base to `main` once 2a merges).\\n\\n## What\\n- One assistant line per model call. Usage is the difference of consecutive cumulative `info.total_token_usage` snapshots, so every `token_count` delta lands on exactly one line (no double counting across reasoning, function_call and message items; no merging of two calls). Repeated snapshots (rate-limit refreshes) are ignored.\\n- `model` from `turn_context` on every line carrying usage (`\\\"unknown\\\"` if none seen); fresh `input_tokens` (input minus cached), `cache_read_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `reasoning_tokens` (subset of output; needs adjacent reported snapshots).\\n- Tool outputs attach to their call by `call_id` and matching output type, including after the call closed (real order is call, output, `token_count`). With usable snapshots an output does not end its call, so interleaved parallel calls and outputs stay one line; snapshots missing a counter are ignored.\\n- A counter decrease stops usage on later lines (reviewed contract: no guessed reset baseline); closing snapshots still set the call's timestamp. `StartLine` replays the skipped prefix so the first delta is not the session aggregate, and the slice includes the call still open at the boundary when the slice completes it.\\n- Real timestamps: the closing snapshot's, else the call's last item's.\\n- `testdata/codex_full.jsonl` moved from an invented flat `token_count` shape to the real nested shape; golden regenerated and reviewed line by line.\\n\\n## Check\\n`mise run check` is green. `go test ./transcript/ -run Codex -count=1`: `TestCodexOneLinePerCall_SumsEqualNativeDeltas` sums per-line usage and compares it to the native deltas.\\n\\n## Notes\\n- Flat per-event `token_count` totals are no longer read (real Codex never writes them).\\n- `cache_write_input_tokens` exists in real Codex `total_token_usage` (0 in every sample seen) and is deliberately not read; open question for Alex whether Codex `input_tokens` could ever include cache writes.\\n- Lines with usage can differ in count from the checkpoint's `APICallCount` (repeated snapshots are not calls here).\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)\\n\\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01VnNMsCn1XfR6wwPTAKFmwL\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes Codex compaction semantics and pricing-grade token accounting; checkpoint slicing can repeat one line’s usage at boundaries, so downstream consumers of compact transcripts need to align with the new contract.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> The Codex converter now emits **one assistant line per model call** instead of grouping assistant text with adjacent tools in a simpler scan. Calls close on cumulative `token_count` snapshots (`info.total_token_usage`); usage on each line is the **delta** between consecutive snapshots (fresh `input_tokens`, `cache_read_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `reasoning_tokens`), with `model` from `turn_context`. Flat per-event token totals are no longer read.\\n> \\n> Tool results are matched by `call_id` and output type and can land **after** the closing snapshot. Interleaved parallel tool calls stay on one line when snapshots are present; without them, tool output still ends a call. Repeated or incomplete snapshots are ignored; counter decreases halt usage attribution on later lines while still closing calls. Reasoning-only calls may emit `content: []`.\\n> \\n> **`StartLine`** replays the skipped native prefix to seed the cumulative usage baseline and can include a one-line overlap when a call straddles the checkpoint boundary. Docs and golden fixtures move to the real nested `token_count` shape.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 109f29b5c8d1dc2c819cc3834f12dea4fb82b245. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2859/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2859/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2636\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2636/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2636/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2636/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2636\",\n            \"id\": 5664184725,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABGHYsHg\",\n            \"number\": 2636,\n            \"title\": \"Support multiple agent homes across session workflows\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"hiddeco\",\n              \"id\": 10063039,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDYzMDM5\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10063039?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hiddeco\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/hiddeco\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hiddeco/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hiddeco/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hiddeco/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hiddeco/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hiddeco/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hiddeco/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hiddeco/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hiddeco/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hiddeco/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-01T14:52:38Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-09T09:05:08Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-09T09:05:04Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2636\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2636\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2636.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2636.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1462\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nAn agent can use a custom storage path, and a user can run several instances with different paths—for example, separate `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` or `CODEX_HOME` values. Entire currently resolves storage from the invoking process’s environment. When that environment differs from the source session’s, `session adopt` can reject a valid transcript and `attach` can fail to find it.\\n\\nRecord the agent home alongside each session and remember independently resolved homes in a bounded per-user registry. Adoption validates the recorded home against locally trusted roots; `attach` searches previously used homes after the active store misses. This lets users continue sessions across repositories and find transcripts from another agent instance without recreating its environment.\\n\\nCarry that root through capture, checkpoint finalization, review, token accounting, and subagent reads. Shared rooted readers enforce containment when opening files, including after adoption, so stored paths and later symlink changes cannot redirect reads outside the authorized home. Preserve compatibility with older sessions and explicit session-directory overrides.\\n\\nAlternatives considered:\\n\\n- Require users to export the original storage variables for every command. This leaves ordinary shell workflows dependent on the source agent’s environment.\\n- Trust the transcript path or home recorded in session metadata. Repository-controlled metadata cannot authorize filesystem access.\\n- Implement confinement separately in each agent. A shared contract keeps the same protections across agents and transcript consumers.\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2636/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2636/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2672\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2672/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2672/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2672/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2672\",\n            \"id\": 5722082736,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABG1OQGw\",\n            \"number\": 2672,\n            \"title\": \"Confirm before session attach links, and link any commit by whether it's pushed\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-06T02:44:17Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-09T08:00:52Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-09T08:00:50Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2672\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2672\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2672.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2672.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-09T08:00:50Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1494\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n`entire session attach` could only link HEAD, by amending it with an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer:\\n- it prompted at a terminal, or amended with `-f`;\\n- without a terminal it printed the trailer and left the checkpoint linked to nothing;\\n- a commit that was already pushed could only be linked by rewriting it;\\n- a session that already had a checkpoint couldn't be attached to another commit.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\n`entire session attach <id> [--commit <rev>]` (default HEAD) decides how to link from two facts about the commit, the same for HEAD and `--commit`: does it already have a checkpoint, and is it pushed. In other words: would this rewrite history?\\n\\n| Commit | What attach does | Rewrites history? |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| already has a checkpoint | adds the session to it; pushes the checkpoint now if the commit is pushed, else with the next `git push` | no |\\n| no checkpoint, pushed | records the link in a new checkpoint (`linked_commits: [{sha, repo}]`), pushes it now and confirms the remote has it | no |\\n| no checkpoint, unpushed | adds the trailer, rewriting the commit and any commits after it on the current branch (content unchanged) | yes |\\n\\n**Confirmation.** Before writing anything, attach prints what it will do: which commits it rewrites, or which remote holds the commit and that the transcript is pushed now, plus author and rebase caveats. At a terminal it asks. Without one (agents, scripts) it changes nothing and exits non-zero. The agent-help entry tells agents to show the user that output and pass `--force` only once they agree.\\n\\n- **Rewriting.** The replay uses `git commit-tree` with the same trees, authors and messages. It moves the branch with a compare-and-swap `update-ref` (the reflog names the attach) and remaps session state through `PostRewrite`. No commit hooks run and the worktree is untouched. It refuses merges after the target, a target that isn't on the current branch, commits with a non-UTF-8 encoding or extra headers (which `commit-tree` can't reproduce), and running mid-rebase, merge, cherry-pick, revert or bisect.\\n- **\\\"Pushed\\\" means** any remote-tracking ref contains the commit (so `upstream` in a fork counts), or a branch on the branch's upstream or push remote does, else on `origin`; attach asks those remotes directly, in one ancestry walk. If one can't be reached, attach refuses rather than risk rewriting a shared commit. The checkpoint goes to the branch's own remote, never to an unrelated one.\\n- **One session, several commits.** The \\\"session already has a checkpoint\\\" special case is gone. Each checkpoint records the turns since the session's previous one: prompts, turn count and tokens are scoped from `CheckpointTranscriptStart`. An ended session's offset then advances; a running session's offset is left to its hooks. Re-attaching a session to the checkpoint that already holds it changes nothing.\\n- **Author warning.** A recorded link counts only when the commit's author attaches it; the server credits it only when the checkpoint pusher authored the commit.\\n- **Second attach to a linked commit** joins that checkpoint, including one that exists only on the remote (both backends), instead of starting a duplicate.\\n- **Rebases.** A recorded link names one exact commit and doesn't follow a rebase the way a trailer does. Attach says so.\\n- **Readers.** `explain <commit>` and `blame`/`why` fall back to recorded links when a commit has no trailer.\\n- **Docs.** `attach --help`, the `agent-help` entry, and `sessions-and-checkpoints.md`.\\n\\nThe server half is entire-api trail [#197](https://entire.io/et/entirehq/entire-api/trails/197). This change needs nothing new from it.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- **Confirmation:** without a terminal or `--force`, nothing is written for an unpushed commit or a pushed one.\\n- **Rewrite:** an unpushed HEAD and an older unpushed commit get the trailer, with descendants replayed and trees unchanged. A merge in the range is refused.\\n- **Pushed commits:** pushed HEAD and pushed older commit are linked in the checkpoint, and nothing is rewritten. A pushed HEAD with a checkpoint is joined, not rewritten.\\n- **Sessions:** a session can be attached to a second commit, recording only its new turn. Re-attaching to the same checkpoint is a no-op.\\n- **Remotes:** refuses when a fetch fails; ignores an unrelated, unreachable remote; sees commits pushed to untracked branches; never rewrites a commit another remote's tracking ref holds, and pushes its checkpoint to the branch's remote; errors when the checkpoint isn't delivered; delivery is confirmed on the git-refs backend too.\\n- **Rewrite limits:** a commit with a non-UTF-8 encoding is refused.\\n- **Push timing:** joining a pushed commit's checkpoint pushes it now; joining an unpushed one waits for `git push`.\\n- **Linked checkpoints:** a remote-only linked checkpoint is joined, including with the refs backend.\\n- **Readers and blame:** the `explain`/`blame` fallbacks; blame reads each remote checkpoint once per run.\\n- `mise run check` passes. I also hand-ran the no-terminal and `--force` flows in a scratch repo.\\n\\n## Not in v1\\n\\n- Linking multiple commits or a range.\\n- Detach or undo.\\n- Remapping recorded links after a rebase or amend.\\n- Sessions that never produce a commit.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2672/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2672/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2052\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2052/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2052/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2052/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2052\",\n            \"id\": 5191709451,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABARJzxQ\",\n            \"number\": 2052,\n            \"title\": \"fix(codex): use repository hook root in linked worktrees\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n              \"id\": 34813274,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 16,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T10:39:06Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-26T20:53:12Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-26T20:53:12Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2052\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2052\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2052.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2052.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-26T20:53:11Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"Fixes #2020.\\n\\nCodex 0.149.0 can load project hooks from a different checkout than the one in which it is running. In a conventional linked worktree, its app-server `hooks/list` response reports the primary checkout's `.codex/hooks.json`; a divergent file present only in the linked worktree is not loaded.\\n\\nThis PR makes that effective location visible without giving Entire ownership of another checkout. Discovery and mutation are deliberately separate: Entire may inspect the file Codex actually loads, but installs, removes, and cleans hooks only in the exact checkout where the command was invoked.\\n\\n## Discovery and ownership\\n\\n- `WorktreeHooksPath` identifies `<current-checkout>/.codex/hooks.json`. It is the only mutation target used by install, uninstall, presence, freshness, deselection, and clean flows.\\n- `DiscoveredHooksPath` identifies the project hooks file Codex is expected to load. It is used only for read-only configuration and trust diagnostics.\\n- `ResolveHookDiscovery` consumes the shared `gitrepo.ResolveGitLayout` classification rather than maintaining a Codex-specific `.git`, `commondir`, or worktree-marker parser.\\n- Conventional linked worktrees discover the primary checkout's hook file. Normal checkouts, ordinary submodules, and separate-Git-directory checkouts discover their own hook file.\\n- `.bare/worktrees`, linked submodules, contradictory metadata, and other behavior not pinned against Codex are reported as unresolved. Entire does not claim an unsupported layout or guess a writable fallback.\\n\\n`HookDiscovery` carries no write target, migration path, cleanup path, or lock path. Its `RepositoryWide` bit describes the reach of the configuration Codex discovers; it does not authorize repository-wide mutation.\\n\\n## Checkout-local mutation\\n\\n`entire enable`, `entire agent remove codex`, agent deselection, and `entire clean` mutate only the current checkout's `.codex/hooks.json`. They do not create another checkout's `.codex` directory, migrate a worktree-local file into the primary checkout, remove a discovered file owned elsewhere, or perform repository-wide cleanup.\\n\\nConcurrent updates are serialized only with `<current-checkout>/.codex/hooks.json.lock`. There is no `entire-codex-hooks.lock` in the Git common directory and no synchronization across worktrees. An old common-directory lock, if present from a previous build, is neither used nor cleaned from another checkout.\\n\\nCurrent-checkout writes are hardened before the final atomic replacement:\\n\\n- the logical target must be exactly `<current-checkout>/.codex/hooks.json`;\\n- redirected `.codex` directories, final-file symlinks, non-regular files, unrelated destinations, and Git-metadata redirection are rejected;\\n- existing user hooks, unknown hook events, and unrelated top-level fields are preserved;\\n- uninstall removes only Entire-managed entries;\\n- an existing file keeps its permission bits, while a new file uses `0600`.\\n\\n## Bounded read-only inspection\\n\\nThe local and discovered files are inspected independently as absent, user-only, Entire-managed, invalid, or unresolved. Inspection is contained to the exact canonical `.codex` directory, requires a stable regular file, caps `hooks.json` at 1 MiB, reads through a limit with one overflow byte, and checks file identity before and after the read. It never creates a directory, rewrites configuration, removes entries, or acquires a mutation lock.\\n\\nThe structured inspection also reports whether the core Entire events are present, which current events are missing, whether managed commands and timeouts match this CLI, whether the current checkout has the project layer Codex requires, whether local trust records were readable, and which declared hooks lack an approval record. Entire does not compute, copy, or synthesize Codex trust hashes.\\n\\n## Diagnostics and remedy\\n\\n- `entire doctor` reports the current-worktree path and Codex-discovered path, invalid or unresolved discovery, a missing project layer, managed hook drift, and trust gaps.\\n- `entire status` keeps current-checkout installation/freshness semantics separate from effective Codex discovery and exposes the mismatch under the existing `codex_hooks` JSON object without changing the warning wording established in this PR.\\n- SessionStart appends a short, bounded, read-only discovery or trust warning when applicable.\\n\\nWhen hooks exist only in a linked worktree, Entire does not repair the primary checkout automatically. The user-owned remedy is to commit `.codex/hooks.json` and apply that commit to the primary checkout (typically by cherry-pick), or run `entire enable` from the primary checkout. Because linked worktrees share Git objects, the commit is immediately available to cherry-pick; no push or fetch is required.\\n\\n## Pinned Codex integration contract\\n\\n`TestCodexAppServerHooksList_LinkedWorktreeUsesPrimaryCheckout` is a no-model integration test pinned to `@openai/codex@0.149.0`. It:\\n\\n1. creates a normal repository and conventional linked worktree with distinct hook markers;\\n2. starts `codex app-server` in the linked worktree with an isolated `CODEX_HOME`;\\n3. sends `initialize`, `initialized`, and `hooks/list` JSONL messages over stdio;\\n4. requires the primary marker and primary `sourcePath`;\\n5. rejects the linked-only marker; and\\n6. requires empty `warnings` and `errors`.\\n\\nThe test makes no model request and needs no OpenAI credentials. Local integration runs skip when the exact Codex binary is unavailable. CI installs version 0.149.0 and sets `ENTIRE_TEST_REQUIRE_CODEX_APP_SERVER=1`, so a missing binary or version drift fails rather than silently skipping.\\n\\n## Verification status\\n\\nThe implementation includes focused unit coverage for Git-layout classification, path-role separation, current-checkout-only install/remove/clean behavior, exact-worktree locking, destination containment, symlink refusal, bounded reads, mode preservation, doctor/status/SessionStart diagnostics, trust inspection, and JSON output, plus the pinned app-server integration contract above.\\n\\nFull formatting, lint, unit, integration, canary, duplication, and `mise run check` verification is intentionally deferred to implementation-order item 9.\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2052/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2052/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1577\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1577/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1577/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1577/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1577\",\n            \"id\": 4776277620,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7sMkfn\",\n            \"number\": 1577,\n            \"title\": \"Tackle failing E2E tests, part 1\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"toothbrush\",\n              \"id\": 423357,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMzM1Nw==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/423357?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/toothbrush\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 4,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-06-30T11:22:38Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-30T12:50:45Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-06-30T12:50:43Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1577\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1577\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1577.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1577.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-06-30T12:50:43Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/704\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\nOur E2E tests on main are basically always red.\\r\\n\\r\\nBroadly:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Always green: claude-code, opencode, gemini-cli, roger-roger, e2e-windows\\r\\n- Always red: cursor-cli, copilot-cli, codex, factoryai-droid\\r\\n\\r\\nThis PR:\\r\\n\\r\\n1. downgrade to a red/yellow indicator: only show red if one of the \\\"always green\\\" ones fails.\\r\\n2. allow one auto-retry on failure\\r\\n3. throttle cursor-cli concurrency - it seems like we really often see \\\"Error: Increase limits for faster responses\\\", maybe this helps.\\r\\n4. fix codex `TestCodexResumeRestoredSessionWithSanitizedCompactedHistory`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Changes are limited to E2E workflows, test harness, and a test helper; no production runtime or auth paths are modified.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **CI reliability** for `main` E2E: Slack no longer treats every agent failure as a regression. Failures are split into **reliable** agents (`claude-code`, `opencode`, `gemini-cli`, `roger-roger`, Windows) → red alert, versus **known-flaky** agents → yellow “investigate” alert with colored attachments.\\n> \\n> The default `test:e2e` task now runs **`gotestsum --rerun-fails=1`** (one retry per failed test, capped so broad breakage isn’t masked). **roger-roger** is routed to **`test:e2e:roger-roger`** so deterministic failures are not retried.\\n> \\n> **Concurrency gates** are registered for **`cursor-cli`** (2) and **`factoryai-droid`** (1) so workflow `E2E_CONCURRENT_TEST_LIMIT` values actually apply via `AcquireSlot`. **`TestCodexResumeRestoredSessionWithSanitizedCompactedHistory`** reads Codex rollout **`session_meta`** via JSONL parsing instead of a field-order-sensitive regex (broken on Codex 0.142.x).\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 810086c27f6c0b09e0d841c15e6af155a2c01111. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1577/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1577/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          }\n        ],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      },\n      \"issues\": {\n        \"total_count\": 1,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2980\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2980/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2980/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2980/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2980\",\n            \"id\": 6110766677,\n            \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABbDrmVQ\",\n            \"number\": 2980,\n            \"title\": \"Post-push session attach publishes linked_commits but checkpoint remains absent from activity and Dispatch\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"lcv-leo\",\n              \"id\": 268063598,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD_pTbg\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/268063598?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/lcv-leo\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/lcv-leo/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 7,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-30T00:14:37Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-05T17:58:31Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-11-05T17:58:31Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n              \"total\": 0,\n              \"completed\": 0,\n              \"percent_completed\": 0\n            },\n            \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n              \"blocked_by\": 0,\n              \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n              \"blocking\": 0,\n              \"total_blocking\": 0\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Context and impact\\n\\nWe use Entire alongside GitHub for real changes to a private web application. We reached this problem while trying to generate the team's Dispatch after a squash merge, not while constructing a synthetic checkpoint test. This report was prepared with Codex assistance at the repository operator's request; the observations below come from the official CLI and API responses.\\n\\nThe original checkpoint is available remotely, but has no branch membership after the feature branch is deleted. We understand why a squash commit without an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer needs repair. The problem reported here is that the documented post-push `session attach` repair reports success and publishes `linked_commits`, yet the activity API still cannot find the new checkpoint or link it to that commit. As a result, a Dispatch for the recent release says there are no checkpoints. A wider-window Dispatch succeeds but omits the recent release.\\n\\n## Environment\\n\\n- Windows, PowerShell; GitHub private repository `LCV-Ideas-Software/astrologo-app`.\\n- Installed CLI: `0.12.2-lcv.windows-console.1+idle-fallback.2`, based on v0.12.2. These are the locally authorized Windows-console and stale sibling-session patches tracked in #2926 / #2972 and #2979. **I have not reproduced this with an unmodified binary**, and am not claiming otherwise. No further binary, Git identity, signing, or hook configuration change was made for this investigation.\\n- Git-ref checkpoint storage, mirror placements ready in BR and US. The repository view resolves the activity API to `aws-us-east-2.api.entire.io` and repo ID `01M5Z457WFR60E17SC5GNHDRH5`.\\n- The affected captured session is about 3.3 MB, not the multi-GB session from #2933. It was captured during actual work on PR #540.\\n\\n## What led us here\\n\\n1. PR #540's signed feature commit was `6405cf2a09b158721a63bcbcdac933067ee188a2`, checkpoint `01M64TPXT3N02BC8RX20YX4XQB`, session `01a1896c-8d01-77d2-afeb-82b5439fbfcc`.\\n2. The published squash commit is `0b227a331c1ea32b594c8916336ac8a42d9a3660`. Its message mentions the checkpoint in prose but does **not** contain an `Entire-Checkpoint:` trailer. The feature branch was deleted after publication.\\n3. `entire checkpoint explain 01M64TPXT3N02BC8RX20YX4XQB --repo gh/LCV-Ideas-Software/astrologo-app --json` succeeds. The activity checkpoint-resolution response reports `branches: []`, `default_branch: null`, and `suggested_branch: null` for that checkpoint.\\n4. The activity API's checkpoint-status response counts 12 checkpoints and reports access allowed. The main-branch list contains only one older checkpoint from PR #528 and reports `history_status: \\\"complete\\\"`. Thus this is not a missing login or an empty repository.\\n5. I queued the native mirror resync. It returned `status: \\\"queued\\\"`; the main list still contained only the older checkpoint.\\n6. I checked the official `session attach` help and preview. It explicitly said the published commit would remain unchanged and a new checkpoint would carry the exact commit link. There were no unrelated outgoing checkpoint refs. The configured Git email equals the target commit author's email.\\n7. I ran:\\n\\n   ```text\\n   entire session attach 01a1896c-8d01-77d2-afeb-82b5439fbfcc --agent codex --commit 0b227a331c1ea32b594c8916336ac8a42d9a3660 --force\\n   ```\\n\\n   The command warned that there were no new turns since the original checkpoint, then returned exit 0:\\n\\n   ```text\\n   Created checkpoint 01M6524YWT7N18SBAWPA444AK6\\n   Linked to commit 0b227a331c1e in the checkpoint; the commit is unchanged (already pushed)\\n   [entire] Pushing 1 checkpoint ref(s) to origin..... done\\n   Pushed checkpoint metadata to origin\\n   ```\\n\\n8. The new checkpoint's `metadata.json` contains:\\n\\n   ```json\\n   \\\"linked_commits\\\": [{\\n     \\\"sha\\\": \\\"0b227a331c1ea32b594c8916336ac8a42d9a3660\\\",\\n     \\\"repo\\\": \\\"gh/LCV-Ideas-Software/astrologo-app\\\"\\n   }]\\n   ```\\n\\n   It also has `files_touched: null` and an empty session prompt. I am not claiming it represents new work; this was a repair of the link to an already captured real session.\\n\\n9. `git ls-remote origin refs/entire/checkpoints/K6/01M6524YWT7N18SBAWPA444AK6` confirms the published ref at `d58987752d72ca61358bbf1103f101c5cb4e308d`. The main commit is unchanged. I queued a second resync **after this new ref was published**.\\n10. Following that resync, the main list still has only the old checkpoint. At 00:12:27 UTC on 30 October 2026 (21:12:27 in Brazil on 29 October), the API still returned HTTP 404 `{\\\"error\\\":\\\"checkpoint not found\\\"}` for the newly attached checkpoint. This observation is bounded to the few minutes after the repair; it is not a claim that ingestion can never complete. The commit-checkpoint endpoint also returned an empty list with complete history.\\n11. A Dispatch covering 25–29 October successfully completed with **one** checkpoint, from PR #528. This is a useful control: generation works for the existing indexed membership. It does not demonstrate coverage of PR #540 or validate the new attachment.\\n\\n## Expected behavior / requested guidance\\n\\nWhat is the supported way to attach an **already captured session with no new turns** to an already-pushed squash commit, without rewriting shared Git history or fabricating another code change?\\n\\nIf `session attach` is that repair, please check whether the empty incremental attachment or `linked_commits` ingestion is preventing the association from becoming visible. If asynchronous indexing needs a different official trigger, please document that trigger and an observable completion status. The CLI success message alone currently does not let us verify the repaired association.\\n\\nI read #321 (closed) and #1889 (regional Dispatch routing). This report concerns the present post-push attachment result and missing activity membership, rather than assuming a new instance of the older routing issue. Full private evidence is retained for the operator; this report intentionally excludes source code, transcripts, prompts, credentials, and personal data.\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2980/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2980/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n            \"pinned_comment\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          }\n        ],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b33\",\n      \"query\": \"repo:entireio/cli followFile cancel\",\n      \"prs\": {\n        \"total_count\": 0,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      },\n      \"issues\": {\n        \"total_count\": 0,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e13\",\n      \"query\": \"repo:entireio/cli sparse clone\",\n      \"prs\": {\n        \"total_count\": 2,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2241\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2241/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2241/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2241/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2241\",\n            \"id\": 5323086804,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABB4qmmA\",\n            \"number\": 2241,\n            \"title\": \"refactor(gitrepo): centralize metadata resolution (split part 1)\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n              \"id\": 34813274,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 5,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-09-02T11:06:38Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-03T20:21:55Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-03T20:21:55Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2241\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2241\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2241.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2241.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-03T20:21:55Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"Refs #2190.\\r\\n\\r\\nPR #2190 moved every Git metadata consumer at once. The review exposed two separate jobs: define one owner for the metadata, then migrate its callers.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is split part 1. It adds the resolver and changes only repository opening. Checkpoint, session, strategy, hooks, and other consumers stay unchanged here.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Files and ownership\\r\\n\\r\\nThree production files and four test files change. All paths below are relative to `cmd/entire/cli/gitrepo/`.\\r\\n\\r\\n| File | Before | After |\\r\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\r\\n| `metadata.go` | No file | Resolves the three metadata facts |\\r\\n| `repository.go` | Opening rediscovered paths | Resolves and passes metadata |\\r\\n| `reftable.go` | Errors looked like absence | Returns inspection errors |\\r\\n| `metadata_guard_test.go` | No guard | Blocks new duplicate traversal |\\r\\n| `metadata_test.go` | No resolver tests | Covers real and broken layouts |\\r\\n| `repository_test.go` | Tested the old path | Covers fallback and failures |\\r\\n| `reftable_test.go` | Tested boolean detection | Covers inspection errors |\\r\\n\\r\\nThe call path changes like this:\\r\\n\\r\\n```text\\r\\nBefore\\r\\n\\r\\nOpenPath\\r\\n  ├── resolve .git and commondir while opening\\r\\n  ├── resolve them again while checking alternates\\r\\n  └── fall back without one validated metadata result\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter\\r\\n\\r\\nOpenPath\\r\\n  └── ResolveWorktreeMetadata\\r\\n        ├── GitDir\\r\\n        ├── CommonDir\\r\\n        └── WorktreeID\\r\\n              │\\r\\n              ├── repository storage\\r\\n              ├── alternates inspection\\r\\n              └── reftable inspection\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n## One resolver for three facts\\r\\n\\r\\n`gitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata` resolves an explicit worktree root into:\\r\\n\\r\\n- `GitDir`\\r\\n- `CommonDir`\\r\\n- `WorktreeID`\\r\\n\\r\\nThe resolver takes a worktree root. It does not discover one from CWD, read Git environment variables, run Git, cache results, or choose a caller's policy.\\r\\n\\r\\nResolution is all-or-error. Malformed or unreadable metadata stops the open.\\r\\n\\r\\n`gitrepo.OpenPath` now resolves metadata once and passes those facts into repository opening, object-alternates detection, and reftable inspection.\\r\\n\\r\\nA bare-repository open is tried only when worktree metadata does not exist.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Symlinks and `..` keep their filesystem meaning\\r\\n\\r\\nLexically cleaning a path through a symlink can change where `..` leads. The resolver checks filesystem identity before it returns a cleaned path.\\r\\n\\r\\nLinked-worktree registrations may use physical aliases. They must still resolve to an immediate child of `CommonDir/worktrees`.\\r\\n\\r\\nInspection errors now reach the caller. They no longer mean \\\"feature absent.\\\" This applies to reftable inspection and malformed `.git` layouts.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Fixes a hang that is already released\\r\\n\\r\\n`OpenPath` on `main` identifies a `.git` entry by reading it: `os.Stat`, then `os.ReadFile`. That works for a directory or a regular file. For three other entry types the read never finishes.\\r\\n\\r\\n| `.git` is | `main` | This PR |\\r\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\r\\n| A FIFO with no writer | Blocks until a writer opens it | Refused on type |\\r\\n| A symlink to such a FIFO | Blocks until a writer opens it | Refused on type |\\r\\n| A symlink to `/dev/zero` | Reads forever, memory grows | Refused on type |\\r\\n\\r\\nThe resolver checks the type first. It opens only a directory or a regular file, and refuses anything else by name.\\r\\n\\r\\nNone of these arrive by clone. Git refuses a `.git` path component in a tree at any depth, so each one needs local write access to the worktree. This is a robustness fix, not a vulnerability.\\r\\n\\r\\n## `gitdir:` strictness now matches Git\\r\\n\\r\\nThe legacy parser accepted pointer files that Git rejects. It cut the prefix at `gitdir:` instead of `gitdir: `, then trimmed whitespace from the remainder. That let `gitdir:target`, ` gitdir: target`, and `gitdir:\\\\ttarget` all resolve. Git requires the single space and trims nothing.\\r\\nThe fixture covers seven `.git` pointer spellings. The new resolver agrees with Git on all seven. The legacy parser agreed on three.\\r\\nThis changes behavior. A `.git` file that worked only because Entire was more permissive than Git now fails, and every other Git tool was already failing it.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Stop new duplicate traversal\\r\\n\\r\\nA source guard scans production Go across the repository. It rejects new `.git`, `gitdir:`, and `commondir` traversal outside `gitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata`.\\r\\nThe guard lists the existing callers that later PRs must migrate:\\r\\n\\r\\n- checkpoint metadata\\r\\n- session metadata\\r\\n- strategy and hooks\\r\\n- remaining product consumers\\r\\n\\r\\nThe exception list records each function and the one `git rev-parse` flag it may use. If that function starts using another metadata flag, the guard fails. The test also fails when a listed exception no longer exists.\\r\\n\\r\\nA temporary multi-file repository test runs the complete scanner. It proves that the scanner follows a package constant into another file, scans production code under `internal/`, and ignores a parameter named `gitDir`.\\r\\n\\r\\nPositive controls cover rooted filesystem APIs, package constants, `Readlink`, aliased imports, and legacy resolver calls.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Verification\\r\\n\\r\\n- `mise run check`\\r\\n  - formatting passed\\r\\n  - lint passed with 0 issues\\r\\n  - race-enabled unit and integration tests passed\\r\\n  - Vogon canary passed 56/56\\r\\n  - external deterministic canary passed 4/4\\r\\n- `git diff main --check`\\r\\n- Real Git fixtures cover ordinary, linked, bare, separate-Git-dir, submodule, symlink-alias, moved-registration, alternates, and reftable layouts.\\r\\n- On the seven `.git` pointer spellings in the fixture, the new resolver matches Git on 7/7. The legacy parser matched 3/7.\\r\\n- Broken fixtures verify fail-closed repository opening and typed absence.\\r\\n\\r\\nNo paid real-agent E2E tests were run.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Deliberately not included\\r\\n\\r\\nCheckpoint, session, strategy, hooks, and other product consumers still use their existing paths. Separate PRs will migrate them without mixing their error and fallback policies into this resolver change. The last migration will remove the legacy resolvers.\\r\\n\\r\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2241/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2241/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/680\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/680/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/680/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/680/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/680\",\n            \"id\": 4057903797,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7JsVXf\",\n            \"number\": 680,\n            \"title\": \"perf: reduce memory and network cost for checkpoint metadata\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"pjbgf\",\n              \"id\": 5452977,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NTI5Nzc=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5452977?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pjbgf\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [\n              {\n                \"id\": 10276683087,\n                \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACZIm9Tw\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/performance\",\n                \"name\": \"performance\",\n                \"color\": \"d4c5f9\",\n                \"default\": false,\n                \"description\": \"Performance issues\",\n                \"archived_at\": null,\n                \"archived_by\": null\n              }\n            ],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-03-11T12:19:25Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-19T10:45:27Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-03-19T10:45:26Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/680\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/680\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/680.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/680.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-03-19T10:45:26Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \" ## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\n   This PR focuses on two key optimisations:\\r\\n\\r\\n   ### 1. Reduce memory allocations when reading checkpoint metadata\\r\\n\\r\\n   - **Streaming `json.Decoder`** replaces `json.Unmarshal` for reading `metadata.json` files, avoiding loading entire JSON documents into memory as intermediate `[]byte`\\r\\n   - **Lite structs** (`sessionMetadataLite`, `checkpointSummaryLite`) replace full `CommittedMetadata`/`CheckpointSummary` when only a few fields are needed — avoids allocating large unused nested objects (`Summary`, `InitialAttribution`, `TokenUsage`, etc.)\\r\\n   - **Shared helpers** (`decodeSummaryLiteFromTree`, `decodeSessionMetadataLite`) deduplicate the metadata reading logic between `ListCheckpoints` and `ReadCheckpointMetadata`\\r\\n\\r\\n   ### 2. Reduce network cost for pulling checkpoint data from remote\\r\\n\\r\\n   - **Shallow treeless fetch** (`--depth=1 --filter=blob:none`) downloads only the tip commit and tree objects for the metadata branch —     no blobs, no history\\r\\n   - **On-demand blob resolution** via `BlobResolver` uses go-git's `HasEncodedObject` to check the local object store (loose objects +    packfile indices) before fetching anything\\r\\n   - **Targeted subtree blobs fetch** via `git fetch-pack` requests all blobs within the checkpoint tree, so that a consistent view is present in disk. Automatically falling back to a full branch fetch if the server doesn't support `allow-reachable-sha1-in-want`\\r\\n\\r\\n   ### Resume flow (before → after)\\r\\n\\r\\n   **Before:** `git fetch origin entire/checkpoints/v1` → downloads entire branch (all commits, trees, and every blob across all\\r\\n   checkpoints)\\r\\n\\r\\n   **After:**\\r\\n   1. `git fetch --depth=1 --filter=blob:none` → tip commit + trees only\\r\\n   2. go-git tree walk → find all blob hashes within the checkpoint sub-tree\\r\\n   3. `HasEncodedObject` → skip blobs already in local store\\r\\n   4. `git fetch-pack <url> <hash>...` → fetch only the missing blobs\\r\\n\\r\\nThis translates into an user upon doing a single branch clone of a repository being able to do a `entire resume <branch>` with a rather efficient network and local storage data consumption. Behind the scenes `entire` will only fetch the blobs contained in the checkpoint subtree, as opposed to the entire branch,\\r\\n\\r\\n   ## Test plan\\r\\n\\r\\n   - [x] `BlobResolver` unit tests: `HasBlob` present/missing, `ReadBlob` present/missing\\r\\n   - [x] `CollectTranscriptBlobHashes`: single session, multi-session, chunked, nonexistent checkpoint\\r\\n   - [x] Existing `ListCheckpoints` and `ReadCheckpointMetadata` tests still pass with lite structs\\r\\n   - [x] Full `mise run lint` clean\\r\\n   - [x] Manual E2E: `entire resume` on a branch with remote-only checkpoint data\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/680/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/680/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          }\n        ],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      },\n      \"issues\": {\n        \"total_count\": 0,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e14\",\n      \"query\": \"repo:entireio/cli review incremental\",\n      \"prs\": {\n        \"total_count\": 47,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2068\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2068/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2068/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2068/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2068\",\n            \"id\": 5195555560,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABAUQiVg\",\n            \"number\": 2068,\n            \"title\": \"fix(claude-code): attribute parallel subagent TodoWrite checkpoints via agent_id\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"id\": 257360244,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 4,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T17:48:42Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-27T01:23:35Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": null,\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2068\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2068\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2068.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2068.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"**Trail:** https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1099\\n\\n**What:** Attribute Claude Code incremental TodoWrite checkpoints to the correct parallel Task using `agent_id` → remembered task links instead of mtime-only `FindActivePreTaskFile`.\\n\\n**Why / how it helps:** Sibling parallel Tasks each write `pre-task-*.json`; the newest-file heuristic misfiles progress under the wrong `tool_use_id`. Claude sends `agent_id` on in-subagent PostToolUse hooks but Entire dropped it.\\n\\n**How:** Capture `agent_id` on `SubagentCheckpointHookInput`; remember/lookup `.entire/tmp/agent-task-<id>.json`; prefer link over mtime; purge links on pre-task cleanup.\\n\\n**Testing:**\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/ -run 'AgentTask|ResolveIncremental|PostTodo|SubagentCheckpoint'`\\n- Package tests green in worktree validation\\n\\nFixes #2062\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2068/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2068/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": {\n              \"id\": 2626939,\n              \"client_id\": \"Iv23lieFG10uOnChW4TN\",\n              \"slug\": \"entire\",\n              \"node_id\": \"A_kwHOAfprLM4AKBV7\",\n              \"owner\": {\n                \"login\": \"entireio\",\n                \"id\": 33188652,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjMzMTg4NjUy\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33188652?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"Organization\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"name\": \"Entire\",\n              \"description\": \"\",\n              \"external_url\": \"https://entire.com\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/entire\",\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-01-09T21:20:56Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-23T08:32:31Z\",\n              \"permissions\": {\n                \"administration\": \"read\",\n                \"checks\": \"write\",\n                \"contents\": \"write\",\n                \"emails\": \"read\",\n                \"members\": \"read\",\n                \"metadata\": \"read\",\n                \"pull_requests\": \"write\",\n                \"statuses\": \"read\",\n                \"workflows\": \"write\"\n              },\n              \"events\": [\n                \"check_suite\",\n                \"create\",\n                \"delete\",\n                \"fork\",\n                \"member\",\n                \"membership\",\n                \"organization\",\n                \"pull_request\",\n                \"push\",\n                \"repository\",\n                \"star\",\n                \"team\"\n              ]\n            },\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2848\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2848/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2848/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2848/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2848\",\n            \"id\": 5961767924,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABJzNDLQ\",\n            \"number\": 2848,\n            \"title\": \"transcript: export the JSONL records adapter for live streams\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"id\": 881031,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-21T13:46:15Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-23T10:20:50Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-23T10:20:47Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2848\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2848\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2848.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2848.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-23T10:20:47Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1641\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Public API addition and rename with parity tests against existing Convert; no auth or data-path changes beyond documented streaming usage.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Exports the incremental JSONL-to-records path for **live streaming**: the former private `jsonlAdapter` is now **`JSONLAdapter`**, with **`NewClaudeAdapter`**, **`NewCursorAdapter`**, and **`NewDroidAdapter`** for agent-specific setup (Droid still unwraps envelopes).\\n> \\n> Adds **`Lines()`** so producers can track how many source transcript lines have been consumed (including blanks/drops; partial lines count only after **`Flush`**). Docs now describe using **`Feed`** / **`Flush`** alongside **`Fold`**, stable fold keys only when replaying from line 1, and redacting before feeding.\\n> \\n> New tests assert exported adapters fold to the same output as **`Convert`** on fixtures, and that **`Lines`** matches the documented counting rules.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 2c19bfcc755111b212f36189066f1ac8382837c8. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2848/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2848/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": {\n              \"id\": 2626939,\n              \"client_id\": \"Iv23lieFG10uOnChW4TN\",\n              \"slug\": \"entire\",\n              \"node_id\": \"A_kwHOAfprLM4AKBV7\",\n              \"owner\": {\n                \"login\": \"entireio\",\n                \"id\": 33188652,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjMzMTg4NjUy\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33188652?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"Organization\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"name\": \"Entire\",\n              \"description\": \"\",\n              \"external_url\": \"https://entire.com\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/entire\",\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-01-09T21:20:56Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-23T08:32:31Z\",\n              \"permissions\": {\n                \"administration\": \"read\",\n                \"checks\": \"write\",\n                \"contents\": \"write\",\n                \"emails\": \"read\",\n                \"members\": \"read\",\n                \"metadata\": \"read\",\n                \"pull_requests\": \"write\",\n                \"statuses\": \"read\",\n                \"workflows\": \"write\"\n              },\n              \"events\": [\n                \"check_suite\",\n                \"create\",\n                \"delete\",\n                \"fork\",\n                \"member\",\n                \"membership\",\n                \"organization\",\n                \"pull_request\",\n                \"push\",\n                \"repository\",\n                \"star\",\n                \"team\"\n              ]\n            },\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3048\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3048/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3048/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3048/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3048\",\n            \"id\": 6251347116,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABNai7aA\",\n            \"number\": 3048,\n            \"title\": \"redact: redact passwords passed on the command line\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n              \"id\": 26940511,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI2OTQwNTEx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Beehtrix\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 13,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-11-06T21:56:41Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-15T18:17:05Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": null,\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3048\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3048\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3048.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3048.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"Fixes #2898.\\n\\nBuilt on @DilpreetBansi's branch from the issue. Their commit comes first, unchanged and with their authorship. The eighty-five commits on top come from my review of it, from @MuskanPaliwal's review and from the automated reviews here, with one merge of `main`. Each commit message says what it fixes and which test covers it, so this description only gives the result.\\n\\n## What it covers\\n\\nA password given to a client on its command line is usually human-chosen (`hunter2`, `Summer2026!`). That is far below the entropy threshold, and no pattern layer matched it, so it reached the checkpoint as typed. This adds a command-line layer inside the connection-string layer (counted as `connection_string`) that redacts:\\n\\n- `--password`, `--passwd` and `--pass` on any command, with `=` or a blank\\n- the short password flags of the clients that define them, each tied to its own command: the `mysql`/`mariadb` tools (`-pSecret`, also after `-f` in a cluster), `docker`/`podman`/`nerdctl`/`buildah`/`skopeo`/`oras`/`helm login -p`, `az login -p`, the mongo tools' `-p`, `sshpass -p`, `redis-cli -a`, and openssl's `pass:` sources (`-pass`, `-passin`, `-passout`, `-password`, with one dash or two)\\n- the `password` of a `.netrc` entry, on one line or several, its keywords in any case, with `login` or `account` given more than once, and also as `printf` or `echo -e` writes it with `\\\\n`, `\\\\r` or `\\\\t`\\n\\nA value is the whole shell word: joined quoted pieces, escapes, substitutions inside a word and continued lines are covered. Commands run inside another command are read too: `sh -c '...'`, `$(...)`, `docker exec`, `kubectl exec ... --`, ssh's remote command and `ProxyCommand=`, wrappers such as `sudo`, `env` and `nice`, and programs that run their operands (`find -exec`, `go run`, `go tool`, `xargs`). So are argument lists in code, where a flag and its value are separate string elements: `[\\\"wget\\\", \\\"--password\\\", \\\"Secret\\\"]`, `subprocess.run([\\\"openssl\\\", \\\"enc\\\", \\\"-pass\\\", r\\\"pass:Secret\\\"])`, Go, Java and C# array literals, and Python's triple-quoted and adjacent strings (`\\\"Sec\\\" \\\"ret\\\"`).\\n\\nThese stay visible:\\n\\n- `$UPPER_VAR`, `${...}`, a `$(...)` that only fetches the secret (`$(cat file)`, `$(gh auth token)`), `--password-stdin`, `--password-file` and the shared placeholders\\n- a client name that another program reads as a path, name or host: `find /etc/mysql -print`, `go test ./mysql -parallel 8`, `tar -C /opt/mysql -pxzf a.tgz`, `nmap mysql -p3306`\\n- a word after a blank long flag that is no value: a prose word (\\\"pass --password to set it\\\"), an error message (`--password requires a value`), a capitalized metavar (`--password PASSWORD`, `-pDB_PASS`), a one-digit pass number (`x264 --pass 2`), and a `{{ ... }}` template that fills in the whole value (`--password {{ .Values.password }}`); text joined after a template is still redacted\\n- a flag quoted on its own before a blank (`grep -rn -- \\\"--password\\\" docs/`, `if arg == \\\"--password\\\" {`), and a parser's declaration of a flag's names (`add_argument(\\\"--password\\\", \\\"-p\\\", required=True)`)\\n- prose that uses the `.netrc` keywords (\\\"Enter machine name, login and password below.\\\")\\n- a flag inside another client's quoted argument (`mysql -e 'select -p1'`), and unrelated short flags (`ssh -p 2222`, `docker run -p 3306:3306 mysql`, `kubectl patch deployment mysql -p='{...}'`)\\n\\n`configFingerprintVersion` goes from 13 to 14, and `docs/security-and-privacy.md` describes the coverage under detection layer 5.\\n\\n## Documented limits\\n\\nThese were raised in review and left as they are on purpose:\\n\\n- **A client name in the operands of a program that is not on the operand list is still read as that client.** `operandCommands` covers the common file, search, archive, network, package and service tools. For others, a client name among the operands starts a command (`mytool ./mysql -p8080` redacts `8080`). This side stays fail-safe.\\n- **A flag quoted on its own before a blank takes no value**, so `wget \\\"--password\\\" Secret` keeps `Secret`. In code and documentation that shape names the flag. After `=` (`\\\"--password\\\"=Secret`) or as an element of an argument list, it is read.\\n- **A `{{ ... }}` template stays visible in single quotes too** (`mysql -p'{{word}}'`). Helm, Jinja, Ansible and Mustache fill it in before the shell reads its quotes, and a password spelled as a template looks the same as a template variable of that name.\\n- **`[\\\"redis-cli\\\", \\\"-a\\\", \\\"$PASSWORD\\\"]` stays visible.** Many languages expand a reference in a double-quoted list element (PHP, Perl, Kotlin, Groovy, Dart), and where one does not, the text is the placeholder's name. A reference that is no placeholder (`\\\"$ecret\\\"`) is redacted.\\n- **A short flag in an argument list inside a quoted string of code is not read** (`python -c 'subprocess.run([\\\"mysql\\\",\\\"-pX\\\"])'`, or the same list in a JSON string). Long flags there are read, and so are short flags in a list on its own.\\n- **`psql --password` takes no value, but the next word is still read as one.** `psql --password production` redacts `production`. A dash-led word stays the next option where psql's name starts a command (`psql --password -h db`), but not where it does not (after `echo`, or after a case pattern), so `-h` is redacted there. An agent that writes `mysql --password Secret1` still puts the password in the transcript, so this side stays fail-safe.\\n- **Quoted strings are read within one line**, so an apostrophe in prose does not pair with one many lines later. A password with a line break inside its quotes, or a flag after a multi-line quoted argument (`mysql -e 'SELECT` and then `1' -phunter2`), is not read. Substitutions are followed across lines.\\n- **Substitutions nested more than three deep are read as text of the command around them**, which keeps the reading linear. Their flags count as the outer command's, so ssh's port in `mysql -h $(ssh -p2222 db echo $(echo $(echo $(echo x))))` is redacted.\\n- **Two shapes of a parameter expansion that never closes are still read in time quadratic in the length of their line**: a double-quoted short-flag value repeated on one line (`mysql -p\\\"${A:-)\\\" mysql -p\\\"${A:-)\\\" ...`, about 1 s at 32 KB here) and commands nested in each other's substitutions (`$(mysql ${A:-) $(mysql ${A:-) ...`, about 1.7 s at 16 KB). Both were slower before this review, and both take many repeats of the same broken command on one line.\\n- **A raw `.netrc` password ends at a quote or a shell operator**, as a shell word does, so `password hunter2\\\";tail` hides `hunter2` and keeps `\\\";tail`. The `.netrc` text in a transcript is mostly written by commands, where those bytes end the word.\\n- **A client's short flags are read on the line of its name**, so in an argument list wrapped across lines a short flag and its value on different lines are not read. Long flags are.\\n- **A client quoted as ssh's remote command inside a substitution in another client's arguments** (`mysql -h $(ssh db \\\"sudo mysql\\\" -ppw) db`) is not read past its string. On its own (`x=$(ssh db \\\"sudo mysql\\\" -ppw)`) it is.\\n- **Backticks are told apart by counting them on their line.** A code span that crosses a line break, or a stray backtick earlier on the line, flips that reading for the rest of the line.\\n- **Text after a `;` in a quoted argument that starts with a client name is read as a command** (`mysql -e 'SELECT 1; mysql -pX'` redacts `X`), and so is a client named anywhere inside another client's quoted argument, since that argument may be a remote command. Past 4 KB of a double-quoted string, an escaped quote after a password is read as closing a string of the command when the piece it opens starts or ends with a blank or holds an operator, which keeps the count of quotes bounded.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- `go test ./redact` passes, including 694 table redaction cases, 4 deep-expansion cases, 1 rejected-value test and 397 must-stay-visible cases for this layer. `go test -race ./redact/...` passes.\\n- `FuzzString_CommandLinePasswordsLinear` builds command lines from shell, client and argument-list words. It redacts each one as it is and repeated to 128 KB, and the long one must take under 5 s (60 s with the race detector). Its seeds are the one-line shapes that were once read in quadratic time; the three from review now take 30 to 83 ms at 32 to 76 KB, and two from a later review pass (client names after an unclosed `${PW:-)`), which took 5.7 and 16 s at 128 KB, take about 0.1 s. A 90-second fuzz run here found nothing.\\n- `go test ./...`: no failures beyond the 12 that `main` (f4327183) has in the same container. `golangci-lint` 2.15.0 reports 0 issues, and `gofmt`, the secret-pattern lint and the complexity gate (`BASE_REF=f4327183`) pass.\\n- False positives, with the layer alone: none in 33 real agent transcripts from this repository's `refs/entire/checkpoints/*` (1,001,602 string values). In the Go module cache (85,479 files) there are the same 37 matches as before review: 36 passwords in test fixtures and one word after `--password` in a comment.\\n- `BenchmarkRedactJSONLBytes/Fixture/ClaudeFull2`: median 615 ms here against 584 ms on `main`, over eight interleaved runs each. That is about 5% slower, inside this container's run-to-run spread of about ±10%. The layer alone takes about 20 ms on the fixture's 8,508 strings.\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- #2963 merged first with `configFingerprintVersion` 13, so this takes 14. #3109 is built on this branch and takes 15.\\n- A default in a positional or special parameter (`mysql -p${1:-hunter2}`) stays visible, as `DB_PASSWORD=${1:-hunter2}` already does on `main`. That is the shared placeholder rule, so it has its own issue, #3077, and pull request, #3078.\\n- `--password=${A:-) mysql ` repeated on one line is slow on `main` too (about 4 s at 16 KB), in the pattern layer's rules rather than in this layer.\\n- A command stored as a JSON array of its arguments (`{\\\"command\\\":[\\\"mysql\\\",\\\"-pX\\\"]}`, as Codex stores the commands it runs) is handled in #3109.\\n- @MuskanPaliwal asked whether a smaller core would do: long flags, a per-client short-flag table, one shared word reader and netrc. I've offered to prototype it on a separate branch and compare it with this one on her inputs, the timings and the same false-positive corpus, if numbers would help decide.\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3048/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3048/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2269\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2269/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2269/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2269/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2269\",\n            \"id\": 5344338182,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCJp5wg\",\n            \"number\": 2269,\n            \"title\": \"feat(tokens): billing-class breakdown for a live session\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T04:50:38Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-11T00:48:36Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": null,\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2269\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2269\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2269.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2269.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1237\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n> **Opens against `pr1-token-class-breakdown` (#2210), not `main`.** It needs that PR's shared\\n> renderer, price-ratio rows and withheld-cost reasons. Retarget once #2210 merges.\\n\\n## What this does\\n\\n`entire session tokens` now shows the \\\"How it was billed\\\" block that #2210 gave\\n`entire checkpoint tokens` — volume and, where a verified per-model ratio row applies, cost share\\nper billing class. On a real live session:\\n\\n```\\nHow it was billed\\n                                     tokens   volume    cost\\n  Fresh input                           42k      10%     15%\\n  Cache write                          118k      29%     58%  (1h TTL 22k)\\n  Cache read                           240k      58%      8%\\n  Output                                11k       3%     19%\\n  Total                                411k\\n  Of the total, subagents used          54k      13%\\nDuration: 2h 14m so far\\n```\\n\\nCache read is 58% of the volume and 8% of the cost. Output is 3% of the volume and 19% of the\\ncost. Volume alone points at the wrong thing to optimise, which is the whole argument for the\\nsecond column — now on the command people actually run mid-task, not only on committed history.\\n\\n## One pricing decision, not two\\n\\nThe interesting part is what *didn't* get duplicated. `checkpointTokenWeights` owned the pricing\\ndecision and read `[]*checkpoint.Metadata`, which live session state does not have. Rather than\\ngrow a second copy, the per-session half was extracted as `tokenWeightsForSession`, and both\\ncommands now route through it.\\n\\nA live session and its own committed checkpoint showing a cost column in one and withholding it in\\nthe other is a contradiction a user cannot resolve. So a parity test runs the same model and usage\\nthrough both report builders and asserts `Priced`, `UnpricedReason`, `Family` and `Total` all agree\\nacross five cases, including both subagent cases.\\n\\nThe one deliberate divergence is `ttlKnown`. Live state is the running binary's own struct and\\n`CacheCreation1hTokens` is written whenever the agent reports it, so absence means zero; a\\ncheckpoint written before that field existed cannot be told apart from one with no 1-hour writes,\\nwhich is what `checkpointTokenTTLKnown`'s version gate is for. A test pins both halves: live stays\\npriced, the same bytes in a legacy checkpoint stay unpriced.\\n\\n## Withheld-cost reasons that are true of the case they name\\n\\nThe reasons print verbatim, so each has to be true — and, now that two commands share them, must\\nnot name one command's scope. Three fixes:\\n\\n- The reason strings dropped \\\"this checkpoint's\\\" (false on `session tokens`). `unpricedUnknownTTL`\\n  keeps saying \\\"checkpoint\\\" because only a committed one can predate the field.\\n- A subagent on an **unrecognised** model was reported as \\\"these tokens span models with different\\n  price ratios\\\". There are no ratios there to differ from, and `unpricedNoModel` is false in the\\n  other direction because the parent model does have a row. It gets its own reason, and the guard\\n  returns a reason instead of a bool, since one bool cannot carry two facts.\\n- A multi-session checkpoint where only *some* models are recognised said \\\"no model with verified\\n  price ratios\\\" — false, the other session's model has one. `checkpointTokenWeights` now decides\\n  from the whole set instead of returning at the first unpriced session, which also removes an\\n  order-dependence: claude + an unknown model + gpt reported differing ratios or no ratios purely\\n  by position. Precedence is documented on the function. Priced/unpriced verdicts are unchanged\\n  throughout; only the stated reason moves, and only toward being true.\\n\\n## The subagent figure appears once\\n\\nIt was a \\\"Likely contributors\\\" entry *and* is folded into the four classes. One figure under two\\nlabels is the duplication this block exists to remove, so the text now renders it inside the block\\nwhere it can carry its share of the total.\\n\\n**The JSON is unchanged.** `contributors[].kind == \\\"subagents\\\"` and `tokens.subagent_total` both\\nstay: the duplication was a rendering artifact of a report that has both a block and a contributors\\nlist, and JSON has neither, so removing an element from an array #2210 shipped would be a breaking\\nchange for a text-only gain. A test pins that decision.\\n\\nTwo consequences worth knowing, both caught here:\\n\\n- The new label is 28 characters, so every `%-14s` in the renderer widened to `%-30s` — including\\n  the two header rows, which carry no label and are the easiest to miss. Verified mechanically.\\n- The contributors section guarded on `len(contributors) > 0`, which counts entries that render\\n  nothing. With the subagent figure moved out, a session with subagent usage but no context data\\n  and no skill events printed the header alone. Lines are now built first and the header printed\\n  only if any survive, so it cannot disagree with its own body. Two tests cover the empty section;\\n  nothing did before.\\n\\n## Verified end to end, not only in tests\\n\\n#2210's lesson was that 1,060 lines of tests left its headline cost column never having rendered\\noutside a unit test. So this was driven by hand: isolated repo, real `session-start` /\\n`user-prompt-submit` / `stop` hooks, real binary, and a `$PATH` shim — the git hooks resolve\\n`entire` from `$PATH`, which is exactly how #2210's first end-to-end run silently tested an\\ninstalled release.\\n\\nThat run found a bug no unit test could: a turn ending in under a second rendered\\n`Duration: 0s so far`. Every duration test uses a synthetic multi-hour span. A zero duration is the\\nsame false claim as the \\\"0m\\\" the empty-string rule already avoided, so sub-second spans now render\\nnothing.\\n\\nAlso confirmed live:\\n\\n- the cost column renders on a live Claude Code session (the table above is that run)\\n- the subagent line renders through the real capture path, and the numbers prove the flattening:\\n  input 72k = 42k parent + 30k subagent, output 30k = 6k + 24k, 54k/242k = 22%\\n- `session tokens` and `checkpoint tokens` agree on the same session: identical volume **and** cost\\n  shares (the checkpoint's class totals are 2x only because it aggregated two sessions)\\n- `--json` is strictly additive against a binary built from `pr1-token-class-breakdown`: exactly\\n  `classes` and `duration` added, no key removed, renamed, or changed in value\\n\\n## Scope, against the budget\\n\\n**1,333 insertions / 263 deletions** — 368 non-test, 965 test. The budget for this PR was 800\\nadded, so it overran by ~67%, and that is reported rather than absorbed (spec Rule 6). Two\\nmitigations for the reader: 257 of the test lines are Task 5b relocating existing tests beside the\\nrenderer rather than new coverage, and the reason-taxonomy fixes above were not in the original\\nestimate — they came out of review of the shared code this PR creates.\\n\\nDeliberately **not** here: per-tool drill-down (needs a transcript walk), `tokens profile`,\\nthe recommendations rewrite, the per-class subagent split, and per-entry cost weighting for\\nsubagents on another provider. Bounding `subagentPricingReason`'s unbounded walk was implemented\\nand then reverted: it belongs to the incremental plan's known-bugs list together with\\n`SubagentTotal`'s unbounded `totalTokens` walk and the un-audited `exactPercents` math, and\\nsplitting one of the three out fragments that follow-up. The reasoning now sits in the function's\\ndoc comment; the disagreement is safe in the meantime, since an entry past the bound withholds cost\\nrather than mispricing it.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- Every behaviour test-first; the command-level test is mutation-checked (forcing the model\\n  unpriced fails it).\\n- `mise run fmt && mise run lint`: 0 issues.\\n- `mise run test:ci`: exit 0, 88 packages, both canaries green (56 and 4).\\n\\n## Changelog additions\\n\\n### Added\\n- `entire session tokens` now shows a \\\"How it was billed\\\" breakdown with each billing class's share\\n  of volume and, where a verified per-model price ratio applies, share of cost — the same block\\n  `entire checkpoint tokens` shows. New `--json` keys: `classes` and `duration`\\n- `entire session tokens` now shows how long the session has been worked on, measured as the span\\n  between its first and last recorded interaction\\n\\n### Changed\\n- The subagent token figure now renders inside the billing-class block with its share of the total,\\n  instead of as a separate \\\"Likely contributors\\\" entry. `--json` is unchanged\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> CLI reporting and display logic only; pricing verdicts are tightened for accuracy with extensive parity tests, no auth or persistence changes.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **`entire session tokens`** now shows the same **\\\"How it was billed\\\"** table as checkpoint tokens (volume plus cost share when ratios apply), adds **`duration`** / JSON **`classes`**, and prints interaction span as e.g. `2h 14m so far` (omitted when there is no interaction or the span is under one second).\\n> \\n> Pricing is unified via **`tokenWeightsForSession`** and shared **`writeTokenClasses`** (`token_classes_render.go`). Subagent mismatches return specific withheld-cost reasons (`unpricedSomeTokensNoRatios` vs mixed models); multi-session **`checkpointTokenWeights`** scans all sessions with documented precedence so reasons are order-independent. User-facing unpriced strings are scope-neutral for both commands.\\n> \\n> Text output moves the subagent total into the billed block (**\\\"Of the total, subagents used\\\"**), widens table columns, and only shows **Likely contributors** when something actually renders (JSON contributors unchanged).\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 27577f4c13349d6219735bc4e67f8b76a6585f42. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2269/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2269/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2953\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2953/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2953/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2953/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2953\",\n            \"id\": 6088151835,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABLX8OCg\",\n            \"number\": 2953,\n            \"title\": \"transcript: a streaming adapter for Codex item-path rollouts\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T21:51:49Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-15T11:09:54Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-11-15T11:09:51Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2953\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2953\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2953.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2953.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-11-15T11:09:51Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2674/changes/cli/1723\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nA streaming adapter for Codex rollout files, so a live consumer can follow a session's saved file with the same mapping `Convert` uses. Stacked on #2897.\\n\\n- `CodexItemRolloutDecided(content) (item, decided bool)`: decides live whether a rollout is on the item path. The first turn runs from the first `task_started` to the next; a \\\"true\\\" never flips, so a reader can trust it on a prefix. `hasCodexItems` is now `item && decided`.\\n- `NewCodexRolloutAdapter()`: feeds complete rollout lines through the item path's line converter (the one `compactCodexItems` already uses), counting every line including empty ones, so folding its records equals `Convert` byte for byte, usage and model included. Use it only on a rollout `CodexItemRolloutDecided` accepts; replay from line 1 with a fresh adapter.\\n\\nTests: the fold equals `Convert` for a fixture with a reasoning-only call (`codex-call:line-N`), a model change and a counter decrease, fed in 1/7/64-byte chunks and whole; partial lines; empty-line numbering; the decision on prefixes. Consumer: `entire stream attach codex:<id>` in entire-stream, which follows any Codex session's saved file — checked end to end against a real plain `codex` session.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Rxmv1Yre5x8Re4F6G9FrUm\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Transcript conversion only; path detection is refactored with expanded tests and no auth or data-handling changes.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **`NewCodexRolloutAdapter`** so live consumers can incrementally feed a growing Codex JSONL rollout and get the same transcript **records** as batch **`Convert`** on the item path—**`Feed`**, **`Flush`**, and **`Lines`** mirror the other JSONL adapters, including partial-line buffering and line-numbered usage-only keys.\\n> \\n> **`CodexItemRolloutDecided(content) (item, decided bool)`** is exported from the former **`hasCodexItems`** scan: it reports when the first turn clearly uses user **`item_completed`** events vs when the rollout must stay on the **`response_item`** path, including an **undecided** state while the first turn is still in flight. **`hasCodexItems`** is now **`item && decided`**. README documents both APIs for live readers.\\n> \\n> Tests assert folded adapter output matches **`Convert`** (chunk sizes, empty lines, flush), partial-line behavior, and stable prefix decisions.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 35380a88d93b483181b53df46c526249a4e8b402. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2953/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2953/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2782\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2782/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2782/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2782/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2782\",\n            \"id\": 5858177451,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABIhLC9A\",\n            \"number\": 2782,\n            \"title\": \"Count session and checkpoint tokens from each agent's running total\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-15T00:58:17Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-10T08:21:03Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-11-10T08:21:00Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2782\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2782\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2782.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2782.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-11-10T08:21:00Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2250/changes/cli/1579\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nMakes token accounting correct by construction. Today `entire` works out each checkpoint's tokens by slicing transcripts at offsets, and every double count and undercount we've found comes from those slices starting or ending in the wrong place: turns without file changes went missing (Claude Code `entire status` showed 64k against 285k actually spent), a repeated Stop on a turn that changed files counts the turn twice, a message whose lines straddle an agent's mid-turn commit counts twice, and Copilot counts cache twice.\\n\\nThis PR has each session keep the agent's own running total (the **token ledger**), and each checkpoint store what that total grew by since the session's previous checkpoint.\\n\\n## 1. One shared reader for every agent\\n`agent.ReadCumulativeUsage` reads a session's running total for any agent. It owns the files:\\n- it reads only the bytes appended since the last reading (a no-op reading costs under 1ms), and waits for a line's end;\\n- it detects a rewritten transcript (the 512 bytes before its last offset no longer match) and reads it again, reporting `Restarted`;\\n- it reads a small or rewritten file (OpenCode's export, Droid's `settings.json`, a Claude Code subagent) whole, only when its size or last bytes changed, and never reports that as a restart;\\n- it never follows a symlink or opens a FIFO beside the transcript, and reads `.entire` through its confined reader.\\n\\nEach agent supplies a `UsageCounter` (50–150 lines) built from shared parts in `agent/usage_counting.go`:\\n- `KeyedUsage` counts per-call records once per key, with the agent's rule for a repeated record (`KeepFirst` for replays, `KeepLast` for records re-written, `KeepMostOutput` for streamed messages), a window of open records per file, and per-child sums;\\n- `RunningTotal` sums running totals across a counter restart; `KeyedUsage.CoveredBy` combines records with a running total where an agent writes both.\\n\\n| Agent | What it counts |\\n|---|---|\\n| Claude Code | Assistant messages by `message.id`, most output winning; subagents (and their subagents, Workflow agents) as children |\\n| Codex | `token_usage_record` by `response_id` (replays keep the first copy), combined with segment-summed `token_count` totals; children from the session's subagent inventory |\\n| Copilot CLI | `session.usage_record` by `apiCallId` (cache split out of input), combined with `session.shutdown` totals, which include subagents, so their records are subtracted |\\n| OpenCode | The export's assistant messages, reasoning counted once |\\n| Pi | Per-message usage on every branch |\\n| Factory Droid | `settings.json`'s `tokenUsage`, one call per assistant message |\\n| Antigravity | `PLANNER_RESPONSE` step usage by step index |\\n\\nChild sessions (Droid Workers, OpenCode child sessions) are not read here: #2824's child-session credit counts them once, and ledger checkpoints add it as the per-turn path does.\\n\\n## 2. The token ledger\\n- `SessionState.TokenLedger` (`session/token_ledger.go`, `strategy/token_ledger.go`) holds the running total, read **under the session lock** at turn start, every Stop and every condensation. `TokenUsage` is its total; a checkpoint stores its pending growth; a successful checkpoint write (or attach) marks it checkpointed, and that mark never moves back.\\n  - A repeated or concurrent Stop reads the same total, so it adds nothing — including on a turn that changed files.\\n  - A commit in the middle of a turn stores everything up to the commit; the rest lands in the next checkpoint. A message straddling that commit counts once.\\n- **Which sessions:** sessions this CLI starts at a turn start, for the seven agents above. Legacy states, states created at Stop or by attach, Cursor, Vogon and external agents keep today's per-turn path unchanged.\\n- **Takes over at the first reading with usage**; what the per-turn accounting already checkpointed counts as checkpointed.\\n- **Rewritten transcripts:** a lower reading is ignored (a stale copy), unless the transcript restarted: then the difference moves to `Base` and the total carries on.\\n- **Stop** skips the per-turn token calculation for ledger sessions (for Claude Code it read every subagent transcript only to be discarded).\\n- **Session end** takes a last reading, so usage an agent writes after its final Stop (Copilot's shutdown totals) is counted.\\n- **A new transcript path** for the session is read as a restart, so history the new file repeats is not counted twice.\\n- **Attach** reads the transcript being attached, updates session state under the session lock, and marks as checkpointed exactly what its checkpoint stored.\\n- **Checkpoint metadata** adds `session_token_usage`, the session's running total at that checkpoint, next to `token_usage`.\\n\\n## Checked\\n- **Real sessions, old vs new:** 726 local sessions across six agents on the final code (154 Copilot, 302 Codex, 149 Claude Code, 39 Antigravity, 37 Pi, 45 Droid), plus 36 OpenCode exports on an earlier revision: the shared reader gives exactly the totals of the per-agent code it replaces, and reading each file in nine pieces gives the same totals as one read. The only difference is intended: Droid Workers are no longer the ledger's children (13 sessions), because #2824's child-session credit counts them. Worst incremental step 126ms; largest cursor 38KB (a Claude session with 190 subagents: 123KB).\\n- **Live sessions** (`e2e/tests/token_ledger_test.go`): turns that changed files, one that changed nothing, and an agent commit mid-turn; for every session, checkpoints plus pending equal the session total, which equals a fresh read of the agent's files. Passes for all seven agents: Claude Code, Codex, Copilot, OpenCode, Pi, Droid and Antigravity.\\n\\n## Tests\\n- `TestUsageCounters_Conformance`: every agent with a counter needs a fixture in `testdata/usage/<agent>/`, read whole, in pieces cut at and around every line end, and after a rewrite.\\n- Reader tests: partial lines, rewrites, whole files, symlinked files beside the transcript, files that fail to read and return, moved files, the per-file window, merge policies.\\n- Ledger unit and strategy tests: repeated readings, growth, stale reads, rewrites, child high-water marks, handover from the per-turn accounting, attach under the lock, adopt's copy.\\n- Integration through the real hooks: Claude Code (repeated Stop on a file-changing turn, no-change turns between commits, mid-turn agent commit, a message straddling it, a subagent finishing in a later turn, a rewritten transcript), Codex (repeated Stop, mid-turn commit), Droid (Worker plus the parent's second Stop). With the ledger off, the repeated Stop and the straddling message fail.\\n\\n`mise run lint`: 0 issues. Unit and integration suites pass.\\n\\nSize: +3016/-56 in total.\\n\\n## Not in this PR / known limits\\n- External agents keep the per-turn accounting (the protocol has no incremental token call).\\n- A session's first reading reads its files whole (1.3s on an 82MB Claude transcript with 190 subagents); every later reading reads what was appended. Codex children are read through the inventory again only when a child file changed.\\n- Only an appended transcript can report a rewrite; for an OpenCode undo, or a Droid rewrite, a lower total is ignored until the total passes the old one — an undercount, not a double count.\\n- A crash between a checkpoint write and the state save can store the same growth twice (true of main's accounting too).\\n- A session whose state was lost counts from its next turn start; seeding from the latest checkpoint's `session_token_usage` is a follow-up. Deleting the per-turn path once legacy states age out, and server use of `session_token_usage`, are follow-ups.\\n- Overlaps #2856 (mid-turn double count): for ledger sessions it is superseded; whichever lands second reconciles.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2782/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2782/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1840\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1840/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1840/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1840/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1840\",\n            \"id\": 4958219657,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M71VVQH\",\n            \"number\": 1840,\n            \"title\": \"perf(codex): incremental turn-end token calc to fix O(N²) reparse\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"id\": 881031,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-07-23T11:09:47Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-10T13:11:35Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-19T11:07:29Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": true,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1840\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1840\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1840.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1840.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/929\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nFixes #1836.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nCodex reports **cumulative** token totals (`event_msg`→`token_count`→`total_token_usage`), so the turn-end token calc re-parsed the **entire rollout from line 0 on every hook** — O(N) per hook, **O(N²) per session** — amplified by large `encrypted_content` reasoning blobs. Long sessions visibly stalled at each turn end. Claude Code avoids this by slicing (its counts are per-message, not cumulative).\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n- **`agent.IncrementalTokenCalculator`** (new, built-in-only capability): scan only the transcript lines added since the last checkpoint, baselining off a cumulative snapshot persisted in `SessionState.CumulativeTokenBaseline`.\\n  - Codex rollouts are **append-only**, use a **per-rollout session id**, and fire **no compaction hook**, so the snapshot always indexes stable content.\\n  - Cold start (first checkpoint / resumed / imported) or a shrunk transcript (`snapshot.LineCount > fromOffset`) falls back to a one-time full scan.\\n  - The delta is **provably identical** to the full-scan `CalculateTokenUsage` — only the amount of parsing changes.\\n- Codex now implements **`SubagentAwareExtractor`** (no subagents) so turn-end modified-file extraction runs on the **in-memory transcript bytes** instead of a second full-file disk read.\\n- `CalculateTokenUsage` (full-scan) kept byte-for-byte identical for back-compat and the fallback path.\\n\\n## Measured win (per-hook, warm baseline)\\n\\n| turns | before (full scan) | after (incremental) | allocs before→after |\\n|------|------|------|------|\\n| 100 | 1251µs | 29µs | 2617 → 32 |\\n| 1000 | 12.3ms | 0.5ms | 26020 → 32 |\\n| 10000 | 119ms | 9ms | 260027 → **32** |\\n\\nAllocs flat at 32/op regardless of session length — the definitive O(delta) proof (residual ns/op is `SliceFromLine`'s cheap byte-walk, not JSON parsing).\\n\\n## Safety (no regressions)\\n\\n- **File-change identification**: bytes extractor uses the same `fromOffset` as the old disk path and produces identical results for JSONL (no blank lines); the skip-checkpoint decision also relies on git-status new/deleted + merged modified, independent of transcript parsing. No missed changes → no spurious carry-over branches.\\n- **Attribution**: token deltas unchanged (verified against fixtures: multi-turn, cached-input, mid-offset); the guard falls back to a full scan on any misalignment, so numbers are never wrong. Line attribution (agent vs human) is computed from git commits and is untouched.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- New unit tests (`incremental_test.go`): incremental == full scan across turns/cached/mid-offset; cold-start reusable baseline; resumed/stale-offset fallback; `DoesNotParseHistory` (corrupted pre-offset lines ignored — proves bounded parsing); bytes extractor == disk extractor.\\n- Validation scenarios (`perf_validation_test.go`) documenting the root cause + benchmarks.\\n- `mise run fmt` / lint (v2.11.3): clean · unit (codex/agent/session/cli): pass · integration: **437 pass** · Vogon canary: **4/4**.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> <sup>[Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) is generating a summary for commit 406904c64eabb2c7dabb7a1fc9bfef9ff14cc176. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1840/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1840/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2786\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2786/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2786/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2786/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2786\",\n            \"id\": 5868164678,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABIpJTpw\",\n            \"number\": 2786,\n            \"title\": \"transcript: split JSONL conversion into records adapter and fold\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-15T14:35:32Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-16T10:21:12Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-16T10:21:10Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2786\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2786\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2786.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2786.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-16T10:21:10Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1583\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nFirst step of live session streaming. Converting Claude Code, Cursor and Droid transcripts is now an incremental records adapter followed by an agent-agnostic fold. Both live in the `transcript` library. The fold is meant to be shared with the backend, so a live session folded from the same records matches the checkpoint the CLI writes; that integration is not part of this PR.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n- `transcript/records.go`: `Record` and its five ops: `message`, `append`, `result`, `usage` and `drop`. Records are append-only, so they can be streamed and stored as plain appends.\\n- `transcript/fold.go`: `Fold` and `Folder`. `Apply` validates a whole batch before changing anything and returns the IDs of the messages it touched; `Line(id)` returns one message's current line, so a live view can re-render only what changed. The fold keeps decoded blocks and encodes a message only when it produces its line, so each record costs time in its own size.\\n- `transcript/jsonl_records.go`: the adapter, unexported until the streaming code needs it. `Convert` for the three JSONL agents now runs the adapter, then the fold. The other converters are unchanged.\\n- `ToolResult` now carries the stored JSON tags and replaces the private `toolResultJSON`, so the converters, `Decode` and records share one result type.\\n- A \\\"Records and fold\\\" section in `transcript/README.md` that specifies the record wire format, the compatibility policy, the visibility rules and the `Folder`'s resource use. The transcript paragraph in `docs/development/checkpoint-implementation.md` is updated.\\n\\n## Output change\\n\\nOutput is byte-identical except for one case: an assistant line with empty content is now always skipped. It used to be written as `\\\"content\\\":[]` when the next user entry had both tool results and text.\\n\\n## Protocol differences from the stream-protocol draft\\n\\nThese still need to go into `entire-stream/docs/stream-protocol.md`:\\n\\n- `synthetic` is replaced by `sourceId`, the agent's message ID that the line prints, next to an opaque fold key `id`. A message ID the agent reuses for a later, non-adjacent message gets the key `<id>@L<line>`; messages without an ID, including all user messages, get `@L<line>`.\\n- A `result` with an empty `toolUseId` targets the last `tool_use` block, searching from the end.\\n- An `append` without `ts` clears the timestamp.\\n- Content may be a non-array. The adapter then restates the message with a new `message` record instead of sending `append`.\\n- An assistant message counts as empty when its content is `[]` or `null`.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- `transcript/legacy_oracle_test.go` keeps the previous two-pass converter as an oracle. The new path is compared with it byte for byte over the fixtures, edge cases, and 500 random transcripts fed in random chunks.\\n- 8 deliberate bugs planted in the fold and adapter were all caught.\\n- Regression tests cover a record stream decoded into one reused `Record`, empty-but-present `content`/`ts`, and a restated message after appends and results.\\n- Benchmarks against the old compactor (`BenchmarkJSONLConversion`): 200 fragments of one message take 1.0ms instead of 8.5ms, and 100 tool results 0.86ms instead of 2.7ms, with fewer allocations.\\n- `mise run check` passes.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2786/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2786/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": {\n              \"id\": 2626939,\n              \"client_id\": \"Iv23lieFG10uOnChW4TN\",\n              \"slug\": \"entire\",\n              \"node_id\": \"A_kwHOAfprLM4AKBV7\",\n              \"owner\": {\n                \"login\": \"entireio\",\n                \"id\": 33188652,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjMzMTg4NjUy\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33188652?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"Organization\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"name\": \"Entire\",\n              \"description\": \"\",\n              \"external_url\": \"https://entire.com\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/entire\",\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-01-09T21:20:56Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-23T08:32:31Z\",\n              \"permissions\": {\n                \"administration\": \"read\",\n                \"checks\": \"write\",\n                \"contents\": \"write\",\n                \"emails\": \"read\",\n                \"members\": \"read\",\n                \"metadata\": \"read\",\n                \"pull_requests\": \"write\",\n                \"statuses\": \"read\",\n                \"workflows\": \"write\"\n              },\n              \"events\": [\n                \"check_suite\",\n                \"create\",\n                \"delete\",\n                \"fork\",\n                \"member\",\n                \"membership\",\n                \"organization\",\n                \"pull_request\",\n                \"push\",\n                \"repository\",\n                \"star\",\n                \"team\"\n              ]\n            },\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2648\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2648/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2648/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2648/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2648\",\n            \"id\": 5693681740,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABGesrlA\",\n            \"number\": 2648,\n            \"title\": \"Stop redacting Claude tool-use ids and Codex agent_message ciphertext\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-03T21:27:36Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-05T10:59:41Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-05T10:59:39Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2648\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2648\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2648.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2648.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-05T10:59:39Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1473\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nTranscript redaction replaces two kinds of non-secret values with `REDACTED`:\\n\\n- Claude Code tool-use ids (`toolu_01` + 22 base62 characters) when they appear in free text, for example `<tool-use-id>toolu_01…</tool-use-id>` inside task-notification messages. Once redacted, a notification can no longer be linked to its task record.\\n- Codex multi-agent `agent_message` response items. In real rollouts under `~/.codex/sessions`, these carry `content: [{\\\"type\\\":\\\"input_text\\\",…},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"encrypted_content\\\",\\\"encrypted_content\\\":\\\"gAAAA…\\\"}]`, where the second part is a ~700-1000 character Fernet ciphertext that only the originating session can decrypt. The entropy layer redacts that ciphertext in every stored transcript.\\n\\n## Cause\\n\\nThe entropy layer in `redact/redact.go` (`[A-Za-z0-9+_=-]{10,}`, Shannon entropy > 4.5) flags any high-entropy run. Its only exemptions are JSON-key based (`shouldSkipJSONLField`), so an id inside a string value such as `message.content` is not protected. Tool-use ids score about 4.6-4.8. Betterleaks does not fire on either sample.\\n\\nThe Codex sanitizer (`SanitizePortableTranscript`) already strips session-bound ciphertext from `reasoning` and `compaction` items, but not from `agent_message` items, so their ciphertext reaches the redactor.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n- `redact/redact.go`: the entropy layer skips a match only when the whole match is exactly `^toolu_01[A-Za-z0-9]{22}$`. The rule is anchored and fixed-length on purpose. The entropy character class includes `_` and `-`, so a secret glued onto an id forms one longer match, and that longer match must stay subject to the entropy check. A prefix rule would let it through. The exemption applies to the entropy layer only: betterleaks, goredact, provider prefixes, and every other layer still scan the id. The shape was checked against 5,814 distinct tool-use ids in local Claude Code transcripts: all of them are exactly `toolu_01` + 22 base62 characters (30 bytes).\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/transcript.go`: the sanitizer drops `{\\\"type\\\":\\\"encrypted_content\\\"}` parts from `agent_message` items, both for top-level response items and inside a `compacted` line's `replacement_history`. The line and its `input_text` parts stay, so stored line numbering still matches the rollout. Lines with nothing to strip keep their original bytes, and a second pass is a byte-for-byte no-op.\\n- `redact/fingerprint.go`: `configFingerprintVersion` 1 → 2, so the incremental redaction cache does not reuse output produced by the old rules.\\n- Docs: the entropy-layer exemption is documented in `docs/security-and-privacy.md`, and the sanitizer's coverage in `docs/development/checkpoint-implementation.md`.\\n\\n### Deliberately not changed\\n\\n- No `gAAAA` prefix allowlist and no `encrypted_content` entry in `shouldSkipJSONLField`. User applications produce identical Fernet tokens, and those can be real secrets. Stripping the ciphertext in the Codex sanitizer is scoped to Codex's own item type and removes the value instead of storing it unscanned.\\n- No shape-based allowlist for Claude project-folder slugs in paths. Slugs are only redacted when they encode temp or scratch directories, and a shape rule broad enough to cover them would also cover real secrets.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nTests were written first and run against unmodified `main` code.\\n\\n`redact/tool_use_id_test.go`:\\n\\n```\\n--- FAIL: TestString_PreservesClaudeToolUseIDInFreeText (0.01s)\\n    tool_use_id_test.go:30: tool-use id was altered:\\n         got  \\\"<task-notification><tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id><status>completed</status></task-notification>\\\"\\n         want \\\"<task-notification><tool-use-id>toolu_01Xk9mQ2vL8nR5tW1yB4cF7d</tool-use-id><status>completed</status></task-notification>\\\"\\n--- FAIL: TestJSONLContent_PreservesClaudeToolUseIDInFreeText (0.01s)\\n    tool_use_id_test.go:43: tool-use id was redacted: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"<task-notification>\\\\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\\\\n</task-notification>\\\"}}\\nFAIL\\nFAIL\\tgithub.com/entireio/cli/redact\\t0.245s\\n```\\n\\n`TestString_ClaudeToolUseIDExemptionIsExact` is a guard: an id with an appended, prepended, or dash/underscore-joined secret, an id one character too long, a `toolu_02` prefix, and a non-base62 body must all still be redacted. It passes on `main` because nothing is exempt there. To confirm it catches the unsafe variant, I temporarily used a `strings.HasPrefix(match, \\\"toolu_01\\\")` exemption, and it failed five subtests:\\n\\n```\\n--- FAIL: TestString_ClaudeToolUseIDExemptionIsExact (0.00s)\\n    --- FAIL: TestString_ClaudeToolUseIDExemptionIsExact/secret_appended_after_underscore (0.01s)\\n    --- FAIL: TestString_ClaudeToolUseIDExemptionIsExact/secret_appended_after_dash (0.01s)\\n    --- FAIL: TestString_ClaudeToolUseIDExemptionIsExact/secret_appended (0.01s)\\n    --- FAIL: TestString_ClaudeToolUseIDExemptionIsExact/id_with_one_extra_char (0.01s)\\n    --- FAIL: TestString_ClaudeToolUseIDExemptionIsExact/non-base62_body (0.01s)\\n```\\n\\n`TestClaudeToolUseIDFixtureIsHighEntropy` pins the fixture above the threshold, so the tests cannot pass without exercising the exemption.\\n\\n`cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/transcript_test.go`, using the item shape from real rollouts:\\n\\n```\\n--- FAIL: TestSanitizePortableTranscript_StripsAgentMessageEncryptedContent (0.00s)\\n    transcript_test.go:478:\\n        \\tError:      \\t\\\"…{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"encrypted_content\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"encrypted_content\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"gAAAAABqwRvDZmFrZS1jaXBoZXJ0ZXh0LWZvci10ZXN0cy1vbmx5\\\\\\\"}]}}…\\\" should not contain \\\"gAAAAABqwRvDZmFrZS1jaXBoZXJ0ZXh0LWZvci10ZXN0cy1vbmx5\\\"\\n        \\tMessages:   \\tagent_message ciphertext survived sanitization\\nFAIL\\nFAIL\\tgithub.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex\\t0.373s\\n```\\n\\nAll of these pass after the fix. As a one-off check that is not committed, I ran sanitize + `redact.JSONLContent` over the 44 local Codex rollouts that contain Fernet ciphertext. Line counts were unchanged, no `agent_message` line was redacted, and the only ciphertext left was in `spawn_agent` function-call arguments (see the open question below).\\n\\nVerification: `mise run fmt && mise run lint` (0 issues), `GOOS=windows go vet` on the touched packages, `mise run test:ci`, and `mise run test:e2e:canary` (pass). In `test:ci`, `TestOpenCodeSeedRepoPlantsDeps` (e2e/agents) fails; it also fails on `main` locally because it needs bootstrap. Two `claudecode` config-probe tests hit their 5s budget under full-suite load and pass when the package is run alone. Neither package is touched here.\\n\\n### Open question\\n\\nCodex `spawn_agent` function calls (namespace `collaboration`) also carry Fernet ciphertext, in `arguments.message`, and that ciphertext is still entropy-redacted. It is out of scope here: rewriting tool-call arguments needs its own decision about whether to strip the value or keep a placeholder.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches the always-on entropy redaction path and Codex transcript sanitization before checkpoint storage; fingerprint bump forces cache misses but behavior is narrowly scoped with tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Fixes two classes of **false-positive `REDACTED`** in stored transcripts: Claude Code **tool-use ids** in free text, and Codex multi-agent **`agent_message`** session-bound ciphertext.\\n> \\n> The **entropy layer** now skips matches that are exactly a `toolu_01` + 22 base62 id (other layers still scan; glued-on secrets stay redacted). **`configFingerprintVersion`** is bumped to **2** so incremental redaction cache does not reuse old output.\\n> \\n> **Codex sanitization** drops `{\\\"type\\\":\\\"encrypted_content\\\"}` parts from `agent_message` items (rollout lines and compacted history) while keeping plaintext and line counts; the reviewer parser uses a shared **`itemTypeAgentMessage`** constant. Docs and tests cover both behaviors.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit e0c63652d89cf34a6691f0ce43e80c26acf31594. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2648/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2648/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2149\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2149/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2149/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2149/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2149\",\n            \"id\": 5270181674,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBPMRcg\",\n            \"number\": 2149,\n            \"title\": \"Changelog 0.10.3\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-08-27T17:09:46Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-27T17:15:55Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-27T17:15:54Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2149\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2149\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2149.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2149.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-27T17:15:54Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1161\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Documentation-only changelog update with no runtime or build changes in this diff.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds the **0.10.3** section to `CHANGELOG.md`, documenting the release rather than changing product code.\\n> \\n> The entry groups shipped work across **Added** (durable subagent data in committed checkpoints, process-identity commit linking, zombie-session sweep, configurable redaction engines, `entire doctor trace` aggregation, trail body `If-Match`, and opt-in telemetry), **Changed** (continuous search TUI, CLI/web search parity, clearer cluster login hints), **Security** (redacted `task_description`, betterleaks 1.8.x), and a long **Fixed** list—highlights include `--no-optional-locks` on internal `git status`, incremental transcript redaction for Stop-hook performance, bounded hook walks, condensation checkpoint-ID durability, `entire disable --uninstall` honesty, Cursor transcript attribution, partial-clone checkpoint reads, and `entire-cli/<version>` User-Agent on control-plane traffic. **Housekeeping** covers CI, lint behavior, dependency bumps, and dropping automatic gemini-cli E2E from main.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 803b2811ba43c4c9c100ea11af6d73394c0d6819. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2149/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2149/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2291\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2291/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2291/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2291/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2291\",\n            \"id\": 5368984828,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCcvasw\",\n            \"number\": 2291,\n            \"title\": \"perf: reduce transcript and repeated-secret scan allocations\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"id\": 257360244,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-09-07T01:34:35Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-08T10:32:20Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-08T10:32:18Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2291\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2291\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2291.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2291.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-08T10:32:18Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1241\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n- Search each distinct betterleaks finding value once per `String` call, avoiding duplicate whole-input searches and duplicate regions. For valid JSONL, this benefit is within one string field, such as a large tool result containing repeated request-log entries; equal values in separate fields or lines are not deduplicated together.\\n- Read transcript blobs directly into a size-reserved byte buffer instead of copying through `File.Contents()` strings; preallocate the chunk slice as well. The size hint covers both normal chunks and current unchunked shadow transcripts, up to a 1 GiB sanity ceiling. Above that, reads retain incremental growth. This ceiling is an allocation hint limit, not a read-size limit.\\n- Preserve transcript bytes, fallback behavior, and redaction output. Each duplicate finding previously generated the same unlabeled regions; eliminating duplicate work does not change output, so no `configFingerprintVersion` bump is needed. No API or configuration changes.\\n- Keep characterization coverage for base, legacy, present-empty, absent, and numerically ordered chunked transcripts. The present-empty result must remain non-nil because ephemeral reads use nil to select the legacy fallback. Use filename constants consistently.\\n\\n## Benchmarks\\n\\nOriginal before/after medians from five runs with `-benchtime=500ms -benchmem`, Go 1.26.6 on darwin/arm64 (Apple M5 Pro):\\n\\n| Workload | Time before → after | Allocated bytes before → after |\\n|---|---:|---:|\\n| 1,000 repeated credentials in one String call | 175.428 → 116.936 ms | 292.007 → 119.687 MB |\\n| 1 MiB transcript read | 380.988 → 69.679 µs | 6,291,204 → 1,057,024 |\\n| 8 MiB transcript read | 1,233.019 → 414.637 µs | 50,331,431 → 8,397,057 |\\n\\nThe existing ClaudeFull2 fixture was effectively unchanged (167.462 → 163.730 ms).\\n\\nSoph's review identified that the original 50 MB hint ceiling excluded current unchunked shadow transcripts. The new 64 MiB benchmark exercises that case. Fresh A/B medians comparing the previous PR implementation (`caf73c69b`) with the amendment, using the same new benchmark, Go 1.26.6, Apple M5 Pro, `GOMAXPROCS=4`, `-benchtime=20x -count=3 -benchmem`:\\n\\n| 64 MiB transcript | Previous PR | Amendment |\\n|---|---:|---:|\\n| Time | 6.299 ms | 2.952 ms |\\n| Allocated bytes | 268,435,280 | 67,117,320 |\\n| Allocations | 24 | 6 |\\n\\nThat is approximately 75% fewer allocated bytes. The 1 MiB and 8 MiB allocation counts remain unchanged. These benchmarks use real in-memory Git objects to isolate read/allocation costs; they are not end-to-end CLI speedup, peak-RSS, or production-frequency claims. The frequency of transcripts above 50 MB has not been measured here.\\n\\nBenchmark output assertions check correctness. Performance comparisons are manual against a base ref; CI does not enforce an allocation or timing baseline.\\n\\n```sh\\ngo test ./redact -run '^$' -bench '^BenchmarkRedactStringRepeatedSecret$/Occurrences1000$' -benchtime=500ms -count=5 -benchmem\\nGOMAXPROCS=4 go test ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint -run '^TestReadTranscriptFromTreeFormats$' -bench '^BenchmarkReadTranscriptFromTree$' -benchtime=20x -count=3 -benchmem\\n```\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n`agent.ReassembleJSONL` pre-sizing, image-asset reads, and direct legacy fallback reads remain separate follow-ups, as requested in review.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- [x] Same-benchmark A/B for 1 MiB, 8 MiB, and 64 MiB; three runs per side.\\n- [x] `TestReadTranscriptFromTreeFormats` and focused redaction checks.\\n- [x] `mise run check`: formatting, lint (0 issues), race-enabled unit/integration suite, and deterministic Vogon/Roger-Roger canaries; exit 0 in 241.96 seconds.\\n- [x] `golangci-lint config verify` separately passed. Its online schema fetch was blocked inside the otherwise network-restricted full-check run; the actual lint analysis passed there.\\n- [x] Independent read-only review and `git diff --check`.\\n\\nVogon reports 56/56 and Roger-Roger 4/4; raw Vogon output includes four expected agent-specific skips. Reassembly and image-read follow-ups were not implemented.\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2291/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2291/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2059\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2059/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2059/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2059/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2059\",\n            \"id\": 5195093879,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABAT478Q\",\n            \"number\": 2059,\n            \"title\": \"remove the unreachable persistent task-checkpoint writer\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T16:52:38Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-20T12:17:18Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-20T12:17:18Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2059\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2059\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2059.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2059.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"[https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1096](<https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1096>)\\n\\n`persistent.go` carried a full task-checkpoint writer — `tasks/<tool-use-id>/` with per-task `checkpoint.json`, incremental `NNN-<id>.json` files, and a redacted subagent transcript — behind `if opts.IsTask && opts.ToolUseID != \\\"\\\"`.\\n\\n**Nothing ever reached it.** No producer in the tree sets `IsTask`: condensation builds one `WriteOptions` per session, and neither `attach` nor `agentimport` sets it. The `api/checkpoint` write union has no task variant at all, so a task write could not even be expressed. Measured on this repo's `entire/checkpoints/v1`: 0 of the 150 newest commits contain any `tasks/` path.\\n\\nDeleting the three functions alone would have left the scaffolding that made this look like working storage, so the always-empty parts go with them:\\n\\n* the `IsTask` guard in `applySessionWrite`, and its `taskMetadataPath` return value\\n* `buildCommitMessage`'s `taskMetadataPath` parameter — so a committed checkpoint no longer advertises an `Entire-Metadata-Task` trailer it never populated\\n* `incrementalCheckpointData` / `taskCheckpointData`\\n* the `WriteOptions` fields only that writer read: `AgentID`, `CheckpointUUID`, `SubagentTranscriptPath`, and the four `Incremental*` fields\\n\\n`IsTask`/`ToolUseID` **stay**: they feed stored metadata that live readers consume (`explain`, `checkpoint list`), and the ephemeral store genuinely sets `IsTaskCheckpoint` on the pending path. They now carry a comment saying no producer sets them and pointing at entireio/cli#2058, so the seam isn't mistaken for storage again.\\n\\nUntouched: the shadow branch's live `tasks/<tool-use-id>/` writer in `ephemeral.go`, and the trailer formatter it uses.\\n\\n## Coverage\\n\\n`TestWriteCommitted_SubagentTranscript_JSONLFallback` exercised only the dead path and goes with it. Its live twin `TestWriteTemporaryTask_SubagentTranscript_RedactsSecrets` covers the same invalid-JSONL redaction fallback on the ephemeral store, so the behaviour stays covered.\\n\\n## Doc and comment fixes\\n\\nThings this made visible:\\n\\n* `manual_commit_condensation.go` claimed re-reading subagent transcripts \\\"finds nothing on this path once the agent has cleaned the transcripts up.\\\" Agents do not clean them up — Claude Code keeps 180 `agent-*.jsonl` (121 older than two days), Codex 164 rollouts (all older). Cost is the real and sufficient reason for `subagentsDir=\\\"\\\"`, so the false sentence is replaced by the measured fact.\\n* `ref-checkpoint-backend.md` listed pre-push OPF among the lifecycle paths that follow the primary, contradicting its own limitations section 200 lines later; and described a checkpoint ref's tree as containing `tasks/…`.\\n* `sessions-and-checkpoints.md` now states outright that a committed checkpoint holds one record per session and none per subagent.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n`mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci` — 0 lint issues, no failures, 56 vogon + 4 roger-roger canary tests pass.\\n\\nRefs entireio/cli#2058. This is the cleanup half of that issue; the storage design (payload location, OPF gate) is still open there.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](<https://claude.com/claude-code>)\\n\\n---\\n\\n> \\\\[!NOTE\\\\] [Cursor Bugbot](<https://cursor.com/bugbot>) is generating a summary for commit 8dae672bc2b428bd70df99844a1cb4d65be4691a. Configure [here](<https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot>).\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2059/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2059/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2107\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2107/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2107/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2107/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2107\",\n            \"id\": 5232715480,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABAxXT3g\",\n            \"number\": 2107,\n            \"title\": \"perf: reuse redaction prefixes at condensation and Stop finalize\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-08-24T08:34:21Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-24T12:37:18Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-24T12:37:16Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2107\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2107\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2107.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2107.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-24T12:37:16Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1129\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nCloses the scope limit #2002 shipped with: prefix reuse covered only the shadow write, while post-commit condensation and the Stop finalize rewrite still re-redacted the whole session transcript on every checkpoint.\\n\\n## Why now\\n\\nA coworker hit **Codex's 30s Stop-hook timeout** on a 65MB rollout. The hook copied the transcript, then reread, sanitized, redacted and rewrote the whole thing — 30.203s, killed, leaving the checkpoint's final full-transcript rewrite incomplete. That is user-visible breakage rather than latency, so it jumped the queue ahead of the other items in #2091.\\n\\nHis numbers also say he already *has* #2002: 28.6s on ~65MB versus the 66.7s/70MB I measured pre-fix is roughly what the sharding buys, with none of the reuse — exactly the uncovered path.\\n\\nCondensation is the same shape, and after #2002 it is the largest remaining non-network cost in slow hook traces (**29.6%** of slow-trace time; `push_checkpoint_refs` is 69.7% but is network I/O).\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\nBoth paths now go through a new `checkpoint.RedactTranscriptIncremental`. Two design points are about correctness, not speed:\\n\\n**The redactor is a parameter, used for both the appended suffix and the whole-content fallback.** Previously the suffix was hardcoded to `RedactBlobBytes` while each caller picked its own fallback, so the two could diverge and splice a prefix produced by one pipeline onto a suffix produced by another. One parameter for both makes that unrepresentable.\\n\\n**Entries are namespaced by `TranscriptScope`**, because these paths do not redact the same bytes — the shadow write stores a *sanitized* transcript, condensation and finalize a *sanitized and image-externalized* one. Sharing one key would have been safe (the prefix hash rejects a mismatch) but would have missed on every checkpoint: a silently useless cache rather than a wrong one. The key also carries the session ID so concurrent sessions in one worktree never share an entry.\\n\\nThe per-subagent transcript opts out with a nil repo — written once per task, not appended across checkpoints.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nThe one that matters is byte-identity: incremental output equals a whole-transcript pass, across five appends. On its own that test would pass just as happily with the cache doing nothing, so there is a second test that counts the bytes handed to the redactor and asserts it sees **only the appended suffix**.\\n\\nAlso covered: scope isolation, session isolation, error propagation on both the full and the suffix path (a degraded scanner must fail the write, never ship a reused prefix alone), and that a single-JSON-value transcript (OpenCode's shape) is never cached for splicing.\\n\\n## One note on the diff\\n\\n`redactFinalizedTranscript` is extracted rather than inlined because eight added lines pushed `finalizeAllTurnCheckpoints` past the `maintidx` threshold. Extracting was the honest fix; a `nolint` would not have been.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `mise run lint` — 0 issues\\n- `mise run test:ci` — green, including `checkpoint` (328s) and `strategy` (111s), 56 vogon + 4 roger-roger canary\\n- Rebased onto main after #2106 unbroke the build\\n\\nRefs #2091.\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> <sup>[Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) is generating a summary for commit 95a7587984f33d13d42a8fdf06d67dbd423e84de. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2107/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2107/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2032\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2032/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2032/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2032/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2032\",\n            \"id\": 5178383961,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABAGbtwQ\",\n            \"number\": 2032,\n            \"title\": \"feat(claude-code): capture background subagent work durably (SubagentStop + task records)\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-08-18T05:19:52Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-20T20:40:44Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-20T20:40:40Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2032\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2032\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2032.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2032.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-20T20:40:40Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1076\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nImplements #2058's durable pointer model for subagent work, with the subtree payload location (`tasks/` inside the parent session's checkpoint).\\n\\n## The incident\\n\\nA real session dispatched ~29 background Claude Code subagents; entire captured nothing beyond a 2–8s launch stub for each one, even though the agents ran 5–18 minutes. The root cause: Claude Code's PostToolUse for a backgrounded Task tool fires at the **launch acknowledgment**, before the subagent has done any work — the real completion is delivered later, out of band, as `SubagentStop`. Entire never registered a hook for that true-completion signal, so every background subagent's edits and transcript were invisible.\\n\\n## Verified hook facts\\n\\n- **`SubagentStop`** fires per-agent at true completion, including after the parent's own turn already ended. Payload carries `session_id` (parent), `agent_id`, `agent_transcript_path` (the subagent's own transcript), `tool_use_id`, `transcript_path`, `cwd`. Notification-only; default timeout 600s.\\n- Subagents fire **no session-lifecycle hooks of their own** (no SessionStart/UserPromptSubmit/Stop/SessionEnd) — `SubagentStop` is the only completion signal, and a finishing subagent does not fire the parent's `Stop`.\\n- Subagent transcripts live at `<project>/<session-id>/subagents/agent-<agent_id>.jsonl`; the launch-time PostToolUse payload's `tool_response.agentId` matches that filename (verified against 29 real transcripts).\\n\\nParsing stays defensive: an absent `agent_transcript_path` degrades to the agent-layout convention (`ResolveAgentTranscriptPath`) rather than failing, and the parser logs the raw payload's key names (never values) at Debug.\\n\\n## Design: durable task records + condensation materializer\\n\\n**Task records** (`session.TaskRecord`, json `task_records`, on session state) are the durable ledger: `ToolUseID`, `AgentID`, `StartedAt`, `SubagentType`, `TaskDescription`, `DeclaredTranscriptPath`, `Files`, `TokenUsage`, `CompletedAt` (zero = live/in-flight). Mid-turn a record is a **pointer, not a payload** — the subagent transcript stays where the agent wrote it, and the record remembers how to find it. Producers:\\n\\n- **Background launch** creates a live record (labels captured at launch because `SubagentStop`'s payload carries none of them).\\n- **Foreground tasks** create-on-completion.\\n- **SubagentStop / foreground post-task / SessionEnd sweep** complete exactly-once via `strategy.CompleteTaskRecord` — one `MutateSessionState` closure: claim `CompletedAt`, attach files/tokens/declared path, merge into the session's `FilesTouched`. Completion happens last, after successful extraction, so a failed capture leaves the record live for the SessionEnd sweep to retry; a racing duplicate completes nothing.\\n- **Factory Droid Workers** upsert (`UpsertCompletedTaskRecord`): multi-turn workers merge files into one record instead of claiming exactly-once.\\n\\n**Materializer**: condensation resolves each record's transcript (declared path first, agent-layout fallback), runs the same sanitize → externalize → redact pipeline as the session transcript (`prepareTaskTranscriptForStorage`), and writes `tasks/<toolUseID>/{agent-<agentID>.jsonl, task.json}` **inside the parent session's checkpoint** on `entire/checkpoints/v1` — both backends, via the shared `applySessionWrite`. An unresolvable/unreadable/empty transcript still gets a `task.json` with a stable, path-free unavailable reason. Poisoned records (empty/unsafe IDs) are skipped-with-warn, never allowed to wedge condensation.\\n\\n**Self-contained checkpoints**: live records store transcript-so-far on every condensation and survive for retry; completed records are removed only after a successful write (`removeCompletedTaskRecords` off `resetCheckpointWindow`). A mid-task commit carries a partial transcript; a later checkpoint carries the full one.\\n\\n**Trigger currency**: `State.HasTaskContent()` (`len(TaskRecords) > 0`) replaces the deleted `TranscriptOnlyTaskSteps` counter everywhere. Records-only sessions (no shadow branch, no steps, empty parent transcript) condense; records never live on the shadow tree, so shadow-branch existence no longer implies task content (shadow pinning keys on `StepCount` only).\\n\\n## Alignment with #2058\\n\\nThis PR implements #2058's core — a durable record that survives until condensation, plus a materializer that makes every checkpoint self-contained — choosing the **subtree payload option** (`tasks/` inside the session checkpoint) over a separate task checkpoint kind. There is now exactly **one producer path** into stored task data (the materializer); the never-reachable per-write `IsTask` persistent route and its `Entire-Metadata-Task` trailer (#2058's \\\"dead writer\\\") are deleted.\\n\\n## What was removed and why\\n\\nOnce every checkpoint is self-contained, the mid-turn backstops are redundant — they existed only because task data used to die if it wasn't snapshotted before the session ended:\\n\\n- The turn-end incremental snapshot backstop (rotation, growth-dedup, cap of 8), `persistCapturedTranscriptSize`, `IncrementalTypeBackgroundProgress` / `FormatBackgroundProgressSubject` / `FormatIncrementalSubject`.\\n- The per-write `IsTask` persistent route + `Entire-Metadata-Task` trailer (dead code, see above).\\n- `claimTaskRecord`-as-removal: completion now marks, never deletes — the materializer needs the record.\\n- `SaveTaskStep` is now formally incremental-only (errors on `!IsIncremental`); its sole production caller is the Claude Code post-todo hook.\\n\\n## Behavioral invariants preserved\\n\\n- Background launches stay lazy: no capture at the launch stub, only a record.\\n- Foreground completion still merges the subagent's files into the session's `FilesTouched`.\\n- Exactly-once completion (the old claim-and-remove dedup, reshaped as mark-completed-once).\\n- SessionEnd ordering: the live-record sweep runs strictly before `endSessionNow`'s eager condense, so that condense materializes it.\\n- Read-only subagents' transcripts are stored: a completed record with no files still materializes, and \\\"has records\\\" makes the session condensable.\\n- The late-arrival zombie guard: a `SubagentStop` for a missing session state skips outright; `PhaseEnded` state → complete + eager condense.\\n\\n## Deliberate behavior changes\\n\\n- (a) Turn-end no longer writes incremental background snapshots — in-flight visibility now comes from condensation materializing the transcript-so-far into each checkpoint.\\n- (b) `doctor --force` **condenses** record-bearing dead-owner sessions instead of discarding them.\\n- (c) Shadow branches are deletable while records exist — records don't live there.\\n- (d) Record-bearing sessions are PrepareCommitMsg trailer candidates via `sessionHasNewContent`.\\n- (e) `checkpoint list --pending --json` task rows carry empty `id`/`metadata_dir` (no shadow commit exists); external consumers keying on `id` should use `tool_use_id`. Rows render with accurate `Running`/`Completed` verbs.\\n- (f) `SaveTaskStep` errors on non-incremental use.\\n\\n## Repairs shipped alongside\\n\\n- Hard-killed agents' live records get a terminal state: `finalizeExitedSessions` (the `entire status`/`doctor` sweep) completes live records before ending the session, so their transcript-so-far reaches a permanent checkpoint.\\n- `CondenseSessionByID` materializes instead of clearing when records exist; orphan cleanup can't `Clear` record-bearing states.\\n- ENDED + `FullyCondensed` is terminal-healthy even with leftover live records — pre-fix states self-resolve, no migration.\\n\\n## On-disk compatibility\\n\\nOld state files' `transcript_only_task_steps`, `last_captured_transcript_bytes`, and `last_snapshot_attempt` keys are silently dropped on the next save; no migration. Nothing durable shipped under the old `in_flight_tasks` schema.\\n\\n## OPF / redaction\\n\\n**git-branch (the default primary): task transcripts get the full 9 layers, automatically.** The pre-push OPF rewrite walks the checkpoint tree subtree-recursively and treats every blob except `content_hash.txt` as redactable, so `tasks/<id>/agent-<id>.jsonl` and `task.json` are covered with no new wiring. This PR writes no `content_hash.txt` into the task directory, so the apply pass's sibling-`full.jsonl` hash recompute is undisturbed.\\n\\n**git-refs: OPF now runs there too — fixed in this PR.** It previously ran on *nothing* on that backend: `prePush` returns for refs before ever reaching the OPF block, and `RewriteUnpushedV1WithOPF`'s only call site was the git-branch path, so session transcripts and task transcripts alike shipped at 8 layers while a user who enabled OPF believed 9 ran. That gap was pre-existing and backend-wide — not a consequence of the subtree design and not specific to tasks — but this PR enlarges it by volume (subagent transcripts are the highest-volume, least-reviewed content in the system), so it is fixed here rather than deferred.\\n\\n`RewriteQueuedCheckpointRefsWithOPF` (`strategy/manual_commit_opf_refs.go`) mirrors the v1 rewrite and reuses its machinery rather than duplicating it — the same blob walk and open blob policy, the same raw-byte and leaf-byte caps, the same single batched OPF shell-out per push, the same error taxonomy, and the same two up-front fail-closed gates in the same order. Only discovery and update differ, and both are simpler on refs: the push queue already names exactly which refs are unpushed, so there is no merge-base or divergence analysis, and each ref is updated independently instead of CAS-ing one branch tip.\\n\\nEvery unpushed commit on a queued ref is rewritten, not just its tip — pushing a ref sends its whole unpushed ancestry, so a tip-only rewrite would have shipped un-redacted ancestor blobs alongside the redacted tip. The walk stops at the first commit already carrying `Entire-OPF-Applied`, which makes the trailer its own watermark: in steady state it stops at the tip's parent and costs nothing. A repo that enables OPF late is bounded by the existing `resolveBootstrapLimit` / `BootstrapTooLargeError` pair rather than rewriting unbounded history.\\n\\n**Failure semantics differ by backend, deliberately.** Both fail closed. git-branch aborts the user's `git push`. On refs, unflushed refs simply stay queued, so an OPF failure or an explicit abort withholds the flush and returns cleanly: nothing un-redacted ships and the user's push still succeeds. It is not silent — a `logging.Warn` plus a stderr line say that checkpoint refs stayed queued and why. `OPFSkip` (the user opting out for one push) is unchanged: flush as-is, 8 layers, no trailer.\\n\\nOne user-visible copy change on the previously-untouched v1 path: `BootstrapTooLargeError` now says \\\"N checkpoint commits\\\" instead of naming `entire/checkpoints/v1`, because the error is shared across both backends and a git-refs user has no v1 branch. The remediation is identical for both.\\n\\n## Known gaps / follow-ups\\n\\n- **Shadow-only capture (#2058) — FIXED on this branch**: subagent transcripts no longer die at the user's commit; the materializer writes them into every permanent checkpoint under `tasks/`, on both backends.\\n- **Sweep-finalize gap — FIXED on this branch**: a session whose agent was hard-killed used to lose in-flight subagent work; `finalizeExitedSessions` now completes live records before ending the session, so the transcript-so-far is condensed.\\n- Commit trailer linkage for mid-task subagent commits is the stacked follow-up (PR #2034), rebuilt on records: the trailer trigger stays, the commit-snapshot capture is replaced by the materializer.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2032/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2032/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2692\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2692/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2692/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2692/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2692\",\n            \"id\": 5747531142,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABHJnjMg\",\n            \"number\": 2692,\n            \"title\": \"Remove shadow branches and line attribution\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-07T15:30:41Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-08T20:34:41Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-08T20:34:37Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2692\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2692\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2692.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2692.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-08T20:34:37Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1509\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAgent turns no longer write anything to git. Older versions committed a full working-tree snapshot to a per-worktree shadow branch (`entire/<commit>-<worktree>`) at every turn end. That was the source of runaway local storage, and cleaning those branches up at the wrong moment made uncondensed work unreachable. Turn ends now record pending work in session state only: the step count, the files the agent touched, and each touched file's git blob hash. A checkpoint is written only when you commit.\\n\\nLine attribution is removed entirely, including the AI/Human/Mixed labels in `entire blame`, which now reports whether each line's commit is linked to a checkpoint. Checkpoint metadata no longer carries `initial_attribution` or `combined_attribution`; entire.io derives the experts counts from those and must be told they stop arriving.\\n\\nCommits link to a session by file name: any committed path the session touched links it, except a new file at a path the agent deleted. Carry-forward after a partial commit compares the recorded hashes with the commit and the worktree, so a `git add -p` remainder, a pending deletion, or a session upgraded from the old state format keeps its uncommitted work. Gitignored files, submodule pointers, and paths inside a submodule or beneath a symlinked directory never enter the tracked files, so they can no longer keep a session pending forever; edits inside a submodule belong to the nested repository's own session. Whether a committed file still has uncommitted agent changes is asked of `git status`, so repositories with `text=auto` or `core.autocrlf` no longer keep fully committed files pending.\\n\\nLifecycle decisions (condensation, the zombie sweep, orphan cleanup, doctor) key on one predicate over session state instead of whether a shadow ref exists. Pending step rows, explain of temporary checkpoints, incremental task checkpoints and the Claude Code post-todo hook install are gone. `checkpoint list --pending` now previews what the next commit's checkpoint will contain.\\n\\nClaude Code gains a transcript prompt extractor, so its prompts no longer depend on `prompt.txt` alone.\\n\\nAddresses #2663, #2378, #2350, #1730, #1807 and #2653. Supersedes trail 1486 (`soph/fix-shadow-after-midturn-commit`), which patches code this PR deletes.\\n\\n## Migrations\\n\\nTurn ends no longer write shadow branches (entire/<commit>-<worktree>): pending work is tracked in session state and checkpoints are written only when you commit. Branches left by older versions are not removed automatically. `entire doctor` and `entire status` report them, and `entire doctor --force` or `entire disable --uninstall` deletes the `entire/<commit>-<worktree>` form without touching session state. The oldest bare `entire/<commit>` form is only ever listed, since a branch of your own named after a short SHA looks the same; `entire clean --all` removes it behind a confirmation. Do not use plain `entire clean` for this: it also clears pending session state. They hold full snapshots of your working tree, so run it once after upgrading. Deleting the branches frees no space by itself: a later `git gc` reclaims it once their objects are two weeks old. `git gc --prune=now` frees it immediately, but it drops every unreachable object in the repository (recently dropped stashes included) and must only run when no other git process is active.\\n\\n`entire blame --json` reports a per-line `status` (`checkpoint`, `commit`, `uncommitted`) instead of `authorship` and `tag`. Its summary reports checkpoint-linked, commit and uncommitted line counts instead of AI/Human/Mixed counts.\\n\\nNew checkpoints no longer include `initial_attribution`, `combined_attribution` or `prompt_attributions`; checkpoints written by older versions keep theirs, and rewrites (explain `--generate`, attach) carry them through unchanged. Session state files written by older versions still load; their attribution and `last_checkpoint_commit_hash` keys are dropped on the next save.\\n\\nThe Claude Code post-todo hook is no longer installed, and any `entire enable` prunes it and says so. Its subcommand stays so older hook configs keep working. An older CLI run against the same tracked `.claude/settings.json` reports the hooks as out of date and re-adds it; this CLI removes it again on the next `entire enable`.\\n\\nCommit pending agent work before downgrading to a previous release: the previous CLI deletes ended but uncondensed session state when its shadow branch is missing, and this release never writes one.\\n\\n`entire session info --json` and `entire session current --json` report the number of turns not yet condensed into a checkpoint as `pending_turns`. The old `checkpoints` field is still emitted with the same value for this release only and will be removed in the next one; switch scripts to `pending_turns`. `entire status --json` adds `legacy_shadow_branches`.\\n\\n## Follow-ups, not in this PR\\n\\nDowngrade safety: the previous CLI deletes ended but uncondensed session state when its shadow branch is missing, and this release never writes one, so rolling back after pending work discards it. The migration note covers it; a patch on the previous release line whose orphan check also requires no pending work, named as the minimum safe downgrade target, is a release-management follow-up (trail finding 01M4DD0R83YC).\\n\\nWorktree scoping, deferred to the #2531 work: scoping the zombie sweep and doctor to the current worktree, retiring the stored transcript copy with the growth check moving to the live transcript position, prompts and transcript for guest-linked commits, and capture following the event's cwd. #2531 itself must be reworked after this lands, since it pins sessions through shadow-branch steps; #2486 is expected to close in its favour.\\n\\nTracked on the priority list for go-git (#DM2KFD6): its worktree hashing lacks gitattributes, filter, and index-aware CRLF handling, which is why this PR asks `git status` instead of hashing; porting that logic into go-git would let the CLI drop the subprocess.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n`mise run check` (fmt, lint, unit, integration, Vogon canary) and `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` on the final tree, with a cold lint cache, after merging main at `375819df95`. Every commit builds and vets on its own. A focused security review of the cross-worktree stored-transcript read (a path taken from on-disk session state, gated by `git worktree list` registration and the `.entire` anchor) found no findings. The only local failures are the known OpenCode seed-cache guard and the Claude config-probe timeout, which passes alone.\\n\\nNew unit, integration and command tests cover: recorded-hash carry-forward (partial commits, pending, committed and re-created deletions, upgraded sessions, an unreadable worktree); name-based linking; gitignored and submodule paths on every capture route; the doctor legacy-branch check; the `--pending` preview in text and JSON without a TTY; and the Claude prompt extractor against the real transcript fixture.\\n\\nReal-agent E2E passed on `44ebccb136` for every leg (claude-code, codex, cursor-cli, copilot-cli, factoryai-droid, opencode, antigravity, roger-roger, and Windows): https://github.com/entireio/cli/actions/runs/37655720329. One changed expectation is `TestInteractiveNewFileLinksAfterUserRewrite`, which now expects a trailer after a user rewrites an agent-created file.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **High Risk**\\n> This rewrites core session-to-checkpoint lifecycle, persistent metadata contracts, and labs blame JSON—high blast radius for upgrades, downstream consumers (e.g. entire.io attribution fields), and real-agent E2E behavior.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Turn-end work stays out of git.** Agent stops no longer commit working-tree snapshots to `entire/<commit>-<worktree>` shadow branches; **SaveStep** only updates local session state (step count, files touched, content hashes, transcript copy). Permanent checkpoints are written at **`git commit`** onto metadata refs, matching the updated README/CLAUDE contract.\\n> \\n> **Checkpoint storage and metadata slim down.** The ephemeral/shadow-branch store (`EphemeralStore`, `WriteTemporary`, task step writes, related benchmarks and tests) is removed. **`CheckpointAttribution`** and all **`Attribution`** fields (`initial_attribution`, `combined_attribution`, `prompt_attributions`, `EphemeralBranch`) drop out of `api/checkpoint` and git/fs backends.\\n> \\n> **`entire blame` / `why` semantics change.** Per-line **AI/Human/Mixed** authorship is gone; JSON uses **`status`** (`checkpoint`, `commit`, `uncommitted`) and summaries count checkpoint-linked vs other commits. Help text states Entire does not attribute lines to AI vs humans—only whether the blame commit carries an **Entire-Checkpoint** trailer.\\n> \\n> **Claude Code hooks and prompts.** The **post-todo** (`TaskCreate|TaskUpdate`) hook is no longer installed; **`entire enable`** prunes stale installs while keeping the subcommand registered. New **`prompts.go`** implements **`PromptExtractor`** / **`TranscriptPromptExtractor`** so user prompts come from transcript bytes with injected/meta lines filtered.\\n> \\n> **Operator/docs touchpoints.** `checkpoint list --pending` documents **`is_next_checkpoint`** preview semantics; legacy shadow branches are called out for **`entire doctor`** / **`entire clean`**. E2E/debug skills swap “attribution” for **file tracking** language.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 19b37c48aedde9efe68606e4a9ca48b42ae13064. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2692/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2692/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2002\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2002/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2002/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2002/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2002\",\n            \"id\": 5153986234,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7_NqeS\",\n            \"number\": 2002,\n            \"title\": \"perf: stop re-redacting whole transcripts on every checkpoint\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-08-14T17:05:59Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-20T21:05:03Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-20T21:05:00Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2002\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2002\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2002.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2002.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-20T21:05:00Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1053\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nA Stop hook on a 70MB Codex transcript took **~67s**. Profiling `createRedactedBlobFromFile` put redaction at **99.7%** of it (git object writing was 174ms), and the CPU profile put **82%** of that in betterleaks' regex ruleset under Go's NFA engine:\\n\\n```\\nregexp.(*machine).add           43%\\nregexp/syntax.(*Inst).MatchRunePos  22%\\nregexp.(*machine).step          15%\\n  └─ betterleaks/detect.(*Detector).Detect   82% cumulative\\n```\\n\\nTwo independent problems: each pass was single-threaded, and the *whole* transcript was re-redacted on every checkpoint even though `full.jsonl` is append-only — so a session with N checkpoints re-redacted O(N²) bytes. That second part is also why these repos accumulate multi-GB packs.\\n\\n## Result\\n\\nSimulated 14-checkpoint session growing to 70MB:\\n\\n| | final Stop | cumulative |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| main | ~66 s | — |\\n| + sharding | 18.5 s | 1m 40s |\\n| + prefix reuse | **2.0 s** | **31 s** |\\n\\n## Commits\\n\\n**1. `perf(redact)`: shard JSONL line redaction across goroutines**\\n\\nEvery line is redacted in isolation by a stateless redactor, so the line pass splits. Output is byte-identical.\\n\\nShards are sized *by bytes*, not one-per-core, for two measured reasons. Per-byte cost climbs with input size (allocation/GC pressure over one large buffer), so small pieces are cheaper per byte **and** run concurrently — 20MB fixture: 43s sequential vs 2.1s across 12 shards, superlinear in shard count and not explainable by parallelism alone. And balancing by bytes rather than line count matters because transcripts mix thousands of short lines with occasional multi-MB tool results, where equal line counts leave one oversized shard as the tail.\\n\\nSharding is gated on an explicit argument describing the **redactor**, not on which entry point was called. `String` is pure and opts in; the OPF collector closures accumulate into a shared map/slice and opt out. Stating it per call site is what lets `batch.go`'s OPF-disabled fast path — same pure redactor, whole transcript blobs — take the win too, which it silently missed.\\n\\nVerified safe to share: betterleaks' `Detect` path never mutates the shared detector (all mutation is confined to `Run`), and the layer config globals are `sync.Once`/`RWMutex` guarded.\\n\\n**2. `redact`: add `ConfigFingerprint`**\\n\\nHashes what changes the regex layers' output — custom rules (sorted, so map order can't leak) plus PII enablement, categories, and patterns. `configFingerprintVersion` is mixed in and must be bumped when the layers change behaviour, making it part of the pipeline's contract. Documents the two things it cannot cover: OPF (not a pure function of local config) and the betterleaks version (not exposed by the library).\\n\\n**3. `perf(checkpoint)`: reuse the redacted transcript prefix across checkpoints**\\n\\nKeeps the redacted prefix and redacts only what was appended. Soundness rests on two properties:\\n\\n- Redaction is per-line and stateless, so `redact(A+B) == redact(A)+redact(B)` — now pinned by a test in `redact` itself, since this cache is what depends on it\\n- A stored prefix always ends immediately after a newline, so the redacted prefix does too and plain byte concatenation reproduces the full result with no boundary fixups\\n\\nReuse is refused unless the prefix bytes still hash the same **and** the fingerprint matches, so a rewritten or compacted transcript, changed custom rules, or a CLI upgrade all fall back to redacting everything.\\n\\nEligibility keys on `paths.TranscriptFileName`, not a `.jsonl` suffix: only `full.jsonl` is appended to — `transcript.jsonl` is regenerated in full each checkpoint and `full.jsonl.001` chunks aren't appended — so neither qualifies by accident. The cache lives in the git common dir, never under `.entire/`, since anything in the metadata directory gets walked into the checkpoint tree and committed.\\n\\n## Scope limit\\n\\nStated in the code and CLAUDE.md rather than implied: this covers the **shadow-branch metadata write only**. Condensation (`manual_commit_condensation.go`) and the Stop finalize rewrite (`manual_commit_hooks.go`) still redact whole transcripts — they inherit the sharding but not the prefix reuse, so a mid-turn-commit Stop and every user commit still pay a full pass. Extending it there is the obvious follow-up.\\n\\nAlso not covered: single-JSON-value transcripts (OpenCode export) get neither mechanism, having no line structure to split on.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\nTests assert the properties, not the timings. Sharded output equals sequential across a fixture exercising every layer, plus shard boundaries and edge shapes. Incremental output equals a full redaction across repeated appends, and every fallback — rewritten prefix, stale fingerprint, corrupt entry, missing blob, partial trailing line, wrong filename, nil cache — produces exactly what redacting the whole file would.\\n\\n`mise run fmt && lint` clean, `mise run test:ci` green (56 unit + 4 canary), `-race` clean on `redact`, `checkpoint`, `gitrepo`.\\n\\n## Review findings addressed\\n\\nAgent review on the trail found two, both fixed in this PR:\\n\\n- **High — single-JSON-value transcripts must not be spliced.** OpenCode writes a single JSON object to the same `full.jsonl` path other agents write JSONL to, so the filename gate admitted non-line-delimited content. Splicing a fragment of it drops out of the field-aware pass into raw entropy detection over partial JSON. Now gated on `redact.IsLineDelimited`, which checks the invariant directly instead of inferring it from a filename.\\n- **Low — the cache is now reclaimed by `entire clean`.** Wired in as `CleanupTypeRedactCache`; the directory is removed wholesale since every entry is rebuildable.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> <sup>[Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) is generating a summary for commit 8b23e43683396b8855d3d7114971b48644a8c9b0. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2002/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2002/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1666\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1666/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1666/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1666/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1666\",\n            \"id\": 4828978069,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7u2G1w\",\n            \"number\": 1666,\n            \"title\": \"feat(review): live token counts for claude and codex reviewers\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-07-07T13:29:33Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-13T17:30:31Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-13T17:30:29Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1666\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1666\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1666.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1666.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-13T17:30:29Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/788\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nSalvages the live-token slices from closed #1370 (per its disposition comment: \\\"live-token tailing … wanted separately\\\"), rebuilt against current main's parsers rather than cherry-picked — #1370 was based on the old redesign stack.\\n\\n## What\\n\\nReviewer token totals previously appeared only at run completion. This PR makes them move during the run:\\n\\n- **Claude**: assistant stream-json envelopes carry a usage snapshot taken at the start of each turn — input/cache counts are real, but `output_tokens` is a 1–8 token \\\"initial decision\\\" stub that never updates as text streams. The parser now emits input-only `Tokens{In, Out: 0}` per usage-carrying assistant envelope (context growth is honest to show; the misleading output stub is not), with the terminal `result` envelope still delivering the final `{In, Out}` aggregate.\\n- **Codex**: `exec --json` stdout only carries usage on `turn.completed`, and a review is usually a single turn — so a new rollout-transcript tailer (`review_tokens.go`) locates the session's rollout file by `thread.started`'s `thread_id` (the same source codex's interactive UI reads for its live counter) and emits cumulative `Tokens` per `token_count` event, deduped on movement. The parser stops the tailer and waits for it before closing the event channel, so a tailer send can never race the close. `turn.completed` now also emits per-turn (multi-turn runs update at each boundary), keeping the old post-loop emission as a defensive backstop.\\n\\nAll consumers already treat `Tokens` as cumulative-overwrite (\\\"overwrite, don't sum\\\"), which is exactly the contract both sources emit.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- TDD throughout — every behavior change had a failing test first; `-race` clean on the codex package.\\n- New wiring test (`TestParseCodexOutput_StartsRolloutTailerOnThreadStarted`) pins that the parser launches the tailer, receives its Tokens through the real event channel, and shuts it down cleanly on stdout EOF.\\n- End-to-end shim smoke: fake `claude`/`codex` binaries drove `entire review` — claude streaming usage-carrying envelopes, codex writing real rollout `token_count` lines picked up by the tailer — both to clean completion (codex wall time == shim sleep budget, i.e. no shutdown hang).\\n- `mise run fmt` + `lint` clean, full unit suite green (7625 tests).\\n\\n## File adjacency (benign)\\n\\nTouches `claudecode/reviewer.go` and `codex/reviewer.go`, which open PRs #1647 (child context + fan-out) and #1669 (codex skills — absorbed #1655) also modify — but different functions (they touch `buildCmd`/prompt composition; this touches the `parse*Output` paths and adds a new file). Merges are expected to be clean in any order; all three were verified together in the live integration runs.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> <sup>[Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) is generating a summary for commit 5860d3a8c3be8c42cf6485d5d391730ff0a522b2. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1666/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1666/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1806\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1806/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1806/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1806/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1806\",\n            \"id\": 4928141236,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7zzcdy\",\n            \"number\": 1806,\n            \"title\": \"fix(claude-code): target current tool matchers for subagent hooks\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"id\": 881031,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 2,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-07-20T10:41:29Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-20T12:05:54Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-20T12:05:51Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1806\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1806\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1806.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1806.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-20T12:05:51Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Problem\\n\\nOur Claude Code `PreToolUse`/`PostToolUse` hooks are installed under the tool matchers `Task` and `TodoWrite`. On current Claude Code neither matches anything, so a class of checkpoints **silently never fires**:\\n\\n- `pre-task` + `post-task` (matcher `Task`) → no per-subagent checkpoints\\n- `post-todo` (matcher `TodoWrite`) → no incremental checkpoints during subagent runs\\n\\nA bad matcher in Claude Code is a silent no-op — no error, no warning, no changelog entry — which is why this went unnoticed.\\n\\n**Not** data loss for the common single-worktree flow: the `Stop` hook (match-all matcher, unaffected) still checkpoints the whole worktree, so subagent edits are captured — just attributed to the main turn, and without subagent/incremental granularity or metadata.\\n\\n### Source of truth (per docs)\\n\\nThe docs don't phrase this as a \\\"deprecated matcher\\\" — the underlying facts are:\\n\\n- **Subagent tool is `Agent`**, not `Task` (there was never a `Task` tool): [tools-reference.md](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/tools-reference.md) (`Agent` entry), [hooks.md](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks.md) (matcher tool-name list).\\n- **`TodoWrite` disabled by default as of v2.1.142** in favor of `TaskCreate`/`TaskGet`/`TaskList`/`TaskUpdate`: [tools-reference.md](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/tools-reference.md) (`TodoWrite` entry, `min-version: 2.1.142`).\\n- **Matcher evaluation**: a matcher of only letters/digits/`_`/`-`/spaces/`,`/`|` is an exact string (or `|`-list), not a regex — so `Task` does **not** match `TaskCreate`; `TaskCreate|TaskUpdate` matches either exactly: [hooks.md](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks.md) (matcher patterns).\\n\\n> Note: there is no dedicated Claude Code changelog/GH-issue \\\"deprecation\\\" entry for these — the authoritative statements are the tools-reference version notes linked above.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n- Generate matchers `Agent` (pre-task/post-task) and `TaskCreate|TaskUpdate` (post-todo). Fresh installs are correct.\\n- **No in-place migration.** `entire enable` deliberately does **not** rewrite existing hook config as a side effect. Configs written by older versions (stale `Task`/`TodoWrite` entries) are repaired by re-running with **`entire enable --force`**, which already strips and reinstalls Entire hooks.\\n- Tests: positive-spec guard pinning matchers to Claude Code's current tool names; a `--force` reinstall test proving stale matchers are stripped and reinstalled. Integration assertions updated.\\n- Architecture doc updated (points stale-config users at `--force`).\\n\\n## Scope note (see comment)\\n\\nThis fix repairs the Claude Code matchers only. Whether the subagent-checkpoint **granularity** is worth keeping at all is deferred — see the follow-up comment: the product consumes session-level data only, so this output is currently unconsumed, and the machinery is shared across Claude Code / Cursor / Factory Droid / Copilot CLI. Merging keeps behavior consistent without committing to keep the granularity.\\n\\n## Known follow-up (out of scope)\\n\\n`post-todo`'s handler still parses the legacy `TodoWrite` `tool_input` schema for its checkpoint **message label**. Under `TaskCreate`/`TaskUpdate` the checkpoint is still created (file-change detection is independent) but the label falls back to `Checkpoint #N`.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/` ✅\\n- `go test -tags integration -run TestSetupClaudeHooks ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/` ✅\\n- `golangci-lint` (v2.11.3) clean on touched packages ✅\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1806/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1806/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2120\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2120/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2120/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2120/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2120\",\n            \"id\": 5239124589,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABA2gl3A\",\n            \"number\": 2120,\n            \"title\": \"fix(cursor): extract modified files from tool_use blocks\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"jdx\",\n              \"id\": 216188,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjE4OA==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216188?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jdx\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/jdx\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-08-24T20:27:26Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-25T11:29:47Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-25T11:29:46Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2120\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2120\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2120.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2120.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-25T11:29:46Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1139\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## The claim\\n\\nSix places in `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/` stated as established fact that \\\"Cursor transcripts do not contain tool_use blocks\\\". They do.\\n\\nThe claim dates to `366e4eeb6` (2026-03-03, \\\"copilot feedback\\\") and **no test pinned it** — `cursor_test.go` asserted the *consequence* (`ModifiedFiles` is empty), which the stub guaranteed regardless of what Cursor actually wrote. So nothing would catch it becoming false, and nothing did.\\n\\n## The cost\\n\\n`ExtractModifiedFilesFromOffset` returned `nil, 0, nil` *because* of the claim, so every Cursor session fell back to git status and hook-provided `modified_files` while real `Write`/`StrReplace` blocks sat unread in the transcript. A file-attribution gap, not a cosmetic comment problem.\\n\\n## Verified\\n\\nAgainst a real Cursor session: **26 `tool_use` blocks** at `message.content[i].type == \\\"tool_use\\\"`, each with `name` and `input`.\\n\\n| Tool | Input keys | Modifies files |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `Write` | `path`, `contents` | yes |\\n| `StrReplace` | `path`, `old_string`, `new_string` | yes |\\n| `Read` | `path`, optional `limit`, `offset` | no |\\n| `Grep` | `pattern`, `path`, optional `glob`, `head_limit` | no |\\n| `Glob` | `glob_pattern`, `target_directory` | no |\\n| `Shell` | `command`, `description`, optional `working_directory` | unattributable |\\n\\nTwo things beyond the key names: `path` values are **absolute**, and blocks carry **no `id`** field.\\n\\n## Implementation notes\\n\\n- Cursor keys the target file as `path` where Claude Code uses `file_path`, so `transcript.ToolInput` does not fit — hence `cursor.toolInput`. Tool names differ too (`Write`/`StrReplace` vs `Write`/`Edit`), so `FileModificationTools` cannot be shared with `claudecode`.\\n- Absolute paths are what the call sites already expect: `manual_commit_hooks.go` documents that tool_use entries carry absolute paths and normalizes against the worktree root. No Cursor-specific handling needed.\\n- `Shell` is deliberately excluded from `FileModificationTools`. It can obviously modify files, but the transcript records only the command string — attributing files to it would mean parsing shell, not reading a path. Git status stays the backstop, which is now the accurate reason rather than the old one.\\n- A missing transcript stays non-error. Cursor reports `transcript_path` as `null` in CLI mode, so `ResolveSessionFile` predicts a path that may not exist yet, and this runs on capture paths that must fail open (matching `GetTranscriptPosition`).\\n- Adds `transcript.ParseFromFileAtLineWithTotal` so the slice from `startOffset` and the new position come from **one** pass. Parse-then-count would read the file twice on hook paths over transcripts that reach tens of megabytes. `ParseFromFileAtLine` delegates to it, so existing callers are unchanged.\\n\\n## Pinning it this time\\n\\n`testdata/real_session_tool_use.jsonl` — nine lines lifted **verbatim** (diff-verified against the source) from that session, covering one call of each tool, captured against a throwaway repo so the fixture contains nothing sensitive.\\n\\n`TestCursorAgent_RealSessionContainsToolUseBlocks` asserts the **premise**: it reads the fixture and fails if the tool_use blocks are absent, listing which tools and input keys are expected. That is the test whose absence let this sit for five months, and it fails in both directions — if Cursor really did stop emitting tool_use, it says so instead of silently returning nothing.\\n\\n## A seventh site\\n\\nThe audit listed six. There was a seventh: a `summarize` test named `..._CursorNoToolUseBlocks`. Its body only checked a text-only transcript, so it was misleading rather than wrong — renamed to `_CursorTextOnly`.\\n\\nWorth noting it was never a functional gap there: Cursor routes through Claude's parser at `summarize.go:165`, so Cursor tool calls always reached the condensed transcript. Nothing covered it, so `_CursorToolUse` now does, and it passes without any production change.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n\\nThe `ToolInvocationScanner` work is **not** in this PR. That capability, `AsToolInvocationScanner`, and `TestCursorAgent_MustNotImplementToolInvocationScanner` exist only on `jdx/missed-opportunity-signal`, not on `main`.\\n\\nIts blocker is now resolved, though: **Cursor's shell tool is `Shell` and its command key is `command`** — the same key Claude uses, so `ToolInvocation.Command` needs no divergence and nothing has to be guessed. That branch can implement the scanner and delete the must-not test; its entire diff is that one test, so it rebases cleanly onto this.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n`mise run fmt`, `mise run lint` (0 issues), unit tests, 530 integration tests, and the E2E canary all pass.\\n\\nTwo failures in the local tree — `TestCommittedDogfoodSettingsIsCurrent` and `TestCommittedHookConfigsAreCurrent` — are pre-existing and unrelated: they are caused by an uncommitted `.claude/settings.json` edit that was already present, pass with that file reverted, and fail again with it restored. It is not part of this commit.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2120/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2120/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2258\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2258/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2258/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2258/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2258\",\n            \"id\": 5336830693,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCDrMNA\",\n            \"number\": 2258,\n            \"title\": \"Retire the .entire/metadata deny rule and release staged transcripts\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-09-03T12:49:17Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-03T13:55:28Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-03T13:55:25Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2258\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2258\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2258.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2258.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-03T13:55:25Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1230\\r\\n\\r\\nThree related changes to `.entire/metadata`: it turns out to be a staging buffer that nothing ever emptied, and the permission rule guarding it was breaking unattended permission modes for a whole class of ordinary commands.\\r\\n\\r\\n## 1. The staged transcript is released after condensation\\r\\n\\r\\n`clearFilesystemPrompt` removed `prompt.txt` once a session's work was condensed, but nothing ever removed `full.jsonl`. Every session left its full transcript in the worktree permanently, after the content was already committed and pushed.\\r\\n\\r\\nMeasured in one checkout: **460 MB across 392 session directories**, largest single transcript 10.2 MB, with sessions going back nine months. Around 400 of those 1124 files were already dead formats — 168 `context.md` (removed by #572) and 232 `summary.txt` (no code has written it for some time).\\r\\n\\r\\nReleasing it is safe, and I checked each coupling rather than assuming:\\r\\n\\r\\n| Concern | Why it holds |\\r\\n| --- | --- |\\r\\n| Does a continuing session lose data? | No — `lifecycle.go` rewrites the file wholesale from the agent's own transcript on every Stop |\\r\\n| Who reads the on-disk copy? | Only `addDirectoryToChanges` (shadow) and `copyEntireMetadataDir` (v1), both of which run *before* this point, plus `review_context.go` for `prompt.txt`. Every other reader goes through a git tree |\\r\\n| `sessionHasNewContent`? | Compares against the **shadow-tree blob size**, not the file |\\r\\n| Incremental redaction cache? | Keyed by prefix content hash in the git common dir, so it does not depend on this path existing |\\r\\n\\r\\nPrompt and transcript are now released together, because they are one operation under one condition rather than two — the call site's guard is shared for a real reason, since carry-forward files mean both must survive for the next condensation. One directory walk covers all three names instead of one walk per file on the PostCommit hook path.\\r\\n\\r\\n## 2. The `Read(./.entire/metadata/**)` deny rule is retired\\r\\n\\r\\nA `deny` rule is a hard block, not a hint. Per [the permissions docs](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/permissions) (\\\"Read and Edit\\\" section), rules resolve deny → ask → allow, first match wins, and *\\\"a deny rule can't carry allowlist exceptions\\\"* — so there is no way to soften it. The same section states Read deny rules apply *\\\"to file commands Claude Code recognizes in Bash, such as `cat`, `head`, `tail`, and `sed`\\\"*, so a recursive grep from the repo root is refused and has to be approved by hand. Auto mode's classifier only sees actions that would *prompt*, never a block, so it cannot get past this.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe match is broader than \\\"commands that read those files\\\": `git check-ignore -v .entire/metadata` is refused, and it reads nothing. Naming the path is enough.\\r\\n\\r\\nIt also protected less than it appeared to:\\r\\n\\r\\n- It guarded a **staging buffer**, not a store. The durable copy lives in the checkpoint tree, which no permission rule covers — the same transcripts are readable with `git show entire/checkpoints/v1:...`.\\r\\n- `.entire/.gitignore` already lists `metadata/`, and [the tools reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/tools-reference) says *\\\"Grep respects `.gitignore`, so gitignored files are skipped\\\"* — so the accidental-bulk-read case was already covered. Glob does not honor gitignore, but Glob returns names, not content.\\r\\n\\r\\nDeliberately **not** replaced with a `PreToolUse` hook on `Read`: that fires a subprocess for every file the agent reads, on a hook path that already dominates turn cost.\\r\\n\\r\\n## How an existing repo heals\\r\\n\\r\\nThere is no per-repo \\\"the CLI was upgraded\\\" trigger — `curl-bash-post-install` only does shell completion and runs outside a repo, and `versioncheck` only notifies. So healing needed a deliberate shape:\\r\\n\\r\\n| Tier | Behavior |\\r\\n| --- | --- |\\r\\n| `entire doctor` | Detects and repairs. **This is the one that heals an existing repo** |\\r\\n| SessionStart hook | Reports it and points at `entire doctor`. **Writes nothing** |\\r\\n| `entire agent add <agent>` | Reaches `InstallHooks`, so it also removes it |\\r\\n| `entire enable` | Removes it on a *fresh* enable only — see the caveat below |\\r\\n\\r\\n**Caveat on `enable`, found while verifying:** removal inside `InstallHooks` is unconditional (no `--force` needed), but `enable` itself returns early with \\\"Entire is already enabled\\\" before it ever reaches `InstallHooks`. So the `enable` tier does not fire for an already-enabled repo — which is exactly the population carrying the stale rule. That is why the SessionStart notice points at `doctor` rather than at `enable`, and `doctor` is the tier I verified end to end. Making `enable` re-run installers on an already-enabled repo is a broader behavior change I did not want to make here.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe hook deliberately does not repair. The agent's config is normally tracked in git (this repo tracks `.claude/settings.json`), so a hook editing it would dirty the worktree unprompted, could land the edit in the user's next checkpoint commit, and would ping-pong across a team on mixed CLI versions.\\r\\n\\r\\nRemoval matches only the exact string Entire wrote, so a user's own deny rules are untouched, and an emptied `deny` array is dropped rather than left behind as `{}`.\\r\\n\\r\\n## One judgment call to confirm\\r\\n\\r\\n`checkRetiredDenyRule` is the only doctor check that **repairs without asking**. My reasoning is ownership — it deletes only a byte-identical copy of a string Entire itself wrote — but it does modify a git-tracked file, and that is a product call rather than mine. Moving it behind doctor's `--force` is a one-line change if you would rather it asked.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Not covered\\r\\n\\r\\n**The 460 MB already on disk is not reclaimed.** This only prevents future growth; existing sessions keep their transcripts because nothing revisits an already-condensed session. Reclaiming them wants the same doctor-tier treatment over `FullyCondensed` sessions, with its own safety question about which sessions are provably done. Happy to follow up.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Separate pre-existing gap, found while verifying:** `agentHookState.unchecked` (`config.go:228`) is populated but has no consumer anywhere, so a repo with an unparseable `.claude/settings.json` gets \\\"Git hooks: OK\\\" from `entire doctor` and no mention of the broken file. Not introduced here, but it is why an error branch I first wrote turned out to be unreachable. Probably worth its own issue.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Test plan\\r\\n\\r\\n- `mise run fmt && mise run lint` → 0 issues; `mise run test:ci` passes (unit + integration + Vogon canary)\\r\\n- New: `permissions_test.go` covers removal, near-miss rules left alone, duplicates, unparseable `deny`, sibling-key preservation, and that the detector does not mutate\\r\\n- New: `TestPermissionConfigOwner_*` exercises the repair path end to end through the real agent — including idempotency and an absent config\\r\\n- Flipped: the install/uninstall tests in both agents now assert the rule is *removed* rather than installed, plus a migration test for a config an older CLI wrote and a safety test that user rules survive\\r\\n- Verified by hand against a scratch repo: `enable` clears it; `doctor` fixes it, is idempotent, preserves `Bash(rm -rf *)` and `allow`, and drops the whole `permissions` block when the rule was its only entry; SessionStart prints the notice and leaves the file byte-identical\\r\\n\\r\\nReviewed for reuse, simplification, efficiency, and altitude before opening — that pass merged the two release functions into one single-walk operation, removed a redundant `Exists()` stat from the SessionStart path, made doctor read the config once instead of twice, and deleted one unreachable branch.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Addressed from review\\r\\n\\r\\nThe trail finding and Copilot both caught the same real bug from different angles: `RemoveMetadataDenyRule` clears the `deny` key but cannot delete the `permissions` key containing it, since it is handed only the inner object — and while `UninstallHooks` and `RepairRetiredMetadataDenyRule` both delete an emptied block, the two `InstallHooks` write paths did not. A plain install that stripped the last deny rule left `\\\"permissions\\\": {}` behind, and this PR's own `.claude/settings.json` diff was the evidence. Both write paths now delete the key when the block is empty, verified against a fresh repo (Entire-owned config loses the key entirely; a config with a user's `allow`/`deny` rules keeps them and loses only the retired rule). The doc comment no longer claims a cleanup that belongs to its callers.\\r\\n\\r\\nAlso fixed two references left stale by the earlier merge of the two release functions: a comment naming `RemoveNoSymlinks`, which that code no longer calls, and the hook docs still naming `clearFilesystemPrompt`.\\r\\n\\r\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\r\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2258/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2258/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2034\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2034/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2034/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2034/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2034\",\n            \"id\": 5179300738,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABAHKkFQ\",\n            \"number\": 2034,\n            \"title\": \"feat: link mid-task background-subagent commits to their session\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-08-18T07:32:46Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-24T17:02:33Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-24T17:02:26Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2034\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2034\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2034.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2034.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-24T17:02:26Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1077\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## The incident\\n\\nBackground Claude Code subagents run `git commit` between the parent session's turns. `tryAgentCommitFastPath` (the prepare-commit-msg fast path) only trusted **ACTIVE** sessions; between turns the session is IDLE, so the fast path declined, and the slow content-detection path then found no evidence linking the commit to the session (the subagent's work wasn't in the parent's shadow baseline). The commit shipped with no `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer at all. On a real subagent-driven feature branch, six of seven commits went unlinked this way.\\n\\n## The design (after merging #2032's durable-record model)\\n\\n1. **Trigger (idle + task content).** `tryAgentCommitFastPath` now treats a session as eligible when it's ACTIVE **or** IDLE with a fresh task record (`idleWithTaskContent`, `strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go`). A record counts whether it's still in flight or completed-but-unmaterialized — the same `HasTaskContent()` shapes condensation keys on — and each record is bounded by its own `StartedAt` against `activeSessionInteractionThreshold` (24h), so a subagent that dies without ever sending `SubagentStop`/`SessionEnd` doesn't leave the session a trailer candidate forever. The same predicate feeds `shouldCondenseWithOverlapCheck`'s overlap-check bypass, so the trigger and the condensation trust share one rule.\\n2. **Content (the condensation materializer).** The base branch (#2032, issue #2058) made `session.TaskRecord` a durable ledger: condensation materializes each record's transcript-so-far into the checkpoint's `tasks/<tool-use-id>/{agent-<agent-id>.jsonl, task.json}` subtree, live records survive for the next condensation, and every checkpoint is self-contained. That means the trailer this PR adds is backed by content *by construction*: the very condensation the trailer triggers stores the subagent's transcript-so-far. The earlier revision of this PR pre-wrote a commit-time transcript snapshot (`captureInFlightTaskCommitSnapshot` / `captureInFlightTasksForCommit`) gated on `headHasCheckpointTrailer` to keep the trailer from dangling — all of that is now removed as redundant, along with its tests and post-commit wiring.\\n\\n## Overlap-trust scoping\\n\\n`idleWithTaskContent` is deliberately scoped to `PhaseIdle` only, not `PhaseEnded`. An earlier version leaked the overlap-check bypass to ended sessions too; that shape was empirically reproduced and fixed (`fe2aa5fdb`), with a regression test pinning that an ended session with a lingering record still declines — its records belong to its own final condensation, not this fast path.\\n\\n## The trade-off\\n\\nBecause eligibility is keyed off a no-TTY commit plus a fresh task record, the trust window spans the entire lifetime of a background task — including raw-mode TUI git clients (lazygit, gitui, tig) that spawn `git commit` without a real terminal. This means an unrelated no-TTY commit made while a background task happens to still be running could get mislinked. We accept this: a mislink is recoverable (and rare — it requires a fresh record plus an unrelated no-TTY commit in the same narrow window), while a silent unlink is not. Records are genuine evidence of live agent work, not a guess. The window is also narrower than it used to be: the base branch's dead-owner sweep completes a crashed agent's records, so orphaned records no longer linger for the full 24h in the common case.\\n\\n## Non-regression pins\\n\\n- An ordinary commit made while IDLE with **no** task records stays exactly as before: no trailer (`TestSubagentCheckpoints_IdleCommitNoMarkers_NoTrailer`).\\n- Record-less behavior (foreground tasks, ACTIVE-session commits) is byte-identical to pre-PR behavior — the new eligibility branch is additive.\\n- The end-to-end arbiter, `TestSubagentCheckpoints_CommitWhileIdleWithLiveMarker_LinksAndCondensesContent`, drives the real prepare-commit-msg + post-commit hook chain and now asserts the strong guarantee: the mid-task commit's condensed checkpoint **contains `tasks/<id>/agent-<id>.jsonl` with the subagent's real transcript content** (stronger than the previous revision, which could only check the pre-written shadow-side snapshot).\\n\\n## Known gaps / follow-ups\\n\\n1. ~~**Pre-existing orphan-prune gap.**~~ **Fixed by #2032.** `findSessionsForWorktree`'s orphan sweep now spares record-bearing sessions (`!state.HasTaskContent()` in the prune predicate), so an idle session whose only activity is one open task record survives to `prepare-commit-msg` — a first-turn background commit links. The integration test's read-only seed-task workaround has been removed accordingly.\\n2. ~~**Sweep-finalize follow-up.**~~ **Fixed by #2032.** `finalizeExitedSessions` now completes a dead-owner session's live records (`sweepCompleteLiveTaskRecords`, `session_finalize.go`) before ending it, exactly as a clean SessionEnd does — preserving transcripts and closing the trust-window trade-off from the other end.\\n3. **Identity/ancestry discovery** (linking a commit to a session by content/authorship signals beyond records) composes into the same fast-path loop later, via #2013. Out of scope here.\\n\\n## Trailer eligibility is bounded; condensability is not\\n\\nA session's task records make it condensable with no freshness bound — that is deliberate, and it is what keeps a stale record's transcript-so-far from being stranded unmaterialized. Claiming a commit is bounded separately: only a record within `idleWithTaskContent`'s 24h window may mint a trailer. Without that split, an IDLE session whose only content was a >24h record got a trailer from the slow path and was then refused by PostCommit, leaving `Entire-Checkpoint` pointing at a checkpoint nothing ever wrote — on an unrelated human commit. Two reviewers reproduced it end to end; `staleRecordIsOnlyContent` closes it, and PostCommit now warns whenever a trailer is minted and no session condenses into it, so any future divergence is visible rather than silent.\\n\\nAn earlier revision of this PR also exempted record-bearing sessions from PostCommit's read-only skip. That is reverted: the skip only fires when another session's files are in the commit, and PostCommit hands one checkpoint ID to every condensing session, so that other session fills the trailer anyway. The exemption prevented no dangling trailer and only let a record-bearing session condense into someone else's commit.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] `mise run fmt && mise run lint` — clean\\n- [x] `mise run test:ci` — unit + integration green, Vogon canary + roger-roger E2E 4/4\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2034/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2034/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1977\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1977/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1977/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1977/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1977\",\n            \"id\": 5136120550,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7-UKLC\",\n            \"number\": 1977,\n            \"title\": \"fix(hooks): bound the agent-hook status walk so pathological repos degrade instead of hanging\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-08-12T23:11:56Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-20T12:42:05Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-20T12:42:04Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1977\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1977\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1977.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1977.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-20T12:42:03Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1033\\r\\n\\r\\n## Motivation\\r\\n\\r\\nLive incident (2026-08-12): a stray `git init` in a user's `$HOME` (no `.gitignore`) meant every agent Stop hook ran a worktree status walk over the entire home directory. The hook hung >120s; Claude Code stopped waiting at its ~60s hook timeout, but the `entire hooks claude-code stop` **process survived** — two zombies were found hours later at ~1.8GB RSS each, one with 25 CPU-minutes, still writing loose objects (200k+ files) into the repo. The failure was completely silent: no session state, no checkpoint, no log line — the session looked tracked. Trail finding `019ff792-3b10-72af-96d1-ddb7a7874064` on the feat/global-invisible trail documents it; this PR is the fix. The hazard exists on main today for any enabled repo with pathological status cost; global enable amplifies it by lazily enrolling uncurated repos.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Fix shape\\r\\n\\r\\ngo-git's `Worktree.Status()` (the single sanctioned call site in `gitrepo/status.go`) is **not context-cancellable**, so the budget is a goroutine+select wrapper, `gitrepo.StatusWithBudget`:\\r\\n\\r\\n- **20s wall-clock budget** (`gitrepo.StatusWalkBudget`): far beyond any healthy repo's walk, while leaving the remaining ~40s of the agent's ~60s hook timeout for the rest of the capture path (transcript copy, tree building, state writes) so the hook exits instead of being orphaned. No new user-facing setting.\\r\\n- **On breach**: the walk goroutine is abandoned (it dies with the one-shot hook process — that is the point; a `recover` guard keeps an orphaned walk from crashing the hook if the caller closes the repo under it), and the returned error wraps the sentinel `gitrepo.ErrStatusBudgetExceeded`. Context cancellation is treated the same way — it arms the latch and carries the sentinel (with `ctx.Err()` still in the chain) — so a walk abandoned by cancellation cannot fail the hook hard or defeat the fail-open guarantee.\\r\\n- **Actionable Warn** at breach names the repo root, elapsed, budget, and consequence (\\\"capture degraded: untracked/new file detection skipped this turn\\\") so `doctor logs` investigation finds it. Operational metadata only.\\r\\n- **Zombie prevention**: a process-local latch makes every later `StatusWithBudget` call in the same hook process fail fast — the turn-start hook walks twice (pre-prompt capture + prompt attribution), and re-entering the walk after a breach is exactly what kept the incident processes alive.\\r\\n- **The C-git half of the zombie**: the first-checkpoint path in the checkpoint store runs `git status --porcelain -z -uall` as a subprocess with no deadline, so after a go-git breach the hook could still get stuck in a child git instead of a goroutine. That subprocess is now bounded by the same `StatusWalkBudget` via `context.WithTimeout` (`exec.CommandContext` kills the child on expiry) and reports the same sentinel; the lifecycle handlers recognize it and warn-and-skip the checkpoint instead of failing the hook.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Call sites bounded (agent-hook paths)\\r\\n\\r\\n- `DetectFileChanges` (turn-end, subagent-end, Claude PostTodo) — errors were already Warn-and-continue.\\r\\n- Pre-prompt / pre-task untracked scans (`CapturePrePromptState` / `CapturePreTaskState`) — these previously **failed the hook** on status error; they now fail open (hooks must never break the agent) and record an `UntrackedScanSkipped` marker in the state file.\\r\\n- Prompt-attribution walk in `calculatePromptAttributionAtStart` — already fully fail-open; now also fails fast via the latch after a pre-prompt breach.\\r\\n- First-checkpoint `git status` subprocess in `checkpoint/ephemeral.go` (`collectChangedFiles`), reached via `SaveStep` — bounded as above; `handleLifecycleTurnEnd` treats the sentinel from a save as warn-and-skip (hook exits 0), and its turn-end tail (LastPrompt backfill, phase transition, pre-prompt cleanup) still runs on that degrade path. The matching branch in `handleLifecycleSubagentEnd` is defensive symmetry, not a live path: task saves write via `writeTask`, which reads no worktree status today. The go-git walk budget and this C-git budget deliberately stack (~40s worst case of the ~60s hook timeout) rather than sharing the breach latch — C git is much faster and honors ignores, so it often produces a real first checkpoint where the go-git walk breached, and unlike the walk it is reliably killed on expiry.\\r\\n\\r\\nLeft unbounded deliberately: `checkCanRewindWithWarning` (rewind machinery, no CLI surface), review-worktree removal, and `entire session adopt` — a user is actively waiting on those commands, they are not hook paths, and a slow-but-healthy repo (NFS, cold cache) should finish rather than error at the budget. Adopt originally inherited the budget through `DetectFileChanges`; it now uses an explicit unbounded variant (`detectFileChangesUnbounded`) so the budget stays a hook-path property. Git-hook paths (post-commit condensation) never call Status.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Degradation semantics\\r\\n\\r\\nOn breach, capture proceeds with transcript-derived files. New-file detection is skipped for the turn: the `UntrackedScanSkipped` marker tells turn-end/subagent-end to drop `changes.New`, because without a pre-prompt baseline every untracked file in the worktree would be misattributed to the agent. This matters precisely in the cross-process shape — turn start breaches (marker written), turn end runs in a fresh process whose walk succeeds — and is covered by dedicated tests that fail if either guard is removed. Modified/deleted detection degrades to nil alongside the status error, as before. A breach inside the save itself (the C-git first-checkpoint read) skips that checkpoint with a Warn and still exits 0.\\r\\n\\r\\nOne deliberate widening beyond the budget feature: the pre-prompt/pre-task untracked scans now fail open on **any** error (repo-open failure, corrupted `.git`, …), not just budget breaches. Previously any status error there failed the TurnStart/SubagentStart hook and broke the agent's turn; that fail-hook behavior was the bug — the scan only feeds new-file detection, so the correct degrade is warn + marker + transcript-derived capture. The code comment at `untrackedFilesOrSkip` states this explicitly.\\r\\n\\r\\nDegradation is visible outside `.entire/logs`: turn end persists `SessionState.CaptureDegradedAt` when any status scan feeding the turn breached (marker, `DetectFileChanges` sentinel, or a breach inside the save), and clears it on the next healthy turn. `entire status` prints a per-session warning (\\\"capture degraded …: status scan over budget; new-file detection skipped\\\") and `entire status --json` carries `capture_degraded` on the session brief, so a repo that breaches every turn no longer reports a healthy session while new-file detection is silently off.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Tests\\r\\n\\r\\n- `TestStatusWithBudget_BreachAbandonsWalkPromptly` — breach surfaces the sentinel at the budget (not when the walk ends) and the latch stops a second walk from starting; pins the zombie regression.\\r\\n- `TestStatusWithBudget_BreachWarnsWithRepoRoot` — the breach Warn carries the `repo_root` attribute (the incident was silent; this pins the observability).\\r\\n- `TestTurnFlow_StatusBudgetBreachDegradesGracefully` — same-process shape: full turn-start + turn-end with the latch set; both hooks return success and the checkpoint contains the transcript-derived file.\\r\\n- `TestHandleLifecycleTurnEnd_ScanSkippedMarkerSkipsNewFileDetection` / `TestHandleLifecycleSubagentEnd_ScanSkippedMarkerSkipsNewFileDetection` — cross-process shape: marker written under a breach, end-hook walk succeeds; the checkpoint must not claim pre-existing untracked files. Verified by mutation: deleting either `changes.New` guard fails the corresponding test.\\r\\n- `TestCollectChangedFiles_BudgetExceededReturnsSentinel` — the first-checkpoint `git status` subprocess had no deadline and could outlive the agent's hook timeout; on expiry the error must wrap `gitrepo.ErrStatusBudgetExceeded` so the lifecycle warn-and-skip path recognizes it.\\r\\n- `TestStatusWithBudget_CancellationArmsLatchAndCarriesSentinel` — a walk abandoned by context cancellation must degrade like a timer breach (sentinel carried, latch armed) while `context.Canceled` stays in the error chain.\\r\\n- `TestHandleLifecycleTurnEnd_SaveBreachStillBackfillsLastPrompt` — a breach inside the save must still run the turn-end tail: checkpoint skipped, hook exits 0, LastPrompt backfilled, `CaptureDegradedAt` persisted.\\r\\n- The marker tests above also pin `CaptureDegradedAt` being set on a degraded turn and cleared by the next healthy one.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Verification\\r\\n\\r\\n- `mise run fmt` + `mise run lint` — clean (lint rerun after fmt, 0 issues)\\r\\n- `mise run test` — 8816 tests passed\\r\\n- `mise run test:integration` — 472 tests passed\\r\\n- `mise run test:e2e:canary` — all 56 + 4 tests passed\\r\\n\\r\\n## Merge note\\r\\n\\r\\nMerging with `feat/global-agent-hooks` needs a small manual conflict resolution in `lifecycle.go` (~569–596, the `handleLifecycleTurnStart` region); `feat/session-binding` conflicts only on the import block.\\r\\n\\r\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\r\\n\\r\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1977/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1977/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1443\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1443/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1443/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1443/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1443\",\n            \"id\": 4683117560,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7ndvck\",\n            \"number\": 1443,\n            \"title\": \"git_operations: stop shallow-fetching the metadata tip (root-cause fix for shallow-metadata false-disconnect)\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-06-17T12:14:40Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-22T12:25:01Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-06-19T14:52:10Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1443\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1443\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1443.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1443.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-06-19T14:52:10Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/578\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n`FetchMetadataTreeOnly` resolves the latest checkpoint on `resume` / `explain` / `attach` by fetching the `entire/checkpoints/v1` tip with `--depth=1`. A depth-1 fetch adds the fetched commit to `.git/shallow`. Once the metadata tip is a shallow boundary, a later `git merge-base` against `refs/remotes/origin/entire/checkpoints/v1` can't reach the real common ancestor (it lives below the boundary), so the disconnection check falsely reports **\\\"no common ancestor\\\"** — aborting `git push` and looping `entire doctor`.\\n\\nThis is the **upstream source** of the shallow-metadata false-disconnect. It's self-inflicted by the CLI's own tip-read, which runs on essentially every `entire resume` when checkpoints live on `origin` (no `checkpoint_remote` to short-circuit it via `getMetadataTree`). The user never has to clone shallowly — the CLI shallows the branch for them.\\n\\n### Why not \\\"fetch the tip into a throwaway ref\\\"?\\n\\nThe shallow boundary is **intrinsic to `--depth=1`**: it truncates the fetched *commit*, regardless of which ref it lands on, and git (2.54) opportunistically points `refs/remotes/origin/<branch>` at that commit anyway (verified against `--refmap=`, fetch-by-URL, FETCH_HEAD-only, and `-c remote.origin.fetch=`). You cannot read a tip via `--depth=1` without creating a shallow boundary on the shared object store.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nStop shallow-fetching. `FetchMetadataTreeOnly` now fetches the metadata commit+tree graph at **full depth**, relying on `--filter=blob:none` (when filtered fetches are enabled) to skip blob content instead of on depth-limiting. No shallow boundary is ever created, so `refs/remotes/origin/<branch>` stays connected and `merge-base` works.\\n\\n`git fetch` is incremental, so after the first fetch only new commits/trees travel — the cheapness now comes from blob filtering + incremental fetch rather than from truncating history.\\n\\n## Test\\n\\n`TestFetchMetadataTreeOnly_DoesNotShallowRepo` seeds a 2-commit metadata branch, runs the tip-read on a clone, and asserts the repo is **not** shallow afterward (`--is-shallow-repository=false`), full history is present, and the local primary ref is advanced. Under the old `--depth=1` behavior the repo would be shallow.\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- Repos with a configured `checkpoint_remote` were never affected (that path short-circuits before the shallow fetch and is already full-depth).\\n- Complements the detection-side hardening in #1434 (`IsMetadataDisconnected` shallow-awareness + `doctor` deepen); this PR removes the source so the boundary isn't created in the first place.\\n- Unit + relevant integration tests (`filtered_fetches` enabled) pass.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes default fetch behavior on a hot path (resume/explain/attach), which can increase first-fetch work on repos without blob filtering, but fixes incorrect disconnect detection tied to git shallow state.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **`FetchMetadataTreeOnly`** (used on resume/explain/attach to read the latest checkpoint) no longer uses **`--depth=1`**. It fetches the metadata branch at **full commit/tree depth** and stays cheap via **`--filter=blob:none`** when filtered fetches are on, instead of truncating history.\\n> \\n> That removes the root cause where a depth-1 fetch wrote a shallow boundary and later **`git merge-base`** / **`strategy.IsMetadataDisconnected`** falsely reported no common ancestor—blocking push and looping **`entire doctor`**.\\n> \\n> The **`Shallow`** option is dropped from **`fetchMetadataOpts`**. **`TestFetchMetadataTreeOnly_DoesNotShallowRepo`** asserts the clone stays non-shallow, keeps two metadata commits, and advances the local primary ref to the origin tip.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit ebe73db181081df993c7cee1f826c2a7eba815f7. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1443/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1443/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1248\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1248/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1248/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1248/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1248\",\n            \"id\": 4497918302,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7eG0W0\",\n            \"number\": 1248,\n            \"title\": \"Improve `cherryPickOnto` performance\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"pjbgf\",\n              \"id\": 5452977,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NTI5Nzc=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5452977?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pjbgf\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-05-21T21:07:25Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-22T10:18:04Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-05-22T10:18:02Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1248\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1248\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1248.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1248.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-05-22T10:18:02Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/412\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nRefactoring for performance, dropping from `~66s` to `~7s` the handling of 50 commits for the current `cli-checkpoints` repository.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Before\\r\\n<img width=\\\"2203\\\" height=\\\"607\\\" alt=\\\"image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fe68c693-4b04-4f1a-b7b3-0d1e08437a32\\\" />\\r\\n\\r\\n### After\\r\\n\\r\\n<img width=\\\"2205\\\" height=\\\"854\\\" alt=\\\"image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/feeae5ac-10c9-49eb-9950-cd42946a102d\\\" />\\r\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes core metadata reconciliation/cherry-pick logic to use go-git tree diffs and incremental tree updates; mistakes here could drop or misapply checkpoint files during repair flows. Dependency bumps to `go-git` also change underlying diff semantics.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Refactors metadata branch reconciliation’s `cherryPickOnto` to avoid full tree flatten/merge per commit: it now computes a commit’s parent→child tree diff via `object.DiffTreeContext`, converts it to `checkpoint.TreeChange`s, and applies them with `checkpoint.ApplyTreeChanges`.\\n> \\n> Adds helpers `treeChangesForCherryPick`/`changeToTreeChange` (handling insert/modify/delete via `merkletrie`) and updates dependencies (`go-git`/`go-billy`, `golang.org/x/net`) to support this faster diff-based approach.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit fb3313263f985e75b8450cbeeb5e2a4903d8207d. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1248/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1248/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1091\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1091/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1091/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1091/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1091\",\n            \"id\": 4362027422,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7XTSpg\",\n            \"number\": 1091,\n            \"title\": \"Fix v2 checkpoint migration generation packing\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"pfleidi\",\n              \"id\": 118549,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjExODU0OQ==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118549?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pfleidi\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-05-01T00:07:13Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-01T21:32:45Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-05-01T21:32:43Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1091\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1091\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1091.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1091.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-05-01T21:32:43Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/275\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What\\n- Pack migrated v1 checkpoints into v2 archived full generations chronologically, so lower generation refs contain older migrated checkpoints.\\n- Repair archived v2 generation metadata for already-migrated repositories without renumbering refs or recopying transcripts.\\n- Keep force migration and rerun repair paths consistent by pruning stale archived generations and repacking only missing raw full artifacts.\\n\\n## How\\n- Sort migratable checkpoints oldest-first, write v2/main, then build archived v2/full generation refs directly from sorted batches.\\n- Recompute archived generation timestamp envelopes from raw transcripts and update local/remote refs with lease-aware pushes.\\n- Add cleanup and migration coverage for chronological packing, generation repair, stale archived refs, partial repairs, and idempotent reruns.\\n\\n## Verification\\n- mise run check\\n- mise run lint\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches checkpoint migration/cleanup logic and rewrites archived `refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/full/*` refs (including optional remote pushes with `--force-with-lease`), so bugs could corrupt or delete retained transcript generations if edge cases are missed.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Fixes v2 checkpoint migration so migrated v1 checkpoints are **packed into archived v2 `/full/<n>` generations in oldest-first order** and `/full/current` is left empty/ready for post-migration writes, rather than relying on incremental writes that could invert generation ordering.\\n> \\n> Adds a new **archived generation metadata repair** flow that recomputes `generation.json` timestamp envelopes from raw transcript timestamps (falling back to checkpoint metadata/generation.json) and can update remote-only archived refs via lease-guarded pushes; `migrate --checkpoints v2` now runs this repair and fails if any generations can’t be repaired.\\n> \\n> Updates retention cleanup to determine v2 generation age from **raw transcript timestamps** (with safer remote candidate tracking), refactors v2 generation timestamp computation to be reusable (`ComputeGenerationTimestampsFromTrees`, exported `NextGenerationNumber`/`MergeGenerationTime`), and expands tests to cover chronological packing, rerun/force pruning of archived generations, task-metadata merge behavior, and metadata repair.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit fb658bc754d848d827cb467f9ab7eaef272fd8b3. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1091/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1091/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1097\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1097/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1097/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1097/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1097\",\n            \"id\": 4367285152,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7XkACA\",\n            \"number\": 1097,\n            \"title\": \"docs(security): refresh security-and-privacy.md against current source\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-05-02T00:38:32Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-04T15:11:49Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-05-04T15:11:46Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1097\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1097\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1097.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1097.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-05-04T15:11:46Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nBring \\\\`docs/security-and-privacy.md\\\\` back in sync with current code. Two scopes in one PR:\\n\\n### Fix outdated claims\\n\\n- **Shadow branches \\\"without redaction\\\" → defense-in-depth.** Shadow-branch writes go through \\\\`redact.JSONLBytes\\\\` per \\\\`cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/temporary.go:319\\\\` (incremental checkpoint), \\\\`:390\\\\` (subagent transcripts), and \\\\`:925\\\\` (metadata blob helper). Restate as: writes are redacted; the branches are local-only and not pushed; don't push manually anyway.\\n- **Five-layer enumeration was incomplete.** The String() function comment at \\\\`redact/redact.go:157-164\\\\` documents 6 passes (5 always-on + 1 opt-in PII). Acknowledge the optional sixth pass and link to the new section.\\n- **Betterleaks key-block list missed OpenSSH.** Tests at \\\\`redact/redact_test.go:701-744\\\\` verify OpenSSH PRIVATE KEY blocks are caught.\\n- **Placeholder handling described too vaguely.** Replace \\\"ignores common placeholder values\\\" with the actual exact-match list (\\\\`changeme\\\\`, \\\\`example\\\\`, \\\\`placeholder\\\\`, \\\\`your_password\\\\`, \\\\`your_secret\\\\`, prior \\\\`REDACTED\\\\` markers) and the shape rules (\\\\`\\\\${VAR}\\\\`, \\\\`<name>\\\\` brackets, mask runs of \\\\`*\\\\`/\\\\`x\\\\`/\\\\`.\\\\`/\\\\`-\\\\` length 3+). Source: \\\\`redact/redact.go\\\\` \\\\`isPlaceholderSecretValue\\\\`, \\\\`isBracketedPlaceholder\\\\`, \\\\`isRepeatedCharPlaceholder\\\\`.\\n- **JSONL skip rules omitted structural-path fields.** Source includes \\\\`filepath\\\\`, \\\\`file_path\\\\`, \\\\`cwd\\\\`, \\\\`root\\\\`, \\\\`directory\\\\`, \\\\`dir\\\\`, \\\\`path\\\\` per \\\\`redact/redact.go:680-699\\\\`.\\n\\n### Add missing coverage\\n\\n- **Optional PII redaction section** — full opt-in layer per \\\\`redact/pii.go\\\\` and \\\\`cmd/entire/cli/strategy/common.go:344-374\\\\`. Three built-in categories (email/phone default on, address default off), email allowlist (\\\\`noreply@\\\\`, \\\\`actions@\\\\`, \\\\`@users.noreply.github.com\\\\`, \\\\`@noreply.github.com\\\\`), \\\\`custom_patterns\\\\` API with worked example, settings JSON snippet, and a note about \\\\`.entire/settings.json\\\\` (team-shared, public-on-push) vs \\\\`.entire/settings.local.json\\\\` (gitignored, personal).\\n- **Telemetry section** — PostHog endpoint with \\\\`DisableGeoIP\\\\` enabled, captured fields, what's not captured, three opt-out paths. Source: \\\\`cmd/entire/cli/telemetry/detached.go\\\\`.\\n- **Reporting a vulnerability** — cross-reference to \\\\`SECURITY.md\\\\` at the repo root.\\n- **Related links** — the checkpoint-signing architecture doc and a one-line external-agent-plugin trust reminder.\\n\\n## Discovered while\\n\\nWriting the corresponding public security docs at https://github.com/entireio/docs/pull/33. The public page is the user-facing version (with accordions, more depth); this CLI-repo doc is the focused reference for people reading the source. Both should agree on the load-bearing facts. After this PR they do.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [ ] No code changes; doc only. \\\\`docs/security-and-privacy.md\\\\` grew from 52 → 108 lines.\\n- [ ] All claims grounded in current source via the file/line refs in the commit messages.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Documentation-only changes; no runtime behavior is modified. Risk is limited to potential user confusion if any of the updated security guidance is inaccurate.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Refreshes `docs/security-and-privacy.md` to match current CLI behavior, clarifying what is stored on `entire/checkpoints/v1` vs local shadow branches and explicitly noting that source snapshots on shadow branches are unredacted.\\n> \\n> Documents an **opt-in** PII redaction layer (`redaction.pii`) alongside always-on secret redaction, expands/clarifies redaction details (OpenSSH key blocks, placeholder handling, JSONL skip fields), and adds new sections for **telemetry** (what’s collected and opt-out paths) and vulnerability reporting/related security links.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 009d90d6b87fffef7f836ce6c501b22e6e1c0819. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1097/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1097/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/407\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/407/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/407/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/407/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/407\",\n            \"id\": 3956971106,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7Eku_m\",\n            \"number\": 407,\n            \"title\": \"perf: optimize stop hook - transcript parsing and tree updates\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"yasunogithub\",\n              \"id\": 29519029,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NTE5MDI5\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29519029?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/yasunogithub\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/yasunogithub\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/yasunogithub/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/yasunogithub/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/yasunogithub/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/yasunogithub/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/yasunogithub/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/yasunogithub/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/yasunogithub/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/yasunogithub/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/yasunogithub/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [\n              {\n                \"id\": 9924477906,\n                \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACT4uD0g\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/enhancement\",\n                \"name\": \"enhancement\",\n                \"color\": \"a2eeef\",\n                \"default\": true,\n                \"description\": \"New feature or request\",\n                \"archived_at\": null,\n                \"archived_by\": null\n              }\n            ],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 2,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-02-18T09:56:35Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-04-07T15:46:53Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-04-07T15:46:52Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/407\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/407\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/407.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/407.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\n- **Transcript parsing 3x → 1x:** `commitWithMetadata()` was parsing the same transcript file three times (for prompt extraction, modified file detection, and token usage calculation). Added `FromLines` variants that accept pre-parsed `[]TranscriptLine`, eliminating redundant file I/O and JSON parsing.\\n\\n- **Incremental git tree updates:** `buildTreeWithChanges()` and `addTaskMetadataToTree()` previously flattened the entire git tree (O(N) total files) then rebuilt from scratch. Replaced with `applyChangesToTree()` which traverses only directories containing changes — unchanged subtrees are reused by hash. Complexity: O(changed_files × tree_depth).\\n\\n- **Hook binary fallback:** Switched `.claude/settings.json` from `go run` (recompiles every invocation ~1s) to pre-built binary with helpful error if missing.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] `mise run fmt` — no formatting issues\\n- [x] `mise run lint` — 0 issues\\n- [x] `mise run test:ci` — all unit + integration tests pass\\n- [ ] Manual: restart Claude Code session and verify hooks execute faster\\n- [ ] Manual: `time ./entire hooks claude-code stop` to measure binary execution time\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/407/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/407/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/964\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/964/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/964/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/964/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/964\",\n            \"id\": 4273238154,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7S2ec4\",\n            \"number\": 964,\n            \"title\": \"feat(explain): live progress and observable-state timeout diagnostic\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n              \"id\": 249787869,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 2,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-04-16T04:26:22Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-23T14:11:42Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-23T14:11:39Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/964\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/964\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/964.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/964.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-23T14:11:39Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/164\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nTwo paired user-facing improvements to `entire explain --generate`, building on PR #1204 (which made the 30s timeout configurable but kept a 5-minute default and didn't change the silent-wait UX):\\n\\n1. **Live progress on TTY.** Real-time phase events (sending request → first token / TTFT → writing tokens → done) instead of silent wait. In-place line updates on TTY; one line per event in CI/piped; ASCII glyphs under `ACCESSIBLE=1`.\\n2. **Observable-state timeout diagnostic.** When `--summary-timeout-seconds` fires, the error message reflects what the subprocess was actually doing. Streaming providers (Claude) get phase-specific attribution; non-streaming providers (Codex/Cursor/Copilot/Gemini) surface captured stderr and distinguish \\\"produced no output\\\" from \\\"was generating output when killed\\\". The three-cause shrug from PR #876 is removed.\\n\\nPlus one policy change that enables both:\\n\\n3. **Automatic deadline removed.** `--generate` no longer has a 5-minute default cap. Timeouts are opt-in only via `--summary-timeout-seconds` flag or `summary_timeout_seconds` setting (both surfaces from #1204 preserved). With no automatic cap, every diagnostic users see is for a timeout they consciously requested.\\n\\n## What users see now\\n\\n**TTY, normal run:**\\n```\\nGenerating checkpoint summary... (transcript: 40.7 KB, provider: claude-code)\\n→ Sending request to provider...\\n→ Provider responded (TTFT 1.6s, 13k cached input tokens) -- generating...\\n→ Writing summary... (~Nk tokens)             ← updates in place\\n✓ Summary generated (7.6s, 420 output tokens)\\n✓ Summary generated for <checkpoint-id>\\n```\\n\\n**TTY, network down + `--summary-timeout-seconds 10`:**\\n```\\nGenerating checkpoint summary... (transcript: 40.7 KB, provider: claude-code)\\n→ Sending request to provider...\\n✗ Timed out after 10s: provider sent request but received no response\\n  cause    network/firewall, provider API degraded, or auth check stuck\\n  try      check connectivity to the provider, then retry\\n```\\n\\n**TTY, transcript too large + `--summary-timeout-seconds 3`:**\\n```\\n→ Provider responded (TTFT 1.6s, 20.2k cached input tokens) -- generating...\\n→ Writing summary... (~24 tokens)\\n✗ Timed out after 3s: model responded but did not finish\\n  cause    transcript may be too large for the chosen cap, or model is slow\\n  try      raise --summary-timeout-seconds or pick a faster model\\n```\\n\\n**Non-TTY (`| cat`):** same lines, one per event, no `\\\\r` in-place updates, no ANSI styling (lipgloss auto-strips).\\n\\n**`ACCESSIBLE=1`:** `→` becomes `->`, no ANSI escapes.\\n\\n## Architecture\\n\\n- **`agent.StreamingTextGenerator`** optional capability interface with `AsStreamingTextGenerator` detector. Defined alongside the existing `TextGenerator` interface. Claude Code is the first (currently only) implementer.\\n- **`(*ClaudeCodeAgent).GenerateTextStreaming`** invokes `claude --print --output-format stream-json --include-partial-messages --verbose`, pipes stdout through a 4 MiB-buffered NDJSON scanner, and dispatches `ProgressPhase` callbacks (`Connecting → FirstToken → Generating(×N) → Done`). Falls back to plain `GenerateText` when stderr indicates the CLI rejected streaming flags (older Claude CLI builds).\\n- **`summarize.TextGeneratorAdapter`** (the production summary-generator path used by all providers via `resolveCheckpointSummaryProvider`) gained streaming-capability detection and dispatches to `GenerateTextStreaming` when available. `summarize.ClaudeGenerator` got the same treatment for legacy callers.\\n- **`summaryProgressWriter`** renders progress events using existing `statusStyles` (lipgloss). In-place `\\\\r` updates on TTY; one line per event otherwise; ASCII glyphs in accessible mode. Throttled to 500ms-OR-25%-jump in non-TTY mode to avoid spam.\\n- **`summaryAttempt`** value type captures observable state during a run (phases reached, captured stderr, stdout byte count) so the diagnostic path can attribute timeouts without depending on the UI struct.\\n- **`*agent.TextGenerationError`** wraps `RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI` failures with captured stderr + stdout byte count, so the diagnostic can surface real subprocess output for non-streaming providers.\\n- **`providerCLIName`** maps `types.AgentName` to the user-facing CLI binary in diagnostic `try:` rows (`run \\\\`claude\\\\` directly to confirm it works`).\\n\\n## What changed from the original draft design (in case you remember the old PR)\\n\\nThe original draft (commits before this rebase) had a TTY-gated deadline strategy with an idle-based 5min watchdog + 30min hard wall-clock cap, plus an opt-in `summary_timeout_seconds` override. This redesign drops the automatic deadline entirely — timeouts are pure opt-in via the flag/setting from #1204. Rationale: the bug behind issue #1198 was that the auto-default truncated legitimate generations. Making the deadline opt-in fixes the root cause and removes a layer of mechanism (no idle watchdog, no separate wall cap, no goroutine).\\n\\nAlso intentionally NOT included: a stderr substring classifier for non-streaming providers (would have been \\\"chunk 8\\\" in the original plan). Decision: ship verbatim stderr passthrough rather than speculative phrase-matching without real CLI fixtures. The raw stderr is always surfaced in the diagnostic rows.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] `mise run check` (fmt + lint + unit + integration + E2E Vogon canary) passes locally\\n- [x] Manual: TTY happy path — progress phases render with in-place updates, final ✓ with duration + token count\\n- [x] Manual: `--summary-timeout-seconds 3` on a real Claude generation → \\\"model responded but did not finish\\\" with cause + try rows\\n- [x] Manual: Network offline + `--summary-timeout-seconds 10` → \\\"provider sent request but received no response\\\" (phase-distinguished from \\\"never sent its request\\\")\\n- [x] Manual: `| cat` → one line per event, no `\\\\r`, no ANSI\\n- [x] Manual: `ACCESSIBLE=1` → `->` instead of `→`\\n- [x] Manual: `entire explain --help | grep summary-timeout` → \\\"no automatic deadline applies\\\"\\n\\nCloses #1198 (issue was already closed at #1204 time; this delivers the diagnostic improvement that #1204 deferred).\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches `explain --generate` execution/timeout behavior and adds a new streaming Claude CLI path; failures could affect summary generation UX and error reporting across providers.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> `entire explain --generate` now reports *live, phase-based progress* during summary generation (TTY in-place updates, non-TTY line output, ASCII in `ACCESSIBLE` mode) and uses an observable-state `summaryAttempt` to produce more actionable timeout messages.\\n> \\n> Adds optional `agent.StreamingTextGenerator` support (capability + detector) and implements Claude Code streaming via `claude --output-format stream-json` with NDJSON parsing, progress callbacks (connecting/TTFT/generating/done), and fallback to non-streaming on older CLIs.\\n> \\n> Removes the implicit 5-minute default deadline for `--generate` (timeouts are now opt-in via flag/setting), and enhances non-streaming provider diagnostics by wrapping CLI errors with captured stderr and stdout byte counts (`TextGenerationError`), plus a shared provider→binary lookup (`SummaryCLIBinaryName`).\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 252e320a537d4c816b105158e835d5b8e59f7c65. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/964/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/964/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1155\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1155/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1155/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1155/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1155\",\n            \"id\": 4405887552,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7ZgUYE\",\n            \"number\": 1155,\n            \"title\": \"Add post-tool-use hook support for codex\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-05-08T11:06:17Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-08T15:18:38Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-05-08T15:18:35Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1155\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1155\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1155.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1155.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-05-08T15:18:35Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/329\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\nTurns out codex added post-tool-use hooks, let's add them! :) \\r\\n\\r\\n## Add Codex PostToolUse + hook drift detection\\r\\n\\r\\nAdds Codex `PostToolUse` hook support so `state.FilesTouched` is populated mid-turn (instead of only at Stop). Brings Codex to parity with Claude Code on tool-level event tracking.\\r\\n\\r\\nAlongside, surface two kinds of Codex hook drift in `entire doctor` and the SessionStart welcome:\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Trust gaps**: hook declared in `.codex/hooks.json` but no `trusted_hash` entry in the user's Codex config — fresh clone or a hook added in a release after the user's last `/hooks` approval.\\r\\n- **Stale file**: `.codex/hooks.json` predates a canonical event (e.g. PostToolUse itself) — fix is re-running `entire enable`.\\r\\n\\r\\nOther bits along the way:\\r\\n- Codex 0.129 feature-flag rename (`codex_hooks` → `hooks`) and per-user trust gate\\r\\n- Pre-trust hooks in the e2e seed so canary runs don't get prompted\\r\\n- Concurrent-write hardening on session state via `MutateSessionState` (per-process gate + flock)\\r\\n- \\r\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n> [!NOTE]\\r\\n> **High Risk**\\r\\n> High risk because it adds a new lifecycle event (`ToolUse`) and refactors many session-state write paths to go through a new cross-process locking/mutation helper, which could impact checkpointing/condensation correctness and introduce deadlocks or missed state updates if wrong.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> **Overview**\\r\\n> Adds Codex `post-tool-use` hook support and propagates `apply_patch` tool calls into a new lifecycle event (`agent.ToolUse`) so mid-turn file mutations are recorded incrementally (including add/update/delete and `*** Move to:` rename handling).\\r\\n> \\r\\n> Introduces `strategy.MutateSessionState` with per-session advisory lock files under `.git/entire-session-locks/` (plus a reentrancy gate) and refactors lifecycle + manual-commit strategy code paths to use it for load/mutate/save, preventing lost updates when hooks fire concurrently. Includes integration/unit tests for PostToolUse end-to-end behavior, apply_patch parsing/classification, and concurrency/locking invariants (parallel merges, nested mutations, and lock-file cleanup behavior).\\r\\n> \\r\\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 21ce8d6d9ef7a8f3d7c187f0979ca1e495f14ef1. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\r\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1155/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1155/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/758\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/758/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/758/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/758/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/758\",\n            \"id\": 4123570711,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7MzW_4\",\n            \"number\": 758,\n            \"title\": \"Handle path filtering and general other filtering\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-03-23T20:36:11Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-02T18:51:58Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-06-02T18:51:58Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": true,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/758\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/758\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/758.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/758.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes how transcripts/prompts are persisted and read back by introducing a clean/smudge pipeline, which could affect checkpoint compatibility and rewind/display behavior if filtering is misconfigured or applied inconsistently. Secrets redaction order and metadata copying paths are also modified, so regressions could impact stored history contents.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds a new `filter` package implementing a git-like **clean/smudge** pipeline to normalize machine-specific paths (repo root, home dir, plus user-configured replacements) in stored transcripts/prompts, and restores them on user-facing reads.\\n> \\n> Checkpoint writing paths (`WriteCommitted`, `UpdateCommitted`, temporary checkpoint metadata capture, and redacted blob creation) now applies `pipeline.Clean(...)` *before* redaction/chunking; new display helpers (`ReadLatestSessionContentForDisplay`, `LookupSessionLogForDisplay`, `GetTranscriptFromCommitForDisplay`, etc.) apply `pipeline.Smudge(...)` and are wired into `explain`, `resume`, `rewind`, and manual restore flows.\\n> \\n> Extends settings with `transcript_filters` and adds unit/integration tests to verify normalization on the metadata branch and restoration during logs-only rewind.\\n> \\n> <sup>Written by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot) for commit 5f35a1662f0a67706a517dc5e18cb442bc28a7ed. Configure [here](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/758/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/758/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/503\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/503/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/503/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/503/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/503\",\n            \"id\": 3992391583,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7GYZbB\",\n            \"number\": 503,\n            \"title\": \"Replace FlattenTree+BuildTreeFromEntries with ApplyTreeChanges in sha…\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"evisdren\",\n              \"id\": 256443556,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD0kEpA\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256443556?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/evisdren\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 2,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-02-25T23:34:48Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-26T02:10:48Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-02-26T02:10:46Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/503\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/503\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/503.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/503.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-02-26T02:10:46Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"update shadowbranch write process to not read every tree entry and insetad be selective in what is needed to be read. Create an array to track changes and then apply those. \\r\\n\\r\\nEntire-Checkpoint: f4c624aac28e\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/503/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/503/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/233\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/233/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/233/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/233/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/233\",\n            \"id\": 3924027225,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7C388C\",\n            \"number\": 233,\n            \"title\": \"feat: Complete Pi coding agent integration\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"hjanuschka\",\n              \"id\": 2891702,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI4OTE3MDI=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2891702?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hjanuschka\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/hjanuschka\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hjanuschka/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hjanuschka/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hjanuschka/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hjanuschka/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hjanuschka/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hjanuschka/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hjanuschka/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hjanuschka/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/hjanuschka/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [\n              {\n                \"id\": 9924477906,\n                \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACT4uD0g\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/enhancement\",\n                \"name\": \"enhancement\",\n                \"color\": \"a2eeef\",\n                \"default\": true,\n                \"description\": \"New feature or request\",\n                \"archived_at\": null,\n                \"archived_by\": null\n              },\n              {\n                \"id\": 10189613733,\n                \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACX1kqpQ\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/agent-support\",\n                \"name\": \"agent-support\",\n                \"color\": \"f3bc57\",\n                \"default\": false,\n                \"description\": \"adding support for additional AI agents\",\n                \"archived_at\": null,\n                \"archived_by\": null\n              },\n              {\n                \"id\": 10224934766,\n                \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACYXQfbg\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/competing-pr\",\n                \"name\": \"competing-pr\",\n                \"color\": \"fbca04\",\n                \"default\": false,\n                \"description\": \"Multiple PRs addressing the same thing — needs team decision\",\n                \"archived_at\": null,\n                \"archived_by\": null\n              },\n              {\n                \"id\": 10224940172,\n                \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACYXQ0jA\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/on-hold\",\n                \"name\": \"on-hold\",\n                \"color\": \"d4c5f9\",\n                \"default\": false,\n                \"description\": \"Blocked on other work\",\n                \"archived_at\": null,\n                \"archived_by\": null\n              }\n            ],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 5,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-02-10T23:36:54Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-30T16:14:56Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-03-30T16:14:55Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/233\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/233\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/233.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/233.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nComplete implementation of Pi coding agent support for Entire CLI. This supersedes the skeleton in #232 with a fully functional implementation.\\n\\n## What's included\\n\\n### Agent Implementation (`cmd/entire/cli/agent/pi/`)\\n\\n**pi.go** - Full Agent interface implementation:\\n- `DetectPresence()` - Checks for `.pi` directory\\n- `ParseHookInput()` - Parses JSON from pi extension hooks\\n- `ReadSession()` / `WriteSession()` - JSONL transcript handling\\n- `GetSessionDir()` - Returns `~/.pi/agent/sessions/<sanitized-path>/`\\n- `extractModifiedFiles()` - Parses write/edit tool calls from transcripts\\n- `TranscriptAnalyzer` interface - Efficient position tracking\\n- `TranscriptChunker` interface - Large transcript handling\\n\\n**hooks.go** - HookSupport and HookHandler:\\n- `InstallHooks()` - Adds `npm:@hjanuschka/pi-entire` to `.pi/settings.json`\\n- `UninstallHooks()` - Removes the extension package\\n- `GetHookNames()` - Returns `session-start`, `session-end`, `stop`, `user-prompt-submit`\\n\\n**types.go** - Pi-specific data structures:\\n- `piHookInput` - JSON input from extension\\n- `piSessionEntry` - JSONL session line format\\n- `piMessage` / `piContentBlock` - Message content types\\n\\n### Registry Updates\\n- Added `AgentNamePi` and `AgentTypePi` constants\\n\\n## How it works\\n\\nPi uses an extension-based architecture rather than external hook scripts. The integration consists of:\\n\\n1. **Entire CLI** (this PR) - Provides the `entire hooks pi <hook>` commands\\n2. **@hjanuschka/pi-entire npm package** - Pi extension that calls these hooks at lifecycle events\\n\\nWhen `entire enable --agent pi` is run:\\n1. The `.pi/settings.json` is updated with `\\\"packages\\\": [\\\"npm:@hjanuschka/pi-entire\\\"]`\\n2. Pi loads the extension on startup\\n3. Extension calls `entire hooks pi session-start`, etc. with JSON on stdin\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n```bash\\n# Enable in a repo\\nentire enable --agent pi\\n\\n# Check status\\nentire status\\n```\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n- Closes #221\\n- Supersedes #232 (skeleton implementation)\\n\\n## Companion package\\n\\nThe npm package `@hjanuschka/pi-entire` provides the pi extension side of this integration:\\nhttps://github.com/hjanuschka/pi-entire\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Adds a new agent integration that reads/writes local files and parses untrusted JSONL transcripts/settings, so bugs could affect hook installation or session processing but core existing agents are largely untouched.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **Pi coding agent support** to Entire CLI via a new `pi` agent implementation.\\n> \\n> This introduces Pi-specific hook handling by installing/uninstalling the `npm:@hjanuschka/pi-entire` extension in `.pi/settings.json`, parsing hook JSON from stdin, and adding Pi session transcript support (JSONL read/write, truncation/checkpoint lookup, modified-file extraction, and transcript position/chunking helpers). The agent registry is updated to include `AgentNamePi`/`AgentTypePi` constants.\\n> \\n> <sup>Written by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot) for commit b78731546a16e1611f3cffd2ae0eff68c9ab85e7. This will update automatically on new commits. Configure [here](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/233/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 6,\n              \"+1\": 4,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 2,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/233/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/922\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/922/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/922/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/922/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/922\",\n            \"id\": 4241596835,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7RkClN\",\n            \"number\": 922,\n            \"title\": \"Clean up condensation logic: type-enforced redaction boundaries\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"pfleidi\",\n              \"id\": 118549,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjExODU0OQ==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118549?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pfleidi\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 3,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-04-10T20:32:53Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-04-11T00:24:18Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-04-11T00:24:17Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/922\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/922\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/922.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/922.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-04-11T00:24:17Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Problem\\n\\nThe condensation path in `CondenseSession()` had three issues:\\n\\n1. **Redundant redaction** — The same transcript was redacted up to 3 times during a v2 condensation: once in `CondenseSession` for the compact transcript input, once in `GitStore.writeTranscript` for v1, and once in `V2GitStore.writeTranscriptBlobs` for v2 full transcript.\\n\\n2. **Scattered v2 checks** — `settings.IsCheckpointsV2Enabled(ctx)` was checked in `CondenseSession`, again redundantly inside `compactTranscriptForV2`, and in `writeCommittedV2IfEnabled`.\\n\\n3. **Implicit redaction contracts** — The `compact` package and checkpoint stores accepted raw `[]byte` transcripts with no indication of whether redaction had been applied. The expectation that data should be redacted was implicit and undocumented.\\n\\n## Solution\\n\\nIntroduce `redact.RedactedBytes` — an opaque struct type (unexported `data` field) that can only be produced by `redact.JSONLBytes()` or the escape-hatch `redact.AlreadyRedacted()` for trusted sources. This establishes compile-time contracts at package boundaries:\\n\\n- **`compact.Compact`** accepts `RedactedBytes`, enforcing that only redacted transcripts are compacted\\n- **`WriteCommittedOptions.Transcript`** and **`UpdateCommittedOptions.Transcript`** use `RedactedBytes`, documenting the store contract\\n- **`replaceTranscript`** and **`writeTranscriptBlobs`** accept `RedactedBytes` at the function parameter level, preventing unredacted writes to permanent storage\\n\\n### Key changes\\n\\n- **`CondenseSession`** redacts the transcript once early, then passes the single `RedactedBytes` result to both the compact path and the checkpoint stores — eliminating 2 redundant redaction passes\\n- **Store write paths** (`writeTranscript`, `writeTranscriptBlobs`, `replaceTranscript`, `UpdateCommitted`) no longer redact internally for in-memory data. The `TranscriptPath` file-read fallback retains its own redaction since data from disk is untrusted\\n- **`attach.go`** now explicitly redacts before calling `WriteCommitted` (previously relied on store-internal redaction)\\n- **`compactTranscriptForV2`** accepts `RedactedBytes` and drops the redundant `IsCheckpointsV2Enabled` guard (both callers already check)\\n- **Hooks finalize path** propagates `RedactedBytes` end-to-end instead of stripping to `[]byte` and re-wrapping\\n\\n### Safety\\n\\nIf transcript redaction fails in `CondenseSession`, the transcript is dropped rather than persisting potentially sensitive content. The checkpoint metadata (files touched, attributions, etc.) is still written — only the transcript is omitted.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] `mise run fmt && mise run lint` — zero issues\\n- [x] `mise run test:ci` — all unit + integration tests pass\\n- [x] `mise run test:e2e:canary` — Vogon E2E tests pass\\n- [ ] Verify `redact.JSONLBytes` calls in store write paths exist only in `TranscriptPath` fallback blocks\\n- [ ] Verify `IsCheckpointsV2Enabled` no longer appears in `compactTranscriptForV2`\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Medium risk because it changes core checkpoint persistence APIs (transcript types and redaction responsibilities) and could affect what transcript data is stored if any call site fails to redact or mishandles the new contract.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Enforces explicit redaction boundaries for checkpoint transcripts** by introducing `redact.RedactedBytes` and requiring callers to pass *pre-redacted* transcript data into checkpoint write/update flows.\\n> \\n> Redaction is moved out of store internals for in-memory transcripts: `WriteCommittedOptions.Transcript`/`UpdateCommittedOptions.Transcript`, transcript replacement, and v2 full-transcript blob writing now operate on `RedactedBytes` as-is, while file-based fallbacks (`TranscriptPath`, subagent transcripts) still redact on read because disk content is treated as untrusted.\\n> \\n> Condensation/finalization paths now redact once (with perf spans) and reuse the result for v1 storage, v2 compact transcript generation, and AI summarization; on redaction failure they **drop the transcript but still write metadata**. Tests/benchmarks/migration/explain/summarize/compact are updated to wrap trusted fixtures and persisted transcripts via `redact.AlreadyRedacted` and to validate the new “store preserves redacted transcript” behavior.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 09c40402e7b32a326913f190e206e6378527c6d9. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/922/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/922/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/257\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/257/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/257/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/257/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/257\",\n            \"id\": 3926675218,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7DAun5\",\n            \"number\": 257,\n            \"title\": \"Add OpenCode and Codex CLI agent support\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Avyukth\",\n              \"id\": 3435944,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MzU5NDQ=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3435944?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Avyukth\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Avyukth\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Avyukth/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Avyukth/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Avyukth/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Avyukth/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Avyukth/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Avyukth/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Avyukth/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Avyukth/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Avyukth/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [\n              {\n                \"id\": 10189613733,\n                \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACX1kqpQ\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/agent-support\",\n                \"name\": \"agent-support\",\n                \"color\": \"f3bc57\",\n                \"default\": false,\n                \"description\": \"adding support for additional AI agents\",\n                \"archived_at\": null,\n                \"archived_by\": null\n              },\n              {\n                \"id\": 10224934766,\n                \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACYXQfbg\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/competing-pr\",\n                \"name\": \"competing-pr\",\n                \"color\": \"fbca04\",\n                \"default\": false,\n                \"description\": \"Multiple PRs addressing the same thing — needs team decision\",\n                \"archived_at\": null,\n                \"archived_by\": null\n              },\n              {\n                \"id\": 10224940172,\n                \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACYXQ0jA\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/on-hold\",\n                \"name\": \"on-hold\",\n                \"color\": \"d4c5f9\",\n                \"default\": false,\n                \"description\": \"Blocked on other work\",\n                \"archived_at\": null,\n                \"archived_by\": null\n              }\n            ],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 3,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-02-11T13:51:16Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-24T16:05:26Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-02-24T16:05:25Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/257\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/257\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/257.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/257.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"Closes #245\\nCloses #266\\nRelates to #281\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAdds two new AI coding agent integrations to the Entire CLI: **OpenCode** and **Codex CLI**. Both agents support full session checkpointing via hooks — capturing transcripts, file changes, prompts, and metadata on shadow branches.\\n\\nAs part of this work, **duplicated framework code was extracted into a shared commit pipeline** (\\\"$(hooks_common_session.go)\\\"), directly addressing issue #281's goal of separating framework from agent-specific logic. The three agent handlers (Codex, OpenCode, Gemini) that previously duplicated ~250 lines of commit logic are now thin wrappers calling a shared \\\"$(commitAgentSession())\\\" function.\\n\\n**~3,000 lines across 16 files** (all new code from main's perspective).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Framework Extraction (addresses #281)\\n\\nThe shared \\\"$(hooks_common_session.go)\\\" consolidates duplicated logic from Codex, OpenCode, and Gemini handlers:\\n\\n| Extracted Function | Replaces | Purpose |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| \\\"$(commitAgentSession())\\\" | \\\"$(commitCodexSession)\\\", \\\"$(commitOpenCodeSession)\\\", \\\"$(commitGeminiSession)\\\" | Core commit pipeline: load state → detect changes → save via strategy |\\n| \\\"$(createContextFile())\\\" | \\\"$(createContextFileForCodex)\\\", \\\"$(createContextFileForOpenCode)\\\", \\\"$(createContextFileForGemini)\\\" | Unified context.md generation (single + multi-prompt) |\\n| \\\"$(transitionSessionTurnEnd())\\\" | Was in Claude Code handlers, used by all agents | Session phase state machine transition |\\n| \\\"$(logFileChanges())\\\" | Was in Gemini handlers, used by all agents | Stderr logging of modified/new/deleted files |\\n\\nEach agent handler is now a thin wrapper that populates an \\\"$(agentCommitContext)\\\" struct:\\n- **Codex**: provides transcript-extracted modified files, single prompt\\n- **OpenCode**: sets \\\"$(useGitStatusForModified: true)\\\" (no transcript parsing), single prompt\\n- **Gemini**: adds token usage calculation, multi-prompt array, transcript step tracking\\n\\nThis reduces the barrier for adding new agents — a new handler only needs to populate the context struct and call \\\"$(commitAgentSession())\\\".\\n\\n**Not yet extracted** (future #281 work): Claude Code's \\\"$(commitWithMetadata)\\\" has unique subagent/summarization/incremental-checkpoint logic that requires its own pattern. The \\\"$(Agent)\\\" interface itself is also unchanged — broader interface refactoring is deferred to the core team per #281.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### OpenCode Agent\\n- TypeScript plugin system: generates \\\"$(.opencode/plugins/entire.ts)\\\" that subscribes to \\\"$(session.created)\\\" and \\\"$(session.status)\\\" (busy/idle) events via BunShell\\n- **3 hooks**: \\\"$(session-created)\\\" (SessionStart), \\\"$(session-busy)\\\" (per-turn state capture), \\\"$(session-idle)\\\" (Stop/checkpoint)\\n- Per-turn pre-prompt state capture via \\\"$(session-busy)\\\" hook — captures untracked files before agent starts each turn for accurate new-file detection\\n- File change detection via git status with pre-prompt untracked baseline (OpenCode sessions are opaque JSON — no transcript-based file extraction possible)\\n- Session storage: reads from XDG data directory (\\\"$(~/.local/share/opencode/storage/session/)\\\")\\n- Recursive session file discovery via \\\"$(filepath.WalkDir)\\\" (OpenCode nests sessions under \\\"$(<projectID>/)\\\" subdirectories)\\n\\n### Codex CLI Agent\\n- TOML-based notify hook: installs \\\"$(notify = [\\\"entire\\\", \\\"hooks\\\", \\\"codex\\\", \\\"agent-turn-complete\\\"])\\\" in \\\"$(.codex/config.toml)\\\"\\n- Parses Codex JSONL rollout transcripts for file change extraction (\\\"$(file_change)\\\", \\\"$(function_call)\\\", \\\"$(event_msg/patch_apply_begin)\\\" items)\\n- **Codex sends notify payload via argv (not stdin)** — handler reads from last positional argument via \\\"$(GetCurrentHookArgs())\\\"\\n- Post-turn state capture — captures untracked files after each turn completes as baseline for next turn's file detection (Codex has no before-turn hook in codex-rs)\\n- Recursive session file discovery via \\\"$(filepath.WalkDir)\\\" (Codex uses date-based \\\"$(YYYY/MM/DD/)\\\" directory structure)\\n- Session storage: reads from \\\"$(~/.codex/sessions/)\\\" (respects \\\"$(CODEX_HOME)\\\" env var)\\n- Local dev mode resolves project path at write-time via \\\"$(paths.RepoRoot())\\\" (Codex executes notify as direct argv without shell expansion)\\n\\n### Shared Infrastructure\\n- **\\\"$(hooks_common_session.go)\\\"** — shared commit pipeline with \\\"$(agentCommitContext)\\\" struct\\n- Hook registry entries for both agents in \\\"$(hook_registry.go)\\\"\\n- \\\"$(currentHookArgs)\\\" + \\\"$(GetCurrentHookArgs())\\\" for agents that pass payloads via positional args\\n- \\\"$(fileExistsAndIsRegular())\\\" helper to distinguish files from directories\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Key Implementation Details\\n\\n**Codex argv payload handling:**\\nCodex's Rust source (\\\"$(user_notification.rs)\\\") calls \\\"$(command.arg(notify_payload))\\\" with \\\"$(stdin(Stdio::null()))\\\". The hook registry captures positional args via \\\"$(cobra.ArbitraryArgs)\\\" and stores them in \\\"$(currentHookArgs)\\\". The handler reads from \\\"$(args[len(args)-1])\\\" when available, falling back to stdin.\\n\\n**OpenCode session-busy hook:**\\nOpenCode fires \\\"$(session.status)\\\" with \\\"$(type: \\\"busy\\\")\\\" when the agent starts processing each turn. The TypeScript plugin pipes this to \\\"$(entire hooks opencode session-busy)\\\", which calls \\\"$(CapturePrePromptState(sessionID, \\\"\\\"))\\\" to snapshot untracked files before the agent modifies anything. The subsequent \\\"$(session-idle)\\\" handler uses \\\"$(commitAgentSession())\\\" with \\\"$(useGitStatusForModified: true)\\\".\\n\\n**Codex post-turn state capture (workaround):**\\nCodex only exposes \\\"$(AfterAgent)\\\" and \\\"$(AfterToolUse)\\\" hooks — no \\\"before turn\\\" event exists. As a workaround, \\\"$(handleCodexAgentTurnComplete)\\\" captures state after each turn completes (\\\"$(CapturePrePromptState)\\\" at the end), which serves as the baseline for the next turn's \\\"$(DetectFileChanges)\\\".\\n\\n**File existence checks:**\\n\\\"$(fileExistsAndIsRegular())\\\" replaces \\\"$(fileExists())\\\" for transcript path validation. Codex's \\\"$(ParseHookInput)\\\" sets \\\"$(SessionRef)\\\" to \\\"$(~/.codex/sessions)\\\" (a directory). Without the regular-file check, \\\"$(copyFile(dir, ...))\\\" would fail with \\\"is a directory\\\".\\n\\n**Codex JSONL file extraction:**\\nSupports three event formats from Codex rollout transcripts:\\n- \\\"$(response_item)\\\" with \\\"$(file_change)\\\" items (direct file path)\\n- \\\"$(response_item)\\\" with \\\"$(function_call)\\\" items (write_file, apply_diff, edit_file, create_file)\\n- \\\"$(event_msg)\\\" with \\\"$(patch_apply_begin)\\\" payload (HashMap keys are file paths — actual production format from \\\"$(exec_events.rs)\\\")\\n\\nUses \\\"$(bufio.NewReader)\\\" + \\\"$(ReadBytes('\\\\n'))\\\" instead of \\\"$(bufio.Scanner)\\\" to handle JSONL lines exceeding 64KB.\\n\\n**TOML hook installation (Codex):**\\n\\\"$(InstallHooks)\\\" parses \\\"$(.codex/config.toml)\\\" line-by-line, preserving user content and comments. When a user-configured \\\"$(notify)\\\" line exists and \\\"$(--force)\\\" isn't set, installation is skipped to avoid duplicate TOML keys.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Feature Comparison: Claude Code vs OpenCode vs Codex\\n\\n### Hook Coverage\\n\\n| Hook Event | Claude Code | OpenCode | Codex |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Session Start | \\\"$(session-start)\\\" | \\\"$(session-created)\\\" | — |\\n| Session End | \\\"$(session-end)\\\" | — | — |\\n| Per-Turn State Capture | \\\"$(user-prompt-submit)\\\" | \\\"$(session-busy)\\\" | post-turn (workaround) |\\n| Turn Complete / Checkpoint | \\\"$(stop)\\\" | \\\"$(session-idle)\\\" | \\\"$(agent-turn-complete)\\\" |\\n| Pre-Task (subagent) | \\\"$(pre-task)\\\" | — | — |\\n| Post-Task (subagent) | \\\"$(post-task)\\\" | — | — |\\n| Post-Todo (incremental) | \\\"$(post-todo)\\\" | — | — |\\n| **Total** | **7** | **3** | **1** |\\n\\n### File Change Detection\\n\\n| Method | Claude Code | Codex | OpenCode |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Transcript-based (modified) | Write/Edit/NotebookEdit tool calls | file_change, function_call, patch_apply_begin | None (opaque JSON) |\\n| Git-status-based (new/deleted) | With pre-prompt baseline | With pre-prompt baseline | With pre-prompt baseline |\\n| Git-status-based (modified) | No | No | Yes (primary method) |\\n\\n### Agent Interfaces Implemented\\n\\n| Interface | Claude Code | Codex | OpenCode |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| \\\"$(Agent)\\\" | Yes | Yes | Yes |\\n| \\\"$(HookSupport)\\\" | Yes | Yes | Yes |\\n| \\\"$(HookHandler)\\\" | Yes | Yes | Yes |\\n| \\\"$(TranscriptAnalyzer)\\\" | Yes | No | No |\\n| \\\"$(TranscriptChunker)\\\" | Yes | Yes | No |\\n\\n### Remaining Gaps (Agent Limitations)\\n\\n| Gap | Reason |\\n|---|---|\\n| Codex: no true before-turn hook | Only \\\"$(AfterAgent)\\\" and \\\"$(AfterToolUse)\\\" exist in codex-rs |\\n| OpenCode: no transcript parsing | Sessions stored as opaque JSON, no tool-call data accessible |\\n| Codex/OpenCode: no token tracking | Neither agent exposes token usage in payloads or transcripts |\\n| Codex/OpenCode: no subagent support | Neither has a subagent/task architecture |\\n| OpenCode: no session-end hook | No event fires when session is explicitly closed |\\n| Codex: no session state machine | Only one hook (`agent-turn-complete`) — no session-start or turn-start events to initialize the phase state machine |\\n| Codex/OpenCode: no summarization | JSONL schemas differ from Claude Code; routed through Claude parser as fallback (produces empty results). Dedicated parsers needed. |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Test Plan\\n\\n- [x] \\\"$(mise run fmt)\\\" — no formatting issues\\n- [x] \\\"$(mise run lint)\\\" — 0 new issues\\n- [x] \\\"$(mise run test)\\\" — all unit tests pass\\n- [x] \\\"$(mise run test:ci)\\\" — full CI suite with race detection passes\\n- [x] \\\"$(mise run test:integration)\\\" — integration tests pass\\n- [x] Manual: \\\"$(entire enable --agent opencode)\\\" installs \\\"$(.opencode/plugins/entire.ts)\\\"\\n- [x] Manual: \\\"$(entire enable --agent codex)\\\" installs notify hook in \\\"$(.codex/config.toml)\\\"\\n- [x] Manual: idempotent re-enable (\\\"$(entire enable --agent opencode)\\\" twice)\\n- [x] Manual: \\\"$(entire hooks codex agent-turn-complete '{...}')\\\" reads from argv\\n- [x] Manual: \\\"$(entire hooks opencode session-idle)\\\" reads from stdin pipe\\n- [x] OpenCode tests verify 3 hooks, session-busy parsing, plugin content includes busy handler\\n- [x] Codex tests verify argv payload reading, JSONL event extraction, TOML hook installation\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/257/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 1,\n              \"+1\": 1,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/257/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/166\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/166/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/166/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/166/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/166\",\n            \"id\": 3905705756,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7B8R6a\",\n            \"number\": 166,\n            \"title\": \"ENT-231: Secrets redaction\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"toothbrush\",\n              \"id\": 423357,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMzM1Nw==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/423357?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/toothbrush\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-02-06T09:08:08Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-08T02:48:24Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-02-08T02:48:22Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/166\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/166\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/166.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/166.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-02-08T02:48:22Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"# Description\\r\\n\\r\\nClaude happily stores scary secrets in session data, which we persist in the `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch.  To avoid folks shooting themselves in the foot and pushing API keys to public repos, we're introducing a filtering mechanism for all files written to the checkpoints branch.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe find secrets by looking for 10+ character strings with a specific threshold Shannon entropy value of > 4.5.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn open question is whether we should skip binary files here:\\r\\n\\r\\nhttps://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/c72f6b751b92e71d3c92d394d50f5c4402063da4/cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go#L1085-L1094\\r\\n\\r\\n..because we don't want to be munging files that aren't plain text.  However, my sense is \\\"no don't bother\\\", because this stuff is in `copyMetadataDir`, which should just contain stuff that we control, right?  Keen to hear from a CLI expert here.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe results of this redaction can be seen here: \\r\\n\\r\\nhttps://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/a0820d46fb9e940468f9dfe76084cba1eca89181/39/7737088f0a/0/full.jsonl#L4-L4\\r\\n\\r\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes what gets persisted into git history for checkpoints (including hashing/chunking inputs) using heuristic entropy-based detection, which could cause unexpected redactions or missed secrets and affect downstream consumers relying on exact content.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds automatic secrets redaction for data written to the `entire/sessions` (checkpoints) branch, replacing high-entropy token-like substrings with `REDACTED`.\\n> \\n> Redaction is applied to committed checkpoint transcripts (before chunking/content-hash), prompts, context, incremental task checkpoint payloads, subagent transcripts, and files copied via `copyMetadataDir` (with JSONL-aware handling and a binary-file skip to avoid corruption). New unit tests cover redaction behavior end-to-end for `WriteCommitted` and `copyMetadataDir`, plus focused tests for the new `redact` package’s entropy-based detection and JSONL field/object skip rules.\\n> \\n> <sup>Written by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot) for commit d0161a4c332584df0b24f5937aa21b0951c5956e. This will update automatically on new commits. Configure [here](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/166/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/166/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/89\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/89/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/89/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/89/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/89\",\n            \"id\": 3843889133,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M6-vzIb\",\n            \"number\": 89,\n            \"title\": \"Do not truncate Logs when storing\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T17:11:54Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-01-23T01:01:57Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-01-23T01:01:27Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/89\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/89\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/89.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/89.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-01-23T01:01:27Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"This removes the logic that would only commit the new log lines since last checkpoint if a session was continued and produced multiple checkpoints.\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/89/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/89/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/538\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/538/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/538/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/538/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/538\",\n            \"id\": 3999191346,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7Gutgg\",\n            \"number\": 538,\n            \"title\": \"Replace fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr) with structured logging in agent hook paths\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"id\": 881031,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 2,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T05:31:44Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-27T12:04:46Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-02-27T12:04:45Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/538\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/538\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/538.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/538.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-02-27T12:04:45Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\n- Replace ~87 `fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, ...)` calls with `logging.Warn/Info/Debug` in agent hook code paths, where stderr is unreliable (OpenCode suppresses it, git hooks redirect to `/dev/null`, other agents have varying stderr handling)\\n- Remove dead `StageFiles` function and associated types from `strategy/common.go` (~70 lines, zero callers)\\n- User-facing commands (resume, rewind, reset, doctor, setup) keep their stderr prints unchanged\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/538/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/538/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/392\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/392/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/392/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/392/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/392\",\n            \"id\": 3953778107,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7EaUsF\",\n            \"number\": 392,\n            \"title\": \"Add Cursor agent support on new agent interface\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"squishykid\",\n              \"id\": 2177912,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNzc5MTI=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2177912?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/squishykid\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [\n              {\n                \"id\": 9924477906,\n                \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACT4uD0g\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/enhancement\",\n                \"name\": \"enhancement\",\n                \"color\": \"a2eeef\",\n                \"default\": true,\n                \"description\": \"New feature or request\",\n                \"archived_at\": null,\n                \"archived_by\": null\n              },\n              {\n                \"id\": 10189613733,\n                \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACX1kqpQ\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/agent-support\",\n                \"name\": \"agent-support\",\n                \"color\": \"f3bc57\",\n                \"default\": false,\n                \"description\": \"adding support for additional AI agents\",\n                \"archived_at\": null,\n                \"archived_by\": null\n              }\n            ],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [\n              {\n                \"login\": \"squishykid\",\n                \"id\": 2177912,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNzc5MTI=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2177912?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/squishykid\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              }\n            ],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 6,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-02-17T17:05:24Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-25T13:33:03Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-02-25T13:33:01Z\",\n            \"assignee\": {\n              \"login\": \"squishykid\",\n              \"id\": 2177912,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNzc5MTI=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2177912?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/squishykid\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/392\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/392\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/392.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/392.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-02-25T13:33:01Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nAdds Cursor as a supported agent with full hook lifecycle, transcript storage, and checkpoint integration.\\n\\n### New: Cursor agent package (`agent/cursor/`)\\n- `types.go` — Cursor-specific types: session info, prompt input, pre-compact, subagent start/stop with native Cursor fields (`conversation_id`, `subagent_id`, `task`, etc.)\\n- `cursor.go` — Agent implementation with JSONL transcript storage (ReadSession, WriteSession, ChunkTranscript, ReassembleTranscript)\\n- `lifecycle.go` — `ParseHookEvent` mapping 7 Cursor hooks (`session-start`, `session-end`, `before-submit-prompt`, `stop`, `pre-compact`, `subagent-start`, `subagent-stop`) to normalized lifecycle events, plus `ReadTranscript`\\n- `hooks.go` — Hook install/uninstall for `.cursor/hooks.json` with unknown field preservation\\n- `hooks_test.go` — 11 hook tests (install, idempotent, force, preserve existing/unknown fields, uninstall)\\n- `lifecycle_test.go` — 14 lifecycle tests covering all hook types, edge cases, conversation_id fallback, and ReadTranscript\\n- `cursor_test.go` — 32 tests covering identity, session storage (ReadSession/WriteSession round-trips), chunking, DetectPresence, and sanitizePathForCursor\\n\\n### Modified\\n- `registry.go` — Adds `AgentNameCursor` and `AgentTypeCursor` constants\\n- `explain.go` — Includes `AgentTypeCursor` in JSONL transcript scoping/offset logic\\n- `hooks_cmd.go` — Blank import for cursor package `init()` registration\\n- `summarize/summarize.go` + `summarize_test.go` — Cursor agent support in summarization\\n- `transcript/types.go` — Documented `Role` field (Cursor uses `role`, Claude Code uses `type`)\\n- `transcript/parse.go` + `parse_test.go` — Added shared `ExtractModifiedFiles` utility for agents with tool_use blocks\\n\\n### Design decisions\\n- **Native Cursor hook format**: Uses Cursor's own subagent fields (`subagent_id`, `task`, `subagent_type`, etc.) rather than mapping to Claude Code conventions\\n- **7 hooks installed**: `session-start`, `session-end`, `before-submit-prompt`, `stop`, `pre-compact`, `subagent-start`, `subagent-stop`\\n- **No TranscriptAnalyzer**: Cursor's transcript format does not contain `tool_use` blocks, so modified file detection relies on git status instead of transcript parsing\\n- **No TokenCalculator**: Cursor's transcript does not include token usage data\\n- **FormatResumeCommand**: Returns a human-readable instruction (\\\"Open this project in Cursor...\\\") since Cursor is a GUI IDE with no CLI resume command\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] Unit tests pass (`mise run test`)\\n- [x] Integration tests pass (`mise run test:integration`)\\n- [x] Lint clean (`mise run lint`)\\n- [x] Builds successfully (`go build ./cmd/entire/`)\\n- [ ] Manual: `entire enable --agent cursor` creates `.cursor/hooks.json`\\n- [ ] Manual: `entire disable` removes hooks from `.cursor/hooks.json`\\n- [ ] Manual: `entire hooks cursor --help` shows all hook verbs\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/392/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/392/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/505\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/505/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/505/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/505/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/505\",\n            \"id\": 3992671000,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7GZShG\",\n            \"number\": 505,\n            \"title\": \"20260226 paul experiment shadowbranchupdates\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"toothbrush\",\n              \"id\": 423357,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMzM1Nw==\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/423357?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/toothbrush\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toothbrush/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": 