\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/280\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/280\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/280.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/280.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-02-12T06:22:20Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": null,\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/280/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/280/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/214\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/214/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/214/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/214/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/214\",\n            \"id\": 3920861770,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7CtgtS\",\n            \"number\": 214,\n            \"title\": \"Make rewind more generic for multi agent support\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"Soph\",\n              \"id\": 70741,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-02-10T11:10:19Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-11T04:02:25Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-02-11T04:02:24Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/214\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/214\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/214.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/214.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-02-11T04:02:24Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"Rewind wasn't working properly with gemini.\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches core rewind/resume and file-deletion exclusion logic; incorrect transcript path resolution or protected-dir detection could cause failed restores or unintended deletions across agents.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Reworks rewind/resume/log-restore to be **agent-aware**: transcript restore now resolves paths via session state (`transcript_path`) or agent-specific `ResolveSessionFile`, and `resume` now selects the agent from checkpoint metadata to match rewind behavior.\\n> \\n> Extends the `Agent` interface with `ProtectedDirs()` and `ResolveSessionFile()`, implements them for Claude and Gemini (including Gemini’s `session-*-<shortid>.json` lookup), and updates destructive operations (untracked collection / file deletion during rewind) to skip a cached union of protected directories from all registered agents.\\n> \\n> Improves session ID handling by preferring trailer-provided `SessionID` over metadata-dir parsing and simplifying `extractSessionIDFromMetadata` to return the directory basename; adds focused unit tests for new path resolution/protection logic and registry aggregation (`AllProtectedDirs`).\\n> \\n> <sup>Written by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot) for commit 303e7983d9aeed8c44d33ad3c1bd9b4499aa5334. This will update automatically on new commits. Configure [here](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/214/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/214/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/392\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/392/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/392/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/392/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/392\",\n            \"id\": 3953778107,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7EaUsF\",\n            \"number\": 392,\n            \"title\": \"Add Cursor agent support on new agent interface\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"squishykid\",\n              \"id\": 2177912,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNzc5MTI=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2177912?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/squishykid\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [\n              {\n                \"id\": 9924477906,\n                \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACT4uD0g\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/enhancement\",\n                \"name\": \"enhancement\",\n                \"color\": \"a2eeef\",\n                \"default\": true,\n                \"description\": \"New feature or request\",\n                \"archived_at\": null,\n                \"archived_by\": null\n              },\n              {\n                \"id\": 10189613733,\n                \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACX1kqpQ\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/agent-support\",\n                \"name\": \"agent-support\",\n                \"color\": \"f3bc57\",\n                \"default\": false,\n                \"description\": \"adding support for additional AI agents\",\n                \"archived_at\": null,\n                \"archived_by\": null\n              }\n            ],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [\n              {\n                \"login\": \"squishykid\",\n                \"id\": 2177912,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNzc5MTI=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2177912?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/squishykid\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              }\n            ],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 6,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-02-17T17:05:24Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-25T13:33:03Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-02-25T13:33:01Z\",\n            \"assignee\": {\n              \"login\": \"squishykid\",\n              \"id\": 2177912,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNzc5MTI=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2177912?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/squishykid\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/392\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/392\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/392.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/392.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-02-25T13:33:01Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nAdds Cursor as a supported agent with full hook lifecycle, transcript storage, and checkpoint integration.\\n\\n### New: Cursor agent package (`agent/cursor/`)\\n- `types.go` — Cursor-specific types: session info, prompt input, pre-compact, subagent start/stop with native Cursor fields (`conversation_id`, `subagent_id`, `task`, etc.)\\n- `cursor.go` — Agent implementation with JSONL transcript storage (ReadSession, WriteSession, ChunkTranscript, ReassembleTranscript)\\n- `lifecycle.go` — `ParseHookEvent` mapping 7 Cursor hooks (`session-start`, `session-end`, `before-submit-prompt`, `stop`, `pre-compact`, `subagent-start`, `subagent-stop`) to normalized lifecycle events, plus `ReadTranscript`\\n- `hooks.go` — Hook install/uninstall for `.cursor/hooks.json` with unknown field preservation\\n- `hooks_test.go` — 11 hook tests (install, idempotent, force, preserve existing/unknown fields, uninstall)\\n- `lifecycle_test.go` — 14 lifecycle tests covering all hook types, edge cases, conversation_id fallback, and ReadTranscript\\n- `cursor_test.go` — 32 tests covering identity, session storage (ReadSession/WriteSession round-trips), chunking, DetectPresence, and sanitizePathForCursor\\n\\n### Modified\\n- `registry.go` — Adds `AgentNameCursor` and `AgentTypeCursor` constants\\n- `explain.go` — Includes `AgentTypeCursor` in JSONL transcript scoping/offset logic\\n- `hooks_cmd.go` — Blank import for cursor package `init()` registration\\n- `summarize/summarize.go` + `summarize_test.go` — Cursor agent support in summarization\\n- `transcript/types.go` — Documented `Role` field (Cursor uses `role`, Claude Code uses `type`)\\n- `transcript/parse.go` + `parse_test.go` — Added shared `ExtractModifiedFiles` utility for agents with tool_use blocks\\n\\n### Design decisions\\n- **Native Cursor hook format**: Uses Cursor's own subagent fields (`subagent_id`, `task`, `subagent_type`, etc.) rather than mapping to Claude Code conventions\\n- **7 hooks installed**: `session-start`, `session-end`, `before-submit-prompt`, `stop`, `pre-compact`, `subagent-start`, `subagent-stop`\\n- **No TranscriptAnalyzer**: Cursor's transcript format does not contain `tool_use` blocks, so modified file detection relies on git status instead of transcript parsing\\n- **No TokenCalculator**: Cursor's transcript does not include token usage data\\n- **FormatResumeCommand**: Returns a human-readable instruction (\\\"Open this project in Cursor...\\\") since Cursor is a GUI IDE with no CLI resume command\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] Unit tests pass (`mise run test`)\\n- [x] Integration tests pass (`mise run test:integration`)\\n- [x] Lint clean (`mise run lint`)\\n- [x] Builds successfully (`go build ./cmd/entire/`)\\n- [ ] Manual: `entire enable --agent cursor` creates `.cursor/hooks.json`\\n- [ ] Manual: `entire disable` removes hooks from `.cursor/hooks.json`\\n- [ ] Manual: `entire hooks cursor --help` shows all hook verbs\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/392/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/392/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          }\n        ],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      },\n      \"issues\": {\n        \"total_count\": 1,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2942\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2942/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2942/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2942/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2942\",\n            \"id\": 6078333470,\n            \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABakwCHg\",\n            \"number\": 2942,\n            \"title\": \"Show transcript images (screenshots) in the entire.com session timeline\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"GarreltMock\",\n              \"id\": 98806671,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOBeOrjw\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98806671?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/GarreltMock\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/GarreltMock\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/GarreltMock/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/GarreltMock/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/GarreltMock/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/GarreltMock/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/GarreltMock/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/GarreltMock/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/GarreltMock/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/GarreltMock/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/GarreltMock/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 6,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T11:49:53Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-30T09:21:39Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": null,\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n              \"total\": 0,\n              \"completed\": 0,\n              \"percent_completed\": 0\n            },\n            \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n              \"blocked_by\": 0,\n              \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n              \"blocking\": 0,\n              \"total_blocking\": 0\n            },\n            \"body\": \"### Problem or use case\\n\\nWe build game prototypes, so most of our agent sessions revolve around images: playtest screenshots, UI bugs, before/after captures. When we review a session on entire.com, none of these images are visible. The session timeline renders `transcript.jsonl`, where each image becomes a text line like `[Image: original 1080x2424, displayed at 891x2000 …]`. The most important context of the session is lost.\\n\\nThe bytes are captured: inline base64 in `full.jsonl`, or as `assets/img-*.png` + `assets/manifest.json` with `redaction.externalize_images: true`. Neither is rendered.\\n\\nRepro (CLI 0.12.2, Claude Code, git-refs backend):\\n1. Set `\\\"redaction\\\": { \\\"externalize_images\\\": true }` in `.entire/settings.json`.\\n2. In a Claude Code session, have the agent open a PNG (Read tool).\\n3. Commit and push. The checkpoint contains `0/assets/img-<hash>.png` and the `entire-asset:` placeholder.\\n4. Open the checkpoint on entire.com: no image, only the placeholder / `[Image …]` text.\\n\\nExample checkpoint: `01M615CCVP9QDWC2VZNQCW1MB0` (repo lotum/team-prototype).\\n\\n### Desired behavior\\n\\n```shell\\nSession timeline on entire.com shows each image inline (thumbnail, click to enlarge)\\nat the point in the conversation where it was pasted or opened by the agent.\\n```\\n\\n### Proposed solution\\n\\nResolve `entire-asset:assets/...` placeholders against the checkpoint's `assets/` store when rendering the timeline. For checkpoints without externalized images, decode the inline base64 images from `full.jsonl`.\\n\\n### Alternatives or workarounds\\n\\nExtracting the base64 images from `full.jsonl` with a local script. Works, but nobody does it while reviewing a session.\\n\\nRelated: #933 (transcript readability), #2063 (subagent image externalization).\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2942/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2942/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"pinned_comment\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          }\n        ],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e16\",\n      \"query\": \"repo:entireio/entire-brain ranking explain\",\n      \"prs\": {\n        \"total_count\": 5,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/277\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/277/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/277/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/277/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/277\",\n            \"id\": 5488060150,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSm5-5c8AAAABD70ARg\",\n            \"number\": 277,\n            \"title\": \"Connect Linear issues to Brain memory and task workflows\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"karthik-rameshkumar\",\n              \"id\": 6728802,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjg4MDI=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6728802?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/karthik-rameshkumar\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-09-17T13:34:00Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-26T16:13:46Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": null,\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/pulls/277\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/277\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/277.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/277.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/1803/changes/entire-brain/197\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nLinear requirements and discussion can now travel with repository memory: import selected projects, retrieve cited issue evidence alongside code and sessions, start work with an issue-aware brief, and retain the outcome of user-requested Linear actions.\\n\\n## What ships\\n\\n- **Repository-scoped issue memory:** project descriptions, issues, and individual comments in immutable snapshots. Resumable imports cover active issues plus those completed/canceled in the last 90 days; explicitly referenced older issues remain fetchable.\\n- **Ordinary Brain retrieval:** BM25 lexical search (the same ranking as every other source; `vsearch` and `--semantic` are compatibility aliases since trail #278 removed semantic retrieval), exact-revision get/multi-get, and `brief --issue`. Results retain source URLs, freshness and completeness caveats; large records expand through snapshot-pinned continuation IDs.\\n- **A host-neutral workflow:** six CLI/MCP issue tools manage local evidence, work links, and operation receipts. The host's Linear MCP handles authentication and requested creates/comments/field updates; Brain receives no Linear credentials.\\n\\n## Demonstrated end to end\\n\\nUsing **Unified, Pluggable Agent Memory**, imported the project and its issues, created sample [COR-1825](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-1825/sample-brain-acceptance-offline-linear-evidence-round-trip), produced a cited brief, posted the authorized test comment, and retrieved the confirmed comment offline.\\n\\n```sh\\nentire brain brief --issue COR-1825 --json\\nentire brain query \\\"brain-linear-comment-20260917-4f1be802\\\" --source issue --json\\n```\\n\\nThe local MCP round trip verified batch replay, default-query recall, pinned briefs, exact snapshot reads, and successful operation receipts with no-egress enabled.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- Storage and affected CLI/MCP, retrieval, brief, workspace, and documentation tests pass.\\n- 2026-10-22 merge with main: the issue vector arm and its `issues/derived/vectors.json` cache were dropped after trail #278 removed semantic retrieval; issue evidence ranks lexically only, and the concurrent-disconnect regression now runs through a test hook. `internal/cli` and `internal/issues` suites, `go vet` and `gofmt -s` pass on the merged head.\\n- Regression tests cover purge during ranking/output, incomplete-to-full refreshes, comments moving with issues, split-batch completion, and paginated Unicode evidence across concurrent refreshes.\\n- Windows arm64, Linux amd64, and macOS arm64 builds pass. Linux/macOS runtime tests were not run here; 37 full-suite Windows failures were independently reproduced on unchanged mainline.\\n- Existing bundle/publish paths exclude issue content.\\n\\n[Workflow and contracts](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/blob/dc30aff132b58d95f852b3b2ebbb163e271beee3/docs/linear-workflow.md) · [Verification details](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/blob/dc30aff132b58d95f852b3b2ebbb163e271beee3/docs/linear-verification.md)\\n\\n## Direction\\n\\nThe provider-neutral issue layer is a foundation for other trackers and a continuous requirements → implementation → evidence loop. Future work could add opt-in durable-fact extraction, incremental synchronization, and shared team memory. This release stays local and on demand; background sync, native OAuth, and hosted issue storage are deferred.\\n\\nThe remaining work is tracked in Linear under [COR-2242](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2242/finish-the-linear-issue-memory-story-pr-277-follow-ups), with sub-issues COR-2244 to COR-2256 in recommended order: agent-facing wiring and typed tool schemas first, then reading work links back and REST parity, then scale and hosted-memory design.\\n\\n## Entire provenance\\n\\n[Checkpoint `a332fa8ca8a6`](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/tree/2d1ae0e96416d0bfcb3491d761edeac586aa132c/a3/32fa8ca8a6) is linked from the final commit and preserves all three related sessions: planning, the separate review, and implementation/live acceptance/review fixes. The original four feature commits are retained.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Captured sessions and parser limitation</summary>\\n\\n| Session | Scope |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `01a0af42-b0e6-7973-a8e7-2d640b09d7d3` | Exploration and agreed plan |\\n| `01a0af7c-2af3-7493-9d97-0345d173d907` | Separate review, tagged as an agent review |\\n| `01a0af4e-2589-7f43-ac5b-7a218f203825` | Implementation, live test, review against main, fixes, and PR request |\\n\\nEntire 0.8.42 reports no parsed prompt summaries for this Codex transcript format. The stored raw transcripts were checked and contain the relevant prompts; the limitation is in prompt indexing, not transcript capture.\\n\\n`entire checkpoint explain a332fa8ca8a6 --json` reports three captured sessions.\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/277/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/277/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/629\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/629/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/629/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/629/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/629\",\n            \"id\": 6314305597,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSm5-5c8AAAABOMfqFg\",\n            \"number\": 629,\n            \"title\": \"perf(recall): one store parse per query (COR-2313)\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"evisdren\",\n              \"id\": 256443556,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD0kEpA\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256443556?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/evisdren\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-11-10T19:32:32Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-10T19:34:01Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-11-10T19:33:38Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/pulls/629\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/629\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/629.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/629.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": null\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Why\\n\\nOne `recall` parsed the full memory store up to three times: `factstore.Load` for the records, `factstore.InspectBrain` for the integrity warning (a second `loadCombined`), and the empty-result blind-spot note (a third, via `factstore.Inspect`). At today's 3.4 MB flat store this is ~0.27s and structural rather than painful; the cost scales with the corpus. Linear: COR-2313.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n- `factstore.LoadWithIntegrity(brainDir)` returns the records and the integrity report from one parse. `Inspect`'s post-load body is extracted as `inspectCombined`; `Inspect`/`InspectBrain` behavior is unchanged.\\n- `recall` uses it and threads the report into the empty-result blind-spot explainer. The explainer's seam (`Deps.EmptyResultBlindSpot`) now takes an optional precomputed `*factstore.Integrity`; `nil` means \\\"compute it yourself\\\", which is what query/retrieve/search still pass — their parse count is COR-2314/scope-adjacent, untouched here.\\n- The integrity check's semantics are pinned by `TestLoadWithIntegrityMatchesSeparateCalls`: one call equals `Load` + `InspectBrain` on a healthy store and after a lost fact.\\n\\n## Receipt decision (ticket bullet 2)\\n\\nThe vitality serve receipt (and its `git rev-parse HEAD`) stays. It is Phase 1 of the lifecycle ledger (`docs/vitality_receipts.md`): receipts are the evidence for the Phase 2 outcome join and Phase 3 decay — the \\\"make it feed ranking\\\" path, which is COR-2311-adjacent territory. The write is best-effort and never fails the read surface by contract. Dropping it would orphan `memories vitality` and the documented plan to save one cheap subprocess.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n`./internal/cli`, `./internal/cli/command/...`, `./internal/cli/internal/factstore` suites pass; `gofmt -s`/`go vet` clean. Acceptance: one store parse per recall (two of three sites eliminated; the remaining parse is the one that loads the records).\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Read-path performance refactor with behavior locked by tests; recall semantics and integrity warnings stay the same aside from avoiding redundant parses.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **`memories recall`** now loads the flat fact store once per query instead of up to three times.\\n> \\n> **`factstore.LoadWithIntegrity`** returns sorted records and the same integrity report as **`Load`** + **`InspectBrain`**, using a shared **`inspectCombined`** path over one **`loadCombined`** parse. **`recall`** uses that for ranking warnings and passes the precomputed report into **`EmptyResultBlindSpot`** so empty results do not trigger another store read.\\n> \\n> The blind-spot seam gains an optional **`*factstore.Integrity`** ( **`nil`** still runs **`factstore.Inspect`** ); **`query`/`search`/`retrieve`** keep passing **`nil`** until a follow-up. A regression test pins **`LoadWithIntegrity`** against separate **`Load`** and **`InspectBrain`** on healthy and lossy stores.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit e7e57e490336f9a7f66eddc99fde52ee3e516c09. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/629/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/629/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/6\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/6/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/6/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/6/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/6\",\n            \"id\": 4605215351,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSm5-5c7jhViP\",\n            \"number\": 6,\n            \"title\": \"Agent-UX improvements: tokenized search, overview, recency, blind-spots, impact/id fixes\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"ashtom\",\n              \"id\": 70720,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzIw\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70720?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/ashtom\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 1,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-06-06T21:45:56Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-07T00:30:42Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-06-07T00:30:42Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/pulls/6\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/6\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/6.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/6.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-06-07T00:30:42Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"Stacked on `claude/semantic-warning-path-fix`. Improves the agent-facing brain surface, driven by actually consuming the brain on a real project (`gh/ashtom/podcasts`) and iterating with a Sonnet evaluator across three rounds.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n**Search that works for natural language**\\n- Route all `inspect` specialist text kinds (decisions/validation/tool-paths) through the tokenized ranker instead of whole-phrase substring matching. A natural-language question now matches on overlapping terms instead of returning nothing unless the exact phrase appears verbatim. (On podcasts, `inspect decisions \\\"why did we choose supabase over convex for the queue\\\"` went from **0 results** to the actual dated decision.)\\n- Semantic symbol `search` gains a token-overlap fallback for multi-word queries (`search \\\"feed refresh worker\\\"`: 0 → 20 results) and resolves a record `id` (from `search`/`overview`) for `context`/`impact`.\\n- Drop common question/filler words (why, did, over, instead, …) from tokenization so high-specificity terms aren't diluted.\\n\\n**Explainability & consistency**\\n- Every text match carries `score`, `matched_terms`, and a `timestamp`; the report carries `query_terms` so a thin/empty result is debuggable. Semantic search results also carry a `score`.\\n- Opt-in `--relax` (and MCP `relax` arg) for best-effort partial matches, flagged `partial`.\\n- Equally-scored history records ordered by recency (parsed from the session path) so \\\"current state of X\\\" surfaces the latest decision first.\\n- Empty result arrays emit `[]` instead of `null` across search/context/impact/boundaries/inspect/tests for one uniform shape.\\n\\n**New capabilities**\\n- `entire brain overview` — a single-call project map: stack stats, route/tool/workflow counts, build/test commands, entrypoints, key documents, and recent decisions.\\n- `entire brain stale --blind-spots` (and MCP `blind_spots` arg) — lists the files the semantic provider couldn't fully index. On podcasts this revealed all 125 \\\"partial failures\\\" are `.sql` migrations, i.e. TypeScript coverage is fully trustworthy.\\n\\n**Correctness fixes**\\n- `inspect impact` no longer returns an empty impacted set when a file resolves to many roots (raised the shared budget); roots: 24 → 200 total symbols (176 impacted) on `feed-refresh.ts`.\\n- Path-like queries skip the token fallback, so a nonexistent path no longer matches half the index on the token \\\"file\\\" and reports a bogus blast radius.\\n- `brief`'s semantic context now populates for natural-language task strings (was always empty).\\n\\n## Validation\\n- `mise run lint`, `go test -race ./...`, and the deterministic Phase 1 suite all pass.\\n- Each change verified against the live `gh/ashtom/podcasts` brain (refreshed with `entire brain refresh`).\\n- One existing test updated where tokenized matching legitimately surfaces a relevant decision the old substring matcher missed.\\n\\n## Deliberately out of scope (provider-side, in `entire-sem`)\\nSQL files unparsed by the bundled tree-sitter grammar; route boundaries lacking `file_path`; low-confidence/spurious CALLS relations. These need provider changes, not plugin changes.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/6/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/6/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/42\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/42/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/42/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/42/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/42\",\n            \"id\": 4657013871,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSm5-5c7mI7AI\",\n            \"number\": 42,\n            \"title\": \"Fix history-delivery (full_cli_compact): self-correcting packet, shell-safe brief, prep rename\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"id\": 257360244,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-06-13T21:33:10Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-13T23:44:13Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-06-13T23:44:13Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/pulls/42\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/42\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/42.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/42.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-06-13T23:44:13Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## What & why\\nThe benchmark's `full_cli_compact` history delivery measured net-harmful on\\ncli-bench (condense 2/4 vs 4/4, redaction 2/4 vs 4/4): the compact policy forced\\nthe agent to blindly trust the brief's `likely_edit_files` pointer and \\\"not\\nbroaden,\\\" so a lexical false positive (e.g. `pickLatestVersion` matching\\n\\\"latest\\\") became a guaranteed wrong edit. Separately, the earlier move of\\n`export` under `refresh sessions` had broken the benchmark's history prep.\\n\\n## Changes\\n**Core fix (`run.py`)**\\n- Rewrite both `full_cli_compact` policies (Opus `--limit 2`, generic `--limit 4`)\\n  into a self-correcting two-step: name the broken invariant from the brief's\\n  history hits, treat `likely_edit_files[0]` as a candidate to *verify*, let the\\n  invariant — not lexical ranking — pick the file. Anti-spiral discipline kept\\n  (one brief, ≤2 searches, one test, stop).\\n- Prep: `export` → `refresh sessions`; cache schema 3→4 so a pre-rename cache\\n  can't be served stale.\\n\\n**Hardening (4 high-recall review rounds)**\\n- Shell-quote the brief query (`shlex.quote`) — run verbatim in the agent's\\n  shell; 13/54 task prompts contain backticks/quotes an unescaped double-quoted\\n  string would command-substitute or truncate. Verified in bash+zsh; shell\\n  round-trip test added.\\n- `capture_brief_packet` made opt-in (`ENTIRE_BENCH_CAPTURE_BRIEF=1`, off by\\n  default), gated to explicit `CLI_BRIEF_CONDITIONS` with a lockstep test,\\n  stdout bounded, `ok` flag, honest docstrings. Single-line query; dead\\n  `export` keyword dropped.\\n\\n**Tests:** full suite green; `mise run check` green.\\n\\n## Evidence (honest)\\n`benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/history-delivery-fix/` — net-harm eliminated:\\nparity pass-rate at −30%/−44% tokens. This is **efficiency-at-parity, not a\\nquality lift** (per-comparison verdict is `brain_negative`). A Provenance\\nsection states the retained numbers are real measurements from the core fix at\\nan earlier commit; later hardening commits are verified benign for these\\n(metacharacter-free) tasks, and the prep rename is verified on shipped HEAD by a\\nfresh `refresh sessions` run. A fingerprint-matched clean re-run was scoped but\\ndeferred (gpt-5.5 codex-quota-blocked; opus rate-throttled).\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/42/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/42/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/55\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/55/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/55/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/55/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/55\",\n            \"id\": 4796582498,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSm5-5c7tO3U2\",\n            \"number\": 55,\n            \"title\": \"feat(viz): local, no-egress visual interface for the brain\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"id\": 257360244,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-07-02T17:00:36Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-02T21:02:32Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-02T21:02:32Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/pulls/55\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/55\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/55.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/55.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-02T21:02:32Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"**What**\\n- Adds `entire brain viz [path]` (in the `explore` group): a local, loopback-only, no-egress web interface that renders the brain as an explorable, force-directed graph. The semantic code graph, facts, sessions, history, and docs each render as their own graph, with search, a ⌘K palette, a node inspector, a node-count slider, and session replay.\\n- Self-contained: a hand-authored, zero-build SPA embedded via `go:embed` — no CDN, no JS toolchain — so the pure-Go single-binary build is preserved.\\n\\n**Why / how it helps**\\n- The brain was only explorable via the CLI and the terminal dashboard. This adds a visual way to navigate a repo's brain in the browser, fully offline.\\n\\n**How**\\n- New `internal/cli/viz.go`: a cobra command + `http.ServeMux` + read-only JSON handlers, each wrapping an existing brain loader. Binds `127.0.0.1` only; a CSP header (`default-src 'self'` …) makes the no-egress guarantee machine-checkable.\\n- New module-root `webui.go` embeds `webui/dist` (mirrors `templates.go`/`embedmodel.go`). Frontend: `graph.js` (Canvas2D Barnes-Hut force sim + renderer), `app.js` (router/fetch/wiring), `index.html`, `style.css`.\\n- One-line command registration in `root.go`.\\n- Scale: the node-count slider reaches each feature's true total, bounded by a 300k safety ceiling; the semantic edge budget scales with node count (~4/node, capped at 90k). The relations query is chunked so a large graph can't exceed SQLite's bound-variable limit.\\n\\n**Testing / verification**\\n- `go build ./...`, `gofmt -l`, and `go vet ./internal/cli/` clean.\\n- `go test ./internal/cli/` — full package green, including the new tests. Confirmed on the committed tree (`git show HEAD`).\\n- New tests: chunked relations query at 20k symbols (the old single query bound 40001 params and errored with \\\"too many SQL variables\\\"); all six feature endpoints degrade to 200 + valid JSON on an unbuilt brain; loopback-only bind asserts `127.0.0.1`; CSP/nosniff applied through the real mux; a huge `?limit` clamps without panic; node/edge JSON field mappings.\\n- Manual: rendered the semantic graph at full scale (11,211 nodes / 44,844 edges) and full history (172,432 nodes) with no collapse or tab crash; exercised session replay, search, and the empty/unbuilt-brain states.\\n- An adversarial audit (7 dimensions, each finding independently verified) surfaced 8 issues; all are fixed in this branch: SQLite IN-clause variable-limit → chunked; `?limit=0` history ceiling bypass → clamped; search/palette stale-response race → sequence guard; plus the test-coverage gaps above.\\n\\n**No-egress**\\n- Loopback bind, embedded assets, disk-only reads, and a CSP enforced on every response. No outbound network of any kind.\\n\\n**Risk / rollback**\\n- Additive: a new command (~2.6k lines) and a one-line `root.go` change. The single shared change is chunking `findSemanticRelationsForSymbolsInSQLite` — behavior is identical for small symbol sets (one batch) and correct for large sets where it previously errored; the full package suite is green. Rollback: drop the branch.\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/55/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/55/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          }\n        ],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      },\n      \"issues\": {\n        \"total_count\": 1,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/335\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/335/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/335/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/335/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/issues/335\",\n            \"id\": 5729150547,\n            \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOSm5-5c8AAAABVXvmUw\",\n            \"number\": 335,\n            \"title\": \"Agents miss facts Brain already retrieved: brief --json puts status before facts/history; query returns no facts for natural questions\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"karthik-rameshkumar\",\n              \"id\": 6728802,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjg4MDI=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6728802?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/karthik-rameshkumar\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [\n              {\n                \"id\": 11043900200,\n                \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOSm5-5c8AAAACkkSLKA\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/labels/bug\",\n                \"name\": \"bug\",\n                \"color\": \"d73a4a\",\n                \"default\": true,\n                \"description\": \"Something isn't working\",\n                \"archived_at\": null,\n                \"archived_by\": null\n              }\n            ],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 4,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-06T13:22:57Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-10T19:06:47Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-11-10T19:06:47Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n              \"total\": 0,\n              \"completed\": 0,\n              \"percent_completed\": 0\n            },\n            \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n              \"blocked_by\": 0,\n              \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n              \"blocking\": 0,\n              \"total_blocking\": 0\n            },\n            \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nIn a controlled comparison, agents using Brain did not use a fact that Brain had already retrieved for them. Retrieval was correct in every run; the agent never saw the result. Two causes: `brief --json` orders its output with a large status block first and facts/history last, and `query` does not surface facts or history for natural-language questions. An agent with plain hosted session search (`entire search` + `checkpoint explain --full`) answered correctly 3/3; Brain with the default generated guide answered 0/3.\\n\\n## Setup\\n\\n- This repository at current `main`. Brain 0.1.0, ~400 distilled facts, index current at HEAD.\\n- Claude Code headless, Sonnet, read-only tool allowlist, fresh clone per run, 3 repetitions per condition.\\n- Each condition received the product's own generated guide (`agent-guide`, standalone or combined) plus a short section describing `entire search` and `checkpoint explain`.\\n- Ground truth: a design decision that was tried, called out as a regression and reversed in an agent session. It exists in session history and as a Brain closed-negative fact. It is not in code, docs or commit messages, which state the resulting rule but not the reason.\\n\\nPrompt, identical in every condition:\\n\\n```\\nA teammate has proposed a product change: when a developer installs the Entire plugins globally, Brain should automatically be activated in every repository they work in, instead of being enabled per repository.\\n\\nBefore we decide, answer three things:\\n1. How does Brain activation work in this codebase today, and which code would need to change? Name the specific files and functions.\\n2. Has this idea, or something close to it, been considered, tried, or decided before in this project? If so, what was decided and why? Only report what you can back with evidence; say clearly if you found none.\\n3. Your recommendation in two or three sentences.\\n\\nCite evidence for each claim (file path and line, command output, checkpoint or session id, or fact id). Keep the whole answer under 400 words. Do not modify any files.\\n```\\n\\n## Results\\n\\n| Condition | Recovered the recorded decision and its reason (not inferred) | Mean input tokens |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| code + git only | 0/3 | 303k |\\n| + hosted sessions (`entire search`, `checkpoint explain --full`) | **3/3** | 203k |\\n| + Graph | 0/3 (1 partial) | 224k |\\n| + Brain, normal combined guide | 0/3 (2 partial) | 219k |\\n| + Brain, strict guide (`init-agents --strict`) | 1/3 | 487k |\\n\\n## Defect 1: `brief --json` buries facts and history under status\\n\\nFor this task the JSON brief is ~27 KB. Top-level sections in output order:\\n\\n```\\nstatus             ~12.8 KB   mostly provider warnings (unreported skips, schema minor mismatch, data-flow evidence notes)\\nsemantic            ~4.3 KB\\nhistory             ~2.3 KB   contains the decisive session line\\nfacts               ~1.2 KB   contains the decisive closed-negative fact\\nlikely_*, guidance, warnings\\n```\\n\\nThe generated guide tells agents to run `entire brain brief \\\"<task>\\\" --json`. In all six Brain runs the agent capped the output at 6 to 9 KB, and the facts and history sections were cut off. The one run that read the full output cited the fact and the session line and produced the best answer in the experiment.\\n\\nThe plain-text brief for the same task is 27 lines (about 4 KB) and contains both.\\n\\n## Defect 2: `query` returns no facts or history for natural phrasings\\n\\nTwo natural-language queries about global installation activating Brain each returned 10 results, all `source=doc`, with no fact and no history record. `recall` with the same wording returned the decisive fact at rank 1 in about 3.4 KB.\\n\\nAgents in the strict condition ran `query` four times across runs and never saw the fact. None ran `recall`, because neither guide names it for \\\"was this decided before\\\" questions. One agent guessed a `facts search` subcommand that does not exist.\\n\\n## Suggested fixes\\n\\n1. In `brief --json`, emit `facts`, `history` and `likely_*` before `status`, or move the full status behind a flag and keep a one-line freshness summary. Agents truncate; the payload they need should come first.\\n2. Alternatively a compact JSON shape: facts, history, likely files, one-line status.\\n3. Make `query` include facts and history for natural-language questions, or have the generated guides name `recall \\\"<question>\\\"` as the first call for prior-decision questions.\\n4. Reconsider the strict guide's mandatory per-session `version` + `capabilities --json` preflight and Graph query cost; strict used 2.4x the input tokens of sessions-only for one extra hit.\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- The published proof-ready result in `docs/benchmarks.md` compares memory vs no memory (checkpoint objects were removed from the baseline). It does not compare Brain against an agent with plain session access. This experiment does, and the current default loses that comparison for the reasons above, not because of retrieval quality.\\n- n=3 per condition, one question, one repository, one model. The Graph index was prewarmed before timing. Harness: scratch clone, PATH shim gating `entire` subcommands per condition, `claude -p --output-format stream-json`. Happy to contribute it under `benchmarks/`.\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/335/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/335/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n            \"pinned_comment\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          }\n        ],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e17\",\n      \"query\": \"repo:entireio/entire-graph incremental worktree\",\n      \"prs\": {\n        \"total_count\": 4,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/322\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/322/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/322/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/322/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/322\",\n            \"id\": 5721597245,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSqVa0c8AAAABG019mQ\",\n            \"number\": 322,\n            \"title\": \"feat(agentsetup): extend graph guidance and register Claude subagent hooks\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"id\": 257360244,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-06T01:46:25Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-15T13:15:36Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-15T13:13:53Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/322\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/322\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/322.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/322.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-15T13:13:53Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"Extends Graph guidance to each later code-location/relationship question, bounds the complete def response across text/agent/JSON and multiple names, and registers a repository-local Claude SubagentStart hook during init-agents. Existing settings/hooks are preserved, unsafe/unknown settings shapes are refused, and --no-claude-hook skips registration. The hook emits bounded static context without indexing or network calls.\\n\\nPublic regressions fix a two-byte multi-name def request printing three bytes and an unusable clipped-body continuation. Continuations now include the symbol, a safely quoted path, repository and original --head/--worktree choice. The real suggested command is decoded by a shell and executed against deliberately differing committed/edited source. Every shipped Graph guide example executes against a committed fixture.\\n\\nWindows explicitly selects a PowerShell 5.1-compatible wrapper; macOS/Linux use POSIX shell. Wrapper tests exercise current, older and missing binaries. Hook/settings/guide and def-budget tests pass locally. The installer leaves ignore policy unchanged: docs explicitly tell the owner to ignore settings.local.json before committing. Preflight catches invalid settings before guide writes, but installation is not a multi-file transaction: later I/O/concurrent-change failures may leave the guides installed without the hook, and an idempotent rerun completes recovery. A real Claude session was not launched.\\n\\nCurrent official contracts were checked: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#subagentstart, https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents#what-loads-at-startup, and https://code.claude.com/docs/en/settings. The platform wrapper and real def continuation also pass under the race detector. All seven evaluations and all 34 technical CI checks passed at standalone head ddb65789ee6ad1fb4e76115bc5bb75a17e41ee65. The predicted main merge tree matched the tested tree. Approved under the user's explicit policy decision and merged normally, without bypass, as ec6e33e69266e7429259e3e9218e7fca1c343bb0.\\n\\nThe user explicitly approved the default hook and continued Graph-use policy. This branch now applies the exact reviewed Trail 242 incremental patch directly to main, separated from the unapproved Trail 236 integration. Its original authorship is credited and its previous stack head remains preserved locally. The documented opt-out remains available.\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/322/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/322/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/329\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/329/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/329/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/329/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/329\",\n            \"id\": 5806277131,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSqVa0c8AAAABH3yZYQ\",\n            \"number\": 329,\n            \"title\": \"fix: agent output diagnostics from #325 (subdir VERIFY, warm coverage, edges --cache-dir)\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"id\": 257360244,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T23:33:45Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-17T08:58:56Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-17T08:58:56Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/329\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/329\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/329.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/329.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-17T08:58:55Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"Targeted edges now honor --cache-dir and reuse the existing unfiltered edges cache. Hits preserve matching output bytes; unreadable entries rebuild before any cached prefix reaches stdout. Search coverage diagnostics use the complete snapshot when available, so cold and warm queries disclose the same warnings, partial failures and completeness. VERIFY can find ancestor manifests after all in-scope derivations decline.\\n\\nThis is Trail 247's isolated incremental delta on main bad496bef88faedeb6aa25977c1931796c77d17a, final head 0f503f6c8c14ec85eda89493ca59becb1ef661aa. The human-approved parent Trail 243 was delivered to main first. Older inherited stack changes are excluded; original 247 source is preserved in local backup codex/trail247-original-20261017. No parser, schema, stable-ID, dependency, runtime network or default agent-policy changes are included.\\n\\nReview gaps are covered directly. The CLI recovery test damages gzip data and NDJSON/relation records inside a valid envelope, then checks stdout/stderr against --no-cache, replacement of the bad entry, and reuse of the repaired entry without rewriting. Overflow must preserve output and cannot persist an incomplete capture. Disabling recovery makes the regression fail. VERIFY tests cover symlinked manifests, Unix FIFOs, relative and symlinked scopes, core.worktree escape refusal, eight build ecosystems and running the emitted Go test command. Native assembly/C package inventory is retained across the ancestor walk, and the original read budget is preserved. Native-input parity and remaining/exhausted-budget regressions failed before the fix and pass after it.\\n\\nAncestor commands intentionally use the absolute physical checkout root, also shown in derivation evidence, so a symlinked scope cannot redirect a relative parent walk. The stale comment and user docs are corrected. Reads remain bounded inside the physical checkout, behind Git-metadata validation, os.Root, regular-file/identity/size checks, or committed-tree readers for --head. VERIFY commands are suggestions printed to the caller.\\n\\nFinal-head verification: all 34 technical checks and 4 workflows pass, including full Linux/macOS/Windows suites, build, vet and security checks. All seven evaluations pass on this exact head with zero open findings; confidence was refreshed after completed CI and is 78%. Windows execution artifacts include passed recovery/overflow, native-inventory, read-budget, manifest-refusal and real-module VERIFY tests. The coverage verifier accounted for 3482 heavy-package roots and 19 other packages. Tested merge fff297ee2ea9aa40acc5150bf50177063bf8bc14 includes this head and has exactly its source tree. The non-Unix file-open path is exercised. Focused local tests and race checks pass; NOTICES and all 49 benchmark-kit checks pass.\\n\\nFinal source checkpoint: 4a6025042cc1; all three source checkpoints are published. Approval is based on this contained bug-fix delta and the final-head evidence above, with normal merge gates and no bypass.\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/329/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/329/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/315\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/315/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/315/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/315/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/315\",\n            \"id\": 5652162606,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSqVa0c8AAAABF9xqKw\",\n            \"number\": 315,\n            \"title\": \"feat(search,sem): integrate declaration-aware output and Go route analysis\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"id\": 257360244,\n              \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-09-30T19:50:52Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-16T11:07:22Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-16T11:07:22Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/315\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/315\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/315.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/315.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-16T11:07:22Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/236\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nIntegrates declaration name-line metadata, exact-identifier answers, bounded declaration-aware source windows, scoped Go router/middleware analysis, and observed follow-up accounting. Current main and the five approved parent trails are incorporated.\\n\\nThe integration preserves the whole-certified-body-or-locator contract, machine JSON fidelity, adaptive ranked-source protection, primary-location floors, and normal-result accounting for mixed callee spans. Exact-name answers preserve certified bodies whole. Prefix-summed window pricing agrees with an independent exhaustive oracle; the previously timing-out verification-budget sweep now passes in 113 seconds.\\n\\nReview fixes include quarantined-row declaration budgeting, dialect-specific bracket attributes, and route parameter-taint convergence under the shared work budget instead of a silent sixteen-round cutoff. A 256-hop real snapshot rejects a false bare route and retains the served-root positive control. Exhausted route analysis masks the entire file and reports a machine-readable partial failure. Malformed Go route recovery now masks the generic literal pass while retaining only conservative named handlers, with explicit parse-loss disclosure. Signature-evidence work/key-size exhaustion is reported per file after relation workers finish; a real exponential-alias snapshot and small positive control cover the loss. Both persisted cache families retire the earlier producer; symbol IDs and IdentityRevision 4 are preserved. The worktree warning now describes the active source view without incorrectly claiming the same default for all command families; 29 regenerated provider goldens differ only in that text, with all 197 symbol IDs unchanged.\\n\\nHistorical pre-flag goldens are unchanged. A separate 44-case current integration golden records agent rendering changes, with all 33 non-agent historical hashes unchanged. Local route/declaration/cache/golden tests, composed CLI suite, independent pricing oracle, Windows runner guards and vet have passed. Focused race-detector checks also pass for route-taint convergence, exhausted snapshot disclosure and bracket-dialect masking. Final-head remote validation is being completed.\\n\\nUser approval is held for the broad default search-output and Go route-analysis changes. The three incremental locator/tail/guard children can be approved against this base, but must not merge into main before this integration is approved.\\n\\n\\nConflict resolution against current main (2026-10-16):\\n\\nUpdated head 77f0bddf0aca3d373c3e1d797bcaa90d61f93e7a merges main 583f90ec760e983e78ef14df166af3a20bc6d0cb. All seven conflict paths are resolved. The stats implementation, v4 memo schema and result-row/shared-read attribution are retained from main, while both plaintext controls and the parent's search/verify-block contracts remain intact. The conflict resolutions match the previously reviewed composition; independent trail 244 changes remain separate.\\n\\nFocused CLI stats/guidance tests (23.020s), setup tests (0.463s), build, formatting, vet and public generated-guide parity pass. The full repository local suite passes. All 34 technical CI checks and every workflow pass at exact head 77f0bddf0aca3d373c3e1d797bcaa90d61f93e7a; all seven evaluations pass, including confidence refreshed after green CI. Zero open findings or unresolved review threads. The branch is conflict-free and zero commits behind current main. Keep this broad integration open and unmerged for the user's manual review; no approval or auto-merge is authorized by this conflict repair.\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/315/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/315/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          },\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/78\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/78/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/78/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/78/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/78\",\n            \"id\": 5039586963,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSqVa0c75gDom\",\n            \"number\": 78,\n            \"title\": \"entire graph: help overhaul, index UX (progress/summary/--force), and completeness fixes\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"ashtom\",\n              \"id\": 70720,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzIw\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70720?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/ashtom\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-08-01T23:42:57Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-02T22:21:53Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-02T22:21:52Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/78\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/78\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/78.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/78.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-02T22:21:52Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"Several related `entire graph` CLI/UX improvements. The JSON payload and its `format_version: 1` schema are unchanged, but **`index` gains flags and changes its default output format** — see Compatibility below. `mise run check` is green.\\n\\n> An earlier revision of this description claimed \\\"no flag, default, or machine-output change.\\\" That was wrong: `index` now defaults to `--format auto`, which prints a human summary when stdout is a terminal. Corrected here rather than left to be discovered.\\n\\n## 1. Grouped, per-command help\\n\\nRoot help was one dense blob and **no subcommand answered `--help`**. New `internal/cli/help.go` holds a `commandDoc` registry driving:\\n\\n- **`renderRootHelp`** — two-column listing grouped by intent: **Set up your agent** · **Inspect the graph** · **Analyze changes & more** · **Help & diagnostics**.\\n- **`renderCommandHelp`** — per-command `Usage` / description / `Arguments` / aligned `Flags` with defaults / `Examples`.\\n\\n`Run` intercepts `--help`/`-h` centrally; unknown-command error hints `entire graph help`; `analyze` is a hidden alias of `diff`; a parity test keeps the registry and dispatch switch in lockstep.\\n\\n## 2. `index`: progress bar + human summary\\n\\n- **Live progress bar** on stderr while building, when stderr is a terminal (dependency-free TTY detection). stdout untouched → piped JSON stays clean.\\n- **Human summary** when stdout is a terminal; piped or `--format json` emits the **same JSON as before** (`format_version: 1`). `--format` accepts `json`, `text` and `auto`, and now **defaults to `auto`** rather than always emitting JSON.\\n\\n## 3. `index`: smooth cadence, phase-aware bar, `--force`\\n\\n- **Cadence.** Replaced one hard-coded \\\"every 1024\\\" threshold (which gave <1024-file repos a single end-of-parse jump) with an adaptive file cadence (~100 updates; every file on small repos) + bounded relation cadence. This repo now emits ~107 incremental parse events instead of 1.\\n- **Phase-aware bar.** Filled bar + ratio while parsing; spinner + climbing relation count while linking (the relations phase has no file total, so a full bar read as \\\"done\\\").\\n- **`--force`** rebuilds and overwrites the cache entry even on an unchanged tree (via `ProviderSnapshotOptions.ForceRebuild`, deliberately not part of the cache key).\\n\\n## 4. Fix the perpetual \\\"completeness: degraded\\\"\\n\\nIndexing this repo always reported **degraded** — caused entirely by 13 vendored, generated tree-sitter grammar C files (`internal/sem/**/parser.c`, some 30–54 MB): 10 over the 4 MiB parser cap (`E_FILE_TOO_LARGE`), 3 tripping tree-sitter (`E_PARSE_ERROR`). None are project source.\\n\\n- **`.graphignore`** — a repo-root ignore list (gitignore syntax) honored by **every** graph command on top of `.gitignore`, for files tracked in git on purpose that should stay out of the graph. Loaded in both matchers with root-`.gitignore` authority, before any `--ignore-file`. A committed `.graphignore` excludes the grammar `parser.c`/`scanner.c` blobs → this repo now indexes **completeness ok, 306/306 files, 0 partial failures**, no flags.\\n- **Heuristic** — `E_FILE_TOO_LARGE`/`E_MINIFIED` are deliberate skips (file still recorded), so they no longer count toward \\\"degraded\\\" on their own. Real gaps (`E_PARSE_ERROR`, `E_UNSUPPORTED_LANGUAGE`) still do; the parsed-ratio / zero-symbol guards still catch a mostly-unparsed repo; skips remain in `partial_failures` for transparency.\\n\\n## Compatibility\\n\\nWhat changes for a machine consumer of `entire graph index`:\\n\\n| | before | after |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| piped / redirected stdout | JSON | JSON (unchanged) |\\n| stdout is a terminal | JSON | **human summary** |\\n| `--format json` | JSON | JSON (unchanged) |\\n| JSON payload + `format_version` | 1 | 1 (unchanged) |\\n\\nOnly the interactive case moves. A script that pipes, redirects, or passes `--format json` — which is every non-interactive invocation — sees exactly what it saw before. A human running `index` in a terminal and parsing the output is the case that breaks, and `--format json` pins the old behavior.\\n\\n`--format auto` resolves by inspecting stdout, and `/dev/null` is explicitly not a terminal, so `index > /dev/null` still yields JSON rather than a summary written into the void.\\n\\nNew flags on `index`: `--force` (rebuild an unchanged tree) and the `text`/`auto` values above. `--head` is accepted for symmetry with the query commands but is a no-op — `index` is always HEAD-only, and `--worktree` is rejected outright.\\n\\n**Cache invalidation.** `.graphignore` now participates in the snapshot cache key. Entries built before this change key differently and will be rebuilt once on first use; that is a one-time cost, not a correctness issue. It is required: without it, editing `.graphignore` against an unchanged tree hit the stale entry and the new rules silently did nothing.\\n\\n## Review\\n\\nCopilot reviewed this branch across five rounds and converged with no open findings. Fixes it prompted, beyond the description correction above:\\n\\n- `.graphignore` was absent from the cache key (above) — reproduced with a two-file repo where adding an ignore returned `index_cache_hit=true` and still counted 2 files.\\n- `isTerminal` accepted any character device, and `/dev/null` is one, so `index --format auto > /dev/null` printed a human summary.\\n- The progress bar rendered the summary phase with the relations label, reading \\\"linking relations\\\" at the moment the run was finishing.\\n- Three comments that contradicted their own code: the per-command help fall-through, the `dispatchCommands` exclusion list, and the `--head` flag description.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n`help_test.go`, `progressbar_test.go`, `search_cache_test.go` (`--force`), `completeness_test.go` (skip-code exclusion + `.graphignore` honored by both matchers), plus updates to existing help-format assertions.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/78/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/78/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          }\n        ],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      },\n      \"issues\": {\n        \"total_count\": 0,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e18\",\n      \"query\": \"repo:entireio/entire-graph walkthrough\",\n      \"prs\": {\n        \"total_count\": 1,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/113\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/113/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/113/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/113/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/113\",\n            \"id\": 5174063592,\n            \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSqVa0c8AAAABAC-rWw\",\n            \"number\": 113,\n            \"title\": \"feat: prose retrieval + benchmark kit, README and docs refresh\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"ashtom\",\n              \"id\": 70720,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzIw\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70720?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/ashtom\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"closed\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-08-17T18:08:23Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-18T21:37:32Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-18T21:37:32Z\",\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"draft\": false,\n            \"pull_request\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/113\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/113\",\n              \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/113.diff\",\n              \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/113.patch\",\n              \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-18T21:37:32Z\"\n            },\n            \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/73\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n- Merges #104 (prose retrieval by section, multi-resolution promotion, and the\\n  full LoCoMo benchmark kit) as the foundation this README documents.\\n- Replaces the console-first landing page with a concise agent-first setup and\\n  usage flow, backed by a captured coding-agent walkthrough with visible graph\\n  queries, source grounding, cache signals, and limitations.\\n- Documents installation, agent activation, commands, search behavior, cache\\n  operation, trust boundaries, and snapshot formats.\\n- Reorganizes active documentation under consistent lowercase names; moves\\n  historical material into `docs/archive`.\\n- Adds the LoCoMo benchmark comparison to `docs/benchmarks.md` (root README\\n  stays number-free per this PR's own `docs/readme-plan.md`), including a\\n  verified BM25 arm — real harness code plus a result confirmed against the\\n  live run log, not asserted.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nEntire Graph is primarily used through a coding agent, but the previous README\\ndid not explain that journey clearly, and the benchmark evidence for the\\nretrieval work in #104 needed a home. This PR gives new users a complete\\nfirst-use path and a complete, sourced accuracy/cost comparison, in one place.\\n\\n## Relationship to #104\\n\\nThis branch contains #104's full diff. #104 remains open for its own review\\nhistory; once this PR merges, #104's commits are already on `main` and it\\nshould be closed as superseded rather than merged separately.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- `mise run test`, `go vet`, `gofmt` clean.\\n- Active Markdown links and heading anchors checked (scripted, all resolve).\\n- `git diff --check`.\\n- BM25 result cross-checked against the harness's own run log: `full_bm25`,\\n  2026-08-15 22:41 UTC, 1415/1540 = 91.88%, `fair_mode: true`.\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/113/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 0,\n              \"+1\": 0,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/113/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          }\n        ],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      },\n      \"issues\": {\n        \"total_count\": 0,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e19\",\n      \"query\": \"repo:entireio/forgemark histogram\",\n      \"prs\": {\n        \"total_count\": 0,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      },\n      \"issues\": {\n        \"total_count\": 0,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e20\",\n      \"query\": \"repo:entireio/forgemark fault injection\",\n      \"prs\": {\n        \"total_count\": 0,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      },\n      \"issues\": {\n        \"total_count\": 0,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e21\",\n      \"query\": \"repo:entireio/git-sync LFS\",\n      \"prs\": {\n        \"total_count\": 0,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      },\n      \"issues\": {\n        \"total_count\": 1,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/59\",\n            \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync\",\n            \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/59/labels{/name}\",\n            \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/59/comments\",\n            \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/59/events\",\n            \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/issues/59\",\n            \"id\": 4480006330,\n            \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOR9SkY88AAAABCwd4ug\",\n            \"number\": 59,\n            \"title\": \"LFS sync support?\",\n            \"user\": {\n              \"login\": \"jessehouwing\",\n              \"id\": 4173387,\n              \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjQxNzMzODc=\",\n              \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4173387?v=4\",\n              \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jessehouwing\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/jessehouwing\",\n              \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jessehouwing/followers\",\n              \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jessehouwing/following{/other_user}\",\n              \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jessehouwing/gists{/gist_id}\",\n              \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jessehouwing/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n              \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jessehouwing/subscriptions\",\n              \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jessehouwing/orgs\",\n              \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jessehouwing/repos\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jessehouwing/events{/privacy}\",\n              \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jessehouwing/received_events\",\n              \"type\": \"User\",\n              \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n              \"site_admin\": false\n            },\n            \"labels\": [],\n            \"state\": \"open\",\n            \"locked\": false,\n            \"assignees\": [],\n            \"milestone\": null,\n            \"comments\": 0,\n            \"created_at\": \"2026-05-19T18:33:44Z\",\n            \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-19T18:33:44Z\",\n            \"closed_at\": null,\n            \"assignee\": null,\n            \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n            \"issue_field_values\": [],\n            \"type\": null,\n            \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n            \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n              \"total\": 0,\n              \"completed\": 0,\n              \"percent_completed\": 0\n            },\n            \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n              \"blocked_by\": 0,\n              \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n              \"blocking\": 0,\n              \"total_blocking\": 0\n            },\n            \"body\": \"What would it take to add LFS support and stream it in the same way without having to store all the blobs locally?\",\n            \"reactions\": {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/59/reactions\",\n              \"total_count\": 1,\n              \"+1\": 1,\n              \"-1\": 0,\n              \"laugh\": 0,\n              \"hooray\": 0,\n              \"confused\": 0,\n              \"heart\": 0,\n              \"rocket\": 0,\n              \"eyes\": 0\n            },\n            \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/59/timeline\",\n            \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n            \"state_reason\": null,\n            \"pinned_comment\": null,\n            \"score\": 1\n          }\n        ],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e22\",\n      \"query\": \"repo:entireio/git-sync bandwidth limit\",\n      \"prs\": {\n        \"total_count\": 0,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      },\n      \"issues\": {\n        \"total_count\": 0,\n        \"incomplete_results\": false,\n        \"items\": [],\n        \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"extra\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b31\",\n      \"q\": \"repo:entireio/cli review moved directory\",\n      \"rr\": [\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 3,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3011\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3011/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3011/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3011/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/3011\",\n              \"id\": 6206060692,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABcej4lA\",\n              \"number\": 3011,\n              \"title\": \"Sessions in a shared checkout claim every dirty tracked file, so idle and ended sessions land on unrelated commits\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"mattjes\",\n                \"id\": 79668769,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NjY4NzY5\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79668769?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mattjes\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/mattjes\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mattjes/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mattjes/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mattjes/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mattjes/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mattjes/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mattjes/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mattjes/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mattjes/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mattjes/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 7,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-04T15:39:47Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-07T04:47:17Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"> **AI disclosure:** this issue was investigated and written by Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic model `claude-opus-5-5`), running in Claude Code, on behalf of the owner of this GitHub account, who approved posting it. \\\"We\\\" below means the two of us. The reproduction was run by the model, as described under Steps to reproduce.\\n\\n### What happened?\\n\\nWhen several agent sessions work in one worktree, each session records every file `git status` reports as modified at its turn end, including files it never touched and files that were dirty before it started. Those files then count as the session's own work:\\n\\n- A commit of another session's file condenses this session into its checkpoint.\\n- Whatever is left carries forward, so the session keeps joining later commits, even after it has ended, until everything it recorded has been committed.\\n- `entire checkpoint explain` can then show the wrong session's prompt as the commit's intent, with a transcript about a different file.\\n\\nExpected: a session is linked to a commit when it changed a file in that commit. `sessions-and-checkpoints.md` describes `FilesTouched` as \\\"files modified, created, or deleted by the session\\\" and says a commit condenses \\\"every session whose touched files overlap the commit\\\". A session that only read files touched none of them.\\n\\nThis is not the documented \\\"Concurrent ACTIVE Sessions May Produce Spurious Checkpoints\\\" limitation. That one covers ACTIVE sessions and entries with minimal content. This happens with IDLE and ENDED sessions, and the checkpoint carries the session's full prompt and transcript.\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\nRun with the real binary and installed git hooks, sending Claude Code hook events to `entire hooks claude-code <event>` with a simulated transcript. No remote, telemetry off.\\n\\n1. `git init`, commit files `a.txt` and `b.txt`, `entire enable --local --agent claude-code`.\\n2. Start sessions A and B. Both get a prompt, so their turns overlap.\\n3. A edits `a.txt`, B edits `b.txt`. Each transcript shows only its own Edit.\\n4. Both Stop. Session state: A and B each have `files_touched: [a.txt, b.txt]`.\\n5. `git add a.txt && git commit`, with no TTY. The checkpoint holds A and B.\\n6. `git add b.txt && git commit`. The checkpoint holds A and B again.\\n7. `entire checkpoint explain <checkpoint of step 5>`: Intent is B's prompt, and the transcript shows the edit to `b.txt`.\\n\\n| Run | Commit | Sessions on the checkpoint |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| Both sessions, shared dirty copy | `a.txt`, then `b.txt` | A+B, A+B |\\n| Same, but A commits mid-turn from its own shell | `a.txt` | A+B (`explain` shows A's prompt here; B is still on the checkpoint) |\\n| Sequential turns, A stopped before `b.txt` was dirty | `a.txt`, then `b.txt` | A+B, B |\\n| Control: copy clean between the sessions | `a.txt`, then `b.txt` | A, B |\\n| Control: separate worktrees | `a.txt` | A |\\n| Read-only session, tracked file dirty before it started | that file | that session |\\n| Same, with an untracked file (has a baseline) | that file | no trailer |\\n| Read-only session, ended, three files dirty | each in turn | that session, until all three are committed |\\n| Same, after they are committed | an unrelated file | no trailer |\\n\\nSame results on the default `commit_linking` and on `always`, and on the latest nightly.\\n\\n### Entire CLI version\\n\\n0.12.2, and 0.12.3-nightly.202611040616.9dcc30a11. The code below is unchanged on `main`.\\n\\n### OS and architecture\\n\\nWindows 11, amd64. Not run on Linux or macOS. From reading the code, the \\\"foreign session\\\" check from #2668 would not stop this there either: over-claimed files are real overlap to it.\\n\\n### Agent\\n\\nClaude Code\\n\\n### Additional context\\n\\nCause: the fallback in `handleLifecycleTurnEnd` (`lifecycle.go`) merges all of `changes.Modified` into the turn's files. Untracked files have a prompt-start baseline, but tracked files don't. `filesOverlapWithContent` counts any modified file by name, and `filesWithRemainingAgentChanges` keeps what wasn't committed.\\n\\nThe fallback has a job: `git status` is how shell edits to tracked files are seen (#2720), so it can't simply go. Possible direction, for you to judge:\\n\\n1. Record dirty tracked files at prompt start and ignore unchanged ones at turn end. #2278 did this, and was closed by its author ten minutes after opening, with no review. The stat data from #2720 might serve as the baseline without extra hashing.\\n2. A baseline doesn't cover overlapping turns, as #2278 says itself. For that, a file known only from `git status` could be skipped if another session in the worktree recorded it, similar to `unrecordedNewFilesSinceLaunch`. The subagent path already avoids a whole-worktree diff for this reason.\\n\\nKNOWN_LIMITATIONS gives separate worktrees as the workaround, and they do avoid this, as the control above shows. A shared worktree is still a useful setup when sessions work on different files, because nothing has to be merged afterwards, so we'd like to keep it if attribution can be made right there. If worktrees are the intended answer, that entry could say the effect also covers IDLE and ENDED sessions and isn't only cosmetic, since `explain` can show another session's prompt and transcript as a commit's intent.\\n\\nIf one of these directions suits you, we're happy to open a PR once you've had a look.\\n\\nRelated: #2278, #2612, #2617, #2668, #2720, #1118.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3011/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3011/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1927\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1927/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1927/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1927/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/1927\",\n              \"id\": 5097932473,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABL9xGuQ\",\n              \"number\": 1927,\n              \"title\": \"Checkpoint metadata.json exceeds GitHub's 100 MB limit: files_touched is never deduplicated, and nested git worktrees are walked\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"ecgang\",\n                \"id\": 3526675,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MjY2NzU=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3526675?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/ecgang\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ecgang/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 4,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-07-25T03:55:27Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-12T19:34:42Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-12T19:34:42Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nOn a repo that uses git worktrees, `entire/checkpoints/v1` grows a\\n`metadata.json` large enough that GitHub refuses the push outright. Once that\\nhappens the checkpoint branch can never be pushed again without rewriting its\\nhistory, and the failure surfaces only as a warning attached to an unrelated\\n`git push`.\\n\\nTwo separate causes compound. Either one alone would be survivable.\\n\\n## Symptom\\n\\nEvery `git push` in the host repo now ends with:\\n\\n```\\n[entire] Warning: failed to push entire/checkpoints/v1 after sync: push failed:\\nremote: error: File 53/596dc8fea0/1/metadata.json is 111.79 MB; this exceeds\\nGitHub's file size limit of 100.00 MB\\nremote: error: GH001: Large files detected.\\n! refs/heads/entire/checkpoints/v1 -> [remote rejected] (pre-receive hook declined)\\n```\\n\\nThe user's own branches push fine, so this is easy to miss for a long time —\\nit reads as noise attached to a successful push.\\n\\nEnvironment: Entire CLI 0.8.42, go1.26.4, darwin/arm64.\\n\\n## Cause 1 — `files_touched` is appended to, never deduplicated\\n\\nThat `metadata.json` is a single checkpoint record with\\n`\\\"checkpoints_count\\\": 213`. Measured on the blob:\\n\\n| | |\\n|---|---|\\n| file size | 111.79 MB |\\n| lines | 1,292,267 |\\n| `files_touched` entries | 1,292,257 |\\n| **unique** entries | **67,340** |\\n| `files_touched` share of the file | 105.6 MB of 111.79 MB (94%) |\\n\\nA 19× duplication factor. No single path dominates — the most repeated one\\nappears 77 times — so this is broad re-appending across checkpoints rather than\\none pathological entry. Deduplicating alone takes the file to roughly 5.5 MB\\nand puts it back under the limit.\\n\\n## Cause 2 — nested git worktrees are walked as if they were project files\\n\\nOf the 67,340 unique paths, broken down by top-level segment:\\n\\n| prefix | unique paths |\\n|---|---|\\n| `.claude/` (agent worktrees live here) | 43,184 |\\n| `worktrees/` | 21,833 |\\n| the actual project | ~1,241 |\\n\\n96% of what is being recorded lives inside *other git checkouts* nested under\\nthe repo root. Linked worktrees have their own `.git` and their own history;\\ntheir contents are not changes to the host repo. `node_modules` is correctly\\nexcluded, so the walker already has an ignore mechanism — nested worktrees just\\naren't in it.\\n\\nThis is the part that makes the growth unbounded in practice. Anyone driving\\nparallel coding agents accumulates worktrees, and each one multiplies the\\nrecorded set.\\n\\n## Scale of the resulting branch\\n\\n| | |\\n|---|---|\\n| commits on `entire/checkpoints/v1` | 8,842 |\\n| files | 32,799 |\\n| unique blob bytes | 1,336.9 MB |\\n| distinct blobs over 50 MB | 3 |\\n\\nMany identical 50 MB `full.jsonl` blobs exist, but git dedupes those by hash,\\nso they cost storage once. The 111.79 MB `metadata.json` is the only blob that\\nactually blocks the push.\\n\\n## Suggested fixes, in order of leverage\\n\\n1. **Deduplicate `files_touched` before writing.** One line, ~19× smaller, no\\n   behaviour change — the array is a set in everything but type.\\n2. **Do not descend into nested git worktrees.** A directory containing a\\n   `.git` entry that is not the repo root is a separate checkout. This is where\\n   the remaining ~50× lives.\\n3. **Store `files_touched` as a newline-delimited sidecar** rather than inline\\n   in a JSON object. It streams, it chunks, and it stops one growing field from\\n   deciding whether the whole record is writable.\\n4. **Check size before pushing and fail loudly.** A blob over the remote's\\n   limit is unrecoverable once committed; catching it at write time is cheap,\\n   and catching it at push time is too late. The current warning is easy to\\n   scroll past.\\n\\nFix 1 is the emergency stop. Fix 2 is the actual bug. Fixes 3 and 4 are what\\nstop the next version of this.\\n\\n## Offer\\n\\nHappy to send a PR for 1 and 2 — they look self-contained and the repo has CI\\nin `test.yml`. Say which shape you'd prefer for 2 (skip any dir containing\\n`.git`, versus consulting `git worktree list`), since that's a design call\\nrather than a mechanical one. I can also supply the checkpoint that triggered\\nthis if a reproduction is useful, though it is 111 MB.\\n\\nDisclosure: this report was researched and written with AI assistance\\n(Claude Code). Every number above is measured from the actual blob with\\n`git cat-file`, not estimated.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1927/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1927/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1471\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1471/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1471/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1471/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/1471\",\n              \"id\": 4696234118,\n              \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABF-rYhg\",\n              \"number\": 1471,\n              \"title\": \"Proposal: Store Checkpoints In Per-Checkpoint Git Refs\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"pfleidi\",\n                \"id\": 118549,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjExODU0OQ==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118549?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pfleidi\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 4,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-06-18T21:56:59Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-16T14:01:16Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-16T14:01:16Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n                \"total\": 0,\n                \"completed\": 0,\n                \"percent_completed\": 0\n              },\n              \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n                \"blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n                \"blocking\": 0,\n                \"total_blocking\": 0\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Problem\\n\\nEntire currently stores committed checkpoints in one append-only Git branch, `entire/checkpoints/v1`. That has a few problems:\\n\\n- The Git repository keeps growing without clear cleanup boundaries.\\n- GitHub treats `entire/checkpoints/v1` like a normal branch and may show “open a pull request” prompts after checkpoint pushes.\\n- In new repositories, GitHub has sometimes selected `entire/checkpoints/v1` as the default branch because no other branch existed yet.\\n- Pushes are broader than necessary because one branch represents all checkpoint history.\\n\\nThe proposed direction is to store each checkpoint under its own Git ref.\\n\\n## Related Work\\n\\nThis should build on the checkpoint-store refactor tracked in https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/1433.\\n\\nIdeally the pluggable store boundary lands before the ref-store work starts. In practice, this work may happen in parallel across 2-4 people. The ref-store design should follow the direction of that issue and avoid introducing a second abstraction that would need to be reconciled later.\\n\\nThe migration approach can reuse ideas from https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1397, but production checkpoint refs should point to commits, not raw tree objects.\\n\\n## Storage Model\\n\\nEach checkpoint gets one stable ref: `refs/entire/checkpoints/<shard>/<checkpoint-id>`.\\n\\nThe ref points to a checkpoint commit containing the checkpoint tree. The first commit for a migrated checkpoint can be an orphan commit that reuses the existing `entire/checkpoints/v1` subtree. Later updates can advance the same ref and preserve per-checkpoint history.\\n\\nThe ref should not point directly to a raw tree object. Commits work better with existing Git tooling and let us keep using Git commit signing.\\n\\nFor new CLI versions, the ref store is authoritative. If a checkpoint is written to refs, the CLI should read it from refs so ref-store issues are visible during rollout.\\n\\n## Metadata Versioning\\n\\nRoot checkpoint metadata should include both `cli_version` and `checkpoints_version`.\\n\\n`cli_version` records the CLI that wrote the checkpoint. `checkpoints_version` records the checkpoint storage format, for example `refs-1`. Session metadata does not need a separate checkpoint storage version.\\n\\n## Checkpoint IDs\\n\\nExisting checkpoint IDs cannot change because they are already referenced from Git history. Legacy IDs should keep the current prefix-shard layout. It would be possible to create a commit/checkpoint mapping using ref structure but that would add additional complexity.\\n\\nFuture checkpoint IDs are expected to be [ULIDs](https://github.com/ulid/spec). New ULID refs should use the last two ULID characters as the shard, for example `refs/entire/checkpoints/ZN/01KVBJCWYA4YW6J5M9GP655HZN`. This is to ensure an even spread of shards across checkpoints while keeping the checkpoint IDs lexicographically sortable.\\n\\nThe ref resolver should support both legacy IDs and ULIDs for the time being.\\n\\n## Rollout Control\\n\\nRollout should use `strategy_options`, consistent with existing settings in `.entire/settings.json`.\\n\\nA possible setting is:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"strategy_options\\\": {\\n    \\\"checkpoint_store\\\": \\\"refs-v1-mirror\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\nExpected modes:\\n\\n- unset: current `entire/checkpoints/v1` behavior\\n- `refs-v1-mirror`: refs are authoritative, and `entire/checkpoints/v1` is still written as a temporary compatibility mirror\\n- `refs-v1`: refs only, after the ref store has proven stable\\n\\nThe exact names can change, but rollout mode should stay separate from checkpoint metadata versioning.\\n\\n## Initial Rollout\\n\\nDuring the initial rollout, the CLI should dual-write:\\n\\n- authoritative per-checkpoint refs\\n- a temporary `entire/checkpoints/v1` compatibility mirror\\n\\nThis is based on prior rollout experience where some repositories moved to a new storage mode too early and reverse-migration tooling had to be built afterwards to avoid data loss.\\n\\nThe `entire/checkpoints/v1` mirror should be removed once the ref store has proven stable.\\n\\n## Migration And Backfill\\n\\n\\nThe first version should create one commit per existing checkpoint by reusing the checkpoint subtree from `entire/checkpoints/v1`. It does not need to reconstruct the full `entire/checkpoints/v1` update history.\\n\\nMigration should preserve useful ordering and timestamps where possible, because some listing flows sort by checkpoint or commit time.\\n\\nMigration commits should use normal checkpoint signing behavior by default. The operator’s Git identity should be the default identity. The migration command may also allow an explicit author, such as `Entire Checkpoint Migration <checkpoints@entire.io>`, and an explicit signing key via `--signing-key`. If we wanted to simplify the migration command, skipping checkpoint signing completely would also be an option.\\n\\nMigration should signal refs for push through the same mechanism as normal checkpoint writes.\\n\\n## Push Discovery\\n\\nThe CLI should not push every local checkpoint ref. That would push refs fetched for local reads, and deleting local refs after push would make normal local workflows worse.\\n\\nInstead, checkpoint writes should enqueue refs that need to be pushed. A simple flock-protected JSONL queue in the Git common directory is enough for the first version. Batch pushes should be used so migrated or newly written refs are not pushed one by one.\\n\\n## Reads And Listings\\n\\nBranch-scoped flows should continue to use code commit history (as opposed to checkpoint commit history) to find relevant checkpoint IDs, then resolve those IDs to checkpoint refs.\\n\\nIf needed refs are missing locally, the CLI should fetch those refs directly and efficiently rather than asking users to run Git commands.\\n\\nStorage-level cleanup and maintenance operations can list local checkpoint refs only for now. No local checkpoint index is needed in the first version.\\n\\n## Out Of Scope\\n\\nThis proposal does not decide:\\n\\n- exact retry or partial-failure behavior\\n- queue compaction or repair mechanics\\n- remote pruning behavior\\n- local indexing\\n- detailed implementation sequencing\\n- session-level refs\\n- imported-transcript association refs\\n\\n## Future Extensions\\n\\nLater work may add refs such as `refs/entire/sessions/...` and `refs/entire/commits/...`.\\n\\nSession refs could expose session-level checkpoint data directly. Commit association refs could link imported transcripts to existing code commits without rewriting Git history.\\n\\nThose are useful future directions, but they should not complicate the checkpoint-ref rollout.\\n\\n## Review Checklist\\n\\nBefore moving this proposal into implementation planning, we should confirm that it addresses the problems with the current monolithic branch design:\\n\\n- Checkpoint storage has cleanup boundaries instead of one ever-growing branch.\\n- GitHub no longer treats `entire/checkpoints/v1` as a normal branch that invites pull requests.\\n- New repositories cannot accidentally get `entire/checkpoints/v1` selected as the default branch.\\n- Ref storage is authoritative during rollout, so new-storage bugs are visible.\\n- The temporary `entire/checkpoints/v1` mirror exists only for rollback and downgrade safety.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1471/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1471/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n              \"pinned_comment\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            }\n          ],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 64,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3073\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3073/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3073/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3073/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3073\",\n              \"id\": 6284538584,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABN0o_HA\",\n              \"number\": 3073,\n              \"title\": \"fix(hooks): refresh a stale moved copy of Entire's hook on the next turn\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n                \"id\": 26940511,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI2OTQwNTEx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Beehtrix\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-09T10:42:28Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-09T11:36:33Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3073\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3073\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3073.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3073.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes #3050.\\n\\n@Soph, this is the per-turn side of your `refreshMovedEntireHooks` and `reclaimFromWrappers`. Codex found it while reviewing #3046, and it is on main, so it gets its own PR off main.\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\n`hookStateIn` reads only the file at the hook's name. Copies of Entire's hook that another hook manager moved aside (`<hook>.<suffix>`, such as `pre-push.old`) are rewritten only during an install, and `EnsureSetup` skips the install while the hooks read Current. So a stale moved copy stays until someone runs `entire enable`.\\n\\nThe copy that matters is one from before the chain guard (`ENTIRE_CHAINING_<HOOK>`). An earlier release could leave this layout:\\n\\n```\\npre-push               Entire's hook, current, chains to pre-push.pre-entire\\npre-push.pre-entire    the manager's wrapper, runs pre-push.old\\npre-push.old           Entire's hook from before the guard, chains to pre-push.pre-entire\\n```\\n\\n`pre-push` reads Current, so no agent turn touches it, and every push goes Entire, wrapper, old copy, wrapper, old copy, and never finishes. `ReinstallGitHooks`' comment says skipping the refresh is safe because a wrapper in the hook's place reads Absent, but here the wrapper sits in the backup, behind a current hook.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\n- `hookStateIn` checks the file at the hook's name as before (now `ownHookStateIn`). If that reads Current, it reads Outdated when a moved copy is stale (`hasStaleMovedEntireHook`). A moved copy is a name `refreshMovedEntireHooks` looks at (`isMovedHookName`, now shared by both) that carries Entire's marker. It is stale when a line that runs (comments don't count) chains to `<hook>.pre-entire` without the guard or runs Entire from the working tree, or when it is a pre-push hook from before the ref list. The hook itself reads Outdated in those last two shapes too. What an install writes there has no chain and is current, so one reinstall clears it. `.legacy` counts too, as it does in `refreshMovedEntireHooks`.\\n- The per-turn reinstall must not rewrite a current Entire hook: it may hold lines the user added, and it gets no backup (the `ReinstallGitHooks` comment). So when a hook reads Outdated only because of a moved copy, `installGitHooks` marks its spec `keepHook`. The install still runs the reclaims and the refresh for that hook and leaves the hook's own text as it is. `entire enable` still rewrites everything, as before.\\n- The per-turn reinstall also rewrites only the stale moved copies (`staleCopiesOnly`). A current copy may hold lines the user added and gets no backup, like the hook itself, so it stays as it is. That holds when the hook itself is outdated too, where main rewrote every copy. For a hook marked `keepHook`, `reclaimFromWrappers` also takes back only stale copies, so a current copy the backup's wrapper runs by name keeps its lines too. It rechecks the hook first, since a manager may have put its wrapper in the hook's place since `keepHook` was decided. `entire enable` still refreshes all of them. A stale copy is rewritten without a backup, the same way the per-turn path already rewrites a stale hook at the hook's own name: Entire can't tell a manager's active copy from a user's own file by its name, and the copy has to change to stop the loop.\\n- Entire will not install through a symlinked hooks directory, so a stale copy behind the link alone must not send every agent turn to a reinstall that fails on that refusal. `EnsureSetup` asks `gitHooksNeedReinstall`, which skips that case, while `CheckGitHookState` still reads Outdated there, so doctor reports the copy next to its existing SYMLINK fix.\\n- The write step moves out of `installHooks` into `writeSpecHook`, which keeps `installHooks` under the complexity gate. `chainGuard` names the guard for both `chainCall` and the check.\\n- `entire doctor` gives the moved copy as a third reason a hook can be out of date.\\n\\nThe check costs one listing of the hooks directory per managed hook, and a read of each `<hook>.*` file there (usually git's `.sample` files), on each agent turn, and only when the hook itself reads Current.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n`cmd/entire/cli/strategy/hook_moved_state_test.go`:\\n\\n- `TestCheckGitHookState_StaleMovedCopy`: a pre-guard chain (in a manager's copy and in `.legacy`), a working-tree launcher and a pre-push copy from before the ref list read Outdated. A guarded chain, what an install writes there, a copy that names the backup or a working-tree launcher only in a comment, a copy that is not Entire's, and an older copy of the backup read Current.\\n- `TestReinstallGitHooks_RepairsStaleMovedCopyAndKeepsHook`: the layout above, with a line the user added to Entire's hook. It reads Outdated, and `ReinstallGitHooks` repairs the copy, keeps the hook and the user's line, and leaves the set Current. The hook then runs to the end. That holds whether the wrapper names the copy (`reclaimFromWrappers` puts the placeholder there) or computes its name (`refreshMovedEntireHooks` rewrites it).\\n- `TestReinstallGitHooks_KeepsCurrentMovedCopy`: a stale `commit-msg.tool-old` beside a current `commit-msg.saved` holding a user line, with the hook current, with it outdated, and with the backup's wrapper running `.saved` by name. The reinstall repairs the stale copy and keeps `.saved` as it was.\\n- `TestHooksNeedReinstall_StaleMovedCopyBehindSymlinkedHooksDir`: a stale copy behind a symlinked hooks directory reads Outdated but needs no reinstall through the link, and needs one in the directory itself.\\n- `TestInstallHooks_KeepHookRechecksTheHookUnderTheLock`: a manager installs between the `keepHook` decision and the install, and the copy it moved still gets the user's hook back.\\n\\nEach fails without its part of the fix, and the second also fails if the hook is rewritten (the user's line is lost).\\n\\nRun in a Linux container: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/` and the doctor git-hook tests pass, `golangci-lint` v2.15.0 reports 0 issues, and the complexity gate reports no new or worsened function.\\n\\n## Overlap\\n\\nThis merges cleanly with main, #3049's fix, #3028 and #3051. It conflicts with #2959 (and so #3003 and #3046), which change `hookStateIn` and `refreshMovedEntireHooks` for entire-brain's wrapper. The conflicts are small, and I'll resolve them in whichever lands second. With #2959, Brain's moved copy (`pre-push.pre-entire-brain`) is one of the names this checks.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3073/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 1,\n                \"+1\": 1,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3073/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2855\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2855/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2855/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2855/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2855\",\n              \"id\": 5968870246,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABJ47hzg\",\n              \"number\": 2855,\n              \"title\": \"Find a session's transcript after its agent moves into a worktree\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-21T21:31:08Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-27T20:49:54Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2855\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2855\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2855.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2855.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2397/changes/cli/1648\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nClaude Code keeps a session's transcript under `~/.claude/projects/<working dir>/`. When a session moves into a worktree with `EnterWorktree`, Claude writes the whole transcript under the worktree's folder. The path its hooks reported at session start never exists, and hooks report the new path only at turn end.\\n\\nIf the agent commits in that first turn, the commit gets an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer, but condensation finds no live transcript at the recorded path. It also finds no stored copy, because no turn has ended yet. So condensation fails with \\\"live transcript is empty or unreadable\\\", and the trailer points to a checkpoint that is never written.\\n\\nMain has the same bug. #2531 handles a session's home worktree, but it doesn't follow a transcript that Claude moved.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nWhen the recorded transcript is missing, `resolveTranscriptPath` now looks for the session's file in the agent's session folders for each worktree of the repo, and for any directory inside one, the current worktree first. It uses the first file it finds, and records that path in the session state so later reads go straight to it.\\n\\nThe lookup runs only when the recorded path is one the agent would derive for the session's home worktree or a directory inside it (Claude names its folder after the launch directory, so a session started in `<repo>/frontend` records `<home>-frontend`), so attached or imported sessions with custom paths are left alone. External agents are skipped, because looking up their session folder starts a process. Only Claude Code's flat folder layout (one sibling folder per working directory) is searched; agents with a nested layout, such as Cursor, return before any worktree is listed. `ctx` is passed through to the callers so the lookup can list worktrees.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- The moved transcript is found from inside the worktree and from the main checkout, and the state follows it.\\n- A session whose file is in no worktree's folder still reports it missing.\\n- A session launched from a subdirectory is followed whether it moves to the worktree root or the same subdirectory.\\n- A custom recorded path, or one under a different projects folder, isn't second-guessed.\\n- A test that runs the commit hooks: a first-turn commit made after moving into a worktree gets its checkpoint written. Run for a launch at the repo root and in a subdirectory; both fail on the base commit (no checkpoint, stale transcript path).\\n\\n## Live check (real Claude Code, headless)\\n\\nOne turn: `EnterWorktree`, edit a file, commit.\\n\\n| Build | Launched in | Trailer | Checkpoint |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| base (`fedd31ca10`, this PR's parent) | repo root | yes | not written (\\\"condensation failed\\\") |\\n| this branch | repo root | yes | written |\\n| base | `frontend/` | yes | not written (\\\"condensation failed\\\") |\\n| this branch | `frontend/` | yes | written |\\n\\nLaunched from `frontend/`, Claude wrote the moved transcript under the worktree root's folder.\\n\\n## Not in this PR\\n\\n- Amend and post-rewrite still use the stored-copy fallback.\\n- Worktree paths that go through a symlink may not match how Claude names its folders.\\n- A session that changes folders in turn 2 or later, while its old file still exists, reads the stale file until the turn ends.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2855/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2855/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3056\",\n              \"id\": 6255425292,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABNdzkwQ\",\n              \"number\": 3056,\n              \"title\": \"fix(strategy): spell agent-reported paths as git does on case-insensitive filesystems\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n                \"id\": 26940511,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI2OTQwNTEx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Beehtrix\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 5,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-07T05:06:26Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-11T18:20:27Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3056\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3056\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3056.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3056.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes #3054\\n\\nOn a case-insensitive filesystem (the macOS and Windows default) an agent can name a tracked file in another case than git does: writing `readme.md` changes `README.md`. Entire recorded the agent's spelling, which never matches a commit, so the session stayed pending after the file was committed. The issue has the two ways it happens (dirty at turn end, committed mid-turn).\\n\\nI reviewed this on my fork first (Beehtrix/cli#22).\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\n`strategy.FilterTrackableChanges`, which every capture route already applies (turn end, task completion, per-tool hooks, Codex child files, and the transcript fallback of a mid-turn commit), now first spells each path as git's index does (`strategy.TrackedSpellings`, in `strategy/path_case.go`):\\n\\n- It only acts where a directory on a reported path, from the one holding the file up to the worktree root, finds its entries under another case, which `worktreedir.CaseProbe` asks the filesystem in process: one of the directory's entries, looked up with its letters' case swapped, opens the same file, and the directory doesn't also list that spelling as an entry of its own (a hard-linked pair, which only a directory that respects case can hold). A directory that is gone, has no entry with a letter in its name, or has over 4096 entries can't tell, and then nothing is rewritten; it doesn't borrow its parent's answer, since Windows lets a directory respect case inside one that ignores it. It doesn't go by git's `core.ignorecase`, one setting for the whole repository, which a linked worktree on another filesystem, a moved repository or a Windows directory with its own case sensitivity can disagree with. Every directory on the path counts, not only the one holding the file: on Windows `SRC/App.go` in a root that ignores case opens `src/App.go` even when `src/` respects case. On a case-sensitive filesystem nothing changes and git isn't asked, since `readme.md` and `README.md` are two files there.\\n- It asks git once per call for the index's spellings (`gitrepo.IndexPathsIgnoringCase`: `git ls-files -z --cached` with `:(literal,icase)` pathspecs, chunked and bounded by `PathClassificationBudget` like the other classifiers).\\n- A spelling is rewritten only when each directory where it differs from the index's spelling ignores case, and it opens the same file (`os.SameFile` on rooted lstats): in a directory that respects case, two hard-linked names are two entries git tracks apart. A deletion has nothing left to open, so it's rewritten when the index has exactly one spelling of it and that one is gone too. Duplicates the rewrite leaves are dropped, keeping the first one's place.\\n- If git can't answer, the paths are kept as reported, as before.\\n\\n`worktreedir/case.go` is the same file as in my shared-checkout PR for #3011, which needs the same check for deletions; whichever lands second loses it from its diff.\\n\\nTurn end now runs `FilterTrackableChanges` before `filterToUncommittedFiles`, so a file committed mid-turn is checked against HEAD under git's spelling. Both only drop paths, so the order doesn't change what either drops. Task completion respells the subagent's transcript paths before `filterToUncommittedFiles` and the committed-file check that attaches the task to a commit. The transcript route a commit hook takes before the session's first turn end (`filterTrackableFiles`) spells its paths first and keeps them in git's spelling.\\n\\n## Trade-offs\\n\\n- On macOS and Windows, each `FilterTrackableChanges` call runs one more `git ls-files`. A path git tracks under its own spelling still costs that call, since only git knows which paths it tracks. On Linux the cost is one read of each directory on the reported paths (each asked once per call), plus two `lstat`s per directory.\\n- A file that isn't tracked keeps the agent's spelling. git status lists such a file under its on-disk spelling, which the agent's tool normally created, so the two agree.\\n- `liveTaskTranscriptFiles` (co-authorship evidence for a running subagent) still compares the transcript's spelling with the commit's. It only decides whether a session counts as a co-author of a commit, and I left it out to keep this to what enters `FilesTouched`.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- `gitrepo.TestIndexPathsIgnoringCase`: index spellings for other-case names, literal brackets, an untracked name, and inherited `GIT_LITERAL_PATHSPECS` / `GIT_GLOB_PATHSPECS`.\\n- `worktreedir.TestCaseProbe_*`: the directory probe, with a lookup that folds case standing in for a directory that ignores case (a directory that respects case, a hard-linked pair of entries that must read as a directory that respects case, a directory that ignores case, one with no entry that tells, one that is gone, one over the entry bound, and paths that differ in several directories). `TestCaseProbeWindows` checks it against the filesystem itself on CI's Windows job.\\n- `strategy.TestTrackedSpelling`: the rule itself, with a hard link standing in for one file under two names and a stand-in probe for a directory that ignores case (same file where the directory ignores case, a hard link where it respects case, another file, no file, a deletion in a directory that respects case and in one that ignores it, two index spellings, git's spelling still present). `strategy.TestAnyDirectoryIgnoresCase`: every directory on a path counts toward asking git, not only the one holding the file.\\n- `strategy.TestFilterTrackableFiles_KeepsGitsSpellingWindows`: the transcript route keeps `README.md` for a transcript's `readme.md`; on a case-insensitive filesystem it fails without that part of the fix.\\n- `strategy.TestTrackedSpellings_CaseInsensitiveFilesystemWindows` and `TestFilterTrackableFiles_KeepsGitsSpellingWindows` are named so that CI's Windows job runs them on a real case-insensitive filesystem; on Linux they check that nothing changes.\\n- `integration_test/transcript_path_case_test.go`: the issue's two cases end to end. They run only where the filesystem ignores case, so CI's Linux job skips them.\\n\\nOn Linux with git 2.43, `go test ./...` and `go test -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/...` pass apart from 13 tests that fail the same way on a clean checkout of main in that environment (no `--ref-format`, SSH, DNS or user XDG cache, and running as root). golangci-lint v2.15.0 reports 0 issues, the complexity gate passes, and the changed packages and the integration package vet for Windows. I also ran the changed packages' tests and the two integration tests on a case-insensitive filesystem in the same container (ciopfs, a FUSE filesystem, mounted with `use_ino` so both spellings report one inode): the case tests pass there, and both integration tests fail on main there (`FilesTouched = [README.md readme.md]`, and `[readme.md]` still pending after the mid-turn commit). Four other `strategy` tests fail on that mount on main too, from the FUSE filesystem (a removed and re-added working directory, and a temp-dir cleanup).\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 1,\n                \"+1\": 1,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3056/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3055\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3055/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3055/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3055/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3055\",\n              \"id\": 6255424042,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABNdzg3w\",\n              \"number\": 3055,\n              \"title\": \"fix(strategy): stop sessions in a shared checkout from claiming each other's files\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n                \"id\": 26940511,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI2OTQwNTEx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Beehtrix\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 5,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-07T05:06:15Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-11T20:00:58Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3055\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3055\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3055.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3055.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes #3011\\n\\n@mattjes reported this and handed it over on the issue. This covers both directions from the issue: the prompt-start baseline (direction 1), and the overlapping-turns case (direction 2), which @mattjes said is the one they run into.\\n\\nI reviewed this on my fork first (Beehtrix/cli#19).\\n\\n## What was wrong\\n\\nAt turn end, `handleLifecycleTurnEnd` merged every file `git status` lists into the turn's files: `changes.Modified`, plus `New` and `Deleted`. git status shows every dirty file in the worktree, not which session changed it, so in a shared checkout a session took:\\n\\n- tracked files that were already dirty when its prompt started (untracked files had a baseline, tracked files didn't), and\\n- files another session changed while their turns overlapped.\\n\\nThose files then counted as the session's own work, so a commit of them linked it, and `entire checkpoint explain` could show its prompt and transcript as the commit's intent. A foreground task's completion (`completeSubagentTaskRecord`) reads git status the same way and had the same problem.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\nBoth narrowings live in `statusClaim` (`shared_worktree_claims.go`) and apply only to what git status contributes. Files the transcript names are always kept.\\n\\n1. **Already dirty at prompt start.** The prompt-start status walk already ran for untracked files. It now also lists the tracked files with staged or unstaged changes, and records their stat with the same fields and bounds as the untracked stats from #2720 (`PrePromptState.DirtyTrackedFileStats`; a deleted file gets the zero stat, a directory such as a submodule gets none). At turn end such a file is left out while its stat still matches. There's no extra status walk and no hashing. The pre-task state gets the same baseline for foreground tasks. State written before this change has no baseline, and turn end then keeps every dirty file as before.\\n2. **Overlapping turns.** If another session homed in the same worktree had a turn running at some point since the prompt started, only files the transcript names are kept; a name spelled in another case than git's counts when both spellings open the same file in the worktree (an agent on macOS or Windows that writes `readme.md` changes `README.md`) and git status doesn't also list that exact spelling. On a case-sensitive filesystem they are two files and don't match. A deleted file has nothing left to open, so for a deletion the directory decides: the transcript's spelling must open no file either, and each directory where the two spellings differ must find its other entries under another case (`worktreedir.CaseProbe`, in `worktreedir` because the fix for transcript spellings, a separate bug (#3054), needs the same check). That asks the filesystem rather than git's `core.ignorecase`, one setting for the whole repository, which a linked worktree on another filesystem, a moved repository or a Windows directory with its own case sensitivity can disagree with. A directory that can't tell (it is gone, has no entry with a letter in its name, or has over 4096 entries) doesn't match, and it doesn't borrow its parent's answer, since Windows lets a directory respect case inside one that ignores it; a directory that lists both spellings of an entry (a hard-linked pair) respects case. `strategy.OtherSessionActiveSince` counts a session that interacted after the prompt started (`LastInteractionTime`: a turn started or ended, or it stopped) or is mid-turn now, unless its agent process has exited or, when that can't be checked, it's stuck past `StuckActiveThreshold` (the rule `attach.go` uses). The prompt-start time is taken before the status walk, so a session whose turn ends during the walk still counts. Sessions linked as parent and subagent session (Factory AI Droid Workers, through the parent's task record, the Worker's transcript while its first turn runs, or the link a Worker's own turn end resolves) don't count, except that a foreground task's completion counts its session's own Workers, which run its other tasks.\\n\\nThe overlap check only runs when git status lists a file the transcript doesn't name, so a turn whose edits are all in its transcript doesn't list sessions.\\n\\n`PrePromptState.Timestamp` and `PreTaskState.Timestamp` are now written with nanoseconds, so the comparison with `LastInteractionTime` doesn't round to the second. `time.Parse(time.RFC3339, ...)` reads both forms, and nothing else reads the field.\\n\\n## Trade-offs\\n\\n- A shell edit made during an overlap is claimed by neither session, so a commit of only that file gets no trailer. The background-task path makes the same choice (`unrecordedNewFilesSinceLaunch` claims nothing when tasks overlap): taking the file would link a session to someone else's commit, which is worse and harder to notice. `KNOWN_LIMITATIONS.md` gets an entry for it. An external agent that names no files in its transcript records nothing during an overlap, and a deletion the transcript names in another case is claimed by neither session when its directory can't tell how it finds its entries.\\n- A background subagent's shell edit to a tracked file, made while its parent is idle, is no longer picked up by the parent's next turn end, because the file is dirty when that prompt starts. That pickup was a side effect of claiming every dirty file. An edit made during one of the parent's turns is still picked up. I updated the line in `sessions-and-checkpoints.md` that described it.\\n- Another session stopping during a turn counts as an overlap, because a stop updates the same `LastInteractionTime`. Telling a stop while idle apart from a turn that just ended would need a new session-state field for the turn-end time; the `KNOWN_LIMITATIONS.md` entry says so.\\n- A staged-only change (`git add`, `git apply --cached`) to a file that was already dirty isn't seen as a change, since the baseline compares the file's stat, not its index entry.\\n- A user's edit to an already-dirty file during a turn is still claimed, like any user edit during a turn.\\n- Mid-turn commits are unchanged. The \\\"Concurrent ACTIVE Sessions\\\" limitation (an ACTIVE session is condensed into any commit in its worktree) still applies, as the issue's second table row shows.\\n- Windows has no process liveness or commit provenance yet: `proclive` has no Windows implementation, which #1488 left out. So there a session mid-turn for over an hour isn't counted as overlapping, as before. And a commit made outside any agent, of a shell edit no session recorded, links a session that is mid-turn, as such a commit already does there for any file no session recorded; on main, the other session's claim on every dirty file happened to keep the mid-turn session off it. @mattjes found both on Windows 11. Both go with Windows support in `proclive`, filed separately as #3053, and `KNOWN_LIMITATIONS.md` describes them.\\n\\nNot checked for overlap: sessions homed in other worktrees that edit this one, and other sessions' background tasks, whose own stop already handles overlap with other tasks.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n`integration_test/shared_checkout_attribution_test.go` covers the rows of the issue's table with simulated hooks:\\n\\n| Case | main | this branch |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Overlapping turns: A edits `a.txt`, B edits `b.txt` | both sessions get both files; both commits link A and B | A gets `a.txt`, B gets `b.txt`; each commit links one session |\\n| Overlap where B's transcript names `readme.md` and git lists `README.md`, on a filesystem that ignores case | the commit links A and B | B gets `README.md`; the commit links B |\\n| The same for a deletion, on a filesystem that ignores case | the commit links A and B | B gets the deletion of `README.md`; the commit links B |\\n| Read-only session, tracked file dirty before its prompt | claimed; the commit gets a trailer | not claimed; no trailer |\\n| Sequential turns | B also takes A's `a.txt` | B gets only `b.txt` |\\n| Overlap with a shell edit and a shell-created file | both sessions claim them | neither does (the trade-off above) |\\n| Foreground task with a file dirty before launch, then with another session's turn running | the task takes `a.txt`, then `a.txt` and `b.txt` | the task takes only its `task.txt`, then nothing |\\n| Shell edit to an already-dirty file, no other session | claimed | still claimed |\\n| Factory AI Droid parent's shell edit while its own Worker's first turn runs | claimed | still claimed |\\n\\nAll but the last two fail on main (3a760b96a). The two case rows run only where the filesystem ignores case (macOS, Windows), so they skip on Linux, where I ran the suite; the other rows pass here. I also ran the `TestSharedCheckout_` tests and the case unit tests on a case-insensitive filesystem in the same container (ciopfs, a FUSE filesystem, mounted with `use_ino` so both spellings report one inode; git sets `core.ignorecase` there): all pass, and both case rows fail on main there. Unit tests cover the status walk, the stat baseline, the no-baseline fallback, case matching of transcript names (on a case-sensitive filesystem, with a hard link standing in for one file under two names, and for deletions, with `core.ignorecase` set against what the filesystem does), the directory probe (`worktreedir.TestCaseProbe_*`, with a lookup that folds case standing in for a directory that ignores case, and a hard-linked pair of entries, which must read as a directory that respects case), and `OtherSessionActiveSince` (stuck, owner alive or gone, ended, other worktree, related, parent and subagent sessions, a Worker's transcript link, and a session's own Workers for its tasks). `TestStatusClaim_DirtyTrackedBaselineWindows` is named so that CI's Windows job runs it: there the stat is only size and modification time, and it checks nested paths from git status, unchanged files, and a same-size edit. `TestCaseProbeWindows`, `TestNamedFiles_OtherCaseIsTheSameFileWindows` and `TestNamedFiles_DeletedInOtherCaseWindows` run there too, where they check the case match itself.\\n\\nOn Linux with git 2.43, `go test ./...` and `go test -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/...` pass apart from 13 tests that fail the same way on a clean checkout of main in that environment (no `--ref-format`, SSH, DNS or user XDG cache, and running as root). golangci-lint v2.15.0 reports 0 issues, and the complexity gate passes. The changed packages and the integration package also compile and vet for Windows (`headCheckpointID` moved from a `linux || darwin` file into `shared_checkout_attribution_test.go`). @mattjes ran the branch on Windows 11 and Ubuntu 24.04: the original bug is fixed on both. The build problem they found is fixed here, and the case fix passes on that FUSE filesystem; their rerun would confirm it on NTFS.\\n\\n@MuskanPaliwal, this is the change I asked you to look at on the issue.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3055/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 1,\n                \"+1\": 1,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3055/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2781\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2781/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2781/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2781/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2781\",\n              \"id\": 5858135146,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABIhI98A\",\n              \"number\": 2781,\n              \"title\": \"attach: save session state before writing the checkpoint\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-15T00:54:11Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-15T03:02:52Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2781\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2781\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2781.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2781.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Follow-up to #2674.\\n\\n## Bug\\n`entire session attach` wrote the checkpoint and only then saved the session state. If that save failed, attach logged a warning and still reported success. The token offset never moved, so the session's next checkpoint counted the attached tokens a second time. In the repro, turn 2 (7 tokens) was attached and turn 3 (3 tokens) was committed by hooks. The checkpoints held 7 and 10 tokens, 17 in total instead of 10.\\n\\n## Fix\\n- The state is now saved **before** the checkpoint write, which records the tokens as counted first. The save runs under the session lock. If that save fails, attach returns an error and nothing is attached.\\n- If the write fails, the earlier state is put back, but only when the write provably stored nothing (no ref it can write to moved, or only the shared v1 branch did and the checkpoint there doesn't hold the session) and no hook has written the state since. In any other case the tokens stay counted, and the error says so.\\n- `BaseCommit` is still seeded after the trailer rewrite, now under the session lock. A failure there is now a stderr warning, because the checkpoint and its tokens are already correct.\\n- The race guard for hook activity while attach waits at its prompt is unchanged. It now reads the counted-from offset from an unmutated copy.\\n\\n## Tests\\n- Integration (`TestTokenScope_AttachStateSaveFailureDoesNotRecount`): the session-state directory is made read-only while attach runs. Attach now fails, writes no checkpoint and leaves HEAD alone, and the next checkpoint counts 10 tokens.\\n- Unit tests cover three cases:\\n  - A failed write restores the earlier state, or removes only the state file attach created, under both the branch and git-refs primaries.\\n  - A write that stores the session and then fails keeps the state.\\n  - The undo leaves alone a state that a hook changed, including a pending-usage update from a Stop.\\n- The existing attach token, race-guard and BaseCommit tests pass.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2781/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2781/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2199\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2199/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2199/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2199/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2199\",\n              \"id\": 5304514449,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBp3OpQ\",\n              \"number\": 2199,\n              \"title\": \"Fix stale lock cleanup\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Rohitkanithi\",\n                \"id\": 63586900,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTg2OTAw\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63586900?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Rohitkanithi\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Rohitkanithi/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 5,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-31T20:23:22Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-05T23:13:02Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2199\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2199\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2199.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2199.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Closes #2197.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAdds cleanup support for stale lock files created under the git common dir:\\n\\n- `entire-shadow-locks`\\n- `entire-persistent-ref-locks`\\n\\n`entire clean --all` now discovers those lock files, reports them in dry-run output, and includes them in deletion summaries.\\n\\n## Review follow-up\\n\\nThis update addresses the lock-safety review feedback:\\n\\n- Revalidates Unix flock acquisitions against the current lock-file inode before returning from both blocking `Acquire` and bounded `AcquireContext` paths.\\n- Moves stale lock cleanup to run after shadow branch, session state, and checkpoint cleanup so normal cleanup operations use their locks first.\\n- Treats actively held lock files as skipped, not failed, so live sessions do not make `entire clean --all` exit non-zero just because a lock is busy.\\n- Adds an active-session guard for `entire clean --all` unless `--force` or `--dry-run` is used.\\n- Keeps lock-directory listing best-effort if one lock directory is unreadable.\\n- Uses platform-specific lock-file removal ordering for Unix and Windows.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n```bash\\nGOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-build-cache go test ./cmd/entire/cli/internal/flock ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy\\nGOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-build-cache go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run TestClean\\nGOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-build-cache go test ./cmd/entire/...\\nGOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-build-cache go build ./cmd/entire\\ngit diff --check\\n```\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2199/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2199/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2320\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2320/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2320/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2320/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2320\",\n              \"id\": 5386576708,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCq1lnw\",\n              \"number\": 2320,\n              \"title\": \"refactor(gitrepo): finish Git metadata consumer migration\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"id\": 34813274,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-08T12:16:46Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-18T08:10:41Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2320\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2320\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2320.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2320.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Part 5 of #2190's [agreed split](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2190#issuecomment-5499945525), following the canonical resolver in #2241 and checkpoint migration in #2254.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis branch includes the session migration from #2285 and strategy migration from #2305. Both prerequisites remain open. Keep this PR **open** until they land, then refresh onto main so reviewers can assess the remaining-consumer changes separately.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Why this change is needed\\r\\n\\r\\nThe earlier migrations introduced `gitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata`, but several consumers still interpreted Git metadata through older code. Codex and status had their own traversal logic. Settings, review, investigation, and trail still depended on forwarding helpers or the common-directory resolver and cache.\\r\\n\\r\\nLeaving those callers behind would preserve the disagreement this refactor is meant to remove. A caller could reuse a cached directory after metadata changed, or interpret a linked worktree differently from the session and checkpoint stores using the same repository.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis PR moves the remaining physical metadata lookups to the canonical resolver and deletes the old implementations after their final callers migrate.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Metadata resolution and storage ownership\\r\\n\\r\\n`gitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata` supplies the per-worktree Git directory, common Git directory, and worktree ID for an explicit worktree root. It returns complete metadata or an error, without running Git or caching the result.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe remaining consumers use those facts for different purposes:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Codex determines which checkout owns the discovered hook configuration. Its backlink, trust, submodule, and bare-layout checks remain consumer policy.\\r\\n- Status reads HEAD from the per-worktree Git directory. Explain and cleanup use the resolved worktree ID when selecting checkpoint or shadow-branch state.\\r\\n- Settings locates clone preferences in the common directory.\\r\\n- Review and investigation locate their shared markers, manifests, and findings.\\r\\n- Trail locates shared metadata and the base directory for checkout paths.\\r\\n- Setup cleanup opens the common directory through the shared rooted API.\\r\\n\\r\\n`paths.WorktreeRoot` still owns CWD discovery and its cache. `gitdir` still owns shared `os.Root` handles, including their lifetime and explicit reset behavior. Reads, writes, and locks continue through the existing rooted/no-follow storage code.\\r\\n\\r\\nGit queries remain where their answer establishes repository membership, validates a reusable worktree, or inspects configuration and history. Replacing those queries with filesystem traversal would remove validation that the resolver does not provide.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Failure behavior and printed paths\\r\\n\\r\\nThe tests exercise callers after a successful lookup, damage `commondir`, then repair it without clearing a metadata cache.\\r\\n\\r\\nRequired operations fail while metadata is broken. These include clone-preference writes, review marker and manifest writes, investigation-store construction, and cleanup preview. Optional callers retain their own behavior: status omits an unavailable branch, explain skips worktree filtering, settings skips an unresolved preferences layer, and trail refresh can still spawn when its throttle metadata cannot resolve. Repair restores access to the previously saved content.\\r\\n\\r\\nTrail checkout also needs to preserve the path it prints. The first full verification run caught a regression where discovery changed macOS `/var` paths to `/private/var`. Trail now recovers the caller's spelling only after confirming that a CWD ancestor identifies the discovered root. Regression tests cover entry from both the checkout root and a nested directory.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Legacy deletion and diff size\\r\\n\\r\\nWith the remaining callers migrated, this removes:\\r\\n\\r\\n- `paths.GetWorktreeID` and its marker-based parser.\\r\\n- The exported `ResolveDotGitPath` and `ResolveCommonGitPath` composition APIs and their old implementations.\\r\\n- Session common-directory forwarding and cache-clearing APIs.\\r\\n- The `gitdir` common-directory resolver/cache, obsolete resets, and cache-only tests.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe final ownership guard has no migration exceptions. It retains individually documented discovery, semantic-query, and policy exceptions, and fails when an exception becomes stale.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe part-5 commit changes 49 files: 18 production files, 30 tests, fixtures, or benchmarks, and one documentation file. Most test edits replace deleted APIs or remove obsolete cache resets. Production Go shrinks by 301 lines.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Verification\\r\\n\\r\\nThe implementation's final `mise run check` passed, including race-enabled unit and integration tests, Vogon 56/56, and the external deterministic canary 4/4. A subsequent pre-push lint run passed with zero issues.\\r\\n\\r\\nIndependent review reran the focused migration tests with race detection, plus the full settings, investigation, and paths suites. Real Git fixtures cover eleven layouts, including ordinary and linked worktrees, bare-backed worktrees, separate Git directories, submodules, relative pointers, moved registrations, and aliases. Tests check actual stored files, recovery after metadata repair, rooted-handle lifetime, lock ordering and release, and printed trail paths.\\r\\n\\r\\nTemporary source mutations confirmed that the ownership guard rejects independent traversal, a metadata query hidden behind a constant, and a stale exception.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe same Trace2 fixture was run against the integrated prerequisite baseline and this implementation:\\r\\n\\r\\n| Operation | Before | After |\\r\\n|---|---:|---:|\\r\\n| Session construction from cold CWD | 1 | 1 |\\r\\n| Session construction with an explicit root | 0 | 0 |\\r\\n| Queue construction from an open repository | 0 | 0 |\\r\\n| Prepare-commit with no session | 2 | 2 |\\r\\n| Enabled text status with no session | 5 | 4 |\\r\\n| Codex discovery from cold CWD | 1 | 1 |\\r\\n\\r\\nThese count Git subprocesses inside the named entry points. They do not measure full CLI startup or establish latency improvements.\\r\\n\\r\\nWindows test binaries cross-compiled during implementation. Windows runtime testing and paid real-agent E2E tests were not performed.\\r\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2320/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2320/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2959\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2959/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2959/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2959/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2959\",\n              \"id\": 6096267049,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABLed7OQ\",\n              \"number\": 2959,\n              \"title\": \"fix(doctor): count Brain's pre-push wrapper as installed hooks\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n                \"id\": 26940511,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI2OTQwNTEx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Beehtrix\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 6,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-29T08:55:07Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-07T01:11:25Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2959\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2959\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2959.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2959.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes #2949\\nRelated to #2960\\n\\n@peyton-alt @Soph: I asked on the issue to be assigned (https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2949#issuecomment-6486951877) and haven't had a reply yet. I'm opening this so it can be reviewed. If you'd rather fix it on the Brain side instead (giving Brain's wrapper a marker `doctor` recognizes), tell me and I'll close this.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\n`entire brain connect` installs its own `pre-push` hook. It moves the hook it finds (Entire's) to `pre-push.pre-entire-brain`, and its own hook ends with:\\n\\n```sh\\nbackup=\\\"$0.pre-entire-brain\\\"\\nif [ -x \\\"$backup\\\" ]; then exec \\\"$backup\\\" \\\"$@\\\"; fi\\n```\\n\\nSo Entire's hook still runs, with git's stdin and arguments. But the new `pre-push` doesn't have the `# Entire CLI hooks` marker, so `hookStateIn` treats it as foreign and reports the whole set as `GitHooksAbsent`. I checked what happens next with the real plugin (brain v0.4.0, and v0.5.0 since its release today, see Verification):\\n\\n- `entire doctor` shows `Git hooks: NOT INSTALLED` / \\\"Commits in this repository are not captured as checkpoints\\\" on a setup that works, and suggests `--force` to fix it.\\n- `EnsureSetup` runs on every agent turn and reinstalls whenever `IsGitHookInstalled` is false. On the first turn after `brain connect`, it backs Brain's hook up to `pre-push.pre-entire`, puts Entire's hook in front, and prints `[entire] Your pre-push hook still runs, after Entire's (moved to .git/hooks/pre-push.pre-entire).` into the agent's hook output. After that, doctor says OK again.\\n\\nPushes keep working after that re-wrap. Entire's new `pre-push` runs Entire, then Brain's hook from `pre-push.pre-entire`. Brain's `$0`-relative chain then looks for `pre-push.pre-entire.pre-entire-brain`, which doesn't exist, so it stops there (Brain's source says that's deliberate, so the host's hook doesn't run twice). The old Entire copy in `pre-push.pre-entire-brain` is left behind and nothing runs it. So the bug users see is doctor's false report (and its `--force` advice) between `brain connect` and the next agent turn, plus a re-wrap that isn't needed. Commits and pushes were always captured.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\nThe changes are in `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks.go`, a `skip` parameter on `refreshMovedEntireHooks` in `hook_backup.go`, and a small per-OS execute check (`hook_exec_unix.go`, `hook_exec_windows.go`).\\n\\n`hookStateIn`: if `pre-push` doesn't have Entire's marker but is Brain's wrapper, it classifies the copy the wrapper runs (`pre-push.pre-entire-brain`) the same way it classifies `pre-push` today:\\n\\n- Entire's current hook there → `GitHooksCurrent`, and doctor says OK.\\n- Entire's hook from before the ref list → `GitHooksOutdated`, and it gets reinstalled (see below).\\n- Anything else → `GitHooksAbsent`, as before.\\n\\n\\\"Brain's wrapper\\\" means exactly the hook entire-brain writes (`pushHookContent` in entire-brain), with only the plugin path left open. The path has to be the same in both places, quoted the way Brain's `shellSingleQuote` quotes it. Any edit to the wrapper reads as another tool's hook and takes the existing re-wrap path. That includes an early `exit`, the chain inside a condition, a second `backup=`, or even a harmless extra command. Earlier versions of this PR matched the marker, `backup=` and `exec` lines one by one. Automated review found several edits that kept those lines but never ran the chain, so I switched to the exact match. It fails safe: anything it doesn't accept gets the behavior `main` has today.\\n\\nBoth files must be regular files (read NoFollow), and the kernel must let this process execute them. The check calls `faccessat(X_OK)` on the hook's name, relative to the hooks directory's own descriptor (opened from the existing `os.Root`), with the real ids. That's what git's `access(X_OK)` and Brain's `[ -x ]` guard ask, so ownership, the permission class that applies, POSIX ACLs and root all count the same way, and no path is resolved outside the root. A check that accepts any execute bit is wrong in both directions:\\n\\n- A copy at mode `0655` owned by the user reads as runnable, but git and `[ -x ]` skip it.\\n- A named-user ACL can deny execute even when the mode allows it, or grant it when the mode doesn't.\\n\\nWindows has no execute bit, so there both files only have to be regular files.\\n\\n`installHooks` (the Brain branch lives in `installBehindBrainWrapper` and `updateEditedBrainCopy`): when `pre-push` is Brain's wrapper and the copy it runs is Entire's (same check), it writes Entire's hook into that copy and leaves the wrapper alone, instead of backing the wrapper up to `pre-push.pre-entire`.\\n\\n- If Entire had already backed up the user's own `pre-push` to `pre-push.pre-entire` before Brain was installed, the copy gets the chained hook, the same content Entire would write at the hook path. Its `$(dirname \\\"$0\\\")`-relative chain still finds the user's hook from there.\\n- Before writing that copy, it refreshes any other moved copies of Entire's hook to the hook that never chains, the same way the normal install path does. Without that, a manager's wrapper in `pre-push.pre-entire` that runs an older Entire copy could chain back to `pre-push.pre-entire` forever.\\n- Right before each write it re-reads the copy. If another tool replaced it after install read it, install stops with `errHookChangedDuringInstall`, as the hook path already does.\\n- The copy is only rewritten whole when it reads Outdated or is exactly a pre-push hook Entire writes (chained or not, for the prefix its own line runs).\\n\\nIf the user added lines to the copy, it still reads Current, so doctor says OK and agent turns leave it alone. That's the same rule `TestCheckGitHookState_UserAdditionsAreNotDrift` and #2878 set for Entire's own hook. Before this change, both re-wrapped Brain's hook.\\n\\nAn explicit install (`entire enable`, `entire configure --force` or `--absolute-git-hook-path`) over such an edited copy replaces only the one line that runs Entire's pre-push handler, keeps the user's lines, and prints `[entire] Updated the line that runs Entire in .git/hooks/pre-push.pre-entire-brain; the lines you added there are kept.` That line has to be exactly one Entire wrote: today's line for any prefix, or a line from before the ref list. Without this, an edited copy with an old line that ignores Entire's exit status (`entire hooks git pre-push \\\"$1\\\" || true`) kept letting a push through after Entire's pre-push check failed, while `configure --force` reported `✓ Reinstalled git hook`, and `--absolute-git-hook-path` left the line bare. (`main` rewrites the whole copy on these commands and drops the user's lines.) The updated copy keeps its permission bits (with owner `rwx`), so a private `0700` copy holding the user's lines doesn't become readable by everyone. Review of an earlier version caught that it was rewritten at `0755`.\\n\\nInstall leaves the copy as it is and prints a warning that the hook in it wasn't updated when the copy has:\\n\\n- no such line, or more than one;\\n- that line continued from or onto another line with `\\\\`;\\n- another uncommented line that runs Entire's handler, such as the user's own `if [ -n \\\"$CI\\\" ]; then entire hooks git pre-push \\\"$1\\\"; fi`.\\n\\nReplacing the line in those cases would change what the user wrote, or break the shell syntax.\\n\\nIn every Absent case above, install still takes the old re-wrap path, which puts Entire's hook in front where it runs.\\n\\nI also updated the `ReinstallGitHooks` doc comment, which said a wrapper without the marker always reads Absent.\\n\\n`main` moved while this was open and now has the complexity gate (`mise run complexity:gate`). With the Brain branch inline, `installHooks` went from 37 to 92, so I split it: the Brain branch is now `installBehindBrainWrapper` and `updateEditedBrainCopy`, and the existing reclaim-from-pre-commit/hook-manager block moved unchanged into `reclaimHookFromOtherTools`, so `installHooks` doesn't end up more complex than on `main`. Behavior didn't change: the same tests and the same manual runs below give the same results as before the split.\\n\\nThe diff is 4 production files (+346/-25) and 2 test files (+486), squashed into one commit on `main` @ 711697e.\\n\\nOverlap: #2640, #2643 and #2388 (still open) touch the same functions in `strategy/hooks.go`. None of them covers the Brain layout. I re-ran `git merge-tree` today against their current heads (84a2d47, b5651f9, fc5d778). Each already conflicts with `main` @ 711697e, and against this head each has the same conflicting files and the same number of conflict hunks (3, 6 and 4) as against `main`.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- `strategy/hooks_test.go` `TestCheckGitHookState_BrainPrePushWrapper` (table, parallel, filesystem-only):\\n  - Brain's wrapper plus Entire's current hook reads Current, and so does a plugin path containing a quote or the word `exit`.\\n  - Brain's wrapper plus Entire's hook from before the ref list reads Outdated.\\n  - These read Absent:\\n    - a hook that isn't Entire's;\\n    - no moved copy;\\n    - a non-Brain wrapper next to Entire's moved copy;\\n    - the `exec` line commented out;\\n    - an `exit 0`, a `[ -n \\\"$SKIP\\\" ] && exit 0` or a `case ... exit` before the chain;\\n    - the chain inside `if false`;\\n    - a second `backup=`;\\n    - a command after the chain, or an `echo` before it;\\n    - two different plugin paths.\\n  - Execute permission (skipped on Windows): no execute bit on the moved copy or on the wrapper reads Absent, and so does an execute bit for group and other only at `0655` (skipped as root). Owner-only `0700` reads Current.\\n- `TestCheckGitHookState_BrainWrapperOnlyCountsForPrePush`: Brain's wrapper in `post-commit`'s place reads Absent.\\n- `TestInstallGitHooks_BrainPrePushWrapperRefreshesOtherMovedCopies`: Brain's layout, plus a manager wrapper in `pre-push.pre-entire` that runs `pre-push.old`, an Entire hook from before the chain guard that chains straight back. After `InstallGitHook`, `pre-push.old` is the hook that never chains, the copy Brain runs is chained, and both wrappers are unchanged.\\n- `TestInstallGitHooks_KeepsBrainPrePushWrapper`: real `InstallGitHook`, with and without the user's own `pre-push` there first, then Brain's layout with a stale moved copy.\\n  - Both `ReinstallGitHooks` (agent turn) and `InstallGitHook` (enable) leave the wrapper byte-for-byte.\\n  - They rewrite the copy to the current hook, chained when the user's hook is in `pre-push.pre-entire`.\\n  - They leave the user's hook where it was, or create no `pre-push.pre-entire` when there wasn't one.\\n  - Afterwards the set reads Current.\\n- `TestInstallGitHooks_BrainCopyKeepsUserAdditions`: an agent turn leaves an edited copy byte-for-byte. `enable` keeps the user's line and replaces only an Entire line that isn't today's. A copy that is exactly Entire's hook is still rewritten.\\n- `TestInstallGitHooks_BrainCopyWithUserLineKeepsItsMode` (skipped on Windows): `enable` updates Entire's line in an edited copy at `0700`, `0750` and `0755`, and the copy keeps its mode.\\n- `TestInstallGitHooks_BrainCopyWithUserLineGetsTheAbsolutePath`: `--absolute-git-hook-path` writes the absolute path into the copy's Entire line, and the user's line stays.\\n- `TestInstallGitHooks_BrainCopyWithoutOneEntireLineIsReported`: two Entire lines, Entire's line inside the user's condition, a commented-out Entire line, and an Entire line continued from or onto another line. Each is left byte-for-byte with the warning.\\n- `TestInstallGitHooks_BrainCopyReplacedDuringInstallIsKept` (not parallel; it swaps `afterHookBackup`): the copy is replaced between read and write, for a stale copy and for one with a user line. The result is `errHookChangedDuringInstall`, and the replacement stays.\\n- `TestInstallGitHooks_BrainCopyWithUserLineStillRefreshesOtherMovedCopies`: the copy has a user line, and `pre-push.old` is still refreshed, so it can't chain back.\\n- `doctor_test.go` `TestCheckGitHooks_BrainPrePushWrapper`: the wrapper Brain writes, then `checkGitHooks` with and without `--force`. Both print `✓ Git hooks: OK` and leave the wrapper byte-for-byte.\\n\\nThe wrapper text in the tests is what `pushHookContent` in entire-brain writes, except for the plugin path. I checked it against entire-brain's source and against real installs: v0.4.0 earlier, v0.5.0 today. `pushHookContent` and `shellSingleQuote` are unchanged between v0.4.0 and v0.5.0.\\n\\n### Failing without the fix\\n\\nI reverted `hooks.go` and `hook_backup.go` to `main` @ 711697e and removed `hook_exec_*.go`, keeping the tests from the branch head, then ran `go test -count=1 -run Brain ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/ ./cmd/entire/cli/`:\\n\\n- Every case that expects Current, Outdated, an unchanged wrapper, a kept user line, a warning or `errHookChangedDuringInstall` fails. That's ten of the eleven tests above, the doctor test included. The tenth, `TestCheckGitHookState_BrainWrapperOnlyCountsForPrePush`, only expects Absent.\\n- The Absent cases pass on `main` too, because `main` reads every Brain layout as Absent. They're there to keep the new check from accepting a layout that doesn't run Entire's hook.\\n\\nEach new check also has a case that failed at the commit before it was added (run when each was added, not re-run on this head):\\n\\n- the `0655` cases, on a check that accepts any execute bit;\\n- the condition, comment and continuation cases, on a substring match for Entire's line;\\n- `exit`/`if false`/`case`/second `backup=`, on the line-by-line wrapper match;\\n- the quoted path;\\n- the mode test (run today);\\n- the replaced-copy test.\\n\\nEverything passes at the branch head.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nLinux amd64 (kernel 6.12), git 2.56.0, go 1.27.3, golangci-lint 2.15.0, mise. Clean environment: `env -i` with only HOME/PATH/Go cache variables, and no agent, plugin or telemetry variables. Throwaway HOME, config dir and cache for the real-plugin runs.\\n\\nRun today on this tree (head d669009, on `main` @ 711697e; the runs used fork commit 73167d6, which has the identical tree):\\n\\n- `mise run lint`: `0 issues`, and gofmt, gomod, shellcheck, secretpatterns and mise all passed. `mise run fmt`: no changes (`git status --short` empty afterwards).\\n- The complexity gate as CI runs it (`cd tools/complexity && go test ./...`, then `BASE_REF=711697e mise run complexity:gate`): `no new or worsened function over cognitive complexity 30`.\\n- `go vet` and `go test` for `./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/` and `./cmd/entire/cli/`: ok. `go test -race ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/`: ok. `GOOS=windows` and `GOOS=darwin` `go vet`, and `go test -c` of strategy: ok.\\n- `mise run test`: 18054 tests, 22 skipped, 1 failure. The failure is `TestClient_Get_NamesUnresolvableHost` in `cmd/entire/cli/api`, a DNS test that fails the same way on `main` @ 711697e in this environment (17991 tests, same single failure).\\n- Real Brain v0.5.0 (`entire plugin install brain`, then `entire enable`, then `entire brain connect` with no account):\\n  - Doctor on `main` @ 711697e: `Git hooks: NOT INSTALLED`. With this PR: `✓ Git hooks: OK`.\\n  - A push through Brain's wrapper runs Entire's `hooks git pre-push origin` (stub `entire` that logs its calls).\\n  - An agent turn (`entire hooks claude-code user-prompt-submit`) leaves Brain's wrapper and the copy in place.\\n- The copy Brain runs set to a v0.5-era hook with a user line, plus a stub `entire` that fails `hooks git pre-push`. Doctor says OK and the push goes through. Then `entire configure --force`, or `entire enable` in a separate run:\\n  - On the previous head of this PR (81db09a, run Nov 2, not re-run today), both reported success and left the copy byte-for-byte, and the next push still went through.\\n  - On this head, only that line is replaced (the user's line stays), and the next push is rejected.\\n  - On `main`, both re-wrap Brain's hook, rewrite the copy from the template and drop the user's line, and the push is rejected.\\n- A bare-`entire` copy with a user line, then `configure --absolute-git-hook-path`. On 81db09a (Nov 2) the copy stayed bare. On this head it has the absolute path, and the user's line stays. On `main` the user's line is dropped.\\n- `chmod 0655` on the copy or on Brain's wrapper (owned by me, so the owner has no execute bit):\\n  - On this head, doctor says `NOT INSTALLED`, the agent turn re-wraps, and the next push runs Entire's hook, as on `main`.\\n  - On the version before the kernel check (Nov 2), doctor said OK, and git skipped the wrapper (`hint: The '.git/hooks/pre-push' hook was ignored…`) or Brain's `[ -x ]` skipped the copy, so Entire's hook never ran.\\n- ACLs, using `sudo` to make the copy root-owned:\\n  - Mode `0755` with `u:<me>:r--` (readable, no execute for me): doctor says `NOT INSTALLED`, then re-wrap, then Entire runs. Before the kernel check (Nov 2), doctor said OK and nothing ran Entire.\\n  - Mode `0750` with `u:<me>:rwx`: doctor says OK, and the push runs Entire through Brain's wrapper.\\n\\nRun on 5e67636/0544a12 (Oct 29), not re-run on this head. The code they exercise hasn't changed since, except for the wrapper match and the execute check, which the tests above cover:\\n\\n- A user line in the copy survives `entire enable`, an agent turn and `entire doctor --force`, and a push runs Entire once and then the user's line.\\n- A stale copy, then an agent turn: doctor says `OUT OF DATE`, the turn rewrites the copy, and Brain's wrapper stays.\\n- `chmod -x` on either file, or Brain's `exec` commented out: `NOT INSTALLED`, then re-wrap, as on `main`.\\n- The user's own `pre-push`, then `enable`, then `brain connect`, then `enable` again: a push runs Entire's hook and then the user's, before and after the second enable. On `main`, the second enable rotates the user's hook away (#2960).\\n- A manager wrapper in `pre-push.pre-entire` running an Entire copy from before the chain guard: the next push finishes, with Entire called twice.\\n- `mise run test:e2e:canary`: passed.\\n\\nWhat I didn't run:\\n\\n- Windows and macOS themselves. They're covered only by cross-compiling (`go vet`, `go test -c`). The Windows CI job only runs tests matching `Windows|MSYS`.\\n- A Linux kernel or filesystem where `faccessat` relative to a directory descriptor behaves differently.\\n- A hosted Brain sync, which needs an account and doesn't touch hooks.\\n- The Entire side of a real push with a real login. I used a stub `entire` to count calls.\\n- CI on this exact head before pushing it. CI ran on my fork on earlier heads.\\n\\n## Known limits / open questions\\n\\n- This takes the CLI-side option from the issue. The other option is for Brain's wrapper to carry a marker `doctor` understands. I asked on the issue which you prefer and haven't heard back yet.\\n- Brain's wrapper is matched exactly. If Brain changes its wrapper, or the user edits it in any way (a harmless added command included), the CLI goes back to reading Absent and re-wrapping, which is today's behavior. That fails safe: pushes still run Entire's hook. It also brings back what happens on `main` after a re-wrap, including #2960 when the user's hook is in `pre-push.pre-entire`.\\n- `entire disable --uninstall` leaves Entire's hook running behind Brain's wrapper, on this branch and on `main` after its re-wrap. `restoreWrapped` matches wrappers by literal file name, and Brain uses `$0`. That bug was already there before this PR and is filed separately as #2957. The fix for it has to adjust one test case to this PR's layout (see the note below).\\n- Agent turns don't touch a copy the user added lines to, because it reads Current. If that copy still has an old fail-open line (`|| true`), doctor says OK and pushes ignore Entire's exit status until an explicit `entire enable` / `configure --force` updates the line. That's the same rule `main` applies to Entire's own edited `pre-push`: I ran the same edited hook at `.git/hooks/pre-push` without Brain on `main`, and doctor says OK and the push goes through there too.\\n- If the user's own hook is in `pre-push.pre-entire` but the edited copy Brain runs has no chain to it, an explicit install replaces only Entire's line and doesn't add the chain, so the user's hook doesn't run. Adding the chain would mean rewriting their file. On `main`, the re-wrap rotates the user's hook away instead (#2960).\\n- A copy the user edited whose Entire line runs the removed local-dev launcher (`./scripts/entire-dev`, `go run ...`) reads Outdated. Agent turns and `enable` rewrite it whole, dropping the user's lines, as `main` does for this copy and for Entire's own `pre-push`. The historical local-dev line forms vary too much to match safely.\\n- Other moved copies, such as a hook manager's `pre-push.old`, are still refreshed from the template, as on `main`.\\n- Without Brain, Entire's own `pre-push` at mode `0655` (owner has no execute bit) still reads OK on `main` and on this branch, while git skips it. I ran that on both. It's an existing gap in how Entire checks its own hook, outside this PR.\\n- An agent turn doesn't repair a loop further down the chain. Example: the copy Brain runs chains to `pre-push.pre-entire`, that is a hook manager's wrapper running `pre-push.old`, and `pre-push.old` is an Entire hook from before the chain guard that chains straight back to `pre-push.pre-entire`. The copy reads Current, so the turn skips it, and pushes loop until an explicit `entire enable`, which refreshes `pre-push.old` (`TestInstallGitHooks_BrainPrePushWrapperRefreshesOtherMovedCopies`). I ran the same layout without Brain on `main`: it also reads Current and loops. On `main` with Brain, the turn's re-wrap happens to refresh `pre-push.old`, but it also moves the manager's wrapper to a dated copy that no longer runs.\\n- When install updates Entire's line in an edited copy, the file is replaced through a temp file and rename. Its mode is kept, but POSIX ACL entries are not: the new file gets the directory's default ACL, if any. Every hook write on `main` does the same, and `main` also drops the user's lines there.\\n- Brain's wrapper isn't recognised when the plugin path contains a newline. The match requires each quoted path to sit on one line. I checked it: such a layout reads Absent and gets `main`'s re-wrap.\\n- If the hooks directory is searchable but not readable, the directory descriptor can't be opened, and the layout reads Absent (main's re-wrap path). Install would need write access there anyway.\\n\\n## Missing Entire-Checkpoint trailers\\n\\nNone of these commits has an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer. CONTRIBUTING asks for them, but this work wasn't done in an Entire-captured session that produced one, and I won't make one up. If you need checkpoint linkage, I can redo the commits inside a captured session.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2959/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 1,\n                \"+1\": 1,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2959/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2190\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2190/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2190/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2190/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2190\",\n              \"id\": 5299600007,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBl6egQ\",\n              \"number\": 2190,\n              \"title\": \"refactor(gitrepo): consolidate worktree metadata traversal\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"id\": 34813274,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 5,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-31T11:27:37Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-02T05:34:59Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2190\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2190\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2190.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2190.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Refs #2052, particularly [the duplicate-traversal finding](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2052#issuecomment-5400538888) and [the follow-up commitment](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2052#issuecomment-5429341093).\\n\\nPR #2052 exposed that several packages independently interpreted `.git`, `gitdir:`, `commondir`, and linked-worktree identity. Those implementations had already diverged on layouts such as bare containers, linked worktrees, and submodules, while session and checkpoint maintained separate caches for answers derived from the same filesystem metadata.\\n\\nThis consolidates those physical Git facts under the existing `gitrepo` ownership boundary and removes the duplicate traversal and cache layers.\\n\\n## Why this touches 67 files\\n\\nThis is one ownership change with a wide dependency graph, not 67 separate features.\\n\\nBefore this change, checkpoint, session, strategy, settings, status, review,\\ninvestigate, trail, setup/cleanup, and Codex independently interpreted some\\ncombination of `.git`, `gitdir:`, `commondir`, and linked-worktree identity:\\n\\n```text\\nBefore\\n\\ncheckpoint ─┐\\nsession ────┤\\nstrategy ───┤ each resolves Git metadata independently\\nsettings ───┤ and some cache the result separately\\nstatus ─────┤\\nreview ─────┤\\nCodex ──────┘\\n\\nAfter\\n\\n                    gitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata\\n                                  │\\n              ┌───────────────────┼───────────────────┐\\n           checkpoint          session            strategy...\\n```\\n\\nThe 67 changed files break down into 37 production files and 30 test files:\\n\\n| Area | Files | Why they changed |\\n| --- | ---: | --- |\\n| Canonical `gitrepo` owner | 7 | Add the resolver, repository-opening boundary, tests, and ownership guard |\\n| Checkpoint migration | 7 | Remove its common-directory cache and migrate consumers |\\n| Session migration | 7 | Remove its separate cache and preserve adoption/sweep behavior |\\n| Strategy and hook paths | 18 | Migrate the hottest and most policy-sensitive consumers |\\n| Other product consumers | 18 | Migrate settings, status, review, investigate, trail, Codex, setup, and cleanup |\\n| Legacy `paths` deletion | 2 | Remove the old marker-based worktree-ID parser |\\n| Cross-cutting proof | 8 | Update fixtures and prove caller policy and subprocess behavior |\\n\\nMost production changes are small call-site migrations. The largest additions\\nare tests proving real Git layouts, failure behavior, ownership boundaries, and\\nsubprocess counts. Despite the broad footprint, production Go decreases by 36\\nlines.\\n\\n## One owner for physical worktree metadata\\n\\n`gitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata` now resolves one explicit worktree root into:\\n\\n- its per-worktree Git directory\\n- its common Git directory\\n- its optional linked-worktree ID\\n\\nThe resolver has no CWD lookup, Git subprocess, cache, context, options, environment interpretation, layout taxonomy, or feature-specific policy.\\n\\nReturned paths remain cleaned absolute lexical paths. Physical filesystem identity is used only to determine whether the Git directory equals the common directory and whether a linked-worktree Git directory is an immediate child of `CommonDir/worktrees`.\\n\\nResolution is all-or-error. Malformed worktree metadata cannot silently downgrade into another repository-opening path, while deliberately opening a validated bare repository remains a separate `gitrepo.OpenPath` operation.\\n\\n## Consolidation and deletion\\n\\nAll former filesystem-metadata consumers now use the canonical resolver while retaining their existing caller-owned error, warning, fallback, trust, and installation policies.\\n\\nThis removes:\\n\\n- the session common-directory cache and its clearing behavior\\n- the checkpoint common-directory cache\\n- duplicate `.git` and `commondir` traversal\\n- marker-based worktree-ID parsing\\n- the old `paths` worktree metadata helpers\\n- migration wrappers that would otherwise preserve fragmented ownership\\n\\nA source guard rejects new production parsing of `gitdir:`, `commondir`, or independent `.git` filesystem traversal outside `gitrepo`, with two documented policy-only exceptions.\\n\\nThe production Go diff is 557 additions and 593 deletions: net 36 lines removed despite adding the canonical resolver.\\n\\n## Hook-path subprocess evidence\\n\\nOperation-level Git tracing records these changes against the historical pre-consolidation counts:\\n\\n| Operation | Before | After |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\\n| Session state construction | 2 | 1 |\\n| Construct and enqueue through checkpoint queue | 1 | 0 |\\n| `prepare-commit-msg` without an active session | 4 | 2 |\\n| `entire status` | 4 | 3 |\\n| Codex hook discovery | 1 | 1 |\\n\\nThese values count Git subprocesses, not whether the operation still occurs. The checkpoint queue retains its locking, append, drain, and removal behavior; it now obtains the common directory through filesystem metadata resolution instead of spawning Git.\\n\\nThe consolidation adds no Git subprocesses and removes the filesystem-metadata `--git-common-dir` queries. The one remaining common-directory query on the prepare-commit path is retained semantic repository-identity behavior rather than metadata traversal.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `mise run check`\\n  - formatting passed\\n  - lint passed with 0 issues\\n  - race-enabled unit and integration tests passed\\n  - Vogon canary passed 56/56\\n  - external deterministic canary passed 4/4\\n- `git diff upstream/main...HEAD --check`\\n- Real Git-created fixtures cover ordinary repositories, linked worktrees, `.bare/worktrees`, bare repositories with linked worktrees, separate Git directories, ordinary and linked submodules, relative pointers, symlink aliases, and moved registrations.\\n- Handmade fixtures cover malformed and broken metadata.\\n- Tests verify caller-owned failure policies, fail-closed repository opening, common-directory/worktree-ID agreement, and physical alias identity.\\n- The source guard was positive-control tested by temporarily adding forbidden independent traversal and observing the expected failure.\\n- No paid real-agent E2E tests were run.\\n\\n## Deliberately unchanged\\n\\nThis does not change Codex backlink, ownership, trust, warning, diagnostic, or installation policy. It does not add cross-worktree writes, resolver flags, a generic Git facade, or replace genuine Git queries for refs, objects, configuration, or repository semantics.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2190/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2190/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2285\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2285/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2285/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2285/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2285\",\n              \"id\": 5363758925,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCY0VLA\",\n              \"number\": 2285,\n              \"title\": \"refactor(session): use canonical Git metadata resolution (split part 3)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"id\": 34813274,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-06T08:03:29Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-16T03:17:33Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2285\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2285\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2285.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2285.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Part 3 of #2190's [agreed split](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2190#issuecomment-5499945525), following the merged canonical resolver in #2241 and checkpoint migration in #2254.\\n\\nSession construction and adoption still use separate paths to resolve Git metadata. This PR moves the explicit-root consumers to `gitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata`, so the canonical resolver supplies the common directory and worktree ID while each caller keeps its own storage and failure policy.\\n\\n## Session-store construction\\n\\nPreviously, constructing a session store for a known worktree root ran `git rev-parse --git-common-dir`, even though the root was already known.\\n\\n`NewStateStoreForWorktree` now resolves `WorktreeMetadata.CommonDir` directly. Known-root construction therefore starts no Git subprocesses and checks the current metadata on every call. For example, if `commondir` is changed to point at a missing directory after a successful construction, the next construction fails. Repairing the metadata makes construction succeed again and preserves access to the saved session. Inherited `GIT_DIR`, `GIT_COMMON_DIR`, and `GIT_WORK_TREE` values also cannot redirect an explicitly scoped store into another repository.\\n\\n`NewStateStore`, the CWD constructor, intentionally stays on `gitdir.CommonDir`. The strategy's per-session state lock resolves through that same function, and the store and its lock must agree on one common directory. If the store moved to the canonical resolver alone, an exported `GIT_DIR` would place state files in the worktree's own `.git` while the lock went to the repository `GIT_DIR` names. Two writers of one state file would then hold different locks. Keeping both on one resolver also keeps split `GIT_DIR`/`GIT_WORK_TREE` setups working for session state. The CWD store moves to the canonical resolver together with the lock.\\n\\nThe common directory still feeds the existing rooted store. Linked worktrees share session files, and empty-root rejection, test isolation, no-follow I/O, atomic writes, and locking remain in place.\\n\\n## Adoption\\n\\nAdoption uses the canonical resolver for source and target worktree IDs. This removes its dependency on the legacy parser's expected directory names. A linked worktree backed by a bare repository named `storage`, for example, can now resolve its ID from `storage/worktrees/<id>`.\\n\\nHook paths still derive worktree IDs with `paths.GetWorktreeID`. Both resolvers yield the same ID for main and linked worktrees under `.git/` or `.bare/`. Only the canonical resolver also accepts a bare repository with any other name, and hooks cannot start sessions in that layout yet. Hook callers move to the canonical resolver with the strategy migration.\\n\\nThe source and target retain different failure policies. If source metadata cannot resolve, adoption can still match the session by its recorded worktree path. If target metadata cannot resolve, adoption stops before saving the adopted state. The combined Git query in `stateStoreForWorktree` stays because it validates an arbitrary user-supplied repository; a directory that merely contains an empty `.git` folder must still be rejected. Source-retirement rollback remains unchanged.\\n\\n## Why the legacy APIs and cache remain\\n\\n`session.GetGitCommonDir`, the cache-clearing API, and `gitdir`'s common-directory resolver and cache still serve the CWD session store, the session lock, the session sweep, strategy, and other consumers outside this slice. Removing them now would require migrating those callers too. Their deletion waits until those callers have migrated and been verified.\\n\\nThe sweep stays on `session.GetGitCommonDir` on purpose. It finds stuck sessions through the CWD store, so its throttle marker has to come from the same resolver. Moving the sweep alone to the canonical resolver would break split `GIT_DIR`/`GIT_WORK_TREE` layouts: the work tree has no `.git`, so the sweep would find stuck sessions and then skip spawning on every session start. The sweep moves together with the CWD store.\\n\\nThis PR changes two production files and their tests, plus a comment-only fix in `gitdir/gitdir.go` that drops a stale list of callers. The ownership guard remains active, and its ledger reasons now name the callers that still use the legacy resolvers. Rooted-handle lifetime and the strategy and session-lock migration stay with their existing owners.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `mise run check`: passed after keeping the sweep on its existing resolver, including formatting, zero-issue lint, unit and integration tests, and the deterministic Vogon and roger-roger canaries.\\n- After merging main: session, gitrepo, strategy session-state, hook, and preview tests, plus adoption and pending-checkpoint tests, pass. The pending-preview tests pass now that #2770 is in.\\n\\nFocused tests cover linked-worktree save/load/clear, invalid roots, explicit-root metadata damage and repair, inherited Git variables on explicit roots, and adoption validation and source-path fallback. They also cover bare-backed worktree IDs. `TestSessionStateAndLockHonorExportedGitDir` pins that the CWD store and its lock land in the same common directory when `GIT_DIR` points at another repository and in a split `GIT_DIR`/`GIT_WORK_TREE` layout. It failed against the earlier revision of this branch and passes now. Existing tests exercise rooted storage, symlink refusal, and adoption rollback.\\n\\nReal Git Trace2 events show constructor subprocess counts:\\n\\n| Construction path | Before | After |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| CWD | 1 common-directory query | 1 common-directory query (unchanged) |\\n| Explicit root | 1 | 0 |\\n\\nThe Trace2 test includes a positive control that launches Git and checks that an additional event is recorded. These measurements cover store construction, not total hook latency.\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2285/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2285/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3045\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3045/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3045/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3045/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3045\",\n              \"id\": 6250176154,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABNZmFPQ\",\n              \"number\": 3045,\n              \"title\": \"codex: offer to install hooks where Codex reads them in linked worktrees\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-06T20:32:10Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-09T03:17:33Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3045\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3045\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3045.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3045.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Problem\\n\\nIn a linked worktree, `entire enable --agent codex` (and `entire agent add codex`) writes `<worktree>/.codex/hooks.json`, but Codex loads the **primary checkout's** `.codex/hooks.json` (the `.bare` layout root for `.bare` worktrees; pinned by the `codex app-server` `hooks/list` tests). With no hooks file there, Codex runs no Entire hooks and nothing is captured. `enable` warned (\\\"Hooks in the current-worktree file will not run here\\\") and `entire status` showed \\\"Codex hooks are not active in this worktree\\\", but nothing fixed it, so people who only work in worktrees got no checkpoints.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nAfter installing in the current worktree, when Codex reads a different hooks file that is absent, has only user hooks, or has outdated Entire hooks, setup asks (default **No**):\\n\\n> Codex reads hooks from `<primary>/.codex/hooks.json`, not from this worktree. Install Entire's Codex hooks there too? This leaves an uncommitted change in `<primary>`.\\n\\n- **Yes:** merges Entire's hooks into that file (never clobbers user hooks) and says: \\\"This is an uncommitted change in that checkout. Open /hooks in Codex to approve them.\\\" (Codex trust records are keyed to that path, so status moves to \\\"N Codex hook(s) need approval\\\".)\\n- **Consent is read from the terminal itself** (`interactive.OpenPromptTTY`), so piped stdin can't answer it; agent sessions (`review.DetectAgentSession`) are never asked.\\n- **No, `--yes`, no terminal, agents/CI:** writes nothing and prints the remedy: re-run `entire agent add codex` in this worktree from a terminal and answer yes. (It does not suggest running enable in the primary, which would enable Entire there.) `.bare` layouts keep the \\\"apply the generated hooks.json at `<root>`\\\" guidance.\\n- **Optional by design:** an aborted prompt or a failed write warns and prints the remedy and setup still completes; only a cancelled command stops setup.\\n\\n### Safety\\n- The write target is the root `ResolveHookDiscovery` derived from Git metadata, carried as a trusted field on `DiscoveredHooksPath` (never recovered from the path with `filepath.Dir`).\\n- Discovery is re-resolved right before the write and must match exactly what the user was shown.\\n- Writes go through `agent.OpenHookConfig(root, \\\".codex/hooks.json\\\")`: anchored root, `MkdirAllNoSymlink`, atomic write, symlinked `.codex`/`hooks.json` refused. Malformed or unreadable files, unresolved discovery, submodules, and a separate Git directory's storage parent (which can hold other repositories' storage; it gets its own remedy) are never offered.\\n- Merging keeps every field of existing user hooks (e.g. `async`, `timeoutSec`, `statusMessage`, extra group keys); this also fixes that loss for the current-worktree install. Duplicate Entire entries are collapsed, and a `null` hooks file no longer panics.\\n- `entire doctor` (including `--force`) never writes; it and `entire status` name the remedy, and only suggest \\\"answer yes\\\" when setup would actually offer the write. Removal stays current-checkout only (documented).\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/AGENT.md` documents the consent exception to \\\"never write another checkout\\\"; `filesystem-safety.md` notes the discovered Codex root under `HookConfigFile`.\\n\\n`InstallHooks` now shares `installHooksInto` with the discovered-root install; the Codex + skill steps after agent setup moved into `finishAgentSetup` (kept `runEnableInteractive` under the complexity limit).\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- Unit (`agent/codex`): create/merge/update the discovered file, `.bare` root, refusal for malformed, symlinked `.codex`/leaf, changed/unresolved discovery; candidate table; normal checkouts, submodules and separate-git-dir worktrees never offered.\\n- CLI: yes writes then no re-prompt; no / cannot-prompt write nothing and print the remedy; cancelled prompt and a symlink appearing after the offer both warn and keep setup going; outdated primary prompts, current doesn't; `--yes` with a TTY never prompts; doctor never writes.\\n- Integration (`codex app-server` `hooks/list`): after answering yes in a linked worktree and in a `.bare` worktree, `hooks/list` from the worktree returns Entire's hooks sourced from the primary / layout-root file; declining writes nothing.\\n- Live with the branch binary: piped (no TTY) → remedy, no write; TTY + `n` → prompt, remedy, no write; TTY + `y` → `main/.codex/hooks.json` with Entire's 7 hooks (untracked in main), and `entire status` in the worktree changes from \\\"not active\\\" to \\\"7 Codex hook(s) need approval · open /hooks\\\".\\n- **Baseline on current main** (real Codex turn in a linked worktree, main binary on PATH): enable wrote only the worktree file, status said \\\"not active\\\", the turn ran but only the user's own `~/.codex` hooks fired, `entire session list` showed no sessions, and the commit got no `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer (0 checkpoints).\\n- **Real Codex sessions** (Codex 0.166, branch binary on PATH) in linked worktrees, on the final build as well: before approval, Codex skipped Entire's project hooks and nothing was recorded (matches the new \\\"open /hooks to approve\\\" message); after approving in `/hooks`, the next `codex exec` turn fired SessionStart, UserPromptSubmit, PostToolUse and Stop, Entire recorded the session, and committing produced an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer and a checkpoint with the prompt. Re-run after the review fixes in a second linked worktree: same result. Live: an existing user hook with `async`/`timeoutSec`/`statusMessage`/extra key in the primary kept all fields; with `AI_AGENT`/`CLAUDECODE` set, no prompt and the remedy printed.\\n- `mise run check`: everything this PR touches passes (cli, agent/codex, integration_test); lint 0 issues; complexity gate clean. Unrelated local failures: `TestProbeConfigDir_AsksClaude` / `TestResolveClaudeConfigDir_PrefersClaudesAnswer` (5s timeouts under load, pass alone) and `TestHandlePush_RealSendPack_ShallowRepoAmendsAgent` (fails on main locally).\\n\\n## Follow-ups (not in this PR)\\n- CI's `test-codex-hooks` job installs the latest Codex rather than the pinned 0.149.0 that AGENT.md describes.\\n- `warnCodexHooksAfterRemoval` says \\\".codex/hooks.json is tracked\\\" even for `.bare` roots.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3045/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3045/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2589\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2589/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2589/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2589/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2589\",\n              \"id\": 5579577830,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABFEjAdA\",\n              \"number\": 2589,\n              \"title\": \"feat(opencode): support OpenCode 2 with V1 fallback\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"postusername\",\n                \"id\": 35779067,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Nzc5MDY3\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35779067?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/postusername\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/postusername\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/postusername/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/postusername/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/postusername/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/postusername/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/postusername/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/postusername/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/postusername/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/postusername/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/postusername/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 3,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-25T07:18:01Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-25T08:36:40Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": true,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2589\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2589\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2589.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2589.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nMakes the OpenCode integration work on OpenCode 2 while keeping OpenCode 1 working from the same generated plugin. Fixes #2588.\\n\\nOpenCode 2 is a hard break in two places:\\n\\n1. It loads a default plugin definition with `id` + `setup`/`effect`, and rejects V1 hook-map plugins with `PluginModule.LoadError: Plugin must export a default definition with an id and an effect or setup function`.\\n2. It moved export/import under `opencode session`; the V1 `opencode export` prints a help page and exits 0.\\n\\nThis builds on the approach in #2397 (thanks @aryasaatvik) but keeps OpenCode 1 plugin support instead of dropping it.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n**Plugin** (`entire_plugin.ts` + committed dogfood copy)\\n- Default export `{ id: \\\"entire\\\", setup(ctx) }` for OpenCode 2: `session.hook(\\\"prompt\\\")` drives turn-start, `session.hook(\\\"context\\\")` applies the turn-start context injection and tracks the model, and `ctx.event.subscribe()` handles `session.created`, `session.idle`/`session.status`/`session.execution.*`, `session.compacted`, `session.deleted`, `global.disposed`, `location.shutdown`.\\n- Keeps the named `EntirePlugin` export (older V1) and adds a `server()` factory on the default export (V1 ≥ 1.18.29).\\n- No runtime dependency on either SDK package (the V1 type import was removed), so the file loads under Bun and Node with no project `node_modules`.\\n\\n**Commands** (`cli_commands.go`)\\n- Try `opencode session export` / `session import` first, fall back to the V1 top-level commands.\\n- Validate export output, so an exit-0 help page is not treated as a transcript, and preserve a classified V2 error across the fallback.\\n\\n**Schema** (`types.go`, `transcript.go`, `transcript/compact/opencode.go`)\\n- Normalize OpenCode 2's flattened messages (`type` + `content`, message-level `text`) to the v1 model for reads, while keeping the raw transcript byte-preserving so `opencode session import` can resume the session.\\n\\n**e2e**\\n- Accept `opencode v2.x` version output and skip V1 plugin-dependency seeding on major ≥ 2.\\n\\n**Docs** — agent guide updated for both plugin APIs and both export commands.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `go build ./...`, `go vet ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/opencode/... ./e2e/agents/...` clean.\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/... ./cmd/entire/cli/transcript/...` pass, including the new `opencode_v2_test.go` schema/export tests and a Node canary that drives the V2 `setup` path (session-start, turn-start, turn-end) alongside the existing V1 canary.\\n- Loaded the generated plugin against real **OpenCode 2.0.16**: the server logs `loading plugin` with no subsequent `failed to load plugin`.\\n- Confirmed the command split on 2.0.16: `opencode session export <id>` returns session JSON; `opencode export <id>` prints `DESCRIPTION`/`USAGE` and exits 0.\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- The V2 event subscription guards turn-end with a `turnActive` flag, because OpenCode 2 can report a turn ending via more than one event.\\n- OpenCode 1 remains fully supported; no config migration is required.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2589/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2589/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2027\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2027/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2027/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2027/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2027\",\n              \"id\": 5175272600,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABAD9H7A\",\n              \"number\": 2027,\n              \"title\": \"fix(opencode): preserve prompts after metadata fallback\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"id\": 34813274,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 2,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-17T20:45:10Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-16T11:44:35Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2027\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2027\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2027.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2027.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes #2001.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Problem\\r\\nOpenCode emits a user `message.updated` event before the `message.part.updated` event containing the prompt text. The plugin starts the turn from that metadata event with an empty prompt so a fast agent commit still sees an ACTIVE session. Because the message was then marked as seen, the later text part was ignored and checkpoints lost the user prompt.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe first version of this PR kept a marker for those promptless starts and fired `turn-start` again when the text arrived. That recovered the prompt, but `turn-start` is not a prompt setter. It captures pre-prompt Git state, creates a new `TurnID`, recalculates prompt attribution, and clears `LastCheckpointID` and `TurnCheckpointIDs`.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe timing this fallback exists for makes that destructive. A checkpoint may already have been created between the empty metadata event and the text event.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe new integration regression exercises exactly that order:\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\nmessage.updated\\r\\n  → turn-start with empty prompt\\r\\n  → agent commit and checkpoint\\r\\n  → message.part.updated with prompt text\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nAgainst the second-`turn-start` implementation, the prompt was recorded, but the original turn ID changed, the pre-prompt snapshot was replaced, attribution was recalculated, and both checkpoint fields were cleared.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Fix\\r\\nKeep the early empty `turn-start`, but repair the missing text through a new internal `PromptUpdate` lifecycle event.\\r\\n\\r\\n`PromptUpdate` writes the late text to `prompt.txt` and updates session `LastPrompt`. It does not call `CapturePrePromptState` or `InitializeSession`, so it cannot start another logical turn or reset checkpoint bookkeeping.\\r\\nThe file and state updates run inside `MutateSessionState`. Checkpoint condensation clears `prompt.txt` while holding the same session lock, so either ordering is safe:\\r\\n\\r\\n- If repair gets the lock first, condensation sees and checkpoints the prompt before clearing the file.\\r\\n- If condensation gets the lock first, repair writes the prompt after condensation finishes, leaving it available for turn-end finalization.\\r\\nThe OpenCode plugin keeps a `promptlessTurnStarts` marker per message. Empty text updates leave the marker pending; the first non-empty part sends one synchronous `prompt-update`; later duplicates do nothing. Multiple pending messages are tracked independently. The set is cleared on session switches, session deletion, and server disposal.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe generated plugin template and the checked-in dogfood plugin remain byte-identical.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Cost\\r\\nThe plugin does expected `O(1)` set work per event and keeps `O(P)` additional state for `P` promptless messages awaiting text.\\r\\nA late repair starts one synchronous hook subprocess, reads and rewrites `prompt.txt` in `O(Q + L)` time for existing prompt data `Q` and incoming prompt length `L`, and performs `O(S)` session-state I/O for state size `S`.\\r\\n\\r\\nIt performs no worktree scan. The earlier second-`turn-start` path repeated work proportional to worktree size `F`, including both status walks used by turn initialization.\\r\\n\\r\\nIn the real OpenCode run, the empty `turn-start` took 74 ms and the subsequent `prompt-update` took 5 ms in the same repository.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Verification\\r\\n\\r\\n- [x] Regression test fails before the fix by capturing only the empty fallback prompt.\\r\\n- [x] Regression test passes after the fix with `turn-start(\\\"\\\")` followed by `prompt-update(\\\"preserve this prompt\\\")`.\\r\\n- [x] Duplicate text-part updates do not trigger additional hooks.\\r\\n- [x] OpenCode package tests pass.\\r\\n- [x] `mise run check` passes, including lint, race-enabled unit and integration tests, and E2E canary tests.\\r\\n- [x] The generated plugin template matches the repository’s installed OpenCode plugin.\\r\\n- [x] A real `opencode run` session produced a checkpoint containing the complete original prompt.\\r\\n- [x] A checkpoint occurring between the metadata event and prompt-text event preserves the original turn and checkpoint bookkeeping.\\r\\n- [x] Prompt repair avoids repeating the complete `turn-start` lifecycle.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Scope\\r\\n`PromptUpdate` is an internal lifecycle event used only by OpenCode in this change. There are no new CLI flags, settings, dependencies, or changes to other agent integrations.\\r\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2027/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2027/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2085\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2085/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2085/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2085/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2085\",\n              \"id\": 5203639663,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABAavyJQ\",\n              \"number\": 2085,\n              \"title\": \"refactor(hooks): stage absolute_git_hook_path scoping, and detect a dead pin\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-20T12:57:16Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-20T14:20:56Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2085\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2085\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2085.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2085.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Two residuals from the local_dev removal (#1999), both about `absolute_git_hook_path` — the setting that makes git hooks embed an absolute binary path instead of bare `entire`, for GUI git clients that never source a shell profile.\\n\\n**The scope change is staged.** Phase one warns and migrates; a later release flips it. See below for why a hard break was wrong.\\n\\n## Why staged\\n\\nVerified against the pre-change binary from `main`:\\n\\n```\\n$ entire configure --absolute-git-hook-path\\n✓ Settings updated (.entire/settings.json)\\nproject: {\\\"enabled\\\":true,\\\"absolute_git_hook_path\\\":true}\\nlocal:   (none)\\n```\\n\\nThe documented way to enable the feature wrote it **exclusively to the tracked file**. So the affected population isn't an edge case — it's every user of it.\\n\\nAnd the failure mode is the worst available: the setting exists because their GUI git client can't find `entire` on PATH. Unpinning means the guard takes `else :` there, capturing nothing, with no error. They'd lose checkpoints in exactly the tool they enabled it for.\\n\\nThis is a **robustness fix, not a security one** — the value only chooses between `entire` and `os.Executable()`, a binary the user already invoked. There's no case for breaking anyone quickly.\\n\\n### Phase one (this PR)\\n\\n- The committed value is **still honored**. Nobody's hooks change.\\n- It reports a deprecation, in `entire status` and `entire doctor`.\\n- `doctor` offers the migration, reusing the confirm/`--force`/non-interactive degradation already here.\\n- **New writes already go local**, so the population stops growing now rather than at phase two.\\n\\n**Copy, not move.** Editing a tracked file would land an unexpected change in the user's next commit. Once the local file sets the key the committed one is redundant, so it simply stops mattering when the scope is retired — and the warning goes quiet at that point, which the \\\"no warning once the local file sets the key\\\" case pins. Verified `git status` shows no tracked-file change after migrating.\\n\\n### Phase two (a release after this reaches stable)\\n\\n`recordAbsoluteGitHookPathDeprecation` becomes the enforcing version and the table in `absolute_hook_path_scope_test.go` flips. Silent for anyone who ran `doctor`.\\n\\n## A dead pin failed silently\\n\\nAn upgrade into a new version directory, a binary built in a temp dir, a `go install` that relocates it — the guard takes its else branch, so git keeps working while nothing is captured. Verified before fixing:\\n\\n```\\n$ git commit -m \\\"after the binary moved\\\"\\nEntire-Checkpoint trailers: 0\\n$ entire doctor\\n✓ Git hooks: OK          ← reported healthy\\n```\\n\\nNow `GitHooksOutdated`, which makes it **self-healing**: reinstalling re-pins to the running binary. Nothing revalidated a pinned path after install before this. This helps the same population as the staged change above.\\n\\nThat gave `GitHooksOutdated` two causes needing different advice, so the check reports which — collapsing them told a user with a moved binary that their hook \\\"runs Entire from the working tree\\\", which is false and points at the wrong fix.\\n\\n## Found by `/simplify`, all reproduced first\\n\\n- **The flag wrote the key into the committed file.** The struct assignment stayed and `saveSettingsToTarget` marshals the whole struct to the target, which defaults to project. My own earlier check missed it because the fixture already contained the key.\\n- **`configure --force` decided pinning from an ungated read.** `settings.LoadFromFile` reads one file verbatim, so it both missed a local-only value and honored a committed one directly. Now reads the merged view; `LoadFromFile`'s doc says it's display-only.\\n- **The pin parser was wrong**: `strings.Index(rest, \\\" ]\\\")` matched inside a path, so `/Users/a ]b/entire` parsed as `'/Users/a` — a permanent false \\\"outdated\\\" plus a reinstall every turn-start that could never repair it.\\n- **Nothing coupled the parser to the generator.** Every existing test installed with `absolutePath=false`, so changing the guard would have silently disabled dead-pin detection with the suite green. Verified by swapping `[ -x ` for `test -x` and watching the new round-trip test fail. Fixtures now come from `buildHookSpecs`, which also deleted a `tc.name` branch inside a table test.\\n\\nPlus: one pass over the invocation line instead of two and one `os.Stat` instead of five; the mid-loop `continue` removed (it sat below two `Absent` returns, so a future Absent check would have been skipped for hooks 2–5); `setEnabledRaw` generalized to `setRawKey`, restoring a doc comment an earlier edit had orphaned and carrying a nil-map guard; provenance from `rawHasKey` rather than call order; three exported entry points → two; the settings test moved to `loadMergedSettings` + `t.Parallel` like its sibling (0.21s → 0.00s, no git subprocess per case).\\n\\n## Deliberately not done\\n\\n- **`saveToFile` stripping machine-local fields.** Tempting as a single choke point, but while the committed value is still honored it would delete a working setting out of a tracked file as a side effect of an unrelated `entire configure`. Revisit at phase two, when the key is inert.\\n- **A declarative per-field scope registry.** Two gates with different verification depth and failure policy aren't a table's worth, and there's no seam to hang it on.\\n- **Unified rejection reporting** across the three existing shapes, and adding it to `status --json`. That's where a fourth such field's cost lands, but it's a separate change.\\n- **A machine-readable pin marker** in the hook format, which would remove the parse coupling entirely — needs a transition release, and the round-trip test buys the protection now.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n`mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci` pass. Every new guard was verified to fail against the defect it protects against.\\n\\nVerified end to end with a built binary: an existing user's hooks stay pinned and they get a warning with a one-command fix; `doctor --force` migrates with no tracked-file change; the warning then stops and the hooks are still pinned; a moved binary is diagnosed with the right message and repaired.\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2085/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2085/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1777\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1777/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1777/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1777/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1777\",\n              \"id\": 4903236698,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7ykb4K\",\n              \"number\": 1777,\n              \"title\": \"fix(session): auto-adopt across git common dirs on commit\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"id\": 257360244,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 2,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-07-16T14:50:38Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T19:17:05Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1777\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1777\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1777.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1777.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"**Trail:** [https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/875](<https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/875>)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nFixes entireio/cli#1439\\n\\n## What\\n\\nAuto-adopt a unique ACTIVE agent session from another git common dir during `prepare-commit-msg`, so commits in an enabled repo B get an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer when the live session state still lives under repo A.\\n\\n## Why / how it helps\\n\\nLong agent sessions often move across independently enabled repos. Hooks fire in B, but B's `.git/entire-sessions` is empty, so the trailer is silently skipped even though Entire is installed. Manual `entire session adopt` (entireio/cli#1472) already exists; this wires a safe automatic path on commit.\\n\\n## How\\n\\n* Maintain a best-effort live-session registry under the user cache whenever an ACTIVE session is saved (cleared on end/clear/tombstone).\\n* On `prepare-commit-msg`, if the current repo is enabled and has no local ACTIVE session, discover exactly one recent cross-common-dir candidate via:\\n  1. live-session registry — reaches **non-sibling** worktrees under unrelated parents (covers #1439's own repro: a session in `…/entire.io/.worktrees/…` committing in an unrelated `/private/tmp/…` checkout), then\\n  2. immediate sibling repos under the parent directory (microservices / seeded repro).\\n* Require a **non-boilerplate** `FilesTouched`∩staged overlap **and** a process-owner match for every candidate (the registry path drops proximity and leans on these stronger guards to prevent cross-repo steals); ambiguous candidates skip.\\n* The adopt is **split across the two commit hooks**: `prepare-commit-msg` registers the adopted session in the target (so the trailer lands) and stamps a `PendingSourceRetire` marker, but leaves the source ACTIVE; `post-commit` completes the destructive source-side retire once the commit is a fact. An aborted commit therefore never strands the source with its checkpointing retired and no commit.\\n* Tradeoff: this is direction-1 handoff (adopt/retire), not a full joint multi-repo session model (issue direction 3). Coordinated A+B commits in one turn still need a future fan-out model.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n* Live repro (before): A trailer present; B message unchanged / no trailer; B `entire-sessions` empty.\\n* Live repro (after, same script with `/tmp/entire-1439`):\\n  * A: `Entire-Checkpoint: …`\\n  * B: `Entire-Checkpoint: …` and session state present under B.\\n* Edges: no FilesTouched overlap → no adopt; two overlapping sibling sources → no adopt.\\n* Unit/regression: `TestAutoAdopt_*`, `TestLiveRegistry_*`, existing `TestSessionAdopt_*`.\\n* Mutation: early-return no-op in `tryAutoAdoptCrossCommonDirSession` → `TestAutoAdopt_PrepareCommitMsg_ViaLiveRegistry` FAIL; restore → PASS.\\n* Audit: two clean passes after requiring overlap (blocks owner-only steal) + wrapcheck/lint fixes.\\n* `mise run fmt && mise run lint` green; `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/session ./cmd/entire/cli` green on committed tree.\\n\\n## Review follow-ups (trail 875)\\n\\nThree architectural review findings addressed on top of the initial change:\\n\\n* **Deferred source retire (HIGH):** the destructive source-side tombstone moved from `prepare-commit-msg` to `post-commit` (`finalizePendingSourceRetires`), so an aborted commit no longer retires the source with no commit. Idempotent, panic-guarded, time-bounded.\\n* **Non-sibling registry reach (HIGH):** dropped the parent-dir proximity gate from the registry discovery path so #1439's own cross-parent repro actually gets a trailer; steal-safety now rests on owner + non-boilerplate-overlap + uniqueness. Removed the now-unused `autoAdoptSiblingProximity` helper.\\n* **Integration coverage (MED):** added `integration_test/auto_adopt_integration_test.go` driving the real `entire hooks git post-commit` binary after a real `git commit` — post-commit finalize retires the source, a held source flock makes finalize give up without corruption, and a disabled target stays inert. Full integration suite green (440 passed).\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1777/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1777/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3108\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3108/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3108/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3108/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3108\",\n              \"id\": 6315846906,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABONvqog\",\n              \"number\": 3108,\n              \"title\": \"fix(gitrepo): accept unregistered commondir checkouts\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-10T21:05:47Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-11T13:51:13Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-11-11T13:51:11Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3108\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3108\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3108.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3108.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-11-11T13:51:10Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Entire fails in a checkout whose `.git` directory holds its own `HEAD` and index and shares another repository's objects and refs through a `commondir` file, without a `<common>/worktrees` registration. Container launchers create checkouts this way over mounted host metadata, and Git accepts the layout (setup.c follows `commondir` without requiring registration).\\n\\n`resolveWorktreeID` in `gitrepo/metadata.go` required every Git directory that differs from the common directory to be an immediate child of `<common>/worktrees`. `ResolveWorktreeMetadata` runs on every repository open, so session init, `checkpoint list`, and the commit hooks all failed with `validate linked-worktree registration ... stat <common>/worktrees: no such file or directory`, and commits got no `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n- A Git directory outside `<common>/worktrees`, by spelling and by resolution, is an unregistered checkout with an empty worktree ID. No consumer reads the resolver's ID (they use `paths.GetWorktreeID`, which already returns empty for a `.git` directory), so the check only ever blocked.\\n- A Git directory that names the registration tree must still be an immediate child: escaping symlinks and nested registrations stay rejected. The check compares the ancestors of the Git directory (its spelling and its resolved location) with `<common>/worktrees` by file identity, so symlink aliases, case variants on case-insensitive filesystems and bind mounts can't pass an escaping or nested registration off as an unregistered checkout.\\n- `openSessionCondensationRepository` now accepts such a checkout as a session's recorded home, since it is the same repository; `checkpoint-implementation.md` says so.\\n- The checkout shares the main worktree's empty ID, so it cannot hold an `OtherWorktrees` entry. `SaveStep` used to record a step there by a session homed in the main checkout as the home's work (its files joined the home's `FilesTouched` and the home's `BaseCommit` moved to the checkout's HEAD). A non-home step that cannot get its own entry is now skipped with a Warn; this also covers a linked worktree whose admin directory cannot be marked, which fell through the same way. The skipped step's files are not recorded, but its tokens are, as for a turn with no file changes. A linked home moved mid-turn by `git worktree move` is still recognised as the home by its marker. A home with the empty ID has no marker, and a renamed main worktree can't be told from an unregistered checkout whose path is gone (a container path seen from the host), so steps after either are skipped rather than risk recording another checkout's work as the home's.\\n- An `OtherWorktrees` entry under the empty ID counts only in the checkout whose path it records, so a session homed in a linked worktree can record the unregistered checkout there without that record linking commits in the main worktree.\\n- `openWorktreeAdmin` refuses `<common>/worktrees/<id>` unless it is the root's Git directory, so a `.git` file whose text names another repository's `worktrees/<id>` can't read or mark the real `<id>` worktree.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- Integration: `TestUnregisteredCommonDirCheckout_CommitGetsCheckpoint` runs enable, a turn, and a commit in the layout, and asserts session state in the host common dir, the trailer, and `checkpoint list`.\\n- Resolver: absolute and relative `commondir`, with and without an existing `worktrees/` directory, and a `.git` file pointing at an unregistered Git directory. The escaping-registration test also covers a `commondir` through an alias of the common directory, a `.git` pointer through an alias of the registration tree, and a case variant of the tree; a nested registration is tested through a case variant too.\\n- Condensation: an unregistered checkout as recorded home and as current worktree.\\n- Turn end: `TestGuestTurnEnd_InUnregisteredCheckoutIsNotRecordedAsHome`, a session homed in the main checkout ending a turn in the unregistered checkout, `TestGuestTurnEnd_UnmarkableWorktreeIsNotRecordedAsHome`, a linked worktree with a malformed incarnation marker (its tokens kept), `TestGuestTurnEnd_EmptyIDEntryBelongsToOneCheckout`, a linked-home session with steps in the unregistered checkout and the main worktree, `TestGuestTurnEnd_HomeMovedMidTurnIsStillHome`, `git worktree move` of a linked home, and `TestGuestTurnEnd_VanishedEmptyIDHomeIsNotAdopted`, a session homed in an unregistered checkout that is gone, then a step in the main worktree.\\n- Marker: `TestMarkWorktree_RefusesAnAdminDirThatIsNotTheCheckouts`, a `.git` file naming another repository's `worktrees/victim`.\\n- All new tests fail on the old code.\\n\\n## Known limitations\\n\\n- A session homed in either the main checkout or the unregistered checkout does not record edits it makes in the other (their tokens are kept). Among several checkouts with the empty ID, only the first to record a step for a session holds its entry; steps in the others are skipped the same way. Other main-ID consumers are path-guarded (`worktree_home.go` skips ID-less sessions; resumed-turn relocation repoints only when the recorded path no longer resolves to the same common dir).\\n- `paths.GetWorktreeID` still errors for a `.git` file whose gitdir is not under `.git/worktrees/` or `.bare/worktrees/` (also `--separate-git-dir` and bare repos with other directory names). In those layouts `SaveStep` fails in session init, which calls `paths.GetWorktreeID` unconditionally, so the new turn-end skip never applies there. That predates this change and is left for a follow-up.\\n\\nTrail: https://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2846\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3108/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3108/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": {\n                \"id\": 2626939,\n                \"client_id\": \"Iv23lieFG10uOnChW4TN\",\n                \"slug\": \"entire\",\n                \"node_id\": \"A_kwHOAfprLM4AKBV7\",\n                \"owner\": {\n                  \"login\": \"entireio\",\n                  \"id\": 33188652,\n                  \"node_id\": \"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjMzMTg4NjUy\",\n                  \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33188652?v=4\",\n                  \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio\",\n                  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio\",\n                  \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/followers\",\n                  \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/following{/other_user}\",\n                  \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                  \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                  \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/subscriptions\",\n                  \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/orgs\",\n                  \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/repos\",\n                  \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/events{/privacy}\",\n                  \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/received_events\",\n                  \"type\": \"Organization\",\n                  \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                  \"site_admin\": false\n                },\n                \"name\": \"Entire\",\n                \"description\": \"\",\n                \"external_url\": \"https://entire.com\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/entire\",\n                \"created_at\": \"2026-01-09T21:20:56Z\",\n                \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-23T08:32:31Z\",\n                \"permissions\": {\n                  \"administration\": \"read\",\n                  \"checks\": \"write\",\n                  \"contents\": \"write\",\n                  \"emails\": \"read\",\n                  \"members\": \"read\",\n                  \"metadata\": \"read\",\n                  \"pull_requests\": \"write\",\n                  \"statuses\": \"read\",\n                  \"workflows\": \"write\"\n                },\n                \"events\": [\n                  \"check_suite\",\n                  \"create\",\n                  \"delete\",\n                  \"fork\",\n                  \"member\",\n                  \"membership\",\n                  \"organization\",\n                  \"pull_request\",\n                  \"push\",\n                  \"repository\",\n                  \"star\",\n                  \"team\"\n                ]\n              },\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3072\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3072/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3072/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3072/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3072\",\n              \"id\": 6284537228,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABN0o6iw\",\n              \"number\": 3072,\n              \"title\": \"fix(hooks): keep a hook's mode when Entire backs it up by copying\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n                \"id\": 26940511,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI2OTQwNTEx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Beehtrix\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Beehtrix/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-09T10:42:22Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-11T08:04:38Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-11-10T22:31:09Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3072\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3072\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3072.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3072.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-11-10T22:31:09Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes #3049.\\n\\n@Soph, this is the copy fallback in `hook_backup.go`. I found it while working on #3046, and it is on main, so it gets its own PR off main.\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\nWhere the hooks directory can't hard-link (some FUSE and network mounts, exFAT), `linkOrCopy` falls back to `copyHookFile`, which always creates the copy as `0755`. Entire's chain call runs `<hook>.pre-entire` only when it is executable, the same rule git applies to the hook itself. So a hook the user switched off with `chmod -x` starts running on every commit or push once `entire enable` backs it up, and a private (`0600`) hook becomes readable by everyone. Older copies (`keepOlderCopy`) go through the same copy.\\n\\nA second path hits this on every filesystem. Taking a moved copy back from pre-commit or another hook manager (`moveUserHookInto`, `refreshKeepCopy`) always copies, since #2790 made them separate files. A switched-off hook in `.pre-entire` therefore lands in `<hook>.legacy` as `0755`, and pre-commit runs `.legacy` when it is executable.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\n`copyHookFile` gives the copy the source's permission bits, which is what a hard link shares. It reads the mode and the bytes through one no-follow descriptor (`readHookFile`), so both come from the same file, and it still sets the mode with `Chmod` after the write, because the umask narrows `OpenFile`'s mode. Symlinks are untouched: `copyOrRelink` still recreates them as links.\\n\\nWith the mode kept, a change of mode alone is a new version of the hook, so `sameHookFile` now compares permission bits as well as bytes. Without that, the same script switched back on in Entire's place would reuse the switched-off backup, and a keep copy would miss the user switching their hook off in `.legacy` or a manager's moved file, and restore it switched on. With hard links, main already had the backup half of this for a hook written over as a new file.\\n\\nTo test the copy path on a filesystem that can link, `linkOrCopy` now calls a `linkHookFile` variable that tests replace. It is the same seam #3046 adds, line for line, so the only overlap with #3046 is `copyHookFile`'s body, where #3046 has `copyHookFileWithMode`. #3046's `*KeepingMode` helpers do this job for its own paths, so whichever PR lands second drops them for the plain helpers.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n`cmd/entire/cli/strategy/hook_copy_mode_test.go`:\\n\\n- `TestInstallHooks_CopiedBackupKeepsHookMode`: with links failing, the backup of a `0644`, `0600`, `0700` or `0755` hook keeps that mode, and a rotation keeps the older copy's mode and the new backup's.\\n- `TestInstallHooks_CopiedBackupOfSwitchedOffHookDoesNotRun`: with links failing, a `0644` pre-push hook is backed up, and running the installed hook runs only Entire's, not the user's.\\n- `TestInstallHooks_ReclaimedUserHookKeepsMode`: with links working, taking the copy back from pre-commit (`.legacy`) or another manager's wrapper keeps the user's `0644` hook at `0644`, keep copy included.\\n- `TestInstallHooks_ModeOnlyChangeRefreshesBackup`: with links failing and with links working, the same script written over Entire's hook switched on becomes a `0755` backup, and the `0644` one becomes an older copy.\\n- `TestInstallHooks_KeepCopyFollowsModeOnlyChange`: after the user switches the reclaimed hook off, the keep copy turns `0644`, and the hook comes back `0644` when pre-commit or another manager next moves Entire's hook onto it.\\n\\nAll five fail on main and pass here. The mode tests skip on Windows, which has no execute bits.\\n\\nRun in a Linux container: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/` passes, `golangci-lint` v2.15.0 reports 0 issues, and the complexity gate reports no new or worsened function.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3072/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 1,\n                \"+1\": 1,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3072/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2131\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2131/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2131/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2131/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2131\",\n              \"id\": 5254301778,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBCi-2g\",\n              \"number\": 2131,\n              \"title\": \"perf(checkpoint): batch persistent session writes with CAS\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"id\": 34813274,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 4,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-26T07:07:48Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-01T06:43:57Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2131\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2131\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2131.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2131.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Problem\\n\\n`process_sessions` still persists each session separately. For every session, it reloads the checkpoint, rebuilds the session index and summary, creates a commit, and advances the checkpoint ref.\\n\\nIssue #2091 measures that work at roughly 73–103 ms per session. The repeated checkpoint load and rebuild make condensation slower as more sessions share a checkpoint.\\n\\nCheckpoint-level batching needs two things first:\\n\\n- Ref updates must detect concurrent writes from hooks, worktrees, CLI processes, and other Git clients.\\n- Both persistent Git layouts must use the same batch algorithm.\\n\\n## Solution\\n\\nThis PR adds native compare-and-swap publication and a shared `BatchSessions` write request.\\n\\nIt lays the storage and concurrency groundwork for #2091 item 2. It does not yet change PostCommit to group and submit sessions in batches. That work is listed below.\\n\\n## Native compare-and-swap publication\\n\\n`CompareAndSwapRef` publishes refs through native Git:\\n\\n```text\\ngit update-ref <ref> <new> <expected-old>\\n```\\n\\nMissing-ref creation passes the correct all-zero object ID in both SHA-1 and SHA-256 repositories.\\n\\n`RunRefTransaction` retries a logical mutation when another writer wins the race. Each attempt reads the current tip, rebuilds from that tip, and publishes with CAS. Conflicts use bounded, cancellation-aware jitter. The transaction stops after 16 attempts.\\n\\nA mutation that reports `changed=false` is an idempotent no-op and does not call `git update-ref`.\\n\\nThe CAS conversion covers persistent v1 metadata refs and per-checkpoint refs, including:\\n\\n- initial ref creation;\\n- v1 migration;\\n- attribution, summary, and transcript backfills;\\n- reconciliation and safe local ref advancement;\\n- orphan cleanup and expected-old deletion;\\n- shadow-branch migration;\\n- rewind publication;\\n- OPF publication.\\n\\nOPF uses one CAS attempt by design. If its expected ref has moved, it fails closed and withholds the push. It does not rebuild sanitized output from newly appeared content.\\n\\nGo-git object construction now takes a process-local lock keyed by `*git.Repository`. This protects go-git state shared by concurrent writers in one process. Native Git CAS handles publication conflicts between processes.\\n\\n## Checkpoint-level batch writes\\n\\n`BatchSessions` is now part of the sealed `WriteRequest` union. One request contains a checkpoint ID and one or more reserved session writes.\\n\\nValidation happens before object construction:\\n\\n- The checkpoint ID must be present and valid.\\n- Every session must reference that checkpoint.\\n- Session IDs must be valid and unique.\\n- Sessions are sorted by `SessionID`.\\n- Task tool-use IDs and agent IDs must be valid.\\n- Duplicate task IDs within or across incoming sessions are rejected.\\n- Sessions without timestamps share one UTC timestamp, truncated to seconds.\\n- Author fallback, commit-message inputs, and prepared tree hashes are fixed before CAS retries.\\n\\n`GitStore` and `gitRefsStore` share the same preparation and checkpoint-tree builder. Their wrappers only locate or splice the checkpoint subtree and choose the ref to publish.\\n\\nFor each CAS attempt, the builder:\\n\\n- loads the existing checkpoint once;\\n- reads each existing session’s metadata once;\\n- reuses the numeric index when updating a session;\\n- preserves untouched session subtree hashes;\\n- appends new sessions in canonical order;\\n- merges the task subtree once and preserves untouched tasks;\\n- reduces the complete final session set into the root summary;\\n- preserves combined attribution and sticky review, investigation, and import flags;\\n- aggregates counts, tokens, files, strategy, branch, and commit SHA deterministically;\\n- creates one checkpoint commit for that backend attempt.\\n\\nExisting `Session` and `ReservedSession` requests pass through the same builder with one session. Their caller contract does not change.\\n\\nCombined attribution stays in its existing backfill transaction. The batch write does not fold it into the checkpoint commit.\\n\\n## Storage and compatibility\\n\\nThe durable checkpoint format does not change:\\n\\n```text\\nmetadata.json\\n0/metadata.json\\n0/full.jsonl\\n0/transcript.jsonl\\n1/...\\ntasks/<tool-use-id>/...\\n```\\n\\nOlder clients already understand checkpoints with multiple numbered session directories. A batch produces the same tree, task subtree, summary, and metadata types that repeated single-session writes produce.\\n\\nCompatibility was checked in separate dimensions:\\n\\n- New clients continue to read existing checkpoint data.\\n- Old clients can read checkpoints written by `BatchSessions`.\\n- Existing callers still use `Writer.Write(context.Context, WriteRequest)`.\\n- Single-session requests keep their existing behavior.\\n- Malformed or ambiguous requests now fail before publication.\\n- Concurrent upgraded writers protect each other with native CAS.\\n- If an old blind writer publishes first, the CAS writer detects the change and rebuilds.\\n- If an old blind writer publishes second, it can still overwrite the newer write. One upgraded participant cannot make a pre-CAS writer safe.\\n\\nRejecting invalid input and replacing last-writer-wins behavior with conflict detection are intentional safety changes, not storage incompatibilities.\\n\\n## Routing and partial success\\n\\nPersistent dispatch, kind routing, fanout, and the filesystem test store support `BatchSessions`.\\n\\nOne Git backend makes every session in the batch visible through one ref update. Fanout writes the primary first. Mirror failures remain logged and best-effort, so they do not turn a successful primary write into an error.\\n\\nRouting follows the backend encoded by the checkpoint ID if configuration changes after reservation. If a readable migrated copy exists, routing updates that copy too. The read-preferred backend is probed before the first physical write.\\n\\nThere is no transaction across physical backends. If the second backend fails, the first may already contain the batch. The writer returns the error. Retrying the same canonical upsert repairs the lagging copy.\\n\\nA future lifecycle caller must therefore treat an error as “some backend may already contain this batch,” not as proof that nothing was written.\\n\\nThe filesystem store replaces one JSON document atomically under a process-local mutex. It is a test backend and does not provide cross-process serialization.\\n\\n## Complexity\\n\\nThe deterministic visitation test uses existing checkpoints with 100, 200, and 500 sessions. With no tasks, it records:\\n\\n```text\\nroot entries visited          N + 1\\nsession entries visited       N\\nexisting metadata reads       N\\ntask entries visited          0\\nfinal-session contributions   N\\ntotal                         4N + 1\\n```\\n\\nThese counters measure visits to checkpoint content, not every CPU operation.\\n\\nOne CAS attempt against one Git backend performs one checkpoint load and build. It does not rescan the checkpoint for each incoming session. Request preparation happens once before the retry loop. A CAS conflict causes one more load and build from the winning tip.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n`mise run check` passed on the committed tree. This included:\\n\\n- formatting;\\n- golangci-lint with zero issues;\\n- the aggregate race-enabled unit and integration suite;\\n- Vogon, 56 of 56;\\n- roger-roger, 4 of 4.\\n\\nFocused race-enabled tests also passed for:\\n\\n- batch validation, ordering, summaries, timestamps, trailers, task collisions, and both Git layouts;\\n- concurrent metadata-ref and per-checkpoint-ref writes;\\n- SHA-1 and SHA-256 CAS;\\n- transaction retries and cancellation;\\n- initialization and migration;\\n- dispatch, kind routing, fanout, and filesystem storage;\\n- reconciliation, cleanup, ref advancement, rewind, and OPF publication;\\n- persistent-ref writer coverage.\\n\\nThe advisory duplication scan found nothing in `persistent_batch.go`. Its production persistent-backend findings come from older read-wrapper patterns. The only related new finding is duplicated routing-test setup.\\n\\nNo paid real-agent E2E tests were run.\\n\\n## Left for the next PR\\n\\nPostCommit still writes sessions one at a time. Completing #2091 item 2 requires the lifecycle layer to:\\n\\n1. Group materialized `process_sessions` results by checkpoint ID.\\n2. Build one `BatchSessions` request per checkpoint.\\n3. Persist enough intent to recover after a process crash.\\n4. Submit one batch write per checkpoint.\\n5. Retry safely when one physical backend may already contain the batch.\\n6. Keep combined attribution as a separate transaction.\\n7. Remove completed intent only after every required primary write succeeds.\\n8. Define when stale intent can be removed without losing recoverable work.\\n9. Test interruption before publication, partial backend success, retry, and cleanup.\\n10. Re-run the commit-hook performance tests and confirm that checkpoint loading and building happen once per checkpoint.\\n\\nUntil that work lands, single-session writes are safer and use the shared builder, but the full `process_sessions` latency reduction is not active.\\n\\nTask-v2 storage, attribution folding, unrelated CLI cleanup, and the existing commit-hook performance-test work remain out of scope.\\n\\n## Review status\\n\\nStages 1 and 2 were reviewed independently. No Critical, High, or Medium correctness defect was found.\\n\\nThe remaining hardening ideas are non-blocking:\\n\\n- Check cancellation again after acquiring the repository object lock.\\n- Replace the lexical persistent-ref writer inventory with an AST-based check.\\n- Narrow native Git’s `cannot lock ref` error classification if callers need more precise operational errors.\\n- Revisit process-lifetime lock-map retention if this code moves into a long-running process that repeatedly opens repositories.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2131/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2131/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2638\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2638/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2638/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2638/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2638\",\n              \"id\": 5667280516,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABGJ59FQ\",\n              \"number\": 2638,\n              \"title\": \"fix(import): only import sessions that belong to this repository\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-01T18:40:34Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-09T11:37:05Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-09T11:37:03Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2638\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2638\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2638.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2638.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-09T11:37:02Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1463\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n`entire import` (and the import offer in `entire enable`) could pick up sessions recorded in a different repository. Claude Code, Pi, Factory AI Droid, and Cursor store sessions in a per-project directory named with a lossy encoding of the repo path, so distinct repos such as `/w/acme/foo-bar` and `/w/acme-foo/bar` share one directory. Import treated everything in that directory as belonging to the current repo.\\n\\n- **Claude Code, Pi, Factory:** discovery keeps only transcripts whose first recorded `cwd` is the repo root or inside it. Transcripts that record no `cwd` are skipped. This also applies with `--path`.\\n- **Cursor:** transcripts record no `cwd`, but the Cursor CLI files each session under `~/.cursor/chats/<md5 of the workspace path>/<session id>/` (newer versions also write `meta.json` with the `cwd`). That key is exact, so recorded sessions are kept or dropped one by one, with or without `--path`; a session filed under this repo and another is dropped, and anything unreadable proves nothing. For sessions nothing recorded (IDE sessions, older stores), the importer refuses its default project directory when another path may use it: when `.workspace-trusted` names a different path (or exists but cannot be read), or when another existing directory has the same encoded name. The check fails closed: a walk that exceeds its budget, or that cannot list a candidate directory (for example under a traverse-only parent), is refused too, and the error names what could not be checked and the `--path` command to import anyway. An explicit `--path` skips the check, which now runs only when unrecorded sessions remain.\\n- The repo check opens each transcript, so it runs after the `--session` and 30-day filters rather than on every file in the directory. Copilot's existing check moved to the same place.\\n- Path matching (shared with Codex and Copilot) now accepts descendants whose name starts with `..` (such as `<repo>/..cache`), and a session recorded in a since-deleted subdirectory through a symlinked spelling of the repo (macOS `/var` → `/private/var`) still matches. A relative recorded `cwd` never matches, and a differently-cased spelling of the repo on a case-insensitive filesystem matches by directory identity.\\n- The `Importer.Discover` contract now says sessions must be attributable to `repoRoot`.\\n\\n## Known limits\\n\\n- `~/.cursor/chats` is undocumented Cursor internals, checked on macOS only; if its layout changes, sessions fall back to the directory check. A moved repo's Cursor CLI sessions hash to the old path and are left out, as Claude's are by their `cwd`. Sessions dropped as another workspace's are not reported.\\n- A colliding Cursor repo that has since been deleted or moved is not detected for unrecorded sessions. Closing that would mean refusing Cursor's default directory outright, since Cursor transcripts carry no workspace.\\n- A recorded `cwd` that no longer exists is matched lexically under the repo, so a deleted symlink inside the repo that pointed elsewhere is not detected (unchanged from before).\\n- Containment is by path: a session in a nested clone or submodule matches its parent repo (unchanged for Codex and Copilot).\\n- Transcripts copied from another machine where the repo lived at a different path no longer import, even with `--path`.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- New `agentimport/repo_scope_test.go` reproduces the collision for Claude, Pi, and Factory, and covers the Cursor refusal and the `--path` behavior.\\n- `agentimport/cursor_chats_test.go`: recorded sessions settle a shared directory, an unrecorded one is still refused, `--path` still drops another workspace's session, and mixed entries, a `meta.json` cwd that doesn't match its directory, a subdirectory cwd, non-key directories and unsafe IDs are classified safely. Tests point the chats store at an empty directory so none read a developer's real sessions.\\n- Further regression tests, each verified to fail without its fix: an unlistable candidate directory makes the Cursor walk fail closed (a dangling link does not), `..`-prefixed descendants match, a deleted subdirectory under a symlinked root matches, and the repo filter never sees files excluded by `--session` or the lookback window, a case-variant spelling matches, and an unreadable `.workspace-trusted` fails closed.\\n- Existing import fixtures (unit and integration) now record a `cwd`; no assertions changed.\\n- End to end with built binaries (main vs this branch), on macOS and on a Windows runner: two repos at colliding paths share one Claude project folder (the default `~/.claude/projects` location; on macOS with real Claude Code transcripts). On main, `entire import claude-code` and `entire enable --import-history` both import the other repo's session and the next `git push` sends it in this repo's checkpoint refs. On this branch only this repo's session is imported and nothing from the other repo is pushed.\\n- On Windows, `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agentimport/` fails the same set of tests on this branch as on main (25 that already fail on Windows on main, mostly temp-dir cleanup hitting a still-open `.git`); none of the new tests fail. CI's Windows job does not run this package.\\n- `mise run fmt`, `mise run lint` and `mise run test:ci` (unit, integration, canary) pass.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Import discovery behavior changes: some previously imported sessions may be skipped or Cursor default-path import may refuse with an error; incorrect cwd or collision logic could block legitimate history.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Agent import now scopes discovery to the current repository**, fixing cases where lossy per-project path encodings caused sessions from a different repo to be imported into the wrong one.\\n> \\n> For **Claude Code, Pi, and Factory**, discovery uses `repoScopedJSONLResolver`, which keeps only JSONL transcripts whose first recorded `cwd` lies under `repoRoot` (including with `--path`). Transcripts with no `cwd` are skipped. **`firstRecordedCwd`** scans JSONL with `bufio.Reader` so very long leading lines do not hide a later `cwd`.\\n> \\n> For **Cursor**, transcripts have no `cwd`, so when using the default project directory (not `--path`), **Discover errors and imports nothing** if the project dir might belong to another path: `.workspace-trusted` disagrees with `repoRoot`, another on-disk path shares the same encoded name (`pathsWithEncoding` + exported **`SanitizePathForCursor`**), or the collision walk hits its read budget (fail closed). Explicit `--path` skips that check.\\n> \\n> The **`Importer.Discover`** contract now requires sessions to be attributable to `repoRoot`. Unit/integration fixtures record `cwd` where needed; **`repo_scope_test.go`** covers collisions and Cursor refusal behavior.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit b7b42d0441863b59e5afcdccf5966f06a1e23043. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2638/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2638/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2671\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2671/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2671/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2671/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2671\",\n              \"id\": 5721717640,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABG076_w\",\n              \"number\": 2671,\n              \"title\": \"Restore full reviewer config; ask before reviewing someone else's code\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-06T02:01:47Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-08T14:20:56Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-08T14:20:53Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2671\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2671\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2671.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2671.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-08T14:20:53Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1493\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nReverts the reviewer isolation from #2598, which made reviews worse by stripping the project's CLAUDE.md, skills, MCP servers and hooks, and replaces it with informed consent: reviews of your own code run as before, reviews of someone else's code need your approval first.\\n\\n## Requirements covered\\n\\n1. **Opt-in.** Reviewing someone else's code needs explicit acceptance at a warning, or a flag to bypass it (`--trust-target <full sha>`). Agents can't accept on the user's behalf.\\n2. **See someone else's work before running it.** The warning and `--show-config` list exactly what the branch would run (hooks, MCP servers, settings, skills) before anything is checked out. Reviewers also report prompt-injection attempts as findings. Scanning the code for injection techniques before the run is a follow-up.\\n3. **Guardrails via system prompt.** Every reviewer is told that its task comes only from the review request: repository content, CLAUDE.md included, informs the review but can't change the task, grant permissions or trigger actions, and attempts to direct the reviewer are reported as findings.\\n\\nDeferred to a follow-up: limits on tokens spent per review. This PR already stops a branch from changing which reviewers, models or judge run, since review settings come from your own checkout.\\n\\n## What changes\\n\\n**1. Revert #2598.** Reviewers load the checkout's full configuration again: hooks, MCP servers, skills, settings.\\n\\n**2. Same guardrail for every reviewer.** One paragraph sets an instruction hierarchy: the task comes only from the review request; repository content (code, comments, docs, CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md) informs the review but can't change the task, grant permissions or trigger actions; attempts to direct the reviewer are reported as findings. Claude Code and Pi get it via `--append-system-prompt`, Codex via `-c developer_instructions=…`, and agents without a review runner at the top of the printed prompt. No tool, hook or MCP server is disabled.\\n\\n> Note: the Codex flag overrides any `developer_instructions` you've set in `~/.codex/config.toml`, for review runs only.\\n\\n**3. Approval gate** for plain `entire review` and `--target`. A commit belongs to its git author, as everywhere else in git.\\n\\n| Commits between your default branch and the head | Result |\\n|---|---|\\n| all authored by your `user.email` | runs as before, no new output |\\n| any authored by someone else | **terminal:** confirm stating that the review agent loads the branch's hooks, MCP servers, settings and skills, and listing what would run; default Cancel. **Agent or no terminal:** fixed refusal telling the agent to stop and ask the user, with `--trust-target <full sha>` to run once approved |\\n\\n- `--show-config [--json]` lists what a review would run and exits: hooks, MCP servers, command-bearing and permission settings, Pi extensions, and skills, commands, prompts and subagents. Entire's own hooks are recognised by exact whole-command match.\\n- With `--target`, the profile is chosen and the branch head pinned in your checkout. The pinned commit's tree is inspected, and only after approval is the worktree created: added with `--no-checkout` and no hooks, its head verified against the pin, then checked out. For someone else's branch the checkout runs with no git hooks, no LFS smudge and no submodule recursion, and `.worktreeinclude` files are not copied.\\n- The re-run inside the worktree reads review settings from your checkout, not the branch's `.entire/settings.json`. It skips the gate only when the forwarded SHA matches its own head.\\n\\n**4. Docs and agent-help** for `review`.\\n\\n## Hardening\\n\\n- The commit range is always counted from your default branch; `--base` only sets the review scope, so it can't hide commits.\\n- Agent config is read with exact JSON keys, so `\\\"Hooks\\\": []`-style decoys can't hide entries. The commit tree is matched case-insensitively, as a macOS or Windows checkout loads it. Symlinks and unparseable files count as unknown, never as nothing.\\n- Inspection runs on branch data before approval, so it's bounded: files over 1 MiB are unknown, at most 100 items are listed per directory, and more than 20,000 config entries fails closed.\\n- `--trust-target` takes the full SHA; a short prefix could be ground to match a different commit.\\n- Without `user.email` (common on CI) or without a default branch, every review needs approval.\\n- Agents are recognised by their session variables (Claude Code, Codex, Copilot, Cursor, Pi, OpenCode, Gemini CLI, Antigravity, Factory Droid), the cross-tool `AI_AGENT`, or `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0`. External agents can declare their own in an optional `caller_env_vars` field of `info`. When an agent passes `--trust-target`, the output says which one (\\\"Approved with --trust-target from a Claude Code session\\\").\\n- The confirm prints its details above the prompt, because huh's accessible confirm renders only the title.\\n\\n## Self-declared authorship\\n\\nThe security monitor flags that git authorship is self-declared, so a branch that copies your email reads as yours. That's true of every git commit and is an accepted decision for this PR. Follow-ups: verify signatures when you sign, and use the trail's authenticated author for trail targets.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- `mise run check` passes.\\n- Unit tests cover the gate decisions, authorship, the inventory (tree vs disk parity, decoy keys, mixed case, symlinks, skills, oversized files, installed-hooks drift check), the pinned checkout and the moved-branch case.\\n- New integration test `review_trust_gate_test.go` replaces the isolation canary the revert removed. It drives the real binary, with no agent CLI on PATH:\\n  - refusal leaves nothing checked out and runs nothing\\n  - `--show-config` lists the branch's hook\\n  - an approved checkout runs no git hooks and the re-run doesn't ask again\\n- Manually ran the new binary in a scratch repo: terminal confirm (Cancel and Run, accessible mode), agent refusal, full vs short SHA, and own-commit review. Ran `--show-config` on a real teammate branch.\\n- Not run: real-agent reviews of the guardrail (paid). That `developer_instructions` reaches the Codex model is unverified beyond the installed binary recognising the key.\\n\\n## Known limits\\n\\n- The re-run still checks which agents have hooks installed in the worktree, not in your checkout.\\n\\n## Follow-ups\\n\\n- Reviewer agent config in review profiles (a reviewer's own hooks, MCP servers and extensions instead of the checkout's): trail [1516](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1516), lands after this one.\\n- Token limits for reviews.\\n- Scan for prompt-injection techniques before the run, shown in the warning.\\n- Signature verification and trail-author ownership.\\n- Optional per-user trusted authors/branches.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2671/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2671/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2789\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2789/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2789/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2789/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2789\",\n              \"id\": 5871991131,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABIsOqzQ\",\n              \"number\": 2789,\n              \"title\": \"execx: a detached child must not inherit parent-held output pipes\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"evisdren\",\n                \"id\": 256443556,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD0kEpA\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256443556?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/evisdren\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-15T18:46:46Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-15T21:56:49Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-15T21:56:46Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2789\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2789\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2789.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2789.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-15T21:56:46Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1586\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\n`SpawnDetached` set Stdout/Stderr to `io.Discard`. A non-`*os.File` writer makes os/exec allocate an OS pipe per stream, drained by a goroutine in the **parent**; `Process.Release` does not sever that. Once a short-lived parent — a git hook — exits, the pipe read ends close, the child's next stdout/stderr write takes EPIPE, and the Go runtime kills a Go child on SIGPIPE to fds 1/2: the detached work dies mid-flight. All three call sites (session sweep, trail-enablement refresh, analytics) carry this today.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n`Stdout`/`Stderr` stay `nil`, so os/exec opens the null device **in the child**: no pipes, no parent coupling. Command construction moves to `newDetachedCmd` so the no-parent-pipes property is unit-testable — a subprocess e2e through `SpawnDetached` is not possible because it deliberately no-ops under `go test`.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n`go test ./cmd/entire/cli/execx` passes (new tests assert nil output streams and the cwd fallback).\\n\\nExtracted from #2784, which is being closed: the brain checkpoint-hint feature moved into the entire-brain plugin as a chained pre-push hook, so the cli side is no longer needed — but this fix stands on its own.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Small, well-tested change to detached process I/O setup; fixes a real failure mode without touching auth, data, or broader control flow.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Fixes detached background children dying with SIGPIPE** when spawned from short-lived parents (e.g. git hooks). `SpawnDetached` no longer sets `Stdout`/`Stderr` to `io.Discard`; those streams stay **nil** so `os/exec` wires the child to the null device instead of parent-held pipes whose read ends close when the parent exits.\\n> \\n> Command setup is extracted to **`newDetachedCmd`** (testable under `go test`, where `SpawnDetached` still no-ops). New unit tests lock in nil I/O streams and the empty-`dir` → temp fallback.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit e65cb6b33367e3b1cd5afd3477f3302eb24724f6. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2789/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2789/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2641\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2641/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2641/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2641/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2641\",\n              \"id\": 5672896751,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABGOYeZQ\",\n              \"number\": 2641,\n              \"title\": \"hooks: say an existing hook still runs after enable, and restore it on uninstall\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-02T04:31:26Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-08T12:36:59Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-08T12:36:57Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2641\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2641\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2641.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2641.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-08T12:36:57Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1466\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n`entire enable` replaces an existing hook (e.g. pre-push) with only `[entire] Backed up existing pre-push to pre-push.pre-entire`. The hook keeps running through the `.pre-entire` chain, but nothing says so and it isn't documented. The README also said plain `entire disable` \\\"removes the git hooks\\\" (only `--uninstall` does).\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n- Backup message (stderr, plus a `logging.Info` line):\\n  `[entire] Your pre-push hook still runs, after Entire's (moved to .git/hooks/pre-push.pre-entire).`\\n- The \\\"replacing\\\" warning (a backup already exists) now says which hook keeps running and that the current one is not kept.\\n- `disable --uninstall` prints \\\"Restored your original <hook> hook\\\" (`RemoveGitHookDetailed` reports what it restored).\\n- README \\\"Existing git hooks\\\" section and corrected `disable` text; one line in `enable` help; `post-rewrite` added to the `disable` help hook list.\\n\\nNot in this PR: the overwrite itself — a changed hook is lost when `<hook>.pre-entire` already exists. That is a separate fix off main (rotation with concurrency/crash safety and pre-commit migration-mode handling). Related: #2640, #2643.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `TestRemoveGitHook_RestoresBackup` asserts the restored hook is reported.\\n- `mise run lint`; strategy, cli and hook/uninstall integration tests pass.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2641/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2641/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2645\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2645/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2645/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2645/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2645\",\n              \"id\": 5692577576,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABGd2Ubg\",\n              \"number\": 2645,\n              \"title\": \"Resolve Codex subagent transcripts through the inventory at condensation\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-03T18:54:04Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-03T19:35:58Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-03T19:35:56Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2645\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2645\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2645.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2645.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-03T19:35:56Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1470\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nCheckpoint 01M414VXYH4236W6PAGSV7QT0F (Codex 0.159.3, single subagent) stored `tasks/<agent_id>/task.json` with `\\\"transcript_unavailable_reason\\\": \\\"transcript path unresolvable\\\"` and no `agent-*.jsonl`, although the child's rollout existed under `~/.codex/sessions`.\\n\\nA Codex child's rollout path reaches its `TaskRecord` only when `refreshCodexInventory` sees a terminal turn, and that runs at the parent's turn end (or SessionEnd). In this run the parent ran `git commit` itself at 15:07:06, after the child finished (15:06:58) but before its own Stop (15:07:08). PostCommit condensation therefore saw a record with no path, and `resolveTaskTranscriptPath` only knows Claude's directory layout.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n`materializeTaskRecords` now passes task records whose declared path is empty or cannot be opened to `resolveInventoryTaskTranscripts`. That function builds refs from `SubagentInventory`, the authoritative child list, and calls the agent's `ExtractWithSubagentInventory`. For Codex this accepts a rollout only when its `session_meta.id` matches the agent ID, and it falls back to the existing budgeted scan of `sessions` and `archived_sessions`. The resolved path is tried after the declared path and before the Claude-layout fallback. Agents without the extractor are unaffected, and session state is not changed.\\n\\nWhether the declared path is usable is checked by the new `agent.CheckTranscriptReadable`, which opens and closes an external path without reading it (so a missing file, a permission error and a directory all count as unusable) and stats only under `.entire`, as `StatTranscriptFile` does. A record whose declared path opens is not passed in, so the common case reads no rollout at commit time. An unreadable file inside the Codex rollout roots still makes the Codex scan fail closed, as it did before; that is the resolver's existing uniqueness guarantee, not something this PR changes. `docs/development/checkpoint-implementation.md` now documents the new resolution order.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- `TestMaterializeTaskRecords_CodexRecordWithoutPathResolvesThroughInventory`: mid-turn commit shape (inventory entry plus pathless in-flight record); a rollout with a matching `session_meta.id` is stored, and one with a mismatched ID stays unresolvable. Fails without the fix with the reported reason.\\n- `TestMaterializeTaskRecords_CodexRelocatedRolloutResolvesThroughInventory`: declared path points at `sessions/`, rollout moved to `archived_sessions/`. Fails without the fix with `transcript unreadable`.\\n- `TestMaterializeTaskRecords_CodexUnreadableDeclaredPathResolvesThroughInventory`: declared path exists with mode 000, outside the rollout roots. Fails with an existence-only check with `transcript unreadable`.\\n- `TestCheckTranscriptReadable_ExternalPaths`: readable, missing, directory, and permission-denied paths.\\n\\n`mise run check` passes except `TestOpenCodeSeedRepoPlantsDeps`, which needs the opencode bootstrap and fails locally regardless of this change. Two `claudecode` config-probe tests hit their 5s fake-`claude` timeout in one full run and pass in isolation; that package is untouched.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes checkpoint task transcript resolution for Codex subagents; wrong matching could attach the wrong rollout, though session_meta.id verification and inventory-only inputs limit that risk.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Fixes **missing Codex subagent transcripts** in checkpoints when a task record has no usable declared path—common after a **mid-turn parent commit** (child finished, inventory not refreshed yet) or when Codex **archives/relocates** a rollout after the path was recorded.\\n> \\n> Condensation now calls **`resolveInventoryTaskTranscripts`**, which finds task records with a missing or stale declared path, builds **`SubagentReference`** entries from **`SubagentInventory`**, and uses **`ExtractWithSubagentInventory`** to resolve rollout files verified by **`session_meta.id`**. **`materializeTaskRecords`** tries candidates in order: declared path → **inventory resolution** → Claude-layout fallback, so a bad declared path does not skip the new step.\\n> \\n> Tests cover mid-turn records with no path, **rejection when `session_meta.id` does not match** the agent ID, and stale declared paths resolved from archived rollout roots.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit e4a961c2ebcfb6ab051f1bb9f32e49c3c35f1b5a. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2645/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2645/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": {\n                \"id\": 2626939,\n                \"client_id\": \"Iv23lieFG10uOnChW4TN\",\n                \"slug\": \"entire\",\n                \"node_id\": \"A_kwHOAfprLM4AKBV7\",\n                \"owner\": {\n                  \"login\": \"entireio\",\n                  \"id\": 33188652,\n                  \"node_id\": \"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjMzMTg4NjUy\",\n                  \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33188652?v=4\",\n                  \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio\",\n                  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio\",\n                  \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/followers\",\n                  \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/following{/other_user}\",\n                  \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                  \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                  \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/subscriptions\",\n                  \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/orgs\",\n                  \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/repos\",\n                  \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/events{/privacy}\",\n                  \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/received_events\",\n                  \"type\": \"Organization\",\n                  \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                  \"site_admin\": false\n                },\n                \"name\": \"Entire\",\n                \"description\": \"\",\n                \"external_url\": \"https://entire.com\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/entire\",\n                \"created_at\": \"2026-01-09T21:20:56Z\",\n                \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-23T08:32:31Z\",\n                \"permissions\": {\n                  \"administration\": \"read\",\n                  \"checks\": \"write\",\n                  \"contents\": \"write\",\n                  \"emails\": \"read\",\n                  \"members\": \"read\",\n                  \"metadata\": \"read\",\n                  \"pull_requests\": \"write\",\n                  \"statuses\": \"read\",\n                  \"workflows\": \"write\"\n                },\n                \"events\": [\n                  \"check_suite\",\n                  \"create\",\n                  \"delete\",\n                  \"fork\",\n                  \"member\",\n                  \"membership\",\n                  \"organization\",\n                  \"pull_request\",\n                  \"push\",\n                  \"repository\",\n                  \"star\",\n                  \"team\"\n                ]\n              },\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2515\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2515/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2515/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2515/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2515\",\n              \"id\": 5488002561,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABD7xB3Q\",\n              \"number\": 2515,\n              \"title\": \"Extract `entire investigate` into the entire-investigate plugin\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-17T13:28:59Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-21T09:48:32Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-21T09:48:31Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2515\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2515\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2515.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2515.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-21T09:48:31Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1362\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nMoves `entire investigate` into [entireio/entire-investigate](https://github.com/entireio/entire-investigate), removing ~13k lines of built-in command code. Existing invocations and flags work unchanged once the plugin is installed.\\n\\n- Offers on-demand installation for `investigate`, alongside `graph`, and refreshes a stale plugin index once before reporting a missing entry.\\n- Preserves session, provenance, and checkpoint metadata contracts for existing hooks and stored checkpoints.\\n- Ignores legacy `investigate` settings without breaking settings loading. Configuration and prompt-trust enforcement now belong to the plugin; existing trust-gate tests are retained using review prompts.\\n\\n## Installation and migration\\n\\nRun `entire plugin install investigate` ([v0.1.0](https://github.com/entireio/entire-investigate/releases/tag/v0.1.0) is published), or accept the install prompt from `entire investigate`.\\n\\nTo retain existing configuration, copy the old `investigate` object into `.entire/investigate.local.json`; otherwise regenerate it with `entire investigate --edit`. Legacy settings blocks are safely ignored.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `mise run check` passes (format, lint, unit, integration, and canary).\\n- `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` passes; CI is green.\\n- Verified external dispatch and installation from the published release.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2515/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2515/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2670\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2670/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2670/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2670/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2670\",\n              \"id\": 5721629083,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABG03jBg\",\n              \"number\": 2670,\n              \"title\": \"hooks: never lose a hook when a backup exists; keep Entire's hook after pre-commit install\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-06T01:50:31Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-09T11:44:21Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-09T11:44:18Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2670\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2670\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2670.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2670.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-09T11:44:18Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1492\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nTwo bugs in how `InstallGitHook` treats hooks that aren't Entire's.\\n\\n1. **A hook is lost when a backup already exists.** If `<hook>.pre-entire` exists and a different hook is now at `<hook>` (a hook manager reinstalled, the user edited it, a checkout restored a tracked `core.hooksPath`), the next install (`entire enable`, or `EnsureSetup` on an agent turn) printed `Warning: replacing <hook>` and wrote Entire's hook over it. The newer hook was gone, and the chain kept running the stale backup.\\n2. **`pre-commit install` after `entire enable` leaves Entire depending on pre-commit.** pre-commit moves Entire's hook to `<hook>.legacy` and runs it from its wrapper. That is unreliable (pre-commit 4.6.2 `hook_impl.py`): `.legacy` gets no stdin except for pre-push, so Entire's post-rewrite remap does nothing; `.legacy` is skipped without `--hook-dir`; if pre-commit isn't on PATH the wrapper exits first, so post-commit silently never runs. And `pre-commit install` → `entire enable` → `pre-commit install` fails every commit: Entire's `.legacy` chains back into pre-commit's wrapper, which trips pre-commit's migration-mode guard.\\n\\n## Fix (`strategy/hook_backup.go`)\\n\\n**Never lose a hook**\\n- A changed hook becomes `<hook>.pre-entire` and runs after Entire's; the previous backup is kept as `<hook>.pre-entire.<timestamp>` (no new copy when an identical one exists).\\n- Crash-safe ordering: hooks are hard-linked into place before anything is replaced (`os.Root.Link`, which links symlinks themselves), so an executable hook stays at `<hook>` and every version stays on disk if the process is killed at any step. Copy fallback (never rename-over) where hard links aren't supported. Nothing is fsynced, so this covers a killed or crashed process, not power loss or a kernel crash.\\n- Just before the write, the hook is re-checked against what was classified and backed up; if another tool replaced it in that gap, the install stops and leaves it in place. A writer outside Entire's lock can still land between that check and the rename itself.\\n- A symlinked hook over Entire's hook in `.legacy` (possibly a linked pre-commit wrapper, which would run Entire again) is refused without changing anything.\\n- Install and uninstall serialize on a lock keyed by the resolved hooks directory (in the user cache dir, 1s timeout), so repos sharing one `core.hooksPath` don't interleave. A timeout is an error; the turn-start path already warns and continues.\\n- Entire never chains to a backup that carries its own marker (covers installers the lock can't see, e.g. an older `entire` on PATH).\\n\\n**Entire keeps the hook path after `pre-commit install`**\\n- When `<hook>` is pre-commit's wrapper (its header/ID, `hook-impl`, `--hook-type=<hook>`, `--hook-dir`; current Bash and older Python templates) and `.legacy` holds Entire's hook, Entire takes the path back: the user's original goes to `.legacy` (pre-commit runs it from there), the wrapper becomes `.pre-entire`, Entire's hook is at `<hook>`. Each hook runs once: Entire → pre-commit → the user's hook.\\n- An Entire-owned copy `<hook>.legacy.pre-entire` keeps the user's hook safe from a later `pre-commit install`, which overwrites `.legacy`.\\n- Uninstall puts pre-commit's wrapper back at `<hook>` with the user's hook in `.legacy`. A failed `.legacy` restore stops work on that hook, leaving it retryable.\\n\\nMessages are printed only for moves that happened; uninstall lists older copies it left in place. #2641 rewrites the backup messages separately; whichever lands second resolves that text.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nBuilt binaries, real pre-commit 4.6.2, fresh repo each, \\\"turn\\\" = re-running `entire enable`:\\n\\n| Scenario | main | this branch |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| user hook → enable → `pre-commit install` → turn | Entire, user hook; pre-commit's check never runs | Entire, user hook, pre-commit |\\n| `pre-commit install` → enable → `pre-commit install` → turn | commit fails (pre-commit migration-mode bug), Entire runs twice | Entire, pre-commit; commit succeeds |\\n| as row 1, then `pre-commit install` → turn again | user hook, no pre-commit | user hook survives, pre-commit runs |\\n| hook USER1 → enable → changed to USER2 → turn | USER2 lost, USER1 runs | USER2 runs, USER1 kept as `.pre-entire.<ts>` |\\n| as row 1, then `disable --uninstall` | user hook only | user hook and pre-commit |\\n\\n- Unit tests (each seen failing first): rotation, identical, symlink, collision, crash ordering, shared-hooks-dir lock, marker-carrying backup, pre-commit detection (Bash and Python templates, negatives), reclaim with/without a user hook, reclaim → `pre-commit install` → reclaim, the chained execution end to end, uninstall after rotation/reclaim, failed `.legacy` restore, a hook replaced between backup and write, a symlinked hook over Entire's `.legacy`.\\n- `mise run lint`; `go test -race ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/` ×3, `./cmd/entire/cli/`, and hook/uninstall/enable integration tests pass.\\n\\nAdversarially reviewed (Codex) before opening; its three findings are fixed in the last three commits.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches on-disk git hook layout on every enable/disable and interacts with pre-commit and shared hooks dirs; mistakes could break hook chains or leave repos in a bad state, though the change is aimed at preventing hook loss.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Reworks **git hook install and uninstall** so user hooks are not dropped when `.pre-entire` already exists or when another tool rewrites hooks, and so Entire stays on the primary hook path after **pre-commit** runs.\\n> \\n> **Backup behavior:** Foreign hooks are copied/linked into `.pre-entire` (with timestamped older copies when the backup diverges) instead of overwriting the live hook or stale backup. Install/uninstall is serialized with a **per-hooks-directory file lock** (shared `core.hooksPath`), and chaining skips backups that still carry Entire’s marker.\\n> \\n> **pre-commit:** Detects pre-commit’s wrapper and reclaims the hook slot when Entire was moved to `.legacy`, restoring the user hook there and chaining **Entire → pre-commit → user hook**. Uninstall reverses `.legacy` / keep-file layout and surfaces leftover rotated copies.\\n> \\n> New logic lives in `hook_backup.go`; `hooks.go` routes through `installHooks` / `removeHooks` with the new backup and reclaim steps. Tests cover rotation, concurrency, symlinks, and pre-commit Bash/Python templates.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 72e36812c818174883a316593f2760bc181e6ec7. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2670/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2670/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2139\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2139/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2139/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2139/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2139\",\n              \"id\": 5260899428,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBH1h5g\",\n              \"number\": 2139,\n              \"title\": \"fix(claude): quote CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR in SessionStart remote-setup hook\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-26T19:52:17Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-27T12:54:34Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-27T12:54:31Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2139\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2139\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2139.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2139.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-27T12:54:31Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1152\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThe committed Claude Code `SessionStart` hook in `.claude/settings.json` ran\\n\\n```\\nbash ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/scripts/remote-setup.sh\\n```\\n\\nwith the placeholder unquoted. Any checkout whose path contains a space fails on every session start with:\\n\\n```\\nSessionStart:startup hook error\\nFailed with non-blocking status code: bash: /Users/<user>/Documents/Documents: No such file or directory\\n```\\n\\n(Seen on a macOS machine where iCloud moved the dev tree under `~/Documents/Documents - <Mac name>/…`.)\\n\\nThis wraps the placeholder in double quotes — the form the [Claude Code hooks docs](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks) recommend for shell-form commands referencing a path placeholder (\\\"In shell form, wrap each placeholder in double quotes\\\").\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nRan the exact command string Claude Code executes, with `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` set to a path containing spaces:\\n\\n- unquoted (before): `bash: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents: No such file or directory`, exit 127\\n- quoted (after): exit 0 (`remote-setup.sh` correctly no-ops outside `CLAUDE_CODE_REMOTE=true`)\\n\\n`mise run lint` passes. No Go code changed; `entire enable` preserves this hook entry verbatim, so the fix survives hook reinstalls.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Single-line hook string change in Claude Code config; no application or security logic affected.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Fixes **SessionStart** failures when the repo lives on a path that contains spaces (e.g. iCloud `Documents - …` layouts on macOS).\\n> \\n> The `remote-setup.sh` hook command in `.claude/settings.json` now wraps `${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}` in double quotes so the shell treats the full directory as one argument instead of splitting at spaces and looking for a non-existent truncated path.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit b8a6ae22c056474c68bd5fb39a1626f91fdf1cac. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2139/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2139/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2782\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2782/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2782/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2782/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2782\",\n              \"id\": 5858177451,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABIhLC9A\",\n              \"number\": 2782,\n              \"title\": \"Count session and checkpoint tokens from each agent's running total\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-15T00:58:17Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-10T08:21:03Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-11-10T08:21:00Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2782\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2782\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2782.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2782.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-11-10T08:21:00Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2250/changes/cli/1579\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nMakes token accounting correct by construction. Today `entire` works out each checkpoint's tokens by slicing transcripts at offsets, and every double count and undercount we've found comes from those slices starting or ending in the wrong place: turns without file changes went missing (Claude Code `entire status` showed 64k against 285k actually spent), a repeated Stop on a turn that changed files counts the turn twice, a message whose lines straddle an agent's mid-turn commit counts twice, and Copilot counts cache twice.\\n\\nThis PR has each session keep the agent's own running total (the **token ledger**), and each checkpoint store what that total grew by since the session's previous checkpoint.\\n\\n## 1. One shared reader for every agent\\n`agent.ReadCumulativeUsage` reads a session's running total for any agent. It owns the files:\\n- it reads only the bytes appended since the last reading (a no-op reading costs under 1ms), and waits for a line's end;\\n- it detects a rewritten transcript (the 512 bytes before its last offset no longer match) and reads it again, reporting `Restarted`;\\n- it reads a small or rewritten file (OpenCode's export, Droid's `settings.json`, a Claude Code subagent) whole, only when its size or last bytes changed, and never reports that as a restart;\\n- it never follows a symlink or opens a FIFO beside the transcript, and reads `.entire` through its confined reader.\\n\\nEach agent supplies a `UsageCounter` (50–150 lines) built from shared parts in `agent/usage_counting.go`:\\n- `KeyedUsage` counts per-call records once per key, with the agent's rule for a repeated record (`KeepFirst` for replays, `KeepLast` for records re-written, `KeepMostOutput` for streamed messages), a window of open records per file, and per-child sums;\\n- `RunningTotal` sums running totals across a counter restart; `KeyedUsage.CoveredBy` combines records with a running total where an agent writes both.\\n\\n| Agent | What it counts |\\n|---|---|\\n| Claude Code | Assistant messages by `message.id`, most output winning; subagents (and their subagents, Workflow agents) as children |\\n| Codex | `token_usage_record` by `response_id` (replays keep the first copy), combined with segment-summed `token_count` totals; children from the session's subagent inventory |\\n| Copilot CLI | `session.usage_record` by `apiCallId` (cache split out of input), combined with `session.shutdown` totals, which include subagents, so their records are subtracted |\\n| OpenCode | The export's assistant messages, reasoning counted once |\\n| Pi | Per-message usage on every branch |\\n| Factory Droid | `settings.json`'s `tokenUsage`, one call per assistant message |\\n| Antigravity | `PLANNER_RESPONSE` step usage by step index |\\n\\nChild sessions (Droid Workers, OpenCode child sessions) are not read here: #2824's child-session credit counts them once, and ledger checkpoints add it as the per-turn path does.\\n\\n## 2. The token ledger\\n- `SessionState.TokenLedger` (`session/token_ledger.go`, `strategy/token_ledger.go`) holds the running total, read **under the session lock** at turn start, every Stop and every condensation. `TokenUsage` is its total; a checkpoint stores its pending growth; a successful checkpoint write (or attach) marks it checkpointed, and that mark never moves back.\\n  - A repeated or concurrent Stop reads the same total, so it adds nothing — including on a turn that changed files.\\n  - A commit in the middle of a turn stores everything up to the commit; the rest lands in the next checkpoint. A message straddling that commit counts once.\\n- **Which sessions:** sessions this CLI starts at a turn start, for the seven agents above. Legacy states, states created at Stop or by attach, Cursor, Vogon and external agents keep today's per-turn path unchanged.\\n- **Takes over at the first reading with usage**; what the per-turn accounting already checkpointed counts as checkpointed.\\n- **Rewritten transcripts:** a lower reading is ignored (a stale copy), unless the transcript restarted: then the difference moves to `Base` and the total carries on.\\n- **Stop** skips the per-turn token calculation for ledger sessions (for Claude Code it read every subagent transcript only to be discarded).\\n- **Session end** takes a last reading, so usage an agent writes after its final Stop (Copilot's shutdown totals) is counted.\\n- **A new transcript path** for the session is read as a restart, so history the new file repeats is not counted twice.\\n- **Attach** reads the transcript being attached, updates session state under the session lock, and marks as checkpointed exactly what its checkpoint stored.\\n- **Checkpoint metadata** adds `session_token_usage`, the session's running total at that checkpoint, next to `token_usage`.\\n\\n## Checked\\n- **Real sessions, old vs new:** 726 local sessions across six agents on the final code (154 Copilot, 302 Codex, 149 Claude Code, 39 Antigravity, 37 Pi, 45 Droid), plus 36 OpenCode exports on an earlier revision: the shared reader gives exactly the totals of the per-agent code it replaces, and reading each file in nine pieces gives the same totals as one read. The only difference is intended: Droid Workers are no longer the ledger's children (13 sessions), because #2824's child-session credit counts them. Worst incremental step 126ms; largest cursor 38KB (a Claude session with 190 subagents: 123KB).\\n- **Live sessions** (`e2e/tests/token_ledger_test.go`): turns that changed files, one that changed nothing, and an agent commit mid-turn; for every session, checkpoints plus pending equal the session total, which equals a fresh read of the agent's files. Passes for all seven agents: Claude Code, Codex, Copilot, OpenCode, Pi, Droid and Antigravity.\\n\\n## Tests\\n- `TestUsageCounters_Conformance`: every agent with a counter needs a fixture in `testdata/usage/<agent>/`, read whole, in pieces cut at and around every line end, and after a rewrite.\\n- Reader tests: partial lines, rewrites, whole files, symlinked files beside the transcript, files that fail to read and return, moved files, the per-file window, merge policies.\\n- Ledger unit and strategy tests: repeated readings, growth, stale reads, rewrites, child high-water marks, handover from the per-turn accounting, attach under the lock, adopt's copy.\\n- Integration through the real hooks: Claude Code (repeated Stop on a file-changing turn, no-change turns between commits, mid-turn agent commit, a message straddling it, a subagent finishing in a later turn, a rewritten transcript), Codex (repeated Stop, mid-turn commit), Droid (Worker plus the parent's second Stop). With the ledger off, the repeated Stop and the straddling message fail.\\n\\n`mise run lint`: 0 issues. Unit and integration suites pass.\\n\\nSize: +3016/-56 in total.\\n\\n## Not in this PR / known limits\\n- External agents keep the per-turn accounting (the protocol has no incremental token call).\\n- A session's first reading reads its files whole (1.3s on an 82MB Claude transcript with 190 subagents); every later reading reads what was appended. Codex children are read through the inventory again only when a child file changed.\\n- Only an appended transcript can report a rewrite; for an OpenCode undo, or a Droid rewrite, a lower total is ignored until the total passes the old one — an undercount, not a double count.\\n- A crash between a checkpoint write and the state save can store the same growth twice (true of main's accounting too).\\n- A session whose state was lost counts from its next turn start; seeding from the latest checkpoint's `session_token_usage` is a follow-up. Deleting the per-turn path once legacy states age out, and server use of `session_token_usage`, are follow-ups.\\n- Overlaps #2856 (mid-turn double count): for ledger sessions it is superseded; whichever lands second reconciles.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2782/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2782/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2290\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2290/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2290/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2290/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2290\",\n              \"id\": 5367496899,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCbm3LA\",\n              \"number\": 2290,\n              \"title\": \"Re-land the os.Root coverage follow-ups dropped from #2220\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-06T20:34:02Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-07T17:43:31Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-07T17:43:29Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2290\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2290\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2290.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2290.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-07T17:43:29Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1240\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nFollow-up to #2220. These seven commits were pushed to `paulo-goroot-ognib` before it merged, but a force-push to that branch dropped them, so none of it reached `main` — every issue below is still live there. Rebased onto current `main` and re-proposed unchanged, apart from three merge resolutions noted at the end.\\n\\nThe first six came out of reviewing #2220; the seventh is a quality pass over the other six.\\n\\n## The one that changes behaviour for users today\\n\\n`entire enable` silently drops Vercel deployment blocking in a repo whose `vercel.json` is an absolute symlink into a monorepo's shared config. `708f78136` moved the detection onto the worktree root and said in two places that in-repo links are still followed. That holds only for *relative* links — `os.Root` refuses an absolute target unconditionally, even one landing inside the root, and the error is not `os.ErrNotExist`:\\n\\n```\\nroot.Stat(\\\"vercel.json\\\")      err=statat vercel.json: path escapes from parent\\nroot.Stat(\\\"vercel-rel.json\\\")  err=<nil>\\n```\\n\\nSo the error branch printed `could not check vercel.json: ... path escapes from parent` and returned false. `worktreeFileName` tries the root first and, on a refusal that is not \\\"absent\\\", resolves through the new `worktreedir.NameFollowingLinks` and retries at the resolved name — following a link that stays inside, refusing one that leaves, with the retried read still going through the root. CLAUDE.md already records this `os.Root` property as why `checkpoint/configloader.go` keeps a symlink-following `billy.Basic`.\\n\\n## Two guards that were not sound\\n\\n`RemoveDir` guarded only the worktree root, so `path.Dir(\\\".claude/settings.json\\\")` is `.claude` and the next agent integration to copy pi's uninstall gets `RemoveAll(\\\".claude\\\")` — the user's hand-written settings, subagents and skills. A blocklist of `AllProtectedDirs()` was the obvious fix and is also unsound: that list holds `.opencode` and `.github/hooks` but not `.opencode/plugins`, `.pi/extensions` or `.github`, so an agent whose config sits one level below its root still reaches `RemoveAll(\\\".opencode/plugins\\\")`. Stated positively instead — the directory has to be one Entire named. Every agent root and shared intermediate fails that; pi's `.pi/extensions/entire` passes because Entire created it.\\n\\n`scanForSymlinkedComponent` tested `Type() == 0`, a blocklist of one, so a FIFO, socket or device node where a directory belongs came back clean and doctor printed nothing — while `os.Root` and every hook install fail on it. Now an allowlist of the traversable shapes, which is what the `.entire` scan's doc argues for at length. `fs.ModeIrregular` stays tolerated: a Windows junction arrives as bare `ModeIrregular` and a cloud placeholder directory as `ModeDir|ModeIrregular`, and both are traversable.\\n\\n## Diagnosis that named the wrong thing, or nothing\\n\\nA regular file at `.claude` was reported as `NOT READABLE` with `Fix: check the ownership and permissions` — a remedy that cannot fix it. That is the else-branch pattern CLAUDE.md's `.entire` section separates two error values to avoid; it now gets its own `BROKEN` heading and the replace remedy.\\n\\n`.claude/agents/` was in no candidate, though `removeLegacySearchSubagent` deletes through it with `osroot.LstatNoSymlinks`, which refuses a symlinked parent. A link there was refused at enable with a best-effort warning and doctor said nothing. `.codex/agents` and `.gemini/agents` were covered only as a side effect of the agent-help template living under them.\\n\\nA worktree root that would not open returned bare, printing nothing on a repo where every hook install also fails.\\n\\n## Smaller correctness\\n\\n`Write`'s error message passed `f.path` to `path.Dir`, which finds no forward slashes on Windows and yielded `\\\".\\\"`.\\n\\nThe build guard compared `len(declared) == len(callers)`, so an added omission offset by a removal in the same change passed — the exact failure it exists to catch, since the agent still works and only doctor's diagnosis goes quiet. It compares sets now (eight packages each side).\\n\\n## Quality pass\\n\\n`printCappedList` replaces four inline copies of the same capped-list loop; `testutil.SkipWithoutSymlinks` replaces six copies of the Windows symlink skip in three wordings; `agentHelpSkillTemplate` is back to one switch so a fourth agent cannot get a path with no body; the `worktreeFileName` tests are one table. Writing that table caught a wrong expectation of mine — a *relative* in-repo link never reaches the resolve, because `os.Root` follows it, so the fast path returns the original name.\\n\\n## Merge resolutions worth a look\\n\\nThree conflicts came from `main` moving under these commits, and all three keep `main`'s side:\\n\\n- `agent_hook_config_guard_test.go` — `main` added `grep.Env = gitrepo.EnvWithoutRepoOverrides()` to the git-grep this commit extracts into a helper. Carried into the helper rather than dropped; it is the CLAUDE.md rule for any git subprocess naming its target with `cmd.Dir`.\\n- `runner_gather_test.go` — `main` created this file for `TestGatherTrailsUsesNativeRepoBaseForFindings`. Both sets of tests kept, imports unioned.\\n- `setup_test.go` — append-vs-append with `TestConfigureCmd_SummarizeProvider_ExternalLocalTarget_GrantSurvives`. Both kept.\\n\\n## Split out\\n\\n`readCapped`'s rune-boundary fix moved to #2307 on review feedback — a byte cap cutting a multi-byte rune in prompt text is unrelated to filesystem anchoring, and it was the one piece of this branch that stood alone. `runner_gather.go` and `runner_gather_test.go` are now identical to `main` here, so the two PRs do not overlap and either can land first. The three commits that developed it plus the revert are still in this branch's history and net to zero; the diff is what matters.\\n\\n## Still open, deliberately not in here\\n\\nA **FIFO at an agent config leaf hangs every command that reads it**, `entire doctor` included. Reproduced on this branch in a repo where Entire is not enabled: `mkdir -p .claude && mkfifo .claude/settings.json && entire doctor` blocks in `openat` until interrupted, because `osroot.OpenNoFollow` opens without `O_NONBLOCK`. Pre-existing and shared by all seven worktree-config agents, so the fix belongs in `OpenNoFollow` rather than here; this PR makes the condition *reportable* (the leaf's type is now checked) but cannot stop the hang. Filed separately.\\n\\n`readCapped` opens with `osroot.OpenNoFollow`, and **this repo's own `AGENTS.md` is a symlink to `CLAUDE.md`** — so `entire runner tune` drops it. Harmless here because `CLAUDE.md` is read anyway, but a repo with only a symlinked `AGENTS.md` loses it. That is a product call (should the runner read symlinked docs at all?) rather than a fix to slip into a follow-up, and it predates these commits.\\n\\nTwo structural follow-ups also left out: making `OpenHookConfig` take a `HookConfigLocator`, which turns the guard test into a compile error but touches nine agent packages; and giving the registry a `ManagedWorktreePaths()` capability so \\\"what does Entire write for this agent?\\\" is the registry's question rather than three `switch agentName` blocks in `cli`.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n`mise run lint` 0 issues and `mise run test:ci` exit 0 on the rebased tree. The touched tests also run 5x together, because one of these commits fixed a `t.Parallel` test that called `osroot.ResetShared` and broke a different test — a single clean run does not catch that class.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches enable/setup (Vercel), recursive delete guards, and doctor path scanning—behavior changes for symlinked configs and mis-typed paths, with broad test coverage but real install/diagnostic surface area.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Re-lands follow-ups from the `os.Root` / worktree safety work: safer uninstalls, clearer `entire doctor` output, and a user-visible fix for Vercel setup when `vercel.json` is symlinked.\\n> \\n> **Vercel / monorepo symlinks:** Setup no longer treats an in-repo **absolute** `vercel.json` symlink as a hard failure (`os.Root` reports “path escapes”). `worktreeFileName` and `worktreedir.NameFollowingLinks` resolve links that stay inside the worktree, refuse escapes, and pass the resolved name into `vercelconfig.LoadIn`.\\n> \\n> **Hook config safety:** `HookConfigFile.RemoveDir` now **refuses** unless the parent directory basename is `entire` (pi’s `.pi/extensions/entire`), so copying that uninstall path cannot `RemoveAll` `.claude` or similar agent-owned trees. `Write` error text uses `filepath.Dir` on Windows.\\n> \\n> **Doctor / agent paths:** Agent-directory scanning adds a **BROKEN** section when a path component is a non-directory (files, FIFOs, etc.) instead of “NOT READABLE”; expands candidates (e.g. `.claude/agents/`, legacy subagent paths) via `searchSkillTemplatePath` / `agentHelpSkillTemplatePath`; reports when the worktree root cannot be opened; dedupes long lists with `printCappedList`. The `OpenHookConfig` ↔ `HookConfigRelPath` guard compares **package sets**, not counts.\\n> \\n> **Smaller fixes:** `readCapped` truncates on UTF-8 rune boundaries; Pi extension dirs use `0750` like other agents; shared `testutil.SkipWithoutSymlinks`; `worktreedir.Name` uses `filepath.IsLocal`.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit edc15a4ce0995dfdab5f35c23020accbc85d5f2e. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2290/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2290/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2340\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2340/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2340/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2340/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2340\",\n              \"id\": 5405139747,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABC5vLxg\",\n              \"number\": 2340,\n              \"title\": \"Gate new complexity in CI via the tools/complexity diff\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-09T21:54:32Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-03T14:28:31Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-11-03T14:28:28Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2340\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2340\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2340.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2340.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-11-03T14:28:28Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1281\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nImplements the two CI follow-ups #2194 flagged when `tools/complexity/` landed: gate new complexity so it cannot accumulate silently, and compare per-feature coverage against the committed baseline. The complexity half ships blocking; the coverage half ships as a working, tested mode that is deliberately not wired into CI yet (reason below).\\n\\n## 1. Gating new complexity — a cxtool diff, not the gocognit linter\\n\\n`gate -base <dir> -head <dir>` compares two cxtool output directories and fails only on functions that are over cognitive complexity 30 **and** new or worse than at the merge base. A function that is over the threshold and did not move does not fail — and that exemption is the whole design: the tree has 127 functions over 30 (of 8,457 total; worst is `newSearchCmd` at 100), and a gate that fired on them would only ever be switched off.\\n\\n**Why not just enable `gocognit` in `.golangci.yaml`:** golangci-lint has no per-linter new-only mode. Enabling it would fail `mise run lint` locally on all 127 legacy offenders at once, and the action-level `only-new-issues: true` would silently flip **every** linter in CI to new-only semantics. So `.golangci.yaml` and `lint.yml` are untouched, and the threshold lives in the gate's own flags (`-cognit-warn`, `COGNIT_WARN=25 mise run complexity:gate`).\\n\\nFunction identity across the two trees is file plus function name — the whole identity the CSVs carry — softened by a by-name fallback: a function whose name is unique in both trees keeps its history when it moves to another file, so splitting a large file (the gate's own advice) does not fire the gate. A moved function whose name is ambiguous still re-reports as new; that is the safe direction for a gate to be wrong in, and `-h` says so.\\n\\nCI runs it as a `complexity-gate` job on pull requests only (a push to main has no merge base to diff against; the aggregate `test` job accepts `skipped` for it so main and `workflow_dispatch` stay green). One script serves CI and the developer, so what fails in a PR is exactly what `mise run complexity:gate` fails locally.\\n\\nTwo deliberate deviations from the brief: the base tree is exported with `git archive` rather than `git worktree add` (an interrupted run leaves nothing in the repo's worktree list, and with no `.gitattributes` in this repo the export is a faithful copy), and the job sets Go up with `jdx/mise-action` rather than `actions/setup-go`, matching the sibling jobs in `ci.yml` that run mise tasks.\\n\\n## 2. Per-feature coverage — advisory, not wired into CI\\n\\n`gate -features <head features.csv> -baseline <committed features.csv> -cov-drop 2.0 -min-stmts 300` warns (`::warning::` annotations plus a step-summary table) on ranked features whose statement coverage fell past the tolerance, and exits 0 even on unreadable inputs, so it can never redden a pull request. Advisory-first because a committed baseline is one commit's numbers and drifts as the tree moves; a hard gate on a drifting reference produces exactly the false positives that get gates switched off.\\n\\nIt is not wired into CI because the numbers would not be comparable: CI's test recipe (`-tags=integration -race`, sharded `-run` filters) compiles different code than the README recipe the committed baseline came from, so the first run would report the recipe difference as a mass coverage regression. The two ways forward — refresh the baseline with the CI recipe and keep them in step, or give the advisory its own non-blocking job reproducing the documented recipe — are written up in `tools/complexity/README.md`; which recipe is the reference is a product call I have not made silently. Refreshing `baseline/<date>/` stays manual for the same reason; the blocking half always diffs against the merge base and cannot go stale.\\n\\n## Gate proof\\n\\nBase = `origin/main` (`git archive` export), head = this branch — zero offenders, because the 127 pre-existing violations did not move:\\n\\n```\\n$ gate -base /tmp/gate/base -head /tmp/gate/head; echo \\\"exit=$?\\\"\\ncomplexity gate: no new or worsened function over cognitive complexity 30 (8457 functions compared against 8457)\\nexit=0\\n```\\n\\nA copy of main with two synthetic worsenings — a new function at 32, and extra nesting in `writeActiveSessions` (already over at 52, so it proves the \\\"grew\\\" branch rather than the \\\"new\\\" one) — fails with both `::error` annotations (`cognitive complexity 62 (limit 30, base 52)` / `32 (limit 30, base new)`) and exit 1, and the same plant fails `mise run complexity:gate` through the real entry point, exercising its own merge-base resolution and tree export. Advisory mode against `baseline/2026-08-31/features.csv` warns on a synthetic 6.3-point drop, stays correctly silent on a 1.2-point drop inside the tolerance, and exits 0 with a warning annotation on an unreadable baseline.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `tools/complexity`: `gofmt -s -l`, `go vet`, `go build`, `go test` all clean (the comparison logic in both modes is table-driven, mostly asserting what must **not** fire); from the repo root `go list ./... | grep -c tools` → `0`, so the nested module stays out of the CLI's build.\\n- Repo root: `mise run fmt` changed nothing; `mise run lint` → 0 issues (shellcheck covers the new `mise-tasks/complexity/gate`); `actionlint` passes clean on `ci.yml` and on main's copy — its pre-existing findings elsewhere (`e2e.yml`, `nightly-e2e.yml`, `release.yml`) are untouched.\\n- No root-module Go files are touched (the diff outside `tools/` is one workflow file, one mise task, two docs). After the rebase onto current main, `go test -tags=integration -race ./...` passes everything except one pre-existing environment-dependent test (`TestOpenCodeSeedRepoPlantsDeps` in `e2e/agents`, which fails identically on an untouched `origin/main` export on the same machine), and the Vogon E2E canary passes in full.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Changes are limited to CI, docs, and the nested `tools/complexity` module; no CLI runtime, auth, or data-path code is modified.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds a **pull-request-only** `complexity-gate` CI job that fails when a function exceeds cognitive complexity 30 **and** is new or worse than the merge base, while leaving ~105 existing over-threshold functions alone. The check uses a new `tools/complexity/gate` binary (diff of `cxtool` `functions.csv` outputs) instead of enabling `gocognit` in golangci-lint, which would fail local lint on all legacy violations.\\n> \\n> **Local/CI entry point:** `mise run complexity:gate` exports the merge-base tree via `git archive`, runs head's `cxtool` on base and working tree, then `gate -base … -head …`. The aggregate `test` job now depends on this job and accepts `skipped` on pushes to main.\\n> \\n> Also ships an **advisory** coverage mode (`gate -features … -baseline …`) with table-driven tests and README/CLAUDE docs; it is **not** wired into CI yet because CI coverage recipes differ from the committed baseline.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 1116c727937b1b38db654146a9104778f8c3cf4f. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2340/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2340/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2480\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2480/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2480/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2480/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2480\",\n              \"id\": 5461350070,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABDmVkAg\",\n              \"number\": 2480,\n              \"title\": \"Add `entire cluster list` for the cluster catalog\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"id\": 881031,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-15T11:33:24Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-16T06:43:03Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-16T06:43:00Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2480\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2480\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2480.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2480.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-16T06:43:00Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1329\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What\\n\\nAdds `entire cluster list`, a read-only control-plane group that renders the cluster catalog (`GET /clusters`) so a user can see where to create a project or a mirror.\\n\\n```\\n$ entire cluster list\\nREGION  CLUSTER             HOST\\nau      aws-ap-southeast-2  aws-ap-southeast-2.entire.io\\neu      aws-eu-central-1    aws-eu-central-1.entire.io\\nin      aws-ap-south-1      aws-ap-south-1.entire.io\\nus      aws-us-east-2       aws-us-east-2.entire.io\\n```\\n\\nEach column is a value another command takes:\\n\\n- **REGION** is the jurisdiction slug behind `org create --region` and `project create --region`.\\n- **CLUSTER** is the placement slug `repo mirror list --cluster` accepts.\\n- **HOST** is the bare host behind `repo create --cluster-host`, `repo mirror create` and `repo clone --cluster`. It goes through the existing `hostFromPublicURL` guard, so a `publicUrl` that fails validation renders `-` rather than a spoofable host.\\n\\n`--json` emits the wire model as a bare array, `apiUrl` and `isDefault` included, plus a synthesized `host` on each object: the same validated host the table shows, absent rather than dashed when `publicUrl` fails validation, so a script never re-implements the guard over the raw URL. `apiUrl` is never a table column, since the CLI dials the API URL itself. `isDefault` becomes a DEFAULT column only when the catalog holds a non-default cluster; with one cluster per region, today's shape, every row would read yes and the column would say nothing.\\n\\n## Why no metrics\\n\\nThe catalog exposes exactly slug, jurisdiction, publicUrl, apiUrl and isDefault. There is no health, capacity or usage data anywhere server-side, and hidden or decommissioned clusters are already filtered out by the server.\\n\\n## `repo create` gets the same host guard\\n\\nReviewing the JSON path showed `repo create` had none: `--cluster-host` went to the wire unvalidated, and `repoRemoteURL` emitted a spoofable `entire://` URL for whatever `clusterHost` the server returned, on the confirmation line, in `repo list`, and in `--json`. Both now run `validateClusterHost`. A bad server host drops the remote and warns on stderr so it cannot be mistaken for a repo still provisioning. The `remote` and `host` merges share one additive-only helper, `mergeSynthesizedField`.\\n\\n## Flagged for a human\\n\\n- **agent-help classification**: `cluster` is classified user-owned and unlisted, the safe default matching org/project/repo. It is a pure read, so it could be moved to read-only.\\n- `login` takes neither a region nor a cluster (the apex login server routes by account), so this list feeds project creation and mirroring but not login.\\n\\n## Wiring\\n\\n- Registered in the Control Plane help group and exempt from the `.entire` directory check like the other control-plane groups (ledger entry added).\\n- README table row and a CLAUDE.md command-layout bullet.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- New tests: table rendering and sort order, `--json` as the sorted wire model, empty catalog.\\n- `mise run fmt` (no changes), `mise run lint` (0 issues), `mise run dup` (nothing in the new files).\\n- `go test -tags=integration -race ./...`: green except the nine `TestRunUninstall_*` tests, a known machine-local issue from stale `entire-agent-*` mise shims (they pass in isolation), and one e2e harness seed test that failed on a half-built temp cache and passed after clearing it.\\n- `mise run test:e2e:canary`: all 56 Vogon tests and all 4 roger-roger tests passed.\\n- Ran read-only against the real control plane, output above.\\n- Second round: DEFAULT column shown and omitted, `--json` host present and absent, empty catalog `[]`, `--cluster-host` rejected before any request, invalid server host yields no remote plus a warning, guard test that the cluster wire type has no `host` field.\\n- `mise run test:integration` 594 tests green, `mise run test:e2e:canary` 112 + 8 green, lint 0 issues.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Read-only catalog listing with no changes to auth, data writes, or existing API behavior; host display reuses existing URL validation.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds a read-only **`entire cluster`** control-plane group with **`list`**, so users can discover region slugs, cluster placement slugs, and public hosts without digging through mirror flows.\\n> \\n> **`entire cluster list`** calls **`GET /clusters`** (same **`coreapi.ListClusters`** path mirror tooling already uses), sorts by jurisdiction then slug, and prints **REGION**, **CLUSTER**, and **HOST** — values wired to **`org`/`project create --region`**, **`repo mirror list --cluster`**, and **`repo create --cluster-host`** / mirror / clone flags. **HOST** is derived via **`hostFromPublicURL`**; bad **`publicUrl`** values show **`-`** instead of a spoofable host. **`--json`** returns the sorted wire model including **`apiUrl`** and **`isDefault`**.\\n> \\n> The command is registered under the Control Plane help group, exempt from the **`.entire`** directory guard like other control-plane commands, classified in **agent-help**, and documented in **README** / **CLAUDE.md**. Tests cover table order, JSON output, malformed URLs, and an empty catalog.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 0efa273bb06905b00e843233be507ac3115f00a1. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2480/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2480/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1954\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1954/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1954/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1954/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1954\",\n              \"id\": 5124263437,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M79t4-M\",\n              \"number\": 1954,\n              \"title\": \"feat: lazy invisible enable for globally tracked repos (global enable: B)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-11T20:22:28Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-24T20:34:54Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-24T20:34:54Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1954\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1954\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1954.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1954.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1013\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nSplit **B** of #1894 (stacked on #1953 — see the stack map there). Adds **lazy invisible enable**: the first hook activity in a globally-tracked repo (no repo-level setup, global tier on) transparently sets the repo up with everything inside `.git/` — the five git hooks installed, clone preferences marked, checkpoint ref ensured — and all runtime state (`.entire/metadata`, `logs`, `tmp`) routes under `<git-common-dir>/entire/worktree/<worktree-key>/` instead of the worktree.\\n\\n**The product promise: `git status --porcelain` stays byte-clean.** Pinned by:\\n- `TestGlobalEnable_LazyInvisibleSetup` — empty porcelain at three points through a full prompt → stop → commit cycle (the commit carries its `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer with all metadata under `.git/`)\\n- `TestGlobalEnable_TierAbsent_CreatesNothing` — the negative: tier absent → zero footprint\\n- `TestAbsPath_InvisibleRouting_RepoLevelSetupWins` — repos with any repo-level setup resolve **byte-identically to before**\\n\\nThe runtime location is namespaced **per worktree** using the same hash derivation shadow branches use (`paths.HashWorktreeID`, moved from `checkpoint` with a pure delegation — existing shadow-branch names cannot change), so linked worktrees of one clone never share or steal each other's session data (`TestAbsPath_InvisibleRouting_LinkedWorktree` pins isolation).\\n\\n**Cherry-pick note:** the second commit carries the *namespacing portion* of a larger reviewed fix — its diagnostics-routing portion lands in split D, migration scoping in split C. One doc comment in `paths/invisible.go` forward-references the enable-time migration that arrives in split C (build-safe; lands one layer up).\\n\\nStack rule: fix-forward only — review fixes land as new commits and merge forward; no rebases. Merge order: #1953 → this → #1955 → #1957. All commits dual-reviewed (spec + adversarial quality with mutation testing); findings on trail #968. Part of #1098.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1954/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1954/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2254\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2254/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2254/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2254/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2254\",\n              \"id\": 5335119781,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCCSMhQ\",\n              \"number\": 2254,\n              \"title\": \"refactor(checkpoint): use canonical Git metadata resolution (split part 2)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"id\": 34813274,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-03T09:59:53Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T15:15:20Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-04T15:15:20Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2254\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2254\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2254.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2254.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-04T15:15:20Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"> **Dependency:** This PR is built on #2241 and must not merge before it. Until #2241 lands, the Files changed view includes both #2241 and this checkpoint refactor. After #2241 merges, this branch will be rebased onto `main` and force-pushed so the PR contains only the checkpoint changes.\\n\\nFor the checkpoint-only change before that rebase, see the [comparison against the prerequisite branch](https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal/cli/compare/refactor-git-metadata-owner...refactor-checkpoint-metadata-resolution).\\n\\nRefs #2052 and #2190.\\n\\nPR #2190 established the broader direction: physical Git worktree metadata should have one canonical owner instead of being rediscovered independently across the CLI. PR #2241 introduces that owner in `gitrepo` and migrates repository opening. This PR follows it by moving the checkpoint subsystem onto the canonical metadata boundary and deleting checkpoint's duplicate traversal and caching implementation.\\n\\nThis is intended as an ownership refactor rather than a checkpoint behavior change. Queue placement, redaction caching, persistent refs, shadow refs, locking, and caller-specific failure policies remain intact.\\n\\n## Broader refactor\\n\\nCheckpoint operations need to know both the current worktree root and the repository's common Git directory. The common directory determines where repository-wide state such as the push queue and redaction cache belongs, particularly when a command runs from a linked worktree.\\n\\nBefore this change, checkpoint resolved that metadata itself:\\n\\n```text\\nCheckpoint operation\\n        │\\n        ▼\\ncheckpoint.resolveGitCommonDir\\n        │\\n        ├── git rev-parse --git-common-dir\\n        ├── package-level mutex\\n        └── per-worktree cache\\n```\\n\\nThat made checkpoint a second owner of the same physical Git facts already being consolidated under `gitrepo`. It also gave checkpoint its own cache lifecycle, cancellation-dependent behavior, and subprocess cost.\\n\\nAfter this change, checkpoint starts from the already-open repository and delegates physical metadata resolution to the canonical owner:\\n\\n```text\\nCheckpoint operation\\n        │\\n        ▼\\ncheckpoint.repositoryDirs\\n        │\\n        ▼\\ngitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata\\n        │\\n        ├── Worktree root\\n        ├── Per-worktree Git directory\\n        └── Common Git directory\\n```\\n\\nThe checkpoint package retains a small adapter because checkpoint callers commonly need the worktree root and common directory together. Interpretation of `.git`, `gitdir:`, `commondir`, and linked-worktree layout remains owned exclusively by `gitrepo`.\\n\\n## Why remove the checkpoint cache\\n\\nThe deleted cache was compensating for a Git subprocess rather than caching an expensive domain object. Once metadata resolution becomes rooted filesystem inspection, the cache no longer provides a useful ownership boundary.\\n\\nRemoving it has three useful consequences:\\n\\n- An already-open repository no longer launches `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` when constructing checkpoint state.\\n- Repairs to `.git` or `commondir` metadata are observed by the next operation instead of remaining hidden behind a stale cached result.\\n- Checkpoint no longer owns a mutex, cache-clearing API, or cancellation-dependent cache semantics for facts owned by `gitrepo`.\\n\\nThis also removes the checkpoint-specific resolver and its cache-only tests.\\n\\n## Checkpoint consumers moved to the canonical boundary\\n\\nThe migration covers the checkpoint paths that depend on repository metadata:\\n\\n- rooted push-queue construction\\n- redaction-cache placement\\n- persistent ref updates\\n- ref-store construction\\n- ephemeral checkpoint storage\\n- shadow-ref operations\\n- file-lock placement\\n\\nThese consumers now receive metadata from the same resolver used when opening the repository, without introducing a generic Git facade or moving checkpoint-specific policy into `gitrepo`.\\n\\n## Caller policy remains local\\n\\nThe canonical resolver reports metadata facts and errors; it does not decide whether an individual checkpoint feature is required or optional.\\n\\nThat distinction remains deliberate:\\n\\n- Push-queue construction fails closed because enqueueing against the wrong repository directory could lose or misdirect required work.\\n- Redaction caching fails open because caching is an optimization and transcript redaction can continue without it.\\n- Persistent ref updates retain their existing locking, compare-and-swap conflict handling, retry, and cancellation behavior.\\n- Linked worktrees continue sharing repository-wide state through the common Git directory.\\n- Shadow refs and ephemeral checkpoint data retain their existing worktree-specific placement.\\n\\n## Observable effect\\n\\nNo user-facing command or checkpoint format changes.\\n\\nThe operational effect is narrower:\\n\\n- checkpoint metadata lookup no longer launches a Git subprocess for an already-open repository\\n- checkpoint metadata is no longer memoized independently from the filesystem\\n- malformed metadata continues to follow each caller's existing required or optional failure policy\\n- ordinary repositories and linked worktrees retain their existing storage locations\\n\\nThe checkpoint-only layer relative to #2241 contains 16 files, with 139 additions and 211 deletions. Most additions are focused behavioral tests; the production change primarily removes duplicate traversal and cache machinery.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `mise run check`\\n  - formatting passed\\n  - lint passed with 0 issues\\n  - race-enabled unit and integration tests passed\\n  - Vogon canary passed 56/56\\n  - external deterministic canary passed 4/4\\n- Pre-PR `mise run lint` passed with 0 issues.\\n- `git diff upstream/main...HEAD --check` passed.\\n- A real linked-worktree fixture proves that its queue is stored in the main repository's common Git directory.\\n- A repair test proves that corrected metadata is observed immediately without clearing a cache.\\n- A Git Trace2 test proves that constructing a checkpoint queue from an already-open repository launches no metadata Git subprocess.\\n- The Trace2 positive control runs `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` and confirms that the subprocess detector records it.\\n- Tests preserve the required queue fail-closed and optional redaction-cache fail-open policies.\\n- The repository ownership guard no longer needs an exception for checkpoint metadata traversal.\\n- Source-built `entire status` passed.\\n- Source-built `entire doctor` reported metadata branches and hooks as healthy; it also found two pre-existing ended sessions awaiting condensation, unrelated to this diff.\\n\\nNo paid real-agent E2E tests were run.\\n\\n## Deliberately not included\\n\\nThis PR does not migrate session, strategy, hook, or other product consumers. Those areas have separate migrations so their error handling, fallback behavior, and performance-sensitive paths can be reviewed independently.\\n\\nIt also does not redesign checkpoint persistence, change ref formats, alter queue semantics, add cross-worktree writes, or replace genuine Git queries for refs, objects, configuration, and repository semantics.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2254/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2254/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2220\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2220/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2220/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2220/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2220\",\n              \"id\": 5314494448,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBx2YyQ\",\n              \"number\": 2220,\n              \"title\": \"Expand on os.Root coverage\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"pjbgf\",\n                \"id\": 5452977,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NTI5Nzc=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5452977?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pjbgf\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 2,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-01T16:49:59Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T04:47:12Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-04T04:47:11Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2220\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2220\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2220.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2220.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-04T04:47:11Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1202\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nFollow-up to #2180. A second pass over the migrated tree found five places still\\r\\ndoing filesystem work outside an anchor, and the diagnostic that would surface the\\r\\ncondition they now refuse. This brings them onto the same footing as the rest of\\r\\nthe tree.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Pi's extension directory\\r\\n\\r\\n`agent/pi/hooks.go` was the last registered agent whose hook-config surface had\\r\\nnot moved. It joined `.pi/extensions/entire/index.ts` onto the repo root and\\r\\nhanded the result to `os.ReadFile` / `os.MkdirAll` / `os.WriteFile` /\\r\\n`os.RemoveAll`, each with a `//nolint:gosec` about where the path was *built*\\r\\nrather than where it *resolves* — the justification `agent.HookConfigFile`'s doc\\r\\ncomment already calls out as the one that says nothing useful. A working tree\\r\\narrives by clone, so `.pi` is a component the repository supplies, and every one\\r\\nof those four calls resolved through it.\\r\\n\\r\\nRouted through `agent.OpenHookConfig`, which the other eight agents already use:\\r\\nthe base is the worktree root, `.pi/extensions/entire/index.ts` is a name inside\\r\\nit, and directories are created with `MkdirAllNoSymlink` so a symlinked compon\\r\\nis refused by name instead of followed. `.opencode/plugins/entire.ts` is the\\r\\nstructurally identical case — embedded TS file, worktree-resident, marker-chec\\r\\n— and was already on this path; pi is now the same shape rather than the exception\\r\\nbeside it. Worth noting for the next integration: pi is auto-detected\\r\\n(`DetectPresence` stats `.pi`), so it reaches these operations without the user\\r\\nnaming it, which is the argument for routing a new agent through the anchor by\\r\\ndefault rather than trusting review to notice.\\r\\n\\r\\nTwo supporting pieces:\\r\\n\\r\\n- **`osroot.RemoveAllNoSymlinks`.** `os.Root.RemoveAll` refuses a descent that\\r\\n  would leave the root and unlinks a symlinked leaf rather than following it, but\\r\\n  it says nothing about the components *above* the leaf — which is where `.pi`\\r\\n  sits. This pins the parent first, then removes a single named component. Same\\r\\n  relationship `OpenChild` has to a bare `Root.OpenRoot`.\\r\\n- **`HookConfigFile.RemoveDir`.** Pi discovers extensions *by directory*, so\\r\\n  removing only the file leaves an empty `.pi/extensions/entire` for pi to find\\r\\n  with nothing to load. Deliberately not general: every other agent writes into a\\r\\n  directory the agent itself owns, where `Remove` of the file is the correct\\r\\n  uninstall and taking the parent would delete the user's own config with it.\\r\\n  Refuses the case where the directory to remove would be the worktree root.\\r\\n\\r\\n`agent.GeneratedHookFileState` — the path-based drift check that predates the\\r\\nrooted `HookConfigFile.GeneratedState` — had pi as its only caller and is\\r\\ndeleted, so there is no unrooted variant left to pick up.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Four sites beside it\\r\\n\\r\\n- **`vercel.json`** (`setup.go`, `vercelconfig`). A working-tree file read wit\\r\\n  `os.Stat` / `os.ReadFile` on a joined path. Now read through the worktree an\\r\\n  as `LoadIn(root, name)`, with a 1 MiB cap: the file arrives with the checkout, so\\r\\n  its size is not ours to choose, and everything downstream of the parse collapses\\r\\n  to a single bool. In-repo symlinks are still followed on purpose — pointing\\r\\n  `vercel.json` at a monorepo's shared config is a real setup, and this file i\\r\\n  user's rather than Entire's — while one leaving the worktree is refused, which is\\r\\n  the property the anchor exists to give.\\r\\n- **`worktreedir.Name`**. Given the `VolumeName` pairing `SessionStore.Name` got in\\r\\n  57b275ac6, which `ValidateSessionID` and gitrepo's alternates checks already\\r\\n  `os.Root` rejects a drive-relative name one layer down (`filepathlite.IsLocal`),\\r\\n  so this changes no behaviour today; it is closed because `Name` exists to an\\r\\n  \\\"is this inside the worktree?\\\" independently of its caller, and\\r\\n  `readWorktreeFileSafely` feeds it paths that arrive from the API. It was the\\r\\n  remaining `IsAbs` in a containment role without the pairing.\\r\\n- **The persistent-ref lock** (`checkpoint/persistent_ref_update.go`). The las\\r\\n  `.git`-resident lock still opening by path rather than through the common dir's\\r\\n  root. Now mirrors `shadowBranchLock`: `gitdir.OpenAt` + `MkdirAllNoSymlink` +\\r\\n  `AcquireContextIn`. Git will not check a path out into `.git`, so this is\\r\\n  consistency and defence in depth — but `openLockFileIn` exists for exactly t\\r\\n  and one caller sitting outside it is how the next one gets written that way\\r\\n- **`readCapped`** (`runner_gather.go`). Bounds the read, not just the result.\\r\\n  These are working-tree files named by convention (`README.md`, `CLAUDE.md`), so\\r\\n  their size is not ours to assume, and the caller has already said how much of one\\r\\n  it will use. Reading a gigabyte to keep its first 4 KB is a cost with no ret\\r\\n\\r\\n## `doctor` now reports symlinked agent directories\\r\\n\\r\\nThe condition these refusals produce was invisible after the fact. `enable` fa\\r\\nloudly on it, but once a repo is enabled `HookConfigFile.Exists()` deliberately\\r\\nreports a symlinked parent as *absent* — so `entire status` showed hooks missi\\r\\nwithout saying why, and `entire clean` skipped the directory on the stated grounds\\r\\nthat doctor reports a symlinked agent directory. Nothing did.\\r\\n\\r\\n`checkAgentDirSymlinks` runs beside `checkEntireDirSymlinks` and names the\\r\\noutermost link, once per finding. Candidates come from the registry and the\\r\\nscaffold templates rather than a list in the function. Unlike `.entire`, these\\r\\ntrees are largely the user's, so it examines only the components Entire itself\\r\\ncreates and writes through: `.claude/skills/my-own -> ../../shared/skills/my-o\\r\\nis a real setup, and reporting it would train people to skip this section.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Follow-up\\r\\n\\r\\n`agentSymlinkCheckPaths` derives from `AllProtectedDirs()` plus the skill\\r\\ntemplates, not from the hook-config relPaths, so the two agents whose config nests\\r\\nbelow their top-level directory have their Entire-created intermediate directories\\r\\nunchecked — a symlink at `.pi/extensions` or `.opencode/plugins` produces no\\r\\ndoctor output. The refusals cover both; this is reporting only.\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches hook install/uninstall and recursive delete paths where symlink mistakes could write or destroy files outside the repo; changes are defensive with new doctor reporting and tests, but they affect every agent’s enable flow.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> This PR finishes **os.Root / worktree anchoring** for agent hook configuration and closes gaps where symlinked repo paths could still be followed or deleted outside the worktree.\\n> \\n> **Pi** is migrated off raw `os.ReadFile` / `MkdirAll` / `WriteFile` / `RemoveAll` onto `agent.HookConfigFile` like the other agents. Uninstall uses new **`HookConfigFile.RemoveDir`** (backed by **`osroot.RemoveAllNoSymlinks`**) so the whole `.pi/extensions/entire` tree is removed without following a symlinked `.pi`. Path-based **`GeneratedHookFileState`** is removed; drift checks go through **`HookConfigFile.GeneratedState`**.\\n> \\n> **`agent.HookConfigLocator`** (`HookConfigRelPath`) centralizes each agent’s config path for **`AllHookConfigRelPaths()`**, refactors all `OpenHookConfig` call sites, and powers a **build guard** ensuring every agent that opens a hook config declares its path.\\n> \\n> **`entire doctor`** gains **`checkAgentDirSymlinks`**, listing symlinked or unreadable components on paths Entire creates (hook config paths from the locator plus skill scaffold parents), so “hooks missing” on `status` gets an explicit cause.\\n> \\n> Additional hardening: **persistent ref flock** via `gitdir` + `flock.AcquireContextIn`; **`vercelconfig.LoadIn`** and setup’s Vercel probe through the worktree with a read cap; **`readCapped`** bounded reads; **`worktreedir.Name`** treats Windows drive-relative paths like other containment checks. Docs in **`CLAUDE.md`** are expanded for symlinked hook files/dirs and Pi auto-detection.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 98bdf18e1e25b02ce9f5f32112eec79bd6503236. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2220/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2220/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2084\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2084/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2084/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2084/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2084\",\n              \"id\": 5203576374,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABAasfnQ\",\n              \"number\": 2084,\n              \"title\": \"test(hooks): guard the committed dogfood configs against template drift\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-20T12:50:08Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-20T21:04:27Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-20T21:04:26Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2084\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2084\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2084.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2084.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-20T21:04:26Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1113\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## TL;DR\\n\\nThis repo's committed dogfood hook configs are generated from templates in the same tree, and nothing checks they stay in sync. `CheckHookConfig` already detects the drift — it just had no caller on the CI path. This wires it up as a test.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n`.pi/extensions/entire/index.ts`, `.opencode/plugins/entire.ts`, and `.claude/settings.json` are committed so every clone gets checkpointing without each person running `entire enable`. They're generated, so they go stale whenever the template moves — and both guards that look at them are blind to it:\\n\\n- `AreHooksInstalled` only greps the ownership marker, which survives any template change.\\n- Pi's `fireHook` swallows every error by design, so broken hooks are silent.\\n\\nThe committed Pi extension sat two commits behind its template for three weeks that way (`ed42608db` → `d55dfa643`). The cost was the `ENTIRE_PI_NESTED` guard: a Pi subagent forwarded its own lifecycle as if it were the user's session. `a9a676e79` swept it up when it removed local_dev mode, but fixed the symptom across all six artifacts by hand, not the cause.\\n\\n`entire doctor` reports this correctly today — but only for whoever happens to run it.\\n\\n## Solution\\n\\nOne test in `cmd/entire/cli` that runs the same `CheckHookConfig` doctor uses, over every registered agent implementing `agent.HookFreshness`, against this repo's own committed configs. `HooksOutdated` fails; `HooksAbsent` is fine (nothing committed for that agent).\\n\\nNo new drift-detection machinery — the check already existed and is already tested. This only puts it on the CI path.\\n\\nCoverage is whatever implements `HookFreshness`, so a future agent is picked up for free. Today that's Claude Code, OpenCode, and Pi — all three currently `HooksCurrent`. Codex, Cursor, Gemini, Copilot CLI and Factory Droid have no drift check at all, so their committed configs stay unguarded; that's a pre-existing gap this PR doesn't widen or close.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\nBoth arms verified by simulating drift and confirming the failure, then reverting:\\n\\n| Simulation | Result |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Added a comment line to `entire_extension.ts` (the historical bug: template moves, committed copy doesn't) | ❌ `committed Pi hook config is stale…` |\\n| Dropped the `TaskCreate\\\\|TaskUpdate` PostToolUse matcher from `.claude/settings.json` | ❌ `committed Claude Code hook config is stale…` |\\n| Clean tree | ✅ passes, 3 configs checked |\\n\\nThe `checked == 0` guard fails loudly if the configs are moved or renamed, so the test can't quietly stop guarding.\\n\\n`mise run lint` → 0 issues.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2084/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2084/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2241\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2241/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2241/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2241/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2241\",\n              \"id\": 5323086804,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABB4qmmA\",\n              \"number\": 2241,\n              \"title\": \"refactor(gitrepo): centralize metadata resolution (split part 1)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"id\": 34813274,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 5,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-02T11:06:38Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-03T20:21:55Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-03T20:21:55Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2241\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2241\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2241.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2241.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-03T20:21:55Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Refs #2190.\\r\\n\\r\\nPR #2190 moved every Git metadata consumer at once. The review exposed two separate jobs: define one owner for the metadata, then migrate its callers.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is split part 1. It adds the resolver and changes only repository opening. Checkpoint, session, strategy, hooks, and other consumers stay unchanged here.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Files and ownership\\r\\n\\r\\nThree production files and four test files change. All paths below are relative to `cmd/entire/cli/gitrepo/`.\\r\\n\\r\\n| File | Before | After |\\r\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\r\\n| `metadata.go` | No file | Resolves the three metadata facts |\\r\\n| `repository.go` | Opening rediscovered paths | Resolves and passes metadata |\\r\\n| `reftable.go` | Errors looked like absence | Returns inspection errors |\\r\\n| `metadata_guard_test.go` | No guard | Blocks new duplicate traversal |\\r\\n| `metadata_test.go` | No resolver tests | Covers real and broken layouts |\\r\\n| `repository_test.go` | Tested the old path | Covers fallback and failures |\\r\\n| `reftable_test.go` | Tested boolean detection | Covers inspection errors |\\r\\n\\r\\nThe call path changes like this:\\r\\n\\r\\n```text\\r\\nBefore\\r\\n\\r\\nOpenPath\\r\\n  ├── resolve .git and commondir while opening\\r\\n  ├── resolve them again while checking alternates\\r\\n  └── fall back without one validated metadata result\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter\\r\\n\\r\\nOpenPath\\r\\n  └── ResolveWorktreeMetadata\\r\\n        ├── GitDir\\r\\n        ├── CommonDir\\r\\n        └── WorktreeID\\r\\n              │\\r\\n              ├── repository storage\\r\\n              ├── alternates inspection\\r\\n              └── reftable inspection\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n## One resolver for three facts\\r\\n\\r\\n`gitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata` resolves an explicit worktree root into:\\r\\n\\r\\n- `GitDir`\\r\\n- `CommonDir`\\r\\n- `WorktreeID`\\r\\n\\r\\nThe resolver takes a worktree root. It does not discover one from CWD, read Git environment variables, run Git, cache results, or choose a caller's policy.\\r\\n\\r\\nResolution is all-or-error. Malformed or unreadable metadata stops the open.\\r\\n\\r\\n`gitrepo.OpenPath` now resolves metadata once and passes those facts into repository opening, object-alternates detection, and reftable inspection.\\r\\n\\r\\nA bare-repository open is tried only when worktree metadata does not exist.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Symlinks and `..` keep their filesystem meaning\\r\\n\\r\\nLexically cleaning a path through a symlink can change where `..` leads. The resolver checks filesystem identity before it returns a cleaned path.\\r\\n\\r\\nLinked-worktree registrations may use physical aliases. They must still resolve to an immediate child of `CommonDir/worktrees`.\\r\\n\\r\\nInspection errors now reach the caller. They no longer mean \\\"feature absent.\\\" This applies to reftable inspection and malformed `.git` layouts.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Fixes a hang that is already released\\r\\n\\r\\n`OpenPath` on `main` identifies a `.git` entry by reading it: `os.Stat`, then `os.ReadFile`. That works for a directory or a regular file. For three other entry types the read never finishes.\\r\\n\\r\\n| `.git` is | `main` | This PR |\\r\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\r\\n| A FIFO with no writer | Blocks until a writer opens it | Refused on type |\\r\\n| A symlink to such a FIFO | Blocks until a writer opens it | Refused on type |\\r\\n| A symlink to `/dev/zero` | Reads forever, memory grows | Refused on type |\\r\\n\\r\\nThe resolver checks the type first. It opens only a directory or a regular file, and refuses anything else by name.\\r\\n\\r\\nNone of these arrive by clone. Git refuses a `.git` path component in a tree at any depth, so each one needs local write access to the worktree. This is a robustness fix, not a vulnerability.\\r\\n\\r\\n## `gitdir:` strictness now matches Git\\r\\n\\r\\nThe legacy parser accepted pointer files that Git rejects. It cut the prefix at `gitdir:` instead of `gitdir: `, then trimmed whitespace from the remainder. That let `gitdir:target`, ` gitdir: target`, and `gitdir:\\\\ttarget` all resolve. Git requires the single space and trims nothing.\\r\\nThe fixture covers seven `.git` pointer spellings. The new resolver agrees with Git on all seven. The legacy parser agreed on three.\\r\\nThis changes behavior. A `.git` file that worked only because Entire was more permissive than Git now fails, and every other Git tool was already failing it.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Stop new duplicate traversal\\r\\n\\r\\nA source guard scans production Go across the repository. It rejects new `.git`, `gitdir:`, and `commondir` traversal outside `gitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata`.\\r\\nThe guard lists the existing callers that later PRs must migrate:\\r\\n\\r\\n- checkpoint metadata\\r\\n- session metadata\\r\\n- strategy and hooks\\r\\n- remaining product consumers\\r\\n\\r\\nThe exception list records each function and the one `git rev-parse` flag it may use. If that function starts using another metadata flag, the guard fails. The test also fails when a listed exception no longer exists.\\r\\n\\r\\nA temporary multi-file repository test runs the complete scanner. It proves that the scanner follows a package constant into another file, scans production code under `internal/`, and ignores a parameter named `gitDir`.\\r\\n\\r\\nPositive controls cover rooted filesystem APIs, package constants, `Readlink`, aliased imports, and legacy resolver calls.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Verification\\r\\n\\r\\n- `mise run check`\\r\\n  - formatting passed\\r\\n  - lint passed with 0 issues\\r\\n  - race-enabled unit and integration tests passed\\r\\n  - Vogon canary passed 56/56\\r\\n  - external deterministic canary passed 4/4\\r\\n- `git diff main --check`\\r\\n- Real Git fixtures cover ordinary, linked, bare, separate-Git-dir, submodule, symlink-alias, moved-registration, alternates, and reftable layouts.\\r\\n- On the seven `.git` pointer spellings in the fixture, the new resolver matches Git on 7/7. The legacy parser matched 3/7.\\r\\n- Broken fixtures verify fail-closed repository opening and typed absence.\\r\\n\\r\\nNo paid real-agent E2E tests were run.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Deliberately not included\\r\\n\\r\\nCheckpoint, session, strategy, hooks, and other product consumers still use their existing paths. Separate PRs will migrate them without mixing their error and fallback policies into this resolver change. The last migration will remove the legacy resolvers.\\r\\n\\r\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2241/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2241/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2194\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2194/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2194/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2194/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2194\",\n              \"id\": 5303551499,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBpFk8w\",\n              \"number\": 2194,\n              \"title\": \"Add deterministic complexity-baseline tooling under tools/complexity\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-31T18:31:26Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-01T14:07:40Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-01T14:07:37Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2194\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2194\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2194.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2194.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-01T14:07:37Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1191\\r\\n\\r\\nAdds `tools/complexity` — a self-contained Go module (`cxtool`) that computes a deterministic complexity baseline for this repo, per feature and per command.\\r\\n\\r\\n## The question it answers\\r\\n\\r\\nFor any feature or command: **how much code is there, how hard is it to read, how much of it do tests exercise, how often does it change, and what would deleting it actually free?** Concretely:\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Per-feature cost** — LOC, cyclomatic and cognitive complexity, test ratio, churn.\\r\\n- **Complexity vs coverage** — the \\\"complex *and* untested\\\" number, so review effort can go where it pays.\\r\\n- **Per-command marginal cost** — what each `entire <cmd>` *exclusively* owns versus what it shares.\\r\\n- **Dead code** — declarations no shipped root reaches.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Pieces\\r\\n\\r\\n| file | what |\\r\\n| --- | --- |\\r\\n| `main.go` | per-function LOC + cyclomatic (`fzipp/gocyclo`) + cognitive (`uudashr/gocognit`) complexity; folds in `go test -coverpkg` profiles and `git log --numstat` churn; rolls up by `features.json` path rules into ~50 features |\\r\\n| `reach/main.go` | SSA + VTA call graph. Every `*cobra.Command` constructor is a root (plus `<init>` and per-`main` pseudo-roots); reports each command's **exclusive** vs shared LOC, and declarations no root reaches. `-who <substr>` explains why one symbol is or isn't reached |\\r\\n| `dupl/main.go` | rolls a golangci `dupl` report up by feature |\\r\\n| `internal/cx/` | the single home of the feature mapping and rank policy, shared by all three binaries |\\r\\n| `render.py` | renders the HTML report page |\\r\\n| `baseline/2026-08-31/` | snapshot of the outputs, taken at `c7530fde0` (recorded in its `COMMIT` file), so later runs can be diffed |\\r\\n| `README.md` | full run recipe, metric definitions, and known limits |\\r\\n\\r\\n## Zero blast radius\\r\\n\\r\\n`tools/complexity` is a **separate Go module**, so its dependencies (`golang.org/x/tools`, gocyclo, gocognit) never enter the CLI's `go.mod`, and the root module cannot see it:\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\n$ go list ./... | grep -c tools\\r\\n0\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nCI, GoReleaser, and golangci are therefore unaffected — golangci only ever sees the root module. **No file outside `tools/` is touched** by this PR, so `test:ci` has nothing to exercise here.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Verification\\r\\n\\r\\n| check | result |\\r\\n| --- | --- |\\r\\n| `gofmt -s -l .` (nested module) | clean |\\r\\n| `go vet ./...` / `go build ./...` (nested module) | clean |\\r\\n| `go test ./...` (nested module) | `ok cxtool/internal/cx` |\\r\\n| `go run . -root ../.. -cover unit.out,int.out` | exit 0, **0 unmapped files** |\\r\\n| `go run ./reach -root ../..` | exit 0; 100 pkgs, 73,702-node callgraph, 161 roots (155 cobra) |\\r\\n| `dupl` scan + rollup | 902 issues (117 prod, 785 test) |\\r\\n| `go list ./... \\\\| grep -c tools` (repo root) | `0` |\\r\\n| `mise run fmt` | no changes (it walks `tools/` too) |\\r\\n| `mise run lint` | 0 issues |\\r\\n\\r\\n## Review findings\\r\\n\\r\\nBoth bot reviewers flagged real things. Fixed:\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Feature globs shadowed later exact rules** (Bugbot). `cmd/entire/cli/setup*.go` is listed before the rules naming `setup_search_skill.go`, `setup_import.go`, and `setup_agent_help_skill.go`, and first match won — so those three rules were dead and 642 prod / 1,134 test LOC sat under `cmd:enable-disable-configure` instead of `cmd:search`, `cmd:import`, and `cmd:agent-help-mcp`. Nothing reported it, because the files landed in a plausible wrong feature rather than in `_unmapped`. Rather than reorder `features.json`, the class is now gone: exact-path rules are tried before globs, so the config is order-independent for exact paths. A test file resolves through its source before the glob on its own path — without that step the three sources moved while their tests stayed behind, splitting each pair and wrecking the test-LOC and ratio columns for four features. The mapping change moves exactly six files, each source with its test.\\r\\n- **An unparseable pattern matched nothing silently** (Copilot). `matchRule` discards `path.Match`'s error, so a malformed glob never matched and its files drifted into `_unmapped` while the rule looked fine. Now rejected at load, naming the feature and the pattern.\\r\\n- **`render.py` ignored a failing `git rev-parse`** (Copilot), emitting a page with an empty commit stamp — the one field that ties a report to a tree. Now fails loudly.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **The duplication rollup attributed nothing to any feature.** golangci reports `Pos.Filename` relative to its *config file's* directory (`../../cmd/...`), while the path quoted inside the issue text is already repo-relative. Resolving both against the repo root put every `Pos.Filename` two levels above it, where no rule can match, so all 117 production findings landed in `_unmapped`. Each path is now resolved against whichever base names a file that exists — containment alone cannot choose, since the config dir is itself inside the repo. `cmd:control-plane` now shows the 16 findings the report's own prose already claimed for it.\\r\\n- **Directory-prefix rules resolved by list order, not specificity.** `features.json` carries both `e2e/` and `e2e/vogon/`, and only their ordering made the narrower one win; alphabetising the file would have silently moved a subtree to the wrong feature. The narrower prefix now wins from either position, and a basename glob beats a prefix containing it — the same invisible-misattribution class as the shadowing fix, for the case that fix did not cover.\\r\\n- **`report.md` and the page did not honour the norank contract their own captions state**, filtering on the literal area name `\\\"generated\\\"` and letting `test-infra` and `agent:vogon` into the ranking tables. They are now excluded and named with their size, so they do not simply vanish.\\r\\n\\r\\nAdds `internal/cx` tests covering the precedence rules and the rejection; the module previously had none.\\r\\n\\r\\nLeft as-is, deliberately:\\r\\n\\r\\n- **`bar()` gives a true zero a 1.5% sliver** (Copilot). Cosmetic, and the cell prints \\\"0%\\\" next to it.\\r\\n- **LOC counts `\\\\n`, so a file with no trailing newline undercounts by one** (Copilot). True as written, but unreachable here: every tracked `.go` file in the repo ends in a newline, because gofmt guarantees one.\\r\\n\\r\\n## What it already found\\r\\n\\r\\n- **The dead rewind cluster.** `reach`'s \\\"reached by no root\\\" list is what started the removal chain #2178 → #2186 → #2187 → #2189.\\r\\n- **`review` is the most expensive command by a wide margin** — 5,664 LOC reachable from that root and no other. Next are `explain` (2,633) and `investigate` (2,165).\\r\\n- **`cmd:trail` carries the most under-covered complexity** — Σcognit 1,697 at 64.8% coverage, i.e. 468 cognitive complexity in functions tests barely reach, the highest of any shipped command feature.\\r\\n- **Control-plane list/paging duplication** — 16 `dupl` findings, the most of any feature, plus a 37-line verbatim duplicate between `org.go` and `project.go`.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Cleanup pass\\r\\n\\r\\nA four-angle review (reuse, simplification, efficiency, altitude) ran over the module and its fixes are in the third commit. Each refactor was verified output-preserving by regenerating the whole pipeline and diffing: the CSVs are byte-identical once the time-based churn columns are excluded.\\r\\n\\r\\n`internal/cx` gains `WriteJSON`, `RelSlash`, and `SplitList`, replacing hand-rolled copies in all three binaries, and exports the unmapped sentinel so callers stop re-spelling `\\\"_unmapped\\\"`. `Func` carries `Ranked`, making the ranking filter a field read instead of a linear scan per function. `siteFan` is computed once and shared, so `explainWho`'s \\\"same map the cutoff uses\\\" is true by construction rather than by coincidence. Coverage folding and churn now overlap — they read the same parsed file set and write disjoint fields, and each takes seconds, so the wall clock is the slower of the two rather than their sum.\\r\\n\\r\\nSkipped: an `errgroup` rewrite of the worker pool (a new direct dependency to remove six lines) and folding `itoa` into `cx` (a one-line alias).\\r\\n\\r\\n## Deliberately not included\\r\\n\\r\\nNo CI wiring and no golangci changes. The README names gocognit-in-lint and `features.csv` diffing in CI as *options*; whether this becomes a gate is a product judgment call, so this PR flags it rather than deciding it. The tool is run by hand today, and the committed snapshot is what makes a later run meaningful.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Re-running\\r\\n\\r\\nSee `tools/complexity/README.md` — the full recipe (coverage profiles → metrics → reach → dupl → HTML page) is there, and every threshold is a flag whose effective value travels in `report.json` meta so the rendered page labels itself from data.\\r\\n\\r\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\r\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2194/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2194/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1911\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1911/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1911/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1911/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1911\",\n              \"id\": 5081638087,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M77m6rk\",\n              \"number\": 1911,\n              \"title\": \"perf: stop go-git walking ignored e2e/artifacts on every agent hook\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-06T13:29:22Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-07T11:30:13Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-07T11:30:11Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1911\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1911\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1911.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1911.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-07T11:30:11Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/984\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nThe `UserPromptSubmit` hook took **~11.4s** in this repo (9.8s of it system time), overshooting Claude Code's 30s hook timeout once the Go build cache was cold — e.g. right after 773db0d34 bumped Go to 1.26.5 and invalidated it.\\n\\nBoth seconds-scale costs were go-git's `Worktree.Status()`, measured here at **5.25s** against **0.013s** for `git status --porcelain`.\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\ngo-git's `gitignore.ReadPatterns` does not thread a parent directory's patterns into its recursive walk. Each recursive call rebuilds its pattern set from that directory's own ignore files, so the prune check only ever matches patterns declared by the directory being scanned.\\n\\n**A rule prunes a subtree only when its target is a direct child of the `.gitignore` declaring it.** Our root-level `e2e/artifacts/` rule was one level too deep, so every `Status()` descended all ~15k artifact directories.\\n\\nVerified against go-git `main` with the same 3,000-directory tree:\\n\\n| root `.gitignore` rule | result |\\n|---|---|\\n| `big/` | **0ms** — pruned |\\n| `e2e/artifacts/` | **121ms** — full descent |\\n\\nReference git prunes both identically. A CPU profile of `Status()` shows **100% of samples inside `collectIgnorePatterns` → `ReadPatterns`**; the diff walk contributes nothing, because it receives the full union of patterns and prunes correctly.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n**1. Move the ignore rule to `e2e/.gitignore` as `artifacts/`** so it is a direct child of its declaring `.gitignore`. Semantically identical to git, which reports the directory as ignored either way.\\n\\n**2. Add `gitrepo.Status(ctx, repo)`** as the single entry point for reading worktree status, with `gitrepo.WithStatusCache(ctx)` memoizing the walk. `handleLifecycleTurnStart` installs a cache: it runs before the agent acts and writes only under `.entire/` and `.git/`, so the status cannot change mid-hook. Previously `CapturePrePromptState` and the strategy's prompt attribution each paid for a full walk.\\n\\nThe cache is deliberately **not** installed on post-agent paths — `DetectFileChanges` on TurnEnd must observe the agent's edits. That constraint is documented on `WithStatusCache`.\\n\\n**3. Make the entry point real** rather than aspirational: migrated the three remaining direct callers (`DetectFileChanges`, `checkCanRewindWithWarning`, `checkResetSafety`) and added a `forbidigo` rule alongside the existing `Reset`/`Checkout` ones. Behavior-preserving — without a cache in `ctx`, `gitrepo.Status` is exactly `worktree.Status()`.\\n\\n**4. Documented both conventions** in `CLAUDE.md` under Git Operations, including the `.gitignore` placement rule.\\n\\n## Results\\n\\n| | before | after |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| hook wall time | 11.36s | **0.91s** |\\n| `Status()` | 5.25s | 0.045s |\\n| second `Status()` call | 5.18s | 0.015s (cache hit) |\\n\\nArtifacts were left in place and grew to 15,742 subdirectories during the test run with no regression.\\n\\n## Upstream\\n\\n[go-git#2284](https://github.com/go-git/go-git/pull/2284) (merged, unreleased — we are on `v6.0.0-alpha.5`, still the newest tag) cuts the blind ignore-file opens and would take `Status()` from 5.24s to 2.47s here, but does not address the pattern-inheritance gap. Its benchmark uses root-level ignore files, the placement that already prunes, so it cannot catch this.\\n\\nThe `.gitignore` placement in this PR is therefore a **workaround pending a proper upstream fix** to `ReadPatterns`. Once that lands and ships in a tag, the placement rule and possibly `WithStatusCache` become removable; `gitrepo.Status` and the `forbidigo` rule are worth keeping regardless.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] `mise run fmt && mise run lint` clean\\n- [x] `mise run test` — 8,534 tests pass\\n- [x] `mise run test:integration` — 448 tests pass\\n- [x] `mise run test:e2e:canary` — 59 + 4 tests pass\\n- [x] `forbidigo` rule verified to fire: reintroducing a bare `worktree.Status()` is reported at the call site\\n- [x] Hook re-timed at 0.76s after the cleanup commit\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Performance and routing changes with behavior-preserving status semantics when no cache is set; stale-cache misuse is documented but limited to the TurnStart window where the worktree is treated as stable.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Fixes TurnStart / `UserPromptSubmit` hooks spending ~5s+ per `go-git` `Worktree.Status()`** by addressing how ignored `e2e/artifacts` is declared and by deduplicating status reads on the turn-start path.\\n> \\n> The root `.gitignore` no longer lists `e2e/artifacts/`; **`e2e/.gitignore` now ignores `artifacts/`** so go-git's `ReadPatterns` can prune that subtree (root-level nested patterns did not). **`gitrepo.Status(ctx, repo)`** is the only supported status API, with **`gitrepo.WithStatusCache(ctx)`** memoizing results per worktree root; **`handleLifecycleTurnStart`** installs the cache so pre-prompt capture and prompt attribution share one walk. Call sites in **`DetectFileChanges`**, rewind safety checks, and strategy rewind warnings now use `gitrepo.Status`. A **forbidigo** rule blocks new direct `Worktree.Status()` usage; **`CLAUDE.md`** documents the `.gitignore` placement rule and when caching is safe (TurnStart yes, TurnEnd no).\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 45406d520091b1de12ed64003228f87752781e95. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1911/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1911/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1896\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1896/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1896/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1896/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1896\",\n              \"id\": 5060434168,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M76iY5n\",\n              \"number\": 1896,\n              \"title\": \"fix(session): reconcile worktree path on resume after repo relocation\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"id\": 881031,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-04T12:27:15Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-14T15:11:14Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-14T15:11:13Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1896\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1896\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1896.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1896.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-14T15:11:13Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/969\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nFixes #1890.\\n\\n## Problem\\nA session records `SessionState.WorktreePath` once at start, and the commit-time\\nmatcher (`findSessionsForWorktree`) uses exact string equality. When the repo\\ndirectory is renamed/moved while the session is stopped and the agent resumes it\\n(Claude Code's own `/resume`) from the new location, the recorded path no longer\\nresolves — every commit silently loses its `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer. #1440's\\nsibling-worktree fallback doesn't cover a whole-repo move: the old path is gone,\\nso nothing matches.\\n\\n## Fix\\nReconcile on the resumed turn, **scoped to main-worktree relocations**. When a\\nturn starts and the recorded path no longer resolves to this repo's git common\\ndir, repoint `WorktreePath` at the current worktree — but only when the session\\nand the current worktree are both the **main** worktree (`WorktreeID == \\\"\\\"` on\\nboth sides). The session store lives in the common dir, so a loaded state is the\\nsame repo by construction; a recorded path that still resolves to this repo (a\\nlive sibling worktree) is left untouched.\\n\\n## Why main-worktree only\\n`WorktreeID` keys the session's shadow branch (`entire/<base>-hash(WorktreeID)`).\\nRepointing a **linked**-worktree session onto the main worktree while keeping its\\n`WorktreeID` would leave `WorktreeID` describing a different worktree than\\n`WorktreePath`. An audit of every `WorktreeID`/`WorktreePath` consumer showed that\\ndisalignment is reachable by code that re-derives the worktree id from the current\\ndirectory instead of reading `state.WorktreeID`:\\n\\n- `entire clean` (and its `--dry-run` preview) compute the wrong shadow-branch\\n  name → the session's real branch is orphaned.\\n- `entire explain` / rewind-point listing filter shadow branches by the current\\n  worktree hash → the session's checkpoints are hidden.\\n- post-commit base/attribution updates follow the wrong worktree's HEAD → skewed\\n  agent-vs-human attribution.\\n\\nThe reported case (#1890) is a whole main-checkout relocation, where `WorktreeID`\\nis `\\\"\\\"` throughout — so restricting to that fixes the bug **without ever creating\\nthe disaligned state**, and `WorktreePath`/`WorktreeID` stay aligned by\\nconstruction. Linked-worktree relocation is a rare, documented non-goal; the\\nzero-match path still warns so the trailer loss is not silent.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n- **RED→GREEN** integration test (`resume_repo_rename_test.go`): start session →\\n  rename repo folder → resumed turn → commit still gets its trailer. Confirmed\\n  failing before the fix, passing after.\\n- Guard unit tests: main relocation reconciles; **linked-worktree session left\\n  untouched**; **resuming into a linked worktree left untouched**; live sibling\\n  untouched; same-path no-op.\\n- Full integration suite green; strategy pkg green; lint clean.\\n\\n## Scope\\nReconciliation only. Follow-ups from the issue (WARN on zero-match, `adopt`\\nwithout a live `--from`, `doctor` flagging stale paths) are deliberately left to\\nseparate PRs.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1896/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1896/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1287\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1287/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1287/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1287/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1287\",\n              \"id\": 4539142975,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7gKoTh\",\n              \"number\": 1287,\n              \"title\": \"feat(agent): add Antigravity (agy) CLI agent\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 2,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-05-28T09:06:05Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-24T13:44:21Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-24T13:44:17Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1287\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1287\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1287.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1287.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-24T13:44:17Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/444\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n> **Status: Preview.** The integration ships with `IsPreview() == true` — users see a \\\"(Preview)\\\" label in the agent selector, `entire agent list`, and the hook-install message. Known limitations are listed below and in `docs/architecture/agent-guide.md` (\\\"Antigravity status: Preview\\\").\\n\\nFirst-class support for **Antigravity CLI** (`agy`), Google's successor to Gemini CLI, as a new Entire agent — the complete integration: lifecycle hooks, transcript decoding, native token counts, review-skill discovery, resume tracking, docs, and E2E wiring. Consolidates the previously stacked PRs #1356 (tokens) and #1381 (transcript decode) plus the gap-fix and review-fix rounds into this single parent.\\n\\n**Scope map** (~7.2k insertions; ~60% tests):\\n\\n| Area | What |\\n|---|---|\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/` | agent package: 3 lifecycle hooks (`pre-tool-use`, `pre-invocation`, `stop`), transcript analyzers (prompts, positions, modified files), async-transcript handling, token tee (`statusline.go`/`title_install.go`), review-skill discovery |\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go`, `state.go`, `event.go` | conditional TurnStart (resume tracking), out-of-band token baseline/delta, committed-state filtering for mid-turn commits |\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/` | empty-transcript degrade (agy-scoped), late-flush prompt recovery, checkpoint-scoped token resolution, agy summary/count cases |\\n| `agent/skilldiscovery/` | shared SKILL.md scanner (claude-code rewired onto it) |\\n| e2e + CI | agy runner with three auth modes (ADC → `GEMINI_API_KEY` → OAuth), trusted-workspace seeding, fatal-vs-transient classification, agy-log + hook-probe artifact capture; **dispatch-only** in workflows (see limitations) |\\n| docs | CLAUDE/AGENTS, architecture guide quirks section, checklist, e2e README |\\n\\n## Real-agy quirks (all hardened in code + tests)\\n\\n- **`invocationNum` is 0-indexed**; PreInvocation fires per *model invocation*. `invocationNum > 0` emits a conditional TurnStart (`Event.SuppressIfSessionActive`) the dispatcher drops only when a turn is genuinely mid-flight — so resumes (`agy --conversation`) are tracked and follow-up invocations don't clobber the pre-prompt baseline.\\n- **agy writes its transcript AFTER `Stop`.** `PrepareTranscript` briefly waits then materializes a placeholder; condensation degrades to a files/prompt-only checkpoint (agy-scoped) and prompts are re-extracted late (`resolvePromptsFromLateFlushedTranscript`).\\n- **Tokens have exactly one surface** — the title/statusline JSON. The global `title` slot is claimed by `entire hooks antigravity title-tee` (wrap-preserving, doctor-checked); TurnStart snapshots a baseline, TurnEnd computes the delta (`OutOfBandTokenSource`).\\n- **Tool args are double-encoded**; `decodeAgyString`/`decodeAgyBool` tolerate both shapes. macOS `/tmp` symlinks resolved.\\n- **No SessionStart hook surface** → silent tracking (same as Cursor/OpenCode/Copilot/Pi). agy's PostToolUse/PostInvocation hooks are deliberately **not installed** — no lifecycle mapping, and they'd spawn a no-op subprocess per tool call.\\n\\n## Review & verification\\n\\n- Three-dimension agent review (correctness / over-engineering / hooks-and-docs-vs-agy-1.0.15) followed by a 28-agent adversarially-verified full-implementation review; **all 10 verified findings fixed** (token double-counting, tokens lost on fully-committed turns, deletion-filter regression, cross-worktree title-tee uninstall, e2e retry masking, degrade scoping, hook-prefix matching, + 3 cleanups).\\n- Hook contract verified byte-for-byte against agy's official docs (1.0.15 changed no hook behavior).\\n- Analyzer methods validated against **385 real captured agy transcripts: 0 errors, 0 offset mismatches**; full-pipeline replay of a real transcript reproduces prompts/files/checkpoint contents.\\n- Live smoke on this tip: `entire agent add antigravity` → real hook wiring → mid-turn commit with unwritten transcript → checkpoint + trailer + scoped tokens + `entire status` all correct. Real `agy` fired PreInvocation live (session state created); the model call itself is quota-gated (below).\\n- **2026-07-13 review round (3-reviewer pass + live testing on real agy)**: `TestSingleSessionManualCommit` passed live with real token counts; fresh-repo smoke verified install → live turn → commit → condensation → resume (`agy --conversation`) → token scoping across two commits. agy auto-updated 1.0.16→1.1.1 mid-session; hook wire contract re-verified unchanged, but agy 1.1 moved the skill-discovery directories — fixed, along with the ADC-mode quota-log peek, a doctor false-positive for non-agy teammates, an explicit Stop-hook timeout, and an `agent remove` warning about the global title-tee. Deferred minors are tracked as findings on trail 444.\\n\\n> **Behavior note (all agents):** the ghost-session fix intentionally changes shadow-branch preservation — a read-only ACTIVE session (no tracked files) no longer keeps its shadow branch alive on commit (`phase_postcommit_test.go` updated accordingly). Both checkpoint writers skip zero-file writes, so nothing such a session wrote can be stranded.\\n\\n## Known limitations (preview)\\n\\n- **Live agy E2E runs in the default matrix in agy's Gemini API-key mode** (no account session; the shared `GEMINI_API_KEY` secret). agy ≤ 1.1.24 loaded `.agents/hooks.json` on that route but never executed the hooks (google-antigravity/antigravity-cli#893, still open upstream); bisecting the release binaries with a probe hook shows **agy ≥ 1.1.25 executes them**, and CI installs `releases/latest` (1.2.7 as of 2026-09-21). The optional `ANTIGRAVITY_GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS_JSON` secret still switches the leg to ADC; the `cloudcode-pa` backend remains entitlement-gated (subject 110002). Fail-fast classification covers quota/entitlement walls plus `GEMINI_API_KEY … not set` / `API_KEY_INVALID`. Details in `e2e/README.md`.\\n- **Transcript-derived file lists can be incomplete** when agy persists a step with `truncated_fields` and drops `TargetFile` (reported by @ecgang, ~0.8% of `replace_file_content` calls in their corpus). Now logged as a WARN per dropped call instead of a silent skip; live PreToolUse stdin is never truncated so only the late-flush / first-turn fallbacks are affected. Awaiting a real fixture.\\n- Mid-turn-commit checkpoints record zero tokens (the turn's delta lands on the next condensation — totals stay correct; documented at the fallback).\\n- No in-agy banner (no SessionStart hook surface) — tracking is silent inside the agy UI; `entire status` is the visibility surface.\\n- First-turn mid-turn commits can produce a files/prompt-only checkpoint (agy's transcript lands after Stop); prompts recover on the next condensation.\\n- Token capture depends on `entire hooks antigravity title-tee` owning/wrapping agy's global `title` slot (doctor-checked, setup-repaired).\\n- Wire format captured on agy 1.0.14/1.0.15, re-verified unchanged on agy 1.1.1 (2026-07-13) and 1.1.22 (2026-08-27: still exactly 5 hook types; statusline/title payload unchanged). agy is fast-moving — 1.1 moved the skill directories (handled), 1.1.10 fixed hook ordering so `Stop`/`PostInvocation` fire reliably, 1.1.12 answers `-p \\\"/hooks\\\"` locally (used by `entire doctor` to verify the workspace hooks actually load, zero quota).\\n\\n## 2026-08-27/28 update\\n\\n- Merged `origin/main` (was 3 months behind): ported to local-dev removal, `IsManagedHookCommand(cmd)`, `AreHooksInstalled → (bool, error)`, 4-value `RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI`, main's `skilldiscovery` extraction.\\n- Fixed the CI install step: the agy release tarball ships the binary as `antigravity`, so the leg had never started in CI.\\n- Added `GEMINI_API_KEY` e2e mode, optional ADC, trusted-workspace seeding, agy-log + hook-probe artifacts (agy emits no log line for hook execution — the probe is how #893 was found).\\n- `entire doctor`: \\\"Antigravity hooks: LOADED/NOT LOADED by agy\\\" via `agy -p /hooks --add-dir <root> --output-format json` (version-gated ≥ 1.1.12), plus the untrusted-workspace trap from the test report.\\n- `truncated_fields` degrade path (above). Docs refreshed for 1.1.22.\\n\\n## 2026-09-22 update (trail-444 review rounds after real Windows/macOS testing)\\n\\n- **Windows (confirmed on Windows 11 ARM64, agy 1.2.7):** agy hands hook commands to cmd.exe, so the sh wrapper failed silently and nothing was tracked. Antigravity now installs the bare direct-shell wrapper (`agent.WrapWindowsProductionSilentHookCommandDirect`) when `HookHostIsWindows()`. The status store's root-relative names were backslash-joined on Windows and never created; they are slash-separated now and `osroot.MkdirAllNoSymlink` refuses backslash names.\\n- **`entire doctor`:** the `agy -p /hooks` probe was observed to run a full model turn on Windows and only proved agy parsed hooks.json, so it is opt-in (`ENTIRE_ANTIGRAVITY_DOCTOR_PROBE=1`). By default doctor now checks, at zero cost, that the installed hook entry is the shape this host needs (`HooksEntryMatchesHost`) and says how to reinstall. An unparseable agy version no longer produces \\\"run `agy update`\\\".\\n- **Prompt loss on later-turn manual commits (user-reported, three checkpoints):** the last rung of the condensation prompt ladder now extracts from the transcript bytes being stored (`agent.TranscriptPromptExtractor`) instead of re-reading the live path, and condensation logs which rung supplied the prompts. A new integration test runs two turns in agy's real order and commits each manually.\\n- Smaller: uninstall leaves a hooks.json with no Entire entry untouched; readers no longer leave orphan lock files; prune pairs a snapshot file with its lock; `--add-dir` must be absolute (documented, and the probe refuses a relative root); the merge-gating `e2e.yml` pins agy to 1.2.7 while nightly keeps `latest`.\\n- **Re-test on the fixed head (2026-09-22):** live two-turn agy conversation with a manual commit after each turn on `entireio/entire-sandbox` — both checkpoints carry the right prompt (the later turn at transcript offset 4), tokens recorded, status store under `~/.cache/entire/antigravity/status` with no orphan locks, doctor clean without the probe. Full antigravity e2e suite: 48 pass / 3 skipped both locally and in CI; the 5 `TestInteractive*` failures were the harness, not the CLI — interactive agy in a never-run HOME shows a color-scheme chooser and a Terms consent before the prompt. The isolated HOME now seeds `cache/onboarding.json` as complete (established by walking onboarding in a scratch HOME and diffing), and the runner clicks through both screens as a fallback.\\n- **Command smoke matrix (2026-09-22, sandbox, agy session present):** `agent list/add/remove`, `status` (+`--json`), `session list/current/info/tokens/stop`, `checkpoint list/explain/tokens/search`, `search`, `recap --static`, `activity`, `agent-help`, `doctor` (default and with the probe opt-in), `configure --summarize-provider antigravity`, `checkpoint explain --generate`, `dispatch --local --agent antigravity`, `clean --dry-run`, `disable`/`enable`. Two real bugs found and fixed: agy 1.2.x ignores stdin in print mode, so `GenerateText` now passes the prompt in argv (`dispatch --local` had handed agy an empty prompt); and the summarizer had no condenser for agy's step JSONL, so `explain --generate` reported an empty transcript — `antigravity.CondenseTranscript` now feeds it. Both re-verified live.\\n- **Shadow-branch pinning (review finding on the smoke-matrix head):** the ghost-session fix had narrowed \\\"active session with uncondensed content\\\" to \\\"active session with tracked files\\\", which would let a sibling's condensation delete the only checkpoint of a session whose first step captured a transcript before any edit. The gate now uses the same test condensation uses (`sessionHasShadowContent`: files, written steps, or task checkpoints); the ghost still has none of those. Table test covers files-only and steps-only.\\n- Merged `origin/main` a third time (session-store tests; no code conflicts).\\n- **Windows, on a real Windows host (2026-09-22 evening):** the antigravity leg is now dispatchable in `e2e-windows.yml` (agy 1.2.7 from `agy_cli_windows_x64.zip`, API-key mode; the harness redirects `USERPROFILE` with `HOME` so agy and the `entire` hooks it spawns agree on the isolated home). `TestSingleSessionManualCommit` passed on `windows-latest` ([run 35803986610](https://github.com/entireio/cli/actions/runs/35803986610)): the cmd.exe wrapper fired PreInvocation/PreToolUse/Stop, agy wrote the file through a PreToolUse hook, the Stop hook saved the shadow checkpoint, and the commit carries its `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer. The first run failed only on the harness's `sh -c` probe hook, which cmd.exe cannot run and which made agy refuse the tool call; the probe now skips itself on Windows. Runner is x64; ARM64 remains the reviewer's manual evidence. Follow-up: add antigravity to the nightly Windows leg.\\n- **2026-09-23:** Victor's Windows and review-round fixes landed directly on the branch. On top of them: the title-tee idempotency test stands up an agy on PATH (the tee is now only claimed where agy exists); the summary prompt's `[Files Modified]` list is bounded like the transcript; the e2e harness removes Antigravity's isolated home with the repo; the commit fast path treats only a missing or store-refused transcript as \\\"no content\\\" (any other stat error fails toward condensing); and **the title-tee now preserves a pre-existing user title command on Windows** — `--wrap-b64 <base64url>` where agy runs the slot through cmd.exe, re-run through cmd.exe by the tee, with uninstall restoring either form byte for byte. Previously that case failed on every model call on Windows (no tokens, user title gone); an older finding had deferred it with \\\"revisit if agy ships on Windows\\\". Review round on that head: a TTY mid-turn commit before agy's first Stop lost its trailer because the slow path required transcript growth before looking at hook-captured files (fixed: files carry the decision, growth is the fallback); the summary-prompt bounds had leaked into `explain --full` (display formatter is unbounded again, LLM callers use `FormatCondensedTranscriptForPrompt`); the Antigravity install hint used backticks the picker mangles.\\n- **Merged main again** for #2554: `agent.IsPreview` is gone, so Antigravity's preview status is documentation only (AGENT.md, agent-guide.md); this branch's own selector/list preview labels were reverted before that.\\n\\n## 2026-09-21 update\\n\\n- Merged `origin/main` again (~905 commits; 14 conflicts). Main deleted `e2e-isolated.yml` / `e2e-checkpoints-v2.yml` and gave `e2e.yml` a `test` regex input, so the antigravity CI wiring now lives only in `e2e.yml`. Adapted to main's checks: `StepContext.MetadataDirAbs` removal, the `writeTestFile` helper removal, `goconst` on the hook type literal, the transcript-read ratchet (`transcript_read_guard_test.go`; antigravity registers one read like every other agent), the e2e prompt-timeout chain (`boundPrompt`), the `userdirs` consumer audit (the statusline tee now resolves through `userdirs.CacheDirChecked`), and the summary-capable provider pin (antigravity has `GenerateText`, so it joins the list and the README).\\n- **#893 verified fixed upstream in agy 1.1.25** by bisecting real release binaries in an isolated HOME with `modelProvider: gemini` and a probe `hooks.json`: 1.1.22/1.1.23/1.1.24 fire nothing, 1.1.25/1.2.0/1.2.7 fire PreInvocation + Stop. The release notes never mention it. The antigravity leg is back in the default `e2e.yml` matrix and the dispatch-only caveats are rewritten (`AGENT.md`, `agent-guide.md`, `e2e/README.md`).\\n- **Nightly install smoke** (`nightly-e2e.yml`) gains an antigravity leg on Linux and macOS (agy from the latest release tarball, API-key mode, 25-minute step cap for the 2.5x multiplier). It can only go green once this PR is in a published nightly, since that workflow checks out the nightly tag.\\n- **Model bump:** agy 1.2.x dropped `gemini-3.5-flash-low` from `agy models` (both auth modes) and rejects it with `invalid model selection`; the harness default is now `gemini-3.8-flash-low`.\\n- CI run [35650998214](https://github.com/entireio/cli/actions/runs/35650998214) then passed `TestSingleSessionManualCommit` for antigravity in API-key mode (no ADC secret present, agy from `releases/latest`): the org `GEMINI_API_KEY` is valid and the full hook set, PreToolUse included, executes on that route.\\n\\n- **Live smoke on entire.io (2026-09-21):** `entire` built from this branch drove real agy 1.2.7 sessions in API-key mode against `entireio/entire-sandbox` on both checkpoint backends — [git-branch session](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-sandbox/session/8dfd5617-4bd3-4dab-aff5-42cc697bb429) (checkpoint `593b557e273d`) and [git-refs session](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-sandbox/session/74e375f5-45f0-47f8-9b0e-e152bdfcb0e9) (checkpoint `01M33B0YNF2RDS4ANXE7H8PZ2E`). Hooks, title-tee, trailer, condensation, push and ingestion all worked; the three trail-444 findings (dedup/append race, bare `os.Remove` in prune, `os.Stat` on the transcript path) are fixed in `9f688a8763` by anchoring the status store on `userdirs.CacheRoot` and locking the dedup-append.\\n\\n## Follow-ups (deliberately out of scope)\\n\\n- Record the model: agy's PreInvocation payload carries `modelName`, but checkpoint metadata leaves `model` empty today.\\n- entire.io's activity view labels these sessions \\\"Unknown\\\" while the search index says `Antigravity` — a web-side display mapping, not this repo.\\n- `entire doctor` could warn when agy < 1.1.25 runs in API-key mode (hooks load but never execute there).\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] `mise run check` green locally (fmt, lint 0 issues, unit + integration + canary) — re-run 2026-09-21 on the merged tree\\n- [ ] CI green on the merged tip\\n- [x] `e2e.yml` antigravity leg green in API-key mode on agy latest, no ADC secret — [run 35650998214](https://github.com/entireio/cli/actions/runs/35650998214) (`TestSingleSessionManualCommit`, 2026-09-21)\\n- [x] Analyzer validation against 385 real transcripts + real-transcript pipeline replay\\n- [x] Live smoke of install → hooks → commit → checkpoint → status on this tip\\n- [x] `mise run test:e2e --agent antigravity TestSingleSessionManualCommit` — passed live 2026-07-13 (real agy, real tokens in the condensed checkpoint)\\n- [x] Live fresh-repo smoke 2026-07-13: enable → live agy turn → commit/trailer/condensation → resume via `agy --conversation` → checkpoint-scoped token deltas across two commits\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> New agent code paths affect session lifecycle, hook-installed repo files, and checkpoint condensation; risk is mitigated by extensive tests but behavior depends on undocumented agy wire formats.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **preview** first-class support for **Antigravity CLI** (`agy`): a new `antigravity` agent package that registers with Entire, installs five workspace hooks into `.agents/hooks.json` (`entire` entry → `entire hooks antigravity <verb>`), and maps hook stdin to lifecycle events (`TurnStart`, `ToolUse`, `TurnEnd`).\\n> \\n> Lifecycle behavior is tailored to real `agy` quirks: **`TurnStart` only when `invocationNum == 0`** (follow-up pre-invocations are ignored so baselines aren’t reset); **`Stop` with `fullyIdle` → `TurnEnd`** (so `SaveStep`/checkpoints run); **post-invocation is a no-op** because transcripts aren’t ready yet; **`PrepareTranscript`** creates an empty placeholder when the transcript file is still missing after stop. **Pre-tool-use** records touched files from mutating tools, including double-encoded args and parent-dir symlink normalization (macOS `/tmp`).\\n> \\n> Also wires **non-interactive `GenerateText`** via `agy -p`, JSONL transcript chunk/reassemble (passthrough v1), registry/hooks CLI imports, integration tests over subprocess hooks, and optional **E2E** registration when `agy` is on `PATH`.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit f141838ceac0e3ae2d7cfea32e5762eaecb2ef72. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1287/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1287/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2211\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2211/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2211/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2211/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2211\",\n              \"id\": 5308899549,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBtW1lw\",\n              \"number\": 2211,\n              \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): serialize OPF ref updates\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"id\": 34813274,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 15,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-01T07:12:39Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-06T16:30:08Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-06T16:30:08Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2211\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2211\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2211.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2211.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-06T16:30:08Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes #2204\\n\\nA native Git checkpoint writer and an OPF rewrite could both read the same ref value and then both report a successful update. The OPF paths used go-git's compare-and-swap, which does not participate in native Git's reference-locking protocol. A native transaction could therefore commit after the OPF rewrite and silently discard it.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\nIntroduce `gitrepo.CompareAndSwapRef`, a shared direct-ref compare-and-swap built on a native `git update-ref --stdin` transaction. The transaction prepares the update first, acquiring Git's ref lock, verifies that the ref is not symbolic while that lock is held, and then commits.\\n\\nThe native helper now backs:\\n\\n- shadow-branch updates\\n- all persistent-ref writers using `updatePersistentRef`, including the Stop hook\\n- both OPF rewrite paths: the shared v1 ref and per-checkpoint refs\\n\\nThe OPF scan remains outside the ref transaction. Its final CAS uses the value observed before the scan, so a concurrent update is rejected instead of overwritten.\\n\\n`CASPersistentRef` deliberately does not acquire Entire's persistent-writer flock. Its expected value predates the call, and native Git is the correctness boundary. Avoiding the flock also prevents deadline-free pre-push operations from waiting indefinitely. Transient native lock contention is retried with a bounded budget; a genuine stale-value conflict is terminal.\\n\\n## Transaction and failure behavior\\n\\nThe separate `git symbolic-ref` invocation is deliberate. Git does not allow `symref-verify` and an update of the same ref in one transaction because it treats them as multiple updates to that ref. Preparing the native update first keeps the ref locked while the symbolic-ref probe runs, closing the conversion race.\\n\\nCAS error classification recognizes only Git's exact stale-value diagnostics. Corrupt refs, unreadable refs, namespace conflicts, and other permanent failures retain their underlying diagnosis rather than being mislabeled and retried. The v1 rewrite reports `V1RefMovedError` only after a successful reread confirms that the ref actually changed.\\n\\nCancellation closes the transaction's stdin so Git can abort cleanly. A three-second `WaitDelay` bounds shutdown if a hook or inherited pipe prevents the process from exiting.\\n\\n## Performance\\n\\nRouting the shared write path through the transaction increases a measured ref update from 13.4 ms to 22.0 ms—an 8.6 ms cost per update. That is under 1% of the roughly 3-second p50 Stop-hook latency.\\n\\nThe extra symbolic-ref process is required for the direct-ref guarantee described above; it is not an accidental round trip.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nRegression tests use real native Git transactions and cover both files and reftable repositories. They exercise:\\n\\n- both OPF lost-update races\\n- symbolic-ref rejection and concurrent symbolic conversion\\n- native lock contention and bounded retry behavior\\n- cancellation and lock release\\n- malformed, corrupt, unreadable, and namespace-conflicting refs\\n- preservation of the original failure when a v1 ref cannot be reread\\n\\nThe focused race tests passed ten consecutive runs.\\n\\n`mise run check` passed after the review fixes, including formatting, lint, race-enabled unit and integration tests, and the Vogon and Roger-Roger canary suites.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2211/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2211/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2547\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2547/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2547/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2547/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2547\",\n              \"id\": 5528562537,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABEcDQdg\",\n              \"number\": 2547,\n              \"title\": \"Make repo view the one place a repository is shown\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"id\": 881031,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-21T14:48:10Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-05T14:49:55Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-05T14:49:52Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2547\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2547\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2547.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2547.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-05T14:49:52Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1392\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n`entire repo mirror get` had quietly become the repository record view — name, visibility, and every cluster holding a copy — while `entire repo view` printed a flat field list that named only the primary. Two verbs answered \\\"show me this repo\\\", and the better answer lived under the `mirror` subtree, where nobody looking for a repository would think to go.\\n\\nThis makes `repo view` that view, for both forges, and deletes `repo mirror get`. Along the way it settles how a cluster is named in output, because the old answer disagreed with how every flag takes one.\\n\\n## What a repo looks like now\\n\\n```\\n$ entire repo view /et/pgrant/rgrant\\nName:\\n  /et/pgrant/rgrant\\nVisibility:\\n  Private\\n\\nCLUSTER                     ROLE     CLONE URL                                             STATUS\\naws-us-east-2.entire.io     primary  entire://aws-us-east-2.entire.io/et/pgrant/rgrant     ready\\naws-eu-central-1.entire.io  mirror   entire://aws-eu-central-1.entire.io/et/pgrant/rgrant  ready\\n```\\n\\n**A repository is named `/<forge>/<a>/<b>` here, and no other way.** `repo view` takes the `/et/<project>/<repo>` path, a `/gh/<owner>/<repo>` ref, and an `entire://` clone URL. The URL matters because it is the only form naming its own cluster, so it is the only one that reaches a repo in a federation other than the active login. A bare `owner/repo` is answered with **both** forge spellings, since this verb serves both.\\n\\nThe repo ULID and the bare name with `--project` are gone. Neither is a repository's *name*: a ULID identifies a row, and a name is unique only inside a project — which is why the flag had to exist to scope it. `--project` leaves with the spelling it scoped. This also settles what a ULID meant here at all: a GitHub-mirror repo has a ULID-addressable record too, so `repo view <mirror ULID>` used to reach the native path and ask `/native-mirrors` about a repo Entire holds no provisioning state for.\\n\\n## Three fixes that were not cosmetic\\n\\n**The CLUSTER column printed a slug the flags reject.** Every targeting `--cluster` takes a public host, so a cell read out of the table could not be pasted back into the flag that acts on it. It prints the host now. This is a bug rather than a preference because `repo mirror list --cluster` is a *client-side* filter over those very rows: a spelling the column did not print matched nothing at all, silently. `--cluster aws-us-east-2.entire.io` returned \\\"No repos found\\\" before this branch; it works now, and a value the catalog cannot name is refused with the spelling that works rather than matching zero rows at exit 0.\\n\\n**The STATUS column spoke two languages.** A repo said `active` where its own mirror said `ready`, and `provisioning` where one said `processing` — the same two facts under two names, sitting in one column, reading as a difference that is not there. The primary now reports in the placement vocabulary. An unrecognised state passes through unchanged, because `state` is an open string on the wire and translating one the server adds later would be a guess printed as fact. The mapping is on the field rather than the rendering, so `--json` and `mirror list --status ready` agree with the table.\\n\\n**The control-plane E2E was broken and nothing caught it.** `waitForRepoClonable` polls `repo view --json` for coordinates the new row shape stopped emitting. It would have spun for its full two-minute deadline and failed *every* test in that suite, including the ones that never call `repo view`. `mise run check` does not run it. Those coordinates are properties of a placement, so they now live on one: `clusterSlug` and `jurisdiction` join each placement as `--json`-only fields, on **both** forges, since the need they serve — keying on a cluster rather than printing it — is not a property of a forge.\\n\\n## What review found\\n\\nCursor, Copilot and the trail reviewer between them raised thirty findings across several rounds; all are addressed. The ones that changed behaviour rather than wording:\\n\\n- **A native `entire://` clone URL was rejected** — the form this view's own CLONE URL column prints. The URL's path is now read by `parseMirrorRepoRef`, the same grammar the bare refs take, so a clone URL and the ref it was built from can never disagree about what a name may contain — a trailing `.git` included, which is part of a native name and decoration on a `/gh/` one.\\n- **`--json` dropped the repo record** (above). Restoring it also un-broke the control-plane E2E, whose `repoJSON` decodes both `create` and `view`.\\n- **A failed provision could not be detected.** Such a repo has no placement, so every placement-shaped check read a zero value and saw nothing wrong: `waitForRepoClonable` burned its full two-minute deadline instead of naming the failure. It reads the repo's own `state` now, and the view leads with `Provisioning failed: <reason>` rather than explaining why a table is missing.\\n- **An absent visibility rendered `Public`.** The old view made no visibility claim at all, so this branch introduced the assertion — and its default was the permissive one. Unknown now prints `-`, omits the JSON key, and matches neither `--private` nor `--private=false`.\\n- **A readiness failure was swallowed on every native invocation**, so a core outage downgraded `repo view` to a table asserting nothing was wrong, at exit 0. It is disclosed on stderr now; an interrupted read fails outright, since a cancelled command must not report success.\\n- **The provision reason printed under every native view.** The field outlives the failure it describes, so a repo reading `ready` carried \\\"max retries exhausted\\\" beneath it. It is scoped to a repo that has actually failed.\\n- **`--authoritative` and `--project` reached the GitHub route and meant nothing there.** Entire holds no repository record for an upstream, only the mirrors of it. Both are reported as ignored rather than silently dropped.\\n- **A pasted clone URL could dial a host it never appeared to name.** `url.Parse` strips userinfo before filling `Host`, so `entire://real-cluster.entire.io@evil.com/...` validated `evil.com` and the CLI would fetch `/.well-known/entire-cluster.json` from it. The authority is now validated as it was typed, which is what puts the userinfo in front of the check that already refuses it.\\n- **An interrupted command could still report success.** Whether the command was stopped is the context's answer, not an inference from the read's error — the old check depended on every wrapper preserving the error chain, and missed the read succeeding just as the cancellation landed.\\n\\n## Breaking changes\\n\\n- **`entire repo mirror get` is gone.** Use `entire repo view`. It is in the deprecation ledger, so no help string can advertise it again.\\n- **No ULID is carried over, and `--project` is gone from `repo view`.** A ULID and a bare name find a repository; they do not name one. `repo edit`, `repo delete` and the `visibility`/`protection` subtrees still take both — narrowing the shared resolver is its own change. `repo create`'s recovery hints print the repo's path now, since a hint has to name a ref the command accepts.\\n- **`repo view --json` gains keys; it does not replace the object.** An earlier revision of this branch substituted the directory row for the repo record, which dropped `capabilities`, `provider`, `owningProjectId` and six more to `null` at exit 0 — `.capabilities.canPush` is a permissions answer, and `null` is falsy to jq. It now answers with the record the server returned plus what the view worked out, the way `repo create --json` has always added `remote`. So create and view describe a repo the same way, and the only changes a consumer must know are:\\n  - `placements[]` is new — one entry per cluster, each with `cluster` (the public **host**), `clusterSlug`, `jurisdiction`, `status`, `cloneUrl`, and `role` for a native repo. Omitted when nothing holds the repo, as a GitHub candidate omits it.\\n  - `repo`, `private` and `status` are added alongside `path`, `visibility` and `state` — the spellings `mirror list --json` uses, so the common core parses the same for either forge. The record's own keys are unchanged.\\n  - `private` is **absent**, never `false`, when the server stated no visibility. An absent field must not read as an answer on the question asked to confirm a repo is restricted.\\n- **`repo mirror list --cluster` takes the public host.** It is a client-side filter over the printed rows, so it can only match the spelling the CLUSTER column carries. A value the catalog cannot name is now an error rather than an empty result — except a cluster whose `publicUrl` is unusable, which the column prints under its slug and the filter therefore accepts.\\n- **`--authoritative` changed meaning, and now keeps its word.** The authoritative read happens either way — it is what makes the primary's STATUS mean anything — so the flag says only whether a readiness answer is *required*. Without it a failed readiness read dashes the cell, warns on stderr, and the view still renders. With it, a 200 whose body omits `state` is a failure too: the read succeeded and still cannot confirm the repo is usable, which is exactly what the flag promises to refuse. `repo create`'s readiness wait has always refused the same answer.\\n\\n## Deliberately left out\\n\\nThe human header is name and visibility only. The owning project is already spelled inside the name, and the repo ULID is an addressing detail on its way out, so both live in `--json`. The provision reason **moved** rather than went: it is the primary's equivalent of a mirror's `lastError` — the STATUS cell says a repo failed to provision and it is the only thing that says why — so it joins the per-placement notes on stderr, where a piped table or `--json` stays clean.\\n\\n`entire cluster list` is now the last place a column headed CLUSTER prints a slug. Settling that is its own change, and so is converging `repo clone` onto the cluster catalog, which lives in a file this branch does not touch.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n`go test ./cmd/entire/cli/... ./docs/development/` and `mise run lint` are green on the merged tree. `mise run check` was last green before the most recent merge from main; it has not completed since, so treat CI as the arbiter for the full `-race` suite.\\n\\nEvery input form was exercised against production: the `/et/` path, a `/gh/` ref, a repo ULID, a bare name with `--project`, and an `entire://` clone URL in **both** forges, including one pasted with a trailing `.git`.\\n\\nThe control-plane E2E was updated but **not run**: it creates real resources on the shared account and needs an explicit go-ahead. That is also the only place the `waitForRepoClonable` fix is exercised, so it is worth running before merge.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2547/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2547/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1995\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1995/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1995/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1995/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1995\",\n              \"id\": 5151833785,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7_GruZ\",\n              \"number\": 1995,\n              \"title\": \"fix(trail): send the pre-image anchor with --patch suggested changes\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-14T13:01:13Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-17T07:30:35Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-17T07:30:33Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1995\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1995\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1995.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1995.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-17T07:30:33Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1048\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\n`entire trail finding add --patch/--patch-file` has **never once succeeded**. The CLI built the suggested change from `change_type` + `patch` + `instruction` and nothing else, but the API requires a full pre-image anchor for any non-`manual_instruction` change:\\n\\n```go\\n// entire-api internal/store/suggested_changes.go (and the identical BFF check)\\npatch → expected_file_path → expected_file_hash\\n      → expected_start_line → expected_end_line → expected_lines\\n```\\n\\n`expected_file_path` was just the first check to fail; filling only that field would have moved the error to `expected_file_hash`. Every call came back with `invalid_request: unified_diff change requires expected_file_path`, so only `--instruction` ever got through — which is why CLI-created findings carry prose instead of diffs, and why `entire trail finding apply` had no CLI-created patches to apply.\\n\\n## Since when\\n\\nBroken since the flags shipped.\\n\\n| When | What |\\n|---|---|\\n| 2026-05-18 | Server-side requirement lands in entire.io |\\n| 2026-06-05 | `43067b86d` adds `--patch`/`--patch-file`, sending only `change_type` + `patch` |\\n| 2026-06-11 | `38e470409` fixes the endpoint and surfaces per-item errors — the failure becomes visible |\\n\\nNo version of `trail_review_cmd.go` has ever assigned `ExpectedFilePath` (verified across all 29 commits touching the file).\\n\\n**Measured impact.** Scanning every agent transcript on one machine (954 files, 142k records): 92 real `trail finding add` invocations, 68 successful — all `-m`/`--instruction` only. 10 used `--patch`; 9 failed with this exact error across 6 review sessions on 3 separate days, and the 1 success is the verification call for this branch. Six times an agent reached for a machine-applicable fix and silently fell back to prose.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\nDerive the anchor from the patch plus the worktree:\\n\\n- **path + line span** — parsed from the diff headers and the old-side `@@` ranges, spanning min-start to max-end across hunks\\n- **`expected_lines`** — the byte-exact pre-image slice, line endings intact (deliberately *not* CRLF-normalized like `selected_text`)\\n- **`expected_file_hash`** — the git blob OID, so it matches `git hash-object <file>`, read through the repository's object format so a sha256 repo isn't handed a sha1 value\\n\\nCases the API would reject now fail locally with an actionable message instead of a server error: multi-file patches, file-creation patches (`--- /dev/null` has no pre-image to anchor to → use `--instruction`), hunks past EOF, missing files. Patch paths run through the same whole-patch safety check the apply path already used, so a patch is held to one standard whether it's being written or applied.\\n\\n## Behavior changes\\n\\nTwo, both deliberate:\\n\\n- **A `--patch` with no `--file` now gets a location.** It previously produced a locationless `whole_change` finding even though the patch named the file and lines exactly. It now lands on the patch's file and full hunk span (`Location: .gitignore:3-5`). An explicit `--file`/`--line` still wins — the anchor only fills a gap.\\n- **A `--file` naming a different file than the patch modifies is rejected**, rather than storing a finding whose location and fix point at different places. The API forces single-file patches, so there's no sensible reading of that state.\\n\\nA line-range disagreement (`--line 45` with hunks at 10–20) is deliberately **not** checked: pointing at where a problem manifests while fixing elsewhere in the same file is legitimate.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- Posted real findings with `--patch-file` to a trail: accepted, `unified_diff` with the right file, location derived correctly. Mismatch guard rejects as expected. Test findings dismissed.\\n- `mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci` all clean.\\n- New unit tests cover the full anchor payload (via `reflect.DeepEqual` on the whole request, which caught that the stored patch is trimmed), the location defaulting and precedence, the mismatch rejection, and six parser rejection cases.\\n\\n## Open questions for review\\n\\n- **`expected_file_hash` has no consumer** anywhere — CLI, cell, or frontend — and no documented algorithm. I picked the git blob OID because it's repo-native and hand-verifiable, and documented the convention on the API type. Worth pinning down while there's still only one producer: a later consumer computing it differently would read every CLI-created suggestion as stale.\\n- **Hash source is the worktree, not the review head blob.** The worktree is consistent with the patch (both written against the same tree); the head blob would be reproducible by the server. Reasonable people differ — flagging rather than deciding unilaterally.\\n\\n## Follow-ups not taken\\n\\n- `gitBlobHash` is now the third \\\"git blob hash of content\\\" in the tree (`strategy/content_overlap.go:534`, `checkpoint/migrate.go:234`); extracting into `gitrepo` is a clean mechanical follow-up.\\n- The anchor parser and the apply path's `validateUnifiedDiffPatchPaths` still scan the patch separately; unifying them means touching the apply path, which deserves its own diff.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> <sup>[Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) is generating a summary for commit ea829fbb1c8e77b835d86071aedd4f92123de489. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1995/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1995/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1747\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1747/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1747/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1747/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1747\",\n              \"id\": 4883662052,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7xkrTG\",\n              \"number\": 1747,\n              \"title\": \"Remove long-deprecated commands and aliases\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"id\": 881031,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-07-14T13:44:29Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-12T13:46:08Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-12T13:46:07Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1747\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1747\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1747.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1747.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-12T13:46:07Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/853\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\n## What\\r\\n\\r\\nDeletes the CLI surface that has carried deprecation notices for a long time:\\r\\n\\r\\n| Removed | Replacement |\\r\\n|---|---|\\r\\n| `entire reset` | `entire clean --session <id>` / `entire clean --all` |\\r\\n| `entire rewind` + `entire checkpoint rewind` | none (deprecation announced removal) |\\r\\n| hidden top-level shortcuts `resume`, `attach`, `explain`, `trace` | `session resume`, `session attach`, `checkpoint explain`, `doctor trace` |\\r\\n\\r\\nAlso removes code that only those commands used: `hideAsAlias` (aliascmd.go), all of rewind.go (~1300 lines), `TruncateTranscriptAtUUID`, and `writeTranscript`. The `unknownSessionID` const moved from rewind.go to state.go.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Test changes\\r\\n\\r\\n`checkpoint rewind --list` was the observability mechanism for many checkpoint tests, so removing the command required reworking them:\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Deleted** tests whose subject was rewind behavior itself: integration `rewind_test.go`, `logs_only_rewind_test.go`, e2e `rewind_test.go`, `TestOpenCodeRewind`, `TestShadow_RewindAndCondensation`, the untracked-file-preservation-during-rewind tests, and rewind phases inside broader workflow tests.\\r\\n- **Adapted** tests that used rewind points only to observe checkpoint creation: they now assert directly against shadow-branch contents (`BranchExists`, `FileExistsInBranch`, `ReadFileFromBranch`, `tasks/<tool-use-id>/` metadata paths, session `StepCount`).\\r\\n- TestEnv rewind helpers and the e2e `RewindList/Rewind/RewindLogsOnly` wrappers are gone; the factory e2e test polls shadow-branch trees for `/tasks/` paths instead.\\r\\n- `attach --review` unit tests now invoke the canonical `session attach` path.\\r\\n- Docs updated: README (quick start, command table, feature claims, troubleshooting), CLAUDE.md command layout, e2e README.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Deliberately out of scope\\r\\n\\r\\nThe strategy-level rewind machinery (`strategy.Rewind`, `GetRewindPoints`, `manual_commit_rewind.go`) still exists but now has no CLI callers. Removing it cascades much wider; follow-up PR if desired.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Verification\\r\\n\\r\\n- `golangci-lint run ./...` — 0 issues\\r\\n- `mise run test` — passes except `TestExplainCmd_PositionalArgConflictsWithFlags` / `TestExplainCmd_SummaryTimeoutSecondsValidation`, which fail identically on an unmodified tree in this environment (the repo's own `.entire/settings.local.json` has `enabled: false`, so `checkDisabledGuard` short-circuits before validation) — pre-existing, unrelated\\r\\n- `mise run test:integration` — pass\\r\\n- `mise run test:e2e:canary` (Vogon) — pass\\r\\n\\r\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\r\\n\\r\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n> [!NOTE]\\r\\n> **High Risk**\\r\\n> This is a breaking CLI change that removes rewind-based file recovery; users and scripts must migrate to `session resume`/`clean`, and leftover strategy rewind code could confuse future maintenance until removed.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> **Overview**\\r\\n> **Removes deprecated CLI surface** that had been announced for removal: `entire reset` (use `entire clean`), `entire rewind` and `entire checkpoint rewind` (no replacement), and hidden shortcuts `resume`, `attach`, `explain`, and `trace` in favor of `session` / `checkpoint` / `doctor` group commands. **`hideAsAlias`**, **`reset.go`**, **`rewind.go`**, and related helpers/tests go away with them.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> **Docs and UX copy** no longer promote rewind; recovery is framed as **`entire session resume`**. README and `CLAUDE.md` command layout are aligned with the slimmer tree.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> **Tests** drop rewind-specific suites (`rewind_test.go`, `logs_only_rewind_test.go`, etc.) and stop using `checkpoint rewind --list` as an observability hook. Remaining integration tests assert checkpoint creation via **shadow branch** state (`BranchExists`, `FileExistsInBranch`, session `StepCount`). Attach tests call **`session attach`** canonically.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> Also bumps **`.opencode`** `@opencode-ai/plugin` **1.4.7 → 1.14.28**. Strategy-level rewind APIs remain in the codebase but have **no CLI callers** (follow-up noted in the PR).\\r\\n> \\r\\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 47f100f192faaf7193ccef5387eba494c013bab7. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\r\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\r\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1747/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1747/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1729\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1729/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1729/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1729/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1729\",\n              \"id\": 4864998186,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7wqDH4\",\n              \"number\": 1729,\n              \"title\": \"fix(codex): write hook config to the location codex expects\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"entire[bot]\",\n                \"id\": 254015822,\n                \"node_id\": \"BOT_kgDODyP5Tg\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/2626939?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/entire\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"Bot\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 2,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-07-12T01:55:03Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-15T08:56:43Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-15T08:56:43Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1729\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1729\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1729.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1729.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Trail: https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/836\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n- `entire enable --agent codex` writes a project-local `.codex/config.toml` to enable the hooks feature. When the repo lives inside `<CODEX_HOME>/agents/...` (the tree Codex recursively scans for custom agent-role TOML files), that config.toml gets picked up by Codex's role-file scanner and rejected at startup as a malformed agent role definition (missing `developer_instructions`).\\n- Scope the feature flag into the global `config.toml` instead, under `[projects.\\\"<repoRoot>\\\".features]`, whenever `repoRoot` falls inside that reserved tree, so no TOML file is ever written there. `hooks.json` (JSON, not scanned by Codex's role discovery) keeps installing at the normal project-local path.\\n- Self-heals: a stale project-local `.codex/config.toml` left behind by an older entire version is removed once it contains nothing but the feature-flag content this package manages; files with unrelated content are left alone.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\nLive-reproduced and verified against the real `codex` binary (`codex-cli 0.139.0`), using an isolated temp `HOME`/`CODEX_HOME` for every run — real `~/.codex` was never touched (confirmed unchanged before/after).\\n\\n**Before fix** — repo at `~/.codex/agents/repos/project`, run `entire enable --agent codex`, then `codex exec`:\\n```\\nwarning: Ignoring malformed agent role definition: agent role file at\\n.../.codex/agents/repos/project/.codex/config.toml must define `developer_instructions`\\n```\\n\\n**After fix** — same repo layout and same `codex exec` invocation: no `.codex/config.toml` is created (only `.codex/hooks.json`), the flag lands in `<CODEX_HOME>/config.toml` under `[projects.\\\"...\\\".features]`, and the warning is gone.\\n\\nAlso verified:\\n- Enable against a pre-existing global `config.toml` carrying unrelated custom keys and another project's own scoped section — both preserved untouched.\\n- Re-enable is idempotent — no duplicate sections or lines.\\n- A stale local `config.toml` left by an older entire version (the exact bug artifact from the issue) is cleaned up on next enable; a local `config.toml` carrying unrelated user content is left alone.\\n\\nNew regression tests cover all of the above in `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/hooks_test.go`.\\n\\n- [x] `gofmt -l` clean\\n- [x] `golangci-lint run` (full repo) — 0 issues\\n- [x] `go test -race ./...` — all packages pass\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/...`\\n\\n## Audit hardening\\n\\nA follow-up audit pass tightened three sharp edges, each with mutation-verified tests:\\n\\n- **No TOML injection into the global config.** `repoRoot` is a filesystem path embedded into `[projects.\\\"<repoRoot>\\\".features]`. The key now escapes every TOML-significant character (quote, backslash, newline, other control chars). Previously a path containing a `\\\"` or a newline could terminate the quoted key early and inject arbitrary lines into the shared global `config.toml`; a newline also split the header across physical lines and broke idempotency. Reproduced live: a repo directory whose name contained a newline injected a rogue line into the global config before the fix, and no longer does.\\n- **No lost updates or torn writes on the global config.** The read-modify-write is now serialized under a cross-process advisory lock (`internal/flock`) and swapped in atomically (`jsonutil.WriteFileAtomic`). Two concurrent `entire enable` runs for different repos under `CODEX_HOME/agents` could previously clobber each other's edits; a concurrent stress test reproduces the lost update without the lock and passes with it (green under `-race`).\\n- **Self-heal never deletes user data.** Stale-config detection is now line-anchored (every non-blank line must be exactly a managed feature line or the `[features]` header) instead of substring stripping, which could collapse unrelated content to whitespace and delete a file this package never wrote.\\n- Also fixed `isUnderCodexAgentsDir` so a directory literally named `..foo` under the agents tree is correctly detected as inside it.\\n\\nRe-verified end-to-end against `codex-cli 0.139.0` in an isolated temp `HOME`/`CODEX_HOME`: fresh install, existing-keys-preserved, idempotent re-enable, stale-heal, and unrelated-content-preserved all behave correctly, and the real `~/.codex` was confirmed untouched (byte-identical `config.toml`/`agents` tree before and after).\\n\\nFixes #842\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1729/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1729/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1495\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1495/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1495/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1495/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1495\",\n              \"id\": 4720509499,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7pXrSG\",\n              \"number\": 1495,\n              \"title\": \"checkpoint: split into persistent/ephemeral stores with generic Read/Write\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-06-22T21:00:42Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-24T11:00:16Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-06-24T11:00:12Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1495\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1495\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1495.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1495.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-06-24T11:00:12Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/639\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What\\n\\nThe persistent/ephemeral rework of the checkpoint store (issue #1433 follow-up; addresses the naming/abstraction review feedback). Done as a series of small, individually reviewable commits, each validated with `codex exec review` before the next.\\n\\n**Structural split** — `GitStore` no longer does both jobs:\\n- `GitStore` is now the **persistent** (committed) store.\\n- a new independent **`ephemeralStore`** owns the shadow-branch (temporary) surface; the two share only package-level helpers.\\n\\n**Generic, symmetric surface** on both stores (the review's `sto.Persistent.Read()` / `sto.Ephemeral().Read()` shape): `Read` (differentiated by return type), `List`, and `Write` (a sealed request union) on each.\\n\\n**Writes named by scope** — the union says *what* is written, not the verb (the method is already `Write`):\\n- Persistent: `Write(Session{…} | SessionTranscript{…} | SessionSummary{…} | CheckpointAttribution{…})` — three session-level requests and one checkpoint-level.\\n- Ephemeral: `Write(Step{…} | TaskStep{…})` — a session step and a subagent task step (both produce an ephemeral shadow-branch checkpoint; named to match the strategy's `SaveStep`/`SaveTaskStep`). Bare nouns like `checkpoint.Checkpoint` were rejected (stutter; both requests write the same artifact).\\n\\n**Reads tiered by the same scope split:**\\n- `CheckpointReader` (`Read`, `List`) — checkpoint-level.\\n- `SessionReader` (`ReadSessionContent`, `ReadSessionMetadata`, `ReadSessionPrompts`, `ReadSessionMetadataAndPrompts`) — session-level.\\n- `PersistentStore` composes `CheckpointReader + SessionReader + Writer`; callers depend on the narrowest tier they need.\\n\\n**Vocabulary** — \\\"Committed\\\"/\\\"Temporary\\\" → \\\"Persistent\\\"/\\\"Ephemeral\\\" throughout (types, methods, the `Type` enum, `CommittedRefs`→`PersistentRefs`, file names), plus `InitialAttribution`→`Attribution` (only one attribution type; \\\"Initial\\\" was misleading).\\n\\n**Facade**: `Stores.Primary`→`Stores.Persistent`, `Stores.Temporary()`→`Stores.Ephemeral()`.\\n\\n## Commits\\n\\nSplit & vocabulary:\\n1. drop redundant `createCommit` wrapper\\n2. **split** the temporary store out of `GitStore` → `ephemeralStore`\\n3. `InitialAttribution` → `Attribution`\\n4. persistent type renames (`CommittedStore`→`PersistentStore`, …)\\n5. persistent reads → generic `Read`/`List`\\n6. persistent writes → `Write(WriteRequest)` only\\n7. ephemeral type renames\\n8. ephemeral reads → generic `Read`/`List`\\n9. ephemeral writes → `Write(EphemeralWriteRequest)`\\n10. facade → `Persistent`/`Ephemeral()`\\n11. file renames (`committed.go`→`persistent.go`, `temporary.go`→`ephemeral.go`, …)\\n12. finish vocabulary (`Type` consts, `CommittedRefs`)\\n13. docs\\n\\nScope-based API (added after review):\\n14. fix stale API references in doc comments\\n15. **name persistent Write requests by scope** (`Session` / `SessionTranscript` / `SessionSummary` / `CheckpointAttribution`) — this commit also keeps the unrelated `agent.Agent.WriteSession` method untouched (an earlier draft over-renamed it; corrected here)\\n16. **tier the read surface** into `CheckpointReader` / `SessionReader`\\n17. **name ephemeral Write requests by scope** (`WriteCheckpoint`→`Step`, `WriteTask`→`TaskStep`)\\n\\nThen: merged latest `main` and moved the store-interface `ireturn` suppressions from inline `//nolint` to the `.golangci.yaml` allow-list (`checkpoint.PersistentStore` / `EphemeralStore` / `CheckpointReader`), matching main's convention.\\n\\n## Notes / known follow-up\\n- Both `Write` unions use value-receiver markers, so a pointer (`*Session`, `*Step`) also satisfies the interface but hits the dispatcher's `default` (errors at runtime via `%T`). Codex flagged this (P3); address both unions together rather than diverging.\\n- Stacked on this: **#1504** extracts the now-persistent-named contract into `github.com/entireio/cli/api/checkpoint`.\\n\\n## Verification\\n`go build ./...`, full `go test ./...`, and `mise run lint` (0 issues) green; commits validated with `codex exec review`.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1495/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1495/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1422\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1422/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1422/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1422/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1422\",\n              \"id\": 4646555505,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7lnoSx\",\n              \"number\": 1422,\n              \"title\": \"Add remote plugin install, index discovery, and plugin dependencies\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"ashtom\",\n                \"id\": 70720,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzIw\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70720?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/ashtom\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 10,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-06-12T05:21:21Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-10T19:42:45Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-10T19:42:44Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1422\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1422\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1422.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1422.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-10T19:42:43Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/973\\r\\n\\r\\n## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nExpands the kubectl-style external-command layer so users can discover and install plugins without cloning anything, from any git host. 18 files, ~5,540 insertions.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Remote install** — `entire plugin install <name|url|path>`. Newest **stable** semver tag via `git ls-remote` (forge-agnostic, inherits git auth and proxies; no forge REST client anywhere). Optional `entire-plugin.yml` metadata read via blobless shallow clone. Release assets download over HTTPS through a small per-host URL convention table (GitHub/Gitea-style, GitLab-style, `download_url` template escape hatch), selected and verified against the release's `checksums.txt`. Binaries land in `pkg/<name>/` with a provenance `manifest.yml`; `bin/` stays the only dispatch surface and the resolver in `plugin.go` is untouched.\\r\\n- **Upgrade** — `entire plugin upgrade [name|--all]`, `--pin` to hold a tag, next-highest-tag fallback for pushed-but-unpublished releases, Windows locked-binary rename-aside.\\r\\n- **Discovery** — krew-style git-synced index ([entireio/plugin-index](https://github.com/entireio/plugin-index)): shallow-cloned into the user cache keyed by URL hash, flock-guarded, 24h TTL, stale-copy-on-offline. Six new subcommands (`upgrade`, `search`, `info`, `browse`, `doctor`, `index update`) join the pre-existing `install`/`list`/`remove`; bare-name installs resolve through the index. Index URL: `--index` > `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_INDEX_URL` > built-in default.\\r\\n- **Dependencies** — `entire-plugin.yml` `requires` (`name` + optional `min_version`, no ranges), resolved by name through the index. Install-time transitive planning, apt-style single confirmation, remove guard for depended-on plugins, and `entire plugin doctor`. Dispatch stays zero-cost — no runtime dependency checks.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Security model\\r\\n\\r\\nThis code ends in downloading a binary and making it executable, so the trust boundaries are the design:\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Transport.** HTTPS required for anything off-machine, re-validated on every redirect hop (Go follows redirects across schemes; validating only the entry point is bypassable). Loopback exempt so `httptest` fixtures work.\\r\\n- **Authentication.** A release that publishes no `checksums.txt` for the platform is **refused by default**; `--allow-unverified` opts in, is recorded in the manifest, reported by `doctor`, and inherited by `upgrade`.\\r\\n- **Integrity.** The installed binary's digest is recorded as `binary_sha256` and re-checked by `doctor`. (`sha256` covers the downloaded *asset*, which is discarded with the staging dir — provenance only.)\\r\\n- **URLs reaching git.** Every repo/index URL is scheme-validated by one definition and every git invocation passes `--` before positionals. Repo URLs are attacker-influenced (index entries, `--index`, env), and git reads an option-shaped positional as an option — `--upload-pack`'s value is shell-interpreted.\\r\\n- **The trust root is not repo-choosable.** The index URL cannot be set from committed settings; see below.\\r\\n- **Names.** The installed name comes from the remote, so callers that already committed to a name pass it as a required argument and a mismatch is fatal.\\r\\n- **Credentials.** Userinfo and query strings are stripped from every URL before printing, logging, or persisting (`.entire/logs/` is inside the working tree and `doctor bundle` collects it wholesale; `manifest.yml` is mode 0644).\\r\\n\\r\\nNot claimed: **authenticity**. `checksums.txt` shares an origin with the asset, so it proves integrity in transit, not publisher identity. Real authenticity needs signatures.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Design notes\\r\\n\\r\\n- Built on the recorded founding decisions of this layer: PATH dispatch unchanged, built-ins win, `agent-` prefix reserved, env filtering untouched, no new telemetry.\\r\\n- The only forge-specific code is the download-URL convention table; version listing, metadata, and the index all ride on the git protocol. No `go-github`-class dependency (uses existing `gopkg.in/yaml.v3` + `golang.org/x/mod`).\\r\\n- **The plugin layer reads no settings at all.** The `settings` package is byte-identical to `main`.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Changed since this description was first written\\r\\n\\r\\nThe branch was reviewed (Bugbot ×5 rounds, Copilot, four trail agent reviews, and a three-agent adversarial pass), then merged with `main` (2053 commits). Reviewers should know these are new:\\r\\n\\r\\n**Behavior changes**\\r\\n1. Checksums are now **required** by default (`--allow-unverified` opts out). Previously a release without them installed silently.\\r\\n2. `http://` and `git://` are no longer accepted for repo or index URLs — unauthenticated transports, and the catalog decides what installs without a prompt.\\r\\n3. Prereleases are excluded from tag resolution. `v2.0.0-rc1` outranks stable `v1.9.0` in semver, so `upgrade --all` was migrating users onto release candidates.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Removals**\\r\\n4. **`plugins.index_url` and `plugins.index_ttl_hours` are gone.** `.entire/settings.json` is committed and resolved from the working directory, while an index-listed plugin installs with *no prompt* — so a cloned repo could redirect the catalog and get an attacker-chosen binary onto `PATH` silently. The setting's value was that contributors got a different catalog *without knowing*, which is the vulnerability stated as a feature. Internal catalogs now use `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_INDEX_URL`, which applies across repos and cannot be chosen by checked-out content. Go takes the same position with `GOPROXY`; npm's per-project registry is the cautionary counter-example.\\r\\n5. **`requires[].repo_url` is gone.** Dependencies resolve by name through the index, so a dependency's URL comes from the curated catalog rather than the requiring plugin's author — planning contacted that URL *before* the confirmation prompt. A user can still install an out-of-catalog dependency themselves, with the usual prompt; the authority moved to the user.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Fixes worth naming**\\r\\n6. Argument injection into the git CLI allowing arbitrary command execution from a malicious index entry or dependency URL — verified live on the pre-fix tree, on a path that never prompts.\\r\\n7. `entire-plugin.yml` now decodes **leniently**. Strict decoding meant the first author to adopt any future field would break installs on every older CLI, permanently. This is also what made removals 4 and 5 migration-free for already-published files.\\r\\n8. Silent truncation of archive entries over 512 MiB, index-cache races (now flock-guarded), a diamond `min_version` skip, `darwin_all` universal binaries never matching, empty `entire-plugin.yml` being fatal, `index_ttl_hours` overflowing to \\\"always stale\\\", and credential leaks through download errors.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Testing\\r\\n\\r\\n- 77 unit tests against `file://` git repos and `httptest` asset servers (zero real network in CI), covering tag resolution, asset selection/verification, extraction guards, index sync/TTL/offline/concurrency, dependency planning, doctor.\\r\\n- 4 integration tests drive the spawned binary end to end (install/dispatch, unlisted-URL gating, dependencies + remove guard, search/info): bare-name install → real dispatch → dependency install → remove guard → doctor exit code. They run the **verified** path — no test passes `--allow-unverified`, so their passing is the proof that verification succeeds.\\r\\n- Security regressions assert the stronger property where it matters: that an injected payload never executes and that credentials never appear, not merely that a call errors. Each was verified RED against the pre-fix tree.\\r\\n- `mise run check` green (fmt, lint, unit + integration + Vogon canary).\\r\\n\\r\\n## Docs\\r\\n\\r\\n- `docs/architecture/external-commands.md` — remote install, plugin index, dependencies, and the trust-boundary sections.\\r\\n- README — user-facing Plugins section.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Open, deliberately\\r\\n\\r\\n- `browse` and `index.json`'s `platforms` are candidates to cut — `browse` adds no capability over `search` + `install` and installs unprompted; `platforms` warns but never enforces.\\r\\n- `min_version` is not enforced on the install *outcome* (the planner computes a constraint nothing downstream checks), and dependencies have no `auto_installed` marker, so orphans leak.\\r\\n- Two notions of \\\"official\\\": the `officialPlugins` telemetry allowlist and `index.json`'s `official` flag.\\r\\n- `entire upgrade` (the self-update plugin) vs `entire plugin upgrade` (plugins).\\r\\n- Follow-up outside this branch: a credential-redaction pass at `main.go`'s error print. `%w`-wrapped `url.Error` leaks the full URL regardless of call-site discipline, because `net/url.Error.Error()` does no redaction.\\r\\n- Outside this repo: `graph` should be added to `entireio/plugin-index`, or `entire plugin install brain` reports its dependency as unindexed.\\r\\n\\r\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\r\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1422/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1422/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1573\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1573/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1573/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1573/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1573\",\n              \"id\": 4772400160,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7r_8KF\",\n              \"number\": 1573,\n              \"title\": \"Add hidden experts CLI command\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"id\": 257360244,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-06-29T23:40:28Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-01T13:27:34Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-01T13:27:32Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1573\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1573\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1573.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1573.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-01T13:27:32Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/709\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\n## What is this?\\r\\n\\r\\nAdds a hidden/labs CLI command: **`entire experts`**.\\r\\n\\r\\nBefore you edit an unfamiliar part of a repo, it answers:\\r\\n\\r\\n> **“Which agents already have real evidence for this code — and what did they use?”**\\r\\n\\r\\nIt is **agent/workflow provenance**, not a human popularity list. The output ranks prior **Codex / Claude / Cursor** (etc.) sessions by evidence: matching checkpoints, agent-attributed lines, skills invoked, tools used, MCP servers, and files touched — **without** exposing raw prompts or chat transcripts.\\r\\n\\r\\nDiscover it via `entire labs` (listed as experimental).\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## Example usage\\r\\n\\r\\n**Directory scope** (most common — “who knows this package?”):\\r\\n\\r\\n```bash\\r\\nentire experts cmd/entire/cli/\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n**Single file**:\\r\\n\\r\\n```bash\\r\\nentire experts cmd/entire/cli/experts_cmd.go\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n**Explicit repo** (`owner/repo` resolves to a repo ULID via your accessible repo list; ULIDs also accepted):\\r\\n\\r\\n```bash\\r\\nentire experts cmd/entire/cli/ --repo entireio/cli --limit 5\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n**Staged files** (what am I about to commit?):\\r\\n\\r\\n```bash\\r\\nentire experts --staged\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n**Interactive browse** (TTY only — two-pane viewer, session links open on entire.io):\\r\\n\\r\\n```bash\\r\\nentire experts cmd/entire/cli/ --tui\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n**JSON** (for scripts / agents):\\r\\n\\r\\n```bash\\r\\nentire experts cmd/entire/cli/ --json\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n**Natural-language query** (requires code-search index on the API cell; otherwise 503 with a setup hint):\\r\\n\\r\\n```bash\\r\\nentire experts \\\"stripe webhook retry logic\\\" --repo entireio/cli\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## Example output (plain text)\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\nAgent provenance for entireio/cli (main)\\r\\n\\r\\nCodex\\r\\n  evidence: 1 sessions, 1 matching checkpoints, 9 steps, 142 agent-attributed lines\\r\\n  skills: go-cli (2)\\r\\n  tools: shell (4), search (3)\\r\\n  mcp: github (1)\\r\\n  files: cmd/entire/cli/experts_cmd.go\\r\\n  - feat: experts provenance  - 1 checkpoints, 9 steps\\r\\n\\r\\nClaude Code\\r\\n  evidence: 1 sessions, 1 matching checkpoints, 14 steps, 210 agent-attributed lines\\r\\n  skills: go-cli (1), tui (1)\\r\\n  tools: fileOps (6)\\r\\n  mcp: github (2)\\r\\n  files: cmd/entire/cli/experts_cmd.go, cmd/entire/cli/experts_tui.go\\r\\n  - TUI polish  - 1 checkpoints, 14 steps\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nSession names are **clickable links** (OSC 8) to `https://entire.io/gh/{owner}/{repo}/session/{id}` when running in a capable terminal.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## How it works (short)\\r\\n\\r\\n1. You pass a **path scope**, **staged files**, or a **natural-language query**.\\r\\n2. The CLI resolves `--repo` (git origin, `owner/repo`, or repo ULID) and calls the data API:\\r\\n   - `GET /api/v1/repos` — resolve `owner/repo` → ULID (authz-safe)\\r\\n   - `POST /api/v1/repos/{id}/experts` — rank agent provenance for the scope\\r\\n3. The API (now on **entire-api**, merged in [entirehq/entire-api#126](https://github.com/entirehq/entire-api/pull/126)) searches checkpoint/session history for file matches and returns residency-safe summaries.\\r\\n4. The CLI renders ranked profiles (plain, `--json`, or `--tui`).\\r\\n\\r\\n**Privacy:** JSON/plain/TUI only surface agent evidence fields (sessions, counts, skills, tools, matched files). No prompts, emails, or human author identity.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## What changed in this PR\\r\\n\\r\\n- Hidden top-level `experts` command + `entire labs` listing\\r\\n- Flags: `--repo`, `--branch`, `--limit`, `--json`, `--staged`, `--tui`, hidden `--insecure-http-auth`\\r\\n- Scope handling: local paths (incl. from subdirs), deleted path-like scopes, absolute paths in worktree, `--staged` additions/renames/deletions\\r\\n- Retarget from legacy cache route to **entire-api** `POST /api/v1/repos/{id}/experts`\\r\\n- TUI: two-pane agent list + evidence detail; `j/k` navigate, `tab` sections, `enter` expand sessions, `o` open session, `q` quit\\r\\n- Data API auth: loopback HTTP discovery for local dev when `--insecure-http-auth` is set\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## Screenshots\\r\\n\\r\\n**TUI (`--tui`)** \\r\\n<img width=\\\"893\\\" height=\\\"506\\\" alt=\\\"Screenshot 2026-07-01 at 9 11 17 AM\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f427a12d-9deb-405e-af6f-a836cee2d674\\\" />\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## Verification\\r\\n\\r\\n- GitHub checks on head `d0c782b5d`: license, lint, binary-size, test-core, test-canary, test-integration (a/b/c), test — all passed\\r\\n- Trail [709](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/709): 0 open findings\\r\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run Experts -count=1`\\r\\n\\r\\n## Companion\\r\\n\\r\\n- API (merged): [entirehq/entire-api#126](https://github.com/entirehq/entire-api/pull/126)\\r\\n- Supersedes retired entire.io cache route PR\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1573/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1573/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1606\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1606/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1606/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1606/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1606\",\n              \"id\": 4795760023,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7tMLf0\",\n              \"number\": 1606,\n              \"title\": \"De-slop: remove dead code, deduplicate hot spots (−5.6k lines)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-07-02T15:12:00Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-03T16:17:54Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-03T16:17:51Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1606\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1606\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1606.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1606.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-03T16:17:51Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/732\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n# De-slop: remove dead code, deduplicate hot spots\\n\\nRepo-wide simplification pass. Signals came from `x/tools deadcode` (rooted at\\n`./cmd/entire` and `./cmd/git-remote-entire`), `mise run dup`, and golangci.\\nEvery deletion was classified first: functions unreachable from the entry\\npoints were only removed when nothing outside their own dead cluster (or tests\\ndedicated solely to them) referenced them. Test seams (`*ForTest`, fault\\nstores, fixtures) that exercise live code were kept.\\n\\nEach commit is self-contained and could be split into its own PR.\\n\\n## Dead code removed\\n\\n- **strategy/trailers/clusterdiscovery**: checkpoint-lite decode cluster + its\\n  bench file, `IsInsideWorktree`/`GetMainRepoRoot`, `extractUserPrompts`\\n  cluster, `subtractFiles`, dead trailer parse/format helpers,\\n  `RenderLoginHint` wrapper.\\n- **cli root package**: dead `metadata.go` (task-checkpoint IO superseded by\\n  the strategy package), dead task-hook parsers, `runExplainDefault` wrappers,\\n  `formatSessionInfo`, `hasCodeChanges`, `GetMergeBase`,\\n  `findNewUntrackedFiles`, dead trail list/context/resume wrappers,\\n  cli-package `GetTranscriptPosition`.\\n- **cli subpackages**: dead `auth/repo_token.go` (superseded by\\n  `internal/entireclient/repocreds`), test-only `checkpoint/blob_resolver.go`,\\n  `CatFiles` cluster in checkpoint/remote, dead path-based transcript variants\\n  in factoryaidroid/geminicli, `agentimport.Get`, `api.ResolveURL`,\\n  `gitremote.ExtractOwnerFromRemoteURL`, and friends.\\n\\n## Deduplication (each backed by existing or backfilled tests)\\n\\n- `agent/capabilities.go`: 13 hand-rolled `As*` gates → two generic helpers.\\n- Per-agent hook parsers (claudecode, geminicli, factoryaidroid, vogon):\\n  repeated `sessionInfoRaw` parsing folded into one helper per agent.\\n- `search`: seven `Result*` accessors → shared `resultField` dispatch, plus\\n  backfilled coverage for the accessors/nil-guards that had none.\\n- `settings`: project/local raw IO pairs and string-map merges unified.\\n- `redact`: OPF span→region conversion shared across the three redaction paths.\\n- `remotehelper`: `InfoRefs`/`InfoRefsV2` share the failover sequence; HTTP\\n  error draining unified.\\n- `api`, `review`, `dispatch`, `sessions`, `setup`, `state`, `rewind`,\\n  opencode/copilotcli transcripts, e2e agent runners: smaller shared helpers.\\n- Package cli standardizes on `printJSON` (was five copies of\\n  encode-with-indent).\\n\\n## Suspicious-but-preserved (documented, unreachable — flagged, not deleted)\\n\\nThese look like missing wiring rather than slop; deleting them would hide a\\npossible bug. Worth a maintainer decision each:\\n\\n- `strategy.HardResetWithProtection` — cited in CLAUDE.md as *the* safe reset\\n  API, but nothing calls it.\\n- `strategy.ListOrphanedSessionStates` — a comment in `manual_commit.go` says\\n  orphan detection uses it; nothing does.\\n- `strategy.PromptOverwriteNewerLogs` / `StatusToText` — user-facing rewind\\n  safety prompt, never invoked from the rewind flow.\\n- `cli.resumeSingleSession` — documented multi-session fallback, no caller.\\n- `cli.ExtractTodoContentFromToolInput` (+ `strategy.ExtractInProgressTodo`) —\\n  siblings are live; this one isn't.\\n- `logging/context.go` session/tool-call context helpers — the slog handler\\n  reads these context keys, but nothing in production sets them.\\n- `discovery.SaveCache` — `LoadCache` is used in prod, the write path never\\n  runs.\\n- `tokenstore.IsTokenExpiredOrExpiring` — expiry is stored but never checked\\n  (no proactive refresh?).\\n- `httputil.BufferRequestBody`/`BodyReader` — oauth retry replay helpers with\\n  zero references.\\n- `repocreds.Cache.Invalidate` — invalidation wrapper never invoked.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- `mise run check` (fmt + lint + unit + integration + Vogon canary) green on\\n  the full series.\\n- `deadcode` findings drop 135 → 63; the remainder are kept test seams and the\\n  flagged suspicious items above.\\n- Net: **−5,608 lines** across 112 files, in 22 topical commits that can be\\n  split into stacked PRs if preferred.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Broad deletion surface across auth, checkpoint, explain, and agent hooks; risk is mainly accidental removal of code still needed indirectly—mitigated by deadcode/dup tooling and full `mise run check`, but reviewers should spot-check auth/git-remote and checkpoint remote paths.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Large cleanup pass across the CLI and agent packages: **~5.6k lines removed** with behavior kept on live paths.\\n> \\n> **Dead code removed** includes unused agent registry `Detect`, checkpoint blob resolver / `CatFiles` / path-based Droid transcript helpers, `auth/repo_token` (repo-scoped exchange), explain branch-default and `formatSessionInfo` / `hasCodeChanges`, task-hook parsers, `GetMergeBase`, `JoinPrompts`, `LookupSessionLog`, and duplicate metadata walking via `addDirectoryToEntriesWithAbsPath` (metadata walks go through `addDirectoryToChanges` only).\\n> \\n> **Deduplication** centralizes repeated patterns: generic `declaredCapability` / `builtinCapability` for all `As*` agent gates; per-agent `parseSessionInfoEvent` for session-shaped hooks; Copilot `lastEventField`; OpenCode `modifiedFilesFromMessages`; API `doJSON` for POST/PUT/PATCH; shared `printJSON` for CLI JSON output; `resolveContextForCluster` wired from `control_plane` instead of a duplicate in deleted `repo_token`.\\n> \\n> **Tests** drop coverage tied only to removed APIs and retarget checkpoint/remote derivation tests to `deriveCheckpointURLFromInfo`; tree-surgery tests now assert `buildTreeWithChanges` behavior directly instead of equivalence with the old flatten/rebuild path.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit ca82a6a25d06551a4d71004ac5dabf8a75f884a5. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1606/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1606/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1723\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1723/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1723/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1723/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1723\",\n              \"id\": 4864862918,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7wppUU\",\n              \"number\": 1723,\n              \"title\": \"fix(gitrepo): support reftable ref storage\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"entire[bot]\",\n                \"id\": 254015822,\n                \"node_id\": \"BOT_kgDODyP5Tg\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/2626939?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/entire\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"Bot\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-07-12T01:04:10Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-28T14:41:27Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-28T14:41:25Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1723\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1723\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1723.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1723.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-28T14:41:24Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/830\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n`entire enable` (and every subsequent capture operation) aborts on any repository that uses the **reftable** ref backend:\\n\\n```\\nfailed to setup strategy: failed to open git repository: ... unknown extension: refstorage\\n```\\n\\nReftable is created by `git init --ref-format=reftable` and `git refs migrate --ref-format=reftable`, and is slated to become git's default. This PR makes the full enable → session → commit → checkpoint flow work on reftable repositories. Fixes #547.\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\nThe vendored `go-git/go-git/v6` alpha has no reftable reader:\\n\\n- its filesystem storer reads refs from `.git/refs`, `.git/packed-refs` and `.git/HEAD` — in a reftable repo the real refs live in a binary reftable stack and `.git/HEAD` is only a `ref: refs/heads/.invalid` stub;\\n- its open-time extension check (`verifyExtensions`) rejects `extensions.refstorage=reftable` outright, which is the exact error users see.\\n\\nUpstream is not fixing this soon: go-git PR #1970 (\\\"Reftable support\\\") was **closed unmerged**, and go-git issue #1827 is still **open**. Waiting on the dependency is not viable.\\n\\n## Approach\\n\\nDetect reftable repositories in `gitrepo.OpenPath` (presence of a `reftable/` directory under the worktree or common git dir) and wrap go-git's filesystem storage with a `reftableStorer`:\\n\\n- object, config, index and shallow storage keep flowing through go-git — reftable changes only *ref* storage, not object storage, so tree/commit building is unaffected;\\n- the `ReferenceStorer` methods (`SetReference`, `CheckAndSetReference`, `Reference`, `IterReferences`, `RemoveReference`, `CountLooseRefs`, `PackRefs`) are overridden to shell out to git ref plumbing (`update-ref`, `symbolic-ref`, `rev-parse`, `for-each-ref`);\\n- the storer implements `SupportsExtension(\\\"refstorage\\\")` so go-git's extension check passes on open.\\n\\nThis extends the codebase's existing \\\"prefer the git CLI where go-git is unsafe or unsupported\\\" seam (already used for `reset`/`checkout` via `HardResetWithProtection`, and for `fetch`) rather than inventing a new architecture. Because every ref read/write in the CLI funnels through `gitrepo.OpenPath`, one wrapper makes all callers — enable, session start, shadow branches, condensation, the `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch, and `checkpoint list` — work unchanged. The ref plumbing used does not fire git hooks, so it cannot recurse back into `entire`.\\n\\nScope note: this covers the local capture flow. Network transport of reftable stacks is out of scope and unaffected (push/fetch already route through the git CLI). No behavior changes for classic files-backend or sha256 repositories.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\nUnit tests (`cmd/entire/cli/gitrepo/reftable_test.go`) and integration tests (`cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/reftable_repo_test.go`) are gated on git reftable support and skip on older git (same pattern as the existing sha256 repo test). Live-verified against the built binary with real git state inspection:\\n\\n| Case | Result |\\n|------|--------|\\n| Reftable repo — `entire enable` | succeeds, creates `entire/checkpoints/v1` |\\n| Reftable repo — session start → file change → stop → user commit | shadow branch + metadata branch advance; user commit carries `Entire-Checkpoint:` trailer |\\n| Reftable repo — `entire checkpoint list` | lists the checkpoint |\\n| Reftable repo with pre-existing history before enable | works |\\n| Linked worktree of a reftable repo | HEAD/branch resolve correctly; enable + metadata branch resolve |\\n| Files-backend repo (regression) | unchanged |\\n| sha256 object-format repo (regression) | unchanged |\\n\\nGates: `gofmt` clean, `golangci-lint` clean on touched packages, and the full integration + strategy suites pass (1119 tests).\\n\\n## Hardening (audit follow-up)\\n\\nA follow-up commit hardens the ref-plumbing seam after an adversarial review:\\n\\n- **CAS error mapping (correctness).** `CheckAndSetReference` previously mapped *every* `git update-ref` failure to `storage.ErrReferenceHasChanged`. `strategy.atomicSetV1Ref` keys a privacy-critical pre-push decision on that sentinel (concurrency conflict → abort as `V1RefMovedError`) and documents that all other errors must be surfaced as-is. The coarse mapping misreported storage errors (nonexistent object, invalid ref name, lock contention, timeout, git spawn failure) as concurrency conflicts, producing a bogus `V1RefMovedError` (\\\"ref moved from X to X\\\"). Now only a genuine compare-and-swap conflict (`is at X but expected Y`, or `reference already exists` for a create race) maps to the sentinel; every other failure is wrapped and surfaced as itself.\\n- **Ref-name argument hardening (defense-in-depth).** All user-controlled ref names are now passed after `--end-of-options`, so a name beginning with `-` is treated as a literal argument rather than a git option. Args were already passed as argv (never a shell string), so there was **no command-injection exposure**; this closes off option-injection for exotic ref names.\\n- **Ref-lookup failure classification (correctness).** `Reference`, the `IterReferences` HEAD path, and `RemoveReference` previously treated *every* git failure as a definitive negative — a spawn failure, the `reftableGitTimeout` kill, or an I/O error was reported as `ErrReferenceNotFound` / a silently-dropped HEAD / a successful deletion. Because `strategy.SafelyAdvanceLocalRef` blind-overwrites a ref it believes absent (no CAS), a transient git failure on a critical ref (e.g. `entire/checkpoints/v1`) could discard real history. A new `refLookupAbsent` classifier maps only a genuine \\\"git ran and exited non-zero with empty stderr\\\" (git's `--quiet` not-found contract) to absence; timeouts (now re-wrapped with the context error), spawn/I-O errors, and non-zero exits carrying stderr are surfaced. `RemoveReference` no longer swallows an empty-stderr failure (git exits 0 for an already-absent ref).\\n- **Tests.** Added mutation-verified regression tests for the CAS conflict-vs-error mapping, ref-lookup failure classification (absence/timeout/spawn/fatal), delete-failure surfacing, HEAD-resolution failure surfacing, and an argv-safety test proving ref names are never shell-evaluated.\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1723/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1723/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1293\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1293/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1293/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1293/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1293\",\n              \"id\": 4543543742,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7gZH-L\",\n              \"number\": 1293,\n              \"title\": \"Bump the go-dependencies group across 1 directory with 2 updates\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"dependabot[bot]\",\n                \"id\": 49699333,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/dependabot\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"Bot\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [\n                {\n                  \"id\": 9981954695,\n                  \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACUviKhw\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/dependencies\",\n                  \"name\": \"dependencies\",\n                  \"color\": \"0366d6\",\n                  \"default\": false,\n                  \"description\": \"Pull requests that update a dependency file\",\n                  \"archived_at\": null,\n                  \"archived_by\": null\n                },\n                {\n                  \"id\": 9981954696,\n                  \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACUviKiA\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/go\",\n                  \"name\": \"go\",\n                  \"color\": \"16e2e2\",\n                  \"default\": false,\n                  \"description\": \"Pull requests that update go code\",\n                  \"archived_at\": null,\n                  \"archived_by\": null\n                }\n              ],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-05-28T20:22:18Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-29T18:49:12Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-05-29T18:49:10Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1293\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1293\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1293.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1293.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-05-29T18:49:10Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/450\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nBumps the go-dependencies group with 2 updates in the / directory: [github.com/entireio/auth-go](https://github.com/entireio/auth-go) and [github.com/posthog/posthog-go](https://github.com/posthog/posthog-go).\\n\\nUpdates `github.com/entireio/auth-go` from 0.3.4 to 0.4.0\\n<details>\\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/auth-go/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\\\">github.com/entireio/auth-go's changelog</a>.</em></p>\\n<blockquote>\\n<h2>v0.4.0 — 2026-05-28</h2>\\n<h3>Added</h3>\\n<ul>\\n<li>New <code>refresh</code> package: an RFC 6749 §6 <code>refresh_token</code> grant client\\n(peer of <code>sts</code>/<code>deviceflow</code>) that re-mints the login JWT from a stored\\nrefresh token. Exposes <code>refresh.ErrInvalidGrant</code> for rotation-race\\nhandling.</li>\\n<li><code>tokenmanager.Token</code> now transparently re-mints an expired/near-expiry\\nlogin JWT from the stored refresh token before resolving the request,\\nre-prompting login only when the refresh token itself is revoked or\\nexpired. New exported <code>tokenmanager.Manager.Refresh</code> lets callers warm\\nthe session proactively.</li>\\n<li>Cross-process single-flight for refresh: an in-process mutex plus an\\ninjectable <code>tokenmanager.ProcessLock</code> (default: an advisory file lock\\nover <code>golang.org/x/sys</code>), with rotation-race tolerance (on\\n<code>invalid_grant</code>, the store is re-read and the refresh retried once\\nagainst a concurrently-rotated successor before concluding re-login).</li>\\n<li>New <code>tokenmanager.Config</code> fields <code>RefreshPath</code> (token endpoint for the\\nrefresh grant) and <code>LockDir</code> (advisory-lock directory; defaults under\\n<code>os.UserCacheDir()</code>).</li>\\n<li>New sentinels <code>tokenmanager.ErrReauthRequired</code> (refresh exhausted —\\ndistinct from <code>ErrNotLoggedIn</code>) and <code>tokenmanager.ErrNoRefreshPath</code>.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<h3>Changed</h3>\\n<ul>\\n<li><code>golang.org/x/sys</code> is now a direct dependency (advisory file lock).</li>\\n<li><code>client_id</code> validation (<code>ValidateClientID</code> / <code>ValidateClientIDConsistency</code>)\\nmoved into <code>internal/oauthhttp</code> and shared by <code>sts</code> and <code>refresh</code>; no\\nbehavioural change to <code>sts</code>.</li>\\n<li>Clamp a server-provided <code>expires_in</code> before converting to a\\n<code>time.Duration</code> (centralised in <code>internal/oauthhttp.ExpiresInDuration</code>),\\napplied across <code>sts</code>, <code>deviceflow</code>, and <code>refresh</code>. Guards against an\\nint64 nanosecond overflow that an absurd value would otherwise wrap into\\na past expiry.</li>\\n<li><code>tokenmanager.SaveCoreToken</code> and <code>tokenmanager.DeleteCoreToken</code> now\\nacquire the refresh lock (<code>refreshMu</code> in-process, the cross-process file\\nlock) before mutating the store, serialising them against in-flight\\nrefreshes. Prevents a refresh whose grant is mid-flight from persisting\\nover a concurrent logout (session resurrection) or overwriting a\\nconcurrent re-login. Both methods can now block up to ~30s under\\ncontention and may return a wrapped lock-acquire error.</li>\\n</ul>\\n</blockquote>\\n</details>\\n<details>\\n<summary>Commits</summary>\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/auth-go/commit/a0b110c9346cf1dcdfbd05e436970af926be515f\\\"><code>a0b110c</code></a> Merge pull request <a href=\\\"https://redirect.github.com/entireio/auth-go/issues/11\\\">#11</a> from entireio/alex/v0.4.0-changelog</li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/auth-go/commit/6d9f7675c121095144c43d0d18e8ae294827ce62\\\"><code>6d9f767</code></a> Finalise v0.4.0 CHANGELOG</li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/auth-go/commit/a853917ff786dd9d6f86304166b7290d20eacdef\\\"><code>a853917</code></a> Merge pull request <a href=\\\"https://redirect.github.com/entireio/auth-go/issues/10\\\">#10</a> from entireio/alex/cor-314-auth-go-refresh-tier-persis...</li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/auth-go/commit/251d8eef6bea9758bbbcf6b1e0011f80c4102266\\\"><code>251d8ee</code></a> Coordinate SaveCoreToken/DeleteCoreToken with the refresh lock</li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/auth-go/commit/975ca748ae84bb1f0806d84ace2cd92577a42656\\\"><code>975ca74</code></a> Centralize expires_in overflow clamp across sts/deviceflow/refresh</li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/auth-go/commit/666ff5f3e32c75d80bbd8aecde4b926874a1b657\\\"><code>666ff5f</code></a> Guard against empty AccessToken in ensureFreshLogin</li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/auth-go/commit/1e6666a0e7c7c0b464579e3dfb9eca2e68269697\\\"><code>1e6666a</code></a> Clamp server expires_in to avoid time.Duration overflow</li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/auth-go/commit/241ab27c6fb14929d8796e769262641ba66fde58\\\"><code>241ab27</code></a> Close refresh/proclock doc + test gaps from PR review</li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/auth-go/commit/b4f3eee2beacaa5fc6205bfd83b969e505c3ee3b\\\"><code>b4f3eee</code></a> Refine doRefresh logout semantics; close test + doc gaps from PR review</li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/auth-go/commit/27169aff722807646040a85a00527099884ccb6c\\\"><code>27169af</code></a> Note JWT-exp refresh trigger in Refresh godoc</li>\\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/auth-go/compare/v0.3.4...v0.4.0\\\">compare view</a></li>\\n</ul>\\n</details>\\n<br />\\n\\nUpdates `github.com/posthog/posthog-go` from 1.12.6 to 1.13.1\\n<details>\\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\\\"https://github.com/posthog/posthog-go/releases\\\">github.com/posthog/posthog-go's releases</a>.</em></p>\\n<blockquote>\\n<h2>1.13.1</h2>\\n<h2>Unreleased</h2>\\n<h2>1.13.0</h2>\\n<h2>Unreleased</h2>\\n</blockquote>\\n</details>\\n<details>\\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\\\"https://github.com/PostHog/posthog-go/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\\\">github.com/posthog/posthog-go's changelog</a>.</em></p>\\n<blockquote>\\n<h2>1.13.1</h2>\\n<h3>Patch Changes</h3>\\n<ul>\\n<li>541b82f: Include group context in the <code>$feature_flag_called</code> LRU dedupe key so group-scoped flags fire a separate event for each group a user is evaluated under, instead of being dedup-ed against the first group context the same <code>(distinct_id, flag, device_id)</code> was seen under.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<h2>1.13.0</h2>\\n<h3>Minor Changes</h3>\\n<ul>\\n<li>dec8ade: Add opt-in panic capture for request context middleware.</li>\\n<li>dec8ade: Add server-side request context helpers for net/http capture and exception events, plus <code>EvaluateFlagsWithContext</code> for using request-scoped distinct IDs during flag evaluation. Request-context flag evaluation does not generate personless IDs.</li>\\n</ul>\\n</blockquote>\\n</details>\\n<details>\\n<summary>Commits</summary>\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/PostHog/posthog-go/commit/f68c74f31334c42921039fa6f19c64620a916548\\\"><code>f68c74f</code></a> chore: release v1.13.1 [version bump] [skip ci]</li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/PostHog/posthog-go/commit/541b82f623cb60016d4a628d180e056707def137\\\"><code>541b82f</code></a> fix: include group context in $feature_flag_called dedupe key (<a href=\\\"https://redirect.github.com/posthog/posthog-go/issues/206\\\">#206</a>)</li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/PostHog/posthog-go/commit/4650ca24c595a4e0a3de29c36047e19c8d0e0677\\\"><code>4650ca2</code></a> chore: use shared semantic PR title workflow (<a href=\\\"https://redirect.github.com/posthog/posthog-go/issues/210\\\">#210</a>)</li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/PostHog/posthog-go/commit/ba838c81f0390d57d050de33df952c69537b1fb4\\\"><code>ba838c8</code></a> chore: validate PR titles with conventional commits (<a href=\\\"https://redirect.github.com/posthog/posthog-go/issues/209\\\">#209</a>)</li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/PostHog/posthog-go/commit/8ceb0de90586cfcb3ebb1a92bd8f5a70e40a01f0\\\"><code>8ceb0de</code></a> docs: document public APIs and hide testing-only flag definitions method (<a href=\\\"https://redirect.github.com/posthog/posthog-go/issues/208\\\">#208</a>)</li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/PostHog/posthog-go/commit/1ce09487804d3c37b1d40152a4508d4bff08c21b\\\"><code>1ce0948</code></a> chore: update PostHog/.github pins (<a href=\\\"https://redirect.github.com/posthog/posthog-go/issues/207\\\">#207</a>)</li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/PostHog/posthog-go/commit/9dbb06161d49f17e8ab91f5502a3656d3930c509\\\"><code>9dbb061</code></a> chore: release v1.13.0 [version bump] [skip ci]</li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/PostHog/posthog-go/commit/dec8adea658fbd7f1b3d2b3c8b7f6379d4a2cea0\\\"><code>dec8ade</code></a> feat: add server-side request context (<a href=\\\"https://redirect.github.com/posthog/posthog-go/issues/201\\\">#201</a>)</li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/PostHog/posthog-go/commit/89147f56f1f445aa96b06d377391f081db7c6355\\\"><code>89147f5</code></a> chore(ci): bump pinned posthog-sdk-test-harness SHA (<a href=\\\"https://redirect.github.com/posthog/posthog-go/issues/204\\\">#204</a>)</li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/PostHog/posthog-go/commit/997865547e721b341b77782ee37e2f4a4aacacc8\\\"><code>9978655</code></a> chore(ci): bump pinned PostHog/.github reusable workflow SHA (<a href=\\\"https://redirect.github.com/posthog/posthog-go/issues/203\\\">#203</a>)</li>\\n<li>See full diff in <a href=\\\"https://github.com/posthog/posthog-go/compare/v1.12.6...v1.13.1\\\">compare view</a></li>\\n</ul>\\n</details>\\n<br />\\n\\n\\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't alter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting `@dependabot rebase`.\\n\\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\\n\\n---\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\\n<br />\\n\\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits that have been made to it\\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all of the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> major version` will close this group update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency's major version (unless you unignore this specific dependency's major version or upgrade to it yourself)\\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> minor version` will close this group update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency's minor version (unless you unignore this specific dependency's minor version or upgrade to it yourself)\\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name>` will close this group update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency (unless you unignore this specific dependency or upgrade to it yourself)\\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name>` will remove all of the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name> <ignore condition>` will remove the ignore condition of the specified dependency and ignore conditions\\n\\n\\n</details>\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1293/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1293/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1027\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1027/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1027/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1027/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1027\",\n              \"id\": 4324068543,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7VZAzz\",\n              \"number\": 1027,\n              \"title\": \"cli: stamp agent hook configs and warn when they fall behind\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"id\": 881031,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-04-24T15:52:31Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-14T08:15:18Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-13T08:16:56Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1027\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1027\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1027.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1027.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nAdds CLI version tracking to every agent's installed hook configuration, then surfaces a clear \\\"your hooks are out of date\\\" warning the next time the user runs any visible `entire` command.\\r\\n\\r\\nUntil now there was no signal anywhere — when a CLI release changed hook wiring, existing users kept running stale hooks silently until something failed cryptically. This PR closes that loop.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Example\\r\\n\\r\\nClaude code settings:\\r\\n<img width=\\\"733\\\" height=\\\"103\\\" alt=\\\"Screenshot 2026-04-27 at 2 22 26 pm\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2ae97050-21df-4a0f-84b0-8cc27f62acf5\\\" />\\r\\n\\r\\nWarning shown on every entire command:\\r\\n<img width=\\\"733\\\" height=\\\"103\\\" alt=\\\"Screenshot 2026-04-27 at 2 21 59 pm\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ebea218a-ef7c-4c82-92fc-449cac2f489a\\\" />\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## What it does\\r\\n\\r\\n**1. Stamp every agent hook config with the CLI version that wrote it.**\\r\\n\\r\\n`entire enable` (and `entire configure`) now writes a top-level `entireMeta.cli_version` field into each installed agent's config:\\r\\n\\r\\n- `.claude/settings.json`\\r\\n- `.cursor/hooks.json`\\r\\n- `.codex/hooks.json`\\r\\n- `.github/hooks/entire.json` (Copilot CLI)\\r\\n- `.factory/settings.json`\\r\\n- `.gemini/settings.json`\\r\\n- `.opencode/plugins/entire.ts` (as a `// entireMeta: {...}` comment line — TS, not JSON)\\r\\n\\r\\nA new `agent.HookVersionSupport` capability lets `drift.go` read the stamp back without knowing the concrete config format. JSON agents share `WriteJSONHookMeta` / `ReadJSONHookMeta`; OpenCode's TS plugin uses `TSHookMetaCommentLine` / `ReadTSHookMeta`.\\r\\n\\r\\n**2. Detect drift against a single global floor.**\\r\\n\\r\\n`agent.CheckHookDrift(ctx)` walks every registered agent with hooks installed and reports any whose stamp normalizes below `agent.MinCompatibleCLIVersion`. Missing/unreadable stamps are treated as `v0.0.0`, which collapses the \\\"no stamp at all\\\" and \\\"stamp older than floor\\\" cases through the same `semver.Compare` gate.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe floor is one package-level constant in `cmd/entire/cli/agent/hook_command.go`, seeded at `\\\"0.0.0\\\"` so no drift warnings fire today. Bump it exactly when a hook-contract change in any agent warrants forcing users to re-run `entire enable --force`.\\r\\n\\r\\nDev builds (`versioninfo.Version == versioninfo.DevVersion`) short-circuit drift detection entirely.\\r\\n\\r\\n**3. Surface the warning broadly and clearly.**\\r\\n\\r\\nA root-level `PersistentPreRun` (`cli.driftWarningPreRun`) prints a yellow two-line warning on stderr before every visible subcommand:\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\nAction required: agent hooks need updating (claude-code)\\r\\n  Run: entire enable --force\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nAction-first wording — no \\\"stale\\\", no abstract \\\"hooks\\\". The user knows what to run.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `sessions` command defines its own `PersistentPreRunE`, which Cobra does not chain to root's, so `sessions.go` calls `driftWarningPreRun` explicitly after its git-repo guard.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Skip rules\\r\\n\\r\\nThe warning is suppressed when any of:\\r\\n\\r\\n- The target command (or any ancestor) has `Hidden: true`. Covers internal / machine-invoked commands (`entire hooks`, `entire migrate`, dev helpers).\\r\\n- The target is the root command itself (`bare entire` prints help or runs first-time setup; neither is the right surface).\\r\\n- The target is `entire enable` / `entire configure` invoked with `--force=true`. The user is already running the exact remediation the warning would suggest. The check inspects the resolved boolean (`Flags().GetBool`), not just `flag.Changed`, so a wrapper that passes `--force=false` explicitly still gets the warning.\\r\\n- The current directory is outside a git worktree. Otherwise a non-repo dir with a stray `.claude/` could warn and then the command itself would bail with \\\"not a git repository\\\".\\r\\n- Stderr is not a TTY. Scripted / CI callers shouldn't have their stderr polluted.\\r\\n- The CLI is a dev build (covered by `CheckHookDrift`'s own short-circuit).\\r\\n\\r\\n## Forcing a re-stamp\\r\\n\\r\\nTwo ways to upgrade an old install:\\r\\n\\r\\n- `entire enable --force` — explicit, the message tells the user this.\\r\\n- `entire enable` against a config with no stamp at all (a pre-stamp install) is automatically promoted to a force-reinstall, so the first `enable` after this lands re-stamps without ceremony.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Test plan\\r\\n\\r\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/... -race` — unit tests cover the skip predicate, the renderer, and `driftWarningPreRun` with stubbed drift / TTY / git-repo so every gate is exercised including the positive emit path.\\r\\n- [x] `mise run lint` — 0 issues.\\r\\n- [x] Manual drift cycle via pty in a fixture repo:\\r\\n  - built CLI with `Version=1.0.0` via ldflag, bumped `MinCompatibleCLIVersion` to `0.9.0`, edited `.claude/settings.json` to stamp `entireMeta.cli_version = \\\"0.0.1-stale\\\"`.\\r\\n  - visible commands (`entire rewind`, `entire status`, `entire sessions list`): yellow two-line warning on stderr.\\r\\n  - hidden commands (`entire hooks claude-code pre-task`): silent.\\r\\n  - non-TTY stderr (`entire rewind 2>/tmp/x`): silent.\\r\\n  - `entire enable --force`: re-stamps to `1.0.0`, subsequent `entire status` is clean.\\r\\n- [ ] E2E canary (`mise run test:e2e:canary`) — kicked off when this comes out of draft.\\r\\n\\r\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1027/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1027/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/720\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/720/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/720/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/720/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/720\",\n              \"id\": 4094041367,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7LfLp3\",\n              \"number\": 720,\n              \"title\": \"Deprecate `reset` command\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"pjbgf\",\n                \"id\": 5452977,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NTI5Nzc=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5452977?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pjbgf\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-03-18T10:00:09Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-31T13:04:41Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-03-31T13:04:39Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/720\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/720\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/720.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/720.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-03-31T13:04:39Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"The reset and clean commands had an overlap which at times made it harder for users to understand the difference between them. This change deprecates reset in favour of a new flag in the clean command.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Changes\\r\\n\\r\\n`cmd/entire/cli/clean.go` — Unified command\\r\\n\\r\\n- New entire clean defaults to cleaning current HEAD sessions (old reset behavior)\\r\\n- --all flag for repo-wide orphan cleanup (old clean behavior)\\r\\n- --session <id> flag for single-session cleanup\\r\\n- --dry-run flag for preview without action\\r\\n- --force flag to skip confirmation and active session guard\\r\\n- --all and --session are mutually exclusive\\r\\n- Moved activeSessionsOnCurrentHead() here from reset.go\\r\\n- Added previewCurrentHead() for dry-run support\\r\\n- Renamed internal functions: runCleanAll, runCleanAllWithItems, runCleanSession\\r\\n\\r\\n`cmd/entire/cli/reset.go` — Deprecated wrapper\\r\\n\\r\\n- Cobra Deprecated field set — auto-prints deprecation warning when used\\r\\n- Delegates to the same underlying strategy methods\\r\\n- Keeps --force and --session flags for backward compatibility\\r\\n\\r\\n`cmd/entire/cli/clean_test.go` — Comprehensive tests\\r\\n\\r\\n- Default mode: nothing to clean, force, dry-run, dry-run empty, sessions without shadow branch, multiple sessions, not git repo\\r\\n- --all mode: no orphans, preview, dry-run, force, sessions branch preserved, not git repo, subdirectory\\r\\n- runCleanAllWithItems unit tests: partial failure, all failures, no items, mixed types preview\\r\\n- Flag validation: mutual exclusion of --all and --session\\r\\n\\r\\n`cmd/entire/cli/reset_test.go` — Deprecated wrapper tests\\r\\n\\r\\n- TestResetCmd_IsDeprecated — verifies deprecation field\\r\\n- Retained core functional tests (nothing to reset, force, not git repo)\\r\\n\\r\\n### Documentation\\r\\n\\r\\n- README.md — updated command table and troubleshooting section\\r\\n- docs/architecture/checkpoint-scenarios.md — updated cleanup examples\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes affect destructive cleanup paths (deleting session files/branches/temp data) and alter the default meaning of `entire clean`, so regressions could cause unintended data loss despite added guards and extensive tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> `entire clean` is repurposed to **clean session state for the current HEAD by default** (previously `entire reset` behavior), with new flags for `--all` (repo-wide orphan cleanup), `--session <id>` (single-session cleanup), and `--dry-run` previews; `--all` and `--session` are enforced as mutually exclusive, and active sessions are guarded unless `--force` is used.\\n> \\n> The old repo-wide orphan cleanup behavior is preserved behind `clean --all`, with improved prompting/preview behavior, stderr reporting for failures, and safer temp-file enumeration/deletion confined to `.entire/tmp` via `os.OpenRoot`/`fs.WalkDir`.\\n> \\n> `entire reset` is now **deprecated** and largely delegates to the unified clean logic for `--session`, while docs and tests are updated to reflect the new command semantics and troubleshooting guidance.\\n> \\n> <sup>Written by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot) for commit a5f3df01d13cca1a2c446dbf1f38d896d44469bf. Configure [here](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/720/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/720/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/145\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/145/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/145/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/145/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/145\",\n              \"id\": 3896022346,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7BcH_y\",\n              \"number\": 145,\n              \"title\": \"refactor: extract git operations to gitutil package\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"khaong\",\n                \"id\": 351934,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTkzNA==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/351934?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/khaong\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-02-04T11:18:54Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-04-13T06:26:46Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-04-13T06:26:46Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": true,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/145\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/145\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/145.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/145.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\n- Extracts all git operations to the `gitutil` package\\n- Deletes `cli/git_operations.go` entirely (no more deprecated wrappers)\\n- Removes thin wrapper functions, calling `gitutil` directly at call sites\\n- Moves tests to `gitutil/repository_test.go` and `gitutil/operations_test.go`\\n- Net reduction of ~139 lines of code\\n\\n## Package structure\\n\\n**gitutil/repository.go** - Repository and branch operations:\\n- `OpenRepository`, `GetWorktreePath`, `IsInsideWorktree`, `GetMainRepoRoot`, `GetGitCommonDir`\\n- `GetGitAuthor`, `GetGitAuthorFromRepo`\\n- `IsOnDefaultBranch`, `GetDefaultBranchFromRemote`, `ShouldSkipOnDefaultBranch`, `ShouldSkipOnDefaultBranchForStrategy`\\n- `GetCurrentBranch`, `GetMergeBase`, `BranchExistsOnRemote`, `BranchExistsLocally`\\n\\n**gitutil/operations.go** - Git CLI wrappers (go-git v5 bug workarounds):\\n- `CheckoutBranch`, `HardResetWithProtection`, `HardReset`\\n- `ValidateBranchName`, `HasUncommittedChanges`, `GetConfigValue`\\n- `FetchBranch`, `FetchFromRemote`, `CreateLocalBranchFromRemote`\\n- `Push`, `GetGitDirInPath`\\n\\n## Key changes\\n\\n- **Inlined fetch helpers**: `FetchAndCheckoutRemoteBranch` and `FetchMetadataBranch` inlined at call sites in `resume.go`\\n- **Avoided circular dependency**: Changed `ShouldSkipOnDefaultBranchForStrategy(strategy)` to accept `allowsMainBranch bool` parameter\\n- **Moved tests**: Git-related tests now live alongside their implementations in `gitutil/`\\n\\n## Stacked PR\\n\\nThis PR stacks on #140 (alex/fix-shadow-branch-performance).\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches branch/checkout/reset/push logic used by hooks and session resume/rewind, so regressions could affect repository state changes. Risk is mitigated by moving existing behavior with added safety checks and relocated tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Refactors git interactions into a dedicated `gitutil` package** (new `repository.go` + `operations.go`) and deletes the old `cli/git_operations.go` implementation/tests, moving coverage into `gitutil/*_test.go`.\\n> \\n> Updates callers across `debug`, `explain`, hooks, `resume`, `rewind`, session state, and strategy code to use `gitutil` directly, including changing `ShouldSkipOnDefaultBranchForStrategy` to accept an `allowsMainBranch` boolean to avoid dependency cycles.\\n> \\n> Adjusts resume/fetch behavior to split remote fetch vs local branch creation (and avoids overwriting an existing local `entire/sessions`), and adds small hardening to git CLI wrappers (e.g., ref validation for `CheckoutBranch`, standardized `Push`/`FetchFromRemote` helpers).\\n> \\n> <sup>Written by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot) for commit 51e96af2207a73640ae77736448b27b3b1a67c36. This will update automatically on new commits. Configure [here](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/145/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/145/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/673\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/673/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/673/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/673/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/673\",\n              \"id\": 4050344309,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7JUJ9b\",\n              \"number\": 673,\n              \"title\": \"feat: windows build (fixes #370)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"talaikis\",\n                \"id\": 7689499,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjc2ODk0OTk=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7689499?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/talaikis\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/talaikis\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/talaikis/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/talaikis/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/talaikis/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/talaikis/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/talaikis/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/talaikis/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/talaikis/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/talaikis/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/talaikis/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-03-10T08:52:22Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-04-08T12:59:59Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-04-08T12:59:59Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/673\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/673\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/673.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/673.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Adds native Windows install (using Golang build) script.\\r\\n\\r\\nUsage:\\r\\n\\r\\n```bash\\r\\n# locally\\r\\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\\\\install.ps1\\r\\n\\r\\n# remotely\\r\\nSet-ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned -Scope Process; iwr https://entire.io/install.ps1 | iex\\r\\n```\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/673/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/673/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/358\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/358/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/358/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/358/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/358\",\n              \"id\": 3948479047,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7EIuxh\",\n              \"number\": 358,\n              \"title\": \"feat: Husky v9 hook compatibility\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"squishykid\",\n                \"id\": 2177912,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNzc5MTI=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2177912?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/squishykid\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/squishykid/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [\n                {\n                  \"id\": 9924477906,\n                  \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOQyo98M8AAAACT4uD0g\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/labels/enhancement\",\n                  \"name\": \"enhancement\",\n                  \"color\": \"a2eeef\",\n                  \"default\": true,\n                  \"description\": \"New feature or request\",\n                  \"archived_at\": null,\n                  \"archived_by\": null\n                }\n              ],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 2,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-02-16T16:05:31Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-17T08:26:33Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-02-17T08:26:32Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": true,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/358\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/358\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/358.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/358.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\n- When Husky v9 is detected (`core.hooksPath` → `.husky/_`), inject Entire's hook commands into `.husky/<hookname>` user-editable files instead of `.husky/_/`\\n- User-facing Husky files are committed to the repo and survive `npm install` (which regenerates `.husky/_/`)\\n- Falls back to standard standalone hook installation when `.husky/` directory doesn't exist on disk\\n- Cleans up stale standalone hooks in `.husky/_/` left by prior installations (PR #355)\\n\\nCloses #228\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] `TestIsHuskyHooksPath` — detection with various path patterns\\n- [x] `TestGetHuskyUserHooksDir` — derives `.husky/` from `.husky/_`\\n- [x] `TestInstallGitHook_HuskyDetected` — injects into `.husky/<hookname>`, not `.husky/_/`\\n- [x] `TestInstallGitHook_HuskyIdempotent` — second install returns 0\\n- [x] `TestInstallGitHook_HuskyExistingContent` — preserves user content, appends block\\n- [x] `TestInstallGitHook_HuskyUpdateBlock` — replaces existing block on re-install\\n- [x] `TestRemoveGitHook_Husky` — strips blocks, removes empty files\\n- [x] `TestRemoveGitHook_HuskyPreservesUserContent` — user content survives removal\\n- [x] `TestIsGitHookInstalled_Husky` — detection works with injected blocks\\n- [x] `TestInstallGitHook_HuskyDirNotExists` — falls back to standard install\\n- [x] `TestInstallGitHook_HuskyCleansUpGenerated` — removes stale `.husky/_/` hooks\\n- [x] All existing hooks tests pass unchanged\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/358/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/358/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/403\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/403/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/403/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/403/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/403\",\n              \"id\": 3956043962,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7Ehrxr\",\n              \"number\": 403,\n              \"title\": \"fix: restore sessions\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"id\": 881031,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https:/