e_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-11-10T19:37:37Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-10T20:11:53Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-11-10T20:11:51Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3107\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3107\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3107.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3107.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-11-10T20:11:51Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"This draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back a trail. Feel free to edit the title or body, but keep the hidden marker below: Entire uses it to close this pull request when the trail closes.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Changelog-only update with no runtime or build changes.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Documents the 0.13.2 release** in `CHANGELOG.md` only—no application code in this diff.\\n> \\n> The new section calls out **service-account secret** CLI commands and `ENTIRE_TOKEN` / `git-remote-entire` behavior, **standalone `git-remote-entire` archives** per platform, and **auto-install for the `entire-rsl` plugin**. **Token usage** for sessions/checkpoints is now taken from each agent’s running total (with `session_token_usage` on checkpoints). **Repository-scoped** `entire trail create` / `update` are removed in favor of project trails; trail output drops assignees and aggregate comment counts. **OpenCode** checkpoint/export and live-view fixes are listed, plus fixes for **Antigravity** transcript paths, **`entire api` / `entire recap` repo cell routing**, and **`install.sh` checksum** verification.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 81c5454dc0a6f1d16497b8126d619ffce215c111. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3107/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3107/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": {\n                \"id\": 2626939,\n                \"client_id\": \"Iv23lieFG10uOnChW4TN\",\n                \"slug\": \"entire\",\n                \"node_id\": \"A_kwHOAfprLM4AKBV7\",\n                \"owner\": {\n                  \"login\": \"entireio\",\n                  \"id\": 33188652,\n                  \"node_id\": \"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjMzMTg4NjUy\",\n                  \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33188652?v=4\",\n                  \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio\",\n                  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio\",\n                  \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/followers\",\n                  \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/following{/other_user}\",\n                  \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                  \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                  \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/subscriptions\",\n                  \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/orgs\",\n                  \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/repos\",\n                  \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/events{/privacy}\",\n                  \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/received_events\",\n                  \"type\": \"Organization\",\n                  \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                  \"site_admin\": false\n                },\n                \"name\": \"Entire\",\n                \"description\": \"\",\n                \"external_url\": \"https://entire.com\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/entire\",\n                \"created_at\": \"2026-01-09T21:20:56Z\",\n                \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-23T08:32:31Z\",\n                \"permissions\": {\n                  \"administration\": \"read\",\n                  \"checks\": \"write\",\n                  \"contents\": \"write\",\n                  \"emails\": \"read\",\n                  \"members\": \"read\",\n                  \"metadata\": \"read\",\n                  \"pull_requests\": \"write\",\n                  \"statuses\": \"read\",\n                  \"workflows\": \"write\"\n                },\n                \"events\": [\n                  \"check_suite\",\n                  \"create\",\n                  \"delete\",\n                  \"fork\",\n                  \"member\",\n                  \"membership\",\n                  \"organization\",\n                  \"pull_request\",\n                  \"push\",\n                  \"repository\",\n                  \"star\",\n                  \"team\"\n                ]\n              },\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2785\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2785/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2785/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2785/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2785\",\n              \"id\": 5865644792,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABInHbWw\",\n              \"number\": 2785,\n              \"title\": \"Redone commits don't mint a fresh checkpoint for inherited work\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-15T11:57:15Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-16T15:18:00Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-16T15:17:57Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2785\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2785\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2785.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2785.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-16T15:17:57Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1582\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nE2E run [38724857355](https://github.com/entireio/cli/actions/runs/38724857355/job/116388096213) failed `TestExplainCheckpoint` (claude-code). Haiku committed `docs/feature.md` itself, then ran `git reset HEAD~1`, and the test's own commit came out with two checkpoint trailers: the inherited `3afa00e9bfa6` (correct, via the redo inheritance from 6170bc1612) and a fresh `93418f0f011f`.\\n\\nThe fresh one was wrong. The reset put the file back in the worktree, the next turn end recorded it as touched again, and session matching saw transcript growth plus an overlapping staged file. The new checkpoint's transcript slice held only the agent's commit and reset, which the turn-end finalize had already folded into `3afa00e9bfa6`.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n- The redo step (`inheritReplacedCommitsTrailers`) now also reports which staged paths the inherited checkpoints already hold. A path counts only when the newest dropped commit that changed it carries a checkpoint that is not deleted and exists in this clone's store (`capturedCheckpoints`), and the staged content and mode both match what that commit left. Inheriting the trailer stays permissive: a trailer whose capture failed still links, but holds nothing, so the session's work gets a fresh checkpoint. Content, mode and deletions come from one rename-free read of the commit index git is preparing (`parseStagedRaw` now also keeps the staged mode, building on #2330), so `git commit -a` and path-limited commits compare what they commit.\\n- `PrepareCommitMsg` returns right after inheriting when every staged path is held, so a pure redo gets no fresh trailer, whatever the session phase.\\n- Otherwise the staged-files overlap check in `filterSessionsWithNewContent` sees only the redo's other staged paths, from the same rename-free view, so only other session work earns a fresh checkpoint. (A rename-detecting list would hide a staged deletion paired with a held file.)\\n- Prepare records the held paths in the inherited-trailers marker. After a redo that stamps no fresh trailer (pure, or partial with no session's other work), which condenses nothing, post-commit (`reconcileRedoneFiles`) drops them from this worktree's sessions' touched files when the commit holds the recorded content, as carry-forward would. Only held files go through that check; other touched files, steps and transcript growth stay pending untouched.\\n- `openRepositoryTimed` is extracted to keep `PrepareCommitMsg` under the `maintidx` limit; the `open_repository` span no longer includes the redo lookup.\\n- The deleted-checkpoint list is loaded once per commit, each dropped commit's diff is computed once, and store lookups are memoized.\\n- Documented in `docs/architecture/sessions-and-checkpoints.md` and `docs/development/checkpoint-implementation.md`.\\n\\n## Deliberately not changed\\n\\nWhenever a fresh trailer is stamped, a redundant checkpoint is preferred to a lost or dangling link:\\n\\n- On a partial redo (redone files staged together with other files), the mid-turn agent fast path still stamps a fresh trailer. Transcripts miss edits made through shell commands (`sed -i`, formatters, codegen), so it cannot rule out new work.\\n- Post-commit judges overlap without the redo, so a session that only redid work may fold into another session's fresh checkpoint. An earlier commit on this branch excluded redone paths there, but that left a fresh trailer with no checkpoint behind it when a stale ACTIVE session tracked only redone files, or when a read-only ACTIVE session was gated out by a redo-only claimant.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nRegression tests in `manual_commit_redo_test.go`. The fixture writes real checkpoints for its trailers through the hooks' own store. Each test fails without its fix (mutation-checked), except the aborted-commit one, which two independent guards cover. Every test that expects a fresh trailer runs prepare, the commit and post-commit, and asserts the trailer resolves in the checkpoint store:\\n\\n- a pure redo, with an ended or an active session, gets only the inherited trailers;\\n- after a pure redo, only the redone file leaves the session's touched files, and a later human edit to it doesn't link back to the session;\\n- a redo plus new session work gets the inherited trailer and a fresh one;\\n- a redo plus a file the session never touched gets only the inherited trailer;\\n- a mode change after the reset gets a fresh trailer;\\n- a later dropped commit without a checkpoint that changed the same file leaves it uncovered;\\n- a partial redo by an active session keeps its fast-path trailer;\\n- a stale ACTIVE session tracking only redone files, a read-only ACTIVE session beside a redo-only claimant, and two ended sessions all leave the fresh trailer resolvable;\\n- a dropped commit whose checkpoint is missing or deleted keeps the session's fresh capture;\\n- a staged deletion git pairs with a held file as a rename stamps no fresh trailer;\\n- content and mode are read from the temporary commit index, not `.git/index`;\\n- an aborted commit's marker never settles files a later commit didn't contain;\\n- the cleanup never prunes touched files the redo doesn't hold.\\n\\n`mise run check` passes.\\n\\n## Follow-ups\\n\\n- The amend fold (`git reset --soft HEAD~1 && git commit --amend`) goes through `stampFreshCheckpointForAmend` and may have the same issue; not checked.\\n- The e2e helpers (`GetCheckpointTrailer` / `AssertHasCheckpointTrailer`) assume a single trailer per commit, though squash and multi-commit redos legitimately produce several.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes prepare-commit-msg trailer stamping and session content matching on reset/redo paths; incorrect logic could omit needed trailers or over-link commits, though behavior is covered by new tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Fixes **prepare-commit-msg** so a pure **redo** after `git reset` inherits dropped commits’ `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers but does **not** mint a new checkpoint when staged files are only recommitted work.\\n> \\n> Redo detection now returns a **`redo`** value (inherited IDs, matched staged paths, and whether every staged path is redone). When all staged paths are redone, the hook exits after inheriting trailers; otherwise **`filterSessionsWithNewContent`** ignores redone paths when deciding if a session has new work, so reset/turn-end “touched again” files are not treated as fresh session content. **`recommitsFilesOf`** returns the matched paths per dropped commit, and only commits that still carry live checkpoints contribute paths.\\n> \\n> Adds regression tests (pure redo, redo plus new session work, redo plus unrelated files) and documents the behavior in **sessions-and-checkpoints**.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit b05ce0e53e1ae0bf30114e863ad6c5acdc87d167. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2785/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2785/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": {\n                \"id\": 2626939,\n                \"client_id\": \"Iv23lieFG10uOnChW4TN\",\n                \"slug\": \"entire\",\n                \"node_id\": \"A_kwHOAfprLM4AKBV7\",\n                \"owner\": {\n                  \"login\": \"entireio\",\n                  \"id\": 33188652,\n                  \"node_id\": \"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjMzMTg4NjUy\",\n                  \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33188652?v=4\",\n                  \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio\",\n                  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio\",\n                  \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/followers\",\n                  \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/following{/other_user}\",\n                  \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                  \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                  \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/subscriptions\",\n                  \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/orgs\",\n                  \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/repos\",\n                  \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/events{/privacy}\",\n                  \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/received_events\",\n                  \"type\": \"Organization\",\n                  \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                  \"site_admin\": false\n                },\n                \"name\": \"Entire\",\n                \"description\": \"\",\n                \"external_url\": \"https://entire.com\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/entire\",\n                \"created_at\": \"2026-01-09T21:20:56Z\",\n                \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-23T08:32:31Z\",\n                \"permissions\": {\n                  \"administration\": \"read\",\n                  \"checks\": \"write\",\n                  \"contents\": \"write\",\n                  \"emails\": \"read\",\n                  \"members\": \"read\",\n                  \"metadata\": \"read\",\n                  \"pull_requests\": \"write\",\n                  \"statuses\": \"read\",\n                  \"workflows\": \"write\"\n                },\n                \"events\": [\n                  \"check_suite\",\n                  \"create\",\n                  \"delete\",\n                  \"fork\",\n                  \"member\",\n                  \"membership\",\n                  \"organization\",\n                  \"pull_request\",\n                  \"push\",\n                  \"repository\",\n                  \"star\",\n                  \"team\"\n                ]\n              },\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1768\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1768/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1768/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1768/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1768\",\n              \"id\": 4895934048,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7yMkxO\",\n              \"number\": 1768,\n              \"title\": \"feat(checkpoint): add checkpoint list --json (machine-readable listing; migrate off rewind --list)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"id\": 257360244,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-07-15T20:04:43Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-15T22:29:52Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-15T22:29:50Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1768\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1768\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1768.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1768.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-15T22:29:50Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"**Trail:** https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/869\\n\\n**What:** Adds `--json` and `--pending` to `entire checkpoint list`, giving a machine-readable checkpoint listing on a non-deprecated command, and migrates every consumer off the deprecated `rewind --list`.\\n\\n**Why:** `rewind --list` was the only machine-readable checkpoint listing, which blocked the announced removal of the deprecated `rewind` command. Addresses #1767.\\n\\n**How:**\\n- `checkpoint list --json` → condensed checkpoints (`entire/checkpoints/v1`) as JSON.\\n- `checkpoint list --pending [--json]` → the live shadow-branch rewind points; `--pending --json` is a **byte-for-byte drop-in for `rewind --list`** (same keys, `omitempty`, RFC3339 date, trailing newline, cap-20), so consumers migrate transparently.\\n- Repointed the `GetRewindPoints` / `RewindList` helpers (`testenv.go`, `e2e/entire.go`, `setup_cmd_test.go`, `testutil.go`) — the ~48 downstream call sites are untouched because the parsed shape is identical.\\n- Removed the `rewind --list` listing surface + now-dead code from `rewind.go` (unused imports, `runRewindList`); extracted the shared label logic. Kept the `checkpoint rewind --to/--logs-only` **action** command and its ~20 regression tests.\\n- Updated docs + dev harness scripts (`WINDOWS.md`, `.claude/skills/test-repo/SKILL.md`, `test-harness.sh`, `scripts/test-attribution-e2e.sh`).\\n\\n**Scope note:** This completes the issue's listing + migration goal. Full removal of the `checkpoint rewind` / top-level `rewind` **command** (the action flow + its ~20 regression tests) is the separate follow-up #1767 itself defers (\\\"whether the interactive rewind flow survives elsewhere is part of that removal decision, not this issue\\\") — not bundled here, so that test coverage isn't silently dropped.\\n\\n**Testing:**\\n- `gofmt` clean; `mise run lint` 0 issues; `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/...` green; `go vet -tags integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/` clean.\\n- New `checkpoint_list_test.go` (5 tests), mutation-verified; the drop-in JSON contract is pinned field-by-field against the old `rewind --list`.\\n- Canary `TestSubmoduleWorktree_SessionCreatesCheckpoint` (drives the migrated `GetRewindPoints`) PASSes end-to-end.\\n- Independent adversarial audit: CONFIRMED-CLEAN (caught + fixed two dev-harness scripts still invoking `rewind --list`).\\n\\n**Known minor follow-up:** the condensed `--json` truncation note suggests re-running with `--limit`, which `checkpoint list` does not yet expose (stderr-only, fires only past the default cap).\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1768/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1768/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2696\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2696/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2696/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2696/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2696\",\n              \"id\": 5752526656,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABHNox6Q\",\n              \"number\": 2696,\n              \"title\": \"Add entire checkpoint delete\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-07T22:03:33Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-08T17:19:20Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-08T17:19:18Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2696\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2696\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2696.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2696.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-08T17:19:18Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1513\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nAdds `entire checkpoint delete <id>`: removes one checkpoint locally and from every checkpoint remote that holds it, on both backends.\\n\\n```\\nentire checkpoint delete <id> [--dry-run] [-f|--force] [--local-only] [--remote <name>]... [--json]\\n```\\n\\n## Behavior\\n\\n- **Plan first.** Lists the local ref / v1 copy, every remote (status per target, URLs redacted), the session(s) and their tokens, session states it will clear, and the session's other local checkpoints. `--dry-run` prints this and changes nothing.\\n- **Confirmation.** Prompts (multi-select of remotes, then confirm). Without a TTY, or with `--json`, it refuses unless `--force`. Active sessions are refused unless `--force`. Exact ids only.\\n- **Order.** Session-state links cleared (never token offsets/usage) → local ref CAS-deleted → push-queue entry removed → remote deletes → one re-check per remote, so a concurrent pre-push can't re-land it.\\n- **Refs backend.** Remote deletes use `--force-with-lease` on the oid seen by ls-remote. A stale lease on an already-absent ref counts as deleted (e.g. one repo reached through two URL spellings).\\n- **v1 branch.** Per target: fetch that remote's v1 tip, commit the subtree removal on it, push with a lease; unrelated local v1 commits are never pushed. When the two removal commits are the only difference, local v1 is rebuilt on the pushed one so the next push (including the OPF rewrite) sees no divergence; any other divergence is left alone for pre-push / OPF to handle as today. History keeps the content; the output says so.\\n- **No resurrection.** The id goes on a local deleted list in the git common dir. `prepare-commit-msg` strips its `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer (amend, `-m`, `-F`, squash, cherry-pick `-x` notes), and the hooks never condense new work into a listed id or restore one on amend; new agent work gets a fresh id. `doctor migrate` skips listed ids. `explain` says the checkpoint was deleted.\\n- **Safety refusals.** On a git-branch primary, a delete that excludes a v1 push destination (`--local-only`, `--remote`, deselection) is refused, because the local removal would reach that remote on the next push anyway.\\n- **Agent help.** User-owned; agents are told never to run it unless the user asks, and never to pass `--force` themselves.\\n\\n## Known limits\\n\\n- `--force` both skips the prompt and overrides the active-session refusal (deliberate: one flag for \\\"I know\\\").\\n- On a git-branch primary, only the first push URL's v1 copy is adopted locally; a capture-elected push remote isn't seen by the refusal check (documented).\\n\\n## Not in this PR\\n\\n- entire.io still shows the checkpoint until the API handles ref deletes (phase 2).\\n- Other clones that still hold it can push it back (tombstones, later).\\n- Deleting a session's other checkpoints too vs rewriting them: undecided; this only lists them.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- Unit + integration (both backends): dry run, refusal matrix, remote rejection + retry, pushurl ≠ fetch URL, same repo under two URLs, `checkpoint_remote` + legacy origin, `--local-only` + next push, `push_sessions=false`, v1 remote ahead, next push after a v1 delete (with unpushed local checkpoints), OPF rewrite after delete, trailer stripping variants, deleted-list record/unrecord.\\n- Real repos: a private GitHub repo (refs) and an Entire-native repo (v1 branch), real Claude Code sessions; deleted on GitHub/Entire, mirror pruned on next sync, fresh clone doesn't get it, push/amend don't bring it back. entire.io still served it (phase 2).\\n- Manual end-to-end with the built binary, real git hooks and a bare remote, both backends: 24/24 checks (dry run, no-TTY refusal, prefix refusal, delete local + remote + queue + session state, sibling untouched, explain, push after delete, amend, re-delete).\\n- `mise run check` and `mise run lint` pass.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2696/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2696/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2127\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2127/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2127/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2127/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2127\",\n              \"id\": 5252204619,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBA7zxw\",\n              \"number\": 2127,\n              \"title\": \"feat(grok): add Grok Build (xAI) agent integration\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n                \"id\": 249787869,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/peyton-alt\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/peyton-alt/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-26T01:00:22Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-02T19:11:33Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2127\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2127\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2127.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2127.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1143\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nAdds Grok Build (xAI) as an Entire agent, registered as `grok`.\\n\\nBuilt through the research → write-tests → implement pipeline. Everything\\nbelow was verified against a real Grok 1.0.5 install, with captured payloads\\nand a real session transcript checked in as test fixtures.\\n\\n## What's here\\n\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/grok/` — the agent. Core `Agent` plus `HookSupport`,\\n  `HookFreshness`, `TranscriptAnalyzer`, `TokenCalculator`, `ModelExtractor`,\\n  and `SubagentSessionResolver`. Marked `IsPreview()`.\\n- `e2e/agents/grok.go` — E2E runner, so the existing `ForEachAgent` suite\\n  covers Grok. No new scenarios were needed.\\n- `scripts/test-grok-agent-integration.sh` — the probe used to capture payloads.\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/grok/AGENT.md` — research one-pager. Every claim is\\n  tagged `(doc)` / `(observed)` / `(unverified)`.\\n\\nHooks live in `.grok/hooks/entire.json`, a file Entire owns outright — Grok\\nmerges every `*.json` under `.grok/hooks/`, so install is a whole-file write and\\nuninstall a delete. A foreign file at that path is refused, not clobbered.\\n\\n## Three Grok behaviours with no analogue in the other agents\\n\\n1. **`StopCancelled` / `StopFailure` map to `TurnEnd`.** Grok fires those\\n   *instead of* `Stop` when a turn is interrupted, has a permission prompt\\n   declined, hits `--max-turns`, or errors upstream. Mapping only `Stop` loses a\\n   checkpoint for every Ctrl+C'd turn.\\n2. **`Stop` fires twice per session.** The teardown one carries\\n   `reason: \\\"shutdown\\\"` and no `promptId`. Treating it as a turn mints a\\n   duplicate, contentless checkpoint every session, so it is dropped.\\n3. **`updates.jsonl` lines are JSON-RPC envelopes.** The event kind is at\\n   `params.update.sessionUpdate`, two levels down — reading the top level yields\\n   nothing on every real transcript.\\n\\n## Test coverage\\n\\n100 unit tests (including subtests) in the grok package, built on verbatim fixtures from a real\\nsession. `mise run test:ci` is green.\\n\\n**E2E: 38 of 56 scenarios verified against real Grok** across four free-quota windows (08-25 through 09-02); the 18 remaining have only ever failed on quota/rate limits, including the\\nsubstantive ones — agent-commits-mid-turn, the subagent flow, stash/partial\\nstaging/split-changes, explain-from-clone, and the deep checkpoint metadata\\nvalidation.\\n\\nThe remaining 26 are unrun because the xAI account exhausted its **free Grok\\nBuild quota** partway through a full-suite run. Every one of those failures is\\n`You've reached your free Grok Build usage limit` or `resource-exhausted`; none\\nis attributable to this code. A full suite run costs roughly \\\\$5–20 at the\\nmeasured rate (\\\\$0.042 for a 2-call turn).\\n\\n## Fixes found along the way\\n\\n- **`content` shape collision** — Grok overloads the transcript `content` key\\n  (array on `tool_call_update`, object on message chunks). Typing it as a slice\\n  made every message chunk fail to unmarshal *silently*, since readers skip\\n  unparseable lines. Caught by a unit test using a real transcript.\\n- **`test:ci` on spaced paths** — `TestBetterleaksDoesNotPoisonGitEnvironment`\\n  interpolated the repo root into a synthesized `go.mod` `replace` directive\\n  unquoted, so it failed in any checkout whose path contains a space. Unrelated\\n  to Grok; fixed.\\n- **`agent` binary collision** — Cursor's CLI is named `agent`, and xAI's\\n  installer force-symlinks the same path. Whichever installs second owns it, so\\n  `$PATH` ordering cannot separate them and the `cursor-cli` E2E leg could\\n  exercise Grok while reporting Cursor. The runner now resolves the unambiguous\\n  `cursor-agent`, honours `E2E_CURSOR_BIN`, and probes `--version` as a backstop.\\n- **Foreign hook payloads** — Grok scans `~/.claude/settings.json` for hooks by\\n  default and treats the user scope as always-trusted, so it executes Entire's\\n  `entire hooks claude-code …` commands. Measured impact is nil (no session, no\\n  state, either side of the change), so the added guard is hardening plus a\\n  warning rather than a corruption fix — the comment says so. The real fix is\\n  `[compat.claude] hooks = false` in the user's `~/.grok/config.toml`.\\n\\n## Reviewer notes\\n\\n- **`grok` is deliberately NOT in the default E2E matrix.** It is wired into all\\n  three workflows as a `workflow_dispatch` choice with an `XAI_API_KEY` env, but\\n  `e2e.yml` runs on push to `main`, and enrolling a leg before the secret exists\\n  would break main. Promote it by adding `\\\"grok\\\"` to the `agents=[...]` arrays\\n  once the secret is configured.\\n- **`SubagentSessionResolver`'s happy path is unverified.** Grok subagents being\\n  independent child sessions is confirmed from a real run (one `spawn_subagent`\\n  produced two session IDs and the checkpoint held two top-level sessions both\\n  claiming the same file). The `subagents/meta.json` *field names* come from\\n  serde strings in the shipping binary, not documentation, and have not been\\n  checked against a real directory. The resolver fails closed — unique match\\n  required, stated parent must agree with the owning directory — so a mismatch\\n  is inert, not wrong. Confirming this is the first thing to do when quota returns.\\n- Agent-help classification: `grok` is registered like the other agents and\\n  inherits the existing agent surface; no new command was added, so there is no\\n  `agentHelpClassification` entry to review.\\n\\n## Since review\\n\\n- **Path traversal (trail finding, GHSA-2h46 class)** — `session_start` is the\\n  one hook without `transcriptPath`, so its `sessionId` became a directory\\n  component unvalidated. `sessionRef` now runs `validation.ValidateSessionID`\\n  at the choke point (as Pi does) and yields no `SessionRef` on an unsafe ID.\\n- **`entire session resume` launches Grok** — `ResumeCommandSpecFor` gained a\\n  `grok` case (`grok --resume <id>`, or `grok --continue` with no ID), with the\\n  same unsafe-ID guard as the other agents.\\n- **Merged `main`** (no rebase, so review threads stay attached) and adopted the\\n  new `AreHooksInstalled(ctx) (bool, error)` contract: missing hook file →\\n  `(false, nil)`, unreadable file or unresolvable root → error.\\n- Grok Build added to the supported-agent lists in `CLAUDE.md`, `e2e/README.md`,\\n  the contributor guide, the security doc, and the integration checklist.\\n- **Subagent double-count root-caused and fixed.** The 08-27 E2E re-run of\\n  `TestSubagentCommitFlow` still produced two top-level sessions both claiming\\n  `docs/red.md`. Logs show the child fires `subagent_stop` and `session_end` but\\n  never `stop`; `subagent_stop` was mapped to `SubagentEnd`, which the handler\\n  drops for lack of an in-flight marker (Grok gives no tool-use ID), so the\\n  `TurnEnd`-only `ResolveSubagentSession` path was never reached. `subagent_stop`\\n  now maps to the child's `TurnEnd` (the Droid Workers path) and `subagent_start`\\n  is a no-op (its pre-task capture failed on every launch). Falls back to the\\n  previous behaviour when no parent link resolves.\\n- All five review threads are addressed in code (three-tier hook timeouts,\\n  `XAI_API_KEY` scoped to the grok leg, `cwd`-keyed session group); the\\n  `parseTime`/`RFC3339` comment is a non-issue — Go's parser accepts fractional\\n  seconds with that layout, verified against the fixture timestamp.\\n\\n## Open product decisions (not decided in this PR)\\n\\n1. **Foreign-config collision.** Grok reads `~/.claude/settings.json` hooks by\\n   default, so it runs Entire's Claude Code hook commands with Grok payloads.\\n   The Claude Code side now ignores those payloads, and the E2E runner sets\\n   `[compat.claude] hooks = false`, but nothing in `entire enable` tells a real\\n   user to do the same. Options: warn during `entire enable grok` when\\n   `~/.grok/config.toml` lacks the compat switch, or leave it to docs.\\n2. **Project-trust gate.** Grok silently skips project hooks in a folder not\\n   listed in `~/.grok/trusted_folders.toml`, so `entire enable grok` can succeed\\n   while no hook ever fires. Options: detect and warn (pointing at\\n   `/hooks-trust`), or install into the always-trusted global `~/.grok/hooks/`\\n   — rejected in AGENT.md because it would fire Entire hooks in every repo.\\n\\n## Still blocked on xAI quota\\n\\n- Full E2E run (`mise run test:e2e --agent grok`, or dispatch `e2e.yml` with\\n  `agent=grok` once `XAI_API_KEY` exists as a repo secret).\\n- ~~Verifying `SubagentSessionResolver` / the subagent checkpoint shape~~ —\\n  **done (09-02)**: the resolver matched a real `subagents/meta.json`, and with\\n  the `FilesTouched` fix the checkpoint holds exactly one session plus\\n  `tasks/<child>/task.json`.\\n- Live observation of `SubagentStart/Stop`, `StopCancelled/Failure`,\\n  `PreCompact/PostCompact`, `Notification` — currently mapped from docs only.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches checkpoint lifecycle, subagent attribution, and cross-agent hook collision behavior; incorrect mappings could miss or duplicate checkpoints, though guards are conservative and E2E is opt-in on CI.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **Grok Build** as a preview Entire agent (`grok`): hooks in `.grok/hooks/entire.json`, lifecycle parsing (including `StopCancelled`/`StopFailure` as turn ends and filtering teardown `Stop`), `updates.jsonl` JSON-RPC transcript handling (tokens, models, file diffs), and a fail-closed **subagent parent linker**.\\n> \\n> **Claude Code** now ignores hook payloads with no `session_id` (with a warning), so Grok-driven invocations of global Claude hooks do not produce empty-session lifecycle events; tests cover real Grok-shaped payloads.\\n> \\n> **E2E**: new `e2e/agents/grok.go` (isolated `GROK_HOME`, compat flags, trust seeding, quota vs transient errors). Workflows expose `grok` on manual dispatch with `XAI_API_KEY` and install steps, but **not** in the default `main` matrix. **Cursor CLI** E2E prefers `cursor-agent` / `E2E_CURSOR_BIN` and fails bootstrap if `agent` resolves to Grok.\\n> \\n> Also adds a Grok integration probe script, registry/hooks wiring, and a small **redact** test fix quoting `go.mod` replace paths with spaces.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 9d6c40b389990d0d9634eb078c9ecbbc8eabfa8e. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2127/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2127/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2327\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2327/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2327/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2327/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2327\",\n              \"id\": 5391178766,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABCuhTvw\",\n              \"number\": 2327,\n              \"title\": \"feat(checkpoint): add `entire checkpoint migrate`\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"toby\",\n                \"id\": 83556,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNTU2\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83556?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toby\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/toby\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toby/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toby/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toby/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toby/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toby/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toby/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toby/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toby/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/toby/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-08T19:45:32Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-15T18:35:00Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2327\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2327\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2327.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2327.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1271\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n> **Stacked on #2335** (`feat(checkpoint): elect the Entire remote for checkpoint sync`). Review that first; this PR's base is its branch and will be retargeted to `main` once it merges. Best reviewed **commit by commit**: the four commits are layered so each builds and is reviewable on its own.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nOnce an Entire remote is elected (#2335), new checkpoints flow there, but the ones already pushed to GitHub stay behind. This PR brings that backlog over, verifies it, and cleans up the old remote with consent, then rewards the user with what they have accumulated.\\n\\n## Commits\\n\\n1. **`feat(strategy): checkpoint artifact migration engine`** — inventory, hydrate into a tmp namespace and promote via `SafelyAdvanceLocalRef`, requeue, verify at the local hash, chunked delete. Removal addresses the old remote by its single push URL so the dedicated-`checkpoint_remote` rewrite can never apply, and refuses fan-out remotes. `batchPushRefs` chunks refspecs (a backlog publish overran ARG_MAX); `PushQueue.EnqueueAll`; `remote.DeleteRefs` (trail cleanup reuses it); the ls-remote parser moves into the `checkpoint` package. **Review question:** can anything be deleted that was not verified? Never force-pushed?\\n2. **`feat(checkpoint): migration planner, copy and value summary`** — the pure planner over the repo's state (no remotes, dedicated store, fail-closed setting, choice among remotes, pinned elsewhere, already home, publish only, migrate, convert first) and every user-facing string in one file; the local value block; `formatTokenCount` gains `M`. **Review question:** are the states and the copy right?\\n3. **`feat(checkpoint): add entire checkpoint migrate`** — the command. Two planning passes (local facts, then ls-remote inventories), pickers whose first option is always no-change, `--to` recorded in `.entire/settings.local.json` only when the election would not already pick it, git-branch repos converted to refs and flipped, publish through the OPF- and policy-gated queue flush, verify, then delete only verified refs and only with consent (`--remove` when non-interactive; `--yes` never implies it). Bare non-interactive runs report and change nothing. Classified user-owned and unlisted in agent-help. **Review question:** is the non-interactive contract safe for agents?\\n4. **`feat(status): surface the checkpoint migration in status, doctor, enable and docs`** — the network-free status nudge and `checkpoint_sync_migration` JSON field, doctor's destination check, the re-enable pointer, the command name restored in the announcement, hint and topology advice, and the docs.\\n\\n## Decisions for reviewers\\n\\n- `checkpoint migrate` is **user-owned and unlisted** in agent-help: it pushes transcripts, deletes remote refs and writes settings.\\n- The backend flip writes the **project** `.entire/settings.json` (a repo-wide format decision) and prints a commit hint; it is skipped under `ENTIRE_CHECKPOINTS_PRIMARY`.\\n- The ledger records `done` once data is verified on the destination, and `declined` when cleanup is refused; both silence the status nudge.\\n- No prompt inside `git push`; the hook announces and points at the command. Offering the migration from `repo mirror use`, which creates the remote, is a natural follow-up.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- `mise run lint`: 0 issues. Full unit and integration suites (both backends) and the Vogon canary pass on the stack.\\n- New: 14 engine tests over two local bares, 30-row planner table, executor tests against a fake engine (verify-missing stops before remove, remove failure keeps the ledger honest, decline records declined, `--yes` never removes, `--dry-run` only lists), status rendering tests, and seven end-to-end `checkpoint migrate` scenarios on both backends.\\n- Copilot's earlier comment that `for i := range count` does not compile is incorrect (Go 1.22+; this module is Go 1.26) and its suggested patch would not compile; the test passes.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2327/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2327/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2180\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2180/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2180/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2180/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2180\",\n              \"id\": 5294323027,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBhzniQ\",\n              \"number\": 2180,\n              \"title\": \"Confine Entire's filesystem use to `os.Root` anchors\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"pjbgf\",\n                \"id\": 5452977,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NTI5Nzc=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5452977?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pjbgf\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-30T20:54:52Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-01T13:15:42Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-01T13:15:40Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2180\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2180\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2180.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2180.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-01T13:15:40Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1184\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\nEstablish os.Root anchors for the seven trees Entire reads and writes using names it does not control, including agent session IDs, tool-use IDs, investigation run IDs, git status output, and checkpoint tree entries fetched from a remote. Each tree has one owning abstraction, and operations beneath an anchor reject symlinks instead of merely relying on os.Root\\r\\n  containment.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ### Anchors\\r\\n\\r\\n  One owning abstraction per tree: entiredir, gitdir, worktreedir, agent.SessionStore, agent.HookConfigFile, userdirs, and pluginRoot.\\r\\n\\r\\n  Long-lived anchors are memoized through a single osroot.Shared registry. agent.SessionStore is intentionally opened per operation because transcript fallback search may probe hundreds of candidate directories; retaining those roots in the non-evicting registry would consume one file descriptor per candidate.\\r\\n\\r\\n  Resolver-derived files must use the anchor for their owning tree. They must not create an anchor from filepath.Dir of the target being opened, because that places the caller-resolved components above the root and leaves them unenforced. Explicit caller-named settings and token-store paths are documented exceptions because the parent directory is itself part of the caller’s selection.\\r\\n\\r\\n  TestRootBasesAreTrusted fails the build when a new root-opening site is not on the allowlist, or when an allowlisted site no longer opens a root.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ### Refusals\\r\\n\\r\\n  - .entire must be a real directory, and every direct entry must be a regular file or directory. Four distinct failure conditions are matched positively so the reported remedy fits the  fault.\\r\\n\\r\\n  - Symlinks are refused, not followed or silently skipped, in trees Entire owns, including at a walk root and in every component beneath an anchor.\\r\\n\\r\\n    fs.WalkDir obtains its root DirEntry using fs.Stat, which follows symlinks, while only entries below the root come from ReadDir. The previous callback guards inspected d.Type(), so\\r\\n    they did not protect the walk root. A symlinked .entire/metadata/<session> could therefore be traversed and have its target committed and pushed. This protection had previously existed\\r\\n    with filepath.Walk, which uses Lstat, and was lost during conversion.\\r\\n\\r\\n  - Filesystem operations pin path components instead of checking and resolving them again. Parent directories are opened one component at a time, with symlinks rejected at every level.\\r\\n    Reads, writes, directory creation, removal, enumeration, and walks then operate relative to those pinned descriptors. This closes the check/use gap where an attacker could replace a\\r\\n    verified directory before the subsequent operation.\\r\\n\\r\\n  - Worktree content read or modified by Entire also rejects symlink components where following them would redirect the operation. This includes agent hook configuration, managed agent\\r\\n    scaffold files, .gitignore, .worktreeinclude, agent session files, and files read for trail-review selected text.\\r\\n\\r\\n  - Settings resolved by Entire are never read through a link, enforced in the settings reader itself because eighteen call sites invoke settings.Load without passing through the pre-run\\r\\n    guard. Explicit caller-selected settings paths trust the caller-selected parent as their root but still refuse a symlink at the target file.\\r\\n\\r\\n  - “We could not find out” is not “there is nothing here.” WorktreeRoot falls back to the current directory only after Git positively reports that the directory is not in a repository. It\\r\\n    does not fall back when Git is absent from $PATH, repository ownership is dubious, the context is cancelled, or repository discovery otherwise fails.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ### Interrupted atomic writes\\r\\n\\r\\n  jsonutil.WriteFileAtomicIn creates a temporary file named <base>.<16 hex>.tmp beside its target. Because .entire/metadata/<session> is copied wholesale into checkpoint trees, a hook\\r\\n  killed during an atomic write could leave an orphan that was committed in every later checkpoint.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ParseChunkIndex also previously used fmt.Sscanf(\\\"%03d\\\"), which stops successfully at the first non-digit. A temporary file whose random suffix began with digits could therefore be\\r\\n  interpreted as a transcript chunk.\\r\\n\\r\\n  Checkpoint walks now recognize and ignore only the complete temporary-file naming pattern, while ParseChunkIndex accepts only an entirely numeric suffix.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ### Repository opening\\r\\n  gitrepo.OpenCurrent no longer falls back to OpenPath(\\\".\\\") when the worktree root cannot be established.\\r\\n\\r\\n  The single caller that intentionally wants best-effort cwd behavior uses OpenCurrentOrCwd explicitly. It is dispatched from main.go after Cobra processing, reads only a policy ref, and\\r\\n  discards every error.\\r\\n\\r\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n> [!NOTE]\\r\\n> **High Risk**\\r\\n> Broad security and correctness changes to path containment, symlink handling, repository resolution, and checkpoint metadata walks; misconfiguration could break enable/hooks, transcript restore, or open the wrong repo in edge cases.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> **Overview**\\r\\n> Routes Entire’s sensitive filesystem work through **trusted `os.Root` anchors** (`.entire`, git common dir, worktree, hook configs, session stores, etc.) instead of assembling absolute paths and calling plain `os.*`. **CLAUDE.md** documents the seven trees, symlink refusal, atomic-write temp handling, and when rooting is deliberately skipped.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> **Agent hook configs** now go through shared **`agent.HookConfigFile`** / `OpenHookConfig` on the worktree root (all built-in agents), so `entire enable` cannot create or write through a checked-in symlinked `.claude` / `.cursor` / `.codex` / etc. **Session transcript writes** are centralized in **`agent.SessionStore`** and **`WriteSessionFile`**, rejecting session IDs that escape the agent’s session directory. **`.entire` transcript caches** (OpenCode export, Pi hook cache, Factory fallback state) use **`entiredir`** + **`ReadTranscriptFile`** / **`StatTranscriptFile`** for reads under `.entire`.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> **Checkpoint safety:** `ParseChunkIndex` only accepts an all-digit suffix (no more `fmt.Sscanf` mis-reading `full.jsonl.<hex>.tmp` as a chunk); walks are documented to skip `jsonutil` temp names. **`gitrepo.OpenCurrent`** no longer falls back to `OpenPath(\\\".\\\")` when the worktree cannot be resolved; **`OpenCurrentOrCwd`** is reserved for the one advisory caller. External-agent discovery tests inject worktree root via **`settings.WithWorktreeRoot`** instead of relying on removed cwd-relative settings fallbacks.\\r\\n> \\r\\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 1d863f6ed67cbd5f95b1a45a26f75a2c386b3143. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\r\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2180/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2180/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2188\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2188/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2188/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2188/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2188\",\n              \"id\": 5298216312,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABBk0ABA\",\n              \"number\": 2188,\n              \"title\": \"fix(strategy): bound turn checkpoint finalization\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"id\": 34813274,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODEzMjc0\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34813274?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/MuskanPaliwal\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/MuskanPaliwal/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-31T08:41:55Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-16T08:29:55Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-16T08:29:55Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2188\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2188\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2188.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2188.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-16T08:29:55Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Closes #2148\\n\\nAt turn end, finalize rewrites every checkpoint the turn created with the full transcript. Each rewrite can fetch refs and blobs from the remote. Every fetch has its own limit, and the dead-network memos keep a remote that is down from costing that limit once per checkpoint. Nothing limited the pass as a whole, though. A slow remote that still answers finishes each fetch just under its limit, trips neither memo, and the total outlasts the host's hook timeout. The host kills the hook before Entire saves session state. The checkpoints keep their provisional transcripts, and the only trace is a few warning logs.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\nThe network phase of `finalizeAllTurnCheckpoints`, meaning the checkpoint store open and the write loop, now runs under a deadline. The deadline comes from the real limit the agent's host puts on the turn-end hook.\\n\\n**Finalize checks the deadline at entry and in the network phase, never in the middle of local work.** If the deadline has already passed at entry, finalize doesn't start. Nothing it prepared could be written by then, and the hook needs that time to save state. Reading, sanitizing, externalizing and redacting the transcript is local work that never looks at the context, so nothing cuts it off halfway. Its time still counts against the budget. If it runs long, finalize stops at the first network step instead of starting fetches it can't finish. Finalize checks again after the store opens, so precompute doesn't hash the transcript for writes that will never start. A write that fails as the deadline passes logs its error, and finalize then counts it as an interruption.\\n\\n**The deadline is `processStart` plus a per-agent budget**, the same pattern `sessionEndCondenseDeadline` uses. The host starts its clock when it spawns the hook, so Entire starts its clock at process start too. The budget comes from the agent running the hook, not from `state.AgentType`, which can be empty.\\n\\n**Each agent declares its host's turn-end hook timeout** through a new `agent.TurnEndHookTimeouter` capability. Entire derives the budget from it in one place, so changing the timeout changes the budget too. #1237 just changed Claude Code's. `agent.TurnEndBudgetWithin` keeps a fifth of the timeout, between 2s and 10s, for saving state after finalize. A timeout of zero or less falls back to the default.\\n\\n| Agent | Turn-end hook limit | Source | Budget |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Claude Code | 120s | `checkpointHookTimeoutSec` | 110s |\\n| Antigravity | 300s | `stopHookTimeoutSeconds` | 290s |\\n| Factory AI Droid | 60s | Host default ([docs](https://docs.factory.com/reference/hooks-reference)) | 50s |\\n| Codex | 30s | `defaultHookTimeoutSec` | 24s |\\n| Copilot CLI | 30s | Host default ([docs](https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/reference/hooks-configuration)) | 24s |\\n| Pi | 10s | The extension's `execFile` timeout, pinned by a test | 8s |\\n| Cursor, OpenCode, Vogon, external agents | Unknown or none | `defaultTurnEndHookTimeout` (30s) | 24s |\\n\\n`TestTurnEndHookTimeoutLedger` makes every built-in agent either declare a timeout or appear in `turnEndHookTimeoutFallbacks` with a reason, and it fails on a stale entry. A new agent can't pick up the default by accident. External agents always get the default, because the protocol has no field for a hook timeout.\\n\\n## When finalize is cut short\\n\\n- Checkpoints finalize already rewrote keep the full transcript. The rest keep their provisional one.\\n- The unfinalized IDs stay in `TurnCheckpointIDs`, as they already do for the late-transcript and degraded-scanner exits. A second Stop in the same turn retries them with a fresh budget. Otherwise the next turn start clears them and the provisional transcripts stay for good. I expect the retry to be rare. Claude Code, Codex, Copilot CLI and most other hosts fire Stop once per turn, so for them a cut-off checkpoint keeps its provisional transcript. That's the price of finishing inside the host's limit, and I think it's the right trade.\\n- Finalize sets `CaptureDegradedAt`, so `entire status` reports the problem. This now covers the host cancelling the hook too (SIGTERM ends the root context), which used to leave no trace.\\n- Finalize records the interruption where it sees it rather than guessing afterwards. An ordinary write error doesn't count as degradation. One older path also keeps the IDs; see \\\"Not included\\\".\\n- A cut-off checkpoint shows up once, as capture degradation, and not again as a finalize error.\\n\\n## Older Antigravity installs\\n\\nThe Antigravity budget assumes the 300s Stop timeout Entire installs. Installs from before bd1e2ff72 have no timeout, so agy's 30s default applies and kills the hook long before the 290s budget runs out. `AntigravityAgent.RepairHookTimeouts` lets `entire doctor` add the missing timeout without asking, the same repair Claude Code already has. It edits the raw JSON, so keys Entire doesn't model survive. It only touches Entire's own Stop handler, which it finds by command. It keeps a timeout that's already set under any key case, skips null entries, and leaves a disabled entry alone. The doctor message now covers an agent default that's too short as well as one that's too long.\\n\\nDoctor only helps people who run it. So Antigravity now also reports a missing Stop timeout through `CheckHookConfig`, and `entire status` shows \\\"Antigravity hooks out of date · run 'entire doctor'\\\". `--json` lists the agent under `hooks_outdated`. The check and the repair share one function, so status flags an install exactly when doctor has a timeout to add. Running doctor always clears the warning. A user's own handlers, a timeout they set, or a disabled entry never trigger it.\\n\\n## Decision for reviewers\\n\\n**The 30s fallback** is a judgment call. Cursor documents only a \\\"platform default\\\". OpenCode has no limit at all. Entire's plugin runs the hook through `spawnSync`, which blocks OpenCode's UI until `entire` exits, so the fallback is the only limit OpenCode gets. 30s matches what Codex and Copilot enforce. It's one constant in `lifecycle.go`.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nFinalize deadline tests:\\n\\n- With no deadline, a future deadline, or slow fetches and no deadline, every checkpoint finalizes.\\n- A deadline that passed before the network phase, a deadline that expires mid-loop while the parent context lives, a context that ends mid-loop, and a parent cancelled before start each leave the right checkpoints provisional. Each records degradation and counts no error.\\n- An expired deadline at entry skips preparation, keeps the IDs and records degradation.\\n- A deadline that passes while finalize prepares the transcript stops it before any fetch or precompute and keeps the IDs.\\n- When the host cancels the hook during preparation, the repository open fails. Finalize counts that as an interruption, not an error, and keeps the IDs.\\n- A second pass over kept IDs finalizes them and clears the list.\\n- An invalid checkpoint ID, or a write that fails while the context is alive, counts as an error and not as degradation.\\n- The degraded-scanner and late-transcript exits keep their IDs under an expired deadline.\\n- The logs give the deadline as its own cause, so a host cancellation never looks like the budget running out.\\n\\nAgent and budget tests:\\n\\n- Every agent that declares a timeout gets a budget above zero and below that timeout.\\n- Pi's Go constant matches the `.ts` extension.\\n- The ledger test above.\\n\\nAntigravity tests:\\n\\n- The repair adds a missing Stop timeout. It keeps an existing timeout, including `\\\"Timeout\\\"` in another case, and keeps unmodeled keys, foreign entries, a user's handler in the Stop list, `null` entries and a disabled entry. It leaves the file alone when there's nothing to add.\\n- The status check reports absent with no Entire entry, and current for a fresh install, an existing timeout in either case, a user's handler, or a disabled entry. It reports outdated only for Entire's Stop handler with no timeout.\\n\\nHow the timing tests stay deterministic:\\n\\n- In the parent-cancel mid-loop case, the fake fetcher ends the context itself.\\n- In the deadline mid-loop case, the second fetch blocks until the deadline fires. A 10s fallback makes a regression fail instead of hang. The deadline is 3s because it also covers transcript preparation and the store open, which leaves a slow runner time to reach the first fetch.\\n- The two preparation tests block the transcript read on a FIFO, so the deadline or the cancellation lands while preparation runs. Each test also fails if finalize exits before it reaches the read, so neither can pass on the entry check. They run on Unix only, since they need a FIFO.\\n\\nI checked each new test against a planted regression, and each one failed. The regressions were the deadline check moved to the top, the checks around the store open removed, the repository-open interruption check removed, writes ignoring the deadline, cancellation not flagged, a write error flagged as degradation, interrupted IDs cleared or kept off by one, Pi's constant drifting, and a missing or stale ledger entry.\\n\\nI also ran it end to end with a built binary. An Antigravity install with the Stop timeout removed shows the `entire status` warning. `entire doctor` adds the 300s timeout and the warning goes away. A fresh install shows no warning.\\n\\nOn the final commit, format, lint (0 issues), and the unit, integration and canary tests all pass.\\n\\n## Not included\\n\\n- No durable retry queue for cut-off checkpoints.\\n- No change to the per-fetch budgets, and no batching of missing-blob fetches.\\n- Entire doesn't read a hook timeout the user lowered themselves in Claude Code, Codex, Antigravity or Copilot CLI. The budget comes from the timeout Entire installs or the host default.\\n- Entire doesn't write an explicit timeout into Cursor's hook config. That would swap the fallback for a known limit. But existing installs only get a hook config change through a doctor repair, so it belongs in its own PR.\\n- Local turn-end work counts against the budget, because the clock starts at process start like the host's. For an agent with no host limit, such as OpenCode, finalize can now give up on checkpoints that used to finish when local work runs long. A longer default for agents we know have no limit would fix that. Follow-up.\\n- Local preparation has no time limit once it starts. Finalize checks the deadline before and after it, so a long preparation never starts fetches, but preparation itself can eat into the headroom. Cursor's sidecar image read can take up to `sqlite3Timeout` (30s) against the assumed 30s hook limit. Pi has 2s of headroom to redact what may be a large transcript. The cheap fix is to cap the sidecar read at whatever deadline is left. Follow-up.\\n- If a turn start is missed because its hook failed or was killed, the kept IDs carry into the next turn. That turn's Stop then rewrites the older checkpoints with the newer turn's transcript and prompts, and skips the prompt backfill. The late-transcript and degraded-scanner exits could already do this. A slow remote makes it more likely. Follow-up.\\n- If the checkpoint store fails to open for any reason other than the deadline, finalize still returns with `TurnCheckpointIDs` set and doesn't record capture degradation. That predates this PR. Follow-up.\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2188/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2188/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1211\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1211/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1211/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1211/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1211\",\n              \"id\": 4443057024,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7bX4-E\",\n              \"number\": 1211,\n              \"title\": \"feat: entire prompts search - searchable prompt history from checkpoints\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"AasheeshLikePanner\",\n                \"id\": 126905285,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOB5BrxQ\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/126905285?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/AasheeshLikePanner\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/AasheeshLikePanner\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/AasheeshLikePanner/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/AasheeshLikePanner/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/AasheeshLikePanner/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/AasheeshLikePanner/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/AasheeshLikePanner/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/AasheeshLikePanner/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/AasheeshLikePanner/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/AasheeshLikePanner/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/AasheeshLikePanner/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 6,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-05-14T04:04:24Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:29:05Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:29:05Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": true,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1211\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1211\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1211.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1211.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary:\\r\\n\\r\\nImplements `entire prompts` — a local, offline-first command for searching the prompts behind your checkpoint history. This is the \\\"search\\\" feature from the roadmap: surfacing the *why* behind commits, not just the *what*.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## What's in this PR\\r\\n\\r\\nFour commands:\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\nentire prompts search \\\"cache decision\\\"     # full-text search with filters\\r\\nentire prompts list                         # recent prompts, newest first\\r\\nentire prompts show <checkpoint-id>        # full prompt text for a checkpoint\\r\\nentire prompts index --rebuild / --status  # manage the local index\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nFilters on search: `--agent`, `--branch`, `--kind`, `--after`, `--files`, `--limit`, `--json`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## How it works \\r\\n\\r\\nOn every commit, the PostCommit hook appends a new entry to `.entire/prompts/index.ndjson` — a gitignored, appendable newline-delimited JSON file that lives next to your repo. No external service, no database, works offline.\\r\\n\\r\\nOn search, the index loads into memory and each entry gets scored:\\r\\n- Exact phrase match → +10\\r\\n- All query tokens found → +5  \\r\\n- Any token found → +1\\r\\n- Term density bonus → up to +2\\r\\n\\r\\nTokenization runs NFC unicode normalization → lowercase → word boundary split → stopword filter → Porter stemmer. So `\\\"caching\\\"` matches prompts containing `\\\"cache\\\"`, `\\\"cached\\\"`, `\\\"caches\\\"`.\\r\\n\\r\\nQueries are sanitised before tokenizing — regex metacharacters stripped, minimum 2-char guard, quoted phrases extracted for exact matching.\\r\\n\\r\\nFile locking on writes: `O_CREATE|O_EXCL` for atomic acquisition, 3 retries with 50ms backoff for concurrent PostCommit hooks, stale lock detection (>30s) to survive crashes.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## Architecture decisions\\r\\n\\r\\n- **NDJSON over SQLite** — appendable without full rewrites, no CGO, human-readable, portable\\r\\n- **Porter stemmer** (`github.com/kljensen/snowball`) — one new pure-Go dependency, zero CGO\\r\\n- **Local index, not cloud** — prompts are personal context, should stay local and work offline\\r\\n- **PostCommit hook integration** — index updates happen transparently, no user action needed\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## Tests\\r\\n\\r\\n19 tests across `rank_test.go` and `store_test.go`:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Tokenizer: stemming, stopwords, unicode normalization, special chars\\r\\n- Query parser: basic, phrase extraction, regex stripping, min length\\r\\n- Scorer: exact phrase, all tokens, term density\\r\\n- Search: ranking, empty query, filter application\\r\\n- Store: concurrent writes, single entry, empty slice, lock contention\\r\\n\\r\\nBenchmarks:\\r\\n- Tokenize: ~0.1ms\\r\\n- Search 1K entries: 5.6ms (target <100ms)\\r\\n- Index load 1K entries: 2.8ms (target <50ms)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Tested live** against 4 real checkpoints, 94 prompts, 98KB index. Search, list, show all working end-to-end.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## Known gaps \\r\\n\\r\\nThree things are stubbed or incomplete — none affect the core feature working:\\r\\n\\r\\n- `ReviewPrompt` for `agent_review` kind not yet wired — entries with `kind: agent_review` fall back to empty prompt text. Will fix in follow-up.\\r\\n- `TokenCount`, `ParentCheckpointID`, `SubagentDepth` fields exist in the schema but aren't populated from metadata yet.\\r\\n- `entire prompts index --verify` flag exists but is a no-op placeholder.\\r\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1211/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1211/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1560\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1560/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1560/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1560/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1560\",\n              \"id\": 4770320551,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7r5DhN\",\n              \"number\": 1560,\n              \"title\": \"explain: enrich JSON summary and surface list truncation\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"computermode\",\n                \"id\": 2917645,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTc2NDU=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2917645?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/computermode\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-06-29T17:37:50Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-29T20:43:53Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-06-29T20:43:52Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1560\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1560\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1560.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1560.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-06-29T20:43:52Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/692\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What\\n\\nEnriches `entire explain` output across four small, related gaps:\\n\\n1. **Full summary in `--json`** — the JSON export previously dropped everything except `intent`/`outcome`, even though the prose view already renders friction, open items, and learnings. `--json` now exposes the full persisted `Summary` (`friction`, `open_items`, and categorized `learnings` → `repo`/`code`/`workflow`).\\n2. **List truncation visibility** — the prose branch list silently capped at 100 checkpoints. It now prints a stderr note when checkpoints are hidden, pointing at `--json --limit <N>`.\\n3. **Fast-fail `--generate` on imported checkpoints** — the read-only rejection now happens on metadata alone, before fetching transcript blobs.\\n4. **Clearer no-trailer message** — distinguishes a commit that exists but wasn't created during an Entire session from a commit that wasn't found.\\n\\n## How\\n\\n- `explain_export.go`: extended `checkpointSessionSummary` with `learnings`/`friction`/`open_items` (all `omitempty`); new `summaryToExportJSON` helper reuses the existing `hasAnyLearning` so empty learnings stay `nil` (no `{}` noise). Redaction is already applied upstream at persist time, so no new privacy surface.\\n- `explain.go`: branch list probes `branchCheckpointsLimit+1` and slices to the cap via the extracted, unit-tested `capBranchCheckpoints`; threaded `errW` through the call chain. Added a metadata-only `ReadCheckpoint` guard before the content load for imported `--generate`. Reworded the no-trailer hint.\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- The `--limit` flag help still reads \\\"Only meaningful with --json\\\" — accurate, since the prose path keeps the fixed 100 cap and points users at `--json --limit` rather than honoring `--limit` itself.\\n- Truncation wording is deliberately vague (\\\"more exist\\\") — the `limit+1` probe only proves ≥1 more exists, never an exact count.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n`mise run check` passes: fmt clean, lint 0 issues, all unit + integration + e2e canary tests green. New tests: `TestSessionMetadataToJSON_FullSummary`, `TestSessionMetadataToJSON_EmptySummaryStaysClean`, `TestCapBranchCheckpoints`, plus a `--generate`-on-imported rejection assertion in `TestImportClaudeCode_EndToEnd`.\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> CLI output and JSON export parity only; no auth, persistence, or security surface changes beyond exposing summary fields already stored and shown in prose.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **`entire checkpoint explain --json`** now includes the full persisted session summary—`friction`, `open_items`, and categorized `learnings`—via `summaryToExportJSON`, matching what the prose view already shows. Empty categories stay omitted (`omitempty`).\\n> \\n> **Branch / list views** (`checkpoint list`, default explain) fetch `limit+1` checkpoints, cap at 100 with `capBranchCheckpoints`, and print a **stderr** note when more exist (pointing at `--json --limit <N>`). `errW` is threaded through the branch explain call chain so truncation never pollutes piped stdout.\\n> \\n> **`--generate`** on imported checkpoints is rejected after a metadata-only `ReadCheckpoint` check, avoiding prefetch and transcript loads for a guaranteed read-only failure.\\n> \\n> The **no Entire-Checkpoint trailer** hint now states the commit exists but was not created in an Entire session (or the trailer was removed).\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit cdd32fa9502414035a774a59b97a3d615ed87bdc. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1560/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1560/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1527\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1527/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1527/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1527/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1527\",\n              \"id\": 4747651055,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7qwUr-\",\n              \"number\": 1527,\n              \"title\": \"Add import tool for sessions prior to enabling Entire\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"computermode\",\n                \"id\": 2917645,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTc2NDU=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2917645?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/computermode\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/computermode/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-06-25T21:52:39Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-26T19:52:05Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-06-26T00:53:21Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1527\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1527\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1527.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1527.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-06-26T00:53:21Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/668\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\n## What\\r\\n\\r\\nAdds the ability to import a coding agent's pre-existing local transcripts into Entire as read-only checkpoints, so a repo adopting Entire isn't starting from zero (`checkpoint list`/`explain`, `search`, `tokens`, and server-side recap/UI work on day-one history). Supports #1336 (enable doesn't prompt to import yet - requires manual kickoff for validation first). Claude Code is the only agent implemented; the package is structured so others can be added.\\r\\n\\r\\nSurface: a hidden command, discoverable via `entire labs`:\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\nentire import claude-code [--path DIR] [--dry-run] [--session ID]...\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nThere is intentionally **no** enable-time prompt this pass — importing is an explicit, opt-in command.\\r\\n\\r\\n## How\\r\\n\\r\\n- New `cmd/entire/cli/agentimport/` package. The orchestration (discovery loop, idempotent per-turn IDs, redaction, checkpoint write) is agent-agnostic; each agent plugs in an `Importer` (`Discover` + `SplitTurns`). A static list of supported importers backs `entire import <agent>` — adding an agent is a new `Importer`, no command wiring.\\r\\n- Discovers `~/.claude/projects/<sanitized-repo-path>/*.jsonl` (fixed **one-month** lookback), splits each session into **per-user-prompt turns**, and writes one checkpoint per turn — reusing existing transcript parsing, per-turn token accounting (incl. subagent rollups), and redaction (`redact.JSONLBytes`).\\r\\n- Imported checkpoints are stored on the normal `entire/checkpoints/v1` metadata branch, tagged `Kind:\\\"imported\\\"` with provenance (source, session/turn UUIDs, line range, content hash, import version). They're **commit-less** (no `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer) and surface in `list`/`explain` via an `Imported` flag, labeled `[imported]`.\\r\\n- **Idempotent**: per-turn checkpoint IDs are `sha256(sessionID + \\\"/\\\" + turnUUID)`, so re-running skips already-imported turns.\\r\\n- **Not rewindable**: `checkpoint rewind` refuses imported checkpoints with a clear read-only message.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Tradeoffs / known limitations (do later)\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Import is manual.** It is not offered during `entire enable` (an earlier iteration prompted at enable time; removed for now). Users run `entire import claude-code` when they want it.\\r\\n- **Imported history is pushed** to the backend like normal checkpoints (it's what lights up server-side search/recap/UI). **Privacy note:** up to a month of old conversations (and provenance such as `transcript_path`) sync on the next push, unless checkpoint pushing is disabled. (An earlier iteration kept imports local-only on a separate `entire/imports/v1` ref; reverted — it caused explain-by-id and `[temporary]`-duplication bugs and was a cross-cutting overhaul. Single-ref is simpler; a local-only/opt-in-to-push mode could be revisited.)\\r\\n- **Read-only** by design: imported checkpoints have no working-tree snapshot, so they are not rewindable.\\r\\n- **Claude Code only** this pass (the package and `entire import <agent>` surface leave room for others).\\r\\n\\r\\n## Reviewer notes\\r\\n\\r\\n- `Kind:\\\"imported\\\"` + `Provenance` + an `Imported` umbrella flag were added to the checkpoint metadata contract (`api/checkpoint`).\\r\\n- Verified locally: `mise run lint` (0 issues) and `mise run test:ci` (unit + integration + e2e canary) green; an end-to-end integration test covers dry-run, import, `[imported]` labeling (no `[temporary]` duplication), explain-by-id, idempotency, and rewind refusal.\\r\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1527/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1527/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1616\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1616/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1616/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1616/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1616\",\n              \"id\": 4798051681,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7tTsv6\",\n              \"number\": 1616,\n              \"title\": \"cli: add code search with multi-region fan-out and TUI tab (ENT-990)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"evisdren\",\n                \"id\": 256443556,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD0kEpA\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256443556?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/evisdren\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/evisdren/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 10,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-07-02T20:43:34Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-07T19:30:45Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-07T19:30:44Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1616\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1616\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1616.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1616.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-07T19:30:44Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\n- Adds `cmd/entire/cli/codesearch/` — client package for peregrine's `/search/api/search` endpoint\\n- Wires `--code` and `--case-sensitive` flags into `entire search`, gated behind `ENTIRE_CODE_SEARCH=1`\\n- Multi-region fan-out using the shared cell-routing foundation (`cell_fanout.go`): list repos → group by cell → parallel search with per-cell timeouts → merge results\\n- Adds a **Code tab** (key `4`) to the interactive search TUI, showing code search results alongside checkpoints, sessions, and commits\\n- Code search runs in parallel with checkpoint search when the TUI launches\\n- Detail pane shows file location, score, and context lines (before/after) for the selected match\\n\\n## How it works\\n\\n| Scenario | Auth path | Behavior |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `--code query` (no filter) | `ListRepos` → group by cell → `fanOutCells` | Fan-out across all cells |\\n| `--code --repo owner/name query` | Single cell via repo filter resolution | Single cell (repo's owner) |\\n| `--code repo:owner/name query` | Same (inline filter parsed) | Single cell |\\n| `--code --all-repos query` | Fan-out (same as no filter) | Fan-out across all cells |\\n| TUI Code tab | Async `performCodeSearch` tea.Cmd | Parallel with checkpoint search |\\n\\n## TUI Code Tab\\n\\n- Hidden behind `ENTIRE_CODE_SEARCH=1` feature flag (tab only appears when enabled)\\n- Results show `repo:path:line` as the title with the matching context line below\\n- Detail pane shows full context (before/after lines), repo, path, line, column, and score\\n- Full-screen detail view via Enter key, same as other tabs\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/codesearch/codesearch.go` — client types and `Search()` function\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/codesearch/codesearch_test.go` — client tests\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search_cmd.go` — command wiring, fan-out via shared `fanOutCells`, output formatters\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search_cmd_test.go` — command tests (merge, output, flags)\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search_tui.go` — Code tab: result rendering, detail pane, async fetch, key bindings\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/search_tui_test.go` — updated for new `newSearchModel` signature\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/codesearch/...` passes\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/ -run TestSearch` passes\\n- [x] `mise run lint` clean\\n- [x] Manual testing with `ENTIRE_CODE_SEARCH=1 entire search auth`\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> New authenticated multi-cell fan-out and repo-index resolution can return incomplete results on truncation or partial failures; behavior is gated but touches core search UX and shared cell routing.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Introduces **code search** for `entire search`, behind **`ENTIRE_CODE_SEARCH=1`**, calling peregrine via a new **`codesearch`** package (`GET /api/v1/search/api/search` through the cell API gateway).\\n> \\n> **CLI:** New **`--code`** and **`--case-sensitive`** flags; checkpoint-only flags (`--author`, `--date`, `--branch`, `--page`) are rejected with `--code`. Repo scoping uses **`--repo`**, **`--all-repos`**, or inline **`repo:`** only—**`author:` / `date:` / `branch:`** stay in the query as literal text. Default scope is the current repo via **`currentRepoSlugWithForge`** (forge-prefixed slugs for index matching). Output is grep-style text or JSON, including **`failed_jurisdictions`** on partial multi-region failures.\\n> \\n> **Routing:** **`searchAllCells`** lists repos from the control plane, resolves filters to ULIDs (**`resolveRepoFilters`**, BFF-aligned), groups by cell, and uses shared **`fanOutCells`** with per-cell timeouts; **`mergeSearchResults`** ranks by score, dedupes, caps **`--limit`**, and tolerates partial cell errors.\\n> \\n> **TUI:** When the flag is on, search gains a **Code** tab (key **4**), async code search alongside checkpoint search, list/detail UI for matches, and generation-guarded stale result handling.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 66a9c67767467f64c0db19841cb1b6b94f9f5faf. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1616/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1616/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1650\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1650/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1650/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1650/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1650\",\n              \"id\": 4819808169,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7uYOwS\",\n              \"number\": 1650,\n              \"title\": \"cli: show recent sessions (not commits) in `entire activity`\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-07-06T13:54:16Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-06T18:24:24Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-06T18:24:22Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1650\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1650\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1650.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1650.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-06T18:24:22Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/769\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nThe entire.io Overview page renders a recent-**sessions** feed from `GET /api/v1/me/sessions`, but `entire activity` rendered a recent-**commits** feed from `/me/commits`. The two surfaces listed different things, so a session with no resulting commit never showed in the CLI, and a commit bundling several sessions showed as one row — the lists never lined up.\\n\\n## What\\n\\nMake sessions the default recent-list in `entire activity`, matching the web exactly. The stat cards, contribution heatmap, and repo chart (all from `/me/activity`) are unchanged; only the bottom list changes.\\n\\n- **Sessions feed** — fetch `/me/sessions` at `limit=50` (mirroring the web's `USER_OVERVIEW_RECENT_SESSIONS_LIMIT`), group by the local day of `lastActivityAt` (newest first, unknown last), and render one row per session with the same fields the web row shows: display name (capped at 120), repo, a `public` tag when `isPublic`, agent badge, friendly model label, and checkpoint count.\\n- **Commits stay available** behind `entire activity --commits`.\\n- **`formatModel` ported** from `entire.io/frontend/src/lib/model.ts` to Go so labels read identically (`claude-opus-4-6` → \\\"Opus 4.6\\\", `gpt-4o` → \\\"GPT-4o\\\", `gemini-2.0-flash` → \\\"Gemini 2.0 Flash\\\", legacy date suffixes stripped). Same test cases as the web's `model.test.ts`.\\n- **Routing** — reuses the existing `runAuthenticatedActivityAPI`, so `/me/sessions` goes to the caller's home entire-api cell with the data-API fallback (the routing landed in #1641).\\n- **Dedup** — extracts `fetchActivityWith` (activity aggregate + chosen list, fetched concurrently) and a generic `groupItemsByDay`, so the session and commit paths don't duplicate the plumbing.\\n\\n`entire agent-help activity` picks up the new `--commits` flag automatically (it renders live from the cobra tree).\\n\\n### Endpoint note\\n\\n`/me/sessions` reports `isPublic: false` unconditionally today (entire-api has no GitHub-login-on-session source), so the `public` tag is implemented for correctness but will rarely render from the cell — matching the repo sessions surface.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- New unit tests: `formatModel` (mirrors the web's `model.test.ts`), `groupSessionsByDay` (ordering + unknown-date handling), `fetchSessions` (path/window/envelope parsing via httptest), and session-row rendering (fields, singular/plural, untitled fallback).\\n- `mise run fmt` clean, `mise run lint` 0 issues, `mise run test:ci` green (unit + integration + Vogon canary).\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> User-facing CLI display and read-only API calls only; commits remain available via `--commits`, with solid unit test coverage.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **`entire activity` now defaults to a recent-sessions list** aligned with the entire.io Overview: it calls `GET /api/v1/me/sessions` with `limit=50`, groups by local day of `lastActivityAt`, and renders rows (title, repo, optional `public`, agent, formatted model, checkpoint count). Stat cards, heatmap, and repo chart from `/me/activity` are unchanged.\\n> \\n> **`entire activity --commits`** restores the previous recent-commits behavior. Static and TUI paths both branch on that flag; the header vs list rendering is split (`renderActivityHeader` + session or commit list).\\n> \\n> **Plumbing:** generic `fetchActivityWith` loads activity and the chosen list concurrently; `groupItemsByDay` / `localDayOf` dedupe day grouping for commits and sessions. **`formatModel`** is added in Go to mirror the web’s friendly model labels.\\n> \\n> Tests cover sessions fetch/render/grouping and `formatModel`; existing `runActivity` tests pass the new `showCommits` argument.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 887f764057293d18909e23374921e993d9606a6c. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1650/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1650/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1270\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1270/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1270/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1270/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1270\",\n              \"id\": 4528085420,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7fmu12\",\n              \"number\": 1270,\n              \"title\": \"Add Go v2 checkpoint migration tool\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"pfleidi\",\n                \"id\": 118549,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjExODU0OQ==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118549?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pfleidi\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 3,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-05-26T23:02:23Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-03T00:25:12Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-03T00:25:12Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": true,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1270\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1270\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1270.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1270.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## What\\nAdds a Go-based migration binary under `cmd/migrate-v2-checkpoints` to restore useful v2-only checkpoint data into v1 storage. It reuses the existing checkpoint stores instead of line-for-line porting the shell script.\\n\\n## How\\n- Adds optional commit timestamp support to committed checkpoint writes.\\n- Discovers checkpoint trailers in branch history after a selected base commit.\\n- Reads v2 metadata and raw transcript content through the v2 store.\\n- Writes restored v1 checkpoints through the production v1 `GitStore` path.\\n- Supports list, dry-run, and apply modes with skipped-data reporting.\\n- Adds focused tests for timestamp preservation, discovery, migration, dry-run, existing v1 data, and incomplete v2 data.\\n\\n## Notes\\nThe migration intentionally skips transcript data that lacks usable v2 metadata, since that data is not useful for v1 restoration by itself.\\n\\n## Verification\\n- `mise run lint`\\n- `go build -ldflags \\\"-X github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/versioninfo.Version=v0.0.0-dev-9df43932c -X github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/versioninfo.Commit=9df43932c\\\" -o /private/tmp/entire-pr-check ./cmd/entire`\\n- `go build -o /private/tmp/migrate-v2-checkpoints-pr-check ./cmd/migrate-v2-checkpoints`\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint ./cmd/migrate-v2-checkpoints -count=1`\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Apply mode rewrites the v1 metadata branch from discovered v2 data; mistakes could affect checkpoint history, though dry-run and skip-existing-session behavior limit exposure.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds a **`migrate-v2-checkpoints`** CLI that discovers checkpoints from **`Entire-Checkpoint`** trailers in normal branch history (with **`--since`**, **`--head`**, list / dry-run / apply) and restores eligible v2 sessions into v1 via the existing **`GitStore`** / **`V2GitStore`** paths, skipping sessions already on v1 and reporting missing v2 metadata or raw transcripts.\\n> \\n> Committed checkpoint writes gain optional **`CommitTime`** so metadata-branch commits can keep historical author/committer times during migration (zero still means “now”; **`CreatedAt`** is not reused as the git timestamp). Checkpoint pushes now use an explicit **`refs/heads/…:refs/heads/…`** refspec so stale **`refs/entire/checkpoints/v1`** refs cannot make the source branch ambiguous.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit f5ef3cab98abe5087b17f8834d8229ecc6cb2036. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1270/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1270/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1330\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1330/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1330/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1330/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1330\",\n              \"id\": 4573853188,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7h6TS3\",\n              \"number\": 1330,\n              \"title\": \"Read session resume checkpoints from v1.1 ref\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"pfleidi\",\n                \"id\": 118549,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjExODU0OQ==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118549?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pfleidi\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pfleidi/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-06-02T18:06:09Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-06-02T20:15:03Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-06-02T20:15:00Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1330\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1330\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1330.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1330.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-06-02T20:15:00Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/483\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What\\n\\nPort `entire session resume <branch>` to read committed checkpoint metadata and transcripts from the configured committed checkpoint read store. When checkpoints v1.1 is enabled, resume now reads from the local custom ref instead of the v1 metadata branch.\\n\\n## How\\n\\n- Use `checkpoint.NewCommittedReadStore(ctx, repo)` in the resume metadata and transcript paths.\\n- Keep v1 remote metadata fetch behavior limited to v1 reads; v1.1 missing metadata is reported against the custom ref instead of falling back to v1.\\n- Update logs-only transcript restoration through `ManualCommitStrategy.RestoreLogsOnly` to use the same committed read store.\\n- Add focused v1 and v1.1 resume tests for metadata selection, squash/latest resolution, missing v1.1 metadata, and transcript restoration.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- [x] `mise run fmt`\\n- [x] `mise run lint`\\n- [x] `mise run build`\\n- [x] `mise run test`\\n\\n## Reviewer Notes\\n\\nThis PR intentionally avoids migrating general `checkpoint rewind` listing/interactive behavior. The shared `RestoreLogsOnly` path is updated because `session resume` uses it for transcript restoration.\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes how resume resolves metadata and transcripts across v1 vs v1.1 refs; wrong ref selection could block resume or restore stale logs, though behavior is covered by new tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **`entire session resume`** now loads committed checkpoint metadata and transcripts through **`checkpoint.NewCommittedReadStore`**, so checkpoints **v1.1** read from the configured local custom ref instead of falling back to **`entire/checkpoints/v1`**.\\n> \\n> The resume path drops direct metadata-branch tree reads and routes remote recovery through the same store/ref. **v1** remote fetch/promotion stays on the v1 branch only; when the active read ref is the v1.1 custom ref, missing metadata is reported as local-only (e.g. **`entire explain`**) rather than seeding from stale v1. Squash commits still pick the latest checkpoint by metadata timestamp. **`ManualCommitStrategy.RestoreLogsOnly`** uses the same committed read store for transcript restore (used by resume).\\n> \\n> Tests cover v1.1-only reads, no stale v1 fallback, squash latest selection, and v1.1 transcript restoration.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 6d37d3dfa447b8c52bbedb91236f9614f05ecd18. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1330/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1330/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1506\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1506/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1506/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1506/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1506\",\n              \"id\": 4728954081,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7pzhtw\",\n              \"number\": 1506,\n              \"title\": \"feat(runner): add `entire runner setup` to scaffold and tailor trail runners\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-06-23T19:32:34Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-01T13:58:31Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-01T13:58:30Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1506\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1506\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1506.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1506.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-07-01T13:58:30Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/648\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What\\n\\nAdds **`entire runner setup [<runner>]`** — one command that both **scaffolds** a repo's trail runners (`.entire/runners/*.json`) and **tailors** their evaluator prompts (risk / confidence / drift / security / review / review-focus / summary) to *this* repository instead of the generic defaults. Also retunes this repo's own runners as the first in-repo consumer.\\n\\n> Renamed from the earlier `entire trail tune`; it now lives in a new (hidden, during maturation) `runner` group.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nThe shipped runner templates are written for a generic web/backend app (payments, DB migrations, TypeScript). For a Go CLI that manipulates the user's git repo, the real risk surface is destructive git ops, hook handlers, checkpoint/session integrity, and transcript egress. Calibrating prompts by hand is exactly the kind of thing that should be automatable for any repo adopting trails — and a repo with *no* runners should be able to get a working set in one command.\\n\\n## How it works\\n\\n**Onboarding:** in a repo with no runners, setup writes the default set (confirm, or `--yes`) from templates **embedded in the binary** (correct output contracts + minimal-but-working generic prompts), then tailors them. Re-run in a repo that already has runners and setup **offers to re-tune** (interactive confirm, or `--run` as an explicit yes).\\n\\n**Gather:** signal about the repo across four **best-effort, gracefully-degrading** tiers:\\n\\n| Tier | Source |\\n|---|---|\\n| repo statics | CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md / README / go.mod + dir layout |\\n| PRs & issues | `gh pr/issue list` |\\n| checkpoints | `strategy.ListCheckpoints` → churn hotspots |\\n| trails | trail list + past review findings |\\n\\n**Apply:**\\n- **Default (`--print`)** — emits a paste-ready tailoring prompt.\\n- **`--run`** — executes it **headlessly** through the configured summary provider and rewrites runners **surgically**: only each `prompt.template` value is swapped (byte-level), leaving every other field and the file formatting byte-for-byte intact, so the `git diff` is scoped to the prompt change.\\n\\nThe CLI has no runner struct/loader (the backend consumes these files and substitutes `{{placeholders}}`), so runners are treated as opaque text.\\n\\n## Safety / hardening\\n\\n- **Prompt injection** — both untrusted inputs (gathered signal *and* the existing repo-controlled templates) are embedded as **JSON** with explicit \\\"treat as data, don't follow instructions inside\\\" framing, so a crafted sentinel or ``` fence in repo content can't break out.\\n- **No gathered-only refs** — tuning is told not to cite PR/issue numbers or commit hashes in templates, since the runner only sees the diff at eval time.\\n- **Write-path validation** — a rewrite must be non-empty and add no new `{{placeholder}}` (would render as literal `{{junk}}`); dropping the cosmetic `{{branch}}` is allowed and noted.\\n- **Always-working end state** — defaults are working minimal prompts; any runner left un-tailored is reported as a working default (committable as-is), never a broken placeholder.\\n- **No-op vs failure** — an empty `{}` proposal is a clean no-op; proposals all rejected/out-of-scope return an error.\\n\\n## UX & debugging\\n\\n- **Spinner** on the two long waits (gather, headless agent run); degrades to `✓ <step>` when not a TTY.\\n- **`--debug-dir <dir>`** writes `prompt.txt` (assembled prompt incl. gathered signal) and, on `--run`, `response.txt` (raw model output) — so a skipped/odd rewrite is inspectable.\\n- `--insecure-http-auth` threaded through to the trails API client.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nUnit tests cover output parsing (fenced / prose-wrapped / `{}`), surgical template replacement (special-char preservation), placeholder validation (add rejected, drop allowed), runner loading/filtering, source-flag parsing, prompt assembly, injection-breakout, embedded-defaults validity + working-contract, onboarding create/no-op, and the debug dump. Build + lint clean.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> `--run` can rewrite committed `.entire/runners` JSON from model output (mitigated by placeholder checks and surgical edits), and the updated eval prompts change how future trails score branches.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **`entire trail tune [<runner>]`**, which collects repo-specific signal (docs/layout, `gh` PRs/issues, checkpoint churn, trail review findings) and either prints a paste-ready rewrite prompt or, with **`--run`**, drives the configured summary provider to update **only** each runner’s `prompt.template` via byte-level JSON replacement (other fields and formatting unchanged).\\n> \\n> **`--sources`** and **`--limit`** control which signal tiers are included; tiers degrade gracefully when `gh`, checkpoints, or trails are unavailable. Before writes, rewritten templates must keep the original **`{{placeholder}}`** set; gathered signal and existing templates are embedded as **JSON** with explicit untrusted-data framing to reduce prompt injection.\\n> \\n> Shipped **risk**, **confidence**, and **review-focus** runner prompts in `.entire/runners/` are retuned for this Go CLI (destructive git ops, hooks, checkpoints, transcript egress) as the first in-repo consumer. Unit tests cover parsing, surgical replacement, validation, loading/filtering, and injection-breakout behavior.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 77524874aef721ac302a59f740e54d5eb5dea2c4. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1506/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1506/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1144\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1144/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1144/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1144/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1144\",\n              \"id\": 4401406800,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7ZR2D4\",\n              \"number\": 1144,\n              \"title\": \"feat: machine-readable export surface for sessions and checkpoints\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"id\": 6415609,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTU2MDk=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6415609?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 3,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-05-07T19:23:03Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-07T22:38:06Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-05-07T22:38:04Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1144\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1144\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1144.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1144.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-05-07T22:38:04Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/320\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAdds a thin, additive CLI surface that exposes session and checkpoint data\\nas a stable contract for external consumers (Baton, eval pipelines, the\\n`session-handoff` skill). Closes #1125.\\n\\nNo new top-level commands, no schema invention. JSON envelopes are\\nmetadata-only; transcript bytes always stream to stdout from a flag.\\n\\n**New flags:**\\n- `entire session info <id> --transcript` / `entire session current --transcript`\\n  — stream the live raw agent transcript to stdout (snapshot semantics:\\n  trailing partial JSONL line is trimmed; `<-ctx.Done()` cancels the read).\\n- `entire session list --json` — same per-entry envelope as\\n  `session info --json`, emitted as an array (`[]` for empty).\\n- `entire checkpoint explain --json` — metadata-only envelope. List view\\n  if no target, single-checkpoint object if a target is given. Per-session\\n  read failures surface an explicit `error` field (no silent stub entries);\\n  list-view non-context errors propagate (no swallowed `[]`).\\n- `entire checkpoint explain <id> --transcript` — stream the normalized\\n  compact transcript (V2 `transcript.jsonl` on `/main`).\\n- `entire checkpoint explain <id> --raw-transcript --session-index N` —\\n  pick a specific session in a multi-session checkpoint (default: latest).\\n  `--session-index` also works with `--transcript`.\\n\\n**Internal:**\\n- Shared `matchCheckpointPrefixWithRemoteFallback` helper used by both the\\n  prose `runExplainCheckpointWithLookup` and the new export resolver.\\n- New `sessionOutputMode` enum replaces `(jsonOutput, transcriptOutput bool)`\\n  so the trichotomy is total in code.\\n- New exported `strategy.ResolveTranscriptPath` for live-transcript callers\\n  outside the strategy package.\\n- New `errCheckpointHasNoSessions` sentinel — distinguishes empty vs\\n  missing checkpoints for callers using `errors.Is`.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] Unit + integration tests pass (`mise run test:ci`)\\n- [x] Lint clean (`mise run lint`)\\n- [x] Manual smoke test against a real repo with v1 + v2 checkpoints\\n- [x] `--json` envelope verified to never embed transcript bytes\\n  (`TestRunExplainExport_JSONNeverEmbedsTranscript`)\\n- [x] `--session-index` distinct content per session verified end-to-end\\n  (264KB session 0 vs 1.4MB session 1, distinct sessionIds)\\n- [x] Positional commit-SHA fallback verified end-to-end\\n- [x] `<-ctx.Done()` cancellation contract verified via close-on-done pattern\\n- [x] Partial trailing line trimmed\\n  (`TestInfoCmd_TranscriptTrimsPartialTrailingLine`)\\n- [x] Missing transcript path surfaces cause to stderr (not silent SilentError)\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Adds new machine-readable CLI output modes that stream transcript bytes and emit JSON envelopes, which could affect scripting/automation and output/exit-code behavior if edge cases are missed.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds a **machine-readable export surface** to existing CLI commands.\\n> \\n> `entire checkpoint explain` gains `--json` (metadata-only list or single-checkpoint envelope with `partial` + per-session `error` reporting), `--transcript` (stream v2 compact transcript), `--session-index` (select session in multi-session checkpoints), and `--limit` (cap JSON list output with truncation note). Export resolution now retries missing checkpoint prefixes via a shared remote-metadata fetch helper, and supports positional fallback to commit-trailer resolution.\\n> \\n> `entire session info` and `entire session current` gain `--transcript` to stream the live on-disk agent transcript with snapshot/cancellation semantics and agent-aware shaping (JSONL line streaming vs whole-JSON validation), while `entire session list` gains `--json` to emit the same per-session JSON envelopes as `session info --json`. Also exports `strategy.ResolveTranscriptPath` for non-strategy callers and adds comprehensive tests for the new flags and edge cases.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 8eedeadd791f4f9456bdcabfb9034d33cf502d2d. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1144/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1144/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1942\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1942/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1942/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1942/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1942\",\n              \"id\": 5114005437,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M79Mu-V\",\n              \"number\": 1942,\n              \"title\": \"feat(explain): cross-repo checkpoint explain via the entire-api cell (ENT-1523)\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-10T20:18:10Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-10T21:43:41Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-10T21:43:40Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1942\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1942\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1942.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1942.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-10T21:43:40Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1003\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n`entire checkpoint explain <id> --repo owner/name` explains a checkpoint owned by another repository, reading it from that repo's entire-api cell over HTTP.\\n\\nThis is an alternative to #— the `--repo` implementation on `surf-lightning` (trail 986), which fetches the checkpoint's git ref into the local repo. Same user-facing feature, different data path. Opening it as a separate PR so the two approaches can be compared directly.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\n`entire search` is cross-repo; `explain` was not. Search hands you an identifier the natural next command cannot resolve:\\n\\n```\\n$ entire checkpoint explain b754d1dae6b8      # a checkpoint in entirehq/entiredb\\nno checkpoint or commit found matching \\\"b754d1dae6b8\\\"\\n```\\n\\nThe compact-search work (trail 982) makes this sharper: its per-hit shape is deliberately too thin to answer anything alone, and its skill template has to tell agents to *give up* on cross-repo hits (\\\"summarize from the compact fields alone; `explain` cannot read them\\\").\\n\\n## Approach\\n\\nThe cell already serves everything explain renders — it's how the web app shows you any repo's checkpoint without cloning it:\\n\\n| Endpoint | Serves |\\n|---|---|\\n| `GET /repos/{repo_id}/checkpoints/{id}` | commit, `filesTouched`, sessions + prompts, per-session and aggregate tokens |\\n| `GET /repos/{repo_id}/checkpoints/{id}/transcript/raw` | the stored transcript bytes |\\n\\n`apiCheckpointReader` implements the two checkpoint reader tiers (`CheckpointReader` + `SessionReader`) plus the optional `AuthorReader`. That's the whole surface the render path consumes, so **every output mode reuses the existing renderers verbatim** — prose, `--short`, `--full`, `--json`, `--transcript`/`--raw-transcript`. No second output implementation.\\n\\nIt deliberately does **not** implement `Writer`. A foreign checkpoint is read-only from here, and leaving `Write` off the type makes that structural instead of a convention the flag layer has to remember (there's a test pinning it).\\n\\n## What this buys over fetching git refs\\n\\n**Nothing is written to the local repository.** Verified from a scratch repo against production, after explaining a real foreign checkpoint:\\n\\n| | git-ref fetch | this PR |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `refs/entire/*` left behind | 1 | **0** |\\n| `.git` size | 3.5 MB | **108 K** |\\n| `entire tokens profile` | 1 checkpoint, 72.4M tokens (another repo's) | **0 checkpoints** |\\n| cleanup path | none (`entire clean --all` doesn't touch checkpoint refs) | nothing to clean |\\n\\n**No `--cluster` flag.** Cell routing is automatic via `resolveRepoCellTarget`. The ref-fetch path resolves mirror placements instead and dead-ends without it:\\n\\n```\\n# git-ref fetch\\n$ entire checkpoint explain <id> --repo entireio/cli\\nrepo is mirrored on 4 clusters; pass --cluster to choose one of: ...\\n\\n# this PR\\n$ entire checkpoint explain <id> --repo entireio/cli\\n● Checkpoint 01KXGTTNGCEACC83QZEJ5YAF0D\\n  ...\\n```\\n\\n**Wider coverage.** Same checkpoint ID, same repo, both binaries:\\n\\n```\\n# git-ref fetch\\ncheckpoint 01KZP3V62DKQBG9ZKS6T2ADR00 not found in the mirror for entireio/cli;\\nrepos using the legacy branch-based checkpoint store ... are not supported cross-repo yet\\n\\n# this PR\\n● Checkpoint 01KZP3V62DKQBG9ZKS6T2ADR00\\n  session  a78beaef-a2ab-4cad-9900-f4d3c3b51959\\n```\\n\\nThe cell resolves the storage layout itself (`checkpointlayout.RefAndFolder(id, data.RefBacked)`), so branch-backed and ref-backed repos both work — the ref-fetch path is ref-layout-only by construction.\\n\\n## Fidelity decisions (both tested)\\n\\n- **`Branch` is left empty**, not filled from the envelope. The cell reports branches *containing* the commit; the local field means the branch the checkpoint was *created* on. A checkpoint made on a feature branch and since merged reports `main`, so putting that behind the same JSON key would mislead every `--json` consumer.\\n- **Transcript bytes come from `.../transcript/raw`**, never the parsed message-tree endpoint. `explain` documents `--transcript` as the same bytes as `--raw-transcript`; sourcing them from a derived shape would quietly break that.\\n- **A missing `checkpointTranscriptStart` reads as 0** (unscoped) rather than an invented offset — identical to how a local checkpoint written before that field existed behaves.\\n- **Oversize transcripts error** instead of truncating into the renderer.\\n\\n## Flag rules\\n\\n`--repo` needs a full checkpoint ID (a prefix would require listing the foreign repo's checkpoints — that's `search`'s job) and is mutually exclusive with `--commit`, `--session`, `--search-all`, and `--generate`. Naming the current repo is a no-op that falls through to the local path, which is faster and can also read unpushed checkpoints.\\n\\nA bare repo ID is not accepted, only `owner/name` / `gh/owner/name` — the control plane and the search index expose different identifiers for a repository, and guessing which space an opaque ID belongs to would key the lookup off the wrong one. `owner/name` is what search's `repo` field gives you.\\n\\n## Error messages\\n\\nA 404 leads with the cause that actually dominates:\\n\\n```\\ncheckpoint 01KV... is not available for entireio/cli yet: it may not have been\\npushed, or Entire may not have finished ingesting it. Checkpoints you have not\\npushed are only readable in the repo that created them\\n```\\n\\n## Drive-bys\\n\\n- Extracted `validateExplainFlagCombinations` out of `newExplainCmd` (it was over the `maintidx` limit with the new flag).\\n- Renamed `resolveCurrentRepoID` → `resolveRepoIDFromMirror`; it takes explicit coordinates and now serves a foreign repo too.\\n- Stopped rendering an empty `<>` when an author has a name but no email.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n`mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci` all green (lint: 0 issues). 25 new tests: envelope mapping, the raw-vs-parsed endpoint assertion, envelope caching (one fetch across all read tiers), 404/403/empty/no-session paths, oversize transcript, `List` unsupported, not-a-`Writer`, flag validation, and all four render modes against a stub reader.\\n\\nManually verified end-to-end against production for prose, `--json`, `--full` (3,273 lines), and `--transcript` (3.1 MB), plus clean stdout JSON with the spinner on stderr.\\n\\n## Known gap\\n\\nThe availability precondition is *pushed and ingested*, so a just-pushed checkpoint may briefly 404. The message above says so; if that lag turns out to be user-visible in practice, a retry hint would be the follow-up.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> New authenticated HTTP read path and flag surface on a heavily used command; risk is moderated by read-only semantics (no local git writes), strict flag mutual exclusion, and extensive tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **`entire checkpoint explain <id> --repo owner/name`** so cross-repo `search` hits can be drilled down without pulling foreign git objects into the local repo.\\n> \\n> **`apiCheckpointReader`** loads checkpoint metadata and raw transcript bytes from the repo’s entire-api cell (`GET .../checkpoints/{id}` and `.../transcript/raw`), maps them into the existing checkpoint reader types, and **does not implement `Writer`**. Prose, `--json`, `--full`, and transcript modes reuse the same renderers as local explain.\\n> \\n> **`runCrossRepoExplain`** resolves mirror `repo_id`, dials the owning cell via `NewAuthenticatedEntireAPICellClient`, and rejects incompatible flags (`--commit`, `--session`, `--search-all`, `--generate`). `--repo` on the current checkout is a no-op to the local path. Cross-repo requires a **full** checkpoint ID.\\n> \\n> Notable fidelity choices: **`Branch` stays empty** (cell “containing branches” ≠ creation branch), transcripts always from **raw** endpoint, oversize transcripts **error** instead of truncating, and 404 messaging calls out unpushed/not-yet-ingested checkpoints.\\n> \\n> Also extracts **`validateExplainFlagCombinations`**, renames **`resolveCurrentRepoID` → `resolveRepoIDFromMirror`** for foreign-repo use, fixes author lines when email is missing, and documents the feature in **CLAUDE.md**. Broad unit test coverage for the API reader and cross-repo explain paths.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 346b7fb5b53078c1a8f46fdce807151a081e4dcd. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1942/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1942/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/954\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/954/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/954/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/954/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/954\",\n              \"id\": 4264173496,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7SaQxJ\",\n              \"number\": 954,\n              \"title\": \"Add summary TUI for browsing checkpoints\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"id\": 6415609,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTU2MDk=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6415609?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/alishakawaguchi\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/alishakawaguchi/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-04-14T19:03:59Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-08T21:05:38Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-05-08T21:05:38Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": true,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/954\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/954\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/954.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/954.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\n- Adds `entire summary` command with an interactive Bubble Tea TUI for browsing checkpoints\\n- Reads session data directly from the checkpoint store (no SQLite/insightsdb dependency)\\n- Users can filter by time (24h/7d/30d/all) and branch (current/repo), and press `g` to generate AI summaries persisted to the checkpoint branch\\n- Includes `summarytui` package (model/update/view, detail rendering, styles, keybindings), `termstyle` shared styling package, and comprehensive tests\\n\\n## Test plan\\n- [ ] Run `mise run check` (fmt + lint + tests)\\n- [ ] Run `entire summary` in a repo with existing checkpoints — verify list loads, detail pane renders\\n- [ ] Press `g` on a checkpoint without a summary — verify generation works and persists\\n- [ ] Test time filter cycling with `1` key and branch filter with `2` key\\n- [ ] Test `entire summary --json` outputs valid JSON\\n- [ ] Test accessible mode with `ACCESSIBLE=1 entire summary`\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Adds a new interactive command that reads and updates checkpoint metadata (including persisting AI-generated summaries) across v1/v2 stores; main risk is regressions in checkpoint I/O and UX edge cases rather than security-critical behavior.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds a new `entire summary` command that loads recent committed checkpoints and lets users browse session metadata and cached AI summaries via an interactive Bubble Tea split-pane TUI, with filters for time range and branch scope and optional `--json` output.\\n> \\n> Supports on-demand summary generation (`g`) that reuses existing transcript-scoping + AI summarization helpers and persists the generated `Summary` back to the checkpoint store (v1 and v2 when available), with an accessible-mode text fallback.\\n> \\n> Introduces the new `summarytui` UI package (rendering, keybindings, pagination, filtering) and a shared `termstyle` utility for terminal color/width-aware formatting, plus comprehensive unit tests and a settings toggle under `strategy_options.summarize.enabled`.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit a456873fdb97b475c349354199776b39388f447c. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/954/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/954/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/144\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/144/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/144/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/144/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/144\",\n              \"id\": 3894737830,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7BX5TX\",\n              \"number\": 144,\n              \"title\": \"feat(explain): improve explain command with author, commits, and filtering\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"khaong\",\n                \"id\": 351934,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTkzNA==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/351934?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/khaong\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/khaong/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-02-04T05:26:30Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-04T07:13:52Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-02-04T07:13:50Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/144\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/144\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/144.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/144.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-02-04T07:13:50Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nImplements ENT-212: Improve `entire explain` command with better checkpoint detail views and filtering.\\n\\n- **`--commit <sha>` now shows checkpoint details**: Extracts `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer from commit and delegates to checkpoint detail view\\n- **`--session` filters list view**: Instead of showing session details, now filters the checkpoint list by session ID (prefix match supported)\\n- **Checkpoint detail shows author**: Retrieves author from `entire/sessions` commit history\\n- **Checkpoint detail shows associated commits**: Lists git commits that reference the checkpoint via trailer\\n- **`--search-all` flag**: Removes branch/depth limits when searching commits (documented as \\\"may be slow\\\")\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] Unit tests for all new functions (`TestGetAssociatedCommits`, `TestGetCheckpointAuthor`, etc.)\\n- [x] Integration tests for new flag behavior (`TestExplain_SessionFilter`, `TestExplain_CommitWithCheckpointTrailer`, etc.)\\n- [x] `mise run test:ci` passes (unit + integration + race detection)\\n- [x] `mise run lint` clean\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Medium risk due to behavior changes in `entire explain` routing/output and new git-history scanning logic that could impact performance or completeness of results, though changes are mostly read-only and guarded with best-effort error handling.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Improves `entire explain` by making `--session` a *list-view filter* (prefix supported) rather than a separate session-detail mode, while keeping `--commit`/`--checkpoint` mutually exclusive.\\n> \\n> Checkpoint detail output now includes **checkpoint author** (derived from the `entire/sessions` history) and a **list of associated git commits** that reference the checkpoint via the `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer; a new `--search-all` flag removes scan limits for this association lookup.\\n> \\n> `--commit` behavior changes to *resolve the `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer and delegate to checkpoint detail view*; commits without the trailer now print a “no associated checkpoint” message instead of showing generic commit info. Adds `trailers.FormatCheckpoint` helper and extensive unit/integration tests covering new routing, filtering, author lookup, and association logic.\\n> \\n> <sup>Written by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot) for commit 3dbf613b1ab881e3d12d4e9daf22a48a60067a20. This will update automatically on new commits. Configure [here](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/144/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/144/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1007\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1007/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1007/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1007/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1007\",\n              \"id\": 4309508151,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7UpZi4\",\n              \"number\": 1007,\n              \"title\": \"Cursor: agent-lifecycle export/import via CheckpointContributor + CheckpointRestorer\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"id\": 881031,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 7,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-04-22T13:57:33Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-14T08:15:52Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-07-14T08:15:51Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": true,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/1007\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1007\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1007.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1007.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nExport and import of Cursor Agent sessions are wired through the agent lifecycle via `CheckpointContributor` and `CheckpointRestorer`. No standalone Cursor commands are needed.\\n\\nThis update also makes the post-restore hint metadata-aware:\\n\\n- Cursor Agent checkpoints print `agent --resume <id>`.\\n- Cursor IDE checkpoints keep the existing `Open this project in Cursor.` message.\\n- Legacy checkpoints fall back to the recorded model so older restored sessions still get the best available hint.\\n\\n## User Flow\\n\\n1. Cursor Agent or Cursor IDE runs with Entire hooks installed.\\n2. On checkpoint save, Cursor contributes its session archive into the checkpoint metadata.\\n3. `entire rewind` restores the worktree and asks Cursor to restore contributed files.\\n4. `entire resume` restores logs from committed checkpoints and prints the correct resume hint for the original Cursor client.\\n\\n## Implementation Notes\\n\\n- Added agent-level resume formatting context with checkpoint metadata.\\n- Cursor hooks now persist whether the checkpoint came from Cursor Agent or Cursor IDE.\\n- Session and checkpoint metadata carry agent-specific key/value data through condensation and restore.\\n- Cursor restore still rebuilds the native chat/transcript state from checkpointed files.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/...`\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor`\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint`\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy`\\n- [x] `mise run lint`\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1007/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/1007/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/112\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/112/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/112/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/112/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/112\",\n              \"id\": 3863305991,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M6_vu9l\",\n              \"number\": 112,\n              \"title\": \"Adds checkpoint-focused explanations and a branch-aware default view to entire explain\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"id\": 881031,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MTAzMQ==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/881031?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/gtrrz-victor\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/gtrrz-victor/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-01-28T02:57:54Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-01-29T04:41:24Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-01-29T04:41:22Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/112\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/112\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/112.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/112.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-01-29T04:41:22Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes `explain`’s default behavior and adds new checkpoint lookup paths that traverse git history and shadow branches, which could affect performance and edge-case correctness on unusual repos. No auth/security-sensitive logic is touched.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> `entire explain` now defaults to a **branch checkpoints view** instead of requiring an active session, listing committed and reachable temporary (shadow) checkpoints grouped by checkpoint/session and filtered against the repo’s default branch.\\n> \\n> Adds `--checkpoint/-c` to explain a single checkpoint by ID or prefix, with `--short` and `--full` verbosity (including transcript output), and improves commit explain to recognize `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers and backfill session IDs via checkpoint metadata.\\n> \\n> Refactors default-branch/ancestry detection into shared strategy helpers (`GetDefaultBranchName`, `IsOnDefaultBranch`, `IsAncestorOf`) and extends the checkpoint store with `ListAllTemporaryCheckpoints`; updates and expands unit/integration tests accordingly.\\n> \\n> <sup>Written by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot) for commit 387eacf47f655c2315edc72a0a627a13bea1511f. This will update automatically on new commits. Configure [here](https://cursor.com/dashboard?tab=bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/112/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/112/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/533\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/533/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/533/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/533/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/533\",\n              \"id\": 3998146752,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M7GrXj-\",\n              \"number\": 533,\n              \"title\": \"fix: detect and repair disconnected metadata branches at read/write time\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"dvydra\",\n                \"id\": 62726,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNzI2\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62726?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dvydra\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/dvydra\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dvydra/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dvydra/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dvydra/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dvydra/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dvydra/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dvydra/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dvydra/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dvydra/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/dvydra/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 6,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T22:50:14Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-06T01:13:13Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-03-06T01:13:11Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/533\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/533\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/533.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/533.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-03-06T01:13:11Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nDetects and repairs disconnected `entire/checkpoints/v1` metadata branches — a state caused by the empty-orphan bug (fixed going forward by #511). Users who hit that bug and continued working have local checkpoint data on a completely disconnected history from remote (no common ancestor).\\n\\n**Key distinction:** *Diverged* (shared ancestor, unique commits on each side) is normal multi-dev flow handled by the push path's tree merge. *Disconnected* (no common ancestor) is the bug state that this PR repairs.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n### New: cherry-pick reconciliation (`strategy/metadata_reconcile.go`)\\n\\nWhen local and remote share no common ancestor, local commits are cherry-picked onto the remote tip:\\n\\n1. Detect via `git merge-base` (exit 0 = shared ancestry, exit 1 = disconnected)\\n2. Walk local branch tip→root, collect commits oldest-first\\n3. Skip empty-tree commits (the orphan bug artifact)\\n4. For each commit: compute full delta from parent (adds + modifies + deletes), apply onto current tip\\n5. Update local branch ref\\n\\nCheckpoint shards use unique paths (`<id[:2]>/<id[2:]>/`), so cherry-picks always apply cleanly. All data is preserved with linear history.\\n\\n### Reconciliation runs at read/write time, not `enable` time\\n\\nRuns once per process (via `sync.Once`) when commands actually access the metadata branch — explain, rewind, resume, clean, condensation. Three call sites:\\n\\n- `ManualCommitStrategy.getCheckpointStore()` — covers strategy-mediated reads/writes\\n- `getBranchCheckpoints()` in `explain.go` — bypasses strategy, creates own GitStore\\n- `ListCheckpoints()` in `strategy/common.go` — opens own repo, reads branch directly\\n\\nThis is the right place because `enable` may run before the user has fetched remote data.\\n\\n### Simplified `EnsureMetadataBranch` (runs during `enable`)\\n\\nNow only handles:\\n- Create local from remote when local doesn't exist\\n- Replace empty orphan with remote\\n- Create empty orphan when neither exists\\n\\nRemoved `syncMetadataBranch` and `isAncestorCLI` — disconnected repair is now handled by `EnsureMetadataReconciled`.\\n\\n### User-facing output\\n\\n```\\n[entire] Detected disconnected session metadata (local and remote share no common ancestor)\\n[entire] Cherry-picking 3 local checkpoint(s) onto remote...\\n[entire] Done — all local and remote checkpoints preserved\\n```\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `strategy/metadata_reconcile.go` | **New** — detection + cherry-pick repair |\\n| `strategy/metadata_reconcile_test.go` | **New** — 7 tests covering no-ops, disconnected repair, multi-commit, modifications |\\n| `strategy/common.go` | `EnsureMetadataReconciled()` gate; simplified `EnsureMetadataBranch`; removed `syncMetadataBranch`/`isAncestorCLI` |\\n| `strategy/manual_commit.go` | Reconciliation call in `getCheckpointStore()` |\\n| `strategy/common_test.go` | Updated existing tests for new behavior |\\n| `cli/explain.go` | Reconciliation call in `getBranchCheckpoints()` |\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] `mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci`\\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/ -run TestReconcileDisconnected -v` — all 7 tests pass\\n- [x] Manual: clone repo with remote checkpoints, create disconnected local orphan, run `entire explain`, verify reconciliation and explain succeeds\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/533/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/533/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            }\n          ],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rate-limit\",\n      \"q\": \"repo:entireio/git-sync \\\"rate limit\\\"\",\n      \"rr\": [\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 0,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 0,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"page-graph\",\n      \"q\": \"repo:entireio/entire-graph \\\"pagination\\\"\",\n      \"rr\": [\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 0,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 1,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/144\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/144/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/144/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/144/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/144\",\n              \"id\": 5198708977,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSqVa0c8AAAABAWyxYw\",\n              \"number\": 144,\n              \"title\": \"Publish re-audited letta and supermemory LoCoMo numbers\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"id\": 257360244,\n                \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-20T01:30:04Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-20T02:10:02Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-20T02:10:01Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/144\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/144\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/144.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/144.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-20T02:10:01Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/104\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nBoth the letta and supermemory rows in the 8-system LoCoMo comparison were flagged **suspect, not\\nyet re-audited** in `FAIR-CONFIG.md`, and supermemory additionally had a confirmed extraction-model\\ndefect (documented in the existing `‡` footnote). This PR rebuilds both arms on fresh\\ninfrastructure, re-runs the full 1,540-question suite under the identical fairness spine every\\nother row uses (`FAIR_MODE=1`, same answerer/judge `gpt-5.6-sol`, same extraction model\\n`azure_ai/gpt-5.6-terra`, `top_k=200`), and publishes the results.\\n\\n- **letta: 80.58 → 84.68** (`field_letta_loco_v3`, 1304/1540). Re-audited clean — zero dropped\\n  questions, zero empty-context retrievals, zero errors across all 1,540 questions. No defect was\\n  found in the original number; the original infrastructure was deleted before it could be\\n  re-audited directly, so this is a clean re-measurement superseding a suspect number, not a bug\\n  fix.\\n- **supermemory: 77.60 → 82.08** (`field_sm_loco_v3`, 1264/1540). Two real, independent defects\\n  found and fixed:\\n  1. supermemory's self-hosted server silently selects the wrong AI SDK provider whenever pointed\\n     at a non-default endpoint (mandatory for our Azure deployment), degrading every\\n     structured-output extraction call to a schema-less response the deployment rejects. Fixed\\n     with a 2-byte binary patch (sha256-verified against the official release manifest) plus a\\n     wire-level parameter adapter.\\n  2. supermemory deduplicates documents by content, so any retry after a transient failure\\n     resubmits identical text — which its own dedup then rejects, guaranteed. Fixed with a stable\\n     content-derived `custom_id`.\\n  \\n  One limitation is disclosed rather than worked around: supermemory's search API hard-caps\\n  `limit` at 100 with no pagination, so it answers from an effective top-100 budget while every\\n  other arm gets the full top-200 — recorded per-question (`requested_top_k`/`limit_used`/\\n  `clamped`) for auditability. 114/1,540 questions (7.4%) returned an empty context; checked\\n  individually (not asserted): zero errors, normal search latency, spread across 9 of 10\\n  conversations (not clustered), consistent with a genuine retrieval-miss characteristic rather\\n  than the original defect.\\n\\n## Files changed\\n\\n- `README.md` — table numbers\\n- `bench/memory/RUN-INDEX.md` — new `field_letta_loco_v3` / `field_sm_loco_v3` rows; old rows\\n  marked superseded\\n- `bench/memory/LOCOMO-COMPARISON.md` — table (rows 10/11), headline numbers, the zero-empty-context\\n  claim (now correctly scoped), the `‡` footnote (full rewrite — defect resolved, new disclosure),\\n  §8's bug-fix list (four competitors now, not three), §10's gate wording\\n- `bench/memory/FAIR-CONFIG.md` — §7 verdicts flipped from suspect to resolved, with outcomes\\n- `bench/memory/RUNNING-LOCOMO.md` — summary table numbers\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- Both final result files' `metadata.run_id`/`total_questions` confirmed directly (1540/1540 each)\\n- Scores extracted from each run's own `metrics_by_cutoff.top_200.overall`, not hand-tallied\\n- Zero `search_dropped` confirmed across all 1,540 questions in both arms, by direct file\\n  inspection\\n- supermemory's extraction calls confirmed landing on `gpt-5.6-terra-2026-07-09` via the token\\n  meter (not asserted)\\n- supermemory's 114 empty-context questions individually inspected: `search_dropped: false`, no\\n  error field, normal latency, spread across 9/10 conversations — ruled out as a repeat of the\\n  original defect\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/144/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/144/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            }\n          ],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"perfetto\",\n      \"q\": \"repo:entireio/cli perfetto\",\n      \"rr\": [\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 0,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 0,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"repo:entireio/git-sync \\\"same repository\\\"\",\n      \"q\": \"repo:entireio/git-sync \\\"same repository\\\"\",\n      \"rr\": [\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 0,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 1,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/18\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/18/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/18/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/18/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/18\",\n              \"id\": 4353589412,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOR9SkY87W3rmJ\",\n              \"number\": 18,\n              \"title\": \"Expand on integration tests\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"pjbgf\",\n                \"id\": 5452977,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NTI5Nzc=\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5452977?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/pjbgf\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/pjbgf/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 0,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-04-29T20:50:39Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-04-30T08:25:27Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-04-30T08:25:24Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/pulls/18\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/18\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/18.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/18.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-04-30T08:25:24Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \" ## Summary\\r\\nExtends integration coverage in `internal/syncer/integration_test.go` in two areas: **sync-mode prune semantics** and **incremental relay push failure handling**.\\r\\n  ### Sync-mode `--prune`\\r\\n  - **`TestRun_IntegrationSyncPruneDeletesOrphanedBranch`** — With no ref filter, `Run` with `--prune` removes a target-only branch absent from the source; checks `Deleted` and that the managed branch still matches the source.\\r\\n  - **`TestRun_IntegrationSyncPrunePreservesTargetTagWithoutIncludeTags`** — With `--prune` but without `--tags`, a target-only tag must survive so branch-only prune does not drop release-style markers.\\r\\n  - **`TestRun_IntegrationPrunePreservesUnrelatedTargetBranchUnderFilter`** — Table-driven cases for `--branch` and `--map`: unrelated branches on the target stay present and their hashes unchanged under filtered prune.\\r\\n  These clarify **prune scope** and guard against deleting refs users expect to keep while still enforcing orphan branch cleanup in sync mode.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ### Incremental push failure and retry\\r\\n  - **`TestRun_IntegrationIncrementalPushFailureRecoversOnRetry`** — Injects a **one-shot `ng`** from the target receive-pack on the **incremental relay** path (after a fast-forward plan). Asserts the first `Run` **errors**, the **target ref is unchanged** (only ok’d commands commit), and a **retry** completes incremental relay with **`RelayMode` incremental**, **two receive-pack attempts**, and the target at the new source head.\\r\\n  This pins the **failure-and-retry contract** for incremental sync and complements bootstrap-focused push tests; it does not replace mid-stream cancel/drop coverage (still mainly on `Bootstrap` via `receivePackRaw`).\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Mostly test-only, but adds a new public-config validation that rejects identical source/target URLs and could break existing workflows that relied on that configuration.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Expands test coverage** for sync/replicate planning and end-to-end `Run` behavior, focusing on `--prune` scoping rules (preserve out-of-scope target-only branches when `--branch`/`--map` is used; delete orphan branches when unfiltered) and tag-prune boundaries (don’t prune tags unless `--tags`, prune target-local tags when `--tags --prune`, and preserve tags created mid-sync).\\n> \\n> Adds an **incremental relay failure/retry integration test** that injects a one-shot `receive-pack` rejection, asserting the first run errors without advancing the target and the retry completes via incremental relay.\\n> \\n> Introduces `validation.ValidateEndpoints` and wires it into `newSession` (only when a target is required) to **reject identical source/target URLs** across `Run`/`Bootstrap`/`Probe`, with unit tests. Integration tests now register an empty go-git config loader in `TestMain` to avoid environment-dependent git config affecting runs.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit c3089e94b311b4cc2d08035b4dcde64491dd33f8. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/18/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/18/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            }\n          ],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"repo:entireio/git-sync \\\"identical\\\" \\\"endpoint\\\"\",\n      \"q\": \"repo:entireio/git-sync \\\"identical\\\" \\\"endpoint\\\"\",\n      \"rr\": [\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 0,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"total_count\": 3,\n          \"incomplete_results\": false,\n          \"items\": [\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/122\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/122/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/122/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/122/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/122\",\n              \"id\": 5562237117,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOR9SkY88AAAABE21FdA\",\n              \"number\": 122,\n              \"title\": \"fix: refuse POST redirects in guardRedirects unless FollowInfoRefsRedirect is set\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"jaysomani\",\n                \"id\": 69755312,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NzU1MzEy\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69755312?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jaysomani\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/jaysomani\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jaysomani/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jaysomani/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jaysomani/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jaysomani/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jaysomani/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jaysomani/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jaysomani/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jaysomani/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/jaysomani/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"open\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 5,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-09-24T02:43:06Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-13T15:35:34Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": null,\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/pulls/122\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/122\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/122.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/122.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": null\n              },\n              \"body\": \"\\r\\nguardRedirects's CheckRedirect closure now returns http.ErrUseLastResponse for POST redirects unless conn.FollowInfoRefsRedirect is set, matching vanilla git's http.followRedirects=initial default where only the /info/refs GET auto-follows. GET redirect behaviour is unchanged.\\r\\n\\r\\nRequired restructuring NewHTTPConnWithClient so guardRedirects closes over the *HTTPConn directly (reading FollowInfoRefsRedirect live at redirect time) rather than running before the struct exists.\\r\\n\\r\\nAlso corrects TestGuardRedirectsAnchorsOnTheIssuedRequest which modelled a post-adoption cross-site redirect but never set FollowInfoRefsRedirect, making the scenario unreachable under the corrected logic.\\r\\n\\r\\nOn a cross-host POST redirect without the flag, the failure mode changes from a delayed opaque 401 (Authorization stripped mid-flight by the existing sameSite guard) to an immediate clear http 307 error — the intended improvement from the issue.\\r\\n\\r\\nFixes #67\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/122/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/122/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/124\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/124/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/124/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/124/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124\",\n              \"id\": 5926912911,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOR9SkY88AAAABJXbk9w\",\n              \"number\": 124,\n              \"title\": \"fix: authenticate the GitHub repo-size preflight and log its outcome\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"nodo\",\n                \"id\": 829178,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjgyOTE3OA==\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/829178?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/nodo\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 8,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-10-19T15:39:13Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-21T15:59:16Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-10-21T15:59:13Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/pulls/124\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-10-21T15:59:13Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"## Problem\\n\\nWhen bootstrapping from a `github.com` source without `--target-max-pack-bytes`, git-sync asks the GitHub REST API (`GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}`) for the repository size. It switches to 512 MiB batches when the size is 1.5 GiB or more. That lookup sent no credentials. For a private repository GitHub answers 404 to an anonymous caller, so every private repository bootstrapped as a single pack, whatever its size.\\n\\nNothing reported this:\\n- Every failure (non-200, transport error, parse error) returned silently.\\n- The \\\"selected batched mode\\\" message only showed with verbose logging.\\n\\nPublic repositories were exposed too: anonymous calls share GitHub's 60 requests/hour limit per egress IP.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n**Authenticated lookup**\\n- The size request now carries the source connection's credentials (basic or bearer): an explicit token, a `user:token@` in the source URL, or credentials the git credential helper supplied when the git server asked for them. A public repository never asks, so with only a helper its lookup stays anonymous. A URL username without a password is not sent: it may be an account name.\\n- If the API refuses the token with 401 or 403 (for example an SSO-unauthorized PAT), the lookup retries once anonymously. A public repository is never worse off than before. If the retry fails too, the refusal is reported rather than hidden behind the retry's 404.\\n- The new `HTTPConn.CredentialsFor(dest)` decides which credentials may go to the API, checking the real destination. Each credential is measured from the URL it is bound to (the endpoint for explicit and URL credentials, the looked-up host for helper ones), the destination must be same-site with it, and with TLS verification off nothing crosses to another host. So helper credentials looked up for a redirect host stay with that host, and an API base on another site gets nothing.\\n- `GitHubOwnerRepo` now treats `github.com` as GitHub only on its scheme's default port. The connection's redirect guard still strips credentials from any hop that leaves the API's site, and the logged `authenticated` reflects the request that actually produced the answer.\\n\\n**Visible outcome**\\n- Every lookup that is attempted is logged through `Options.BootstrapLogger`. This does not need verbose mode.\\n- Fields: `repository`, `authenticated`, `http_status`, `refused_auth_status`, `refused_auth_error`, `size_kb` or `error`, `threshold_kb`, `mode`, `target_max_pack_bytes`.\\n- A failed lookup logs at WARN and also prints a notice that the bootstrap starts with a single pack, so CLI users see it without `-v` (it can still switch to batches if the target rejects the pack). The notice names the token refusal when there was one. Under `-v` the failure is printed once, and the verbose log and `BootstrapLogger` use the same record name.\\n\\n**Hardening**\\n- A reported size of 0 counts as unknown, like a missing or negative size: bootstrap only runs with source refs, so 0 means GitHub has not sized the repo yet. It warns and prints the notice.\\n- A cancelled run reports nothing. Every error text (transport errors included) is cleaned before it is logged or printed.\\n- A 401/403 counts as a refused token only when the request still carried it, so a redirect that stripped the credentials is neither retried nor blamed on the token.\\n- Wiki sources (`owner/repo.wiki`) get no lookup: the API has nothing to size.\\n- Each lookup request has its own 30s timeout, so a slow refusal does not starve the anonymous retry.\\n- GitHub's error message is cleaned (control characters including C1, bidi formatting) and truncated before it is logged.\\n\\n**Docs**\\n- `docs/usage.md` documents the lookup and its credential scope.\\n- Updated the `BootstrapLogger` doc comments and `CHANGELOG.md`.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nNew file `internal/strategy/bootstrap/github_preflight_test.go`, written test-first. It covers:\\n- a private repo: 404 without auth, 200 with auth, so batched (also end-to-end through `Execute`);\\n- a bearer token, `user:token@` URL credentials, and a bare URL username not being sent;\\n- no credentials with TLS verification off, or to an API base on another site;\\n- lookup failure: one-shot, a WARN record and a notice;\\n- the anonymous retry on 401/403, the refusal reported when the retry fails too, and no retry on other failures;\\n- a transport error, and unusable bodies (not JSON, no size, negative size);\\n- sanitizing GitHub's error message;\\n- a small repo staying one-shot without a warning, and one reporting size 0 warning as unknown;\\n- a cancelled run, unclean transport errors, an unauthenticated 403 after a redirect, and the per-attempt timeout;\\n- skipped lookups (caller already batching, non-default port, non-GitHub host);\\n- a redirect that leaves the API's site dropping credentials (asserting the target was reached, and logged as unauthenticated);\\n- `CredentialsFor` in `internal/gitproto/smarthttp_test.go`: explicit, helper and URL credentials, helper credentials bound to a redirect host, and TLS verification off.\\n\\nThe preflight tests reach a local TLS server as `https://api.github.com`, so the destination check runs as in production.\\n\\nThe new tests fail against the previous implementation. `go test ./...`, `go test -race` on the affected packages and `golangci-lint run` (v2.11.4) all pass.\\n\\n---\\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FUdEhv4HALJ9DCRUP7GzTw)_\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches credential scoping for cross-host API calls and bootstrap batching decisions; mistakes could leak tokens or mis-size packs, but changes are heavily tested and fail closed on redirects/TLS-off.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Fixes batched bootstrap for large private GitHub repos** by sending source credentials on the `GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}` size preflight (scoped to `api.github.com` via new `HTTPConn.CredentialsFor`), with same-site/TLS rules aligned to redirect handling and helper creds bound to `authOrigin`.\\n> \\n> The preflight moves into `github_preflight.go` with structured **`BootstrapLogger` / `PushLogger`** records, CLI **notices** on lookup failure, **401/403 → one anonymous retry**, stricter **`GitHubOwnerRepo`** parsing, and **`sanitize.Line`** for API/error text in logs. Docs and changelog describe the behavior.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit d0e7b7873bb287a3c90f5ed779923b16b26d5b15. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\\n\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/124/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/124/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": {\n                \"id\": 1236702,\n                \"client_id\": \"Iv23liqTIFEtdIu6Vn1r\",\n                \"slug\": \"claude\",\n                \"node_id\": \"A_kwHOBIuudM4AEt7e\",\n                \"owner\": {\n                  \"login\": \"anthropics\",\n                  \"id\": 76263028,\n                  \"node_id\": \"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjc2MjYzMDI4\",\n                  \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76263028?v=4\",\n                  \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics\",\n                  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/anthropics\",\n                  \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/followers\",\n                  \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/following{/other_user}\",\n                  \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                  \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                  \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/subscriptions\",\n                  \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/orgs\",\n                  \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/repos\",\n                  \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/events{/privacy}\",\n                  \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/received_events\",\n                  \"type\": \"Organization\",\n                  \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                  \"site_admin\": false\n                },\n                \"name\": \"Claude\",\n                \"description\": \"Run Claude Code from your GitHub Pull Requests and Issues to respond to reviewer feedback, fix CI errors, or modify code, turning it into a virtual teammate that works alongside your development pipelines.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is built on the publicly available Claude Code SDK.\",\n                \"external_url\": \"https://anthropic.com/claude-code\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/claude\",\n                \"created_at\": \"2025-04-30T17:54:24Z\",\n                \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-12T22:28:30Z\",\n                \"permissions\": {\n                  \"actions\": \"write\",\n                  \"administration\": \"read\",\n                  \"checks\": \"write\",\n                  \"contents\": \"write\",\n                  \"discussions\": \"write\",\n                  \"issues\": \"write\",\n                  \"members\": \"read\",\n                  \"merge_queues\": \"read\",\n                  \"metadata\": \"read\",\n                  \"pull_requests\": \"write\",\n                  \"repository_creation\": \"write\",\n                  \"repository_hooks\": \"write\",\n                  \"statuses\": \"read\",\n                  \"vulnerability_alerts\": \"read\",\n                  \"workflows\": \"write\"\n                },\n                \"events\": [\n                  \"branch_protection_rule\",\n                  \"check_run\",\n                  \"check_suite\",\n                  \"commit_comment\",\n                  \"discussion\",\n                  \"discussion_comment\",\n                  \"issues\",\n                  \"issue_comment\",\n                  \"merge_group\",\n                  \"merge_queue_entry\",\n                  \"pull_request\",\n                  \"pull_request_review\",\n                  \"pull_request_review_comment\",\n                  \"pull_request_review_thread\",\n                  \"push\",\n                  \"release\",\n                  \"repository_ruleset\",\n                  \"status\",\n                  \"sub_issues\"\n                ]\n              },\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/108\",\n              \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync\",\n              \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/108/labels{/name}\",\n              \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/108/comments\",\n              \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/108/events\",\n              \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/108\",\n              \"id\": 5192976034,\n              \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOR9SkY88AAAABASLszQ\",\n              \"number\": 108,\n              \"title\": \"Bind explicit credentials to the host they were configured for\",\n              \"user\": {\n                \"login\": \"Soph\",\n                \"id\": 70741,\n                \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n                \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n                \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n                \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n                \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n                \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n                \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n                \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n                \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n                \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n                \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n                \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n                \"type\": \"User\",\n                \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n                \"site_admin\": false\n              },\n              \"labels\": [],\n              \"state\": \"closed\",\n              \"locked\": false,\n              \"assignees\": [],\n              \"milestone\": null,\n              \"comments\": 1,\n              \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T13:09:08Z\",\n              \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-20T15:36:34Z\",\n              \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-20T15:36:30Z\",\n              \"assignee\": null,\n              \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n              \"issue_field_values\": [],\n              \"type\": null,\n              \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n              \"draft\": false,\n              \"pull_request\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/pulls/108\",\n                \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/108\",\n                \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/108.diff\",\n                \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/108.patch\",\n                \"merged_at\": \"2026-08-20T15:36:30Z\"\n              },\n              \"body\": \"Fixes the highest-severity item left from the security review. **Stacked on #107** so the `smarthttp.go` changes don't conflict — the base is that branch, so this diff shows only its own changes. I'll rebase onto `main` once #107 merges.\\n\\n## The problem\\n\\nWith `--source-follow-info-refs-redirect` / `--target-follow-info-refs-redirect`, git-sync adopts the host `/info/refs` redirected to and addresses it directly for follow-up RPCs — re-attaching the configured token to requests aimed at that host, *after* Go's `http.Client` had deliberately stripped `Authorization` on the cross-host hop.\\n\\nReproduced with two local servers, where the endpoint 307s to an unrelated host:\\n\\n```\\n[LEGIT] GET  Authorization=\\\"Basic Z2l0OlNVUEVSX1NFQ1JFVF9QQVRfMTIzNDU=\\\"\\n[EVIL]  GET  Authorization=\\\"\\\"                    ← stdlib stripped it\\n[EVIL]  POST Authorization=\\\"Basic Z2l0OlNVUEVS…\\\" ← git-sync re-sent it\\n```\\n\\nAny redirect an attacker can cause is enough: an open redirect on the real host, a hostile mirror, or a MITM on a plain-`http` source. On the target side the token usually carries write access.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\nAn explicitly supplied credential — token flags, bearer flags, or userinfo in the URL — now goes only to the host named on the command line and its subdomains, on the same scheme and port. Anything else gets nothing, plus a warning naming the withheld host, and the credential helper is consulted for that host instead:\\n\\n```\\nsource: withholding the configured credentials from http://localhost:64772/repo.git:\\n/info/refs redirected outside 127.0.0.1. Consulting the git credential helper for that host instead.\\n```\\n\\nCredentials resolved *from* the helper are untouched — they're looked up keyed on the host being challenged, so they were already bound to their destination. The subdomain allowance keeps the case the flag exists for working: `example.com` → `replica.example.com` still authenticates.\\n\\n## Why redirect policy moved into git-sync\\n\\nThe same-site rule is stricter than the stdlib's on purpose. Go compares hostnames only, ignoring scheme and port, so it forwards `Authorization` from `host:443` to `host:9999` — a different service, potentially a different tenant. My first version of the end-to-end test caught exactly this: both `httptest` servers are on `127.0.0.1`, so the stdlib happily carried the token across the port boundary and the test failed.\\n\\nThat hop isn't visible from the request-building code, because the redirect is followed *inside* a single `http.Client.Do`. So policy now lives in a per-connection `CheckRedirect` that strips the header on any hop leaving the endpoint's site, layered over whatever policy the caller set (theirs still runs and can still veto). Setting `CheckRedirect` replaces the stdlib's ten-redirect default, so that cap is reimposed explicitly — otherwise this fix would have introduced a redirect-loop hang.\\n\\nThe client is shallow-copied per connection, sharing the caller's `Transport`, so nothing the caller passed in is mutated or reconfigured.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- `sameSite` in isolation, including the near-misses: suffix without a dot boundary (`notgithub.com` vs `github.com`), attacker-controlled prefix domain (`github.com.evil.example`), scheme downgrade, port change, and IP addresses having no subdomains.\\n- End to end against `httptest`: the cross-site POST must carry no credentials, and a same-site redirect must still carry them.\\n- By hand: the original two-server reproduction now logs an empty `Authorization` on both requests to the redirect target.\\n\\n`gofmt`, `go vet`, `golangci-lint` (0 issues), `go test ./...` 17/17, `-race` on `gitproto` and `syncer`.\\n\\n## Behavior change to be aware of\\n\\nIf a deployment today relies on the redirect target receiving the configured token and that target is **not** same-site with the endpoint, it will start getting 401s. The fix is to store those credentials in the git credential helper against the redirect host — git-sync will find them there, and the helper is now installed alongside an explicit token so that path actually works.\\n\\nWhat counts as same-site, precisely:\\n\\n| redirect | credentials |\\n|---|---|\\n| same host, any path | kept |\\n| subdomain of the endpoint host | kept |\\n| `http` → `https`, same host | kept (upgrade) |\\n| `https` → `http` | **withheld** (downgrade) |\\n| different host | **withheld** |\\n| different port (default ports normalized) | **withheld** |\\n\\n`docs/usage.md` gains a \\\"Credentials and redirects\\\" section explaining this; the flags were previously documented only in their flag help text.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **High Risk**\\n> Changes authentication and credential routing on HTTP redirects—a security-critical path—with behavior change for deployments that relied on sending configured tokens to non-same-site redirect hosts.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Fixes a **credential leak** when `--source-follow-info-refs-redirect` / `--target-follow-info-refs-redirect` is enabled: after `/info/refs` redirects, follow-up RPCs hit the redirect host directly and git-sync was re-attaching CLI/URL tokens that Go’s client had already stripped on the cross-host hop.\\n> \\n> **Explicit credentials** (tokens, bearer flags, URL userinfo) are now sent only to the configured host’s **same site** — matching host or subdomain, **same scheme and port** — via new `sameSite` logic and `outgoingAuth` on `HTTPConn`. Off-site redirect targets get no token, a one-time stderr warning, and the git credential helper on 401. Helper-resolved creds are unchanged.\\n> \\n> Redirect handling adds **`guardRedirects`**: a shallow `http.Client` copy with `CheckRedirect` that drops `Authorization` on hops leaving the endpoint site (tighter than stdlib hostname-only rules) and re-applies the 10-redirect cap. Info/refs and RPC paths use `outgoingAuth` instead of raw `c.Auth`; helper attach paths mark `authIsExplicit = false`.\\n> \\n> Docs add **Credentials and redirects** in `usage.md`; CHANGELOG documents the security fix. Tests cover `sameSite` edge cases and end-to-end cross-site vs same-site redirect behavior.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit b0e0f88541d3bbbe472233a7ce0bbe63124c4115. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n\",\n              \"reactions\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/108/reactions\",\n                \"total_count\": 0,\n                \"+1\": 0,\n                \"-1\": 0,\n                \"laugh\": 0,\n                \"hooray\": 0,\n                \"confused\": 0,\n                \"heart\": 0,\n                \"rocket\": 0,\n                \"eyes\": 0\n              },\n              \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/issues/108/timeline\",\n              \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n              \"state_reason\": null,\n              \"score\": 1\n            }\n          ],\n          \"search_type\": \"lexical\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"diff-specific\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"sparse-specific\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"tour-specific\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assets-specific\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\nTWENTY_PUBLIC_EVIDENCE_7D9A"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"Failed to create unified exec process: Argument list too long (os error 7)","exit_code":-1,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":0}},"started_at_ms":1794842078955,"completed_at_ms":1794842078960}}
