{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:27.494Z","ordinal":3009,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-741f6076-aea5-4b21-b164-a110bd970279","process_id":"60943","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import pathlib,sys;p=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]);p.parent.mkdir(exist_ok=True);p.write_bytes(b\"\")' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"list_files","cmd":"python3 -c 'import pathlib,sys;p=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]);p.parent.mkdir(exist_ok=True);p.write_bytes(b\"\")' /Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json","path":null}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":11625}},"started_at_ms":1794842127494,"completed_at_ms":1794842127494}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:27.645Z","ordinal":3010,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-5497f9ca-969f-42ff-92fb-d3e4b8a94111","process_id":"28031","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' '{\n  \"cli\": [\n    {\n      \"number\": 3165,\n      \"title\": \"ENT-2652: the CLI invites accounts and manages their invitations\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3165\",\n      \"head\": \"142f800b17cf9ac3d6d0c7ae3c81d78b08e6c505\",\n      \"branch\": \"dip/ent-2652-grant-invites\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Companion to entirehq/entiredb#5546 (ENT-2652). Safe to ship before that Core change: today'\"'\"'s Core ignores the new field and answers 201 as before.\\n\\nCore stops a manager from giving an existing account access without its consent. An account outside the parent scope gets an invitation, and only when the request sets `allow_invitation`.\\n\\n## Grant add\\n- `org|project|repo grant add` send `allow_invitation: true`.\\n- A 201 prints the granted line as before. A 202 prints `✓ Invited … No access until they accept; the invitation expires YYYY-MM-DD`. `--json` emits the 202 body (`status: invited`, `invitation_id`, `expires_at`).\\n- A picker run continues past a grantee Core refuses (already a member, a\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3164,\n      \"title\": \"ashtom/ssh-alias-repository-identity\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3164\",\n      \"head\": \"df41d4bfd551583c18957634ed731615b5771658\",\n      \"branch\": \"ashtom/ssh-alias-repository-identity\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back a trail. Feel free to edit the title or body, but keep the hidden marker below: Entire uses it to close this pull request when the trail closes.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches identity resolution for search, dispatch, trails caching, and checkpoint sync via subprocess `ssh -G`/`git config`, with strict timeout/cancellation handling but still new behavior on aliased remotes.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **SSH alias–aware remote identity resolution** so checkouts whose `origin` uses a custom SSH host (e.g. `git@github-work:…`) still map to the correct forge-qua\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3163,\n      \"title\": \"Codex hooks: emit native commandWindows and keep user hook fields\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3163\",\n      \"head\": \"dc774d30a0d69ec1817eea784a81de88c90e4688\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-codex-windows-hooks-2884\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2884.\\n\\nBuilds on #3075, which made every Windows hook wrapper look programs up on PATH only. The Windows commands here are built from that PR'\"'\"'s wrappers. What this adds on top is Codex'\"'\"'s native `commandWindows`, preservation of fields Entire doesn'\"'\"'t model, and trust coverage for the Windows command.\\n\\n@AppSolves, you offered to validate this on Windows. Could you try it with Codex 0.131 or later? The checks that matter most are `entire enable --agent codex`, the one-time trust prompt, a session'\"'\"'s checkpoint capture, and `entire doctor` from both PowerShell and Git Bash.\\n\\n## What this changes\\n\\n- **Native `commandWindows` on every managed Codex hook.** `.codex/hooks.json` keeps the POSIX\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3161,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): keep linked sessions through the multi-worktree recency filter\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3161\",\n      \"head\": \"b53ee194b726281fa46e59c78f3a9d2a5d6a2aae\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-multi-worktree-long-wait\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Stacked on #3005: until it merges, this diff also shows #3005'\"'\"'s commits. This PR'\"'\"'s own change is 9691b960 and b53ee194.\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\nA commit made in a worktree with no session of its own falls back to the sessions of other worktrees (`findSessionsForCommitLinking`). When those sessions span several worktrees, `resolveWorktreeCandidates` (`strategy/manual_commit_session.go`) keeps only the ones that interacted within `recentSessionWindow` (15 minutes), judged against the clock when the hook runs. prepare-commit-msg and post-commit each run that check, so they can disagree:\\n\\n1. A session in worktree B interacted a few minutes ago. A session in worktree C has been idle for a day. You commit in\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3160,\n      \"title\": \"e2e(controlplane): retry the device login and record GitHub'\"'\"'s page on failure\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3160\",\n      \"head\": \"5ac249a20ea4dec1daa9ae5fcecc2869be814e7d\",\n      \"branch\": \"victor/controlplane-login-retry\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Why\\n\\nThe control-plane E2E suite occasionally fails before any test runs:\\n\\n```\\ncontrol-plane e2e: login failed: browser approval: login stalled on github.com/login for 1m0s\\n```\\n\\nSeen in 43448670103 (`/login`), 43236603939 and 41816823508 (`/login/oauth/authorize`). The approver submits the sign-in form once and has no recovery when GitHub doesn'\"'\"'t advance, and nothing is captured about what GitHub actually showed (e.g. a captcha loads in an iframe, invisible to the body-text checks).\\n\\n## What\\n\\n- **Retry**: up to 3 attempts, each with a fresh browser and device code and a 3-minute budget, 30s apart (new TOTP window; GitHub rejects a reused code). Best-effort `entire logout` before a retry s\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3155,\n      \"title\": \"docs(windows): correct the agent hook, test and OpenCode notes\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3155\",\n      \"head\": \"7d58d6c6e98fe3aa86a0eb24a43b37f8abe105fd\",\n      \"branch\": \"docs/windows-md-hooks-and-tests\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Docs only: three statements in `WINDOWS.md` no longer match the code.\\n\\n| `WINDOWS.md` said | What the code does |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Agent hooks \\\"call `entire.exe` directly via `exec.Command`, not through a shell\\\" | Hooks are command lines the agent runs in its hook shell: the `sh -c` wrapper by default, and a `cmd.exe` wrapper for Codex, Cursor, Factory AI Droid and Antigravity on Windows (`agent/hook_command.go`, `docs/development/git-safety.md`) |\\n| `go test ./...` is the Windows unit test command | `test-windows` in `ci.yml` runs `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/... -run '\"'\"'(Windows\\\\|MSYS)'\"'\"'`, with the comment that this avoids \\\"running POSIX-only harnesses\\\" |\\n| The OpenCode plugin uses `Bun.spawnSync\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3153,\n      \"title\": \"muskan/test-resuming-sessions-with-dropped-image-placeholders\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3153\",\n      \"head\": \"558dda73aa56f798fd6a992a07c315f30f62b15d\",\n      \"branch\": \"muskan/test-resuming-sessions-with-dropped-image-placeholders\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back a trail. Feel free to edit the title or body, but keep the hidden marker below: Entire uses it to close this pull request when the trail closes.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3152,\n      \"title\": \"fix(copilot-cli): write a powershell command for every hook\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3152\",\n      \"head\": \"9a9910c2d4537d1c764b39b6cadaa38f7e8283db\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/copilot-cli-powershell-hooks\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #1675\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nCopilot CLI runs a hook entry'\"'\"'s `powershell` command on Windows and its `bash` command elsewhere. Entire wrote only `bash`. On Windows, Copilot then ran the sh wrapper through `bash`, and on a machine with WSL installed `bash` is `C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\bash.exe`, the WSL launcher. The hook ran inside the distro, so the session was recorded under `/mnt/c/...` paths (or not at all when the distro has no `entire`), and commits got no `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer. Nothing reported an error.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\n- Every Entire entry in `.github/hooks/entire.json` now carries a `powershell` command next to `bash`. The file is committed and read on every platform, so both are written w\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3151,\n      \"title\": \"muskan/externalize-images-codex-generates\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3151\",\n      \"head\": \"8e05cb3cab6f6e9dbd23099ced4744ffd7a18906\",\n      \"branch\": \"muskan/externalize-images-codex-generates\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back a trail. Feel free to edit the title or body, but keep the hidden marker below: Entire uses it to close this pull request when the trail closes.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3148,\n      \"title\": \"build(deps): bump github.com/betterleaks/betterleaks from 1.10.0 to 1.10.1 in the go-dependencies group across 1 directory\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3148\",\n      \"head\": \"d81adf8d7d64d5f2c70173aded776cafbfeb9211\",\n      \"branch\": \"dependabot/go_modules/go-dependencies-d6f60f25c1\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Bumps the go-dependencies group with 1 update in the / directory: [github.com/betterleaks/betterleaks](https://github.com/betterleaks/betterleaks).\\n\\nUpdates `github.com/betterleaks/betterleaks` from 1.10.0 to 1.10.1\\n<details>\\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\\\"https://github.com/betterleaks/betterleaks/releases\\\">github.com/betterleaks/betterleaks'\"'\"'s releases</a>.</em></p>\\n<blockquote>\\n<h2>v1.10.1</h2>\\n<h2>Changelog</h2>\\n<ul>\\n<li>39d5bdcf34db54e944facac5cf6e8b03db5e2b99 fix(deps): update brotli to fix CVE-2026-111497 (<a href=\\\"https://redirect.github.com/betterleaks/betterleaks/issues/458\\\">#458</a>)</li>\\n</ul>\\n</blockquote>\\n</details>\\n<details>\\n<summary>Commits</summ\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3140,\n      \"title\": \"redact: preserve only whole images, and scan them under keys that name a secret\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3140\",\n      \"head\": \"d4a4393e7684c47ed3c2f5d666ed38cde74c88ad\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-image-uri-secret-keys\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3139.\\n\\n#2963 skips every scanner for a string that is exactly an image data URI whose decoded bytes start with an image magic number, unless its key is a credential key. That leaves three gaps:\\n\\n1. Outside a connection object a bare `password`, `passwd`, `pwd`, `pass`, `secret` or `token` key isn'\"'\"'t a credential key, so an image-shaped value under it is stored as written where it used to redact.\\n2. Only the first bytes are checked, so any base64 after `/9j/` or `iVBORw0KGgo` is skipped under any key, and so is a token appended to a real image.\\n3. A custom rule written for one field, such as `\\\"auth_blob\\\":\\\"[^\\\"]+\\\"`, no longer redacts an image under it.\\n\\nWith scanners on, `JSONLContent` fo\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3137,\n      \"title\": \"redact: read defaults on positional, special and array parameters\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3137\",\n      \"head\": \"c36b64f0bcfa78219afd17b46e8f8cdbc3a817fd\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-shell-parameter-defaults\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Part of #3077: its first two bugs, split out of #3078 as @MuskanPaliwal asked there, so they can land while the joined-word part is settled. Both are on main.\\n\\n## The bugs\\n\\n1. **Defaults on parameters that aren'\"'\"'t identifiers.** `isPlaceholderShellExpansion` only recognized identifier names, so any other `${…}` fell through to \\\"plain reference\\\" and its default was never checked. `DB_PASSWORD=REDACTED, `PGPASSWORD=REDACTED, `DB_PASSWORD=REDACTED, `DB_PASSWORD=REDACTED, `DB_PASSWORD=REDACTED, `DB_PASSWORD=REDACTED and `REDACTED` stay visible on main. So do keyword DSNs, ODBC strings and JDBC URLs that hold them, and scanner findin\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3135,\n      \"title\": \"git-remote-entire: take a pack without side-band after a single ACK\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3135\",\n      \"head\": \"9660202358b8b0ecc4b908dc3be2e8842e3e0b1b\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-single-ack-no-sideband\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3134\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\nWithout `multi_ack`, upload-pack ACKs the first common have and sends the pack right after it. Without side-band that pack is raw, so `relaySingleACKRound`'\"'\"'s done round runs `pktline.PeekLine` on the `PACK` header, fails (`invalid pkt-len found`), and git reports `protocol error: bad pack header`. With side-band the pack'\"'\"'s first packet ends the loop, which is the only case the tests ran. The issue has the details.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\nThe done round now stops when the next bytes are a pack header (`PACK`, which can'\"'\"'t be a pkt-line length) and copies the rest unchanged. The peek moved into `peekRoundLine` (EOF, the server'\"'\"'s ERR, the raw pack, or a line) to keep `relaySingleAC\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3133,\n      \"title\": \"fix(session): don'\"'\"'t mark subagent tokens complete while a subagent is uncounted\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3133\",\n      \"head\": \"a4a686b6db963191ca79ebdbaecd0566fb3460aa\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-ledger-uncounted-children\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3132\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\n`TokenLedger.withSubagents` marks the subagent total complete whenever there is one, but a reading skips any child it can'\"'\"'t read: a Codex inventoried child whose rollout can'\"'\"'t be found or read, or a Claude Code subagent transcript that can'\"'\"'t be opened. The checkpoint then records `subagent_tokens_complete: true` for a total missing that child, where the per-turn Codex extraction says false. The issue has the details.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\n- A reading lists a child it knows of but couldn'\"'\"'t count with a nil total. Codex adds these from its inventory. For Claude Code, the usage reader now tells a counter that implements the new `UnreadFileCounter` which files it couldn'\"'\"'t read, a\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3131,\n      \"title\": \"fix(codex): save the child token cache with the cursor\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3131\",\n      \"head\": \"4c1f6ffe350f6bec882ac1e5f4475ee32269d10f\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-codex-child-cache\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3130\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\n`ReadCumulativeUsage` saves the counter into the cursor before it calls `Totals`. The Codex counter fills its child cache (`ChildKey`, `ChildTotals`) in `Totals`, so the cache never reaches the cursor and every reading re-reads each inventoried child rollout. The issue has the details.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\n- `Totals` runs before the counter is saved, and the `UsageCounter` interface doc says so. None of the other counters'\"'\"' `Totals` change any state (pi, copilotcli, claudecode, antigravity, opencode, factoryaidroid), so for them the order makes no difference.\\n- Once the cache is saved, two gaps in it reach later readings, so this PR closes them too:\\n  - `childFingerprint` cov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3129,\n      \"title\": \"fix(transcript): keep a failed OpenCode tool'\"'\"'s error message\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3129\",\n      \"head\": \"4bcb048cb69d46f1daebe40b9e0dfc4ba3451866\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-opencode-tool-error\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3128\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\nOpenCode stores a failed tool'\"'\"'s message in its state'\"'\"'s `error` and gives that state no `output` (1.x `ToolStateError`; the 2.x export'\"'\"'s `error.message`, which `opencodev2.convertOpenCodeV2Content` also writes to `error`). `openCodeToolResult` reads only `output`, so every failed OpenCode tool in the compact transcript is `{\\\"output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"error\\\"}`. The issue has the details.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\nWhen a result is an error and has no output, it carries the state'\"'\"'s `error` message, as Codex'\"'\"'s MCP calls already do in `codexItemLines`. A failed tool that does have output keeps it.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n`TestCompact_OpenCodeFailedToolKeepsError` runs a failed `read` in a 1.x export and\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3127,\n      \"title\": \"redact: keep a custom ip match inside a built-in IP match\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3127\",\n      \"head\": \"11fbbfe517bb7631d8913e202baf602f933f9f74\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-custom-ip-inside-version-value\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3126\\n\\nWith a custom PII pattern named `ip`, a match inside a built-in IP match was left as written under a version key. `dropNestedIPRegions` dropped any IP region nested in the region kept before it, so for `{\\\"version\\\":\\\"::ffff:10.0.0.5\\\"}` and a custom `ip` pattern `0\\\\.0\\\\.5` the custom region went, and then `redactLeafValue` removed the built-in regions because the key is `version`. Nothing was left to redact `0.0.5`. Split out of #3065 as @MuskanPaliwal asked there.\\n\\n| custom patterns | main (f4327183) | this PR |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `ip: 0\\\\.0\\\\.5` | `{\\\"version\\\":\\\"::ffff:10.0.0.5\\\"}` | `{\\\"version\\\":\\\"::ffff:10.[REDACTED_IP]\\\"}` |\\n| `ip: 0\\\\.0\\\\.5`, `marker: ffff\\\\|10` | `{\\\"version\\\":\\\"::[REDA\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3122,\n      \"title\": \"soph/codex-windows-sessionstart\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3122\",\n      \"head\": \"d6c0ba9470f9dbe3717bdce3effc06eb3e39df9f\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/codex-windows-sessionstart\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Stacked on #3075 (trail cli/1792), and must ship in the same release. The base is `main`, so GitHub'\"'\"'s diff also shows #3075'\"'\"'s commits; this PR'\"'\"'s own change is the top commit, d6c0ba9470.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nOn native Windows, Codex'\"'\"'s SessionStart hook was installed in the direct JSON-warning form: a cmd.exe line with no nested `cmd.exe`. Codex runs hooks in the session shell, which is PowerShell by default, and that line does not parse there. So the hook never ran, and Codex reported it as failed every session.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\n- On native Windows, SessionStart now uses the silent nested wrapper, like Codex'\"'\"'s other hooks. It runs under both PowerShell and cmd.exe (`codex.jsonWarningHookCommand`).\\n- sh h\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3116,\n      \"title\": \"soph/linux-keyring-service-missing\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3116\",\n      \"head\": \"7a592c70b05a4524932b506489c94fde624c5bf6\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/linux-keyring-service-missing\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back a trail. Feel free to edit the title or body, but keep the hidden marker below: Entire uses it to close this pull request when the trail closes.\\n\\n'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' '{\n  \"cli\": [\n    {\n      \"number\": 3165,\n      \"title\": \"ENT-2652: the CLI invites accounts and manages their invitations\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3165\",\n      \"head\": \"142f800b17cf9ac3d6d0c7ae3c81d78b08e6c505\",\n      \"branch\": \"dip/ent-2652-grant-invites\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Companion to entirehq/entiredb#5546 (ENT-2652). Safe to ship before that Core change: today'\"'\"'s Core ignores the new field and answers 201 as before.\\n\\nCore stops a manager from giving an existing account access without its consent. An account outside the parent scope gets an invitation, and only when the request sets `allow_invitation`.\\n\\n## Grant add\\n- `org|project|repo grant add` send `allow_invitation: true`.\\n- A 201 prints the granted line as before. A 202 prints `✓ Invited … No access until they accept; the invitation expires YYYY-MM-DD`. `--json` emits the 202 body (`status: invited`, `invitation_id`, `expires_at`).\\n- A picker run continues past a grantee Core refuses (already a member, a\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3164,\n      \"title\": \"ashtom/ssh-alias-repository-identity\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3164\",\n      \"head\": \"df41d4bfd551583c18957634ed731615b5771658\",\n      \"branch\": \"ashtom/ssh-alias-repository-identity\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back a trail. Feel free to edit the title or body, but keep the hidden marker below: Entire uses it to close this pull request when the trail closes.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches identity resolution for search, dispatch, trails caching, and checkpoint sync via subprocess `ssh -G`/`git config`, with strict timeout/cancellation handling but still new behavior on aliased remotes.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **SSH alias–aware remote identity resolution** so checkouts whose `origin` uses a custom SSH host (e.g. `git@github-work:…`) still map to the correct forge-qua\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3163,\n      \"title\": \"Codex hooks: emit native commandWindows and keep user hook fields\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3163\",\n      \"head\": \"dc774d30a0d69ec1817eea784a81de88c90e4688\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-codex-windows-hooks-2884\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2884.\\n\\nBuilds on #3075, which made every Windows hook wrapper look programs up on PATH only. The Windows commands here are built from that PR'\"'\"'s wrappers. What this adds on top is Codex'\"'\"'s native `commandWindows`, preservation of fields Entire doesn'\"'\"'t model, and trust coverage for the Windows command.\\n\\n@AppSolves, you offered to validate this on Windows. Could you try it with Codex 0.131 or later? The checks that matter most are `entire enable --agent codex`, the one-time trust prompt, a session'\"'\"'s checkpoint capture, and `entire doctor` from both PowerShell and Git Bash.\\n\\n## What this changes\\n\\n- **Native `commandWindows` on every managed Codex hook.** `.codex/hooks.json` keeps the POSIX\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3161,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): keep linked sessions through the multi-worktree recency filter\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3161\",\n      \"head\": \"b53ee194b726281fa46e59c78f3a9d2a5d6a2aae\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-multi-worktree-long-wait\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Stacked on #3005: until it merges, this diff also shows #3005'\"'\"'s commits. This PR'\"'\"'s own change is 9691b960 and b53ee194.\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\nA commit made in a worktree with no session of its own falls back to the sessions of other worktrees (`findSessionsForCommitLinking`). When those sessions span several worktrees, `resolveWorktreeCandidates` (`strategy/manual_commit_session.go`) keeps only the ones that interacted within `recentSessionWindow` (15 minutes), judged against the clock when the hook runs. prepare-commit-msg and post-commit each run that check, so they can disagree:\\n\\n1. A session in worktree B interacted a few minutes ago. A session in worktree C has been idle for a day. You commit in\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3160,\n      \"title\": \"e2e(controlplane): retry the device login and record GitHub'\"'\"'s page on failure\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3160\",\n      \"head\": \"5ac249a20ea4dec1daa9ae5fcecc2869be814e7d\",\n      \"branch\": \"victor/controlplane-login-retry\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Why\\n\\nThe control-plane E2E suite occasionally fails before any test runs:\\n\\n```\\ncontrol-plane e2e: login failed: browser approval: login stalled on github.com/login for 1m0s\\n```\\n\\nSeen in 43448670103 (`/login`), 43236603939 and 41816823508 (`/login/oauth/authorize`). The approver submits the sign-in form once and has no recovery when GitHub doesn'\"'\"'t advance, and nothing is captured about what GitHub actually showed (e.g. a captcha loads in an iframe, invisible to the body-text checks).\\n\\n## What\\n\\n- **Retry**: up to 3 attempts, each with a fresh browser and device code and a 3-minute budget, 30s apart (new TOTP window; GitHub rejects a reused code). Best-effort `entire logout` before a retry s\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3155,\n      \"title\": \"docs(windows): correct the agent hook, test and OpenCode notes\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3155\",\n      \"head\": \"7d58d6c6e98fe3aa86a0eb24a43b37f8abe105fd\",\n      \"branch\": \"docs/windows-md-hooks-and-tests\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Docs only: three statements in `WINDOWS.md` no longer match the code.\\n\\n| `WINDOWS.md` said | What the code does |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Agent hooks \\\"call `entire.exe` directly via `exec.Command`, not through a shell\\\" | Hooks are command lines the agent runs in its hook shell: the `sh -c` wrapper by default, and a `cmd.exe` wrapper for Codex, Cursor, Factory AI Droid and Antigravity on Windows (`agent/hook_command.go`, `docs/development/git-safety.md`) |\\n| `go test ./...` is the Windows unit test command | `test-windows` in `ci.yml` runs `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/... -run '\"'\"'(Windows\\\\|MSYS)'\"'\"'`, with the comment that this avoids \\\"running POSIX-only harnesses\\\" |\\n| The OpenCode plugin uses `Bun.spawnSync\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3153,\n      \"title\": \"muskan/test-resuming-sessions-with-dropped-image-placeholders\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3153\",\n      \"head\": \"558dda73aa56f798fd6a992a07c315f30f62b15d\",\n      \"branch\": \"muskan/test-resuming-sessions-with-dropped-image-placeholders\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back a trail. Feel free to edit the title or body, but keep the hidden marker below: Entire uses it to close this pull request when the trail closes.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3152,\n      \"title\": \"fix(copilot-cli): write a powershell command for every hook\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3152\",\n      \"head\": \"9a9910c2d4537d1c764b39b6cadaa38f7e8283db\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/copilot-cli-powershell-hooks\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #1675\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nCopilot CLI runs a hook entry'\"'\"'s `powershell` command on Windows and its `bash` command elsewhere. Entire wrote only `bash`. On Windows, Copilot then ran the sh wrapper through `bash`, and on a machine with WSL installed `bash` is `C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\bash.exe`, the WSL launcher. The hook ran inside the distro, so the session was recorded under `/mnt/c/...` paths (or not at all when the distro has no `entire`), and commits got no `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer. Nothing reported an error.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\n- Every Entire entry in `.github/hooks/entire.json` now carries a `powershell` command next to `bash`. The file is committed and read on every platform, so both are written w\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3151,\n      \"title\": \"muskan/externalize-images-codex-generates\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3151\",\n      \"head\": \"8e05cb3cab6f6e9dbd23099ced4744ffd7a18906\",\n      \"branch\": \"muskan/externalize-images-codex-generates\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back a trail. Feel free to edit the title or body, but keep the hidden marker below: Entire uses it to close this pull request when the trail closes.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3148,\n      \"title\": \"build(deps): bump github.com/betterleaks/betterleaks from 1.10.0 to 1.10.1 in the go-dependencies group across 1 directory\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3148\",\n      \"head\": \"d81adf8d7d64d5f2c70173aded776cafbfeb9211\",\n      \"branch\": \"dependabot/go_modules/go-dependencies-d6f60f25c1\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Bumps the go-dependencies group with 1 update in the / directory: [github.com/betterleaks/betterleaks](https://github.com/betterleaks/betterleaks).\\n\\nUpdates `github.com/betterleaks/betterleaks` from 1.10.0 to 1.10.1\\n<details>\\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\\\"https://github.com/betterleaks/betterleaks/releases\\\">github.com/betterleaks/betterleaks'\"'\"'s releases</a>.</em></p>\\n<blockquote>\\n<h2>v1.10.1</h2>\\n<h2>Changelog</h2>\\n<ul>\\n<li>39d5bdcf34db54e944facac5cf6e8b03db5e2b99 fix(deps): update brotli to fix CVE-2026-111497 (<a href=\\\"https://redirect.github.com/betterleaks/betterleaks/issues/458\\\">#458</a>)</li>\\n</ul>\\n</blockquote>\\n</details>\\n<details>\\n<summary>Commits</summ\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3140,\n      \"title\": \"redact: preserve only whole images, and scan them under keys that name a secret\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3140\",\n      \"head\": \"d4a4393e7684c47ed3c2f5d666ed38cde74c88ad\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-image-uri-secret-keys\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3139.\\n\\n#2963 skips every scanner for a string that is exactly an image data URI whose decoded bytes start with an image magic number, unless its key is a credential key. That leaves three gaps:\\n\\n1. Outside a connection object a bare `password`, `passwd`, `pwd`, `pass`, `secret` or `token` key isn'\"'\"'t a credential key, so an image-shaped value under it is stored as written where it used to redact.\\n2. Only the first bytes are checked, so any base64 after `/9j/` or `iVBORw0KGgo` is skipped under any key, and so is a token appended to a real image.\\n3. A custom rule written for one field, such as `\\\"auth_blob\\\":\\\"[^\\\"]+\\\"`, no longer redacts an image under it.\\n\\nWith scanners on, `JSONLContent` fo\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3137,\n      \"title\": \"redact: read defaults on positional, special and array parameters\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3137\",\n      \"head\": \"c36b64f0bcfa78219afd17b46e8f8cdbc3a817fd\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-shell-parameter-defaults\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Part of #3077: its first two bugs, split out of #3078 as @MuskanPaliwal asked there, so they can land while the joined-word part is settled. Both are on main.\\n\\n## The bugs\\n\\n1. **Defaults on parameters that aren'\"'\"'t identifiers.** `isPlaceholderShellExpansion` only recognized identifier names, so any other `${…}` fell through to \\\"plain reference\\\" and its default was never checked. `DB_PASSWORD=REDACTED, `PGPASSWORD=REDACTED, `DB_PASSWORD=REDACTED, `DB_PASSWORD=REDACTED, `DB_PASSWORD=REDACTED, `DB_PASSWORD=REDACTED and `REDACTED` stay visible on main. So do keyword DSNs, ODBC strings and JDBC URLs that hold them, and scanner findin\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3135,\n      \"title\": \"git-remote-entire: take a pack without side-band after a single ACK\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3135\",\n      \"head\": \"9660202358b8b0ecc4b908dc3be2e8842e3e0b1b\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-single-ack-no-sideband\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3134\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\nWithout `multi_ack`, upload-pack ACKs the first common have and sends the pack right after it. Without side-band that pack is raw, so `relaySingleACKRound`'\"'\"'s done round runs `pktline.PeekLine` on the `PACK` header, fails (`invalid pkt-len found`), and git reports `protocol error: bad pack header`. With side-band the pack'\"'\"'s first packet ends the loop, which is the only case the tests ran. The issue has the details.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\nThe done round now stops when the next bytes are a pack header (`PACK`, which can'\"'\"'t be a pkt-line length) and copies the rest unchanged. The peek moved into `peekRoundLine` (EOF, the server'\"'\"'s ERR, the raw pack, or a line) to keep `relaySingleAC\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3133,\n      \"title\": \"fix(session): don'\"'\"'t mark subagent tokens complete while a subagent is uncounted\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3133\",\n      \"head\": \"a4a686b6db963191ca79ebdbaecd0566fb3460aa\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-ledger-uncounted-children\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3132\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\n`TokenLedger.withSubagents` marks the subagent total complete whenever there is one, but a reading skips any child it can'\"'\"'t read: a Codex inventoried child whose rollout can'\"'\"'t be found or read, or a Claude Code subagent transcript that can'\"'\"'t be opened. The checkpoint then records `subagent_tokens_complete: true` for a total missing that child, where the per-turn Codex extraction says false. The issue has the details.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\n- A reading lists a child it knows of but couldn'\"'\"'t count with a nil total. Codex adds these from its inventory. For Claude Code, the usage reader now tells a counter that implements the new `UnreadFileCounter` which files it couldn'\"'\"'t read, a\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3131,\n      \"title\": \"fix(codex): save the child token cache with the cursor\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3131\",\n      \"head\": \"4c1f6ffe350f6bec882ac1e5f4475ee32269d10f\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-codex-child-cache\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3130\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\n`ReadCumulativeUsage` saves the counter into the cursor before it calls `Totals`. The Codex counter fills its child cache (`ChildKey`, `ChildTotals`) in `Totals`, so the cache never reaches the cursor and every reading re-reads each inventoried child rollout. The issue has the details.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\n- `Totals` runs before the counter is saved, and the `UsageCounter` interface doc says so. None of the other counters'\"'\"' `Totals` change any state (pi, copilotcli, claudecode, antigravity, opencode, factoryaidroid), so for them the order makes no difference.\\n- Once the cache is saved, two gaps in it reach later readings, so this PR closes them too:\\n  - `childFingerprint` cov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3129,\n      \"title\": \"fix(transcript): keep a failed OpenCode tool'\"'\"'s error message\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3129\",\n      \"head\": \"4bcb048cb69d46f1daebe40b9e0dfc4ba3451866\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-opencode-tool-error\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3128\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\nOpenCode stores a failed tool'\"'\"'s message in its state'\"'\"'s `error` and gives that state no `output` (1.x `ToolStateError`; the 2.x export'\"'\"'s `error.message`, which `opencodev2.convertOpenCodeV2Content` also writes to `error`). `openCodeToolResult` reads only `output`, so every failed OpenCode tool in the compact transcript is `{\\\"output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"error\\\"}`. The issue has the details.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\nWhen a result is an error and has no output, it carries the state'\"'\"'s `error` message, as Codex'\"'\"'s MCP calls already do in `codexItemLines`. A failed tool that does have output keeps it.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n`TestCompact_OpenCodeFailedToolKeepsError` runs a failed `read` in a 1.x export and\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3127,\n      \"title\": \"redact: keep a custom ip match inside a built-in IP match\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3127\",\n      \"head\": \"11fbbfe517bb7631d8913e202baf602f933f9f74\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-custom-ip-inside-version-value\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3126\\n\\nWith a custom PII pattern named `ip`, a match inside a built-in IP match was left as written under a version key. `dropNestedIPRegions` dropped any IP region nested in the region kept before it, so for `{\\\"version\\\":\\\"::ffff:10.0.0.5\\\"}` and a custom `ip` pattern `0\\\\.0\\\\.5` the custom region went, and then `redactLeafValue` removed the built-in regions because the key is `version`. Nothing was left to redact `0.0.5`. Split out of #3065 as @MuskanPaliwal asked there.\\n\\n| custom patterns | main (f4327183) | this PR |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `ip: 0\\\\.0\\\\.5` | `{\\\"version\\\":\\\"::ffff:10.0.0.5\\\"}` | `{\\\"version\\\":\\\"::ffff:10.[REDACTED_IP]\\\"}` |\\n| `ip: 0\\\\.0\\\\.5`, `marker: ffff\\\\|10` | `{\\\"version\\\":\\\"::[REDA\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3122,\n      \"title\": \"soph/codex-windows-sessionstart\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3122\",\n      \"head\": \"d6c0ba9470f9dbe3717bdce3effc06eb3e39df9f\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/codex-windows-sessionstart\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Stacked on #3075 (trail cli/1792), and must ship in the same release. The base is `main`, so GitHub'\"'\"'s diff also shows #3075'\"'\"'s commits; this PR'\"'\"'s own change is the top commit, d6c0ba9470.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nOn native Windows, Codex'\"'\"'s SessionStart hook was installed in the direct JSON-warning form: a cmd.exe line with no nested `cmd.exe`. Codex runs hooks in the session shell, which is PowerShell by default, and that line does not parse there. So the hook never ran, and Codex reported it as failed every session.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\n- On native Windows, SessionStart now uses the silent nested wrapper, like Codex'\"'\"'s other hooks. It runs under both PowerShell and cmd.exe (`codex.jsonWarningHookCommand`).\\n- sh h\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3116,\n      \"title\": \"soph/linux-keyring-service-missing\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3116\",\n      \"head\": \"7a592c70b05a4524932b506489c94fde624c5bf6\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/linux-keyring-service-missing\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back a trail. Feel free to edit the title or body, but keep the hidden marker below: Entire uses it to close this pull request when the trail closes.\\n\\n'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":14000}},"started_at_ms":1794842127643,"completed_at_ms":1794842127645}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:27.790Z","ordinal":3011,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-960ca42b-23c7-40a3-b6b4-5754bf2f83d1","process_id":"28243","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' '<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes how credential-store and auth resolution failures are classified and messaged; behavior is clearer for users but touches login, status, and token refresh paths on Linux/BSD keyring backends.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Linux/BSD OS keyring failures caused by a **missing or unreachable Secret Service** (D-Bus) are now classified as `ErrKeyringServiceMissing` instead of looking like a blank l\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3113,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): give a reserved checkpoint ID to one commit only\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3113\",\n      \"head\": \"7988c5736ff20d7c8a656205d689091b6afb03b1\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-shared-reservation-3069\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3069.\\n\\nStacked on #3068, which is stacked on #3034 and #3005. The fix needs #3068'\"'\"'s per-commit take: without it, the first commit'\"'\"'s post-commit takes every stamp, including the fresh one the next commit now gets, and that commit would keep a trailer for a checkpoint that is never written (#3030). So this branch is built on #3068'\"'\"'s head (e8250a77), and until those merge the diff here also shows their commits. This PR'\"'\"'s own changes are the seven commits on top of e8250a77. After them, main is merged in (ae1c9ec3) to clear a conflict in `docs/development/checkpoint-implementation.md`: #3108 rewrote the session-state bullet right next to the commit-linking bullet that #3034 and #3068 chan\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3112,\n      \"title\": \"redact: cap the expansions the placeholder rule reads\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3112\",\n      \"head\": \"7f5e03ea0718c0b3ac7d0ded17246a4f327a3edc\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-placeholder-nesting\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3111\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\n`isPlaceholderSecretValue` and `isPlaceholderShellExpansion` call each other once per level of a `${NAME:-word}` default whose word is another default, and each level reads the whole rest of the value again. A value nested n deep is read n times: `DB_PASSWORD=REDACTED nested 4000 deep takes about 3.7 s on main, and each doubling of the depth costs about 14x. The issue has the numbers for each shape.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\n- `maxPlaceholderExpansions = 8`. A value with more `${` than that is not read as a placeholder, so it redacts (fail closed). Each level of the recursion holds one more `${`, so the count bounds it: the rule reads at most eight levels of any value.\\n-\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3110,\n      \"title\": \"fix(hooks): identify a chained Trunk launcher without grep\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3110\",\n      \"head\": \"663435fac27f5068d696f5c3b4abd919df7d53c6\",\n      \"branch\": \"trunk-chain-no-grep\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Review after entireio/cli#3051 merges. Until then this PR also contains that PR'\"'\"'s commits. It now includes #3051'\"'\"'s current head (`b6335784`), so only these commits are new here:\\n\\n- `0177d8e9a` fix(hooks): identify a chained Trunk launcher without grep\\n- `43eb8416c` fix(hooks): bound the no-grep Trunk launcher scan\\n- `3be66e57f` Merge #3051'\"'\"'s head into trunk-chain-no-grep\\n- `b46370d3a` test(hooks): check the 64KiB scan cap instead of a 2s wall clock\\n- `807b2a206` test(hooks): share the Trunk chain test helpers\\n- `e32a8f2f5` fix(hooks): keep the user'\"'\"'s lines when upgrading a Trunk chain\\n- `1b84203c1` refactor(hooks): choose the installed hook'\"'\"'s content in one helper\\n- `2b158373b` fix(hooks): r\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3109,\n      \"title\": \"redact: read JSONL argv arrays as one command line\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3109\",\n      \"head\": \"e4213f1ea8c3c2815cbbce94e739cf159b5c9946\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-argv-command-passwords-up\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Please review this after #3048 merges. Until then, this pull request includes #3048'\"'\"'s commits as well; only these thirteen commits are new here, with merges of #3048'\"'\"'s newer commits between them:\\n\\n- `a01c5c43a` redact: read JSONL argv arrays as one command line\\n- `4dfb1f32b` redact: argv option values, line breaks, shared copies, object keys\\n- `6a801efc7` redact: argv line breaks, credential keys, escaped quotes, region sets\\n- `6b8423086` redact: read a netrc password quoted with an escaped apostrophe\\n- `f72e3481f` redact: keep argv password copies in skipped fields\\n- `0efca0d21` redact: hide self-detected argv tokens in keys and quote dashed netrc passwords\\n- `ed98bc035` redact: keep skippe\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3106,\n      \"title\": \"soph/explain-tests-isolate-settings\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3106\",\n      \"head\": \"6d6d2450155b43c1f753827db275d6d347e2b5d8\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/explain-tests-isolate-settings\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back a trail. Feel free to edit the title or body, but keep the hidden marker below: Entire uses it to close this pull request when the trail closes.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Test-only changes with no production behavior impact.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Makes **`explain`** flag-validation tests deterministic by running them against a **temporary git repo** with Entire **enabled**, instead of the developer'\"'\"'s checkout.\\n> \\n> Adds **`explainEnabledContext`**, which initializes a repo, writes `.entire/settings.json` with `enabled: true`, and attaches it via `settings.WithWor\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3104,\n      \"title\": \"fix(cli): provide actionable file-store hint when OS keyring is unavailable\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3104\",\n      \"head\": \"56ddb69ac46e74bba9d951a61b230ab3559bebf4\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/keyring-headless-error-hint\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Description\\nFixes #3058.\\n\\n### Problem\\nWhen running on headless Linux, Docker containers, CI, or minimal server environments without a running DBus Secret Service, commands that read or refresh credentials fail with cryptic messages such as:\\n```\\nresolve repo: refresh login token: load core token: read access token: The name org.freedesktop.secrets was not provided by any .service files\\n```\\nor:\\n```\\nread access token: Cannot autolaunch D-Bus without X11 $DISPLAY\\n```\\n\\nPreviously, only `entire login` included an actionable headless hint via `withHeadlessStoreHint`. Other subcommands (such as `entire repo remote add origin`, `entire status`, `entire checkpoint`, etc.) bubbled up the raw store e\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3103,\n      \"title\": \"perf(redact): apply JSONL replacements in a single linear pass\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3103\",\n      \"head\": \"3696d866c354b21ae0a46d3e8b2c7a21d57a8ed5\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/jsonl-redaction-single-pass\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Description\\nFixes #3081.\\n\\n### Problem\\nIn `applyJSONReplacements` (`redact/redact.go`), replacements were previously applied in an outer loop over each collected `jsonReplacement`, invoking `strings.Count` + `strings.ReplaceAll` for unkeyed replacements and `replaceKeyedJSONValue` (full line scan and copy) for keyed replacements.\\n\\nWhen a JSONL line contains $N$ distinct secrets (e.g. an environment dump, database connection strings, config files), this cost $O(N \\\\times \\\\text{line length})$, scaling quadratically in $N$. On 16,000 secrets, the splice alone took ~14.5 seconds.\\n\\n### Solution\\n1. **Single-Pass Linear Splice**:\\n   - Pre-encodes replacements into `keyedMap` (`(keyJSON, origJSON) \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3102,\n      \"title\": \"feat(execx,procutil): terminate process tree on Windows when context is cancelled\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3102\",\n      \"head\": \"4e71fdf3bed859c1042c90942ad6e4e6714dd76e\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/windows-process-tree-cancel\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Description\\nFixes #3052.\\n\\n### Background\\nOn Unix, `execx.TerminateOnCancel` and `procutil.TerminateOnCancel` configure a new process group (`Setpgid = true`) and send `SIGKILL` to `-cmd.Process.Pid` on cancellation to terminate the entire process group.\\nOn Windows, `killProcessGroupOnCancel` was previously a no-op stub:\\n```go\\nfunc killProcessGroupOnCancel(_ *exec.Cmd) {}\\n```\\nThis fell back to Go'\"'\"'s default `Cancel` behavior, which calls `TerminateProcess` on the direct child only. Because Windows does not automatically terminate child processes when a parent process exits, any descendants spawned by the child (such as `git-remote-https.exe`, `ssh.exe`, MCP servers, subagents, or clean filt\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3101,\n      \"title\": \"test(osroot): skip symlink traversal tests when symlinks cannot be created\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3101\",\n      \"head\": \"0d8b03be8d9c1416693890f537e6d1bf8d631d48\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/osroot-test-symlink-skip\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Description\\nFixes #3100.\\n\\nIn `cmd/entire/cli/osroot/osroot_test.go`, other tests that create symbolic links (lines 703 and 722) handle environments where symlink creation lacks privileges by checking:\\n```go\\nif err := os.Symlink(outside, filepath.Join(base, \\\"link\\\")); err != nil {\\n\\tt.Skipf(\\\"symlink not supported: %v\\\", err)\\n}\\n```\\n\\nHowever, `TestSymlinkTraversal_ReadBlocked` and `TestSymlinkTraversal_WriteBlocked` asserted `require.NoError(t, os.Symlink(...))` directly. On Windows without Developer Mode or elevation (`SeCreateSymbolicLinkPrivilege`), creating symlinks fails with `A required privilege is not held by the client`.\\n\\nThis PR skips the tests gracefully if `os.Symlink` returns an er\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3099,\n      \"title\": \"feat(osroot): add ForgetTree and release directory handles during test cleanup\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3099\",\n      \"head\": \"22cc7c2ce095f7cd4bb00321fe87a989cc884bb0\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/osroot-forget-tree\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Description\\nFixes #3098.\\n\\n`osroot.Shared` and `osroot.SharedChild` memoize open `*os.Root` directory handles in the global `sharedRoots` registry.\\nOn Windows (NTFS), open directory handles lock the directory and all of its parent directories from being deleted.\\n\\nWhen unit tests initialize temporary git repositories (via `testutil.InitRepo(t, dir)`) and exercise code paths that query `.entire` or `.git` via `osroot.Shared`, directory handles remain open in `sharedRoots`. When `t.TempDir()` cleanup subsequently executes `os.RemoveAll(tempDir)`, Windows fails with `ERROR_SHARING_VIOLATION`:\\n`unlinkat ... The process cannot access the file because it is being used by another process.`\\n\\nWhile \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3097,\n      \"title\": \"test(checkpoint): resolve repo root via runtime.Caller in open_test\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3097\",\n      \"head\": \"5be869459bae5e8fe83d342baaa1e3fded904fc5\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/checkpoint-open-test-root-discovery\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Description\\nFixes #3096.\\n\\nIn `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/open_test.go`, `TestOpenOptionsLiteralsDeclareReadRemotes` walks the repo'\"'\"'s `cmd/` tree to verify AST literals.\\nTo locate the repository root, it previously called:\\n`root, err := filepath.Abs(filepath.Join(\\\"..\\\", \\\"..\\\", \\\"..\\\", \\\"..\\\"))`\\n\\nThis relies on the test execution working directory being `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint`. If tests are run from the repo root (or via test runners / precompiled test binaries where `cwd` is not the package dir), relative path traversal resolves above the workspace rather than at the repository root, failing with:\\n`walk root D:\\\\ does not look like the repo root: GetFileAttributesEx D:\\\\cmd\\\\entire: The system c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3095,\n      \"title\": \"test(checkpoint): skip TestCopyMetadataDir_RefusesSymlinks when symlinks cannot be created\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3095\",\n      \"head\": \"440f3bda45156d00cc022cc31600e45585eb70ab\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/checkpoint-test-symlink-skip\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Description\\nFixes #3094.\\n\\nOn Windows, creating symbolic links requires elevated privileges (`SeCreateSymbolicLinkPrivilege`) or Developer Mode enabled.\\nWhile other tests across the repository use `testutil.SkipWithoutSymlinks(t)` to gracefully skip tests when running unprivileged on Windows, `TestCopyMetadataDir_RefusesSymlinks` directly called `os.Symlink` without this check, resulting in test failure when run in unprivileged environments.\\n\\nThis PR adds `testutil.SkipWithoutSymlinks(t)` at the beginning of `TestCopyMetadataDir_RefusesSymlinks`.\\n\\n## Before and After Test Results\\n\\n### Before\\n```\\n=== RUN   TestCopyMetadataDir_RefusesSymlinks\\n    checkpoint_test.go:69: failed to create symli\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3093,\n      \"title\": \"test(checkpoint): isolate USERPROFILE in git config author tests\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3093\",\n      \"head\": \"f38963101dddf140882f96005ae9a1cd6efb5239\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/checkpoint-test-userprofile-isolation\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Description\\nFixes #3092.\\n\\nIn `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/persistent_update_test.go`, several tests (`TestUpdateCommitted_UsesCorrectAuthor`, `TestGetGitAuthorFromRepo_GlobalFallback`, and `TestGetGitAuthorFromRepo_NoConfig`) attempt to isolate global git config resolution by setting `HOME` to a temporary directory.\\n\\nOn Windows, Go'\"'\"'s `os.UserHomeDir()` (called by `go-git`'\"'\"'s global config loader) prioritizes `%USERPROFILE%` over `%HOME%`. Because `USERPROFILE` was not overridden, `go-git` continued to load the host developer'\"'\"'s global `~/.gitconfig`, causing these tests to fail on Windows whenever a global git config exists on the host machine.\\n\\n### Fix\\n1. Updated `pointHomeAt(t, home)` in `c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3091,\n      \"title\": \"test(settings): disable core.protectNTFS when staging trailing char variants\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3091\",\n      \"head\": \"1f224935f211c8066a10ebe11a07df7c5cc93835\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/settings-protectntfs-test\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Description\\nFixes #3090.\\n\\nIn `cmd/entire/cli/settings/opf_command_trust_test.go`, `TestPathIsVersioned_Win32TrailingCharVariantsAreTracked` tests that trailing-space and trailing-dot path variants (such as `.entire/settings.local.json.` and `.entire/settings.local.json `) staged into the index are properly recognized as versioned and untrusted.\\n\\nTo stage these paths directly into the index, `stageBlobAt` invokes:\\n`git update-index --add --cacheinfo 100644,<hash>,<repoPath>`\\n\\nOn Windows (where `core.protectNTFS` is typically true by default in Git for Windows), git forbids indexing paths containing trailing spaces or trailing periods, resulting in:\\n`fatal: git update-index: --cacheinfo can\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3088,\n      \"title\": \"soph/attach-trailer-first\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3088\",\n      \"head\": \"5bd298f61fbe2dfa0b38786ba9b41309b115767c\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/attach-trailer-first\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back a trail. Feel free to edit the title or body, but keep the hidden marker below: Entire uses it to close this pull request when the trail closes.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes default attach behavior for pushed commits (history rewrite + force-push on feature branches) and git remote inspection; mistakes could surprise users or agents, though refusals and confirmations aim to limit damage.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **`entire session attach` now defaults to adding the `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer** instead of silently recording a SHA in checkpoint metadata when t\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3087,\n      \"title\": \"Offer to install entire-stream when `entire stream` is missing\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3087\",\n      \"head\": \"5e01552d2bba39da4d6885a2443ea1d2997f8c72\",\n      \"branch\": \"victor/install-stream\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Adds `stream` to `onDemandInstallPluginNames`, so `entire stream` without the plugin installed offers to install entire-stream from the plugin index — same as `graph`, `brain`, `investigate` and `rsl` (mirrors #3076).\\n\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/plugin.go`: add `stream` to the set and its rationale comment.\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/plugin_on_demand_test.go`: pin `stream` in `TestOffersOnDemandInstall_IsNarrow`.\\n- `docs/architecture/external-commands.md`: list `stream` in rule 5.\\n\\n**Depends on** entireio/plugin-index#6: the on-demand path resolves the name only through the plugin index, so until that lands `entire stream` reports \\\"not listed in the plugin index\\\" instead of offering the install. Note the inde\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3086,\n      \"title\": \"peyton/trail-show-readiness\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3086\",\n      \"head\": \"871682b51fe950a6efac321f03694f69c6d22621\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/trail-show-readiness\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\n`entire trail show` never said whether a change was a draft or ready for review. `entire trail ready` exists, but even it has to send you to the web page to confirm the result, because `trail show` can'\"'\"'t.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\n- **`trail show`:** for each change it reads gates for, a `Review:` line says `draft` or `ready for review`, above `Mergeable:`.\\n- **`trail show --json`:** each such change carries `readyForReview` (true or false).\\n- **No extra requests:** the value comes from the change record `trail show` already fetches for its gates.\\n- **Approvals gate only:** readiness is recorded only on changes with an approvals gate. Without one the stored value is always false and would read\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3084,\n      \"title\": \"peyton/trail-finding-visibility\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3084\",\n      \"head\": \"86ceb24a7c4d54b5d8651465aaeda1ebe6448e59\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/trail-finding-visib'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' '<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes how credential-store and auth resolution failures are classified and messaged; behavior is clearer for users but touches login, status, and token refresh paths on Linux/BSD keyring backends.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Linux/BSD OS keyring failures caused by a **missing or unreachable Secret Service** (D-Bus) are now classified as `ErrKeyringServiceMissing` instead of looking like a blank l\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3113,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): give a reserved checkpoint ID to one commit only\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3113\",\n      \"head\": \"7988c5736ff20d7c8a656205d689091b6afb03b1\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-shared-reservation-3069\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3069.\\n\\nStacked on #3068, which is stacked on #3034 and #3005. The fix needs #3068'\"'\"'s per-commit take: without it, the first commit'\"'\"'s post-commit takes every stamp, including the fresh one the next commit now gets, and that commit would keep a trailer for a checkpoint that is never written (#3030). So this branch is built on #3068'\"'\"'s head (e8250a77), and until those merge the diff here also shows their commits. This PR'\"'\"'s own changes are the seven commits on top of e8250a77. After them, main is merged in (ae1c9ec3) to clear a conflict in `docs/development/checkpoint-implementation.md`: #3108 rewrote the session-state bullet right next to the commit-linking bullet that #3034 and #3068 chan\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3112,\n      \"title\": \"redact: cap the expansions the placeholder rule reads\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3112\",\n      \"head\": \"7f5e03ea0718c0b3ac7d0ded17246a4f327a3edc\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-placeholder-nesting\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3111\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\n`isPlaceholderSecretValue` and `isPlaceholderShellExpansion` call each other once per level of a `${NAME:-word}` default whose word is another default, and each level reads the whole rest of the value again. A value nested n deep is read n times: `DB_PASSWORD=REDACTED nested 4000 deep takes about 3.7 s on main, and each doubling of the depth costs about 14x. The issue has the numbers for each shape.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\n- `maxPlaceholderExpansions = 8`. A value with more `${` than that is not read as a placeholder, so it redacts (fail closed). Each level of the recursion holds one more `${`, so the count bounds it: the rule reads at most eight levels of any value.\\n-\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3110,\n      \"title\": \"fix(hooks): identify a chained Trunk launcher without grep\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3110\",\n      \"head\": \"663435fac27f5068d696f5c3b4abd919df7d53c6\",\n      \"branch\": \"trunk-chain-no-grep\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Review after entireio/cli#3051 merges. Until then this PR also contains that PR'\"'\"'s commits. It now includes #3051'\"'\"'s current head (`b6335784`), so only these commits are new here:\\n\\n- `0177d8e9a` fix(hooks): identify a chained Trunk launcher without grep\\n- `43eb8416c` fix(hooks): bound the no-grep Trunk launcher scan\\n- `3be66e57f` Merge #3051'\"'\"'s head into trunk-chain-no-grep\\n- `b46370d3a` test(hooks): check the 64KiB scan cap instead of a 2s wall clock\\n- `807b2a206` test(hooks): share the Trunk chain test helpers\\n- `e32a8f2f5` fix(hooks): keep the user'\"'\"'s lines when upgrading a Trunk chain\\n- `1b84203c1` refactor(hooks): choose the installed hook'\"'\"'s content in one helper\\n- `2b158373b` fix(hooks): r\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3109,\n      \"title\": \"redact: read JSONL argv arrays as one command line\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3109\",\n      \"head\": \"e4213f1ea8c3c2815cbbce94e739cf159b5c9946\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-argv-command-passwords-up\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Please review this after #3048 merges. Until then, this pull request includes #3048'\"'\"'s commits as well; only these thirteen commits are new here, with merges of #3048'\"'\"'s newer commits between them:\\n\\n- `a01c5c43a` redact: read JSONL argv arrays as one command line\\n- `4dfb1f32b` redact: argv option values, line breaks, shared copies, object keys\\n- `6a801efc7` redact: argv line breaks, credential keys, escaped quotes, region sets\\n- `6b8423086` redact: read a netrc password quoted with an escaped apostrophe\\n- `f72e3481f` redact: keep argv password copies in skipped fields\\n- `0efca0d21` redact: hide self-detected argv tokens in keys and quote dashed netrc passwords\\n- `ed98bc035` redact: keep skippe\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3106,\n      \"title\": \"soph/explain-tests-isolate-settings\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3106\",\n      \"head\": \"6d6d2450155b43c1f753827db275d6d347e2b5d8\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/explain-tests-isolate-settings\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back a trail. Feel free to edit the title or body, but keep the hidden marker below: Entire uses it to close this pull request when the trail closes.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Test-only changes with no production behavior impact.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Makes **`explain`** flag-validation tests deterministic by running them against a **temporary git repo** with Entire **enabled**, instead of the developer'\"'\"'s checkout.\\n> \\n> Adds **`explainEnabledContext`**, which initializes a repo, writes `.entire/settings.json` with `enabled: true`, and attaches it via `settings.WithWor\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3104,\n      \"title\": \"fix(cli): provide actionable file-store hint when OS keyring is unavailable\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3104\",\n      \"head\": \"56ddb69ac46e74bba9d951a61b230ab3559bebf4\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/keyring-headless-error-hint\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Description\\nFixes #3058.\\n\\n### Problem\\nWhen running on headless Linux, Docker containers, CI, or minimal server environments without a running DBus Secret Service, commands that read or refresh credentials fail with cryptic messages such as:\\n```\\nresolve repo: refresh login token: load core token: read access token: The name org.freedesktop.secrets was not provided by any .service files\\n```\\nor:\\n```\\nread access token: Cannot autolaunch D-Bus without X11 $DISPLAY\\n```\\n\\nPreviously, only `entire login` included an actionable headless hint via `withHeadlessStoreHint`. Other subcommands (such as `entire repo remote add origin`, `entire status`, `entire checkpoint`, etc.) bubbled up the raw store e\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3103,\n      \"title\": \"perf(redact): apply JSONL replacements in a single linear pass\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3103\",\n      \"head\": \"3696d866c354b21ae0a46d3e8b2c7a21d57a8ed5\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/jsonl-redaction-single-pass\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Description\\nFixes #3081.\\n\\n### Problem\\nIn `applyJSONReplacements` (`redact/redact.go`), replacements were previously applied in an outer loop over each collected `jsonReplacement`, invoking `strings.Count` + `strings.ReplaceAll` for unkeyed replacements and `replaceKeyedJSONValue` (full line scan and copy) for keyed replacements.\\n\\nWhen a JSONL line contains $N$ distinct secrets (e.g. an environment dump, database connection strings, config files), this cost $O(N \\\\times \\\\text{line length})$, scaling quadratically in $N$. On 16,000 secrets, the splice alone took ~14.5 seconds.\\n\\n### Solution\\n1. **Single-Pass Linear Splice**:\\n   - Pre-encodes replacements into `keyedMap` (`(keyJSON, origJSON) \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3102,\n      \"title\": \"feat(execx,procutil): terminate process tree on Windows when context is cancelled\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3102\",\n      \"head\": \"4e71fdf3bed859c1042c90942ad6e4e6714dd76e\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/windows-process-tree-cancel\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Description\\nFixes #3052.\\n\\n### Background\\nOn Unix, `execx.TerminateOnCancel` and `procutil.TerminateOnCancel` configure a new process group (`Setpgid = true`) and send `SIGKILL` to `-cmd.Process.Pid` on cancellation to terminate the entire process group.\\nOn Windows, `killProcessGroupOnCancel` was previously a no-op stub:\\n```go\\nfunc killProcessGroupOnCancel(_ *exec.Cmd) {}\\n```\\nThis fell back to Go'\"'\"'s default `Cancel` behavior, which calls `TerminateProcess` on the direct child only. Because Windows does not automatically terminate child processes when a parent process exits, any descendants spawned by the child (such as `git-remote-https.exe`, `ssh.exe`, MCP servers, subagents, or clean filt\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3101,\n      \"title\": \"test(osroot): skip symlink traversal tests when symlinks cannot be created\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3101\",\n      \"head\": \"0d8b03be8d9c1416693890f537e6d1bf8d631d48\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/osroot-test-symlink-skip\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Description\\nFixes #3100.\\n\\nIn `cmd/entire/cli/osroot/osroot_test.go`, other tests that create symbolic links (lines 703 and 722) handle environments where symlink creation lacks privileges by checking:\\n```go\\nif err := os.Symlink(outside, filepath.Join(base, \\\"link\\\")); err != nil {\\n\\tt.Skipf(\\\"symlink not supported: %v\\\", err)\\n}\\n```\\n\\nHowever, `TestSymlinkTraversal_ReadBlocked` and `TestSymlinkTraversal_WriteBlocked` asserted `require.NoError(t, os.Symlink(...))` directly. On Windows without Developer Mode or elevation (`SeCreateSymbolicLinkPrivilege`), creating symlinks fails with `A required privilege is not held by the client`.\\n\\nThis PR skips the tests gracefully if `os.Symlink` returns an er\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3099,\n      \"title\": \"feat(osroot): add ForgetTree and release directory handles during test cleanup\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3099\",\n      \"head\": \"22cc7c2ce095f7cd4bb00321fe87a989cc884bb0\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/osroot-forget-tree\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Description\\nFixes #3098.\\n\\n`osroot.Shared` and `osroot.SharedChild` memoize open `*os.Root` directory handles in the global `sharedRoots` registry.\\nOn Windows (NTFS), open directory handles lock the directory and all of its parent directories from being deleted.\\n\\nWhen unit tests initialize temporary git repositories (via `testutil.InitRepo(t, dir)`) and exercise code paths that query `.entire` or `.git` via `osroot.Shared`, directory handles remain open in `sharedRoots`. When `t.TempDir()` cleanup subsequently executes `os.RemoveAll(tempDir)`, Windows fails with `ERROR_SHARING_VIOLATION`:\\n`unlinkat ... The process cannot access the file because it is being used by another process.`\\n\\nWhile \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3097,\n      \"title\": \"test(checkpoint): resolve repo root via runtime.Caller in open_test\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3097\",\n      \"head\": \"5be869459bae5e8fe83d342baaa1e3fded904fc5\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/checkpoint-open-test-root-discovery\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Description\\nFixes #3096.\\n\\nIn `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/open_test.go`, `TestOpenOptionsLiteralsDeclareReadRemotes` walks the repo'\"'\"'s `cmd/` tree to verify AST literals.\\nTo locate the repository root, it previously called:\\n`root, err := filepath.Abs(filepath.Join(\\\"..\\\", \\\"..\\\", \\\"..\\\", \\\"..\\\"))`\\n\\nThis relies on the test execution working directory being `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint`. If tests are run from the repo root (or via test runners / precompiled test binaries where `cwd` is not the package dir), relative path traversal resolves above the workspace rather than at the repository root, failing with:\\n`walk root D:\\\\ does not look like the repo root: GetFileAttributesEx D:\\\\cmd\\\\entire: The system c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3095,\n      \"title\": \"test(checkpoint): skip TestCopyMetadataDir_RefusesSymlinks when symlinks cannot be created\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3095\",\n      \"head\": \"440f3bda45156d00cc022cc31600e45585eb70ab\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/checkpoint-test-symlink-skip\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Description\\nFixes #3094.\\n\\nOn Windows, creating symbolic links requires elevated privileges (`SeCreateSymbolicLinkPrivilege`) or Developer Mode enabled.\\nWhile other tests across the repository use `testutil.SkipWithoutSymlinks(t)` to gracefully skip tests when running unprivileged on Windows, `TestCopyMetadataDir_RefusesSymlinks` directly called `os.Symlink` without this check, resulting in test failure when run in unprivileged environments.\\n\\nThis PR adds `testutil.SkipWithoutSymlinks(t)` at the beginning of `TestCopyMetadataDir_RefusesSymlinks`.\\n\\n## Before and After Test Results\\n\\n### Before\\n```\\n=== RUN   TestCopyMetadataDir_RefusesSymlinks\\n    checkpoint_test.go:69: failed to create symli\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3093,\n      \"title\": \"test(checkpoint): isolate USERPROFILE in git config author tests\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3093\",\n      \"head\": \"f38963101dddf140882f96005ae9a1cd6efb5239\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/checkpoint-test-userprofile-isolation\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Description\\nFixes #3092.\\n\\nIn `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/persistent_update_test.go`, several tests (`TestUpdateCommitted_UsesCorrectAuthor`, `TestGetGitAuthorFromRepo_GlobalFallback`, and `TestGetGitAuthorFromRepo_NoConfig`) attempt to isolate global git config resolution by setting `HOME` to a temporary directory.\\n\\nOn Windows, Go'\"'\"'s `os.UserHomeDir()` (called by `go-git`'\"'\"'s global config loader) prioritizes `%USERPROFILE%` over `%HOME%`. Because `USERPROFILE` was not overridden, `go-git` continued to load the host developer'\"'\"'s global `~/.gitconfig`, causing these tests to fail on Windows whenever a global git config exists on the host machine.\\n\\n### Fix\\n1. Updated `pointHomeAt(t, home)` in `c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3091,\n      \"title\": \"test(settings): disable core.protectNTFS when staging trailing char variants\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3091\",\n      \"head\": \"1f224935f211c8066a10ebe11a07df7c5cc93835\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/settings-protectntfs-test\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Description\\nFixes #3090.\\n\\nIn `cmd/entire/cli/settings/opf_command_trust_test.go`, `TestPathIsVersioned_Win32TrailingCharVariantsAreTracked` tests that trailing-space and trailing-dot path variants (such as `.entire/settings.local.json.` and `.entire/settings.local.json `) staged into the index are properly recognized as versioned and untrusted.\\n\\nTo stage these paths directly into the index, `stageBlobAt` invokes:\\n`git update-index --add --cacheinfo 100644,<hash>,<repoPath>`\\n\\nOn Windows (where `core.protectNTFS` is typically true by default in Git for Windows), git forbids indexing paths containing trailing spaces or trailing periods, resulting in:\\n`fatal: git update-index: --cacheinfo can\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3088,\n      \"title\": \"soph/attach-trailer-first\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3088\",\n      \"head\": \"5bd298f61fbe2dfa0b38786ba9b41309b115767c\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/attach-trailer-first\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back a trail. Feel free to edit the title or body, but keep the hidden marker below: Entire uses it to close this pull request when the trail closes.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes default attach behavior for pushed commits (history rewrite + force-push on feature branches) and git remote inspection; mistakes could surprise users or agents, though refusals and confirmations aim to limit damage.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **`entire session attach` now defaults to adding the `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer** instead of silently recording a SHA in checkpoint metadata when t\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3087,\n      \"title\": \"Offer to install entire-stream when `entire stream` is missing\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3087\",\n      \"head\": \"5e01552d2bba39da4d6885a2443ea1d2997f8c72\",\n      \"branch\": \"victor/install-stream\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Adds `stream` to `onDemandInstallPluginNames`, so `entire stream` without the plugin installed offers to install entire-stream from the plugin index — same as `graph`, `brain`, `investigate` and `rsl` (mirrors #3076).\\n\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/plugin.go`: add `stream` to the set and its rationale comment.\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/plugin_on_demand_test.go`: pin `stream` in `TestOffersOnDemandInstall_IsNarrow`.\\n- `docs/architecture/external-commands.md`: list `stream` in rule 5.\\n\\n**Depends on** entireio/plugin-index#6: the on-demand path resolves the name only through the plugin index, so until that lands `entire stream` reports \\\"not listed in the plugin index\\\" instead of offering the install. Note the inde\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3086,\n      \"title\": \"peyton/trail-show-readiness\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3086\",\n      \"head\": \"871682b51fe950a6efac321f03694f69c6d22621\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/trail-show-readiness\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\n`entire trail show` never said whether a change was a draft or ready for review. `entire trail ready` exists, but even it has to send you to the web page to confirm the result, because `trail show` can'\"'\"'t.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\n- **`trail show`:** for each change it reads gates for, a `Review:` line says `draft` or `ready for review`, above `Mergeable:`.\\n- **`trail show --json`:** each such change carries `readyForReview` (true or false).\\n- **No extra requests:** the value comes from the change record `trail show` already fetches for its gates.\\n- **Approvals gate only:** readiness is recorded only on changes with an approvals gate. Without one the stored value is always false and would read\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3084,\n      \"title\": \"peyton/trail-finding-visibility\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3084\",\n      \"head\": \"86ceb24a7c4d54b5d8651465aaeda1ebe6448e59\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/trail-finding-visib'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":11416}},"started_at_ms":1794842127789,"completed_at_ms":1794842127790}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:27.988Z","ordinal":3012,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-6f264744-f8b1-43cd-9764-c81aa09e4005","process_id":"10975","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' 'ility\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\n`entire trail finding` showed only current findings. A stale open finding (its code changed after it was raised) was counted in the header but never listed, so the plain output agents read said:\\n\\n```\\n  Open findings: 1  high 0  medium 1  low 0\\nNo findings match the current filters.\\n```\\n\\nInteractive terminals got a hint; plain output and `finding list` got none.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\n- **Dashboard:** the main table is unchanged (current findings; paging unaffected). Below it, a **Stale open findings** section lists stale open findings from the data the dashboard already loads, noting they don'\"'\"'t block the merge gate. Both the plain and terminal views show it.\\n- **Header:** `Open findings: 1 \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3082,\n      \"title\": \"Write the checkpoint a stamped agent commit names when its transcript is unreadable\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3082\",\n      \"head\": \"49d2dcd3564c3fba1bbffe903267a60136ca7e24\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/condense-unreadable-transcript\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\nWhen an agent'\"'\"'s transcript can never be read, every commit the agent makes gets an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer, but no checkpoint is ever written for it. In #3059, 53 commits ended up this way: the OpenCode binary wasn'\"'\"'t on the hook'\"'\"'s PATH (OpenCode running as a service), so every transcript export failed. `entire checkpoint explain` then reports `checkpoint not found`, and `entire session attach` refuses those commits.\\n\\nThe agent-commit fast path in `prepare-commit-msg` stamps the trailer. Post-commit condensation then drops the session at one of three checks:\\n1. **Reading the transcript:** an empty transcript is treated as a transient race and returns an error, unless the sessi\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3080,\n      \"title\": \"strategy: keep an ended session ended when condensing it by ID\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3080\",\n      \"head\": \"d37527b2db0f439903afd2c3ce42703a21708db4\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/sweep-keeps-ended-sessions-ended\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3079.\\n\\nAn ended session that `entire doctor --force` or the background sweep condensed became idle with its end time still set. Commits then kept rereading its transcript, and resuming it left a live session that `entire session list` showed as ended.\\n\\nWhen `CondenseSessionByID` writes a checkpoint for an ended session, it now leaves the session ended and marks it fully condensed, the state session-end condensation already leaves. A session in any other phase still becomes idle without the flag, since nothing clears the flag when an idle session'\"'\"'s next turn starts. The phase is read under the session lock, so a session resumed between the sweep'\"'\"'s check and the condense has left `ended\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3078,\n      \"title\": \"redact: read values joined from quoted pieces as one shell word\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3078\",\n      \"head\": \"47b57f02a15ec2e56770fdd413b3146114af32f8\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-positional-default-redaction\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3077\\n\\nThis is the joined-word part of #3077, reworked after @MuskanPaliwal'\"'\"'s review. The positional and single-quoted default fixes moved to #3137, as she asked, and this branch is built on it. Until #3137 merges, this diff includes it too. Values that start inside another value'\"'\"'s word and run past it are left for #3138.\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\nThe key/value patterns stop at the first closing quote, or, for a bare value, at a blank inside a later quoted string. The shell joins quoted strings and bare text with nothing between them into one word:\\n\\n- `DB_PASSWORD=REDACTED is the literal `$X`, but it'\"'\"'s judged by its empty first string.\\n- `DB_PASSWORD=REDACTED and `DB_PASSWORD=REDACTED leave\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3073,\n      \"title\": \"fix(hooks): refresh a stale moved copy of Entire'\"'\"'s hook on the next turn\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3073\",\n      \"head\": \"408f49e4be66caf40bb373ec03460008924a5c6a\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-moved-hook-state-3050\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3050.\\n\\n@Soph, this is the per-turn side of your `refreshMovedEntireHooks` and `reclaimFromWrappers`. Codex found it while reviewing #3046, and it is on main, so it gets its own PR off main.\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\n`hookStateIn` reads only the file at the hook'\"'\"'s name. Copies of Entire'\"'\"'s hook that another hook manager moved aside (`<hook>.<suffix>`, such as `pre-push.old`) are rewritten only during an install, and `EnsureSetup` skips the install while the hooks read Current. So a stale moved copy stays until someone runs `entire enable`.\\n\\nThe copy that matters is one from before the chain guard (`ENTIRE_CHAINING_<HOOK>`). An earlier release could leave this layout:\\n\\n```\\npre-push               Enti\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3071,\n      \"title\": \"feat(proclive): track agent process liveness on Windows\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3071\",\n      \"head\": \"2b1b55d09da43a388de356d6509b4b70c0a6d393\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-windows-proclive-3053\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3053: `proclive` has no Windows implementation, so no Windows session records an owner.\\n\\n## What changes on Windows\\n\\n`proclive` returned \\\"unsupported\\\" on Windows (#1488 left it out of scope). So until now:\\n\\n- **Liveness** of a mid-turn session was always unknown. `entire status`, `entire doctor`, attach and the exited-owner sweep fell back to `IsStuckActive`, which counts a turn over an hour as stuck even while its agent still runs.\\n- **Commit provenance** never marked a session foreign. With no TTY, `prepare-commit-msg`'\"'\"'s fast path stamped any mid-turn session, so a script'\"'\"'s commit during another session'\"'\"'s turn went to that session.\\n\\nWith this PR, a Windows session records its agent'\"'\"'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3070,\n      \"title\": \"fix(execx): kill the whole process tree when a command is cancelled on Windows\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3070\",\n      \"head\": \"437e36feff38b45846e186bc41a83032ce9e99f2\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-windows-tree-kill-3052\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3052: on Windows, cancelling a subprocess at its deadline killed only the direct child, so its children kept running.\\n\\n## What happened\\n\\nOn Unix, `execx.TerminateOnCancel` and `procutil.TerminateOnCancel` start the command in its own process group and kill the whole group when the context is cancelled. On Windows both were no-ops, so cancellation fell back to `exec.Cmd`'\"'\"'s default `Cancel`, which terminates the direct child only. Windows doesn'\"'\"'t kill a process'\"'\"'s children when it dies. A child that inherited stdout (`git-remote-https` behind `git`, a sandbox helper or MCP server behind an agent CLI) kept running, and `Wait` blocked until `WaitDelay` force-closed the pipe: 10 s late in e\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3068,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): lock the commit stamp records and keep later commits'\"'\"' stamps\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3068\",\n      \"head\": \"62a06a0dc28000b9a7953e6a764365953d19c4ad\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-stamp-record-lock-3030\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3030.\\n\\nStacked on #3034, which is stacked on #3005. #3005 adds the sessions record this lock also covers, and #3034 changes the same functions, so this branch is built on #3034'\"'\"'s head (now 5ff58dc5, which merges main ce16562b and #3005'\"'\"'s amend fix). Until both merge, the diff here also shows their commits. This PR'\"'\"'s own change is the commits from 4206adaf to e8250a77, 1a8adbe9 and a73bfe46; 9e683b95, 5e5483de and 62a06a0d merge #3034'\"'\"'s head into it. I'\"'\"'ll merge main in as they land.\\n\\n@peyton-alt, this is the lock I asked about on #3005. I went ahead rather than wait, so it'\"'\"'s here to look at whenever you have time.\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\nprepare-commit-msg leaves three records for post-commit in \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3066,\n      \"title\": \"redact: redact Italian, Spanish, French and German street lines\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3066\",\n      \"head\": \"728b6b3228ce3402d7e1d6d068d00add9a03ffb8\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-eu-address-redaction-2977\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2977\\n\\n@rennf93 offered on the issue to write this once a maintainer said whether you want it. No maintainer has answered since Oct 29, and I had it ready on my fork, so here it is to look at. If you'\"'\"'d rather @rennf93 take it, or don'\"'\"'t want European addresses in `pii.address`, say so and I'\"'\"'ll close this. cc @MuskanPaliwal\\n\\nI reviewed this on my fork first (Beehtrix/cli#16).\\n\\n## What was wrong\\n\\n`pii.address` only matched the US shape: a number, capitalized words, then a suffix such as `St` or `Ave` (`addressRegex` in `redact/pii.go`). European street lines put the type first or the number after the name, so with the category on, none of these were redacted:\\n\\n```\\nVia Roma 12, 20121 Milan\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3065,\n      \"title\": \"redact: redact international phone numbers in pii.phone\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3065\",\n      \"head\": \"7e8bb994a88c0433be9fca05b1db0b787c9a35e8\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-intl-phone-redaction-2976\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2976\\n\\n@rennf93 proposed this on the issue and planned to send it once a maintainer agreed. No maintainer has replied since Oct 29, so I'\"'\"'m opening it to give you something concrete to look at. It follows the issue'\"'\"'s design, a fourth E.164 branch with their per-country test table. If you'\"'\"'d rather @rennf93 send their own PR, say so and I'\"'\"'ll close this one. cc @MuskanPaliwal\\n\\nI reviewed this on my fork first (Beehtrix/cli#17).\\n\\n## What was wrong\\n\\nWith `pii.phone` on, `phoneRegex` in `redact/pii.go` only matches North American numbers, so a number in international format outside `+1` stayed in the transcript:\\n\\n```\\n+44 20 7946 0958       unchanged\\n+54 9 11 0000-0001     unchanged\\n+39 347 00\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3060,\n      \"title\": \"fix(opencode): find opencode in its install directory off PATH\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3060\",\n      \"head\": \"ec56f770f5bc0834935f3b011dad60ed8842b188\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/opencode-binary-off-path\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3059\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n**Problem:** OpenCode'\"'\"'s installer adds `~/.opencode/bin` to PATH only in `~/.zshrc` or `~/.bashrc`. When OpenCode runs outside an interactive shell (OpenCode Desktop, a systemd or launchd service), Entire'\"'\"'s hooks can'\"'\"'t find `opencode`. Every commit then gets a checkpoint with no transcript, and nothing reports it.\\n\\n**Fix:** if `opencode` is not on PATH, use `~/.opencode/bin/opencode`.\\n\\n**As-is**\\n\\n```mermaid\\nflowchart TD\\n  A[\\\"OpenCode not started from a shell\\\"] --> B[\\\"entire hook runs '\"'\"'opencode'\"'\"'\\\"]\\n  B -- \\\"not on PATH\\\" --> C[\\\"checkpoint saved without transcript<br/>(no warning)\\\"]\\n```\\n\\n**To-be**\\n\\n```mermaid\\nflowchart TD\\n  A[\\\"OpenCode not started from a shell\\\"] --> B[\\\"en\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3057,\n      \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): remove the partial pack a failed checkpoint fetch leaves\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3057\",\n      \"head\": \"ff7bb05e9c1391536c989991d5d808eac956e0df\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-tmp-pack-cleanup-2895\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2895: a `tmp_pack_*` of about 115 MB left in `.git/objects/pack` after every commit.\\n\\n## What happens\\n\\nWhen a fetch'\"'\"'s receive dies partway through the pack, git leaves behind the files index-pack was writing in `objects/pack`:\\n\\n- `tmp_pack_XXXXXX`: read-only (0444), and as large as what it had received.\\n- `tmp_idx_` and `tmp_rev_`: present once the pack itself is in.\\n\\nThat covers an early EOF from the remote and a fetch killed at its deadline (Entire'\"'\"'s `TerminateOnCancel` SIGKILLs the whole process group, and index-pack is in it). Git removes none of these files. Entire'\"'\"'s fetches pass `--no-auto-gc`, so nothing else removes them either until someone runs a manual gc after git'\"'\"'s two-we\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3056,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): spell agent-reported paths as git does on case-insensitive filesystems\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3056\",\n      \"head\": \"a47eb10afce65b1fe88d854215ab65b237e92299\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-transcript-path-case-3054\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3054\\n\\nOn a case-insensitive filesystem (the macOS and Windows default) an agent can name a tracked file in another case than git does: writing `readme.md` changes `README.md`. Entire recorded the agent'\"'\"'s spelling, which never matches a commit, so the session stayed pending after the file was committed. The issue has the two ways it happens (dirty at turn end, committed mid-turn).\\n\\nI reviewed this on my fork first (Beehtrix/cli#22).\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\n`strategy.FilterTrackableChanges`, which every capture route already applies (turn end, task completion, per-tool hooks, Codex child files, and the transcript fallback of a mid-turn commit), now first spells each path as git'\"'\"'s index does (`stra\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3055,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): stop sessions in a shared checkout from claiming each other'\"'\"'s files\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3055\",\n      \"head\": \"00f378cebe11d7676c7571f869590b023456de90\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-shared-checkout-attribution-3011\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3011\\n\\n@mattjes reported this and handed it over on the issue. This covers both directions from the issue: the prompt-start baseline (direction 1), and the overlapping-turns case (direction 2), which @mattjes said is the one they run into.\\n\\nI reviewed this on my fork first (Beehtrix/cli#19).\\n\\n## What was wrong\\n\\nAt turn end, `handleLifecycleTurnEnd` merged every file `git status` lists into the turn'\"'\"'s files: `changes.Modified`, plus `New` and `Deleted`. git status shows every dirty file in the worktree, not which session changed it, so in a shared checkout a session took:\\n\\n- tracked files that were already dirty when its prompt started (untracked files had a baseline, tracked files didn\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3051,\n      \"title\": \"fix(hooks): run a chained Trunk launcher under its own hook name\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3051\",\n      \"head\": \"b63357841f702644474a6d2b743f2c702b02d6c4\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-trunk-hook-name-2673\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2673.\\n\\nI asked on the issue whether this approach is OK and haven'\"'\"'t heard back yet, so I'\"'\"'m opening it to let the approach be judged on the code. Happy to rework it if you'\"'\"'d prefer another way. cc @MuskanPaliwal, since you'\"'\"'ve done most of the hook-chaining work.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nEntire moves a hook it replaces to `<hook>.pre-entire` and executes it from there. Trunk'\"'\"'s git-hook launcher, the one script `trunk git-hooks sync` writes for every hook, passes its own file name to `trunk git-hooks callback`. Under the renamed path Trunk refuses the callback (`Unknown git-hooks callback '\"'\"'pre-push.pre-entire'\"'\"'`) and exits 2, so git aborts every commit and push in a repo whose hooks Trunk manages.\\n\\n#\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3048,\n      \"title\": \"redact: redact passwords passed on the command line\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3048\",\n      \"head\": \"528ddf9a05ac20b17c94df4e0496dbc656e7838e\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-command-line-passwords-2898\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2898.\\n\\nBuilt on @DilpreetBansi'\"'\"'s branch from the issue. Their commit comes first, unchanged and with their authorship. The eighty-five commits on top come from my review of it, from @MuskanPaliwal'\"'\"'s review and from the automated reviews here, with one merge of `main`. Each commit message says what it fixes and which test covers it, so this description only gives the result.\\n\\n## What it covers\\n\\nA password given to a client on its command line is usually human-chosen (`hunter2`, `Summer2026!`). That is far below the entropy threshold, and no pattern layer matched it, so it reached the checkpoint as typed. This adds a command-line layer inside the connection-string layer (counted as `con\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3046,\n      \"title\": \"fix(hooks): keep the user'\"'\"'s pre-push hook in entire-brain'\"'\"'s chain on re-wrap\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3046\",\n      \"head\": \"84bca441f543a7e1425a5536968724a8e626bfc3\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-rewrap-brain-chain-2960-up\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"**Review after #3003, which builds on #2959.** A fork PR can'\"'\"'t target another PR'\"'\"'s branch, so this diff also carries those two commits (`edb1ccba` from #2959 and `d18031fc` from #3003). Only the last three commits, `cfaa8fef`, `31d2e568` and `a378498e`, are new here. The branch merges cleanly with main.\\n\\nFixes #2960.\\n\\nI asked on #2960 on Oct 29 whether this approach works for you and haven'\"'\"'t heard back, so this PR is there to make the proposal concrete. I'\"'\"'m happy to change direction.\\n\\n## The bug (the case left after #2959)\\n\\nAfter `entire enable` backs up the user'\"'\"'s pre-push hook and entire-brain connects, the chain is:\\n\\n```\\npre-push                    Brain'\"'\"'s wrapper   -> exec \\\"$0.pre-entire\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3045,\n      \"title\": \"codex: offer to install hooks where Codex reads them in linked worktrees\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3045\",\n      \"head\": \"b1aba8dabbd46fdf429cdfd68392cfb8975dc5b4\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/codex-linked-worktree-hooks\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\nIn a linked worktree, `entire enable --agent codex` (and `entire agent add codex`) writes `<worktree>/.codex/hooks.json`, but Codex loads the **primary checkout'\"'\"'s** `.codex/hooks.json` (the `.bare` layout root for `.bare` worktrees; pinned by the `codex app-server` `hooks/list` tests). With no hooks file there, Codex runs no Entire hooks and nothing is captured. `enable` warned (\\\"Hooks in the current-worktree file will not run here\\\") and `entire status` showed \\\"Codex hooks are not active in this worktree\\\", but nothing fixed it, so people wh'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' 'ility\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\n`entire trail finding` showed only current findings. A stale open finding (its code changed after it was raised) was counted in the header but never listed, so the plain output agents read said:\\n\\n```\\n  Open findings: 1  high 0  medium 1  low 0\\nNo findings match the current filters.\\n```\\n\\nInteractive terminals got a hint; plain output and `finding list` got none.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\n- **Dashboard:** the main table is unchanged (current findings; paging unaffected). Below it, a **Stale open findings** section lists stale open findings from the data the dashboard already loads, noting they don'\"'\"'t block the merge gate. Both the plain and terminal views show it.\\n- **Header:** `Open findings: 1 \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3082,\n      \"title\": \"Write the checkpoint a stamped agent commit names when its transcript is unreadable\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3082\",\n      \"head\": \"49d2dcd3564c3fba1bbffe903267a60136ca7e24\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/condense-unreadable-transcript\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\nWhen an agent'\"'\"'s transcript can never be read, every commit the agent makes gets an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer, but no checkpoint is ever written for it. In #3059, 53 commits ended up this way: the OpenCode binary wasn'\"'\"'t on the hook'\"'\"'s PATH (OpenCode running as a service), so every transcript export failed. `entire checkpoint explain` then reports `checkpoint not found`, and `entire session attach` refuses those commits.\\n\\nThe agent-commit fast path in `prepare-commit-msg` stamps the trailer. Post-commit condensation then drops the session at one of three checks:\\n1. **Reading the transcript:** an empty transcript is treated as a transient race and returns an error, unless the sessi\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3080,\n      \"title\": \"strategy: keep an ended session ended when condensing it by ID\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3080\",\n      \"head\": \"d37527b2db0f439903afd2c3ce42703a21708db4\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/sweep-keeps-ended-sessions-ended\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3079.\\n\\nAn ended session that `entire doctor --force` or the background sweep condensed became idle with its end time still set. Commits then kept rereading its transcript, and resuming it left a live session that `entire session list` showed as ended.\\n\\nWhen `CondenseSessionByID` writes a checkpoint for an ended session, it now leaves the session ended and marks it fully condensed, the state session-end condensation already leaves. A session in any other phase still becomes idle without the flag, since nothing clears the flag when an idle session'\"'\"'s next turn starts. The phase is read under the session lock, so a session resumed between the sweep'\"'\"'s check and the condense has left `ended\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3078,\n      \"title\": \"redact: read values joined from quoted pieces as one shell word\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3078\",\n      \"head\": \"47b57f02a15ec2e56770fdd413b3146114af32f8\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-positional-default-redaction\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3077\\n\\nThis is the joined-word part of #3077, reworked after @MuskanPaliwal'\"'\"'s review. The positional and single-quoted default fixes moved to #3137, as she asked, and this branch is built on it. Until #3137 merges, this diff includes it too. Values that start inside another value'\"'\"'s word and run past it are left for #3138.\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\nThe key/value patterns stop at the first closing quote, or, for a bare value, at a blank inside a later quoted string. The shell joins quoted strings and bare text with nothing between them into one word:\\n\\n- `DB_PASSWORD=REDACTED is the literal `$X`, but it'\"'\"'s judged by its empty first string.\\n- `DB_PASSWORD=REDACTED and `DB_PASSWORD=REDACTED leave\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3073,\n      \"title\": \"fix(hooks): refresh a stale moved copy of Entire'\"'\"'s hook on the next turn\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3073\",\n      \"head\": \"408f49e4be66caf40bb373ec03460008924a5c6a\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-moved-hook-state-3050\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3050.\\n\\n@Soph, this is the per-turn side of your `refreshMovedEntireHooks` and `reclaimFromWrappers`. Codex found it while reviewing #3046, and it is on main, so it gets its own PR off main.\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\n`hookStateIn` reads only the file at the hook'\"'\"'s name. Copies of Entire'\"'\"'s hook that another hook manager moved aside (`<hook>.<suffix>`, such as `pre-push.old`) are rewritten only during an install, and `EnsureSetup` skips the install while the hooks read Current. So a stale moved copy stays until someone runs `entire enable`.\\n\\nThe copy that matters is one from before the chain guard (`ENTIRE_CHAINING_<HOOK>`). An earlier release could leave this layout:\\n\\n```\\npre-push               Enti\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3071,\n      \"title\": \"feat(proclive): track agent process liveness on Windows\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3071\",\n      \"head\": \"2b1b55d09da43a388de356d6509b4b70c0a6d393\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-windows-proclive-3053\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3053: `proclive` has no Windows implementation, so no Windows session records an owner.\\n\\n## What changes on Windows\\n\\n`proclive` returned \\\"unsupported\\\" on Windows (#1488 left it out of scope). So until now:\\n\\n- **Liveness** of a mid-turn session was always unknown. `entire status`, `entire doctor`, attach and the exited-owner sweep fell back to `IsStuckActive`, which counts a turn over an hour as stuck even while its agent still runs.\\n- **Commit provenance** never marked a session foreign. With no TTY, `prepare-commit-msg`'\"'\"'s fast path stamped any mid-turn session, so a script'\"'\"'s commit during another session'\"'\"'s turn went to that session.\\n\\nWith this PR, a Windows session records its agent'\"'\"'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3070,\n      \"title\": \"fix(execx): kill the whole process tree when a command is cancelled on Windows\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3070\",\n      \"head\": \"437e36feff38b45846e186bc41a83032ce9e99f2\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-windows-tree-kill-3052\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3052: on Windows, cancelling a subprocess at its deadline killed only the direct child, so its children kept running.\\n\\n## What happened\\n\\nOn Unix, `execx.TerminateOnCancel` and `procutil.TerminateOnCancel` start the command in its own process group and kill the whole group when the context is cancelled. On Windows both were no-ops, so cancellation fell back to `exec.Cmd`'\"'\"'s default `Cancel`, which terminates the direct child only. Windows doesn'\"'\"'t kill a process'\"'\"'s children when it dies. A child that inherited stdout (`git-remote-https` behind `git`, a sandbox helper or MCP server behind an agent CLI) kept running, and `Wait` blocked until `WaitDelay` force-closed the pipe: 10 s late in e\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3068,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): lock the commit stamp records and keep later commits'\"'\"' stamps\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3068\",\n      \"head\": \"62a06a0dc28000b9a7953e6a764365953d19c4ad\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-stamp-record-lock-3030\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3030.\\n\\nStacked on #3034, which is stacked on #3005. #3005 adds the sessions record this lock also covers, and #3034 changes the same functions, so this branch is built on #3034'\"'\"'s head (now 5ff58dc5, which merges main ce16562b and #3005'\"'\"'s amend fix). Until both merge, the diff here also shows their commits. This PR'\"'\"'s own change is the commits from 4206adaf to e8250a77, 1a8adbe9 and a73bfe46; 9e683b95, 5e5483de and 62a06a0d merge #3034'\"'\"'s head into it. I'\"'\"'ll merge main in as they land.\\n\\n@peyton-alt, this is the lock I asked about on #3005. I went ahead rather than wait, so it'\"'\"'s here to look at whenever you have time.\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\nprepare-commit-msg leaves three records for post-commit in \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3066,\n      \"title\": \"redact: redact Italian, Spanish, French and German street lines\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3066\",\n      \"head\": \"728b6b3228ce3402d7e1d6d068d00add9a03ffb8\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-eu-address-redaction-2977\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2977\\n\\n@rennf93 offered on the issue to write this once a maintainer said whether you want it. No maintainer has answered since Oct 29, and I had it ready on my fork, so here it is to look at. If you'\"'\"'d rather @rennf93 take it, or don'\"'\"'t want European addresses in `pii.address`, say so and I'\"'\"'ll close this. cc @MuskanPaliwal\\n\\nI reviewed this on my fork first (Beehtrix/cli#16).\\n\\n## What was wrong\\n\\n`pii.address` only matched the US shape: a number, capitalized words, then a suffix such as `St` or `Ave` (`addressRegex` in `redact/pii.go`). European street lines put the type first or the number after the name, so with the category on, none of these were redacted:\\n\\n```\\nVia Roma 12, 20121 Milan\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3065,\n      \"title\": \"redact: redact international phone numbers in pii.phone\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3065\",\n      \"head\": \"7e8bb994a88c0433be9fca05b1db0b787c9a35e8\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-intl-phone-redaction-2976\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2976\\n\\n@rennf93 proposed this on the issue and planned to send it once a maintainer agreed. No maintainer has replied since Oct 29, so I'\"'\"'m opening it to give you something concrete to look at. It follows the issue'\"'\"'s design, a fourth E.164 branch with their per-country test table. If you'\"'\"'d rather @rennf93 send their own PR, say so and I'\"'\"'ll close this one. cc @MuskanPaliwal\\n\\nI reviewed this on my fork first (Beehtrix/cli#17).\\n\\n## What was wrong\\n\\nWith `pii.phone` on, `phoneRegex` in `redact/pii.go` only matches North American numbers, so a number in international format outside `+1` stayed in the transcript:\\n\\n```\\n+44 20 7946 0958       unchanged\\n+54 9 11 0000-0001     unchanged\\n+39 347 00\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3060,\n      \"title\": \"fix(opencode): find opencode in its install directory off PATH\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3060\",\n      \"head\": \"ec56f770f5bc0834935f3b011dad60ed8842b188\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/opencode-binary-off-path\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3059\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n**Problem:** OpenCode'\"'\"'s installer adds `~/.opencode/bin` to PATH only in `~/.zshrc` or `~/.bashrc`. When OpenCode runs outside an interactive shell (OpenCode Desktop, a systemd or launchd service), Entire'\"'\"'s hooks can'\"'\"'t find `opencode`. Every commit then gets a checkpoint with no transcript, and nothing reports it.\\n\\n**Fix:** if `opencode` is not on PATH, use `~/.opencode/bin/opencode`.\\n\\n**As-is**\\n\\n```mermaid\\nflowchart TD\\n  A[\\\"OpenCode not started from a shell\\\"] --> B[\\\"entire hook runs '\"'\"'opencode'\"'\"'\\\"]\\n  B -- \\\"not on PATH\\\" --> C[\\\"checkpoint saved without transcript<br/>(no warning)\\\"]\\n```\\n\\n**To-be**\\n\\n```mermaid\\nflowchart TD\\n  A[\\\"OpenCode not started from a shell\\\"] --> B[\\\"en\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3057,\n      \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): remove the partial pack a failed checkpoint fetch leaves\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3057\",\n      \"head\": \"ff7bb05e9c1391536c989991d5d808eac956e0df\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-tmp-pack-cleanup-2895\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2895: a `tmp_pack_*` of about 115 MB left in `.git/objects/pack` after every commit.\\n\\n## What happens\\n\\nWhen a fetch'\"'\"'s receive dies partway through the pack, git leaves behind the files index-pack was writing in `objects/pack`:\\n\\n- `tmp_pack_XXXXXX`: read-only (0444), and as large as what it had received.\\n- `tmp_idx_` and `tmp_rev_`: present once the pack itself is in.\\n\\nThat covers an early EOF from the remote and a fetch killed at its deadline (Entire'\"'\"'s `TerminateOnCancel` SIGKILLs the whole process group, and index-pack is in it). Git removes none of these files. Entire'\"'\"'s fetches pass `--no-auto-gc`, so nothing else removes them either until someone runs a manual gc after git'\"'\"'s two-we\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3056,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): spell agent-reported paths as git does on case-insensitive filesystems\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3056\",\n      \"head\": \"a47eb10afce65b1fe88d854215ab65b237e92299\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-transcript-path-case-3054\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3054\\n\\nOn a case-insensitive filesystem (the macOS and Windows default) an agent can name a tracked file in another case than git does: writing `readme.md` changes `README.md`. Entire recorded the agent'\"'\"'s spelling, which never matches a commit, so the session stayed pending after the file was committed. The issue has the two ways it happens (dirty at turn end, committed mid-turn).\\n\\nI reviewed this on my fork first (Beehtrix/cli#22).\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\n`strategy.FilterTrackableChanges`, which every capture route already applies (turn end, task completion, per-tool hooks, Codex child files, and the transcript fallback of a mid-turn commit), now first spells each path as git'\"'\"'s index does (`stra\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3055,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): stop sessions in a shared checkout from claiming each other'\"'\"'s files\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3055\",\n      \"head\": \"00f378cebe11d7676c7571f869590b023456de90\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-shared-checkout-attribution-3011\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3011\\n\\n@mattjes reported this and handed it over on the issue. This covers both directions from the issue: the prompt-start baseline (direction 1), and the overlapping-turns case (direction 2), which @mattjes said is the one they run into.\\n\\nI reviewed this on my fork first (Beehtrix/cli#19).\\n\\n## What was wrong\\n\\nAt turn end, `handleLifecycleTurnEnd` merged every file `git status` lists into the turn'\"'\"'s files: `changes.Modified`, plus `New` and `Deleted`. git status shows every dirty file in the worktree, not which session changed it, so in a shared checkout a session took:\\n\\n- tracked files that were already dirty when its prompt started (untracked files had a baseline, tracked files didn\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3051,\n      \"title\": \"fix(hooks): run a chained Trunk launcher under its own hook name\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3051\",\n      \"head\": \"b63357841f702644474a6d2b743f2c702b02d6c4\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-trunk-hook-name-2673\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2673.\\n\\nI asked on the issue whether this approach is OK and haven'\"'\"'t heard back yet, so I'\"'\"'m opening it to let the approach be judged on the code. Happy to rework it if you'\"'\"'d prefer another way. cc @MuskanPaliwal, since you'\"'\"'ve done most of the hook-chaining work.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nEntire moves a hook it replaces to `<hook>.pre-entire` and executes it from there. Trunk'\"'\"'s git-hook launcher, the one script `trunk git-hooks sync` writes for every hook, passes its own file name to `trunk git-hooks callback`. Under the renamed path Trunk refuses the callback (`Unknown git-hooks callback '\"'\"'pre-push.pre-entire'\"'\"'`) and exits 2, so git aborts every commit and push in a repo whose hooks Trunk manages.\\n\\n#\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3048,\n      \"title\": \"redact: redact passwords passed on the command line\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3048\",\n      \"head\": \"528ddf9a05ac20b17c94df4e0496dbc656e7838e\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-command-line-passwords-2898\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2898.\\n\\nBuilt on @DilpreetBansi'\"'\"'s branch from the issue. Their commit comes first, unchanged and with their authorship. The eighty-five commits on top come from my review of it, from @MuskanPaliwal'\"'\"'s review and from the automated reviews here, with one merge of `main`. Each commit message says what it fixes and which test covers it, so this description only gives the result.\\n\\n## What it covers\\n\\nA password given to a client on its command line is usually human-chosen (`hunter2`, `Summer2026!`). That is far below the entropy threshold, and no pattern layer matched it, so it reached the checkpoint as typed. This adds a command-line layer inside the connection-string layer (counted as `con\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3046,\n      \"title\": \"fix(hooks): keep the user'\"'\"'s pre-push hook in entire-brain'\"'\"'s chain on re-wrap\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3046\",\n      \"head\": \"84bca441f543a7e1425a5536968724a8e626bfc3\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-rewrap-brain-chain-2960-up\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"**Review after #3003, which builds on #2959.** A fork PR can'\"'\"'t target another PR'\"'\"'s branch, so this diff also carries those two commits (`edb1ccba` from #2959 and `d18031fc` from #3003). Only the last three commits, `cfaa8fef`, `31d2e568` and `a378498e`, are new here. The branch merges cleanly with main.\\n\\nFixes #2960.\\n\\nI asked on #2960 on Oct 29 whether this approach works for you and haven'\"'\"'t heard back, so this PR is there to make the proposal concrete. I'\"'\"'m happy to change direction.\\n\\n## The bug (the case left after #2959)\\n\\nAfter `entire enable` backs up the user'\"'\"'s pre-push hook and entire-brain connects, the chain is:\\n\\n```\\npre-push                    Brain'\"'\"'s wrapper   -> exec \\\"$0.pre-entire\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3045,\n      \"title\": \"codex: offer to install hooks where Codex reads them in linked worktrees\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3045\",\n      \"head\": \"b1aba8dabbd46fdf429cdfd68392cfb8975dc5b4\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/codex-linked-worktree-hooks\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\nIn a linked worktree, `entire enable --agent codex` (and `entire agent add codex`) writes `<worktree>/.codex/hooks.json`, but Codex loads the **primary checkout'\"'\"'s** `.codex/hooks.json` (the `.bare` layout root for `.bare` worktrees; pinned by the `codex app-server` `hooks/list` tests). With no hooks file there, Codex runs no Entire hooks and nothing is captured. `enable` warned (\\\"Hooks in the current-worktree file will not run here\\\") and `entire status` showed \\\"Codex hooks are not active in this worktree\\\", but nothing fixed it, so people wh'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":11625}},"started_at_ms":1794842127987,"completed_at_ms":1794842127988}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:28.127Z","ordinal":3013,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-fe3759bd-577d-4a46-93f3-bb6a7bac3366","process_id":"90061","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' 'o only work in worktrees got no checkpoints.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nAfter installing in the current worktree, when Codex reads a different hooks file that i\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3044,\n      \"title\": \"fix(push): let the remote settle before git sends the user'\"'\"'s push\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3044\",\n      \"head\": \"b388839111113db196d4e3d4d6b36c566b0fabee\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-checkpoint-push-race-2794\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2794\\n\\nOn the git-branch backend (the default), the pre-push hook pushes `entire/checkpoints/v1` to the user'\"'\"'s push remote and returns, and git sends the user'\"'\"'s own pack a few milliseconds later. GitHub rejects the later of two pushes to one repository when its pack arrives within about a second of the other finishing, so the push that fails is the user'\"'\"'s. This makes the hook wait 1.2s after a v1 push that moved the ref on any destination, and only then.\\n\\nI reviewed this on my fork first (Beehtrix/cli#14).\\n\\n## What was wrong\\n\\n`prePush` pushes v1 through `pushRefIfNeeded` and returns. git has already read the remote'\"'\"'s refs before the hook ran, and sends the user'\"'\"'s pack as soon as the ho\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3043,\n      \"title\": \"trail watch: start at the latest push, with --full for the whole history\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3043\",\n      \"head\": \"b7a21c078a97ed9f1e0109ccbe3c33d38bc49179\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/trail-watch-from-head\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\n`entire trail watch` replays the trail'\"'\"'s whole event history every time it connects, so a person or agent re-running it after a push first scrolls through every earlier push'\"'\"'s reviews, gates and agent runs.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nentire-api now accepts `from=head` on the trail events stream (et/entirehq/entire-api change 807, merged): it starts at the current head'\"'\"'s first event and never skips one of that push'\"'\"'s events.\\n\\n- `trail watch` sends `from=head` on every request. A resume cursor (`Last-Event-ID`) outranks it on the server, and sending it every time means a retry before any event can'\"'\"'t fall back to a full replay. Servers without it ignore the parameter (old behavior).\\n- `--full` replay\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3041,\n      \"title\": \"build(deps): bump the codeql-action group across 1 directory with 2 updates\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3041\",\n      \"head\": \"42ab43d53c24303ccde9a639604cf029318b74ad\",\n      \"branch\": \"dependabot/github_actions/codeql-action-54bdb232ba\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Bumps the codeql-action group with 2 updates in the / directory: [github/codeql-action/init](https://github.com/github/codeql-action) and [github/codeql-action/analyze](https://github.com/github/codeql-action).\\n\\nUpdates `github/codeql-action/init` from 4.39.1 to 4.39.3\\n<details>\\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\\\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases\\\">github/codeql-action/init'\"'\"'s releases</a>.</em></p>\\n<blockquote>\\n<h2>v4.39.3</h2>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Fixed diff-informed alert filtering incorrectly removing alerts in changed files whose paths contain spaces, special characters, or non-ASCII characters. <a href=\\\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3040,\n      \"title\": \"Fix setup commit hangs when a hook opens a Git pager\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3040\",\n      \"head\": \"c47eb0685c10858c51a77df8c64e6c836f618d88\",\n      \"branch\": \"setup-commit-pager\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3025.\\n\\nAccepting the setup commit during `entire enable` can hang when a pre-commit hook runs a Git command with paging enabled. Git runs in a separate process group, so a pager reading the terminal can be suspended while Entire waits for the commit.\\n\\nSet `GIT_PAGER=cat` for `CommitPaths` commands. Nested Git commands in hooks inherit it and write directly to the supplied output. This keeps the existing process-group cancellation and does not change repository pager settings. It is a narrower fix than the terminal handoff suggested in the issue; arbitrary interactive hooks still need separate consideration.\\n\\nTests:\\n- A real pseudo-terminal reproduction with `less` and `git diff --cach\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3034,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): keep prepare'\"'\"'s trust in a session after it settles\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3034\",\n      \"head\": \"5ff58dc5cbb894e0002b59ea705b60a7e0b13a76\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-subagent-dangling-trailer-3029\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3029.\\n\\nStacked on #3005. This branch is built on #3005'\"'\"'s head (ea0833d9), so until #3005 merges the diff here also shows its commits. This PR'\"'\"'s own change is 4723f4f1 and 2bc1b2b6; the two merge commits only bring in #3005'\"'\"'s later commits. I'\"'\"'ll merge main in once #3005 lands.\\n\\n## The bug (on main as well)\\n\\nprepare-commit-msg stamps an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer for a session on its shape alone in two cases: the session is IDLE with a background subagent in flight (`idleWithLiveTaskRecord`), or it'\"'\"'s ACTIVE mid-turn on the no-TTY / `commit_linking=always` fast path. Neither case needs a staged file of the session'\"'\"'s own.\\n\\nThe commit can then wait on the link prompt or the message editor\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3031,\n      \"title\": \"feat(agent-help): make the trail the record agents keep and link\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3031\",\n      \"head\": \"e7a4e754832b420283920c890018713a0903b4f9\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/trail-agent-guidance\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\nAgents working in Entire repos treat the pull request as the record of the work. They:\\n- open a pull request when asked to push, instead of a trail;\\n- edit only the PR body and share PR links, not the trail;\\n- act on bare numbers that are really PR numbers, including writing into another person'\"'\"'s trail;\\n- call a change ready while open findings are hidden by the default filters;\\n- merge when the user says \\\"looks good\\\".\\n\\nSome existing agent guidance also no longer matched the commands on main.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\nAgent-only text; human `--help` is unchanged.\\n\\n- **First-turn injection** (`entireContextInjection`). The trail, not the pull request, is the record of the work:\\n  - **Push:** as\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3028,\n      \"title\": \"hooks: chain through prek'\"'\"'s shim the way Entire chains through pre-commit'\"'\"'s\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3028\",\n      \"head\": \"e63520a9fe3491c62e8724445f508972fc5346fb\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/prek-hook-chain\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Why\\n[prek](https://github.com/j178/prek) reimplements pre-commit and installs the same kind of hook shim: `prek install` moves the existing hook to `<hook>.legacy` and runs it with `PREK_RUNNING_LEGACY=1`, and refuses to run its shim again under that variable. Entire special-cases exactly this for pre-commit (`PRE_COMMIT_RUNNING_LEGACY` + pre-commit'\"'\"'s header) but not for prek. With prek'\"'\"'s shim as Entire'\"'\"'s backup (`pre-push.pre-entire`), prek runs Entire'\"'\"'s hook as `.legacy`, Entire'\"'\"'s chain runs the shim again, and the push fails:\\n\\n```\\nerror: prek'\"'\"'s Git shim is installed in migration mode\\nrun `prek install -f --hook-type pre-push` to reinstall the shim\\n```\\n\\n## What\\n- `preCommitSignatures` g\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3015,\n      \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): preserve concurrent sessions during replay\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3015\",\n      \"head\": \"5acf539b796d4742755019c05ade180a988fb271\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/preserve-concurrent-checkpoint-sessions\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Closes #3014.\\n\\nTwo clones can append different sessions to the same numeric checkpoint slot. Recovery currently reports a successful push and clears the queue after replacing the remote clone'\"'\"'s session. This merges sessions by ID so both additions reach the published checkpoint.\\n\\nReady for review. #3014 is newly filed and maintainer agreement on the approach is pending. The four full-suite failures below also reproduce on untouched upstream `955fc9ede`; this PR does not claim a green full check.\\n\\n## Reproduction\\n\\nThe standalone test in #3014 uses real checkpoint writers, the generation-aware queue and a local bare remote. I ran the same test against untouched `955fc9ede` and this implementat\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3010,\n      \"title\": \"Add entire project agent create for custom review agents\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3010\",\n      \"head\": \"47e95f29c2c5d9d11127c3ee99e814eb2ce414ed\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/project-agent-create\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Trail: https://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2688/changes/cli/1761\\n\\n`entire project agent` could only add Entire'\"'\"'s presets; a custom agent needed the web UI or raw `entire api` calls. This adds `entire project agent create`, which creates a custom review agent for the current repository.\\n\\n```\\nentire project agent create --name \\\"Migration Risk\\\" --harness claude \\\\\\n  --signal percent --polarity lower_is_better --instructions-file review.md\\n```\\n\\n- **Definition:** `--name`, `--description`, `--harness` (claude, codex), `--model`, `--reasoning-effort`, `--timeout` (default 10m, at most 30m), `--signal` (boolean, percent, size) and `--polarity`. The instructions come from `--instructions` or `--i\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3005,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): don'\"'\"'t link a sibling worktree'\"'\"'s idle session to a commit\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3005\",\n      \"head\": \"04b996df6ff0832cafb7dd739d00cc558e9db5c6\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-worktree-sibling-idle-2979-up\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2979\\n\\n@lcv-leo, thank you for the report. You traced the bug to the exact line in `resolveWorktreeCandidates`, and you'\"'\"'d already written and verified a patch, so this PR builds on your fix. Earlier today [I asked](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2979#issuecomment-6618856546) whether you planned to open a PR, and asked @peyton-alt to assign the issue to me if you weren'\"'\"'t. I'\"'\"'m opening this now because I have the fix reproduced, with tests that fail on `main` and pass here. If you'\"'\"'d rather open your own PR, just say so and I'\"'\"'ll close this one.\\n\\n## What was wrong\\n\\nIf you commit from a worktree that has no Entire session, the CLI falls back to sessions from other worktrees of the sa\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3003,\n      \"title\": \"fix(hooks): take Entire'\"'\"'s hook out of entire-brain'\"'\"'s chain on uninstall\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3003\",\n      \"head\": \"d18031fc0565428086edf2e481ba0830a2fc47c1\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-uninstall-brain-chain-2957-up\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2957\\n\\n**Please review this after #2959.** This branch sits on top of #2959 (`d6690097c`), so until that merges the diff here also shows #2959'\"'\"'s commit. The change for this PR is only the last commit, `a4ef1e8ba`, which touches `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/hook_backup.go` and its test file (+435/−1). One test case needs #2959 (details below). If #2959 changes or merges, I'\"'\"'ll rebase this onto main.\\n\\n@peyton-alt @Soph: I filed #2957 and nobody is assigned yet. Could you assign it to me? This is the uninstall half of the Brain hook problem; #2959 is the doctor/install half.\\n\\n## What was wrong\\n\\n`entire brain connect` moves the `pre-push` hook it finds to `pre-push.pre-entire-brain` and runs it\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2997,\n      \"title\": \"fix/claude-hook-version-preflight\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2997\",\n      \"head\": \"e8684a4ae86dd64e0a5a331b031ecbb0ed22004a\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/claude-hook-version-preflight\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back a trail. Feel free to edit the title or body, but keep the hidden marker below: Entire uses it to close this pull request when the trail closes.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes Claude hook install and doctor behavior for all claude-code users; mis-parsed versions or semver edge cases could block installs, but failures are fail-closed without rewriting settings.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds a **Claude Code version gate** (minimum **2.1.78**) before Entire writes hooks that use **`StopFailure`**. Older Claude builds ignore the whole project hook file when that e\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2996,\n      \"title\": \"fix(review): persist findings when session matching fails\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2996\",\n      \"head\": \"0e0ada68ca0ef457a5ea4483552cd1f7d0a9646f\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/review-worktree-findings\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\nA local review can finish and print its verdict but leave `entire review --findings` empty. The manifest currently depends on matching a tagged lifecycle session for each reviewer. If no session matches the current worktree, the command drops the captured output; sessions from sibling worktrees can make the resulting diagnostic look like a worktree mismatch. The command also returns success when writing the manifest fails.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- Save every reviewer'\"'\"'s captured output and the judge'\"'\"'s aggregate verdict in the local manifest even when session state is missing, cannot be read, or does not match. Attach a session ID only when the existing matcher finds a suitable session, so a\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2993,\n      \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): cap the legacy prompt_attributions carry-forward\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2993\",\n      \"head\": \"f8872e6be650bf127c6b1817a730a4eb4574d8b3\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/cap-legacy-prompt-attributions\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"`Metadata.LegacyPromptAttributions` is dead data — no CLI version computes, reads or sets it, and the field survives only so that rewriting an old checkpoint does not strip what entire.io still reads. But its carry-forward has no exit. Every path that re-emits a session'\"'\"'s `metadata.json` decodes the whole `Metadata` and re-encodes it, so an oversized value an older CLI recorded is copied into a fresh blob on each rewrite — for the life of the session, and regardless of whether the rewrite had anything to do with attribution. A summary backfill re-commits it. So does a transcript finalize, a skill-events replacement, and a compact-transcript marker update.\\n\\nThat matters because this is the on\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2992,\n      \"title\": \"Poll mirror requests by requestId, not the Location header\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2992\",\n      \"head\": \"c0d703dad182ca614f7b7e9c942288b2cb62b225\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/mirror-poll-by-request-id\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Supersedes #2242, re-cut against current main. Most of #2242 no longer applies (the sync route, the settings switch and `CreatedMirror` are all gone). This is the part that still does.\\n\\n## What was wrong\\n\\n`awaitMirrorPlacement` took its poll target from the 202'\"'\"'s `Location` header: it required the header, parsed the request id out of its path, and for an absolute `Location` pointed the client'\"'\"'s base URL at the header'\"'\"'s origin via `coreapi.WithServerURL`. That caused three problems on what is now the only `mirror add` path:\\n\\n- **A missing or differently-shaped header failed a successful add.** `Location` is optional in the spec, and the body already carries the required `requestId`. A relativ\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2988,\n      \"title\": \"matthias/eval-gates-trail-show\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2988\",\n      \"head\": \"1294b230fd516c5c3c54cf7a61e4e066b0807ee6\",\n      \"branch\": \"matthias/eval-gates-trail-show\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back a trail. Feel free to edit the title or body, but keep the hidden marker below: Entire uses it to close this pull request when the trail closes.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes the merge command'\"'\"'s user-visible behavior (stderr warnings) and gate messaging on a sensitive workflow, though blocking rules are unchanged.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds first-class support for **agent eval** merge gates in the CLI mergeability snapshot.\\n> \\n> **`entire trail show`** (text) now splits eval gates under an **Evals:** section with agent names, readings vs thresholds (percen\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2982,\n      \"title\": \"peyton/claude-tool-result-blocks\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2982\",\n      \"head\": \"0572a0ee5191930f6a8d1ff68622daefd4530102\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/claude-tool-result-blocks\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back a trail. Feel free to edit the title or body, but keep the hidden marker below: Entire uses it to close this pull request when the trail closes.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Scoped to transcript compaction and fixture expectations; improves correctness of tool output text without touching auth or persistence beyond transcript content.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Claude/MCP tools can return **tool_result** `content` as an array of typed blocks (text + images), not only a plain string. Compaction previously treated that JSON as a string and produced empty or wrong **tool ou\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2975,\n      \"title\": \"import: anchor a turn that ran git commit -q to its own commit, not the branch tip\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2975\",\n      \"head\": \"7bf7d2c22a622c682f88c34689ca3b173b9eec62\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/import-quiet-commit-anchor\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2908. Builds on #2911 by @levelorbit (their two commits are kept as authored).\\n\\n## Why\\n`entire import claude-code` learns a turn'\"'\"'s commits only from the `gitOperation` record Claude Code writes on a Bash result, and Claude Code writes it only when git prints the new commi'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' 'o only work in worktrees got no checkpoints.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nAfter installing in the current worktree, when Codex reads a different hooks file that i\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3044,\n      \"title\": \"fix(push): let the remote settle before git sends the user'\"'\"'s push\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3044\",\n      \"head\": \"b388839111113db196d4e3d4d6b36c566b0fabee\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-checkpoint-push-race-2794\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2794\\n\\nOn the git-branch backend (the default), the pre-push hook pushes `entire/checkpoints/v1` to the user'\"'\"'s push remote and returns, and git sends the user'\"'\"'s own pack a few milliseconds later. GitHub rejects the later of two pushes to one repository when its pack arrives within about a second of the other finishing, so the push that fails is the user'\"'\"'s. This makes the hook wait 1.2s after a v1 push that moved the ref on any destination, and only then.\\n\\nI reviewed this on my fork first (Beehtrix/cli#14).\\n\\n## What was wrong\\n\\n`prePush` pushes v1 through `pushRefIfNeeded` and returns. git has already read the remote'\"'\"'s refs before the hook ran, and sends the user'\"'\"'s pack as soon as the ho\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3043,\n      \"title\": \"trail watch: start at the latest push, with --full for the whole history\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3043\",\n      \"head\": \"b7a21c078a97ed9f1e0109ccbe3c33d38bc49179\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/trail-watch-from-head\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\n`entire trail watch` replays the trail'\"'\"'s whole event history every time it connects, so a person or agent re-running it after a push first scrolls through every earlier push'\"'\"'s reviews, gates and agent runs.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nentire-api now accepts `from=head` on the trail events stream (et/entirehq/entire-api change 807, merged): it starts at the current head'\"'\"'s first event and never skips one of that push'\"'\"'s events.\\n\\n- `trail watch` sends `from=head` on every request. A resume cursor (`Last-Event-ID`) outranks it on the server, and sending it every time means a retry before any event can'\"'\"'t fall back to a full replay. Servers without it ignore the parameter (old behavior).\\n- `--full` replay\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3041,\n      \"title\": \"build(deps): bump the codeql-action group across 1 directory with 2 updates\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3041\",\n      \"head\": \"42ab43d53c24303ccde9a639604cf029318b74ad\",\n      \"branch\": \"dependabot/github_actions/codeql-action-54bdb232ba\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Bumps the codeql-action group with 2 updates in the / directory: [github/codeql-action/init](https://github.com/github/codeql-action) and [github/codeql-action/analyze](https://github.com/github/codeql-action).\\n\\nUpdates `github/codeql-action/init` from 4.39.1 to 4.39.3\\n<details>\\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\\\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases\\\">github/codeql-action/init'\"'\"'s releases</a>.</em></p>\\n<blockquote>\\n<h2>v4.39.3</h2>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Fixed diff-informed alert filtering incorrectly removing alerts in changed files whose paths contain spaces, special characters, or non-ASCII characters. <a href=\\\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3040,\n      \"title\": \"Fix setup commit hangs when a hook opens a Git pager\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3040\",\n      \"head\": \"c47eb0685c10858c51a77df8c64e6c836f618d88\",\n      \"branch\": \"setup-commit-pager\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3025.\\n\\nAccepting the setup commit during `entire enable` can hang when a pre-commit hook runs a Git command with paging enabled. Git runs in a separate process group, so a pager reading the terminal can be suspended while Entire waits for the commit.\\n\\nSet `GIT_PAGER=cat` for `CommitPaths` commands. Nested Git commands in hooks inherit it and write directly to the supplied output. This keeps the existing process-group cancellation and does not change repository pager settings. It is a narrower fix than the terminal handoff suggested in the issue; arbitrary interactive hooks still need separate consideration.\\n\\nTests:\\n- A real pseudo-terminal reproduction with `less` and `git diff --cach\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3034,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): keep prepare'\"'\"'s trust in a session after it settles\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3034\",\n      \"head\": \"5ff58dc5cbb894e0002b59ea705b60a7e0b13a76\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-subagent-dangling-trailer-3029\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #3029.\\n\\nStacked on #3005. This branch is built on #3005'\"'\"'s head (ea0833d9), so until #3005 merges the diff here also shows its commits. This PR'\"'\"'s own change is 4723f4f1 and 2bc1b2b6; the two merge commits only bring in #3005'\"'\"'s later commits. I'\"'\"'ll merge main in once #3005 lands.\\n\\n## The bug (on main as well)\\n\\nprepare-commit-msg stamps an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer for a session on its shape alone in two cases: the session is IDLE with a background subagent in flight (`idleWithLiveTaskRecord`), or it'\"'\"'s ACTIVE mid-turn on the no-TTY / `commit_linking=always` fast path. Neither case needs a staged file of the session'\"'\"'s own.\\n\\nThe commit can then wait on the link prompt or the message editor\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3031,\n      \"title\": \"feat(agent-help): make the trail the record agents keep and link\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3031\",\n      \"head\": \"e7a4e754832b420283920c890018713a0903b4f9\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/trail-agent-guidance\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\nAgents working in Entire repos treat the pull request as the record of the work. They:\\n- open a pull request when asked to push, instead of a trail;\\n- edit only the PR body and share PR links, not the trail;\\n- act on bare numbers that are really PR numbers, including writing into another person'\"'\"'s trail;\\n- call a change ready while open findings are hidden by the default filters;\\n- merge when the user says \\\"looks good\\\".\\n\\nSome existing agent guidance also no longer matched the commands on main.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\nAgent-only text; human `--help` is unchanged.\\n\\n- **First-turn injection** (`entireContextInjection`). The trail, not the pull request, is the record of the work:\\n  - **Push:** as\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3028,\n      \"title\": \"hooks: chain through prek'\"'\"'s shim the way Entire chains through pre-commit'\"'\"'s\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3028\",\n      \"head\": \"e63520a9fe3491c62e8724445f508972fc5346fb\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/prek-hook-chain\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Why\\n[prek](https://github.com/j178/prek) reimplements pre-commit and installs the same kind of hook shim: `prek install` moves the existing hook to `<hook>.legacy` and runs it with `PREK_RUNNING_LEGACY=1`, and refuses to run its shim again under that variable. Entire special-cases exactly this for pre-commit (`PRE_COMMIT_RUNNING_LEGACY` + pre-commit'\"'\"'s header) but not for prek. With prek'\"'\"'s shim as Entire'\"'\"'s backup (`pre-push.pre-entire`), prek runs Entire'\"'\"'s hook as `.legacy`, Entire'\"'\"'s chain runs the shim again, and the push fails:\\n\\n```\\nerror: prek'\"'\"'s Git shim is installed in migration mode\\nrun `prek install -f --hook-type pre-push` to reinstall the shim\\n```\\n\\n## What\\n- `preCommitSignatures` g\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3015,\n      \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): preserve concurrent sessions during replay\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3015\",\n      \"head\": \"5acf539b796d4742755019c05ade180a988fb271\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/preserve-concurrent-checkpoint-sessions\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Closes #3014.\\n\\nTwo clones can append different sessions to the same numeric checkpoint slot. Recovery currently reports a successful push and clears the queue after replacing the remote clone'\"'\"'s session. This merges sessions by ID so both additions reach the published checkpoint.\\n\\nReady for review. #3014 is newly filed and maintainer agreement on the approach is pending. The four full-suite failures below also reproduce on untouched upstream `955fc9ede`; this PR does not claim a green full check.\\n\\n## Reproduction\\n\\nThe standalone test in #3014 uses real checkpoint writers, the generation-aware queue and a local bare remote. I ran the same test against untouched `955fc9ede` and this implementat\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3010,\n      \"title\": \"Add entire project agent create for custom review agents\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3010\",\n      \"head\": \"47e95f29c2c5d9d11127c3ee99e814eb2ce414ed\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/project-agent-create\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Trail: https://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2688/changes/cli/1761\\n\\n`entire project agent` could only add Entire'\"'\"'s presets; a custom agent needed the web UI or raw `entire api` calls. This adds `entire project agent create`, which creates a custom review agent for the current repository.\\n\\n```\\nentire project agent create --name \\\"Migration Risk\\\" --harness claude \\\\\\n  --signal percent --polarity lower_is_better --instructions-file review.md\\n```\\n\\n- **Definition:** `--name`, `--description`, `--harness` (claude, codex), `--model`, `--reasoning-effort`, `--timeout` (default 10m, at most 30m), `--signal` (boolean, percent, size) and `--polarity`. The instructions come from `--instructions` or `--i\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3005,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): don'\"'\"'t link a sibling worktree'\"'\"'s idle session to a commit\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3005\",\n      \"head\": \"04b996df6ff0832cafb7dd739d00cc558e9db5c6\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-worktree-sibling-idle-2979-up\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2979\\n\\n@lcv-leo, thank you for the report. You traced the bug to the exact line in `resolveWorktreeCandidates`, and you'\"'\"'d already written and verified a patch, so this PR builds on your fix. Earlier today [I asked](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2979#issuecomment-6618856546) whether you planned to open a PR, and asked @peyton-alt to assign the issue to me if you weren'\"'\"'t. I'\"'\"'m opening this now because I have the fix reproduced, with tests that fail on `main` and pass here. If you'\"'\"'d rather open your own PR, just say so and I'\"'\"'ll close this one.\\n\\n## What was wrong\\n\\nIf you commit from a worktree that has no Entire session, the CLI falls back to sessions from other worktrees of the sa\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3003,\n      \"title\": \"fix(hooks): take Entire'\"'\"'s hook out of entire-brain'\"'\"'s chain on uninstall\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3003\",\n      \"head\": \"d18031fc0565428086edf2e481ba0830a2fc47c1\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-uninstall-brain-chain-2957-up\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2957\\n\\n**Please review this after #2959.** This branch sits on top of #2959 (`d6690097c`), so until that merges the diff here also shows #2959'\"'\"'s commit. The change for this PR is only the last commit, `a4ef1e8ba`, which touches `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/hook_backup.go` and its test file (+435/−1). One test case needs #2959 (details below). If #2959 changes or merges, I'\"'\"'ll rebase this onto main.\\n\\n@peyton-alt @Soph: I filed #2957 and nobody is assigned yet. Could you assign it to me? This is the uninstall half of the Brain hook problem; #2959 is the doctor/install half.\\n\\n## What was wrong\\n\\n`entire brain connect` moves the `pre-push` hook it finds to `pre-push.pre-entire-brain` and runs it\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2997,\n      \"title\": \"fix/claude-hook-version-preflight\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2997\",\n      \"head\": \"e8684a4ae86dd64e0a5a331b031ecbb0ed22004a\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/claude-hook-version-preflight\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back a trail. Feel free to edit the title or body, but keep the hidden marker below: Entire uses it to close this pull request when the trail closes.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes Claude hook install and doctor behavior for all claude-code users; mis-parsed versions or semver edge cases could block installs, but failures are fail-closed without rewriting settings.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds a **Claude Code version gate** (minimum **2.1.78**) before Entire writes hooks that use **`StopFailure`**. Older Claude builds ignore the whole project hook file when that e\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2996,\n      \"title\": \"fix(review): persist findings when session matching fails\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2996\",\n      \"head\": \"0e0ada68ca0ef457a5ea4483552cd1f7d0a9646f\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/review-worktree-findings\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\nA local review can finish and print its verdict but leave `entire review --findings` empty. The manifest currently depends on matching a tagged lifecycle session for each reviewer. If no session matches the current worktree, the command drops the captured output; sessions from sibling worktrees can make the resulting diagnostic look like a worktree mismatch. The command also returns success when writing the manifest fails.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- Save every reviewer'\"'\"'s captured output and the judge'\"'\"'s aggregate verdict in the local manifest even when session state is missing, cannot be read, or does not match. Attach a session ID only when the existing matcher finds a suitable session, so a\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2993,\n      \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): cap the legacy prompt_attributions carry-forward\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2993\",\n      \"head\": \"f8872e6be650bf127c6b1817a730a4eb4574d8b3\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/cap-legacy-prompt-attributions\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"`Metadata.LegacyPromptAttributions` is dead data — no CLI version computes, reads or sets it, and the field survives only so that rewriting an old checkpoint does not strip what entire.io still reads. But its carry-forward has no exit. Every path that re-emits a session'\"'\"'s `metadata.json` decodes the whole `Metadata` and re-encodes it, so an oversized value an older CLI recorded is copied into a fresh blob on each rewrite — for the life of the session, and regardless of whether the rewrite had anything to do with attribution. A summary backfill re-commits it. So does a transcript finalize, a skill-events replacement, and a compact-transcript marker update.\\n\\nThat matters because this is the on\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2992,\n      \"title\": \"Poll mirror requests by requestId, not the Location header\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2992\",\n      \"head\": \"c0d703dad182ca614f7b7e9c942288b2cb62b225\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/mirror-poll-by-request-id\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Supersedes #2242, re-cut against current main. Most of #2242 no longer applies (the sync route, the settings switch and `CreatedMirror` are all gone). This is the part that still does.\\n\\n## What was wrong\\n\\n`awaitMirrorPlacement` took its poll target from the 202'\"'\"'s `Location` header: it required the header, parsed the request id out of its path, and for an absolute `Location` pointed the client'\"'\"'s base URL at the header'\"'\"'s origin via `coreapi.WithServerURL`. That caused three problems on what is now the only `mirror add` path:\\n\\n- **A missing or differently-shaped header failed a successful add.** `Location` is optional in the spec, and the body already carries the required `requestId`. A relativ\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2988,\n      \"title\": \"matthias/eval-gates-trail-show\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2988\",\n      \"head\": \"1294b230fd516c5c3c54cf7a61e4e066b0807ee6\",\n      \"branch\": \"matthias/eval-gates-trail-show\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back a trail. Feel free to edit the title or body, but keep the hidden marker below: Entire uses it to close this pull request when the trail closes.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes the merge command'\"'\"'s user-visible behavior (stderr warnings) and gate messaging on a sensitive workflow, though blocking rules are unchanged.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds first-class support for **agent eval** merge gates in the CLI mergeability snapshot.\\n> \\n> **`entire trail show`** (text) now splits eval gates under an **Evals:** section with agent names, readings vs thresholds (percen\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2982,\n      \"title\": \"peyton/claude-tool-result-blocks\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2982\",\n      \"head\": \"0572a0ee5191930f6a8d1ff68622daefd4530102\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/claude-tool-result-blocks\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back a trail. Feel free to edit the title or body, but keep the hidden marker below: Entire uses it to close this pull request when the trail closes.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Scoped to transcript compaction and fixture expectations; improves correctness of tool output text without touching auth or persistence beyond transcript content.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Claude/MCP tools can return **tool_result** `content` as an array of typed blocks (text + images), not only a plain string. Compaction previously treated that JSON as a string and produced empty or wrong **tool ou\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2975,\n      \"title\": \"import: anchor a turn that ran git commit -q to its own commit, not the branch tip\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2975\",\n      \"head\": \"7bf7d2c22a622c682f88c34689ca3b173b9eec62\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/import-quiet-commit-anchor\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2908. Builds on #2911 by @levelorbit (their two commits are kept as authored).\\n\\n## Why\\n`entire import claude-code` learns a turn'\"'\"'s commits only from the `gitOperation` record Claude Code writes on a Bash result, and Claude Code writes it only when git prints the new commi'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":10875}},"started_at_ms":1794842128127,"completed_at_ms":1794842128127}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:28.263Z","ordinal":3014,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-efc71745-7498-4579-9324-20ca045cf6f5","process_id":"90435","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' 't'\"'\"'s SHA. A quiet `git commit -q` leaves none, so the turn falls back to the default-branch tip, which is often a later commit by someone else. Agents commit quietly most of the time (the reporter measured 253 of 262 commit commands), and a re-import skips turns already imported, so the wrong anchor sticks.\\n\\n## What\\n- From #2911: for each Bash call in a turn that runs `git commit`, `cherry-pick`, `revert`, `merge`, `re\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2966,\n      \"title\": \"fix: edit tracked core.hooksPath shell hooks in place\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2966\",\n      \"head\": \"41b51b292cd76492df21d9a7c5d2456ab440a5f0\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/tracked-hooks-path-in-place\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2965\\n\\n`entire enable` copied a git-tracked `core.hooksPath` shell hook to an untracked `*.pre-entire` file and replaced the tracked path with Entire'\"'\"'s wrapper. Committing that wrapper dropped the project'\"'\"'s hook in every other clone, because the backup was never in the tree.\\n\\nA tracked shell hook is now edited in place. The project'\"'\"'s script stays in the tracked file and runs after Entire. A fresh clone of the committed file still runs the project hook. Hooks in `.git/hooks` and in gitignored directories are still backed up to `*.pre-entire` and chained. A tracked hook that is not a shell script, or is a symbolic link, is left unchanged.\\n\\nOn Windows, a relative `core.hooksPath` whose di\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2964,\n      \"title\": \"soph/service-account-keys\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2964\",\n      \"head\": \"4b9af7ffdc991443c8a414fe31a3945706f59325\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/service-account-keys\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2687/changes/cli/1731\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **High Risk**\\n> Changes how authentication is resolved across the CLI and git helper, adds local private-key storage and STS token minting; server-side enrollment/STS assertion support is not implemented yet.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **experimental** `entire auth service-account` for machine auth without exporting \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2959,\n      \"title\": \"fix(doctor): count Brain'\"'\"'s pre-push wrapper as installed hooks\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2959\",\n      \"head\": \"edb1ccba85a107e6bfd4a64b4278e19d287a7bdd\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-doctor-2949-brain-chain\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2949\\nRelated to #2960\\n\\n@peyton-alt @Soph: I asked on the issue to be assigned (https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2949#issuecomment-6486951877) and haven'\"'\"'t had a reply yet. I'\"'\"'m opening this so it can be reviewed. If you'\"'\"'d rather fix it on the Brain side instead (giving Brain'\"'\"'s wrapper a marker `doctor` recognizes), tell me and I'\"'\"'ll close this.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\n`entire brain connect` installs its own `pre-push` hook. It moves the hook it finds (Entire'\"'\"'s) to `pre-push.pre-entire-brain`, and its own hook ends with:\\n\\n```sh\\nbackup=\\\"$0.pre-entire-brain\\\"\\nif [ -x \\\"$backup\\\" ]; then exec \\\"$backup\\\" \\\"$@\\\"; fi\\n```\\n\\nSo Entire'\"'\"'s hook still runs, with git'\"'\"'s stdin and arguments. But the new `pre-push` does\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2956,\n      \"title\": \"feat(trail): accept pasted trail URLs as selectors\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2956\",\n      \"head\": \"7712dbd9156fe876c14633675d936807dd8f1310\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/trail-url-selectors\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2681/changes/cli/1726\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nUsers and their agents paste trail URLs from the web app (`https://entire.com/gh/acme/-/trails/600`). Project trail commands rejected them with `use a project trail ID or number; select a branch with --branch`. Agent guidance told agents to map the URL by hand and add `--project`; when an agent dropped `--project`, a bare `600` silently resolved in origin'\"'\"'s namespace — a different trail whenever the clone'\"'\"'s origin belongs to another owner.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nThe project trail tree gets a persistent pre-run, `normalizeProjectTrailURLArgs`, that rewrites URL selector\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2954,\n      \"title\": \"trail: only suggest `entire login` on a 401\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2954\",\n      \"head\": \"72b5ed75ef9f5591dca774e6fca8ee2f67d3b81e\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/trail-403-hint\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2676/changes/cli/1724\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\nTrail commands append \\\"run '\"'\"'entire login'\"'\"' to re-authenticate\\\" to every 401 **and** 403 (`checkTrailResponse`). A 403 means the login is valid but lacks access, so logging in again does not help, and the hint sent a user down the wrong path. One cause of such a 403 was the trails API matching GitHub repo names case-sensitively; that is fixed in entire-api separately.\\n\\n## What\\n- 401: unchanged (`run '\"'\"'entire login'\"'\"' to re-authenticate`).\\n- 403: the server'\"'\"'s message alone, as `trail merge` already does.\\n- One test covering both.\\n\\n+26/−2, 2 files.\\n\\n## Verification\\n-\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2952,\n      \"title\": \"Name Cursor'\"'\"'s project directory the way Cursor does\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2952\",\n      \"head\": \"7d1ba720b05f4426bf0d10dac8c00f8ca53eb52f\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/cursor-path-sanitize\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\n`SanitizePathForCursor` builds the name of Cursor'\"'\"'s project directory (`~/.cursor/projects/<name>`) from the repo path, but not the way Cursor does. Cursor collapses runs of non-alphanumeric characters into one `-` and trims `-` from both ends; Entire only stripped the leading `/` and replaced each character separately. Any path with two separators in a row (a `.worktrees` checkout, `/-…` segments) or any Windows path (`C:\\\\…` → `C--…`) got a directory Cursor never writes to.\\n\\nEverything Entire computes from that directory is then wrong: resume restores a transcript where Cursor never reads it, attach and history import look in the wrong place, transcript discovery misses the sess\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2945,\n      \"title\": \"soph/transcript-tool-result-images\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2945\",\n      \"head\": \"35615fe2ddcb4b361b4a124c32a4263f7471d3d9\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/transcript-tool-result-images\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2660/changes/cli/1718\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Additive optional JSON fields and converter output changes; no auth or persistence logic, with broad test coverage per agent.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds an optional **`images`** array on inlined **`tool_use` results** so screenshots and other visuals returned by tools survive conversion instead of bein\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2927,\n      \"title\": \"Keep a running turn'\"'\"'s baseline when Claude reports a background task finished\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2927\",\n      \"head\": \"c7e215100ebcf3d5ab0bad3d2e3a2e8578256d6b\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/turn-start-overlap\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2638/changes/cli/1708\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nClaude Code fires `UserPromptSubmit` for the `<task-notification>` it injects when a background agent or task finishes. When that happens while a turn is still running, the notice is folded into the running turn, but Entire handled it as a new turn start:\\n\\n- `CapturePrePromptState` rewrote the turn'\"'\"'s pre-prompt state, moving the transcript offset forward and retaking the untracked-files snapshot;\\n- the notification was appended to `prompt.txt` and became `LastPrompt`;\\n- `InitializeSession` gave the turn a new `TurnID` and cleared `TurnCheckpointIDs`.\\n\\nAt \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2912,\n      \"title\": \"enable: save --telemetry and --absolute-git-hook-path on a configured repo\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2912\",\n      \"head\": \"f14c55b57e8358e0490426e2d2a3fd41c734d7a8\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/enable-telemetry-flag-saved\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2614/changes/cli/1695\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nOn a repository that is already set up, `entire enable --telemetry=false` (without `--agent`) saved nothing:\\n\\n```\\n$ entire enable --telemetry=false\\nCannot show agent selection in non-interactive mode.\\n...\\n$ cat .entire/settings.json\\n{\\\"enabled\\\":true,\\\"checkpoints\\\":{\\\"primary\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"git-refs\\\"}}}   # no telemetry\\n```\\n\\n`--absolute-git-hook-path` was dropped the same way. The configured-repo path (`runEnableOnConfiguredRepoWithPreflight`) writes strategy and checkpoint-backend flags after agent management, but these two settings were only ever saved by `entir\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2911,\n      \"title\": \"import: anchor turns to commits made while their git command ran\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2911\",\n      \"head\": \"8bc873772ace176a922c9b4dbe66424cb66d983d\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/import-quiet-commit-anchor\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2908.\\n\\n`entire import claude-code` now anchors a turn that committed with `git commit -q` to the commit it made, not to the default-branch tip.\\n\\n### Change\\n\\n- `agentimport/claude.go`: `commitWindowsInRange` records, for each Bash call in a turn that runs `git commit`, `cherry-pick`, `revert`, `merge`, `rebase` or `am`, the span from its `tool_use` line to its `tool_result` line.\\n- `agentimport/turn_anchor.go`: when the turn'\"'\"'s recorded `gitOperation` SHAs anchor nothing, `resolve` picks the newest default-branch ancestor whose committer time falls inside one of those spans. Recorded SHAs keep priority. Ancestors are kept sorted by committer time and searched per span, so a turn costs a\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2910,\n      \"title\": \"settings: keep configure --local from re-enabling a disabled repo\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2910\",\n      \"head\": \"cbfe33732b1ae7af9d7754c061a6ac5a712b801d\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/configure-local-keeps-disabled\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2613/changes/cli/1694\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nIn a repository whose `.entire/settings.json` has `\\\"enabled\\\": false`, running any local setting change, e.g. `entire configure --local --telemetry=false`, turned Entire back on:\\n\\n```\\n$ entire status          → ○ Disabled\\n$ entire configure --local --telemetry=false\\n$ cat .entire/settings.local.json\\n{ \\\"enabled\\\": true, \\\"telemetry\\\": false }\\n$ entire status          → ● Enabled\\n```\\n\\nA settings file without an `\\\"enabled\\\"` key loads as enabled (the default). Every field-update writer loads the target file, changes one field and saves it, so that default was wri\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2872,\n      \"title\": \"Finalize cross-repo checkpoints at turn end\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2872\",\n      \"head\": \"cc0787cb13d8692fc9721be82091d3f0056806be\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/cross-repo-turn-end-finalize\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1665\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nStacked on #2844 (base branch `peyton/cross-repo-agent-commit-link`).\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nIn #2844, a checkpoint an agent'\"'\"'s commit writes in another repository (B) keeps only the transcript up to the commit. Local mid-turn checkpoints are finalized at turn end with the full prompt-to-stop transcript; B'\"'\"'s were not, so they miss everything after the commit, such as the agent'\"'\"'s final reply.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\n- Condensing a foreign commit records the checkpoint and B'\"'\"'s worktree in the home session'\"'\"'s state (`ForeignTurnCheckpoints`, same lifecycle as `TurnCheckpointIDs`).\\n- At turn end, the home'\"'\"'s h\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2868,\n      \"title\": \"fix(status): show enabled external agents\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2868\",\n      \"head\": \"755703a09a4b0c240cfe1f1333ee6aff95105c1b\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/status-discover-external-agents\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1661\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n`entire status` never ran external agent discovery, so the Agents line (and `agents` in `--json`), which reads the agent registry, listed only built-ins even when an `entire-agent-*` plugin had hooks installed and `external_agents` was enabled.\\n\\nThis runs the gated `external.DiscoverAndRegister` at the top of `runStatus`, the same call `entire agent list`, `resume`, `attach` and `explain` use. Status names no agent, so it may only execute plugins in a repo that opted into `external_agents`; the ungated `DiscoverAndRegisterAlways` is reserved for interactive setup.\\n\\nSupersedes #1066\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2867,\n      \"title\": \"fix: never write transcript-less checkpoints from the session sweep\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2867\",\n      \"head\": \"134a284cf2af0c3241d73442212727d26c1a7365\",\n      \"branch\": \"nodo/sweep-transcript-less-checkpoints\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1660\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes checkpoint write/skip behavior for sweep and doctor across worktrees; incorrect handling could drop salvageable sessions or leave stale state, but commit hooks are explicitly unchanged.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Commit-less session salvage (`CondenseSessionByID` for sweep/doctor) now **refuses to write checkpo\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2856,\n      \"title\": \"Stop double-counting tokens around a mid-turn commit\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2856\",\n      \"head\": \"050f4a795da493634e9a8cdaaae77e466b887245\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/midturn-token-double-count\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2398/changes/cli/1649\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nTwo paths count the same model calls in two checkpoints when a commit lands in the middle of a turn.\\n\\n**A. Pending tokens after a mid-turn commit.** The agent commits mid-turn, so a checkpoint stores the turn so far and `TokenStart` moves to the commit'\"'\"'s transcript end. At Stop, `resolveTurnTokenUsage` counts the whole turn from the turn start and adds it to `CheckpointTokenUsage`. If no model call followed the commit, the next condensation'\"'\"'s recount from `TokenStart` is empty and falls back to that pending usage, so it stores the pre-commit calls again. \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2855,\n      \"title\": \"Find a session'\"'\"'s transcript after its agent moves into a worktree\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2855\",\n      \"head\": \"7c0727f0e1a1bb29896400a02520c64aec76d55d\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/follow-moved-transcript\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2397/changes/cli/1648\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nClaude Code keeps a session'\"'\"'s transcript under `~/.claude/projects/<working dir>/`. When a session moves into a worktree with `EnterWorktree`, Claude writes the whole transcript under the worktree'\"'\"'s folder. The path its hooks reported at session start never exists, and hooks report the new path only at turn end.\\n\\nIf the agent commits in that first turn, the commit gets an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer, but condensation finds no live transcript at the recorded path. It also finds no stored copy, because no turn has ended yet. So condensation fails with \\\"live\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2844,\n      \"title\": \"Link an agent'\"'\"'s own commit in another repository\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2844\",\n      \"head\": \"71f4466f1a2628ddf36c9ee176a99ed1a113edc9\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/cross-repo-agent-commit-link\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2375/changes/cli/1636\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nFixes #1439 (narrowed to the agent'\"'\"'s own commits).\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nSession state lives per git common dir. A session homed in repo A whose agent commits in another Entire-enabled repo B gets no `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer: B'\"'\"'s hooks only see B'\"'\"'s sessions, and nothing records where the session lives.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\n- **Session-home index.** Turn start records the session'\"'\"'s worktree and owner process in a per-user cache (`session-homes/<id>.json` under `userdirs.CacheRoot`). It'\"'\"'s only a pointer: B asks git for the worktree'\"'\"'s common dir (with `GIT_DIR`/`GIT_INDEX_FILE` scrubb\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2827,\n      \"title\": \"Antigravity: track subagents as tasks on the parent, and count tokens from the transcript\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2827\",\n      \"head\": \"1d6bfce6d610577eacbbf6e7e49783824d600efc\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/antigravity-subagents\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-s'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' 't'\"'\"'s SHA. A quiet `git commit -q` leaves none, so the turn falls back to the default-branch tip, which is often a later commit by someone else. Agents commit quietly most of the time (the reporter measured 253 of 262 commit commands), and a re-import skips turns already imported, so the wrong anchor sticks.\\n\\n## What\\n- From #2911: for each Bash call in a turn that runs `git commit`, `cherry-pick`, `revert`, `merge`, `re\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2966,\n      \"title\": \"fix: edit tracked core.hooksPath shell hooks in place\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2966\",\n      \"head\": \"41b51b292cd76492df21d9a7c5d2456ab440a5f0\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/tracked-hooks-path-in-place\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2965\\n\\n`entire enable` copied a git-tracked `core.hooksPath` shell hook to an untracked `*.pre-entire` file and replaced the tracked path with Entire'\"'\"'s wrapper. Committing that wrapper dropped the project'\"'\"'s hook in every other clone, because the backup was never in the tree.\\n\\nA tracked shell hook is now edited in place. The project'\"'\"'s script stays in the tracked file and runs after Entire. A fresh clone of the committed file still runs the project hook. Hooks in `.git/hooks` and in gitignored directories are still backed up to `*.pre-entire` and chained. A tracked hook that is not a shell script, or is a symbolic link, is left unchanged.\\n\\nOn Windows, a relative `core.hooksPath` whose di\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2964,\n      \"title\": \"soph/service-account-keys\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2964\",\n      \"head\": \"4b9af7ffdc991443c8a414fe31a3945706f59325\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/service-account-keys\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2687/changes/cli/1731\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **High Risk**\\n> Changes how authentication is resolved across the CLI and git helper, adds local private-key storage and STS token minting; server-side enrollment/STS assertion support is not implemented yet.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **experimental** `entire auth service-account` for machine auth without exporting \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2959,\n      \"title\": \"fix(doctor): count Brain'\"'\"'s pre-push wrapper as installed hooks\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2959\",\n      \"head\": \"edb1ccba85a107e6bfd4a64b4278e19d287a7bdd\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-doctor-2949-brain-chain\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2949\\nRelated to #2960\\n\\n@peyton-alt @Soph: I asked on the issue to be assigned (https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2949#issuecomment-6486951877) and haven'\"'\"'t had a reply yet. I'\"'\"'m opening this so it can be reviewed. If you'\"'\"'d rather fix it on the Brain side instead (giving Brain'\"'\"'s wrapper a marker `doctor` recognizes), tell me and I'\"'\"'ll close this.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\n`entire brain connect` installs its own `pre-push` hook. It moves the hook it finds (Entire'\"'\"'s) to `pre-push.pre-entire-brain`, and its own hook ends with:\\n\\n```sh\\nbackup=\\\"$0.pre-entire-brain\\\"\\nif [ -x \\\"$backup\\\" ]; then exec \\\"$backup\\\" \\\"$@\\\"; fi\\n```\\n\\nSo Entire'\"'\"'s hook still runs, with git'\"'\"'s stdin and arguments. But the new `pre-push` does\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2956,\n      \"title\": \"feat(trail): accept pasted trail URLs as selectors\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2956\",\n      \"head\": \"7712dbd9156fe876c14633675d936807dd8f1310\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/trail-url-selectors\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2681/changes/cli/1726\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nUsers and their agents paste trail URLs from the web app (`https://entire.com/gh/acme/-/trails/600`). Project trail commands rejected them with `use a project trail ID or number; select a branch with --branch`. Agent guidance told agents to map the URL by hand and add `--project`; when an agent dropped `--project`, a bare `600` silently resolved in origin'\"'\"'s namespace — a different trail whenever the clone'\"'\"'s origin belongs to another owner.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nThe project trail tree gets a persistent pre-run, `normalizeProjectTrailURLArgs`, that rewrites URL selector\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2954,\n      \"title\": \"trail: only suggest `entire login` on a 401\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2954\",\n      \"head\": \"72b5ed75ef9f5591dca774e6fca8ee2f67d3b81e\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/trail-403-hint\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2676/changes/cli/1724\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\nTrail commands append \\\"run '\"'\"'entire login'\"'\"' to re-authenticate\\\" to every 401 **and** 403 (`checkTrailResponse`). A 403 means the login is valid but lacks access, so logging in again does not help, and the hint sent a user down the wrong path. One cause of such a 403 was the trails API matching GitHub repo names case-sensitively; that is fixed in entire-api separately.\\n\\n## What\\n- 401: unchanged (`run '\"'\"'entire login'\"'\"' to re-authenticate`).\\n- 403: the server'\"'\"'s message alone, as `trail merge` already does.\\n- One test covering both.\\n\\n+26/−2, 2 files.\\n\\n## Verification\\n-\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2952,\n      \"title\": \"Name Cursor'\"'\"'s project directory the way Cursor does\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2952\",\n      \"head\": \"7d1ba720b05f4426bf0d10dac8c00f8ca53eb52f\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/cursor-path-sanitize\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\n`SanitizePathForCursor` builds the name of Cursor'\"'\"'s project directory (`~/.cursor/projects/<name>`) from the repo path, but not the way Cursor does. Cursor collapses runs of non-alphanumeric characters into one `-` and trims `-` from both ends; Entire only stripped the leading `/` and replaced each character separately. Any path with two separators in a row (a `.worktrees` checkout, `/-…` segments) or any Windows path (`C:\\\\…` → `C--…`) got a directory Cursor never writes to.\\n\\nEverything Entire computes from that directory is then wrong: resume restores a transcript where Cursor never reads it, attach and history import look in the wrong place, transcript discovery misses the sess\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2945,\n      \"title\": \"soph/transcript-tool-result-images\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2945\",\n      \"head\": \"35615fe2ddcb4b361b4a124c32a4263f7471d3d9\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/transcript-tool-result-images\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2660/changes/cli/1718\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Additive optional JSON fields and converter output changes; no auth or persistence logic, with broad test coverage per agent.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds an optional **`images`** array on inlined **`tool_use` results** so screenshots and other visuals returned by tools survive conversion instead of bein\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2927,\n      \"title\": \"Keep a running turn'\"'\"'s baseline when Claude reports a background task finished\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2927\",\n      \"head\": \"c7e215100ebcf3d5ab0bad3d2e3a2e8578256d6b\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/turn-start-overlap\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2638/changes/cli/1708\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nClaude Code fires `UserPromptSubmit` for the `<task-notification>` it injects when a background agent or task finishes. When that happens while a turn is still running, the notice is folded into the running turn, but Entire handled it as a new turn start:\\n\\n- `CapturePrePromptState` rewrote the turn'\"'\"'s pre-prompt state, moving the transcript offset forward and retaking the untracked-files snapshot;\\n- the notification was appended to `prompt.txt` and became `LastPrompt`;\\n- `InitializeSession` gave the turn a new `TurnID` and cleared `TurnCheckpointIDs`.\\n\\nAt \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2912,\n      \"title\": \"enable: save --telemetry and --absolute-git-hook-path on a configured repo\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2912\",\n      \"head\": \"f14c55b57e8358e0490426e2d2a3fd41c734d7a8\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/enable-telemetry-flag-saved\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2614/changes/cli/1695\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nOn a repository that is already set up, `entire enable --telemetry=false` (without `--agent`) saved nothing:\\n\\n```\\n$ entire enable --telemetry=false\\nCannot show agent selection in non-interactive mode.\\n...\\n$ cat .entire/settings.json\\n{\\\"enabled\\\":true,\\\"checkpoints\\\":{\\\"primary\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"git-refs\\\"}}}   # no telemetry\\n```\\n\\n`--absolute-git-hook-path` was dropped the same way. The configured-repo path (`runEnableOnConfiguredRepoWithPreflight`) writes strategy and checkpoint-backend flags after agent management, but these two settings were only ever saved by `entir\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2911,\n      \"title\": \"import: anchor turns to commits made while their git command ran\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2911\",\n      \"head\": \"8bc873772ace176a922c9b4dbe66424cb66d983d\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/import-quiet-commit-anchor\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2908.\\n\\n`entire import claude-code` now anchors a turn that committed with `git commit -q` to the commit it made, not to the default-branch tip.\\n\\n### Change\\n\\n- `agentimport/claude.go`: `commitWindowsInRange` records, for each Bash call in a turn that runs `git commit`, `cherry-pick`, `revert`, `merge`, `rebase` or `am`, the span from its `tool_use` line to its `tool_result` line.\\n- `agentimport/turn_anchor.go`: when the turn'\"'\"'s recorded `gitOperation` SHAs anchor nothing, `resolve` picks the newest default-branch ancestor whose committer time falls inside one of those spans. Recorded SHAs keep priority. Ancestors are kept sorted by committer time and searched per span, so a turn costs a\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2910,\n      \"title\": \"settings: keep configure --local from re-enabling a disabled repo\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2910\",\n      \"head\": \"cbfe33732b1ae7af9d7754c061a6ac5a712b801d\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/configure-local-keeps-disabled\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2613/changes/cli/1694\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nIn a repository whose `.entire/settings.json` has `\\\"enabled\\\": false`, running any local setting change, e.g. `entire configure --local --telemetry=false`, turned Entire back on:\\n\\n```\\n$ entire status          → ○ Disabled\\n$ entire configure --local --telemetry=false\\n$ cat .entire/settings.local.json\\n{ \\\"enabled\\\": true, \\\"telemetry\\\": false }\\n$ entire status          → ● Enabled\\n```\\n\\nA settings file without an `\\\"enabled\\\"` key loads as enabled (the default). Every field-update writer loads the target file, changes one field and saves it, so that default was wri\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2872,\n      \"title\": \"Finalize cross-repo checkpoints at turn end\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2872\",\n      \"head\": \"cc0787cb13d8692fc9721be82091d3f0056806be\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/cross-repo-turn-end-finalize\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1665\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nStacked on #2844 (base branch `peyton/cross-repo-agent-commit-link`).\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nIn #2844, a checkpoint an agent'\"'\"'s commit writes in another repository (B) keeps only the transcript up to the commit. Local mid-turn checkpoints are finalized at turn end with the full prompt-to-stop transcript; B'\"'\"'s were not, so they miss everything after the commit, such as the agent'\"'\"'s final reply.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\n- Condensing a foreign commit records the checkpoint and B'\"'\"'s worktree in the home session'\"'\"'s state (`ForeignTurnCheckpoints`, same lifecycle as `TurnCheckpointIDs`).\\n- At turn end, the home'\"'\"'s h\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2868,\n      \"title\": \"fix(status): show enabled external agents\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2868\",\n      \"head\": \"755703a09a4b0c240cfe1f1333ee6aff95105c1b\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/status-discover-external-agents\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1661\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n`entire status` never ran external agent discovery, so the Agents line (and `agents` in `--json`), which reads the agent registry, listed only built-ins even when an `entire-agent-*` plugin had hooks installed and `external_agents` was enabled.\\n\\nThis runs the gated `external.DiscoverAndRegister` at the top of `runStatus`, the same call `entire agent list`, `resume`, `attach` and `explain` use. Status names no agent, so it may only execute plugins in a repo that opted into `external_agents`; the ungated `DiscoverAndRegisterAlways` is reserved for interactive setup.\\n\\nSupersedes #1066\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2867,\n      \"title\": \"fix: never write transcript-less checkpoints from the session sweep\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2867\",\n      \"head\": \"134a284cf2af0c3241d73442212727d26c1a7365\",\n      \"branch\": \"nodo/sweep-transcript-less-checkpoints\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1660\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes checkpoint write/skip behavior for sweep and doctor across worktrees; incorrect handling could drop salvageable sessions or leave stale state, but commit hooks are explicitly unchanged.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Commit-less session salvage (`CondenseSessionByID` for sweep/doctor) now **refuses to write checkpo\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2856,\n      \"title\": \"Stop double-counting tokens around a mid-turn commit\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2856\",\n      \"head\": \"050f4a795da493634e9a8cdaaae77e466b887245\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/midturn-token-double-count\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2398/changes/cli/1649\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nTwo paths count the same model calls in two checkpoints when a commit lands in the middle of a turn.\\n\\n**A. Pending tokens after a mid-turn commit.** The agent commits mid-turn, so a checkpoint stores the turn so far and `TokenStart` moves to the commit'\"'\"'s transcript end. At Stop, `resolveTurnTokenUsage` counts the whole turn from the turn start and adds it to `CheckpointTokenUsage`. If no model call followed the commit, the next condensation'\"'\"'s recount from `TokenStart` is empty and falls back to that pending usage, so it stores the pre-commit calls again. \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2855,\n      \"title\": \"Find a session'\"'\"'s transcript after its agent moves into a worktree\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2855\",\n      \"head\": \"7c0727f0e1a1bb29896400a02520c64aec76d55d\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/follow-moved-transcript\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2397/changes/cli/1648\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nClaude Code keeps a session'\"'\"'s transcript under `~/.claude/projects/<working dir>/`. When a session moves into a worktree with `EnterWorktree`, Claude writes the whole transcript under the worktree'\"'\"'s folder. The path its hooks reported at session start never exists, and hooks report the new path only at turn end.\\n\\nIf the agent commits in that first turn, the commit gets an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer, but condensation finds no live transcript at the recorded path. It also finds no stored copy, because no turn has ended yet. So condensation fails with \\\"live\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2844,\n      \"title\": \"Link an agent'\"'\"'s own commit in another repository\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2844\",\n      \"head\": \"71f4466f1a2628ddf36c9ee176a99ed1a113edc9\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/cross-repo-agent-commit-link\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2375/changes/cli/1636\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nFixes #1439 (narrowed to the agent'\"'\"'s own commits).\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nSession state lives per git common dir. A session homed in repo A whose agent commits in another Entire-enabled repo B gets no `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer: B'\"'\"'s hooks only see B'\"'\"'s sessions, and nothing records where the session lives.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\n- **Session-home index.** Turn start records the session'\"'\"'s worktree and owner process in a per-user cache (`session-homes/<id>.json` under `userdirs.CacheRoot`). It'\"'\"'s only a pointer: B asks git for the worktree'\"'\"'s common dir (with `GIT_DIR`/`GIT_INDEX_FILE` scrubb\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2827,\n      \"title\": \"Antigravity: track subagents as tasks on the parent, and count tokens from the transcript\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2827\",\n      \"head\": \"1d6bfce6d610577eacbbf6e7e49783824d600efc\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/antigravity-subagents\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-s'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":10750}},"started_at_ms":1794842128262,"completed_at_ms":1794842128263}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:28.401Z","ordinal":3015,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-bee10a18-e7bf-4930-9c75-52d12f9505ee","process_id":"44775","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' 'tart -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2343/changes/cli/1619\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nEntire tracks Antigravity (agy) subagents as unrelated top-level sessions and counts agy'\"'\"'s tokens from the wrong source. A live run on main (agy 1.4.2, one subagent):\\n\\n| | Entire on main | agy'\"'\"'s own per-call records |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Parent session | 16,478 in / 134 out, 2 calls | 81,107 / 926, 10 calls |\\n| Subagent | 0 | 18,519 / 254, 3 calls |\\n| Plain session, 4 turns | 95 / 27 | 48,383 / 98 |\\n\\nThe causes:\\n\\n- **Wrong token source.** Entire reads agy'\"'\"'s tokens only from the title/statusline feed, which has three problems:\\n  - the snapshot carrying a turn'\"'\"'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2825,\n      \"title\": \"Record each subagent'\"'\"'s model, split per model\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2825\",\n      \"head\": \"bf8ce3df4f8efbd5449980d8feae54f9b8c20532\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/subagent-token-models\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1617\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What was missing\\n\\nNo agent stored a subagent'\"'\"'s model. Subagent tokens were priced at the parent'\"'\"'s model, even when a subagent ran on a cheaper or more expensive one.\\n\\n## The change\\n\\n`TokenUsage` gains `Model` and `ByModel` (JSON `model` and `by_model`). An entry from one model carries `model`. An entry from several models carries a `by_model` split, which always sums to the entry. A model that was not recorded counts as its own `\\\"\\\"` bucket.\\n\\nWhere the model comes from:\\n\\n- Claude Code: `message.model` in each subagent transcript, including subagents launched by subagents (read in \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2823,\n      \"title\": \"Count OpenCode reasoning tokens once in output totals\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2823\",\n      \"head\": \"b2f247bea56bf0d67841a8f6c227187dfc0d55d5\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/opencode-reasoning-in-totals\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1615\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What was wrong\\n\\nOpenCode 1.3.16 and later store reasoning tokens apart from output tokens. `CalculateTokenUsage` summed `tokens.output` only, so reasoning was dropped. On a local OpenCode database that is an ~8% undercount of output tokens.\\n\\n## The rule\\n\\nPer assistant message, output = `output + reasoning`, unless the message'\"'\"'s `total` equals `input + output + cache`. That identity means reasoning is already inside output (messages written before 1.3.16), so it is not added again. `total` has been recorded since OpenCode 1.1.57. Messages without a `total` (zero-usage messages, or\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2781,\n      \"title\": \"attach: save session state before writing the checkpoint\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2781\",\n      \"head\": \"da631742f3c966b7aef881852cb22d19d4e5606f\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/attach-save-failure\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Follow-up to #2674.\\n\\n## Bug\\n`entire session attach` wrote the checkpoint and only then saved the session state. If that save failed, attach logged a warning and still reported success. The token offset never moved, so the session'\"'\"'s next checkpoint counted the attached tokens a second time. In the repro, turn 2 (7 tokens) was attached and turn 3 (3 tokens) was committed by hooks. The checkpoints held 7 and 10 tokens, 17 in total instead of 10.\\n\\n## Fix\\n- The state is now saved **before** the checkpoint write, which records the tokens as counted first. The save runs under the session lock. If that save fails, attach returns an error and nothing is attached.\\n- If the write fails, the earlier sta\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2778,\n      \"title\": \"entire api: resolve {repo_id} to the processing placement and route to its cell\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2778\",\n      \"head\": \"73df2c32881282aea451e971cbecb931e387ca6e\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/api-repo-id-processing-placement\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1575\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.io) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes authenticated data-plane routing for `entire api --to cell`; wrong cell choice would surface as 404s or cross-region reads, though behavior now matches other repo-scoped CLI commands.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **`entire api --to cell` now picks the entire-api cell from the path and `{repo_id}` placement**, not o\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2760,\n      \"title\": \"copilot-cli: count tokens from session.usage_record\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2760\",\n      \"head\": \"36eecf7fbc42af56a17f31cc907da65add8acf9c\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/copilot-usage-records\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1557\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What Copilot changed\\n\\nCopilot CLI no longer puts `outputTokens` on `assistant.message`. Starting with 1.0.94, it writes a `session.usage_record` for each API call (main agent and subagents) instead. The record carries `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, `cacheReadTokens`, `cacheWriteTokens` and `reasoningTokens`, and joins to its message by `apiCallId`. Local sessions from 1.0.83 through 1.0.93 have neither field, and 1.0.63 and earlier have only `outputTokens`. As a result, every checkpoint from a current Copilot session recorded zero tokens.\\n\\n## Audit\\n\\n| Path | Verdict | Action |\\n|-\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2756,\n      \"title\": \"repo: address repositories by /et/<project>/<repo> path only\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2756\",\n      \"head\": \"45f78931d7e5dbbbe937c94cb5deeb1517b3dc1a\",\n      \"branch\": \"remove-project-flag-repo-commands\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1553\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nRepositories are now addressed by their path and nothing else. `--project` is gone from every `entire repo` verb that acts on one repository, and those verbs refuse a bare repo name or a repo ULID before making any request.\\n\\n| Command | Before | After |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `repo edit`, `repo visibility get`, `repo protection list\\\\|add\\\\|remove` | path, ULID, or bare name + `--project <name\\\\|ULID>` | `/et/<project>/<repo>` only |\\n| `repo delete`, `repo view` | path (an unadvertised ULID still worked) | `/et/<project>/<repo>` only (`view` also keeps `/gh/` and `entire://`) |\\n| \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2754,\n      \"title\": \"Run the strategy package on Windows, and fix what that found\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2754\",\n      \"head\": \"71e8709d7b390a06d3db6ad11a314ce25dd1e44c\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/windows-strategy-suite\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1551\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nFollow-up to #2727 and #2731. The `strategy` package had never run on Windows in CI (`test-windows` only selected tests named `*Windows*`/`*MSYS*`). On a `windows-latest` runner it failed 542 tests and timed out at 20 minutes. This makes it pass and adds it to `test-windows`.\\n\\n## One real bug\\n\\n`entire enable` refused a `core.hooksPath` whose parent directory did not exist yet, such as Husky'\"'\"'s `.husky/_` before `.husky` exists. The guard treated stat'\"'\"'s `ENOTDIR` as \\\"a path component is a file\\\", but on Windows `syscall.ENOTDIR` is `ERROR_PATH_NOT_FOUND`, which a plain missing parent a\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2749,\n      \"title\": \"feat(trail): add retarget command for branch merge targets\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2749\",\n      \"head\": \"5328b8630db12fbd02b7292ffd2f6ae10f0a2a35\",\n      \"branch\": \"alex/trail-retarget-command\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1546\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAdd `entire trail retarget [<trail>] --base <branch>` for stacked work whose previous merge target has merged or been deleted. It changes the selected work'\"'\"'s API metadata without fetching, checking out, rebasing, or pushing local Git branches.\\n\\n- Reuse existing legacy/project Trail selectors, repository routing, and authentication.\\n- Treat unchanged targets as successful no-ops; reject empty/invalid targets, local reflog expressions, self-targets, and branchless/closed/merged work.\\n- Handle short and `refs/heads/` branch spellings consistently; never resolve the old targ\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2747,\n      \"title\": \"fix(git-remote-entire): ignore non-JWT credential helper passwords\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2747\",\n      \"head\": \"99ec1b1c2fe248107fbf969049a9c118ba0f9601\",\n      \"branch\": \"worktree-credential-helper-non-jwt-fallback\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Fix `entire://` failing for anyone with a catch-all git credential helper\\r\\n\\r\\n### What broke\\r\\n\\r\\nSince #2729 (`e1df1fdb9`, in `v0.11.5-nightly.202610120640`), every `entire://` fetch and push fails if the user has a git credential helper that answers every request:\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\nfatal: parse git credential helper token claims: malformed JWT: expected 3 segments, got 1\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n#2729 lets CI pass a token through a git credential helper. `resolveCreds()` runs `git credential fill` with `protocol=entire` and treats any non-empty password as an Entire JWT. If validation fails, that'\"'\"'s fatal, and it never falls back to the saved login.\\r\\n\\r\\nMost helpers (`osxkeychain`, `store`, `gh auth git-credential`) m\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2730,\n      \"title\": \"trail create: say why a create is refused before pushing the branch\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2730\",\n      \"head\": \"6d46d87a07e1fa9f93e3dd7d41ea3c1a633ff7bb\",\n      \"branch\": \"paul/trail-create-trails-disabled\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1539\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nA hackathon attendee ran `entire trail create` on a GitHub mirror whose Trails toggle was never switched on. The trail routes answer \\\"trails off\\\", \\\"no write access\\\" and \\\"unknown repo\\\" with one collapsed 404 `repository not found`, so the failure read as a placement bug, and the branch had already been pushed for the trail by then. Thread: https://entireio.slack.com/archives/C0AP1917D1S/p1791724235416279\\n\\n## What\\n\\n- `trail create` (local and `--repo`) reads `GET /api/v1/repos/{repo_id}` first. Trails off: `trails are not enabled for gh/owner/repo` plus a hint at Settings > Tr\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2724,\n      \"title\": \"Say where install.sh puts entire on Linux\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2724\",\n      \"head\": \"a9de743058e44d784f583a0544646437e6235ecb\",\n      \"branch\": \"firstrun/linux-install-path\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"On a fresh Linux shell, `curl -fsSL https://entire.io/install.sh | bash` succeeds, and the next step, `entire version`, fails with `entire: command not found`. The script installs `entire` and `git-remote-entire` to `~/.local/bin`, which is not on `PATH` in a clean shell.\\n\\nThe Windows section already says where the binaries go and that the installer adds the folder to `PATH`. This PR adds the Linux equivalent after the install block.\\n\\nThank you for Entire. I used it to record every agent session behind every commit while building [FirstRun](https://github.com/HighnessAtharva/firstrun) at neatHack, and FirstRun found this on its own run of the Entire install docs in a clean `python:3.11-slim`\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2715,\n      \"title\": \"feat(checkpoint): upload checkpoints in the background after the user'\"'\"'s push\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2715\",\n      \"head\": \"4793643daafc9d8f420a3dfe8e3b0d127bc2f4b4\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/bound-checkpoint-ref-push\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1530\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n> **Scope:** the main change here is the background checkpoint upload (section 2). Section 1, the bounded chunked push, is also split out on its own as #3018 (fixes #2986, the Windows command-line limit). Once #3018 merges, merging main into this branch drops it from this diff.\\n\\n## Problem\\nThe pre-push hook pushed every queued checkpoint ref in one `git push` with no deadline. #2522 bounded only the per-ref retry fallback. A large backlog, a slow uplink or an unreachable SSH host could hold the user'\"'\"'s own `git push` for minutes or indefinitely, which pushes users toward `--no-verify\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2713,\n      \"title\": \"fix: preserve checkpoint links across message amends\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2713\",\n      \"head\": \"dc3ecf8b1916c550ca10345f165ca089ba052ee1\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/amend-checkpoint-links-rebased\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\nAddresses the CLI-side linkage loss in #2637. `git commit --amend -m/-F` reaches `prepare-commit-msg` as source `message`, so the hook cannot distinguish it from an ordinary commit. After the amend, `post-rewrite` provides the old/new SHA pair.\\n\\n- Record checkpoint-side `linked_commits` for associations missing from the amended commit'\"'\"'s trailers, including links inherited from an earlier trailerless amend.\\n- Leave code commits and stored transcripts untouched. Repair does not require live session state and does not re-condense old checkpoints.\\n- Support the write across git-branch, git-refs, filesystem mirrors, and ID-kind fallback routing. Preserve links through later metadata u\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2684,\n      \"title\": \"Add strategy_options.sync_prompts to keep prompts out of checkpoints\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2684\",\n      \"head\": \"d4e85d5721cf7b63de57fe846770241b9651e85d\",\n      \"branch\": \"disable-prompt-sync\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\nAdds `strategy_options.sync_prompts` (default `true`). When set to `false`, prompt-bearing content is kept out of committed checkpoints, so it never reaches the checkpoint remote. Checkpoint metadata, attribution, files touched, token usage, and metrics are still recorded and synced.\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"strategy_options\\\": { \\\"sync_prompts\\\": false } }\\n```\\n\\n## What is omitted\\n\\n- `prompt.txt`\\n- `full.jsonl` / `transcript.jsonl` and their image assets (also `TranscriptPath`, which the writer would otherwise re-read from disk)\\n- subagent transcripts and task descriptions (`task.json` records `transcript omitted by settings`)\\n- AI summaries (`SessionSummary` backfills are dropped)\\n- review prom\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2683,\n      \"title\": \"refactor(trails): isolate legacy and project trail models\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2683\",\n      \"head\": \"cb96efebdba5d0ae431a615313f55202a8f58cd8\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/project-trails-split\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1504\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nStacked on #2659 (`dip/project-trails-cli`). Refactor coexistence of legacy repository-scoped and opt-in project-scoped trails around one `trailMode` seam. The same branch'\"'\"'s full change against `main` is #2682; project intent is tracked in trail #2074.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- Choose the model once in `newTrailCmdForMode`; keep model-specific intent commands in separate command trees.\\n- Share checkout, resume, findings, watch, and approval workflows through mode-specific working-context resolution and help.\\n- Restore legacy help and local handling of unnumbered trails while keepin\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2678,\n      \"title\": \"Wait for Claude Code'\"'\"'s final message instead of the stop marker\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2678\",\n      \"head\": \"e7b84035e1993294337be1392bf61f9696fe5c28\",\n      \"branch\": \"victor/stop-sentinel-comment\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1499\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nFollow-up to #2656.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nWhen a Claude Code turn ends, `waitForTranscriptFlush` waits for the async transcript writes to finish before Entire reads the file. Its fast path looked for a `hook_progress` entry naming our stop hook (`hooks claude-code stop`).\\n\\n- **The marker used to work.** Claude Code 2.1.78 wrote that entry when a hook started (see `transcript/compact/testdata/claude_full.jsonl`).\\n- **It no longer matches.** None of the 113 local transcripts on 2.1.281–2.1.291 contain a `hook_progress` entry. Hooks are now recorded only after they finish (`system`/`stop_hook_s\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2669,\n      \"title\": \"fix(opf): push the v1 commit the OPF rewrite verified, not the branch tip\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2669\",\n      \"head\": \"c97efe2028da503bab827deba79e612d12752bd9\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/opf-v1-pinned-push\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1491\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nOn the `git-branch` backend with the OpenAI Privacy Filter (OPF) on, pre-push rewrites the unpushed `entire/checkpoints/v1` commits and then pushes v1 **by name**. `pushRefIfNeeded` re-reads the branch, and `git push` resolves it again. If another session appends a checkpoint between the rewrite and the push, that untrailered, unscanned commit becomes the pushed tip.\\n\\nThis is on main today. It was found in an adversarial review of the OPF PRs (#2533, #2631) and gets more likely once checkpoints are delivered in the background.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n- The OPF rewrite'\"'\"'s returned hash i\"\n    },\n    {\n'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' 'tart -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2343/changes/cli/1619\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nEntire tracks Antigravity (agy) subagents as unrelated top-level sessions and counts agy'\"'\"'s tokens from the wrong source. A live run on main (agy 1.4.2, one subagent):\\n\\n| | Entire on main | agy'\"'\"'s own per-call records |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Parent session | 16,478 in / 134 out, 2 calls | 81,107 / 926, 10 calls |\\n| Subagent | 0 | 18,519 / 254, 3 calls |\\n| Plain session, 4 turns | 95 / 27 | 48,383 / 98 |\\n\\nThe causes:\\n\\n- **Wrong token source.** Entire reads agy'\"'\"'s tokens only from the title/statusline feed, which has three problems:\\n  - the snapshot carrying a turn'\"'\"'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2825,\n      \"title\": \"Record each subagent'\"'\"'s model, split per model\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2825\",\n      \"head\": \"bf8ce3df4f8efbd5449980d8feae54f9b8c20532\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/subagent-token-models\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1617\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What was missing\\n\\nNo agent stored a subagent'\"'\"'s model. Subagent tokens were priced at the parent'\"'\"'s model, even when a subagent ran on a cheaper or more expensive one.\\n\\n## The change\\n\\n`TokenUsage` gains `Model` and `ByModel` (JSON `model` and `by_model`). An entry from one model carries `model`. An entry from several models carries a `by_model` split, which always sums to the entry. A model that was not recorded counts as its own `\\\"\\\"` bucket.\\n\\nWhere the model comes from:\\n\\n- Claude Code: `message.model` in each subagent transcript, including subagents launched by subagents (read in \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2823,\n      \"title\": \"Count OpenCode reasoning tokens once in output totals\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2823\",\n      \"head\": \"b2f247bea56bf0d67841a8f6c227187dfc0d55d5\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/opencode-reasoning-in-totals\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1615\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What was wrong\\n\\nOpenCode 1.3.16 and later store reasoning tokens apart from output tokens. `CalculateTokenUsage` summed `tokens.output` only, so reasoning was dropped. On a local OpenCode database that is an ~8% undercount of output tokens.\\n\\n## The rule\\n\\nPer assistant message, output = `output + reasoning`, unless the message'\"'\"'s `total` equals `input + output + cache`. That identity means reasoning is already inside output (messages written before 1.3.16), so it is not added again. `total` has been recorded since OpenCode 1.1.57. Messages without a `total` (zero-usage messages, or\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2781,\n      \"title\": \"attach: save session state before writing the checkpoint\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2781\",\n      \"head\": \"da631742f3c966b7aef881852cb22d19d4e5606f\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/attach-save-failure\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Follow-up to #2674.\\n\\n## Bug\\n`entire session attach` wrote the checkpoint and only then saved the session state. If that save failed, attach logged a warning and still reported success. The token offset never moved, so the session'\"'\"'s next checkpoint counted the attached tokens a second time. In the repro, turn 2 (7 tokens) was attached and turn 3 (3 tokens) was committed by hooks. The checkpoints held 7 and 10 tokens, 17 in total instead of 10.\\n\\n## Fix\\n- The state is now saved **before** the checkpoint write, which records the tokens as counted first. The save runs under the session lock. If that save fails, attach returns an error and nothing is attached.\\n- If the write fails, the earlier sta\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2778,\n      \"title\": \"entire api: resolve {repo_id} to the processing placement and route to its cell\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2778\",\n      \"head\": \"73df2c32881282aea451e971cbecb931e387ca6e\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/api-repo-id-processing-placement\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1575\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.io) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes authenticated data-plane routing for `entire api --to cell`; wrong cell choice would surface as 404s or cross-region reads, though behavior now matches other repo-scoped CLI commands.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **`entire api --to cell` now picks the entire-api cell from the path and `{repo_id}` placement**, not o\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2760,\n      \"title\": \"copilot-cli: count tokens from session.usage_record\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2760\",\n      \"head\": \"36eecf7fbc42af56a17f31cc907da65add8acf9c\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/copilot-usage-records\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1557\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What Copilot changed\\n\\nCopilot CLI no longer puts `outputTokens` on `assistant.message`. Starting with 1.0.94, it writes a `session.usage_record` for each API call (main agent and subagents) instead. The record carries `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, `cacheReadTokens`, `cacheWriteTokens` and `reasoningTokens`, and joins to its message by `apiCallId`. Local sessions from 1.0.83 through 1.0.93 have neither field, and 1.0.63 and earlier have only `outputTokens`. As a result, every checkpoint from a current Copilot session recorded zero tokens.\\n\\n## Audit\\n\\n| Path | Verdict | Action |\\n|-\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2756,\n      \"title\": \"repo: address repositories by /et/<project>/<repo> path only\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2756\",\n      \"head\": \"45f78931d7e5dbbbe937c94cb5deeb1517b3dc1a\",\n      \"branch\": \"remove-project-flag-repo-commands\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1553\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nRepositories are now addressed by their path and nothing else. `--project` is gone from every `entire repo` verb that acts on one repository, and those verbs refuse a bare repo name or a repo ULID before making any request.\\n\\n| Command | Before | After |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `repo edit`, `repo visibility get`, `repo protection list\\\\|add\\\\|remove` | path, ULID, or bare name + `--project <name\\\\|ULID>` | `/et/<project>/<repo>` only |\\n| `repo delete`, `repo view` | path (an unadvertised ULID still worked) | `/et/<project>/<repo>` only (`view` also keeps `/gh/` and `entire://`) |\\n| \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2754,\n      \"title\": \"Run the strategy package on Windows, and fix what that found\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2754\",\n      \"head\": \"71e8709d7b390a06d3db6ad11a314ce25dd1e44c\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/windows-strategy-suite\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1551\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nFollow-up to #2727 and #2731. The `strategy` package had never run on Windows in CI (`test-windows` only selected tests named `*Windows*`/`*MSYS*`). On a `windows-latest` runner it failed 542 tests and timed out at 20 minutes. This makes it pass and adds it to `test-windows`.\\n\\n## One real bug\\n\\n`entire enable` refused a `core.hooksPath` whose parent directory did not exist yet, such as Husky'\"'\"'s `.husky/_` before `.husky` exists. The guard treated stat'\"'\"'s `ENOTDIR` as \\\"a path component is a file\\\", but on Windows `syscall.ENOTDIR` is `ERROR_PATH_NOT_FOUND`, which a plain missing parent a\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2749,\n      \"title\": \"feat(trail): add retarget command for branch merge targets\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2749\",\n      \"head\": \"5328b8630db12fbd02b7292ffd2f6ae10f0a2a35\",\n      \"branch\": \"alex/trail-retarget-command\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1546\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAdd `entire trail retarget [<trail>] --base <branch>` for stacked work whose previous merge target has merged or been deleted. It changes the selected work'\"'\"'s API metadata without fetching, checking out, rebasing, or pushing local Git branches.\\n\\n- Reuse existing legacy/project Trail selectors, repository routing, and authentication.\\n- Treat unchanged targets as successful no-ops; reject empty/invalid targets, local reflog expressions, self-targets, and branchless/closed/merged work.\\n- Handle short and `refs/heads/` branch spellings consistently; never resolve the old targ\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2747,\n      \"title\": \"fix(git-remote-entire): ignore non-JWT credential helper passwords\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2747\",\n      \"head\": \"99ec1b1c2fe248107fbf969049a9c118ba0f9601\",\n      \"branch\": \"worktree-credential-helper-non-jwt-fallback\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Fix `entire://` failing for anyone with a catch-all git credential helper\\r\\n\\r\\n### What broke\\r\\n\\r\\nSince #2729 (`e1df1fdb9`, in `v0.11.5-nightly.202610120640`), every `entire://` fetch and push fails if the user has a git credential helper that answers every request:\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\nfatal: parse git credential helper token claims: malformed JWT: expected 3 segments, got 1\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n#2729 lets CI pass a token through a git credential helper. `resolveCreds()` runs `git credential fill` with `protocol=entire` and treats any non-empty password as an Entire JWT. If validation fails, that'\"'\"'s fatal, and it never falls back to the saved login.\\r\\n\\r\\nMost helpers (`osxkeychain`, `store`, `gh auth git-credential`) m\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2730,\n      \"title\": \"trail create: say why a create is refused before pushing the branch\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2730\",\n      \"head\": \"6d46d87a07e1fa9f93e3dd7d41ea3c1a633ff7bb\",\n      \"branch\": \"paul/trail-create-trails-disabled\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1539\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nA hackathon attendee ran `entire trail create` on a GitHub mirror whose Trails toggle was never switched on. The trail routes answer \\\"trails off\\\", \\\"no write access\\\" and \\\"unknown repo\\\" with one collapsed 404 `repository not found`, so the failure read as a placement bug, and the branch had already been pushed for the trail by then. Thread: https://entireio.slack.com/archives/C0AP1917D1S/p1791724235416279\\n\\n## What\\n\\n- `trail create` (local and `--repo`) reads `GET /api/v1/repos/{repo_id}` first. Trails off: `trails are not enabled for gh/owner/repo` plus a hint at Settings > Tr\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2724,\n      \"title\": \"Say where install.sh puts entire on Linux\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2724\",\n      \"head\": \"a9de743058e44d784f583a0544646437e6235ecb\",\n      \"branch\": \"firstrun/linux-install-path\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"On a fresh Linux shell, `curl -fsSL https://entire.io/install.sh | bash` succeeds, and the next step, `entire version`, fails with `entire: command not found`. The script installs `entire` and `git-remote-entire` to `~/.local/bin`, which is not on `PATH` in a clean shell.\\n\\nThe Windows section already says where the binaries go and that the installer adds the folder to `PATH`. This PR adds the Linux equivalent after the install block.\\n\\nThank you for Entire. I used it to record every agent session behind every commit while building [FirstRun](https://github.com/HighnessAtharva/firstrun) at neatHack, and FirstRun found this on its own run of the Entire install docs in a clean `python:3.11-slim`\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2715,\n      \"title\": \"feat(checkpoint): upload checkpoints in the background after the user'\"'\"'s push\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2715\",\n      \"head\": \"4793643daafc9d8f420a3dfe8e3b0d127bc2f4b4\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/bound-checkpoint-ref-push\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1530\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n> **Scope:** the main change here is the background checkpoint upload (section 2). Section 1, the bounded chunked push, is also split out on its own as #3018 (fixes #2986, the Windows command-line limit). Once #3018 merges, merging main into this branch drops it from this diff.\\n\\n## Problem\\nThe pre-push hook pushed every queued checkpoint ref in one `git push` with no deadline. #2522 bounded only the per-ref retry fallback. A large backlog, a slow uplink or an unreachable SSH host could hold the user'\"'\"'s own `git push` for minutes or indefinitely, which pushes users toward `--no-verify\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2713,\n      \"title\": \"fix: preserve checkpoint links across message amends\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2713\",\n      \"head\": \"dc3ecf8b1916c550ca10345f165ca089ba052ee1\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/amend-checkpoint-links-rebased\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\nAddresses the CLI-side linkage loss in #2637. `git commit --amend -m/-F` reaches `prepare-commit-msg` as source `message`, so the hook cannot distinguish it from an ordinary commit. After the amend, `post-rewrite` provides the old/new SHA pair.\\n\\n- Record checkpoint-side `linked_commits` for associations missing from the amended commit'\"'\"'s trailers, including links inherited from an earlier trailerless amend.\\n- Leave code commits and stored transcripts untouched. Repair does not require live session state and does not re-condense old checkpoints.\\n- Support the write across git-branch, git-refs, filesystem mirrors, and ID-kind fallback routing. Preserve links through later metadata u\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2684,\n      \"title\": \"Add strategy_options.sync_prompts to keep prompts out of checkpoints\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2684\",\n      \"head\": \"d4e85d5721cf7b63de57fe846770241b9651e85d\",\n      \"branch\": \"disable-prompt-sync\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\nAdds `strategy_options.sync_prompts` (default `true`). When set to `false`, prompt-bearing content is kept out of committed checkpoints, so it never reaches the checkpoint remote. Checkpoint metadata, attribution, files touched, token usage, and metrics are still recorded and synced.\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"strategy_options\\\": { \\\"sync_prompts\\\": false } }\\n```\\n\\n## What is omitted\\n\\n- `prompt.txt`\\n- `full.jsonl` / `transcript.jsonl` and their image assets (also `TranscriptPath`, which the writer would otherwise re-read from disk)\\n- subagent transcripts and task descriptions (`task.json` records `transcript omitted by settings`)\\n- AI summaries (`SessionSummary` backfills are dropped)\\n- review prom\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2683,\n      \"title\": \"refactor(trails): isolate legacy and project trail models\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2683\",\n      \"head\": \"cb96efebdba5d0ae431a615313f55202a8f58cd8\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/project-trails-split\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1504\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nStacked on #2659 (`dip/project-trails-cli`). Refactor coexistence of legacy repository-scoped and opt-in project-scoped trails around one `trailMode` seam. The same branch'\"'\"'s full change against `main` is #2682; project intent is tracked in trail #2074.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- Choose the model once in `newTrailCmdForMode`; keep model-specific intent commands in separate command trees.\\n- Share checkout, resume, findings, watch, and approval workflows through mode-specific working-context resolution and help.\\n- Restore legacy help and local handling of unnumbered trails while keepin\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2678,\n      \"title\": \"Wait for Claude Code'\"'\"'s final message instead of the stop marker\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2678\",\n      \"head\": \"e7b84035e1993294337be1392bf61f9696fe5c28\",\n      \"branch\": \"victor/stop-sentinel-comment\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1499\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nFollow-up to #2656.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nWhen a Claude Code turn ends, `waitForTranscriptFlush` waits for the async transcript writes to finish before Entire reads the file. Its fast path looked for a `hook_progress` entry naming our stop hook (`hooks claude-code stop`).\\n\\n- **The marker used to work.** Claude Code 2.1.78 wrote that entry when a hook started (see `transcript/compact/testdata/claude_full.jsonl`).\\n- **It no longer matches.** None of the 113 local transcripts on 2.1.281–2.1.291 contain a `hook_progress` entry. Hooks are now recorded only after they finish (`system`/`stop_hook_s\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2669,\n      \"title\": \"fix(opf): push the v1 commit the OPF rewrite verified, not the branch tip\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2669\",\n      \"head\": \"c97efe2028da503bab827deba79e612d12752bd9\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/opf-v1-pinned-push\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1491\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nOn the `git-branch` backend with the OpenAI Privacy Filter (OPF) on, pre-push rewrites the unpushed `entire/checkpoints/v1` commits and then pushes v1 **by name**. `pushRefIfNeeded` re-reads the branch, and `git push` resolves it again. If another session appends a checkpoint between the rewrite and the push, that untrailered, unscanned commit becomes the pushed tip.\\n\\nThis is on main today. It was found in an adversarial review of the OPF PRs (#2533, #2631) and gets more likely once checkpoints are delivered in the background.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n- The OPF rewrite'\"'\"'s returned hash i\"\n    },\n    {\n'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":10500}},"started_at_ms":1794842128400,"completed_at_ms":1794842128401}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:28.550Z","ordinal":3016,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-fdbf812f-c90f-4a8b-846e-aaa0c69eb627","process_id":"83504","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' '      \"number\": 2654,\n      \"title\": \"Resume a session without a branch, and share one to be resumed\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2654\",\n      \"head\": \"1cd760fc39986664a9d799db13984a9c5c220622\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/session-share\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1478\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.io) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Publishes session transcripts to remotes and broadens resume target resolution; push/redaction gates and strict session identification mitigate misuse, but delivery and OPF paths are security-sensitive.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **`entire session share`** to snapshot a session (via the same path as `checkpoint crea\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2643,\n      \"title\": \"hooks: keep Husky v9 hooks running when Entire chains them\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2643\",\n      \"head\": \"b5651f965dbea7901e6c0e12d9775b776c2c5370\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/husky-v9-chain\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1468\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nFound while investigating hook chaining (not user-reported). Husky v9 sets `core.hooksPath=.husky/_` and writes one wrapper per hook there (`. \\\"$(dirname \\\"$0\\\")/h\\\"`, or `. \\\"${0%/*}/h\\\"` in 9.0.1–9.1.0). Husky'\"'\"'s `h` finds the user'\"'\"'s hook from the wrapper'\"'\"'s own file name. `entire enable` renames each wrapper to `<hook>.pre-entire` and *executes* it from its chain, so `h` looks for `.husky/<hook>.pre-entire`, finds nothing, and exits 0: **every Husky hook silently stops running** (a failing `.husky/pre-push` no longer blocks the push; `commit-msg` checks are skipped), and `en\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2642,\n      \"title\": \"fix: capture growing sessions on later attaches\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2642\",\n      \"head\": \"35509341f8f6f21d8d64e0fc50764c83c3275cf3\",\n      \"branch\": \"nodo/fix-attach-growing-session\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1467\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nRepeated `entire session attach` reused a session'\"'\"'s `LastCheckpointID` and returned before reading its updated transcript. An agent started at a workspace root could therefore continue the same conversation across several repository commits, but every attach after the first linked the initial conversation snapshot.\\n\\nAttachment now checks whether HEAD'\"'\"'s checkpoint already contains the requested session. A new commit captures the latest transcript; an existing checkpoint with other sessions receives the session; repeating attach to an already-attached commit preserves its snapshot, ev\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2640,\n      \"title\": \"hooks: stop a chained pre-push from swallowing Entire'\"'\"'s failure\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2640\",\n      \"head\": \"84a2d4775b31f9762913ac4183c7b5fb150ab45e\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/pre-push-chain-exit-code\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\nWhen `entire enable` finds an existing pre-push hook (husky, lefthook, git-lfs, a custom script), it backs it up to `pre-push.pre-entire` and chains to it after Entire'\"'\"'s own invocation. The script'\"'\"'s exit status was then the chained hook'\"'\"'s. Entire'\"'\"'s pre-push deliberately fails to abort `git push` when OPF refuses to redact, so with a chain in place a refusal was silently ignored whenever the user'\"'\"'s own hook passed.\\n\\n\\n## Who is affected\\n\\nOnly repos with **OPF enabled** that had a pre-push hook before `entire enable`. Without OPF, Entire'\"'\"'s pre-push does not exit non-zero: every error-returning branch of `prePush` is inside `if redact.OPFEnabled()`, and checkpoint push failures are f\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2635,\n      \"title\": \"Secure Enclave-protected tokens\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2635\",\n      \"head\": \"ea5363c6ae15982b7771a4de47234d8d594b315f\",\n      \"branch\": \"paul/se-protected-tokens\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1461\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n# Description\\r\\n\\r\\nFor old-timey SSH keys, i really like how [Secretive.app](https://github.com/maxgoedjen/secretive/) works.  I can require a TouchID unlock every time my SSH key is needed.\\r\\n\\r\\nI'\"'\"'m wondering if we can bring something like that into Entire, optionally, for paranoid users.  Every time an `entire` or `git-remote-entire` process tries to talk to our Git data plane or control plane, we can throw up an auth gate:\\r\\n\\r\\n<img width=\\\"282\\\" height=\\\"379\\\" alt=\\\"image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/81ea462c-3552-428f-a329-9e13021f41c7\\\" />\\r\\n\\r\\n## Limitations\\r\\n\\r\\n- The en\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2634,\n      \"title\": \"Linked worktrees use the main worktree'\"'\"'s local settings\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2634\",\n      \"head\": \"266d063be0069da286827ace1e875f1e4e3f358c\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/worktree-local-settings\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2003/changes/cli/1460\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Linked worktrees use the main worktree'\"'\"'s local settings\\n\\n**Problem.** `git worktree add` creates a worktree without the gitignored `.entire/settings.local.json`, so every developer-only setting stops applying there. Reproduced with real binaries on main:\\n- **External agent** (`external_agents: true` is honored only from the local file): in the worktree every hook fails with `unknown agent \\\"roger-roger\\\" (not found as built-in or external plugin)`, no session is recorded, and the worktree'\"'\"'s commit links to the **main tree'\"'\"'s** live session when both touched the same \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2633,\n      \"title\": \"auth: fail closed when a jurisdiction'\"'\"'s clusters disagree on apiUrl\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2633\",\n      \"head\": \"3c858122345419f9eb02bdfe80c00605b48a6a3e\",\n      \"branch\": \"nina/cor-1896-fail-closed-home-cell-pick\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1459\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nentiredb#4129 (COR-1896) derives `Cluster.apiUrl` per cell, so two clusters in one jurisdiction can advertise different values. `resolveCellAPIBaseURL` — the home-cell pick behind `/me/*` routing and `--jurisdiction` — assumed they never differ and fell back to the first match when no default cluster matched, which would route home-scoped reads to an arbitrary cell with no error. Today the default-cluster preference masks it (the default sits in the home cell); moving the default, or the default row losing its `apiUrl`, would misroute silently. Same fix as entire.io#4889 mak\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2631,\n      \"title\": \"feat(opf): scan in the background so git push never waits on the privacy filter\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2631\",\n      \"head\": \"1e56a1f3287803161534ee0ef5ee5f921a63b177\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/opf-scan-worker\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1457\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nStacked on #2533, which merges first; this PR depends on it.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nOPF inference is slow, about 1.14 s per KB of prose on CPU, so one real session is minutes to hours of model time. The model ran inside the pre-push hook, which left two bad options. With the old 2 MiB cap, every real session was refused, so OPF could not ship real checkpoints at all. With the cap raised, `git push` would wait for the whole scan, which on `git-branch` (the default backend) could take hours.\\n\\n## Result\\n\\n`git push` never waits on the model, on either backend. Checkpoints still reach the remote o\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2621,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): break shared-owner ties by environment and phase, not recency\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2621\",\n      \"head\": \"417b43a046a0df1d1a65ac571c4f18e5cfa0841b\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/codex-daemon-session-resolution\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2612\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nSince Codex 0.157 the TUI runs its sessions in one `codex app-server --managed-daemon`, so each of them records the daemon as its owner. A commit made by any of them matches all of them at the same ancestry depth, and `isNearerOwner` broke that tie by the latest `LastInteractionTime`, which moves at turn boundaries:\\n\\n- commit linking guest-condensed a live session from another worktree into the commit;\\n- caller resolution returned that same session as `ancestry`, so `IsCaller()` held, even while `CODEX_SESSION_ID` named the committing session. The post-commit hook logs under that session ID.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\nCommit linking and caller resolution now share one rule, `pickO\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2615,\n      \"title\": \"Withdraw history import until it is redesigned\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2615\",\n      \"head\": \"0349d5d1eb58fe18ccc30d88bd2e706260df625c\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/remove-history-import\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1445\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nHistory import (`entire import <agent>` and the first-time `entire enable` offer) creates checkpoints that nothing references. No commit carries their trailer, so every consumer has to enumerate them separately. That falls apart on git-refs. A fresh clone lists no imports (the case #2605 works on). Telling an import apart from a native checkpoint by name alone requires either fetching refs to check, or encoding a marker into IDs or ref names. Import'\"'\"'s idempotency depends on derived IDs. We reviewed six designs plus two follow-ups adversarially, and none holds up without a bi\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2613,\n      \"title\": \"Show monitors and runners in trail show (for Fried Green Loops)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2613\",\n      \"head\": \"3d673a83718ff3e7691d6ca915c6da557c68a395\",\n      \"branch\": \"trail-show-monitors\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1443\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.io) after CI was requested for the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2611,\n      \"title\": \"fix(git): protect ignored files during branch checkout\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2611\",\n      \"head\": \"cf71f02f471eae3085c4e5f59c44e50a122bc451\",\n      \"branch\": \"codex/issue-2604-safe-checkout\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\n- pass `--no-overwrite-ignore` through the shared branch-checkout helper so a target tree cannot silently replace ignored, untracked local files\\r\\n- add helper-level and real-binary resume regressions that verify checkout refusal, unchanged branch state, and byte-for-byte file preservation\\r\\n- document the ignored-file checkout safety requirement\\r\\n\\r\\nFixes #2604.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Testing\\r\\n\\r\\n- focused checkout-helper regression\\r\\n- adjacent resume integration tests\\r\\n- repository formatting, module, mise, secret-pattern, ShellCheck, and full Go lint checks\\r\\n- both CLI builds\\r\\n- six-case synthetic post-fix matrix covering repository ignores, `core.excludesFile`, remote-only resume, and existing \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2605,\n      \"title\": \"List remote-only imported checkpoints in fresh git-refs clones\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2605\",\n      \"head\": \"2eae3f976cbd218b17a5a6233a21277ecced2c73\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/list-remote-imported-checkpoints\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1438\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\n## Problem\\r\\n\\r\\n`entire checkpoint list` shows 0 checkpoints in a fresh clone of a git-refs repo whose checkpoints are all imported, although `git ls-remote origin '\"'\"'refs/entire/checkpoints/*'\"'\"'` shows them.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Root cause\\r\\n\\r\\nNot the remote selection: `ListCheckpointRefsOnRemote` already queries origin when no `checkpoint_remote` is set (the #1771 description is outdated there).\\r\\n\\r\\nImported checkpoints carry no commit trailer, so they only surface through `getImportedPendingCheckpoints`. That function opened a second store and listed **local refs only**. Remote-discovered stubs wou\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2589,\n      \"title\": \"feat(opencode): support OpenCode 2 with V1 fallback\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2589\",\n      \"head\": \"c7d0c8549e332767ffc3e57aa2178c5ecc727c31\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/opencode-v2-dual\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\nMakes the OpenCode integration work on OpenCode 2 while keeping OpenCode 1 working from the same generated plugin. Fixes #2588.\\n\\nOpenCode 2 is a hard break in two places:\\n\\n1. It loads a default plugin definition with `id` + `setup`/`effect`, and rejects V1 hook-map plugins with `PluginModule.LoadError: Plugin must export a default definition with an id and an effect or setup function`.\\n2. It moved export/import under `opencode session`; the V1 `opencode export` prints a help page and exits 0.\\n\\nThis builds on the approach in #2397 (thanks @aryasaatvik) but keeps OpenCode 1 plugin support instead of dropping it.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n**Plugin** (`entire_plugin.ts` + committed dogfood copy)\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2586,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): preserve non-ASCII staged filenames\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2586\",\n      \"head\": \"cd98162248e63f0ceae40b61f556b583b7dcae7e\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/2398-non-ascii-staged-files\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nFixes #2398.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Preserve non-ASCII staged filenames during checkpoint linking.\\r\\n* Use Git'\"'\"'s NUL-delimited output format to avoid C-escaped filenames.\\r\\n* Add a regression test covering non-ASCII filenames such as `café.go`.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Problem\\r\\n\\r\\nWhen Git is configured with `core.quotePath=true`, commands such as:\\r\\n\\r\\n```text\\r\\ngit diff --cached --name-only\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\ncan return non-ASCII filenames in a C-escaped form instead of their literal path.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor example, `café.go` may be returned as an escaped filename. Entire then compares this value against the literal filename stored in `SessionState.FilesTouched`, causing the overlap check to fail and potentially preventing the `Entire-Chec\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2577,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): stop carrying forward files a skipped-hook commit already took\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2577\",\n      \"head\": \"84e9735a2754da65e80089633f28abe6788d624d\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/skipped-commit-carry-forward\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1416\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\nA commit made with every Git hook skipped (`LEFTHOOK=0` under the Lefthook integration in #2388, a GUI client with no hooks, a crashed hook) is invisible to Entire. The session'\"'\"'s files from that turn land in HEAD, but the next hooked commit'\"'\"'s diff doesn'\"'\"'t contain them, so `filesWithRemainingAgentChanges` counts them as uncommitted and `carryForwardToNewShadowBranch` moves them onto a fresh shadow branch. No later commit ever contains them, so it repeats on **every** commit: `entire checkpoint list` shows a permanent `[temporary] carry forward: uncommitted session files` \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2576,\n      \"title\": \"fix(cli): keep records for Claude Code default background subagents\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2576\",\n      \"head\": \"367a00c5e8cc4b4c2ff64b2565c06ccd0bb30d7a\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/claude-code-default-background-subagents\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2556\\r\\n\\r\\nClaude Code launches subagents in the background by default and reports the launch as async (`tool_response.status: \\\"async_launched\\\"`,`tool_response.isAsync: true`) even when `run_in_background` is omitted from the Task `tool_input`. Detection keyed only on the flag, so that omitted-flag launch was treated as a finished foreground task and its record was dropped at launch; SubagentStop then found no marker and the subagent'\"'\"'s transcript never landed under the checkpoint'\"'\"'s `tasks/`.\\r\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2568,\n      \"title\": \"auth: refuse cross-site cells; cache a 401 trails probe (ENT-2573)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2568\",\n      \"head\": \"b4549b975a5d798b5f3377348f3b2e0e1e88e0a9\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/ent-2573-cli-sends-prod-issued-login-jwts-to-staging-entire-api-cells\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1408\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nFixes the CLI half of [ENT-2573](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/ENT-2573). Staging entire-api cells logged 17 `token_forgery` / `untrusted_issuer` events from prod-issued login JWTs. APM user agents show 13 came from `entire-cli/0.10.5`/`0.10.6`, whose data API auto-selected a saved prod login while routing to the staging cell (already removed in v0.11.0 by 455f8d5e47). The other 4 were `curl`. This PR adds defense in depth so a mismatched login and cell can'\"'\"'t reach the network again, and stops the retry loop that turned one misconfigured machine into repeated alarms.\\n\\n## Changes\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2564,\n      \"title\": \"Make AGENTS.md the real instruction file, drop CLAUDE.md\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2564\",\n      \"head\": \"158a8076976f1b2b51084bc8a01a31336e183'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' '      \"number\": 2654,\n      \"title\": \"Resume a session without a branch, and share one to be resumed\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2654\",\n      \"head\": \"1cd760fc39986664a9d799db13984a9c5c220622\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/session-share\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1478\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.io) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Publishes session transcripts to remotes and broadens resume target resolution; push/redaction gates and strict session identification mitigate misuse, but delivery and OPF paths are security-sensitive.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **`entire session share`** to snapshot a session (via the same path as `checkpoint crea\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2643,\n      \"title\": \"hooks: keep Husky v9 hooks running when Entire chains them\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2643\",\n      \"head\": \"b5651f965dbea7901e6c0e12d9775b776c2c5370\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/husky-v9-chain\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1468\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nFound while investigating hook chaining (not user-reported). Husky v9 sets `core.hooksPath=.husky/_` and writes one wrapper per hook there (`. \\\"$(dirname \\\"$0\\\")/h\\\"`, or `. \\\"${0%/*}/h\\\"` in 9.0.1–9.1.0). Husky'\"'\"'s `h` finds the user'\"'\"'s hook from the wrapper'\"'\"'s own file name. `entire enable` renames each wrapper to `<hook>.pre-entire` and *executes* it from its chain, so `h` looks for `.husky/<hook>.pre-entire`, finds nothing, and exits 0: **every Husky hook silently stops running** (a failing `.husky/pre-push` no longer blocks the push; `commit-msg` checks are skipped), and `en\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2642,\n      \"title\": \"fix: capture growing sessions on later attaches\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2642\",\n      \"head\": \"35509341f8f6f21d8d64e0fc50764c83c3275cf3\",\n      \"branch\": \"nodo/fix-attach-growing-session\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1467\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nRepeated `entire session attach` reused a session'\"'\"'s `LastCheckpointID` and returned before reading its updated transcript. An agent started at a workspace root could therefore continue the same conversation across several repository commits, but every attach after the first linked the initial conversation snapshot.\\n\\nAttachment now checks whether HEAD'\"'\"'s checkpoint already contains the requested session. A new commit captures the latest transcript; an existing checkpoint with other sessions receives the session; repeating attach to an already-attached commit preserves its snapshot, ev\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2640,\n      \"title\": \"hooks: stop a chained pre-push from swallowing Entire'\"'\"'s failure\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2640\",\n      \"head\": \"84a2d4775b31f9762913ac4183c7b5fb150ab45e\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/pre-push-chain-exit-code\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\nWhen `entire enable` finds an existing pre-push hook (husky, lefthook, git-lfs, a custom script), it backs it up to `pre-push.pre-entire` and chains to it after Entire'\"'\"'s own invocation. The script'\"'\"'s exit status was then the chained hook'\"'\"'s. Entire'\"'\"'s pre-push deliberately fails to abort `git push` when OPF refuses to redact, so with a chain in place a refusal was silently ignored whenever the user'\"'\"'s own hook passed.\\n\\n\\n## Who is affected\\n\\nOnly repos with **OPF enabled** that had a pre-push hook before `entire enable`. Without OPF, Entire'\"'\"'s pre-push does not exit non-zero: every error-returning branch of `prePush` is inside `if redact.OPFEnabled()`, and checkpoint push failures are f\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2635,\n      \"title\": \"Secure Enclave-protected tokens\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2635\",\n      \"head\": \"ea5363c6ae15982b7771a4de47234d8d594b315f\",\n      \"branch\": \"paul/se-protected-tokens\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1461\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n# Description\\r\\n\\r\\nFor old-timey SSH keys, i really like how [Secretive.app](https://github.com/maxgoedjen/secretive/) works.  I can require a TouchID unlock every time my SSH key is needed.\\r\\n\\r\\nI'\"'\"'m wondering if we can bring something like that into Entire, optionally, for paranoid users.  Every time an `entire` or `git-remote-entire` process tries to talk to our Git data plane or control plane, we can throw up an auth gate:\\r\\n\\r\\n<img width=\\\"282\\\" height=\\\"379\\\" alt=\\\"image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/81ea462c-3552-428f-a329-9e13021f41c7\\\" />\\r\\n\\r\\n## Limitations\\r\\n\\r\\n- The en\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2634,\n      \"title\": \"Linked worktrees use the main worktree'\"'\"'s local settings\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2634\",\n      \"head\": \"266d063be0069da286827ace1e875f1e4e3f358c\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/worktree-local-settings\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2003/changes/cli/1460\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Linked worktrees use the main worktree'\"'\"'s local settings\\n\\n**Problem.** `git worktree add` creates a worktree without the gitignored `.entire/settings.local.json`, so every developer-only setting stops applying there. Reproduced with real binaries on main:\\n- **External agent** (`external_agents: true` is honored only from the local file): in the worktree every hook fails with `unknown agent \\\"roger-roger\\\" (not found as built-in or external plugin)`, no session is recorded, and the worktree'\"'\"'s commit links to the **main tree'\"'\"'s** live session when both touched the same \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2633,\n      \"title\": \"auth: fail closed when a jurisdiction'\"'\"'s clusters disagree on apiUrl\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2633\",\n      \"head\": \"3c858122345419f9eb02bdfe80c00605b48a6a3e\",\n      \"branch\": \"nina/cor-1896-fail-closed-home-cell-pick\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1459\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nentiredb#4129 (COR-1896) derives `Cluster.apiUrl` per cell, so two clusters in one jurisdiction can advertise different values. `resolveCellAPIBaseURL` — the home-cell pick behind `/me/*` routing and `--jurisdiction` — assumed they never differ and fell back to the first match when no default cluster matched, which would route home-scoped reads to an arbitrary cell with no error. Today the default-cluster preference masks it (the default sits in the home cell); moving the default, or the default row losing its `apiUrl`, would misroute silently. Same fix as entire.io#4889 mak\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2631,\n      \"title\": \"feat(opf): scan in the background so git push never waits on the privacy filter\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2631\",\n      \"head\": \"1e56a1f3287803161534ee0ef5ee5f921a63b177\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/opf-scan-worker\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1457\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nStacked on #2533, which merges first; this PR depends on it.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nOPF inference is slow, about 1.14 s per KB of prose on CPU, so one real session is minutes to hours of model time. The model ran inside the pre-push hook, which left two bad options. With the old 2 MiB cap, every real session was refused, so OPF could not ship real checkpoints at all. With the cap raised, `git push` would wait for the whole scan, which on `git-branch` (the default backend) could take hours.\\n\\n## Result\\n\\n`git push` never waits on the model, on either backend. Checkpoints still reach the remote o\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2621,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): break shared-owner ties by environment and phase, not recency\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2621\",\n      \"head\": \"417b43a046a0df1d1a65ac571c4f18e5cfa0841b\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/codex-daemon-session-resolution\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2612\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nSince Codex 0.157 the TUI runs its sessions in one `codex app-server --managed-daemon`, so each of them records the daemon as its owner. A commit made by any of them matches all of them at the same ancestry depth, and `isNearerOwner` broke that tie by the latest `LastInteractionTime`, which moves at turn boundaries:\\n\\n- commit linking guest-condensed a live session from another worktree into the commit;\\n- caller resolution returned that same session as `ancestry`, so `IsCaller()` held, even while `CODEX_SESSION_ID` named the committing session. The post-commit hook logs under that session ID.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\nCommit linking and caller resolution now share one rule, `pickO\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2615,\n      \"title\": \"Withdraw history import until it is redesigned\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2615\",\n      \"head\": \"0349d5d1eb58fe18ccc30d88bd2e706260df625c\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/remove-history-import\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1445\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nHistory import (`entire import <agent>` and the first-time `entire enable` offer) creates checkpoints that nothing references. No commit carries their trailer, so every consumer has to enumerate them separately. That falls apart on git-refs. A fresh clone lists no imports (the case #2605 works on). Telling an import apart from a native checkpoint by name alone requires either fetching refs to check, or encoding a marker into IDs or ref names. Import'\"'\"'s idempotency depends on derived IDs. We reviewed six designs plus two follow-ups adversarially, and none holds up without a bi\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2613,\n      \"title\": \"Show monitors and runners in trail show (for Fried Green Loops)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2613\",\n      \"head\": \"3d673a83718ff3e7691d6ca915c6da557c68a395\",\n      \"branch\": \"trail-show-monitors\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1443\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.io) after CI was requested for the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2611,\n      \"title\": \"fix(git): protect ignored files during branch checkout\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2611\",\n      \"head\": \"cf71f02f471eae3085c4e5f59c44e50a122bc451\",\n      \"branch\": \"codex/issue-2604-safe-checkout\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\n- pass `--no-overwrite-ignore` through the shared branch-checkout helper so a target tree cannot silently replace ignored, untracked local files\\r\\n- add helper-level and real-binary resume regressions that verify checkout refusal, unchanged branch state, and byte-for-byte file preservation\\r\\n- document the ignored-file checkout safety requirement\\r\\n\\r\\nFixes #2604.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Testing\\r\\n\\r\\n- focused checkout-helper regression\\r\\n- adjacent resume integration tests\\r\\n- repository formatting, module, mise, secret-pattern, ShellCheck, and full Go lint checks\\r\\n- both CLI builds\\r\\n- six-case synthetic post-fix matrix covering repository ignores, `core.excludesFile`, remote-only resume, and existing \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2605,\n      \"title\": \"List remote-only imported checkpoints in fresh git-refs clones\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2605\",\n      \"head\": \"2eae3f976cbd218b17a5a6233a21277ecced2c73\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/list-remote-imported-checkpoints\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1438\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\n## Problem\\r\\n\\r\\n`entire checkpoint list` shows 0 checkpoints in a fresh clone of a git-refs repo whose checkpoints are all imported, although `git ls-remote origin '\"'\"'refs/entire/checkpoints/*'\"'\"'` shows them.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Root cause\\r\\n\\r\\nNot the remote selection: `ListCheckpointRefsOnRemote` already queries origin when no `checkpoint_remote` is set (the #1771 description is outdated there).\\r\\n\\r\\nImported checkpoints carry no commit trailer, so they only surface through `getImportedPendingCheckpoints`. That function opened a second store and listed **local refs only**. Remote-discovered stubs wou\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2589,\n      \"title\": \"feat(opencode): support OpenCode 2 with V1 fallback\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2589\",\n      \"head\": \"c7d0c8549e332767ffc3e57aa2178c5ecc727c31\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/opencode-v2-dual\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\nMakes the OpenCode integration work on OpenCode 2 while keeping OpenCode 1 working from the same generated plugin. Fixes #2588.\\n\\nOpenCode 2 is a hard break in two places:\\n\\n1. It loads a default plugin definition with `id` + `setup`/`effect`, and rejects V1 hook-map plugins with `PluginModule.LoadError: Plugin must export a default definition with an id and an effect or setup function`.\\n2. It moved export/import under `opencode session`; the V1 `opencode export` prints a help page and exits 0.\\n\\nThis builds on the approach in #2397 (thanks @aryasaatvik) but keeps OpenCode 1 plugin support instead of dropping it.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n**Plugin** (`entire_plugin.ts` + committed dogfood copy)\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2586,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): preserve non-ASCII staged filenames\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2586\",\n      \"head\": \"cd98162248e63f0ceae40b61f556b583b7dcae7e\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/2398-non-ascii-staged-files\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nFixes #2398.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Preserve non-ASCII staged filenames during checkpoint linking.\\r\\n* Use Git'\"'\"'s NUL-delimited output format to avoid C-escaped filenames.\\r\\n* Add a regression test covering non-ASCII filenames such as `café.go`.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Problem\\r\\n\\r\\nWhen Git is configured with `core.quotePath=true`, commands such as:\\r\\n\\r\\n```text\\r\\ngit diff --cached --name-only\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\ncan return non-ASCII filenames in a C-escaped form instead of their literal path.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor example, `café.go` may be returned as an escaped filename. Entire then compares this value against the literal filename stored in `SessionState.FilesTouched`, causing the overlap check to fail and potentially preventing the `Entire-Chec\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2577,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): stop carrying forward files a skipped-hook commit already took\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2577\",\n      \"head\": \"84e9735a2754da65e80089633f28abe6788d624d\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/skipped-commit-carry-forward\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1416\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\nA commit made with every Git hook skipped (`LEFTHOOK=0` under the Lefthook integration in #2388, a GUI client with no hooks, a crashed hook) is invisible to Entire. The session'\"'\"'s files from that turn land in HEAD, but the next hooked commit'\"'\"'s diff doesn'\"'\"'t contain them, so `filesWithRemainingAgentChanges` counts them as uncommitted and `carryForwardToNewShadowBranch` moves them onto a fresh shadow branch. No later commit ever contains them, so it repeats on **every** commit: `entire checkpoint list` shows a permanent `[temporary] carry forward: uncommitted session files` \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2576,\n      \"title\": \"fix(cli): keep records for Claude Code default background subagents\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2576\",\n      \"head\": \"367a00c5e8cc4b4c2ff64b2565c06ccd0bb30d7a\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/claude-code-default-background-subagents\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2556\\r\\n\\r\\nClaude Code launches subagents in the background by default and reports the launch as async (`tool_response.status: \\\"async_launched\\\"`,`tool_response.isAsync: true`) even when `run_in_background` is omitted from the Task `tool_input`. Detection keyed only on the flag, so that omitted-flag launch was treated as a finished foreground task and its record was dropped at launch; SubagentStop then found no marker and the subagent'\"'\"'s transcript never landed under the checkpoint'\"'\"'s `tasks/`.\\r\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2568,\n      \"title\": \"auth: refuse cross-site cells; cache a 401 trails probe (ENT-2573)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2568\",\n      \"head\": \"b4549b975a5d798b5f3377348f3b2e0e1e88e0a9\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/ent-2573-cli-sends-prod-issued-login-jwts-to-staging-entire-api-cells\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1408\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nFixes the CLI half of [ENT-2573](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/ENT-2573). Staging entire-api cells logged 17 `token_forgery` / `untrusted_issuer` events from prod-issued login JWTs. APM user agents show 13 came from `entire-cli/0.10.5`/`0.10.6`, whose data API auto-selected a saved prod login while routing to the staging cell (already removed in v0.11.0 by 455f8d5e47). The other 4 were `curl`. This PR adds defense in depth so a mismatched login and cell can'\"'\"'t reach the network again, and stops the retry loop that turned one misconfigured machine into repeated alarms.\\n\\n## Changes\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2564,\n      \"title\": \"Make AGENTS.md the real instruction file, drop CLAUDE.md\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2564\",\n      \"head\": \"158a8076976f1b2b51084bc8a01a31336e183'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":11417}},"started_at_ms":1794842128549,"completed_at_ms":1794842128550}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:28.703Z","ordinal":3017,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-d0aacf3d-b850-4bad-9187-ea5840839d57","process_id":"99281","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' '3a1\",\n      \"branch\": \"docs/agents-md-replaces-claude-md\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1404\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What\\n\\n`AGENTS.md` was a symlink to `CLAUDE.md`. Every agent that reads repository instructions now supports `AGENTS.md` directly, so the indirection buys nothing. This promotes `AGENTS.md` to the regular file (`120000` → `100644`) and deletes the symlink.\\n\\n## Reference updates\\n\\nRepository-side references follow the rename:\\n\\n- `docs/development/docs_test.go` — the 20 KiB budget read, its error message, the link-check list, and the \\\"routing table has no links\\\" assertion. Without this the test `t.Fatal`s on the missing file.\\n- `CONTRIBUTING.md` — three anchor links, plus the doc ind\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2552,\n      \"title\": \"fix(resume): resolve branch names Unicode-normalization-insensitively (NFC/NFD)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2552\",\n      \"head\": \"dcd1cfad190324f751245b609530f424fc1ba9eb\",\n      \"branch\": \"kc/2551-normalize-branch-name-resume\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2551.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n`entire session resume <branch>` compared and looked up branch names byte-for-byte, with no Unicode normalization. Git treats a precomposed (NFC, `é` U+00E9) and decomposed (NFD, `e` + U+0301) spelling of the same accented branch as one branch (`core.precomposeUnicode`), so `git checkout` finds it either way — but entire would report `branch '\"'\"'<name>'\"'\"' not found locally or on origin` when the supplied name'\"'\"'s normalization differed from the on-disk ref. It bit cross-platform teams: a branch created on Linux (NFD) and synced couldn'\"'\"'t be resumed on a macOS checkout (NFC), especially once refs were packed (`git gc`), where go-git matches `packed-refs` byte-exact.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2550,\n      \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): preserve newer same-ref queue updates\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2550\",\n      \"head\": \"978f25b9623e479c08b9a180dc342d1a4239f3fd\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/2008-preserve-same-ref-queue\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nFixes #2008.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Preserve a newer same-ref queue entry added while a checkpoint push is in flight.\\r\\n* Keep `readLocked` de-duplication behavior for `Drain` and `Peek`.\\r\\n* Add a regression test covering the same-ref enqueue race.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Testing\\r\\n\\r\\n* `git diff --check`\\r\\n* Added `TestPushQueue_RemovePreservesNewerSameRefEntry`\\r\\n\\r\\nNote: The Go test suite was not run locally because Go is not installed in the environment.\\r\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2541,\n      \"title\": \"Track all four Entire-shipped plugins, not just ci\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2541\",\n      \"head\": \"47297a33c0ca7339cc75475e990a1aa2267e5448\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/official-plugins-allowlist\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1386\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nFollow-up to #2515. `officialPlugins` gates plugin telemetry — an invocation emits `cli_plugin_executed` only if its name is listed, and everything else runs silently. It was introduced with the note *\\\"currently empty — populate as Entire ships its own plugins\\\"*, and [external-commands.md](https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/main/docs/architecture/external-commands.md#adding-an-entire-shipped-command-to-the-allowlist) documents appending to it as step 1 of publishing an Entire-owned command.\\n\\nOnly `ci` was ever added. `graph`, `run` and `upgrade` have all shipped and been invisible\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2536,\n      \"title\": \"fix(codex): preserve attachment models and desktop transcript content\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2536\",\n      \"head\": \"fa8ed3d6c295739777e39fd0cad38cfdaa46d620\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/codex-attachment-transcripts\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1381\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nManual attachment of Codex desktop rollouts stored an empty model and dropped visible assistant messages and custom-tool array outputs from compact transcripts. This adds native model extraction from the latest valid `turn_context.payload.model`, supports desktop `agent_message` response items and text-block output arrays, and shows custom-tool `input` in readable tool details.\\n\\nEvent mirrors and encrypted reasoning remain excluded, tool outputs retain call-ID association, and `--full` retains its existing condensed full-session presentation. Existing checkpoint data is not migrated\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2534,\n      \"title\": \"test(strategy): cover symlinked hook with an existing backup (#2410)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2534\",\n      \"head\": \"1ebd5055302f8caf5d52f957258f6fb492cfc46f\",\n      \"branch\": \"kc/2410-symlink-backup-regression-test\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## What\\n\\nAdds a regression test for #2410 — a symlinked hook that also has a pre-existing\\n`<hook>.pre-entire` backup (the second-`enable` path).\\n\\n**This is a test-only change.** #2410 is already fixed on `main`: `writeHookFile`\\nwrites via `jsonutil.WriteFileAtomicIn` (temp file + `rename`, which replaces a\\nleaf symlink instead of following it), and `classifyExistingHook` treats a symlink\\nas foreign. 0.10.6'\"'\"'s bare `os.WriteFile` followed the symlink. So this doesn'\"'\"'t\\nchange behaviour — it pins the fixed behaviour so it can'\"'\"'t silently regress.\\n\\n## Why the existing tests don'\"'\"'t cover it\\n\\nTwo tests each cover only half of the reported scenario:\\n\\n- `TestInstallGitHook_SymlinkedHookIsBackedUpNotFoll\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2533,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): dedup OPF byte cap, scope it per checkpoint ref, run it off git push'\"'\"'s blocking path\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2533\",\n      \"head\": \"10b3797a4b1baec530511a6b99e2f9fa4c9acea4\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/opf-batch-cap-fix\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1380\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nWith OPF on, the git-refs backend had four delivery-correctness bugs:\\n\\n- Delivery checked the OPF trailer on one ref tip and then pushed the symbolic ref, so a concurrent write could ship a later tip that was never checked.\\n- Queue cleanup removed refs by name, so it could erase a newer generation of the same ref.\\n- The byte caps were counted across every queued ref, so one large session withheld all of them.\\n- The prose-leaf cap counted a repeated leaf every time it appeared, although OPF processes it once.\\n\\n## Result\\n\\n- The push queue records `(ref, hash)` generations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2532,\n      \"title\": \"feat(settings): add the user settings tier\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2532\",\n      \"head\": \"4e20cd063a9765dc988a2a71738cbc5a77ad13f2\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/settings-user-tier\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/1822/changes/cli/1379\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n`.entire/settings.local.json` is documented as per-clone and per-developer. It resolves to the **worktree root**, and it is gitignored, so a clone with several worktrees holds several copies and `git worktree add` produces one with none.\\n\\nThat placement was incidental. `95f8b907c2` (Jan 2026) created the file as a write target for `entire disable`, with no scope or trust reasoning. It decides two unrelated things at once: gitignored makes it per-developer, which was the intent, and living inside the worktree makes it per-worktree, which nobody chose.\\n\\n## What breaks \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2524,\n      \"title\": \"doctor/status: detect and link unattributed reserved-host authors (COR-1289)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2524\",\n      \"head\": \"e1870115074d0235cd8aed0e833b009b8da68144\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/cor-1289-unattributed-authors\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1370\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nPart two of COR-1289: part one made `entire enable` catch an unset `user.email`; this recovers the commits already authored under a synthesized reserved-host address (`you@Your-Laptop.local`).\\n\\n## Behaviour\\n- **`entire doctor`** gains an \\\"Unattributed authors\\\" check: it lists reserved-host author addresses in this repo whose local part equals the current OS username, asks the repo'\"'\"'s cell (`POST /repos/{repo_id}/authors:resolve-unattributed`) how many commits Entire could not attribute, and offers to link each address to the logged-in account via `POST /me/aliases`. Doctor'\"'\"'s own `Lab\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2523,\n      \"title\": \"coreapi: hand-add the alias declare/release operations to the core spec (COR-1289)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2523\",\n      \"head\": \"13668cadb2c35e42d0668aab5c19084352ca1ed3\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/cor-1289-coreapi-alias-spec-v2\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1369\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nGenerated-only companion to the COR-1289 doctor work: hand-adds `POST /me/aliases` (`declareAlias`) and `DELETE /me/aliases/{email}` (`releaseAlias`) plus `DeclareAliasInputBody`/`DeclareAliasOutputBody` to `internal/coreapi/spec/core.openapi.json`, then regenerates the ogen client. +1307, ~99% generated; the hand-written part is the two path items, two schemas, and `UPSTREAM.md` §4.\\n\\nWhy hand-added: the spec is fetched from prod, and prod will not serve these operations until entiredb `peyton/cor-1289-declared-alias-min` is deployed **and** `ENTIRE_ALIAS_DECLARATION_ENABLED` is on.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2519,\n      \"title\": \"Re-deliver checkpoints when their destination changes\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2519\",\n      \"head\": \"6f22f803011c9cd8af8cde6c8e41407c0cf6a14f\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/checkpoint-destination-redelivery\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1365\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nWhen a repo'\"'\"'s `checkpoint_remote` is refused by the ownership check, checkpoints go to the code repo instead. Claiming the store later fixed every future checkpoint and stranded every earlier one where it had landed. This makes the fix retroactive.\\n\\n## Both backends\\n\\n**git-branch needs no code.** Its push sends the whole `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch, so a destination change carries the full history already. That'\"'\"'s a property of `pushRefIfNeeded`'\"'\"'s remote-keyed shortcut rather than an accident, so it'\"'\"'s pinned across both transitions that clear it — swapping one remote name for anot\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2501,\n      \"title\": \"fix(codex): preserve last assistant message\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2501\",\n      \"head\": \"7623f3165c329610830c32b75d2d0d69d52f3c90\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/2064-codex-last-assistant-message\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Description\\r\\n\\r\\nThis PR fixes an issue where Codex'\"'\"'s `last_assistant_message` field was parsed from `Stop` and `SubagentStop` hook payloads but was not propagated to the resulting `agent.Event`.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe parsed `last_assistant_message` is now mapped to `Event.TaskDescription` for both lifecycle events.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Changes\\r\\n\\r\\n* Preserve `last_assistant_message` for `Stop` events.\\r\\n* Preserve `last_assistant_message` for `SubagentStop` events.\\r\\n* Use `derefString()` so nullable values are handled safely.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Issue\\r\\n\\r\\nFixes #2064\\r\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2499,\n      \"title\": \"fix(agent): make installed external agents visible and removable\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2499\",\n      \"head\": \"a66c362966b56afc7c2a03aea3d10badb3aab9e1\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/external-agents-visible-removable\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1348\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nAn external agent plugin that `entire enable` installs is invisible to every surface that reports agents, and there is no supported way to remove it.\\n\\nReproduced on `main` (21155beb4) with a mock `entire-agent-faux` plugin on `$PATH` in a throwaway repo:\\n\\n```\\n$ entire enable --agent faux\\n  Agent: Faux Agent\\n  Installed 1 hooks for Fake external agent\\n  Ready.\\n# .faux/settings.json written, .entire/settings.local.json = {\\\"external_agents\\\":true}\\n\\n$ entire agent list\\nAgents:\\n    claude-code\\n    codex\\n    copilot-cli\\n    cursor\\n    factoryai-droid\\n    gemini\\n    opencode\\n   \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2498,\n      \"title\": \"fix(cli): show checkpoint ID in `checkpoint list --pending`; disambiguate `session info` checkpoint labels\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2498\",\n      \"head\": \"04f910302dbdff944fb9694ec138a48a285f43d0\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/checkpoint-pending-and-session-info-display\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1347\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nTwo small display bugs in the CLI'\"'\"'s plain-text output. Both fixes are presentation-only: no field values, no semantics, no `--json` shape changes.\\n\\n## Bug A — `checkpoint list --pending` dropped the checkpoint ID\\n\\nThe text renderer printed a date and a message, preceded by eight literal spaces where the ID column belongs. The data was there the whole time: `--pending --json` returns `id`, and the sibling `checkpoint list` table prints the same short sha.\\n\\nAn agent or human reading the text output had nothing to act on — no identifier to carry into `checkpoint explain`. That is the f\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2497,\n      \"title\": \"fix(investigate): degrade --edit gracefully without a TTY\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2497\",\n      \"head\": \"4fa73460130ce6927d135c862891a4eb03f60098\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/investigate-edit-noninteractive\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1346\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n`entire investigate --edit` leaks a raw internal TUI-library error and exits 1 in any non-interactive environment — after first printing a progress line implying it was working:\\n\\n```\\n$ CI=1 entire investigate --edit\\nConfiguring investigate with 1 eligible agent(s).\\n(Space to toggle, enter to confirm.)\\n\\ninvestigate picker: picker form: huh: bubbletea: error opening TTY: bubbletea: could not open TTY: open /dev/tty: device not configured\\nexit 1\\n```\\n\\n`RunInvestigateConfigPicker` printed the \\\"Configuring investigate with N eligible agent(s)\\\" banner and then called `runInvest\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2496,\n      \"title\": \"fix(setup): don'\"'\"'t fail `entire enable` on the telemetry prompt without a TTY\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2496\",\n      \"head\": \"63fb61ec3b670d2aefd5aca6dfbdb2a8a330f1ef\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/enable-noninteractive-telemetry-prompt\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1345\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n`entire enable` fails in any non-interactive environment, with a raw internal library error, **after it has already succeeded**:\\n\\n```\\n$ CI=1 entire enable\\nDetected agent: Claude Code\\n\\n  ✓ Installed hooks\\n  ✓ Configured project\\n    .entire/settings.json\\ntelemetry consent: telemetry prompt: huh: bubbletea: error opening TTY: bubbletea: could not open TTY: open /dev/tty: device not configured\\n$ echo $?\\n1\\n```\\n\\nThe hooks are installed and `.entire/settings.json` is written with `\\\"enabled\\\": true` before this point — the repo *is* enabled. Only the exit code says otherwise, so \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2495,\n      \"title\": \"auth: fall back to the file token store when the Linux keyring is unavailable, and remember the choice\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2495\",\n      \"head\": \"c3fbb403b594b71d73e305b5fd8140f71f0b0f2c\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/token-store-fallback\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1344\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nFixes two customer-reported failures on headless Linux (CLI 0.10.6, Ubuntu VPS with no keyring daemon):\\n\\n1. `entire login --device` authenticated, then failed on the first keyring write with `The name org.freedesktop.secrets was not provided by any .service files` and discarded the fresh token; the `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file` hint only appeared after the loss.\\n2. `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file` had to be set on every command. With a valid `~/.config/entire/tokens.json`, plain `entire activity` tried the keyring, failed, and reported \\\"Not logged in\\\".\\n\\nRoot cause: backend selectio\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2487,\n      \"title\": \"agent: keep the worktree out of the Windows hook wrapper'\"'\"'s command search\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2487\",\n      \"head\": \"3fdf05da33fcf0e4f560474fcadd00fc12eaa6c7\",\n      \"branch\": \"harden-windows-hook-wrapper-search\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1336\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\ncmd.exe searches the current directory ahead of PATH, and the directory a hook runs in is the worktree — so the Windows hook wrapper resolved both `where.exe` and `entire` from the repository first. A committed `entire.bat` was what ran when the agent started a session. Live today for Codex; droid (#2349) and Cursor (#2352) are adding callers, so it is fixed once in the shared wrapper.\\n\\n`where.exe` is now named under `%SystemRoot%`, which is true by construction. The bare `entire` has no absolute spelling, so that half rests on `NoDefaultCurrentDirectoryInExePath` — and since the do\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2479,\n      \"title\": \"doctor_te'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' '3a1\",\n      \"branch\": \"docs/agents-md-replaces-claude-md\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1404\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What\\n\\n`AGENTS.md` was a symlink to `CLAUDE.md`. Every agent that reads repository instructions now supports `AGENTS.md` directly, so the indirection buys nothing. This promotes `AGENTS.md` to the regular file (`120000` → `100644`) and deletes the symlink.\\n\\n## Reference updates\\n\\nRepository-side references follow the rename:\\n\\n- `docs/development/docs_test.go` — the 20 KiB budget read, its error message, the link-check list, and the \\\"routing table has no links\\\" assertion. Without this the test `t.Fatal`s on the missing file.\\n- `CONTRIBUTING.md` — three anchor links, plus the doc ind\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2552,\n      \"title\": \"fix(resume): resolve branch names Unicode-normalization-insensitively (NFC/NFD)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2552\",\n      \"head\": \"dcd1cfad190324f751245b609530f424fc1ba9eb\",\n      \"branch\": \"kc/2551-normalize-branch-name-resume\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2551.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n`entire session resume <branch>` compared and looked up branch names byte-for-byte, with no Unicode normalization. Git treats a precomposed (NFC, `é` U+00E9) and decomposed (NFD, `e` + U+0301) spelling of the same accented branch as one branch (`core.precomposeUnicode`), so `git checkout` finds it either way — but entire would report `branch '\"'\"'<name>'\"'\"' not found locally or on origin` when the supplied name'\"'\"'s normalization differed from the on-disk ref. It bit cross-platform teams: a branch created on Linux (NFD) and synced couldn'\"'\"'t be resumed on a macOS checkout (NFC), especially once refs were packed (`git gc`), where go-git matches `packed-refs` byte-exact.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2550,\n      \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): preserve newer same-ref queue updates\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2550\",\n      \"head\": \"978f25b9623e479c08b9a180dc342d1a4239f3fd\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/2008-preserve-same-ref-queue\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nFixes #2008.\\r\\n\\r\\n* Preserve a newer same-ref queue entry added while a checkpoint push is in flight.\\r\\n* Keep `readLocked` de-duplication behavior for `Drain` and `Peek`.\\r\\n* Add a regression test covering the same-ref enqueue race.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Testing\\r\\n\\r\\n* `git diff --check`\\r\\n* Added `TestPushQueue_RemovePreservesNewerSameRefEntry`\\r\\n\\r\\nNote: The Go test suite was not run locally because Go is not installed in the environment.\\r\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2541,\n      \"title\": \"Track all four Entire-shipped plugins, not just ci\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2541\",\n      \"head\": \"47297a33c0ca7339cc75475e990a1aa2267e5448\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/official-plugins-allowlist\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1386\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nFollow-up to #2515. `officialPlugins` gates plugin telemetry — an invocation emits `cli_plugin_executed` only if its name is listed, and everything else runs silently. It was introduced with the note *\\\"currently empty — populate as Entire ships its own plugins\\\"*, and [external-commands.md](https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/main/docs/architecture/external-commands.md#adding-an-entire-shipped-command-to-the-allowlist) documents appending to it as step 1 of publishing an Entire-owned command.\\n\\nOnly `ci` was ever added. `graph`, `run` and `upgrade` have all shipped and been invisible\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2536,\n      \"title\": \"fix(codex): preserve attachment models and desktop transcript content\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2536\",\n      \"head\": \"fa8ed3d6c295739777e39fd0cad38cfdaa46d620\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/codex-attachment-transcripts\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1381\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nManual attachment of Codex desktop rollouts stored an empty model and dropped visible assistant messages and custom-tool array outputs from compact transcripts. This adds native model extraction from the latest valid `turn_context.payload.model`, supports desktop `agent_message` response items and text-block output arrays, and shows custom-tool `input` in readable tool details.\\n\\nEvent mirrors and encrypted reasoning remain excluded, tool outputs retain call-ID association, and `--full` retains its existing condensed full-session presentation. Existing checkpoint data is not migrated\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2534,\n      \"title\": \"test(strategy): cover symlinked hook with an existing backup (#2410)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2534\",\n      \"head\": \"1ebd5055302f8caf5d52f957258f6fb492cfc46f\",\n      \"branch\": \"kc/2410-symlink-backup-regression-test\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## What\\n\\nAdds a regression test for #2410 — a symlinked hook that also has a pre-existing\\n`<hook>.pre-entire` backup (the second-`enable` path).\\n\\n**This is a test-only change.** #2410 is already fixed on `main`: `writeHookFile`\\nwrites via `jsonutil.WriteFileAtomicIn` (temp file + `rename`, which replaces a\\nleaf symlink instead of following it), and `classifyExistingHook` treats a symlink\\nas foreign. 0.10.6'\"'\"'s bare `os.WriteFile` followed the symlink. So this doesn'\"'\"'t\\nchange behaviour — it pins the fixed behaviour so it can'\"'\"'t silently regress.\\n\\n## Why the existing tests don'\"'\"'t cover it\\n\\nTwo tests each cover only half of the reported scenario:\\n\\n- `TestInstallGitHook_SymlinkedHookIsBackedUpNotFoll\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2533,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): dedup OPF byte cap, scope it per checkpoint ref, run it off git push'\"'\"'s blocking path\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2533\",\n      \"head\": \"10b3797a4b1baec530511a6b99e2f9fa4c9acea4\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/opf-batch-cap-fix\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1380\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nWith OPF on, the git-refs backend had four delivery-correctness bugs:\\n\\n- Delivery checked the OPF trailer on one ref tip and then pushed the symbolic ref, so a concurrent write could ship a later tip that was never checked.\\n- Queue cleanup removed refs by name, so it could erase a newer generation of the same ref.\\n- The byte caps were counted across every queued ref, so one large session withheld all of them.\\n- The prose-leaf cap counted a repeated leaf every time it appeared, although OPF processes it once.\\n\\n## Result\\n\\n- The push queue records `(ref, hash)` generations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2532,\n      \"title\": \"feat(settings): add the user settings tier\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2532\",\n      \"head\": \"4e20cd063a9765dc988a2a71738cbc5a77ad13f2\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/settings-user-tier\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/1822/changes/cli/1379\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n`.entire/settings.local.json` is documented as per-clone and per-developer. It resolves to the **worktree root**, and it is gitignored, so a clone with several worktrees holds several copies and `git worktree add` produces one with none.\\n\\nThat placement was incidental. `95f8b907c2` (Jan 2026) created the file as a write target for `entire disable`, with no scope or trust reasoning. It decides two unrelated things at once: gitignored makes it per-developer, which was the intent, and living inside the worktree makes it per-worktree, which nobody chose.\\n\\n## What breaks \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2524,\n      \"title\": \"doctor/status: detect and link unattributed reserved-host authors (COR-1289)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2524\",\n      \"head\": \"e1870115074d0235cd8aed0e833b009b8da68144\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/cor-1289-unattributed-authors\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1370\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nPart two of COR-1289: part one made `entire enable` catch an unset `user.email`; this recovers the commits already authored under a synthesized reserved-host address (`you@Your-Laptop.local`).\\n\\n## Behaviour\\n- **`entire doctor`** gains an \\\"Unattributed authors\\\" check: it lists reserved-host author addresses in this repo whose local part equals the current OS username, asks the repo'\"'\"'s cell (`POST /repos/{repo_id}/authors:resolve-unattributed`) how many commits Entire could not attribute, and offers to link each address to the logged-in account via `POST /me/aliases`. Doctor'\"'\"'s own `Lab\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2523,\n      \"title\": \"coreapi: hand-add the alias declare/release operations to the core spec (COR-1289)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2523\",\n      \"head\": \"13668cadb2c35e42d0668aab5c19084352ca1ed3\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/cor-1289-coreapi-alias-spec-v2\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1369\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nGenerated-only companion to the COR-1289 doctor work: hand-adds `POST /me/aliases` (`declareAlias`) and `DELETE /me/aliases/{email}` (`releaseAlias`) plus `DeclareAliasInputBody`/`DeclareAliasOutputBody` to `internal/coreapi/spec/core.openapi.json`, then regenerates the ogen client. +1307, ~99% generated; the hand-written part is the two path items, two schemas, and `UPSTREAM.md` §4.\\n\\nWhy hand-added: the spec is fetched from prod, and prod will not serve these operations until entiredb `peyton/cor-1289-declared-alias-min` is deployed **and** `ENTIRE_ALIAS_DECLARATION_ENABLED` is on.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2519,\n      \"title\": \"Re-deliver checkpoints when their destination changes\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2519\",\n      \"head\": \"6f22f803011c9cd8af8cde6c8e41407c0cf6a14f\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/checkpoint-destination-redelivery\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1365\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nWhen a repo'\"'\"'s `checkpoint_remote` is refused by the ownership check, checkpoints go to the code repo instead. Claiming the store later fixed every future checkpoint and stranded every earlier one where it had landed. This makes the fix retroactive.\\n\\n## Both backends\\n\\n**git-branch needs no code.** Its push sends the whole `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch, so a destination change carries the full history already. That'\"'\"'s a property of `pushRefIfNeeded`'\"'\"'s remote-keyed shortcut rather than an accident, so it'\"'\"'s pinned across both transitions that clear it — swapping one remote name for anot\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2501,\n      \"title\": \"fix(codex): preserve last assistant message\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2501\",\n      \"head\": \"7623f3165c329610830c32b75d2d0d69d52f3c90\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/2064-codex-last-assistant-message\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Description\\r\\n\\r\\nThis PR fixes an issue where Codex'\"'\"'s `last_assistant_message` field was parsed from `Stop` and `SubagentStop` hook payloads but was not propagated to the resulting `agent.Event`.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe parsed `last_assistant_message` is now mapped to `Event.TaskDescription` for both lifecycle events.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Changes\\r\\n\\r\\n* Preserve `last_assistant_message` for `Stop` events.\\r\\n* Preserve `last_assistant_message` for `SubagentStop` events.\\r\\n* Use `derefString()` so nullable values are handled safely.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Issue\\r\\n\\r\\nFixes #2064\\r\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2499,\n      \"title\": \"fix(agent): make installed external agents visible and removable\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2499\",\n      \"head\": \"a66c362966b56afc7c2a03aea3d10badb3aab9e1\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/external-agents-visible-removable\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1348\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nAn external agent plugin that `entire enable` installs is invisible to every surface that reports agents, and there is no supported way to remove it.\\n\\nReproduced on `main` (21155beb4) with a mock `entire-agent-faux` plugin on `$PATH` in a throwaway repo:\\n\\n```\\n$ entire enable --agent faux\\n  Agent: Faux Agent\\n  Installed 1 hooks for Fake external agent\\n  Ready.\\n# .faux/settings.json written, .entire/settings.local.json = {\\\"external_agents\\\":true}\\n\\n$ entire agent list\\nAgents:\\n    claude-code\\n    codex\\n    copilot-cli\\n    cursor\\n    factoryai-droid\\n    gemini\\n    opencode\\n   \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2498,\n      \"title\": \"fix(cli): show checkpoint ID in `checkpoint list --pending`; disambiguate `session info` checkpoint labels\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2498\",\n      \"head\": \"04f910302dbdff944fb9694ec138a48a285f43d0\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/checkpoint-pending-and-session-info-display\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1347\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nTwo small display bugs in the CLI'\"'\"'s plain-text output. Both fixes are presentation-only: no field values, no semantics, no `--json` shape changes.\\n\\n## Bug A — `checkpoint list --pending` dropped the checkpoint ID\\n\\nThe text renderer printed a date and a message, preceded by eight literal spaces where the ID column belongs. The data was there the whole time: `--pending --json` returns `id`, and the sibling `checkpoint list` table prints the same short sha.\\n\\nAn agent or human reading the text output had nothing to act on — no identifier to carry into `checkpoint explain`. That is the f\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2497,\n      \"title\": \"fix(investigate): degrade --edit gracefully without a TTY\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2497\",\n      \"head\": \"4fa73460130ce6927d135c862891a4eb03f60098\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/investigate-edit-noninteractive\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1346\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n`entire investigate --edit` leaks a raw internal TUI-library error and exits 1 in any non-interactive environment — after first printing a progress line implying it was working:\\n\\n```\\n$ CI=1 entire investigate --edit\\nConfiguring investigate with 1 eligible agent(s).\\n(Space to toggle, enter to confirm.)\\n\\ninvestigate picker: picker form: huh: bubbletea: error opening TTY: bubbletea: could not open TTY: open /dev/tty: device not configured\\nexit 1\\n```\\n\\n`RunInvestigateConfigPicker` printed the \\\"Configuring investigate with N eligible agent(s)\\\" banner and then called `runInvest\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2496,\n      \"title\": \"fix(setup): don'\"'\"'t fail `entire enable` on the telemetry prompt without a TTY\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2496\",\n      \"head\": \"63fb61ec3b670d2aefd5aca6dfbdb2a8a330f1ef\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/enable-noninteractive-telemetry-prompt\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1345\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n`entire enable` fails in any non-interactive environment, with a raw internal library error, **after it has already succeeded**:\\n\\n```\\n$ CI=1 entire enable\\nDetected agent: Claude Code\\n\\n  ✓ Installed hooks\\n  ✓ Configured project\\n    .entire/settings.json\\ntelemetry consent: telemetry prompt: huh: bubbletea: error opening TTY: bubbletea: could not open TTY: open /dev/tty: device not configured\\n$ echo $?\\n1\\n```\\n\\nThe hooks are installed and `.entire/settings.json` is written with `\\\"enabled\\\": true` before this point — the repo *is* enabled. Only the exit code says otherwise, so \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2495,\n      \"title\": \"auth: fall back to the file token store when the Linux keyring is unavailable, and remember the choice\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2495\",\n      \"head\": \"c3fbb403b594b71d73e305b5fd8140f71f0b0f2c\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/token-store-fallback\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1344\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nFixes two customer-reported failures on headless Linux (CLI 0.10.6, Ubuntu VPS with no keyring daemon):\\n\\n1. `entire login --device` authenticated, then failed on the first keyring write with `The name org.freedesktop.secrets was not provided by any .service files` and discarded the fresh token; the `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file` hint only appeared after the loss.\\n2. `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file` had to be set on every command. With a valid `~/.config/entire/tokens.json`, plain `entire activity` tried the keyring, failed, and reported \\\"Not logged in\\\".\\n\\nRoot cause: backend selectio\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2487,\n      \"title\": \"agent: keep the worktree out of the Windows hook wrapper'\"'\"'s command search\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2487\",\n      \"head\": \"3fdf05da33fcf0e4f560474fcadd00fc12eaa6c7\",\n      \"branch\": \"harden-windows-hook-wrapper-search\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1336\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\ncmd.exe searches the current directory ahead of PATH, and the directory a hook runs in is the worktree — so the Windows hook wrapper resolved both `where.exe` and `entire` from the repository first. A committed `entire.bat` was what ran when the agent started a session. Live today for Codex; droid (#2349) and Cursor (#2352) are adding callers, so it is fixed once in the shared wrapper.\\n\\n`where.exe` is now named under `%SystemRoot%`, which is true by construction. The bare `entire` has no absolute spelling, so that half rests on `NoDefaultCurrentDirectoryInExePath` — and since the do\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2479,\n      \"title\": \"doctor_te'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":11292}},"started_at_ms":1794842128703,"completed_at_ms":1794842128703}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:28.839Z","ordinal":3018,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-0a185c8e-42da-4ea8-b99b-993cfd7d4aad","process_id":"12125","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' 'st: pin ENTIRE_TEST_TTY in non-interactive tests\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2479\",\n      \"head\": \"9cc8df071906c0b2c08d2d14eb8dabbfeed3e007\",\n      \"branch\": \"doctor-test-pin-tty\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"These two tests assert the non-interactive path of runSessionsFix. If a dev shell happens to set ENTIRE_TEST_TTY=1, CanPromptInteractively() returns true and the test falls through to the real huh form instead of exercising the guard. Pinning it to 0 makes the environment deterministic.\\r\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2408,\n      \"title\": \"fix: repair stale checkpoints and flag worktree setup gaps\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2408\",\n      \"head\": \"ed846bbd6232f7af00050776e94a8fc50792067b\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-checkpoint-metadata-followups\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This PR is stacked on #2404. It should target `krk/doctor-shrink-checkpoint-metadata` while that PR is open, then be retargeted to `main` after #2404 lands.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n#2404 prevents new oversized `prompt_attributions` metadata and adds an explicit doctor repair. Two cases remain.\\n\\nA stale clone can still contain the original oversized history plus newer local checkpoints after another clone repairs the remote. Its next push may reject the repaired history as unrelated or replay the old commits and reintroduce the oversized blobs.\\n\\nCommit hashes cannot identify the shared boundary reliably because rewriting metadata and signing commits both change commit IDs. OPF also runs before ordinary \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2404,\n      \"title\": \"fix(doctor): repair and prevent oversized checkpoint metadata.json blobs\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2404\",\n      \"head\": \"878a05e1829aa7a010e06ea06f7fd21ff70b5f39\",\n      \"branch\": \"krk/doctor-shrink-checkpoint-metadata\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1320\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nCLI versions before v0.10.1 walked nested git checkouts (Claude Code'\"'\"'s `.claude/worktrees/`) into `prompt_attributions.user_added_per_file` on every prompt, producing 70MB and 106MB per-session `metadata.json` blobs on `entire/checkpoints/v1`. GitHub refuses blobs over 100 MiB, so one such blob anywhere in the branch history makes it unpushable and unmirrorable there. A customer hit exactly this (Plain T-88, Gitea push-mirrored to GitHub). The v0.10.1 fix (#1937, #1969) stopped new bloat but left the history behind, and the only remedy was a hand-written `git filter-repo` sc\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2400,\n      \"title\": \"Add product changelog commands\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2400\",\n      \"head\": \"28697d63bfd523ac2790450348722a778c09483e\",\n      \"branch\": \"ashtom/product-changelog\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1319\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.io) after CI was requested for the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Read-only outbound HTTP to a fixed origin with URL validation and no auth or local repo state; main operational risk is search fetching many posts when there are no matches.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds a **public, repo-independent** `entire changelog` command (plus `changelog search`) that fetches Ent\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2395,\n      \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): surface git-refs push queue failures\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2395\",\n      \"head\": \"2569fb7d9801e026462047659b187bdc2b4ee74f\",\n      \"branch\": \"codex/issue-2393-push-bookkeeping\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\n- return an explicit partial failure when a git-refs checkpoint is written locally but cannot be added to the push queue\\r\\n- preserve the local ref and retryable condensation state, then re-enqueue on a later write\\r\\n- add store-level and condensation-level regressions and update the architecture contract\\r\\n\\r\\nCloses #2393\\r\\n\\r\\n## Why this approach\\r\\n\\r\\nThe ref update and queue append cannot be one atomic operation. Rolling back a valid local ref would discard recoverable data, while scanning every local checkpoint ref during pre-push would conflict with the queue'\"'\"'s purpose and with fetched-ref semantics. This change therefore makes the partial outcome explicit at the store boundary. T\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2391,\n      \"title\": \"Recommendations v2 (PR 5a): three noisy rules deleted, the rest cite their rows\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2391\",\n      \"head\": \"6c90ab513467c0843e79500096d63417e849e2ed\",\n      \"branch\": \"pr5a-recommendations-v2\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1317\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nTask 1–4 of `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-11-pr5-recommendations-v2.md`.\\n\\n**This PR: +616/-222. Cumulative across the stack (PR1+PR2+this vs `main`): +63158/-13182.**\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n`entire checkpoint tokens` on a real 286.3M-token checkpoint printed **seven** recommendations, two of which said the same thing and none of which named a number a reader could find. It now prints two:\\n\\n```\\nToken usage\\nTotal:  286.3M tokens\\n  Input: 110.2k | Cache read: 269.4M | Cache write: 16M | Output: 824.2k | API calls: 509 | Per call: 562.6k\\n\\nHow it was billed\\n  ...\\n  Of the total, subagents u\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2388,\n      \"title\": \"fix(hooks): register Entire with Lefthook instead of owning its hook files\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2388\",\n      \"head\": \"fc5d778c4d54a11bdf5f8cad885f09ab028bda3a\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/lefthook-integration\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1314\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\nLefthook regenerates **every** file in `.git/hooks` from its own config, gated by a checksum of that config — and it does so at the top of whatever hook fires next, typically the `pre-commit` of the very commit being made. Entire'\"'\"'s turn-start self-heal (`EnsureSetup` → reinstall if not installed) therefore always loses the race:\\n\\n- `lefthook install -f` (what Lefthook'\"'\"'s own npm postinstall runs) takes the hook back;\\n- so does any `lefthook.yml` edit, via the checksum;\\n- and the reclaim lands *during* the commit, not in some window before the next agent turn.\\n\\nThe user-vi\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2385,\n      \"title\": \"fix(cleanup): fail closed before deleting shadow history\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2385\",\n      \"head\": \"c164844c20a61501538054d9f381e63f59fdd591\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-session-cleanup-safety\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Closes #2378\\n\\nRelated to #2350 and #2358.\\n\\nEntire keeps uncondensed checkpoint commits reachable through shadow branches. Cleanup could mistake incomplete safety evidence for proof that a branch was unused: expired state with pending work could be removed, a ref read failure could be treated as absence, and malformed records could be omitted from cleanup inventory. Each path could leave shadow-only checkpoint history unreachable.\\n\\n## Why cleanup could orphan history\\n\\nSession state older than seven days was purged based on age even when it still recorded uncondensed checkpoint work. Separately, go-git can report an unreadable loose ref as not found, and session discovery treated that result a\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2382,\n      \"title\": \"status: drop the manual-commit strategy name (only strategy; jargon)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2382\",\n      \"head\": \"6461e7d13eb06e483bb5843132815cf4b4bc2254\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/status-drop-strategy-name\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/887\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.io) after CI was requested for the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2381,\n      \"title\": \"Slow Codex In Review\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2381\",\n      \"head\": \"0646d5f3438fcfd45397e2961d028eb7a8cfef15\",\n      \"branch\": \"slow-codex-in-review\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/373\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.io) after CI was requested for the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2380,\n      \"title\": \"cli: add code search via peregrine (ENT-993, ENT-994)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2380\",\n      \"head\": \"55ceb6eebbf97ce18b63a2f5d1f5f25b2f1fd3a9\",\n      \"branch\": \"evis/ent-990-cross-region-code-search-cli-peregrine-us-first-then-eu\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/739\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.io) after CI was requested for the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2379,\n      \"title\": \"feat(claudecode): estimate session cost from token usage\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2379\",\n      \"head\": \"45de14c0ae8bdae833a0d0e5b5d428bcecfdae41\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/claudecode-cost\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/812\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.io) after CI was requested for the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2374,\n      \"title\": \"Fail E2E tasks when the test regex selects no tests\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2374\",\n      \"head\": \"e97ae2111efd6eef9e8877abb3e017083bff1075\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/e2e-empty-test-runs\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1307\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAn E2E regex matching no tests made gotestsum exit successfully and the reporter print `ALL 0 TESTS PASSED`. The existing E2E mise tasks now fail that selection after writing their reports. Truncated event streams with no completed parent tests also fail instead of reporting success.\\n\\n## What Changed\\n\\n- Add an opt-in `-fail-on-empty` reporter flag. Only terminal parent `pass`, `fail`, or `skip` events satisfy it. Skipped tests still count, and a retry needs its own terminal event.\\n- Show `NO TESTS RAN` for empty input and an incomplete count and `INCOMPLETE` banner for u\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2373,\n      \"title\": \"e2e: pin the cursor model, and scale a per-test prompt timeout\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2373\",\n      \"head\": \"034a91c358691e32963407f8b655f56747fe13f1\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/more-e2e-followup\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Two follow-ups from the prompt-timeout review, plus three adjacent findings I left for a maintainer.\\n\\nRebased 2026-11-02 onto a main that removed Gemini CLI and added Antigravity. Neither half of this change has been superseded: `promptTimeout` on main still takes `(agentDefault, cfg)` with no scaling and no exact-timeout split, `E2E_CLAUDE_MODEL` / `E2E_COPILOT_MODEL` / `E2E_CURSOR_MODEL` still do not exist, and `opencode.go:221` still passes the warmup budget through the scaling option.\\n\\n## Cursor pinned no model\\n\\n`cursor_cli.go` built `agent --force --workspace <dir>` with no `--model`, and the isolated E2E config seeds `cli-config.json` with `{}`, so nothing pinned a model from either di\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2369,\n      \"title\": \"fix(doctor): report a fail-closed checkpoint sync election\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2369\",\n      \"head\": \"dcbe78ec6ce4774fe1166f0606af1bb86412a40d\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/doctor-failed-sync-election\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1303\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nWhen `checkpoint_push_remote` names a missing remote, checkpoint sync fails closed. `entire doctor` previously either claimed a remote was elected or, in single-remote repos, said nothing.\\n\\nThis change makes the shared doctor/enable note consult the actual election result and report `Checkpoint sync: DISABLED` with targeted guidance. A typed error distinguishes a missing configured remote from other settings failures, while dedicated `checkpoint_remote` destinations remain exempt because they bypass election.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- `mise run check`\\n- `GOOS=windows go vet ./...`\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2358,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): prevent shadow cleanup with malformed session state\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2358\",\n      \"head\": \"ac06cb619697bfa0a808625e6bbfed0739e4cf4d\",\n      \"branch\": \"codex/malformed-state-cleanup\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\n- keep `StateStore.List` tolerant for observational callers\\r\\n- add `StateStore.ListStrict` for operations requiring a complete inventory\\r\\n- make both unattended shadow-cleanup paths fail closed when any session state cannot be loaded\\r\\n- document the cleanup safety contract\\r\\n\\r\\nWhen persisted session state is malformed, cleanup now aborts instead of potentially deleting a still-needed shadow ref.\\r\\n\\r\\nCloses #2350\\r\\n\\r\\n## Testing\\r\\n\\r\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/session -run '\"'\"'TestStateStore_List_(SkipsMalformedState|Strict_RejectsMalformedState)$'\"'\"' -count=1`\\r\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run '\"'\"'Test(CleanupPushedShadowBranches_MalformedStateFailsClosed|DeleteShadowBranchesIfUncha\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2352,\n      \"title\": \"cursor: install the cmd.exe hook wrappers on Windows, and tolerate a BOM on hook input\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2352\",\n      \"head\": \"c4120b12f530cb8b703d52b7bfcf40cfe976f26a\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-cursor-ai-windows-test\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Makes Cursor hooks fire on Windows, so sessions and checkpoints get recorded there. Fixes #1424.\\n\\nTwo things stopped them: the wrapper Entire installs cannot run under Cursor'\"'\"'s PowerShell hook runner, and the payload arrives with a UTF-8 BOM our JSON decode rejects. Both fixed here; the BOM fix is at the shared chokepoint, so it covers every agent.\\n\\nTrail: https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1291\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2338,\n      \"title\": \"Spike: run the repo'\"'\"'s trail runner configs locally with entire review\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2338\",\n      \"head\": \"5bbb03515250c69fb1f6a1d27a7c98156051cd9d\",\n      \"branch\": \"peter/spike-review-use-runner-config\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1279\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n**Problem:** review feedback only arrives after a push. Every finding from the trail'\"'\"'s runners costs a round trip through the server, and the fix for one often surfaces the next.\\n\\n**Solution:** `entire review --use-runner-config` reads `.entire/runners/*.json` and runs those runners locally, so you can see what the trail will say before pushing.\\n\\nThis is a spike, opened as a draft. It came out of [a Slack thread](https://entireio.slack.com/archives/C0A095SNK32/p1788784813352809); the flag shape is Stefan'\"'\"'s suggestion, so the existing `entire review` keeps working untouched and this \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2335,\n      \"title\": \"feat(checkpoint): elect the Entire remote for checkpoint sync\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2335\",\n      \"head\": \"c59bd41276cb2943556b9176483fc4bd78c9e14d\",\n      \"branch\": \"toby/entire-remote-election\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1276\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nRepos with several remotes were told to set `checkpoint_remote`, which names a dedicated GitHub checkpoint repository and silently ignores a remote name. The remote picker is `strategy_options.checkpoint_push_remote` in `.entire/settings.local.json`; the topology note and the git-refs multi-URL warning now say so, and tests pin both strings.\\n\\nEntire'\"'\"'s own `entire://` remote is the store built for checkpoint data, and refs pushed to an Entire mirror stay on Entire. When a repo has one, checkpoints should sync there without configuration.\\n\\n## What\\n\\n**Entire tier in the electio\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2332,\n      \"title\": \"session adopt: refuse a session that is not this command'\"'\"'s caller\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2332\",\n      \"head\": \"302cc23cb64e1f8f43f71fede58692b7b53132ca\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/adopt-caller-guard\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1273\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\n`session adopt` moves a live session into the current worktree and resets its checkpoint bookkeeping (`StepCount`, `CheckpointTranscriptStart`, `LastCheckpointID`, and `FilesTouched`). Selecting the wrong session can therefore mutate another agent'\"'\"'s running session and detach its next commit from its work.\\n\\nThat happened when an agent read a foreign session ID from `entire session current` and passed it to `session adopt`. #2322 made ca'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' 'st: pin ENTIRE_TEST_TTY in non-interactive tests\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2479\",\n      \"head\": \"9cc8df071906c0b2c08d2d14eb8dabbfeed3e007\",\n      \"branch\": \"doctor-test-pin-tty\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"These two tests assert the non-interactive path of runSessionsFix. If a dev shell happens to set ENTIRE_TEST_TTY=1, CanPromptInteractively() returns true and the test falls through to the real huh form instead of exercising the guard. Pinning it to 0 makes the environment deterministic.\\r\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2408,\n      \"title\": \"fix: repair stale checkpoints and flag worktree setup gaps\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2408\",\n      \"head\": \"ed846bbd6232f7af00050776e94a8fc50792067b\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-checkpoint-metadata-followups\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This PR is stacked on #2404. It should target `krk/doctor-shrink-checkpoint-metadata` while that PR is open, then be retargeted to `main` after #2404 lands.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n#2404 prevents new oversized `prompt_attributions` metadata and adds an explicit doctor repair. Two cases remain.\\n\\nA stale clone can still contain the original oversized history plus newer local checkpoints after another clone repairs the remote. Its next push may reject the repaired history as unrelated or replay the old commits and reintroduce the oversized blobs.\\n\\nCommit hashes cannot identify the shared boundary reliably because rewriting metadata and signing commits both change commit IDs. OPF also runs before ordinary \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2404,\n      \"title\": \"fix(doctor): repair and prevent oversized checkpoint metadata.json blobs\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2404\",\n      \"head\": \"878a05e1829aa7a010e06ea06f7fd21ff70b5f39\",\n      \"branch\": \"krk/doctor-shrink-checkpoint-metadata\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1320\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nCLI versions before v0.10.1 walked nested git checkouts (Claude Code'\"'\"'s `.claude/worktrees/`) into `prompt_attributions.user_added_per_file` on every prompt, producing 70MB and 106MB per-session `metadata.json` blobs on `entire/checkpoints/v1`. GitHub refuses blobs over 100 MiB, so one such blob anywhere in the branch history makes it unpushable and unmirrorable there. A customer hit exactly this (Plain T-88, Gitea push-mirrored to GitHub). The v0.10.1 fix (#1937, #1969) stopped new bloat but left the history behind, and the only remedy was a hand-written `git filter-repo` sc\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2400,\n      \"title\": \"Add product changelog commands\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2400\",\n      \"head\": \"28697d63bfd523ac2790450348722a778c09483e\",\n      \"branch\": \"ashtom/product-changelog\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1319\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.io) after CI was requested for the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Read-only outbound HTTP to a fixed origin with URL validation and no auth or local repo state; main operational risk is search fetching many posts when there are no matches.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds a **public, repo-independent** `entire changelog` command (plus `changelog search`) that fetches Ent\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2395,\n      \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): surface git-refs push queue failures\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2395\",\n      \"head\": \"2569fb7d9801e026462047659b187bdc2b4ee74f\",\n      \"branch\": \"codex/issue-2393-push-bookkeeping\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\n- return an explicit partial failure when a git-refs checkpoint is written locally but cannot be added to the push queue\\r\\n- preserve the local ref and retryable condensation state, then re-enqueue on a later write\\r\\n- add store-level and condensation-level regressions and update the architecture contract\\r\\n\\r\\nCloses #2393\\r\\n\\r\\n## Why this approach\\r\\n\\r\\nThe ref update and queue append cannot be one atomic operation. Rolling back a valid local ref would discard recoverable data, while scanning every local checkpoint ref during pre-push would conflict with the queue'\"'\"'s purpose and with fetched-ref semantics. This change therefore makes the partial outcome explicit at the store boundary. T\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2391,\n      \"title\": \"Recommendations v2 (PR 5a): three noisy rules deleted, the rest cite their rows\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2391\",\n      \"head\": \"6c90ab513467c0843e79500096d63417e849e2ed\",\n      \"branch\": \"pr5a-recommendations-v2\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1317\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nTask 1–4 of `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-11-pr5-recommendations-v2.md`.\\n\\n**This PR: +616/-222. Cumulative across the stack (PR1+PR2+this vs `main`): +63158/-13182.**\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n`entire checkpoint tokens` on a real 286.3M-token checkpoint printed **seven** recommendations, two of which said the same thing and none of which named a number a reader could find. It now prints two:\\n\\n```\\nToken usage\\nTotal:  286.3M tokens\\n  Input: 110.2k | Cache read: 269.4M | Cache write: 16M | Output: 824.2k | API calls: 509 | Per call: 562.6k\\n\\nHow it was billed\\n  ...\\n  Of the total, subagents u\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2388,\n      \"title\": \"fix(hooks): register Entire with Lefthook instead of owning its hook files\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2388\",\n      \"head\": \"fc5d778c4d54a11bdf5f8cad885f09ab028bda3a\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/lefthook-integration\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1314\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\nLefthook regenerates **every** file in `.git/hooks` from its own config, gated by a checksum of that config — and it does so at the top of whatever hook fires next, typically the `pre-commit` of the very commit being made. Entire'\"'\"'s turn-start self-heal (`EnsureSetup` → reinstall if not installed) therefore always loses the race:\\n\\n- `lefthook install -f` (what Lefthook'\"'\"'s own npm postinstall runs) takes the hook back;\\n- so does any `lefthook.yml` edit, via the checksum;\\n- and the reclaim lands *during* the commit, not in some window before the next agent turn.\\n\\nThe user-vi\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2385,\n      \"title\": \"fix(cleanup): fail closed before deleting shadow history\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2385\",\n      \"head\": \"c164844c20a61501538054d9f381e63f59fdd591\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-session-cleanup-safety\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Closes #2378\\n\\nRelated to #2350 and #2358.\\n\\nEntire keeps uncondensed checkpoint commits reachable through shadow branches. Cleanup could mistake incomplete safety evidence for proof that a branch was unused: expired state with pending work could be removed, a ref read failure could be treated as absence, and malformed records could be omitted from cleanup inventory. Each path could leave shadow-only checkpoint history unreachable.\\n\\n## Why cleanup could orphan history\\n\\nSession state older than seven days was purged based on age even when it still recorded uncondensed checkpoint work. Separately, go-git can report an unreadable loose ref as not found, and session discovery treated that result a\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2382,\n      \"title\": \"status: drop the manual-commit strategy name (only strategy; jargon)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2382\",\n      \"head\": \"6461e7d13eb06e483bb5843132815cf4b4bc2254\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/status-drop-strategy-name\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/887\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.io) after CI was requested for the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2381,\n      \"title\": \"Slow Codex In Review\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2381\",\n      \"head\": \"0646d5f3438fcfd45397e2961d028eb7a8cfef15\",\n      \"branch\": \"slow-codex-in-review\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/373\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.io) after CI was requested for the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2380,\n      \"title\": \"cli: add code search via peregrine (ENT-993, ENT-994)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2380\",\n      \"head\": \"55ceb6eebbf97ce18b63a2f5d1f5f25b2f1fd3a9\",\n      \"branch\": \"evis/ent-990-cross-region-code-search-cli-peregrine-us-first-then-eu\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/739\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.io) after CI was requested for the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2379,\n      \"title\": \"feat(claudecode): estimate session cost from token usage\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2379\",\n      \"head\": \"45de14c0ae8bdae833a0d0e5b5d428bcecfdae41\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/claudecode-cost\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/812\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.io) after CI was requested for the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2374,\n      \"title\": \"Fail E2E tasks when the test regex selects no tests\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2374\",\n      \"head\": \"e97ae2111efd6eef9e8877abb3e017083bff1075\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/e2e-empty-test-runs\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1307\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAn E2E regex matching no tests made gotestsum exit successfully and the reporter print `ALL 0 TESTS PASSED`. The existing E2E mise tasks now fail that selection after writing their reports. Truncated event streams with no completed parent tests also fail instead of reporting success.\\n\\n## What Changed\\n\\n- Add an opt-in `-fail-on-empty` reporter flag. Only terminal parent `pass`, `fail`, or `skip` events satisfy it. Skipped tests still count, and a retry needs its own terminal event.\\n- Show `NO TESTS RAN` for empty input and an incomplete count and `INCOMPLETE` banner for u\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2373,\n      \"title\": \"e2e: pin the cursor model, and scale a per-test prompt timeout\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2373\",\n      \"head\": \"034a91c358691e32963407f8b655f56747fe13f1\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/more-e2e-followup\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Two follow-ups from the prompt-timeout review, plus three adjacent findings I left for a maintainer.\\n\\nRebased 2026-11-02 onto a main that removed Gemini CLI and added Antigravity. Neither half of this change has been superseded: `promptTimeout` on main still takes `(agentDefault, cfg)` with no scaling and no exact-timeout split, `E2E_CLAUDE_MODEL` / `E2E_COPILOT_MODEL` / `E2E_CURSOR_MODEL` still do not exist, and `opencode.go:221` still passes the warmup budget through the scaling option.\\n\\n## Cursor pinned no model\\n\\n`cursor_cli.go` built `agent --force --workspace <dir>` with no `--model`, and the isolated E2E config seeds `cli-config.json` with `{}`, so nothing pinned a model from either di\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2369,\n      \"title\": \"fix(doctor): report a fail-closed checkpoint sync election\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2369\",\n      \"head\": \"dcbe78ec6ce4774fe1166f0606af1bb86412a40d\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/doctor-failed-sync-election\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1303\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nWhen `checkpoint_push_remote` names a missing remote, checkpoint sync fails closed. `entire doctor` previously either claimed a remote was elected or, in single-remote repos, said nothing.\\n\\nThis change makes the shared doctor/enable note consult the actual election result and report `Checkpoint sync: DISABLED` with targeted guidance. A typed error distinguishes a missing configured remote from other settings failures, while dedicated `checkpoint_remote` destinations remain exempt because they bypass election.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- `mise run check`\\n- `GOOS=windows go vet ./...`\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2358,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): prevent shadow cleanup with malformed session state\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2358\",\n      \"head\": \"ac06cb619697bfa0a808625e6bbfed0739e4cf4d\",\n      \"branch\": \"codex/malformed-state-cleanup\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\n- keep `StateStore.List` tolerant for observational callers\\r\\n- add `StateStore.ListStrict` for operations requiring a complete inventory\\r\\n- make both unattended shadow-cleanup paths fail closed when any session state cannot be loaded\\r\\n- document the cleanup safety contract\\r\\n\\r\\nWhen persisted session state is malformed, cleanup now aborts instead of potentially deleting a still-needed shadow ref.\\r\\n\\r\\nCloses #2350\\r\\n\\r\\n## Testing\\r\\n\\r\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/session -run '\"'\"'TestStateStore_List_(SkipsMalformedState|Strict_RejectsMalformedState)$'\"'\"' -count=1`\\r\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run '\"'\"'Test(CleanupPushedShadowBranches_MalformedStateFailsClosed|DeleteShadowBranchesIfUncha\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2352,\n      \"title\": \"cursor: install the cmd.exe hook wrappers on Windows, and tolerate a BOM on hook input\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2352\",\n      \"head\": \"c4120b12f530cb8b703d52b7bfcf40cfe976f26a\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-cursor-ai-windows-test\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Makes Cursor hooks fire on Windows, so sessions and checkpoints get recorded there. Fixes #1424.\\n\\nTwo things stopped them: the wrapper Entire installs cannot run under Cursor'\"'\"'s PowerShell hook runner, and the payload arrives with a UTF-8 BOM our JSON decode rejects. Both fixed here; the BOM fix is at the shared chokepoint, so it covers every agent.\\n\\nTrail: https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1291\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2338,\n      \"title\": \"Spike: run the repo'\"'\"'s trail runner configs locally with entire review\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2338\",\n      \"head\": \"5bbb03515250c69fb1f6a1d27a7c98156051cd9d\",\n      \"branch\": \"peter/spike-review-use-runner-config\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1279\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n**Problem:** review feedback only arrives after a push. Every finding from the trail'\"'\"'s runners costs a round trip through the server, and the fix for one often surfaces the next.\\n\\n**Solution:** `entire review --use-runner-config` reads `.entire/runners/*.json` and runs those runners locally, so you can see what the trail will say before pushing.\\n\\nThis is a spike, opened as a draft. It came out of [a Slack thread](https://entireio.slack.com/archives/C0A095SNK32/p1788784813352809); the flag shape is Stefan'\"'\"'s suggestion, so the existing `entire review` keeps working untouched and this \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2335,\n      \"title\": \"feat(checkpoint): elect the Entire remote for checkpoint sync\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2335\",\n      \"head\": \"c59bd41276cb2943556b9176483fc4bd78c9e14d\",\n      \"branch\": \"toby/entire-remote-election\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1276\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nRepos with several remotes were told to set `checkpoint_remote`, which names a dedicated GitHub checkpoint repository and silently ignores a remote name. The remote picker is `strategy_options.checkpoint_push_remote` in `.entire/settings.local.json`; the topology note and the git-refs multi-URL warning now say so, and tests pin both strings.\\n\\nEntire'\"'\"'s own `entire://` remote is the store built for checkpoint data, and refs pushed to an Entire mirror stay on Entire. When a repo has one, checkpoints should sync there without configuration.\\n\\n## What\\n\\n**Entire tier in the electio\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2332,\n      \"title\": \"session adopt: refuse a session that is not this command'\"'\"'s caller\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2332\",\n      \"head\": \"302cc23cb64e1f8f43f71fede58692b7b53132ca\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/adopt-caller-guard\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1273\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\n`session adopt` moves a live session into the current worktree and resets its checkpoint bookkeeping (`StepCount`, `CheckpointTranscriptStart`, `LastCheckpointID`, and `FilesTouched`). Selecting the wrong session can therefore mutate another agent'\"'\"'s running session and detach its next commit from its work.\\n\\nThat happened when an agent read a foreign session ID from `entire session current` and passed it to `session adopt`. #2322 made ca'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":12708}},"started_at_ms":1794842128838,"completed_at_ms":1794842128839}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:28.970Z","ordinal":3019,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-19eb1e68-30d8-483e-a0c5-b94bceafaff7","process_id":"15847","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' 'ller resolution explicit through `SessionResolution` and `IsCaller()`; this PR applies that ownership boundary to the command that mutates a \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2331,\n      \"title\": \"Fix Lefthook overwrite detection and remediation guidance\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2331\",\n      \"head\": \"777fb981d4992ce80369812ddf47ff6586afc7ba\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/lefthook-overwrite-warning\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \" ## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\n  - Classify Lefthook as a hook manager that can overwrite Entire hooks.\\r\\n  - Add Lefthook-specific remediation guidance using scripts.\\r\\n  - Preserve Git hook arguments, including `pre-push` arguments and stdin.\\r\\n  - Avoid invalid hook paths such as `lefthook.ymlpre-push`.\\r\\n  - Reference the detected Lefthook config path.\\r\\n  - Account for custom Lefthook `source_dir` values.\\r\\n  - Add focused regression tests.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ## Validation\\r\\n\\r\\n  ```text\\r\\n  go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run '\"'\"'TestHookManagerWarning_(Lefthook|Husky|Multiple)$|\\r\\n  TestHookManagerWarning_LefthookConfigPath'\"'\"' -count=1\\r\\n  ```\\r\\n\\r\\n  Fixes #2263\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2327,\n      \"title\": \"feat(checkpoint): add `entire checkpoint migrate`\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2327\",\n      \"head\": \"73ef6f3dc487185ac242217932ed9f9b80f1cdba\",\n      \"branch\": \"toby/checkpoint-sync\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1271\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n> **Stacked on #2335** (`feat(checkpoint): elect the Entire remote for checkpoint sync`). Review that first; this PR'\"'\"'s base is its branch and will be retargeted to `main` once it merges. Best reviewed **commit by commit**: the four commits are layered so each builds and is reviewable on its own.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nOnce an Entire remote is elected (#2335), new checkpoints flow there, but the ones already pushed to GitHub stay behind. This PR brings that backlog over, verifies it, and cleans up the old remote with consent, then rewards the user with what they have accumulated.\\n\\n## Commits\\n\\n1. *\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2320,\n      \"title\": \"refactor(gitrepo): finish Git metadata consumer migration\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2320\",\n      \"head\": \"28729ce33996d37830578d9736fa89ea5788f44e\",\n      \"branch\": \"refactor-remaining-git-metadata-consumers\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Part 5 of #2190'\"'\"'s [agreed split](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2190#issuecomment-5499945525), following the canonical resolver in #2241 and checkpoint migration in #2254.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis branch includes the session migration from #2285 and strategy migration from #2305. Both prerequisites remain open. Keep this PR **open** until they land, then refresh onto main so reviewers can assess the remaining-consumer changes separately.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Why this change is needed\\r\\n\\r\\nThe earlier migrations introduced `gitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata`, but several consumers still interpreted Git metadata through older code. Codex and status had their own traversal logic. Settings, review, investigation, and trail \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2319,\n      \"title\": \"fix: report GitHub errors in install script\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2319\",\n      \"head\": \"4d53c2e9570cd9464c8a566c45a6f154a2e21c25\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/installer-github-errors\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\n- distinguish GitHub HTTP failures from curl transport failures\\r\\n- report actionable errors for invalid tokens and GitHub API failures\\r\\n- include GitHub'\"'\"'s error message for rejected requests when available\\r\\n- preserve curl diagnostics for DNS, TLS, timeout, and connection failures\\r\\n- detect successful responses that do not contain the expected release tag\\r\\n- add GitHub'\"'\"'s recommended REST API headers\\r\\n- integrate with the existing `install.entire.com` → GitHub fallback and its metadata timeouts\\r\\n\\r\\nThe installer does not print or otherwise expose `GITHUB_TOKEN`.\\r\\n\\r\\nCloses #2318\\r\\n\\r\\n## Testing\\r\\n\\r\\n- `bash -n scripts/install.sh`\\r\\n- `shellcheck scripts/install.sh`\\r\\n- `bash scripts/tes\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2312,\n      \"title\": \"fix: explain checkpoint HTTPS auth failures and skip futile retries\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2312\",\n      \"head\": \"81270ffe35885973f50deee3369f4de6f7e87c6a\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/checkpoint-https-auth-help\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1259\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nWhen a user pastes a GitHub username/PAT into `git push`, the parent push can succeed while Entire'\"'\"'s separate non-interactive policy/push subprocesses cannot authenticate. Today that produces an opaque failure followed by futile per-ref retries and fetch/replay attempts.\\n\\n- Preserve typed missing-credential and rejected-HTTP-authentication causes at the Git wrapper boundary, without putting potentially credential-bearing output into the error. Keep the original exec error available through wrapping.\\n- Stop recovery immediately for recognized HTTP auth failures in both ch\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2305,\n      \"title\": \"refactor(strategy): use canonical git metadata resolution (split part 4)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2305\",\n      \"head\": \"62d3545787fa18cd0b4ec356b27d34e4e7620945\",\n      \"branch\": \"refactor-strategy-hook-metadata-resolution\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Strategy and hook paths still resolve Git metadata through separate helpers and subprocesses. This moves their physical directory and worktree-ID lookups to `gitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata`, using explicit worktree roots while preserving rooted storage access and caller-owned failure policy.\\n\\nPart 4 of #2190’s [agreed split](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2190#issuecomment-5499945525), following #2241 and #2254. **Depends on #2285 (part 3).** Keep this PR **open** until part 3 lands; then rebase onto refreshed main and rerun checks before requesting review.\\n\\n## Before requesting review\\n\\n- Move `session.NewStateStore` in this PR together with the session lock. This PR moves `stateLockF\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2303,\n      \"title\": \"fix: detect empty-tree commits and stop condensing over them\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2303\",\n      \"head\": \"5b0359e43980b7d9624e5666b9de67e534f9b86a\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/2111-index-emptied-mid-commit\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1253\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThe root corruption is git'\"'\"'s own bug, not Entire'\"'\"'s, and cannot be prevented from a hook: git (and go-git v6, independently) treats a missing \\\\`.git/index\\\\` (ENOENT) as an empty in-core index, and \\\\`git status\\\\` renames a fresh index over the real one as a side effect — so any concurrent process running \\\\`git status\\\\` at the wrong moment can cause a commit to record an empty tree. The previously-merged mitigation (#2143) already scrubs Entire'\"'\"'s own \\\\`git status\\\\` calls, but by the time any hook runs, git has already read the index — prevention was never available from her\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2302,\n      \"title\": \"feat: differentiated per-hook timeouts, replacing the flat 30s cap\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2302\",\n      \"head\": \"3b167700db4fd023f0141596f7c45d2977eaf1e3\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/2115-differentiated-hook-timeouts\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1252\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- A flat 30-second hook timeout applied to every agent/hook combination. #2115 argued this is wrong in both directions and proposed differentiation like the existing SessionEnd=3s budgeter precedent; #1137/#957 report repeated real timeouts (Codex hooks externally enforce this same 30s and kill the process, matching their symptoms exactly).\\n- This PR builds the **mechanism**, not new guessed values: a new optional \\\\`agent.HookTimeoutProvider\\\\` capability (mirroring the existing \\\\`SessionEndBudgeter\\\\` pattern exactly), resolved via \\\\`agent.HookTimeoutFor(agent, hookName)\\\\`\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2301,\n      \"title\": \"feat: support a generic git provider for --checkpoint-remote\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2301\",\n      \"head\": \"339383eb25ce9159f4cd34f8485afd28af408eb4\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/2033-checkpoint-remote-generic-provider\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1251\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- \\\\`--checkpoint-remote\\\\` (and the \\\\`.entire/settings.json\\\\` \\\\`checkpoint_remote\\\\` config) only accepted \\\\`{\\\"provider\\\":\\\"github\\\",\\\"repo\\\":\\\"owner/repo\\\"}\\\\` — no way to point checkpoint storage at a self-hosted git server (Gitea, GitLab CE, a bare git server).\\n- Adds an additive \\\\`\\\"provider\\\":\\\"git\\\"\\\\` option that accepts an explicit remote URL (\\\\`--checkpoint-remote git:<url>\\\\`) instead of an owner/repo pair resolved against a hardcoded \\\\`github.com\\\\` template. The existing \\\\`github:owner/repo\\\\` shorthand is completely unchanged.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n- Real validation/URL-construction fu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2300,\n      \"title\": \"feat: surface progress during the OPF re-redaction phase of checkpoint sync\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2300\",\n      \"head\": \"6d64da8674cade8c20bf13f7e23a88bf5a2fc560\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/1683-pre-push-sync-progress\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1250\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- Long git pushes that trigger checkpoint sync showed only a static \\\"Pushing...\\\" line, feeling stuck on slow pushes. Auditing the real pre-push flow (both the git-branch and git-refs backends) found that nearly every phase already had a progress label except one: the OPF re-redaction shell-out, the single genuinely silent multi-second phase (5-100s per existing code comments).\\n- Added a progress line for that phase specifically, reusing the existing dots-progress convention (\\\\`startProgressDots\\\\`) rather than inventing new UI.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n- Real \\\\`testutil.InitRepo\\\\` rep\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2299,\n      \"title\": \"feat: discover untracked OpenCode sessions on entire session attach\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2299\",\n      \"head\": \"433596f6526232b5337660cf91c9863c5eabf428\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/1992-opencode-session-attach-discovery\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1249\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- \\\\`entire session attach --agent opencode\\\\` (no ID) required first manually running \\\\`opencode session list\\\\` to find an untracked native OpenCode session. Now Entire does that lookup itself.\\n- New optional agent capability \\\\`agent.NativeSessionLister\\\\` (same resolution pattern as the existing \\\\`TranscriptFetcher\\\\` capability), implemented for OpenCode via \\\\`opencode session list --format json\\\\`.\\n- Scoping matches the issue'\"'\"'s own rule: a session is offered only if its working directory is the current worktree root or below it. Already-tracked sessions are excluded via En\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2298,\n      \"title\": \"fix: fall back to reasoningText in the compacted Copilot transcript builder\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2298\",\n      \"head\": \"ddd64adff4e0bf025e6e16a2b0b73f1fdf43e7ca\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/copilot-compact-reasoning-text-fallback\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1248\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- Follow-up to the Copilot CLI empty-transcript fix (#1070): the same class of bug existed independently in \\\\`transcript/compact/copilot.go\\\\`'\"'\"'s \\\\`copilotAssistantLine\\\\`, which builds the compacted \\\\`transcript.jsonl\\\\` stored in checkpoints — a different consumer than the live CLI-side extraction #1070 fixed. It dropped \\\\`reasoningText\\\\` content whenever the primary \\\\`content\\\\` field was empty.\\n- No GitHub issue was filed for this — found via direct fixture inspection while investigating #1070, confirmed still current on \\\\`main\\\\` before fixing.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n- Real fixture \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2297,\n      \"title\": \"fix: correlate Claude Code SubagentStop on agent_id, not tool_use_id\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2297\",\n      \"head\": \"87308552efec1ab3cec788fc52a002e898ecffe3\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/2215-claudecode-subagentstop-correlation\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1247\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- Every Claude Code subagent run was silently discarded — only the parent session got recorded. Root cause: Entire correlated a \\\\`SubagentStop\\\\` hook event back to its in-flight task record via \\\\`tool_use_id\\\\`, but Claude Code'\"'\"'s real \\\\`SubagentStop\\\\` payload never carries that field (it'\"'\"'s documented only on tool events, not subagent lifecycle events). The lookup always missed and the handler returned early.\\n- Fix falls back to \\\\`agent_id\\\\` — the field genuinely shared between a subagent'\"'\"'s \\\\`SubagentStart\\\\` (via \\\\`PostToolUse[Agent]\\\\`'\"'\"'s \\\\`tool_response.agentId\\\\`) and its \\\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2296,\n      \"title\": \"fix: fall back to transformedContent/reasoningText when Copilot CLI content is empty\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2296\",\n      \"head\": \"0bb470e12245ee0ead70075f3a355260a6383a87\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/1070-copilot-empty-transcript-fallback\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1246\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- Copilot CLI sessions captured checkpoints fine, but the transcript detail view was empty/incomplete: Entire'\"'\"'s extraction only read the primary \\\\`content\\\\` field of user/assistant message events, with no fallback for when Copilot CLI populates \\\\`transformedContent\\\\`/\\\\`reasoningText\\\\` instead.\\n- Prompts now fall back to \\\\`transformedContent\\\\` (stripped of Copilot'\"'\"'s injected wrapper blocks); summaries fall back to \\\\`reasoningText\\\\`. Populated \\\\`content\\\\` still always wins.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n- Real fixture lifted from an actual captured Copilot CLI transcript.\\n- Before: \\\\`extrac\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2295,\n      \"title\": \"fix: give each Pi subagent run a unique session identifier\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2295\",\n      \"head\": \"2f9a64cb8702f68951b3d197d22d71589b3a33f5\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/1870-pi-subagent-session-collision\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1245\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- Every Pi subagent transcript file is named \\\\`session.jsonl\\\\` regardless of which subagent/run produced it, so the session-ID resolver collapsed every subagent invocation to the literal ID \\\\`\\\"session\\\"\\\\`. Concurrent or sequential subagent runs overwrote each other'\"'\"'s staged/archived transcript copy, and a checkpoint could end up storing a different subagent'\"'\"'s content than the one it was supposedly capturing.\\n- Fix derives a unique ID per invocation (\\\\`<parentUUID>_<subagentID>_run-<n>\\\\`) by walking up the real nested directory structure Pi already writes, instead of using \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2294,\n      \"title\": \"fix: warn visibly when an agent commits with no active session recorded\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2294\",\n      \"head\": \"2f07df61fe7a555771f93f06660fa86e05bdb911\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/1965-warn-commit-no-session\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1244\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- When a commit landed in an Entire-enabled repo with no active/recent session found (e.g. agent launched from a parent or bare-clone directory with no hook config), Entire only logged a debug-level line — invisible to a normal user. Now prints a visible stderr warning, rate-limited to once per 24h.\\n- Only fires when a coding-agent environment marker is actually present (\\\\`CLAUDECODE\\\\`/\\\\`GEMINI_CLI\\\\`/\\\\`COPILOT_CLI\\\\`/\\\\`PI_CODING_AGENT\\\\`) — a human'\"'\"'s own commit with no marker never warns, even with zero sessions ever recorded. This mirrors the existing agent-detection prece\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2293,\n      \"title\": \"fix: qualify \\\"no checkpoints found\\\" when the scan limit truncated\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2293\",\n      \"head\": \"864d979249302c4705d24383d89bb135ab7af902\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/2089-explain-session-truncation-message\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1243\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- \\\\`entire checkpoint explain --session <id>\\\\` (default scan limit) printed an unqualified \\\"No checkpoints found on this branch\\\" even when the scan hit its budget before reaching a real match — an explicit \\\\`--limit\\\\` returned results fine. The truncation signal already existed internally but never reached the zero-results message.\\n- Now: when the scan was truncated before finding anything, the message says so and points at \\\\`--limit\\\\`. A genuinely empty branch still gets the plain message, unchanged.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n- Real repro: 5 committed checkpoints via \\\\`checkpoint.New\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2292,\n      \"title\": \"fix: point investigate/review error hints at entire agent add\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2292\",\n      \"head\": \"f1e2c6cad72c72fa2fc995ae2062f79664f42343\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/2249-stale-configure-agent-hints\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' 'ller resolution explicit through `SessionResolution` and `IsCaller()`; this PR applies that ownership boundary to the command that mutates a \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2331,\n      \"title\": \"Fix Lefthook overwrite detection and remediation guidance\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2331\",\n      \"head\": \"777fb981d4992ce80369812ddf47ff6586afc7ba\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/lefthook-overwrite-warning\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \" ## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\n  - Classify Lefthook as a hook manager that can overwrite Entire hooks.\\r\\n  - Add Lefthook-specific remediation guidance using scripts.\\r\\n  - Preserve Git hook arguments, including `pre-push` arguments and stdin.\\r\\n  - Avoid invalid hook paths such as `lefthook.ymlpre-push`.\\r\\n  - Reference the detected Lefthook config path.\\r\\n  - Account for custom Lefthook `source_dir` values.\\r\\n  - Add focused regression tests.\\r\\n\\r\\n  ## Validation\\r\\n\\r\\n  ```text\\r\\n  go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run '\"'\"'TestHookManagerWarning_(Lefthook|Husky|Multiple)$|\\r\\n  TestHookManagerWarning_LefthookConfigPath'\"'\"' -count=1\\r\\n  ```\\r\\n\\r\\n  Fixes #2263\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2327,\n      \"title\": \"feat(checkpoint): add `entire checkpoint migrate`\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2327\",\n      \"head\": \"73ef6f3dc487185ac242217932ed9f9b80f1cdba\",\n      \"branch\": \"toby/checkpoint-sync\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1271\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n> **Stacked on #2335** (`feat(checkpoint): elect the Entire remote for checkpoint sync`). Review that first; this PR'\"'\"'s base is its branch and will be retargeted to `main` once it merges. Best reviewed **commit by commit**: the four commits are layered so each builds and is reviewable on its own.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nOnce an Entire remote is elected (#2335), new checkpoints flow there, but the ones already pushed to GitHub stay behind. This PR brings that backlog over, verifies it, and cleans up the old remote with consent, then rewards the user with what they have accumulated.\\n\\n## Commits\\n\\n1. *\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2320,\n      \"title\": \"refactor(gitrepo): finish Git metadata consumer migration\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2320\",\n      \"head\": \"28729ce33996d37830578d9736fa89ea5788f44e\",\n      \"branch\": \"refactor-remaining-git-metadata-consumers\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Part 5 of #2190'\"'\"'s [agreed split](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2190#issuecomment-5499945525), following the canonical resolver in #2241 and checkpoint migration in #2254.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis branch includes the session migration from #2285 and strategy migration from #2305. Both prerequisites remain open. Keep this PR **open** until they land, then refresh onto main so reviewers can assess the remaining-consumer changes separately.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Why this change is needed\\r\\n\\r\\nThe earlier migrations introduced `gitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata`, but several consumers still interpreted Git metadata through older code. Codex and status had their own traversal logic. Settings, review, investigation, and trail \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2319,\n      \"title\": \"fix: report GitHub errors in install script\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2319\",\n      \"head\": \"4d53c2e9570cd9464c8a566c45a6f154a2e21c25\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/installer-github-errors\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\n- distinguish GitHub HTTP failures from curl transport failures\\r\\n- report actionable errors for invalid tokens and GitHub API failures\\r\\n- include GitHub'\"'\"'s error message for rejected requests when available\\r\\n- preserve curl diagnostics for DNS, TLS, timeout, and connection failures\\r\\n- detect successful responses that do not contain the expected release tag\\r\\n- add GitHub'\"'\"'s recommended REST API headers\\r\\n- integrate with the existing `install.entire.com` → GitHub fallback and its metadata timeouts\\r\\n\\r\\nThe installer does not print or otherwise expose `GITHUB_TOKEN`.\\r\\n\\r\\nCloses #2318\\r\\n\\r\\n## Testing\\r\\n\\r\\n- `bash -n scripts/install.sh`\\r\\n- `shellcheck scripts/install.sh`\\r\\n- `bash scripts/tes\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2312,\n      \"title\": \"fix: explain checkpoint HTTPS auth failures and skip futile retries\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2312\",\n      \"head\": \"81270ffe35885973f50deee3369f4de6f7e87c6a\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/checkpoint-https-auth-help\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1259\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nWhen a user pastes a GitHub username/PAT into `git push`, the parent push can succeed while Entire'\"'\"'s separate non-interactive policy/push subprocesses cannot authenticate. Today that produces an opaque failure followed by futile per-ref retries and fetch/replay attempts.\\n\\n- Preserve typed missing-credential and rejected-HTTP-authentication causes at the Git wrapper boundary, without putting potentially credential-bearing output into the error. Keep the original exec error available through wrapping.\\n- Stop recovery immediately for recognized HTTP auth failures in both ch\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2305,\n      \"title\": \"refactor(strategy): use canonical git metadata resolution (split part 4)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2305\",\n      \"head\": \"62d3545787fa18cd0b4ec356b27d34e4e7620945\",\n      \"branch\": \"refactor-strategy-hook-metadata-resolution\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Strategy and hook paths still resolve Git metadata through separate helpers and subprocesses. This moves their physical directory and worktree-ID lookups to `gitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata`, using explicit worktree roots while preserving rooted storage access and caller-owned failure policy.\\n\\nPart 4 of #2190’s [agreed split](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2190#issuecomment-5499945525), following #2241 and #2254. **Depends on #2285 (part 3).** Keep this PR **open** until part 3 lands; then rebase onto refreshed main and rerun checks before requesting review.\\n\\n## Before requesting review\\n\\n- Move `session.NewStateStore` in this PR together with the session lock. This PR moves `stateLockF\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2303,\n      \"title\": \"fix: detect empty-tree commits and stop condensing over them\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2303\",\n      \"head\": \"5b0359e43980b7d9624e5666b9de67e534f9b86a\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/2111-index-emptied-mid-commit\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1253\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThe root corruption is git'\"'\"'s own bug, not Entire'\"'\"'s, and cannot be prevented from a hook: git (and go-git v6, independently) treats a missing \\\\`.git/index\\\\` (ENOENT) as an empty in-core index, and \\\\`git status\\\\` renames a fresh index over the real one as a side effect — so any concurrent process running \\\\`git status\\\\` at the wrong moment can cause a commit to record an empty tree. The previously-merged mitigation (#2143) already scrubs Entire'\"'\"'s own \\\\`git status\\\\` calls, but by the time any hook runs, git has already read the index — prevention was never available from her\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2302,\n      \"title\": \"feat: differentiated per-hook timeouts, replacing the flat 30s cap\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2302\",\n      \"head\": \"3b167700db4fd023f0141596f7c45d2977eaf1e3\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/2115-differentiated-hook-timeouts\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1252\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- A flat 30-second hook timeout applied to every agent/hook combination. #2115 argued this is wrong in both directions and proposed differentiation like the existing SessionEnd=3s budgeter precedent; #1137/#957 report repeated real timeouts (Codex hooks externally enforce this same 30s and kill the process, matching their symptoms exactly).\\n- This PR builds the **mechanism**, not new guessed values: a new optional \\\\`agent.HookTimeoutProvider\\\\` capability (mirroring the existing \\\\`SessionEndBudgeter\\\\` pattern exactly), resolved via \\\\`agent.HookTimeoutFor(agent, hookName)\\\\`\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2301,\n      \"title\": \"feat: support a generic git provider for --checkpoint-remote\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2301\",\n      \"head\": \"339383eb25ce9159f4cd34f8485afd28af408eb4\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/2033-checkpoint-remote-generic-provider\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1251\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- \\\\`--checkpoint-remote\\\\` (and the \\\\`.entire/settings.json\\\\` \\\\`checkpoint_remote\\\\` config) only accepted \\\\`{\\\"provider\\\":\\\"github\\\",\\\"repo\\\":\\\"owner/repo\\\"}\\\\` — no way to point checkpoint storage at a self-hosted git server (Gitea, GitLab CE, a bare git server).\\n- Adds an additive \\\\`\\\"provider\\\":\\\"git\\\"\\\\` option that accepts an explicit remote URL (\\\\`--checkpoint-remote git:<url>\\\\`) instead of an owner/repo pair resolved against a hardcoded \\\\`github.com\\\\` template. The existing \\\\`github:owner/repo\\\\` shorthand is completely unchanged.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n- Real validation/URL-construction fu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2300,\n      \"title\": \"feat: surface progress during the OPF re-redaction phase of checkpoint sync\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2300\",\n      \"head\": \"6d64da8674cade8c20bf13f7e23a88bf5a2fc560\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/1683-pre-push-sync-progress\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1250\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- Long git pushes that trigger checkpoint sync showed only a static \\\"Pushing...\\\" line, feeling stuck on slow pushes. Auditing the real pre-push flow (both the git-branch and git-refs backends) found that nearly every phase already had a progress label except one: the OPF re-redaction shell-out, the single genuinely silent multi-second phase (5-100s per existing code comments).\\n- Added a progress line for that phase specifically, reusing the existing dots-progress convention (\\\\`startProgressDots\\\\`) rather than inventing new UI.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n- Real \\\\`testutil.InitRepo\\\\` rep\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2299,\n      \"title\": \"feat: discover untracked OpenCode sessions on entire session attach\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2299\",\n      \"head\": \"433596f6526232b5337660cf91c9863c5eabf428\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/1992-opencode-session-attach-discovery\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1249\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- \\\\`entire session attach --agent opencode\\\\` (no ID) required first manually running \\\\`opencode session list\\\\` to find an untracked native OpenCode session. Now Entire does that lookup itself.\\n- New optional agent capability \\\\`agent.NativeSessionLister\\\\` (same resolution pattern as the existing \\\\`TranscriptFetcher\\\\` capability), implemented for OpenCode via \\\\`opencode session list --format json\\\\`.\\n- Scoping matches the issue'\"'\"'s own rule: a session is offered only if its working directory is the current worktree root or below it. Already-tracked sessions are excluded via En\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2298,\n      \"title\": \"fix: fall back to reasoningText in the compacted Copilot transcript builder\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2298\",\n      \"head\": \"ddd64adff4e0bf025e6e16a2b0b73f1fdf43e7ca\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/copilot-compact-reasoning-text-fallback\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1248\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- Follow-up to the Copilot CLI empty-transcript fix (#1070): the same class of bug existed independently in \\\\`transcript/compact/copilot.go\\\\`'\"'\"'s \\\\`copilotAssistantLine\\\\`, which builds the compacted \\\\`transcript.jsonl\\\\` stored in checkpoints — a different consumer than the live CLI-side extraction #1070 fixed. It dropped \\\\`reasoningText\\\\` content whenever the primary \\\\`content\\\\` field was empty.\\n- No GitHub issue was filed for this — found via direct fixture inspection while investigating #1070, confirmed still current on \\\\`main\\\\` before fixing.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n- Real fixture \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2297,\n      \"title\": \"fix: correlate Claude Code SubagentStop on agent_id, not tool_use_id\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2297\",\n      \"head\": \"87308552efec1ab3cec788fc52a002e898ecffe3\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/2215-claudecode-subagentstop-correlation\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1247\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- Every Claude Code subagent run was silently discarded — only the parent session got recorded. Root cause: Entire correlated a \\\\`SubagentStop\\\\` hook event back to its in-flight task record via \\\\`tool_use_id\\\\`, but Claude Code'\"'\"'s real \\\\`SubagentStop\\\\` payload never carries that field (it'\"'\"'s documented only on tool events, not subagent lifecycle events). The lookup always missed and the handler returned early.\\n- Fix falls back to \\\\`agent_id\\\\` — the field genuinely shared between a subagent'\"'\"'s \\\\`SubagentStart\\\\` (via \\\\`PostToolUse[Agent]\\\\`'\"'\"'s \\\\`tool_response.agentId\\\\`) and its \\\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2296,\n      \"title\": \"fix: fall back to transformedContent/reasoningText when Copilot CLI content is empty\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2296\",\n      \"head\": \"0bb470e12245ee0ead70075f3a355260a6383a87\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/1070-copilot-empty-transcript-fallback\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1246\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- Copilot CLI sessions captured checkpoints fine, but the transcript detail view was empty/incomplete: Entire'\"'\"'s extraction only read the primary \\\\`content\\\\` field of user/assistant message events, with no fallback for when Copilot CLI populates \\\\`transformedContent\\\\`/\\\\`reasoningText\\\\` instead.\\n- Prompts now fall back to \\\\`transformedContent\\\\` (stripped of Copilot'\"'\"'s injected wrapper blocks); summaries fall back to \\\\`reasoningText\\\\`. Populated \\\\`content\\\\` still always wins.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n- Real fixture lifted from an actual captured Copilot CLI transcript.\\n- Before: \\\\`extrac\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2295,\n      \"title\": \"fix: give each Pi subagent run a unique session identifier\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2295\",\n      \"head\": \"2f9a64cb8702f68951b3d197d22d71589b3a33f5\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/1870-pi-subagent-session-collision\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1245\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- Every Pi subagent transcript file is named \\\\`session.jsonl\\\\` regardless of which subagent/run produced it, so the session-ID resolver collapsed every subagent invocation to the literal ID \\\\`\\\"session\\\"\\\\`. Concurrent or sequential subagent runs overwrote each other'\"'\"'s staged/archived transcript copy, and a checkpoint could end up storing a different subagent'\"'\"'s content than the one it was supposedly capturing.\\n- Fix derives a unique ID per invocation (\\\\`<parentUUID>_<subagentID>_run-<n>\\\\`) by walking up the real nested directory structure Pi already writes, instead of using \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2294,\n      \"title\": \"fix: warn visibly when an agent commits with no active session recorded\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2294\",\n      \"head\": \"2f07df61fe7a555771f93f06660fa86e05bdb911\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/1965-warn-commit-no-session\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1244\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- When a commit landed in an Entire-enabled repo with no active/recent session found (e.g. agent launched from a parent or bare-clone directory with no hook config), Entire only logged a debug-level line — invisible to a normal user. Now prints a visible stderr warning, rate-limited to once per 24h.\\n- Only fires when a coding-agent environment marker is actually present (\\\\`CLAUDECODE\\\\`/\\\\`GEMINI_CLI\\\\`/\\\\`COPILOT_CLI\\\\`/\\\\`PI_CODING_AGENT\\\\`) — a human'\"'\"'s own commit with no marker never warns, even with zero sessions ever recorded. This mirrors the existing agent-detection prece\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2293,\n      \"title\": \"fix: qualify \\\"no checkpoints found\\\" when the scan limit truncated\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2293\",\n      \"head\": \"864d979249302c4705d24383d89bb135ab7af902\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/2089-explain-session-truncation-message\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1243\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- \\\\`entire checkpoint explain --session <id>\\\\` (default scan limit) printed an unqualified \\\"No checkpoints found on this branch\\\" even when the scan hit its budget before reaching a real match — an explicit \\\\`--limit\\\\` returned results fine. The truncation signal already existed internally but never reached the zero-results message.\\n- Now: when the scan was truncated before finding anything, the message says so and points at \\\\`--limit\\\\`. A genuinely empty branch still gets the plain message, unchanged.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n- Real repro: 5 committed checkpoints via \\\\`checkpoint.New\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2292,\n      \"title\": \"fix: point investigate/review error hints at entire agent add\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2292\",\n      \"head\": \"f1e2c6cad72c72fa2fc995ae2062f79664f42343\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/2249-stale-configure-agent-hints\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":12292}},"started_at_ms":1794842128968,"completed_at_ms":1794842128970}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:29.104Z","ordinal":3020,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f529f547-d0c1-40a2-a87c-617498dd9f5c","process_id":"74549","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' ' -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1242\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- \\\\`entire investigate\\\\`/\\\\`entire review\\\\` error messages told users to run a nonexistent \\\\`entire configure --agent <name>\\\\` flag. Replaced all 11 instances across 5 files with the correct \\\\`entire agent add <name>\\\\`.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n- Repo-wide grep before/after: 11 lines / 17 substring occurrences of \\\\`configure --agent\\\\` in production code → 0.\\n- 8 tests added/extended, each calling the real error-producing function (not a hardcoded string comparison) and asserting the message names \\\\`entire agent add\\\\` and never the stale flag.\\n- Proved the tests have teeth: reverted on\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2285,\n      \"title\": \"refactor(session): use canonical Git metadata resolution (split part 3)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2285\",\n      \"head\": \"8dd1d6c61c4f274d4ee02b3843ecd30866d745c4\",\n      \"branch\": \"refactor-session-metadata-resolution\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Part 3 of #2190'\"'\"'s [agreed split](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2190#issuecomment-5499945525), following the merged canonical resolver in #2241 and checkpoint migration in #2254.\\n\\nSession construction and adoption still use separate paths to resolve Git metadata. This PR moves the explicit-root consumers to `gitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata`, so the canonical resolver supplies the common directory and worktree ID while each caller keeps its own storage and failure policy.\\n\\n## Session-store construction\\n\\nPreviously, constructing a session store for a known worktree root ran `git rev-parse --git-common-dir`, even though the root was already known.\\n\\n`NewStateStoreForWorktree` now resolves \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2277,\n      \"title\": \"fix(clean): reap accumulated ref/shadow lock files\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2277\",\n      \"head\": \"bca1b2f42d92927b75e3cd1ceb1e0a31c042afb9\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/2197-reap-ref-lock-dirs\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Closes #2197.\\n\\nTwo design questions from my [claim comment](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2197#issuecomment-5553909120) are still open — flagged at the bottom rather than blocking on them. Happy to adjust the diff either way.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n`persistentRefLock` creates one flock file per checkpoint ref under `<git-common-dir>/entire-persistent-ref-locks/` and nothing ever removes them, so the directory grows monotonically with checkpoint count. `entire-shadow-locks/` has the same shape (bounded by branch activity, but equally unreaped). `strategy/cleanup.go` had no reference to either, so `entire clean` never reclaimed them.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\nWired both into `entire clean --all`, mirroring t\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2275,\n      \"title\": \"fix: apply personal entire disable across all worktrees of a clone\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2275\",\n      \"head\": \"39b8b930e013c5a5755d13a0ebebeaec0aa75938\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/disable-spans-worktrees\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"fixes  #2274\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## Problem\\r\\n\\r\\nWe roll Entire out per repository with a committed `.entire/settings.json` (`\\\"enabled\\\": true`) and let individual developers opt out with `entire disable`. That writes `\\\"enabled\\\": false` to `.entire/settings.local.json`, which is gitignored — so it exists only in the worktree it was written in.\\r\\n\\r\\nAnyone who works with linked worktrees (`git worktree add`, or agents such as Claude Code that create worktrees on their own) gets re-enabled every time a worktree is created: the new checkout carries only the committed `settings.json`, `settings.Load` finds no local override, and every agent hook and git hook starts recording again.\\r\\n\\r\\nReproduced on current `main`:\\r\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2269,\n      \"title\": \"feat(tokens): billing-class breakdown for a live session\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2269\",\n      \"head\": \"995a4b5e182add3bde332532021b568c901ef9c2\",\n      \"branch\": \"pr2-session-tokens-block\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1237\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n> **Opens against `pr1-token-class-breakdown` (#2210), not `main`.** It needs that PR'\"'\"'s shared\\n> renderer, price-ratio rows and withheld-cost reasons. Retarget once #2210 merges.\\n\\n## What this does\\n\\n`entire session tokens` now shows the \\\"How it was billed\\\" block that #2210 gave\\n`entire checkpoint tokens` — volume and, where a verified per-model ratio row applies, cost share\\nper billing class. On a real live session:\\n\\n```\\nHow it was billed\\n                                     tokens   volume    cost\\n  Fresh input                           42k      10%     15%\\n  Cache write           \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2243,\n      \"title\": \"fix(test-repo skill): verify git-refs checkpoint storage, drop removed --strategy flag\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2243\",\n      \"head\": \"d8a5f5bc7cf205dea25a0d3f0034d6261e2a743f\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/test-repo-skill-refs\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1222\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThe test-repo skill harness was stale on two era assumptions, found while validating the user-settings work on #2166:\\n\\n- `configure-strategy` passed `enable --strategy`, a flag that no longer exists (manual-commit is the only strategy) — the harness failed at setup.\\n- `verify-metadata-branch` asserted the `entire/checkpoints/v1` **branch**, but `enable` defaults to the **git-refs** backend, where a condensed checkpoint lives at `refs/entire/checkpoints/<shard>/<ULID>` — so it failed a perfectly healthy run.\\n\\nChanges:\\n- `verify-metadata-branch` checks `refs/entire/checkpoints/*` firs\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2234,\n      \"title\": \"fix: don'\"'\"'t let a tool call'\"'\"'s own payload spoof the image-object redaction skip\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2234\",\n      \"head\": \"a71196b98cd405480e3742db20545836d2e3dc03\",\n      \"branch\": \"security/redaction-skiplist-scoping\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1216\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- `collectJSONLReplacements`'\"'\"'s `shouldSkipJSONLObject` check (skip an entire subtree when an object'\"'\"'s `\\\"type\\\"` field starts with `\\\"image\\\"` or equals `\\\"base64\\\"`) applied unconditionally anywhere in a transcript line'\"'\"'s JSON tree — including inside a `tool_use` block'\"'\"'s own `\\\"input\\\"` or a `tool_result`'\"'\"'s `\\\"content\\\"`/`\\\"output\\\"`, fields whose shape is controlled by whatever tool declared them. For an MCP tool, that'\"'\"'s a third party, not Entire'\"'\"'s transcript writer.\\n- A tool call argument or response deliberately shaped as `{\\\"type\\\":\\\"base64\\\", ...}` hid an arbitrarily large sibling \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2229,\n      \"title\": \"fix: cap local git-blob reads on checkpoint trees\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2229\",\n      \"head\": \"13bea3e33a3404e4ad61935b39f895b9a88b125e\",\n      \"branch\": \"security/unbounded-blob-read-dos\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1211\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- `readSummaryFromCheckpointTree` and sibling readers pulled checkpoint metadata/prompt/transcript content via go-git'\"'\"'s `file.Contents()` with no size cap. Checkpoint trees are not always locally authored — they can be fetched from a shared/pushed remote (`entire/checkpoints/v1`, or a per-checkpoint ref), which any collaborator with checkpoint-push access, or a compromised/malicious remote, controls the bytes of. An oversized blob was read into memory in full — a memory-exhaustion DoS reachable via routine commands (`entire checkpoint explain`, `checkpoint list`, `entire \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2226,\n      \"title\": \"fix: serialize shadow-branch migration against concurrent checkpoint writes\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2226\",\n      \"head\": \"fb68988646778e922cf07e69f703a25aa61c7395\",\n      \"branch\": \"security/shadow-branch-migration-race\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1208\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- `migrateShadowBranchToBaseCommit` moved a session'\"'\"'s shadow branch to a new base-commit-derived name via an unlocked go-git `Reference` read, a non-CAS `SetReference`, and an unconditional `git branch -D` — entirely outside the flock+CAS discipline `writeCheckpoint`/`writeTask` use for the exact same refs (`withShadowBranchFlock` + `casUpdateShadowBranchRef`, `checkpoint/ephemeral.go`).\\n- Two sessions sharing a worktree'\"'\"'s shadow branch is a documented, supported configuration (main agent + Task-tool subagent). A checkpoint write racing this migration could have its work \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2210,\n      \"title\": \"feat(tokens): billing-class breakdown for every agent\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2210\",\n      \"head\": \"e09a82674f0cf36e3b198318fcbc54fba3e94538\",\n      \"branch\": \"pr1-token-class-breakdown\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1198\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n> **Opens against `tokens` (#2155), not `main`.** It needs the `thinking_tokens` /\\n> `cache_creation_1h_tokens` subset fields and the corrected per-checkpoint scoping from that PR.\\n> Retarget to `main` once #2155 merges.\\n\\n## What this does\\n\\n`entire checkpoint tokens` now says where a checkpoint'\"'\"'s tokens went, by billing class, with each\\nclass'\"'\"'s share of **volume** and — where a verified per-model price ratio applies — share of **cost**.\\n\\n```\\nHow it was billed\\n                     tokens   volume    cost\\n  Fresh input         42.1k      10%     15%\\n  Cache write        118.4k      29\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2199,\n      \"title\": \"Fix stale lock cleanup\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2199\",\n      \"head\": \"b3445a6416712a1063fbac551aa40970c5e231a2\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/reap-entire-lock-files\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Closes #2197.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAdds cleanup support for stale lock files created under the git common dir:\\n\\n- `entire-shadow-locks`\\n- `entire-persistent-ref-locks`\\n\\n`entire clean --all` now discovers those lock files, reports them in dry-run output, and includes them in deletion summaries.\\n\\n## Review follow-up\\n\\nThis update addresses the lock-safety review feedback:\\n\\n- Revalidates Unix flock acquisitions against the current lock-file inode before returning from both blocking `Acquire` and bounded `AcquireContext` paths.\\n- Moves stale lock cleanup to run after shadow branch, session state, and checkpoint cleanup so normal cleanup operations use their locks first.\\n- Treats actively held lock files \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2190,\n      \"title\": \"refactor(gitrepo): consolidate worktree metadata traversal\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2190\",\n      \"head\": \"522959a8a121082e08b3a8772097f13a26254039\",\n      \"branch\": \"refactor-git-metadata-traversal\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Refs #2052, particularly [the duplicate-traversal finding](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2052#issuecomment-5400538888) and [the follow-up commitment](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2052#issuecomment-5429341093).\\n\\nPR #2052 exposed that several packages independently interpreted `.git`, `gitdir:`, `commondir`, and linked-worktree identity. Those implementations had already diverged on layouts such as bare containers, linked worktrees, and submodules, while session and checkpoint maintained separate caches for answers derived from the same filesystem metadata.\\n\\nThis consolidates those physical Git facts under the existing `gitrepo` ownership boundary and removes the duplicate trave\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2168,\n      \"title\": \"fix(trailers): stop untrusted commit subjects from forging Entire trailers\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2168\",\n      \"head\": \"52503e37486def0a79333f24a3cec7e5a7d3f947\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/shadow-commit-trailer-forgery\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1176\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nA shadow checkpoint'\"'\"'s commit subject is built from text Entire does not author:\\n\\n- `strategy.FormatIncrementalMessage(step.TodoContent, ...)` — the `content` of a TodoWrite item the model wrote, verbatim apart from a 60-rune truncation.\\n- `generateCommitMessage` → `cleanPromptForCommit` — the session'\"'\"'s first prompt, verbatim apart from prefix trimming and a 72-rune truncation.\\n\\nNeither strips newlines. That text is steerable by anything the agent read into its context, including a file in the repository it is working on.\\n\\n`FormatShadowCommit` / `FormatShadowTaskCommit` w\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2167,\n      \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): never store a shadow checkpoint with a transcript chunk hole\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2167\",\n      \"head\": \"b4d36e5a68829d29f0b53ca73f69a573943b934e\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/ephemeral-transcript-chunk-hole\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1175\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nA transcript larger than `agent.MaxChunkSize` (50 MB) is stored as `full.jsonl`, `full.jsonl.001`, `full.jsonl.002` … and every consumer reassembles it from whatever chunk files are present, in index order, with **no gap marker** (`agent.SortChunkFiles` + `agent.ReassembleTranscript`, and the same `base + \\\".%03d\\\"` convention elsewhere).\\n\\n`addTaskMetadataToTree` logged a warning and `continue`d when a chunk'\"'\"'s blob write failed:\\n\\n```go\\nblobHash, blobErr := CreateBlobFromContent(s.repo, chunk)\\nif blobErr != nil {\\n    logging.Warn(ctx, \\\"failed to create blob for transcript c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2161,\n      \"title\": \"feat: add OrcaRouter as a named summary-generation provider\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2161\",\n      \"head\": \"26d5007ace66d60243d6bfb85f1d29024ff2ae71\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/orcarouter-summary-provider\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\n[Entire](https://github.com/entireio/cli) hooks into your Git workflow to capture AI agent sessions as you work — but capturing the *why* is only half the value. When you run `entire explain --generate` or turn on checkpoint auto-summarize, Entire asks a locally-installed agent CLI to turn a session transcript into a structured summary.\\n\\nThat provider is always a coding-agent CLI today (`claude`, `codex`, `gemini`, `pi`, …) — it has to be a binary on `$PATH`, and it has to be a CLI that happens to expose a `--print` text mode. This PR makes [OrcaRouter](https://www.orcarouter.ai) available as a first-class, named summary provider through the exact same machinery, so Entire users \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2155,\n      \"title\": \"Fix token counting and persist what agents record (thinking, cache TTL, subagent model, token_usage_version)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2155\",\n      \"head\": \"6be00eb664fe27de50c699c7f70882c415087a0c\",\n      \"branch\": \"tokens\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1167\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nWrite-side fixes for the token data behind `session tokens`, `checkpoint tokens`, and `tokens profile`. This PR makes the numbers written into checkpoints correct and complete; the report redesign follows in a separate PR off main. **One visible change:** `entire status`'\"'\"' per-session token total is now the session total again (see review fix 2 below) — everything else is metadata only.\\n\\nFive commits, each independently reviewable:\\n\\n### 1. `fix(tokens)`: Gemini and OpenCode parsers\\n- **Gemini** counted `cached` twice (it is a subset of `input`) and dropped `thoughts` (rep\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2150,\n      \"title\": \"fix(agent): bound the Claude text-generation paths too\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2150\",\n      \"head\": \"00b25f79e823b184123a7d1cc8d4b13e26d86e3d\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/terminate-on-cancel-followup\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1162\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nFollow-up to #2140, from findings left on [trail #1153](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1153) that weren'\"'\"'t picked up before it merged.\\n\\n## The judge still hung\\n\\n#2140 applied `execx.TerminateOnCancel` to `RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI`, covering codex, cursor, gemini, copilot and pi. Claude Code deliberately runs the CLI itself on both its text-generation paths (`generate.go`, `generate_streaming.go`), so neither was bounded — and `defaultJudge` prefers claude-code, so `entire review`'\"'\"'s judge still hung in the default configuration.\\n\\n- **`generate.go`** is the judge'\"'\"'s path: `\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2144,\n      \"title\": \"Derive AreHooksInstalled from removal so it can be trusted as a gate\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2144\",\n      \"head\": \"f5110d5adf4b98ac93f7c463e9f25ec46442268d\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-asymmetry-uninstallhooks-vs-arehooksinstalled\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1157\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\n`AreHooksInstalled` is not just a display signal — `entire agent remove` and the\\n`entire enable` deselect path skip an agent that answers false. But for most built-in\\nagents it was written independently of `UninstallHooks`, and had drifted narrower:\\n\\n| agent | detection inspected | removal touched |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| claudecode | `Stop` only | 6 hook types + `permissions.deny` metadata rule |\\n| factoryaidroid | `Stop` only | 7 hook types + deny rule |\\n| codex | **all 4** core events, AND-wise | '"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' ' -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1242\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- \\\\`entire investigate\\\\`/\\\\`entire review\\\\` error messages told users to run a nonexistent \\\\`entire configure --agent <name>\\\\` flag. Replaced all 11 instances across 5 files with the correct \\\\`entire agent add <name>\\\\`.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n- Repo-wide grep before/after: 11 lines / 17 substring occurrences of \\\\`configure --agent\\\\` in production code → 0.\\n- 8 tests added/extended, each calling the real error-producing function (not a hardcoded string comparison) and asserting the message names \\\\`entire agent add\\\\` and never the stale flag.\\n- Proved the tests have teeth: reverted on\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2285,\n      \"title\": \"refactor(session): use canonical Git metadata resolution (split part 3)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2285\",\n      \"head\": \"8dd1d6c61c4f274d4ee02b3843ecd30866d745c4\",\n      \"branch\": \"refactor-session-metadata-resolution\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Part 3 of #2190'\"'\"'s [agreed split](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2190#issuecomment-5499945525), following the merged canonical resolver in #2241 and checkpoint migration in #2254.\\n\\nSession construction and adoption still use separate paths to resolve Git metadata. This PR moves the explicit-root consumers to `gitrepo.ResolveWorktreeMetadata`, so the canonical resolver supplies the common directory and worktree ID while each caller keeps its own storage and failure policy.\\n\\n## Session-store construction\\n\\nPreviously, constructing a session store for a known worktree root ran `git rev-parse --git-common-dir`, even though the root was already known.\\n\\n`NewStateStoreForWorktree` now resolves \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2277,\n      \"title\": \"fix(clean): reap accumulated ref/shadow lock files\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2277\",\n      \"head\": \"bca1b2f42d92927b75e3cd1ceb1e0a31c042afb9\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/2197-reap-ref-lock-dirs\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Closes #2197.\\n\\nTwo design questions from my [claim comment](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2197#issuecomment-5553909120) are still open — flagged at the bottom rather than blocking on them. Happy to adjust the diff either way.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n`persistentRefLock` creates one flock file per checkpoint ref under `<git-common-dir>/entire-persistent-ref-locks/` and nothing ever removes them, so the directory grows monotonically with checkpoint count. `entire-shadow-locks/` has the same shape (bounded by branch activity, but equally unreaped). `strategy/cleanup.go` had no reference to either, so `entire clean` never reclaimed them.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\nWired both into `entire clean --all`, mirroring t\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2275,\n      \"title\": \"fix: apply personal entire disable across all worktrees of a clone\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2275\",\n      \"head\": \"39b8b930e013c5a5755d13a0ebebeaec0aa75938\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/disable-spans-worktrees\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"fixes  #2274\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## Problem\\r\\n\\r\\nWe roll Entire out per repository with a committed `.entire/settings.json` (`\\\"enabled\\\": true`) and let individual developers opt out with `entire disable`. That writes `\\\"enabled\\\": false` to `.entire/settings.local.json`, which is gitignored — so it exists only in the worktree it was written in.\\r\\n\\r\\nAnyone who works with linked worktrees (`git worktree add`, or agents such as Claude Code that create worktrees on their own) gets re-enabled every time a worktree is created: the new checkout carries only the committed `settings.json`, `settings.Load` finds no local override, and every agent hook and git hook starts recording again.\\r\\n\\r\\nReproduced on current `main`:\\r\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2269,\n      \"title\": \"feat(tokens): billing-class breakdown for a live session\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2269\",\n      \"head\": \"995a4b5e182add3bde332532021b568c901ef9c2\",\n      \"branch\": \"pr2-session-tokens-block\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1237\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n> **Opens against `pr1-token-class-breakdown` (#2210), not `main`.** It needs that PR'\"'\"'s shared\\n> renderer, price-ratio rows and withheld-cost reasons. Retarget once #2210 merges.\\n\\n## What this does\\n\\n`entire session tokens` now shows the \\\"How it was billed\\\" block that #2210 gave\\n`entire checkpoint tokens` — volume and, where a verified per-model ratio row applies, cost share\\nper billing class. On a real live session:\\n\\n```\\nHow it was billed\\n                                     tokens   volume    cost\\n  Fresh input                           42k      10%     15%\\n  Cache write           \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2243,\n      \"title\": \"fix(test-repo skill): verify git-refs checkpoint storage, drop removed --strategy flag\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2243\",\n      \"head\": \"d8a5f5bc7cf205dea25a0d3f0034d6261e2a743f\",\n      \"branch\": \"peyton/test-repo-skill-refs\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1222\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThe test-repo skill harness was stale on two era assumptions, found while validating the user-settings work on #2166:\\n\\n- `configure-strategy` passed `enable --strategy`, a flag that no longer exists (manual-commit is the only strategy) — the harness failed at setup.\\n- `verify-metadata-branch` asserted the `entire/checkpoints/v1` **branch**, but `enable` defaults to the **git-refs** backend, where a condensed checkpoint lives at `refs/entire/checkpoints/<shard>/<ULID>` — so it failed a perfectly healthy run.\\n\\nChanges:\\n- `verify-metadata-branch` checks `refs/entire/checkpoints/*` firs\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2234,\n      \"title\": \"fix: don'\"'\"'t let a tool call'\"'\"'s own payload spoof the image-object redaction skip\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2234\",\n      \"head\": \"a71196b98cd405480e3742db20545836d2e3dc03\",\n      \"branch\": \"security/redaction-skiplist-scoping\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1216\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- `collectJSONLReplacements`'\"'\"'s `shouldSkipJSONLObject` check (skip an entire subtree when an object'\"'\"'s `\\\"type\\\"` field starts with `\\\"image\\\"` or equals `\\\"base64\\\"`) applied unconditionally anywhere in a transcript line'\"'\"'s JSON tree — including inside a `tool_use` block'\"'\"'s own `\\\"input\\\"` or a `tool_result`'\"'\"'s `\\\"content\\\"`/`\\\"output\\\"`, fields whose shape is controlled by whatever tool declared them. For an MCP tool, that'\"'\"'s a third party, not Entire'\"'\"'s transcript writer.\\n- A tool call argument or response deliberately shaped as `{\\\"type\\\":\\\"base64\\\", ...}` hid an arbitrarily large sibling \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2229,\n      \"title\": \"fix: cap local git-blob reads on checkpoint trees\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2229\",\n      \"head\": \"13bea3e33a3404e4ad61935b39f895b9a88b125e\",\n      \"branch\": \"security/unbounded-blob-read-dos\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1211\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- `readSummaryFromCheckpointTree` and sibling readers pulled checkpoint metadata/prompt/transcript content via go-git'\"'\"'s `file.Contents()` with no size cap. Checkpoint trees are not always locally authored — they can be fetched from a shared/pushed remote (`entire/checkpoints/v1`, or a per-checkpoint ref), which any collaborator with checkpoint-push access, or a compromised/malicious remote, controls the bytes of. An oversized blob was read into memory in full — a memory-exhaustion DoS reachable via routine commands (`entire checkpoint explain`, `checkpoint list`, `entire \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2226,\n      \"title\": \"fix: serialize shadow-branch migration against concurrent checkpoint writes\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2226\",\n      \"head\": \"fb68988646778e922cf07e69f703a25aa61c7395\",\n      \"branch\": \"security/shadow-branch-migration-race\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1208\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- `migrateShadowBranchToBaseCommit` moved a session'\"'\"'s shadow branch to a new base-commit-derived name via an unlocked go-git `Reference` read, a non-CAS `SetReference`, and an unconditional `git branch -D` — entirely outside the flock+CAS discipline `writeCheckpoint`/`writeTask` use for the exact same refs (`withShadowBranchFlock` + `casUpdateShadowBranchRef`, `checkpoint/ephemeral.go`).\\n- Two sessions sharing a worktree'\"'\"'s shadow branch is a documented, supported configuration (main agent + Task-tool subagent). A checkpoint write racing this migration could have its work \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2210,\n      \"title\": \"feat(tokens): billing-class breakdown for every agent\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2210\",\n      \"head\": \"e09a82674f0cf36e3b198318fcbc54fba3e94538\",\n      \"branch\": \"pr1-token-class-breakdown\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1198\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n> **Opens against `tokens` (#2155), not `main`.** It needs the `thinking_tokens` /\\n> `cache_creation_1h_tokens` subset fields and the corrected per-checkpoint scoping from that PR.\\n> Retarget to `main` once #2155 merges.\\n\\n## What this does\\n\\n`entire checkpoint tokens` now says where a checkpoint'\"'\"'s tokens went, by billing class, with each\\nclass'\"'\"'s share of **volume** and — where a verified per-model price ratio applies — share of **cost**.\\n\\n```\\nHow it was billed\\n                     tokens   volume    cost\\n  Fresh input         42.1k      10%     15%\\n  Cache write        118.4k      29\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2199,\n      \"title\": \"Fix stale lock cleanup\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2199\",\n      \"head\": \"b3445a6416712a1063fbac551aa40970c5e231a2\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/reap-entire-lock-files\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Closes #2197.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAdds cleanup support for stale lock files created under the git common dir:\\n\\n- `entire-shadow-locks`\\n- `entire-persistent-ref-locks`\\n\\n`entire clean --all` now discovers those lock files, reports them in dry-run output, and includes them in deletion summaries.\\n\\n## Review follow-up\\n\\nThis update addresses the lock-safety review feedback:\\n\\n- Revalidates Unix flock acquisitions against the current lock-file inode before returning from both blocking `Acquire` and bounded `AcquireContext` paths.\\n- Moves stale lock cleanup to run after shadow branch, session state, and checkpoint cleanup so normal cleanup operations use their locks first.\\n- Treats actively held lock files \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2190,\n      \"title\": \"refactor(gitrepo): consolidate worktree metadata traversal\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2190\",\n      \"head\": \"522959a8a121082e08b3a8772097f13a26254039\",\n      \"branch\": \"refactor-git-metadata-traversal\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Refs #2052, particularly [the duplicate-traversal finding](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2052#issuecomment-5400538888) and [the follow-up commitment](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2052#issuecomment-5429341093).\\n\\nPR #2052 exposed that several packages independently interpreted `.git`, `gitdir:`, `commondir`, and linked-worktree identity. Those implementations had already diverged on layouts such as bare containers, linked worktrees, and submodules, while session and checkpoint maintained separate caches for answers derived from the same filesystem metadata.\\n\\nThis consolidates those physical Git facts under the existing `gitrepo` ownership boundary and removes the duplicate trave\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2168,\n      \"title\": \"fix(trailers): stop untrusted commit subjects from forging Entire trailers\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2168\",\n      \"head\": \"52503e37486def0a79333f24a3cec7e5a7d3f947\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/shadow-commit-trailer-forgery\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1176\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nA shadow checkpoint'\"'\"'s commit subject is built from text Entire does not author:\\n\\n- `strategy.FormatIncrementalMessage(step.TodoContent, ...)` — the `content` of a TodoWrite item the model wrote, verbatim apart from a 60-rune truncation.\\n- `generateCommitMessage` → `cleanPromptForCommit` — the session'\"'\"'s first prompt, verbatim apart from prefix trimming and a 72-rune truncation.\\n\\nNeither strips newlines. That text is steerable by anything the agent read into its context, including a file in the repository it is working on.\\n\\n`FormatShadowCommit` / `FormatShadowTaskCommit` w\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2167,\n      \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): never store a shadow checkpoint with a transcript chunk hole\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2167\",\n      \"head\": \"b4d36e5a68829d29f0b53ca73f69a573943b934e\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/ephemeral-transcript-chunk-hole\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1175\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nA transcript larger than `agent.MaxChunkSize` (50 MB) is stored as `full.jsonl`, `full.jsonl.001`, `full.jsonl.002` … and every consumer reassembles it from whatever chunk files are present, in index order, with **no gap marker** (`agent.SortChunkFiles` + `agent.ReassembleTranscript`, and the same `base + \\\".%03d\\\"` convention elsewhere).\\n\\n`addTaskMetadataToTree` logged a warning and `continue`d when a chunk'\"'\"'s blob write failed:\\n\\n```go\\nblobHash, blobErr := CreateBlobFromContent(s.repo, chunk)\\nif blobErr != nil {\\n    logging.Warn(ctx, \\\"failed to create blob for transcript c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2161,\n      \"title\": \"feat: add OrcaRouter as a named summary-generation provider\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2161\",\n      \"head\": \"26d5007ace66d60243d6bfb85f1d29024ff2ae71\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/orcarouter-summary-provider\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\n[Entire](https://github.com/entireio/cli) hooks into your Git workflow to capture AI agent sessions as you work — but capturing the *why* is only half the value. When you run `entire explain --generate` or turn on checkpoint auto-summarize, Entire asks a locally-installed agent CLI to turn a session transcript into a structured summary.\\n\\nThat provider is always a coding-agent CLI today (`claude`, `codex`, `gemini`, `pi`, …) — it has to be a binary on `$PATH`, and it has to be a CLI that happens to expose a `--print` text mode. This PR makes [OrcaRouter](https://www.orcarouter.ai) available as a first-class, named summary provider through the exact same machinery, so Entire users \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2155,\n      \"title\": \"Fix token counting and persist what agents record (thinking, cache TTL, subagent model, token_usage_version)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2155\",\n      \"head\": \"6be00eb664fe27de50c699c7f70882c415087a0c\",\n      \"branch\": \"tokens\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1167\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nWrite-side fixes for the token data behind `session tokens`, `checkpoint tokens`, and `tokens profile`. This PR makes the numbers written into checkpoints correct and complete; the report redesign follows in a separate PR off main. **One visible change:** `entire status`'\"'\"' per-session token total is now the session total again (see review fix 2 below) — everything else is metadata only.\\n\\nFive commits, each independently reviewable:\\n\\n### 1. `fix(tokens)`: Gemini and OpenCode parsers\\n- **Gemini** counted `cached` twice (it is a subset of `input`) and dropped `thoughts` (rep\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2150,\n      \"title\": \"fix(agent): bound the Claude text-generation paths too\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2150\",\n      \"head\": \"00b25f79e823b184123a7d1cc8d4b13e26d86e3d\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/terminate-on-cancel-followup\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1162\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nFollow-up to #2140, from findings left on [trail #1153](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1153) that weren'\"'\"'t picked up before it merged.\\n\\n## The judge still hung\\n\\n#2140 applied `execx.TerminateOnCancel` to `RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI`, covering codex, cursor, gemini, copilot and pi. Claude Code deliberately runs the CLI itself on both its text-generation paths (`generate.go`, `generate_streaming.go`), so neither was bounded — and `defaultJudge` prefers claude-code, so `entire review`'\"'\"'s judge still hung in the default configuration.\\n\\n- **`generate.go`** is the judge'\"'\"'s path: `\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2144,\n      \"title\": \"Derive AreHooksInstalled from removal so it can be trusted as a gate\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2144\",\n      \"head\": \"f5110d5adf4b98ac93f7c463e9f25ec46442268d\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-asymmetry-uninstallhooks-vs-arehooksinstalled\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1157\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\n`AreHooksInstalled` is not just a display signal — `entire agent remove` and the\\n`entire enable` deselect path skip an agent that answers false. But for most built-in\\nagents it was written independently of `UninstallHooks`, and had drifted narrower:\\n\\n| agent | detection inspected | removal touched |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| claudecode | `Stop` only | 6 hook types + `permissions.deny` metadata rule |\\n| factoryaidroid | `Stop` only | 7 hook types + deny rule |\\n| codex | **all 4** core events, AND-wise | '"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":12417}},"started_at_ms":1794842129104,"completed_at_ms":1794842129104}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:29.246Z","ordinal":3021,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-dcc8ac76-009f-4edb-a8b7-8378a3400498","process_id":"32015","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' '7 events |\\n| copilotcli | 8 struct fields, hand-copied | the same 8, from a t\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2136,\n      \"title\": \"refactor(external): probe agent binaries in parallel and record failures\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2136\",\n      \"head\": \"00e9813c7b3bc7037162f414d1cc35c281ca5a23\",\n      \"branch\": \"refactor-discover-external-agents-claude-version\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1150\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nStacked on #2134, which contains the two implementation plans. This PR implements the `claude-version.md` design and incorporates the follow-up review fixes.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nExternal agent discovery now collects candidates without executing them, probes each binary concurrently under its own budget, and applies results in stable PATH order. A slow or broken plugin no longer blocks later plugins, and load failures remain visible instead of disappearing into debug logs.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n- Store usable and broken external agents in the central agent registry. Registry walks still expose \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2134,\n      \"title\": \"docs(external-agents): add claude-version discovery refactor plan\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2134\",\n      \"head\": \"1c5bda9bb267d33c51f4116cbc4bfb33792a7fc2\",\n      \"branch\": \"refactor-discover-and-register-external-agents\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1148\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What\\n\\nAdds `docs/external-agents/claude-version.md` — a plan for reworking external agent discovery, sitting alongside the existing `pi-version.md` so the two can be compared section for section.\\n\\nDocs only. No code, no behaviour change.\\n\\n## The plan in one line\\n\\nCollect candidate `entire-agent-*` binaries from `$PATH` (filesystem only), probe each one'\"'\"'s `info` in parallel under a per-binary budget, then record both ready and unloadable agents so `entire agent list` can explain why a plugin is missing.\\n\\n## Where it differs from pi-version\\n\\n| | pi-version | claude-version |\\n|---|-\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2131,\n      \"title\": \"perf(checkpoint): batch persistent session writes with CAS\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2131\",\n      \"head\": \"56e583e0e2f34abd5ee17319e745d509a1245bc3\",\n      \"branch\": \"improve-process-sessions-condensation\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\n`process_sessions` still persists each session separately. For every session, it reloads the checkpoint, rebuilds the session index and summary, creates a commit, and advances the checkpoint ref.\\n\\nIssue #2091 measures that work at roughly 73–103 ms per session. The repeated checkpoint load and rebuild make condensation slower as more sessions share a checkpoint.\\n\\nCheckpoint-level batching needs two things first:\\n\\n- Ref updates must detect concurrent writes from hooks, worktrees, CLI processes, and other Git clients.\\n- Both persistent Git layouts must use the same batch algorithm.\\n\\n## Solution\\n\\nThis PR adds native compare-and-swap publication and a shared `BatchSessions` write req\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2127,\n      \"title\": \"feat(grok): add Grok Build (xAI) agent integration\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2127\",\n      \"head\": \"f9001c7a9f108364e95b8695930ee550b0ca6447\",\n      \"branch\": \"add_grok_agent\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1143\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nAdds Grok Build (xAI) as an Entire agent, registered as `grok`.\\n\\nBuilt through the research → write-tests → implement pipeline. Everything\\nbelow was verified against a real Grok 1.0.5 install, with captured payloads\\nand a real session transcript checked in as test fixtures.\\n\\n## What'\"'\"'s here\\n\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/grok/` — the agent. Core `Agent` plus `HookSupport`,\\n  `HookFreshness`, `TranscriptAnalyzer`, `TokenCalculator`, `ModelExtractor`,\\n  and `SubagentSessionResolver`. Marked `IsPreview()`.\\n- `e2e/agents/grok.go` — E2E runner, so the existing `ForEachAgent` suite\\n  covers Grok\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2124,\n      \"title\": \"Classify a cell'\"'\"'s 401 as a credential rejection, not a raw error\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2124\",\n      \"head\": \"f5df2877a58cc7c9469eacb274c0b04c181c375d\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/search-401-classification\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\nAn account whose `home_jurisdiction` is `eu` gets a 401 from every cell'\"'\"'s semantic-search route, and we printed the service'\"'\"'s body verbatim ([#2121](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2121)):\\n\\n```\\nsearch failed: semantic search: search service error (401): Unauthorized\\n```\\n\\nThat names no region, offers no next step, and invites the one action that cannot possibly work — logging in again. The rejection is server-side and account-scoped ([entirehq/entire-search#196](https://github.com/entirehq/entire-search/issues/196)); the *same bearer* is accepted by code search at the same host.\\n\\nNow:\\n\\n```\\nsearch failed: semantic search: your credentials were rejected in aws-eu-central-1 — \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2122,\n      \"title\": \"Install Entire CLI in Cursor Cloud Agent environments on enable\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2122\",\n      \"head\": \"afbc67abcce876dd039ab7de3624dd43514ec802\",\n      \"branch\": \"cursor/cursor-cloud-env-entire-cli-2123\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1140\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_BEGIN -->\\n## Summary\\n\\nCursor Cloud Agents do not inherit a developer’s local `entire` install, so committed hooks that invoke `entire` silently no-op there.\\n\\n`entire enable` now writes a shared, idempotent helper (`.entire/install-cli.sh`) that any remote environment can run. When Cursor is selected **and** the repo already has `.cursor/environment.json`, enable appends `bash .entire/install-cli.sh` to that file’s `install` command.\\n\\nIt does **not** create `.cursor/environment.json`. A committed copy overrides dashboard-managed personal/team Cloud Agent env\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2112,\n      \"title\": \"fix(cursor): detect Cursor by its project state dir, not just .cursor/\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2112\",\n      \"head\": \"a5aa8656fc24c05deb500210cddaabedceb4a6ae\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/cursor-detect-project-state\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1132\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nEvery agent'\"'\"'s `DetectPresence` asks *\\\"does `<repo>/.<agent>/` exist\\\"*. That'\"'\"'s a fair test for Claude Code, Codex, and Gemini, which all create repo-local config as a matter of course. It'\"'\"'s structurally unfair to Cursor: project rules are optional, and Cursor'\"'\"'s real per-project state lives in `~/.cursor/projects/<sanitized-repo-path>`.\\n\\nSo a repo driven daily from Cursor reports \\\"not present\\\". `entire enable` enables only detected agents when non-interactive, and pre-selects only detected ones on first run (`selectAgents`, `setup.go:1771-1795`). The observed result is worse than Curs\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2109,\n      \"title\": \"feat(import): anchor Codex turns to recorded commits\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2109\",\n      \"head\": \"d3496bfbb66d1c41fe29a163f05f8bdc14858657\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/import-codex-commit-sha\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\n`entire import codex` already restores historical Codex turns, but the Codex importer never populated `Turn.CommitSHAs`. Every imported turn therefore used the default-branch fallback introduced in #1825, even when the rollout recorded the exact `git commit` invocation and its resulting SHA.\\n\\nThis PR extracts explicit commit candidates from current Codex rollout formats and hands them to the existing `turnAnchorResolver`:\\n\\n- pairs calls and outputs by `call_id`\\n- supports standard `function_call` / `exec_command` and `custom_tool_call` / `exec` envelopes\\n- unwraps static `tools.exec_command({cmd: ...})` JavaScript calls, while rejecting dynamic template interpolation\\n- recognizes\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2103,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): externalize task images before applying transcript cap\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2103\",\n      \"head\": \"862d9f4440770cd87fa0115c857106e7114f0e2d\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/issue-2063-transcript-cap\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This PR fixes issue #2063 where large task transcripts containing base64 images were being capped before externalization, leading to lost transcripts even when externalization was enabled.\\r\\n\\r\\nChanges:\\r\\n- Reordered the condensation strategy to externalize images BEFORE applying the transcript cap.\\r\\n- Added a targeted boundary test to verify that images up to the 50MB cap are externalized and transcripts are preserved.\\r\\n- Verified that transcripts exceeding the cap after externalization are still safely handled.\\r\\n\\r\\nNative test passed: TestCondenseSession_TaskRecordImageExternalizationBoundary\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2102,\n      \"title\": \"fix(sweep): own the half-ended session shape\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2102\",\n      \"head\": \"422cb0146d0ba45f7e01b3011f75a7b37d1be409\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/sweep-half-ended-sessions\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1126\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nFollow-up to #2029 (trail 1073), from re-reviewing it after the fixes landed.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nA session state can carry `EndedAt` without `PhaseEnded`. `State.IsEnded` exists for exactly that shape, and its doc names it:\\n\\n> Both halves matter and neither implies the other in practice: Phase is what the state machine sets, EndedAt is what the finalizing write stamps, and a state file can carry one without the other (a legacy record, or a partial write). Callers that filter for active sessions must agree on this rule, so it lives here rather than being re-spelled at each site.\\n\\nThe sweep\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2099,\n      \"title\": \"fix(claude-code): capture Stop transcripts as validated snapshots\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2099\",\n      \"head\": \"4e2cccb854fe0736b5268a40d34c57bc031dee61\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-claude-transcript-readiness\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Refs #2091, item 3 only.\\n\\nBefore this change, Claude Code'\"'\"'s Stop hook waited for a transcript sentinel that no longer appears, then fell back to a 500 ms quiet window. The wait only validated a mutable path. Lifecycle copied that path later, and provisional-checkpoint finalization opened it once more. Entire could therefore store bytes other than the ones it had treated as ready.\\n\\nThis PR replaces that sequence with one owned, validated snapshot for Claude Stop. Modern Claude payloads provide the final assistant response, so Entire can validate a transcript immediately with no artificial wait. Older payloads retain the 500 ms quiet-window fallback. The lifecycle also keeps checkpoints refres\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2085,\n      \"title\": \"refactor(hooks): stage absolute_git_hook_path scoping, and detect a dead pin\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2085\",\n      \"head\": \"9b6d0ebbd57f9744c0a62eb67db11bca3845fdd2\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/absolute-hook-path-scope\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Two residuals from the local_dev removal (#1999), both about `absolute_git_hook_path` — the setting that makes git hooks embed an absolute binary path instead of bare `entire`, for GUI git clients that never source a shell profile.\\n\\n**The scope change is staged.** Phase one warns and migrates; a later release flips it. See below for why a hard break was wrong.\\n\\n## Why staged\\n\\nVerified against the pre-change binary from `main`:\\n\\n```\\n$ entire configure --absolute-git-hook-path\\n✓ Settings updated (.entire/settings.json)\\nproject: {\\\"enabled\\\":true,\\\"absolute_git_hook_path\\\":true}\\nlocal:   (none)\\n```\\n\\nThe documented way to enable the feature wrote it **exclusively to the tracked file**. So the affect\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2080,\n      \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): name the sync remote in the multi-remote note\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2080\",\n      \"head\": \"e40f28ef11303e96196d8ee815a87d8684036c15\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/checkpoint-destination-note-capture\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1108\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## The problem\\n\\nThe several-remotes note printed by `entire enable` / `entire doctor` says:\\n\\n> Checkpoints sync to a single elected remote — not to whichever one you push to. **A push to any other remote carries your code but no session history.** Run `entire status` to see the elected destination and how many checkpoints are waiting for it.\\n\\nThat bolded sentence is not true of the one push that matters most. `pendingCaptureCheckpointSyncRemote` runs **before** the single-remote gate in `prePush`, so a push whose target agrees with the branch'\"'\"'s declared push destination elects that \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2078,\n      \"title\": \"feat(doctor): detect Cursor IDE UNC-mode WSL repos where hooks never fire\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2078\",\n      \"head\": \"c3f3da458d5845a0065a926a3e4eb59466d7e231\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/cursor-unc-mode-doctor\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1106\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nCustomer report: Cursor IDE sessions on Windows + WSL2 never appear in `entire session list` until a manual `entire session attach`, while Cursor CLI in the same repo tracks fine.\\n\\nRoot cause, verified empirically on a Windows Server 2022 + WSL2 + Cursor 3.16.29 VM with paired sh-vs-cmd discriminator hooks: **Cursor IDE executes zero hooks when a WSL repo is opened via a `\\\\\\\\wsl$` UNC path** (agent runs, transcript saves, not one hook fires, no log mention — Cursor'\"'\"'s own dialog marks the mode \\\"not recommended\\\"). In WSL-remote mode (\\\"Reopen Folder in WSL\\\") the same repo'\"'\"'s \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2077,\n      \"title\": \"feat(agent): add Goose and Qwen Code integrations\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2077\",\n      \"head\": \"a9730b3a69055f1ef5968250fa346d93b7966e9d\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/agents-goose-qwen\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Closes #2160.\\n\\nAdds two agents: **Goose** (Agentic AI Foundation) and **Qwen Code** (Alibaba).\\n\\n```\\nentire enable --agent goose\\nentire enable --agent qwen-code\\n```\\n\\n![enable](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ar9av/cli/assets-goose/goose/01-enable.png)\\n\\n## Both agents'\"'\"' hooks are verified firing\\n\\nNeither agent completes a turn without a paid provider, so I ran each against a local OpenAI-compatible endpoint with Entire'\"'\"'s hooks installed. These counts come from Entire'\"'\"'s own logs after a real session:\\n\\n![hooks fire](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ar9av/cli/assets-goose/goose/07-hooks-fire.png)\\n\\nQwen fires `session-start` once, `turn-start` twice and `turn-end` once. The second `turn-start` c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2074,\n      \"title\": \"Add cross-repository context sharing to the CLI\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2074\",\n      \"head\": \"c75aefeca26c13684a028bc29d475eaa1d0c5c1d\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/cross-repo-context-sharing\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1105\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n- add `entire context enable`, `disable`, `status`, `query`, and `inspect`\\n- retrieve authorized evidence per cell with bounded fanout, redaction, sanitization, deterministic merging, and fail-closed completeness checks\\n- support consent-gated local-live session discovery with serialized cleanup, heartbeat refresh, and bounded evidence retention\\n- inject untrusted evidence through native Copilot CLI and Factory Droid hook transports while stripping injected blocks from stored transcripts\\n- add organization context-sharing policy commands and the generated Core API client\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2070,\n      \"title\": \"fix(codex): map last_assistant_message onto Event.TaskDescription\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2070\",\n      \"head\": \"49456fb8a73bea66df57050fb688e2e6373d3df1\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/track-2064\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1101\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n## Scope (updated)\\n\\nThis branch establishes a shared cross-agent sanitization boundary before text reaches Git or checkpoint metadata:\\n\\n- Codex lifecycle: map last_assistant_message to Event.TaskDescription\\n- SanitizeSubjectContent: redact secrets, strip unsafe controls; fail closed when input exceeds the 4096-rune window\\n- Persistence: lifecycle launch/completion, manual-commit condensation, checkpoint task.json, Git commit subjects\\n- Agents: Codex primary; any path through strategy.SanitizeSubjectContent\\n\\nVerification: go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/... plus lifecycle/checkpoint\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2069,\n      \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): externalize images in subagent transcripts before size cap\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2069\",\n      \"head\": \"1ea47d133a344b9274f06859e64b261d23807078\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/track-2063\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"**Trail:** https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1100\\n\\n**What:** Run image externalization on subagent transcripts (when enabled) before the 50MB size check, and store returned assets under `tasks/<id>/assets/`.\\n\\n**Why / how it helps:** Subagent path only sanitized then size-checked/redacted, so image-heavy transcripts were dropped whole and Codex `input_image` base64 reached'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' '7 events |\\n| copilotcli | 8 struct fields, hand-copied | the same 8, from a t\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2136,\n      \"title\": \"refactor(external): probe agent binaries in parallel and record failures\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2136\",\n      \"head\": \"00e9813c7b3bc7037162f414d1cc35c281ca5a23\",\n      \"branch\": \"refactor-discover-external-agents-claude-version\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1150\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nStacked on #2134, which contains the two implementation plans. This PR implements the `claude-version.md` design and incorporates the follow-up review fixes.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nExternal agent discovery now collects candidates without executing them, probes each binary concurrently under its own budget, and applies results in stable PATH order. A slow or broken plugin no longer blocks later plugins, and load failures remain visible instead of disappearing into debug logs.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n- Store usable and broken external agents in the central agent registry. Registry walks still expose \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2134,\n      \"title\": \"docs(external-agents): add claude-version discovery refactor plan\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2134\",\n      \"head\": \"1c5bda9bb267d33c51f4116cbc4bfb33792a7fc2\",\n      \"branch\": \"refactor-discover-and-register-external-agents\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1148\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What\\n\\nAdds `docs/external-agents/claude-version.md` — a plan for reworking external agent discovery, sitting alongside the existing `pi-version.md` so the two can be compared section for section.\\n\\nDocs only. No code, no behaviour change.\\n\\n## The plan in one line\\n\\nCollect candidate `entire-agent-*` binaries from `$PATH` (filesystem only), probe each one'\"'\"'s `info` in parallel under a per-binary budget, then record both ready and unloadable agents so `entire agent list` can explain why a plugin is missing.\\n\\n## Where it differs from pi-version\\n\\n| | pi-version | claude-version |\\n|---|-\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2131,\n      \"title\": \"perf(checkpoint): batch persistent session writes with CAS\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2131\",\n      \"head\": \"56e583e0e2f34abd5ee17319e745d509a1245bc3\",\n      \"branch\": \"improve-process-sessions-condensation\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\n`process_sessions` still persists each session separately. For every session, it reloads the checkpoint, rebuilds the session index and summary, creates a commit, and advances the checkpoint ref.\\n\\nIssue #2091 measures that work at roughly 73–103 ms per session. The repeated checkpoint load and rebuild make condensation slower as more sessions share a checkpoint.\\n\\nCheckpoint-level batching needs two things first:\\n\\n- Ref updates must detect concurrent writes from hooks, worktrees, CLI processes, and other Git clients.\\n- Both persistent Git layouts must use the same batch algorithm.\\n\\n## Solution\\n\\nThis PR adds native compare-and-swap publication and a shared `BatchSessions` write req\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2127,\n      \"title\": \"feat(grok): add Grok Build (xAI) agent integration\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2127\",\n      \"head\": \"f9001c7a9f108364e95b8695930ee550b0ca6447\",\n      \"branch\": \"add_grok_agent\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1143\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nAdds Grok Build (xAI) as an Entire agent, registered as `grok`.\\n\\nBuilt through the research → write-tests → implement pipeline. Everything\\nbelow was verified against a real Grok 1.0.5 install, with captured payloads\\nand a real session transcript checked in as test fixtures.\\n\\n## What'\"'\"'s here\\n\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/grok/` — the agent. Core `Agent` plus `HookSupport`,\\n  `HookFreshness`, `TranscriptAnalyzer`, `TokenCalculator`, `ModelExtractor`,\\n  and `SubagentSessionResolver`. Marked `IsPreview()`.\\n- `e2e/agents/grok.go` — E2E runner, so the existing `ForEachAgent` suite\\n  covers Grok\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2124,\n      \"title\": \"Classify a cell'\"'\"'s 401 as a credential rejection, not a raw error\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2124\",\n      \"head\": \"f5df2877a58cc7c9469eacb274c0b04c181c375d\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/search-401-classification\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\nAn account whose `home_jurisdiction` is `eu` gets a 401 from every cell'\"'\"'s semantic-search route, and we printed the service'\"'\"'s body verbatim ([#2121](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2121)):\\n\\n```\\nsearch failed: semantic search: search service error (401): Unauthorized\\n```\\n\\nThat names no region, offers no next step, and invites the one action that cannot possibly work — logging in again. The rejection is server-side and account-scoped ([entirehq/entire-search#196](https://github.com/entirehq/entire-search/issues/196)); the *same bearer* is accepted by code search at the same host.\\n\\nNow:\\n\\n```\\nsearch failed: semantic search: your credentials were rejected in aws-eu-central-1 — \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2122,\n      \"title\": \"Install Entire CLI in Cursor Cloud Agent environments on enable\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2122\",\n      \"head\": \"afbc67abcce876dd039ab7de3624dd43514ec802\",\n      \"branch\": \"cursor/cursor-cloud-env-entire-cli-2123\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1140\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_BEGIN -->\\n## Summary\\n\\nCursor Cloud Agents do not inherit a developer’s local `entire` install, so committed hooks that invoke `entire` silently no-op there.\\n\\n`entire enable` now writes a shared, idempotent helper (`.entire/install-cli.sh`) that any remote environment can run. When Cursor is selected **and** the repo already has `.cursor/environment.json`, enable appends `bash .entire/install-cli.sh` to that file’s `install` command.\\n\\nIt does **not** create `.cursor/environment.json`. A committed copy overrides dashboard-managed personal/team Cloud Agent env\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2112,\n      \"title\": \"fix(cursor): detect Cursor by its project state dir, not just .cursor/\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2112\",\n      \"head\": \"a5aa8656fc24c05deb500210cddaabedceb4a6ae\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/cursor-detect-project-state\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1132\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nEvery agent'\"'\"'s `DetectPresence` asks *\\\"does `<repo>/.<agent>/` exist\\\"*. That'\"'\"'s a fair test for Claude Code, Codex, and Gemini, which all create repo-local config as a matter of course. It'\"'\"'s structurally unfair to Cursor: project rules are optional, and Cursor'\"'\"'s real per-project state lives in `~/.cursor/projects/<sanitized-repo-path>`.\\n\\nSo a repo driven daily from Cursor reports \\\"not present\\\". `entire enable` enables only detected agents when non-interactive, and pre-selects only detected ones on first run (`selectAgents`, `setup.go:1771-1795`). The observed result is worse than Curs\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2109,\n      \"title\": \"feat(import): anchor Codex turns to recorded commits\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2109\",\n      \"head\": \"d3496bfbb66d1c41fe29a163f05f8bdc14858657\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/import-codex-commit-sha\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\n`entire import codex` already restores historical Codex turns, but the Codex importer never populated `Turn.CommitSHAs`. Every imported turn therefore used the default-branch fallback introduced in #1825, even when the rollout recorded the exact `git commit` invocation and its resulting SHA.\\n\\nThis PR extracts explicit commit candidates from current Codex rollout formats and hands them to the existing `turnAnchorResolver`:\\n\\n- pairs calls and outputs by `call_id`\\n- supports standard `function_call` / `exec_command` and `custom_tool_call` / `exec` envelopes\\n- unwraps static `tools.exec_command({cmd: ...})` JavaScript calls, while rejecting dynamic template interpolation\\n- recognizes\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2103,\n      \"title\": \"fix(strategy): externalize task images before applying transcript cap\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2103\",\n      \"head\": \"862d9f4440770cd87fa0115c857106e7114f0e2d\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/issue-2063-transcript-cap\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This PR fixes issue #2063 where large task transcripts containing base64 images were being capped before externalization, leading to lost transcripts even when externalization was enabled.\\r\\n\\r\\nChanges:\\r\\n- Reordered the condensation strategy to externalize images BEFORE applying the transcript cap.\\r\\n- Added a targeted boundary test to verify that images up to the 50MB cap are externalized and transcripts are preserved.\\r\\n- Verified that transcripts exceeding the cap after externalization are still safely handled.\\r\\n\\r\\nNative test passed: TestCondenseSession_TaskRecordImageExternalizationBoundary\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2102,\n      \"title\": \"fix(sweep): own the half-ended session shape\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2102\",\n      \"head\": \"422cb0146d0ba45f7e01b3011f75a7b37d1be409\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/sweep-half-ended-sessions\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1126\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nFollow-up to #2029 (trail 1073), from re-reviewing it after the fixes landed.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nA session state can carry `EndedAt` without `PhaseEnded`. `State.IsEnded` exists for exactly that shape, and its doc names it:\\n\\n> Both halves matter and neither implies the other in practice: Phase is what the state machine sets, EndedAt is what the finalizing write stamps, and a state file can carry one without the other (a legacy record, or a partial write). Callers that filter for active sessions must agree on this rule, so it lives here rather than being re-spelled at each site.\\n\\nThe sweep\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2099,\n      \"title\": \"fix(claude-code): capture Stop transcripts as validated snapshots\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2099\",\n      \"head\": \"4e2cccb854fe0736b5268a40d34c57bc031dee61\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-claude-transcript-readiness\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Refs #2091, item 3 only.\\n\\nBefore this change, Claude Code'\"'\"'s Stop hook waited for a transcript sentinel that no longer appears, then fell back to a 500 ms quiet window. The wait only validated a mutable path. Lifecycle copied that path later, and provisional-checkpoint finalization opened it once more. Entire could therefore store bytes other than the ones it had treated as ready.\\n\\nThis PR replaces that sequence with one owned, validated snapshot for Claude Stop. Modern Claude payloads provide the final assistant response, so Entire can validate a transcript immediately with no artificial wait. Older payloads retain the 500 ms quiet-window fallback. The lifecycle also keeps checkpoints refres\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2085,\n      \"title\": \"refactor(hooks): stage absolute_git_hook_path scoping, and detect a dead pin\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2085\",\n      \"head\": \"9b6d0ebbd57f9744c0a62eb67db11bca3845fdd2\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/absolute-hook-path-scope\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Two residuals from the local_dev removal (#1999), both about `absolute_git_hook_path` — the setting that makes git hooks embed an absolute binary path instead of bare `entire`, for GUI git clients that never source a shell profile.\\n\\n**The scope change is staged.** Phase one warns and migrates; a later release flips it. See below for why a hard break was wrong.\\n\\n## Why staged\\n\\nVerified against the pre-change binary from `main`:\\n\\n```\\n$ entire configure --absolute-git-hook-path\\n✓ Settings updated (.entire/settings.json)\\nproject: {\\\"enabled\\\":true,\\\"absolute_git_hook_path\\\":true}\\nlocal:   (none)\\n```\\n\\nThe documented way to enable the feature wrote it **exclusively to the tracked file**. So the affect\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2080,\n      \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): name the sync remote in the multi-remote note\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2080\",\n      \"head\": \"e40f28ef11303e96196d8ee815a87d8684036c15\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/checkpoint-destination-note-capture\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1108\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## The problem\\n\\nThe several-remotes note printed by `entire enable` / `entire doctor` says:\\n\\n> Checkpoints sync to a single elected remote — not to whichever one you push to. **A push to any other remote carries your code but no session history.** Run `entire status` to see the elected destination and how many checkpoints are waiting for it.\\n\\nThat bolded sentence is not true of the one push that matters most. `pendingCaptureCheckpointSyncRemote` runs **before** the single-remote gate in `prePush`, so a push whose target agrees with the branch'\"'\"'s declared push destination elects that \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2078,\n      \"title\": \"feat(doctor): detect Cursor IDE UNC-mode WSL repos where hooks never fire\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2078\",\n      \"head\": \"c3f3da458d5845a0065a926a3e4eb59466d7e231\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/cursor-unc-mode-doctor\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1106\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nCustomer report: Cursor IDE sessions on Windows + WSL2 never appear in `entire session list` until a manual `entire session attach`, while Cursor CLI in the same repo tracks fine.\\n\\nRoot cause, verified empirically on a Windows Server 2022 + WSL2 + Cursor 3.16.29 VM with paired sh-vs-cmd discriminator hooks: **Cursor IDE executes zero hooks when a WSL repo is opened via a `\\\\\\\\wsl$` UNC path** (agent runs, transcript saves, not one hook fires, no log mention — Cursor'\"'\"'s own dialog marks the mode \\\"not recommended\\\"). In WSL-remote mode (\\\"Reopen Folder in WSL\\\") the same repo'\"'\"'s \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2077,\n      \"title\": \"feat(agent): add Goose and Qwen Code integrations\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2077\",\n      \"head\": \"a9730b3a69055f1ef5968250fa346d93b7966e9d\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/agents-goose-qwen\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Closes #2160.\\n\\nAdds two agents: **Goose** (Agentic AI Foundation) and **Qwen Code** (Alibaba).\\n\\n```\\nentire enable --agent goose\\nentire enable --agent qwen-code\\n```\\n\\n![enable](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ar9av/cli/assets-goose/goose/01-enable.png)\\n\\n## Both agents'\"'\"' hooks are verified firing\\n\\nNeither agent completes a turn without a paid provider, so I ran each against a local OpenAI-compatible endpoint with Entire'\"'\"'s hooks installed. These counts come from Entire'\"'\"'s own logs after a real session:\\n\\n![hooks fire](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ar9av/cli/assets-goose/goose/07-hooks-fire.png)\\n\\nQwen fires `session-start` once, `turn-start` twice and `turn-end` once. The second `turn-start` c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2074,\n      \"title\": \"Add cross-repository context sharing to the CLI\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2074\",\n      \"head\": \"c75aefeca26c13684a028bc29d475eaa1d0c5c1d\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/cross-repo-context-sharing\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1105\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n- add `entire context enable`, `disable`, `status`, `query`, and `inspect`\\n- retrieve authorized evidence per cell with bounded fanout, redaction, sanitization, deterministic merging, and fail-closed completeness checks\\n- support consent-gated local-live session discovery with serialized cleanup, heartbeat refresh, and bounded evidence retention\\n- inject untrusted evidence through native Copilot CLI and Factory Droid hook transports while stripping injected blocks from stored transcripts\\n- add organization context-sharing policy commands and the generated Core API client\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2070,\n      \"title\": \"fix(codex): map last_assistant_message onto Event.TaskDescription\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2070\",\n      \"head\": \"49456fb8a73bea66df57050fb688e2e6373d3df1\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/track-2064\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1101\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n## Scope (updated)\\n\\nThis branch establishes a shared cross-agent sanitization boundary before text reaches Git or checkpoint metadata:\\n\\n- Codex lifecycle: map last_assistant_message to Event.TaskDescription\\n- SanitizeSubjectContent: redact secrets, strip unsafe controls; fail closed when input exceeds the 4096-rune window\\n- Persistence: lifecycle launch/completion, manual-commit condensation, checkpoint task.json, Git commit subjects\\n- Agents: Codex primary; any path through strategy.SanitizeSubjectContent\\n\\nVerification: go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/... plus lifecycle/checkpoint\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2069,\n      \"title\": \"fix(checkpoint): externalize images in subagent transcripts before size cap\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2069\",\n      \"head\": \"1ea47d133a344b9274f06859e64b261d23807078\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/track-2063\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"**Trail:** https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1100\\n\\n**What:** Run image externalization on subagent transcripts (when enabled) before the 50MB size check, and store returned assets under `tasks/<id>/assets/`.\\n\\n**Why / how it helps:** Subagent path only sanitized then size-checked/redacted, so image-heavy transcripts were dropped whole and Codex `input_image` base64 reached'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":11000}},"started_at_ms":1794842129246,"completed_at_ms":1794842129246}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:29.413Z","ordinal":3022,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-da480894-1ab5-44da-b1ec-e5bd4a3977bb","process_id":"45803","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' ' redaction intact (corruption risk).\\n\\n**How:** `prepareSubagentTranscript`: sanitize → optional `imageextract` → size-check externalized bytes; wire assets into persistent + ephemeral task writers.\\n\\n**Testing:**\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/ -count=1` (375 passed)\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/transcript/image\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2068,\n      \"title\": \"fix(claude-code): attribute parallel subagent TodoWrite checkpoints via agent_id\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2068\",\n      \"head\": \"8dfc6511d7911f40ed2735e721b6518c5a194dac\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/track-2062\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"**Trail:** https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1099\\n\\n**What:** Attribute Claude Code incremental TodoWrite checkpoints to the correct parallel Task using `agent_id` → remembered task links instead of mtime-only `FindActivePreTaskFile`.\\n\\n**Why / how it helps:** Sibling parallel Tasks each write `pre-task-*.json`; the newest-file heuristic misfiles progress under the wrong `tool_use_id`. Claude sends `agent_id` on in-subagent PostToolUse hooks but Entire dropped it.\\n\\n**How:** Capture `agent_id` on `SubagentCheckpointHookInput`; remember/lookup `.entire/tmp/agent-task-<id>.json`; prefer link over mtime; purge links on pre-task cleanup.\\n\\n**Testing:**\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/ -run '\"'\"'Agent\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2067,\n      \"title\": \"fix(cursor): correlate subagentStop without subagent_id via task description\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2067\",\n      \"head\": \"b9a8e4b659d671bfbad8f3ab9ccc71eacf3a46b3\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/track-2061\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"**Trail:** https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1098\\n\\n**What:** Recover the Cursor subagent correlation id on Stop when Cursor omits `subagent_id`, using the stored task description (or a single unambiguous active pre-task).\\n\\n**Why / how it helps:** Official Cursor `subagentStop` payloads have no `subagent_id` (only Start does). Empty ToolUseID made Stop miss `pre-task-<id>.json`, orphan state files, and collide parallel Stops.\\n\\n**How:** Store `TaskDescription` on `PreTaskState`; add `ResolvePreTaskToolUseID`; resolve empty ids in `handleLifecycleSubagentEnd` before load/cleanup.\\n\\n**Testing:**\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/ -run '\"'\"'TestResolvePreTask|TestHandleLifecycleSubagentEnd_Resolves|T\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2053,\n      \"title\": \"refactor(`jsonutil`): centralize streaming atomic replacement\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2053\",\n      \"head\": \"c7b2d57fa45b6a05e86a9cb76d5ae36ef2bb8b23\",\n      \"branch\": \"refactor-streaming-atomic-write\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Depends on #1877. Until that PR merges, review the stacked range `3a39273b..7c62491a5`.\\n\\nThis change moves OpenCode’s staged transcript publication into `jsonutil.WriteFileAtomicStream`. The previous implementation kept temporary-file creation, validation, rename retries, and recovery inside OpenCode even though most of that lifecycle is general atomic-write behavior. The shared implementation keeps publication ordered as produce, sync, close, validate, chmod, rename, and best-effort directory sync.\\n\\n## Core Changes\\n\\n`WriteFileAtomicStream` now owns the staging file from creation through publication. Producer and validator errors are returned unchanged. Any failure before publication leaves \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2041,\n      \"title\": \"Record changed code entities in checkpoint metadata (gated, off by default)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2041\",\n      \"head\": \"4c5a097da8dda2fb09c9e55089c9a9c78b4c3671\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/checkpoint-entity-deltas\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1083\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nImplements the entity-deltas half of the VCS keystone (COR-782): each persistent checkpoint gains an `entity_deltas.json` in its per-session tree dir recording which code entities (functions/types/methods) the session changed — schema_version 1.0, shared contract with entire-brain'\"'\"'s entity→checkpoint index.\\n\\n**Off by default.** Gated on `entity_deltas` settings key / `ENTIRE_ENTITY_DELTAS` env (tri-state: force-on, force-off, fall-through). With the gate off the only cost is the settings read.\\n\\n**Design — nothing runs in the hook path:**\\n- Post-commit condense writes a job file and \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2031,\n      \"title\": \"docs: add the Tests and Comments policy section to CLAUDE.md\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2031\",\n      \"head\": \"e9f6de619d5339865414872884eb9e8114a2a24c\",\n      \"branch\": \"docs/tests-and-comments-policy\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Checks in the test/comment discipline that reviews have enforced for months but that never existed as written policy — reviewers (human and agent) have been citing a \\\"Tests and Comments\\\" section that wasn'\"'\"'t in the file.\\n\\nThe text codifies: tests only for observable behavior/invariants/concrete regressions (never coverage or symmetry); no tombstone tests; prefer integration/snapshot coverage over redundant partial-string assertions; extend existing tests over new files/fixtures; comments state non-obvious rationale and constraints, never restatements.\\n\\nAGENTS.md picks it up via the existing symlink. Docs-only, no code changes.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2030,\n      \"title\": \"Add entire enable --global\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2030\",\n      \"head\": \"5e4fe117f51ad2da431eb3fc4856524f4592d288\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/global-trust\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/1142/changes/cli/1074\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What\\n\\n`entire enable --global` turns Entire on in every repo you work in. It writes one key to the user settings file (`~/.config/entire/settings.json`):\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"global_enable\\\": true }\\n```\\n\\nWith it on, Claude Code sessions are recorded in every repo, as if `entire enable` had run there. Checkpoints from a repo that is on only through global enable stay local until you agree to push them for that repo, or until its owner is on your global-enable owner list. Other agents are recorded only in repos where `entire enable` ran, because only Claude Code has user-leve\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2027,\n      \"title\": \"fix(opencode): preserve prompts after metadata fallback\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2027\",\n      \"head\": \"28931fedd6211c96e248cc59aa1d7eba88ffd8c4\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-opencode-user-prompt-events\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2001.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Problem\\r\\nOpenCode emits a user `message.updated` event before the `message.part.updated` event containing the prompt text. The plugin starts the turn from that metadata event with an empty prompt so a fast agent commit still sees an ACTIVE session. Because the message was then marked as seen, the later text part was ignored and checkpoints lost the user prompt.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe first version of this PR kept a marker for those promptless starts and fired `turn-start` again when the text arrived. That recovered the prompt, but `turn-start` is not a prompt setter. It captures pre-prompt Git state, creates a new `TurnID`, recalculates prompt attribution, and clears `LastCheckpointID` an\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2019,\n      \"title\": \"feat(release): add a dev channel that tracks main\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2019\",\n      \"head\": \"1a5bd6c31d3260c4701ba70951522c75d1480010\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/dev-release-channel\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1067\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nRemoving local-dev mode (#1999) took away how this repo'\"'\"'s developers ran their own code, without shipping the replacement. Hooks now name the `entire` binary and resolve it through PATH, so dogfooding means having a current build installed — and nothing built one automatically.\\n\\nThis adds a **`dev` channel: one release, replaced on every merge to main that passes tests.** `install.sh --channel dev` (or `mise run dev:sync`) therefore always fetches current main, through the same install path users take.\\n\\n## Why not just retrigger nightly\\n\\nNightly is a daily, externally consum\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1993,\n      \"title\": \"feat(doctor): add flutter-doctor-style environment sweep\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1993\",\n      \"head\": \"8d724923f9c3f9ce69e8c56591d875a764ef33ab\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/doctor-env-sweep\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\n`entire doctor` now opens with a flutter-doctor-style, read-only environment/installation/configuration sweep before the existing session repair flow runs unchanged. Each finding is reported with the command to fix it.\\n\\n## Checks added\\n\\n1. **Entire CLI version** — current version, plus update availability for the active channel (nightly vs stable) with the exact update command (`brew upgrade`, `mise upgrade`, `scoop update`, install script). Dev builds skip the fetch.\\n2. **Git** — present on PATH and runnable (core runtime dependency).\\n3. **Repository** — inside a git repo? Entire enabled? (`entire enable` hint when disabled)\\n4. **Agent hooks** — which agents have hooks installed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1989,\n      \"title\": \"chore(pi): regenerate the stale committed dogfood extension\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1989\",\n      \"head\": \"64bc658c6a987a4f043e5981a14577b2cf277831\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/pi-dogfood-extension-stale\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1045\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## TL;DR\\n\\n`entire doctor` reports `Pi hooks: OUT OF DATE` in this repo because the committed dogfood extension drifted from the embedded template. Regenerated it.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nThis repo commits `.pi/extensions/entire/index.ts` (rendered in `--local-dev` mode) so the dogfood setup works out of the box. The embedded template moved on; the committed copy didn'\"'\"'t.\\n\\n| File | Last touched |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/agent/pi/entire_extension.ts` (template) | `d55dfa643` — 2026-08-10 |\\n| `.pi/extensions/entire/index.ts` (committed copy) | `ed42608db` — 2026-07-24 |\\n\\nTwo commits landed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1960,\n      \"title\": \"Add search_id, explain hints, and search relevance telemetry (ENT-1528)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1960\",\n      \"head\": \"acb14e59ff1a1ade906f4f0f528637190a651bc7\",\n      \"branch\": \"porting-agent-chat-context\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\nAgent-driven search (~80% of expected search traffic) has no web-style click signal, so we can'\"'\"'t tell whether the results we return are relevant. This closes the loop statelessly — no local correlation files ([ENT-1528](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/ENT-1528), full plan + updates in the ticket comments).\\n\\n- **`search_id` in every search JSON envelope** (`--json` and `--compact`): a client-minted ULID — the server response carries no request id and the CLI merges per-cell responses, so it can'\"'\"'t come from the server. Also the future seam for server-side impression logging in query-serve.\\n- **Per-hit `explain` hint in `--compact` output**: `\\\"explain\\\": \\\"entire checkpoint explain \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1943,\n      \"title\": \"fix(search): 1 MiB cell response cap truncated large-region results; surface per-region fan-out errors\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1943\",\n      \"head\": \"fb983446380db12d116bf443fc7bf0327dcdce8e\",\n      \"branch\": \"search-fanout-1mib-truncation\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1005\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n`entire search --all-repos` (or `repo:*`) fans out to every regional query-serve cell in parallel and merges the results. On high-hit queries (e.g. `transcript`, `backfill`, `indexer`), the busiest cell silently dropped out of the results and the CLI printed only `search failed in 1 of 4 regions; results may be incomplete` — with no way to tell which region or why. **Silent, incomplete cross-region results.**\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\n**Bug 2 — the defect.** `search.CellV4` read each cell'\"'\"'s response body with `io.ReadAll(io.LimitReader(resp.Body, 1<<20))` — a hard **1 MiB** cap. T\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1930,\n      \"title\": \"fix: agent add/list/remove now discover external agents (#1928)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1930\",\n      \"head\": \"eb70fb2cf24eca5ac17469bad432447144b1f56f\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/1928-agent-group-external-discovery\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n`entire agent add/list/remove` omitted external agents (e.g. `zed`), failing with `Unknown agent`, even though `entire enable --agent <name>` and the git-hook paths worked. The `agent` noun-group never invoked external-agent discovery, so `agent.Get` / `agent.List` only saw statically-registered built-ins.\\n\\nFixes #1928.\\n\\n## Changes\\n- `add` / `remove` `RunE`: resolve the single named plugin via the shared `resolveNamedExternalAgent` helper (`external.DiscoverAndRegisterNamedAlways(ctx, name)`) before `agent.Get` / `runRemoveAgent`. Targeting the exact name (rather than a full `$PATH` scan) avoids executing every unrelated `entire-agent-*` binary, and surfaces a real plugin load err\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1929,\n      \"title\": \"fix(import): sync imported checkpoints once logged in\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1929\",\n      \"head\": \"9212599eb292128ce4efebc3d774a4eac9ad80ef\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/1773-sync-imported-checkpoints\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #1773 (fix 2 — sync after login). @karthik-rameshkumar handed this over on the issue after landing fix 1 (#1774).\\n\\n## The problem\\n\\n`entire import` writes read-only checkpoints and **creates no commit**, so the pre-push git hook — the only sync trigger — never fires for it. Because idempotency is keyed on *local* existence, history imported while logged out is stranded permanently: the post-login re-run reports `0 turn(s) (N already imported)` and makes no attempt to sync.\\n\\n## The insight that keeps this small\\n\\nThe git-refs store **already enqueues every checkpoint ref as it writes it** (`gitRefsStore.setRef` → `enqueueForPush`, `checkpoint/refs_store.go:209`), and nothing drains that q\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1920,\n      \"title\": \"test(checkpoint): failing repro for concurrent checkpoint-write lost update (#1917)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1920\",\n      \"head\": \"af59539f48227a0e91eaa31a34e2eaaf06dbb3df\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/concurrent-checkpoint-write-race\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Draft — **this PR is a reproduction, not a fix.** The concurrent subtests are\\nred on purpose, so CI will fail. It exists to make #1917 concrete and to pin\\ndown which scenario is actually reachable.\\n\\n## What it reproduces\\n\\nTwo agents working in one worktree, whose uncondensed work lands in a **single\\ncommit**, end up sharing **one** checkpoint: post-commit condenses both\\nsessions into it and records it in each session'\"'\"'s `TurnCheckpointIDs`. When\\nboth turns end, both Stop hooks run `finalizeAllTurnCheckpoints` over that same\\ncheckpoint.\\n\\nNothing serializes them:\\n\\n- each Stop hook holds only its own per-session flock — `stateLockPath` is\\n  keyed by session ID, and these are legitimately *differ\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1891,\n      \"title\": \"Fix Fish installer setup\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1891\",\n      \"head\": \"ed9c46b648bdcae2d7a6ae3dba0ce0bee2340b14\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/install-fish-support\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\n- detect the invoking shell before falling back to `$SHELL`\\n- use the Fish-native `fish_add_path` flow and preserve XDG-aware completion config\\n- run post-install actions on first-time installs and add installer regression coverage\\n- clarify that Fish users should still pipe the Bash installer to `bash`\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\nThe installer was Bash-only, but its Fish handoff relied solely on `$SHELL` and appended `fish_add_path` to a hard-coded `~/.config/fish/config.fish`. That could select the wrong shell, ignore `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`, leave the current Fish session without the new path, and skip post-install actions during the normal first install.\\n\\n## User impact\\n\\nFish users now receive\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1884,\n      \"title\": \"trail resume: finish the non-interactive contract\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1884\",\n      \"head\": \"5a1c663cf5fd49fa598e4fde8e631bcee24fa666\",\n      \"branch\": \"trail-resume\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/961\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n`entire trail resume` was designed interactive-first; for agent callers (the most common caller) the non-interactive path was never finished. This PR completes it without touching the core semantics — checkpoint discovery, restore, and interactive launch all stay as they are.\\n\\n**Breaking for scripts**: resume commands (`trail resume`, `session resume`, `checkpoint resume`) now exit non-zero whenever nothing was resumed; callers that relied on exit 0 in those cases must update. Interactive prompt declines still exit zero.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n**Never block, never need `--force` to comple\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1879,\n      \"title\": \"perf(codex): stop unmarshalling the whole rollout to compute token usage\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1879\",\n      \"head\": \"cc956ea9fddfbf88323e3ea29a35e02f2856b0c2\",\n      \"branch\": \"eric/staqpro-802-codex-token-prefilter\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #1836.\\n\\nPer @gtrrz-victor'\"'\"'s direction on the issue, this reevaluates the Codex token-usage path rather than porting Claude'\"'\"'s sli'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' ' redaction intact (corruption risk).\\n\\n**How:** `prepareSubagentTranscript`: sanitize → optional `imageextract` → size-check externalized bytes; wire assets into persistent + ephemeral task writers.\\n\\n**Testing:**\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/ -count=1` (375 passed)\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/transcript/image\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2068,\n      \"title\": \"fix(claude-code): attribute parallel subagent TodoWrite checkpoints via agent_id\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2068\",\n      \"head\": \"8dfc6511d7911f40ed2735e721b6518c5a194dac\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/track-2062\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"**Trail:** https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1099\\n\\n**What:** Attribute Claude Code incremental TodoWrite checkpoints to the correct parallel Task using `agent_id` → remembered task links instead of mtime-only `FindActivePreTaskFile`.\\n\\n**Why / how it helps:** Sibling parallel Tasks each write `pre-task-*.json`; the newest-file heuristic misfiles progress under the wrong `tool_use_id`. Claude sends `agent_id` on in-subagent PostToolUse hooks but Entire dropped it.\\n\\n**How:** Capture `agent_id` on `SubagentCheckpointHookInput`; remember/lookup `.entire/tmp/agent-task-<id>.json`; prefer link over mtime; purge links on pre-task cleanup.\\n\\n**Testing:**\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/ -run '\"'\"'Agent\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2067,\n      \"title\": \"fix(cursor): correlate subagentStop without subagent_id via task description\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2067\",\n      \"head\": \"b9a8e4b659d671bfbad8f3ab9ccc71eacf3a46b3\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/track-2061\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"**Trail:** https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1098\\n\\n**What:** Recover the Cursor subagent correlation id on Stop when Cursor omits `subagent_id`, using the stored task description (or a single unambiguous active pre-task).\\n\\n**Why / how it helps:** Official Cursor `subagentStop` payloads have no `subagent_id` (only Start does). Empty ToolUseID made Stop miss `pre-task-<id>.json`, orphan state files, and collide parallel Stops.\\n\\n**How:** Store `TaskDescription` on `PreTaskState`; add `ResolvePreTaskToolUseID`; resolve empty ids in `handleLifecycleSubagentEnd` before load/cleanup.\\n\\n**Testing:**\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/ -run '\"'\"'TestResolvePreTask|TestHandleLifecycleSubagentEnd_Resolves|T\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2053,\n      \"title\": \"refactor(`jsonutil`): centralize streaming atomic replacement\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2053\",\n      \"head\": \"c7b2d57fa45b6a05e86a9cb76d5ae36ef2bb8b23\",\n      \"branch\": \"refactor-streaming-atomic-write\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Depends on #1877. Until that PR merges, review the stacked range `3a39273b..7c62491a5`.\\n\\nThis change moves OpenCode’s staged transcript publication into `jsonutil.WriteFileAtomicStream`. The previous implementation kept temporary-file creation, validation, rename retries, and recovery inside OpenCode even though most of that lifecycle is general atomic-write behavior. The shared implementation keeps publication ordered as produce, sync, close, validate, chmod, rename, and best-effort directory sync.\\n\\n## Core Changes\\n\\n`WriteFileAtomicStream` now owns the staging file from creation through publication. Producer and validator errors are returned unchanged. Any failure before publication leaves \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2041,\n      \"title\": \"Record changed code entities in checkpoint metadata (gated, off by default)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2041\",\n      \"head\": \"4c5a097da8dda2fb09c9e55089c9a9c78b4c3671\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/checkpoint-entity-deltas\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1083\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nImplements the entity-deltas half of the VCS keystone (COR-782): each persistent checkpoint gains an `entity_deltas.json` in its per-session tree dir recording which code entities (functions/types/methods) the session changed — schema_version 1.0, shared contract with entire-brain'\"'\"'s entity→checkpoint index.\\n\\n**Off by default.** Gated on `entity_deltas` settings key / `ENTIRE_ENTITY_DELTAS` env (tri-state: force-on, force-off, fall-through). With the gate off the only cost is the settings read.\\n\\n**Design — nothing runs in the hook path:**\\n- Post-commit condense writes a job file and \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2031,\n      \"title\": \"docs: add the Tests and Comments policy section to CLAUDE.md\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2031\",\n      \"head\": \"e9f6de619d5339865414872884eb9e8114a2a24c\",\n      \"branch\": \"docs/tests-and-comments-policy\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Checks in the test/comment discipline that reviews have enforced for months but that never existed as written policy — reviewers (human and agent) have been citing a \\\"Tests and Comments\\\" section that wasn'\"'\"'t in the file.\\n\\nThe text codifies: tests only for observable behavior/invariants/concrete regressions (never coverage or symmetry); no tombstone tests; prefer integration/snapshot coverage over redundant partial-string assertions; extend existing tests over new files/fixtures; comments state non-obvious rationale and constraints, never restatements.\\n\\nAGENTS.md picks it up via the existing symlink. Docs-only, no code changes.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2030,\n      \"title\": \"Add entire enable --global\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2030\",\n      \"head\": \"5e4fe117f51ad2da431eb3fc4856524f4592d288\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/global-trust\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/1142/changes/cli/1074\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What\\n\\n`entire enable --global` turns Entire on in every repo you work in. It writes one key to the user settings file (`~/.config/entire/settings.json`):\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\\"global_enable\\\": true }\\n```\\n\\nWith it on, Claude Code sessions are recorded in every repo, as if `entire enable` had run there. Checkpoints from a repo that is on only through global enable stay local until you agree to push them for that repo, or until its owner is on your global-enable owner list. Other agents are recorded only in repos where `entire enable` ran, because only Claude Code has user-leve\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2027,\n      \"title\": \"fix(opencode): preserve prompts after metadata fallback\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2027\",\n      \"head\": \"28931fedd6211c96e248cc59aa1d7eba88ffd8c4\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-opencode-user-prompt-events\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #2001.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Problem\\r\\nOpenCode emits a user `message.updated` event before the `message.part.updated` event containing the prompt text. The plugin starts the turn from that metadata event with an empty prompt so a fast agent commit still sees an ACTIVE session. Because the message was then marked as seen, the later text part was ignored and checkpoints lost the user prompt.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe first version of this PR kept a marker for those promptless starts and fired `turn-start` again when the text arrived. That recovered the prompt, but `turn-start` is not a prompt setter. It captures pre-prompt Git state, creates a new `TurnID`, recalculates prompt attribution, and clears `LastCheckpointID` an\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2019,\n      \"title\": \"feat(release): add a dev channel that tracks main\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2019\",\n      \"head\": \"1a5bd6c31d3260c4701ba70951522c75d1480010\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/dev-release-channel\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1067\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nRemoving local-dev mode (#1999) took away how this repo'\"'\"'s developers ran their own code, without shipping the replacement. Hooks now name the `entire` binary and resolve it through PATH, so dogfooding means having a current build installed — and nothing built one automatically.\\n\\nThis adds a **`dev` channel: one release, replaced on every merge to main that passes tests.** `install.sh --channel dev` (or `mise run dev:sync`) therefore always fetches current main, through the same install path users take.\\n\\n## Why not just retrigger nightly\\n\\nNightly is a daily, externally consum\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1993,\n      \"title\": \"feat(doctor): add flutter-doctor-style environment sweep\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1993\",\n      \"head\": \"8d724923f9c3f9ce69e8c56591d875a764ef33ab\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/doctor-env-sweep\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\n`entire doctor` now opens with a flutter-doctor-style, read-only environment/installation/configuration sweep before the existing session repair flow runs unchanged. Each finding is reported with the command to fix it.\\n\\n## Checks added\\n\\n1. **Entire CLI version** — current version, plus update availability for the active channel (nightly vs stable) with the exact update command (`brew upgrade`, `mise upgrade`, `scoop update`, install script). Dev builds skip the fetch.\\n2. **Git** — present on PATH and runnable (core runtime dependency).\\n3. **Repository** — inside a git repo? Entire enabled? (`entire enable` hint when disabled)\\n4. **Agent hooks** — which agents have hooks installed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1989,\n      \"title\": \"chore(pi): regenerate the stale committed dogfood extension\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1989\",\n      \"head\": \"64bc658c6a987a4f043e5981a14577b2cf277831\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/pi-dogfood-extension-stale\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1045\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## TL;DR\\n\\n`entire doctor` reports `Pi hooks: OUT OF DATE` in this repo because the committed dogfood extension drifted from the embedded template. Regenerated it.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nThis repo commits `.pi/extensions/entire/index.ts` (rendered in `--local-dev` mode) so the dogfood setup works out of the box. The embedded template moved on; the committed copy didn'\"'\"'t.\\n\\n| File | Last touched |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/agent/pi/entire_extension.ts` (template) | `d55dfa643` — 2026-08-10 |\\n| `.pi/extensions/entire/index.ts` (committed copy) | `ed42608db` — 2026-07-24 |\\n\\nTwo commits landed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1960,\n      \"title\": \"Add search_id, explain hints, and search relevance telemetry (ENT-1528)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1960\",\n      \"head\": \"acb14e59ff1a1ade906f4f0f528637190a651bc7\",\n      \"branch\": \"porting-agent-chat-context\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\nAgent-driven search (~80% of expected search traffic) has no web-style click signal, so we can'\"'\"'t tell whether the results we return are relevant. This closes the loop statelessly — no local correlation files ([ENT-1528](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/ENT-1528), full plan + updates in the ticket comments).\\n\\n- **`search_id` in every search JSON envelope** (`--json` and `--compact`): a client-minted ULID — the server response carries no request id and the CLI merges per-cell responses, so it can'\"'\"'t come from the server. Also the future seam for server-side impression logging in query-serve.\\n- **Per-hit `explain` hint in `--compact` output**: `\\\"explain\\\": \\\"entire checkpoint explain \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1943,\n      \"title\": \"fix(search): 1 MiB cell response cap truncated large-region results; surface per-region fan-out errors\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1943\",\n      \"head\": \"fb983446380db12d116bf443fc7bf0327dcdce8e\",\n      \"branch\": \"search-fanout-1mib-truncation\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1005\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n`entire search --all-repos` (or `repo:*`) fans out to every regional query-serve cell in parallel and merges the results. On high-hit queries (e.g. `transcript`, `backfill`, `indexer`), the busiest cell silently dropped out of the results and the CLI printed only `search failed in 1 of 4 regions; results may be incomplete` — with no way to tell which region or why. **Silent, incomplete cross-region results.**\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\n**Bug 2 — the defect.** `search.CellV4` read each cell'\"'\"'s response body with `io.ReadAll(io.LimitReader(resp.Body, 1<<20))` — a hard **1 MiB** cap. T\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1930,\n      \"title\": \"fix: agent add/list/remove now discover external agents (#1928)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1930\",\n      \"head\": \"eb70fb2cf24eca5ac17469bad432447144b1f56f\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/1928-agent-group-external-discovery\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n`entire agent add/list/remove` omitted external agents (e.g. `zed`), failing with `Unknown agent`, even though `entire enable --agent <name>` and the git-hook paths worked. The `agent` noun-group never invoked external-agent discovery, so `agent.Get` / `agent.List` only saw statically-registered built-ins.\\n\\nFixes #1928.\\n\\n## Changes\\n- `add` / `remove` `RunE`: resolve the single named plugin via the shared `resolveNamedExternalAgent` helper (`external.DiscoverAndRegisterNamedAlways(ctx, name)`) before `agent.Get` / `runRemoveAgent`. Targeting the exact name (rather than a full `$PATH` scan) avoids executing every unrelated `entire-agent-*` binary, and surfaces a real plugin load err\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1929,\n      \"title\": \"fix(import): sync imported checkpoints once logged in\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1929\",\n      \"head\": \"9212599eb292128ce4efebc3d774a4eac9ad80ef\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/1773-sync-imported-checkpoints\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #1773 (fix 2 — sync after login). @karthik-rameshkumar handed this over on the issue after landing fix 1 (#1774).\\n\\n## The problem\\n\\n`entire import` writes read-only checkpoints and **creates no commit**, so the pre-push git hook — the only sync trigger — never fires for it. Because idempotency is keyed on *local* existence, history imported while logged out is stranded permanently: the post-login re-run reports `0 turn(s) (N already imported)` and makes no attempt to sync.\\n\\n## The insight that keeps this small\\n\\nThe git-refs store **already enqueues every checkpoint ref as it writes it** (`gitRefsStore.setRef` → `enqueueForPush`, `checkpoint/refs_store.go:209`), and nothing drains that q\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1920,\n      \"title\": \"test(checkpoint): failing repro for concurrent checkpoint-write lost update (#1917)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1920\",\n      \"head\": \"af59539f48227a0e91eaa31a34e2eaaf06dbb3df\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/concurrent-checkpoint-write-race\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Draft — **this PR is a reproduction, not a fix.** The concurrent subtests are\\nred on purpose, so CI will fail. It exists to make #1917 concrete and to pin\\ndown which scenario is actually reachable.\\n\\n## What it reproduces\\n\\nTwo agents working in one worktree, whose uncondensed work lands in a **single\\ncommit**, end up sharing **one** checkpoint: post-commit condenses both\\nsessions into it and records it in each session'\"'\"'s `TurnCheckpointIDs`. When\\nboth turns end, both Stop hooks run `finalizeAllTurnCheckpoints` over that same\\ncheckpoint.\\n\\nNothing serializes them:\\n\\n- each Stop hook holds only its own per-session flock — `stateLockPath` is\\n  keyed by session ID, and these are legitimately *differ\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1891,\n      \"title\": \"Fix Fish installer setup\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1891\",\n      \"head\": \"ed9c46b648bdcae2d7a6ae3dba0ce0bee2340b14\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/install-fish-support\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\n- detect the invoking shell before falling back to `$SHELL`\\n- use the Fish-native `fish_add_path` flow and preserve XDG-aware completion config\\n- run post-install actions on first-time installs and add installer regression coverage\\n- clarify that Fish users should still pipe the Bash installer to `bash`\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\nThe installer was Bash-only, but its Fish handoff relied solely on `$SHELL` and appended `fish_add_path` to a hard-coded `~/.config/fish/config.fish`. That could select the wrong shell, ignore `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`, leave the current Fish session without the new path, and skip post-install actions during the normal first install.\\n\\n## User impact\\n\\nFish users now receive\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1884,\n      \"title\": \"trail resume: finish the non-interactive contract\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1884\",\n      \"head\": \"5a1c663cf5fd49fa598e4fde8e631bcee24fa666\",\n      \"branch\": \"trail-resume\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/961\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n`entire trail resume` was designed interactive-first; for agent callers (the most common caller) the non-interactive path was never finished. This PR completes it without touching the core semantics — checkpoint discovery, restore, and interactive launch all stay as they are.\\n\\n**Breaking for scripts**: resume commands (`trail resume`, `session resume`, `checkpoint resume`) now exit non-zero whenever nothing was resumed; callers that relied on exit 0 in those cases must update. Interactive prompt declines still exit zero.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n**Never block, never need `--force` to comple\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1879,\n      \"title\": \"perf(codex): stop unmarshalling the whole rollout to compute token usage\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1879\",\n      \"head\": \"cc956ea9fddfbf88323e3ea29a35e02f2856b0c2\",\n      \"branch\": \"eric/staqpro-802-codex-token-prefilter\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #1836.\\n\\nPer @gtrrz-victor'\"'\"'s direction on the issue, this reevaluates the Codex token-usage path rather than porting Claude'\"'\"'s sli'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":10625}},"started_at_ms":1794842129412,"completed_at_ms":1794842129413}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:29.539Z","ordinal":3023,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-897b34af-f945-4ecd-9d0b-1ce4b163cb43","process_id":"47313","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' 'ce-first pattern. Scope held to Codex-only, token-usage calculation only, same numbers out.\\n\\n## Where the cost was\\n\\nNot the whole-file split — `splitJSONL`'\"'\"'s `bytes.Split`/`TrimSpace` return subslices and copy nothing. It'\"'\"'s `json.RawMessage.UnmarshalJSON`, which is `*m = append((*m)[0:0], data...)`: it **copies**. So every `response_item` line'\"'\"'s `encrypted_content` reasoning blob was scanned, validated and heap-copied on every hook, then thrown away unread. The old path measured ~280 MB/s — unmarshal-bound.\\n\\n`CalculateTokenUsage` needs three things from all th\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1859,\n      \"title\": \" fix(strategy): surface ambiguous-worktree warning to the user with a runnable remedy.\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1859\",\n      \"head\": \"4ff48cf3e753727c25dbde464721b034aab4b4ed\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/ambiguous-worktree-warning-visibility\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## What & why\\r\\n\\r\\n#1856 added `warnAmbiguousWorktreeSessions` for the #1852 case where live sessions span multiple worktrees, matching refuses to guess, and the commit is left unlinked. But it only logs to the internal `.entire/logs` file and prints no remedy — so the person running `git commit` still sees nothing. The \\\"silent\\\" part of #1852 is unchanged for them.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Change\\r\\n\\r\\nKeeps the structured `WARN` (diagnostics) and additionally writes a user-facing notice to `stderrWriter` — the same channel `warnIfAttributionDiverged` and `warnStaleEndedSessions` use — with a directly runnable remedy:\\r\\n\\r\\n    entire: this commit was not linked to a checkpoint (live agent sessions span multiple workt\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1826,\n      \"title\": \"test(hooks): cover ended→idle prepare-commit-msg (#411)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1826\",\n      \"head\": \"1f5f9eaad7da974446264fe278ca03fd4299f96d\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/411-ended-idle-prepare-commit\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/917\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- Adds an integration regression for [#411](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/411): `session-end` → `session-start` (ENDED→IDLE) → new turn → `git commit`.\\n- Confirms `prepare-commit-msg` still attaches `Entire-Checkpoint` on current `main` (natural repro does not fail).\\n\\n## Test plan\\n- [x] `go test -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/ -run TestIssue411_EndedToIdle_PrepareCommitMsgAddsTrailer`\\n\\n\\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1803,\n      \"title\": \"fix(codex): parse config.toml structurally for hook trust detection\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1803\",\n      \"head\": \"1b3f387bc0d8823ca2cea1d3edf0a8f6f2fde10e\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/codex-toml-trust-keys-1761\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes entireio/cli#1761\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nOn Windows, `entire doctor` reported every approved Codex hook as `REVIEW NEEDED`, and the SessionStart banner nagged about approvals that already existed. The trust check scraped the user'\"'\"'s `config.toml` with a regex that only matches **double-quoted** TOML state keys, while current Codex writes **single-quoted literal** keys — the natural serialization on Windows, where backslashes need no escaping:\\n\\n```toml\\n[hooks.state.'\"'\"'C:\\\\repo\\\\.codex\\\\hooks.json:session_start:0:0'\"'\"']\\ntrusted_hash = \\\"sha256:...\\\"\\n```\\n\\nAs the issue notes, even accepting double quotes wouldn'\"'\"'t be enough on Windows: a valid basic-string key carries escaped backslashes (`\\\"C:\\\\\\\\repo\\\\\\\\...\\\"`), an\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1801,\n      \"title\": \"fix(dispatch): surface merged work on feature branches with no own commits (ENT-1201)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1801\",\n      \"head\": \"f70b18a82b294ffee609d4ed53164070f22d2885\",\n      \"branch\": \"ent-1201-dispatch-empty\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/898\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\n`dispatch --local` returned an empty dispatch when run from a feature-branch\\r\\nworktree that has no commits of its own \\r\\n\\r\\nThe local engine scopes a non-default branch to <default>..HEAD to isolate the\\r\\nbranch'\"'\"'s own work. When the branch has no unique commits that range is empty,\\r\\nso the reachable-checkpoint-trailer set is empty and every merged checkpoint is\\r\\ndropped — \\\"no activity\\\" reported while HEAD is sitting on a full window of\\r\\nmerged work.\\r\\n\\r\\nENT-1188 already recognized this empty-range problem but patched it only for the\\r\\nliteral default branch, matched by name. The real \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1778,\n      \"title\": \"fix(hooks): install Entire into husky user hooks\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1778\",\n      \"head\": \"941eeea6270c864a03130b43c3f031232a95b41c\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/784-husky-mid-turn-trailer\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"**Trail:** https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/876\\n\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/876\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n**What:** Install Entire git hooks into husky'\"'\"'s user-hook directory (parent of `core.hooksPath=.husky/_`) instead of into regenerable `.husky/_`.\\n\\n**Why / how it helps:** `npm install` / `husky` prepare rewrites `.husky/_` mid-turn and previously removed Entire'\"'\"'s wrappers, so later commits in the same turn silently lost `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers (Fixes #784). User hooks under `.husky/` survive prepare, so mid-turn commits keep trailers without per-tool-hook recovery.\\n\\n**How:**\\n- When `core.hooksPath` is a husky `_` dir with \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1777,\n      \"title\": \"fix(session): auto-adopt across git common dirs on commit\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1777\",\n      \"head\": \"143885e02e85b318be43f8ead456f500533e30b1\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/1439-auto-adopt-cross-common-dir\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"**Trail:** [https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/875](<https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/875>)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nFixes entireio/cli#1439\\n\\n## What\\n\\nAuto-adopt a unique ACTIVE agent session from another git common dir during `prepare-commit-msg`, so commits in an enabled repo B get an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer when the live session state still lives under repo A.\\n\\n## Why / how it helps\\n\\nLong agent sessions often move across independently enabled repos. Hooks fire in B, but B'\"'\"'s `.git/entire-sessions` is empty, so the trailer is silently skipped even though Entire is installed. Manual `entire session adopt` (entireio/cli#1472) already exists; this wires a safe automatic path on commit.\\n\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1763,\n      \"title\": \"feat(cost): persist spend-time cost in checkpoints, sync pricing from entire-api (supersedes #1702)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1763\",\n      \"head\": \"e211d41d814a3f205a24612b8a32b768cf9bed6e\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/cli-cost-tokens-only\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"**Trail:** https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/865\\n\\n> **Draft — direction change pending team sign-off.** Reverses the round-2 decision that \\\"the CLI is the single source of truth\\\" for cost. Opening as a draft so it can be reviewed alongside #1702 before committing to the reversal. Pairs with entirehq/entire-api (platform computes cost).\\n\\n## What\\n\\nThe CLI stops **persisting** cost into checkpoint metadata. It keeps persisting the token facts the platform prices from (`model_usage` with all four token fields per model + model id, flat token counts, model, api-call counts). Cost is now shown only as a clearly-labeled **local estimate** in the token commands.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nPer team discussion (\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1727,\n      \"title\": \"fix(explain): find checkpoints merged into non-default target branches\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1727\",\n      \"head\": \"381b727b543ab0cd092ae6da9a0623ccb614a0d5\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/931-ff-merge-session-refs\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Trail: https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/834\\n\\nFixes #931.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nMerging a feature branch into a target branch dropped every session reference — checkpoint links and agent labels — from the target branch whenever the merge produced a merge commit and the target was not the repository'\"'\"'s default branch. `entire checkpoint list` and `entire checkpoint explain` showed nothing for the merged work on that branch.\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\n`getBranchCheckpoints` and `getAssociatedCommits` scan history for `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers. On every branch that is not the repository default, they used a **first-parent-only** walk. Checkpoints brought in by a merge live on the merge commit'\"'\"'s **second**\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1711,\n      \"title\": \"fix(gitrepo): tolerate negative fetch refspecs when opening repositories\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1711\",\n      \"head\": \"793f137ce1f546941d425b402ba3964d3a14ca95\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/778-negative-refspecs\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"**Trail:** https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/818\\n\\n**What:** Repository opening now tolerates git 2.29+ negative (exclusion) fetch refspecs (`fetch = ^refs/...`) in `.git/config`.\\n\\n**Why / how it helps:** go-git'\"'\"'s refspec parser rejects the `^` form, so **every** entire command (`enable`, `doctor`, hooks, …) failed on a repo that used negative refspecs: `metadata check failed: failed to open repository: … read config: malformed refspec, separators are wrong`. Negative refspecs are valid, supported git config (used to keep specific refs out of fetches), so the CLI should honor repos that use them. Fixes #778.\\n\\n**How:** A filesystem wrapper (`configSanitizeFS`, mirroring the existing `al\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1708,\n      \"title\": \"login: open the Windows browser under WSL, with device-flow fallback\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1708\",\n      \"head\": \"c33d86728aa19aee6320cc319698c49f2487fdee\",\n      \"branch\": \"wsl-windows-browser-login\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #1707. Makes `entire login` under WSL open the Windows browser (where users are already signed in) and recover when the OAuth redirect can'\"'\"'t reach WSL.\\n\\n- Open the Windows default browser under WSL (wslview, else cmd.exe) instead of a Linux WSLg browser\\n- Detect WSL from /proc/version, so detection survives hooks/services that strip WSL env vars\\n- On WSL, let the user fall back to device-code sign-in when the browser redirect can'\"'\"'t reach the loopback listener (extends the #1403 `loginFlowFacts` pattern with a `wsl` fact, mirroring its SSH fallback)\\n- Shared launcher, so `entire experts` also opens the Windows browser\\n- Non-WSL platforms unchanged; launcher selection and the fallback ra\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1704,\n      \"title\": \"test(strategy): prove dangling checkpoint trailer for IDLE + empty FilesTouched\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1704\",\n      \"head\": \"c511f36edd7af6990e5f7950d42551a90f50d365\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/idle-empty-filestouched-dangling-trailer\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## What\\n\\nAdds a **RED** regression test that reproduces and proves a silent `prepare-commit-msg` / `post-commit` mismatch: a commit can end up carrying an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer that points at a checkpoint **that was never materialized locally** (a *dangling trailer*).\\n\\nThis is a test-only, TDD-first PR — the test is **intentionally failing** and documents the invariant a follow-up fix must restore. CI will be red until the fix lands.\\n\\nNew file: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/phase_postcommit_dangling_trailer_test.go` → `TestPostCommit_IdleSession_NewLiveTranscriptEdits_DanglingTrailer`.\\n\\n## Scenario (reconstructed from a real Pi session)\\n\\n1. A session is condensed (clears `state.FilesTouched\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1698,\n      \"title\": \"Support plugin-style hook payloads for Codex and Claude Code\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1698\",\n      \"head\": \"5b0a0ce895f4e1dd7d266c6ff9bb9ebd46167655\",\n      \"branch\": \"feature/plugin-hook-payload-compat\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n- Accept plugin-style camelCase hook payload fields for Codex and Claude Code lifecycle hooks (`sessionId`, `transcriptPath`, `hookEventName`, etc.).\\n- Add shared hook payload compatibility helpers for snake_case/camelCase field extraction, RFC3339/epoch-millis timestamps, and hook event validation.\\n- Document VS Code/plugin compatibility boundaries and the Desktop limitation when no hook or transcript export exists.\\n\\n## Behavior\\n- Existing native CLI hook payloads continue to work unchanged.\\n- VS Code/plugin-style hosts work when they invoke compatible `entire hooks ...` commands or provide standard transcript paths.\\n- This does not add Desktop live capture for hosts that do not \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1696,\n      \"title\": \"Trail branch update support\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1696\",\n      \"head\": \"78ade6db4d078700b9c080ae2f470bb5d93f040d\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/trail-update-branch\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/787\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.io) after CI was requested for the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1687,\n      \"title\": \"Support updating trails by number\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1687\",\n      \"head\": \"645f0060ecac056d1e390288e9cd5cec2c2385ca\",\n      \"branch\": \"branchless-trails-updating\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n- add `entire trail update --number` for branchless trails\\n- fetch trail details by number before patching metadata and labels\\n- keep branch-based update behavior unchanged\\n\\n## Tests\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli`\\n- `mise run lint`\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> CLI-only extension of an existing update command; branch-based updates are unchanged and the change is covered by new tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **`entire trail update`** can target a trail by **`--number`** (in addition to **`--branch`** / current branch), so branchless trails can be updated without a branch lookup.\\n> \\n> When **`--number`** is set, the command loads the trail via a **GET** on the p\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1686,\n      \"title\": \"Add worktree checkout for trails\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1686\",\n      \"head\": \"c32690ebc07ce1feb8489b5358d9f29b884f0849\",\n      \"branch\": \"peter/trail-checkout-worktree\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n- add `entire trail checkout --worktree` to create/reuse repo-local worktrees under `.entire/worktrees`\\n- print a shell-safe `cd` hint for the worktree path\\n- add local `.git/info/exclude` entry for `.entire/worktrees/` to avoid dirtying tracked `.gitignore`\\n\\n## Testing\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run '\"'\"'TrailCheckout|TestResolveTrailBySelector|TestDescribeTrailRef'\"'\"'`\\n- `mise run lint`\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> The command runs `git worktree`/`fetch` and writes to `.git/info/exclude`, which affects local git state; scope is limited to trail checkout and is covered by integration tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **`entire trail checkout --worktree`** \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1647,\n      \"title\": \"feat(review): exact scope and parallel skills for reviewer agents\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1647\",\n      \"head\": \"818eb75910beada4d35c7ff6f237f05eac373c74\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/review-child-context\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/766\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## One-sentence summary\\n\\nWhen `entire review` launches a reviewer, it now hands that reviewer everything the CLI already knows — exactly which code to review, how long it may run, which tools it may use, and how to start its configured skill — instead of a vague instruction each reviewer had to interpret for itself.\\n\\n## Problems, as observed in real runs\\n\\n1. **Reviewers re-derived — and sometimes got wrong — what code to review.** The composed prompt only said *\\\"review the commits unique to this branch vs origin/HEAD.\\\"* Each reviewer then ran its own git commands to work out what tha\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1643,\n      \"title\": \"Use native git CLI for worktree status on hook hot paths (45.9s -> 193ms on large worktrees)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1643\",\n      \"head\": \"76150b0390bab4a72aa1a06c17cc8526f9ab0e27\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/native-git-status-hot-paths\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\nFixes #1642 — on worktrees with large gitignored trees, the Claude Code `user-prompt-submit` hook takes 40–55s per prompt and every turn-end checkpoint pays the same cost again. Root cause: three hot paths still used go-git'\"'\"'s `worktree.Status()`, which stats and hashes every file on disk including gitignored directories. Several sibling call sites had already been converted to the native git CLI for exactly this reason (see the existing comments in `checkpoint/ephemeral.go` and `getStagedFiles` in `strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go`); this PR finishes the job.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- **`strategy/common.go`**: new exported `GitCLIStatus(ctx)` helper — runs `git status --porcelain=v1 -z -uall\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1639,\n      \"title\": \"test: git-remote coverage (4/4) — OPF pre-push, degraded remotes, shallow/partial clones, e2e\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1639\",\n      \"head\": \"2182fe09c3f0170a6086ee38424d57756a77d772\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/git-remote-test-coverage\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/760\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nPart 4 (final) of the stack on #1638. First integration-level coverage for t'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' 'ce-first pattern. Scope held to Codex-only, token-usage calculation only, same numbers out.\\n\\n## Where the cost was\\n\\nNot the whole-file split — `splitJSONL`'\"'\"'s `bytes.Split`/`TrimSpace` return subslices and copy nothing. It'\"'\"'s `json.RawMessage.UnmarshalJSON`, which is `*m = append((*m)[0:0], data...)`: it **copies**. So every `response_item` line'\"'\"'s `encrypted_content` reasoning blob was scanned, validated and heap-copied on every hook, then thrown away unread. The old path measured ~280 MB/s — unmarshal-bound.\\n\\n`CalculateTokenUsage` needs three things from all th\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1859,\n      \"title\": \" fix(strategy): surface ambiguous-worktree warning to the user with a runnable remedy.\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1859\",\n      \"head\": \"4ff48cf3e753727c25dbde464721b034aab4b4ed\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/ambiguous-worktree-warning-visibility\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## What & why\\r\\n\\r\\n#1856 added `warnAmbiguousWorktreeSessions` for the #1852 case where live sessions span multiple worktrees, matching refuses to guess, and the commit is left unlinked. But it only logs to the internal `.entire/logs` file and prints no remedy — so the person running `git commit` still sees nothing. The \\\"silent\\\" part of #1852 is unchanged for them.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Change\\r\\n\\r\\nKeeps the structured `WARN` (diagnostics) and additionally writes a user-facing notice to `stderrWriter` — the same channel `warnIfAttributionDiverged` and `warnStaleEndedSessions` use — with a directly runnable remedy:\\r\\n\\r\\n    entire: this commit was not linked to a checkpoint (live agent sessions span multiple workt\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1826,\n      \"title\": \"test(hooks): cover ended→idle prepare-commit-msg (#411)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1826\",\n      \"head\": \"1f5f9eaad7da974446264fe278ca03fd4299f96d\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/411-ended-idle-prepare-commit\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/917\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- Adds an integration regression for [#411](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/411): `session-end` → `session-start` (ENDED→IDLE) → new turn → `git commit`.\\n- Confirms `prepare-commit-msg` still attaches `Entire-Checkpoint` on current `main` (natural repro does not fail).\\n\\n## Test plan\\n- [x] `go test -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/ -run TestIssue411_EndedToIdle_PrepareCommitMsgAddsTrailer`\\n\\n\\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1803,\n      \"title\": \"fix(codex): parse config.toml structurally for hook trust detection\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1803\",\n      \"head\": \"1b3f387bc0d8823ca2cea1d3edf0a8f6f2fde10e\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/codex-toml-trust-keys-1761\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes entireio/cli#1761\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nOn Windows, `entire doctor` reported every approved Codex hook as `REVIEW NEEDED`, and the SessionStart banner nagged about approvals that already existed. The trust check scraped the user'\"'\"'s `config.toml` with a regex that only matches **double-quoted** TOML state keys, while current Codex writes **single-quoted literal** keys — the natural serialization on Windows, where backslashes need no escaping:\\n\\n```toml\\n[hooks.state.'\"'\"'C:\\\\repo\\\\.codex\\\\hooks.json:session_start:0:0'\"'\"']\\ntrusted_hash = \\\"sha256:...\\\"\\n```\\n\\nAs the issue notes, even accepting double quotes wouldn'\"'\"'t be enough on Windows: a valid basic-string key carries escaped backslashes (`\\\"C:\\\\\\\\repo\\\\\\\\...\\\"`), an\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1801,\n      \"title\": \"fix(dispatch): surface merged work on feature branches with no own commits (ENT-1201)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1801\",\n      \"head\": \"f70b18a82b294ffee609d4ed53164070f22d2885\",\n      \"branch\": \"ent-1201-dispatch-empty\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/898\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\n`dispatch --local` returned an empty dispatch when run from a feature-branch\\r\\nworktree that has no commits of its own \\r\\n\\r\\nThe local engine scopes a non-default branch to <default>..HEAD to isolate the\\r\\nbranch'\"'\"'s own work. When the branch has no unique commits that range is empty,\\r\\nso the reachable-checkpoint-trailer set is empty and every merged checkpoint is\\r\\ndropped — \\\"no activity\\\" reported while HEAD is sitting on a full window of\\r\\nmerged work.\\r\\n\\r\\nENT-1188 already recognized this empty-range problem but patched it only for the\\r\\nliteral default branch, matched by name. The real \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1778,\n      \"title\": \"fix(hooks): install Entire into husky user hooks\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1778\",\n      \"head\": \"941eeea6270c864a03130b43c3f031232a95b41c\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/784-husky-mid-turn-trailer\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"**Trail:** https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/876\\n\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/876\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n**What:** Install Entire git hooks into husky'\"'\"'s user-hook directory (parent of `core.hooksPath=.husky/_`) instead of into regenerable `.husky/_`.\\n\\n**Why / how it helps:** `npm install` / `husky` prepare rewrites `.husky/_` mid-turn and previously removed Entire'\"'\"'s wrappers, so later commits in the same turn silently lost `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers (Fixes #784). User hooks under `.husky/` survive prepare, so mid-turn commits keep trailers without per-tool-hook recovery.\\n\\n**How:**\\n- When `core.hooksPath` is a husky `_` dir with \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1777,\n      \"title\": \"fix(session): auto-adopt across git common dirs on commit\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1777\",\n      \"head\": \"143885e02e85b318be43f8ead456f500533e30b1\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/1439-auto-adopt-cross-common-dir\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"**Trail:** [https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/875](<https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/875>)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nFixes entireio/cli#1439\\n\\n## What\\n\\nAuto-adopt a unique ACTIVE agent session from another git common dir during `prepare-commit-msg`, so commits in an enabled repo B get an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer when the live session state still lives under repo A.\\n\\n## Why / how it helps\\n\\nLong agent sessions often move across independently enabled repos. Hooks fire in B, but B'\"'\"'s `.git/entire-sessions` is empty, so the trailer is silently skipped even though Entire is installed. Manual `entire session adopt` (entireio/cli#1472) already exists; this wires a safe automatic path on commit.\\n\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1763,\n      \"title\": \"feat(cost): persist spend-time cost in checkpoints, sync pricing from entire-api (supersedes #1702)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1763\",\n      \"head\": \"e211d41d814a3f205a24612b8a32b768cf9bed6e\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/cli-cost-tokens-only\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"**Trail:** https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/865\\n\\n> **Draft — direction change pending team sign-off.** Reverses the round-2 decision that \\\"the CLI is the single source of truth\\\" for cost. Opening as a draft so it can be reviewed alongside #1702 before committing to the reversal. Pairs with entirehq/entire-api (platform computes cost).\\n\\n## What\\n\\nThe CLI stops **persisting** cost into checkpoint metadata. It keeps persisting the token facts the platform prices from (`model_usage` with all four token fields per model + model id, flat token counts, model, api-call counts). Cost is now shown only as a clearly-labeled **local estimate** in the token commands.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nPer team discussion (\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1727,\n      \"title\": \"fix(explain): find checkpoints merged into non-default target branches\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1727\",\n      \"head\": \"381b727b543ab0cd092ae6da9a0623ccb614a0d5\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/931-ff-merge-session-refs\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Trail: https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/834\\n\\nFixes #931.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nMerging a feature branch into a target branch dropped every session reference — checkpoint links and agent labels — from the target branch whenever the merge produced a merge commit and the target was not the repository'\"'\"'s default branch. `entire checkpoint list` and `entire checkpoint explain` showed nothing for the merged work on that branch.\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\n`getBranchCheckpoints` and `getAssociatedCommits` scan history for `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers. On every branch that is not the repository default, they used a **first-parent-only** walk. Checkpoints brought in by a merge live on the merge commit'\"'\"'s **second**\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1711,\n      \"title\": \"fix(gitrepo): tolerate negative fetch refspecs when opening repositories\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1711\",\n      \"head\": \"793f137ce1f546941d425b402ba3964d3a14ca95\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/778-negative-refspecs\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"**Trail:** https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/818\\n\\n**What:** Repository opening now tolerates git 2.29+ negative (exclusion) fetch refspecs (`fetch = ^refs/...`) in `.git/config`.\\n\\n**Why / how it helps:** go-git'\"'\"'s refspec parser rejects the `^` form, so **every** entire command (`enable`, `doctor`, hooks, …) failed on a repo that used negative refspecs: `metadata check failed: failed to open repository: … read config: malformed refspec, separators are wrong`. Negative refspecs are valid, supported git config (used to keep specific refs out of fetches), so the CLI should honor repos that use them. Fixes #778.\\n\\n**How:** A filesystem wrapper (`configSanitizeFS`, mirroring the existing `al\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1708,\n      \"title\": \"login: open the Windows browser under WSL, with device-flow fallback\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1708\",\n      \"head\": \"c33d86728aa19aee6320cc319698c49f2487fdee\",\n      \"branch\": \"wsl-windows-browser-login\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #1707. Makes `entire login` under WSL open the Windows browser (where users are already signed in) and recover when the OAuth redirect can'\"'\"'t reach WSL.\\n\\n- Open the Windows default browser under WSL (wslview, else cmd.exe) instead of a Linux WSLg browser\\n- Detect WSL from /proc/version, so detection survives hooks/services that strip WSL env vars\\n- On WSL, let the user fall back to device-code sign-in when the browser redirect can'\"'\"'t reach the loopback listener (extends the #1403 `loginFlowFacts` pattern with a `wsl` fact, mirroring its SSH fallback)\\n- Shared launcher, so `entire experts` also opens the Windows browser\\n- Non-WSL platforms unchanged; launcher selection and the fallback ra\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1704,\n      \"title\": \"test(strategy): prove dangling checkpoint trailer for IDLE + empty FilesTouched\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1704\",\n      \"head\": \"c511f36edd7af6990e5f7950d42551a90f50d365\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/idle-empty-filestouched-dangling-trailer\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## What\\n\\nAdds a **RED** regression test that reproduces and proves a silent `prepare-commit-msg` / `post-commit` mismatch: a commit can end up carrying an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer that points at a checkpoint **that was never materialized locally** (a *dangling trailer*).\\n\\nThis is a test-only, TDD-first PR — the test is **intentionally failing** and documents the invariant a follow-up fix must restore. CI will be red until the fix lands.\\n\\nNew file: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/phase_postcommit_dangling_trailer_test.go` → `TestPostCommit_IdleSession_NewLiveTranscriptEdits_DanglingTrailer`.\\n\\n## Scenario (reconstructed from a real Pi session)\\n\\n1. A session is condensed (clears `state.FilesTouched\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1698,\n      \"title\": \"Support plugin-style hook payloads for Codex and Claude Code\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1698\",\n      \"head\": \"5b0a0ce895f4e1dd7d266c6ff9bb9ebd46167655\",\n      \"branch\": \"feature/plugin-hook-payload-compat\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n- Accept plugin-style camelCase hook payload fields for Codex and Claude Code lifecycle hooks (`sessionId`, `transcriptPath`, `hookEventName`, etc.).\\n- Add shared hook payload compatibility helpers for snake_case/camelCase field extraction, RFC3339/epoch-millis timestamps, and hook event validation.\\n- Document VS Code/plugin compatibility boundaries and the Desktop limitation when no hook or transcript export exists.\\n\\n## Behavior\\n- Existing native CLI hook payloads continue to work unchanged.\\n- VS Code/plugin-style hosts work when they invoke compatible `entire hooks ...` commands or provide standard transcript paths.\\n- This does not add Desktop live capture for hosts that do not \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1696,\n      \"title\": \"Trail branch update support\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1696\",\n      \"head\": \"78ade6db4d078700b9c080ae2f470bb5d93f040d\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/trail-update-branch\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/787\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.io) after CI was requested for the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1687,\n      \"title\": \"Support updating trails by number\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1687\",\n      \"head\": \"645f0060ecac056d1e390288e9cd5cec2c2385ca\",\n      \"branch\": \"branchless-trails-updating\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n- add `entire trail update --number` for branchless trails\\n- fetch trail details by number before patching metadata and labels\\n- keep branch-based update behavior unchanged\\n\\n## Tests\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli`\\n- `mise run lint`\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> CLI-only extension of an existing update command; branch-based updates are unchanged and the change is covered by new tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **`entire trail update`** can target a trail by **`--number`** (in addition to **`--branch`** / current branch), so branchless trails can be updated without a branch lookup.\\n> \\n> When **`--number`** is set, the command loads the trail via a **GET** on the p\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1686,\n      \"title\": \"Add worktree checkout for trails\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1686\",\n      \"head\": \"c32690ebc07ce1feb8489b5358d9f29b884f0849\",\n      \"branch\": \"peter/trail-checkout-worktree\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n- add `entire trail checkout --worktree` to create/reuse repo-local worktrees under `.entire/worktrees`\\n- print a shell-safe `cd` hint for the worktree path\\n- add local `.git/info/exclude` entry for `.entire/worktrees/` to avoid dirtying tracked `.gitignore`\\n\\n## Testing\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run '\"'\"'TrailCheckout|TestResolveTrailBySelector|TestDescribeTrailRef'\"'\"'`\\n- `mise run lint`\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> The command runs `git worktree`/`fetch` and writes to `.git/info/exclude`, which affects local git state; scope is limited to trail checkout and is covered by integration tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **`entire trail checkout --worktree`** \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1647,\n      \"title\": \"feat(review): exact scope and parallel skills for reviewer agents\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1647\",\n      \"head\": \"818eb75910beada4d35c7ff6f237f05eac373c74\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/review-child-context\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/766\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## One-sentence summary\\n\\nWhen `entire review` launches a reviewer, it now hands that reviewer everything the CLI already knows — exactly which code to review, how long it may run, which tools it may use, and how to start its configured skill — instead of a vague instruction each reviewer had to interpret for itself.\\n\\n## Problems, as observed in real runs\\n\\n1. **Reviewers re-derived — and sometimes got wrong — what code to review.** The composed prompt only said *\\\"review the commits unique to this branch vs origin/HEAD.\\\"* Each reviewer then ran its own git commands to work out what tha\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1643,\n      \"title\": \"Use native git CLI for worktree status on hook hot paths (45.9s -> 193ms on large worktrees)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1643\",\n      \"head\": \"76150b0390bab4a72aa1a06c17cc8526f9ab0e27\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/native-git-status-hot-paths\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\nFixes #1642 — on worktrees with large gitignored trees, the Claude Code `user-prompt-submit` hook takes 40–55s per prompt and every turn-end checkpoint pays the same cost again. Root cause: three hot paths still used go-git'\"'\"'s `worktree.Status()`, which stats and hashes every file on disk including gitignored directories. Several sibling call sites had already been converted to the native git CLI for exactly this reason (see the existing comments in `checkpoint/ephemeral.go` and `getStagedFiles` in `strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go`); this PR finishes the job.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- **`strategy/common.go`**: new exported `GitCLIStatus(ctx)` helper — runs `git status --porcelain=v1 -z -uall\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1639,\n      \"title\": \"test: git-remote coverage (4/4) — OPF pre-push, degraded remotes, shallow/partial clones, e2e\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1639\",\n      \"head\": \"2182fe09c3f0170a6086ee38424d57756a77d772\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/git-remote-test-coverage\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/760\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nPart 4 (final) of the stack on #1638. First integration-level coverage for t'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":10416}},"started_at_ms":1794842129538,"completed_at_ms":1794842129539}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:29.681Z","ordinal":3024,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-634bb8c7-53ee-4926-931f-fce36825fe72","process_id":"2757","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' 'he OPF pre-push rewrite, degraded-remote/protocol edges, shallow and partial user clones, and the two remaining e2e scenarios.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- **E-group (OPF over a real remote, git-branch)**: happy path via real hook — remote v1 tip carries `Entire-OPF-Applied: true` with the OPF binary invocation proven via a fake `opf` script seam (the in-process runtime seam can'\"'\"'t cross the hook process boundary; content-level redaction stays unit-covered); diverged v1 → `V1DivergedError` aborts the user push; CAS `V1RefMove\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1638,\n      \"title\": \"test: git-remote coverage (3/4) — divergence & recovery matrix\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1638\",\n      \"head\": \"56408fafa3f21180363937cf3bb69e6989ce0358\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/git-remote-tests-3-divergence\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/759\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nPart 3 of the stack on #1637. Systematizes the historically most re-broken area (#953, #1251, #1252, #1260: destructive local-v1-ref moves) into an explicit matrix, and covers the git-refs equivalents that only had unit coverage.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- **D1 (git-branch)**: table-driven matrix — local v1 {ahead, behind, diverged, disconnected} × {pre-push (real hook), explain fetch-on-miss, doctor}: local-only commits always survive, behind→FF, diverged→both sides preserved with linear tip (double-replay guard), repeated pre-push leaves the remote byte-identical. Cells already covered by `safel\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1637,\n      \"title\": \"test: git-remote coverage (2/4) — real-hook P0 tests, cross-machine fetch, explain fix\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1637\",\n      \"head\": \"a9b0334c49a63253cd67d994fa72d9cef2ed1c3d\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/git-remote-tests-2-p0\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/758\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nPart 2 of the stack on #1636. The P0 test groups from the plan, plus two fixes they surfaced.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- **A-group (real pre-push hook, both backends)**: plain-push checkpoint sync with user-push assertions (A1), no-new-checkpoints no-op via remote digest (A2), branch-delete and tag-only pushes through the hook (A3), unreachable checkpoint target degrades gracefully under the real hook (A4), git-refs queue drain via real push (A6 slice).\\n- **C-group (cross-machine clone flows)**: production `fetchMetadataBranchIfMissing` exercised for real over HTTPS (C1 — previous clone tests subs\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1633,\n      \"title\": \"feat(ticket): entire ticket — link external tickets to branches, checkpoints & reviews\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1633\",\n      \"head\": \"80477c315284130a410acff455f768e35bb29a5a\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/entire-ticket\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Overview\\n\\n`entire ticket` links an external tracker ticket (Linear today, Jira-ready) to a branch and session, so work stays grounded in its original intent — and freezes that ticket into checkpoint provenance so the checkpoint chain becomes the ticket'\"'\"'s timeline, surfaced across `status`, `session info`, `explain`, and `review`.\\n\\nThe command group is platform-agnostic: every tracker implements one `Provider` interface and registers with a single `switch` case, so adding Jira later never touches the command surface.\\n\\n## What'\"'\"'s in it\\n\\n- **Commands:** `entire ticket setup` (store platform + team + API token in the OS keychain), `link` / `unlink`, `start` (ticket → new branch + grounding pro\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1628,\n      \"title\": \"Add hidden `doctor rewrite-checkpoints` test tooling (git-branch → git-refs)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1628\",\n      \"head\": \"b24e3ba909d620ff8f988393aaae89f4bc5b97d0\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/checkpoint-rewrite\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/752\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nHidden test tooling for evaluating the **git-refs** checkpoint store against real branch data: it re-materializes every checkpoint on the `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch as a per-checkpoint ref by re-driving the git-refs store'\"'\"'s write path. Independent of the (still-undecided) byte-identical migration — standalone off `main`.\\n\\n## What it does\\n`entire doctor rewrite-checkpoints` (hidden). For each checkpoint on the v1 branch:\\n- Replays each session'\"'\"'s transcript through `Write`, so the compact `transcript.jsonl` is **regenerated**, the tree is **rooted at the checkpoint** (no shard fold\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1613,\n      \"title\": \"fix(attribution): deterministic why metadata + interactive viewer + honest tag legend\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1613\",\n      \"head\": \"2534f41f77a0c4ccf66a816e743a61d99e10129e\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-why-metadata-consistency\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"**Trail:** https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/737\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## What\\r\\n\\r\\n`entire why <file>[:<line>]` could show three different answers on three equivalent clones of the same repo at the same commit — full metadata on one, partial on another, bare `CheckpointID` on a third. This makes the resolution deterministic: given the same remote state, every clone converges on the same output, and when it can'\"'\"'t, the miss reason says exactly why and how to recover.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Root cause (what remained after #1535 / `4f435384d`)\\r\\n\\r\\nEarlier work already added `MetadataMissingReason`, file-level enrichment, and the fetch suggestion. Two residual defects kept the issue alive:\\r\\n\\r\\n1. **The partial-blob divergence\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1579,\n      \"title\": \"fix(enable): detect Codex during agent setup\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1579\",\n      \"head\": \"be7c0235a1aa300cd27210d22dcffc2f0bff6923\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-enable-detect-multiple-agents\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Detect Codex from repository-level .codex configuration instead of requiring Entire hooks to already be installed.\\r\\n    \\r\\nKeep the existing multiple-agent enable flow intact: when Claude Code and Codex are both configured, enable reports multiple detected agents and reaches the multi-select path instead of auto-selecting Claude Code via the single-agent shortcut.\\r\\n    \\r\\nAdd regression coverage for Claude Code plus Codex detection.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1547,\n      \"title\": \"resume: refresh stale logs, fetch remote checkpoints, show progress\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1547\",\n      \"head\": \"9a2b3b58a443b6e60938c6724b4a470954ac5c94\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/resume-improve\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/679\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\nImprove entire resume so it reflects the latest session state and never silently loses local work:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRefresh on checkpoint-newer when the checkpoint cleanly extends the local log (local is a prefix).\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDivergence guard: a newer checkpoint timestamp alone no longer authorizes overwrite; if the local log holds entries the checkpoint lacks (or is strictly newer), prompt and keep when non-interactive. --force still overwrites.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFetch the checkpoint metadata branch from the remote before reading, so a remotely-updated checkpoint is picked up even when its ID resolv\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1536,\n      \"title\": \"Support colon line syntax for trail findings\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1536\",\n      \"head\": \"a07101962e7cd75cc201c822b11807d0090672e1\",\n      \"branch\": \"codex/trail-finding-colon-line\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/674\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- Let `entire trail finding add --file` accept `path:line` and `path:start-end` location syntax.\\n- Keep `--line`, `--start-line`, and `--end-line` as compatibility aliases.\\n- Update the trail finding dashboard action hint to use the colon form.\\n\\n## Why\\nThe rest of the CLI generally represents source locations as `file:line` or `file:start-end`; `trail finding add --file path --line 42` was an outlier.\\n\\n## Validation\\n- `mise run check`\\n- `mise run lint`\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1493,\n      \"title\": \"feat(trail): update body/metadata by number, id, or branch (incl. branchless)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1493\",\n      \"head\": \"87d359d1c47fb0f4ec088e3422e9c334f5c08a85\",\n      \"branch\": \"paxos/cli-trail-body-write\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/637\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nTL;DR — Makes `entire trail update` address **any** trail by number, id, or branch — including **branchless** trails — so their **body *and* metadata** (status/title/labels) become editable from the CLI, plus file/stdin body input. CLI-only, no API changes. Stacked on #1476 (the body-*read* PR).\\n\\n## Problem\\n`entire trail update` was `NoArgs` + `--branch`-only, so a branchless trail (no branch) could not be targeted at all — neither its body nor its metadata was editable from the CLI. `show`/`checkout`/`delete` already resolve trails by number/id/branch; `update` did not.\\n\\n## What cha\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1479,\n      \"title\": \"feat(claude-code): add opt-in trail status line\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1479\",\n      \"head\": \"345fce6c3d36135c7e6d0a58af01dd404df775ee\",\n      \"branch\": \"cli-claude-statusline\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/621\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nShips the Entire trail status line for Claude Code as a native CLI feature, replacing the standalone Pi `entire-trail-statusline.mjs` script. When the current branch has an Entire trail, Claude Code'\"'\"'s status bar shows a clickable, cyan **`Trail #N <status>`** OSC-8 hyperlink to the trail on entire.io.\\n\\nIt'\"'\"'s **opt-in** and **no Node dependency** — it reuses the CLI'\"'\"'s own trail/auth/git internals.\\n\\n## How a user activates it\\n\\n```bash\\nentire enable --agent claude-code --claude-statusline\\n```\\n\\nThis writes a `statusLine` block into `.claude/settings.json` pointing at `entire h\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1462,\n      \"title\": \"Add `entire trail merge` subcommand\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1462\",\n      \"head\": \"0b76faf4c4d51894c9aac7cdb5bd886e0f67575f\",\n      \"branch\": \"cli-trail-merge\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/604\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAdds an `entire trail merge` subcommand that merges a trail'\"'\"'s branch into its base, after first checking the trail is mergeable. A `--dry-run` flag reports mergeability without performing the merge.\\n\\nThe Entire API already exposes the needed endpoints (`GET .../{number}/mergeability` and `POST .../{number}/merge`); this wires the CLI up to them.\\n\\n## Behavior\\n\\n- Resolves the trail from `--trail` (number, id, or branch), or the current branch'\"'\"'s trail when omitted.\\n- **Always checks mergeability first** and prints a readiness summary (approvals, CI checks, up-to-date with ba\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1459,\n      \"title\": \"feat(copilot): capture Copilot sessions from VS Code agent hooks (Preview)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1459\",\n      \"head\": \"91ddd5cbb9fdeaae1108f7e764204d9ff810099e\",\n      \"branch\": \"copilot-vscode-hooks\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/601\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\n## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nAdds capture support for GitHub Copilot sessions driven from **VS Code'\"'\"'s agent hooks (Preview)**, on top of the existing Copilot CLI support.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Why a separate hook file\\r\\n\\r\\nVS Code auto-discovers `.github/hooks/*.json` and reads Copilot CLI configs by converting lowerCamelCase event names to PascalCase (`userPromptSubmitted` → `UserPromptSubmitted`, `agentStop` → `AgentStop`). Those converted names are **not** real VS Code events, so the capture-critical turn hooks never fire from `entire.json` inside VS Code.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe events whose converted names *do* line up with\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1444,\n      \"title\": \"trail finding: populate selected_text for line/range findings\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1444\",\n      \"head\": \"7335c7df5f3ddffec210b398a06e0ce1de4c8075\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/trail-finding-selected-text\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/580/trail-finding-populate-selected-text-for-line-range-findings\\r\\n\\r\\n## Problem\\r\\n\\r\\n`entire trail finding add --line` / `--start-line` always failed against the control plane with:\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\nlocation.granularity=line requires non-empty selected_text\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nThe CLI built a `line`/`range` location but **never set `selected_text`**, and there was no flag to supply it (`TrailReviewLocationCreateRequest.SelectedText` existed but nothing ever assigned it). The server requires it for line/range granularity (`validateLocationShape` in the BFF). Only `--file` (which maps to `file` granularity, no `selected_text` requirement) worked — so line-anchored findings wer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1396,\n      \"title\": \"[bug]Restore native Windows interactive prompts\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1396\",\n      \"head\": \"53fdb57dda190ec5ba6547495f63a180e2b91d04\",\n      \"branch\": \"stale2000/windows-interactive-prompts\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Entire Logs: https://entire.io/gh/stale2000/cli/session/019eaad9-6a88-78a0-94c4-0fe99696aefa\\r\\n\\r\\n## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nThis fixes native Windows interactive prompt detection. The CLI previously treated Windows terminals as non-interactive because `interactive.CanPromptInteractively()` always tried to open `/dev/tty`, which only exists on Unix-like systems. `login.waitForEnter()` and the commit-link prompt path also depended on the same Unix terminal assumption.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Bug and impact\\r\\n\\r\\nOn native Windows, `/dev/tty` does not exist. That meant `CanPromptInteractively()` returned `false` even when a real user was running Entire from an interactive PowerShell, Command Prompt, or Windows Terminal session.\\r\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1394,\n      \"title\": \"[bug]Preserve Claude subagent token totals during condensation\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1394\",\n      \"head\": \"3a0722365045eef00aa0707e291cfdd24c18382b\",\n      \"branch\": \"stale2000/condense-subagent-tokens\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Entire Logs: https://entire.io/gh/stale2000/cli/session/019eaa64-5270-74c0-9f8a-e4df88c7014e\\r\\nSUMMARY:\\r\\nAfter finding and making the fix, I noticed the log saying that the \\\"bug\\\" might be intentional?  Or it is unknown why it is written this way?  \\r\\n\\r\\nI did an analysis as for why it might have been written this way and got the following response that implies that its indeed a bug, and the previous implementation didn'\"'\"'t know how to solve it.  But this PR does fix the issue.  \\r\\n\\r\\nExplanation/response to the TODO statement:\\r\\n\\\"\\r\\nSo the nuanced answer is:\\r\\n\\r\\nFor live transcript condensation: bug.\\r\\nFor shadow-only fallback with no live path: empty dir may be unavoidable.\\r\\nThe TODO was probably some\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1388,\n      \"title\": \"test: pin down Cursor token-usage condensation gap (stacked on #1263)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1388\",\n      \"head\": \"0ac052e1363bfbb5be21c17019959124c033e374\",\n      \"branch\": \"sh/cursor-token-condensation-gap-test\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Stacked on #1263 (draft)\\n\\nThis PR stacks **two integration tests** on top of @SnowingFox'\"'\"'s #1263 to pin down a gap in the Cursor token-usage work. **No production code changes** — it adds one test file. Base is `cursor-pr-1263-base` (a mirror of #1263'\"'\"'s head) so the diff shows only the new tests; once #1263 merges this can be retargeted to `main`.\\n\\nThese tests are **expected to fail** on #1263 as written — they'\"'\"'re the acceptance criteria for the fix.\\n\\n### The gap\\n\\n#1263 correctly threads the Cursor `stop` hook'\"'\"'s token usage into **live session state** (so `entire status` shows it). But at commit time, condensation recomputes `TokenUsage` from the transcript (`manual_commit_condensation.go\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1386,\n      \"title\": \"Fix: Keep Entire pre-push alive after Lefthook reinstalls hooks\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1386\",\n      \"head\": \"fa3b7b936ad12660eb8948ef0ea222cbb96fbd34\",\n      \"branch\": \"codex/issue-1349-lefthook-safety-net\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/stale2000/cli/session/019ea5bb-9549-7083-b95f-7ecb498cbc24 \\r\\n\\r\\nCloses #1349.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis keeps Entire'\"'\"'s existing Git hook ownership behavior unchanged while adding a Lefthook-local safety net for the failure mode reported in the issue.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhen a repository has a YAML Lefthook config, `entire enable` still installs the normal Entire `.git/hooks/pre-push` wrapper. It now also ensures `lefthook-local.yml` contains an `entire-push-sessions` pre-push command that only runs if Lefthook has reclaimed `.git/hooks/pre-push` and removed the `Entire CLI hooks` marker.\\r\\n\\r\\nNormal state:\\r\\n- Git runs Entire'\"'\"'s `pre-push` wrapper.\\r\\n- Entire chains to Lefthook.\\r\\n- The Lefthook-l\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1235,\n      \"title\": \"Harden opencode session dir, copyFile streaming, FetchBlobs argv batching\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1235\",\n      \"head\": \"3ef968c618c01f6bbbcb5852598fa9f48c2c805d\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/cli-hardening\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/400\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThree independent hardening fixes carried forward fro'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' 'he OPF pre-push rewrite, degraded-remote/protocol edges, shallow and partial user clones, and the two remaining e2e scenarios.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- **E-group (OPF over a real remote, git-branch)**: happy path via real hook — remote v1 tip carries `Entire-OPF-Applied: true` with the OPF binary invocation proven via a fake `opf` script seam (the in-process runtime seam can'\"'\"'t cross the hook process boundary; content-level redaction stays unit-covered); diverged v1 → `V1DivergedError` aborts the user push; CAS `V1RefMove\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1638,\n      \"title\": \"test: git-remote coverage (3/4) — divergence & recovery matrix\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1638\",\n      \"head\": \"56408fafa3f21180363937cf3bb69e6989ce0358\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/git-remote-tests-3-divergence\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/759\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nPart 3 of the stack on #1637. Systematizes the historically most re-broken area (#953, #1251, #1252, #1260: destructive local-v1-ref moves) into an explicit matrix, and covers the git-refs equivalents that only had unit coverage.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- **D1 (git-branch)**: table-driven matrix — local v1 {ahead, behind, diverged, disconnected} × {pre-push (real hook), explain fetch-on-miss, doctor}: local-only commits always survive, behind→FF, diverged→both sides preserved with linear tip (double-replay guard), repeated pre-push leaves the remote byte-identical. Cells already covered by `safel\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1637,\n      \"title\": \"test: git-remote coverage (2/4) — real-hook P0 tests, cross-machine fetch, explain fix\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1637\",\n      \"head\": \"a9b0334c49a63253cd67d994fa72d9cef2ed1c3d\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/git-remote-tests-2-p0\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/758\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nPart 2 of the stack on #1636. The P0 test groups from the plan, plus two fixes they surfaced.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- **A-group (real pre-push hook, both backends)**: plain-push checkpoint sync with user-push assertions (A1), no-new-checkpoints no-op via remote digest (A2), branch-delete and tag-only pushes through the hook (A3), unreachable checkpoint target degrades gracefully under the real hook (A4), git-refs queue drain via real push (A6 slice).\\n- **C-group (cross-machine clone flows)**: production `fetchMetadataBranchIfMissing` exercised for real over HTTPS (C1 — previous clone tests subs\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1633,\n      \"title\": \"feat(ticket): entire ticket — link external tickets to branches, checkpoints & reviews\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1633\",\n      \"head\": \"80477c315284130a410acff455f768e35bb29a5a\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/entire-ticket\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Overview\\n\\n`entire ticket` links an external tracker ticket (Linear today, Jira-ready) to a branch and session, so work stays grounded in its original intent — and freezes that ticket into checkpoint provenance so the checkpoint chain becomes the ticket'\"'\"'s timeline, surfaced across `status`, `session info`, `explain`, and `review`.\\n\\nThe command group is platform-agnostic: every tracker implements one `Provider` interface and registers with a single `switch` case, so adding Jira later never touches the command surface.\\n\\n## What'\"'\"'s in it\\n\\n- **Commands:** `entire ticket setup` (store platform + team + API token in the OS keychain), `link` / `unlink`, `start` (ticket → new branch + grounding pro\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1628,\n      \"title\": \"Add hidden `doctor rewrite-checkpoints` test tooling (git-branch → git-refs)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1628\",\n      \"head\": \"b24e3ba909d620ff8f988393aaae89f4bc5b97d0\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/checkpoint-rewrite\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/752\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nHidden test tooling for evaluating the **git-refs** checkpoint store against real branch data: it re-materializes every checkpoint on the `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch as a per-checkpoint ref by re-driving the git-refs store'\"'\"'s write path. Independent of the (still-undecided) byte-identical migration — standalone off `main`.\\n\\n## What it does\\n`entire doctor rewrite-checkpoints` (hidden). For each checkpoint on the v1 branch:\\n- Replays each session'\"'\"'s transcript through `Write`, so the compact `transcript.jsonl` is **regenerated**, the tree is **rooted at the checkpoint** (no shard fold\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1613,\n      \"title\": \"fix(attribution): deterministic why metadata + interactive viewer + honest tag legend\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1613\",\n      \"head\": \"2534f41f77a0c4ccf66a816e743a61d99e10129e\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-why-metadata-consistency\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"**Trail:** https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/737\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## What\\r\\n\\r\\n`entire why <file>[:<line>]` could show three different answers on three equivalent clones of the same repo at the same commit — full metadata on one, partial on another, bare `CheckpointID` on a third. This makes the resolution deterministic: given the same remote state, every clone converges on the same output, and when it can'\"'\"'t, the miss reason says exactly why and how to recover.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Root cause (what remained after #1535 / `4f435384d`)\\r\\n\\r\\nEarlier work already added `MetadataMissingReason`, file-level enrichment, and the fetch suggestion. Two residual defects kept the issue alive:\\r\\n\\r\\n1. **The partial-blob divergence\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1579,\n      \"title\": \"fix(enable): detect Codex during agent setup\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1579\",\n      \"head\": \"be7c0235a1aa300cd27210d22dcffc2f0bff6923\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-enable-detect-multiple-agents\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Detect Codex from repository-level .codex configuration instead of requiring Entire hooks to already be installed.\\r\\n    \\r\\nKeep the existing multiple-agent enable flow intact: when Claude Code and Codex are both configured, enable reports multiple detected agents and reaches the multi-select path instead of auto-selecting Claude Code via the single-agent shortcut.\\r\\n    \\r\\nAdd regression coverage for Claude Code plus Codex detection.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1547,\n      \"title\": \"resume: refresh stale logs, fetch remote checkpoints, show progress\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1547\",\n      \"head\": \"9a2b3b58a443b6e60938c6724b4a470954ac5c94\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/resume-improve\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/679\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\nImprove entire resume so it reflects the latest session state and never silently loses local work:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRefresh on checkpoint-newer when the checkpoint cleanly extends the local log (local is a prefix).\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDivergence guard: a newer checkpoint timestamp alone no longer authorizes overwrite; if the local log holds entries the checkpoint lacks (or is strictly newer), prompt and keep when non-interactive. --force still overwrites.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFetch the checkpoint metadata branch from the remote before reading, so a remotely-updated checkpoint is picked up even when its ID resolv\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1536,\n      \"title\": \"Support colon line syntax for trail findings\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1536\",\n      \"head\": \"a07101962e7cd75cc201c822b11807d0090672e1\",\n      \"branch\": \"codex/trail-finding-colon-line\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/674\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n- Let `entire trail finding add --file` accept `path:line` and `path:start-end` location syntax.\\n- Keep `--line`, `--start-line`, and `--end-line` as compatibility aliases.\\n- Update the trail finding dashboard action hint to use the colon form.\\n\\n## Why\\nThe rest of the CLI generally represents source locations as `file:line` or `file:start-end`; `trail finding add --file path --line 42` was an outlier.\\n\\n## Validation\\n- `mise run check`\\n- `mise run lint`\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1493,\n      \"title\": \"feat(trail): update body/metadata by number, id, or branch (incl. branchless)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1493\",\n      \"head\": \"87d359d1c47fb0f4ec088e3422e9c334f5c08a85\",\n      \"branch\": \"paxos/cli-trail-body-write\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/637\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nTL;DR — Makes `entire trail update` address **any** trail by number, id, or branch — including **branchless** trails — so their **body *and* metadata** (status/title/labels) become editable from the CLI, plus file/stdin body input. CLI-only, no API changes. Stacked on #1476 (the body-*read* PR).\\n\\n## Problem\\n`entire trail update` was `NoArgs` + `--branch`-only, so a branchless trail (no branch) could not be targeted at all — neither its body nor its metadata was editable from the CLI. `show`/`checkout`/`delete` already resolve trails by number/id/branch; `update` did not.\\n\\n## What cha\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1479,\n      \"title\": \"feat(claude-code): add opt-in trail status line\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1479\",\n      \"head\": \"345fce6c3d36135c7e6d0a58af01dd404df775ee\",\n      \"branch\": \"cli-claude-statusline\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/621\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nShips the Entire trail status line for Claude Code as a native CLI feature, replacing the standalone Pi `entire-trail-statusline.mjs` script. When the current branch has an Entire trail, Claude Code'\"'\"'s status bar shows a clickable, cyan **`Trail #N <status>`** OSC-8 hyperlink to the trail on entire.io.\\n\\nIt'\"'\"'s **opt-in** and **no Node dependency** — it reuses the CLI'\"'\"'s own trail/auth/git internals.\\n\\n## How a user activates it\\n\\n```bash\\nentire enable --agent claude-code --claude-statusline\\n```\\n\\nThis writes a `statusLine` block into `.claude/settings.json` pointing at `entire h\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1462,\n      \"title\": \"Add `entire trail merge` subcommand\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1462\",\n      \"head\": \"0b76faf4c4d51894c9aac7cdb5bd886e0f67575f\",\n      \"branch\": \"cli-trail-merge\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/604\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAdds an `entire trail merge` subcommand that merges a trail'\"'\"'s branch into its base, after first checking the trail is mergeable. A `--dry-run` flag reports mergeability without performing the merge.\\n\\nThe Entire API already exposes the needed endpoints (`GET .../{number}/mergeability` and `POST .../{number}/merge`); this wires the CLI up to them.\\n\\n## Behavior\\n\\n- Resolves the trail from `--trail` (number, id, or branch), or the current branch'\"'\"'s trail when omitted.\\n- **Always checks mergeability first** and prints a readiness summary (approvals, CI checks, up-to-date with ba\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1459,\n      \"title\": \"feat(copilot): capture Copilot sessions from VS Code agent hooks (Preview)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1459\",\n      \"head\": \"91ddd5cbb9fdeaae1108f7e764204d9ff810099e\",\n      \"branch\": \"copilot-vscode-hooks\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/601\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\n## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nAdds capture support for GitHub Copilot sessions driven from **VS Code'\"'\"'s agent hooks (Preview)**, on top of the existing Copilot CLI support.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Why a separate hook file\\r\\n\\r\\nVS Code auto-discovers `.github/hooks/*.json` and reads Copilot CLI configs by converting lowerCamelCase event names to PascalCase (`userPromptSubmitted` → `UserPromptSubmitted`, `agentStop` → `AgentStop`). Those converted names are **not** real VS Code events, so the capture-critical turn hooks never fire from `entire.json` inside VS Code.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe events whose converted names *do* line up with\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1444,\n      \"title\": \"trail finding: populate selected_text for line/range findings\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1444\",\n      \"head\": \"7335c7df5f3ddffec210b398a06e0ce1de4c8075\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/trail-finding-selected-text\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/580/trail-finding-populate-selected-text-for-line-range-findings\\r\\n\\r\\n## Problem\\r\\n\\r\\n`entire trail finding add --line` / `--start-line` always failed against the control plane with:\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\nlocation.granularity=line requires non-empty selected_text\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nThe CLI built a `line`/`range` location but **never set `selected_text`**, and there was no flag to supply it (`TrailReviewLocationCreateRequest.SelectedText` existed but nothing ever assigned it). The server requires it for line/range granularity (`validateLocationShape` in the BFF). Only `--file` (which maps to `file` granularity, no `selected_text` requirement) worked — so line-anchored findings wer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1396,\n      \"title\": \"[bug]Restore native Windows interactive prompts\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1396\",\n      \"head\": \"53fdb57dda190ec5ba6547495f63a180e2b91d04\",\n      \"branch\": \"stale2000/windows-interactive-prompts\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Entire Logs: https://entire.io/gh/stale2000/cli/session/019eaad9-6a88-78a0-94c4-0fe99696aefa\\r\\n\\r\\n## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nThis fixes native Windows interactive prompt detection. The CLI previously treated Windows terminals as non-interactive because `interactive.CanPromptInteractively()` always tried to open `/dev/tty`, which only exists on Unix-like systems. `login.waitForEnter()` and the commit-link prompt path also depended on the same Unix terminal assumption.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Bug and impact\\r\\n\\r\\nOn native Windows, `/dev/tty` does not exist. That meant `CanPromptInteractively()` returned `false` even when a real user was running Entire from an interactive PowerShell, Command Prompt, or Windows Terminal session.\\r\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1394,\n      \"title\": \"[bug]Preserve Claude subagent token totals during condensation\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1394\",\n      \"head\": \"3a0722365045eef00aa0707e291cfdd24c18382b\",\n      \"branch\": \"stale2000/condense-subagent-tokens\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Entire Logs: https://entire.io/gh/stale2000/cli/session/019eaa64-5270-74c0-9f8a-e4df88c7014e\\r\\nSUMMARY:\\r\\nAfter finding and making the fix, I noticed the log saying that the \\\"bug\\\" might be intentional?  Or it is unknown why it is written this way?  \\r\\n\\r\\nI did an analysis as for why it might have been written this way and got the following response that implies that its indeed a bug, and the previous implementation didn'\"'\"'t know how to solve it.  But this PR does fix the issue.  \\r\\n\\r\\nExplanation/response to the TODO statement:\\r\\n\\\"\\r\\nSo the nuanced answer is:\\r\\n\\r\\nFor live transcript condensation: bug.\\r\\nFor shadow-only fallback with no live path: empty dir may be unavoidable.\\r\\nThe TODO was probably some\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1388,\n      \"title\": \"test: pin down Cursor token-usage condensation gap (stacked on #1263)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1388\",\n      \"head\": \"0ac052e1363bfbb5be21c17019959124c033e374\",\n      \"branch\": \"sh/cursor-token-condensation-gap-test\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Stacked on #1263 (draft)\\n\\nThis PR stacks **two integration tests** on top of @SnowingFox'\"'\"'s #1263 to pin down a gap in the Cursor token-usage work. **No production code changes** — it adds one test file. Base is `cursor-pr-1263-base` (a mirror of #1263'\"'\"'s head) so the diff shows only the new tests; once #1263 merges this can be retargeted to `main`.\\n\\nThese tests are **expected to fail** on #1263 as written — they'\"'\"'re the acceptance criteria for the fix.\\n\\n### The gap\\n\\n#1263 correctly threads the Cursor `stop` hook'\"'\"'s token usage into **live session state** (so `entire status` shows it). But at commit time, condensation recomputes `TokenUsage` from the transcript (`manual_commit_condensation.go\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1386,\n      \"title\": \"Fix: Keep Entire pre-push alive after Lefthook reinstalls hooks\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1386\",\n      \"head\": \"fa3b7b936ad12660eb8948ef0ea222cbb96fbd34\",\n      \"branch\": \"codex/issue-1349-lefthook-safety-net\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/stale2000/cli/session/019ea5bb-9549-7083-b95f-7ecb498cbc24 \\r\\n\\r\\nCloses #1349.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis keeps Entire'\"'\"'s existing Git hook ownership behavior unchanged while adding a Lefthook-local safety net for the failure mode reported in the issue.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhen a repository has a YAML Lefthook config, `entire enable` still installs the normal Entire `.git/hooks/pre-push` wrapper. It now also ensures `lefthook-local.yml` contains an `entire-push-sessions` pre-push command that only runs if Lefthook has reclaimed `.git/hooks/pre-push` and removed the `Entire CLI hooks` marker.\\r\\n\\r\\nNormal state:\\r\\n- Git runs Entire'\"'\"'s `pre-push` wrapper.\\r\\n- Entire chains to Lefthook.\\r\\n- The Lefthook-l\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1235,\n      \"title\": \"Harden opencode session dir, copyFile streaming, FetchBlobs argv batching\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1235\",\n      \"head\": \"3ef968c618c01f6bbbcb5852598fa9f48c2c805d\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/cli-hardening\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/400\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThree independent hardening fixes carried forward fro'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":11167}},"started_at_ms":1794842129681,"completed_at_ms":1794842129681}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:29.801Z","ordinal":3025,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-d0fe8b28-3914-4519-b1d1-25b59f60def9","process_id":"90990","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' 'm the analysis of #799, each narrowed to what'\"'\"'s actually reachable on current code, with tests.\\n\\n- **opencode session dir** — move from `/tmp/entire-opencode/<sanitized-path>/` to `<repoPath>/.entire/tmp/opencode/`. Closes a cross-user transcript exfil window on shared Linux machines (other local users can pre-create the predictable `/tmp` path and read whatever `entire rewind`/`entire resume` stashes there — `os.Root` already blocks symlink-redirected *writes* but not *reads* once the dir is owned by them). The new loc\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1210,\n      \"title\": \"feat(search): add --local fallback that greps the local checkpoint branch\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1210\",\n      \"head\": \"7d6324ec73126b520878762fb90e02e809d205e5\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/1195-local-checkpoint-search\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\nAdds `--local` to `entire search` / `entire checkpoint search`. Skips the remote service and does case-insensitive substring matching over the local `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch (prompts, transcripts, file paths, branch name).\\n\\nRefs #1195, #1171. The remote indexing bug isn'\"'\"'t fixed here — but users with confirmed-captured checkpoints (visible in `activity` / `dispatch` / `explain`) get an immediate working path while it'\"'\"'s diagnosed.\\n\\n- Honors `--branch`, `--json`, piped/accessibility output.\\n- Reuses the existing JSON shape so scripted consumers don'\"'\"'t branch on source.\\n- Skips auth entirely (works offline).\\n- Out of scope: TUI, `--repo *`, author/date filters.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1193,\n      \"title\": \"Handle failing push better\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1193\",\n      \"head\": \"7d7276baa1a891b34dd074305f7bf9e1677214e2\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/handle-failing-push-better\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/365\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Make a stuck `entire/checkpoints/v1` push diagnosable and bounded\\r\\n\\r\\nA colleague'\"'\"'s `git push` hung with an unbounded stream of dots on the pre-push hook'\"'\"'s `[entire] Pushing entire/checkpoints/v1 to origin...` line. Only Ctrl-C broke it, and the resulting `Warning: couldn'\"'\"'t sync ...: fetch failed:` had nothing after the colon — the doctor bundle showed no push events at all.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Root cause\\r\\n\\r\\n`exec.CommandContext`'\"'\"'s default cancellation only SIGKILLs the direct child. `git push` over HTTPS spawns `git-remote-https` + credential helpers that inherit our stdio pipes; killing git l\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1172,\n      \"title\": \"Add checkpoint sync destination picker to entire enable\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1172\",\n      \"head\": \"a02450c9a81e6734290c67bad00cda4c64db7f95\",\n      \"branch\": \"evis/public-repo-warning\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/346\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\n## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/780c02c4-dc14-4a66-a5bb-04e3ac80d0e4\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- Adds an interactive picker during `entire enable` asking where checkpoints should sync: this repo'\"'\"'s remote, a separate private checkpoint repo, or local-only\\r\\n- Non-interactive mode (`--yes`/CI) prints an informational notice with the `entire configure --checkpoint-remote` command\\r\\n- Selecting \\\"A separate private checkpoint repo\\\" prompts for the repo in `github:owner/repo` format and validates the input\\r\\n- Selecting \\\"Keep checkpoints local only\\\" sets `--skip-push-sessions`\\r\\n- Incl\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1118,\n      \"title\": \"Stop stale ACTIVE sessions from inheriting another session'\"'\"'s committed files\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1118\",\n      \"head\": \"dcd95e2da8fc347c1073ec5dad1dd1e081d32ff2\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/checkpoint-session-bug\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/301\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nA recent ACTIVE session that did no real work (e.g. a Codex shell where the user typed `exit` hours ago — phase still ACTIVE, `LastInteractionTime` within 24h, no `FilesTouched`, transcript only contains a startup banner) was being condensed onto a commit authored entirely by a different ACTIVE session and inheriting that commit'\"'\"'s file list via `filterFilesTouched`'\"'\"'s evidence-of-work fallback.\\n\\nThe trigger was a hole in `shouldCondenseWithOverlapCheck`: the read-only-skip clause only fired when `sessionsWithCommittedFiles > 0`. When the working session'\"'\"'s `state.FilesTouch\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 974,\n      \"title\": \"feat: add sidecar commit log for session timeline reconstruction\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/974\",\n      \"head\": \"b7f714b8b327a5f5352025a8fdde840e7200d119\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/experiment-tombstones\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nAdd a sidecar commit log that enables session timeline reconstruction from any checkpoint, without complex cross-referencing or git log scanning.\\r\\n\\r\\n### The problem\\r\\n\\r\\nToday, if you want to see \\\"what commits happened during this session,\\\" you'\"'\"'d need to cross-reference checkpoint IDs across git history, session metadata, and the checkpoint branch. For a UI timeline view — where you pick checkpoint 4 and want to see the full session history including checkpoints 1-3 — this requires expensive backward lookups across potentially weeks of git history.\\r\\n\\r\\n### The approach\\r\\n\\r\\nEach time PostCommit condenses a session, we append a one-line JSON entry to `.entire/metadata/<session-id>/co\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 799,\n      \"title\": \"fix: patch systemic OS-level vulnerabilities, OOM risks, and concurre…\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/799\",\n      \"head\": \"7974cfc4c54057e18eefa84c813d872f21a94e71\",\n      \"branch\": \"main\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"fix: patch critical OS-level, memory, and concurrency vulnerabilities\\r\\n\\r\\nThis commit addresses four systemic failure points in the core CLI runtime \\r\\nthat cause silent failures, panics, and security risks under edge conditions:\\r\\n\\r\\n- opencode: Scope session temp dirs to the repository `.git` directory to \\r\\n  prevent local symlink attacks and arbitrary file overwrites via `/tmp`.\\r\\n- git_operations: Batch `git fetch` arguments by hash chunks (500 max) to \\r\\n  prevent operating system `ARG_MAX` exhaustion on heavy repository syncs.\\r\\n- redact: Return deep copies of `PIIConfig` maps in `getPIIConfig()` to \\r\\n  prevent concurrent map read/write panics across concurrent goroutines.\\r\\n- utils: Refactor \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 734,\n      \"title\": \"Add cosign keyless signing for release artifacts\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/734\",\n      \"head\": \"176abe392dedf85e09c22831f301874cb6e8b431\",\n      \"branch\": \"pjbgf/cosign\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Configure goreleaser to sign `checksums.txt` using cosign with Sigstore OIDC-based ephemeral keys. Install cosign in the release workflow and grant id-token permission for the OIDC token. Add download and verification instructions to the README Quick Start.\\r\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes the release pipeline to use GitHub OIDC and `cosign` for keyless signing, which could break or block publishing if CI permissions or signing steps are misconfigured.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **keyless Sigstore/cosign signing** to the release process by granting `id-token: write` and installing `cosign` in the GitHub Actions release workflow.\\n> \\n> Configures GoReleaser to\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"entire-brain\": [\n    {\n      \"number\": 648,\n      \"title\": \"fix(history): one oversized transcript line costs that line, not the session\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/648\",\n      \"head\": \"7c46e04c930c2c6220fcf458f8e4a3a4bb395426\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-oversized-transcript-line-641\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #641. Thanks @petercr for the detailed report and the line-size measurements.\\n\\nFork pre-review with the review bots: https://github.com/Beehtrix/entire-brain/pull/34\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nOne transcript line over `historyMaxLineBytes` (1 MiB) ended every line scanner with `bufio.ErrTooLong`, and each caller treated that as \\\"this transcript cannot be read\\\". So one line dropped the whole session from history and conversation memory, on every refresh, delta and rebuild. The short-term delta listed it in `failed_files` on every tick, and the watcher said \\\"consolidation will repair\\\", which it never did.\\n\\nThese lines are common. A Claude Code image Read stores the base64 image twice, and a Codex comm\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 647,\n      \"title\": \"fix(push-hook): a rotated copy is not chained; join the CLI'\"'\"'s chain\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/647\",\n      \"head\": \"f694ab87e7e59944d2c852a4586d6ecac8998d7c\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-rotated-push-hook-645\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #645.\\n\\n@dake84, thanks for the detailed report: the four steps and the `movedPushHookCandidates` pointer matched what I found.\\n\\nPre-review on my fork: https://github.com/Beehtrix/entire-brain/pull/33\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nAfter a Husky reinstall, Brain'\"'\"'s push hook stops running, and nothing puts it back. In a repo with `core.hooksPath = .husky/_` and the Entire CLI'\"'\"'s hooks installed:\\n\\n1. `connect` moves the CLI'\"'\"'s `pre-push` to `pre-push.pre-entire-brain` and writes Brain'\"'\"'s hook in its place.\\n2. The CLI'\"'\"'s next check finds a hook that isn'\"'\"'t its own in `pre-push`. It backs it up to `pre-push.pre-entire` and writes its own hook in front, so Brain'\"'\"'s hook still runs through the CLI'\"'\"'s chain. The hook \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 646,\n      \"title\": \"chore(deps): bump the go-minor-and-patch group across 1 directory with 5 updates\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/646\",\n      \"head\": \"54bd04044b7e653e2f49a9d59f879743dc598b80\",\n      \"branch\": \"dependabot/go_modules/go-minor-and-patch-c1a469a4f0\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Bumps the go-minor-and-patch group with 5 updates in the / directory:\\n\\n| Package | From | To |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| [github.com/entireio/cli](https://github.com/entireio/cli) | `0.13.1` | `0.13.3` |\\n| [github.com/spf13/pflag](https://github.com/spf13/pflag) | `1.0.10` | `1.1.0` |\\n| [golang.org/x/mod](https://github.com/golang/mod) | `0.42.0` | `0.43.0` |\\n| [golang.org/x/sys](https://github.com/golang/sys) | `0.49.0` | `0.50.0` |\\n| [modernc.org/sqlite](https://gitlab.com/cznic/sqlite) | `1.60.1` | `1.62.0` |\\n\\n\\nUpdates `github.com/entireio/cli` from 0.13.1 to 0.13.3\\n<details>\\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/cli/releases\\\">github.com/ent\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 644,\n      \"title\": \"Bound workspace retrieval concurrency and propagate cancellation\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/644\",\n      \"head\": \"fd10c02bfa92479321e989819ff8e8a3aa8f6918\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/workspace-bounded-retrieval\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Closes https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/issues/643\\n\\nA cancelled workspace query currently searches its members and can return success. On a synthetic eight-member workspace, serial member retrieval takes about 4.30 s. This change runs at most two independent member reads at once and carries caller cancellation into retrieval, returning the context error after joining the workers.\\n\\n### Implementation\\n\\n- An unbuffered, fixed-size worker pool writes to each member'\"'\"'s manifest position. Rendering remains on the caller. Member failures stay in their groups and do not cancel healthy members.\\n- Reuse `ConcurrentCommandRunner`: custom runners that do not opt in remain serial.\\n- Pass context t\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 640,\n      \"title\": \"soph/windows-path-only-exe-lookup\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/640\",\n      \"head\": \"e6316ec14b3b36b7ea586b1c1e22fbee1e4a330f\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/windows-path-only-exe-lookup\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back a trail. Feel free to edit the title or body, but keep the hidden marker below: Entire uses it to close this pull request when the trail closes.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches hook wiring in committed `.claude/settings.json` and every Windows child-process launch in the repo; behaviour change is intentional but broad across setup, distill, and refresh paths.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> On **Windows**, bare program names were resolving from the **repository working directory** before `PATH`, so `entire-brain.cmd` / similar at the repo root could run on every edit \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 622,\n      \"title\": \"refactor(patterns): read a Codex session'\"'\"'s FileChange root and refs through one walker\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/622\",\n      \"head\": \"e4eebe5ef0929e58e8a19ad026a087dbd6d96c5f\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-codex-filechange-walker-612\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Follows up #612. @evisdren, this is the first follow-up you listed when you merged it: one FileChange walker. I looked at the second, a `files_touched` fingerprint instead of `checkpoint_id`, and left it out; the reason is below. Fork pre-review: Beehtrix/entire-brain#29\\n\\n## One walker for a session'\"'\"'s FileChange root and its refs\\n\\n`codexFileChangePaths` (root inference) walked the transcript itself: a case-sensitive `\\\"FileChange\\\"` name, on any block of any line, and a `move_path` whatever the change'\"'\"'s kind. The episode ops read a FileChange only as a tool call (lowercased name, `tool_use` or `tool` block) on an assistant line, and a `move_path` only on an `update`. So a block one side read c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 617,\n      \"title\": \"chore(deps-dev): bump @playwright/test from 1.64.1 to 1.65.0 in /webui in the npm-minor-and-patch group across 1 directory\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/617\",\n      \"head\": \"fcfcdee798aad7db6eb1f4a076a6f0bb0dcc1f27\",\n      \"branch\": \"dependabot/npm_and_yarn/webui/npm-minor-and-patch-43e562a727\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Bumps the npm-minor-and-patch group with 1 update in the /webui directory: [@playwright/test](https://github.com/microsoft/playwright).\\n\\nUpdates `@playwright/test` from 1.64.1 to 1.65.0\\n<details>\\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\\\"https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/releases\\\">@​playwright/test'\"'\"'s releases</a>.</em></p>\\n<blockquote>\\n<h2>v1.65.0</h2>\\n<h2>🥟 Run tests with Bun</h2>\\n<p>The test runner now runs under <a href=\\\"https://bun.com\\\">Bun</a>. Bun transpiles your TypeScript test files itself, so Playwright does not use Babel or its compilation cache. Pass the <code>--bun</code> flag, because without it <code>bunx playwright test</code> runs on Node.js:</p>\\n<p\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 616,\n      \"title\": \"chore(deps): bump actions/setup-go from 90ad2b35f69faf97585ad74d28fa006d2739b7af to 802e89cd7394b98352d79117a8b463bbfc2fdacf\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/616\",\n      \"head\": \"8581c8d340de6fa6f874298c9ab963d297a95b94\",\n      \"branch\": \"dependabot/github_actions/actions/setup-go-802e89cd7394b98352d79117a8b463bbfc2fdacf\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Bumps [actions/setup-go](https://github.com/actions/setup-go) from 90ad2b35f69faf97585ad74d28fa006d2739b7af to 802e89cd7394b98352d79117a8b463bbfc2fdacf.\\n<details>\\n<summary>Commits</summary>\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/actions/setup-go/commit/802e89cd7394b98352d79117a8b463bbfc2fdacf\\\"><code>802e89c</code></a> chore(deps-dev): bump handlebars from 4.7.9 to 4.7.10 (<a href=\\\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-go/issues/802\\\">#802</a>)</li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/actions/setup-go/commit/7d2730e317c8366225b42fced34583b26440a9cc\\\"><code>7d2730e</code></a> Add support for rc and beta versions in go.mod file (<a href=\\\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-go/issues/701\\\">#701\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 614,\n      \"title\": \"fix(agents): keep user hooks and plugins out of claude children\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/614\",\n      \"head\": \"b02bdc7c97910762cd829dd404ae091f97b62fe7\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-claude-child-hooks-552\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #552.\\n\\n@evisdren this is option 2 from my test comment on the issue. I opened it so there'\"'\"'s a concrete change to look at, not to skip your pick: if you'\"'\"'d rather have option 1 or 3, I'\"'\"'ll switch it over, or close it. @KHAEntertainment, thanks for the report.\\n\\nPre-review on my fork: https://github.com/Beehtrix/entire-brain/pull/26\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nBrain'\"'\"'s built-in claude-code children run with `--setting-sources user`, which still loads the user'\"'\"'s plugins and settings hooks. With a session-memory plugin installed, its SessionStart context went into every extraction prompt, and its Stop and SessionEnd hooks recorded each extraction call as a new session. The user'\"'\"'s global `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 610,\n      \"title\": \"fix(seed): remove seed documents the new scan did not write\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/610\",\n      \"head\": \"d64adfb97101cd758c2852ca54d8660d83c12e7f\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-seed-stale-docs-608\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #608.\\n\\nPre-review on my fork: https://github.com/Beehtrix/entire-brain/pull/24\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nA reseed only ever added to `seed/docs/`. `writeSeedDocs` writes the documents in the new scan, but nothing removed the ones that were no longer in it. The doc index (`loadDocRecordsFromSeed`) reads every `.md` under `seed/`, so a removed document stayed searchable although `file-index.json` and the manifest no longer listed it. There were two ways to get there:\\n\\n- A doc is deleted and the deletion is committed. The next reseed still had `seed/docs/docs/old'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' 'm the analysis of #799, each narrowed to what'\"'\"'s actually reachable on current code, with tests.\\n\\n- **opencode session dir** — move from `/tmp/entire-opencode/<sanitized-path>/` to `<repoPath>/.entire/tmp/opencode/`. Closes a cross-user transcript exfil window on shared Linux machines (other local users can pre-create the predictable `/tmp` path and read whatever `entire rewind`/`entire resume` stashes there — `os.Root` already blocks symlink-redirected *writes* but not *reads* once the dir is owned by them). The new loc\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1210,\n      \"title\": \"feat(search): add --local fallback that greps the local checkpoint branch\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1210\",\n      \"head\": \"7d6324ec73126b520878762fb90e02e809d205e5\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/1195-local-checkpoint-search\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\nAdds `--local` to `entire search` / `entire checkpoint search`. Skips the remote service and does case-insensitive substring matching over the local `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch (prompts, transcripts, file paths, branch name).\\n\\nRefs #1195, #1171. The remote indexing bug isn'\"'\"'t fixed here — but users with confirmed-captured checkpoints (visible in `activity` / `dispatch` / `explain`) get an immediate working path while it'\"'\"'s diagnosed.\\n\\n- Honors `--branch`, `--json`, piped/accessibility output.\\n- Reuses the existing JSON shape so scripted consumers don'\"'\"'t branch on source.\\n- Skips auth entirely (works offline).\\n- Out of scope: TUI, `--repo *`, author/date filters.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1193,\n      \"title\": \"Handle failing push better\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1193\",\n      \"head\": \"7d7276baa1a891b34dd074305f7bf9e1677214e2\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/handle-failing-push-better\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/365\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Make a stuck `entire/checkpoints/v1` push diagnosable and bounded\\r\\n\\r\\nA colleague'\"'\"'s `git push` hung with an unbounded stream of dots on the pre-push hook'\"'\"'s `[entire] Pushing entire/checkpoints/v1 to origin...` line. Only Ctrl-C broke it, and the resulting `Warning: couldn'\"'\"'t sync ...: fetch failed:` had nothing after the colon — the doctor bundle showed no push events at all.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Root cause\\r\\n\\r\\n`exec.CommandContext`'\"'\"'s default cancellation only SIGKILLs the direct child. `git push` over HTTPS spawns `git-remote-https` + credential helpers that inherit our stdio pipes; killing git l\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1172,\n      \"title\": \"Add checkpoint sync destination picker to entire enable\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1172\",\n      \"head\": \"a02450c9a81e6734290c67bad00cda4c64db7f95\",\n      \"branch\": \"evis/public-repo-warning\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\r\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/346\\r\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\r\\n\\r\\n## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/780c02c4-dc14-4a66-a5bb-04e3ac80d0e4\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- Adds an interactive picker during `entire enable` asking where checkpoints should sync: this repo'\"'\"'s remote, a separate private checkpoint repo, or local-only\\r\\n- Non-interactive mode (`--yes`/CI) prints an informational notice with the `entire configure --checkpoint-remote` command\\r\\n- Selecting \\\"A separate private checkpoint repo\\\" prompts for the repo in `github:owner/repo` format and validates the input\\r\\n- Selecting \\\"Keep checkpoints local only\\\" sets `--skip-push-sessions`\\r\\n- Incl\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1118,\n      \"title\": \"Stop stale ACTIVE sessions from inheriting another session'\"'\"'s committed files\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1118\",\n      \"head\": \"dcd95e2da8fc347c1073ec5dad1dd1e081d32ff2\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/checkpoint-session-bug\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/301\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nA recent ACTIVE session that did no real work (e.g. a Codex shell where the user typed `exit` hours ago — phase still ACTIVE, `LastInteractionTime` within 24h, no `FilesTouched`, transcript only contains a startup banner) was being condensed onto a commit authored entirely by a different ACTIVE session and inheriting that commit'\"'\"'s file list via `filterFilesTouched`'\"'\"'s evidence-of-work fallback.\\n\\nThe trigger was a hole in `shouldCondenseWithOverlapCheck`: the read-only-skip clause only fired when `sessionsWithCommittedFiles > 0`. When the working session'\"'\"'s `state.FilesTouch\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 974,\n      \"title\": \"feat: add sidecar commit log for session timeline reconstruction\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/974\",\n      \"head\": \"b7f714b8b327a5f5352025a8fdde840e7200d119\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/experiment-tombstones\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nAdd a sidecar commit log that enables session timeline reconstruction from any checkpoint, without complex cross-referencing or git log scanning.\\r\\n\\r\\n### The problem\\r\\n\\r\\nToday, if you want to see \\\"what commits happened during this session,\\\" you'\"'\"'d need to cross-reference checkpoint IDs across git history, session metadata, and the checkpoint branch. For a UI timeline view — where you pick checkpoint 4 and want to see the full session history including checkpoints 1-3 — this requires expensive backward lookups across potentially weeks of git history.\\r\\n\\r\\n### The approach\\r\\n\\r\\nEach time PostCommit condenses a session, we append a one-line JSON entry to `.entire/metadata/<session-id>/co\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 799,\n      \"title\": \"fix: patch systemic OS-level vulnerabilities, OOM risks, and concurre…\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/799\",\n      \"head\": \"7974cfc4c54057e18eefa84c813d872f21a94e71\",\n      \"branch\": \"main\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"fix: patch critical OS-level, memory, and concurrency vulnerabilities\\r\\n\\r\\nThis commit addresses four systemic failure points in the core CLI runtime \\r\\nthat cause silent failures, panics, and security risks under edge conditions:\\r\\n\\r\\n- opencode: Scope session temp dirs to the repository `.git` directory to \\r\\n  prevent local symlink attacks and arbitrary file overwrites via `/tmp`.\\r\\n- git_operations: Batch `git fetch` arguments by hash chunks (500 max) to \\r\\n  prevent operating system `ARG_MAX` exhaustion on heavy repository syncs.\\r\\n- redact: Return deep copies of `PIIConfig` maps in `getPIIConfig()` to \\r\\n  prevent concurrent map read/write panics across concurrent goroutines.\\r\\n- utils: Refactor \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 734,\n      \"title\": \"Add cosign keyless signing for release artifacts\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/734\",\n      \"head\": \"176abe392dedf85e09c22831f301874cb6e8b431\",\n      \"branch\": \"pjbgf/cosign\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Configure goreleaser to sign `checksums.txt` using cosign with Sigstore OIDC-based ephemeral keys. Install cosign in the release workflow and grant id-token permission for the OIDC token. Add download and verification instructions to the README Quick Start.\\r\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes the release pipeline to use GitHub OIDC and `cosign` for keyless signing, which could break or block publishing if CI permissions or signing steps are misconfigured.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds **keyless Sigstore/cosign signing** to the release process by granting `id-token: write` and installing `cosign` in the GitHub Actions release workflow.\\n> \\n> Configures GoReleaser to\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"entire-brain\": [\n    {\n      \"number\": 648,\n      \"title\": \"fix(history): one oversized transcript line costs that line, not the session\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/648\",\n      \"head\": \"7c46e04c930c2c6220fcf458f8e4a3a4bb395426\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-oversized-transcript-line-641\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #641. Thanks @petercr for the detailed report and the line-size measurements.\\n\\nFork pre-review with the review bots: https://github.com/Beehtrix/entire-brain/pull/34\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nOne transcript line over `historyMaxLineBytes` (1 MiB) ended every line scanner with `bufio.ErrTooLong`, and each caller treated that as \\\"this transcript cannot be read\\\". So one line dropped the whole session from history and conversation memory, on every refresh, delta and rebuild. The short-term delta listed it in `failed_files` on every tick, and the watcher said \\\"consolidation will repair\\\", which it never did.\\n\\nThese lines are common. A Claude Code image Read stores the base64 image twice, and a Codex comm\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 647,\n      \"title\": \"fix(push-hook): a rotated copy is not chained; join the CLI'\"'\"'s chain\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/647\",\n      \"head\": \"f694ab87e7e59944d2c852a4586d6ecac8998d7c\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-rotated-push-hook-645\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #645.\\n\\n@dake84, thanks for the detailed report: the four steps and the `movedPushHookCandidates` pointer matched what I found.\\n\\nPre-review on my fork: https://github.com/Beehtrix/entire-brain/pull/33\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nAfter a Husky reinstall, Brain'\"'\"'s push hook stops running, and nothing puts it back. In a repo with `core.hooksPath = .husky/_` and the Entire CLI'\"'\"'s hooks installed:\\n\\n1. `connect` moves the CLI'\"'\"'s `pre-push` to `pre-push.pre-entire-brain` and writes Brain'\"'\"'s hook in its place.\\n2. The CLI'\"'\"'s next check finds a hook that isn'\"'\"'t its own in `pre-push`. It backs it up to `pre-push.pre-entire` and writes its own hook in front, so Brain'\"'\"'s hook still runs through the CLI'\"'\"'s chain. The hook \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 646,\n      \"title\": \"chore(deps): bump the go-minor-and-patch group across 1 directory with 5 updates\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/646\",\n      \"head\": \"54bd04044b7e653e2f49a9d59f879743dc598b80\",\n      \"branch\": \"dependabot/go_modules/go-minor-and-patch-c1a469a4f0\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Bumps the go-minor-and-patch group with 5 updates in the / directory:\\n\\n| Package | From | To |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| [github.com/entireio/cli](https://github.com/entireio/cli) | `0.13.1` | `0.13.3` |\\n| [github.com/spf13/pflag](https://github.com/spf13/pflag) | `1.0.10` | `1.1.0` |\\n| [golang.org/x/mod](https://github.com/golang/mod) | `0.42.0` | `0.43.0` |\\n| [golang.org/x/sys](https://github.com/golang/sys) | `0.49.0` | `0.50.0` |\\n| [modernc.org/sqlite](https://gitlab.com/cznic/sqlite) | `1.60.1` | `1.62.0` |\\n\\n\\nUpdates `github.com/entireio/cli` from 0.13.1 to 0.13.3\\n<details>\\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/cli/releases\\\">github.com/ent\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 644,\n      \"title\": \"Bound workspace retrieval concurrency and propagate cancellation\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/644\",\n      \"head\": \"fd10c02bfa92479321e989819ff8e8a3aa8f6918\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/workspace-bounded-retrieval\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Closes https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/issues/643\\n\\nA cancelled workspace query currently searches its members and can return success. On a synthetic eight-member workspace, serial member retrieval takes about 4.30 s. This change runs at most two independent member reads at once and carries caller cancellation into retrieval, returning the context error after joining the workers.\\n\\n### Implementation\\n\\n- An unbuffered, fixed-size worker pool writes to each member'\"'\"'s manifest position. Rendering remains on the caller. Member failures stay in their groups and do not cancel healthy members.\\n- Reuse `ConcurrentCommandRunner`: custom runners that do not opt in remain serial.\\n- Pass context t\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 640,\n      \"title\": \"soph/windows-path-only-exe-lookup\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/640\",\n      \"head\": \"e6316ec14b3b36b7ea586b1c1e22fbee1e4a330f\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/windows-path-only-exe-lookup\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back a trail. Feel free to edit the title or body, but keep the hidden marker below: Entire uses it to close this pull request when the trail closes.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches hook wiring in committed `.claude/settings.json` and every Windows child-process launch in the repo; behaviour change is intentional but broad across setup, distill, and refresh paths.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> On **Windows**, bare program names were resolving from the **repository working directory** before `PATH`, so `entire-brain.cmd` / similar at the repo root could run on every edit \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 622,\n      \"title\": \"refactor(patterns): read a Codex session'\"'\"'s FileChange root and refs through one walker\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/622\",\n      \"head\": \"e4eebe5ef0929e58e8a19ad026a087dbd6d96c5f\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-codex-filechange-walker-612\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Follows up #612. @evisdren, this is the first follow-up you listed when you merged it: one FileChange walker. I looked at the second, a `files_touched` fingerprint instead of `checkpoint_id`, and left it out; the reason is below. Fork pre-review: Beehtrix/entire-brain#29\\n\\n## One walker for a session'\"'\"'s FileChange root and its refs\\n\\n`codexFileChangePaths` (root inference) walked the transcript itself: a case-sensitive `\\\"FileChange\\\"` name, on any block of any line, and a `move_path` whatever the change'\"'\"'s kind. The episode ops read a FileChange only as a tool call (lowercased name, `tool_use` or `tool` block) on an assistant line, and a `move_path` only on an `update`. So a block one side read c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 617,\n      \"title\": \"chore(deps-dev): bump @playwright/test from 1.64.1 to 1.65.0 in /webui in the npm-minor-and-patch group across 1 directory\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/617\",\n      \"head\": \"fcfcdee798aad7db6eb1f4a076a6f0bb0dcc1f27\",\n      \"branch\": \"dependabot/npm_and_yarn/webui/npm-minor-and-patch-43e562a727\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Bumps the npm-minor-and-patch group with 1 update in the /webui directory: [@playwright/test](https://github.com/microsoft/playwright).\\n\\nUpdates `@playwright/test` from 1.64.1 to 1.65.0\\n<details>\\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\\\"https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/releases\\\">@​playwright/test'\"'\"'s releases</a>.</em></p>\\n<blockquote>\\n<h2>v1.65.0</h2>\\n<h2>🥟 Run tests with Bun</h2>\\n<p>The test runner now runs under <a href=\\\"https://bun.com\\\">Bun</a>. Bun transpiles your TypeScript test files itself, so Playwright does not use Babel or its compilation cache. Pass the <code>--bun</code> flag, because without it <code>bunx playwright test</code> runs on Node.js:</p>\\n<p\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 616,\n      \"title\": \"chore(deps): bump actions/setup-go from 90ad2b35f69faf97585ad74d28fa006d2739b7af to 802e89cd7394b98352d79117a8b463bbfc2fdacf\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/616\",\n      \"head\": \"8581c8d340de6fa6f874298c9ab963d297a95b94\",\n      \"branch\": \"dependabot/github_actions/actions/setup-go-802e89cd7394b98352d79117a8b463bbfc2fdacf\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Bumps [actions/setup-go](https://github.com/actions/setup-go) from 90ad2b35f69faf97585ad74d28fa006d2739b7af to 802e89cd7394b98352d79117a8b463bbfc2fdacf.\\n<details>\\n<summary>Commits</summary>\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/actions/setup-go/commit/802e89cd7394b98352d79117a8b463bbfc2fdacf\\\"><code>802e89c</code></a> chore(deps-dev): bump handlebars from 4.7.9 to 4.7.10 (<a href=\\\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-go/issues/802\\\">#802</a>)</li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/actions/setup-go/commit/7d2730e317c8366225b42fced34583b26440a9cc\\\"><code>7d2730e</code></a> Add support for rc and beta versions in go.mod file (<a href=\\\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-go/issues/701\\\">#701\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 614,\n      \"title\": \"fix(agents): keep user hooks and plugins out of claude children\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/614\",\n      \"head\": \"b02bdc7c97910762cd829dd404ae091f97b62fe7\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-claude-child-hooks-552\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #552.\\n\\n@evisdren this is option 2 from my test comment on the issue. I opened it so there'\"'\"'s a concrete change to look at, not to skip your pick: if you'\"'\"'d rather have option 1 or 3, I'\"'\"'ll switch it over, or close it. @KHAEntertainment, thanks for the report.\\n\\nPre-review on my fork: https://github.com/Beehtrix/entire-brain/pull/26\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nBrain'\"'\"'s built-in claude-code children run with `--setting-sources user`, which still loads the user'\"'\"'s plugins and settings hooks. With a session-memory plugin installed, its SessionStart context went into every extraction prompt, and its Stop and SessionEnd hooks recorded each extraction call as a new session. The user'\"'\"'s global `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 610,\n      \"title\": \"fix(seed): remove seed documents the new scan did not write\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/610\",\n      \"head\": \"d64adfb97101cd758c2852ca54d8660d83c12e7f\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-seed-stale-docs-608\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #608.\\n\\nPre-review on my fork: https://github.com/Beehtrix/entire-brain/pull/24\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nA reseed only ever added to `seed/docs/`. `writeSeedDocs` writes the documents in the new scan, but nothing removed the ones that were no longer in it. The doc index (`loadDocRecordsFromSeed`) reads every `.md` under `seed/`, so a removed document stayed searchable although `file-index.json` and the manifest no longer listed it. There were two ways to get there:\\n\\n- A doc is deleted and the deletion is committed. The next reseed still had `seed/docs/docs/old'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":27292}},"started_at_ms":1794842129800,"completed_at_ms":1794842129801}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:29.924Z","ordinal":3026,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-34703dc7-132e-4a65-b6b8-fc50304cc3d5","process_id":"94594","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' '.md`, and `query \\\"zebra pipeline\\\"` still returned it.\\n- `refresh --worktree` copies an untracked doc. The doc is then deleted and a clean res\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 595,\n      \"title\": \"feat(memories): typed records, review write-back, and a provenance walk\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/595\",\n      \"head\": \"40309b025e01c8b13f23f5614b9b6e9c42abc2df\",\n      \"branch\": \"rc/m1-record-schema\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Why\\n\\nA review'\"'\"'s reasoning died with the run. Findings were printed and then lost, so the same regression could be re-derived from scratch on every pass, and nothing recorded what a memory was derived from or what replaced it.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n- `factmerge` records carry typed relations, a closed origin set, and `Record.Validate`, so a malformed record is rejected at the boundary rather than discovered later.\\n- `brain review --remember` writes findings back as durable memories, into the same store the review itself read, idempotently: a re-review of an unchanged tree records nothing, and a human retraction is never revived by a later detector run.\\n- `memories provenance` walks a memory'\"'\"'s \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 594,\n      \"title\": \"feat(memories): deliver memories unprompted, and make reuse measurable\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/594\",\n      \"head\": \"10943b41bd4c5686d3ce3ca8ba3f93f57d9bba0e\",\n      \"branch\": \"rc/m05-surface-fixes\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Why\\n\\nMemories were only delivered when someone asked for them, and nothing measured whether a delivered memory was ever used. That makes the retrieval surface unfalsifiable: you cannot tell a memory that helped from a memory that was never read.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n- `UserPromptSubmit` delivers relevant memories unprompted, so retrieval does not depend on the agent remembering to ask.\\n- A `PostToolUseFailure` hook answers the host'\"'\"'s own failure event, which is the event that actually carries `error`; the terminal guard the old wiring expressed was dropped because post-failure cannot express it correctly.\\n- The reuse metric is durable, and delivery is separated from pull, so `status` reports\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 593,\n      \"title\": \"fix(entities): disclose what the entity index cannot answer\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/593\",\n      \"head\": \"47afd3b1b2b22cdd8a15a0b4f38be6587532b937\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/entity-delta-disclosure\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Why\\n\\nThe entity index answered with silent gaps: where it could not resolve part of a delta, the output looked complete rather than partial. A reader cannot tell \\\"no consumers\\\" from \\\"I could not look\\\".\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\nThe delta discloses what it could not answer, so an empty answer is distinguishable from an unanswered one.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n`go test` green on the two affected packages, 131 and 72 tests.\\nTrail: https://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2730\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\nhttps://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 592,\n      \"title\": \"fix(entities): refuse a migration only for failures that could reach it\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/592\",\n      \"head\": \"b3bb4a727ce1dc339a42cb992afe2da28b114636\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/migrate-warning-relevance\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Why\\n\\n`blockingWarnings` excused any provider warning whose file was absent from the delta'\"'\"'s `files[]`, on the theory that a failure about an untouched file cannot affect this migration. But `W_UNSUPPORTED_FILE` and `E_PARSE_ERROR` both mean \\\"I could not read this file\\\", which is also a reason a *touched* file would be missing from `files[]`. So absence from the list was being read as evidence of irrelevance when it was really evidence of the failure itself. A second excuse accepted `severity: info` on its own, which let a provider downgrade its way past the gate.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n- Reachability now excuses only `E_FILE_TOO_LARGE` and `E_MINIFIED`, where \\\"this file is too big / is generat\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 591,\n      \"title\": \"fix(distill): let one over-cap transcript cost its own session, not the pass\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/591\",\n      \"head\": \"17e4755d5ad4c38314b08b2021a82cab57ca07db\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/distill-oversize-transcript\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Why\\n\\nA single transcript over the size cap aborted the whole distill pass, so one oversized session could cost every other session in the batch.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\nThe over-cap transcript fails its own session and the pass continues with the rest.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n`go test ./internal/distill/...` green, 335 tests.\\nTrail: https://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2728\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\nhttps://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 583,\n      \"title\": \"fix(agent-guide): stop advertising removed semantic retrieval\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/583\",\n      \"head\": \"022e7c576e2611c497193d7d301c622e78ff7cb9\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/agent-guide-bm25\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Follows #626 (#569).\\n\\n#626 fixed `brain-reference.md`. This PR fixes the same present-tense claims in the docs main still carries, and adds a test that ties the guide to what the binary says about itself. Semantic retrieval is gone since trail #278: the `--semantic` flag'\"'\"'s own help says \\\"Compatibility alias: semantic retrieval was removed; ranking is BM25 lexical\\\" (`internal/cli/command/retrieve/retrieve.go:629`).\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n1. Brain was still marked Yes for vector and hybrid retrieval in `docs/feature-matrix.csv:11-13`, with notes pointing at the `brain_cgo` embedder and a hybrid RRF default mode. I recounted the totals in `README.md` and `docs/feature-matrix.md` to match (51 rows, 2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 556,\n      \"title\": \"prichodko/remove-file-runners-20261028\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/556\",\n      \"head\": \"95719f004f0a66d5d5904bd3eb3883c909fe7f4b\",\n      \"branch\": \"prichodko/remove-file-runners-20261028\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2667/changes/entire-brain/462\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Config-only deletions with no runtime code changes; the main effect is turning off or relocating Entire trail automation that previously lived in these JSON files.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Removes seven **trail-scoped** prompt runner definitions from `.entire/runners/`, so those automations are no\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 554,\n      \"title\": \"fix(cli): report remote-keyed brain in repo-identity\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/554\",\n      \"head\": \"7e264764cef40a41ba6621cdc0f0912430eb81f4\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-repo-identity-remote-keyed-brain\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #413\\n\\n`resolveRepoStorageSetWithSlug` returned early for non-local (remote-keyed) identities before checking whether the canonical store had any state. So `repo-identity` said \\\"no brain yet\\\" for repos keyed by their GitHub remote, and `--keep gh/<owner>/<repo>` was rejected.\\n\\nThe fix moves the canonical-store check ahead of the early return. Local identities behave as before.\\n\\n**Before (unpatched `main`)**, from the new test:\\n```\\ncanonical repo key: gh/example/repo\\nstores with state:  none (this repository has no brain yet)\\n```\\n\\n**After:**\\n```\\ncanonical repo key: gh/example/repo\\nstores with state:  1 (gh/example/repo), no conflict\\n```\\n\\n`TestRepoIdentityReportsARemoteKeyedBrain` fails o\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 471,\n      \"title\": \"Memory-generation eval loop: facts distill-eval\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/471\",\n      \"head\": \"2968ba627abbe98f1655a5b23e928a9809ef4e6b\",\n      \"branch\": \"memory-generation-eval-loop\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2498/changes/entire-brain/382\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Changes are mostly hidden eval commands and env-gated distill overrides; production distill behavior is unchanged unless those env vars or `--raw-facts-out` are set.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds an offline **memory-generation eval** path under hidden `facts distill-eval`, scoring whether distille\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 467,\n      \"title\": \"Cut 0.2.1: semantic schema 1.4 ingested in full\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/467\",\n      \"head\": \"fae5fb3f39609c1d4341bb42cb6f319ca11fff18\",\n      \"branch\": \"evis/cut-0.2.1\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/378\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nRelease prep per `docs/releasing.md` step 1: move #466 into a dated `## [0.2.1]` changelog section. The 0.2.0 / graph v0.5.0 released pair skewed on the semantic schema (1.3 reader against a 1.4 provider), so `doctor` reports the graph axis degraded on a clean released install until this ships.\\n\\n## What\\n\\nChangelog only. After merge, step 2 cuts the release:\\n\\n```sh\\ngit tag v0.2.1\\ngit push origin v0.2.1\\n```\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Documentation-only changelog edit for a p\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 442,\n      \"title\": \"Stop the watch tick losing write.lock to the worker it just launched\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/442\",\n      \"head\": \"8c46bcaadc2190ede8645aee6961ec40dfc6daa3\",\n      \"branch\": \"claude/inspiring-wright-68270a\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2433/changes/entire-brain/353\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nThe supervised watch daemon (`entire-brain workspace watch --distill`, launchd `io.entire.brain-watch.*`) is the only automatic path that runs fact distillation, and on one machine it lost `locks/write.lock` on **576 of 724 ticks over 20 days**. A failed refresh skips the tick'\"'\"'s agent work, so the 24h-gated distill ran **3 times in 20 days**.\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\n| Fact | Value | Where |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Brain write-lock timeout | 10s | `internal/cli/brain.go:33` (`brainWriteLockTimeout`), shared by ~375 `withBrainWriteLock` callers |\\n| Holder named in \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 441,\n      \"title\": \"demo: carry a brain memory\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/441\",\n      \"head\": \"3d126de974a4c872d2be909342da6ffb4ff60dcb\",\n      \"branch\": \"demo-memory\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/352\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> No code, config, or data changes are present in the diff, so there is no implementation risk to review.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **No file changes** appear in this PR’s diff—the patch is empty aside from a `/dev/null` placeholder.\\n> \\n> This is a **draft Entire shadow PR** tied to [trail 352](https://entire.com/g\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 440,\n      \"title\": \"fix(distill): make the cache salt independent of agent, model and effort\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/440\",\n      \"head\": \"0086a6e75d46b207e5b0fb60a7e1d2fab59b5eb8\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/distill-cache-salt-agent-independent\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2426/changes/entire-brain/351\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nThe distill cache salt hashed the agent, model and effort alongside the prompt, reconcile prompt and threshold. The facts are the product, not the model that produced them, so keying on the model meant the setup backfill (a resolved agent, effort low) and the session-end hook (auto, no effort) never shared a cache entry. Each re-spent on every session the other had already distilled.\\n\\nOn a real 289-session brain: a bare `entire brain distill --dry-run` reported **0 cached**, while `--agent codex --effort low` reported 72 of the same sessions. No f\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 368,\n      \"title\": \"fix(agent-guide): use Graph search with older releases\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/368\",\n      \"head\": \"32215f1ace363a301c9eda76d9c4a22d3726031a\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/graph-guide-legacy-search\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n- Use `entire graph search` in generated normal and strict Graph/Brain guides so the guidance works with Graph v0.4.0; current Graph retains `search` as a compatibility alias.\\n- Update the matching guide documentation and add a regression check for all generated Graph guide modes.\\n\\nFixes #323.\\n\\n## Verification\\n- `go test ./internal/agentsetup -run '\"'\"'TestGeneratedGraphGuidesUseCompatibleSearchCommand|TestStrictGuidanceContentAndScope|TestAgentGuidePrintsDoctrine'\"'\"' -count=1` (passed)\\n- `go vet ./internal/agentsetup` (passed)\\n- `git diff --check` (passed)\\n\\nThe `entire` binary was unavailable for this checkout'\"'\"'s Graph/Brain preflight, so I inspected the current Graph command alias and t\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 367,\n      \"title\": \"fix(cli): avoid Git index locks during brief reads\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/367\",\n      \"head\": \"33090ae851e5abfac60c92b3020f206f160129ff\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/brief-avoid-git-index-lock\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\n- Pass `--no-optional-locks` on Brain'\"'\"'s Git subprocesses so read commands do not refresh and lock the shared index.\\n- Use `git diff-index --shortstat HEAD` for the brief'\"'\"'s diff summary, avoiding the remaining `git diff` index refresh.\\n- Pin both invocations and the resulting diff stat in regression tests.\\n\\nRefs #326.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `go test ./internal/cli -run '\"'\"'TestHardenedGitArgs|TestGitHardenConfigIsPinned|TestLiveState'\"'\"' -count=1` passed on Windows with Go 1.27.1.\\n- `go build ./cmd/entire-brain` and `git diff --check` passed.\\n- `go test ./... -count=1` did not pass on Windows. The broad suite hit Windows symlink/setup failures and the CLI package timed out at 10 minutes; t\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 277,\n      \"title\": \"Connect Linear issues to Brain memory and task workflows\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/277\",\n      \"head\": \"45972a1e1c2ead450d6335826c7a06314e74dc87\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/linear-issue-memory\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/1803/changes/entire-brain/197\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nLinear requirements and discussion can now travel with repository memory: import selected projects, retrieve cited issue evidence alongside code and sessions, start work with an issue-aware brief, and retain the outcome of user-requested Linear actions.\\n\\n## What ships\\n\\n- **Repository-scoped issue memory:** project descriptions, issues, and individual comments in immutable snapshots. Resumable imports cover active issues plus those completed/canceled in the last 90 days; explicitly referenced older issues remain fetchable.\\n- **Ordinary Brain retrieval:** BM25 \"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"entire-graph\": [\n    {\n      \"number\": 410,\n      \"title\": \"Skip Linux mount points inside the worktree instead of failing every working-tree query\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/410\",\n      \"head\": \"c47915e9103244fae7d72ab024bbe290c02aed21\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-worktree-mount-skip-393\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #393. @stlindenau, this is the fix for the sandbox failure you reported there.\\n\\n### Problem\\n\\nOn Linux, any mount inside a checkout makes every working-tree command fail. The Claude Code sandbox mounts a read-only tmpfs at `.claude/.cc-writes` inside the project, so in a sandboxed session `query`, `def`, `neighbors`, `impact` and snapshots without `--head` all stop with:\\n\\n```\\nGit worktree preflight declined subprocess enumeration: filesystem worktree fallback cannot safely traverse the refused path: open directory \\\".claude/.cc-writes\\\": symlink chain resolves off the expected volume\\n```\\n\\nThe preflight that runs before `git ls-files --others` treats every mount boundary as fatal (`errSyml\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 407,\n      \"title\": \"perf(store): answer `--head` lookups from a focused subgraph of the sqlite store\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/407\",\n      \"head\": \"dafb7add95441989f4c081ebf879f83c9fc9b172\",\n      \"branch\": \"perf/kernel-scale-lookups\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"\\nA `--head` `def`, `neighbors`, `impact` or `explain` decoded the whole committed-tree snapshot to answer a question about one symbol: about 55 s and 16-46 GB on the Linux kernel. They now read only what the answer can reach from the sqlite store: about 1 s and under 200 MB, with identical output.\\n\\n## What changes\\n\\n- The sqlite search store is on by default (`ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEARCH_STORE=0` turns it off). `index --head` and a cold `--head` lookup write it beside t'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' '.md`, and `query \\\"zebra pipeline\\\"` still returned it.\\n- `refresh --worktree` copies an untracked doc. The doc is then deleted and a clean res\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 595,\n      \"title\": \"feat(memories): typed records, review write-back, and a provenance walk\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/595\",\n      \"head\": \"40309b025e01c8b13f23f5614b9b6e9c42abc2df\",\n      \"branch\": \"rc/m1-record-schema\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Why\\n\\nA review'\"'\"'s reasoning died with the run. Findings were printed and then lost, so the same regression could be re-derived from scratch on every pass, and nothing recorded what a memory was derived from or what replaced it.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n- `factmerge` records carry typed relations, a closed origin set, and `Record.Validate`, so a malformed record is rejected at the boundary rather than discovered later.\\n- `brain review --remember` writes findings back as durable memories, into the same store the review itself read, idempotently: a re-review of an unchanged tree records nothing, and a human retraction is never revived by a later detector run.\\n- `memories provenance` walks a memory'\"'\"'s \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 594,\n      \"title\": \"feat(memories): deliver memories unprompted, and make reuse measurable\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/594\",\n      \"head\": \"10943b41bd4c5686d3ce3ca8ba3f93f57d9bba0e\",\n      \"branch\": \"rc/m05-surface-fixes\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Why\\n\\nMemories were only delivered when someone asked for them, and nothing measured whether a delivered memory was ever used. That makes the retrieval surface unfalsifiable: you cannot tell a memory that helped from a memory that was never read.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n- `UserPromptSubmit` delivers relevant memories unprompted, so retrieval does not depend on the agent remembering to ask.\\n- A `PostToolUseFailure` hook answers the host'\"'\"'s own failure event, which is the event that actually carries `error`; the terminal guard the old wiring expressed was dropped because post-failure cannot express it correctly.\\n- The reuse metric is durable, and delivery is separated from pull, so `status` reports\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 593,\n      \"title\": \"fix(entities): disclose what the entity index cannot answer\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/593\",\n      \"head\": \"47afd3b1b2b22cdd8a15a0b4f38be6587532b937\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/entity-delta-disclosure\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Why\\n\\nThe entity index answered with silent gaps: where it could not resolve part of a delta, the output looked complete rather than partial. A reader cannot tell \\\"no consumers\\\" from \\\"I could not look\\\".\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\nThe delta discloses what it could not answer, so an empty answer is distinguishable from an unanswered one.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n`go test` green on the two affected packages, 131 and 72 tests.\\nTrail: https://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2730\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\nhttps://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 592,\n      \"title\": \"fix(entities): refuse a migration only for failures that could reach it\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/592\",\n      \"head\": \"b3bb4a727ce1dc339a42cb992afe2da28b114636\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/migrate-warning-relevance\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Why\\n\\n`blockingWarnings` excused any provider warning whose file was absent from the delta'\"'\"'s `files[]`, on the theory that a failure about an untouched file cannot affect this migration. But `W_UNSUPPORTED_FILE` and `E_PARSE_ERROR` both mean \\\"I could not read this file\\\", which is also a reason a *touched* file would be missing from `files[]`. So absence from the list was being read as evidence of irrelevance when it was really evidence of the failure itself. A second excuse accepted `severity: info` on its own, which let a provider downgrade its way past the gate.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n- Reachability now excuses only `E_FILE_TOO_LARGE` and `E_MINIFIED`, where \\\"this file is too big / is generat\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 591,\n      \"title\": \"fix(distill): let one over-cap transcript cost its own session, not the pass\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/591\",\n      \"head\": \"17e4755d5ad4c38314b08b2021a82cab57ca07db\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/distill-oversize-transcript\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Why\\n\\nA single transcript over the size cap aborted the whole distill pass, so one oversized session could cost every other session in the batch.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\nThe over-cap transcript fails its own session and the pass continues with the rest.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n`go test ./internal/distill/...` green, 335 tests.\\nTrail: https://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2728\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\nhttps://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 583,\n      \"title\": \"fix(agent-guide): stop advertising removed semantic retrieval\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/583\",\n      \"head\": \"022e7c576e2611c497193d7d301c622e78ff7cb9\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/agent-guide-bm25\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Follows #626 (#569).\\n\\n#626 fixed `brain-reference.md`. This PR fixes the same present-tense claims in the docs main still carries, and adds a test that ties the guide to what the binary says about itself. Semantic retrieval is gone since trail #278: the `--semantic` flag'\"'\"'s own help says \\\"Compatibility alias: semantic retrieval was removed; ranking is BM25 lexical\\\" (`internal/cli/command/retrieve/retrieve.go:629`).\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n1. Brain was still marked Yes for vector and hybrid retrieval in `docs/feature-matrix.csv:11-13`, with notes pointing at the `brain_cgo` embedder and a hybrid RRF default mode. I recounted the totals in `README.md` and `docs/feature-matrix.md` to match (51 rows, 2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 556,\n      \"title\": \"prichodko/remove-file-runners-20261028\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/556\",\n      \"head\": \"95719f004f0a66d5d5904bd3eb3883c909fe7f4b\",\n      \"branch\": \"prichodko/remove-file-runners-20261028\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2667/changes/entire-brain/462\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Config-only deletions with no runtime code changes; the main effect is turning off or relocating Entire trail automation that previously lived in these JSON files.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Removes seven **trail-scoped** prompt runner definitions from `.entire/runners/`, so those automations are no\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 554,\n      \"title\": \"fix(cli): report remote-keyed brain in repo-identity\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/554\",\n      \"head\": \"7e264764cef40a41ba6621cdc0f0912430eb81f4\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-repo-identity-remote-keyed-brain\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #413\\n\\n`resolveRepoStorageSetWithSlug` returned early for non-local (remote-keyed) identities before checking whether the canonical store had any state. So `repo-identity` said \\\"no brain yet\\\" for repos keyed by their GitHub remote, and `--keep gh/<owner>/<repo>` was rejected.\\n\\nThe fix moves the canonical-store check ahead of the early return. Local identities behave as before.\\n\\n**Before (unpatched `main`)**, from the new test:\\n```\\ncanonical repo key: gh/example/repo\\nstores with state:  none (this repository has no brain yet)\\n```\\n\\n**After:**\\n```\\ncanonical repo key: gh/example/repo\\nstores with state:  1 (gh/example/repo), no conflict\\n```\\n\\n`TestRepoIdentityReportsARemoteKeyedBrain` fails o\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 471,\n      \"title\": \"Memory-generation eval loop: facts distill-eval\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/471\",\n      \"head\": \"2968ba627abbe98f1655a5b23e928a9809ef4e6b\",\n      \"branch\": \"memory-generation-eval-loop\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2498/changes/entire-brain/382\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Changes are mostly hidden eval commands and env-gated distill overrides; production distill behavior is unchanged unless those env vars or `--raw-facts-out` are set.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Adds an offline **memory-generation eval** path under hidden `facts distill-eval`, scoring whether distille\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 467,\n      \"title\": \"Cut 0.2.1: semantic schema 1.4 ingested in full\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/467\",\n      \"head\": \"fae5fb3f39609c1d4341bb42cb6f319ca11fff18\",\n      \"branch\": \"evis/cut-0.2.1\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/378\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nRelease prep per `docs/releasing.md` step 1: move #466 into a dated `## [0.2.1]` changelog section. The 0.2.0 / graph v0.5.0 released pair skewed on the semantic schema (1.3 reader against a 1.4 provider), so `doctor` reports the graph axis degraded on a clean released install until this ships.\\n\\n## What\\n\\nChangelog only. After merge, step 2 cuts the release:\\n\\n```sh\\ngit tag v0.2.1\\ngit push origin v0.2.1\\n```\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Documentation-only changelog edit for a p\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 442,\n      \"title\": \"Stop the watch tick losing write.lock to the worker it just launched\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/442\",\n      \"head\": \"8c46bcaadc2190ede8645aee6961ec40dfc6daa3\",\n      \"branch\": \"claude/inspiring-wright-68270a\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2433/changes/entire-brain/353\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nThe supervised watch daemon (`entire-brain workspace watch --distill`, launchd `io.entire.brain-watch.*`) is the only automatic path that runs fact distillation, and on one machine it lost `locks/write.lock` on **576 of 724 ticks over 20 days**. A failed refresh skips the tick'\"'\"'s agent work, so the 24h-gated distill ran **3 times in 20 days**.\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\n| Fact | Value | Where |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Brain write-lock timeout | 10s | `internal/cli/brain.go:33` (`brainWriteLockTimeout`), shared by ~375 `withBrainWriteLock` callers |\\n| Holder named in \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 441,\n      \"title\": \"demo: carry a brain memory\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/441\",\n      \"head\": \"3d126de974a4c872d2be909342da6ffb4ff60dcb\",\n      \"branch\": \"demo-memory\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/352\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> No code, config, or data changes are present in the diff, so there is no implementation risk to review.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **No file changes** appear in this PR’s diff—the patch is empty aside from a `/dev/null` placeholder.\\n> \\n> This is a **draft Entire shadow PR** tied to [trail 352](https://entire.com/g\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 440,\n      \"title\": \"fix(distill): make the cache salt independent of agent, model and effort\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/440\",\n      \"head\": \"0086a6e75d46b207e5b0fb60a7e1d2fab59b5eb8\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/distill-cache-salt-agent-independent\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2426/changes/entire-brain/351\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nThe distill cache salt hashed the agent, model and effort alongside the prompt, reconcile prompt and threshold. The facts are the product, not the model that produced them, so keying on the model meant the setup backfill (a resolved agent, effort low) and the session-end hook (auto, no effort) never shared a cache entry. Each re-spent on every session the other had already distilled.\\n\\nOn a real 289-session brain: a bare `entire brain distill --dry-run` reported **0 cached**, while `--agent codex --effort low` reported 72 of the same sessions. No f\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 368,\n      \"title\": \"fix(agent-guide): use Graph search with older releases\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/368\",\n      \"head\": \"32215f1ace363a301c9eda76d9c4a22d3726031a\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/graph-guide-legacy-search\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n- Use `entire graph search` in generated normal and strict Graph/Brain guides so the guidance works with Graph v0.4.0; current Graph retains `search` as a compatibility alias.\\n- Update the matching guide documentation and add a regression check for all generated Graph guide modes.\\n\\nFixes #323.\\n\\n## Verification\\n- `go test ./internal/agentsetup -run '\"'\"'TestGeneratedGraphGuidesUseCompatibleSearchCommand|TestStrictGuidanceContentAndScope|TestAgentGuidePrintsDoctrine'\"'\"' -count=1` (passed)\\n- `go vet ./internal/agentsetup` (passed)\\n- `git diff --check` (passed)\\n\\nThe `entire` binary was unavailable for this checkout'\"'\"'s Graph/Brain preflight, so I inspected the current Graph command alias and t\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 367,\n      \"title\": \"fix(cli): avoid Git index locks during brief reads\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/367\",\n      \"head\": \"33090ae851e5abfac60c92b3020f206f160129ff\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/brief-avoid-git-index-lock\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\n- Pass `--no-optional-locks` on Brain'\"'\"'s Git subprocesses so read commands do not refresh and lock the shared index.\\n- Use `git diff-index --shortstat HEAD` for the brief'\"'\"'s diff summary, avoiding the remaining `git diff` index refresh.\\n- Pin both invocations and the resulting diff stat in regression tests.\\n\\nRefs #326.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `go test ./internal/cli -run '\"'\"'TestHardenedGitArgs|TestGitHardenConfigIsPinned|TestLiveState'\"'\"' -count=1` passed on Windows with Go 1.27.1.\\n- `go build ./cmd/entire-brain` and `git diff --check` passed.\\n- `go test ./... -count=1` did not pass on Windows. The broad suite hit Windows symlink/setup failures and the CLI package timed out at 10 minutes; t\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 277,\n      \"title\": \"Connect Linear issues to Brain memory and task workflows\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/277\",\n      \"head\": \"45972a1e1c2ead450d6335826c7a06314e74dc87\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/linear-issue-memory\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/1803/changes/entire-brain/197\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nLinear requirements and discussion can now travel with repository memory: import selected projects, retrieve cited issue evidence alongside code and sessions, start work with an issue-aware brief, and retain the outcome of user-requested Linear actions.\\n\\n## What ships\\n\\n- **Repository-scoped issue memory:** project descriptions, issues, and individual comments in immutable snapshots. Resumable imports cover active issues plus those completed/canceled in the last 90 days; explicitly referenced older issues remain fetchable.\\n- **Ordinary Brain retrieval:** BM25 \"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"entire-graph\": [\n    {\n      \"number\": 410,\n      \"title\": \"Skip Linux mount points inside the worktree instead of failing every working-tree query\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/410\",\n      \"head\": \"c47915e9103244fae7d72ab024bbe290c02aed21\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-worktree-mount-skip-393\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #393. @stlindenau, this is the fix for the sandbox failure you reported there.\\n\\n### Problem\\n\\nOn Linux, any mount inside a checkout makes every working-tree command fail. The Claude Code sandbox mounts a read-only tmpfs at `.claude/.cc-writes` inside the project, so in a sandboxed session `query`, `def`, `neighbors`, `impact` and snapshots without `--head` all stop with:\\n\\n```\\nGit worktree preflight declined subprocess enumeration: filesystem worktree fallback cannot safely traverse the refused path: open directory \\\".claude/.cc-writes\\\": symlink chain resolves off the expected volume\\n```\\n\\nThe preflight that runs before `git ls-files --others` treats every mount boundary as fatal (`errSyml\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 407,\n      \"title\": \"perf(store): answer `--head` lookups from a focused subgraph of the sqlite store\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/407\",\n      \"head\": \"dafb7add95441989f4c081ebf879f83c9fc9b172\",\n      \"branch\": \"perf/kernel-scale-lookups\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"\\nA `--head` `def`, `neighbors`, `impact` or `explain` decoded the whole committed-tree snapshot to answer a question about one symbol: about 55 s and 16-46 GB on the Linux kernel. They now read only what the answer can reach from the sqlite store: about 1 s and under 200 MB, with identical output.\\n\\n## What changes\\n\\n- The sqlite search store is on by default (`ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEARCH_STORE=0` turns it off). `index --head` and a cold `--head` lookup write it beside t'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":10708}},"started_at_ms":1794842129924,"completed_at_ms":1794842129924}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:30.104Z","ordinal":3027,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-1be1fa28-b9e5-4ee0-bf9a-46b0b25ddcb5","process_id":"46719","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' 'he gz entry.\\n- Focused reads live in `internal/sem/search_store_focus.go` and `internal/cli/lookup_snapshot.go`; `docs/perf/focus-read-sets.md` lists what each verb reads. A name with no exact match still loads the full snapshot for th\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 399,\n      \"title\": \"sem(rust): vendor tree-sitter-rust v0.24.2 at ABI 14\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/399\",\n      \"head\": \"8696fd0f242ebc87e831d6b6af2db9270637be8c\",\n      \"branch\": \"feature/rust-grammar-v0.24.2\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"> Written by Claude Code (an AI agent) working under Rod'\"'\"'s direction; Rod reviewed the code and edited the description before this PR was opened.\\n\\nRust moves from the grammar bundled with go-tree-sitter to a vendored tree-sitter-rust v0.24.2, built with the tool from #394.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nWhile the Swift grammar refresh was under way, @thomaseleff pointed out in [a comment on #345](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/issues/345#issuecomment-6532737539) that Rust has the same root cause. The bundled grammar (August 2024) predates raw borrows, `&raw const x` and `&raw mut x`, which have been stable since Rust 1.82. Any file that uses one gets `E_PARSE_ERROR`.\\n\\nThis fixes it. (I primarily did thi\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 398,\n      \"title\": \"sem(grammars): build F# from a patch and drop `local_changes`\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/398\",\n      \"head\": \"dcb2aa1788d97f8fe920b8fd78b12a694ddc015b\",\n      \"branch\": \"feature/grammar-refresh-fsharp-patch\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"> Written by Claude Code (an AI agent) working under Rod'\"'\"'s direction; Rod reviewed the code & edited the description before opening this PR.\\n\\nFollow-up to #394, which taught `grammar-refresh` to patch and regenerate grammars. F# was the last grammar in grammars.json with `local_changes`, so its two hand edits become a patch and the field, the `-allow-local-changes` flag and the refusal go away.\\n\\n## What changes\\n\\n- `fsharp/scanner-header.patch` adds upstream'\"'\"'s `common/scanner.h` as `src/scanner.h` and points `scanner.c`'\"'\"'s include at it. It is 775 lines, because `git apply` will not copy a file from outside the grammar directory; the alternative was a new manifest field, which felt like more m\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 397,\n      \"title\": \"fix(sem): prune older, idle cache version directories\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/397\",\n      \"head\": \"204901e0ddfd3a04b87ba9a97ee46eddf521c9bf\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/prune-stale-cache-versions\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Part of #271 (item 2: no stale-version pruning).\\n\\nA cache version is hashed into every entry key, so bumping it moves new entries to a fresh directory and leaves the old one unreachable. Nothing removed the old directory: the issue measured 667 MB of 705 MB in a real cache root as dead versions.\\n\\n`PruneStaleCacheVersions` removes sibling version directories under the `search` and `records` families that this build cannot address. It runs on the first cache use of a command (`BeginProviderRecordsCache`, `PreindexProviderSnapshot`, and `loadOrBuildSearchSnapshotPersisting`), keeps the current version, ignores names that do not carry the family'\"'\"'s version prefix, and never follows a symlink.\\n\\nA \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 390,\n      \"title\": \"chore(deps): bump the go-minor-and-patch group across 1 directory with 3 updates\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/390\",\n      \"head\": \"dc2bf00cdc7eb9653e2a050830ec0311426ffb97\",\n      \"branch\": \"dependabot/go_modules/go-minor-and-patch-b3e20c3488\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Bumps the go-minor-and-patch group with 3 updates in the / directory: charm.land/bubbletea/v2, [github.com/entireio/cli](https://github.com/entireio/cli) and [modernc.org/sqlite](https://gitlab.com/cznic/sqlite).\\n\\nUpdates `charm.land/bubbletea/v2` from 2.1.0 to 2.1.1\\nUpdates `github.com/entireio/cli` from 0.7.8-nightly.202606270713.37c158f81.0.20260702100228-bc9a821d41e5 to 0.13.2-nightly.202611061535.3a760b96a\\n<details>\\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/cli/releases\\\">github.com/entireio/cli'\"'\"'s releases</a>.</em></p>\\n<blockquote>\\n<h2>v0.13.2-nightly.202611061535.3a760b96a</h2>\\n<h2>Nightly Build (v0.13.2-nightly.202611061535.3a760b96a)</h\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 388,\n      \"title\": \"prichodko/remove-file-runners-20261028\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/388\",\n      \"head\": \"85f04f9b1653e13acaffd874eb2f66d147d6176a\",\n      \"branch\": \"prichodko/remove-file-runners-20261028\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2668/changes/entire-graph/301\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Configuration-only deletions with no runtime code paths changed; impact is limited to Entire trail automation behavior for this repository.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Removes all seven JSON prompt runners under **`.entire/runners/`**, so this repo no longer defines trail automation via checked-in ru\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 386,\n      \"title\": \"chore(deps): bump actions/setup-python from 7.0.0 to 7.1.0 in the actions-minor-and-patch group across 1 directory\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/386\",\n      \"head\": \"1ba2a3b9c5455b553d19d62036feb8445f237859\",\n      \"branch\": \"dependabot/github_actions/actions-minor-and-patch-d87422eef0\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Bumps the actions-minor-and-patch group with 1 update in the / directory: [actions/setup-python](https://github.com/actions/setup-python).\\n\\nUpdates `actions/setup-python` from 7.0.0 to 7.1.0\\n<details>\\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\\\"https://github.com/actions/setup-python/releases\\\">actions/setup-python'\"'\"'s releases</a>.</em></p>\\n<blockquote>\\n<h2>v7.1.0</h2>\\n<h2>What'\"'\"'s Changed</h2>\\n<h3>Enhancements</h3>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Add <code>mirror</code> and <code>mirror-token</code> inputs for custom Python distribution sources by <a href=\\\"https://github.com/luhenry\\\"><code>@​luhenry</code></a> in <a href=\\\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-python/pull/1302\\\">actions/setup-pyth\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 300,\n      \"title\": \"feat(query): opt-in local semantic retrieval channel (draft, needs product decision)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/300\",\n      \"head\": \"254f5c7b5d1adddc79084d0ec63ee73f282307f0\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/semantic-channel\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/221\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n**DRAFT — do not merge.** An unresolved product decision blocks merge (see below). Updated onto main (c27f3a3e); the former bench/locate-cost base is already included in main.\\n\\n## What\\nAdds an **opt-in** semantic retrieval channel to `entire graph query`. A local embedding model nominates files and symbols, and the results are fused embedding-first with the lexical ranking.\\n- **Off by default.** It turns on only when both `ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEMANTIC_ENDPOINT` and `ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEMANTIC_MODEL` are set. When unconfigured, output is byte-identical to the base across 32 queries × 4 f\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 249,\n      \"title\": \"fix(sem): verify Gradle project ownership before deriving tests\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/249\",\n      \"head\": \"8b62e45058d0882b4c917be2544e3e6ba98b65a4\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-gradle-verify-project-membership-219\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Closes #219\\n\\n`entire graph search` can suggest a VERIFY command after locating relevant code. Before this change, its Gradle logic could return a command that failed outright or passed without testing the edited project.\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\nThe narrow verifier treated a source directory as proof of Gradle project membership. Finding `lib/build.gradle` was enough to emit:\\n\\n```sh\\n./gradlew :lib:test --tests '\"'\"'ATest'\"'\"'\\n```\\n\\nBut the directory `lib/` does not establish a project named `:lib`. That membership comes from `settings.gradle` or `settings.gradle.kts`.\\n\\nIf the settings file omits `:lib`, Gradle rejects the task. If it remaps `:lib` to another directory, the command can pass while testing code oth\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 237,\n      \"title\": \"feat(cli): add requirement traceability and review workflows with GPS\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/237\",\n      \"head\": \"927e31e1715720f876978399a3f2cd3b0eaaf004\",\n      \"branch\": \"docs/gps-design\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"(description updated by @ashtom, written by Codex)\\r\\n\\r\\n## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nAdds **Graph Parser System (GPS)**, a repository-local layer that connects authored requirements and acceptance criteria to code symbols, declared tests, and verification evidence.\\r\\n\\r\\nDevelopers define intent in Git-tracked YAML under `.entire/graph/`, bind requirements to stable symbols, and inspect how implementation changes affect those bindings.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Changes\\r\\n\\r\\n- Add `spec` commands to initialize, validate, and inspect specifications.\\r\\n- Add `anchor` commands to bind symbols and report missing bindings, ambiguity, and structural or content drift.\\r\\n- Add `context` to assemble bounded requirement, code, dependency, and te\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 232,\n      \"title\": \"feat(pact): add graph-guided verification of confirmed requirements\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/232\",\n      \"head\": \"f8b89de44f07077f7060342b4c51a73c95860f07\",\n      \"branch\": \"pact/implementation\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"(written by Codex, added by @ashtom)\\r\\n\\r\\n## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nAdds **PACT**, a Python application that uses Entire Graph to select behavioral checks and compare their results against human-confirmed requirements across two commits.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe application lives under `pact/`; the Go graph engine is unchanged.\\r\\n\\r\\n## What’s included\\r\\n\\r\\n- Requirement confirmation and revision history, with optional Entire Checkpoint source references.\\r\\n- Version-specific graph analysis that traces changed functions to registered entrypoints.\\r\\n- Conservative fallback to all confirmed registered checks when graph evidence is incomplete or unavailable.\\r\\n- Local and Databricks execution, with classifications for regressions, ex\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 152,\n      \"title\": \"RFD 0006: reference positions in the SCIP export\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/152\",\n      \"head\": \"5c7fec71f3ad2879aa29bc3556e2f81d9ad319a8\",\n      \"branch\": \"rfd/reference-positions\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/111\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What this is\\n\\nAn RFD, not a fix. It documents a measured gap in `snapshot --format scip` and proposes what to do\\nabout it. Opened as a **draft** because it asks for a decision.\\n\\n## The finding\\n\\n`snapshot --format scip` emits **25,716 SCIP reference occurrences** for this repository, and **none\\nof them is located at a reference**. Every one carries the enclosing caller'\"'\"'s whole declaration\\nspan, mean width **100.66 lines**.\\n\\n```\\nCALLS relations                                    19,233\\npositioned evidence records                        18,988\\n  …byte-identical to the caller\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 146,\n      \"title\": \"RFD 0005: converge code search on one engine (P2.M1 / COR-786)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/146\",\n      \"head\": \"2ca4b8fc736c027d88c7d10f2b684f52785d2f6c\",\n      \"branch\": \"rfd/converge-code-search\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/106\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n**RFC / discussion only. Not for merge yet.** This is a decision doc, no code changes. It opens P2 (Unified Memory) with P2.M1 / COR-786: \\\"converge code search on one engine, deprecate duplicates.\\\"\\n\\nDoc: `docs/adr/0004-converge-code-search.md` (continues this repo'\"'\"'s existing `docs/adr/` convention; Status is Proposed).\\n\\n### The proposal in three lines\\n\\n**entire-graph becomes the precision symbol PRODUCER**, emitting a SCIP index per `repo@commit` into peregrine'\"'\"'s already-reserved `SymbolSource::Scip` / `SymbolPrecision::Semantic` slots. **peregrine remains the find-text-fast\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"forgemark\": [\n    {\n      \"number\": 27,\n      \"title\": \"bench: add -strategy contention, racing all agents on one shared ref\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/27\",\n      \"head\": \"39dbec1f97a1bfcc8608aef67ee6927fca1c90bd\",\n      \"branch\": \"contention-strategy\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\n- New \\\\`-strategy contention\\\\`: all agents in a level push non-force to **one shared destination ref** (\\\\`refs/<ns>/<prefix><run>-c<level>-a0\\\\`), so CAS / non-fast-forward rejections become the measured signal rather than a theoretical category.\\n- A losing agent **fetches the shared tip, hard-resets onto it, and retries** — the push → reject → fetch → rebase → push loop real agents run when they collide on a hot ref. \\\\`push_ok/s\\\\` now measures the serialized update rate a forge can sustain on one ref; \\\\`cas\\\\` counts rejected races.\\n- The shared ref reuses \\\\`DestRef\\\\`'\"'\"'s \\\\`-a0\\\\` shape, so it stays inside the existing stale-bench-ref sweep with no cleanup changes.\\n\\nMotivation: every\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 26,\n      \"title\": \"prichodko/remove-file-runners-20261028\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/26\",\n      \"head\": \"2fd149f0f9eea89297993ed0bb7eddf3d801b6a6\",\n      \"branch\": \"prichodko/remove-file-runners-20261028\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2671/changes/forgemark/15\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Metadata-only removal with no runtime code changes; risk is limited to losing repo-defined Entire trail automation unless runners are configured elsewhere.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Removes five **file-based Entire trail runners** under `.entire/runners/`: contract review (`trail-review`), risk eval (`\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 25,\n      \"title\": \"Sweep: ignore clock skew\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/25\",\n      \"head\": \"8871c9262664b8f876effca01d52a8ba0a7cff89\",\n      \"branch\": \"demo/sweep-new\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/forgemark/trails/14\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 24,\n      \"title\": \"Sweep: ignore clock skew\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/24\",\n      \"head\": \"8b87a55352523ff348d8f589c51d057ba14d3fc6\",\n      \"branch\": \"demo/sweep-live\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/forgemark/trails/13\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 19,\n      \"title\": \"Brainstore test, do not merge\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/19\",\n      \"head\": \"4a85f98b85ce3ec3aa504a596f931d2a9d805389\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/sweep-command\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/forgemark/trails/8\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.io) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 14,\n      \"title\": \"feat: monitor output + CI performance gate\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/14\",\n      \"head\": \"2ce331e59038961ccfe065a71d773206920020c4\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/monitor-adapter\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\nTwo halves of the same story: **emit a gateable number, then gate on it.**\\n\\n1. **`forgemark report --emit monitor <results.json>`** reduces a stored result doc to one headline metric — **peak sustained ops/sec across the sweep** — in the Entire trail runner'\"'\"'s `last_json_line` monitor contract:\\n\\n   ```\\n   {\\\"value\\\":42.7,\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"peak push 42.7 ops/s @ c=32 | c=1 8.1, c=8 28.4, c=32 42.7 | p95 210ms | 0 errors\\\"}\\n   ```\\n\\n2. **`.github/workflows/perf-gate.yml`** consumes that value: it runs forgemark against a real forge and fails when peak throughput drops below a floor.\\n\\n### report\\n\\n- `--emit monitor` (default) prints exactly the `{\\\"value\\\",\\\"rationale\\\"}` object as the last JSON l\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 6,\n      \"title\": \"feat: add threshold flags for CI regression gating\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/6\",\n      \"head\": \"4492df3c22c07729070edf65b373895da562447f\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/forgemark-threshold-gate\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\nforgemark can now gate CI runs: set `-min-push-rate`, `-max-p95`, or `-max-errors` and a sweep that misses any of them prints per-level breach lines to stderr and exits 2. All three flags default off; unset flags chang'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' 'he gz entry.\\n- Focused reads live in `internal/sem/search_store_focus.go` and `internal/cli/lookup_snapshot.go`; `docs/perf/focus-read-sets.md` lists what each verb reads. A name with no exact match still loads the full snapshot for th\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 399,\n      \"title\": \"sem(rust): vendor tree-sitter-rust v0.24.2 at ABI 14\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/399\",\n      \"head\": \"8696fd0f242ebc87e831d6b6af2db9270637be8c\",\n      \"branch\": \"feature/rust-grammar-v0.24.2\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"> Written by Claude Code (an AI agent) working under Rod'\"'\"'s direction; Rod reviewed the code and edited the description before this PR was opened.\\n\\nRust moves from the grammar bundled with go-tree-sitter to a vendored tree-sitter-rust v0.24.2, built with the tool from #394.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nWhile the Swift grammar refresh was under way, @thomaseleff pointed out in [a comment on #345](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/issues/345#issuecomment-6532737539) that Rust has the same root cause. The bundled grammar (August 2024) predates raw borrows, `&raw const x` and `&raw mut x`, which have been stable since Rust 1.82. Any file that uses one gets `E_PARSE_ERROR`.\\n\\nThis fixes it. (I primarily did thi\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 398,\n      \"title\": \"sem(grammars): build F# from a patch and drop `local_changes`\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/398\",\n      \"head\": \"dcb2aa1788d97f8fe920b8fd78b12a694ddc015b\",\n      \"branch\": \"feature/grammar-refresh-fsharp-patch\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"> Written by Claude Code (an AI agent) working under Rod'\"'\"'s direction; Rod reviewed the code & edited the description before opening this PR.\\n\\nFollow-up to #394, which taught `grammar-refresh` to patch and regenerate grammars. F# was the last grammar in grammars.json with `local_changes`, so its two hand edits become a patch and the field, the `-allow-local-changes` flag and the refusal go away.\\n\\n## What changes\\n\\n- `fsharp/scanner-header.patch` adds upstream'\"'\"'s `common/scanner.h` as `src/scanner.h` and points `scanner.c`'\"'\"'s include at it. It is 775 lines, because `git apply` will not copy a file from outside the grammar directory; the alternative was a new manifest field, which felt like more m\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 397,\n      \"title\": \"fix(sem): prune older, idle cache version directories\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/397\",\n      \"head\": \"204901e0ddfd3a04b87ba9a97ee46eddf521c9bf\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/prune-stale-cache-versions\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Part of #271 (item 2: no stale-version pruning).\\n\\nA cache version is hashed into every entry key, so bumping it moves new entries to a fresh directory and leaves the old one unreachable. Nothing removed the old directory: the issue measured 667 MB of 705 MB in a real cache root as dead versions.\\n\\n`PruneStaleCacheVersions` removes sibling version directories under the `search` and `records` families that this build cannot address. It runs on the first cache use of a command (`BeginProviderRecordsCache`, `PreindexProviderSnapshot`, and `loadOrBuildSearchSnapshotPersisting`), keeps the current version, ignores names that do not carry the family'\"'\"'s version prefix, and never follows a symlink.\\n\\nA \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 390,\n      \"title\": \"chore(deps): bump the go-minor-and-patch group across 1 directory with 3 updates\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/390\",\n      \"head\": \"dc2bf00cdc7eb9653e2a050830ec0311426ffb97\",\n      \"branch\": \"dependabot/go_modules/go-minor-and-patch-b3e20c3488\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Bumps the go-minor-and-patch group with 3 updates in the / directory: charm.land/bubbletea/v2, [github.com/entireio/cli](https://github.com/entireio/cli) and [modernc.org/sqlite](https://gitlab.com/cznic/sqlite).\\n\\nUpdates `charm.land/bubbletea/v2` from 2.1.0 to 2.1.1\\nUpdates `github.com/entireio/cli` from 0.7.8-nightly.202606270713.37c158f81.0.20260702100228-bc9a821d41e5 to 0.13.2-nightly.202611061535.3a760b96a\\n<details>\\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/cli/releases\\\">github.com/entireio/cli'\"'\"'s releases</a>.</em></p>\\n<blockquote>\\n<h2>v0.13.2-nightly.202611061535.3a760b96a</h2>\\n<h2>Nightly Build (v0.13.2-nightly.202611061535.3a760b96a)</h\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 388,\n      \"title\": \"prichodko/remove-file-runners-20261028\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/388\",\n      \"head\": \"85f04f9b1653e13acaffd874eb2f66d147d6176a\",\n      \"branch\": \"prichodko/remove-file-runners-20261028\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2668/changes/entire-graph/301\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Configuration-only deletions with no runtime code paths changed; impact is limited to Entire trail automation behavior for this repository.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Removes all seven JSON prompt runners under **`.entire/runners/`**, so this repo no longer defines trail automation via checked-in ru\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 386,\n      \"title\": \"chore(deps): bump actions/setup-python from 7.0.0 to 7.1.0 in the actions-minor-and-patch group across 1 directory\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/386\",\n      \"head\": \"1ba2a3b9c5455b553d19d62036feb8445f237859\",\n      \"branch\": \"dependabot/github_actions/actions-minor-and-patch-d87422eef0\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Bumps the actions-minor-and-patch group with 1 update in the / directory: [actions/setup-python](https://github.com/actions/setup-python).\\n\\nUpdates `actions/setup-python` from 7.0.0 to 7.1.0\\n<details>\\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\\\"https://github.com/actions/setup-python/releases\\\">actions/setup-python'\"'\"'s releases</a>.</em></p>\\n<blockquote>\\n<h2>v7.1.0</h2>\\n<h2>What'\"'\"'s Changed</h2>\\n<h3>Enhancements</h3>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Add <code>mirror</code> and <code>mirror-token</code> inputs for custom Python distribution sources by <a href=\\\"https://github.com/luhenry\\\"><code>@​luhenry</code></a> in <a href=\\\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-python/pull/1302\\\">actions/setup-pyth\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 300,\n      \"title\": \"feat(query): opt-in local semantic retrieval channel (draft, needs product decision)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/300\",\n      \"head\": \"254f5c7b5d1adddc79084d0ec63ee73f282307f0\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/semantic-channel\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/221\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n**DRAFT — do not merge.** An unresolved product decision blocks merge (see below). Updated onto main (c27f3a3e); the former bench/locate-cost base is already included in main.\\n\\n## What\\nAdds an **opt-in** semantic retrieval channel to `entire graph query`. A local embedding model nominates files and symbols, and the results are fused embedding-first with the lexical ranking.\\n- **Off by default.** It turns on only when both `ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEMANTIC_ENDPOINT` and `ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEMANTIC_MODEL` are set. When unconfigured, output is byte-identical to the base across 32 queries × 4 f\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 249,\n      \"title\": \"fix(sem): verify Gradle project ownership before deriving tests\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/249\",\n      \"head\": \"8b62e45058d0882b4c917be2544e3e6ba98b65a4\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix-gradle-verify-project-membership-219\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Closes #219\\n\\n`entire graph search` can suggest a VERIFY command after locating relevant code. Before this change, its Gradle logic could return a command that failed outright or passed without testing the edited project.\\n\\n## The bug\\n\\nThe narrow verifier treated a source directory as proof of Gradle project membership. Finding `lib/build.gradle` was enough to emit:\\n\\n```sh\\n./gradlew :lib:test --tests '\"'\"'ATest'\"'\"'\\n```\\n\\nBut the directory `lib/` does not establish a project named `:lib`. That membership comes from `settings.gradle` or `settings.gradle.kts`.\\n\\nIf the settings file omits `:lib`, Gradle rejects the task. If it remaps `:lib` to another directory, the command can pass while testing code oth\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 237,\n      \"title\": \"feat(cli): add requirement traceability and review workflows with GPS\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/237\",\n      \"head\": \"927e31e1715720f876978399a3f2cd3b0eaaf004\",\n      \"branch\": \"docs/gps-design\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"(description updated by @ashtom, written by Codex)\\r\\n\\r\\n## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nAdds **Graph Parser System (GPS)**, a repository-local layer that connects authored requirements and acceptance criteria to code symbols, declared tests, and verification evidence.\\r\\n\\r\\nDevelopers define intent in Git-tracked YAML under `.entire/graph/`, bind requirements to stable symbols, and inspect how implementation changes affect those bindings.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Changes\\r\\n\\r\\n- Add `spec` commands to initialize, validate, and inspect specifications.\\r\\n- Add `anchor` commands to bind symbols and report missing bindings, ambiguity, and structural or content drift.\\r\\n- Add `context` to assemble bounded requirement, code, dependency, and te\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 232,\n      \"title\": \"feat(pact): add graph-guided verification of confirmed requirements\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/232\",\n      \"head\": \"f8b89de44f07077f7060342b4c51a73c95860f07\",\n      \"branch\": \"pact/implementation\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"(written by Codex, added by @ashtom)\\r\\n\\r\\n## Summary\\r\\n\\r\\nAdds **PACT**, a Python application that uses Entire Graph to select behavioral checks and compare their results against human-confirmed requirements across two commits.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe application lives under `pact/`; the Go graph engine is unchanged.\\r\\n\\r\\n## What’s included\\r\\n\\r\\n- Requirement confirmation and revision history, with optional Entire Checkpoint source references.\\r\\n- Version-specific graph analysis that traces changed functions to registered entrypoints.\\r\\n- Conservative fallback to all confirmed registered checks when graph evidence is incomplete or unavailable.\\r\\n- Local and Databricks execution, with classifications for regressions, ex\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 152,\n      \"title\": \"RFD 0006: reference positions in the SCIP export\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/152\",\n      \"head\": \"5c7fec71f3ad2879aa29bc3556e2f81d9ad319a8\",\n      \"branch\": \"rfd/reference-positions\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/111\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What this is\\n\\nAn RFD, not a fix. It documents a measured gap in `snapshot --format scip` and proposes what to do\\nabout it. Opened as a **draft** because it asks for a decision.\\n\\n## The finding\\n\\n`snapshot --format scip` emits **25,716 SCIP reference occurrences** for this repository, and **none\\nof them is located at a reference**. Every one carries the enclosing caller'\"'\"'s whole declaration\\nspan, mean width **100.66 lines**.\\n\\n```\\nCALLS relations                                    19,233\\npositioned evidence records                        18,988\\n  …byte-identical to the caller\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 146,\n      \"title\": \"RFD 0005: converge code search on one engine (P2.M1 / COR-786)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/146\",\n      \"head\": \"2ca4b8fc736c027d88c7d10f2b684f52785d2f6c\",\n      \"branch\": \"rfd/converge-code-search\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/106\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n**RFC / discussion only. Not for merge yet.** This is a decision doc, no code changes. It opens P2 (Unified Memory) with P2.M1 / COR-786: \\\"converge code search on one engine, deprecate duplicates.\\\"\\n\\nDoc: `docs/adr/0004-converge-code-search.md` (continues this repo'\"'\"'s existing `docs/adr/` convention; Status is Proposed).\\n\\n### The proposal in three lines\\n\\n**entire-graph becomes the precision symbol PRODUCER**, emitting a SCIP index per `repo@commit` into peregrine'\"'\"'s already-reserved `SymbolSource::Scip` / `SymbolPrecision::Semantic` slots. **peregrine remains the find-text-fast\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"forgemark\": [\n    {\n      \"number\": 27,\n      \"title\": \"bench: add -strategy contention, racing all agents on one shared ref\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/27\",\n      \"head\": \"39dbec1f97a1bfcc8608aef67ee6927fca1c90bd\",\n      \"branch\": \"contention-strategy\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\n- New \\\\`-strategy contention\\\\`: all agents in a level push non-force to **one shared destination ref** (\\\\`refs/<ns>/<prefix><run>-c<level>-a0\\\\`), so CAS / non-fast-forward rejections become the measured signal rather than a theoretical category.\\n- A losing agent **fetches the shared tip, hard-resets onto it, and retries** — the push → reject → fetch → rebase → push loop real agents run when they collide on a hot ref. \\\\`push_ok/s\\\\` now measures the serialized update rate a forge can sustain on one ref; \\\\`cas\\\\` counts rejected races.\\n- The shared ref reuses \\\\`DestRef\\\\`'\"'\"'s \\\\`-a0\\\\` shape, so it stays inside the existing stale-bench-ref sweep with no cleanup changes.\\n\\nMotivation: every\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 26,\n      \"title\": \"prichodko/remove-file-runners-20261028\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/26\",\n      \"head\": \"2fd149f0f9eea89297993ed0bb7eddf3d801b6a6\",\n      \"branch\": \"prichodko/remove-file-runners-20261028\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2671/changes/forgemark/15\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Low Risk**\\n> Metadata-only removal with no runtime code changes; risk is limited to losing repo-defined Entire trail automation unless runners are configured elsewhere.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Removes five **file-based Entire trail runners** under `.entire/runners/`: contract review (`trail-review`), risk eval (`\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 25,\n      \"title\": \"Sweep: ignore clock skew\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/25\",\n      \"head\": \"8871c9262664b8f876effca01d52a8ba0a7cff89\",\n      \"branch\": \"demo/sweep-new\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/forgemark/trails/14\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 24,\n      \"title\": \"Sweep: ignore clock skew\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/24\",\n      \"head\": \"8b87a55352523ff348d8f589c51d057ba14d3fc6\",\n      \"branch\": \"demo/sweep-live\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/forgemark/trails/13\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.com) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 19,\n      \"title\": \"Brainstore test, do not merge\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/19\",\n      \"head\": \"4a85f98b85ce3ec3aa504a596f931d2a9d805389\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/sweep-command\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/forgemark/trails/8\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nThis draft pull request was opened by [Entire](https://entire.io) to back the linked trail. Feel free to edit the title or body — the link above is what keeps the trail and PR connected.\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 14,\n      \"title\": \"feat: monitor output + CI performance gate\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/14\",\n      \"head\": \"2ce331e59038961ccfe065a71d773206920020c4\",\n      \"branch\": \"feat/monitor-adapter\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\n\\nTwo halves of the same story: **emit a gateable number, then gate on it.**\\n\\n1. **`forgemark report --emit monitor <results.json>`** reduces a stored result doc to one headline metric — **peak sustained ops/sec across the sweep** — in the Entire trail runner'\"'\"'s `last_json_line` monitor contract:\\n\\n   ```\\n   {\\\"value\\\":42.7,\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"peak push 42.7 ops/s @ c=32 | c=1 8.1, c=8 28.4, c=32 42.7 | p95 210ms | 0 errors\\\"}\\n   ```\\n\\n2. **`.github/workflows/perf-gate.yml`** consumes that value: it runs forgemark against a real forge and fails when peak throughput drops below a floor.\\n\\n### report\\n\\n- `--emit monitor` (default) prints exactly the `{\\\"value\\\",\\\"rationale\\\"}` object as the last JSON l\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 6,\n      \"title\": \"feat: add threshold flags for CI regression gating\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/6\",\n      \"head\": \"4492df3c22c07729070edf65b373895da562447f\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/forgemark-threshold-gate\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Summary\\nforgemark can now gate CI runs: set `-min-push-rate`, `-max-p95`, or `-max-errors` and a sweep that misses any of them prints per-level breach lines to stderr and exits 2. All three flags default off; unset flags chang'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":11709}},"started_at_ms":1794842130104,"completed_at_ms":1794842130104}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:30.262Z","ordinal":3028,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-2f7c4615-90d4-42ef-b2c3-2af37e8a5cbb","process_id":"84506","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' 'e nothing.\\n\\n## Why this matters\\nThe results JSON is written \\\"for charting\\\" (README), but the process itself always exits 0 - `run()` returns `writeResults(...)` without inspecting the measured levels, so a deploy that halves push throughput still reads as a passing benchmark. Both reference tools in this space gate on results: [GitLab Performance Tool](https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/support/workflows/gpt_quick_start/) ships built-in success thresholds on throug\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"git-sync\": [\n    {\n      \"number\": 147,\n      \"title\": \"relay: request a thin pack when the target accepts one\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/147\",\n      \"head\": \"5729286c90689a8fa1535a96243ed6b2515cf01b\",\n      \"branch\": \"thin-pack-relay\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Closes #146.\\n\\nRelay fetches always ask the source for a self-contained pack (#4, #33), which `no-thin` targets such as go-git'\"'\"'s receive-pack and entire-server need. Against git'\"'\"'s own receive-pack (GitLab/Gitaly, `git http-backend`), a changed object then travels whole instead of as a delta against the version the target holds.\\n\\n`RefService` gets a `ThinPack` field, which the syncer sets once from `planner.ThinPackAllowed`: true only when the target'\"'\"'s advertisement is known and lacks `no-thin`. `FetchPack` then requests `thin-pack`, whose delta bases can only be objects reachable from the haves the target holds. The strategies are unchanged; `FetchToStore` and `FetchCommitParents` stay self-c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 145,\n      \"title\": \"relay: drop redundant haves with entire-maximal\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/145\",\n      \"head\": \"c74de38f8078c4fff7dd40c16358b97fca82f33f\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/entire-maximal-haves\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Adds git-sync support for entiredb'\"'\"'s `entire-maximal` ls-refs argument (entiredb change 4746). The target marks each listed ref that no other listed ref reaches, and relay fetches leave the unmarked target refs out of the haves they send the source. The goal is a lighter request for the source: the listing goes to the target, so the source gets no extra request.\\n\\n## What changes\\n\\n- `gitproto.ListMaximalTips` lists the target'\"'\"'s upload-pack refs with the marks, and `MaximalTips.Reduce` drops an unmarked ref only when every marked ref is still at its listed hash.\\n- Sync'\"'\"'s closure fetch, sync'\"'\"'s incremental relay, and replicate use the reduced haves. Bootstrap is unchanged.\\n- The listing runs at \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 142,\n      \"title\": \"gitproto: don'\"'\"'t let NoErrAlreadyUpToDate mask cancellation\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/142\",\n      \"head\": \"ff809e6e0b662db13a73a194265dddaa1f899df5\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/fetch-cancel-masks-uptodate\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #141.\\n\\n`FetchToStore` joins `ctx.Err()` with the fetch error whenever the context is canceled. When the fetch had no wants, that error is `git.NoErrAlreadyUpToDate`, and `errors.Is` matches the sentinel through the join, so every caller treated a canceled run as up to date. The fetch-only path in `syncer` then reported success.\\n\\nThe sentinel is returned before any I/O, so it is never a side effect of cancellation. `FetchToStore` now returns the cancellation alone in that case; other errors are still joined with the cancellation as before. Fixing it there covers all four callers (sync closure fetch, fetch-only, materialized tag refill, sha256convert) without touching them.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 123,\n      \"title\": \"Preserve concurrent updates and recognize already-current refs\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/123\",\n      \"head\": \"6547c9dfc7f43fe679e33d5d8c38a24c0bdd20db\",\n      \"branch\": \"nodo/read-target-before-source\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\nTwo syncs running at the same time can undo each other'\"'\"'s work. git-sync used to read source refs and then target refs. If another sync finished between those two reads, its newer target state became our expected-old value. The lease check then passed, and we pushed an older source snapshot over it, rewinding a branch or pruning a ref the other sync had just created.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- **Read target refs before source refs.** The expected-old snapshot can then never be newer than the source snapshot pushed over it.\\n- **Count work another sync already did as skipped.** A rejection can mean another writer moved the ref. These messages count: `remote ref has changed`, `stale info` and `a\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 122,\n      \"title\": \"fix: refuse POST redirects in guardRedirects unless FollowInfoRefsRedirect is set\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/122\",\n      \"head\": \"cbb8a22b1d7310b8a4ff736431513466c446c701\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/redirect-post-follows-only-with-flag\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"\\r\\nguardRedirects'\"'\"'s CheckRedirect closure now returns http.ErrUseLastResponse for POST redirects unless conn.FollowInfoRefsRedirect is set, matching vanilla git'\"'\"'s http.followRedirects=initial default where only the /info/refs GET auto-follows. GET redirect behaviour is unchanged.\\r\\n\\r\\nRequired restructuring NewHTTPConnWithClient so guardRedirects closes over the *HTTPConn directly (reading FollowInfoRefsRedirect live at redirect time) rather than running before the struct exists.\\r\\n\\r\\nAlso corrects TestGuardRedirectsAnchorsOnTheIssuedRequest which modelled a post-adoption cross-site redirect but never set FollowInfoRefsRedirect, making the scenario unreachable under the corrected logic.\\r\\n\\r\\nOn a c\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"entire-run\": []\n}'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/open-prs.json' 'e nothing.\\n\\n## Why this matters\\nThe results JSON is written \\\"for charting\\\" (README), but the process itself always exits 0 - `run()` returns `writeResults(...)` without inspecting the measured levels, so a deploy that halves push throughput still reads as a passing benchmark. Both reference tools in this space gate on results: [GitLab Performance Tool](https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/support/workflows/gpt_quick_start/) ships built-in success thresholds on throug\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"git-sync\": [\n    {\n      \"number\": 147,\n      \"title\": \"relay: request a thin pack when the target accepts one\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/147\",\n      \"head\": \"5729286c90689a8fa1535a96243ed6b2515cf01b\",\n      \"branch\": \"thin-pack-relay\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Closes #146.\\n\\nRelay fetches always ask the source for a self-contained pack (#4, #33), which `no-thin` targets such as go-git'\"'\"'s receive-pack and entire-server need. Against git'\"'\"'s own receive-pack (GitLab/Gitaly, `git http-backend`), a changed object then travels whole instead of as a delta against the version the target holds.\\n\\n`RefService` gets a `ThinPack` field, which the syncer sets once from `planner.ThinPackAllowed`: true only when the target'\"'\"'s advertisement is known and lacks `no-thin`. `FetchPack` then requests `thin-pack`, whose delta bases can only be objects reachable from the haves the target holds. The strategies are unchanged; `FetchToStore` and `FetchCommitParents` stay self-c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 145,\n      \"title\": \"relay: drop redundant haves with entire-maximal\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/145\",\n      \"head\": \"c74de38f8078c4fff7dd40c16358b97fca82f33f\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/entire-maximal-haves\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Adds git-sync support for entiredb'\"'\"'s `entire-maximal` ls-refs argument (entiredb change 4746). The target marks each listed ref that no other listed ref reaches, and relay fetches leave the unmarked target refs out of the haves they send the source. The goal is a lighter request for the source: the listing goes to the target, so the source gets no extra request.\\n\\n## What changes\\n\\n- `gitproto.ListMaximalTips` lists the target'\"'\"'s upload-pack refs with the marks, and `MaximalTips.Reduce` drops an unmarked ref only when every marked ref is still at its listed hash.\\n- Sync'\"'\"'s closure fetch, sync'\"'\"'s incremental relay, and replicate use the reduced haves. Bootstrap is unchanged.\\n- The listing runs at \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 142,\n      \"title\": \"gitproto: don'\"'\"'t let NoErrAlreadyUpToDate mask cancellation\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/142\",\n      \"head\": \"ff809e6e0b662db13a73a194265dddaa1f899df5\",\n      \"branch\": \"soph/fetch-cancel-masks-uptodate\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Fixes #141.\\n\\n`FetchToStore` joins `ctx.Err()` with the fetch error whenever the context is canceled. When the fetch had no wants, that error is `git.NoErrAlreadyUpToDate`, and `errors.Is` matches the sentinel through the join, so every caller treated a canceled run as up to date. The fetch-only path in `syncer` then reported success.\\n\\nThe sentinel is returned before any I/O, so it is never a side effect of cancellation. `FetchToStore` now returns the cancellation alone in that case; other errors are still joined with the cancellation as before. Fixing it there covers all four callers (sync closure fetch, fetch-only, materialized tag refill, sha256convert) without touching them.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 123,\n      \"title\": \"Preserve concurrent updates and recognize already-current refs\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/123\",\n      \"head\": \"6547c9dfc7f43fe679e33d5d8c38a24c0bdd20db\",\n      \"branch\": \"nodo/read-target-before-source\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"## Problem\\n\\nTwo syncs running at the same time can undo each other'\"'\"'s work. git-sync used to read source refs and then target refs. If another sync finished between those two reads, its newer target state became our expected-old value. The lease check then passed, and we pushed an older source snapshot over it, rewinding a branch or pruning a ref the other sync had just created.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- **Read target refs before source refs.** The expected-old snapshot can then never be newer than the source snapshot pushed over it.\\n- **Count work another sync already did as skipped.** A rejection can mean another writer moved the ref. These messages count: `remote ref has changed`, `stale info` and `a\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 122,\n      \"title\": \"fix: refuse POST redirects in guardRedirects unless FollowInfoRefsRedirect is set\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/122\",\n      \"head\": \"cbb8a22b1d7310b8a4ff736431513466c446c701\",\n      \"branch\": \"fix/redirect-post-follows-only-with-flag\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"\\r\\nguardRedirects'\"'\"'s CheckRedirect closure now returns http.ErrUseLastResponse for POST redirects unless conn.FollowInfoRefsRedirect is set, matching vanilla git'\"'\"'s http.followRedirects=initial default where only the /info/refs GET auto-follows. GET redirect behaviour is unchanged.\\r\\n\\r\\nRequired restructuring NewHTTPConnWithClient so guardRedirects closes over the *HTTPConn directly (reading FollowInfoRefsRedirect live at redirect time) rather than running before the struct exists.\\r\\n\\r\\nAlso corrects TestGuardRedirectsAnchorsOnTheIssuedRequest which modelled a post-adoption cross-site redirect but never set FollowInfoRefsRedirect, making the scenario unreachable under the corrected logic.\\r\\n\\r\\nOn a c\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"entire-run\": []\n}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":80209}},"started_at_ms":1794842130261,"completed_at_ms":1794842130262}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:30.404Z","ordinal":3029,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-bcdbf8a7-fdc8-4d11-b482-948460fbec45","process_id":"62697","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import pathlib,sys;p=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]);p.parent.mkdir(exist_ok=True);p.write_bytes(b\"\")' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/validation-history.json'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"list_files","cmd":"python3 -c 'import pathlib,sys;p=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]);p.parent.mkdir(exist_ok=True);p.write_bytes(b\"\")' /Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/validation-history.json","path":null}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":11458}},"started_at_ms":1794842130404,"completed_at_ms":1794842130404}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:30.551Z","ordinal":3030,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-6e645f2e-dc9f-4225-8a08-9c52b6cad1c0","process_id":"62689","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/validation-history.json' '{\n  \"commits\": [\n    {\n      \"sha\": \"9273a9f46bc3f3fd6c8bdaafe027b158b3a56d51\",\n      \"node_id\": \"REDACTED\",\n      \"commit\": {\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Stefan Haubold\",\n          \"email\": \"stefan@entire.io\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-11-04T12:34:59Z\"\n        },\n        \"committer\": {\n          \"name\": \"Stefan Haubold\",\n          \"email\": \"stefan@entire.io\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-11-04T15:49:31Z\"\n        },\n        \"message\": \"relay: cover shared history under the prefix; tighten the docs\\n\\nReview follow-up. Two integration tests name a prefix over refs that do\\nshare history: a new ref built on an existing one under the prefix, and\\na branch moved onto a commit the target holds only under the prefix.\\nBoth must leave a complete copy. assertSameRefs now reads every commit,\\ntree and blob reachable from each target ref, not only the tips.\\n\\nThe field'\"'\"'s doc states that entries are literal prefixes of target ref\\nnames after mappings, with a trailing-slash example, and that naming\\nshared history keeps the copy correct but can push a pack over a size\\nlimit. The validator'\"'\"'s doc says what it checks and what it does not.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M6K8WCDXZ3XP6CPD85W0XCV9\",\n        \"tree\": {\n          \"sha\": \"9402c76f8e3fcfc58e5684fad3ae8ddf625e206a\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/trees/9402c76f8e3fcfc58e5684fad3ae8ddf625e206a\"\n        },\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/commits/9273a9f46bc3f3fd6c8bdaafe027b158b3a56d51\",\n        \"comment_count\": 0,\n        \"verification\": {\n          \"verified\": false,\n          \"reason\": \"unsigned\",\n          \"signature\": null,\n          \"payload\": null,\n          \"verified_at\": null\n        }\n      },\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/9273a9f46bc3f3fd6c8bdaafe027b158b3a56d51\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/9273a9f46bc3f3fd6c8bdaafe027b158b3a56d51\",\n      \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/9273a9f46bc3f3fd6c8bdaafe027b158b3a56d51/comments\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"Soph\",\n        \"id\": 70741,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"committer\": {\n        \"login\": \"Soph\",\n        \"id\": 70741,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"parents\": [\n        {\n          \"sha\": \"ffa894e77a0f4f59ef7d83403a64446df9d236e0\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/ffa894e77a0f4f59ef7d83403a64446df9d236e0\",\n          \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/ffa894e77a0f4f59ef7d83403a64446df9d236e0\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"sha\": \"ffa894e77a0f4f59ef7d83403a64446df9d236e0\",\n      \"node_id\": \"REDACTED\",\n      \"commit\": {\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Stefan Haubold\",\n          \"email\": \"stefan@entire.io\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-11-04T11:19:44Z\"\n        },\n        \"committer\": {\n          \"name\": \"Stefan Haubold\",\n          \"email\": \"stefan@entire.io\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-11-04T15:49:30Z\"\n        },\n        \"message\": \"relay: leave unchanged independent-history tips out of the haves\\n\\nA relay fetch offers the source every target tip as a have. Refs that\\neach carry their own history, such as one orphan history per session\\ncheckpoint, cannot shorten a pack the run needs, so a repository with\\nthousands of them sent thousands of have lines for a run that moved one\\nbranch.\\n\\nRefScope.IndependentHistoryRefPrefixes names such namespaces. Under them\\na target ref is offered only when the run updates it, as its own old\\nvalue. Replicate and sync'\"'\"'s incremental relay honor it; sync'\"'\"'s closure\\nfetch and bootstrap keep every tip. Scope and prune are unchanged.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M6K4JKK20C9GY0A26BDZE14F\",\n        \"tree\": {\n          \"sha\": \"d09713862cccd011c3312352542d7edc34ee3909\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/trees/d09713862cccd011c3312352542d7edc34ee3909\"\n        },\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/commits/ffa894e77a0f4f59ef7d83403a64446df9d236e0\",\n        \"comment_count\": 0,\n        \"verification\": {\n          \"verified\": false,\n          \"reason\": \"unsigned\",\n          \"signature\": null,\n          \"payload\": null,\n          \"verified_at\": null\n        }\n      },\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/ffa894e77a0f4f59ef7d83403a64446df9d236e0\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/ffa894e77a0f4f59ef7d83403a64446df9d236e0\",\n      \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/ffa894e77a0f4f59ef7d83403a64446df9d236e0/comments\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"Soph\",\n        \"id\": 70741,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"committer\": {\n        \"login\": \"Soph\",\n        \"id\": 70741,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"parents\": [\n        {\n          \"sha\": \"a870385c5c973bd251e0218032b5fd1af8368ee9\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/a870385c5c973bd251e0218032b5fd1af8368ee9\",\n          \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/a870385c5c973bd251e0218032b5fd1af8368ee9\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"sha\": \"a81db6a5d51320d109eaf08f117808e687120189\",\n      \"node_id\": \"REDACTED\",\n      \"commit\": {\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Andrea Nodari\",\n          \"email\": \"and.nodari@gmail.com\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-09-11T15:43:41Z\"\n        },\n        \"committer\": {\n          \"name\": \"Andrea Nodari\",\n          \"email\": \"and.nodari@gmail.com\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-09-11T15:43:41Z\"\n        },\n        \"message\": \"fix: reject inert and unmatchable scoped empty policies\\n\\nThree review findings on the include-prefix scope.\\n\\nAllowEmptyScope was silently inert outside replicate: nothing else has an\\nempty-set branch to reach, so a sync-mode caller with the policy set got\\nthe historical \\\"no source refs matched\\\" and kept the stale target refs it\\nasked to prune. Rejected now at both edges, like the AllowEmptySource\\nmode rule it mirrors.\\n\\nAn include prefix that is blank or does not start with refs/ scopes a\\nrequest to nothing, and nothing is a legal scope: the run plans zero refs\\nand succeeds, so under AllowEmptyScope and prune the typo reports a\\nhealthy no-op forever. validation.ValidateIncludeRefPrefixes rejects the\\nshape at the request edge and at the syncer edge every entry shares.\\n\\nhasBootstrapResumeMarker and pruneDeletesNothingInScope still asked about\\nexclusions directly, which the include prefixes would not have reached.\\nBoth now ask planner.InScope, so the promise in its doc holds across the\\ntwo packages. Safe since replicateBootstrapRoute stands down on an empty\\ndesired set: the prune-scope walk can no longer send such a run to\\nbootstrap.\\n\\nAlso fixes the hasAnyPrefix comment, which had the inclusion half\\nbackwards — honoring a blank prefix would widen an inclusion to\\neverything, not narrow it to nothing.\\n\\nCOR-1642\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XKc1v3szE19sjrjWAzo7cz\",\n        \"tree\": {\n          \"sha\": \"91d95cf38929e8fd3d3170d3bde760c5c9ca2acc\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/trees/91d95cf38929e8fd3d3170d3bde760c5c9ca2acc\"\n        },\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/commits/a81db6a5d51320d109eaf08f117808e687120189\",\n        \"comment_count\": 0,\n        \"verification\": {\n          \"verified\": false,\n          \"reason\": \"unsigned\",\n          \"signature\": null,\n          \"payload\": null,\n          \"verified_at\": null\n        }\n      },\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/a81db6a5d51320d109eaf08f117808e687120189\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/a81db6a5d51320d109eaf08f117808e687120189\",\n      \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/a81db6a5d51320d109eaf08f117808e687120189/comments\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"nodo\",\n        \"id\": 829178,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjgyOTE3OA==\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/829178?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/nodo\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"committer\": {\n        \"login\": \"nodo\",\n        \"id\": 829178,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjgyOTE3OA==\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/829178?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/nodo\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"parents\": [\n        {\n          \"sha\": \"4e4568358ae9b781b5996d7e7417a5d2c21f56bc\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/4e4568358ae9b781b5996d7e7417a5d2c21f56bc\",\n          \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/4e4568358ae9b781b5996d7e7417a5d2c21f56bc\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"sha\": \"0f6a015e5a43857a0d579facf607c25a86126124\",\n      \"node_id\": \"REDACTED\",\n      \"commit\": {\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Stefan Haubold\",\n          \"email\": \"stefan@entire.io\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-19T13:14:37Z\"\n        },\n        \"committer\": {\n          \"name\": \"GitHub\",\n          \"email\": \"noreply@github.com\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-20T15:49:02Z\"\n        },\n        \"message\": \"Validate ref names arriving from a remote\\n\\nNothing checked the names a remote advertises, and git-sync acts on them\\nin two ways that make a malformed one dangerous.\\n\\nconvert-sha256 writes them to disk. go-git resolves a ref name through\\nthe repository filesystem, so \\\"refs/heads/../../config\\\" escapes\\nrefs/heads. go-billy clamps the traversal at the repository root, so this\\nis repository corruption rather than arbitrary file write — but config,\\nHEAD, and packed-refs are all in range, with the content constrained to\\nan object hash.\\n\\nRef-update commands embed them in the receive-pack request. receive-pack\\nreads a feature list from everything after the first NUL on a command\\nline, so a source advertising a name containing NUL can inject\\ncapabilities into the push git-sync sends to the target.\\n\\nValidation defers to plumbing.ReferenceName.Validate, which implements\\ngit'\"'\"'s check_refname_format: \\\"..\\\", NUL, CR, LF, other control characters,\\nDEL, space, \\\"~^:?*[\\\", backslash, \\\"@{\\\", a \\\".lock\\\" suffix, a leading dot,\\nempty components, and a leading dash on a branch or tag. Deferring rather\\nthan hand-rolling keeps git-sync'\"'\"'s notion of a valid ref identical to\\ngit'\"'\"'s, so nothing git considers legitimate gets skipped — verified\\nagainst refs/pull/*, refs/notes/*, and nested branch names.\\n\\nIt runs at the two decode boundaries (AdvRefsToSlice and decodeV2LSRefs)\\nrather than at each call site, so every path that reads an advertisement\\nis covered by construction, on both the source and target side. A skipped\\ntarget ref is also one the planner never sees, so it is never picked as a\\nprune candidate — the safe direction.\\n\\nBad names are skipped with a warning rather than failing the run,\\nmatching how per-ref push rejections behave under BestEffort: one\\nmalformed ref upstream should not stop a mirror. The warning prints names\\nwith %q, because they are remote-controlled and an embedded escape\\nsequence would otherwise reach the terminal; the individual list is\\ncapped while the count still covers everything skipped.\\n\\n--map values get the same validation but are rejected outright rather\\nthan skipped. They are configuration, and a mapped target ref reaches the\\nsame places an advertised one does, so failing at startup beats silently\\nnot mirroring what was asked for.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M0D2HM0JN5QVYSWAPFZCSPNR\",\n        \"tree\": {\n          \"sha\": \"f061341c01a34e463333a1a1a84c12d39e2f24b8\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/trees/f061341c01a34e463333a1a1a84c12d39e2f24b8\"\n        },\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/g'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/validation-history.json' '{\n  \"commits\": [\n    {\n      \"sha\": \"9273a9f46bc3f3fd6c8bdaafe027b158b3a56d51\",\n      \"node_id\": \"REDACTED\",\n      \"commit\": {\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Stefan Haubold\",\n          \"email\": \"stefan@entire.io\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-11-04T12:34:59Z\"\n        },\n        \"committer\": {\n          \"name\": \"Stefan Haubold\",\n          \"email\": \"stefan@entire.io\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-11-04T15:49:31Z\"\n        },\n        \"message\": \"relay: cover shared history under the prefix; tighten the docs\\n\\nReview follow-up. Two integration tests name a prefix over refs that do\\nshare history: a new ref built on an existing one under the prefix, and\\na branch moved onto a commit the target holds only under the prefix.\\nBoth must leave a complete copy. assertSameRefs now reads every commit,\\ntree and blob reachable from each target ref, not only the tips.\\n\\nThe field'\"'\"'s doc states that entries are literal prefixes of target ref\\nnames after mappings, with a trailing-slash example, and that naming\\nshared history keeps the copy correct but can push a pack over a size\\nlimit. The validator'\"'\"'s doc says what it checks and what it does not.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M6K8WCDXZ3XP6CPD85W0XCV9\",\n        \"tree\": {\n          \"sha\": \"9402c76f8e3fcfc58e5684fad3ae8ddf625e206a\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/trees/9402c76f8e3fcfc58e5684fad3ae8ddf625e206a\"\n        },\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/commits/9273a9f46bc3f3fd6c8bdaafe027b158b3a56d51\",\n        \"comment_count\": 0,\n        \"verification\": {\n          \"verified\": false,\n          \"reason\": \"unsigned\",\n          \"signature\": null,\n          \"payload\": null,\n          \"verified_at\": null\n        }\n      },\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/9273a9f46bc3f3fd6c8bdaafe027b158b3a56d51\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/9273a9f46bc3f3fd6c8bdaafe027b158b3a56d51\",\n      \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/9273a9f46bc3f3fd6c8bdaafe027b158b3a56d51/comments\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"Soph\",\n        \"id\": 70741,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"committer\": {\n        \"login\": \"Soph\",\n        \"id\": 70741,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"parents\": [\n        {\n          \"sha\": \"ffa894e77a0f4f59ef7d83403a64446df9d236e0\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/ffa894e77a0f4f59ef7d83403a64446df9d236e0\",\n          \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/ffa894e77a0f4f59ef7d83403a64446df9d236e0\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"sha\": \"ffa894e77a0f4f59ef7d83403a64446df9d236e0\",\n      \"node_id\": \"REDACTED\",\n      \"commit\": {\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Stefan Haubold\",\n          \"email\": \"stefan@entire.io\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-11-04T11:19:44Z\"\n        },\n        \"committer\": {\n          \"name\": \"Stefan Haubold\",\n          \"email\": \"stefan@entire.io\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-11-04T15:49:30Z\"\n        },\n        \"message\": \"relay: leave unchanged independent-history tips out of the haves\\n\\nA relay fetch offers the source every target tip as a have. Refs that\\neach carry their own history, such as one orphan history per session\\ncheckpoint, cannot shorten a pack the run needs, so a repository with\\nthousands of them sent thousands of have lines for a run that moved one\\nbranch.\\n\\nRefScope.IndependentHistoryRefPrefixes names such namespaces. Under them\\na target ref is offered only when the run updates it, as its own old\\nvalue. Replicate and sync'\"'\"'s incremental relay honor it; sync'\"'\"'s closure\\nfetch and bootstrap keep every tip. Scope and prune are unchanged.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M6K4JKK20C9GY0A26BDZE14F\",\n        \"tree\": {\n          \"sha\": \"d09713862cccd011c3312352542d7edc34ee3909\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/trees/d09713862cccd011c3312352542d7edc34ee3909\"\n        },\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/commits/ffa894e77a0f4f59ef7d83403a64446df9d236e0\",\n        \"comment_count\": 0,\n        \"verification\": {\n          \"verified\": false,\n          \"reason\": \"unsigned\",\n          \"signature\": null,\n          \"payload\": null,\n          \"verified_at\": null\n        }\n      },\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/ffa894e77a0f4f59ef7d83403a64446df9d236e0\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/ffa894e77a0f4f59ef7d83403a64446df9d236e0\",\n      \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/ffa894e77a0f4f59ef7d83403a64446df9d236e0/comments\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"Soph\",\n        \"id\": 70741,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"committer\": {\n        \"login\": \"Soph\",\n        \"id\": 70741,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"parents\": [\n        {\n          \"sha\": \"a870385c5c973bd251e0218032b5fd1af8368ee9\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/a870385c5c973bd251e0218032b5fd1af8368ee9\",\n          \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/a870385c5c973bd251e0218032b5fd1af8368ee9\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"sha\": \"a81db6a5d51320d109eaf08f117808e687120189\",\n      \"node_id\": \"REDACTED\",\n      \"commit\": {\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Andrea Nodari\",\n          \"email\": \"and.nodari@gmail.com\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-09-11T15:43:41Z\"\n        },\n        \"committer\": {\n          \"name\": \"Andrea Nodari\",\n          \"email\": \"and.nodari@gmail.com\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-09-11T15:43:41Z\"\n        },\n        \"message\": \"fix: reject inert and unmatchable scoped empty policies\\n\\nThree review findings on the include-prefix scope.\\n\\nAllowEmptyScope was silently inert outside replicate: nothing else has an\\nempty-set branch to reach, so a sync-mode caller with the policy set got\\nthe historical \\\"no source refs matched\\\" and kept the stale target refs it\\nasked to prune. Rejected now at both edges, like the AllowEmptySource\\nmode rule it mirrors.\\n\\nAn include prefix that is blank or does not start with refs/ scopes a\\nrequest to nothing, and nothing is a legal scope: the run plans zero refs\\nand succeeds, so under AllowEmptyScope and prune the typo reports a\\nhealthy no-op forever. validation.ValidateIncludeRefPrefixes rejects the\\nshape at the request edge and at the syncer edge every entry shares.\\n\\nhasBootstrapResumeMarker and pruneDeletesNothingInScope still asked about\\nexclusions directly, which the include prefixes would not have reached.\\nBoth now ask planner.InScope, so the promise in its doc holds across the\\ntwo packages. Safe since replicateBootstrapRoute stands down on an empty\\ndesired set: the prune-scope walk can no longer send such a run to\\nbootstrap.\\n\\nAlso fixes the hasAnyPrefix comment, which had the inclusion half\\nbackwards — honoring a blank prefix would widen an inclusion to\\neverything, not narrow it to nothing.\\n\\nCOR-1642\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XKc1v3szE19sjrjWAzo7cz\",\n        \"tree\": {\n          \"sha\": \"91d95cf38929e8fd3d3170d3bde760c5c9ca2acc\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/trees/91d95cf38929e8fd3d3170d3bde760c5c9ca2acc\"\n        },\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/commits/a81db6a5d51320d109eaf08f117808e687120189\",\n        \"comment_count\": 0,\n        \"verification\": {\n          \"verified\": false,\n          \"reason\": \"unsigned\",\n          \"signature\": null,\n          \"payload\": null,\n          \"verified_at\": null\n        }\n      },\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/a81db6a5d51320d109eaf08f117808e687120189\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/a81db6a5d51320d109eaf08f117808e687120189\",\n      \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/a81db6a5d51320d109eaf08f117808e687120189/comments\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"nodo\",\n        \"id\": 829178,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjgyOTE3OA==\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/829178?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/nodo\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"committer\": {\n        \"login\": \"nodo\",\n        \"id\": 829178,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjgyOTE3OA==\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/829178?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/nodo\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nodo/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"parents\": [\n        {\n          \"sha\": \"4e4568358ae9b781b5996d7e7417a5d2c21f56bc\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/4e4568358ae9b781b5996d7e7417a5d2c21f56bc\",\n          \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/4e4568358ae9b781b5996d7e7417a5d2c21f56bc\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"sha\": \"0f6a015e5a43857a0d579facf607c25a86126124\",\n      \"node_id\": \"REDACTED\",\n      \"commit\": {\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Stefan Haubold\",\n          \"email\": \"stefan@entire.io\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-19T13:14:37Z\"\n        },\n        \"committer\": {\n          \"name\": \"GitHub\",\n          \"email\": \"noreply@github.com\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-08-20T15:49:02Z\"\n        },\n        \"message\": \"Validate ref names arriving from a remote\\n\\nNothing checked the names a remote advertises, and git-sync acts on them\\nin two ways that make a malformed one dangerous.\\n\\nconvert-sha256 writes them to disk. go-git resolves a ref name through\\nthe repository filesystem, so \\\"refs/heads/../../config\\\" escapes\\nrefs/heads. go-billy clamps the traversal at the repository root, so this\\nis repository corruption rather than arbitrary file write — but config,\\nHEAD, and packed-refs are all in range, with the content constrained to\\nan object hash.\\n\\nRef-update commands embed them in the receive-pack request. receive-pack\\nreads a feature list from everything after the first NUL on a command\\nline, so a source advertising a name containing NUL can inject\\ncapabilities into the push git-sync sends to the target.\\n\\nValidation defers to plumbing.ReferenceName.Validate, which implements\\ngit'\"'\"'s check_refname_format: \\\"..\\\", NUL, CR, LF, other control characters,\\nDEL, space, \\\"~^:?*[\\\", backslash, \\\"@{\\\", a \\\".lock\\\" suffix, a leading dot,\\nempty components, and a leading dash on a branch or tag. Deferring rather\\nthan hand-rolling keeps git-sync'\"'\"'s notion of a valid ref identical to\\ngit'\"'\"'s, so nothing git considers legitimate gets skipped — verified\\nagainst refs/pull/*, refs/notes/*, and nested branch names.\\n\\nIt runs at the two decode boundaries (AdvRefsToSlice and decodeV2LSRefs)\\nrather than at each call site, so every path that reads an advertisement\\nis covered by construction, on both the source and target side. A skipped\\ntarget ref is also one the planner never sees, so it is never picked as a\\nprune candidate — the safe direction.\\n\\nBad names are skipped with a warning rather than failing the run,\\nmatching how per-ref push rejections behave under BestEffort: one\\nmalformed ref upstream should not stop a mirror. The warning prints names\\nwith %q, because they are remote-controlled and an embedded escape\\nsequence would otherwise reach the terminal; the individual list is\\ncapped while the count still covers everything skipped.\\n\\n--map values get the same validation but are rejected outright rather\\nthan skipped. They are configuration, and a mapped target ref reaches the\\nsame places an advertised one does, so failing at startup beats silently\\nnot mirroring what was asked for.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M0D2HM0JN5QVYSWAPFZCSPNR\",\n        \"tree\": {\n          \"sha\": \"f061341c01a34e463333a1a1a84c12d39e2f24b8\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/trees/f061341c01a34e463333a1a1a84c12d39e2f24b8\"\n        },\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/g'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":11125}},"started_at_ms":1794842130550,"completed_at_ms":1794842130551}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:30.690Z","ordinal":3031,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ed0743da-5360-4064-ad81-2cf112e561c6","process_id":"28943","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/validation-history.json' 'it-sync/git/commits/0f6a015e5a43857a0d579facf607c25a86126124\",\n        \"comment_count\": 0,\n        \"verification\": {\n          \"verified\": true,\n          \"reason\": \"valid\",\n          \"signature\": \"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\\n\\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhyHuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/5MQAAwO+IOJ6mN0zJRAOuC3EF1F\\nHrJkt8pXaZ/wa5mw/REDACTED\\n8ydq3Hok6GADdsjqc4ddqT8BJt9dN/REDACTED\\n5g2dzJ4JCMoX//REDACTED\\nREDACTED\\n+h63PoQOdtu/REDACTED/sJHeIp/cl0bS\\nREDACTED\\nREDACTED/C7Q1d/kyHy6urd\\nREDACTED/REDACTED\\nREDACTED/FKGhxAc3m4Kz6sOEEZ\\nREDACTED\\n5IvwHStKSfQPLjxwO1OV\\n=qJF/\\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\\n\",\n          \"payload\": \"tree f061341c01a34e463333a1a1a84c12d39e2f24b8\\nparent 4e816de76249ee4a91659879d57fa0e0fe9ae240\\nauthor Stefan Haubold <stefan@entire.io> 1787145277 +0200\\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787240942 +0200\\n\\nValidate ref names arriving from a remote\\n\\nNothing checked the names a remote advertises, and git-sync acts on them\\nin two ways that make a malformed one dangerous.\\n\\nconvert-sha256 writes them to disk. go-git resolves a ref name through\\nthe repository filesystem, so \\\"refs/heads/../../config\\\" escapes\\nrefs/heads. go-billy clamps the traversal at the repository root, so this\\nis repository corruption rather than arbitrary file write — but config,\\nHEAD, and packed-refs are all in range, with the content constrained to\\nan object hash.\\n\\nRef-update commands embed them in the receive-pack request. receive-pack\\nreads a feature list from everything after the first NUL on a command\\nline, so a source advertising a name containing NUL can inject\\ncapabilities into the push git-sync sends to the target.\\n\\nValidation defers to plumbing.ReferenceName.Validate, which implements\\ngit'\"'\"'s check_refname_format: \\\"..\\\", NUL, CR, LF, other control characters,\\nDEL, space, \\\"~^:?*[\\\", backslash, \\\"@{\\\", a \\\".lock\\\" suffix, a leading dot,\\nempty components, and a leading dash on a branch or tag. Deferring rather\\nthan hand-rolling keeps git-sync'\"'\"'s notion of a valid ref identical to\\ngit'\"'\"'s, so nothing git considers legitimate gets skipped — verified\\nagainst refs/pull/*, refs/notes/*, and nested branch names.\\n\\nIt runs at the two decode boundaries (AdvRefsToSlice and decodeV2LSRefs)\\nrather than at each call site, so every path that reads an advertisement\\nis covered by construction, on both the source and target side. A skipped\\ntarget ref is also one the planner never sees, so it is never picked as a\\nprune candidate — the safe direction.\\n\\nBad names are skipped with a warning rather than failing the run,\\nmatching how per-ref push rejections behave under BestEffort: one\\nmalformed ref upstream should not stop a mirror. The warning prints names\\nwith %q, because they are remote-controlled and an embedded escape\\nsequence would otherwise reach the terminal; the individual list is\\ncapped while the count still covers everything skipped.\\n\\n--map values get the same validation but are rejected outright rather\\nthan skipped. They are configuration, and a mapped target ref reaches the\\nsame places an advertised one does, so failing at startup beats silently\\nnot mirroring what was asked for.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M0D2HM0JN5QVYSWAPFZCSPNR\\n\",\n          \"verified_at\": \"2026-08-20T15:49:11Z\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/0f6a015e5a43857a0d579facf607c25a86126124\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/0f6a015e5a43857a0d579facf607c25a86126124\",\n      \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/0f6a015e5a43857a0d579facf607c25a86126124/comments\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"Soph\",\n        \"id\": 70741,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"committer\": {\n        \"login\": \"web-flow\",\n        \"id\": 19864447,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/web-flow\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"parents\": [\n        {\n          \"sha\": \"4e816de76249ee4a91659879d57fa0e0fe9ae240\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/4e816de76249ee4a91659879d57fa0e0fe9ae240\",\n          \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/4e816de76249ee4a91659879d57fa0e0fe9ae240\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"sha\": \"720b519abd4a1361b470c02f356a8bc697d754be\",\n      \"node_id\": \"REDACTED\",\n      \"commit\": {\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Stefan Haubold\",\n          \"email\": \"stefan@entire.io\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-05-09T19:37:35Z\"\n        },\n        \"committer\": {\n          \"name\": \"Stefan Haubold\",\n          \"email\": \"stefan@entire.io\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-05-09T19:37:35Z\"\n        },\n        \"message\": \"Simplify after review: dedupe, trim comments, flatten conditionals\\n\\n- Extract addPruneCandidates helper; the prune-managed switch is no\\n  longer pasted into both BuildPlans and BuildReplicationPlans.\\n- Extract syncSession.finalizeCounts; the applyRejections + counter\\n  loop block is no longer duplicated between runSync and runReplicate.\\n- Use convert.DesiredRefsForPlans in the bootstrap tail phase instead\\n  of building gitproto.DesiredRef inline.\\n- Drop the defensive pushed < 0 clamp in bootstrapWithInputs; if\\n  Pushed and Warned ever disagreed, masking it would hide the bug.\\n- Fold the \\\"AllRefs implies BestEffort\\\" coupling into allRefsFlag via\\n  cobra PreRunE instead of pasting the if-statement into two RunE\\n  bodies.\\n- Flatten the 3-level nested conditional in NormalizeMapping.\\n- Trim verbose doc blocks: RefKind, ActionWarn, RefScope.AllRefs,\\n  SyncPolicy.BestEffort, Pusher.OnRejection, syncSession.rejections,\\n  the bootstrap tail-phase comment, and the test docstrings that\\n  narrated motivation rather than the assertion. Removes the two\\n  empty-branch comments in the count switches by collapsing\\n  ActionWarn/Skip/Block into one no-op branch.\\n\\nNet: -89 lines, all 8 AllRefs integration + smoke tests still pass.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nEntire-Checkpoint: f8bbc26df8b3\",\n        \"tree\": {\n          \"sha\": \"90c554eafa29a89ebd94d1baf8738cf217d9beac\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/trees/90c554eafa29a89ebd94d1baf8738cf217d9beac\"\n        },\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/commits/720b519abd4a1361b470c02f356a8bc697d754be\",\n        \"comment_count\": 0,\n        \"verification\": {\n          \"verified\": false,\n          \"reason\": \"unsigned\",\n          \"signature\": null,\n          \"payload\": null,\n          \"verified_at\": null\n        }\n      },\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/720b519abd4a1361b470c02f356a8bc697d754be\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/720b519abd4a1361b470c02f356a8bc697d754be\",\n      \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/720b519abd4a1361b470c02f356a8bc697d754be/comments\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"Soph\",\n        \"id\": 70741,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"committer\": {\n        \"login\": \"Soph\",\n        \"id\": 70741,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"parents\": [\n        {\n          \"sha\": \"b79fc08a90738048d74c6f619dd202e122659879\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/b79fc08a90738048d74c6f619dd202e122659879\",\n          \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/b79fc08a90738048d74c6f619dd202e122659879\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"sha\": \"6814963e14df05bbb824f4466051aeed27c970cd\",\n      \"node_id\": \"REDACTED\",\n      \"commit\": {\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Stefan Haubold\",\n          \"email\": \"stefan@entire.io\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-05-09T17:53:02Z\"\n        },\n        \"committer\": {\n          \"name\": \"Stefan Haubold\",\n          \"email\": \"stefan@entire.io\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-05-09T17:53:02Z\"\n        },\n        \"message\": \"Add RefScope.AllRefs to broaden mirroring beyond branches and tags\\n\\nIntroduce a third RefKindOther for refs/* namespaces outside refs/heads/\\nand refs/tags/ (notes, pulls, replace, custom). Validation accepts those\\nmappings only when the new RefScope.AllRefs flag is set; without it the\\nexisting strict branch/tag flow stays loud about unsupported refs.\\n\\nWhen AllRefs is set, BuildDesiredRefs picks up every refs/* on the\\nsource, RefPrefixes collapses to a single \\\"refs/\\\" so v2 ls-refs returns\\nthe broader set, and prune treats unmanaged other-kind target refs as\\ndelete candidates. Other-kind refs follow branch-style semantics\\n(fast-forward / force) in PlanRef, and the existing relay paths fall\\nthrough to the materialized push because their kind switches default\\nto \\\"unsupported\\\", which is the right behavior for a first cut.\\n\\nThis wires the field through the public RefScope, ProbeRequest,\\ninternalbridge, syncer.Config, and the unstable client. CLI surface\\nand best-effort failure handling come in follow-up commits.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 82d903ebce8d\",\n        \"tree\": {\n          \"sha\": \"a500cf65bdb1d7c4c263e481ce57fa40d6d225b8\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/trees/a500cf65bdb1d7c4c263e481ce57fa40d6d225b8\"\n        },\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/commits/6814963e14df05bbb824f4466051aeed27c970cd\",\n        \"comment_count\": 0,\n        \"verification\": {\n          \"verified\": false,\n          \"reason\": \"unsigned\",\n          \"signature\": null,\n          \"payload\": null,\n          \"verified_at\": null\n        }\n      },\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/6814963e14df05bbb824f4466051aeed27c970cd\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/6814963e14df05bbb824f4466051aeed27c970cd\",\n      \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/6814963e14df05bbb824f4466051aeed27c970cd/comments\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"Soph\",\n        \"id\": 70741,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"committer\": {\n        \"login\": \"Soph\",\n        \"id\": 70741,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"parents\": [\n        {\n          \"sha\": \"dbd5151fea14090590de08d293c14a5d1677fb0b\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/dbd5151fea14090590de08d293c14a5d1677fb0b\",\n          \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/dbd5151fea14090590de08d293c14a5d1677fb0b\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"sha\": \"5c60d93026dabd1538705d512e2250c362fde1e1\",\n      \"node_id\": \"REDACTED\",\n      \"commit\": {\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Stefan Haubold\",\n          \"email\": \"stefan@entire.io\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-04-30T08:21:37Z\"\n        },\n        \"committer\": {\n          \"name\": \"Stefan Haubold\",\n          \"email\": \"stefan@entire.io\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-04-30T08:21:37Z\"\n        },\n        \"message\": \"even more general url validation\\n\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 8feaf84a600f\",\n        \"tree\": {\n          \"sha\": \"44ee5aa847d3fc7c432a1d743bc1fbddaa023cd2\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/trees/44ee5aa847d3fc7c432a1d743bc1fbddaa023cd2\"\n        },\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/commits/5c60d93026dabd1538705d512e2250c362fde1e1\",\n        \"comment_count\": 0,\n        \"verification\": {\n          \"verified\": false,\n          \"reason\": \"un'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/validation-history.json' 'it-sync/git/commits/0f6a015e5a43857a0d579facf607c25a86126124\",\n        \"comment_count\": 0,\n        \"verification\": {\n          \"verified\": true,\n          \"reason\": \"valid\",\n          \"signature\": \"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\\n\\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhyHuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/5MQAAwO+IOJ6mN0zJRAOuC3EF1F\\nHrJkt8pXaZ/wa5mw/REDACTED\\n8ydq3Hok6GADdsjqc4ddqT8BJt9dN/REDACTED\\n5g2dzJ4JCMoX//REDACTED\\nREDACTED\\n+h63PoQOdtu/REDACTED/sJHeIp/cl0bS\\nREDACTED\\nREDACTED/C7Q1d/kyHy6urd\\nREDACTED/REDACTED\\nREDACTED/FKGhxAc3m4Kz6sOEEZ\\nREDACTED\\n5IvwHStKSfQPLjxwO1OV\\n=qJF/\\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\\n\",\n          \"payload\": \"tree f061341c01a34e463333a1a1a84c12d39e2f24b8\\nparent 4e816de76249ee4a91659879d57fa0e0fe9ae240\\nauthor Stefan Haubold <stefan@entire.io> 1787145277 +0200\\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787240942 +0200\\n\\nValidate ref names arriving from a remote\\n\\nNothing checked the names a remote advertises, and git-sync acts on them\\nin two ways that make a malformed one dangerous.\\n\\nconvert-sha256 writes them to disk. go-git resolves a ref name through\\nthe repository filesystem, so \\\"refs/heads/../../config\\\" escapes\\nrefs/heads. go-billy clamps the traversal at the repository root, so this\\nis repository corruption rather than arbitrary file write — but config,\\nHEAD, and packed-refs are all in range, with the content constrained to\\nan object hash.\\n\\nRef-update commands embed them in the receive-pack request. receive-pack\\nreads a feature list from everything after the first NUL on a command\\nline, so a source advertising a name containing NUL can inject\\ncapabilities into the push git-sync sends to the target.\\n\\nValidation defers to plumbing.ReferenceName.Validate, which implements\\ngit'\"'\"'s check_refname_format: \\\"..\\\", NUL, CR, LF, other control characters,\\nDEL, space, \\\"~^:?*[\\\", backslash, \\\"@{\\\", a \\\".lock\\\" suffix, a leading dot,\\nempty components, and a leading dash on a branch or tag. Deferring rather\\nthan hand-rolling keeps git-sync'\"'\"'s notion of a valid ref identical to\\ngit'\"'\"'s, so nothing git considers legitimate gets skipped — verified\\nagainst refs/pull/*, refs/notes/*, and nested branch names.\\n\\nIt runs at the two decode boundaries (AdvRefsToSlice and decodeV2LSRefs)\\nrather than at each call site, so every path that reads an advertisement\\nis covered by construction, on both the source and target side. A skipped\\ntarget ref is also one the planner never sees, so it is never picked as a\\nprune candidate — the safe direction.\\n\\nBad names are skipped with a warning rather than failing the run,\\nmatching how per-ref push rejections behave under BestEffort: one\\nmalformed ref upstream should not stop a mirror. The warning prints names\\nwith %q, because they are remote-controlled and an embedded escape\\nsequence would otherwise reach the terminal; the individual list is\\ncapped while the count still covers everything skipped.\\n\\n--map values get the same validation but are rejected outright rather\\nthan skipped. They are configuration, and a mapped target ref reaches the\\nsame places an advertised one does, so failing at startup beats silently\\nnot mirroring what was asked for.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M0D2HM0JN5QVYSWAPFZCSPNR\\n\",\n          \"verified_at\": \"2026-08-20T15:49:11Z\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/0f6a015e5a43857a0d579facf607c25a86126124\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/0f6a015e5a43857a0d579facf607c25a86126124\",\n      \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/0f6a015e5a43857a0d579facf607c25a86126124/comments\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"Soph\",\n        \"id\": 70741,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"committer\": {\n        \"login\": \"web-flow\",\n        \"id\": 19864447,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/web-flow\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"parents\": [\n        {\n          \"sha\": \"4e816de76249ee4a91659879d57fa0e0fe9ae240\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/4e816de76249ee4a91659879d57fa0e0fe9ae240\",\n          \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/4e816de76249ee4a91659879d57fa0e0fe9ae240\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"sha\": \"720b519abd4a1361b470c02f356a8bc697d754be\",\n      \"node_id\": \"REDACTED\",\n      \"commit\": {\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Stefan Haubold\",\n          \"email\": \"stefan@entire.io\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-05-09T19:37:35Z\"\n        },\n        \"committer\": {\n          \"name\": \"Stefan Haubold\",\n          \"email\": \"stefan@entire.io\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-05-09T19:37:35Z\"\n        },\n        \"message\": \"Simplify after review: dedupe, trim comments, flatten conditionals\\n\\n- Extract addPruneCandidates helper; the prune-managed switch is no\\n  longer pasted into both BuildPlans and BuildReplicationPlans.\\n- Extract syncSession.finalizeCounts; the applyRejections + counter\\n  loop block is no longer duplicated between runSync and runReplicate.\\n- Use convert.DesiredRefsForPlans in the bootstrap tail phase instead\\n  of building gitproto.DesiredRef inline.\\n- Drop the defensive pushed < 0 clamp in bootstrapWithInputs; if\\n  Pushed and Warned ever disagreed, masking it would hide the bug.\\n- Fold the \\\"AllRefs implies BestEffort\\\" coupling into allRefsFlag via\\n  cobra PreRunE instead of pasting the if-statement into two RunE\\n  bodies.\\n- Flatten the 3-level nested conditional in NormalizeMapping.\\n- Trim verbose doc blocks: RefKind, ActionWarn, RefScope.AllRefs,\\n  SyncPolicy.BestEffort, Pusher.OnRejection, syncSession.rejections,\\n  the bootstrap tail-phase comment, and the test docstrings that\\n  narrated motivation rather than the assertion. Removes the two\\n  empty-branch comments in the count switches by collapsing\\n  ActionWarn/Skip/Block into one no-op branch.\\n\\nNet: -89 lines, all 8 AllRefs integration + smoke tests still pass.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nEntire-Checkpoint: f8bbc26df8b3\",\n        \"tree\": {\n          \"sha\": \"90c554eafa29a89ebd94d1baf8738cf217d9beac\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/trees/90c554eafa29a89ebd94d1baf8738cf217d9beac\"\n        },\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/commits/720b519abd4a1361b470c02f356a8bc697d754be\",\n        \"comment_count\": 0,\n        \"verification\": {\n          \"verified\": false,\n          \"reason\": \"unsigned\",\n          \"signature\": null,\n          \"payload\": null,\n          \"verified_at\": null\n        }\n      },\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/720b519abd4a1361b470c02f356a8bc697d754be\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/720b519abd4a1361b470c02f356a8bc697d754be\",\n      \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/720b519abd4a1361b470c02f356a8bc697d754be/comments\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"Soph\",\n        \"id\": 70741,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"committer\": {\n        \"login\": \"Soph\",\n        \"id\": 70741,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"parents\": [\n        {\n          \"sha\": \"b79fc08a90738048d74c6f619dd202e122659879\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/b79fc08a90738048d74c6f619dd202e122659879\",\n          \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/b79fc08a90738048d74c6f619dd202e122659879\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"sha\": \"6814963e14df05bbb824f4466051aeed27c970cd\",\n      \"node_id\": \"REDACTED\",\n      \"commit\": {\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Stefan Haubold\",\n          \"email\": \"stefan@entire.io\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-05-09T17:53:02Z\"\n        },\n        \"committer\": {\n          \"name\": \"Stefan Haubold\",\n          \"email\": \"stefan@entire.io\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-05-09T17:53:02Z\"\n        },\n        \"message\": \"Add RefScope.AllRefs to broaden mirroring beyond branches and tags\\n\\nIntroduce a third RefKindOther for refs/* namespaces outside refs/heads/\\nand refs/tags/ (notes, pulls, replace, custom). Validation accepts those\\nmappings only when the new RefScope.AllRefs flag is set; without it the\\nexisting strict branch/tag flow stays loud about unsupported refs.\\n\\nWhen AllRefs is set, BuildDesiredRefs picks up every refs/* on the\\nsource, RefPrefixes collapses to a single \\\"refs/\\\" so v2 ls-refs returns\\nthe broader set, and prune treats unmanaged other-kind target refs as\\ndelete candidates. Other-kind refs follow branch-style semantics\\n(fast-forward / force) in PlanRef, and the existing relay paths fall\\nthrough to the materialized push because their kind switches default\\nto \\\"unsupported\\\", which is the right behavior for a first cut.\\n\\nThis wires the field through the public RefScope, ProbeRequest,\\ninternalbridge, syncer.Config, and the unstable client. CLI surface\\nand best-effort failure handling come in follow-up commits.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 82d903ebce8d\",\n        \"tree\": {\n          \"sha\": \"a500cf65bdb1d7c4c263e481ce57fa40d6d225b8\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/trees/a500cf65bdb1d7c4c263e481ce57fa40d6d225b8\"\n        },\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/commits/6814963e14df05bbb824f4466051aeed27c970cd\",\n        \"comment_count\": 0,\n        \"verification\": {\n          \"verified\": false,\n          \"reason\": \"unsigned\",\n          \"signature\": null,\n          \"payload\": null,\n          \"verified_at\": null\n        }\n      },\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/6814963e14df05bbb824f4466051aeed27c970cd\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/6814963e14df05bbb824f4466051aeed27c970cd\",\n      \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/6814963e14df05bbb824f4466051aeed27c970cd/comments\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"Soph\",\n        \"id\": 70741,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"committer\": {\n        \"login\": \"Soph\",\n        \"id\": 70741,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"parents\": [\n        {\n          \"sha\": \"dbd5151fea14090590de08d293c14a5d1677fb0b\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/commits/dbd5151fea14090590de08d293c14a5d1677fb0b\",\n          \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/dbd5151fea14090590de08d293c14a5d1677fb0b\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"sha\": \"5c60d93026dabd1538705d512e2250c362fde1e1\",\n      \"node_id\": \"REDACTED\",\n      \"commit\": {\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Stefan Haubold\",\n          \"email\": \"stefan@entire.io\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-04-30T08:21:37Z\"\n        },\n        \"committer\": {\n          \"name\": \"Stefan Haubold\",\n          \"email\": \"stefan@entire.io\",\n          \"date\": \"2026-04-30T08:21:37Z\"\n        },\n        \"message\": \"even more general url validation\\n\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 8feaf84a600f\",\n        \"tree\": {\n          \"sha\": \"44ee5aa847d3fc7c432a1d743bc1fbddaa023cd2\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/trees/44ee5aa847d3fc7c432a1d743bc1fbddaa023cd2\"\n        },\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/git-sync/git/commits/5c60d93026dabd1538705d512e2250c362fde1e1\",\n        \"comment_count\": 0,\n        \"verification\": {\n          \"verified\": false,\n          \"reason\": \"un'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"dura