3T05:35:31Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": \"internal/cli/facts_sync_cmd.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Fixed in <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/commit/0e353c1f410e0328e94d8181220ecac3486ae559/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/commit/0e353c1f410e0328e94d8181220ecac3486ae559\\\"><tt>0e353c1</tt></a>: a corrupt binding now fails the sync with a rebind remedy instead of warning. The stale-gitmeta fallback it could reach is gone entirely — COR-2236 removed the local-gitmeta backend, so no code path merges against the stale local head anymore.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/452#pullrequestreview-5624332394\",\n        \"body\": \"\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"evisdren\",\n          \"name\": \"evisdren\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256443556?u=db6e15770a2509911d4dfcbe8135d205d74825f1&v=4\",\n          \"id\": 256443556\n        },\n        \"id\": 5624332394,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-23T05:35:31Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/452\",\n    \"title\": \"entireio/entire-brain PR #452 comments\",\n    \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/452\",\n    \"display_title\": \"entireio/entire-brain PR #452 comments\"\n  }\n}'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/entire-brain-452.json' 'll_request_review_id\": 5623995692,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-23T04:46:10Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-23T04:46:10Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": \"internal/cli/facts_sync_cmd.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<h3 dir=\\\"auto\\\">Corrupt binding syncs stale git-meta</h3>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>Medium Severity</strong></p>\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">When <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">readHostedRepoBinding</code> returns an error, plain <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">memories sync</code> warns and runs the local git-meta merge. That error means the binding file exists but is untrusted, so the repo is still connected or opted out. A keep-both merge against the stale local head re-raises deferred per-fact conflicts into the review queue.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<div dir=\\\"auto\\\"><a href=\\\"https://cursor.com/open?REDACTED\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\"><themed-picture data-catalyst-inline=\\\"true\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/a3745bd9c9e494e3d083228c1efdaf4ec2d519ad1c6adb4160d1c56c1ddeeb7b/68747470733a2f2f637572736f722e636f6d2f6173736574732f696d616765732f6669782d696e2d637572736f722d6461726b2e706e67\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/8f892a2b1c7e36d49621daf12d83d3200c0ad6842ca1f6d8422631d06c99b3b2/68747470733a2f2f637572736f722e636f6d2f6173736574732f696d616765732f6669782d696e2d637572736f722d6c696768742e706e67\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-light.png\\\"><img alt=\\\"Fix in 