{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:34.812Z","ordinal":3054,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-00d009d6-aa24-404e-a047-28ca65522693","process_id":"25704","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/entire-graph-213.json' '{\n  \"p\": {\n    \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/213\",\n    \"id\": 4447221837,\n    \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSqVa0c8AAAABCRM4TQ\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/213\",\n    \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/213.diff\",\n    \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/213.patch\",\n    \"issue_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/213\",\n    \"commits_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/213/commits\",\n    \"review_comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/213/comments\",\n    \"review_comment_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/comments{/number}\",\n    \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/213/comments\",\n    \"statuses_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/statuses/d864df453fd8c496afbce5918339dc5d7387ba03\",\n    \"number\": 213,\n    \"state\": \"closed\",\n    \"locked\": false,\n    \"title\": \"perf(stats): one-line answer, and stop burning the machine to get it\",\n    \"user\": {\n      \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n      \"id\": 257360244,\n      \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n      \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n      \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n      \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n      \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n      \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n      \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n      \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n      \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n      \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n      \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n      \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n      \"type\": \"User\",\n      \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n      \"site_admin\": false\n    },\n    \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/165\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n`entire graph stats` was reported as (a) pegging the machine and (b) printing a report when the\\nuser wants one number. Both are fixed, and the fix for the weak part of the estimate turned out\\nto be the same change as half the performance fix.\\n\\n## Before / after, on the reported directory\\n\\nThe machine that reported this has **1.9 GB across 3,323 `*.jsonl`** under one project\\n(`~/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv`). Wall clock and peak RSS from `/usr/bin/time -l`,\\ntwo to three runs per cell:\\n\\n| `--since` | before | after, cold (`--no-cache`) | after, warm memo |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `30d` (the default) | **60.1–70.0 s**, 99–101 MB | 14.9–15.4 s, 108 MB | **0.34–0.64 s**, 191–259 MB |\\n| `all` | 49.6–61.6 s, 99–101 MB | 13.5–13.8 s, 110–112 MB | 0.64–1.00 s, 259–264 MB |\\n| `1d` | 39.3 s, 101 MB | 3.1–4.1 s, 45–46 MB | 0.28–0.65 s, 153–233 MB |\\n\\nThe default run is **~180x faster warm and ~4x faster cold**. Peak RSS is the honest cost: the\\nwarm path holds the memo (6.6 MB gzipped on disk) in memory, so peak rises from ~100 MB to\\n~190–264 MB. `--no-cache` keeps it at ~110 MB.\\n\\nWhere the time went, and why it is gone:\\n\\n* **Half of it was system time, not parsing.** The old estimator priced its counterfactual by\\n  resolving the top-hit file of every credited graph call, which ran two regexes over the whole\\n  tool result and then an `os.OpenRoot` plus a per-component `Lstat` for up to 72 path candidates.\\n  Baseline runs spent **16–35 s in `sys`**; the new ones spend **0.7–1.0 s**. Replacing the model\\n  deleted that work outright.\\n* **`--since` was applied after the scan.** `--since 1d` JSON-parsed all 1.9 GB and then threw it\\n  away in the per-session filter. Candidates are now pruned by file mtime first: `1d` parses 683\\n  of 3,323 files, `7d` 2,325, `30d` 3,322, `all` 3,323. (Pruning is per *session*, so a project\\n  with a handful of long-lived sessions — this one has ten — prunes little at 30d and a lot at 1d.\\n  The memo is what makes the wide windows fast.)\\n* **Nothing was cached across runs.** Transcripts are append-mostly, so a per-file summary memo\\n  makes repeat runs near-instant.\\n\\n## What is measured and what is estimated\\n\\n**Estimated — and it stays labelled as such.** The counterfactual cannot be observed. The `~` is\\nin the default line for that reason, and the full model text is printed under `--verbose` and\\ncarried verbatim in `savings_model` in the JSON.\\n\\n**What changed is that both of the model'\"'\"'s prices are now measured**, per session, from the\\nsession'\"'\"'s own transcript:\\n\\n```\\ngraph cost/call         = locate result bytes      / locate results observed\\nexploration cost/call   = exploration result bytes / exploration results observed\\nsaving per substitution = max(0, exploration cost/call - graph cost/call)\\ntokens saved            = credited locate calls x saving per substitution / 4\\n```\\n\\nThe only assumption left is the 1:1 substitution ratio, and it is not invented: a paired A/B\\nbenchmark of this tool measured **0.980 exploration calls displaced per graph call**. It is\\ncarried as 1:1, which understates. The old model guessed *both* inputs — the counterfactual was\\n\\\"one whole file\\\", sized by whatever file the result happened to name, falling back to the repo'\"'\"'s\\nmedian tracked-file size — and on this directory that produced **82.9 M tokens** where the\\nmeasured-input model produces **46 k**. The estimator no longer touches the repository'\"'\"'s\\nfilesystem at all.\\n\\n**Consistency check against our own benchmark.** This repo'\"'\"'s paired A/B puts the effect at\\nCOST +2.49 %, CI [−6.83, +11.18], median negative, with graph output *larger* per call than the\\nbaseline'\"'\"'s. The new model on ten real sessions:\\n\\n| sessions | per-call delta (exploration − graph, bytes) |\\n|---|---|\\n| 4 positive | +665, +1131, +1177, +1411 |\\n| 4 negative | −118, −525, −3641, −4095 |\\n| 2 | no locate calls at all |\\n\\nMean per-call delta is **negative** (−424 B/call); 4 of 8 sessions with locate calls saved\\nnothing. Aggregate: 45,963 tokens against 33.5 B billed. That sits inside a CI that straddles\\nzero and reproduces the \\\"graph output is often larger per call\\\" finding rather than contradicting\\nit — the model reports **0 for a session where the graph cost more than it displaced, and that is\\nnot floored away at the total**, which is a sum of per-session results.\\n\\n## New default output\\n\\n```\\n$ entire graph stats --repo .\\n[entire-graph] ~45,963 tokens saved\\n```\\n\\nOne line. Green on a terminal; plain text under `NO_COLOR`, a pipe or a redirect, via the same\\n`shouldUseColor` rules the rest of the binary uses. The two degenerate cases stay one line too\\n(\\\"no coding-agent session transcripts for this repo yet…\\\", \\\"no sessions in this window…\\\").\\n\\n**`--verbose` restores the full report** — repo/sessions/window lines, the graph-calls-vs-\\nexploration line, both tables, billed tokens, the new measured per-call costs, and the wrapped\\nmodel text.\\n\\n**`--format json` is unchanged in shape.** `scripts/entire-graph-statusline.sh` reads\\n`estimated_savings_est_tokens` and `estimated_savings_pct_of_session_tokens` on every prompt\\nrender, so keys are only ever added: `transcripts_considered`, `transcripts_from_cache`,\\n`graph_locate_calls`, `graph_locate_returned_bytes`, `graph_bytes_per_locate_call`,\\n`exploration_bytes_per_call`, `sessions_with_positive_savings`, `substitution_ratio`.\\n`median_tracked_file_bytes` is retired but stays in the contract, always 0.\\n`TestStatsJSONContractKeepsEveryPublishedKey` asserts the 29 previously published keys against a\\ngolden list, and `--verbose` is asserted not to change the JSON.\\n\\n## Accuracy audit (independent of the model)\\n\\n* **Cross-transcript double counting — real, and measured.** Across the 3,316 real transcripts,\\n  **215 `tool_use` ids and 168 usage-bearing `message.id`s appear in more than one transcript of\\n  the same session** (Claude Code replays a forked subagent'\"'\"'s history into the new file; zero\\n  collisions cross session boundaries). The old code billed each of those twice, in both call\\n  counts and bytes. Sessions are now assembled from per-call and per-message identities, so one\\n  API call counts once however many transcripts carry it.\\n* **Tool-result pairing is strictly file-local** — 0 of 155,343 results pair with a `tool_use` in\\n  a different file — which is what makes a per-file summary a faithful unit and the memo sound.\\n* **Per-call prices divide by results observed, never calls issued**, so a call whose result never\\n  reached the transcript cannot deflate a price.\\n* **`mulDiv`** replaces `a*b/c`. The product already reaches ~10^13 on real volumes and would\\n  silently wrap int64; it is now exact via `bits.Mul64`/`bits.Div64`, saturating instead of\\n  wrapping, with the `hi >= c` boundary pinned (`bits.Div64` *panics* at `hi == c`).\\n* **`roundTo`** uses `math.Round` instead of an int64 truncation that rounded negatives toward\\n  zero and was undefined outside int64 range.\\n* **Determinism**: two runs over an unchanged directory are byte-identical, asserted for the\\n  default text, `--verbose` and JSON.\\n* The memo'\"'\"'s key is file *identity* (path + size + mtime) salted with the summary schema, the CLI\\n  version and the running executable'\"'\"'s own size and mtime — a rebuilt binary misses rather than\\n  trusting a summary written by different parsing code. A missing, truncated, corrupt or\\n  foreign-schema memo is treated as empty and recomputed, never served. Entries for transcripts\\n  no longer on disk are dropped each run, driven by the full candidate list so a narrow `--since`\\n  does not evict what a later `--since all` wants.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n19 new tests; every behaviour change has one that fails on a compile-clean revert (14 reverts\\napplied, built, and run: mtime prune, session-scoped prune, cross-transcript tool_use dedup,\\ncross-transcript usage dedup, terse default, locate-only pricing, `roundTo`, `mulDiv`, colour\\ngating, JSON contract, memo lookup, memo key, memo salt, memo pruning). 20 mutants applied to the\\nnew decision helpers in both directions; 15 killed, 5 survived and were adjudicated — one was a\\ngenuine escape (`hi >= c` → `hi > c`, a `bits.Div64` panic path) and is now killed by\\n`mulDiv(1<<32, 1<<32, 1)`; the other four are equivalent mutants with proofs in the review notes\\n(`a <= 0`→`a < 0` and `displaced <= x`→`<` differ only where both branches return 0;\\n`||`→`&&` in the savings precondition is unreachable because `mulDiv` is total; dropping\\n`cutoff.IsZero()` is equivalent because no `time.Time` is `Before` the zero time).\\n\\nTests changed rather than deleted where they encoded the old shape:\\n`TestStatsTextOutputCarriesRatioAndCaveat` now drives `--verbose` (that is where the report went)\\nand additionally asserts the new measured-per-call line; the missing-dir and empty-dir tests were\\nupdated to the new one-line wording; `TestStatsSavingsModelMath` and\\n`TestStatsSavingsFlooredAtZeroWhenGraphCostsMore` were rewritten around the new arithmetic; the\\nstatus-line fixture'\"'\"'s exploration results were enlarged, because the badge exists to show a\\nsession where exploration cost more per call than the graph did.\\n\\nDeleted with the code they covered: `TestStatsMedianFallbackWhenTopHitUnresolvable`,\\n`TestStatsFileSizeStaysInsideTheSelectedRepository` and `stats_mount_windows_test.go` (both\\njunction tests) all exercised the repository-filesystem probing that no longer exists — `stats`\\nnow never opens a file in the scanned repository, which removes that traversal surface entirely.\\n\\n`go build ./...`, `go vet ./...` (also `GOOS=windows` and `GOOS=linux`), `gofmt -l -s .` clean;\\n`go test ./... -count=1` and `go test -race ./... -count=1` green (4,951 tests);\\n`scripts/entire-graph-statusline_test.sh` 151/151.\\n\",\n    \"labels\": [],\n    \"milestone\": null,\n    \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T22:29:40Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-05T12:29:23Z\",\n    \"closed_at\": \"2026-09-05T12:29:22Z\",\n    \"merged_at\": \"2026-09-05T12:29:22Z\",\n    \"merge_commit_sha\": \"e8c11a33245ff2744af5978b257140c4949f2443\",\n    \"assignee\": null,\n    \"assignees\": [],\n    \"requested_reviewers\": [],\n    \"requested_teams\": [],\n    \"head\": {\n      \"label\": \"entireio:fix/stats-fast-and-plain\",\n      \"ref\": \"fix/stats-fast-and-plain\",\n      \"repo\": {\n        \"id\": 1252350673,\n        \"node_id\": \"R_kgDOSqVa0Q\",\n        \"name\": \"entire-graph\",\n        \"full_name\": \"entireio/entire-graph\",\n        \"owner\": {\n          \"login\": \"entireio\",\n          \"id\": 33188652,\n          \"node_id\": \"REDACTED\",\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33188652?v=4\",\n          \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio\",\n          \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio\",\n          \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/followers\",\n          \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/following{/other_user}\",\n          \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/gists{/gist_id}\",\n          \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n          \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/subscriptions\",\n          \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/orgs\",\n          \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/repos\",\n          \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/events{/privacy}\",\n          \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/received_events\",\n          \"type\": \"Organization\",\n          \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n          \"site_admin\": false\n        },\n        \"private\": false,\n        \"fork\": false,\n        \"archived\": false,\n        \"disabled\": false,\n        \"description\": \"🪾 Make your agents more efficient with a precomputed map of your Git repository: ranked code search plus definitions, callers, types, routes, and change impact, each with file:line locations.\",\n        \"homepage\": \"\",\n        \"language\": \"C\",\n        \"visibility\": \"public\",\n        \"is_template\": false,\n        \"topics\": [],\n        \"forks_count\": 82,\n        \"forks\": 82,\n        \"stargazers_count\": 138,\n        \"watchers_count\": 138,\n        \"watchers\": 138,\n        \"open_issues_count\": 37,\n        \"open_issues\": 37,\n        \"size\": 546697,\n        \"default_branch\": \"main\",\n        \"has_issues\": true,\n        \"ha