{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:36.168Z","ordinal":3063,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-d40e2017-a026-4242-9b6a-8b47e6a82dee","process_id":"72882","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/cli-2996.json' '{\n  \"p\": {\n    \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2996\",\n    \"id\": 5126806906,\n    \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABMZTdeg\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2996\",\n    \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2996.diff\",\n    \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2996.patch\",\n    \"issue_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2996\",\n    \"commits_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2996/commits\",\n    \"review_comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2996/comments\",\n    \"review_comment_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/comments{/number}\",\n    \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2996/comments\",\n    \"statuses_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/statuses/0e0ada68ca0ef457a5ea4483552cd1f7d0a9646f\",\n    \"number\": 2996,\n    \"state\": \"open\",\n    \"locked\": false,\n    \"title\": \"fix(review): persist findings when session matching fails\",\n    \"user\": {\n      \"login\": \"d5v7\",\n      \"id\": 128817931,\n      \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOB62bCw\",\n      \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128817931?v=4\",\n      \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/d5v7\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/d5v7\",\n      \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/d5v7/followers\",\n      \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/d5v7/following{/other_user}\",\n      \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/d5v7/gists{/gist_id}\",\n      \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/d5v7/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n      \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/d5v7/subscriptions\",\n      \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/d5v7/orgs\",\n      \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/d5v7/repos\",\n      \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/d5v7/events{/privacy}\",\n      \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/d5v7/received_events\",\n      \"type\": \"User\",\n      \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n      \"site_admin\": false\n    },\n    \"body\": \"## Problem\\n\\nA local review can finish and print its verdict but leave `entire review --findings` empty. The manifest currently depends on matching a tagged lifecycle session for each reviewer. If no session matches the current worktree, the command drops the captured output; sessions from sibling worktrees can make the resulting diagnostic look like a worktree mismatch. The command also returns success when writing the manifest fails.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- Save every reviewer'\"'\"'s captured output and the judge'\"'\"'s aggregate verdict in the local manifest even when session state is missing, cannot be read, or does not match. Attach a session ID only when the existing matcher finds a suitable session, so a sibling worktree'\"'\"'s session is not attributed to the run.\\n- Return a nonzero error if the manifest cannot be written, while printing the existing user-visible warning only once.\\n- Use subsecond timestamps for manifest filenames and findings handles so reviews started in the same second can be saved and selected separately. Continue accepting existing second-resolution handles.\\n- Remove the empty-manifest matcher diagnostics and their tests: an unmatched session no longer prevents saving a review. A saved run without a session ID does not currently explain why session matching failed.\\n- Update the review architecture documentation and cover missing or partial session matches, command-level write failures for single and multi-reviewer runs, and reviews started in the same second.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- Reproduced the reported diagnostic with Pi in two isolated worktrees: a successful review in worktree B printed its verdict but did not persist it when a tagged session existed in worktree A. With this change, the same review was available through `entire review --findings` in B and did not appear in A.\\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/review ./docs/development` — passed after the review feedback changes.\\n- `mise run lint` — passed locally.\\n- Deterministic Vogon and Roger Roger canaries — passed locally.\\n- [GitHub Actions Tests](https://github.com/dhanushk-offl/entire-cli/actions/runs/41516324184) and [Lint](https://github.com/dhanushk-offl/entire-cli/actions/runs/41516370800) — passed on the initial PR commit (`e6b472929`); the latest commit awaits CI approval.\\n\\nCloses #2990\\n\\n\",\n    \"labels\": [],\n    \"milestone\": null,\n    \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-11-02T20:18:10Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-12T11:36:59Z\",\n    \"closed_at\": null,\n    \"merged_at\": null,\n    \"merge_commit_sha\": \"eaf0c1797b9d6edfddc7fcacd63b9e1d977622de\",\n    \"assignee\": null,\n    \"assignees\": [],\n    \"requested_reviewers\": [],\n    \"requested_teams\": [],\n    \"head\": {\n      \"label\": \"d5v7:fix/review-worktree-findings\",\n      \"ref\": \"fix/review-worktree-findings\",\n      \"repo\": {\n        \"id\": 1349478780,\n        \"node_id\": \"R_kgDOUG9pfA\",\n        \"name\": \"entire-cli\",\n        \"full_name\": \"d5v7/entire-cli\",\n        \"owner\": {\n          \"login\": \"d5v7\",\n          \"id\": 128817931,\n          \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOB62bCw\",\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubu