"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"Organization\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      }\n    },\n    \"_links\": {\n      \"comments\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2996/comments\"\n      },\n      \"commits\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2996/commits\"\n      },\n      \"statuses\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/statuses/0e0ada68ca0ef457a5ea4483552cd1f7d0a9646f\"\n      },\n      \"html\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2996\"\n      },\n      \"issue\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/2996\"\n      },\n      \"review_comments\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2996/comments\"\n      },\n      \"review_comment\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/comments{/number}\"\n      },\n      \"self\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/2996\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n    \"auto_merge\": null,\n    \"draft\": false,\n    \"merged\": false,\n    \"mergeable\": true,\n    \"rebaseable\": true,\n    \"mergeable_state\": \"blocked\",\n    \"merged_by\": null,\n    \"comments\": 3,\n    \"review_comments\": 0,\n    \"maintainer_can_modify\": true,\n    \"commits\": 10,\n    \"additions\": 142,\n    \"deletions\": 529,\n    \"changed_files\": 6\n  },\n  \"c\": {\n    \"comments\": [\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2996#pullrequestreview-5742761200\",\n        \"body\": \"Copilot was unable to review this pull request because the user who requested the review has insufficient remaining quota. Try requesting a review at a lower effort level.\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"name\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 5742761200,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-11-02T20:18:21Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Copilot was unable to review this pull request because the user who requested the review has insufficient remaining quota. Try requesting a review at a lower effort level.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2996#issuecomment-6594325314\",\n        \"body\": \"@dhanushk-offl thanks for this. I checked it locally against main (`37bdccdde`) at `aa714cafd`. cc @Soph @peyton-alt, since this removes the empty-manifest explainer from #1185.\\n\\n**What I ran:** the #2990 scenario with two worktrees. Main exits 0 with empty findings. With this PR the run is saved, shows under `--findings` in B but not in A, and has no wrong session attached. With a read-only manifest directory the PR now exits 1, but the error prints twice. `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/review/... ./docs/development` passes and golangci-lint on that package reports 0 issues. I didn'\"'\"'t run the full lint or test suite.\\n\\n**Two things worth adding:**\\n1. The description says the existing explanation is kept. That holds for write failures, but the PR also removes `explainEmptyManifest`/`applyExplainerFilter`, the drift warning, the \\\"could not load session state\\\" note, and 10 `TestExplainEmptyManifest_*` tests. Removing them makes sense now that a run is always saved, but the description should say so, and mention that a run saved without a session ID gives no hint about why no session matched.\\n2. Nothing tests that a manifest write failure becomes a nonzero exit at the command level. Replacing `return manifestErr` with `return nil` in both `runSingleAgentPath` and `runMultiAgentPath` still passes every test.\\n\\n**Not checked:** a real Pi agent, multi-agent profiles end to end, macOS and Windows, and `entire review fix` on a manifest with no session ID.\\n\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n          \"name\": \"Beehtrix\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 26940511\n        },\n        \"id\": 6594325314,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-11-03T03:00:26Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-03T03:00:26Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">@dhanushk-offl thanks for this. I checked it locally against main (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">37bdccdde</code>) at <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">aa714cafd</code>. cc <a class=\\\"user-mention notranslate\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"user\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/users/Soph/hovercard\\\" data-octo-click=\\\"hovercard-link-click\\\" data-octo-dimensions=\\\"link_type:self\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/Soph\\\">@Soph</a> <a class=\\\"user-mention notranslate\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"user\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/users/peyton-alt/hovercard\\\" data-octo-click=\\\"hovercard-link-click\\\" data-octo-dimensions=\\\"link_type:self\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/peyton-alt\\\">@peyton-alt</a>, since this removes the empty-manifest explainer from <a class=\\\"issue-link js-issue-link\\\" data-error-text=\\\"Failed to load title\\\" data-id=\\\"4425799252\\\" data-permission-text=\\\"Title is private\\\" data-url=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/1185\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"pull_request\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/entireio/cli/pull/1185/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1185\\\">#1185</a>.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>What I ran:</strong> the <a class=\\\"issue-link js-issue-link\\\" data-error-text=\\\"Failed to load title\\\" data-id=\\\"6157444618\\\" data-permission-text=\\\"Title is private\\\" data-url=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2990\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"issue\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/entireio/cli/issues/2990/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2990\\\">#2990</a> scenario with two worktrees. Main exits 0 with empty findings. With this PR the run is saved, shows under <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--findings</code> in B but not in A, and has no wrong session attached. With a read-only manifest directory the PR now exits 1, but the error prints twice. <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">go test ./cmd/entire/cli/review/... ./docs/development</code> passes and golangci-lint on that package reports 0 issues. I didn'\"'\"'t run the full lint or test suite.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>Two things worth adding:</strong></p>\\n<ol dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>The description says the existing explanation is kept. That holds for write failures, but the PR also removes <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">explainEmptyManifest</code>/<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">applyExplainerFilter</code>, the drift warning, the \\\"could not load session state\\\" note, and 10 <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">TestExplainEmptyManifest_*</code> tests. Removing them makes sense now that a run is always saved, but the description should say so, and mention that a run saved without a session ID gives no hint about why no session matched.</li>\\n<li>Nothing tests that a manifest write failure becomes a nonzero exit at the command level. Replacing <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">return manifestErr</code> with <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">return nil</code> in both <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">runSingleAgentPath</code> and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">runMultiAgentPath</code> still passes every test.</li>\\n</ol>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>Not checked:</strong> a real Pi agent, multi-agent profiles end to end, macOS and Windows, and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">entire review fix</code> on a manifest with no session ID.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2996#issuecomment-6595470851\",\n        \"body\": \"Hey @Beehtrix, Thanks for the thorough testing and helpful suggestions! I’ve updated the PR to address them:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Manifest write failures now print the warning once and still return a nonzero error.\\r\\n- Added command-level tests for write failures in both single- and multi-reviewer runs.\\r\\n- Updated the PR description to explain that the empty-manifest diagnostics were removed and that saved runs without a session ID don’t currently say why matching failed.\\r\\n\\r\\nI also tested the worktree scenario with a real Pi agent on my machine. With one reviewer, I reproduced the mismatch on the baseline and confirmed that the fixed CLI saved the verdict in worktree B without showing it in A. I also ran a two-reviewer-and-judge profile on the baseline.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe review package tests and local lint pass.\\r\\n\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"d5v7\",\n          \"name\": \"d5v7\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128817931?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 128817931\n        },\n        \"id\": 6595470851,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-11-03T04:28:50Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-03T04:30:20Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Hey <a class=\\\"user-mention notranslate\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"user\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/users/Beehtrix/hovercard\\\" data-octo-click=\\\"hovercard-link-click\\\" data-octo-dimensions=\\\"link_type:self\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/Beehtrix\\\">@Beehtrix</a>, Thanks for the thorough testing and helpful suggestions! I’ve updated the PR to address them:</p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>Manifest write failures now print the warning once and still return a nonzero error.</li>\\n<li>Added command-level tests for write failures in both single- and multi-reviewer runs.</li>\\n<li>Updated the PR description to explain that the empty-manifest diagnostics were removed and that saved runs without a session ID don’t currently say why matching failed.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">I also tested the worktree scenario with a real Pi agent on my machine. With one reviewer, I reproduced the mismatch on the baseline and confirmed that the fixed CLI saved the verdict in worktree B without showing it in A. I also ran a two-reviewer-and-judge profile on the baseline.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">The review package tests and local lint pass.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2996#issuecomment-6725711419\",\n        \"body\": \"@dhanushk-offl, thanks, both are covered. The description now says the empty-manifest explainer is gone. `TestReviewCommand_ManifestWriteFailureReturnsSilentError` runs both the single and multi-reviewer paths, so it fails if either one swallows the write error. @Soph @peyton-alt, from my side this is ready for a maintainer look. The latest commit still needs CI approval.\\n\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n          \"name\": \"Beehtrix\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 26940511\n        },\n        \"id\": 6725711419,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-11-08T19:01:04Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-08T19:01:04Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">@dhanushk-offl, thanks, both are covered. The description now says the empty-manifest explainer is gone. <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">TestReviewCommand_ManifestWriteFailureReturnsSilentError</code> runs both the single and multi-reviewer paths, so it fails if either one swallows the write error. <a class=\\\"user-mention notranslate\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"user\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/users/Soph/hovercard\\\" data-octo-click=\\\"hovercard-link-click\\\" data-octo-dimensions=\\\"link_type:self\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/Soph\\\">@Soph</a> <a class=\\\"user-mention notranslate\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"user\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/users/peyton-alt/hovercard\\\" data-octo-click=\\\"hovercard-link-click\\\" data-octo-dimensions=\\\"link_type:self\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/peyton-alt\\\">@peyton-alt</a>, from my side this is ready for a maintainer look. The latest commit still needs CI approval.</p>\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2996\",\n    \"title\": \"entireio/cli PR #2996 comments\",\n    \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2996\",\n    \"display_title\": \"entireio/cli PR #2996 comments\"\n  }\n}'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").writ