     \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 5742761200,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-11-02T20:18:21Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Copilot was unable to review this pull request because the user who requested the review has insufficient remaining quota. Try requesting a review at a lower effort level.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2996#issuecomment-6594325314\",\n        \"body\": \"@dhanushk-offl thanks for this. I checked it locally against main (`37bdccdde`) at `aa714cafd`. cc @Soph @peyton-alt, since this removes the empty-manifest explainer from #1185.\\n\\n**What I ran:** the #2990 scenario with two worktrees. Main exits 0 with empty findings. With this PR the run is saved, shows under `--findings` in B but not in A, and has no wrong session attached. With a read-only manifest directory the PR now exits 1, but the error prints twice. `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/review/... ./docs/development` passes and golangci-lint on that package reports 0 issues. I didn'\"'\"'t run the full lint or test suite.\\n\\n**Two things worth adding:**\\n1. The description says the existing explanation is kept. That holds for write failures, but the PR also removes `explainEmptyManifest`/`applyExplainerFilter`, the drift warning, the \\\"could not load session state\\\" note, and 10 `TestExplainEmptyManifest_*` tests. Removing them makes sense now that a run is always saved, but the description should say so, and mention that a run saved without a session ID gives no hint about why no session matched.\\n2. Nothing tests that a manifest write failure becomes a nonzero exit at the command level. Replacing `return manifestErr` with `return nil` in both `runSingleAgentPath` and `runMultiAgentPath` still passes every test.\\n\\n**Not checked:** a real Pi agent, multi-agent profiles end to end, macOS and Windows, and `entire review fix` on a manifest with no session ID.\\n\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n          \"name\": \"Beehtrix\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 26940511\n        },\n        \"id\": 6594325314,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-11-03T03:00:26Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-03T03:00:26Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">@dhanushk-offl thanks for this. I checked it locally against main (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">37bdccdde</code>) at <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">aa714cafd</code>. cc <a class=\\\"user-mention notranslate\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"user\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/users/Soph/hovercard\\\" data-octo-click=\\\"hovercard-link-click\\\" data-octo-dimensions=\\\"link_type:self\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/Soph\\\">@Soph</a> <a class=\\\"user-mention notranslate\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"user\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/users/peyton-alt/hovercard\\\" data-octo-click=\\\"hovercard-link-click\\\" data-octo-dimensions=\\\"link_type:self\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/peyton-alt\\\">@peyton-alt</a>, since this removes the empty-manifest explainer from <a class=\\\"issue-link js-issue-link\\\" data-error-text=\\\"Failed to load title\\\" data-id=\\\"4425799252\\\" data-permission-text=\\\"Title is private\\\" data-url=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/1185\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"pull_request\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/entireio/cli/pull/1185/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1185\\\">#1185</a>.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>What I ran:</strong> the <a class=\\\"issue-link js-issue-link\\\" data-error-text=\\\"Failed to load title\\\" data-id=\\\"6157444618\\\" data-permission-text=\\\"Title is private\\\" data-url=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2990\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"issue\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/entireio/cli/issues/2990/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2990\\\">#2990</a> scenario with two worktrees. Main exits 0 with empty findings. With this PR the run is saved, shows under <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--findings</code> in B but not in A, and has no wrong session attached. With a read-only manifest directory the PR now exits 1, but the error prints twice. <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">go test ./cmd/entire/cli/review/... ./docs/development</code> passes and golangci-lint on that package reports 0 issues. I didn'\"'\"'t run the full lint or test suite.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>Two things worth adding:</strong></p>\\n<ol dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>The description says the existing explanation is kept. That holds for write failures, but the PR also removes <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">explainEmptyManifest</code>/<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">applyExplainerFilter</code>, the drift warning, the \\\"could not load session state\\\" note, and 10 <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">TestExplainEmptyManifest_*</code> tests. Removing them makes sense now that a run is always saved, but the description should say so, and mention that a run saved without a session ID gives no hint about why no session matched.</li>\\n<li>Nothing tests that a manifest write failure becomes a nonzero exit at the command level. Replacing <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">return manifestErr</code> with <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">return nil</code> in both <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">runSingleAgentPath</code> and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">runMultiAgentPath</code> still passes every test.</li>\\n</ol>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>Not checked:</strong> a real Pi agent, multi-agent profiles end to end, macOS and Windows, and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">entire review fix</code> on a manifest with no session ID.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2996#issuecomment-6595470851\",\n        \"body\": \"Hey @Beehtrix, Thanks for the thorough testing and helpful suggestions! I’ve updated the PR to address them:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Manifest write failures now print the warning once and still return a nonzero error.\\r\\n- Added command-level tests for write failures in both single- and multi-reviewer runs.\\r\\n- Updated the PR description to explain that the empty-manifest diagnostics were removed and that saved runs without a session ID don’t currently say why matching failed.\\r\\n\\r\\nI also tested the worktree scenario with a real Pi agent on my machine. With one reviewer, I reproduced the mismatch on the baseline and confirmed that the fixed CLI saved the verdict in worktree B without showing it in A. I also ran a two-reviewer-and-judge profile on the baseline.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe review package tests and local lint pass.\\r\\n\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"d5v7\",\n          \"name\": \"d5v7\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128817931?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 128817931\n        },\n        \"id\": 6595470851,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-11-03T04:28:50Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-03T04:30:20Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Hey <a class=\\\"user-mention notranslate\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"user\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/users/Beehtrix/hovercard\\\" data-octo-click=\\\"hovercard-link-click\\\" data-octo-dimensions=\\\"link_type:self\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/Beehtrix\\\">@Beehtrix</a>, Thanks for the thorough testing and helpful suggestions! I’ve updated the PR to address them:</p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>Manifest write failures now print the warning once and still return a nonzero error.</li>\\n<li>Added command-level tests for write failures in both single- and multi-reviewer runs.</li>\\n<li>Updated the PR description to explain that the empty-manifest diagnostics were removed and that saved runs without a session ID don’t currently say why matching failed.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">I also tested the worktree scenario with a real Pi agent on my machine. With one reviewer, I reproduced the mismatch on the baseline and confirmed that the fixed CLI saved the verdict in worktree B without showing it in A. I also ran a two-reviewer-and-judge profile on the baseline.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">The review package tests and local lint pass.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2996#issuecomment-6725711419\",\n        \"body\": \"@dhanushk-offl, thanks, both are covered. The description now says the empty-manifest explainer is gone. `TestReviewCommand_ManifestWriteFailureReturnsSilentError` runs both the single and multi-reviewer paths, so it fails if either one swallows the write error. @Soph @peyton-alt, from my side this is ready for a maintainer look. The latest commit still needs CI approval.\\n\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"Beehtrix\",\n          \"name\": \"Beehtrix\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26940511?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 26940511\n        },\n        \"id\": 6725711419,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-11-08T19:01:04Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-08T19:01:04Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">@dhanushk-offl, thanks, both are covered. The description now says the empty-manifest explainer is gone. <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">TestReviewCommand_ManifestWriteFailureReturnsSilentError</code> runs both the single and multi-reviewer paths, so it fails if either one swallows the write error. <a class=\\\"user-mention notranslate\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"user\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/users/Soph/hovercard\\\" data-octo-click=\\\"hovercard-link-click\\\" data-octo-dimensions=\\\"link_type:self\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/Soph\\\">@Soph</a> <a class=\\\"user-mention notranslate\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"user\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/users/peyton-alt/hovercard\\\" data-octo-click=\\\"hovercard-link-click\\\" data-octo-dimensions=\\\"link_type:self\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/peyton-alt\\\">@peyton-alt</a>, from my side this is ready for a maintainer look. The latest commit still needs CI approval.</p>\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2996\",\n    \"title\": \"entireio/cli PR #2996 comments\",\n    \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2996\",\n    \"display_title\": \"entireio/cli PR #2996 comments\"\n  }\n}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":11667}},"started_at_ms":1794842136323,"completed_at_ms":1794842136324}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:36.454Z","ordinal":3065,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-cf53b60c-572b-45eb-bd45-0456818f87d8","process_id":"60281","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import pathlib,sys;p=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]);p.parent.mkdir(exist_ok=True);p.write_bytes(b\"\")' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/cli-3002.json'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"list_files","cmd":"python3 -c 'import pathlib,sys;p=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]);p.parent.mkdir(exist_ok=True);p.write_bytes(b\"\")' /Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/cli-3002.json","path":null}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":11208}},"started_at_ms":1794842136454,"completed_at_ms":1794842136454}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:36.616Z","ordinal":3066,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-7d9bb780-172b-4c34-a079-0a5cf08a43bf","process_id":"35467","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/cli-3002.json' '{\n  \"p\": {\n    \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3002\",\n    \"id\": 5141387584,\n    \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOQyo98M8AAAABMnNZQA\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3002\",\n    \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3002.diff\",\n    \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3002.patch\",\n    \"issue_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3002\",\n    \"commits_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3002/commits\",\n    \"review_comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/3002/comments\",\n    \"review_comment_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/pulls/comments{/number}\",\n    \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/issues/3002/comments\",\n    \"statuses_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/cli/statuses/a92b57d47a6a9e1deaa7d437becb70041558a7ab\",\n    \"number\": 3002,\n    \"state\": \"closed\",\n    \"locked\": false,\n    \"title\": \"Add trail attachment add, list, and remove\",\n    \"user\": {\n      \"login\": \"entire[bot]\",\n      \"id\": 254015822,\n      \"node_id\": \"BOT_kgDODyP5Tg\",\n      \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/2626939?v=4\",\n      \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/apps/entire\",\n      \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\n      \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\n      \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\n      \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n      \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\n      \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\n      \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\n      \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\n      \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entire%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\n      \"type\": \"Bot\",\n      \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n      \"site_admin\": false\n    },\n    \"body\": \"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2688/changes/cli/1737\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\nPart of trail #2688 (closing CLI trail command gaps), change cli/1737.\\n\\n## What\\n\\n`entire trail attachment` manages the images a project trail'\"'\"'s description shows, through `/{host}/{project}/trails/{trail}/attachments`:\\n\\n- `entire trail attachment add <file>` uploads an image and prints the line that shows it in the description: `![image](attachment:<id>)`. It registers the upload with an `Idempotency-Key`, PUTs the bytes to the presigned URL, and completes it. If anything after registering fails (the server'\"'\"'s size limit, a refused PUT, a failed completion), it deletes the attachment it registered, so a failed upload leaves nothing behind. `--json` prints the attachment and the line.\\n- `entire trail attachment list` lists the trail'\"'\"'s attachments, including uploads that never completed, with the reference for each ready image.\\n- `entire trail attachment remove <id> --force` deletes one.\\n\\nThe trail is selected like `trail comment`: `--trail <number|ULID|repo/number>`, `--branch`, or the current branch'\"'\"'s parent, with `--project`.\\n\\n## Why it works now\\n\\nentire-api change entire-api/734 (et/entirehq trail 1492) gave attachment images a Markdown form: a line holding only `![alt](attachment:<ULID>)` becomes an image when a project trail body is written as Markdown, and a body read back renders each image as `![image](attachment:<ULID>)`. Before it, `trail update --body` replaced any image added in the web editor with the text `[image]`. The CLI prints the reference in exactly the form the server renders back, so a description read with `trail show --json`, edited, and written back keeps its images.\\n\\n## Decisions to review\\n\\n- **Type from the bytes.** `add` detects the type from the file'\"'\"'s contents and accepts only PNG, JPEG, GIF, and WebP up to 10 MiB, before any request. The cell trusts the declared type, and only those four render inline; any other reference stays literal text. Width and height are sent for PNG, JPEG, and GIF (the standard library has no WebP decoder; they are optional).\\n- **The presigned PUT never gets the caller'\"'\"'s token.** It uses its own client from `httpclient.New` (so it keeps the shared HTTPS-downgrade redirect policy), sends the declared `Content-Type`, and refuses a non-HTTPS URL except on loopback (tests).\\n- **`remove` requires `--force`**, like deleting a project trail comment message, since it cannot be undone and the image disappears from any description that references it.\\n- **Classification:** `trail attachment` is `task-driven`, unlisted, like `trail update`, whose description it feeds. Agent guidance says to keep existing `attachment:` lines when writing a body back, and never to run `remove` or pass `--force` unless the user asks for that attachment to be deleted.\\n- **Not included:** inserting the reference into the description automatically, and downloading an attachment. Both are easy to add if wanted.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- Tests cover the full upload (intent body with type and dimensions, Idempotency-Key, the exact bytes and Content-Type at the storage URL with no Authorization header, completion), `--json`, files refused before any request (SVG named `.png`, empty, over 10 MiB, a directory, missing), a plaintext upload URL, `list` with and without a reference, `remove` requiring `--force` and an attachment ID, a refused PUT removing the registered attachment, and the URL'\"'\"'s expiry left to storage (a local clock running ahead must not refuse a valid URL). `list`, `add`, and `remove` are classified separately: `list` read-only, the others task-driven.\\n- Live, read-only, against production: `trail attachment list --trail 2688 --project gh/entireio` reaches the route and returns the empty list. I did not upload to a real trail.\\n- `mise run fmt`, `mise run lint`, the complexity gate, and `GOOS=windows go vet` are clean; `go test ./internal/... ./cmd/entire/cli/ ./docs/...` passes.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n<!-- entire-shadow-pr -->\\n\",\n    \"labels\": [],\n    \"milestone\": null,\n    \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-11-03T17:07:47Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-05T19:08:30Z\",\n    \"closed_at\": \"2026-11-05T19:08:27Z\",\n    \"merged_at\": \"2026-11-05T19:08:27Z\",\n    \"merge_commit_sha\": \"aa0c90c9770a460092103214b608247a8b2623ae\",\n    \"assignee\": null,\n    \"assignees\": [],\n    \"requested_reviewers\": [],\n    \"requested_teams\": [],\n    \"head\": {\n      \"label\": \"entireio:soph/trail-attachments\",\n      \"ref\": \"soph/trail-attachments\",\n      \"repo\": {\n        \"id\": 1126841840,\n        \"node_id\": \"R_kgDOQyo98A\",\n        \"name\": \"cli\",\n        \"full_name\": \"entireio/cli\",\n        \"owner\": {\n          \"login\": \"entireio\",\n          \"id\": 33188652,\n          \"node_id\": \"REDACTED\",\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33188652?v=4\",\n          \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio\",\n          \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio\",\n          \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/followers\",\n          \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/following{/other_user}\",\n          \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/gists{/gist_id}\",\n          \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n          \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/subscriptions\",\n          \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/orgs\",\n          \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/repos\",\n          \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/events{/privacy}\",\n          \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/received_events\",\n          \"type\": \"Organization\",\n          \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n          \"site_admin\": false\n        },\n        \"private\": false,\n        \"fork\": false,\n        \"archived\": false,\n        \"disabled\": false,\n        \"description\": \"📜 Entire CLI hooks into your Git workflow to capture AI agent sessions as you work. Sessions are indexed alongside commits, creating a searchable record of how code was written in your repo.\",\n        \"homepage\": \"https://entire.io\",\n        \"language\": \"Go\",\n        \"visibility\": \"public\",\n        \"is_template\": false,\n        \"topics\": [\n          \"agents\",\n          \"ai\",\n          \"claude\",\n          \"developer\",\n          \"developer-platform\",\n          \"gemini\"\n        ],\n        \"forks_count\": 499,\n        \"forks\": 499,\n        \"stargazers_count\": 5339,\n        \"watchers_count\": 5339,\n        \"watchers\": 5339,\n        \"open_issues_count\": 440,\n        \"open_issues\": 440,\n        \"size\": 