  \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzIw\",\n      \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70720?v=4\",\n      \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/ashtom\",\n      \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/followers\",\n      \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/following{/other_user}\",\n      \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/gists{/gist_id}\",\n      \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n      \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/subscriptions\",\n      \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/orgs\",\n      \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/repos\",\n      \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/events{/privacy}\",\n      \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/received_events\",\n      \"type\": \"User\",\n      \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n      \"site_admin\": false\n    },\n    \"comments\": 0,\n    \"review_comments\": 4,\n    \"maintainer_can_modify\": false,\n    \"commits\": 9,\n    \"additions\": 1313,\n    \"deletions\": 92,\n    \"changed_files\": 14\n  },\n  \"c\": {\n    \"comments\": [\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/78#discussion_r3699968046\",\n        \"body\": \"`isTerminal` treats any character device as a terminal. On Unix, that includes `/dev/null`, so `--format auto` could incorrectly choose the human text output even when stdout/stderr are redirected to `/dev/null` (not interactive). Consider at least excluding `os.DevNull` to keep the “terminal vs piped” behavior accurate without adding dependencies.\\n\\nThis issue also appears on line 57 of the same file.\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"name\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 3699968046,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 4839415591,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-08-02T18:18:29Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-02T18:18:30Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": 35,\n        \"start_line\": 12,\n        \"path\": \"internal/cli/progressbar.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">isTerminal</code> treats any character device as a terminal. On Unix, that includes <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">/dev/null</code>, so <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--format auto</code> could incorrectly choose the human text output even when stdout/stderr are redirected to <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">/dev/null</code> (not interactive). Consider at least excluding <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">os.DevNull</code> to keep the “terminal vs piped” behavior accurate without adding dependencies.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">This issue also appears on line 57 of the same file.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/78#discussion_r3699968055\",\n        \"body\": \"This comment says \\\"`help`/`--help` still fall through to the root help\\\", but `help --help` is now intercepted by the per-command help block and prints the detail view instead. Updating the comment avoids confusing future readers about the control flow.\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"name\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 3699968055,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 4839415591,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-08-02T18:18:29Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-02T18:18:30Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": 56,\n        \"start_line\": 51,\n        \"path\": \"internal/cli/root.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">This comment says \\\"<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">help</code>/<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--help</code> still fall through to the root help\\\", but <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">help --help</code> is now intercepted by the per-command help block and prints the detail view instead. Updating the comment avoids confusing future readers about the control flow.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/78#discussion_r3699968064\",\n        \"body\": \"`index` help text says `--format` supports `auto` (default), but the usage line omits it. Keeping these consistent helps users discover the default behavior.\\n\\nThis issue also appears on line 95 of the same file.\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"name\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 3699968064,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 4839415591,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-08-02T18:18:30Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-02T18:18:30Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": 92,\n        \"start_line\": 88,\n        \"path\": \"internal/cli/help.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">index</code> help text says <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--format</code> supports <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">auto</code> (default), but the usage line omits it. Keeping these consistent helps users discover the default behavior.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">This issue also appears on line 95 of the same file.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/78#discussion_r3699968072\",\n        \"body\": \"`index` now defaults to `--format auto` (text when stdout is a terminal). Previously it always emitted JSON unless an invalid format was supplied, so this is a behavior change for any caller that parses `index` output from an interactive terminal. If backward compatibility for machine consumers is a goal, consider keeping the default as JSON and requiring `--format auto`/`--format text` explicitly.\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"name\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 3699968072,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 4839415591,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-08-02T18:18:30Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-02T18:18:30Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": 70,\n        \"start_line\": 57,\n        \"path\": \"internal/cli/index.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">index</code> now defaults to <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--format auto</code> (text when stdout is a terminal). Previously it always emitted JSON unless an invalid format was supplied, so this is a behavior change for any caller that parses <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">index</code> output from an interactive terminal. If backward compatibility for machine consumers is a goal, consider keeping the default as JSON and requiring <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--format auto</code>/<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--format text</code> explicitly.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/78#pullrequestreview-4839415591\",\n        \"body\": \"## Pull request overview\\n\\nThis PR overhauls the `entire graph` CLI help system, improves `index` UX (progress + human summary + `--force`), and fixes completeness reporting by introducing a repo-root `.graphignore` and adjusting which partial failures count toward “degraded”.\\n\\n**Changes:**\\n- Replace the monolithic help blob with a centralized help registry that powers grouped root help plus per-command `--help`.\\n- Improve `index` usability with a terminal-only progress bar, optional human-readable summary, and `--force` cache refresh behavior.\\n- Reduce false “completeness: degraded” reports via `.graphignore` and excluding intentional-skip failure codes from completeness level calculation.\\n\\n### Reviewed changes\\n\\nCopilot reviewed 14 out of 14 changed files in this pull request and generated 4 comments.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>\\n\\n| File | Description |\\r\\n| ---- | ----------- |\\r\\n| internal/sem/search_cache.go | Adds `ForceRebuild` handling to preindex snapshot creation/persistence. |\\r\\n| internal/sem/search_cache_test.go | Adds regression test pinning `--force` preindex cache overwrite behavior. |\\r\\n| internal/sem/provider.go | Improves progress cadence and adjusts completeness computation to ignore intentional skips. |\\r\\n| internal/sem/ignore.go | Loads repo-root `.graphignore` for both worktree and explicit ignore matchers. |\\r\\n| internal/sem/completeness_test.go | Tests `.graphignore` matcher behavior and skip-code exclusion from completeness. |\\r\\n| internal/cli/stats_test.go | Updates help assertions to reflect new per-command `--help` behavior. |\\r\\n| internal/cli/root.go | Centralizes per-command help interception and improves unknown-command messaging. |\\r\\n| internal/cli/root_test.go | Adjusts help-related test to assert per-command help output. |\\r\\n| internal/cli/progressbar.go | Adds dependency-free terminal progress bar rendering utilities. |\\r\\n| internal/cli/progressbar_test.go | Adds tests for TTY detection and progress bar rendering/clearing. |\\r\\n| internal/cli/index.go | Implements `--force`, progress bar wiring, and `--format`-based text/JSON output selection. |\\r\\n| internal/cli/help.go | Introduces command help registry + renderers for grouped root help and per-command help. |\\r\\n| internal/cli/help_test.go | Adds parity tests between dispatch switch and help registry; tests `--help` interception. |\\r\\n| .graphignore | Adds repo-root ignore patterns to exclude generated tree-sitter `parser.c`/`scanner.c` files. |\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Suppressed comments (2)</summary>\\n\\n**internal/cli/progressbar.go:60**\\n* The progress bar treats the \\\"summary\\\" phase as \\\"relations\\\" and prints \\\"linking relations\\\" even though work is complete. Letting \\\"summary\\\" fall through to the default branch will render the final 100% file bar instead, which reads as completion.\\n```\\n\\tswitch e.Phase {\\n\\tcase \\\"relations\\\", \\\"summary\\\":\\n\\t\\tline = fmt.Sprintf(\\\"%s %c linking relations · %s relations · %s symbols · %s\\\",\\n\\t\\t\\tb.label, spin, humanInt(int64(e.Relations)), humanInt(int64(e.Symbols)), elapsed)\\n```\\n**internal/cli/help.go:99**\\n'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":14666}},"started_at_ms":1794842137594,"completed_at_ms":1794842137595}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:37.794Z","ordinal":3072,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-4293c56d-2f11-4535-81cd-09d2d240d0ae","process_id":"17019","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/entire-graph-78.json' '* `index --help` currently documents `--head` as if it changes behavior, but `parseIndexFlags` explicitly ignores `--head` (indexing is always committed HEAD). Either remove `--head` from the index docs, or document it as a no-op/compatibility flag to avoid misleading users.\\n```\\n\\t\\t\\t{name: \\\"--repo\\\", arg: \\\"path\\\", desc: \\\"Repository to index (default: current repo)\\\"},\\n\\t\\t\\t{name: \\\"--head\\\", desc: \\\"Index the committed tree (cached, reusable) instead of the working tree\\\"},\\n\\t\\t\\t{name: \\\"--force\\\", desc: \\\"Rebuild from scratch and overwrite the cache even if the tree is unchanged\\\"},\\n\\t\\t\\t{name: \\\"--profile\\\", arg: \\\"syntax-only|fast|full\\\", def: \\\"full\\\", desc: \\\"Parsing depth; full favors call-graph correctness\\\"},\\n\\t\\t\\t{name: \\\"--cache-dir\\\", arg: \\\"path\\\", desc: \\\"Override the committed-tree cache directory\\\"},\\n```\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n💡 <a href=\\\"/entireio/entire-graph/new/main?filename=.github/instructions/*.instructions.md\\\" class=\\\"Link--inTextBlock\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\\\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\\\" class=\\\"Link--inTextBlock\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Learn how to get started</a>.\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"name\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 4839415591,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-08-02T18:18:30Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<h2 dir=\\\"auto\\\">Pull request overview</h2>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">This PR overhauls the <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">entire graph</code> CLI help system, improves <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">index</code> UX (progress + human summary + <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--force</code>), and fixes completeness reporting by introducing a repo-root <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">.graphignore</code> and adjusting which partial failures count toward “degraded”.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>Changes:</strong></p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>Replace the monolithic help blob with a centralized help registry that powers grouped root help plus per-command <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--help</code>.</li>\\n<li>Improve <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">index</code> usability with a terminal-only progress bar, optional human-readable summary, and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--force</code> cache refresh behavior.</li>\\n<li>Reduce false “completeness: degraded” reports via <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">.graphignore</code> and excluding intentional-skip failure codes from completeness level calculation.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<h3 dir=\\\"auto\\\">Reviewed changes</h3>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Copilot reviewed 14 out of 14 changed files in this pull request and generated 4 comments.</p>\\n<details>\\n<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>\\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role=\\\"table\\\">\\n<thead>\\n<tr>\\n<th>File</th>\\n<th>Description</th>\\n</tr>\\n</thead>\\n<tbody>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/sem/search_cache.go</td>\\n<td>Adds <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">ForceRebuild</code> handling to preindex snapshot creation/persistence.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/sem/search_cache_test.go</td>\\n<td>Adds regression test pinning <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--force</code> preindex cache overwrite behavior.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/sem/provider.go</td>\\n<td>Improves progress cadence and adjusts completeness computation to ignore intentional skips.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/sem/ignore.go</td>\\n<td>Loads repo-root <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">.graphignore</code> for both worktree and explicit ignore matchers.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/sem/completeness_test.go</td>\\n<td>Tests <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">.graphignore</code> matcher behavior and skip-code exclusion from completeness.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/cli/stats_test.go</td>\\n<td>Updates help assertions to reflect new per-command <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--help</code> behavior.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/cli/root.go</td>\\n<td>Centralizes per-command help interception and improves unknown-command messaging.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/cli/root_test.go</td>\\n<td>Adjusts help-related test to assert per-command help output.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/cli/progressbar.go</td>\\n<td>Adds dependency-free terminal progress bar rendering utilities.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/cli/progressbar_test.go</td>\\n<td>Adds tests for TTY detection and progress bar rendering/clearing.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/cli/index.go</td>\\n<td>Implements <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--force</code>, progress bar wiring, and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--format</code>-based text/JSON output selection.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/cli/help.go</td>\\n<td>Introduces command help registry + renderers for grouped root help and per-command help.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/cli/help_test.go</td>\\n<td>Adds parity tests between dispatch switch and help registry; tests <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--help</code> interception.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>.graphignore</td>\\n<td>Adds repo-root ignore patterns to exclude generated tree-sitter <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">parser.c</code>/<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">scanner.c</code> files.</td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody>\\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\\n</details>\\n<details>\\n<summary>Suppressed comments (2)</summary>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>internal/cli/progressbar.go:60</strong></p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>The progress bar treats the \\\"summary\\\" phase as \\\"relations\\\" and prints \\\"linking relations\\\" even though work is complete. Letting \\\"summary\\\" fall through to the default branch will render the final 100% file bar instead, which reads as completion.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<div class=\\\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\\\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\\\"\\tswitch e.Phase {\\n\\tcase &quot;relations&quot;, &quot;summary&quot;:\\n\\t\\tline = fmt.Sprintf(&quot;%s %c linking relations · %s relations · %s symbols · %s&quot;,\\n\\t\\t\\tb.label, spin, humanInt(int64(e.Relations)), humanInt(int64(e.Symbols)), elapsed)\\\"><pre class=\\\"notranslate\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">\\tswitch e.Phase {\\n\\tcase \\\"relations\\\", \\\"summary\\\":\\n\\t\\tline = fmt.Sprintf(\\\"%s %c linking relations · %s relations · %s symbols · %s\\\",\\n\\t\\t\\tb.label, spin, humanInt(int64(e.Relations)), humanInt(int64(e.Symbols)), elapsed)\\n</code></pre></div>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>internal/cli/help.go:99</strong></p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">index --help</code> currently documents <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--head</code> as if it changes behavior, but <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">parseIndexFlags</code> explicitly ignores <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--head</code> (indexing is always committed HEAD). Either remove <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--head</code> from the index docs, or document it as a no-op/compatibility flag to avoid misleading users.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<div class=\\\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\\\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\\\"\\t\\t\\t{name: &quot;--repo&quot;, arg: &quot;path&quot;, desc: &quot;Repository to index (default: current repo)&quot;},\\n\\t\\t\\t{name: &quot;--head&quot;, desc: &quot;Index the committed tree (cached, reusable) instead of the working tree&quot;},\\n\\t\\t\\t{name: &quot;--force&quot;, desc: &quot;Rebuild from scratch and overwrite the cache even if the tree is unchanged&quot;},\\n\\t\\t\\t{name: &quot;--profile&quot;, arg: &quot;syntax-only|fast|full&quot;, def: &quot;full&quot;, desc: &quot;Parsing depth; full favors call-graph correctness&quot;},\\n\\t\\t\\t{name: &quot;--cache-dir&quot;, arg: &quot;path&quot;, desc: &quot;Override the committed-tree cache directory&quot;},\\\"><pre class=\\\"notranslate\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">\\t\\t\\t{name: \\\"--repo\\\", arg: \\\"path\\\", desc: \\\"Repository to index (default: current repo)\\\"},\\n\\t\\t\\t{name: \\\"--head\\\", desc: \\\"Index the committed tree (cached, reusable) instead of the working tree\\\"},\\n\\t\\t\\t{name: \\\"--force\\\", desc: \\\"Rebuild from scratch and overwrite the cache even if the tree is unchanged\\\"},\\n\\t\\t\\t{name: \\\"--profile\\\", arg: \\\"syntax-only|fast|full\\\", def: \\\"full\\\", desc: \\\"Parsing depth; full favors call-graph correctness\\\"},\\n\\t\\t\\t{name: \\\"--cache-dir\\\", arg: \\\"path\\\", desc: \\\"Override the committed-tree cache directory\\\"},\\n</code></pre></div>\\n</details>\\n<hr>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">💡 <a href=\\\"/entireio/entire-graph/new/main?filename=.github/instructions/*.instructions.md\\\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\\\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\\\">Learn how to get started</a>.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/78#pullrequestreview-4839497058\",\n        \"body\": \"## Pull request overview\\n\\nCopilot reviewed 14 out of 14 changed files in this pull request and generated no new comments.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Suppressed comments (2)</summary>\\n\\n**internal/cli/index.go:67**\\n* Current logic treats an omitted --format as \\\"auto\\\" (case \\\"\\\", \\\"auto\\\"), which changes the default stdout format from JSON to text when stdout is a terminal. The PR description states there is no flag/default/machine-output change; this default change can break scripts that run `entire graph index` interactively and parse JSON. If compatibility is required, keep the historical default as JSON and require explicit `--format auto`/`--format text` for the human summary (or update the PR description/release notes to acknowledge the default change).\\n```\\n\\t\\toutputText = false\\n\\tcase \\\"text\\\":\\n\\t\\toutputText = true\\n\\tcase \\\"\\\", \\\"auto\\\":\\n\\t\\toutputText = isTerminal(opts.Stdout)\\n```\\n**internal/cli/help_test.go:11**\\n* The comment says dispatchCommands excludes the help/version aliases, but the slice includes both \\\"help\\\" and \\\"version\\\". This makes the test guidance confusing for future edits.\\n```\\n// dispatchCommands mirrors the real command tokens handled by Run'\"'\"'s switch in\\n// root.go (excluding the help/version meta aliases: help, --help, -h, --version,\\n// -v). If you add a command to the switch, add it here and give it a commandDoc.\\n```\\n</details>\\n\\n\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"name\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 4839497058,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-08-02T19:04:22Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<h2 dir=\\\"auto\\\">Pull request overview</h2>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Copilot reviewed 14 out of 14 changed files in this pull request and generated no new comments.</p>\\n<details>\\n<summary>Suppressed comments (2)</summary>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>internal/cli/index.go:67</strong></p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>Current logic treats an omitted --format as \\\"auto\\\" (case \\\"\\\", \\\"auto\\\"), which changes the default stdout format from JSON to text when stdout is a terminal. The PR description states there is no flag/default/machine-output change; this default change can break scripts that run <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">entire graph index</code> interactively and parse JSON. If compatibility is required, keep the historical default as JSON and require explicit <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--format auto</code>/<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--format text</code> for the human summary (or update the PR description/release notes to acknowledge the default change).</li>\\n</ul>\\n<div class=\\\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\\\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\\\"\\t\\toutputText = false\\n\\tcase &quot;text&quot;:\\n\\t\\toutputText = true\\n\\tcase &quot;&quot;, &quot;auto&quot;:\\n\\t\\toutputText = isTerminal(opts.Stdout)\\\"><pre class=\\\"notranslate\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">\\t\\toutputText = false\\n\\tcase \\\"text\\\":\\n\\t\\toutputText = true\\n\\tcase \\\"\\\", \\\"auto\\\":\\n\\t\\toutputText = isTerminal(opts.Stdout)\\n</code></pre></div>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>internal/cli/help_test.go:11</strong></p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>The comment says dispatchCommands excludes the help/version aliases, but the slice includes both \\\"help\\\" and \\\"version\\\". This makes the test guidance confusing for future edits.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<div class=\\\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\\\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\\\"// dispatchCommands mirrors the real command tokens handled by Run'\"'\"'s switch in\\n// root.go (excluding the help/version meta aliases: help, --help, -h, --version,\\n// -v). If you add a command to the switch, add it here and give it a commandDoc.\\\"><pre class=\\\"notranslate\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">// dispatchCommands mirrors the real command tokens handled by Run'\"'\"'s switch in\\n// root.go (excluding the help/version meta aliases: help, --help, -h, --version,\\n// -v). If you add a command to the switch, add it here and give it a commandDoc.\\n</code></pre></div>\\n</details>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/78#pullrequestreview-4839589781\",\n        \"body\": \"## Pull request overview\\n\\nCopilot reviewed 14 out of 14 changed files in this pull request and generated no new comments.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Suppressed comments (2)</summary>\\n\\n**internal/cli/index.go:70**\\n* The new default behavior for `index` is now format auto (text when stdout is a terminal), and `--format` accepts new values (`text|auto`) instead of requiring JSON. That’s a user-visible default/flag-surface change, which contradicts the PR description’s claim of “No ... flag [or] default ... change”.\\n\\nEither update the PR description to reflect the intentional default/flag expansion, or keep the previous default (`json`) and require an explicit `--format auto|text` opt-in for the new human-friendly output.\\n```\\n\\tcase \\\"\\\", \\\"auto\\\":\\n\\t\\toutputText = isTerminal(opts.Stdout)\\n\\tdefault:\\n\\t\\treturn fmt.Errorf(\\\"index --format must be json, text, or auto, got %q\\\", flags.Format)\\n\\t}\\n```\\n**internal/sem/ignore.go:52**\\n* `.graphignore` is now implicitly loaded and affects which paths are included in snapshots, but it is not part of the snapshot cache key (the key only hashes the git tree plus explicit --ignore-file/--include-file contents). If a user edits or adds `.graphignore` without changing the committed tree (e.g. uncommitted local change), a previously cached snapshot for the same tree can be reused even though the effective ignore rules changed, leading to stale/incorrect results.\\n\\nConsider incorporating the resolved `.graphignore` content into the cache key (similar to how explicit ignore/include files are hashed), or reading `.graphignore` from the committed tree for --head snapshots so cache keys remain correct and deterministic.\\n```\\n\\tif err := matcher.loadOptional(filepath.Join(repo, \\\".gitignore\\\"), false); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn ignoreMatcher{}, err\\n\\t}\\n\\tif err := matcher.loadOptional(filepath.Join(repo, graphIgnoreFileName), false); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn ignoreMatcher{}, err\\n```\\n</details>\\n\\n\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"name\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 4839589781,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-08-02T20:00:05Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<h2 dir=\\\"auto\\\">Pull request overview</h2>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Copilot reviewed 14 out of 14 changed files in this pull request and generated no new comments.</p>\\n<details>\\n<summary>Suppressed comments (2)</summary>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>internal/cli/index.go:70</strong></p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>The new default behavior for <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">index</code> is now format auto (text when stdout is a terminal), and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--format</code> accepts new values (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">text|auto</code>) instead of requiring JSON. That’s a user-visible default/flag-surface change, which contradicts the PR description’s claim of “No ... flag [or] default ... change”.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Either update the PR description to reflect the intentional default/flag expansion, or keep the previous default (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">json</code>) and require an explicit <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--format auto|text</code> opt-in for the new human-friendly output.</p>\\n<div class=\\\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\\\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\\\"\\tcase &quot;&quot;, &quot;auto&quot;:\\n\\t\\toutputText = isTerminal(opts.Stdout)\\n\\tdefault:\\n\\t\\treturn fmt.Errorf(&quot;index --format must be json, text, or auto, got %q&quot;, flags.Format)\\n\\t}\\\"><pre class=\\\"notranslate\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">\\tcase \\\"\\\", \\\"auto\\\":\\n\\t\\toutputText = isTerminal(opts.Stdout)\\n\\tdefault:\\n\\t\\treturn fmt.Errorf(\\\"index --format must be json, text, or auto, got %q\\\", flags.Format)\\n\\t}\\n</code></pre></div>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>intern'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/entire-graph-78.json' '* `index --help` currently documents `--head` as if it changes behavior, but `parseIndexFlags` explicitly ignores `--head` (indexing is always committed HEAD). Either remove `--head` from the index docs, or document it as a no-op/compatibility flag to avoid misleading users.\\n```\\n\\t\\t\\t{name: \\\"--repo\\\", arg: \\\"path\\\", desc: \\\"Repository to index (default: current repo)\\\"},\\n\\t\\t\\t{name: \\\"--head\\\", desc: \\\"Index the committed tree (cached, reusable) instead of the working tree\\\"},\\n\\t\\t\\t{name: \\\"--force\\\", desc: \\\"Rebuild from scratch and overwrite the cache even if the tree is unchanged\\\"},\\n\\t\\t\\t{name: \\\"--profile\\\", arg: \\\"syntax-only|fast|full\\\", def: \\\"full\\\", desc: \\\"Parsing depth; full favors call-graph correctness\\\"},\\n\\t\\t\\t{name: \\\"--cache-dir\\\", arg: \\\"path\\\", desc: \\\"Override the committed-tree cache directory\\\"},\\n```\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n💡 <a href=\\\"/entireio/entire-graph/new/main?filename=.github/instructions/*.instructions.md\\\" class=\\\"Link--inTextBlock\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\\\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\\\" class=\\\"Link--inTextBlock\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Learn how to get started</a>.\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"name\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 4839415591,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-08-02T18:18:30Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<h2 dir=\\\"auto\\\">Pull request overview</h2>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">This PR overhauls the <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">entire graph</code> CLI help system, improves <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">index</code> UX (progress + human summary + <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--force</code>), and fixes completeness reporting by introducing a repo-root <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">.graphignore</code> and adjusting which partial failures count toward “degraded”.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>Changes:</strong></p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>Replace the monolithic help blob with a centralized help registry that powers grouped root help plus per-command <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--help</code>.</li>\\n<li>Improve <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">index</code> usability with a terminal-only progress bar, optional human-readable summary, and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--force</code> cache refresh behavior.</li>\\n<li>Reduce false “completeness: degraded” reports via <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">.graphignore</code> and excluding intentional-skip failure codes from completeness level calculation.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<h3 dir=\\\"auto\\\">Reviewed changes</h3>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Copilot reviewed 14 out of 14 changed files in this pull request and generated 4 comments.</p>\\n<details>\\n<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>\\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role=\\\"table\\\">\\n<thead>\\n<tr>\\n<th>File</th>\\n<th>Description</th>\\n</tr>\\n</thead>\\n<tbody>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/sem/search_cache.go</td>\\n<td>Adds <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">ForceRebuild</code> handling to preindex snapshot creation/persistence.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/sem/search_cache_test.go</td>\\n<td>Adds regression test pinning <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--force</code> preindex cache overwrite behavior.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/sem/provider.go</td>\\n<td>Improves progress cadence and adjusts completeness computation to ignore intentional skips.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/sem/ignore.go</td>\\n<td>Loads repo-root <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">.graphignore</code> for both worktree and explicit ignore matchers.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/sem/completeness_test.go</td>\\n<td>Tests <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">.graphignore</code> matcher behavior and skip-code exclusion from completeness.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/cli/stats_test.go</td>\\n<td>Updates help assertions to reflect new per-command <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--help</code> behavior.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/cli/root.go</td>\\n<td>Centralizes per-command help interception and improves unknown-command messaging.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/cli/root_test.go</td>\\n<td>Adjusts help-related test to assert per-command help output.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/cli/progressbar.go</td>\\n<td>Adds dependency-free terminal progress bar rendering utilities.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/cli/progressbar_test.go</td>\\n<td>Adds tests for TTY detection and progress bar rendering/clearing.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/cli/index.go</td>\\n<td>Implements <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--force</code>, progress bar wiring, and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--format</code>-based text/JSON output selection.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/cli/help.go</td>\\n<td>Introduces command help registry + renderers for grouped root help and per-command help.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>internal/cli/help_test.go</td>\\n<td>Adds parity tests between dispatch switch and help registry; tests <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--help</code> interception.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>.graphignore</td>\\n<td>Adds repo-root ignore patterns to exclude generated tree-sitter <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">parser.c</code>/<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">scanner.c</code> files.</td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody>\\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\\n</details>\\n<details>\\n<summary>Suppressed comments (2)</summary>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>internal/cli/progressbar.go:60</strong></p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>The progress bar treats the \\\"summary\\\" phase as \\\"relations\\\" and prints \\\"linking relations\\\" even though work is complete. Letting \\\"summary\\\" fall through to the default branch will render the final 100% file bar instead, which reads as completion.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<div class=\\\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\\\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\\\"\\tswitch e.Phase {\\n\\tcase &quot;relations&quot;, &quot;summary&quot;:\\n\\t\\tline = fmt.Sprintf(&quot;%s %c linking relations · %s relations · %s symbols · %s&quot;,\\n\\t\\t\\tb.label, spin, humanInt(int64(e.Relations)), humanInt(int64(e.Symbols)), elapsed)\\\"><pre class=\\\"notranslate\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">\\tswitch e.Phase {\\n\\tcase \\\"relations\\\", \\\"summary\\\":\\n\\t\\tline = fmt.Sprintf(\\\"%s %c linking relations · %s relations · %s symbols · %s\\\",\\n\\t\\t\\tb.label, spin, humanInt(int64(e.Relations)), humanInt(int64(e.Symbols)), elapsed)\\n</code></pre></div>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>internal/cli/help.go:99</strong></p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">index --help</code> currently documents <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--head</code> as if it changes behavior, but <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">parseIndexFlags</code> explicitly ignores <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--head</code> (indexing is always committed HEAD). Either remove <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--head</code> from the index docs, or document it as a no-op/compatibility flag to avoid misleading users.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<div class=\\\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\\\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\\\"\\t\\t\\t{name: &quot;--repo&quot;, arg: &quot;path&quot;, desc: &quot;Repository to index (default: current repo)&quot;},\\n\\t\\t\\t{name: &quot;-