ex.go:67**\\n* Current logic treats an omitted --format as \\\"auto\\\" (case \\\"\\\", \\\"auto\\\"), which changes the default stdout format from JSON to text when stdout is a terminal. The PR description states there is no flag/default/machine-output change; this default change can break scripts that run `entire graph index` interactively and parse JSON. If compatibility is required, keep the historical default as JSON and require explicit `--format auto`/`--format text` for the human summary (or update the PR description/release notes to acknowledge the default change).\\n```\\n\\t\\toutputText = false\\n\\tcase \\\"text\\\":\\n\\t\\toutputText = true\\n\\tcase \\\"\\\", \\\"auto\\\":\\n\\t\\toutputText = isTerminal(opts.Stdout)\\n```\\n**internal/cli/help_test.go:11**\\n* The comment says dispatchCommands excludes the help/version aliases, but the slice includes both \\\"help\\\" and \\\"version\\\". This makes the test guidance confusing for future edits.\\n```\\n// dispatchCommands mirrors the real command tokens handled by Run'\"'\"'s switch in\\n// root.go (excluding the help/version meta aliases: help, --help, -h, --version,\\n// -v). If you add a command to the switch, add it here and give it a commandDoc.\\n```\\n</details>\\n\\n\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"name\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 4839497058,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-08-02T19:04:22Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<h2 dir=\\\"auto\\\">Pull request overview</h2>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Copilot reviewed 14 out of 14 changed files in this pull request and generated no new comments.</p>\\n<details>\\n<summary>Suppressed comments (2)</summary>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>internal/cli/index.go:67</strong></p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>Current logic treats an omitted --format as \\\"auto\\\" (case \\\"\\\", \\\"auto\\\"), which changes the default stdout format from JSON to text when stdout is a terminal. The PR description states there is no flag/default/machine-output change; this default change can break scripts that run <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">entire graph index</code> interactively and parse JSON. If compatibility is required, keep the historical default as JSON and require explicit <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--format auto</code>/<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--format text</code> for the human summary (or update the PR description/release notes to acknowledge the default change).</li>\\n</ul>\\n<div class=\\\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\\\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\\\"\\t\\toutputText = false\\n\\tcase &quot;text&quot;:\\n\\t\\toutputText = true\\n\\tcase &quot;&quot;, &quot;auto&quot;:\\n\\t\\toutputText = isTerminal(opts.Stdout)\\\"><pre class=\\\"notranslate\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">\\t\\toutputText = false\\n\\tcase \\\"text\\\":\\n\\t\\toutputText = true\\n\\tcase \\\"\\\", \\\"auto\\\":\\n\\t\\toutputText = isTerminal(opts.Stdout)\\n</code></pre></div>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>internal/cli/help_test.go:11</strong></p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>The comment says dispatchCommands excludes the help/version aliases, but the slice includes both \\\"help\\\" and \\\"version\\\". This makes the test guidance confusing for future edits.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<div class=\\\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\\\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\\\"// dispatchCommands mirrors the real command tokens handled by Run'\"'\"'s switch in\\n// root.go (excluding the help/version meta aliases: help, --help, -h, --version,\\n// -v). If you add a command to the switch, add it here and give it a commandDoc.\\\"><pre class=\\\"notranslate\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">// dispatchCommands mirrors the real command tokens handled by Run'\"'\"'s switch in\\n// root.go (excluding the help/version meta aliases: help, --help, -h, --version,\\n// -v). If you add a command to the switch, add it here and give it a commandDoc.\\n</code></pre></div>\\n</details>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/78#pullrequestreview-4839589781\",\n        \"body\": \"## Pull request overview\\n\\nCopilot reviewed 14 out of 14 changed files in this pull request and generated no new comments.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Suppressed comments (2)</summary>\\n\\n**internal/cli/index.go:70**\\n* The new default behavior for `index` is now format auto (text when stdout is a terminal), and `--format` accepts new values (`text|auto`) instead of requiring JSON. That’s a user-visible default/flag-surface change, which contradicts the PR description’s claim of “No ... flag [or] default ... change”.\\n\\nEither update the PR description to reflect the intentional default/flag expansion, or keep the previous default (`json`) and require an explicit `--format auto|text` opt-in for the new human-friendly output.\\n```\\n\\tcase \\\"\\\", \\\"auto\\\":\\n\\t\\toutputText = isTerminal(opts.Stdout)\\n\\tdefault:\\n\\t\\treturn fmt.Errorf(\\\"index --format must be json, text, or auto, got %q\\\", flags.Format)\\n\\t}\\n```\\n**internal/sem/ignore.go:52**\\n* `.graphignore` is now implicitly loaded and affects which paths are included in snapshots, but it is not part of the snapshot cache key (the key only hashes the git tree plus explicit --ignore-file/--include-file contents). If a user edits or adds `.graphignore` without changing the committed tree (e.g. uncommitted local change), a previously cached snapshot for the same tree can be reused even though the effective ignore rules changed, leading to stale/incorrect results.\\n\\nConsider incorporating the resolved `.graphignore` content into the cache key (similar to how explicit ignore/include files are hashed), or reading `.graphignore` from the committed tree for --head snapshots so cache keys remain correct and deterministic.\\n```\\n\\tif err := matcher.loadOptional(filepath.Join(repo, \\\".gitignore\\\"), false); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn ignoreMatcher{}, err\\n\\t}\\n\\tif err := matcher.loadOptional(filepath.Join(repo, graphIgnoreFileName), false); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn ignoreMatcher{}, err\\n```\\n</details>\\n\\n\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"name\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 4839589781,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-08-02T20:00:05Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<h2 dir=\\\"auto\\\">Pull request overview</h2>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Copilot reviewed 14 out of 14 changed files in this pull request and generated no new comments.</p>\\n<details>\\n<summary>Suppressed comments (2)</summary>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>internal/cli/index.go:70</strong></p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>The new default behavior for <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">index</code> is now format auto (text when stdout is a terminal), and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--format</code> accepts new values (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">text|auto</code>) instead of requiring JSON. That’s a user-visible default/flag-surface change, which contradicts the PR description’s claim of “No ... flag [or] default ... change”.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Either update the PR description to reflect the intentional default/flag expansion, or keep the previous default (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">json</code>) and require an explicit <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--format auto|text</code> opt-in for the new human-friendly output.</p>\\n<div class=\\\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\\\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\\\"\\tcase &quot;&quot;, &quot;auto&quot;:\\n\\t\\toutputText = isTerminal(opts.Stdout)\\n\\tdefault:\\n\\t\\treturn fmt.Errorf(&quot;index --format must be json, text, or auto, got %q&quot;, flags.Format)\\n\\t}\\\"><pre class=\\\"notranslate\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">\\tcase \\\"\\\", \\\"auto\\\":\\n\\t\\toutputText = isTerminal(opts.Stdout)\\n\\tdefault:\\n\\t\\treturn fmt.Errorf(\\\"index --format must be json, text, or auto, got %q\\\", flags.Format)\\n\\t}\\n</code></pre></div>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>intern'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":39042}},"started_at_ms":1794842137793,"completed_at_ms":1794842137793}}
