request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-08-02T20:52:03Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<h2 dir=\\\"auto\\\">Pull request overview</h2>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Copilot reviewed 14 out of 14 changed files in this pull request and generated no new comments.</p>\\n<details>\\n<summary>Suppressed comments (2)</summary>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>internal/cli/progressbar.go:70</strong></p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>The progress bar treats the final \\\"summary\\\" phase as if it were still \\\"relations\\\" and prints \\\"linking relations\\\". That’s misleading at the moment the run is finishing (after relations are fully linked). Consider rendering a distinct message for the summary/finalization tick.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<div class=\\\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\\\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\\\"\\tswitch e.Phase {\\n\\tcase &quot;relations&quot;, &quot;summary&quot;:\\n\\t\\tline = fmt.Sprintf(&quot;%s %c linking relations · %s relations · %s symbols · %s&quot;,\\n\\t\\t\\tb.label, spin, humanInt(int64(e.Relations)), humanInt(int64(e.Symbols)), elapsed)\\n\\tdefault: // start, parse — file parsing, with a known total\\\"><pre class=\\\"notranslate\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">\\tswitch e.Phase {\\n\\tcase \\\"relations\\\", \\\"summary\\\":\\n\\t\\tline = fmt.Sprintf(\\\"%s %c linking relations · %s relations · %s symbols · %s\\\",\\n\\t\\t\\tb.label, spin, humanInt(int64(e.Relations)), humanInt(int64(e.Symbols)), elapsed)\\n\\tdefault: // start, parse — file parsing, with a known total\\n</code></pre></div>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>internal/cli/help.go:96</strong></p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>The index command always targets committed HEAD (parseIndexFlags treats --head as a no-