wner}{/repo}\",\n      \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/subscriptions\",\n      \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/orgs\",\n      \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/repos\",\n      \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/events{/privacy}\",\n      \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ashtom/received_events\",\n      \"type\": \"User\",\n      \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n      \"site_admin\": false\n    },\n    \"comments\": 0,\n    \"review_comments\": 1,\n    \"maintainer_can_modify\": false,\n    \"commits\": 17,\n    \"additions\": 2947,\n    \"deletions\": 513,\n    \"changed_files\": 43\n  },\n  \"c\": {\n    \"comments\": [\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/113#discussion_r3798725112\",\n        \"body\": \"This drops the only concrete, checkable claim the docs made about no-egress.\\n\\nThe archived version pointed to `entire graph doctor --json` reporting `no_egress=true` — a command a reader or a CI job can actually run to verify it. This PR removes every mention of `doctor` from all active docs (AGENTS.md, README.md, docs/operations.md, docs/commands.md, docs/semantic-provider-requirements.md) and replaces the concrete claim here with \\\"does not fetch remote code... send telemetry,\\\" which names nothing a reader can run to check it themselves.\\n\\n`doctor` still exists, still does exactly this job (`internal/cli/help.go:402-414`, \\\"Diagnose the environment and confirm no-egress\\\"). It just is not discoverable from the one doc that is specifically about trust. Worth adding it back here, since this page'\"'\"'s own framing is \\\"scoped precisely enough to be checked.\\\"\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n          \"name\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 257360244\n        },\n        \"id\": 3798725112,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 4954478699,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-08-17T20:53:14Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-17T20:53:14Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": 7,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": \"docs/trust-and-security.md\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">This drops the only concrete, checkable claim the docs made about no-egress.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">The archived version pointed to <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">entire graph doctor --json</code> reporting <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">no_egress=true</code> — a command a reader or a CI job can actually run to verify it. This PR removes every mention of <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">doctor</code> from all active docs (AGENTS.md, README.md, docs/operations.md, docs/commands.md, docs/semantic-provider-requirements.md) and replaces the concrete claim here with \\\"does not fetch remote code... send telemetry,\\\" which names nothing a reader can run to check it themselves.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">doctor</code> still exists, still does exactly this job (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">internal/cli/help.go:402-414</code>, \\\"Diagnose the environment and confirm no-egress\\\"). It just is not discoverable from the one doc that is specifically about trust. Worth adding it back here, since this page'\"'\"'s own framing is \\\"scoped precisely enough to be checked.\\\"</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/113#pullrequestreview-4954478699\",\n        \"body\": \"\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n          \"name\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?u=a1498efdbbb40213f50947343a04d90cdc980730&v=4\",\n          \"id\": 257360244\n        },\n        \"id\": 4954478699,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-08-17T20:53:14Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/113\",\n    \"title\": \"entireio/entire-graph PR #113 comments\",\n    \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/113\",\n    \"display_title\": \"entireio/entire-graph PR #113 comments\"\n  }\n}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":12042}},"started_at_ms":1794842138516,"completed_at_ms":1794842138517}}
