{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:38.813Z","ordinal":3078,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-795c3f11-fee0-4d2d-af90-d4253c8ad0fd","process_id":"36007","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/forgemark-14.json' '{\n  \"p\": {\n    \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/forgemark/pulls/14\",\n    \"id\": 4158623182,\n    \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOTKIlTs73343O\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/14\",\n    \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/14.diff\",\n    \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/14.patch\",\n    \"issue_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/forgemark/issues/14\",\n    \"commits_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/forgemark/pulls/14/commits\",\n    \"review_comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/forgemark/pulls/14/comments\",\n    \"review_comment_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/forgemark/pulls/comments{/number}\",\n    \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/forgemark/issues/14/comments\",\n    \"statuses_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/forgemark/statuses/2ce331e59038961ccfe065a71d773206920020c4\",\n    \"number\": 14,\n    \"state\": \"open\",\n    \"locked\": false,\n    \"title\": \"feat: monitor output + CI performance gate\",\n    \"user\": {\n      \"login\": \"karthik-rameshkumar\",\n      \"id\": 6728802,\n      \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjg4MDI=\",\n      \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6728802?v=4\",\n      \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/karthik-rameshkumar\",\n      \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/followers\",\n      \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/following{/other_user}\",\n      \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/gists{/gist_id}\",\n      \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n      \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/subscriptions\",\n      \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/orgs\",\n      \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/repos\",\n      \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/events{/privacy}\",\n      \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/karthik-rameshkumar/received_events\",\n      \"type\": \"User\",\n      \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n      \"site_admin\": false\n    },\n    \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nTwo halves of the same story: **emit a gateable number, then gate on it.**\\n\\n1. **`forgemark report --emit monitor <results.json>`** reduces a stored result doc to one headline metric — **peak sustained ops/sec across the sweep** — in the Entire trail runner'\"'\"'s `last_json_line` monitor contract:\\n\\n   ```\\n   {\\\"value\\\":42.7,\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"peak push 42.7 ops/s @ c=32 | c=1 8.1, c=8 28.4, c=32 42.7 | p95 210ms | 0 errors\\\"}\\n   ```\\n\\n2. **`.github/workflows/perf-gate.yml`** consumes that value: it runs forgemark against a real forge and fails when peak throughput drops below a floor.\\n\\n### report\\n\\n- `--emit monitor` (default) prints exactly the `{\\\"value\\\",\\\"rationale\\\"}` object as the last JSON line of stdout. `--emit text` prints a human summary.\\n- `value` = peak OK ops/sec of the selected target (push side; clone/sec for `-strategy clone`, labeled accordingly).\\n- A target that **died or measured nothing reports `value: 0`**, so a gate reads it as a regression, not a silent pass.\\n- `-target <name>` selects among a multi-target comparison doc; default is the first target.\\n- Reads legacy format-1 and format-2 docs — `results.LoadPath` applies the same normalization `Load` does, with normalization now in one shared decoder.\\n\\n### perf gate\\n\\n- `workflow_dispatch` + nightly `schedule`, **not** `pull_request`: a live git load test needs a credential and sustained egress, so it runs on demand / on a schedule, never blocking every PR. GitHub-hosted runners have egress but no regional placement (see README caveat).\\n- Live job uses `FORGEMARK_REMOTE` / `FORGEMARK_REPOS` / `FORGEMARK_TOKEN` secrets and skips cleanly when they'\"'\"'re absent.\\n- Gates purely on the monitor value (jq + a value floor), so it depends only on `report` here — it does **not** require the threshold flags in #6, though it composes with them.\\n- A secret-free `gate-smoke` job reduces `examples/sample-results.json` and asserts the floor logic both ways, covering the gate plumbing even when the live job skips.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- `TestMonitorFor` (peak selection incl. a non-monotonic dip, clone labeling, dead/empty → 0, error summing), `TestSelectTarget`, `TestRound1`, `results.TestLoadPath`.\\n- Verified the report live against synthetic format-2, legacy format-1, clone, and dead-target docs; verified the workflow smoke steps (build → report → jq → awk floor) locally, both pass-above-floor and fail-below-floor. `go build`, `go test ./...`, `gofmt -l`, `golangci-lint`, and workflow YAML all clean.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\n    \"labels\": [],\n    \"milestone\": null,\n    \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-07-29T08:32:36Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-29T09:18:44Z\",\n    \"closed_at\": null,\n    \"merged_at\": null,\n    \"merge_commit_sha\": null,\n    \"assignee\": null,\n    \"assignees\": [],\n    \"requested_reviewers\": [],\n    \"requested_teams\": [],\n    \"head\": {\n      \"label\": \"entireio:feat/monitor-adapter\",\n      \"ref\": \"feat/monitor-adapter\",\n      \"repo\": {\n        \"id\": 1285694798,\n        \"node_id\": \"R_kgDOTKIlTg\",\n        \"name\": \"forgemark\",\n        \"full_name\": \"entireio/forgemark\",\n        \"owner\": {\n          \"login\": \"entireio\",\n          \"id\": 33188652,\n          \"node_id\": \"REDACTED\",\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33188652?v=4\",\n          \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio\",\n          \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio\",\n          \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/followers\",\n          \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/following{/other_user}\",\n          \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/gists{/gist_id}\",\n          \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n          \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/subscriptions\",\n          \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/orgs\",\n          \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/repos\",\n          \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/events{/privacy}\",\n          \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/received_events\",\n          \"type\": \"Organization\",\n          \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n          \"site_admin\": false\n        },\n        \"private\": false,\n        \"fork\": false,\n        \"archived\": false,\n        \"disabled\": false,\n        \"description\": \"A concurrent git push/clone throughput benchmark for any smart-HTTP git forge.\",\n        \"homepage\": \"\",\n        \"language\": \"Go\",\n        \"visibility\": \"public\",\n        \"is_template\": false,\n        \"topics\": [],\n        \"forks_count\": 17,\n        \"forks\": 17,\n     