{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:39.206Z","ordinal":3081,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-d4095b2e-6d41-49dc-8ded-371c01854cf1","process_id":"53040","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/forgemark-6.json' '{\n  \"p\": {\n    \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/forgemark/pulls/6\",\n    \"id\": 4015961478,\n    \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOTKIlTs7vXrWG\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/6\",\n    \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/6.diff\",\n    \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark/pull/6.patch\",\n    \"issue_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/forgemark/issues/6\",\n    \"commits_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/forgemark/pulls/6/commits\",\n    \"review_comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/forgemark/pulls/6/comments\",\n    \"review_comment_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/forgemark/pulls/comments{/number}\",\n    \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/forgemark/issues/6/comments\",\n    \"statuses_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/forgemark/statuses/4492df3c22c07729070edf65b373895da562447f\",\n    \"number\": 6,\n    \"state\": \"open\",\n    \"locked\": false,\n    \"title\": \"feat: add threshold flags for CI regression gating\",\n    \"user\": {\n      \"login\": \"mvanhorn\",\n      \"id\": 455140,\n      \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NTE0MA==\",\n      \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/455140?v=4\",\n      \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mvanhorn\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/mvanhorn\",\n      \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mvanhorn/followers\",\n      \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mvanhorn/following{/other_user}\",\n      \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mvanhorn/gists{/gist_id}\",\n      \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mvanhorn/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n      \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mvanhorn/subscriptions\",\n      \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mvanhorn/orgs\",\n      \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mvanhorn/repos\",\n      \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mvanhorn/events{/privacy}\",\n      \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/mvanhorn/received_events\",\n      \"type\": \"User\",\n      \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n      \"site_admin\": false\n    },\n    \"body\": \"## Summary\\nforgemark can now gate CI runs: set `-min-push-rate`, `-max-p95`, or `-max-errors` and a sweep that misses any of them prints per-level breach lines to stderr and exits 2. All three flags default off; unset flags change nothing.\\n\\n## Why this matters\\nThe results JSON is written \\\"for charting\\\" (README), but the process itself always exits 0 - `run()` returns `writeResults(...)` without inspecting the measured levels, so a deploy that halves push throughput still reads as a passing benchmark. Both reference tools in this space gate on results: [GitLab Performance Tool](https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/support/workflows/gpt_quick_start/) ships built-in success thresholds on throughput and latency, and [k6](https://grafana.com/docs/k6/latest/using-k6/thresholds/) fails the process on a threshold breach. This adds the equivalent with three stdlib flags and a distinct exit code (0 ok, 1 operational error, 2 threshold breach), so a forge team can pin a floor on push/s and a ceiling on p95 in CI.\\n\\n## Demo\\nSimulated demo:\\n![demo](https://files.catbox.moe/abecxl.gif)\\n\\nVerified live against github.com: a c=1 run sustaining 1.0 push/s with `-min-push-rate 5 -max-p95 500ms` printed both breach lines and exited 2; the same run with `-min-push-rate 0.2 -max-p95 5s` exited 0 with `\\\"thresholds_ok\\\": true` in the JSON.\\n\\n## Changes\\n- Threshold evaluation is a pure function over the existing `levelResult` fields (`checkThresholds` in stats.go), run after `writeResults` so the JSON is always written even when the run fails the gate.\\n- Exit 2 is reserved for breaches via a sentinel error in `main()`, keeping it distinguishable from the hard-error exit 1 path.\\n- The `thresholds` block (configured values plus breach list) only appears in the results JSON when at least one flag is set; unset runs produce byte-identical output.\\n\\n## Testing\\nTable-driven `TestCheckThresholds` (breach / no-breach / unset), `TestParseFlagsThresholds`, and two `writeResults` JSON tests (thresholds present when configured, absent when unset). `go test ./...`, `go vet`, `gofmt`, and `golangci-lint` all pass locally.\\n\",\n    \"labels\": [],\n    \"milestone\": null,\n    \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-07-08T16:16:31Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-29T13:58:00Z\",\n    \"closed_at\": null,\n    \"merged_at\": null,\n    \"merge_commit_sha\": \"c9b214960bbaf62fede02e3204c5c66e1f7c35ff\",\n    \"assignee\": null,\n    \"assignees\": [],\n    \"requested_reviewers\": [],\n    \"requested_teams\": [],\n    \"head\": {\n      \"label\": \"mvanhorn:fix/forgemark-threshold-gate\",\n      \"ref\": \"fix/forgemark-threshold-gate\",\n      \"repo\": {\n        \"id\": 1293806585,\n        \"node_id\": \"R_kgDOTR3r-Q\",\n        \"name\": \"forgemark\",\n        \"full_name\": \"mvanhorn/forgemark\",\n        \"owner\": {\n          \"login\": \"mvanhorn\",\n          \"id\": 455140,\n          \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NTE0MA==\",\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/455140?v=4\",\n          \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.