{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:39.858Z","ordinal":3086,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-cfa3f586-ae0d-4a0c-9aca-9ee93ad992df","process_id":"72883","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/cli-1647.json' 'REDACTED\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-light.png\\\"><img alt=\\\"Fix All in Cursor\\\" width=\\\"115\\\" height=\\\"28\\\" src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"></picture></a>\\n<!-- /BUGBOT_FIX_ALL -->\\n\\n<!-- BUGBOT_AUTOFIX_REVIEW_FOOTNOTE_BEGIN -->\\n<sup>❌ Bugbot Autofix is OFF. To automatically fix reported issues with cloud agents, enable autofix in the [Cursor dashboard](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- BUGBOT_AUTOFIX_REVIEW_FOOTNOTE_END -->\\n\\nWant fixes drafted automatically? **Bugbot Autofix** can create code changes for findings. A team admin can enable Autofix in the [Cursor dashboard](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot/installation/1441364).\\n\\n_Comment `@cursor review` or `bugbot run` to trigger another review on this PR_\\n\\n\\n<sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit ac36d1773c3d0c7e7623550add333fbd3b56512b. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"cursor[bot]\",\n          \"name\": \"cursor[bot]\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1210556?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 206951365\n        },\n        \"id\": 4635418375,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-07-06T11:33:45Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Cursor Bugbot has reviewed your changes and found 1 potential issue.</p>\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><a href=\\\"https://cursor.com/open?REDACTED\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\"><themed-picture data-catalyst-inline=\\\"true\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/a3745bd9c9e494e3d083228c1efdaf4ec2d519ad1c6adb4160d1c56c1ddeeb7b/68747470733a2f2f637572736f722e636f6d2f6173736574732f696d616765732f6669782d696e2d637572736f722d6461726b2e706e67\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/8f892a2b1c7e36d49621daf12d83d3200c0ad6842ca1f6d8422631d06c99b3b2/68747470733a2f2f637572736f722e636f6d2f6173736574732f696d616765732f6669782d696e2d637572736f722d6c696768742e706e67\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-light.png\\\"><img alt=\\\"Fix All in Cursor\\\" width=\\\"115\\\" height=\\\"28\\\" src=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/a3745bd9c9e494e3d083228c1efdaf4ec2d519ad1c6adb4160d1c56c1ddeeb7b/68747470733a2f2f637572736f722e636f6d2f6173736574732f696d616765732f6669782d696e2d637572736f722d6461726b2e706e67\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"></picture></themed-picture></a></p>\\n\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><sup>❌ Bugbot Autofix is OFF. To automatically fix reported issues with cloud agents, enable autofix in the <a href=\\\"https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">Cursor dashboard</a>.</sup></p>\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Want fixes drafted automatically? <strong>Bugbot Autofix</strong> can create code changes for findings. A team admin can enable Autofix in the <a href=\\\"https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot/installation/1441364\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">Cursor dashboard</a>.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><em>Comment <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">@cursor review</code> or <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">bugbot run</code> to trigger another review on this PR</em></p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><sup>Reviewed by <a href=\\\"https://cursor.com/bugbot\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">Cursor Bugbot</a> for commit <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/cli/commit/ac36d1773c3d0c7e7623550add333fbd3b56512b/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/cli/commit/ac36d1773c3d0c7e7623550add333fbd3b56512b\\\"><tt>ac36d17</tt></a>. Configure <a href=\\\"https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">here</a>.</sup></p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1647#discussion_r3528517118\",\n        \"body\": \"scopeDiffInlineLimit is set to 48KiB, but the review prompt is passed both as a command-line argument (e.g. `claude -p <prompt>`) and via ENTIRE_REVIEW_PROMPT. On Windows, the command-line limit is ~32KiB, so a 48KiB inline diff can make reviewer spawning fail (and the env var value may also exceed platform/process limits). Consider lowering the inline diff budget (or making it OS-dependent) so prompts remain safely spawnable across platforms.\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"name\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 3528517118,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 4635440917,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-07-06T11:37:00Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-06T11:37:01Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": 276,\n        \"start_line\": 258,\n        \"path\": \"cmd/entire/cli/review/scope.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">scopeDiffInlineLimit is set to 48KiB, but the review prompt is passed both as a command-line argument (e.g. <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">claude -p &lt;prompt&gt;</code>) and via ENTIRE_REVIEW_PROMPT. On Windows, the command-line limit is ~32KiB, so a 48KiB inline diff can make reviewer spawning fail (and the env var value may also exceed platform/process limits). Consider lowering the inline diff budget (or making it OS-dependent) so prompts remain safely spawnable across platforms.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1647#discussion_r3528517144\",\n        \"body\": \"The diff is embedded inside a Markdown ```diff fence using raw `git diff` output. If the diff contains triple backticks (which can appear in code or docs), it can prematurely close the fence and corrupt the prompt structure (and potentially enable prompt-injection-style breakout into subsequent instructions). Escaping/sanitizing fence sequences before writing the diff avoids this.\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"name\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 3528517144,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 4635440917,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-07-06T11:37:01Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-06T11:37:01Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": 136,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": \"cmd/entire/cli/review/prompt.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">The diff is embedded inside a Markdown ```diff fence using raw <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">git diff</code> output. If the diff contains triple backticks (which can appear in code or docs), it can prematurely close the fence and corrupt the prompt structure (and potentially enable prompt-injection-style breakout into subsequent instructions). Escaping/sanitizing fence sequences before writing the diff avoids this.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1647#discussion_r3528517169\",\n        \"body\": \"The tool allowlist is intended to be read-only, but `Bash(git branch:*)` permits mutating operations like `git branch -d/-D/-m`, which can delete or rename branches. To keep reviewer children unable to modify repo state, remove this entry (or replace it with a narrower, listing-only alternative).\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"name\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 3528517169,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 4635440917,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-07-06T11:37:01Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-06T11:37:01Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": \"cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/reviewer.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">The tool allowlist is intended to be read-only, but <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Bash(git branch:*)</code> permits mutating operations like <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">git branch -d/-D/-m</code>, which can delete or rename branches. To keep reviewer children unable to modify repo state, remove this entry (or replace it with a narrower, listing-only alternative).</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1647#pullrequestreview-4635440917\",\n        \"body\": \"## Pull request overview\\n\\nThis PR improves `entire review` orchestration by passing parent-computed review scope into spawned reviewer agents and the consolidating judge, adding explicit per-reviewer pacing guidance from the effective timeout, and pre-approving a constrained tool allowlist for headless Claude review children so read-only inspection commands aren’t auto-denied.\\n\\n**Changes:**\\n- Add `ScopeContext` to `RunConfig`, build it from git (commits/files/uncommitted + optionally inline diff), and inject it into reviewer prompts.\\n- Thread authoritative scope into the judge/synthesis prompt so it can discard out-of-scope findings.\\n- Add reviewer time-budget hint rendering, and pass per-agent timeouts in the multi-agent path.\\n- Add `--allowedTools` allowlist to Claude review child invocation.\\n\\n### Reviewed changes\\n\\nCopilot reviewed 13 out of 13 changed files in this pull request and generated 3 comments.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>\\n\\n| File | Description |\\r\\n| ---- | ----------- |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/review/types/reviewer.go | Introduces `ScopeContext` on `RunConfig` and defines scope payload shape/zero check. |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/review/synthesis_sink.go | Threads authoritative scope into synthesis prompt composition. |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/review/synthesis_prompt.go | Adds “scope gate” section to judge prompt to discard out-of-scope findings. |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/review/synthesis_prompt_test.go | Tests that synthesis prompt includes (or omits) the scope gate correctly. |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/review/scope.go | Builds bounded scope context (commits/files/uncommitted + inline diff budget). |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/review/scope_test.go | Adds coverage for scope context building, three-dot semantics, and caps. |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/review/prompt.go | Renders scope context + time budget into reviewer prompt; optionally inlines diff. |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/review/prompt_test.go | Tests scope injection and time budget hint behavior. |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/review/export_test.go | Updates/export helpers for new synthesis prompt signature and scoped testing. |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/review/cmd.go | Injects scope context into single/multi-agent configs; threads scope to sinks; sets per-agent timeout. |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/review/cmd_test.go | Extends tests to validate per-agent timeout threading and scope context injection. |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/reviewer.go | Adds `--allowedTools` allowlist to headless Claude review child. |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/reviewer_test.go | Tests that allowlist is present and does not enable unsafe flags. |\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"name\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 4635440917,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-07-06T11:37:01Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<h2 dir=\\\"auto\\\">Pull request overview</h2>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">This PR improves <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">entire review</code> orchestration by passing parent-computed review scope into spawned reviewer agents and the consolidating judge, adding explicit per-reviewer pacing guidance from the effective timeout, and pre-approving a constrained tool allowlist for headless Claude review children so read-only inspection commands aren’t auto-denied.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>Changes:</strong></p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>Add <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">ScopeContext</code> to <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">RunConfig</code>, build it from git (commits/files/uncommitted + optionally inline diff), and inject it into reviewer prompts.</li>\\n<li>Thread authoritative scope into the judge/synthesis prompt so it can discard out-of-scope findings.</li>\\n<li>Add reviewer time-budget hint rendering, and pass per-agent timeouts in the multi-agent path.</li>\\n<li>Add <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--allowedTools</code> allowlist to Claude review child invocation.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<h3 dir=\\\"auto\\\">Reviewed changes</h3>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Copilot reviewed 13 out of 13 changed files in this pull request and generated 3 comments.</p>\\n<details>\\n<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>\\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role=\\\"table\\\">\\n<thead>\\n<tr>\\n<th>File</th>\\n<th>Description</th>\\n</tr>\\n</thead>\\n<tbody>\\n<tr>\\n<td>cmd/entire/cli/review/types/reviewer.go</td>\\n<td>Introduces <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">ScopeContext</code> on <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">RunConfig</code> and defines scope payload shape/zero check.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>cmd/entire/cli/review/synthesis_sink.go</td>\\n<td>Threads authoritative scope into synthesis prompt composition.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>cmd/entire/cli/review/synthesis_prompt.go</td>\\n<td>Adds “scope gate” section to judge prompt to discard out-of-scope findings.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>cmd/entire/cli/review/synthesis_prompt_test.go</td>\\n<td>Tests that synthesis prompt includes (or omits) the scope gate correctly.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>cmd/entire/cli/review/scope.go</td>\\n<td>Builds bounded scope context (commits/files/uncommitted + inline diff budget).</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>cmd/entire/cli/review/scope_test.go</td>\\n<td>Adds coverage for scope context building, three-dot semantics, and caps.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>cmd/entire/cli/review/prompt.go</td>\\n<td>Renders scope context + time budget into reviewer prompt; optionally inlines diff.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>cmd/entire/cli/review/prompt_test.go</td>\\n<td>Tests scope injection and time budget hint behavior.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>cmd/entire/cli/review/export_test.go</td>\\n<td>Updates/export helpers for new synthesis prompt signature and scoped testing.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>cmd/entire/cli/review/cmd.go</td>\\n<td>Injects scope context into single/multi-agent configs; threads scope to sinks; sets per-agent timeout.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>cmd/entire/cli/review/cmd_test.go</td>\\n<td>Extends tests to validate per-agent timeout threading and scope context injection.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/reviewer.go</td>\\n<td>Adds <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--allowedTools</code> allowlist to headless Claude review child.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/reviewer_test.go</td>\\n<td>Tests that allowlist is present and does not enable unsafe flags.</td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody>\\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\\n</details>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1647#issuecomment-4902313555\",\n        \"body\": \"**Relationship to #1312'\"'\"'s task design** (for reviewers wondering whether the no-injected-task commits undo something intentional):\\n\\nThe default-task machinery (`profileTask`, `defaultGeneralTask`, the `Task:` prompt section + output-format protocol) all came from #1312. This PR preserves three of its four purposes and reverses exactly one, deliberately:\\n\\n| #1312 intent | here |\\n|---|---|\\n| Judge receives a canonical task for consolidation | **kept** — still resolved and threaded to the synthesis prompt |\\n| Skill-less workers (gemini/pi, whose default prompt says \\\"according to the profile task\\\") need a brief | **kept** — `workerTask` falls back to the built-in task for skill-less workers only |\\n| User-configured tasks survive configure edits (#1312 follow-ups df29bfbd0/e0d56ac6d) | **kept** — `guidedProfileTask` honors custom + existing tasks; only the built-in text is no longer persisted |\\n| Skill-bearing workers get the uniform audit brief + output protocol | **reversed** — product decision: entire invokes configured skills and adds no prompts the user didn'\"'\"'t write. Measured: the injected brief ordered a maximal ~15-minute audit regardless of what the user configured |\\n\\nDefault task texts remain in the code as runtime fallbacks (and `TestDefaultReviewTasksRejectSlop` still validates them).\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n          \"name\": \"peyton-alt\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 249787869\n        },\n        \"id\": 4902313555,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-07-07T09:33:50Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-07T09:33:50Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": null,'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/cli-1647.json' 'REDACTED\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-light.png\\\"><img alt=\\\"Fix All in Cursor\\\" width=\\\"115\\\" height=\\\"28\\\" src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"></picture></a>\\n<!-- /BUGBOT_FIX_ALL -->\\n\\n<!-- BUGBOT_AUTOFIX_REVIEW_FOOTNOTE_BEGIN -->\\n<sup>❌ Bugbot Autofix is OFF. To automatically fix reported issues with cloud agents, enable autofix in the [Cursor dashboard](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- BUG