eContext_ListsCountAgainstDiffBudget`.\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n          \"name\": \"peyton-alt\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 249787869\n        },\n        \"id\": 3536377746,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 4645033035,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": 3528517118,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-07-07T12:23:56Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-07T12:23:57Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": 276,\n        \"start_line\": 258,\n        \"path\": \"cmd/entire/cli/review/scope.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Fixed: <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">scopeDiffInlineLimit</code> lowered to 24KiB, and the rendered commit/file/porcelain lists are charged against the same budget before the diff (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">allowance := caps.diffInlineLimit - scopeListBytes(sc)</code>), so the composed prompt stays bounded under ~32KiB platform limits (argv + <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">ENTIRE_REVIEW_PROMPT</code>). Guarded by <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">TestBuildScopeContext_ListsCountAgainstDiffBudget</code>.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1647#pullrequestreview-4645033035\",\n        \"body\": \"\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n          \"name\": \"peyton-alt\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?u=a3ad5ad82f69e47f529e865376424c6bd35bc305&v=4\",\n          \"id\": 249787869\n        },\n        \"id\": 4645033035,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-07-07T12:23:56Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1647#discussion_r3536377916\",\n        \"body\": \"Fixed: the fence is now always one backtick longer than the longest backtick run inside the diff (`diffFence`), so embedded ``` lines cannot close it early. Guarded by `TestComposeReviewPrompt_DiffWithBackticksKeepsFenceIntact`.\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n          \"name\": \"peyton-alt\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 249787869\n        },\n        \"id\": 3536377916,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 4645033233,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": 3528517144,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-07-07T12:23:58Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-07T12:23:58Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": 136,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": \"cmd/entire/cli/review/prompt.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Fixed: the fence is now always one backtick longer than the longest backtick run inside the diff (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">diffFence</code>), so embedded ``` lines cannot close it early. Guarded by <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">TestComposeReviewPrompt_DiffWithBackticksKeepsFenceIntact</code>.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1647#pullrequestreview-4645033233\",\n        \"body\": \"\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n          \"name\": \"peyton-alt\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?u=a3ad5ad82f69e47f529e865376424c6bd35bc305&v=4\",\n          \"id\": 249787869\n        },\n        \"id\": 4645033233,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-07-07T12:23:58Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1647#discussion_r3536378060\",\n        \"body\": \"Fixed: `Bash(git branch:*)` removed from the allowlist (mutating via `-d`/`-D`/`-m`); the allowlist test asserts its absence alongside the other banned patterns (`TestReviewer_ArgvIncludesReadOnlyAllowlist`). The comment now also documents the accepted `--output` write residual instead of claiming blanket write-safety.\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n          \"name\": \"peyton-alt\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 249787869\n        },\n        \"id\": 3536378060,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 4645033408,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": 3528517169,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-07-07T12:23:59Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-07T12:23:59Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": \"cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/reviewer.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Fixed: <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Bash(git branch:*)</code> removed from the allowlist (mutating via <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">-d</code>/<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">-D</code>/<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">-m</code>); the allowlist test asserts its absence alongside the other banned patterns (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">TestReviewer_ArgvIncludesReadOnlyAllowlist</code>). The comment now also documents the accepted <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--output</code> write residual instead of claiming blanket write-safety.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1647#pullrequestreview-4645033408\",\n        \"body\": \"\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"peyton-alt\",\n          \"name\": \"peyton-alt\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?u=a3ad5ad82f69e47f529e865376424c6bd35bc305&v=4\",\n          \"id\": 249787869\n        },\n        \"id\": 4645033408,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-07-07T12:23:59Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1647\",\n    \"title\": \"entireio/cli PR #1647 comments\",\n    \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1647\",\n    \"display_title\": \"entireio/cli PR #1647 comments\"\n  }\n}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":11375}},"started_at_ms":1794842139996,"completed_at_ms":1794842139996}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:40.130Z","ordinal":3088,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-4646690f-ba3d-4d62-8752-5f2f3eb4d332","process_id":"20188","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import pathlib,sys;p=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]);p.parent.mkdir(exist_ok=True);p.write_bytes(b\"\")' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/entire-graph-407.json'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"list_files","cmd":"python3 -c 'import pathlib,sys;p=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]);p.parent.mkdir(exist_ok=True);p.write_bytes(b\"\")' /Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/entire-graph-407.json","path":null}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":11291}},"started_at_ms":1794842140130,"completed_at_ms":1794842140130}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:40.258Z","ordinal":3089,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-7c280e35-d75b-4770-9db2-6e002f4ed8fe","process_id":"17152","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/entire-graph-407.json' '{\n  \"p\": {\n    \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/407\",\n    \"id\": 5262839493,\n    \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSqVa0c8AAAABObCOxQ\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/407\",\n    \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/407.diff\",\n    \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/407.patch\",\n    \"issue_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/407\",\n    \"commits_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/407/commits\",\n    \"review_comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/407/comments\",\n    \"review_comment_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/comments{/number}\",\n    \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/407/comments\",\n    \"statuses_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/statuses/dafb7add95441989f4c081ebf879f83c9fc9b172\",\n    \"number\": 407,\n    \"state\": \"open\",\n    \"locked\": false,\n    \"title\": \"perf(store): answer `--head` lookups from a focused subgraph of the sqlite store\",\n    \"user\": {\n      \"login\": \"csm-kb\",\n      \"id\": 54819806,\n      \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjU0ODE5ODA2\",\n      \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54819806?v=4\",\n      \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/csm-kb\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/csm-kb\",\n      \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/csm-kb/followers\",\n      \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/csm-kb/following{/other_user}\",\n      \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/csm-kb/gists{/gist_id}\",\n      \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/csm-kb/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n      \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/csm-kb/subscriptions\",\n      \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/csm-kb/orgs\",\n      \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/csm-kb/repos\",\n      \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/csm-kb/events{/privacy}\",\n      \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/csm-kb/received_events\",\n      \"type\": \"User\",\n      \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n      \"site_admin\": false\n    },\n    \"body\": \"\\nA `--head` `def`, `neighbors`, `impact` or `explain` decoded the whole committed-tree snapshot to answer a question about one symbol: about 55 s and 16-46 GB on the Linux kernel. They now read only what the answer can reach from the sqlite store: about 1 s and under 200 MB, with identical output.\\n\\n## What changes\\n\\n- The sqlite search store is on by default (`ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEARCH_STORE=0` turns it off). `index --head` and a cold `--head` lookup write it beside the gz entry.\\n- Focused reads live in `internal/sem/search_store_focus.go` and `internal/cli/lookup_snapshot.go`; `docs/perf/focus-read-sets.md` lists what each verb reads. A name with no exact match still loads the full snapshot for the fuzzy ladder.\\n- `impact` walks only callers a second hop; callee and type hops are terminal.\\n- A lookup trusts the store'\"'\"'s recorded entry digest while the gz entry'\"'\"'s size and mtime still match, instead of hashing it (0.3 s per kernel lookup).\\n- If the store can'\"'\"'t be written, the command still succeeds, falls back to the full load, and reports `W_SEARCH_STORE_UNAVAILABLE` (effect scope `snapshot`), printed after the answer in text and agent output. `explain` gains an optional `warnings` array.\\n- Store format v5 (`docs/store-contract.md`). `-tags pprof` builds add a profiling hook.\\n\\n## Measurements\\n\\nKernel, `--head`, store off / store on before this change → this branch (`docs/perf-ledger.md` has the rest):\\n\\n| lookup | before | after |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `neighbors` | 53.4 s, 43.1 GB / 54.0 s, 16.3 GB | 1.14 s, 164 MB |\\n| `def` | 54.5 s, 46.0 GB / 57.7 s, 18.1 GB | 1.02 s, 158 MB |\\n| `impact` | 55.2 s, 44.3 GB / 56.4 s, 18.6 GB | 1.15 s, 167 MB |\\n\\nThe worst hub, `impact` on `struct dev`, takes 4.7 s and 604 MB. The cost is the store build: a cold kernel `index` goes from 854 s to about 1150 s.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- `TestLookupsAnswerIdenticallyFromSidecarAndFullLoad` runs every lookup verb and variant over 32 fixtures with the store on and off and requires identical output. A new CI job runs it under `-race`.\\n- The branch includes a merge of current `main`. The full suite passes on Windows, apart from failures this machine has on every branch (`graph-bench`'\"'\"'s `TestEnsureRepo*`, two `gitutil` ownership tests).\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- `docs/superpowers/` holds the design and plan, which also cover #408 (status line) and #406 (Windows consoles). The store-native index design there is later work, not implemented here.\\n- #408 also adds `docs/perf-ledger.md`; whichever lands second keeps both sets of rows.\",\n    \"labels\": [],\n    \"milestone\": null,\n    \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-11-11T16:14:51Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-12T13:50:32Z\",\n    \"closed_at\": null,\n    \"merged_at\": null,\n    \"merge_commit_sha\": \"4f33c845ab180048328e13089771c48146ec1679\",\n    \"assignee\": null,\n    \"assignees\": [],\n    \"requested_reviewers\": [],\n    \"requested_teams\": [],\n    \"head\": {\n      \"label\": \"csm-kb:perf/kernel-scale-lookups\",\n      \"ref\": \"perf/kernel-scale-lookups\",\n      \"repo\": {\n        \"id\": 1454206033,\n        \"node_id\": \"R_kgDOVq1sUQ\",\n        \"name\": \"entire-graph\",\n        \"full_name\": \"csm-kb/entire-graph\",\n        \"owner\": {\n          \"login\": \"csm-kb\",\n          \"id\": 54819806,\n          \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjU0ODE5ODA2\",\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54819806?v=4\",\n          \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/csm-kb\",\n          \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/csm-kb\",\n          \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/csm-kb/followers\",\n          \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/csm-kb/following{/other_user}\",\n          \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/csm-kb/gists{/gist_id}\",\n          \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/csm-kb/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n          \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/csm-kb/subscriptions\",\n          \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/csm-kb/orgs\",\n          \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/csm-kb/repos\",\n          \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/csm-kb/events{/privacy}\",\n          \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/csm-kb/received_events\",\n          \"type\": \"User\",\n          \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n          \"site_admin\": false\n        },\n        \"private\": false,\n        \"fork\": true,\n        \"archived\": false,\n        \"disabled\": false,\n        \"description\": \"🪾 Make your agents more efficient with a precomputed map of your Git repository: ranked code search plus definitions, callers, types, routes, and change impact, each with file:line locations.\",\n        \"homepage\": \"\",\n        \"language\": null,\n        \"visibility\": \"public\",\n        \"is_template\": false,\n        \"topics\": [],\n        \"forks_count\": 0,\n        \"forks\": 0,\n        \"stargazers_count\": 0,\n        \"watchers_count\": 0,\n        \"watchers\": 0,\n        \"open_issues_count\": 0,\n        \"open_issues\": 0,\n        \"size\": 33873,\n        \"default_branch\": \"main\",\n        \"has_issues\": false,\n        \"has_projects\": true,\n        \"has_wiki\": true,\n        \"has_pages\": false,\n        \"has_downloads\": false,\n        \"has_discussions\": false,\n        \"has_pull_requests\": true,\n        \"pushed_at\": \"2026-11-15T02:13:23Z\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-11-11T16:14:36Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-11T16:14:36Z\",\n        \"allow_forking\": true,\n        \"web_commit_signoff_required\": false,\n        \"pull_request_creation_policy\": \"all\",\n        \"license\": {\n          \"key\": \"mit\",\n          \"name\": \"MIT License\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit\",\n          \"spdx_id\": \"MIT\",\n          \"node_id\": \"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz\"\n        },\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/csm-kb/entire-graph\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/csm-kb/entire-graph\",\n        \"archive_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/csm-kb/entire-graph/{archive_format}{/ref}\",\n        \"assignees_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/csm-kb/entire-graph/assignees{/user}\",\n        \"blobs_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/csm-kb/entire-graph/git/blobs{/sha}\",\n        \"branches_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/csm-kb/entire-graph/branches{/branch}\",\n        \"collaborators_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/csm-kb/entire-graph/collaborators{/collaborator}\",\n        \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/csm-kb/entire-graph/comments{/number}\",\n        \"commits_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/csm-kb/entire-graph/commits{/sha}\",\n        \"compare_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/csm-kb/entire-graph/compare/{base}...{head}\",\n        \"contents_url\": \"https://api.github.