{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:40.374Z","ordinal":3090,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-94b1b54b-e4ce-4851-a836-711f09bc01b5","process_id":"29757","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/entire-graph-407.json' '/api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/languages\",\n        \"merges_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/merges\",\n        \"milestones_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/milestones{/number}\",\n        \"notifications_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/notifications{?since,all,participating}\",\n        \"pulls_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls{/number}\",\n        \"releases_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/releases{/id}\",\n        \"ssh_url\": \"git@github.com:entireio/entire-graph.git\",\n        \"stargazers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/stargazers\",\n        \"statuses_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/statuses/{sha}\",\n        \"subscribers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/subscribers\",\n        \"subscription_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/subscription\",\n        \"tags_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/tags\",\n        \"teams_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/teams\",\n        \"trees_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/git/trees{/sha}\",\n        \"clone_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph.git\",\n        \"mirror_url\": null,\n        \"hooks_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/hooks\",\n        \"svn_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph\"\n      },\n      \"sha\": \"a11c08cab530ff86be89ac45fa3a66dfb84c4df5\",\n      \"user\": {\n        \"login\": \"entireio\",\n        \"id\": 33188652,\n        \"node_id\": \"REDACTED\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33188652?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"Organization\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      }\n    },\n    \"_links\": {\n      \"comments\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/407/comments\"\n      },\n      \"commits\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/407/commits\"\n      },\n      \"statuses\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/statuses/dafb7add95441989f4c081ebf879f83c9fc9b172\"\n      },\n      \"html\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/407\"\n      },\n      \"issue\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/407\"\n      },\n      \"review_comments\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/407/comments\"\n      },\n      \"review_comment\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/comments{/number}\"\n      },\n      \"self\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/407\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n    \"auto_merge\": null,\n    \"draft\": false,\n    \"merged\": false,\n    \"mergeable\": true,\n    \"rebaseable\": false,\n    \"mergeable_state\": \"clean\",\n    \"merged_by\": null,\n    \"comments\": 1,\n    \"review_comments\": 0,\n    \"maintainer_can_modify\": true,\n    \"commits\": 49,\n    \"additions\": 6005,\n    \"deletions\": 237,\n    \"changed_files\": 58\n  },\n  \"c\": {\n    \"comments\": [\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/407#issuecomment-6825432323\",\n        \"body\": \"**Risk assessment for `dafb7add`: medium risk, with strong mitigation.** I would merge once the remaining CI checks pass.\\n\\n| Area | Risk | Assessment |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Answer correctness | Medium | The biggest concern is a focused read omitting a relation or symbol needed by the answer. A successful but incomplete read would not trigger fallback. Differential tests substantially reduce this risk. |\\n| Cold indexing and disk use | Medium | SQLite generation is now enabled by default. Recorded kernel benchmarks show cold indexing increasing from 854 to roughly 1,150 seconds—about 35% slower—plus additional cache storage. Warm lookups improve dramatically. |\\n| Cache integrity | Low–medium | Focused lookups trust matching file size and modification time instead of hashing every time. Same-size rewrites with unchanged timestamps can escape detection. Publication-time hashing and atomic replacement mitigate normal write races. |\\n| Upgrades and compatibility | Low–medium | Store format v5 invalidates older stores. Answers fall back to the full snapshot until the store is rebuilt, potentially causing temporary latency and memory spikes. Symbol IDs and the stable consumer views remain unchanged. |\\n| Failure handling and recovery | Low–medium | The FIFO hang is fixed and regression-tested. Store failures preserve the full-load path, although that path can be expensive on large repositories. `ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEARCH_STORE=0` provides a straightforward operational rollback. |\\n\\nSupporting references: [performance measurements](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/blob/dafb7add/docs/perf-ledger.md), [cache integrity implementation](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/blob/dafb7add/internal/sem/search_store.go#L947), [store contract](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/blob/dafb7add/docs/store-contract.md).\\n\\nConfidence comes from the full affected suites passing after the merge, the equivalence guard passing under `-race`, and an end-to-end check confirming that cold lookups create both SQLite and counts files, warm lookups use the focused reader, and the statusline reads matching counts.\\n\\nValidation limits:\\n\\n- My equivalence runs used the default sample, not the exhaustive `ENTIRE_GRAPH_EQUIV_FULL=1` sweep.\\n- At assessment time, the complete cross-platform [CI run](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/actions/runs/43222924001) was still running; that is not a statement about its current status.\\n\\nI found no remaining confirmed blocker. The medium rating reflects the breadth of the retrieval-path change and the default indexing cost.\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"ashtom\",\n          \"name\": \"ashtom\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70720?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 70720\n        },\n        \"id\": 6825432323,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-11-12T13:50:32Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-12T13:50:32Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>Risk assessment for <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">dafb7add</code>: medium risk, with strong mitigation.</strong> I would merge once the remaining CI checks pass.</p>\\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role=\\\"table\\\">\\n<thead>\\n<tr>\\n<th>Area</th>\\n<th>Risk</th>\\n<th>Assessment</th>\\n</tr>\\n</thead>\\n<tbody>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Answer correctness</td>\\n<td>Medium</td>\\n<td>The biggest concern is a focused read omitting a relation or symbol needed by the answer. A successful but incomplete read would not trigger fallback. Differential tests substantially reduce this risk.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Cold indexing and disk use</td>\\n<td>Medium</td>\\n<td>SQLite generation is now enabled by default. Recorded kernel benchmarks show cold indexing increasing from 854 to roughly 1,150 seconds—about 35% slower—plus additional cache storage. Warm lookups improve dramatically.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Cache integrity</td>\\n<td>Low–medium</td>\\n<td>Focused lookups trust matching file size and modification time instead of hashing every time. Same-size rewrites with unchanged timestamps can escape detection. Publication-time hashing and atomic replacement mitigate normal write races.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Upgrades and compatibility</td>\\n<td>Low–medium</td>\\n<td>Store format v5 invalidates older stores. Answers fall back to the full snapshot until the store is rebuilt, potentially causing temporary latency and memory spikes. Symbol IDs and the stable consumer views remain unchanged.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Failure handling and recovery</td>\\n<td>Low–medium</td>\\n<td>The FIFO hang is fixed and regression-tested. Store failures preserve the full-load path, although that path can be expensive on large repositories. <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEARCH_STORE=0</code> provides a straightforward operational rollback.</td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody>\\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Supporting references: <a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/blob/dafb7add/docs/perf-ledger.md\\\">performance measurements</a>, <a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/blob/dafb7add/internal/sem/search_store.go#L947\\\">cache integrity implementation</a>, <a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/blob/dafb7add/docs/store-contract.md\\\">store contract</a>.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Confidence comes from the full affected suites passing after the merge, the equivalence guard passing under <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">-race</code>, and an end-to-end check confirming that cold lookups create both SQLite and counts files, warm lookups use the focused reader, and the statusline reads matching counts.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Validation limits:</p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>My equivalence runs used the default sample, not the exhaustive <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">ENTIRE_GRAPH_EQUIV_FULL=1</code> sweep.</li>\\n<li>At assessment time, the complete cross-platform <a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/actions/runs/43222924001\\\">CI run</a> was still running; that is not a statement about its current status.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">I found no remaining confirmed blocker. The medium rating reflects the breadth of the retrieval-path change and the default indexing cost.</p>\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/407\",\n    \"title\": \"entireio/entire-graph PR #407 comments\",\n    \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/407\",\n    \"display_title\": \"entireio/entire-graph PR #407 comments\"\n  }\n}'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/entire-graph-407.json' '/api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/languages\",\n        \"merges_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/merges\",\n        \"milestones_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/milestones{/number}\",\n        \"notifications_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/notifications{?since,all,participating}\",\n        \"pulls_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls{/number}\",\n        \"releases_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/releases{/id}\",\n        \"ssh_url\": \"git@github.com:entireio/entire-graph.git\",\n        \"stargazers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/stargazers\",\n        \"statuses_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/statuses/{sha}\",\n        \"subscribers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/subscribers\",\n        \"subscription_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/subscription\",\n        \"tags_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/tags\",\n        \"teams_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/teams\",\n        \"trees_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/git/trees{/sha}\",\n        \"clone_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph.git\",\n        \"mirror_url\": null,\n        \"hooks_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/hooks\",\n        \"svn_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph\"\n      },\n      \"sha\": \"a11c08cab530ff86be89ac45fa3a66dfb84c4df5\",\n      \"user\": {\n        \"login\": \"entireio\",\n        \"id\": 33188652,\n        \"node_id\": \"REDACTED\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33188652?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"Organization\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      }\n    },\n    \"_links\": {\n      \"comments\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/407/comments\"\n      },\n      \"commits\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/407/commits\"\n      },\n      \"statuses\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/statuses/dafb7add95441989f4c081ebf879f83c9fc9b172\"\n      },\n      \"html\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/407\"\n      },\n      \"issue\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/issues/407\"\n      },\n      \"review_comments\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/407/comments\"\n      },\n      \"review_comment\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/comments{/number}\"\n      },\n      \"self\": {\n        \"href\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-graph/pulls/407\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"author_association\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n    \"auto_merge\": null,\n    \"draft\": false,\n    \"merged\": false,\n    \"mergeable\": true,\n    \"rebaseable\": false,\n    \"mergeable_state\": \"clean\",\n    \"merged_by\": null,\n    \"comments\": 1,\n    \"review_comments\": 0,\n    \"maintainer_can_modify\": true,\n    \"commits\": 49,\n    \"additions\": 6005,\n    \"deletions\": 237,\n    \"changed_files\": 58\n  },\n  \"c\": {\n    \"comments\": [\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/407#issuecomment-6825432323\",\n        \"body\": \"**Risk assessment for `dafb7add`: medium risk, with strong mitigation.** I would merge once the remaining CI checks pass.\\n\\n| Area | Risk | Assessment |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Answer correctness | Medium | The biggest concern is a focused read omitting a relation or symbol needed by the answer. A successful but incomplete read would not trigger fallback. Differential tests substantially reduce this risk. |\\n| Cold indexing and disk use | Medium | SQLite generation is now enabled by default. Recorded kernel benchmarks show cold indexing increasing from 854 to roughly 1,150 seconds—about 35% slower—plus additional cache storage. Warm lookups improve dramatically. |\\n| Cache integrity | Low–medium | Focused lookups trust matching file size and modification time instead of hashing every time. Same-size rewrites with unchanged timestamps can escape detection. Publication-time hashing and atomic replacement mitigate normal write races. |\\n| Upgrades and compatibility | Low–medium | Store format v5 invalidates older stores. Answers fall back to the full snapshot until the store is rebuilt, potentially causing temporary latency and memory spikes. Symbol IDs and the stable consumer views remain unchanged. |\\n| Failure handling and recovery | Low–medium | The FIFO hang is fixed and regression-tested. Store failures preserve the full-load path, although that path can be expensive on large repositories. `ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEARCH_STORE=0` provides a straightforward operational rollback. |\\n\\nSupporting references: [performance measurements](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/blob/dafb7add/docs/perf-ledger.md), [cache integrity implementation](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/blob/dafb7add/internal/sem/search_store.go#L947), [store contract](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/blob/dafb7add/docs/store-contract.md).\\n\\nConfidence comes from the full affected suites passing after the merge, the equivalence guard passing under `-race`, and an end-to-end check confirming that cold lookups create both SQLite and counts files, warm lookups use the focused reader, and the statusline reads matching counts.\\n\\nValidation limits:\\n\\n- My equivalence runs used the default sample, not the exhaustive `ENTIRE_GRAPH_EQUIV_FULL=1` sweep.\\n- At assessment time, the complete cross-platform [CI run](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/actions/runs/43222924001) was still running; that is not a statement about its current status.\\n\\nI found no remaining confirmed blocker. The medium rating reflects the breadth of the retrieval-path change and the default indexing cost.\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"ashtom\",\n          \"name\": \"ashtom\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70720?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 70720\n        },\n        \"id\": 6825432323,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-11-12T13:50:32Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-12T13:50:32Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>Risk assessment for <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">dafb7add</code>: medium risk, with strong mitigation.</strong> I would merge once the remaining CI checks pass.</p>\\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role=\\\"table\\\">\\n<thead>\\n<tr>\\n<th>Area</th>\\n<th>Risk</th>\\n<th>Assessment</th>\\n</tr>\\n</thead>\\n<tbody>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Answer correctness</td>\\n<td>Medium</td>\\n<td>The biggest concern is a focused read omitting a relation or symbol needed by the answer. A successful but incomplete read would not trigger fallback. Differential tests substantially reduce this risk.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Cold indexing and disk use</td>\\n<td>Medium</td>\\n<td>SQLite generation is now enabled by default. Recorded kernel benchmarks show cold indexing increasing from 854 to roughly 1,150 seconds—about 35% slower—plus additional cache storage. Warm lookups improve dramatically.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Cache integrity</td>\\n<td>Low–medium</td>\\n<td>Focused lookups trust matching file size and modification time instead of hashing every time. Same-size rewrites with unchanged timestamps can escape detection. Publication-time hashing and atomic replacement mitigate normal write races.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Upgrades and compatibility</td>\\n<td>Low–medium</td>\\n<td>Store format v5 invalidates older stores. Answers fall back to the full snapshot until the store is rebuilt, potentially causing temporary latency and memory spikes. Symbol IDs and the stable consumer views remain unchanged.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>Failure handling and recovery</td>\\n<td>Low–medium</td>\\n<td>The FIFO hang is fixed and regression-tested. Store failures preserve the full-load path, although that path can be expensive on large repositories. <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEARCH_STORE=0</code> provides a straightforward operational rollback.</td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody>\\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Supporting references: <a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/blob/dafb7add/docs/perf-ledger.md\\\">performance measurements</a>, <a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/blob/dafb7add/internal/sem/search_store.go#L947\\\">cache integrity implementation</a>, <a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/blob/dafb7add/docs/store-contract.md\\\">store contract</a>.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Confidence comes from the full affected suites passing after the merge, the equivalence guard passing under <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">-race</code>, and an end-to-end check confirming that cold lookups create both SQLite and counts files, warm lookups use the focused reader, and the statusline reads matching counts.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Validation limits:</p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>My equivalence runs used the default sample, not the exhaustive <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">ENTIRE_GRAPH_EQUIV_FULL=1</code> sweep.</li>\\n<li>At assessment time, the complete cross-platform <a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/actions/runs/43222924001\\\">CI run</a> was still running; that is not a statement about its current status.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">I found no remaining confirmed blocker. The medium rating reflects the breadth of the retrieval-path change and the default indexing cost.</p>\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/407\",\n    \"title\": \"entireio/entire-graph PR #407 comments\",\n    \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/407\",\n    \"display_title\": \"entireio/entire-graph PR #407 comments\"\n  }\n}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":10583}},"started_at_ms":1794842140374,"completed_at_ms":1794842140374}}
