{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:40.613Z","ordinal":3092,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-75473829-152a-457d-aba9-423d90a11ad9","process_id":"75601","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/entire-brain-595.json' '{\n  \"p\": {\n    \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/pulls/595\",\n    \"id\": 5130795697,\n    \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOSm5-5c8AAAABMdG6sQ\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/595\",\n    \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/595.diff\",\n    \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/595.patch\",\n    \"issue_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/595\",\n    \"commits_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/pulls/595/commits\",\n    \"review_comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/pulls/595/comments\",\n    \"review_comment_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/pulls/comments{/number}\",\n    \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/issues/595/comments\",\n    \"statuses_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/entireio/entire-brain/statuses/40309b025e01c8b13f23f5614b9b6e9c42abc2df\",\n    \"number\": 595,\n    \"state\": \"open\",\n    \"locked\": false,\n    \"title\": \"feat(memories): typed records, review write-back, and a provenance walk\",\n    \"user\": {\n      \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",\n      \"id\": 257360244,\n      \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOD1cBdA\",\n      \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257360244?v=4\",\n      \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/suhaanthayyil\",\n      \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/followers\",\n      \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/following{/other_user}\",\n      \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/gists{/gist_id}\",\n      \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n      \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/subscriptions\",\n      \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/orgs\",\n      \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/repos\",\n      \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/events{/privacy}\",\n      \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/suhaanthayyil/received_events\",\n      \"type\": \"User\",\n      \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n      \"site_admin\": false\n    },\n    \"body\": \"## Why\\n\\nA review'\"'\"'s reasoning died with the run. Findings were printed and then lost, so the same regression could be re-derived from scratch on every pass, and nothing recorded what a memory was derived from or what replaced it.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n- `factmerge` records carry typed relations, a closed origin set, and `Record.Validate`, so a malformed record is rejected at the boundary rather than discovered later.\\n- `brain review --remember` writes findings back as durable memories, into the same store the review itself read, idempotently: a re-review of an unchanged tree records nothing, and a human retraction is never revived by a later detector run.\\n- `memories provenance` walks a memory'\"'\"'s lineage: what it was derived from, what disagrees with it, what replaced it. It traverses superseded and retracted records, which recall cannot, and records no serve receipt, so inspecting lineage never moves the reuse metrics.\\n- The diff-less review seam contract is documented, including what `--remember` does and does not promise.\\n\\n## Rebase note\\n\\nRebased onto main at `6c4b11de`. Three of main'\"'\"'s overnight commits land directly on this work: the flat per-repo store (`73b62b21`), the removal of the fact-proposal framework (`6c53c114`) and the removal of the brain-local privacy layer (`63c524e3`). Consequences, all recorded in-code:\\n\\n- `factstore.Load`/`Write` lost their branch parameter. `Record.Branch` survives as metadata, so the provenance walk now spans branches deliberately: an ancestor recorded on another branch is still its ancestor, and filtering the walk would answer \\\"nothing replaced this\\\" when something did.\\n- The write-back'\"'\"'s presence check is repository-wide, so a finding first recorded on another branch counts as already-present.\\n- The privacy gate on `--remember` is gone because the layer it called is gone product-wide, not because it was relaxed for this flag. If a privacy layer returns, this is the surface to wire to its strictest setting first.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\nFull `go test ./...` green: exit 0, 42 packages, zero FAIL lines.\\nTrail: https://entire.com/gh/entireio/-/trails/2732\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\nhttps://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\\n\",\n    \"labels\": [],\n    \"milestone\": null,\n    \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-11-03T02:20:23Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-03T02:21:10Z\",\n    \"closed_at\": null,\n    \"merged_at\": null,\n    \"merge_commit_sha\": null,\n    \"assignee\": null,\n    \"assignees\": [],\n    \"requested_reviewers\": [],\n    \"requested_teams\": [],\n    \"head\": {\n      \"label\": \"entireio:rc/m1-record-schema\",\n      \"ref\": \"rc/m1-record-schema\",\n      \"repo\": {\n        \"id\": 1248755429,\n        \"node_id\": \"R_kgDOSm5-5Q\",\n        \"name\": \"entire-brain\",\n        \"full_name\": \"entireio/entire-brain\",\n        \"owner\": {\n          \"login\": \"entireio\",\n          \"id\": 33188652,\n          \"node_id\": \"REDACTED\",\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33188652?v=4\",\n          \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio\",\n          \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio\",\n          \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/followers\",\n          \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/following{/other_user}\",\n          \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/gists{/gist_id}\",\n          \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n          \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/subscriptions\",\n          \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/orgs\",\n          \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/repos\",\n          \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/events{/privacy}\",\n          \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/entireio/received_events\",\n          \"type\": \"Organization\",\n          \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n          \"site_admin\": false\n        },\n        \"private\": false,\n        \"fork\": false,\n        \"archived\": false,\n        \"disabled\": false,\n        \"description\": \"🧠 The memory layer for your Git repository. Turn retained agent sessions, checkpoint history, docs, code structure, and durable facts into something you and your coding agents can actually query.\",\n        \"homepage\": \"\",\n        \"language\": \"Go\",\n        \"visibility\": \"public\",\n        \"is_template\": false,\n        \"topics\": [],\n        \"forks_count\": 15,\n        \"forks\": 15,\n        \"stargazers_count\": 99,\n        \"watchers_count\": 99,\n        \"watchers\": 99,\n        \"open_issues_count\": 45,\n        \"open_issues\": 45,\n        \"size\": 944031,\n        \"default_branch\": \"main\",\n        \"