ssage to an error writer (e.g., plumb cmd.ErrOrStderr()/root.ErrOrStderr() into executeTour/translateTourError) before returning SilentError, or return a non-Silent error so main prints it.\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"name\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 3205144849,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 4248211003,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-05-07T22:56:05Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-07T22:56:07Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": \"cmd/entire/cli/tour_cmd.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">translateTourError wraps ErrNot'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":10250}},"started_at_ms":1794842141227,"completed_at_ms":1794842141228}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:41.355Z","ordinal":3098,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-828abf24-00db-4a33-b94f-4166ddcb369d","process_id":"17535","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/cli-1146.json' 'GitRepo in SilentError but does not print tourNotGitRepoMessage anywhere. Since main.go suppresses output for SilentError, this will cause <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">entire tour</code> outside a git repo to exit non-zero with no user-facing message. Consider printing the friendly message to an error writer (e.g., plumb cmd.ErrOrStderr()/root.ErrOrStderr() into executeTour/translateTourError) before returning SilentError, or return a non-Silent error so main prints it.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1146#discussion_r3205144874\",\n        \"body\": \"tourNoTextGeneratorMessage says \\\"'\"'\"'entire tour'\"'\"' renders the tour by piping the discovered command surface through your locally-installed agent\\\", but the default `entire tour` path renders embedded markdown and does not require an agent; only `--latest`/`--regenerate` do. This message will be misleading in the error case—consider explicitly referencing those flags and clarifying that the embedded tour works without an agent.\\n\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"name\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 3205144874,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 4248211003,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-05-07T22:56:06Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-07T22:56:07Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": \"cmd/entire/cli/tour_cmd.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">tourNoTextGeneratorMessage says \\\"'\"'\"'entire tour'\"'\"' renders the tour by piping the discovered command surface through your locally-installed agent\\\", but the default <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">entire tour</code> path renders embedded markdown and does not require an agent; only <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--latest</code>/<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--regenerate</code> do. This message will be misleading in the error case—consider explicitly referencing those flags and clarifying that the embedded tour works without an agent.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1146#discussion_r3205144888\",\n        \"body\": \"The loading UI title says \\\"Fetching the latest dispatch\\\", but this command fetches the latest blog post and renders a digest. Using the wrong noun here is confusing for users; consider renaming to something like \\\"Fetching the latest post\\\" / \\\"Generating latest digest\\\" to match `--latest` behavior and other messaging.\\n\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"name\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 3205144888,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 4248211003,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-05-07T22:56:06Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-07T22:56:07Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": \"cmd/entire/cli/tour_cmd.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">The loading UI title says \\\"Fetching the latest dispatch\\\", but this command fetches the latest blog post and renders a digest. Using the wrong noun here is confusing for users; consider renaming to something like \\\"Fetching the latest post\\\" / \\\"Generating latest digest\\\" to match <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--latest</code> behavior and other messaging.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1146#discussion_r3205144908\",\n        \"body\": \"This error wrap says \\\"generate latest dispatch\\\", but this path generates a blog-post digest for `entire tour --latest` rather than a dispatch. Consider renaming the message to reflect the tour/latest digest so errors are easier to understand and grep.\\n\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"name\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 3205144908,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 4248211003,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-05-07T22:56:06Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-07T22:56:07Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": \"cmd/entire/cli/tour/run.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">This error wrap says \\\"generate latest dispatch\\\", but this path generates a blog-post digest for <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">entire tour --latest</code> rather than a dispatch. Consider renaming the message to reflect the tour/latest digest so errors are easier to understand and grep.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1146#discussion_r3205144936\",\n        \"body\": \"The comment claims json.Marshal'\"'\"'s default escaping would turn \\\"<id|sha>\\\" into \\\"<id|sha>\\\", but the actual default behavior is to HTML-escape angle brackets (e.g. to \\\\u003c...\\\\u003e). Consider updating the example in this comment to show the real escaped form so future readers understand why SetEscapeHTML(false) matters.\\n\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"name\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 3205144936,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 4248211003,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-05-07T22:56:06Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-07T22:56:07Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": \"cmd/entire/cli/tour/prompt.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">The comment claims json.Marshal'\"'\"'s default escaping would turn \\\"&lt;id|sha&gt;\\\" into \\\"&lt;id|sha&gt;\\\", but the actual default behavior is to HTML-escape angle brackets (e.g. to \\\\u003c...\\\\u003e). Consider updating the example in this comment to show the real escaped form so future readers understand why SetEscapeHTML(false) matters.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1146#pullrequestreview-4248211003\",\n        \"body\": \"## Pull request overview\\n\\nAdds an experimental, hidden top-level `entire tour` command (discoverable via `entire labs`) that renders a state-aware CLI tour, primarily from embedded pre-rendered markdown, with optional agent-driven regeneration and a `--latest` blog-digest mode. It also wires release-time regeneration into CI and extends markdown rendering to support per-command style overrides.\\n\\n**Changes:**\\n- Introduces the `tour` package (repo state classification, cobra surface discovery, prompt construction + sanitization, RSS fetch, agent selection, and embedded markdown plumbing).\\n- Adds the `entire tour` command + spinner TUI integration, and lists it under `entire labs`.\\n- Adds `mise run tour:regenerate` and a best-effort release workflow step to regenerate `embedded/tour.md` before GoReleaser.\\n\\n### Reviewed changes\\n\\nCopilot reviewed 17 out of 17 changed files in this pull request and generated 5 comments.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>\\n\\n| File | Description |\\r\\n| ---- | ----------- |\\r\\n| `mise.toml` | Adds an atomic, validated `tour:regenerate` task for release/local regeneration. |\\r\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/tour/state.go` | Implements repo “stage” classification and TextGenerator agent resolution (incl. external plugins). |\\r\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/tour/run.go` | Implements tour generation paths (embedded vs agent), `--latest` digest, and control-sequence stripping for persisted output. |\\r\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/tour/prompt.go` | Builds the system prompts and escapes/untrusts payloads (tag-escape + invisible stripping). |\\r\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/tour/prompt_test.go` | Adds table tests for tag-escape hardening and control-sequence stripping. |\\r\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/tour/embedded/tour.md` | Adds a committed stub placeholder to be overwritten at release time. |\\r\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/tour/embedded.go` | Embeds the tour markdown and provides static text for setup/agent-install stages. |\\r\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/tour/discovery.go` | Discovers a user-facing cobra command surface for prompting (filters hidden/deprecated/plumbing). |\\r\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/tour/discovery_test.go` | Tests discovery filtering and long-help paragraph trimming. |\\r\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/tour/blog.go` | Fetches/parses the RSS feed to get the latest blog post for `--latest`. |\\r\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/tour_tui.go` | Adds a bubbletea spinner program used while agent-backed generation runs. |\\r\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/tour_cmd.go` | Adds the hidden `entire tour` cobra command, wiring options, rendering, and error translation. |\\r\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/root.go` | Registers `tour` at the top level (hidden). |\\r\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/mdrender/mdrender.go` | Adds `Render*WithOverride` hooks to allow palette tweaks (used to recolor H2 in tour). |\\r\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/labs.go` | Adds `tour` to the labs registry; improves unknown-topic hinting and aligns listing width dynamically. |\\r\\n| `cmd/entire/cli/labs_test.go` | Updates canonical-path verification to use `Invocation` segments (supports multi-segment entries). |\\r\\n| `.github/workflows/release.yml` | Adds best-effort tour regeneration (install Claude CLI, run task, annotate + Slack notify on failure). |\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"name\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 4248211003,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-05-07T22:56:07Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<h2 dir=\\\"auto\\\">Pull request overview</h2>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Adds an experimental, hidden top-level <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">entire tour</code> command (discoverable via <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">entire labs</code>) that renders a state-aware CLI tour, primarily from embedded pre-rendered markdown, with optional agent-driven regeneration and a <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--latest</code> blog-digest mode. It also wires release-time regeneration into CI and extends markdown rendering to support per-command style overrides.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>Changes:</strong></p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>Introduces the <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">tour</code> package (repo state classification, cobra surface discovery, prompt construction + sanitization, RSS fetch, agent selection, and embedded markdown plumbing).</li>\\n<li>Adds the <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">entire tour</code> command + spinner TUI integration, and lists it under <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">entire labs</code>.</li>\\n<li>Adds <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">mise run tour:regenerate</code> and a best-effort release workflow step to regenerate <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">embedded/tour.md</code> before GoReleaser.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<h3 dir=\\\"auto\\\">Reviewed changes</h3>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Copilot reviewed 17 out of 17 changed files in this pull request and generated 5 comments.</p>\\n<details>\\n<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>\\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role=\\\"table\\\">\\n<thead>\\n<tr>\\n<th>File</th>\\n<th>Description</th>\\n</tr>\\n</thead>\\n<tbody>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">mise.toml</code></td>\\n<td>Adds an atomic, validated <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">tour:regenerate</code> task for release/local regeneration.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">cmd/entire/cli/tour/state.go</code></td>\\n<td>Implements repo “stage” classification and TextGenerator agent resolution (incl. external plugins).</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">cmd/entire/cli/tour/run.go</code></td>\\n<td>Implements tour generation paths (embedded vs agent), <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--latest</code> digest, and control-sequence stripping for persisted output.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">cmd/entire/cli/tour/prompt.go</code></td>\\n<td>Builds the system prompts and escapes/untrusts payloads (tag-escape + invisible stripping).</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">cmd/entire/cli/tour/prompt_test.go</code></td>\\n<td>Adds table tests for tag-escape hardening and control-sequence stripping.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">cmd/entire/cli/tour/embedded/tour.md</code></td>\\n<td>Adds a committed stub placeholder to be overwritten at release time.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">cmd/entire/cli/tour/embedded.go</code></td>\\n<td>Embeds the tour markdown and provides static text for setup/agent-install stages.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">cmd/entire/cli/tour/discovery.go</code></td>\\n<td>Discovers a user-facing cobra command surface for prompting (filters hidden/deprecated/plumbing).</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">cmd/entire/cli/tour/discovery_test.go</code></td>\\n<td>Tests discovery filtering and long-help paragraph trimming.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">cmd/entire/cli/tour/blog.go</code></td>\\n<td>Fetches/parses the RSS feed to get the latest blog post for <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--latest</code>.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">cmd/entire/cli/tour_tui.go</code></td>\\n<td>Adds a bubbletea spinner program used while agent-backed generation runs.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">cmd/entire/cli/tour_cmd.go</code></td>\\n<td>Adds the hidden <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">entire tour</code> cobra command, wiring options, rendering, and error translation.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">cmd/entire/cli/root.go</code></td>\\n<td>Registers <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">tour</code> at the top level (hidden).</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">cmd/entire/cli/mdrender/mdrender.go</code></td>\\n<td>Adds <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Render*WithOverride</code> hooks to allow palette tweaks (used to recolor H2 in tour).</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">cmd/entire/cli/labs.go</code></td>\\n<td>Adds <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">tour</code> to the labs registry; improves unknown-topic hinting and aligns listing width dynamically.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">cmd/en