rge\": null,\n    \"draft\": false,\n    \"merged\": true,\n    \"mergeable\": null,\n    \"rebaseable\": null,\n    \"mergeable_state\": \"unknown\",\n    \"merged_by\": {\n      \"login\": \"Soph\",\n      \"id\": 70741,\n      \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\n      \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n      \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/Soph\",\n      \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/followers\",\n      \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/following{/other_user}\",\n      \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/gists{/gist_id}\",\n      \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n      \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/subscriptions\",\n      \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/orgs\",\n      \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/repos\",\n      \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/events{/privacy}\",\n      \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/Soph/received_events\",\n      \"type\": \"User\",\n      \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n      \"site_admin\": false\n    },\n    \"comments\": 1,\n    \"review_comments\": 6,\n    \"maintainer_can_modify\": false,\n    \"commits\": 3,\n    \"additions\": 650,\n    \"deletions\": 17,\n    \"changed_files\": 7\n  },\n  \"c\": {\n    \"comments\": [\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/108#discussion_r3813268165\",\n        \"body\": \"### URL userinfo still follows redirects\\n\\n**High Severity**\\n\\n<!-- DESCRIPTION START -->\\n`outgoingAuth` only withholds `c.Auth`, but requests are built from `requestURL().String()`, which still embeds URL userinfo. After a cross-site `/info/refs` redirect, Go'\"'\"'s client sends Basic auth from that userinfo even when the explicit REDACTED is withheld, so `REDACTED` (and any URL that still carries userinfo) can leak to the redirect host. Docs claim userinfo is bound like flag REDACTEDs.\\n<!-- DESCRIPTION END -->\\n\\n<!-- BUGBOT_BUG_ID: ecd83ecb-3078-444e-90ad-017ab2c5fc34 -->\\n\\n<!-- LOCATIONS START\\ninternal/gitproto/smarthttp.go#L383-L393\\ninternal/gitproto/smarthttp.go#L615-L621\\ndocs/usage.md#L375-L379\\nLOCATIONS END -->\\n<details>\\n<summary>Additional Locations (2)</summary>\\n\\n- [`internal/gitproto/smarthttp.go#L615-L621`](https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/blob/b0e0f88541d3bbbe472233a7ce0bbe63124c4115/internal/gitproto/smarthttp.go#L615-L621)\\n- [`docs/usage.md#L375-L379`](https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/blob/b0e0f88541d3bbbe472233a7ce0bbe63124c4115/docs/usage.md#L375-L379)\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<div><a href=\\\"https://cursor.com/open?REDACTED\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-light.png\\\"><img alt=\\\"Fix in Cursor\\\" width=\\\"115\\\" height=\\\"28\\\" src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https://cursor.com/agents?REDACTED\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\\\"><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-light.png\\\"><img alt=\\\"Fix in Web\\\" width=\\\"99\\\" height=\\\"28\\\" src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\\\"></picture></a></div>\\n\\n\\n<sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit b0e0f88541d3bbbe472233a7ce0bbe63124c4115. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"cursor[bot]\",\n          \"name\": \"cursor[bot]\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1210556?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 206951365\n        },\n        \"id\": 3813268165,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 4972490799,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T13:13:18Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-19T13:13:18Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": 409,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": \"internal/gitproto/smarthttp.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<h3 dir=\\\"auto\\\">URL userinfo still follows redirects</h3>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>High Severity</strong></p>\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">outgoingAuth</code> only withholds <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">c.Auth</code>, but requests are built from <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">requestURL().String()</code>, which still embeds URL userinfo. After a cross-site <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">/info/refs</code> redirect, Go'\"'\"'s client sends Basic auth from that userinfo even when the explicit REDACTED is withheld, so <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">REDACTED</code> (and any URL that still carries userinfo) can leak to the redirect host. Docs claim userinfo is bound like flag REDACTEDs.</p>\\n\\n\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Additional Locations (2)</summary>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/blob/b0e0f88541d3bbbe472233a7ce0bbe63124c4115/internal/gitproto/smarthttp.go#L615-L621\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">internal/gitproto/smarthttp.go#L615-L621</code></a></li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/blob/b0e0f88541d3bbbe472233a7ce0bbe63124c4115/docs/usage.md#L375-L379\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">docs/usage.md#L375-L379</code></a></li>\\n</ul>\\n</details>\\n<div dir=\\\"auto\\\"><a href=\\\"https://curs