pload-pack  Authorization=&quot;&quot;      ← stripped on a same-host hop\\\"><pre class=\\\"notranslate\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">GET  /repo.git/info/refs              Authorization=\\\"\\\"\\nPOST /repo.git/git-upload-pack        Authorization=\\\"Basic Z2l0OkhFTFBFUkNSRUQ=\\\"\\nPOST /final/repo.git/git-upload-pack  Authorization=\\\"\\\"      ← stripped on a same-host hop\\n</code></pre></div>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">That'\"'\"'s exactly the path the PR'\"'\"'s own documented remedy sends people down, so it undercuts the fix. The credential is bound to the host the <em>request</em> was aimed at, which the callback already has: use <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">via[0].URL</code> instead of the captured <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">endpoint</code>. That'\"'\"'s per-request accurate for the token case (identical when <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">requestURL() == EndpointURL</code>) and for the helper-retry case (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">via[0].URL</code> is the challenge URL), and it lets the closure drop the captured endpoint entirely.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/108#issuecomment-5344059196\",\n        \"body\": \"Both fixed in 503ac1ba. You were right on both counts, and I verified each directly before changing anything — thank you, these were the two cases my own test table was blind to.\\n\\n## 1. `http` → `https` upgrade\\n\\nConfirmed: `sameSite(http://host, https://host)` was `false`, and so was `http://host:80 → https://host:443`. My stated rationale only justified blocking the *downgrade*, so the exact-match check was overreach.\\n\\nTook your suggestion, factored into a named helper so the asymmetry is explicit:\\n\\n```go\\nfunc schemeCompatible(src, dst string) bool {\\n\\tif src == dst { return true }\\n\\treturn src == \\\"http\\\" && dst == \\\"https\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\nTest table gained five cases: the upgrade on the same host, the upgrade with default ports spelled out, the upgrade onto a subdomain, and — importantly — that the allowance can'\"'\"'t smuggle in a host or port change (`http://github.com` → `https://evil.example` and `http://host` → `https://host:8443` both stay cross-site).\\n\\nWorth noting the reasoning that convinced me it'\"'\"'s safe rather than just convenient: for an `http` endpoint the credential was already going to that host in the clear, so an upgrade strictly improves matters. There'\"'\"'s no configuration where withholding on an upgrade protects anything.\\n\\n## 2. `guardRedirects` anchoring\\n\\nConfirmed, and this was the more consequential one — it broke the exact remedy the PR documents. Reproduced your trace as a test, and verified it **fails** against the construction-time anchor:\\n\\n```\\n--- FAIL: TestGuardRedirectsAnchorsOnTheIssuedRequest\\n    credentials were stripped on a hop that never left the adopted host\\n```\\n\\n`via[0].URL` is the right anchor for the reason you give: it'\"'\"'s whatever `requestURL()` or the helper-retry target actually pointed at, so it'\"'\"'s accurate per request in both cases instead of describing a connection-level state that has since moved. The closure no longer captures the endpoint at all, and `guardRedirects` lost its `*url.URL` parameter as a result.\\n\\nOne addition: a nil anchor now fails closed. Go guarantees `len(via) >= 1` so it'\"'\"'s defensive only, but `sameSite(nil, x)` returning `false` means unknown provenance strips rather than forwards.\\n\\nA second test covers the other direction — a hop that genuinely leaves the issued request'\"'\"'s site still loses the header — so the two aren'\"'\"'t traded off against each other.\\n\\n## Docs\\n\\nBoth `docs/usage.md` and the changelog said \\\"same scheme and port\\\" and now describe the downgrade rule. I'\"'\"'ve also replaced the PR'\"'\"'s behavior-change section with an explicit table of what'\"'\"'s kept versus withheld, since the previous wording only mentioned hosts.\\n\\nRebased onto `main` now that #107 has merged. `gofmt`, `go vet`, `golangci-lint` (0 issues), `go test ./...` 18/18.\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"Soph\",\n          \"name\": \"Soph\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70741?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 70741\n        },\n        \"id\": 5344059196,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T15:08:44Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-19T15:08:44Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Both fixed in <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/503ac1ba90d9be140bf6c4c348cc0b5b249eaf5d/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/503ac1ba90d9be140bf6c4c348cc0b5b249eaf5d\\\"><tt>503ac1b</tt></a>. You were right on both counts, and I verified each directly before changing anything — thank you, these were the two cases my own test table was blind to.</p>\\n<h2 dir=\\\"auto\\\">1. <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">http</code> → <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">https</code> upgrade</h2>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Confirmed: <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">sameSite(http://host, https://host)</code> was <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">false</code>, and so was <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">http://host:80 → https://host:443</code>. My stated rationale only justified blocking the <em>downgrade</em>, so the exact-match check was overreach.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Took your suggestion, factored into a named helper so the asymmetry is explicit:</p>\\n<div class=\\\"highlight highlight-source-go notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\\\" dir=\\\"auto\\\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\\\"func schemeCompatible(src, dst string) bool {\\n\\tif src == dst { return true }\\n\\treturn src == &quot;http&quot; &amp;&amp; dst == &quot;https&quot;\\n}\\\"><pre class=\\\"notranslate\\\"><span class=\\\"pl-k\\\">func</span> <span class=\\\"pl-s1\\\">schemeCompatible</span>(<span class=\\\"pl-s1\\\">src</span>, <span class=\\\"pl-s1\\\">dst</span> <span class=\\\"pl-smi\\\">string</span>) <span class=\\\"pl-smi\\\">bool</span> {\\n\\t<span class=\\\"pl-k\\\">if</span> <span class=\\\"pl-s1\\\">src</span> <span class=\\\"pl-c1\\\">==</span> <span class=\\\"pl-s1\\\">dst</span> { <span class=\\\"pl-k\\\">return</span> <span class=\\\"pl-c1\\\">true</span> }\\n\\t<span class=\\\"pl-k\\\">return</span> <span class=\\\"pl-s1\\\">src</span> <span class=\\\"pl-c1\\\">==</span> <span class=\\\"pl-s\\\">\\\"http\\\"</span> <span class=\\\"pl-c1\\\">&amp;&amp;</span> <span class=\\\"pl-s1\\\">dst</span> <span class=\\\"pl-c1\\\">==</span> <span class=\\\"pl-s\\\">\\\"https\\\"</span>\\n}</pre></div>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Test table gained five cases: the upgrade on the same host, the upgrade with default ports spelled out, the upgrade onto a subdomain, and — importantly — that the allowance can'\"'\"'t smuggle in a host or port change (<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">http://github.com</code> → <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">https://evil.example</code> and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">http://host</code> → <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">https://host:8443</code> both stay cross-site).</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Worth noting the reasoning that convinced me it'\"'\"'s safe rather than just convenient: for an <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">http</code> endpoint the credential was already going to that host in the clear, so an upgrade strictly improves matters. There'\"'\"'s no configuration where withholding on an upgrade protects anything.</p>\\n<h2 dir=\\\"auto\\\">2. <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">guardRedirects</code> anchoring</h2>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Confirmed, and this was the more consequential one — it broke the exact remedy the PR documents. Reproduced your trace as a test, and verified it <strong>fails</strong> against the construction-time anchor:</p>\\n<div class=\\\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\\\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\\\"--- FAIL: TestGuardRedirectsAnchorsOnTheIssuedRequest\\n    credentials were stripped on a hop that never left the adopted host\\\"><pre class=\\\"notranslate\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">--- FAIL: TestGuardRedirectsAnchorsOnTheIssuedRequest\\n    credentials were stripped on a hop that never left the adopted host\\n</code></pre></div>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">via[0].URL</code> is the right anchor for the reason you give: it'\"'\"'s whatever <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">requestURL()</code> or the helper-retry target actually pointed at, so it'\"'\"'s accurate per request in both cases instead of describing a connection-level state that has since moved. The closure no longer captures the endpoint at all, and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">guardRedirects</code> lost its <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">*url.URL</code> parameter as a result.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">One addition: a nil anchor now fails closed. Go guarantees <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">len(via) &gt;= 1</code> so it'\"'\"'s defensive only, but <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">sameSite(nil, x)</code> returning <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">false</code> means unknown provenance strips rather than forwards.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">A second test covers the other direction — a hop that genuinely leaves the issued request'\"'\"'s site still loses the header — so the two aren'\"'\"'t traded off against each other.</p>\\n<h2 dir=\\\"auto\\\">Docs</h2>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Both <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">docs/usage.md</code> and the changelog said \\\"same scheme and port\\\" and now describe the downgrade rule. I'\"'\"'ve also replaced the PR'\"'\"'s behavior-change section with an explicit table of what'\"'\"'s kept versus withheld, since the previous wording only mentioned hosts.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Rebased onto <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">main</code> now that <a class=\\\"issue-link js-issue-link\\\" data-error-text=\\\"Failed to load title\\\" data-id=\\\"5192270519\\\" data-permission-text=\\\"Title is private\\\" data-url=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/issues/107\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"pull_request\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/entireio/git-sync/pull/107/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/107\\\">#107</a> has merged. <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">gofmt</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">go vet</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">golangci-lint</code> (0 issues), <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">go test ./...</code> 18/18.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/108#pullrequestreview-4983011272\",\n        \"body\": \"\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"nodo\",\n          \"name\": \"nodo\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/829178?u=2f501cf3464df66b7ec3a6ab1eafc90d41b97974&v=4\",\n          \"id\": 829178\n        },\n        \"id\": 4983011272,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-08-20T13:06:02Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"APPROVED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/108\",\n    \"title\": \"entireio/git-sync PR #108 comments\",\n    \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/108\",\n    \"display_title\": \"entireio/git-sync PR #108 comments\"\n  }\n}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":12500}},"started_at_ms":1794842143175,"completed_at_ms":1794842143176}}
