\\"auto\\\"><strong>No open issues</strong> 🎉</p>\\n<details>\\n<summary><strong>2 resolved since last review</strong></summary>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li><themed-picture data-catalyst-inline=\\\"true\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/834ba6f0360a8652493651579db001bd13eb0b882cde8bf4f2f072b3355c6eab/68747470733a2f2f6769746875622e6769746875626173736574732e636f6d2f7374617469632f696d616765732f69636f6e732f636f70696c6f742d636f64652d7265766965772f686967682d76322d6461726b2e737667\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-dark.svg\\\"><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/2c56fed1b4cb242f21b21df88fd6fe98ee4b87e75beaa2a986dbc0cceb751596/68747470733a2f2f6769746875622e6769746875626173736574732e636f6d2f7374617469632f696d616765732f69636f6e732f636f70696c6f742d636f64652d7265766965772f686967682d76322d6c696768742e737667\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-light.svg\\\"><img src=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/9c0cde422fad508ba32001d32aff9e03628698080e0e469cb49a00c7e0c6cc01/68747470733a2f2f6769746875622e6769746875626173736574732e636f6d2f7374617469632f696d616765732f69636f6e732f636f70696c6f742d636f64652d7265766965772f686967682d76322d6c696768742e706e67\\\" alt=\\\"High severity\\\" width=\\\"62\\\" height=\\\"18\\\" align=\\\"texttop\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-light.png\\\"></picture></themed-picture> <a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#discussion_r4315859003\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"pull_request\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/entireio/git-sync/pull/124/hovercard\\\">Redirected helper credentials reused across hosts</a></li>\\n<li><themed-picture data-catalyst-inline=\\\"true\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/3868f518af8a13817c492e417e4bcdd49346975a4f3786c3e8dda094400fe94a/68747470733a2f2f6769746875622e6769746875626173736574732e636f6d2f7374617469632f696d616765732f69636f6e732f636f70696c6f742d636f64652d7265766965772f6d656469756d2d76322d6461726b2e737667\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\\\"><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/4e401c45fe265191ce60dd43159ae6873ccb06626b2c0546f0b466d3511d457d/68747470733a2f2f6769746875622e6769746875626173736574732e636f6d2f7374617469632f696d616765732f69636f6e732f636f70696c6f742d636f64652d7265766965772f6d656469756d2d76322d6c696768742e737667\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\\\"><img src=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/7dc8929f1372d7be218d83fe61e6c3fb67ed8bc61cd50c1e8e4696827da90595/68747470733a2f2f6769746875622e6769746875626173736574732e636f6d2f7374617469632f696d616765732f69636f6e732f636f70696c6f742d636f64652d7265766965772f6d656469756d2d76322d6c696768742e706e67\\\" alt=\\\"Medium severity\\\" width=\\\"62\\\" height=\\\"18\\\" align=\\\"texttop\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\\\"></picture></themed-picture> <a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#discussion_r4315859072\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"pull_request\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/entireio/git-sync/pull/124/hovercard\\\">URL userinfo credentials omitted from API lookup</a></li>\\n</ul>\\n</details>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub></p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#pullrequestreview-5575071294\",\n        \"body\": \"<!-- BUGBOT_REVIEW -->\\n<!-- BUGBOT_REVIEW_STALE -->\\nStale Bugbot comment from a previous run.\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"cursor[bot]\",\n          \"name\": \"cursor[bot]\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1210556?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 206951365\n        },\n        \"id\": 5575071294,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-19T17:11:18Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Stale Bugbot comment from a previous run.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#discussion_r4317975038\",\n        \"body\": \"**Low:** `GitHubOwnerRepo` does not validate `owner`/`repo`, so a `..` segment changes the API path that the credentials now go to.\\n\\n`url.Parse` keeps `..` in `ep.Path`. `JoinPath` then cleans it away. I checked it:\\n\\n```\\nhttps://github.com/../user     -> GET https://api.github.com/user\\nhttps://github.com/%2e%2e/user -> GET https://api.github.com/user\\n```\\n\\n`CredentialsFor` gives the token to that request, because it is the same host. The request reaches the authenticated-user endpoint, not `/repos/{owner}/{repo}`. The impact is small: it is the same host and only a GET, the response has no `size` and becomes a lookup failure, and info/refs would probably fail first. But now that this request carries credentials, it should go only to the endpoint it is meant for.\\n\\nSuggested fix in `GitHubOwnerRepo`: reject `.` and `..`, and accept only GitHub'\"'\"'s name characters, e.g. `^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$` for each part. Add a test case for `https://github.com/../user`.\\n\\n---\\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"pjbgf\",\n          \"name\": \"pjbgf\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5452977?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 5452977\n        },\n        \"id\": 4317975038,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 5576687758,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-19T19:32:42Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-19T19:32:47Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": \"internal/strategy/bootstrap/bootstrap.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>Low:</strong> <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">GitHubOwnerRepo</code> does not validate <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">owner</code>/<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">repo</code>, so a <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">..</code> segment changes the API path that the credentials now go to.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">url.Parse</code> keeps <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">..</code> in <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">ep.Path</code>. <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">JoinPath</code> then cleans it away. I checked it:</p>\\n<div class=\\\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\\\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\\\"https://github.com/../user     -&gt; GET https://api.github.com/user\\nhttps://github.com/%2e%2e/user -&gt; GET https://api.github.com/user\\\"><pre class=\\\"notranslate\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">https://github.com/../user     -&gt; GET https://api.github.com/user\\nhttps://github.com/%2e%2e/user -&gt; GET https://api.github.com/user\\n</code></pre></div>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">CredentialsFor</code> gives the token to that request, because it is the same host. The request reaches the authenticated-user endpoint, not <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">/repos/{owner}/{repo}</code>. The impact is small: it is the same host and only a GET, the response has no <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">size</code> and becomes a lookup failure, and info/refs would probably fail first. But now that this request carries credentials, it should go only to the endpoint it is meant for.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Suggested fix in <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">GitHubOwnerRepo</code>: reject <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">.</code> and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">..</code>, and accept only GitHub'\"'\"'s name characters, e.g. <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$</code> for each part. Add a test case for <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">https://github.com/../user</code>.</p>\\n<hr>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><em>Generated by <a href=\\\"https://claude.ai/code\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">Claude Code</a></em></p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#pullrequestreview-5576687758\",\n        \"body\": \"One low-severity finding from a git-conformance, security and performance review. The rest of the credential scoping (redirect binding, helper origin, TLS-off, log sanitisation) checked out.\\n\\n---\\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"pjbgf\",\n          \"name\": \"pjbgf\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5452977?u=12b07e2a98b008e521f0b845fd1c9e251d0375c4&v=4\",\n          \"id\": 5452977\n        },\n        \"id\": 5576687758,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-19T19:32:47Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"pa'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/git-sync-124.json' '      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-19T16:11:29Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Ported the Go 1.27.2 bump from <a class=\\\"issue-link js-issue-link\\\" data-error-text=\\\"Failed to load title\\\" data-id=\\\"5908744772\\\" data-permission-text=\\\"Title is private\\\" data-url=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/issues/123\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"pull_request\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/entireio/git-sync/pull/123/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/123\\\">#123</a> as <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/58e81acbd41faf553b497d30faba9c5ff7bf129b/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/58e81acbd41faf553b497d30faba9c5ff7bf129b\\\"><tt>58e81ac</tt></a> (cherry-pick of <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/8484a5f2fd482c67bc6d7ed3585a2f9b78ef7493/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/8484a5f2fd482c67bc6d7ed3585a2f9b78ef7493\\\"><tt>8484a5f</tt></a>). It no-ops once <a class=\\\"issue-link js-issue-link\\\" data-error-text=\\\"Failed to load title\\\" data-id=\\\"5908744772\\\" data-permission-text=\\\"Title is private\\\" data-url=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/issues/123\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"pull_request\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/entireio/git-sync/pull/123/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/123\\\">#123</a> lands. Verified locally on go1.27.2:</p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">govulncheck</code> reports 0 vulnerabilities in called code;</li>\\n<li><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">go test ./...</code> passes;</li>\\n<li><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">golangci-lint</code> v2.15.0 reports 0 issues.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<hr>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><em>Generated by <a href=\\\"https://claude.ai/code\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">Claude Code</a></em></p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#issuecomment-6272192444\",\n        \"body\": \"Update: the Go 1.27.2 port (58e81ac) is no longer on this branch. 6e75338 was pushed on top of 068547f, so `go.mod` is back on go1.26.6 and `govulncheck` fails again for the same standard-library advisories as `main`.\\n\\n58e81ac itself passed every check, `govulncheck` included. The fix is still #123'\"'\"'s toolchain bump: either re-apply it here or merge `main` in once #123 lands.\\n\\n---\\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"nodo\",\n          \"name\": \"nodo\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/829178?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 829178\n        },\n        \"id\": 6272192444,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-19T16:38:10Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-19T16:38:10Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Update: the Go 1.27.2 port (<a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/58e81acbd41faf553b497d30faba9c5ff7bf129b/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/58e81acbd41faf553b497d30faba9c5ff7bf129b\\\"><tt>58e81ac</tt></a>) is no longer on this branch. <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/6e7533849bf78f7c2ca259331a4736a325abc9b3/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/6e7533849bf78f7c2ca259331a4736