ttps://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\\\"><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\\\"><img src=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\\\" alt=\\\"Medium severity\\\" width=\\\"62\\\" height=\\\"18\\\" align=\\\"texttop\\\"></picture> [URL userinfo credentials omitted from API lookup](https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#discussion_r4315859072)\\n</details>\\n\\n<sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub>\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"name\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 5575049483,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-19T17:09:19Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"\\n<h3 dir=\\\"auto\\\">🔵 Needs a closer look</h3>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Cross-service credential reuse and redirect-sensitive authentication warrant final human security review.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>No open issues</strong> 🎉</p>\\n<details>\\n<summary><strong>2 resolved since last review</strong></summary>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li><themed-picture data-catalyst-inline=\\\"true\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/834ba6f0360a8652493651579db001bd13eb0b882cde8bf4f2f072b3355c6eab/68747470733a2f2f6769746875622e6769746875626173736574732e636f6d2f7374617469632f696d616765732f69636f6e732f636f70696c6f742d636f64652d7265766965772f686967682d76322d6461726b2e737667\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-dark.svg\\\"><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/2c56fed1b4cb242f21b21df88fd6fe98ee4b87e75beaa2a986dbc0cceb751596/68747470733a2f2f6769746875622e6769746875626173736574732e636f6d2f7374617469632f696d616765732f69636f6e732f636f70696c6f742d636f64652d7265766965772f686967682d76322d6c696768742e737667\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-light.svg\\\"><img src=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/9c0cde422fad508ba32001d32aff9e03628698080e0e469cb49a00c7e0c6cc01/68747470733a2f2f6769746875622e6769746875626173736574732e636f6d2f7374617469632f696d616765732f69636f6e732f636f70696c6f742d636f64652d7265766965772f686967682d76322d6c696768742e706e67\\\" alt=\\\"High severity\\\" width=\\\"62\\\" height=\\\"18\\\" align=\\\"texttop\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-light.png\\\"></picture></themed-picture> <a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#discussion_r4315859003\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"pull_request\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/entireio/git-sync/pull/124/hovercard\\\">Redirected helper credentials reused across hosts</a></li>\\n<li><themed-picture data-catalyst-inline=\\\"true\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/3868f518af8a13817c492e417e4bcdd49346975a4f3786c3e8dda094400fe94a/68747470733a2f2f6769746875622e6769746875626173736574732e636f6d2f7374617469632f696d616765732f69636f6e732f636f70696c6f742d636f64652d7265766965772f6d656469756d2d76322d6461726b2e737667\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\\\"><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/4e401c45fe265191ce60dd43159ae6873ccb06626b2c0546f0b466d3511d457d/68747470733a2f2f6769746875622e6769746875626173736574732e636f6d2f7374617469632f696d616765732f69636f6e732f636f70696c6f742d636f64652d7265766965772f6d656469756d2d76322d6c696768742e737667\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\\\"><img src=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/7dc8929f1372d7be218d83fe61e6c3fb67ed8bc61cd50c1e8e4696827da90595/68747470733a2f2f6769746875622e6769746875626173736574732e636f6d2f7374617469632f696d616765732f69636f6e732f636f70696c6f742d636f64652d7265766965772f6d656469756d2d76322d6c696768742e706e67\\\" alt=\\\"Medium severity\\\" width=\\\"62\\\" height=\\\"18\\\" align=\\\"texttop\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\\\"></picture></themed-picture> <a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#discussion_r4315859072\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"pull_request\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/entireio/git-sync/pull/124/hovercard\\\">URL userinfo credentials omitted from API lookup</a></li>\\n</ul>\\n</details>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub></p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#pullrequestreview-5575071294\",\n        \"body\": \"<!-- BUGBOT_REVIEW -->\\n<!-- BUGBOT_REVIEW_STALE -->\\nStale Bugbot comment from a previous run.\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"cursor[bot]\",\n          \"name\": \"cursor[bot]\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1210556?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 206951365\n        },\n        \"id\": 5575071294,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-19T17:11:18Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Stale Bugbot comment from a previous run.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#discussion_r4317975038\",\n        \"body\": \"**Low:** `GitHubOwnerRepo` does not validate `owner`/`repo`, so a `..` segment changes the API path that the credentials now go to.\\n\\n`url.Parse` keeps `..` in `ep.Path`. `JoinPath` then cleans it away. I checked it:\\n\\n```\\nhttps://github.com/../user     -> GET https://api.github.com/user\\nhttps://github.com/%2e%2e/user -> GET https://api.github.com/user\\n```\\n\\n`CredentialsFor` gives the token to that request, because it is the same host. The request reaches the authenticated-user endpoint, not `/repos/{owner}/{repo}`. The impact is small: it is the same host and only a GET, the response has no `size` and becomes a lookup failure, and info/refs would probably fail first. But now that this request carries credentials, it should go only to the endpoint it is meant for.\\n\\nSuggested fix in `GitHubOwnerRepo`: reject `.` and `..`, and accept only GitHub'\"'\"'s name characters, e.g. `^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$` for each part. Add a test case for `https://github.com/../user`.\\n\\n---\\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"pjbgf\",\n          \"name\": \"pjbgf\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5452977?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 5452977\n        },\n        \"id\": 4317975038,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 5576687758,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-19T19:32:42Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-19T19:32:47Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": \"internal/strategy/bootstrap/bootstrap.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>Low:</strong> <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">GitHubOwnerRepo</code> does not validate <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">owner</code>/<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">repo</code>, so a <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">..</code> segment changes the API path that the credentials now go to.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">url.Parse</code> keeps <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">..</code> in <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">ep.Path</code>. <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">JoinPath</code> then cleans it away. I checked it:</p>\\n<div class=\\\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\\\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\\\"https://github.com/../user     -&gt; GET https://api.github.com/user\\nhttps://github.com/%2e%2e/user -&gt; GET https://api.github.com/user\\\"><pre class=\\\"notranslate\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">https://github.com/../user     -&gt; GET https://api.github.com/user\\nhttps://github.com/%2e%2e/user -&gt; GET https://api.github.com/user\\n</code></pre></div>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">CredentialsFor</code> gives the token to that request, because it is the same host. The request reaches the authenticated-user endpoint, not <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">/repos/{owner}/{repo}</code>. The impact is small: it is the same host and only a GET, the response has no <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">size</code> and becomes a lookup failure, and info/refs would probably fail first. But now that this request carries credentials, it should go only to the endpoint it is meant for.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Suggested fix in <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">GitHubOwnerRepo</code>: reject <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">.</code> and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">..</code>, and accept only GitHub'\"'\"'s name characters, e.g. <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$</code> for each part. Add a test case for <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">https://github.com/../user</code>.</p>\\n<hr>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><em>Generated by <a href=\\\"https://claude.ai/code\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">Claude Code</a></em></p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#pullrequestreview-5576687758\",\n        \"body\": \"One low-severity finding from a git-conformance, security and performance review. The rest of the credential scoping (redirect binding, helper origin, TLS-off, log sanitisation) checked out.\\n\\n---\\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"pjbgf\",\n          \"name\": \"pjbgf\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5452977?u=12b07e2a98b008e521f0b845fd1c9e251d0375c4&v=4\",\n          \"id\": 5452977\n        },\n        \"id\": 5576687758,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-19T19:32:47Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"pa'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":10542}},"started_at_ms":1794842144149,"completed_at_ms":1794842144149}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:15:44.271Z","ordinal":3121,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-367e8525-66a1-4d05-8bfb-5e3c670ac80d","process_id":"54721","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/git-sync-124.json' 'th\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">One low-severity finding from a git-conformance, security and performance review. The rest of the credential scoping (redirect binding, helper origin, TLS-off, log sanitisation) checked out.</p>\\n<hr>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><em>Generated by <a href=\\\"https://claude.ai/code\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">Claude Code</a></em></p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#discussion_r4317992510\",\n        \"body\": \"Good catch, fixed in 29f63a4. `GitHubOwnerRepo` now accepts each part only if it matches `^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$` and rejects `.` and `..` outright. With an invalid name the lookup is skipped entirely, so no request is made.\\n\\nNew cases in `TestGitHubPreflightSkippedLogsNothing` cover `https://github.com/../user`, `https://github.com/%2e%2e/user`, `https://github.com/acme/.` and a name containing an encoded `?`. Each asserts that no request reaches the API and nothing is logged.\\n\\n---\\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"nodo\",\n          \"name\": \"nodo\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/829178?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 829178\n        },\n        \"id\": 4317992510,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 5576709563,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": 4317975038,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-19T19:34:39Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-19T19:34:39Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": \"internal/strategy/bootstrap/bootstrap.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Good catch, fixed in <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/29f63a4576a3df259c8262a2119b478d65daa072/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/29f63a4576a3df259c8262a2119b478d65daa072\\\"><tt>29f63a4</tt></a>. <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">GitHubOwnerRepo</code> now accepts each part only if it matches <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$</code> and rejects <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">.</code> and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">..</code> outright. With an invalid name the lookup is skipped entirely, so no request is made.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">New cases in <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">TestGitHubPreflightSkippedLogsNothing</code> cover <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">https://github.com/../user</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">https://github.com/%2e%2e/user</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">https://github.com/acme/.</code> and a name containing an encoded <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">?</code>. Each asserts that no request reaches the API and nothing is logged.</p>\\n<hr>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><em>Generated by <a href=\\\"https://claude.ai/code\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">Claude Code</a></em></p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#pullrequestreview-5576709563\",\n        \"body\": \"\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"nodo\",\n          \"name\": \"nodo\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/829178?u=2f501cf3464df66b7ec3a6ab1eafc90d41b97974&v=4\",\n          \"id\": 829178\n        },\n        \"id\": 5576709563,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-19T19:34:39Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#pullrequestreview-5581437770\",\n        \"body\": \"\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"pjbgf\",\n          \"name\": \"pjbgf\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5452977?u=12b07e2a98b008e521f0b845fd1c9e251d0375c4&v=4\",\n          \"id\": 5452977\n        },\n        \"id\": 5581437770,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-20T06:21:28Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"DISMISSED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#issuecomment-6288610871\",\n        \"body\": \"bugbot run\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"nodo\",\n          \"name\": \"nodo\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/829178?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 829178\n        },\n        \"id\": 6288610871,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:13:32Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:13:32Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">bugbot run</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#discussion_r4323882698\",\n        \"body\": \"A custom `RoundTripper` can receive Authorization but return a response with `Response.Request == nil`, as the new `TestGitHubPreflightResponseWithoutRequest` already allows. If it returns 401/403, this assignment sets `authenticated` to false and `lookupGitHubRepoSize` skips the anonymous retry. A large public repository then starts with a single pack even when an anonymous lookup would succeed. Track the outgoing request'\"'\"'s authentication after the redirect policy has run, rather than treating missing response provenance as proof that no credentials were sent. Add a nil-`Response.Request` refusal/retry regression while preserving the no-retry behavior for redirects that actually stripped credentials.\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"name\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 4323882698,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 5583725121,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:18:05Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:18:05Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": \"internal/strategy/bootstrap/github_preflight.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">A custom <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">RoundTripper</code> can receive Authorization but return a response with <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Response.Request == nil</code>, as the new <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">TestGitHubPreflightResponseWithoutRequest</code> already allows. If it returns 401/403, this assignment sets <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">authenticated</code> to false and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">lookupGitHubRepoSize</code> skips the anonymous retry. A large public repository then starts with a single pack even when an anonymous lookup would succeed. Track the outgoing request'\"'\"'s authentication after the redirect policy has run, rather than treating missing response provenance as proof that no credentials were sent. Add a nil-<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Response.Request</code> refusal/retry regression while preserving the no-retry behavior for redirects that actually stripped credentials.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#pullrequestreview-5583725121\",\n        \"body\": \"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\\n\\n### 🟡 Changes recommended\\n\\nCustom transports with missing response provenance can incorrectly suppress the anonymous retry after token refusal.\\n\\n<details open>\\n<summary><strong>1 open issue</strong></summary>\\n\\n- <picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\\\"><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\\\"><img src=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\\\" alt=\\\"Medium severity\\\" width=\\\"62\\\" height=\\\"18\\\" align=\\\"texttop\\\"></picture> [Preserve authentication when Response.Request is nil](https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#discussion_r4323882698) · New\\n</details>\\n\\n<sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub>\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"name\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 5583725121,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:18:05Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"\\n<h3 dir=\\\"auto\\\">🟡 Changes recommended</h3>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Custom transports with missing response provenance can incorrectly suppress the anonymous retry after token refusal.</p>\\n<details open=\\\"\\\">\\n<summary><strong>1 open issue</strong></summary>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li><themed-picture data-catalyst-inline=\\\"true\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/3868f518af8a13817c492e417e4bcdd49346975a4f3786c3e8dda094400fe94a/68747470733a2f2f6769746875622e6769746875626173736574732e636f6d2f7374617469632f696d616765732f69636f6e732f636f70696c6f742d636f64652d7265766965772f6d656469756d2d76322d6461726b2e737667\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\\\"><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/4e401c45fe265191ce60dd43159ae6873ccb06626b2c0546f0b466d3511d457d/68747470733a2f2f6769746875622e6769746875626173736574732e636f6d2f7374617469632f696d616765732f69636f6e732f636f70696c6f742d636f64652d7265766965772f6d656469756d2d76322d6c696768742e737667\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\\\"><img src=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/7dc8929f1372d7be218d83fe61e6c3fb67ed8bc61cd50c1e8e4696827da90595/68747470733a2f2f6769746875622e6769746875626173736574732e636f6d2f7374617469632f696d616765732f69636f6e732f636f70696c6f742d636f64652d7265766965772f6d656469756d2d76322d6c696768742e706e67\\\" alt=\\\"Medium severity\\\" width=\\\"62\\\" height=\\\"18\\\" align=\\\"texttop\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\\\"></picture></themed-picture> <a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#discussion_r4323882698\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"pull_request\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/entireio/git-sync/pull/124/hovercard\\\">Preserve authentication when Response.Request is nil</a> · New</li>\\n</ul>\\n</details>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub></p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#discussion_r4323887494\",\n        \"body\": \"Confirmed, but the trigger is narrow. `http.Client` never fills in `Response.Request` itself; the standard `http.Transport` does, and wrappers like `otelhttp` pass the inner response through. So the retry is lost only when all of these hold:\\n- a caller-supplied transport builds the response itself without setting `Request`;\\n- the API refuses the token with 401 or 403;\\n- the repository is public and over the threshold.\\n\\nThere are two possible fixes:\\n- **Keep the pre-send flag when `Response.Request` is nil.** This is one line, but it reverses what `TestGitHubPreflightResponseWithoutRequest` currently asserts, which is not claiming authentication when provenance is unknown.\\n- **Record the outgoing request'\"'\"'s auth state in a `CheckRedirect` hook.** This keeps the redirect case exact, at the cost of more code.\\n\\nThe current behavior was a deliberate choice in 19751f4, so I'\"'\"'m leaving the decision to the author rather than pushing over it.\\n\\n---\\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"nodo\",\n          \"name\": \"nodo\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/829178?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 829178\n        },\n        \"id\": 4323887494,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 5583730852,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": 4323882698,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:18:42Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:18:42Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": \"internal/strategy/bootstrap/github_preflight.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Confirmed, but the trigger is narrow. <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">http.Client</code> never fills in <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Response.Request</code> itself; the standard <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">http.Transport</code> does, and wrappers like <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">otelhttp</code> pass the inner response through. So the retry is lost only when all of these hold:</p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>a caller-supplied transport builds the response itself without setting <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Request</code>;</li>\\n<li>the API refuses the token with 401 or 403;</li>\\n<li>the repository is public and over the threshold.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">There are two possible fixes:</p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li><strong>Keep the pre-send flag when <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Response.Request</code> is nil.</strong> This is one line, but it reverses what <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">TestGitHubPreflightResponseWithoutRequest</code> currently asserts, which is not claiming authentication when provenance is unknown.</li>\\n<li><strong>Record the outgoing request'\"'\"'s auth state in a <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">CheckRedirect</code> hook.</strong> This keeps the redirect case exact, at the cost of more code.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">The current behavior was a deliberate choice in <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/19751f4500576dea28c61945b39b7543e38fc031/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/19751f4500576dea28c61945b39b7543e38fc031\\\"><tt>19751f4</tt></a>, so I'\"'\"'m leaving the decision to the author rather than pushing over it.</p>\\n<hr>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><em>Generated by <a href=\\\"https://claude.ai/code\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">Claude Code</a></em></p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#pullrequestreview-5583730852\",\n        \"body\": \"\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"nodo\",\n          \"name\": \"nodo\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/829178?u=2f501cf3464df66b7ec3a6ab1eafc90d41b97974&v=4\",\n          \"id\": 829178\n        },\n        \"id\": 5583730852,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:18:42Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#pullrequestreview-5583738220\",\n        \"body\": \"<!-- BUGBOT_REVIEW -->\\n<!-- BUGBOT_REVIEW_STALE -->\\nStale Bugbot comment from a previous run.\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"cursor[bot]\",\n          \"name\": \"cursor[bot]\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1210556?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 206951365\n        },\n        \"id\": 5583738220,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:19:30Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"\\n\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Stale Bugbot comment from a previous run.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#issuecomment-6288726136\",\n        \"body\": \"bugbot run\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"nodo\",\n          \"name\": \"nodo\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/829178?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 829178\n        },\n        \"id\": 6288726136,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:20:31Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:20:31Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">bugbot run</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#pullrequestreview-5583777173\",\n        \"body\": \"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\\n\\n### 🟢 Approval recommended\\n\\nCredential scoping, retry behavior, and diagnostics have targeted regression coverage, with no unresolved blocking findings.\\n\\n**No open issues** 🎉\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary><strong>1 resolved since last review</strong></summary>\\n\\n- <picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\\\"><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\\\"><img src=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\\\" alt=\\\"Medium severity\\\" width=\\\"62\\\" height=\\\"18\\\" align=\\\"texttop\\\"></picture> [Preserve authentication when Response.Request is nil](https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#discussion_r4323882698)\\n</details>\\n\\n<sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub>\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"name\": \"copilot-pull-requ'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import sys;open(sys.argv[1],\"ab\").write(sys.argv[2].encode())' '/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/public/git-sync-124.json' 'th\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">One low-severity finding from a git-conformance, security and performance review. The rest of the credential scoping (redirect binding, helper origin, TLS-off, log sanitisation) checked out.</p>\\n<hr>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><em>Generated by <a href=\\\"https://claude.ai/code\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">Claude Code</a></em></p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#discussion_r4317992510\",\n        \"body\": \"Good catch, fixed in 29f63a4. `GitHubOwnerRepo` now accepts each part only if it matches `^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$` and rejects `.` and `..` outright. With an invalid name the lookup is skipped entirely, so no request is made.\\n\\nNew cases in `TestGitHubPreflightSkippedLogsNothing` cover `https://github.com/../user`, `https://github.com/%2e%2e/user`, `https://github.com/acme/.` and a name containing an encoded `?`. Each asserts that no request reaches the API and nothing is logged.\\n\\n---\\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"nodo\",\n          \"name\": \"nodo\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/829178?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 829178\n        },\n        \"id\": 4317992510,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 5576709563,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": 4317975038,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-19T19:34:39Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-19T19:34:39Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": \"internal/strategy/bootstrap/bootstrap.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Good catch, fixed in <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/29f63a4576a3df259c8262a2119b478d65daa072/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/29f63a4576a3df259c8262a2119b478d65daa072\\\"><tt>29f63a4</tt></a>. <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">GitHubOwnerRepo</code> now accepts each part only if it matches <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$</code> and rejects <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">.</code> and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">..</code> outright. With an invalid name the lookup is skipped entirely, so no request is made.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">New cases in <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">TestGitHubPreflightSkippedLogsNothing</code> cover <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">https://github.com/../user</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">https://github.com/%2e%2e/user</code>, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">https://github.com/acme/.</code> and a name containing an encoded <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">?</code>. Each asserts that no request reaches the API and nothing is logged.</p>\\n<hr>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><em>Generated by <a href=\\\"https://claude.ai/code\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">Claude Code</a></em></p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#pullrequestreview-5576709563\",\n        \"body\": \"\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"nodo\",\n          \"name\": \"nodo\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/829178?u=2f501cf3464df66b7ec3a6ab1eafc90d41b97974&v=4\",\n          \"id\": 829178\n        },\n        \"id\": 5576709563,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-19T19:34:39Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#pullrequestreview-5581437770\",\n        \"body\": \"\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"pjbgf\",\n          \"name\": \"pjbgf\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5452977?u=12b07e2a98b008e521f0b845fd1c9e251d0375c4&v=4\",\n          \"id\": 5452977\n        },\n        \"id\": 5581437770,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-20T06:21:28Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"DISMISSED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#issuecomment-6288610871\",\n        \"body\": \"bugbot run\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"nodo\",\n          \"name\": \"nodo\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/829178?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 829178\n        },\n        \"id\": 6288610871,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:13:32Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:13:32Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">bugbot run</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#discussion_r4323882698\",\n        \"body\": \"A custom `RoundTripper` can receive Authorization but return a response with `Response.Request == nil`, as the new `TestGitHubPreflightResponseWithoutRequest` already allows. If it returns 401/403, this assignment sets `authenticated` to false and `lookupGitHubRepoSize` skips the anonymous retry. A large public repository then starts with a single pack even when an anonymous lookup would succeed. Track the outgoing request'\"'\"'s authentication after the redirect policy has run, rather than treating missing response provenance as proof that no credentials were sent. Add a nil-`Response.Request` refusal/retry regression while preserving the no-retry behavior for redirects that actually stripped credentials.\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"name\": \"Copilot\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 4323882698,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 5583725121,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:18:05Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:18:05Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": \"internal/strategy/bootstrap/github_preflight.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">A custom <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">RoundTripper</code> can receive Authorization but return a response with <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Response.Request == nil</code>, as the new <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">TestGitHubPreflightResponseWithoutRequest</code> already allows. If it returns 401/403, this assignment sets <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">authenticated</code> to false and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">lookupGitHubRepoSize</code> skips the anonymous retry. A large public repository then starts with a single pack even when an anonymous lookup would succeed. Track the outgoing request'\"'\"'s authentication after the redirect policy has run, rather than treating missing response provenance as proof that no credentials were sent. Add a nil-<code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Response.Request</code> refusal/retry regression while preserving the no-retry behavior for redirects that actually stripped credentials.</p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#pullrequestreview-5583725121\",\n        \"body\": \"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\\n\\n### 🟡 Changes recommended\\n\\nCustom transports with missing response provenance can incorrectly suppress the anonymous retry after token refusal.\\n\\n<details open>\\n<summary><strong>1 open issue</strong></summary>\\n\\n- <picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\\\"><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\\\"><img src=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\\\" alt=\\\"Medium severity\\\" width=\\\"62\\\" height=\\\"18\\\" align=\\\"texttop\\\"></picture> [Preserve authentication when Response.Request is nil](https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#discussion_r4323882698) · New\\n</details>\\n\\n<sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub>\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"name\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/946600?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 175728472\n        },\n        \"id\": 5583725121,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:18:05Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"\\n<h3 dir=\\\"auto\\\">🟡 Changes recommended</h3>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Custom transports with missing response provenance can incorrectly suppress the anonymous retry after token refusal.</p>\\n<details open=\\\"\\\">\\n<summary><strong>1 open issue</strong></summary>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li><themed-picture data-catalyst-inline=\\\"true\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/3868f518af8a13817c492e417e4bcdd49346975a4f3786c3e8dda094400fe94a/68747470733a2f2f6769746875622e6769746875626173736574732e636f6d2f7374617469632f696d616765732f69636f6e732f636f70696c6f742d636f64652d7265766965772f6d656469756d2d76322d6461726b2e737667\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\\\"><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/4e401c45fe265191ce60dd43159ae6873ccb06626b2c0546f0b466d3511d457d/68747470733a2f2f6769746875622e6769746875626173736574732e636f6d2f7374617469632f696d616765732f69636f6e732f636f70696c6f742d636f64652d7265766965772f6d656469756d2d76322d6c696768742e737667\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\\\"><img src=\\\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/7dc8929f1372d7be218d83fe61e6c3fb67ed8bc61cd50c1e8e4696827da90595/68747470733a2f2f6769746875622e6769746875626173736574732e636f6d2f7374617469632f696d616765732f69636f6e732f636f70696c6f742d636f64652d7265766965772f6d656469756d2d76322d6c696768742e706e67\\\" alt=\\\"Medium severity\\\" width=\\\"62\\\" height=\\\"18\\\" align=\\\"texttop\\\" data-canonical-src=\\\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\\\"></picture></themed-picture> <a href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#discussion_r4323882698\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"pull_request\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"/entireio/git-sync/pull/124/hovercard\\\">Preserve authentication when Response.Request is nil</a> · New</li>\\n</ul>\\n</details>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub></p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#discussion_r4323887494\",\n        \"body\": \"Confirmed, but the trigger is narrow. `http.Client` never fills in `Response.Request` itself; the standard `http.Transport` does, and wrappers like `otelhttp` pass the inner response through. So the retry is lost only when all of these hold:\\n- a caller-supplied transport builds the response itself without setting `Request`;\\n- the API refuses the token with 401 or 403;\\n- the repository is public and over the threshold.\\n\\nThere are two possible fixes:\\n- **Keep the pre-send flag when `Response.Request` is nil.** This is one line, but it reverses what `TestGitHubPreflightResponseWithoutRequest` currently asserts, which is not claiming authentication when provenance is unknown.\\n- **Record the outgoing request'\"'\"'s auth state in a `CheckRedirect` hook.** This keeps the redirect case exact, at the cost of more code.\\n\\nThe current behavior was a deliberate choice in 19751f4, so I'\"'\"'m leaving the decision to the author rather than pushing over it.\\n\\n---\\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"nodo\",\n          \"name\": \"nodo\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/829178?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 829178\n        },\n        \"id\": 4323887494,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": 5583730852,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": 4323882698,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:18:42Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-20T10:18:42Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": \"RIGHT\",\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": \"internal/strategy/bootstrap/github_preflight.go\",\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Confirmed, but the trigger is narrow. <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">http.Client</code> never fills in <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Response.Request</code> itself; the standard <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">http.Transport</code> does, and wrappers like <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">otelhttp</code> pass the inner response through. So the retry is lost only when all of these hold:</p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>a caller-supplied transport builds the response itself without setting <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Request</code>;</li>\\n<li>the API refuses the token with 401 or 403;</li>\\n<li>the repository is public and over the threshold.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">There are two possible fixes:</p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li><strong>Keep the pre-send flag when <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">Response.Request</code> is nil.</strong> This is one line, but it reverses what <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">TestGitHubPreflightResponseWithoutRequest</code> currently asserts, which is not claiming authentication when provenance is unknown.</li>\\n<li><strong>Record the outgoing request'\"'\"'s auth state in a <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">CheckRedirect</code> hook.</strong> This keeps the redirect case exact, at the cost of more code.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">The current behavior was a deliberate choice in <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/19751f4500576dea28c61945b39b7543e38fc031/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/19751f4500576dea28c61945b39b7543e38fc031\\\"><tt>19751f4</tt></a>, so I'\"'\"'m leaving the decision to the author rather than pushing over it.</p>\\n<hr>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><em>Generated by <a href=\\\"https://claude.ai/code\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">Claude Code</a></em></p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#pullrequestreview-5583730852\",\n        \"body\": \"\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"nodo\",\n          \"name\": \"nodo\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/829178?u=2f501cf3464df66b7ec3a6ab1eafc90d41b97974&v=4\",\n          \"id\": 829178\n        },\n        \"id