   \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"\\n<h3 dir=\\\"auto\\\">🟢 Approval recommended</h3>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">No unresolved blocking issues remain, and targeted regression coverage addresses credential scoping, retries, diagnostics, and batching selection.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>No open issues</strong> 🎉</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub></p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#pullrequestreview-5601608172\",\n        \"body\": \"<!-- BUGBOT_REVIEW -->\\n✅ Bugbot reviewed your changes and found no new issues!\\n\\n_Comment `@cursor review` or `bugbot run` to trigger another review on this PR_\\n\\n<sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit d0e7b7873bb287a3c90f5ed779923b16b26d5b15. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"cursor[bot]\",\n          \"name\": \"cursor[bot]\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1210556?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 206951365\n        },\n        \"id\": 5601608172,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-21T14:50:18Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": null,\n        \"review\": \"COMMENTED\",\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">✅ Bugbot reviewed your changes and found no new issues!</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><em>Comment <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">@cursor review</code> or <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">bugbot run</code> to trigger another review on this PR</em></p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><sup>Reviewed by <a href=\\\"https://cursor.com/bugbot\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">Cursor Bugbot</a> for commit <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/d0e7b7873bb287a3c90f5ed779923b16b26d5b15/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/d0e7b7873bb287a3c90f5ed779923b16b26d5b15\\\"><tt>d0e7b78</tt></a>. Configure <a href=\\\"https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">here</a>.</sup></p>\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/124#issuecomment-6319003076\",\n        \"body\": \"`govulncheck` is red on d0e7b78 because of a newly published standard-library advisory, [GO-2026-6809](https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-6809): `crypto/x509` should distrust compromised intermediate certificates. This PR'\"'\"'s code doesn'\"'\"'t cause it. The advisory affects go1.27.2, which `main` also pins, and is fixed in go1.27.3. `main`'\"'\"'s last scan predates the advisory, so `main` will fail the next one too. Re-running the check would fail the same way, so I haven'\"'\"'t.\\n\\nNo fix PR exists yet. Verified locally:\\n- go1.27.2: GO-2026-6809 reported;\\n- go1.27.3: `govulncheck` reports 0 vulnerabilities in called code, `go test ./...` passes, and `golangci-lint` v2.15.0 reports 0 issues.\\n\\nProposed patch:\\n\\n```diff\\n--- a/go.mod\\n+++ b/go.mod\\n-toolchain go1.27.2\\n+toolchain go1.27.3\\n--- a/mise.toml\\n+++ b/mise.toml\\n-go = { version = '\"'\"'1.27.2'\"'\"', ...\\n+go = { version = '\"'\"'1.27.3'\"'\"', ...\\n```\\n\\nThis can land on its own against `main` (preferable) or ride along here.\\n\\n---\\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\",\n        \"user\": {\n          \"login\": \"nodo\",\n          \"name\": \"nodo\",\n          \"email\": null,\n          \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/829178?v=4\",\n          \"id\": 829178\n        },\n        \"id\": 6319003076,\n        \"pull_request_review_id\": null,\n        \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-21T14:51:51Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-21T14:51:51Z\",\n        \"review\": null,\n        \"side\": null,\n        \"line\": null,\n        \"start_line\": null,\n        \"path\": null,\n        \"body_html\": \"<p dir=\\\"auto\\\"><code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">govulncheck</code> is red on <a class=\\\"commit-link\\\" data-hovercard-type=\\\"commit\\\" data-hovercard-url=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/d0e7b7873bb287a3c90f5ed779923b16b26d5b15/hovercard\\\" href=\\\"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/commit/d0e7b7873bb287a3c90f5ed779923b16b26d5b15\\\"><tt>d0e7b78</tt></a> because of a newly published standard-library advisory, <a href=\\\"https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-6809\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">GO-2026-6809</a>: <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">crypto/x509</code> should distrust compromised intermediate certificates. This PR'\"'\"'s code doesn'\"'\"'t cause it. The advisory affects go1.27.2, which <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">main</code> also pins, and is fixed in go1.27.3. <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">main</code>'\"'\"'s last scan predates the advisory, so <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">main</code> will fail the next one too. Re-running the check would fail the same way, so I haven'\"'\"'t.</p>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">No fix PR exists yet. Verified locally:</p>\\n<ul dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\n<li>go1.27.2: GO-2026-6809 reported;</li>\\n<li>go1.27.3: <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">govulncheck</code> reports 0 vulnerabilities in called code, <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">go test ./...</code> passes, and <code class=\\\"notranslate\\\">golangci-lint</code> v2.15.0 reports 0 issues.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p dir=\\\"auto\\\">Proposed patch:</p>\\n<div class=\\\"highlight highlight-source-diff notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\\\" dir=\\\"auto\\\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\\\"--- a/go.mod\\n+++ b/go.mod\\n-toolchain go1.27.2\\n+toolchain go1.27.3\\n--- a/mise.toml\\n+++ b/mise.toml\\n-go = { version = '\"'\"'1.27.2'\"'\"', ...\\n+go = { version = '\"'\"'1.27.3'\"'\"', ...\\\"><pre class=\\\"notranslate\