{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:17:41.176Z","ordinal":3137,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_05a7fc4dc4b68e03016afb1e5d021c87d0bd001c4aa7d5a73c","status":"completed","call_id":"call_312f0185275c4ba38bffa050f1009ac6","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"python3 - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nimport json,hashlib\\np=Path('/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16');data=json.loads((p/'candidates.json').read_text())\\ndata['stage']='Discovery; one focused candidate READY in scoped checks; nineteen HOLD; no production implementation'\\ndata['decisions']={r[0]:('READY — focused, scoped public check' if r[0]=='AUD-026' else 'HOLD') for r in data['bugs']+data['features']}\\nfor row in data['bugs']:\\n if row[0]=='AUD-026':\\n  row[7]='Direct validation and public SyncRequest validation accept fragment-only aliases; two real loopback HTTP GETs reached the identical /repo.git resource. Exact fragment-free guard control rejects equal endpoints.'\\n  row[8]='Scoped gates PASS: current contract reproduction; minimal HTTP URL identity fix; no exact fragment report in all-state searches, related #18/#108/#122/#124 reviews, five open PR metadata and27 branch names. #18 reports a different trailing-slash case. Refresh immediately before a task-owned implementation; no public reservation.'\\n if row[0]=='AUD-027':row[8]+=' Source commit a81db6 already reports blank/outside-refs prefixes; character-validity cases must not be represented as that old report. Strict novelty of this extension remains HOLD.'\\n if row[0]=='AUD-028':row[9]='stats-key-probe.json'\\nversions={'cli':'76f1b5129b974afdf8e59e4ae3755083c10ff8ff','entire-brain':'12e1b0d95a078cf4b57c3c8b38bc0aeec4fb9a55','entire-graph':'3f632e403e6bd70ac015f3a80980ca39e4dadd0d','git-sync':'67dd3a4e083e4faae4417c1849035c7c4638112c','forgemark':'654e95a18db7ad690165b519eb151ecc4fc1e2f0'}\\ndata['versions']=versions\\n(p/'candidates.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\\nlines=['Entire contribution discovery: ten additional issue candidates and ten additional enhancements','16 November 2026','',data['stage'],'', 'These are additional to ENH-012 and AUD-023. ENH-004 belongs to its existing implementation owner and is excluded. Small focused tasks are included at the user\\\\'s latest request; this does not waive current-need or novelty checks. A probe PASS records current behavior, not a fix. Seven distinct behaviors have direct/fixture/verbatim-function probes. The stats-key formula is separately demonstrated; workspace graph cancellation remains source-only; checkpoint --limit has source plus installed-binary evidence, not a fresh built-source truncation fixture. No twenty-ready-PR claim.','', 'Pinned source revisions:']\\nlines += [f'  {k}: {v}' for k,v in versions.items()]\\nlines += ['', 'ISSUE CANDIDATES']\\nfor r in data['bugs']:\\n id,title,size,repo,path,line,kind,obs,remain,log=r\\n lines += ['',f'{id} — {title} [{size}; {data[\\\"decisions\\\"][id]}]',f'Evidence: {kind}. {obs}',f'Source: https://github.com/entireio/{repo}/blob/{versions[repo]}/{path}#L{line}',f'Gate / next proof: {remain}']\\n if log:lines.append('Artifact: '+str(p/log))\\nlines += ['', 'ENHANCEMENT CANDIDATES — source-backed designs, not implemented or certified unavailable upstream']\\nfor r in data['features']:\\n id,title,size,repo,path,line,scope,insp,link,remain=r\\n lines += ['',f'{id} — {title} [{size}; HOLD]',scope,f'Current public implementation seam: https://github.com/entireio/{repo}/blob/{versions[repo]}/{path}#L{line}',f'Precedent / rationale: {insp}',f'Primary source: {link}',f'Missing proof: {remain}']\\nlines += ['', 'ADDITIONAL SCOPE LIMITS',\\n'ENH-013: proposed sparse/shallow Git profiles are a public CLI contribution. Origin\\\\'s prebuilt CloneKit service is precedent for reducing setup cost, not a promised feature we can implement in Entire\\\\'s private forge. Server protocol support is unverified.',\\n'ENH-014 versus ENH-021: incremental review selects what reviewer execution covers; a revision-bound walkthrough presents grouped changes to humans. Their manifest/baseline plumbing may belong together. Do not manufacture two PRs for a single coherent implementation.',\\n'ENH-015: selected extraction of existing checkpoint assets, not a new storage backend, generic session handoff, or the already-reported web timeline rendering #2942. No Trail attachment download API is invented.',\\n'ENH-016: explain score contributions and exclusions rather than replacing the scorer. ENH-004 owns prepared-index/runtime changes and #595 owns typed provenance; coordinate their seams.',\\n'ENH-017: current logs emit nested durations but do not emit child start offsets. An accurate Perfetto export requires real span offsets/tracks; summing sibling durations into a pretend timeline is invalid. Keep default capture/outputs and no-egress behavior.',\\n'ENH-018: existing limits/truncation are not bugs by themselves. Need a large-hub pagination workflow and current #407 focused SQLite integration; do not claim its existing latency work.',\\n'ENH-019: ForgeMark already uses live histograms. The new proposal is saved, versioned, mergeable distributions for compatible repeated runs; preserve the current exact-percentile contract or negotiate an explicit approximate mode. It is not merely adding a live histogram.',\\n'ENH-020: current demo generates synthetic timing; proposed fault scenarios exercise actual Git protocol boundaries locally. Unit-test mocking already exists; reusable scenario/replay demand still needs validation. No paid or live remote load is authorized.',\\n'ENH-021: Entire already has repo onboarding code-tour skill PR skills#9 and CLI learn/tour work #1146. Proposed revision-bound change walkthrough is adjacent, not claimed cleared. Product fit and exact novelty need resolving before implementation.',\\n'ENH-022: an embedding consumer can already inject HTTPClient, so a standalone rate limiter may belong outside the core. Only proceed with a demonstrated CLI/SSH/multiple-request consistency need; lowest-priority design lead.',\\n'', 'REJECTED DURING THIS PASS',\\n'- Git Sync LFS mirroring: existing exact issue #59, excluded under the strict novelty rule.',\\n'- Graph worktree caching: existing exact issue #271 and adjacent #323/#397; excluded as a new contribution.',\\n'- ForgeMark threshold/monitor gates: open #6 and #14 already own them; excluded.',\\n'- ForgeMark retaining unlimited completed runs: disproved; keepFinishedRuns=20 and pruneLocked already bound it.',\\n'- Git Sync custom mapping prefix bug: disproved; arbitrary ref mappings require AllRefs, which requests refs/.',\\n'- Broad checkpoint listing filters: existing issue CLI#2718 and truncation issue #2089; not offered as a new feature.',\\n'- Dropped/parked ENH-005 through ENH-011 are not revived. No CI-failure-memory proposal.',\\n'', 'VALIDATION / REPRODUCTION',\\n'Logs: review-probes.log; git-sync-probes.log; feed-probe.log; sse-probe.log; follow-probe.log; stats-key-probe.json; installed-list-limit.txt.',\\n'Actual package tests ran uncached against the pinned source archives/isolated CLI clone. Brain feed reader and CLI followFile use verbatim function extractions in minimal packages, with source hashes in extracted-probes.json. They are not full command integrations. The SSE probe uses a controllably blocked ResponseWriter, not a real slow network client. Review relocation is a path-identity fixture, not an operating-system move of an active linked worktree.',\\n'Original commands are reproducible with GOMAXPROCS=2 and mise exec -- go test -p=1 -count=1 -run ^TestDiscovery -v on the indicated package. Do not run all real-agent E2E tests.',\\n'Brain and Graph installed version/capability preflight returns unknown command; pinned-source fallback used. No product installation/configuration was performed. Mise automatically downloaded pinned Go toolchains/dependencies for local probes.',\\n'Public inventories: 277 open CLI PR metadata records,26 Brain,14 Graph,5 Git Sync,7 ForgeMark,0 Entire Run. All-state keyword searches and selected related full discussions/inline reviews were retained in public/. Broad capped results are not exhaustive; there is no universal unclaimed/private-work assertion. New implementation requires the canonical tracker gates and a fresh refresh.',\\n'No production changes, commit, push, issue/PR publication, external messages, paid models or external forge load. Original CLI staging/config and other research owners preserved. All new artifacts and local instruction pointers stay out of upstream contributions.',\\n'', 'RECOMMENDED ORDER',\\n'Focused cleared fix: AUD-026. Next bug validations: AUD-024 then AUD-025 then AUD-032. Next enhancement validations: ENH-015, ENH-016, ENH-017; larger candidates ENH-013/014/018/020 need workload or integration proof first. Keep ENH-012 as the already-cleared image feature; do not count it among these ten new enhancements.']\\n(p/'REPORT.txt').write_text('\\\\n'.join(lines)+'\\\\n')\\nfiles=[x for x in p.rglob('*') if x.is_file() and (x.name.endswith('.log') or x.name in ['candidates.json','extracted-probes.json','stats-key-probe.json'])]\\n(p/'evidence-hashes.json').write_text(json.dumps({str(x.relative_to(p)):hashlib.sha256(x.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for x in files},indent=2)+'\\\\n')\\nprint('Saved 20-entry report, decisions, source links and evidence hashes.')\\nPY\",\"max_output_tokens\":150}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","create_time":1794842205.017109}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":551,"sampled_through_sequence":548,"client_authored":false}}
