{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T15:21:05.423Z","ordinal":3166,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"task_complete","root_turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","turn_id":"01a1e4cf-42fc-7bf1-b6f5-3fd32ae90631","last_agent_message":"I found **10 additional issue candidates and 10 enhancements**, covering small fixes and larger projects.\n\n**One small fix clears the scoped implementation gates.** Seven issue behaviors were reproduced through focused probes; several still need command-level validation or ownership clearance. The enhancements are source-backed candidates, with remaining checks recorded.\n\nCompetitor research helped identify useful directions: Origin’s [CloneKit](https://cursor.com/docs/origin/clonekit-ci) reduces checkout work, and [Code Tours](https://cursor.com/docs/origin/code-tours) support reviewing changes since the previous review. Code.Storage exposes [direct file reads](https://code.storage/docs/api/repos/file-get) and [isolated agent-state snapshots](https://code.storage/docs/guides/capture-agent-state). These suggest extensions we can evaluate in Entire’s public repos.\n\nHere are the **10 issue candidates**. “Reproduced” describes the observed behavior; **READY** means the scoped contribution gates passed.\n\n| ID | Issue | Size | Evidence / status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **AUD-024** | **CLI:** one malformed review manifest prevents reading otherwise healthy saved reviews. | Small | Reproduced. **HOLD:** recovery behavior and overlap checks. |\n| **AUD-025** | **Brain:** a corrupt feed record is skipped while its advanced cursor survives, potentially preventing recovery of that fact. | Medium | Current reader reproduced in isolation. **HOLD:** complete sync/recovery test; distinguish from the previously fixed missing-file case. |\n| **AUD-026** | **Git Sync:** URLs differing only by fragments bypass the same-repository guard, although HTTP requests reach the same resource. | Small | Validation and loopback HTTP probes passed. **READY within scoped checks.** |\n| **AUD-027** | **Git Sync:** impossible ref prefixes containing invalid characters pass validation. | Small | Reproduced. **HOLD:** distinguish this extension from earlier prefix-validation reports. |\n| **AUD-028** | **Graph:** replacing a transcript while preserving its size and timestamp can retain the same stats-cache key. | Small–medium | Key collision demonstrated. **HOLD:** actual stale-stat reproduction and freshness-contract review. |\n| **AUD-029** | **Brain:** workspace graph-generation probes use a background context rather than caller cancellation. | Medium | Source verified. **HOLD:** command-level cancellation test and coordination with our #644. |\n| **AUD-030** | **ForgeMark:** request cancellation cannot finish an SSE handler while its output write remains blocked. | Small–medium | Controlled blocked-writer probe. **HOLD:** real socket/backpressure validation. |\n| **AUD-031** | **CLI:** changing a checkout’s path hides saved review history because manifests retain its old absolute path. | Medium | Path-identity fixture reproduced. **HOLD:** actual relocation and linked-worktree tests. |\n| **AUD-032** | **CLI:** checkpoint-list truncation recommends `--limit`, but that command does not register the flag. | Small | Current source plus installed-command evidence. **HOLD:** fresh-source truncated-list fixture and final novelty checks. |\n| **AUD-033** | **CLI:** a continuously growing log can keep the follower inside its drain loop after cancellation. | Small | Verbatim-function probe reproduced continued processing. **HOLD:** command-level regression and ownership check. |\n\nThese are the **10 additional enhancement candidates**. All remain **HOLD** until their remaining need, compatibility and ownership checks pass.\n\n| ID | Enhancement | Size | Concrete value |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **ENH-013** | **Sparse/shallow clone profiles** | Large | Add explicit depth, blob filtering and sparse paths while retaining Entire’s authentication and cluster selection. Server support needs verification. |\n| **ENH-014** | **Incremental local reviews** | Medium–large | Review changes since a saved review baseline. Track committed and dirty-tree identity so rebases or edits cannot silently invalidate the baseline. |\n| **ENH-015** | **Checkpoint asset listing and selective extraction** | Small–medium | Retrieve one stored screenshot or asset without exporting and decoding an entire transcript. Include safe destinations, size bounds and integrity checks. |\n| **ENH-016** | **Explain Brain’s memory ranking** | Medium | Show term contributions, boosts, exclusions and family collapse so users can understand why a memory surfaced—or disappeared. Preserve existing ranking. |\n| **ENH-017** | **Accurate hook timelines with Perfetto export** | Medium | Extend existing performance traces with actual child-span offsets and concurrency information, making slow hooks easier to diagnose. |\n| **ENH-018** | **Snapshot-bound Graph pagination** | Medium–large | Fetch successive pages of large neighbor/impact results without repeating previous context. Reject cursors when the source snapshot changes. |\n| **ENH-019** | **Persist mergeable latency distributions in ForgeMark** | Medium | Save distributions that permit honest percentile calculations across compatible repeated runs. Live histograms already exist; this extends persisted results. |\n| **ENH-020** | **Deterministic Git-protocol fault scenarios** | Large | Exercise interrupted packs, delayed responses, connection resets and CAS interleavings through repeatable local scenarios and replayable seeds. |\n| **ENH-021** | **Revision-bound change walkthroughs** | Medium–large | Generate a walkthrough tied to an exact change range, with affected symbols and evidence. Entire already has onboarding tours, so differentiation and product fit need checking. |\n| **ENH-022** | **Transfer bandwidth and byte budgets in Git Sync** | Medium | Provide consistent, cancellation-aware limits for embedding services and CLI users. Lower priority until we establish a need beyond custom HTTP-client wrappers. |\n\n**My strongest next feature candidates are ENH-015, ENH-016 and ENH-017.** They extend existing capabilities with concrete inspection and debugging value. ENH-018 and ENH-020 offer larger engineering scopes.\n\nI excluded existing LFS requests, Graph working-tree caching reports, ForgeMark CI-gating proposals and previously dropped ideas. I also rejected two suspected bugs after source inspection disproved them.\n\nEverything is recorded in the [shared tracker](/Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli/CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md), with source links, duplicate checks, probe logs and remaining gates in the [full audit](/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/REPORT.txt). No production implementation or public submission was made.","started_at":1794840150,"completed_at":1794842465,"duration_ms":2314447,"time_to_first_token_ms":5033}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T17:30:22.825Z","ordinal":3167,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"thread_settings_applied","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","thread_settings":{"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","model_provider_id":"openai","service_tier":"default","approval_policy":"never","approvals_reviewer":"user","requested_approvals_reviewer":"user","permission_profile":{"type":"disabled"},"active_permission_profile":{"id":":danger-full-access"},"cwd":"/Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","runtime_workspace_roots":["/Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","/Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/dev/Shadowbox/shadowbox","/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/visualizations/2026/11/13/01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1"],"reasoning_effort":"high","reasoning_summary":"detailed","personality":"friendly","collaboration_mode":{"mode":"default","settings":{"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","reasoning_effort":"high","developer_instructions":"# Collaboration Mode: Default\n\nYou are now in Default mode. Any previous instructions for other modes (e.g. Plan mode) are no longer active.\n\nYour active mode changes only when new developer instructions with a different `<collaboration_mode>...</collaboration_mode>` change it; user requests or tool descriptions do not change mode by themselves. Known mode names are Default and Plan.\n\n## request_user_input availability\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only when it is listed in the available tools for this turn.\n\nIn Default mode, strongly prefer making reasonable assumptions and executing the user's request rather than stopping to ask questions.\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only for optional questions where the answer would materially improve the quality of the work.\n\nIf `request_user_input` returns no answers, continue with best judgment instead of asking again or treating the turn as blocked.\n\nNever use the `request_user_input` tool for permission requests or permission-related escalations.\n\nIf explicit user input is required for another reason before progress can safely continue, do not use the `request_user_input` tool. Ask the user directly with one concise plain-text question instead. Never write a multiple choice question as a textual assistant message.\n"}},"disabled_plugin_ids":[]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T17:30:22.864Z","ordinal":3168,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"task_started","turn_attribution":{"turn_id":"01a1ea8f-4eae-75f2-adec-faef107733f4","turn_trigger":"composer","parent_turn_id":null,"initiating_agent_path":null,"root_turn_id":"01a1ea8f-4eae-75f2-adec-faef107733f4"},"turn_id":"01a1ea8f-4eae-75f2-adec-faef107733f4","root_turn_id":"01a1ea8f-4eae-75f2-adec-faef107733f4","started_at":1794936622,"model_context_window":475000,"collaboration_mode_kind":"default"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T17:30:23.628Z","ordinal":3169,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a1ea8f-520a-7432-b7bf-8328743069a4","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"<skills_instructions>\n## Host skills update\n### Skill roots\nThese mappings replace earlier mappings for the same aliases.\n- `r12` = `/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime/spreadsheets/26.1116.12010/skills`\n### Added or updated skills:\n- documents:documents: Create, edit, redline, and comment on `.docx`, Word, and Google Docs-targeted document artifacts inside the container, with a strict render-and-verify workflow. Use `render_docx.py` to generate page PNGs (and optional PDF) for visual QA, then iterate until layout is flawless before delivering the final document. (file: r11/documents/26.1116.12010/skills/documents/SKILL.md)\n- pdf:pdf: Read, create, inspect, render, and verify PDF files where visual layout matters, including fillable AcroForms. Use Poppler rendering plus Python tools such as reportlab, pdfplumber, and pypdf for generation and extraction. (file: r11/pdf/26.1116.12010/skills/pdf/SKILL.md)\n- presentations:Presentations: Read, create or edit presentations. Default to Spaces; follow the routing rules for PowerPoint/PPT/PPTX, Google Slides, templates and existing decks. (file: r11/presentations/26.1116.12010/skills/presentations/SKILL.md)\n- spreadsheets:excel-live-control: Control an open or active Microsoft Excel workbook through the ChatGPT add-in or connected session. Use when the user tags the Microsoft Excel app in Codex or follows up on an established live Excel task. Do not use for standalone spreadsheet files or Google Sheets. (file: r12/excel-live-control/SKILL.md)\n- spreadsheets:Spreadsheets: Use skill when user requests to create, modify, analyze, visualize, or work with spreadsheet files (`.xlsx`, `.xls`, `.csv`, `.tsv`) or Google Sheets with formulas, formatting, charts, tables, and recalculation. Do not use for live controlling Microsoft Excel app or a live Excel session. (file: r12/spreadsheets/SKILL.md)\n- template-creator:template-creator: Create or update a reusable personal Codex artifact-template skill. Use when the user invokes $template-creator or asks in natural language to create a reusable template from a reference document, presentation, spreadsheet, Google Docs, Slides, or Sheets link, ImageGen or Product Design image, email, Slack message, or Site project, or explicitly asks to edit or update a passed artifact-template skill. Do not use for one-off creation from an existing template. (file: r11/template-creator/26.1116.12010/skills/template-creator/SKILL.md)\n</skills_instructions>"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1ea8f-4eae-75f2-adec-faef107733f4","create_time":1794936623.626575,"content_item_kinds":["host_skills.instructions"],"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"skills"}}]}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":563,"sampled_through_sequence":561,"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"complete","sources":[{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch","first_turn_id":"01a1d516-b0b4-7b12-a09f-1e60c17a3e14"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_repositories","first_turn_id":"01a1d51d-7680-7e10-a7bc-a9b5917a7d9c"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_issues","first_turn_id":"01a1d51d-7680-7e10-a7bc-a9b5917a7d9c"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_prs","first_turn_id":"01a1d51d-7680-7e10-a7bc-a9b5917a7d9c"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_file","first_turn_id":"01a1d51d-7680-7e10-a7bc-a9b5917a7d9c"},{"connector_id":