{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T17:30:42.539Z","ordinal":3180,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0b823400861c2c3d016afc8f40900087d09eff4162de17689c","status":"completed","call_id":"call_a14d497606b14557ad311e855c42bbc0","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat CLAUDE.md\",\"max_output_tokens\":8000}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"python3 - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\np=Path('CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md');s=p.read_text();print(s[:7000]);i=s.find('### Ten further issues and ten enhancements');print(s[i:] if i>=0 else s[-11000:])\\nPY\",\"max_output_tokens\":10500}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat /Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/candidates.json\",\"max_output_tokens\":9700}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1ea8f-4eae-75f2-adec-faef107733f4","create_time":1794936640.5670776}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":570,"sampled_through_sequence":568,"client_authored":false}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T17:30:42.585Z","ordinal":3181,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1ea8f-4eae-75f2-adec-faef107733f4","session_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","root_turn_id":"01a1ea8f-4eae-75f2-adec-faef107733f4","response_id":"resp_0b823400861c2c3d016afc8f32055887d08163528136ee395a","usage":{"input_tokens":386856,"cached_input_tokens":13056,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":214,"reasoning_output_tokens":0,"total_tokens":387070},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":386856,"cached_input_tokens":13056,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":214,"reasoning_output_tokens":0,"total_tokens":387070},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":57667277,"cached_input_tokens":55413120,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":221392,"reasoning_output_tokens":91042,"total_tokens":57888669}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T17:30:42.623Z","ordinal":3182,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1ea8f-4eae-75f2-adec-faef107733f4","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-36c44315-3c96-4653-9020-07c29df432ea","process_id":"17284","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat CLAUDE.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat CLAUDE.md","name":"CLAUDE.md","path":"CLAUDE.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Entire CLI — repository instructions\n\nGo CLI built with Cobra and Charmbracelet Huh. `AGENTS.md` is a symlink to this\nfile. Keep this entry point short: repo-wide rules and pointers, not command\ncatalogs, implementation histories, or subsystem specifications.\n\n## Project map\n\n- `cmd/entire/`: entry point and external-command dispatch.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/`: Cobra commands, group roots, and CLI helpers. Group/verb files\n  use `<noun>_group.go` and `<noun>_<verb>.go`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/`: built-in agent integrations and external-agent protocol.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/`: manual-commit strategy and lifecycle/git hooks.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/`: persistent checkpoint storage (written at commit).\n- `cmd/entire/cli/session/`: session state shared across worktrees.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/`: simulated-hook integration tests.\n- `e2e/`: real-agent tests and deterministic Vogon canary.\n- `internal/entireclient/`: API clients, authentication, and user directories.\n\nUse the Go version pinned by `go.mod` and tools configured in `mise.toml`.\nFor installed CLI usage, run `entire agent-help`, then\n`entire agent-help <command>` for current flags; do not guess from a static list.\n\n## Read when relevant\n\nRead the applicable reference **before changing that area**, not every reference\nat session start. Follow its related links when the task crosses those boundaries.\n\n| Area being changed | Reference |\n| --- | --- |\n| Commands, help, experimental visibility, repo refs, prompts | [CLI conventions](docs/development/cli-conventions.md) |\n| Test harnesses, isolation, TTY behavior, source guards | [Testing](docs/development/testing.md) |\n| Filesystem I/O, `.entire`, symlinks, hook configs, root anchors | [Filesystem safety](docs/development/filesystem-safety.md) |\n| Git operations, executable lookup, subprocesses, Windows launching | [Git and subprocess safety](docs/development/git-safety.md) |\n| Caller identification or session current/tokens/adopt | [Caller-session resolution](docs/development/caller-session-resolution.md) |\n| Control-plane auth or data-plane routing | [API routing](docs/development/api-routing.md) |\n| Checkpoint writes, lifecycle, sync, settings trust, redaction | [Implementation contracts](docs/development/checkpoint-implementation.md), [domain model](docs/architecture/sessions-and-checkpoints.md), [scenarios](docs/architecture/checkpoint-scenarios.md) |\n| Ref-based checkpoint backend | [Ref backend](docs/architecture/ref-checkpoint-backend.md) |\n| Agent integrations | [Agent guide](docs/architecture/agent-guide.md), [integration checklist](docs/architecture/agent-integration-checklist.md) |\n| External commands or agents | [External commands](docs/architecture/external-commands.md), [agent protocol](docs/architecture/external-agent-protocol.md) |\n| Security, privacy, scanners | [Security and privacy](docs/security-and-privacy.md), [implementation contracts](docs/development/checkpoint-implementation.md) |\n| Review command | [Review architecture](docs/architecture/review-command.md) |\n| Release artifacts, install scripts, version-check origins | [Release origins](docs/architecture/release-origins.md) |\n| E2E tests | [E2E guide](e2e/README.md) |\n| Complexity/coverage measurement and the CI complexity gate | [Complexity tooling](tools/complexity/README.md) |\n\n## Verification\n\n| Task | Command / requirement |\n| --- | --- |\n| Unit tests | `mise run test` |\n| Integration tests | `mise run test:integration`; required when changing integration test code |\n| Deterministic E2E canary | `mise run test:e2e:canary`; safe without API calls |\n| All CI tests | `mise run test:ci` (unit + integration + canary) |\n| Format and lint | `mise run fmt && mise run lint` |\n| Before every commit | **`mise run check`** (format, lint, all CI tests) |\n| Before any push or remote code update | **`mise run lint` on the current tree**, after the latest formatting pass |\n| After every push to an open PR | **check the trail's findings** (`entire trail finding list cli/<n> --freshness any`; `<n>` is the PR branch's cli trail number, not the PR number); fix real ones, resolve with `-m`, and re-check after the fix lands. Not done until findings are clear |\n| Duplication checks | `mise run dup` or `mise run dup:staged`; normal lint also checks duplication |\n| Complexity gate | `mise run complexity:gate`; CI fails a PR on functions over cognitive complexity 30 that are new or worsened against the merge base. The threshold is a gate flag (`COGNIT_WARN`), not a `.golangci.yaml` setting |\n| Windows installer | `mise run test:ps1`; see testing reference for prerequisites |\n\n**Do not run real-agent E2E tests unless the user explicitly requests them.** They\nmake paid API calls. Vogon is the exception: its canary is deterministic and free.\nWhen changing E2E prompt wording, run the canary and update Vogon's regex parsing\nif needed. Formatting can rewrite files; an earlier lint pass is not sufficient.\n\nBefore implementing Go code, search nearby packages and helpers for reusable\npatterns. Use `/go:discover-related` when available, otherwise `rg` and related\nimplementations/tests. Check `.golangci.yaml`; handle errors and avoid duplication.\n\n## Test safety\n\n- Every top-level test and subtest calls `t.Parallel()` unless it changes\n  process-global state (`t.Chdir`, `t.Setenv`, or their `os` equivalents).\n- Git tests use isolated temporary repositories, preferably\n  `testutil.InitRepo(t, dir)` plus its file/add/commit helpers. Redirect CWD before\n  calling CWD-based handlers. Never mutate the real checkout's git/session state.\n- Tests must not access the developer's real config, cache, or keychain.\n  In-process fallbacks are shared per process; use per-test overrides and\n  `tokenstore.UseFileBackendForTesting` when isolation between tests is needed.\n  Tests that can reach the OS keyring need `keyring.MockInit()` in `TestMain`.\n- Spawned binaries do not inherit Go's test detection. Harnesses must isolate\n  `ENTIRE_CONFIG_DIR`, `XDG_CACHE_HOME`, `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file`,\n  `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE_PATH`, and `ENTIRE_TEST_AUTH_STORE_FILE`.\n- Prefer `execx.NonInteractive` for real CLI/git test subprocesses so a developer's\n  terminal cannot make them prompt or hang.\n- Caller-resolution tests clear every variable from `agent.CallerSessionEnvVars()`;\n  never hand-maintain a partial list or inherit the developer's agent identity.\n- Source-scanning guards discover files through testutil's guard helpers\n  (`GitGrepGuard`, `GuardGoFiles`), restrict pathspecs to Go files, and fail on\n  zero matches. Do not weaken guard ledgers to silence failures.\n\n## Filesystem and settings safety\n\n**Use the existing anchor for each tree; never assemble a path and perform bare\nI/O beneath it.** Read the filesystem reference before adding or changing I/O.\n\n| Tree | Canonical owner |\n| --- | --- |\n| `.entire` | `entiredir` |\n| Git common directory | `gitdir` |\n| Working tree | `worktreedir` |\n| Agent hook configuration | `agent.HookConfigFile` |\n| Agent session store | `agent.SessionStore` |\n| Active git hooks directory | `strategy.hooksRootForInstall` / `ForRemoval` |\n| Per-user config/cache | `userdirs.ConfigRoot` / `CacheRoot` |\n| Managed plugins | `pluginRoot` |\n\n- Root bases come from trusted resolvers, **not `filepath.Dir(target)`**. Confining\n  a file to its own derived parent proves nothing. Prefer an existing anchor.\n- Roots share the `osroot.Shared` registry. Open child roots with\n  `osroot.SharedChild` / `OpenChild`, not bare `parent.OpenRoot`.\n- Use `osroot` operations and `jsonutil.WriteFileAtomicIn` / `CreateTempIn`.\n  Directories use `MkdirAllNoSymlink`; rooted read-only operations must also\n  enforce symlink policy. Atomic writes replace leaf links rather than follow them.\n- `.entire` must be a real directory; validate through\n  `paths.ValidateEntireDirAt` / `RequireEntireDir`. Do not treat an unresolved\n  repository as absent. Settings reads must also refuse symlinks themselves.\n- Do not broaden symlink exceptions. Developer-vouched agent config directories\n  are scoped, locally trusted exceptions; `.entire` and git hooks are not vouchable.\n- `entiredir.OpenForRead` must not create directories. Reset cached roots before\n  deleting/recreating their directories. Use `entiredir.Name` / `MustName` to\n  bridge repo-relative constants and root-relative I/O names.\n- All settings access goes through `settings`; never read or parse settings JSON\n  ad hoc. Per-user config/cache resolution belongs only to `userdirs`.\n- Repository-controlled settings must not authorize executable discovery, custom\n  executables, or instructions for permission-bypassed agents. Preserve the\n  existing local-provenance gates and their rejection reporting.\n- Existing exceptions (explicit user paths, global git config, transcript-read\n  protocol gaps) are documented in the references; do not generalize them.\n\n## Git and subprocess safety\n\n- Open repositories only through `gitrepo.OpenCurrent(ctx)` or\n  `gitrepo.OpenPath(root)`, never direct go-git opens. This preserves alternates\n  and reftable support. Do not fall back to CWD after failed repo resolution.\n- Use `gitrepo.Status`, never `worktree.Status()`. Agent-hook capture paths use\n  `StatusWithBudget` and preserve degraded-capture reporting on budget exhaustion.\n- Every `git status` subprocess passes **`--no-optional-locks`**. This does not\n  protect worktree-comparing `git diff` from refreshing the index; use the\n  hook-safe alternatives in the git reference.\n- Use the git CLI, not go-git v5, for checkout and hard reset; go-git can delete\n  ignored/untracked directories. This is an implementation rule, not permission\n  to run destructive git commands.\n- Git-relative paths resolve against `paths.WorktreeRoot`, never process CWD.\n- A git subprocess targeting a repository independently of the current hook must\n  use `gitrepo.EnvWithoutRepoOverrides()`; `Dir` or `-C` alone does not override\n  inherited selectors. Queries inspecting the commit Git is preparing must retain\n  the hook environment, including its temporary `GIT_INDEX_FILE`. Hook queries\n  reading only the hook's own refs or reflog may strip selectors and resolve from\n  `paths.WorktreeRoot`. User-invoked CWD commands also honor intentionally\n  exported repo selectors.\n- PATH scanners use `execx.PathScanDirs()`; external-agent execution requires\n  absolute binary paths. User-directory overrides use the checked `userdirs`\n  resolvers before any I/O.\n- When Entire owns execution, pass arguments separately; never interpolate\n  dynamic values into `cmd.exe`. Agent-owned shell execution uses the shared\n  escaping helper. See the reference for the literal-only Unix updater exception.\n\n## CLI behavior and output\n\n- Load settings through the `settings` package, not new helpers in CLI consumers.\n- Operational/debug messages use `logging.Debug/Info/Warn/Error`; user output uses\n  `cmd.OutOrStdout()` / `cmd.ErrOrStderr()`. Never log prompts, file contents, or\n  commit messages; log operational metadata only.\n- Cobra suppresses errors globally; `main.go` prints returned errors. Return\n  `NewSilentError(err)` only after printing a custom error yourself.\n- Every read-only workflow must work without a TUI: provide complete text/JSON,\n  stable IDs and detail commands, or direct selection flags. Test that path.\n- Use `uiform.New` (or `NewAccessibleForm` in `cli`) for Huh forms; these wire\n  accessibility and theming centrally. Do not hand-roll `WithAccessible`.\n- Separately opened prompt terminals use `interactive.OpenPromptTTY()` and\n  `PromptTTY.Close()`, not a bare file close (Windows pending reads can hang).\n- Register experimental commands with `experimental.Register`. Classify new\n  commands in `agentHelpClassification`; default to unlisted/user-owned and\n  flag the product choice for review. Agent guidance belongs in `agentHelpGuidance`,\n  not Cobra `Short`/`Long` or first-turn injection.\n\n## Session, checkpoint, and API contracts\n\n- `*strategy.ManualCommitStrategy` is the only strategy; there is no interface or\n  worktree restore path. Turn ends write session state only; checkpoints are\n  metadata refs written at commit, never working-branch commits. Log resume is distinct from restoring worktree files.\n- Caller identity comes from `strategy.ResolveCallerSession`, not newest state.\n  Preserve resolution provenance; do not narrate worktree fallback or ambiguous\n  matches as identified callers. `IsCaller()` excludes those guesses; consult\n  the caller-resolution reference for current enforcement gaps.\n- Preserve sanitize → image externalization → redact ordering where all apply,\n  fail-closed scanner behavior, and checkpoint-scoped token accounting. Read the\n  implementation contracts before modifying any transcript/storage pipeline.\n- Control-plane precedence belongs to `coreapi`; display `client.CoreOrigin()`\n  rather than independently resolving a possibly different target.\n- Repo-scoped data-plane requests resolve the repo's cell and fail on resolution\n  failure. `/me` uses the home cell; repo-set queries use shared fanout helpers.\n  Multi-cell operations share one `auth.CellClientFactory` per operation.\n\n## Maintaining these instructions\n\nUpdate the relevant reference when subsystem behavior changes. Update this file\nonly for repository-wide development rules or routing links. Preserve safety\ncontracts in references and regression tests rather than accumulating incident\nnarratives here. Prefer existing docs over a second account of the same behavior.\n\nThe root-file budget is **20 KiB**, enforced alongside local documentation links\nby `go test ./docs/development`. Extract specialized material instead of expanding\nthat budget. Do not require every linked document\nto be loaded on every task. Keep `AGENTS.md` as the symlink to this file.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":11250}},"started_at_ms":1794936642622,"completed_at_ms":1794936642623}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T17:30:42.803Z","ordinal":3183,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1ea8f-4eae-75f2-adec-faef107733f4","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-223eb872-0d56-46c4-b486-66263a0e5d99","process_id":"13721","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md');s=p.read_text();print(s[:7000]);i=s.find('### Ten further issues and ten enhancements');print(s[i:] if i>=0 else s[-11000:])\nPY"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md');s=p.read_text();print(s[:7000]);i=s.find('### Ten further issues and ten enhancements');print(s[i:] if i>=0 else s[-11000:])\nPY"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Entire contribution tracker\n\nPersonal, shared project record for Puneet's Entire contributions. Created 6 November 2026 from the earlier audits and our decisions. **Assembly date is not verification date.** Public statuses below are dated snapshots; recheck before starting work.\n\nCanonical file: `/Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli/CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md`.\nAll project chats and worktrees should read and update this file rather than maintain separate copies. This is local coordination material, excluded from Git; it is not part of the upstream contribution.\n\n## Start here\n\n| Priority | Local ID | Decision | Next action |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Scheduled priority 1 | AUD-019 | **IMPLEMENTED LOCALLY; pending baseline-test exception.** See the existing worker's final 6 November record. | Continue the same owner after required input; do not create another implementation chat. |\n| Scheduled priority 2 | AUD-020 | Cross-backend fallback returns the wrong session. **READY in scoped checks.** | Start only after priority 1 completes or fails a gate. |\n| Scheduled priority 3 | AUD-021 | Exact session cleanup plus linear stale sweep. **READY in scoped checks.** | Start only after prior queued work completes or fails a gate. |\n| Alternate target, outside scheduled batch | AUD-006 | Idle MCP server ignores cancellation; real CLI SIGTERM case reproduced. **READY** after scoped three-gate check. | Local fix in MCP shutdown chat/worktree; see cross-chat log and validation limits. |\n| Second verification target | AUD-009 | SSE cursor-only/reset failures reproduced; server contract still unverified. | **HOLD.** Verify practical contract before implementing. |\n| Focused fallback | AUD-005 | Failed bundle overwrites existing output; freshly reproduced. | **HOLD.** Useful focused fix, not a cleared senior flagship; novelty review incomplete. |\n| Existing contribution — review only | AUD-001 | Our replay fix is implemented; PR #3015 is still open and unmerged, verified 13 November. | Continue the existing PR. Do not open another issue or PR for it. |\n| Enhancement published; outside scheduled bug-fix batch | ENH-001 | Brain workspace retrieval: measured serial scaling and ignored cancellation. **CONTINUE OUR PR — #644**, 14 November. | [Issue #643](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/issues/643), [PR #644](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/644). Six checked commits; final memory target PASS (83.42 MiB peak). Remote CI awaits maintainer approval; trail findings unavailable. Existing bug-fix batch unchanged. |\n| Stop new work / duplicate risk | AUD-016 | Real, substantial bug, but **already reported exactly** in #2696's review. User also reports an existing PR. | Fails the novelty gate. Retain the record of Puneet's work; do not start another implementation. A separate exact fixing PR has not been independently identified. |\n| Hold — feature withdrawal proposed | AUD-017 | Cursor permission bug freshly reproduced at current upstream on 6 November. | Open #2615 proposes removing the entire affected package. Do not start before ownership/direction is resolved. |\n| Hold — feature withdrawal proposed | AUD-018 | Cursor attribution cost measured; code still present. | Open #2615 proposes removing the package. Do not start an optimization that conflicts with that work. |\n| Excluded | AUD-002 | User confirmed another contributor already has a summary-target PR. | Add the exact PR link when identified; do not pick it up as ours. |\n\n## Mandatory decision table — three gates before starting\n\n**User rule, 6 November 2026: start a new implementation only after all three gates pass.** Unknown, conditional, stale, or not checked does not mean pass. Previous words such as “candidate” or “available” in historical evidence below are not permission to start.\n\n1. **Legitimate:** reproduce a current failure against the intended contract, or measure a meaningful performance problem. An intentional behavior, hypothetical concern, or missing field alone does not pass.\n2. **Substantial / senior scope:** identify the actual engineering judgment involved: failure atomicity, concurrency, identity, privacy boundaries, scaling or lifecycle ownership. Assess the necessary solution, not an artificially enlarged patch. A useful focused fix can still fail our present flagship-selection goal; that says nothing about its author's seniority.\n3. **New and clear to work on:** check issues, all-state PRs, bodies, comments, inline review findings, prototypes, claims and relevant changed files. An existing exact report fails the user's strict new-issue requirement even if unfixed. An issue-only pickup requires an explicit later decision from the user. Adjacent work is not automatically an exact duplicate, but unresolved overlap is a hold.\n\nOnly **READY** means all three passed with dated evidence. **CONTINUE OUR PR** applies to work already published by us; it is not a new-work approval. **HOLD** permits research/verification, not a production implementation. **SKIP** records a failed gate. The latest deep pass cleared **AUD-019, AUD-020 and AUD-021** as the scheduled three-item queue, subject to fresh gate checks. AUD-006 is an alternate previously cleared target, not one of this batch’s three. AUD-009 and AUD-005 remain held.\n\nLatest deep-audit upstream: `aa0c90c9770a460092103214b608247a8b2623ae`, 6 November 2026. The earlier gate pass used `3c299b94f8595bdfc3aa2ecdc0bd199d856f15a2`. The older evidence retains its original dates; this pass did not rerun every historical reproduction.\n\n| ID / finding | 1. Legitimate issue? | 2. Substantial senior scope? | 3. New / already raised or worked on? | Decision / missing proof |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| AUD-001 — replay loses sessions | **PASS:** reproduced; our fix already exists. | **PASS:** cross-clone identity, checked merge, queue/CAS safety. | **EXISTING OUR WORK:** [#3014](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/3014), [#3015](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3015), still open on 6 November. | **CONTINUE OUR PR.** No duplicate issue/PR. |\n| AUD-002 — summary targets another session | **PASS on 3 November:** deterministic reproduction; not refreshed today. | **PASS in scoped design:** source identity and concurrent storage update. | **FAIL:** user confirmed somebody else's PR; exact link still unknown. | **SKIP.** Do not override the user's ownership correction because a search is inconclusive. |\n| AUD-003 — runner tailoring overwrite | **FAIL as current candidate:** feature removed. | Not evaluated further. | **FAIL:** merged [#2946](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2946) removed the feature. | **SKIP — obsolete.** |\n| AUD-004 — staged filename corruption | **PENDING:** older audit; affected file unchanged through current upstream. No fresh runtime test today. | **FOCUSED:** parser/filename fidelity; no demonstrated wider design problem. | **NOT CLEARED:** no exact match in targeted searches; [#1573 review](https://g\n### Ten further issues and ten enhancements — competitor-informed discovery, 16 November 2026\n\n- User requests ten more issues and ten enhancements, explicitly including big and small tasks, with Code.Storage and Cursor Origin research. This broadens discovery sizes; it does not waive the three implementation gates, duplicate exclusions or other owners. No production implementation/publication is authorized by this discovery request. Research owner: this workflow-discovery chat; isolated archives/probes under `/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/` plus the existing owned CLI audit clone. Canonical tracker remains here; local pointers carried forward; existing CLI staging/config/symlink and ENH-004 implementation owner preserved.\n- Exact sources: CLI76f1b512, Brain12e1b0d9, Graph3f632e40, GitSync67dd3a4e, ForgeMark654e95a1. Full revisions in candidates.json. Installed Brain/Graph still unknown commands: source fallback disclosed. Public refresh:277 open CLI PR metadata,26 Brain,14 Graph,5 GitSync,7 ForgeMark; targeted all-state search results and selected related bodies/inline discussions/submissions retained. Broad capped queries are not exhaustive ownership clearance.\n- **AUD-026 READY as a focused scope in documented public checks.** Gate1 PASS: current endpoint guard and public SyncRequest validation accept fragment-only aliases, while actual loopback HTTP requests target the same `/repo.git`; direct identical-endpoint control rejects. Gate2 PASS for the minimum HTTP repository-identity normalization fix and regression matrix, not a large security redesign or a demonstrated destructive mirror incident. Gate3 scoped PASS: fragment/endpoint all-state searches, five open PR metadata records,27 upstream branch names, source history and related #18/#108/#122/#124 full discussions/reviews. #18 reports a different trailing-slash bypass. No exact fragment report/claim found. Refresh before implementation, record owner/worktree/base, and follow required checks. No production fix yet.\n- **Other19 entries are HOLD.** Seven distinct current behaviors have direct/fixture/verbatim-function probes; this does not certify seven complete bugs or all production workflows. stats-key-probe.json demonstrates key equality only. Brain workspace Graph cancellation is source-only. Broken checkpoint-list --limit advice has current source and installed binary proof, not a fresh built-source truncated-list fixture. User-requested count is a discovery inventory, not20 new unclaimed or implementation-ready PRs.\n\n| ID | New issue candidate | Size | Evidence / remaining clearance |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| AUD-024 | CLI: one malformed review manifest blocks healthy saved reviews | S | **HOLD**; REPRODUCED. Need corrupt-entry reporting/recovery contract and final ownership clearance around #2996. |\n| AUD-025 | Brain: corrupt feed record keeps a cursor that skips its recovery | M | **HOLD**; FUNCTION PROBE. Complete sync/recovery reproduction and distinguish from #403's exact missing-file report; do not claim that already-fixed defect. |\n| AUD-026 | Git Sync: fragment-only URL differences bypass same-repository guard | S | **READY — focused, scoped public check**; REPRODUCED. Scoped gates PASS: current contract reproduction; minimal HTTP URL identity fix; no exact fragment report in all-state searches, related #18/#108/#122/#124 reviews, five open PR metadata and27 branch names. #18 reports a different trailing-slash case. Refresh immediately before a task-owned implementation; no public reservation. |\n| AUD-027 | Git Sync: impossible include prefixes pass request validation | S | **HOLD**; REPRODUCED. Check prefix grammar permits legitimate partial names; review equivalent independent-history-prefix validation in one scope; final novelty clearance. Source commit a81db6 already reports blank/outside-refs prefixes; character-validity cases must not be represented as that old report. Strict novelty of this extension remains HOLD. |\n| AUD-028 | Graph: same-size, same-mtime transcript replacement can reuse stale stats | S/M | **HOLD**; SOURCE LEAD. Need actual stats CLI reproduction and establish intended freshness/performance contract. Existing metadata cache design is documented, so this is not a certified bug. |\n| AUD-029 | Brain: workspace graph-generation probes discard caller cancellation | M | **HOLD**; SOURCE LEAD. Need cancellation reproduction at the public graph command and coordination with #644; do not duplicate its query/search worker work. |\n| AUD-030 | ForgeMark: blocked SSE output outlives request cancellation | S/M | **HOLD**; BLOCKED-WRITER PROBE. Need real socket/backpressure/shutdown test and write-deadline contract; custom writer mechanism is not a production incident. |\n| AUD-031 | CLI: moved checkout path hides existing local review history | M | **HOLD**; IDENTITY FIXTURE. Need actual checkout relocation/worktree identity matrix and #2996 integration clearance. This is read-time history filtering, not that PR's missing-session capture fix. |\n| AUD-032 | CLI: checkpoint list truncation recommends an unavailable --limit flag | S | **HOLD**; SOURCE + INSTALLED COMMAND. Need current-source command fixture with a truncated result and finish novelty checks around #1768/#2089; installed binary alone is not exact-revision proof. |\n| AUD-033 | CLI: busy log follower ignores cancellation inside its drain loop | S | **HOLD**; VERBATIM FUNCTION PROBE. Need command-level cancellation regression and fresh ownership. Separate from AUD-007's copy-truncation case; do not count that old issue again. |\n\n| ID | Additional enhancement | Size | Scope / next gate |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ENH-013 | CLI: sparse/shallow clone profiles | L | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Explicit depth, blob filtering and sparse paths while retaining Entire cluster selection/auth. Validate supported server protocol; do not promise a hosted CloneKit service. Next: Server filter/depth support, representative monorepo savings and final novelty clearance. |\n| ENH-014 | CLI: incremental review since a saved review baseline | M/L | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Persist reviewed commit/tree/dirty-state identity and explicitly review only the new range, retaining dependency context. Refuse stale/rebased baselines. Next: Need scope correctness on uncommitted work and integration with exact-scope PR #1647 and persistence PR #2996. |\n| ENH-015 | CLI: checkpoint asset list and selective extraction | S/M | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Expose stored asset metadata and export a selected binary without dumping/reinjecting an entire transcript; byte bounds, hash checks and safe explicit destinations. Next: Need supported-agent storage/restore matrix and public novelty clearance; not the already-reported entire.com image timeline #2942. |\n| ENH-016 | Brain: explain memory ranking and exclusions | M | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Opt-in deterministic trace of term contributions, corpus scope, locus/recency/negative boosts, filtered candidates and family collapse. Preserve scores/output defaults. Next: Need representative confusing query, exact score decomposition and separation from #595 provenance / #335 packet presentation. |\n| ENH-017 | CLI: accurate hook timelines and Perfetto export | M | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Retain relative child start times and export local trace events with correct overlap, IDs and bounded size. Existing durations alone cannot reconstruct overlapping spans honestly. Next: Need measured diagnostic need/overhead and completed review/claim clearance; existing doctor trace JSON is already shipped. |\n| ENH-018 | Graph: snapshot-bound pagination for large neighbor/impact results | M/L | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Opaque continuation pinned to source snapshot, symbol, relation filters and ordering; reject stale cursors. Fetch the next page without repeating earlier context. Next: Need existing truncation semantics and large-hub workload; coordinate focused SQLite read PR #407 rather than copying its implementation. |\n| ENH-019 | ForgeMark: persist mergeable latency distributions | M | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Versioned mergeable histogram metadata for compatible repeated runs; recompute percentiles honestly and bound retained samples, with documented precision/error. Next: Need memory measurements, compatible-run rules and preserve exact-percentile behavior; not duplicate CI threshold PRs #6/#14. |\n| ENH-020 | ForgeMark: deterministic Git protocol fault scenarios | L | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Opt-in local scenario harness for bounded delays, interrupted packs, reset/retry and stale-ref/CAS interleavings, with seed, injection schedule and recovery assertions. Next: Need maintainer agreement on harness scope and a real uncovered recovery case. Current demo simulation and transport tests are not this operator-facing scenario mode. |\n| ENH-021 | Graph/CLI: revision-bound change walkthrough artifacts | M/L | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Read-only report groups changed symbols, callers/tests and checkpoint rationale at fixed base/head revisions; incomplete edges remain disclosed. Start with deterministic structured/text output. Next: Product-fit/ownership HOLD: Entire already has skills #9 code-tour for onboarding and CLI #1146 learn. Must establish a distinct change-review outcome before implementation. |\n| ENH-022 | Git Sync: cancel-aware transfer bandwidth budgets | M | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Optional upload/download byte-rate budgets over relay and materialized paths, with progress distinguishing throttling from network wait. Keep defaults unchanged and cancellation prompt. Next: Need a real shared-runner/network constraint and show why existing injected HTTP client cannot sufficiently solve it. Lowest-confidence product-need candidate. |\n\n- Competitor evidence: Code.Storage direct file reads, ephemeral agent-state refs and parallel attempts; Origin CloneKit and changes-since-last-review tours. Inspiration is not proof of Entire feature absence or need. Hosted server capabilities are not assumed publicly contributable. ENH-017 requires real child-span timestamps/offsets before exporting a timeline; never invent timings by summing durations. ENH-019 extends persisted distributions; live histograms already exist. ENH-022 is lower-priority until a need beyond injected HTTP-client rate limiting is proven. ENH-014/021 may share one coherent baseline scope; do not split PRs to satisfy a count.\n- Exclusions retained: GitSync LFS is existing issue#59; Graph working-tree caching is existing issue#271; ForgeMark CI gates already have PR#6/#14; code-tour onboarding already has skills#9 and CLI learn#1146 (ENH-021 therefore remains adjacent/HOLD). CLI checkpoint filters already have issue#2718; not offered again. Unlimited ForgeMark finished-run retention and GitSync custom-ref mapping prefix failure were disproved in source. AUD-027 extends the character-validity question beyond source commit a81db6's existing blank/outside-refs report; strict novelty remains HOLD. No ENH-009 CI memory revival, no ENH-004 or ENH-012 duplication.\n- Validation PASS: nine focused observation test functions across actual review/GitSync/ForgeMark packages and the two verbatim-function probes; no full repository check, paid model, live forge load or production incident claimed. Brain cache reader and doctor followFile extracted unchanged with hashes; SSE uses a controlled blocking writer; moved-review case is a path identity fixture. Ordinary pinned Go toolchain/dependency downloads occurred through mise. No production edits, commits, pushes, public issues/PRs or outreach. Evidence/limits/commands/source URLs and ranked next work in `REPORT.txt`, `candidates.json`, `evidence-hashes.json`, probe logs and `public/` under the evidence directory. Baseline probe PASS is not a fix.\n\n\n### ENH-004 implementation convergence and stronger crash proof — 16 November 2026\n\n- All gates remain PASS for the same local prepared-data-only scope/worktree. Fresh canonical decoding remains authoritative. Final source now uses compact prepared metadata with fresh full-record signatures by ordinal; full ordered source digest + SQL source/count + committed DB SHA provide the binding. Redundant persisted signatures and a slower reflection experiment were removed. Controlled builder comparison chose simpler individual prepared inserts (140.0ms vs194.2ms/128-row batch, +13.8% cumulative allocated bytes in that isolated build test); no batching abstraction remains.\n- Executable crossover probes justify a conservative runtime scanner bypass: selected text <64KiB or <75% of full source text avoids cache I/O. Tiny44/128 stores had negligible/negative warm value;512/1k stores improved. Public branch probes showed real regressions for small selected subsets, but75%/90% selections improved. Forced-index oracle/phase tests remain separate so bypass cannot make differential tests vacuous. Dedicated runtime tests prove bypass leaves cache untouched and preserve results.\n- A newly added same-source publication regression FAILED before fix with `same-source failed publication lost the committed generation: fact index database failed its committed digest`. Fixed with immutable `<sourceSHA>-<databaseSHA>.sqlite` blobs and descriptor-last atomic commit. Old referenced blobs remain until new descriptor sync. Direct regression and same/changed-source SIGKILL at both publication boundaries now PASS; uncertainty/unsafe I/O prevents pruning.\n- Main-based and separate#644-combined focused suites PASS after convergence. Three compiling negative controls and actual poisoned-tokenizer CLI reuse proof PASS (latest filename/policy final rerun still pending). Current full5-binary/7-sample latency/RSS/disk/build/rebuild/write matrix is running in `final-cli-v2`; final small/filter/fallback comparisons and exact-tree `mise run check`, pinned Graph integration and released-client checks remain. No commit/publication yet; do not describe final performance acceptance as complete.\n- Local disk pressure required removing only this task's obsolete feasibility/proof executables and reproducible v1 large fixtures; SHA manifests/raw measurements/source recipes retained. Current five CLI comparison binaries, both owner checkouts, their history/work and shared caches remain untouched.\n\n\n### Private review of existing OpenCode-created PRs #3174 / #3175 — 17 November 2026\n\n- User asks whether to refine or close these two already-published contributions. Review only; no implementation, remote comments/reviews, closure or push authorized/inferred. Both live connector snapshots OPEN/unmerged under Puneet-Pal-Singh: #3174 at `83fa5560a274d1e967e30670d9f604cb43834129`, #3175 at `8a9ee8ccdb99d9a3d850ce94bab33c773c0f8c7c`; shared base `76f1b5129b974afdf8e59e4ae3755083c10ff8ff`. No submitted reviews/discussion/inline threads returned. Only listed check for each is skipped Entire Gates; no full-CI success established.\n- **Recommendation: KEEP / REFINE both existing PRs, #3174 first.** Useful focused contributions, not two cleared new senior flagship implementations. Original committed regressions independently FAIL against shared-base production files and PASS with respective patches. Focused review/transcript/internal-transcript suites PASS in isolated source archive combining disjoint changes. No full `mise run check`/lint rerun here; PR bodies evidence focused tests plus lint:go, not required complete verification.\n- **#3174 confirmed refinement:** cmd.Start failure closes owned stderr reader but leaks writer. Deterministic audit checks cmd.Stderr file after failed Start: Stat succeeds instead of os.ErrClosed. Close writer on every failure and cover cleanup/diagnostics. Existing inherited-stderr test proves redirected-stdout case, not arbitrary stdout inheritance. Necessary lifecycle fix appears sound enough to retain.\n- **#3175 confirmed synthetic coverage gap:** assistant with no content, input/output=0 and cache.read=50/cache.write=20 converts to no line; existing content eligibility still checks input/output only. This omission predates PR, but conflicts with its broader cache-retention objective. Native occurrence/frequency unverified; no production incident claim. Retain cache/model mapping, extend eligibility/tests and cover normalized-v2/streaming usage. #2823 fixes checkpoint CalculateTokenUsage, a different consumer; base already contains the accounting helper. #2155/#2767 are adjacent. Scoped searches/relevant inline reviews did not establish an exact converter duplicate; full strict novelty clearance remains UNKNOWN/HOLD, not READY.\n- This chat owns audit-only evidence `/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-pr-review-2026-11-17/review.txt` and probes; disposable source archive `/private/tmp/entire-pr3174-3175-review`. No contribution implementation owner assigned or existing queue changed. Preserve main staged replay work/config/AGENTS symlink and OpenCode worktrees. Separate `opencode_tracker.md` is evidence only: its instruction to ignore this canonical tracker does not override user coordination rules. No production changes, commit, push, public message/review or PR state change made.\n\n\n### Existing PR refinement authorized — 17 November 2026\n\n- User explicitly requests refining code/tests/title/body of #3174 and #3175 only if legitimate. Continue existing contributions; no new PR or issue. Same review chat now owns refinements, serially, starting #3174. Worktree `Entire/cli-pr3174`, branch `refine/pr3174`, base published head83fa5560a; intended fast-forward destination `fix/review-wait-inherited-stderr`. Main replay staging/config and existing OpenCode worktree preserved. #3175 remains unchanged at8a9ee8ccd until its refinement stage.\n- Current upstream main unchanged76f1b512. Legitimacy PASS from independent red/green proofs at this exact source; lifecycle ownership/bounded draining and version-sensitive transcript accounting justify necessary focused engineering scope. These are useful focused scopes, not flagship size claims. Public inventory refreshed: all288open PRs and complete changed-file pages. Only adjacent overlaps #3129 (tool-error text) and #2683 (legacy/project model refactor); inspected actual patches differ from these fixes. All-state targeted searches, source-history PR discussion/inline reviews and current relevant plans reviewed. #1559/#1561/#3052/#3102 cover cancelled processes/Windows tree termination, not a normal-exit stderr drain; #2834's shipped field-reader/followups #2858/#2859 cover Claude/Codex conversion, not a claimed OpenCode converter patch. #2823/#2155/#2767 concern checkpoint/session accounting, distinct consumer. Scoped novelty/ownership PASS for continuing our published PRs, private work unknown; retain original attribution and no first-discovery claim. Evidence in `entire-pr-review-2026-11-17/public`. No new contribution gate bypass or permission to ignore checks/baseline policy.\n- Stage: ownership recorded before production refinements; required per-PR exact-tree check before commit, latest fmt/lint before push, verified trail lookup/findings after push. No blanket exception for baseline failures inferred.\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":10375}},"started_at_ms":1794936642803,"completed_at_ms":1794936642803}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T17:30:42.906Z","ordinal":3184,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1ea8f-4eae-75f2-adec-faef107733f4","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-bd21b9e9-1336-4081-9790-94b2351fc5d0","process_id":"73318","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat /Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/candidates.json"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat /Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/candidates.json","name":"candidates.json","path":"/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/candidates.json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"date\": \"2026-11-16\",\n  \"scope\": \"Discovery only. All new entries HOLD; small scopes requested, but no gate waived. No production implementation or publication.\",\n  \"revisions\": {\n    \"cli\": \"76f1b5129b974afdf8e59e4ae3755083c10ff8ff\",\n    \"brain\": \"12e1b0d95a078cf4b57c3c8b38bc0aeec4fb9a55\",\n    \"graph\": \"3f632e403e6bd70ac015f3a80980ca39e4dadd0d\",\n    \"git_sync\": \"67dd3a4e083e4faae4417c1849035c7c4638112c\",\n    \"forgemark\": \"654e95a18db7ad690165b519eb151ecc4fc1e2f0\"\n  },\n  \"bug_columns\": [\n    \"id\",\n    \"title\",\n    \"size\",\n    \"repo\",\n    \"file\",\n    \"line\",\n    \"evidence\",\n    \"observation\",\n    \"remaining_gate\",\n    \"log\"\n  ],\n  \"bugs\": [\n    [\n      \"AUD-024\",\n      \"CLI: one malformed review manifest blocks healthy saved reviews\",\n      \"S\",\n      \"cli\",\n      \"cmd/entire/cli/review/manifest.go\",\n      725,\n      \"REPRODUCED\",\n      \"A valid saved review plus broken.json makes loadLocalReviewManifests return an error before any findings are served.\",\n      \"Need corrupt-entry reporting/recovery contract and final ownership clearance around #2996.\",\n      \"review-probes.log\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"AUD-025\",\n      \"Brain: corrupt feed record keeps a cursor that skips its recovery\",\n      \"M\",\n      \"entire-brain\",\n      \"internal/cli/hosted_feed_cache.go\",\n      55,\n      \"FUNCTION PROBE\",\n      \"Verbatim current reader skips malformed records and returns cursor-7 with a partial map and no error.\",\n      \"Complete sync/recovery reproduction and distinguish from #403's exact missing-file report; do not claim that already-fixed defect.\",\n      \"feed-probe.log\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"AUD-026\",\n      \"Git Sync: fragment-only URL differences bypass same-repository guard\",\n      \"S\",\n      \"git-sync\",\n      \"internal/validation/validation.go\",\n      61,\n      \"REPRODUCED\",\n      \"Direct validation and public SyncRequest validation accept fragment-only aliases; two real loopback HTTP GETs reached the identical /repo.git resource. Exact fragment-free guard control rejects equal endpoints.\",\n      \"Scoped gates PASS: current contract reproduction; minimal HTTP URL identity fix; no exact fragment report in all-state searches, related #18/#108/#122/#124 reviews, five open PR metadata and27 branch names. #18 reports a different trailing-slash case. Refresh immediately before a task-owned implementation; no public reservation.\",\n      \"git-sync-probes.log\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"AUD-027\",\n      \"Git Sync: impossible include prefixes pass request validation\",\n      \"S\",\n      \"git-sync\",\n      \"internal/validation/validation.go\",\n      15,\n      \"REPRODUCED\",\n      \"refs/../, refs/heads/a[, whitespace and backslash prefixes pass; git check-ref-format rejects their extended names.\",\n      \"Check prefix grammar permits legitimate partial names; review equivalent independent-history-prefix validation in one scope; final novelty clearance. Source commit a81db6 already reports blank/outside-refs prefixes; character-validity cases must not be represented as that old report. Strict novelty of this extension remains HOLD.\",\n      \"git-sync-probes.log\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"AUD-028\",\n      \"Graph: same-size, same-mtime transcript replacement can reuse stale stats\",\n      \"S/M\",\n      \"entire-graph\",\n      \"internal/cli/stats_cache.go\",\n      139,\n      \"SOURCE LEAD\",\n      \"Memo key includes resolved path, size and mtime, but no content revision; a timestamp-preserving rewrite can have the same key.\",\n      \"Need actual stats CLI reproduction and establish intended freshness/performance contract. Existing metadata cache design is documented, so this is not a certified bug.\",\n      \"stats-key-probe.json\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"AUD-029\",\n      \"Brain: workspace graph-generation probes discard caller cancellation\",\n      \"M\",\n      \"entire-brain\",\n      \"internal/cli/workspace.go\",\n      2167,\n      \"SOURCE LEAD\",\n      \"workspaceGraphGeneration has no context parameter and fetches each member Graph store with context.Background and a real ExecRunner.\",\n      \"Need cancellation reproduction at the public graph command and coordination with #644; do not duplicate its query/search worker work.\",\n      \"\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"AUD-030\",\n      \"ForgeMark: blocked SSE output outlives request cancellation\",\n      \"S/M\",\n      \"forgemark\",\n      \"internal/server/events.go\",\n      136,\n      \"BLOCKED-WRITER PROBE\",\n      \"Cancelling request context while replay Write is blocked does not finish handler until the writer is released.\",\n      \"Need real socket/backpressure/shutdown test and write-deadline contract; custom writer mechanism is not a production incident.\",\n      \"sse-probe.log\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"AUD-031\",\n      \"CLI: moved checkout path hides existing local review history\",\n      \"M\",\n      \"cli\",\n      \"cmd/entire/cli/review/manifest.go\",\n      751,\n      \"IDENTITY FIXTURE\",\n      \"Same common-dir review store returns one manifest for saved path and zero for current moved path.\",\n      \"Need actual checkout relocation/worktree identity matrix and #2996 integration clearance. This is read-time history filtering, not that PR's missing-session capture fix.\",\n      \"review-probes.log\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"AUD-032\",\n      \"CLI: checkpoint list truncation recommends an unavailable --limit flag\",\n      \"S\",\n      \"cli\",\n      \"cmd/entire/cli/explain_export.go\",\n      875,\n      \"SOURCE + INSTALLED COMMAND\",\n      \"Current list registers no --limit; runExplainListJSON truncation note recommends it. Installed command exits unknown flag: --limit.\",\n      \"Need current-source command fixture with a truncated result and finish novelty checks around #1768/#2089; installed binary alone is not exact-revision proof.\",\n      \"installed-list-limit.txt\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"AUD-033\",\n      \"CLI: busy log follower ignores cancellation inside its drain loop\",\n      \"S\",\n      \"cli\",\n      \"cmd/entire/cli/doctor_logs.go\",\n      124,\n      \"VERBATIM FUNCTION PROBE\",\n      \"A continuously appended temporary log kept processing 24 writes after cancellation; stopping writer let cleanup finish.\",\n      \"Need command-level cancellation regression and fresh ownership. Separate from AUD-007's copy-truncation case; do not count that old issue again.\",\n      \"follow-probe.log\"\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"feature_columns\": [\n    \"id\",\n    \"title\",\n    \"size\",\n    \"repo\",\n    \"file\",\n    \"line\",\n    \"scope\",\n    \"inspiration\",\n    \"primary_link\",\n    \"remaining_gate\"\n  ],\n  \"features\": [\n    [\n      \"ENH-013\",\n      \"CLI: sparse/shallow clone profiles\",\n      \"L\",\n      \"cli\",\n      \"cmd/entire/cli/repo_clone.go\",\n      1021,\n      \"Explicit depth, blob filtering and sparse paths while retaining Entire cluster selection/auth. Validate supported server protocol; do not promise a hosted CloneKit service.\",\n      \"Origin CloneKit and Code.Storage's selected-file reads suggest minimizing cold-start transfer.\",\n      \"https://cursor.com/docs/origin/clonekit-ci\",\n      \"Server filter/depth support, representative monorepo savings and final novelty clearance.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"ENH-014\",\n      \"CLI: incremental review since a saved review baseline\",\n      \"M/L\",\n      \"cli\",\n      \"cmd/entire/cli/review/manifest.go\",\n      40,\n      \"Persist reviewed commit/tree/dirty-state identity and explicitly review only the new range, retaining dependency context. Refuse stale/rebased baselines.\",\n      \"Origin supports reviewing changes since the last review; this proposal concerns local reviewer execution, not adding more agents.\",\n      \"https://cursor.com/docs/origin/code-tours\",\n      \"Need scope correctness on uncommitted work and integration with exact-scope PR #1647 and persistence PR #2996.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"ENH-015\",\n      \"CLI: checkpoint asset list and selective extraction\",\n      \"S/M\",\n      \"cli\",\n      \"cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/persistent.go\",\n      1850,\n      \"Expose stored asset metadata and export a selected binary without dumping/reinjecting an entire transcript; byte bounds, hash checks and safe explicit destinations.\",\n      \"Code.Storage treats generated artifacts as first-class files with direct reads.\",\n      \"https://code.storage/docs/api/repos/file-get\",\n      \"Need supported-agent storage/restore matrix and public novelty clearance; not the already-reported entire.com image timeline #2942.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"ENH-016\",\n      \"Brain: explain memory ranking and exclusions\",\n      \"M\",\n      \"entire-brain\",\n      \"internal/cli/facts_bm25.go\",\n      1,\n      \"Opt-in deterministic trace of term contributions, corpus scope, locus/recency/negative boosts, filtered candidates and family collapse. Preserve scores/output defaults.\",\n      \"Useful debugging surface for a memory product; not a new embedding backend or ENH-004 index.\",\n      \"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain\",\n      \"Need representative confusing query, exact score decomposition and separation from #595 provenance / #335 packet presentation.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"ENH-017\",\n      \"CLI: accurate hook timelines and Perfetto export\",\n      \"M\",\n      \"cli\",\n      \"perf/span.go\",\n      149,\n      \"Retain relative child start times and export local trace events with correct overlap, IDs and bounded size. Existing durations alone cannot reconstruct overlapping spans honestly.\",\n      \"Code.Storage advertises telemetry; Perfetto supports custom timestamped trace imports.\",\n      \"https://perfetto.dev/docs/getting-started/other-formats\",\n      \"Need measured diagnostic need/overhead and completed review/claim clearance; existing doctor trace JSON is already shipped.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"ENH-018\",\n      \"Graph: snapshot-bound pagination for large neighbor/impact results\",\n      \"M/L\",\n      \"entire-graph\",\n      \"internal/cli/neighbors.go\",\n      219,\n      \"Opaque continuation pinned to source snapshot, symbol, relation filters and ordering; reject stale cursors. Fetch the next page without repeating earlier context.\",\n      \"Code.Storage exposes cursor-paginated repository reads; the same interaction helps large graph hubs.\",\n      \"https://code.storage/docs/api/repos/grep\",\n      \"Need existing truncation semantics and large-hub workload; coordinate focused SQLite read PR #407 rather than copying its implementation.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"ENH-019\",\n      \"ForgeMark: persist mergeable latency distributions\",\n      \"M\",\n      \"forgemark\",\n      \"internal/bench/stats.go\",\n      66,\n      \"Versioned mergeable histogram metadata for compatible repeated runs; recompute percentiles honestly and bound retained samples, with documented precision/error.\",\n      \"A benchmark harness improvement: current live collector has histograms, while saved LevelResult contains scalar percentiles.\",\n      \"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark\",\n      \"Need memory measurements, compatible-run rules and preserve exact-percentile behavior; not duplicate CI threshold PRs #6/#14.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"ENH-020\",\n      \"ForgeMark: deterministic Git protocol fault scenarios\",\n      \"L\",\n      \"forgemark\",\n      \"internal/bench/runner.go\",\n      1,\n      \"Opt-in local scenario harness for bounded delays, interrupted packs, reset/retry and stale-ref/CAS interleavings, with seed, injection schedule and recovery assertions.\",\n      \"Code.Storage's concurrent agent writes make correctness under controlled disruption worth testing alongside throughput.\",\n      \"https://code.storage/docs/guides/parallel-attempts\",\n      \"Need maintainer agreement on harness scope and a real uncovered recovery case. Current demo simulation and transport tests are not this operator-facing scenario mode.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"ENH-021\",\n      \"Graph/CLI: revision-bound change walkthrough artifacts\",\n      \"M/L\",\n      \"entire-graph\",\n      \"internal/cli/impact.go\",\n      245,\n      \"Read-only report groups changed symbols, callers/tests and checkpoint rationale at fixed base/head revisions; incomplete edges remain disclosed. Start with deterministic structured/text output.\",\n      \"Origin Code Tours show review explanations tied to the change and chosen version.\",\n      \"https://cursor.com/docs/origin/code-tours\",\n      \"Product-fit/ownership HOLD: Entire already has skills #9 code-tour for onboarding and CLI #1146 learn. Must establish a distinct change-review outcome before implementation.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"ENH-022\",\n      \"Git Sync: cancel-aware transfer bandwidth budgets\",\n      \"M\",\n      \"git-sync\",\n      \"types.go\",\n      1,\n      \"Optional upload/download byte-rate budgets over relay and materialized paths, with progress distinguishing throttling from network wait. Keep defaults unchanged and cancellation prompt.\",\n      \"Potential operational complement to high-scale agent traffic; competitor scale claims do not establish customer demand.\",\n      \"https://code.storage/\",\n      \"Need a real shared-runner/network constraint and show why existing injected HTTP client cannot sufficiently solve it. Lowest-confidence product-need candidate.\"\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"stage\": \"Discovery; one focused candidate READY in scoped checks; nineteen HOLD; no production implementation\",\n  \"decisions\": {\n    \"AUD-024\": \"HOLD\",\n    \"AUD-025\": \"HOLD\",\n    \"AUD-026\": \"READY \\u2014 focused, scoped public check\",\n    \"AUD-027\": \"HOLD\",\n    \"AUD-028\": \"HOLD\",\n    \"AUD-029\": \"HOLD\",\n    \"AUD-030\": \"HOLD\",\n    \"AUD-031\": \"HOLD\",\n    \"AUD-032\": \"HOLD\",\n    \"AUD-033\": \"HOLD\",\n    \"ENH-013\": \"HOLD\",\n    \"ENH-014\": \"HOLD\",\n    \"ENH-015\": \"HOLD\",\n    \"ENH-016\": \"HOLD\",\n    \"ENH-017\": \"HOLD\",\n    \"ENH-018\": \"HOLD\",\n    \"ENH-019\": \"HOLD\",\n    \"ENH-020\": \"HOLD\",\n    \"ENH-021\": \"HOLD\",\n    \"ENH-022\": \"HOLD\"\n  },\n  \"versions\": {\n    \"cli\": \"76f1b5129b974afdf8e59e4ae3755083c10ff8ff\",\n    \"entire-brain\": \"12e1b0d95a078cf4b57c3c8b38bc0aeec4fb9a55\",\n    \"entire-graph\": \"3f632e403e6bd70ac015f3a80980ca39e4dadd0d\",\n    \"git-sync\": \"67dd3a4e083e4faae4417c1849035c7c4638112c\",\n    \"forgemark\": \"654e95a18db7ad690165b519eb151ecc4fc1e2f0\"\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":23667}},"started_at_ms":1794936642906,"completed_at_ms":1794936642906}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T17:30:42.969Z","ordinal":3185,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1ea8f-9d99-76b0-8e4e-88c7f8445e1e","call_id":"call_a14d497606b14557ad311e855c42bbc0","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 13884)\nTotal output lines: 3\n\n{\"chunk_id\":\"d0a406\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00001125,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":3458,\"output\":\"# Entire CLI — repository instructions\\n\\nGo CLI built with Cobra and Charmbracelet Huh. `AGENTS.md` is a symlink to this\\nfile. Keep this entry point short: repo-wide rules and pointers, not command\\ncatalogs, implementation histories, or subsystem specifications.\\n\\n## Project map\\n\\n- `cmd/entire/`: entry point and external-command dispatch.\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/`: Cobra commands, group roots, and CLI helpers. Group/verb files\\n  use `<noun>_group.go` and `<noun>_<verb>.go`.\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/`: built-in agent integrations and external-agent protocol.\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/`: manual-commit strategy and lifecycle/git hooks.\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/`: persistent checkpoint storage (written at commit).\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/session/`: session state shared across worktrees.\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/`: simulated-hook integration tests.\\n- `e2e/`: real-agent tests and deterministic Vogon canary.\\n- `internal/entireclient/`: API clients, authentication, and user directories.\\n\\nUse the Go version pinned by `go.mod` and tools configured in `mise.toml`.\\nFor installed CLI usage, run `entire agent-help`, then\\n`entire agent-help <command>` for current flags; do not guess from a static list.\\n\\n## Read when relevant\\n\\nRead the applicable reference **before changing that area**, not every reference\\nat session start. Follow its related links when the task crosses those boundaries.\\n\\n| Area being changed | Reference |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Commands, help, experimental visibility, repo refs, prompts | [CLI conventions](docs/development/cli-conventions.md) |\\n| Test harnesses, isolation, TTY behavior, source guards | [Testing](docs/development/testing.md) |\\n| Filesystem I/O, `.entire`, symlinks, hook configs, root anchors | [Filesystem safety](docs/development/filesystem-safety.md) |\\n| Git operations, executable lookup, subprocesses, Windows launching | [Git and subprocess safety](docs/development/git-safety.md) |\\n| Caller identification or session current/tokens/adopt | [Caller-session resolution](docs/development/caller-session-resolution.md) |\\n| Control-plane auth or data-plane routing | [API routing](docs/development/api-routing.md) |\\n| Checkpoint writes, lifecycle, sync, settings trust, redaction | [Implementation contracts](docs/development/checkpoint-implementation.md), [domain model](docs/architecture/sessions-and-checkpoints.md), [scenarios](docs/architecture/checkpoint-scenarios.md) |\\n| Ref-based checkpoint backend | [Ref backend](docs/architecture/ref-checkpoint-backend.md) |\\n| Agent integrations | [Agent guide](docs/architecture/agent-guide.md), [integration checklist](docs/architecture/agent-integration-checklist.md) |\\n| External commands or agents | [External commands](docs/architecture/external-commands.md), [agent protocol](docs/architecture/external-agent-protocol.md) |\\n| Security, privacy, scanners | [Security and privacy](docs/security-and-privacy.md), [implementation contracts](docs/development/checkpoint-implementation.md) |\\n| Review command | [Review architecture](docs/architecture/review-command.md) |\\n| Release artifacts, install scripts, version-check origins | [Release origins](docs/architecture/release-origins.md) |\\n| E2E tests | [E2E guide](e2e/README.md) |\\n| Complexity/coverage measurement and the CI complexity gate | [Complexity tooling](tools/complexity/README.md) |\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n| Task | Command / requirement |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Unit tests | `mise run test` |\\n| Integration tests | `mise run test:integration`; required when changing integration test code |\\n| Deterministic E2E canary | `mise run test:e2e:canary`; safe without API calls |\\n| All CI tests | `mise run test:ci` (unit + integration + canary) |\\n| Format and lint | `mise run fmt && mise run lint` |\\n| Before every commit | **`mise run check`** (format, lint, all CI tests) |\\n| Before any push or remote code update | **`mise run lint` on the current tree**, after the latest formatting pass |\\n| After every push to an open PR | **check the trail's findings** (`entire trail finding list cli/<n> --freshness any`; `<n>` is the PR branch's cli trail number, not the PR number); fix real ones, resolve with `-m`, and re-check after the fix lands. Not done until findings are clear |\\n| Duplication checks | `mise run dup` or `mise run dup:staged`; normal lint also checks duplication |\\n| Complexity gate | `mise run complexity:gate`; CI fails a PR on functions over cognitive complexity 30 that are new or worsened against the merge base. The threshold is a gate flag (`COGNIT_WARN`), not a `.golangci.yaml` setting |\\n| Windows installer | `mise run test:ps1`; see testing reference for prerequisites |\\n\\n**Do not run real-agent E2E tests unless the user explicitly requests them.** They\\nmake paid API calls. Vogon is the exception: its canary is deterministic and free.\\nWhen changing E2E prompt wording, run the canary and update Vogon's regex parsing\\nif needed. Formatting can rewrite files; an earlier lint pass is not sufficient.\\n\\nBefore implementing Go code, search nearby packages and helpers for reusable\\npatterns. Use `/go:discover-related` when available, otherwise `rg` and related\\nimplementations/tests. Check `.golangci.yaml`; handle errors and avoid duplication.\\n\\n## Test safety\\n\\n- Every top-level test and subtest calls `t.Parallel()` unless it changes\\n  process-global state (`t.Chdir`, `t.Setenv`, or their `os` equivalents).\\n- Git tests use isolated temporary repositories, preferably\\n  `testutil.InitRepo(t, dir)` plus its file/add/commit helpers. Redirect CWD before\\n  calling CWD-based handlers. Never mutate the real checkout's git/session state.\\n- Tests must not access the developer's real config, cache, or keychain.\\n  In-process fallbacks are shared per process; use per-test overrides and\\n  `tokenstore.UseFileBackendForTesting` when isolation between tests is needed.\\n  Tests that can reach the OS keyring need `keyring.MockInit()` in `TestMain`.\\n- Spawned binaries do not inherit Go's test detection. Harnesses must isolate\\n  `ENTIRE_CONFIG_DIR`, `XDG_CACHE_HOME`, `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file`,\\n  `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE_PATH`, and `ENTIRE_TEST_AUTH_STORE_FILE`.\\n- Prefer `execx.NonInteractive` for real CLI/git test subprocesses so a developer's\\n  terminal cannot make them prompt or hang.\\n- Caller-resolution tests clear every variable from `agent.CallerSessionEnvVars()`;\\n  never hand-maintain a partial list or inherit the developer's agent identity.\\n- Source-scanning guards discover files through testutil's guard helpers\\n  (`GitGrepGuard`, `GuardGoFiles`), restrict pathspecs to Go files, and fail on\\n  zero matches. Do not weaken guard ledgers to silence failures.\\n\\n## Filesystem and settings safety\\n\\n**Use the existing anchor for each tree; never assemble a path and perform bare\\nI/O beneath it.** Read the filesystem reference before adding or changing I/O.\\n\\n| Tree | Canonical owner |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `.entire` | `entiredir` |\\n| Git common directory | `gitdir` |\\n| Working tree | `worktreedir` |\\n| Agent hook configuration | `agent.HookConfigFile` |\\n| Agent session store | `agent.SessionStore` |\\n| Active git hooks directory | `strategy.hooksRootForInstall` / `ForRemoval` |\\n| Per-user config/cache | `userdirs.ConfigRoot` / `CacheRoot` |\\n| Managed plugins | `pluginRoot` |\\n\\n- Root bases come from trusted resolvers, **not `filepath.Dir(target)`**. Confining\\n  a file to its own derived parent proves nothing. Prefer an existing anchor.\\n- Roots share the `osroot.Shared` registry. Open child roots with\\n  `osroot.SharedChild` / `OpenChild`, not bare `parent.OpenRoot`.\\n- Use `osroot` operations and `jsonutil.WriteFileAtomicIn` / `CreateTempIn`.\\n  Directories use `MkdirAllNoSymlink`; rooted read-only operations must also\\n  enforce symlink policy. Atomic writes replace leaf links rather than follow them.\\n- `.entire` must be a real directory; validate through\\n  `paths.ValidateEntireDirAt` / `RequireEntireDir`. Do not treat an unresolved\\n  repository as absent. Settings reads must also refuse symlinks themselves.\\n- Do not broaden symlink exceptions. Developer-vouched agent config directories\\n  are scoped, locally trusted exceptions; `.entire` and git hooks are not vouchable.\\n- `entiredir.OpenForRead` must not create directories. Reset cached roots before\\n  deleting/recreating their directories. Use `entiredir.Name` / `MustName` to\\n  bridge repo-relative constants and root-relative I/O names.\\n- All settings access goes through `settings`; never read or parse settings JSON\\n  ad hoc. Per-user config/cache resolution belongs only to `userdirs`.\\n- Repository-controlled settings must not authorize executable discovery, custom\\n  executables, or instructions for permission-bypassed agents. Preserve the\\n  existing local-provenance gates and their rejection reporting.\\n- Existing exceptions (explicit user paths, global git config, transcript-read\\n  protocol gaps) are documented in the references; do not generalize them.\\n\\n## Git and subprocess safety\\n\\n- Open repositories only through `gitrepo.OpenCurrent(ctx)` or\\n  `gitrepo.OpenPath(root)`, never direct go-git opens. This preserves alternates\\n  and reftable support. Do not fall back to CWD after failed repo resolution.\\n- Use `gitrepo.Status`, never `worktree.Status()`. Agent-hook capture paths use\\n  `StatusWithBudget` and preserve degraded-capture reporting on budget exhaustion.\\n- Every `git status` subprocess passes **`--no-optional-locks`**. This does not\\n  protect worktree-comparing `git diff` from refreshing the index; use the\\n  hook-safe alternatives in the git reference.\\n- Use the git CLI, not go-git v5, for checkout and hard reset; go-git can delete\\n  ignored/untracked directories. This is an implementation rule, not permission\\n  to run destructive git commands.\\n- Git-relative paths resolve against `paths.WorktreeRoot`, never process CWD.\\n- A git subprocess targeting a repository independently of the current hook must\\n  use `gitrepo.EnvWithoutRepoOverrides()`; `Dir` or `-C` alone does not override\\n  inherited selectors. Queries inspecting the commit Git is preparing must retain\\n  the hook environment, including its temporary `GIT_INDEX_FILE`. Hook queries\\n  reading only the hook's own refs or reflog may strip selectors and resolve from\\n  `paths.WorktreeRoot`. User-invoked CWD commands also honor intentionally\\n  exported repo selectors.\\n- PATH scanners use `execx.PathScanDirs()`; external-agent execution requires\\n  absolute binary paths. User-directory overrides use the checked `userdirs`\\n  resolvers before any I/O.\\n- When Entire owns execution, pass arguments separately; never interpolate\\n  dynamic values into `cmd.exe`. Agent-owned shell execution uses the shared\\n  escaping helper. See the reference for the literal-only Unix updater exception.\\n\\n## CLI behavior and output\\n\\n- Load settings through the `settings` package, not new helpers in CLI consumers.\\n- Operational/debug messages use `logging.Debug/Info/Warn/Error`; user output uses\\n  `cmd.OutOrStdout()` / `cmd.ErrOrStderr()`. Never log prompts, file contents, or\\n  commit messages; log operational metadata only.\\n- Cobra suppresses errors globally; `main.go` prints returned errors. Return\\n  `NewSilentError(err)` only after printing a custom error yourself.\\n- Every read-only workflow must work without a TUI: provide complete text/JSON,\\n  stable IDs and detail commands, or direct selection flags. Test that path.\\n- Use `uiform.New` (or `NewAccessibleForm` in `cli`) for Huh forms; these wire\\n  accessibility and theming centrally. Do not hand-roll `WithAccessible`.\\n- Separately opened prompt terminals use `interactive.OpenPromptTTY()` and\\n  `PromptTTY.Close()`, not a bare file close (Windows pending reads can hang).\\n- Register experimental commands with `experimental.Register`. Classify new\\n  commands in `agentHelpClassification`; default to unlisted/user-owned and\\n  flag the product choice for review. Agent guidance belongs in `agentHelpGuidance`,\\n  not Cobra `Short`/`Long` or first-turn injection.\\n\\n## Session, checkpoint, and API contracts\\n\\n- `*strategy.ManualCommitStrategy` is the only strategy; there is no interface or\\n  worktree restore path. Turn ends write session state only; checkpoints are\\n  metadata refs written at commit, never working-branch commits. Log resume is distinct from restoring worktree files.\\n- Caller identity comes from `strategy.ResolveCallerSession`, not newest state.\\n  Preserve resolution provenance; do not narrate worktree fallback or ambiguous\\n  matches as identified callers. `IsCaller()` excludes those guesses; consult\\n  the caller-resolution reference for current enforcement gaps.\\n- Preserve sanitize → image externalization → redact ordering where all apply,\\n  fail-closed scanner behavior, and checkpoint-scoped token accounting. Read the\\n  implementation contracts before modifying any transcript/storage pipeline.\\n- Control-plane precedence belongs to `coreapi`; display `client.CoreOrigin()`\\n  rather than independently resolving a possibly different target.\\n- Repo-scoped data-plane requests resolve the repo's cell and fail on resolution\\n  failure. `/me` uses the home cell; repo-set queries use shared fanout helpers.\\n  Multi-cell operations share one `auth.CellClientFactory` per operation.\\n\\n## Maintaining these instructions\\n\\nUpdate the relevant reference when subsystem behavior changes. Update this file\\nonly for repository-wide development rules or routing links. Preserve safety\\ncontracts in references and regression tests rather than accumulating incident\\nnarratives here. Prefer existing docs over a second account of the same behavior.\\n\\nThe root-file budget is **20 KiB**, enforced alongside local documentation links\\nby `go test ./docs/development`. Extract specialized material instead of expanding\\nthat budget. Do not require every linked document\\nto be loaded on every task. Keep `AGENTS.md` as the symlink to this file.\\n\"}\n{\"chunk_id\":\"0e7d95\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000010375,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":6580,\"output\":\"# Entire contribution tracker\\n\\nPersonal, shared project record for Puneet's Entire contributions. Created 6 November 2026 from the earlier audits and our decisions. **Assembly date is not verification date.** Public statuses below are dated snapshots; recheck before starting work.\\n\\nCanonical file: `/Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli/CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md`.\\nAll project chats and worktrees should read and update this file rather than maintain separate copies. This is local coordination material, excluded from Git; it is not part of the upstream contribution.\\n\\n## Start here\\n\\n| Priority | Local ID | Decision | Next action |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Scheduled priority 1 | AUD-019 | **IMPLEMENTED LOCALLY; pending baseline-test exception.** See the existing worker's final 6 November record. | Continue the same owner after required input; do not create another implementation chat. |\\n| Scheduled priority 2 | AUD-020 | Cross-backend fallback returns the wrong session. **READY in scoped checks.** | Start only after priority 1 completes or fails a gate. |\\n| Scheduled priority 3 | AUD-021 | Exact session cleanup plus linear stale sweep. **READY in scoped checks.** | Start only after prior queued work completes or fails a gate. |\\n| Alternate target, outside scheduled batch | AUD-006 | Idle MCP server ignores cancellation; real CLI SIGTERM case reproduced. **READY** after scoped three-gate check. | Local fix in MCP shutdown chat/worktree; see cross-chat log and validation limits. |\\n| Second verification target | AUD-009 | SSE cursor-only/reset failures reproduced; server contract still unverified. | **HOLD.** Verify practical contract before implementing. |\\n| Focused fallback | AUD-005 | Failed bundle overwrites existing output; freshly reproduced. | **HOLD.** Useful focused fix, not a cleared senior flagship; novelty review incomplete. |\\n| Existing contribution — review only | AUD-001 | Our replay fix is implemented; PR #3015 is still open and unmerged, verified 13 November. | Continue the existing PR. Do not open another issue or PR for it. |\\n| Enhancement published; outside scheduled bug-fix batch | ENH-001 | Brain workspace retrieval: measured serial scaling and ignored cancellation. **CONTINUE OUR PR — #644**, 14 November. | [Issue #643](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/issues/643), [PR #644](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/644). Six checked commits; final memory target PASS (83.42 MiB peak). Remote CI awaits maintainer approval; trail findings unavailable. Existing bug-fix batch unchanged. |\\n| Stop new work / duplicate risk | AUD-016 | Real, substantial bug, but **already reported exactly** in #2696's review. User also reports an existing PR. | Fails the novelty gate. Retain the record of Puneet's work; do not start another implementation. A separate exact fixing PR has not been independently identified. |\\n| Hold — feature withdrawal proposed | AUD-017 | Cursor permission bug freshly reproduced at current upstream on 6 November. | Open #2615 proposes removing the entire affected package. Do not start before ownership/direction is resolved. |\\n| Hold — feature withdrawal proposed | AUD-018 | Cursor attribution cost measured; code still present. | Open #2615 proposes removing the package. Do not start an optimization that conflicts with that work. |\\n| Excluded | AUD-002 | User confirmed another contributor already has a summary-target PR. | Add the exact PR link when identified; do not pick it up as ours. |\\n\\n## Mandatory decision table — three gates before starting\\n\\n**User rule, 6 November 2026: start a new implementation only after all three gates pass.** Unknown, conditional, stale, or not checked does not mean pass. Previous words such as “candidate” or “available” in historical evidence below are not permission to start.\\n\\n1. **Legitimate:** reproduce a current failure against the intended contract, or measure a meaningful performance problem. An intentional behavior, hypothetical concern, or missing field alone does not pass.\\n2. **Substantial / senior scope:** identify the actual engineering judgment involved: failure atomicity, concurrency, identity, privacy boundaries, scaling or lifecycle ownership. Assess the necessary solution, not an artificially enlarged patch. A useful focused fix can still fail our present flagship-selection goal; that says nothing about its author's seniority.\\n3. **New and clear to work on:** check issues, all-state PRs, bodies, comments, inline review findings, prototypes, claims and relevant changed files. An existing exact report fails the user's strict new-issue requirement even if unfixed. An issue-only pickup requires an explicit later decision from the user. Adjacent work is not automatically an exact duplicate, but unresolved overlap is a hold.\\n\\nOnly **READY** means all three passed with dated evidence. **CONTINUE OUR PR** applies to work already published by us; it is not a new-work approval. **HOLD** permits research/verification, not a production implementation. **SKIP** records a failed gate. The latest deep pass cleared **AUD-019, AUD-020 and AUD-021** as the scheduled three-item queue, subject to fresh gate checks. AUD-006 is an alternate previously cleared target, not one of this batch’s three. AUD-009 and AUD-005 remain held.\\n\\nLatest deep-audit upstream: `aa0c90c9770a460092103214b608247a8b2623ae`, 6 November 2026. The earlier gate pass used `3c299b94f8595bdfc3aa2ecdc0bd199d856f15a2`. The older evidence retains its original dates; this pass did not rerun every historical reproduction.\\n\\n| ID / finding | 1. Legitimate issue? | 2. Substantial senior scope? | 3. New / already raised or worked on? | Decis…3884 tokens truncated… task's obsolete feasibility/proof executables and reproducible v1 large fixtures; SHA manifests/raw measurements/source recipes retained. Current five CLI comparison binaries, both owner checkouts, their history/work and shared caches remain untouched.\\n\\n\\n### Private review of existing OpenCode-created PRs #3174 / #3175 — 17 November 2026\\n\\n- User asks whether to refine or close these two already-published contributions. Review only; no implementation, remote comments/reviews, closure or push authorized/inferred. Both live connector snapshots OPEN/unmerged under Puneet-Pal-Singh: #3174 at `83fa5560a274d1e967e30670d9f604cb43834129`, #3175 at `8a9ee8ccdb99d9a3d850ce94bab33c773c0f8c7c`; shared base `76f1b5129b974afdf8e59e4ae3755083c10ff8ff`. No submitted reviews/discussion/inline threads returned. Only listed check for each is skipped Entire Gates; no full-CI success established.\\n- **Recommendation: KEEP / REFINE both existing PRs, #3174 first.** Useful focused contributions, not two cleared new senior flagship implementations. Original committed regressions independently FAIL against shared-base production files and PASS with respective patches. Focused review/transcript/internal-transcript suites PASS in isolated source archive combining disjoint changes. No full `mise run check`/lint rerun here; PR bodies evidence focused tests plus lint:go, not required complete verification.\\n- **#3174 confirmed refinement:** cmd.Start failure closes owned stderr reader but leaks writer. Deterministic audit checks cmd.Stderr file after failed Start: Stat succeeds instead of os.ErrClosed. Close writer on every failure and cover cleanup/diagnostics. Existing inherited-stderr test proves redirected-stdout case, not arbitrary stdout inheritance. Necessary lifecycle fix appears sound enough to retain.\\n- **#3175 confirmed synthetic coverage gap:** assistant with no content, input/output=0 and cache.read=50/cache.write=20 converts to no line; existing content eligibility still checks input/output only. This omission predates PR, but conflicts with its broader cache-retention objective. Native occurrence/frequency unverified; no production incident claim. Retain cache/model mapping, extend eligibility/tests and cover normalized-v2/streaming usage. #2823 fixes checkpoint CalculateTokenUsage, a different consumer; base already contains the accounting helper. #2155/#2767 are adjacent. Scoped searches/relevant inline reviews did not establish an exact converter duplicate; full strict novelty clearance remains UNKNOWN/HOLD, not READY.\\n- This chat owns audit-only evidence `/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-pr-review-2026-11-17/review.txt` and probes; disposable source archive `/private/tmp/entire-pr3174-3175-review`. No contribution implementation owner assigned or existing queue changed. Preserve main staged replay work/config/AGENTS symlink and OpenCode worktrees. Separate `opencode_tracker.md` is evidence only: its instruction to ignore this canonical tracker does not override user coordination rules. No production changes, commit, push, public message/review or PR state change made.\\n\\n\\n### Existing PR refinement authorized — 17 November 2026\\n\\n- User explicitly requests refining code/tests/title/body of #3174 and #3175 only if legitimate. Continue existing contributions; no new PR or issue. Same review chat now owns refinements, serially, starting #3174. Worktree `Entire/cli-pr3174`, branch `refine/pr3174`, base published head83fa5560a; intended fast-forward destination `fix/review-wait-inherited-stderr`. Main replay staging/config and existing OpenCode worktree preserved. #3175 remains unchanged at8a9ee8ccd until its refinement stage.\\n- Current upstream main unchanged76f1b512. Legitimacy PASS from independent red/green proofs at this exact source; lifecycle ownership/bounded draining and version-sensitive transcript accounting justify necessary focused engineering scope. These are useful focused scopes, not flagship size claims. Public inventory refreshed: all288open PRs and complete changed-file pages. Only adjacent overlaps #3129 (tool-error text) and #2683 (legacy/project model refactor); inspected actual patches differ from these fixes. All-state targeted searches, source-history PR discussion/inline reviews and current relevant plans reviewed. #1559/#1561/#3052/#3102 cover cancelled processes/Windows tree termination, not a normal-exit stderr drain; #2834's shipped field-reader/followups #2858/#2859 cover Claude/Codex conversion, not a claimed OpenCode converter patch. #2823/#2155/#2767 concern checkpoint/session accounting, distinct consumer. Scoped novelty/ownership PASS for continuing our published PRs, private work unknown; retain original attribution and no first-discovery claim. Evidence in `entire-pr-review-2026-11-17/public`. No new contribution gate bypass or permission to ignore checks/baseline policy.\\n- Stage: ownership recorded before production refinements; required per-PR exact-tree check before commit, latest fmt/lint before push, verified trail lookup/findings after push. No blanket exception for baseline failures inferred.\\n\\n\"}\n{\"chunk_id\":\"53a924\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000023667,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":3474,\"output\":\"{\\n  \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-16\\\",\\n  \\\"scope\\\": \\\"Discovery only. All new entries HOLD; small scopes requested, but no gate waived. No production implementation or publication.\\\",\\n  \\\"revisions\\\": {\\n    \\\"cli\\\": \\\"76f1b5129b974afdf8e59e4ae3755083c10ff8ff\\\",\\n    \\\"brain\\\": \\\"12e1b0d95a078cf4b57c3c8b38bc0aeec4fb9a55\\\",\\n    \\\"graph\\\": \\\"3f632e403e6bd70ac015f3a80980ca39e4dadd0d\\\",\\n    \\\"git_sync\\\": \\\"67dd3a4e083e4faae4417c1849035c7c4638112c\\\",\\n    \\\"forgemark\\\": \\\"654e95a18db7ad690165b519eb151ecc4fc1e2f0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"bug_columns\\\": [\\n    \\\"id\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\",\\n    \\\"size\\\",\\n    \\\"repo\\\",\\n    \\\"file\\\",\\n    \\\"line\\\",\\n    \\\"evidence\\\",\\n    \\\"observation\\\",\\n    \\\"remaining_gate\\\",\\n    \\\"log\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"bugs\\\": [\\n    [\\n      \\\"AUD-024\\\",\\n      \\\"CLI: one malformed review manifest blocks healthy saved reviews\\\",\\n      \\\"S\\\",\\n      \\\"cli\\\",\\n      \\\"cmd/entire/cli/review/manifest.go\\\",\\n      725,\\n      \\\"REPRODUCED\\\",\\n      \\\"A valid saved review plus broken.json makes loadLocalReviewManifests return an error before any findings are served.\\\",\\n      \\\"Need corrupt-entry reporting/recovery contract and final ownership clearance around #2996.\\\",\\n      \\\"review-probes.log\\\"\\n    ],\\n    [\\n      \\\"AUD-025\\\",\\n      \\\"Brain: corrupt feed record keeps a cursor that skips its recovery\\\",\\n      \\\"M\\\",\\n      \\\"entire-brain\\\",\\n      \\\"internal/cli/hosted_feed_cache.go\\\",\\n      55,\\n      \\\"FUNCTION PROBE\\\",\\n      \\\"Verbatim current reader skips malformed records and returns cursor-7 with a partial map and no error.\\\",\\n      \\\"Complete sync/recovery reproduction and distinguish from #403's exact missing-file report; do not claim that already-fixed defect.\\\",\\n      \\\"feed-probe.log\\\"\\n    ],\\n    [\\n      \\\"AUD-026\\\",\\n      \\\"Git Sync: fragment-only URL differences bypass same-repository guard\\\",\\n      \\\"S\\\",\\n      \\\"git-sync\\\",\\n      \\\"internal/validation/validation.go\\\",\\n      61,\\n      \\\"REPRODUCED\\\",\\n      \\\"Direct validation and public SyncRequest validation accept fragment-only aliases; two real loopback HTTP GETs reached the identical /repo.git resource. Exact fragment-free guard control rejects equal endpoints.\\\",\\n      \\\"Scoped gates PASS: current contract reproduction; minimal HTTP URL identity fix; no exact fragment report in all-state searches, related #18/#108/#122/#124 reviews, five open PR metadata and27 branch names. #18 reports a different trailing-slash case. Refresh immediately before a task-owned implementation; no public reservation.\\\",\\n      \\\"git-sync-probes.log\\\"\\n    ],\\n    [\\n      \\\"AUD-027\\\",\\n      \\\"Git Sync: impossible include prefixes pass request validation\\\",\\n      \\\"S\\\",\\n      \\\"git-sync\\\",\\n      \\\"internal/validation/validation.go\\\",\\n      15,\\n      \\\"REPRODUCED\\\",\\n      \\\"refs/../, refs/heads/a[, whitespace and backslash prefixes pass; git check-ref-format rejects their extended names.\\\",\\n      \\\"Check prefix grammar permits legitimate partial names; review equivalent independent-history-prefix validation in one scope; final novelty clearance. Source commit a81db6 already reports blank/outside-refs prefixes; character-validity cases must not be represented as that old report. Strict novelty of this extension remains HOLD.\\\",\\n      \\\"git-sync-probes.log\\\"\\n    ],\\n    [\\n      \\\"AUD-028\\\",\\n      \\\"Graph: same-size, same-mtime transcript replacement can reuse stale stats\\\",\\n      \\\"S/M\\\",\\n      \\\"entire-graph\\\",\\n      \\\"internal/cli/stats_cache.go\\\",\\n      139,\\n      \\\"SOURCE LEAD\\\",\\n      \\\"Memo key includes resolved path, size and mtime, but no content revision; a timestamp-preserving rewrite can have the same key.\\\",\\n      \\\"Need actual stats CLI reproduction and establish intended freshness/performance contract. Existing metadata cache design is documented, so this is not a certified bug.\\\",\\n      \\\"stats-key-probe.json\\\"\\n    ],\\n    [\\n      \\\"AUD-029\\\",\\n      \\\"Brain: workspace graph-generation probes discard caller cancellation\\\",\\n      \\\"M\\\",\\n      \\\"entire-brain\\\",\\n      \\\"internal/cli/workspace.go\\\",\\n      2167,\\n      \\\"SOURCE LEAD\\\",\\n      \\\"workspaceGraphGeneration has no context parameter and fetches each member Graph store with context.Background and a real ExecRunner.\\\",\\n      \\\"Need cancellation reproduction at the public graph command and coordination with #644; do not duplicate its query/search worker work.\\\",\\n      \\\"\\\"\\n    ],\\n    [\\n      \\\"AUD-030\\\",\\n      \\\"ForgeMark: blocked SSE output outlives request cancellation\\\",\\n      \\\"S/M\\\",\\n      \\\"forgemark\\\",\\n      \\\"internal/server/events.go\\\",\\n      136,\\n      \\\"BLOCKED-WRITER PROBE\\\",\\n      \\\"Cancelling request context while replay Write is blocked does not finish handler until the writer is released.\\\",\\n      \\\"Need real socket/backpressure/shutdown test and write-deadline contract; custom writer mechanism is not a production incident.\\\",\\n      \\\"sse-probe.log\\\"\\n    ],\\n    [\\n      \\\"AUD-031\\\",\\n      \\\"CLI: moved checkout path hides existing local review history\\\",\\n      \\\"M\\\",\\n      \\\"cli\\\",\\n      \\\"cmd/entire/cli/review/manifest.go\\\",\\n      751,\\n      \\\"IDENTITY FIXTURE\\\",\\n      \\\"Same common-dir review store returns one manifest for saved path and zero for current moved path.\\\",\\n      \\\"Need actual checkout relocation/worktree identity matrix and #2996 integration clearance. This is read-time history filtering, not that PR's missing-session capture fix.\\\",\\n      \\\"review-probes.log\\\"\\n    ],\\n    [\\n      \\\"AUD-032\\\",\\n      \\\"CLI: