/docs/origin/clonekit-ci\\\",\\n      \\\"Server filter/depth support, representative monorepo savings and final novelty clearance.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    [\\n      \\\"ENH-014\\\",\\n      \\\"CLI: incremental review since a saved review baseline\\\",\\n      \\\"M/L\\\",\\n      \\\"cli\\\",\\n      \\\"cmd/entire/cli/review/manifest.go\\\",\\n      40,\\n      \\\"Persist reviewed commit/tree/dirty-state identity and explicitly review only the new range, retaining dependency context. Refuse stale/rebased baselines.\\\",\\n      \\\"Origin supports reviewing changes since the last review; this proposal concerns local reviewer execution, not adding more agents.\\\",\\n      \\\"https://cursor.com/docs/origin/code-tours\\\",\\n      \\\"Need scope correctness on uncommitted work and integration with exact-scope PR #1647 and persistence PR #2996.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    [\\n      \\\"ENH-015\\\",\\n      \\\"CLI: checkpoint asset list and selective extraction\\\",\\n      \\\"S/M\\\",\\n      \\\"cli\\\",\\n      \\\"cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/persistent.go\\\",\\n      1850,\\n      \\\"Expose stored asset metadata and export a selected binary without dumping/reinjecting an entire transcript; byte bounds, hash checks and safe explicit destinations.\\\",\\n      \\\"Code.Storage treats generated artifacts as first-class files with direct reads.\\\",\\n      \\\"https://code.storage/docs/api/repos/file-get\\\",\\n      \\\"Need supported-agent storage/restore matrix and public novelty clearance; not the already-reported entire.com image timeline #2942.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    [\\n      \\\"ENH-016\\\",\\n      \\\"Brain: explain memory ranking and exclusions\\\",\\n      \\\"M\\\",\\n      \\\"entire-brain\\\",\\n      \\\"internal/cli/facts_bm25.go\\\",\\n      1,\\n      \\\"Opt-in deterministic trace of term contributions, corpus scope, locus/recency/negative boosts, filtered candidates and family collapse. Preserve scores/output defaults.\\\",\\n      \\\"Useful debugging surface for a memory product; not a new embedding backend or ENH-004 index.\\\",\\n      \\\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain\\\",\\n      \\\"Need representative confusing query, exact score decomposition and separation from #595 provenance / #335 packet presentation.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    [\\n      \\\"ENH-017\\\",\\n      \\\"CLI: accurate hook timelines and Perfetto export\\\",\\n      \\\"M\\\",\\n      \\\"cli\\\",\\n      \\\"perf/span.go\\\",\\n      149,\\n      \\\"Retain relative child start times and export local trace events with correct overlap, IDs and bounded size. Existing durations alone cannot reconstruct overlapping spans honestly.\\\",\\n      \\\"Code.Storage advertises telemetry; Perfetto supports custom timestamped trace imports.\\\",\\n      \\\"https://perfetto.dev/docs/getting-started/other-formats\\\",\\n      \\\"Need measured diagnostic need/overhead and completed review/claim clearance; existing doctor trace JSON is already shipped.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    [\\n      \\\"ENH-018\\\",\\n      \\\"Graph: snapshot-bound pagination for large neighbor/impact results\\\",\\n      \\\"M/L\\\",\\n      \\\"entire-graph\\\",\\n      \\\"internal/cli/neighbors.go\\\",\\n      219,\\n      \\\"Opaque continuation pinned to source snapshot, symbol, relation filters and ordering; reject stale cursors. Fetch the next page without repeating earlier context.\\\",\\n      \\\"Code.Storage exposes cursor-paginated repository reads; the same interaction helps large graph hubs.\\\",\\n      \\\"https://code.storage/docs/api/repos/grep\\\",\\n      \\\"Need existing truncation semantics and large-hub workload; coordinate focused SQLite read PR #407 rather than copying its implementation.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    [\\n      \\\"ENH-019\\\",\\n      \\\"ForgeMark: persist mergeable latency distributions\\\",\\n      \\\"M\\\",\\n      \\\"forgemark\\\",\\n      \\\"internal/bench/stats.go\\\",\\n      66,\\n      \\\"Versioned mergeable histogram metadata for compatible repeated runs; recompute percentiles honestly and bound retained samples, with documented precision/error.\\\",\\n      \\\"A benchmark harness improvement: current live collector has histograms, while saved LevelResult contains scalar percentiles.\\\",\\n      \\\"https://github.com/entireio/forgemark\\\",\\n      \\\"Need memory measurements, compatible-run rules and preserve exact-percentile behavior; not duplicate CI threshold PRs #6/#14.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    [\\n      \\\"ENH-020\\\",\\n      \\\"ForgeMark: deterministic Git protocol fault scenarios\\\",\\n      \\\"L\\\",\\n      \\\"forgemark\\\",\\n      \\\"internal/bench/runner.go\\\",\\n      1,\\n      \\\"Opt-in local scenario harness for bounded delays, interrupted packs, reset/retry and stale-ref/CAS interleavings, with seed, injection schedule and recovery assertions.\\\",\\n      \\\"Code.Storage's concurrent agent writes make correctness under controlled disruption worth testing alongside throughput.\\\",\\n      \\\"https://code.storage/docs/guides/parallel-attempts\\\",\\n      \\\"Need maintainer agreement on harness scope and a real uncovered recovery case. Current demo simulation and transport tests are not this operator-facing scenario mode.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    [\\n      \\\"ENH-021\\\",\\n      \\\"Graph/CLI: revision-bound change walkthrough artifacts\\\",\\n      \\\"M/L\\\",\\n      \\\"entire-graph\\\",\\n      \\\"internal/cli/impact.go\\\",\\n      245,\\n      \\\"Read-only report groups changed symbols, callers/tests and checkpoint rationale at fixed base/head revisions; incomplete edges remain disclosed. Start with deterministic structured/text output.\\\",\\n      \\\"Origin Code Tours show review explanations tied to the change and chosen version.\\\",\\n      \\\"https://cursor.com/docs/origin/code-tours\\\",\\n      \\\"Product-fit/ownership HOLD: Entire already has skills #9 code-tour for onboarding and CLI #1146 learn. Must establish a distinct change-review outcome before implementation.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    [\\n      \\\"ENH-022\\\",\\n      \\\"Git Sync: cancel-aware transfer bandwidth budgets\\\",\\n      \\\"M\\\",\\n      \\\"git-sync\\\",\\n      \\\"types.go\\\",\\n      1,\\n      \\\"Optional upload/download byte-rate budgets over relay and materialized paths, with progress distinguishing throttling from network wait. Keep defaults unchanged and cancellation prompt.\\\",\\n      \\\"Potential operational complement to high-scale agent traffic; competitor scale claims do not establish customer demand.\\\",\\n      \\\"https://code.storage/\\\",\\n      \\\"Need a real shared-runner/network constraint and show why existing injected HTTP client cannot sufficiently solve it. Lowest-confidence product-need candidate.\\\"\\n    ]\\n  ],\\n  \\\"stage\\\": \\\"Discovery; one focused candidate READY in scoped checks; nineteen HOLD; no production implementation\\\",\\n  \\\"decisions\\\": {\\n    \\\"AUD-024\\\": \\\"HOLD\\\",\\n    \\\"AUD-025\\\": \\\"HOLD\\\",\\n    \\\"AUD-026\\\": \\\"READY \\\\u2014 focused, scoped public check\\\",\\n    \\\"AUD-027\\\": \\\"HOLD\\\",\\n    \\\"AUD-028\\\": \\\"HOLD\\\",\\n    \\\"AUD-029\\\": \\\"HOLD\\\",\\n    \\\"AUD-030\\\": \\\"HOLD\\\",\\n    \\\"AUD-031\\\": \\\"HOLD\\\",\\n    \\\"AUD-032\\\": \\\"HOLD\\\",\\n    \\\"AUD-033\\\": \\\"HOLD\\\",\\n    \\\"ENH-013\\\": \\\"HOLD\\\",\\n    \\\"ENH-014\\\": \\\"HOLD\\\",\\n    \\\"ENH-015\\\": \\\"HOLD\\\",\\n    \\\"ENH-016\\\": \\\"HOLD\\\",\\n    \\\"ENH-017\\\": \\\"HOLD\\\",\\n    \\\"ENH-018\\\": \\\"HOLD\\\",\\n    \\\"ENH-019\\\": \\\"HOLD\\\",\\n    \\\"ENH-020\\\": \\\"HOLD\\\",\\n    \\\"ENH-021\\\": \\\"HOLD\\\",\\n    \\\"ENH-022\\\": \\\"HOLD\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"versions\\\": {\\n    \\\"cli\\\": \\\"76f1b5129b974afdf8e59e4ae3755083c10ff8ff\\\",\\n    \\\"entire-brain\\\": \\\"12e1b0d95a078cf4b57c3c8b38bc0aeec4fb9a55\\\",\\n    \\\"entire-graph\\\": \\\"3f632e403e6bd70ac015f3a80980ca39e4dadd0d\\\",\\n    \\\"git-sync\\\": \\\"67dd3a4e083e4faae4417c1849035c7c4638112c\\\",\\n    \\\"forgemark\\\": \\\"654e95a18db7ad690165b519eb151ecc4fc1e2f0\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1ea8f-4eae-75f2-adec-faef107733f4","create_time":1794936642.96934}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":571,"sampled_through_sequence":568,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
