\n792: | ENH-014 | CLI: incremental review since a saved review baseline | M/L | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Persist reviewed commit/tree/dirty-state identity and explicitly review only the new range, retaining dependency context. Refuse stale/reb\n793: | ENH-015 | CLI: checkpoint asset list and selective extraction | S/M | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Expose stored asset metadata and export a selected binary without dumping/reinjecting an entire transcript; byte bounds, hash checks and saf\n794: | ENH-016 | Brain: explain memory ranking and exclusions | M | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Opt-in deterministic trace of term contributions, corpus scope, locus/recency/negative boosts, filtered candidates and family collapse. Preserve scor\n795: | ENH-017 | CLI: accurate hook timelines and Perfetto export | M | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Retain relative child start times and export local trace events with correct overlap, IDs and bounded size. Existing durations alone cannot recon\n796: | ENH-018 | Graph: snapshot-bound pagination for large neighbor/impact results | M/L | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Opaque continuation pinned to source snapshot, symbol, relation filters and ordering; reject stale cursors. Fetch the next pa\n797: | ENH-019 | ForgeMark: persist mergeable latency distributions | M | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Versioned mergeable histogram metadata for compatible repeated runs; recompute percentiles honestly and bound retained samples, with documented\n798: | ENH-020 | ForgeMark: deterministic Git protocol fault scenarios | L | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Opt-in local scenario harness for bounded delays, interrupted packs, reset/retry and stale-ref/CAS interleavings, with seed, injection sched\n799: | ENH-021 | Graph/CLI: revision-bound change walkthrough artifacts | M/L | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Read-only report groups changed symbols, callers/tests and checkpoint rationale at fixed base/head revisions; incomplete edges remain dis\n800: | ENH-022 | Git Sync: cancel-aware transfer bandwidth budgets | M | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Optional upload/download byte-rate budgets over relay and materialized paths, with progress distinguishing throttling from network wait. Keep de\n802: - Competitor evidence: Code.Storage direct file reads, ephemeral agent-state refs and parallel attempts; Origin CloneKit and changes-since-last-review tours. Inspiration is not proof of Entire feature absence or need. Hosted server capabilities \n803: - Exclusions retained: GitSync LFS is existing issue#59; Graph working-tree caching is existing issue#271; ForgeMark CI gates already have PR#6/#14; code-tour onboarding already has skills#9 and CLI learn#1146 (ENH-021 therefore remains adjacent\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":11333}},"started_at_ms":1794936759890,"completed_at_ms":1794936759890}}
