iscovery_test.go:33: accepted impossible Git ref prefix: \"refs/heads/a[\"\n    discovery_test.go:33: accepted impossible Git ref prefix: \"refs/heads/a b\"\n    discovery_test.go:33: accepted impossible Git ref prefix: \"refs/heads/a\\\\b\"\n    discovery_test.go:26: validation accepted both URLs; real HTTP request target is identical: \"/repo.git\"\nfeed-probe.log:\n    cache_test.go:9: corrupt record skipped; returned cursor=\"cursor-7\", parsed items=1, error=nil\nsse-probe.log:\n    discovery_test.go:25: cancelled request remains blocked inside replay Write\nfollow-probe.log:\n\nstats-key-probe.json:\n  \"same_cache_key\": true,\n  \"different_content_hash\": true,\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":21500}},"started_at_ms":1794936760241,"completed_at_ms":1794936760242}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T17:32:40.314Z","ordinal":3201,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1ea91-67fa-7d71-b101-6a7fdac578d8","call_id":"call_83810e91e51d42c5b126f2df4dae1c07","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"aa874b\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000011333,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1435,\"output\":\"773: - **AUD-026 READY as a focused scope in documented public checks.** Gate1 PASS: current endpoint guard and public SyncRequest validation accept fragment-only aliases, while actual loopback HTTP requests target the same `/repo.git`; direct identi\\n778: | AUD-024 | CLI: one malformed review manifest blocks healthy saved reviews | S | **HOLD**; REPRODUCED. Need corrupt-entry reporting/recovery contract and final ownership clearance around #2996. |\\n779: | AUD-025 | Brain: corrupt feed record keeps a cursor that skips its recovery | M | **HOLD**; FUNCTION PROBE. Complete sync/recovery reproduction and distinguish from #403's exact missing-file report; do not claim that already-fixed defect. |\\n780: | AUD-026 | Git Sync: fragment-only URL differences bypass same-repository guard | S | **READY — focused, scoped public check**; REPRODUCED. Scoped gates PASS: current contract reproduction; minimal HTTP URL identity fix; no exact fragment repor\\n781: | AUD-027 | Git Sync: impossible include prefixes pass request validation | S | **HOLD**; REPRODUCED. Check prefix grammar permits legitimate partial names; review equivalent independent-history-prefix validation in one scope; final novelty clea\\n782: | AUD-028 | Graph: same-size, same-mtime transcript replacement can reuse stale stats | S/M | **HOLD**; SOURCE LEAD. Need actual stats CLI reproduction and establish intended freshness/performance contract. Existing metadata cache design is docu\\n783: | AUD-029 | Brain: workspace graph-generation probes discard caller cancellation | M | **HOLD**; SOURCE LEAD. Need cancellation reproduction at the public graph command and coordination with #644; do not duplicate its query/search worker work. |\\n784: | AUD-030 | ForgeMark: blocked SSE output outlives request cancellation | S/M | **HOLD**; BLOCKED-WRITER PROBE. Need real socket/backpressure/shutdown test and write-deadline contract; custom writer mechanism is not a production incident. |\\n785: | AUD-031 | CLI: moved checkout path hides existing local review history | M | **HOLD**; IDENTITY FIXTURE. Need actual checkout relocation/worktree identity matrix and #2996 integration clearance. This is read-time history filtering, not that PR\\n786: | AUD-032 | CLI: checkpoint list truncation recommends an unavailable --limit flag | S | **HOLD**; SOURCE + INSTALLED COMMAND. Need current-source command fixture with a truncated result and finish novelty checks around #1768/#2089; installed bi\\n787: | AUD-033 | CLI: busy log follower ignores cancellation inside its drain loop | S | **HOLD**; VERBATIM FUNCTION PROBE. Need command-level cancellation regression and fresh ownership. Separate from AUD-007's copy-truncation case; do not count tha\\n791: | ENH-013 | CLI: sparse/shallow clone profiles | L | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Explicit depth, blob filtering and sparse paths while retaining Entire cluster selection/auth. Validate supported server protocol; do not promise a hosted Clon\\n792: | ENH-014 | CLI: incremental review since a saved review baseline | M/L | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Persist reviewed commit/tree/dirty-state identity and explicitly review only the new range, retaining dependency context. Refuse stale/reb\\n793: | ENH-015 | CLI: checkpoint asset list and selective extraction | S/M | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Expose stored asset metadata and export a selected binary without dumping/reinjecting an entire transcript; byte bounds, hash checks and saf\\n794: | ENH-016 | Brain: explain memory ranking and exclusions | M | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Opt-in deterministic trace of term contributions, corpus scope, locus/recency/negative boosts, filtered candidates and family collapse. Preserve scor\\n795: | ENH-017 | CLI: accurate hook timelines and Perfetto export | M | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Retain relative child start times and export local trace events with correct overlap, IDs and bounded size. Existing durations alone cannot recon\\n796: | ENH-018 | Graph: snapshot-bound pagination for large neighbor/impact results | M/L | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Opaque continuation pinned to source snapshot, symbol, relation filters and ordering; reject stale cursors. Fetch the next pa\\n797: | ENH-019 | ForgeMark: persist mergeable latency distributions | M | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Versioned mergeable histogram metadata for compatible repeated runs; recompute percentiles honestly and bound retained samples, with documented\\n798: | ENH-020 | ForgeMark: deterministic Git protocol fault scenarios | L | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Opt-in local scenario harness for bounded delays, interrupted packs, reset/retry and stale-ref/CAS interleavings, with seed, injection sched\\n799: | ENH-021 | Graph/CLI: revision-bound change walkthrough artifacts | M/L | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Read-only report groups changed symbols, callers/tests and checkpoint rationale at fixed base/head revisions; incomplete edges remain dis\\n800: | ENH-022 | Git Sync: cancel-aware transfer bandwidth budgets | M | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Optional upload/download byte-rate budgets over relay and materialized paths, with progress distinguishing throttling from network wait. Keep de\\n802: - Competitor evidence: Code.Storage direct file reads, ephemeral agent-state refs and parallel attempts; Origin CloneKit and changes-since-last-review tours. Inspiration is not proof of Entire feature absence or need. Hosted server capabilities \\n803: - Exclusions retained: GitSync LFS is existing issue#59; Graph working-tree caching is existing issue#271; ForgeMark CI gates already have PR#6/#14; code-tour onboarding already has skills#9 and CLI learn#1146 (ENH-021 therefore remains adjacent\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"19596c\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.0000215,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":307,\"output\":\"review-probes.log:\\n    discovery_history_test.go:19: one malformed manifest blocks one valid saved review: decode review manifest broken.json: unexpected end of JSON input\\n    discovery_history_test.go:31: unchanged common-dir store: saved-path query=1, current moved-path query=0\\ngit-sync-probes.log:\\n    discovery_validation_test.go:9: public SyncRequest.Validate accepts fragment-only same-endpoint alias\\n    discovery_test.go:14: same HTTP endpoint is accepted when only URL fragments differ\\n    discovery_test.go:33: accepted impossible Git ref prefix: \\\"refs/../\\\"\\n    discovery_test.go:33: accepted impossible Git ref prefix: \\\"refs/heads/a[\\\"\\n    discovery_test.go:33: accepted impossible Git ref prefix: \\\"refs/heads/a b\\\"\\n    discovery_test.go:33: accepted impossible Git ref prefix: \\\"refs/heads/a\\\\\\\\b\\\"\\n    discovery_test.go:26: validation accepted both URLs; real HTTP request target is identical: \\\"/repo.git\\\"\\nfeed-probe.log:\\n    cache_test.go:9: corrupt record skipped; returned cursor=\\\"cursor-7\\\", parsed items=1, error=nil\\nsse-probe.log:\\n    discovery_test.go:25: cancelled request remains blocked inside replay Write\\nfollow-probe.log:\\n\\nstats-key-probe.json:\\n  \\\"same_cache_key\\\": true,\\n  \\\"different_content_hash\\\": true,\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1ea8f-4eae-75f2-adec-faef107733f4","create_time":1794936760.314688}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":578,"sampled_through_sequence":571,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
