{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T17:33:24.266Z","ordinal":3207,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1ea8f-4eae-75f2-adec-faef107733f4","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0b823400861c2c3d016afc8fe03ef087d0b5eee84246d8f764","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The main weakness is product need: several proposed features add machinery before showing a painful workflow. I’d move Perfetto export, a standalone fault-injection mode, change tours and bandwidth budgets down the list. Asset extraction, ranking explanations and incremental review have clearer uses, though each still needs evidence.\n\nFor bugs, I’m separating reproduced behavior from contract failures. Metadata caching may be an intentional tradeoff, and the blocked-writer probe alone doesn’t establish a production SSE defect."}],"phase":"commentary"},"content_token_count":96,"started_at_ms":1794936800181,"completed_at_ms":1794936804266}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T17:33:24.275Z","ordinal":3208,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_0b823400861c2c3d016afc8fe03ef087d0b5eee84246d8f764","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The main weakness is product need: several proposed features add machinery before showing a painful workflow. I’d move Perfetto export, a standalone fault-injection mode, change tours and bandwidth budgets down the list. Asset extraction, ranking explanations and incremental review have clearer uses, though each still needs evidence.\n\nFor bugs, I’m separating reproduced behavior from contract failures. Metadata caching may be an intentional tradeoff, and the blocked-writer probe alone doesn’t establish a production SSE defect.","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1ea8f-4eae-75f2-adec-faef107733f4","create_time":1794936800.2559683,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":581,"sampled_through_sequence":578,"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_0b823400861c2c3d016afc8fe03ef087d0b5eee84246d8f764","turn_id":"01a1ea8f-4eae-75f2-adec-faef107733f4","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a1ea92-13b2-7e30-96c3-71e263694776","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":78}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T17:34:19.060Z","ordinal":3209,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0b823400861c2c3d016afc8fe42af887d09993a17a1f027440","status":"completed","call_id":"call_3e0b6551fa714199990c4356894679ce","name":"exec","input":"const rows=[\n[\"AUD-024\",\"Corrupt review manifest\",\"1) Healthy saved reviews become inaccessible.\",\"2) Isolating a bad entry can preserve useful user data.\",\"1) No normal-workflow corruption incident was shown.\",\"2) Recovery must disclose damage and fit ongoing persistence work.\",\"Prioritize validation\",\"Keep HOLD; reproduce named-review access and define partial-history/error behavior.\"],\n[\"AUD-025\",\"Brain feed cursor recovery\",\"1) A surviving cursor could prevent refetching lost facts.\",\"2) The current reader demonstrably accepts a partial cache.\",\"1) The full sync consequence remains untested.\",\"2) Existing missing-cache-file work creates strict novelty risk.\",\"Prioritize validation\",\"Keep HOLD; demonstrate lost-fact recovery through a complete synthetic feed pull.\"],\n[\"AUD-026\",\"Same-repo URL fragments\",\"1) It violates the documented endpoint-identity guard.\",\"2) A focused fix can have clear regression controls.\",\"1) Fragment-bearing Git URLs are unusual.\",\"2) Reproduction establishes guard bypass, not destructive impact.\",\"Keep as small fix\",\"Preserve 16-Nov scoped READY only; refresh upstream/claims before implementation. Do not sell as a flagship or high-severity exploit.\"],\n[\"AUD-027\",\"Impossible ref prefixes\",\"1) Invalid configurations can appear to be healthy empty scopes.\",\"2) Early rejection gives callers an actionable error.\",\"1) Previous prefix-validation reports may encompass this extension.\",\"2) Prefixes are partial names, so full-ref validation can reject valid input.\",\"Park pending novelty\",\"Remain HOLD; first settle whether this is new and specify extendable-prefix grammar.\"],\n[\"AUD-028\",\"Stats-cache metadata collision\",\"1) Timestamp-preserving edits can retain an identical cache key.\",\"2) Stale statistics could mislead users if that workflow is supported.\",\"1) Metadata-based memoization is an intentional performance tradeoff.\",\"2) Rehashing gigabytes could cost more than the proposed correction saves.\",\"Park pending contract\",\"Remain HOLD; key equality alone is not proof of an intended freshness-contract violation.\"],\n[\"AUD-029\",\"Workspace Graph cancellation\",\"1) Background contexts detach probes from caller cancellation.\",\"2) Repeated member probes could magnify cancellation latency.\",\"1) No public-command cancellation failure was reproduced.\",\"2) Related workspace work already belongs to our #644 owner.\",\"Coordinate\",\"Remain HOLD; send no public claim and leave any implementation with the relevant owner after a real reproduction.\"],\n[\"AUD-030\",\"Blocked SSE cancellation\",\"1) Slow consumers can retain server resources.\",\"2) Bounded shutdown is a useful lifecycle invariant.\",\"1) A deliberately blocked writer is weaker evidence than a real socket test.\",\"2) Aggressive write deadlines can disconnect legitimate slow consumers.\",\"Validate conditionally\",\"Remain HOLD; require actual backpressure/disconnect/shutdown tests before choosing timeout behavior.\"],\n[\"AUD-031\",\"Review history after relocation\",\"1) Saved findings become hidden when their absolute path changes.\",\"2) A correct fix exercises stable worktree identity and migration.\",\"1) The test simulates path identity, rather than moving a real checkout.\",\"2) Relocation frequency and ambiguous old-path attribution are unproven.\",\"Validate conditionally\",\"Remain HOLD; exercise moved main clones and linked worktrees with no cross-worktree leakage.\"],\n[\"AUD-032\",\"Unusable --limit advice\",\"1) A recovery hint names a flag the list command rejects.\",\"2) It is a small, understandable user-facing correction.\",\"1) It carries limited engineering depth.\",\"2) The exact-source truncated-list command path still needs a fixture.\",\"Prioritize small validation\",\"Remain HOLD until current-source reproduction and novelty refresh; choose the smallest truthful correction.\"],\n[\"AUD-033\",\"Busy log follower cancellation\",\"1) The inner drain loop demonstrably continues after cancellation.\",\"2) Cancellation checks can likely remain small and localized.\",\"1) The probe forces sustained appends that may be rare with real logs.\",\"2) This is another edge in an already-known log-following area.\",\"Park as lower priority\",\"Remain HOLD; do not turn it into a separate flagship or inflate its scope.\"],\n[\"ENH-013\",\"Sparse/shallow clone options\",\"1) Smaller checkouts can reduce agent startup time and transfer.\",\"2) Existing Git mechanisms may supply most of the implementation.\",\"1) Entire server/helper support remains unverified.\",\"2) A handful of forwarded flags may be the whole useful feature.\",\"Narrow and validate\",\"Keep HOLD; test explicit clone options before designing named profiles or a hosted CloneKit service.\"],\n[\"ENH-014\",\"Incremental local reviews\",\"1) Repeated reviews could avoid unnecessary latency and model cost.\",\"2) A saved baseline can make the selected revision range explicit.\",\"1) Reviewing only a delta can miss interactions with earlier changes.\",\"2) Dirty files, rebases and existing scope/persistence work complicate correctness.\",\"Prioritize validation\",\"Keep HOLD; prove reduced work while preserving finding quality and required context.\"],\n[\"ENH-015\",\"Selective checkpoint assets\",\"1) Users can inspect actual screenshots and other stored assets.\",\"2) Selection can avoid full transcript export and base64 reinjection.\",\"1) No concrete consumer workflow was reproduced yet.\",\"2) Existing low-level Git access may suffice for occasional use.\",\"Prioritize validation\",\"Keep HOLD; demonstrate one supported artifact-retrieval workflow and preserve a small inspection/export scope.\"],\n[\"ENH-016\",\"Memory-ranking explanations\",\"1) It can explain why a useful memory was filtered or ranked poorly.\",\"2) It can support retrieval tuning without changing the scorer.\",\"1) It may mainly serve maintainers rather than ordinary users.\",\"2) A larger diagnostics surface adds maintenance and privacy obligations.\",\"Prioritize narrowly\",\"Keep HOLD; use one confusing query that current outputs cannot explain. Coordinate with ENH-004 scorer work and #595 provenance.\"],\n[\"ENH-017\",\"Perfetto hook timelines\",\"1) Real overlap information could expose concurrency bottlenecks.\",\"2) Standard viewers can make a complex trace easier to inspect.\",\"1) Existing duration traces already explain many slow hooks.\",\"2) New timestamps, tracks and export contracts add cost without a demonstrated unresolved case.\",\"Park\",\"Keep HOLD; move below the earlier shortlist until an actual diagnostic ambiguity is reproduced.\"],\n[\"ENH-018\",\"Paged Graph traversal\",\"1) Large hubs can be explored within a bounded context budget.\",\"2) Continuation avoids repeatedly returning earlier neighbors.\",\"1) Raising the existing limit may solve many cases more simply.\",\"2) Snapshot-bound cursors are difficult across changing working trees.\",\"Validate conditionally\",\"Keep HOLD; first prove a large-hub workflow, consider committed snapshots only, and coordinate with #407.\"],\n[\"ENH-019\",\"Saved latency histograms\",\"1) Distributions support valid combined percentile calculations.\",\"2) They could bound retention costs for long benchmark runs.\",\"1) ForgeMark already has live histograms.\",\"2) No repeated-run aggregation consumer or acceptable approximation contract was established.\",\"Park\",\"Keep HOLD; measure a concrete consumer and distinguish saved distributions from already-shipped live aggregation.\"],\n[\"ENH-020\",\"Git fault-scenario harness\",\"1) Reproducible faults can expose difficult recovery defects.\",\"2) Seeds and schedules can make failures easier to debug.\",\"1) Existing transport/integration tests may cover the necessary cases.\",\"2) A standalone scenario platform may exceed ForgeMark's product scope.\",\"Park as product feature\",\"Keep HOLD; start from an uncovered failure and a targeted regression test before proposing a reusable platform.\"],\n[\"ENH-021\",\"Change walkthrough artifacts\",\"1) Revision-bound explanations could help humans review large changes.\",\"2) Graph relations could supply grounded navigation and evidence.\",\"1) Entire already has adjacent onboarding/tour work.\",\"2) Much of the outcome may be achievable with an existing skill and report.\",\"Park\",\"Keep HOLD; establish a distinct change-review need and maintainer direction before adding core commands or UI.\"],\n[\"ENH-022\",\"Transfer bandwidth budgets\",\"1) Shared runners might need predictable network consumption.\",\"2) Cancellation-aware throttling could be reusable across transfers.\",\"1) Embedders can already inject an HTTP client.\",\"2) No actual constrained-network user or workload was established.\",\"Park\",\"Keep HOLD; prove a CLI/SSH consistency need that existing wrappers cannot meet.\"]\n];\nif(rows.length!==20||rows.some(r=>r.length!==8))throw Error(\"Bad assessment shape\");\nconst data={date:\"2026-11-17\",basis:\"Recorded 16-Nov evidence and latest local canonical tracker; no fresh upstream availability or competitor-capability claim.\",rule:\"Two supporting arguments cannot compensate for a failed legitimacy, scope or novelty gate. Prioritize means validate first, not implement.\",rows,columns:[\"id\",\"candidate\",\"support_1\",\"support_2\",\"challenge_1\",\"challenge_2\",\"assessment\",\"next_gate\"]};\nstore(\"two-by-two-assessment\",data);\nconst path=\"/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/two-by-two-2026-11-17.json\";\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat > '\"+path+\"' <<'TWO_BY_TWO_REVIEW_171126'\\n\"+JSON.stringify(data,null,2)+\"\\nTWO_BY_TWO_REVIEW_171126\",\"max_output_tokens\":30}));\ntext({assessed:20,prioritize:[\"AUD-024\",\"AUD-025\",\"AUD-026\",\"AUD-032\",\"ENH-013 (narrow)\",\"ENH-014\",\"ENH-015\",\"ENH-016\"],conditional:[\"AUD-029\",\"AUD-030\",\"AUD-031\",\"ENH-018\"],park:[\"AUD-027\",\"AUD-028\",\"AUD-033\",\"ENH-017\",\"ENH-019\",\"ENH-020\",\"ENH-021\",\"ENH-022\"]});\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1ea8f-4eae-75f2-adec-faef107733f4","create_time":1794936804.305522}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":582,"sampled_through_sequence":578,"client_authored":false}}
