{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T17:35:05.570Z","ordinal":3218,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0b823400861c2c3d016afc90370ad887d097609935836c4954","status":"completed","call_id":"call_91b514e5b6ac4fd9aefa13ef90ea215f","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"python3 - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nimport json\\nbase=Path('/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16');d=json.loads((base/'two-by-two-2026-11-17.json').read_text())\\ntext=['Twenty candidates: two supporting arguments and two challenges','17 November 2026','',d['basis'],d['rule'],'']\\nfor r in d['rows']:\\n text += [r[0]+' — '+r[1], 'Support: '+r[2]+' '+r[3], 'Challenge: '+r[4]+' '+r[5], 'Assessment: '+r[6], 'Remaining proof: '+r[7], '']\\n(base/'two-by-two-2026-11-17.txt').write_text('\\\\n'.join(text))\\ntracker=Path('/Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli/CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md')\\nheader='### Two-support / two-challenge assessment of the20 candidates — 17 November 2026'\\nif header in tracker.read_text():raise SystemExit('Assessment entry already exists; refusing duplicate append')\\nlines=['','',header,'',\\n'- User requests a legitimacy review of all20 new candidates using two supporting arguments and two challenges each. Re-read repository rules, canonical tracker/current ownership and retained Nov16 candidate/probe evidence. This is a product/engineering assessment of recorded evidence, not a fresh public availability audit, gate pass, implementation or publication request.',\\n'- Result: **8 worth prioritized validation (including one deliberately narrowed feature),4 conditional/coordination cases,8 parked from the active shortlist.** Park means our recommendation to defer, not user-dropped/obsolete/known duplicate. Retain all stable IDs and evidence; reconsider only with concrete missing proof. Supporting arguments do not offset a failed reproduction, intended-contract, necessary-scope or novelty gate.',\\n'', '| ID | Revised discovery priority | Required next evidence |','| --- | --- | --- |']\\nfor r in d['rows']:lines.append('| '+r[0]+' | '+r[6]+' | '+r[7]+' |')\\nlines += ['',\\n'- Strongest feature-validation targets: ENH-014 incremental review, ENH-015 selected asset extraction, ENH-016 ranking explanations. ENH-013 should first be a small set of verified Git clone options, not presumed named profiles/a new clone service. ENH-018 stays conditional: show that raising --limit is inadequate, consider committed snapshots first and respect#407 ownership.',\\n'- **Assessment correction:** move ENH-017 below the earlier top feature shortlist. Existing duration traces may already solve the diagnostic need; accurate timelines require additional instrumentation and have no demonstrated unresolved user case yet. ENH-019/020/021/022 also remain parked until actual aggregation/scenario/change-review/network constraints justify core features over existing histograms/tests/skills/client wrappers. Existing tools or competitor precedent alone are insufficient product need.',\\n'- Bug priorities: validate AUD-024/AUD-025 and the small AUD-032 correction. AUD-026 retains only its dated16Nov scoped READY record; this assessment does not refresh its availability or establish destructive impact. AUD-029 is coordination with existing workspace owner, not a new competing implementation. AUD-030 needs real sockets rather than only the blocked-writer mechanism; AUD-031 needs actual moved checkout/worktree tests. AUD-027 novelty/prefix grammar, AUD-028 intended metadata-cache freshness and AUD-033 normal-workload frequency remain unresolved.',\\n'- Full80-argument assessment with remaining proof: `/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/two-by-two-2026-11-17.txt` and structured JSON beside it. No production source/test changes, test reruns, remote messages, commit/push/issue/PR changes or paid execution. Preserve main replay staging/config/AGENTS symlink, ENH-004 owner and existing #3174/#3175 refinement ownership. Formal HOLDs unchanged; no new READY grants.',\\n'']\\nwith tracker.open('a') as f:f.write('\\\\n'.join(lines))\\nassert len(d['rows'])==20\\nassert len({r[0] for r in d['rows']})==20\\nprint('Saved all80 arguments and appended dated prioritization without changing implementation gates.')\\nPY\\ngit status --short\\nreadlink AGENTS.md\",\"max_output_tokens\":300}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1ea8f-4eae-75f2-adec-faef107733f4","create_time":1794936887.054649}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":586,"sampled_through_sequence":583,"client_authored":false}}
