{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T18:32:32.371Z","ordinal":3252,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1eac8-376f-7d83-bc02-19085af0c1e2","call_id":"call_20SdTbnHsUEuGcAIvYSawjPn","output":"Chunk ID: ed75cb\nWall time: 0.0867 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 4575\nOutput:\nWarning: truncated output (original token count: 4575)\nTotal output lines: 280\n\n# Entire CLI — repository instructions\n\nGo CLI built with Cobra and Charmbracelet Huh. `AGENTS.md` is a symlink to this\nfile. Keep this entry point short: repo-wide rules and pointers, not command\ncatalogs, implementation histories, or subsystem specifications.\n\n## Project map\n\n- `cmd/entire/`: entry point and external-command dispatch.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/`: Cobra commands, group roots, and CLI helpers. Group/verb files\n  use `<noun>_group.go` and `<noun>_<verb>.go`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/`: built-in agent integrations and external-agent protocol.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/`: manual-commit strategy and lifecycle/git hooks.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/`: persistent checkpoint storage (written at commit).\n- `cmd/entire/cli/session/`: session state shared across worktrees.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/`: simulated-hook integration tests.\n- `e2e/`: real-agent tests and deterministic Vogon canary.\n- `internal/entireclient/`: API clients, authentication, and user directories.\n\nUse the Go version pinned by `go.mod` and tools configured in `mise.toml`.\nFor installed CLI usage, run `entire agent-help`, then\n`entire agent-help <command>` for current flags; do not guess from a static list.\n\n## Read when relevant\n\nRead the applicable reference **before changing that area**, not every reference\nat session start. Follow its related links when the task crosses those boundaries.\n\n| Area being changed | Reference |\n| --- | --- |\n| Commands, help, experimental visibility, repo refs, prompts | [CLI conventions](docs/development/cli-conventions.md) |\n| Test harnesses, isolation, TTY behavior, source guards | [Testing](docs/development/testing.md) |\n| Filesystem I/O, `.entire`, symlinks, hook configs, root anchors | [Filesystem safety](docs/development/filesystem-safety.md) |\n| Git operations, executable lookup, subprocesses, Windows launching | [Git and subprocess safety](docs/development/git-safety.md) |\n| Caller identification or session current/tokens/adopt | [Caller-session resolution](docs/development/caller-session-resolution.md) |\n| Control-plane auth or data-plane routing | [API routing](docs/development/api-routing.md) |\n| Checkpoint writes, lifecycle, sync, settings trust, redaction | [Implementation contracts](docs/development/checkpoint-implementation.md), [domain model](docs/architecture/sessions-and-checkpoints.md), [scenarios](docs/architecture/checkpoint-scenarios.md) |\n| Ref-based checkpoint backend | [Ref backend](docs/architecture/ref-checkpoint-backend.md) |\n| Agent integrations | [Agent guide](docs/architecture/agent-guide.md), [integration checklist](docs/architecture/agent-integration-checklist.md) |\n| External commands or agents | [External commands](docs/architecture/external-commands.md), [agent protocol](docs/architecture/external-agent-protocol.md) |\n| Security, privacy, scanners | [Security and privacy](docs/security-and-privacy.md), [implementation contracts](docs/development/checkpoint-implementation.md) |\n| Review command | [Review architecture](docs/architecture/review-command.md) |\n| Release artifacts, install scripts, version-check origins | [Release origins](docs/architecture/release-origins.md) |\n| E2E tests | [E2E guide](e2e/README.md) |\n| Complexity/coverage measurement and the CI complexity gate | [Complexity tooling](tools/complexity/README.md) |\n\n## Verification\n\n| Task | Command / requirement |\n| --- | --- |\n| Unit tests | `mise run test` |\n| Integration tests | `mise run test:integration`; required when changing integration test code |\n| Deterministic E2E canary | `mise run test:e2e:canary`; safe without API calls |\n| All CI tests | `mise run test:ci` (unit + integration + canary) |\n| Format and lint | `mise run fmt && mise run lint` |\n| Before every commit | **`mise run check`** (format, lint, all CI tests) |\n| Before any push or remote code update | **`mise run lint` on the current tree**, after the latest formatting pass |\n| After every push to an open PR | **check the trail's findings** (`entire trail finding list cli/<n> --freshness any`; `<n>` is the PR branch's cli trail number, not the PR number); fix real ones, resolve with `-m`, and re-check after the fix lands. Not done until findings are clear |\n| Duplication checks | `mise run dup` or `mise run dup:staged`; normal lint also checks duplication |\n| Complexity gate | `mise run complexity:gate`; CI fails a PR on functions over cognitive complexity 30 that are new or worsened against the merge base. The threshold is a gate flag (`COGNIT_WARN`), not a `.golangci.yaml` setting |\n| Windows installer | `mise run test:ps1`; see testing reference for prerequisites |\n\n**Do not run real-agent E2E tests unless the user explicitly requests them.** They\nmake paid API calls. Vogon is the exception: its canary is deterministic and free.\nWhen changing E2E prompt wording, run the canary and update Vogon's regex parsing\nif needed. Formatting can rewrite files; an earlier lint pass is not sufficient.\n\nBefore implementing Go code, s…8296 chars truncated…ile\nonly for repository-wide development rules or routing links. Preserve safety\ncontracts in references and regression tests rather than accumulating incident\nnarratives here. Prefer existing docs over a second account of the same behavior.\n\nThe root-file budget is **20 KiB**, enforced alongside local documentation links\nby `go test ./docs/development`. Extract specialized material instead of expanding\nthat budget. Do not require every linked document\nto be loaded on every task. Keep `AGENTS.md` as the symlink to this file.\n     884 CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md\n1:# Entire contribution tracker\n8:## Start here\n25:## Mandatory decision table — three gates before starting\n75:### Verification scope for this gate pass\n84:## Status and evidence rules\n97:## Concrete findings: work done, ownership and disposition\n128:## Existing larger issues considered\n139:## Other contributors' work and explicit exclusions\n166:## Team / assigned umbrella issues from earlier research\n181:## Earlier proposals: retain decisions, do not recycle as new bugs\n193:## Evidence files and preserved local work\n214:## Cross-chat work log\n227:## AUD-016 fresh gate check — 6 November 2026\n237:## Scheduled contribution batch and commit policy\n260:## Updating this tracker\n269:## Discovery from other chats\n275:## Change log\n286:## AUD-006 implementation gate refresh — 6 November 2026\n295:### AUD-006 implementation progress — 6 November 2026\n309:## AUD-019 implementation gate refresh — 6 November 2026\n317:### AUD-006 publication requested — 6 November 2026\n325:### Scheduled coordinator recovery — 6 November 2026, ~07:14 IST\n332:### AUD-019 resumed recovery — 6 November 2026\n348:### AUD-019 verification complete / explicit exception required — 6 November 2026\n355:### Scheduled coordinator: baseline-exception handoff — 6 November 2026, ~07:50 IST\n360:## Hiring strategy discussion — 13 November 2026\n368:### Hiring strategy correction — 13 November 2026\n374:## Cross-repository enhancement audit — 13 November 2026\n378:### Scope and freshness\n386:### New enhancement decisions\n396:### Eliminate these as new enhancement ideas\n409:### ENH-001 versus Brain #277 — explicit recheck, 13 November 2026\n416:## INT-001 — LegionCode / Entire integration strategy — 13 November 2026\n427:### INT-001 integration precedent follow-up — 13 November 2026\n433:### ENH-001 implementation ownership and refreshed gates — 13 November 2026\n443:### Scheduled coordinator deleted — 13 November 2026\n463:### ENH-001 completed locally — 13 November 2026\n472:## Four additional large-feature proposals — 13 November 2026\n485:### Explicit exclusions from this large-feature pass\n496:### ENH-001 publication authorized — 14 November 2026\n509:## New capabilities above the November launches — 14 November 2026\n522:### What can already be used, rather than proposed again\n528:### Supplemental performance probe, outside the clarified feature request\n536:### ENH-001 published — 14 November 2026\n544:## Product-fit correction and ENH-009 dropped — 14 November 2026\n554:## ENH-004–007 product-fit reassessment — 14 November 2026\n569:### ENH-001 memory follow-up owned — 14 November 2026\n576:## Private maintainer review — 14 November 2026\n585:### Private maintainer review completed — 14 November 2026\n610:### ENH-001 memory acceptance published — 14 November 2026\n619:### Private review recheck of Brain #644 — 14 November 2026\n628:### AUD-001 replay claim independently rechecked — 14 November 2026\n636:### AUD-001 cumulative replay correction started — 14 November 2026\n643:### ENH-004 competitor indexing research — 14 November 2026\n655:### ENH-004 implementation handoff plan written — 14 November 2026\n666:### AUD-001 cumulative replay correction validation in progress — 14 November 2026\n674:### ENH-004 gate refresh in progress — 15 November 2026\n682:### AUD-001 correction ready; baseline exception required — 15 November 2026\n695:### ENH-004 research complete; implementation remains HOLD — 15 November 2026\n706:### ENH-004 practical-workflow search resumed — 15 November 2026\n711:### ENH-004 public practical case reproduced — 15 November 2026\n719:### ENH-004 status clarified and replay count corrected — 16 November 2026\n726:### ENH-004 renewed completion work and fresh sources — 16 November 2026\n735:### Workflow-led enhancement discovery — 16 November 2026\n746:### ENH-004 READY for local implementation — 16 November 2026\n761:### ENH-004 local implementation and first executable proof — 16 November 2026\n769:### Ten further issues and ten enhancements — competitor-informed discovery, 16 November 2026\n807:### ENH-004 implementation convergence and stronger crash proof — 16 November 2026\n816:### Private review of existing OpenCode-created PRs #3174 / #3175 — 17 November 2026\n825:### Existing PR refinement authorized — 17 November 2026\n835:### Two-support / two-challenge assessment of the20 candidates — 17 November 2026\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1eac6-41d3-7143-a221-cf44a37b6525","create_time":1794940352.36751}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":600,"sampled_through_sequence":597,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":3000}}
