{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T18:32:44.200Z","ordinal":3260,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1eac6-41d3-7143-a221-cf44a37b6525","session_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","root_turn_id":"01a1eac6-41d3-7143-a221-cf44a37b6525","response_id":"resp_05a7fc4dc4b68e03016afc9dc7781887d09595b54565a56e4f","usage":{"input_tokens":120134,"cached_input_tokens":117504,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":67,"reasoning_output_tokens":0,"total_tokens":120201},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":761919,"cached_input_tokens":249216,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":7283,"reasoning_output_tokens":0,"total_tokens":769202},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":60037631,"cached_input_tokens":57258368,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":238779,"reasoning_output_tokens":96130,"total_tokens":60276410}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T18:32:44.619Z","ordinal":3261,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1eac6-41d3-7143-a221-cf44a37b6525","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"call_9DxIPN53XBJ2223eaKC076vm","process_id":"23003","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '68,143p' CLAUDE.md; sed -n '1,100p;237,269p;735,746p;769,884p' CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '68,143p' CLAUDE.md","name":"CLAUDE.md","path":"CLAUDE.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"Before implementing Go code, search nearby packages and helpers for reusable\npatterns. Use `/go:discover-related` when available, otherwise `rg` and related\nimplementations/tests. Check `.golangci.yaml`; handle errors and avoid duplication.\n\n## Test safety\n\n- Every top-level test and subtest calls `t.Parallel()` unless it changes\n  process-global state (`t.Chdir`, `t.Setenv`, or their `os` equivalents).\n- Git tests use isolated temporary repositories, preferably\n  `testutil.InitRepo(t, dir)` plus its file/add/commit helpers. Redirect CWD before\n  calling CWD-based handlers. Never mutate the real checkout's git/session state.\n- Tests must not access the developer's real config, cache, or keychain.\n  In-process fallbacks are shared per process; use per-test overrides and\n  `tokenstore.UseFileBackendForTesting` when isolation between tests is needed.\n  Tests that can reach the OS keyring need `keyring.MockInit()` in `TestMain`.\n- Spawned binaries do not inherit Go's test detection. Harnesses must isolate\n  `ENTIRE_CONFIG_DIR`, `XDG_CACHE_HOME`, `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file`,\n  `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE_PATH`, and `ENTIRE_TEST_AUTH_STORE_FILE`.\n- Prefer `execx.NonInteractive` for real CLI/git test subprocesses so a developer's\n  terminal cannot make them prompt or hang.\n- Caller-resolution tests clear every variable from `agent.CallerSessionEnvVars()`;\n  never hand-maintain a partial list or inherit the developer's agent identity.\n- Source-scanning guards discover files through testutil's guard helpers\n  (`GitGrepGuard`, `GuardGoFiles`), restrict pathspecs to Go files, and fail on\n  zero matches. Do not weaken guard ledgers to silence failures.\n\n## Filesystem and settings safety\n\n**Use the existing anchor for each tree; never assemble a path and perform bare\nI/O beneath it.** Read the filesystem reference before adding or changing I/O.\n\n| Tree | Canonical owner |\n| --- | --- |\n| `.entire` | `entiredir` |\n| Git common directory | `gitdir` |\n| Working tree | `worktreedir` |\n| Agent hook configuration | `agent.HookConfigFile` |\n| Agent session store | `agent.SessionStore` |\n| Active git hooks directory | `strategy.hooksRootForInstall` / `ForRemoval` |\n| Per-user config/cache | `userdirs.ConfigRoot` / `CacheRoot` |\n| Managed plugins | `pluginRoot` |\n\n- Root bases come from trusted resolvers, **not `filepath.Dir(target)`**. Confining\n  a file to its own derived parent proves nothing. Prefer an existing anchor.\n- Roots share the `osroot.Shared` registry. Open child roots with\n  `osroot.SharedChild` / `OpenChild`, not bare `parent.OpenRoot`.\n- Use `osroot` operations and `jsonutil.WriteFileAtomicIn` / `CreateTempIn`.\n  Directories use `MkdirAllNoSymlink`; rooted read-only operations must also\n  enforce symlink policy. Atomic writes replace leaf links rather than follow them.\n- `.entire` must be a real directory; validate through\n  `paths.ValidateEntireDirAt` / `RequireEntireDir`. Do not treat an unresolved\n  repository as absent. Settings reads must also refuse symlinks themselves.\n- Do not broaden symlink exceptions. Developer-vouched agent config directories\n  are scoped, locally trusted exceptions; `.entire` and git hooks are not vouchable.\n- `entiredir.OpenForRead` must not create directories. Reset cached roots before\n  deleting/recreating their directories. Use `entiredir.Name` / `MustName` to\n  bridge repo-relative constants and root-relative I/O names.\n- All settings access goes through `settings`; never read or parse settings JSON\n  ad hoc. Per-user config/cache resolution belongs only to `userdirs`.\n- Repository-controlled settings must not authorize executable discovery, custom\n  executables, or instructions for permission-bypassed agents. Preserve the\n  existing local-provenance gates and their rejection reporting.\n- Existing exceptions (explicit user paths, global git config, transcript-read\n  protocol gaps) are documented in the references; do not generalize them.\n\n## Git and subprocess safety\n\n- Open repositories only through `gitrepo.OpenCurrent(ctx)` or\n  `gitrepo.OpenPath(root)`, never direct go-git opens. This preserves alternates\n  and reftable support. Do not fall back to CWD after failed repo resolution.\n- Use `gitrepo.Status`, never `worktree.Status()`. Agent-hook capture paths use\n  `StatusWithBudget` and preserve degraded-capture reporting on budget exhaustion.\n- Every `git status` subprocess passes **`--no-optional-locks`**. This does not\n  protect worktree-comparing `git diff` from refreshing the index; use the\n  hook-safe alternatives in the git reference.\n- Use the git CLI, not go-git v5, for checkout and hard reset; go-git can delete\n# Entire contribution tracker\n\nPersonal, shared project record for Puneet's Entire contributions. Created 6 November 2026 from the earlier audits and our decisions. **Assembly date is not verification date.** Public statuses below are dated snapshots; recheck before starting work.\n\nCanonical file: `/Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli/CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md`.\nAll project chats and worktrees should read and update this file rather than maintain separate copies. This is local coordination material, excluded from Git; it is not part of the upstream contribution.\n\n## Start here\n\n| Priority | Local ID | Decision | Next action |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Scheduled priority 1 | AUD-019 | **IMPLEMENTED LOCALLY; pending baseline-test exception.** See the existing worker's final 6 November record. | Continue the same owner after required input; do not create another implementation chat. |\n| Scheduled priority 2 | AUD-020 | Cross-backend fallback returns the wrong session. **READY in scoped checks.** | Start only after priority 1 completes or fails a gate. |\n| Scheduled priority 3 | AUD-021 | Exact session cleanup plus linear stale sweep. **READY in scoped checks.** | Start only after prior queued work completes or fails a gate. |\n| Alternate target, outside scheduled batch | AUD-006 | Idle MCP server ignores cancellation; real CLI SIGTERM case reproduced. **READY** after scoped three-gate check. | Local fix in MCP shutdown chat/worktree; see cross-chat log and validation limits. |\n| Second verification target | AUD-009 | SSE cursor-only/reset failures reproduced; server contract still unverified. | **HOLD.** Verify practical contract before implementing. |\n| Focused fallback | AUD-005 | Failed bundle overwrites existing output; freshly reproduced. | **HOLD.** Useful focused fix, not a cleared senior flagship; novelty review incomplete. |\n| Existing contribution — review only | AUD-001 | Our replay fix is implemented; PR #3015 is still open and unmerged, verified 13 November. | Continue the existing PR. Do not open another issue or PR for it. |\n| Enhancement published; outside scheduled bug-fix batch | ENH-001 | Brain workspace retrieval: measured serial scaling and ignored cancellation. **CONTINUE OUR PR — #644**, 14 November. | [Issue #643](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/issues/643), [PR #644](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/644). Six checked commits; final memory target PASS (83.42 MiB peak). Remote CI awaits maintainer approval; trail findings unavailable. Existing bug-fix batch unchanged. |\n| Stop new work / duplicate risk | AUD-016 | Real, substantial bug, but **already reported exactly** in #2696's review. User also reports an existing PR. | Fails the novelty gate. Retain the record of Puneet's work; do not start another implementation. A separate exact fixing PR has not been independently identified. |\n| Hold — feature withdrawal proposed | AUD-017 | Cursor permission bug freshly reproduced at current upstream on 6 November. | Open #2615 proposes removing the entire affected package. Do not start before ownership/direction is resolved. |\n| Hold — feature withdrawal proposed | AUD-018 | Cursor attribution cost measured; code still present. | Open #2615 proposes removing the package. Do not start an optimization that conflicts with that work. |\n| Excluded | AUD-002 | User confirmed another contributor already has a summary-target PR. | Add the exact PR link when identified; do not pick it up as ours. |\n\n## Mandatory decision table — three gates before starting\n\n**User rule, 6 November 2026: start a new implementation only after all three gates pass.** Unknown, conditional, stale, or not checked does not mean pass. Previous words such as “candidate” or “available” in historical evidence below are not permission to start.\n\n1. **Legitimate:** reproduce a current failure against the intended contract, or measure a meaningful performance problem. An intentional behavior, hypothetical concern, or missing field alone does not pass.\n2. **Substantial / senior scope:** identify the actual engineering judgment involved: failure atomicity, concurrency, identity, privacy boundaries, scaling or lifecycle ownership. Assess the necessary solution, not an artificially enlarged patch. A useful focused fix can still fail our present flagship-selection goal; that says nothing about its author's seniority.\n3. **New and clear to work on:** check issues, all-state PRs, bodies, comments, inline review findings, prototypes, claims and relevant changed files. An existing exact report fails the user's strict new-issue requirement even if unfixed. An issue-only pickup requires an explicit later decision from the user. Adjacent work is not automatically an exact duplicate, but unresolved overlap is a hold.\n\nOnly **READY** means all three passed with dated evidence. **CONTINUE OUR PR** applies to work already published by us; it is not a new-work approval. **HOLD** permits research/verification, not a production implementation. **SKIP** records a failed gate. The latest deep pass cleared **AUD-019, AUD-020 and AUD-021** as the scheduled three-item queue, subject to fresh gate checks. AUD-006 is an alternate previously cleared target, not one of this batch’s three. AUD-009 and AUD-005 remain held.\n\nLatest deep-audit upstream: `aa0c90c9770a460092103214b608247a8b2623ae`, 6 November 2026. The earlier gate pass used `3c299b94f8595bdfc3aa2ecdc0bd199d856f15a2`. The older evidence retains its original dates; this pass did not rerun every historical reproduction.\n\n| ID / finding | 1. Legitimate issue? | 2. Substantial senior scope? | 3. New / already raised or worked on? | Decision / missing proof |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| AUD-001 — replay loses sessions | **PASS:** reproduced; our fix already exists. | **PASS:** cross-clone identity, checked merge, queue/CAS safety. | **EXISTING OUR WORK:** [#3014](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/3014), [#3015](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3015), still open on 6 November. | **CONTINUE OUR PR.** No duplicate issue/PR. |\n| AUD-002 — summary targets another session | **PASS on 3 November:** deterministic reproduction; not refreshed today. | **PASS in scoped design:** source identity and concurrent storage update. | **FAIL:** user confirmed somebody else's PR; exact link still unknown. | **SKIP.** Do not override the user's ownership correction because a search is inconclusive. |\n| AUD-003 — runner tailoring overwrite | **FAIL as current candidate:** feature removed. | Not evaluated further. | **FAIL:** merged [#2946](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2946) removed the feature. | **SKIP — obsolete.** |\n| AUD-004 — staged filename corruption | **PENDING:** older audit; affected file unchanged through current upstream. No fresh runtime test today. | **FOCUSED:** parser/filename fidelity; no demonstrated wider design problem. | **NOT CLEARED:** no exact match in targeted searches; [#1573 review](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1573#discussion_r3495312963) reports a different CRLF problem, and #2586 changes a different parser. | **HOLD / lower priority.** Refresh test; do not inflate parser work into a flagship. |\n| AUD-005 — bundle truncates existing archive | **PASS:** current-upstream refusal changed a 25-byte existing output into a 22-byte empty ZIP. | **FOCUSED:** useful atomic-output/data-preservation work; not established as a senior flagship. | **NOT CLEARED:** no exact targeted match found; originating #1061 inline-review access returned connector 403. | **HOLD / focused fallback.** Not approved under all three gates. |\n| AUD-006 — idle MCP cancellation | **PASS:** current-upstream pipe test blocks after cancellation; real CLI answers ping, survives first SIGTERM with stdin open, exits on second. | **PASS, scoped judgment:** safe shutdown, input ownership, reader/goroutine lifetime and platform behavior; do not expand into an MCP rewrite. | **PASS in dated checks:** no exact report/fix found; introducing #1585 inline review (six comments) and discussion checked, plus targeted issue/all-state PR searches. Not a reservation. | **IMPLEMENTED LOCALLY after refreshed gates.** MCP tests/signal smoke pass; see validation limits and worktree log. Recheck ownership before publishing. |\n| AUD-007 — copy-truncated log follow | **PENDING:** source unchanged; no fresh runtime reproduction today. | **FOCUSED:** offset/rotation handling. | **NOT CLEARED:** no exact match found in targeted search; review coverage incomplete. | **HOLD / lower priority.** |\n| AUD-008 — insertion into empty file | **PENDING:** depends on supported server anchor contract. | **FOCUSED / UNCLEAR:** no broader apply-transaction failure demonstrated. | **NOT CLEARED:** adjacent #2984; no exact anchor fix identified. | **HOLD.** Contract and reproduction first. |\n| AUD-009 — SSE ID-only / empty ID reset | **PASS for parser behavior:** two current-upstream failures match standard SSE cursor cases. Entire server use of these frames is not verified. | **POSSIBLE:** protocol/reconnect correctness; confirm practical contract and impact first. | **NOT FULLY CLEARED:** no exact match found; relevant #1177/#1447/#1522/#1949/#2507 reviews checked. Earlier EOF findings are different. | **HOLD — rank 2 for validation**, not permission to implement. |\n| AUD-010 — SSE JSON precision | **PENDING:** decode/re-encode path unchanged; fresh runtime check not run. | **FOCUSED:** numeric passthrough fidelity. | **NOT CLEARED:** no exact targeted search match; inline-review coverage incomplete. | **HOLD / lower priority.** |\n| AUD-011 — api -F precision | **PENDING:** numeric fallback unchanged; accepted CLI value contract unverified. | **FOCUSED:** value coercion. | **NOT CLEARED:** no exact targeted search match; inline-review coverage incomplete. | **HOLD / lower priority.** |\n| AUD-012 — recursive token subtraction | **PENDING:** no demonstrated reachable exhaustion case; recursive data alone is insufficient. | **UNCLEAR:** a reachable accounting invariant could be substantial; a hypothetical depth cap is not enough. | **HOLD:** overlapping #2155/#2825/#2782; exact fix not established. | **HOLD.** Reachability, impact and coordination first. |\n| AUD-013 — stale semantic-search response | **PENDING:** generation gap remains; fresh out-of-order test needed. | **FOCUSED:** ordinary stale UI response guard unless wider request-lifecycle failure is shown. | **NOT CLEARED:** no exact targeted match; introducing-review coverage incomplete. | **HOLD /