 enhancement:** baseline cost reproduced; no production-user frequency or optimization speedup established. | **PASS if needed:** bounded indexing with equivalent permission/duplicate semantics and scaling proof. | **HOLD:** no exact index implementation found, but open [#2615](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2615) proposes removing the affected package. | **HOLD — avoid optimizing a package proposed for removal.** Same component as AUD-017. |\n| AUD-019 — cleanup deletes a new turn’s staged copy | **PASS:** actual CondenseSessionByID interleaving loses newly published full.jsonl while newer pending state survives. | **PASS, scoped judgment:** generation-aware publication/cleanup and state persistence across concurrent hooks. | **PASS in scoped checks:** no exact issue/fix found; #2692 reviews and adjacent #2754/#2867 patches checked. Those do not close this window. | **READY — scheduled priority 1.** Recheck gates before implementation/publishing. |\n| AUD-020 — fallback substitutes a different session | **PASS:** real Git stores and an actually absent transcript blob yield metadata for ref-session but content for legacy-session at slot 1, with no error. | **PASS:** stable identity/provenance across partial-clone failures and backend coexistence. | **PASS in scoped checks:** #1630’s fallback requirement is a different case; no exact report/fix found. | **READY — scheduled priority 2.** Preserve genuine absent-checkpoint fallback. |\n| AUD-021 — identity-safe, linear session cleanup | **PASS:** both clear APIs delete valid chat.child when clearing chat; 2,000 stale sessions benchmark at 3.42–3.45 s and ~764–765 MB cumulative allocation. | **PASS for this combined scope:** session ownership, two clear paths, on-disk compatibility and quadratic sweep work share the directory-wide matching helper. | **PASS in scoped checks:** #1365 reports glob expansion, #2232 locking, not these dotted-ID and inventory-traversal cases. No exact implementation found. | **READY — scheduled priority 3.** One coherent cleanup PR, not two padded contributions. |\n| AUD-022 — task-ID collisions across parents | **PASS storage reproduction**, but current native producer frequency unverified. | Potential identity/schema problem; scope unagreed. | **HOLD:** active #2131 validates duplicate task IDs and changes merging. | **COORDINATE / SKIP as a clean pickup.** Do not duplicate that work. |\n| EXT-001 — config-based hooks | Supported feature request; no failure reproduced by us. | Potentially substantial migration/mixed-version work. | **FAIL strict novelty:** existing [#2580](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2580); adjacent #2388. | **EXISTING-ISSUE BACKLOG**, not new work approval. |\n| EXT-002 — pre-flight context metadata | **PENDING:** product contract, not demonstrated defect. | Potentially substantial schema work; direction unagreed. | **FAIL strict novelty:** existing [#763](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/763). | **DESIGN / EXISTING-ISSUE BACKLOG.** |\n| EXT-003 — checkpoint push blocks code push | **PENDING:** existing report; no independent reproduction by us. | Potentially substantial delivery/lifecycle design. | **FAIL strict novelty:** [#2794](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2794), active #2715. | **COORDINATE**, not new work approval. |\n| EXT-004 — winget | **PENDING:** live catalog not verified. | Packaging scope; insufficient demonstrated systems-design work for this goal. | **FAIL strict novelty:** existing [#1304](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/1304). | **BACKLOG**, not new work approval. |\n| OWN-001 through OWN-020 | Historical reports; not all independently reproduced or freshly rechecked. | Not reassessed after failing ownership/novelty. | **FAIL / HOLD:** existing reports, claims, prototypes, PRs, superseded paths or non-CLI scope; individual links/reasons below. | **SKIP / COORDINATE** as individually recorded. None READY. |\n| TEAM-001 through TEAM-008 | Existing team/assigned umbrellas; no independent current reproduction by us. | Some substantial, but umbrella size alone is not a contribution scope. | **FAIL:** already filed/assigned or implementation exists; links below. | **SKIP wholesale pickup.** None READY. |\n| IDEA-001 — discovery scaling | **PENDING:** no precise remaining measured regression. | Potentially substantial if a real scaling invariant is shown. | **NOT CLEARED:** merged #1771/#1956 and related discovery work. | **PARKED.** |\n| IDEA-002 — overlap warnings | **FAIL:** no accepted problem; user rejected the product behavior. | Not evaluated further. | Not evaluated after user rejection. | **DROPPED BY USER.** |\n| IDEA-003 — durable handoff segments | **PENDING:** desired product/schema contract unconfirmed. | Potentially substantial; that does not establish need. | **NOT CLEARED:** no fresh novelty/ownership audit. | **DESIGN ONLY.** |\n| IDEA-004 — immutable review snapshot | **FAIL:** no accepted failure case; user rejected proposal. | Not evaluated further. | Not evaluated after user rejection. | **DROPPED BY USER.** |\n| IDEA-005 — native dispatch local | **PENDING:** disputed hypothesis, no supported reproduction. | Unknown. | **NOT CLEARED.** | **PARKED.** |\n| IDEA-006 — temporary checkpoint inspection | **PENDING:** may conflict with intentional state-only turn-end model. | Unknown until product contract is established. | **NOT CLEARED:** #1139 is a different migration problem. | **PARKED.** |\n| IDEA-007 — ref-write generation races | Existing publicly demonstrated work; not a new bug established here. | Substantial concurrency work, already undertaken. | **FAIL:** #2876/#2131/#2550. | **OTHER CONTRIBUTORS' WORK.** |\n\n### Verification scope for this gate pass\n\n- Fetched current upstream SHA, current #3015/#2696/#2638/#2952/#2615 metadata, all returned inline comments on #2696/#2638/#2952/#1572/#1573/#2090/#1177/#1522, and targeted all-state PR and issue searches for each concrete finding. Some broad searches exceeded one page or were noisy; those are **not cleared**, not proof of absence.\n- Compared affected candidate files from `711697ee5` to `3c299b94f`: the checked files are unchanged except help wording in `trail_watch_cmd.go`. Source equality preserves the old hypothesis, not a fresh runtime reproduction.\n- Re-ran AUD-017's isolated permission reproduction on an exported current-upstream tree. It failed on the two expected ownership assertions; the permission precondition was enforced, not skipped. Existing Cursor scope controls passed separately. Synthetic performance baseline was rerun once; this is not an end-to-end production workload.\n- Cursor's #2638 inline review report concerns collision-walk uncertainty in `cursor.go`; AUD-017 concerns session evidence in `cursor_chats.go`. They share a safety principle but are not claimed to be identical implementations. #2615's proposed package removal is the immediate reason to hold both Cursor candidates.\n- An exact old review report does **not** prove a current fixing PR exists or the bug is fixed. AUD-016 remains reproduced; it fails the user's strict novelty gate regardless. A separate exact fixing PR remains unidentified in this audit.\n- No new production implementation, issue, PR, commit or push was made. This tracker no longer recommends starting any historical candidate without clearing the missing gates.\n\n## Status and evidence rules\n\n- **OURS / PR OPEN**: we implemented it and have a public PR. This does not mean merged or accepted.\n- **REPRODUCED**: a focused failing safety-contract test exists at the recorded revision. Test-only work is not an implemented fix.\n- **BENCHMARKED**: current cost was measured; no optimized implementation or speedup is implied.\n- **SOURCE CHECKED**: affected source was inspected; no fresh runtime reproduction is claimed for that date.\n- **TAKEN**: an explicit claim, prototype or PR exists. An issue does not become available merely because GitHub shows no linked PR.\n- **COORDINATE**: related work or a reporter-led proposal exists; it is not proof someone fixed the exact defect.\n- **DESIGN / UNCONFIRMED**: a proposal or disputed hypothesis, not a confirmed bug.\n- **SKIP / DROPPED / OBSOLETE**: retain the reason; do not rediscover and recommend it as new.\n\n“No exact public match found” is limited to the searches documented in the evidence reports. It is not a reservation, assignment, maintainer approval or proof of no private work. Public GitHub association is not employment verification. Local IDs are stable tracker IDs, not GitHub issue numbers.\n\n## Concrete findings: work done, ownership and disposition\n\nIDs AUD-001 through AUD-015 preserve the numbering of the 3 November report. Dates are evidence dates, not automatic freshness guarantees. “Us” means Puneet's local research/implementation, not public ownership of unfiled candidates.\n\n## Scheduled contribution batch and commit policy\n\nUser authorized on 6 November 2026: create separate chats to complete and raise three vetted contributions, one at a time, and resume those chats after usage limits restore. Initial queue: **AUD-019 → AUD-020 → AUD-021**. Each must pass fresh legitimacy, substantial engineering scope and exact novelty/ownership checks before production implementation and again before filing. Skip an existing exact issue, PR, inline report or claimed prototype; never duplicate another contributor. If any queued item fails, record it and select the next truly eligible substantial item rather than force a third PR.\n\nWork through one active implementation chat at a time. Record each chat ID/host, branch/worktree, stage, next command, tests and issue/PR/trail links here. Continue the same chat after rate limits, rather than making duplicate chats for the same item. Do not resume work the user paused/cancelled or a chat waiting for required approval/input. The user authorizes continuation messages to the implementation chats created for this batch; unrelated project chats are outside this authorization.\n\n- **Batch execution permissions (user authorized 6 November):** start new contribution chats with Full Access and command approval `never` (`sandbox_mode = \"danger-full-access\"`, `approval_policy = \"never\"`). The trusted main Entire checkout has these project-local defaults in `.codex/config.toml`; global defaults and unrelated projects are unchanged. This is a tracked file with a local-only override: never stage/commit/push its permission lines in a contribution PR. Carry the local override to isolated checkouts if needed, separately from production changes. The scheduler/create-thread tools expose no permission arguments; inspect each worker's actual runtime permissions after launch/resume. Configuration and prompt text do not prove an existing chat changed modes. If app overrides or managed policy prevent Full Access, report the exact required user setting; never bypass enforcement or approve a blocked request automatically. Existing active worker was running without pending approval at this update; its launch permissions have not been changed or independently verified. Keep all gates, checks, serial scheduling and publishing limits in force.\n- **Pending approvals:** user requests that the batch not remain blocked indefinitely. Coordinator must surface a newly observed approval with the exact chat/action (or say action details are unavailable), record it and deduplicate unchanged alerts. On 6 November, AUD-019 chat `01a1ad2f-dc25-7103-ab06-dcf9f6c1ee1e` reported `waitingOnApproval`; supported thread output did not expose the pending command. The app tools have no approval operation, and Codex computer control is denied. User must select Full Access in the existing chat and handle its outstanding prompt; project defaults do not retroactively prove a change. Do not bypass enforcement, mutate internal approvals or execute a blocked action in another chat. Recheck status and resume the same authorized worker once clear.\n- **One coherent task scope per commit.** Keep the fix and its meaningful regression tests together; use separate small commits for independent hardening or documentation scopes. Do not collect unrelated tasks or an entire multi-issue batch into one large commit. Do not manufacture tiny commits or commit intentionally failing tests just to increase count.\n- **Before every commit:** run the repository-required `mise run check` on that tree. Before each push/remote code update: latest formatting, then `mise run lint`. Do not bypass failing checks or claim unrun suites passed. Document genuine baseline failures and resolve them before committing unless the user explicitly authorizes an exception.\n- Use a separate branch and isolated checkout per issue. Preserve the existing replay PR branch and all other chats’ uncommitted work. Do not merge our PRs, force-push, or run paid real-agent E2E tests. Deterministic canaries and normal Go tests are authorized.\n- Once the three gates pass and implementation is concrete/validated, the user authorizes opening the issue and matching PR and pushing the contribution branch to their fork. PR descriptions must show trigger, reproduction, root cause, solution, validation, limits and linked issue. Do the final duplicate check immediately before publishing.\n- After a push to an open PR, follow the repository rule to check its verified cli trail’s findings (not the PR number), fix/resolve real findings with explanations and recheck. Record completion only after the requested PR and required verification/review steps are complete, not merely because code compiles.\n- Save progress before stopping whenever possible: commit completed coherent scopes only after checks; record unfinished uncommitted work, current branch, validation state and precise next action. Usage exhaustion is not implementation completion.\n- Scheduled coordinator must use live `get_usage_limits` data. A missing reading is unknown, not a reset. Do not buy credits, redeem reset credits or switch billing/API authentication. Resume when ordinary allowance is available. Keep unchanged quota-wait runs quiet; notify on a completed PR, an actionable failure, or required user input.\n- Finite batch: stop scheduling new work after three qualifying PRs are raised and required findings/checks are handled. This does not authorize merging them or starting unlimited extra PRs.\n\n| Queue ID | Implementation chat / host | State | Next action |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| AUD-019 | `01a1ad2f-dc25-7103-ab06-dcf9f6c1ee1e` / `local` — Fix condensation cleanup generation safety | IMPLEMENTED LOCALLY; verification complete with two upstream integration failures; user exception required before commit | Await explicit baseline-test exception; no commit/push/issue/PR. After approval, refresh novelty, commit coherent seven-file scope, latest fmt+lint, fork push, issue/PR, verify trail findings. Preserve this chat/worktree; no second worker. |\n| AUD-020 | Not created | Queued | Wait for preceding item, then fresh gate check. |\n| AUD-021 | Not created | Queued | Wait for preceding item, then fresh gate check. |\n\n## Updating this tracker\n\n1. **Do not start a new implementation until every gate in the mandatory decision table passes.** Unknown/not checked/stale evidence is a hold. Check current code, intended contract, reproduction or benchmark, necessary senior engineering scope, issues, all-state PRs, comments, inline reviews, assignments and prototype claims. \n... command output truncated for persistence ...\ncheck, production fix, commit, push, public issue/PR, outreach or paid/real-agent run. Report, exact logs, source hashes, public snapshots, branch inventory and reproduction commands: `/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-workflow-audit-2026-11-16/REPORT.txt`, `measurements.json`, `discovery-tests-final.log`, `image-measurements.log`, `public/`. Observation-test PASS means the current behavior was measured, not fixed.\n\n\n### ENH-004 READY for local implementation — 16 November 2026\n### Ten further issues and ten enhancements — competitor-informed discovery, 16 November 2026\n\n- User requests ten more issues and ten enhancements, explicitly including big and small tasks, with Code.Storage and Cursor Origin research. This broadens discovery sizes; it does not waive the three implementation gates, duplicate exclusions or other owners. No production implementation/publication is authorized by this discovery request. Research owner: this workflow-discovery chat; isolated archives/probes under `/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/entire-20-audit-2026-11-16/` plus the existing owned CLI audit clone. Canonical tracker remains here; local pointers carried forward; existing CLI staging/config/symlink and ENH-004 implementation owner preserved.\n- Exact sources: CLI76f1b512, Brain12e1b0d9, Graph3f632e40, GitSync67dd3a4e, ForgeMark654e95a1. Full revisions in candidates.json. Installed Brain/Graph still unknown commands: source fallback disclosed. Public refresh:277 open CLI PR metadata,26 Brain,14 Graph,5 GitSync,7 ForgeMark; targeted all-state search results and selected related bodies/inline discussions/submissions retained. Broad capped queries are not exhaustive ownership clearance.\n- **AUD-026 READY as a focused scope in documented public checks.** Gate1 PASS: current endpoint guard and public SyncRequest validation accept fragment-only aliases, while actual loopback HTTP requests target the same `/repo.git`; direct identical-endpoint control rejects. Gate2 PASS for the minimum HTTP repository-identity normalization fix and regression matrix, not a large security redesign or a demonstrated destructive mirror incident. Gate3 scoped PASS: fragment/endpoint all-state searches, five open PR metadata records,27 upstream branch names, source history and related #18/#108/#122/#124 full discussions/reviews. #18 reports a different trailing-slash bypass. No exact fragment report/claim found. Refresh before implementation, record owner/worktree/base, and follow required checks. No production fix yet.\n- **Other19 entries are HOLD.** Seven distinct current behaviors have direct/fixture/verbatim-function probes; this does not certify seven complete bugs or all production workflows. stats-key-probe.json demonstrates key equality only. Brain workspace Graph cancellation is source-only. Broken checkpoint-list --limit advice has current source and installed binary proof, not a fresh built-source truncated-list fixture. User-requested count is a discovery inventory, not20 new unclaimed or implementation-ready PRs.\n\n| ID | New issue candidate | Size | Evidence / remaining clearance |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| AUD-024 | CLI: one malformed review manifest blocks healthy saved reviews | S | **HOLD**; REPRODUCED. Need corrupt-entry reporting/recovery contract and final ownership clearance around #2996. |\n| AUD-025 | Brain: corrupt feed record keeps a cursor that skips its recovery | M | **HOLD**; FUNCTION PROBE. Complete sync/recovery reproduction and distinguish from #403's exact missing-file report; do not claim that already-fixed defect. |\n| AUD-026 | Git Sync: fragment-only URL differences bypass same-repository guard | S | **READY — focused, scoped public check**; REPRODUCED. Scoped gates PASS: current contract reproduction; minimal HTTP URL identity fix; no exact fragment report in all-state searches, related #18/#108/#122/#124 reviews, five open PR metadata and27 branch names. #18 reports a different trailing-slash case. Refresh immediately before a task-owned implementation; no public reservation. |\n| AUD-027 | Git Sync: impossible include prefixes pass request validation | S | **HOLD**; REPRODUCED. Check prefix grammar permits legitimate partial names; review equivalent independent-history-prefix validation in one scope; final novelty clearance. Source commit a81db6 already reports blank/outside-refs prefixes; character-validity cases must not be represented as that old report