{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T18:32:49.510Z","ordinal":3262,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1eac8-7a66-7873-ac6d-925af6066720","call_id":"call_9DxIPN53XBJ2223eaKC076vm","output":"Chunk ID: db78a4\nWall time: 0.4137 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 17783\nOutput:\nWarning: truncated output (original token count: 17783)\nTotal output lines: 337\n\nBefore implementing Go code, search nearby packages and helpers for reusable\npatterns. Use `/go:discover-related` when available, otherwise `rg` and related\nimplementations/tests. Check `.golangci.yaml`; handle errors and avoid duplication.\n\n## Test safety\n\n- Every top-level test and subtest calls `t.Parallel()` unless it changes\n  process-global state (`t.Chdir`, `t.Setenv`, or their `os` equivalents).\n- Git tests use isolated temporary repositories, preferably\n  `testutil.InitRepo(t, dir)` plus its file/add/commit helpers. Redirect CWD before\n  calling CWD-based handlers. Never mutate the real checkout's git/session state.\n- Tests must not access the developer's real config, cache, or keychain.\n  In-process fallbacks are shared per process; use per-test overrides and\n  `tokenstore.UseFileBackendForTesting` when isolation between tests is needed.\n  Tests that can reach the OS keyring need `keyring.MockInit()` in `TestMain`.\n- Spawned binaries do not inherit Go's test detection. Harnesses must isolate\n  `ENTIRE_CONFIG_DIR`, `XDG_CACHE_HOME`, `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file`,\n  `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE_PATH`, and `ENTIRE_TEST_AUTH_STORE_FILE`.\n- Prefer `execx.NonInteractive` for real CLI/git test subprocesses so a developer's\n  terminal cannot make them prompt or hang.\n- Caller-resolution tests clear every variable from `agent.CallerSessionEnvVars()`;\n  never hand-maintain a partial list or inherit the developer's agent identity.\n- Source-scanning guards discover files through testutil's guard helpers\n  (`GitGrepGuard`, `GuardGoFiles`), restrict pathspecs to Go files, and fail on\n  zero matches. Do not weaken guard ledgers to silence failures.\n\n## Filesystem and settings safety\n\n**Use the existing anchor for each tree; never assemble a path and perform bare\nI/O beneath it.** Read the filesystem reference before adding or changing I/O.\n\n| Tree | Canonical owner |\n| --- | --- |\n| `.entire` | `entiredir` |\n| Git common directory | `gitdir` |\n| Working tree | `worktreedir` |\n| Agent hook configuration | `agent.HookConfigFile` |\n| Agent session store | `agent.SessionStore` |\n| Active git hooks directory | `strategy.hooksRootForInstall` / `ForRemoval` |\n| Per-user config/cache | `userdirs.ConfigRoot` / `CacheRoot` |\n| Managed plugins | `pluginRoot` |\n\n- Root bases come from trusted resolvers, **not `filepath.Dir(target)`**. Confining\n  a file to its own derived parent proves nothing. Prefer an existing anchor.\n- Roots share the `osroot.Shared` registry. Open child roots with\n  `osroot.SharedChild` / `OpenChild`, not bare `parent.OpenRoot`.\n- Use `osroot` operations and `jsonutil.WriteFileAtomicIn` / `CreateTempIn`.\n  Directories use `MkdirAllNoSymlink`; rooted read-only operations must also\n  enforce symlink policy. Atomic writes replace leaf links rather than follow them.\n- `.entire` must be a real directory; validate through\n  `paths.ValidateEntireDirAt` / `RequireEntireDir`. Do not treat an unresolved\n  repository as absent. Settings reads must also refuse symlinks themselves.\n- Do not broaden symlink exceptions. Developer-vouched agent config directories\n  are scoped, locally trusted exceptions; `.entire` and git hooks are not vouchable.\n- `entiredir.OpenForRead` must not create directories. Reset cached roots before\n  deleting/recreating their directories. Use `entiredir.Name` / `MustName` to\n  bridge repo-relative constants and root-relative I/O names.\n- All settings access goes through `settings`; never read or parse settings JSON\n  ad hoc. Per-user config/cache resolution belongs only to `userdirs`.\n- Repository-controlled settings must not authorize executable discovery, custom\n  executables, or instructions for permission-bypassed agents. Preserve the\n  existing local-provenance gates and their rejection reporting.\n- Existing exceptions (explicit user paths, global git config, transcript-read\n  protocol gaps) are documented in the references; do not generalize them.\n\n## Git and subprocess safety\n\n- Open repositories only through `gitrepo.OpenCurrent(ctx)` or\n  `gitrepo.OpenPath(root)`, never direct go-git opens. This preserves alternates\n  and reftable support. Do not fall back to CWD after failed repo resolution.\n- Use `gitrepo.Status`, never `worktree.Status()`. Agent-hook capture paths use\n  `StatusWithBudget` and preserve degraded-capture reporting on budget exhaustion.\n- Every `git status` subprocess passes **`--no-optional-locks`**. This does not\n  protect worktree-comparing `git diff` from refreshing the index; use the\n  hook-safe alternatives in the git reference.\n- Use the git CLI, not go-git v5, for checkout and hard reset; go-git can delete\n# Entire contribution tracker\n\nPersonal, shared project record for Puneet's Entire contributions. Created 6 November 2026 from the earlier audits and our decisions. **Assembly date is not verification date.** Public statuses below are dated snapshots; recheck before starting work.\n\nCanonical file: `/Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli/CONTRIBUT…60961 chars truncated…review lint now0issues; exact final-tree full check still required before commit. No exception assumed; all changes remain local.\n\n- #3174 full lint after latest formatting PASS0issues179.40s. First required check exit1 in836.12s, exactly the two baseline integration tests, other packages PASS including transcript162.513s; seed test nowPASS. Current-tree check rerun after test-local stdout errcheck correction, `pr3174-check-final.log`, lower package parallelism for disk. Only five rebuildable cache archives containing this task's unique superseded review/baseline paths were removed after validation, with exact inventory `obsolete-owned-cache-inventory.json`; original disposable source archive removed after preserving source probes/logs. No general/shared cache clear or other chats' entries removed. Baseline checkout/evidence and production branches retained. Disk had reached~450MiB; no new compilation suite started concurrently.\n\n- Disk recovered to2.5GiB and #3174 final check is in its remaining integration phase with earlier packages cached. Starting #3175's mandatory full check in its isolated worktree now, within this same chat (no worker/delegation). This supersedes the earlier choice to serialize all verification, with at most two bounded local builds and no performance claims from timings. Publication remains gated/serial. The narrowly scoped baseline-exception question has been sent to the user; no answer/waiver inferred.\n\n- Additional patch-local compatibility issue found before publication: owned stderr assignment overwrote an existing BuildCmd stderr destination, unlike old StderrPipe validation. Preserved original rejection before pipe allocation; focused regression proves no replacement/no launch. New review race suitePASS. This same lifecycle/ownership scope remains one coherent refinement commit. Earlier check-final completed exit1 in673.84s with only the same two baseline failures; it predates this last guard. Latest exact-tree full run is `pr3174-check-complete.log`. #3175 full check is running concurrently in isolated sibling; no commits/pushes. No approval answer yet.\n\n- Resource correction: overlapping full checks exhausted disk (compiler/linker and fixture `no space left on device`). `pr3174-check-complete.log` exit1/333.20s and `pr3175-check.log` exit1/589.90s are INVALID environment runs, not baseline-only verification or patch failures. Both commands finished; temporary Go build trees released, free space~2.4GiB. Restore strictly serialized full checks at package parallelism1. The user baseline exception, still unanswered, covers neither disk exhaustion nor any other new failure. Do not commit/push from these invalid runs. Current lifecycle/source refinements remain staged and focused racesPASS; full current-tree verification outstanding.\n\n- User replied to the scoped baseline-exception question: “fix only those two PRs please.” Continue only existing #3174/#3175, leaving the unrelated upstream failures out of these fixes and disclosing them in the PRs. This reply is treated in the context of the explicit conditional commit/update request: publication is limited to these two PRs and still requires all other checks to pass. No blanket exception for other contributions, no baseline production changes, and no waiver of disk-exhaustion/other failures. Existing AUD-019/AUD-001 pending exceptions and queued work unchanged.\n\n- Resource state changed materially: free disk now9.9GiB (previously~2GiB); current #3175 Go temporary build tree95MiB and integration phase already running. Starting #3174's final guarded-tree check with package parallelism1 while that phase completes; this supersedes strict serialization only with the measured~10GiB headroom. No third check/worker; no production changes outside the two PRs. Keep monitoring and discard any environment-failed run rather than broadening the allowed baseline exception.\n\n- Verification isolation: `pr3175-check-serial.log` exit1/524.56s after missing shared Go cache objects (including testify/testutil); this is not a code/baseline verdict. No repo command clearing that cache found; cause outside this task is unverified. The task removed only its previously listed five unrelated-path archives, whose IDs differ from these missing objects. Stopped only verified #3174 default-cache check process tree (cwd cli-pr3174, root PID82620) to avoid continuing an unreliable run; no other processes touched. New task-private GOCACHE and GOLANGCI_LINT_CACHE under evidence directory, seeded by COPYING available cache data without altering default cache; all2354 copied content objects SHA256-verified,0partial copies. Copied existing Node24 binary to task-private bin for stable subprocess tests. No global tool/config/auth change. Full final validations now use these isolated process-only caches and~7.5GiB headroom; start #3174 `pr3174-check-private.log`, then #3175. Both PR code scopes remain READY for continuation, all source frozen; no commit/push yet.\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1eac6-41d3-7143-a221-cf44a37b6525","create_time":1794940369.510021}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":604,"sampled_through_sequence":602,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":3000}}
