{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T18:33:06.374Z","ordinal":3267,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d516-ad7f-7071-81ac-409a5dad90b1","turn_id":"01a1eac6-41d3-7143-a221-cf44a37b6525","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"call_0xvIJadKNVqNNc5ffA0wieDW","process_id":"57380","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,96p' CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md; sed -n '237,268p' CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,96p' CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md","name":"CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md","path":"CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '237,268p' CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md","name":"CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md","path":"CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Entire contribution tracker\n\nPersonal, shared project record for Puneet's Entire contributions. Created 6 November 2026 from the earlier audits and our decisions. **Assembly date is not verification date.** Public statuses below are dated snapshots; recheck before starting work.\n\nCanonical file: `/Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli/CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md`.\nAll project chats and worktrees should read and update this file rather than maintain separate copies. This is local coordination material, excluded from Git; it is not part of the upstream contribution.\n\n## Start here\n\n| Priority | Local ID | Decision | Next action |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Scheduled priority 1 | AUD-019 | **IMPLEMENTED LOCALLY; pending baseline-test exception.** See the existing worker's final 6 November record. | Continue the same owner after required input; do not create another implementation chat. |\n| Scheduled priority 2 | AUD-020 | Cross-backend fallback returns the wrong session. **READY in scoped checks.** | Start only after priority 1 completes or fails a gate. |\n| Scheduled priority 3 | AUD-021 | Exact session cleanup plus linear stale sweep. **READY in scoped checks.** | Start only after prior queued work completes or fails a gate. |\n| Alternate target, outside scheduled batch | AUD-006 | Idle MCP server ignores cancellation; real CLI SIGTERM case reproduced. **READY** after scoped three-gate check. | Local fix in MCP shutdown chat/worktree; see cross-chat log and validation limits. |\n| Second verification target | AUD-009 | SSE cursor-only/reset failures reproduced; server contract still unverified. | **HOLD.** Verify practical contract before implementing. |\n| Focused fallback | AUD-005 | Failed bundle overwrites existing output; freshly reproduced. | **HOLD.** Useful focused fix, not a cleared senior flagship; novelty review incomplete. |\n| Existing contribution — review only | AUD-001 | Our replay fix is implemented; PR #3015 is still open and unmerged, verified 13 November. | Continue the existing PR. Do not open another issue or PR for it. |\n| Enhancement published; outside scheduled bug-fix batch | ENH-001 | Brain workspace retrieval: measured serial scaling and ignored cancellation. **CONTINUE OUR PR — #644**, 14 November. | [Issue #643](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/issues/643), [PR #644](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/644). Six checked commits; final memory target PASS (83.42 MiB peak). Remote CI awaits maintainer approval; trail findings unavailable. Existing bug-fix batch unchanged. |\n| Stop new work / duplicate risk | AUD-016 | Real, substantial bug, but **already reported exactly** in #2696's review. User also reports an existing PR. | Fails the novelty gate. Retain the record of Puneet's work; do not start another implementation. A separate exact fixing PR has not been independently identified. |\n| Hold — feature withdrawal proposed | AUD-017 | Cursor permission bug freshly reproduced at current upstream on 6 November. | Open #2615 proposes removing the entire affected package. Do not start before ownership/direction is resolved. |\n| Hold — feature withdrawal proposed | AUD-018 | Cursor attribution cost measured; code still present. | Open #2615 proposes removing the package. Do not start an optimization that conflicts with that work. |\n| Excluded | AUD-002 | User confirmed another contributor already has a summary-target PR. | Add the exact PR link when identified; do not pick it up as ours. |\n\n## Mandatory decision table — three gates before starting\n\n**User rule, 6 November 2026: start a new implementation only after all three gates pass.** Unknown, conditional, stale, or not checked does not mean pass. Previous words such as “candidate” or “available” in historical evidence below are not permission to start.\n\n1. **Legitimate:** reproduce a current failure against the intended contract, or measure a meaningful performance problem. An intentional behavior, hypothetical concern, or missing field alone does not pass.\n2. **Substantial / senior scope:** identify the actual engineering judgment involved: failure atomicity, concurrency, identity, privacy boundaries, scaling or lifecycle ownership. Assess the necessary solution, not an artificially enlarged patch. A useful focused fix can still fail our present flagship-selection goal; that says nothing about its author's seniority.\n3. **New and clear to work on:** check issues, all-state PRs, bodies, comments, inline review findings, prototypes, claims and relevant changed files. An existing exact report fails the user's strict new-issue requirement even if unfixed. An issue-only pickup requires an explicit later decision from the user. Adjacent work is not automatically an exact duplicate, but unresolved overlap is a hold.\n\nOnly **READY** means all three passed with dated evidence. **CONTINUE OUR PR** applies to work already published by us; it is not a new-work approval. **HOLD** permits research/verification, not a production implementation. **SKIP** records a failed gate. The latest deep pass cleared **AUD-019, AUD-020 and AUD-021** as the scheduled three-item queue, subject to fresh gate checks. AUD-006 is an alternate previously cleared target, not one of this batch’s three. AUD-009 and AUD-005 remain held.\n\nLatest deep-audit upstream: `aa0c90c9770a460092103214b608247a8b2623ae`, 6 November 2026. The earlier gate pass used `3c299b94f8595bdfc3aa2ecdc0bd199d856f15a2`. The older evidence retains its original dates; this pass did not rerun every historical reproduction.\n\n| ID / finding | 1. Legitimate issue? | 2. Substantial senior scope? | 3. New / already raised or worked on? | Decision / missing proof |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| AUD-001 — replay loses sessions | **PASS:** reproduced; our fix already exists. | **PASS:** cross-clone identity, checked merge, queue/CAS safety. | **EXISTING OUR WORK:** [#3014](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/3014), [#3015](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/3015), still open on 6 November. | **CONTINUE OUR PR.** No duplicate issue/PR. |\n| AUD-002 — summary targets another session | **PASS on 3 November:** deterministic reproduction; not refreshed today. | **PASS in scoped design:** source identity and concurrent storage update. | **FAIL:** user confirmed somebody else's PR; exact link still unknown. | **SKIP.** Do not override the user's ownership correction because a search is inconclusive. |\n| AUD-003 — runner tailoring overwrite | **FAIL as current candidate:** feature removed. | Not evaluated further. | **FAIL:** merged [#2946](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2946) removed the feature. | **SKIP — obsolete.** |\n| AUD-004 — staged filename corruption | **PENDING:** older audit; affected file unchanged through current upstream. No fresh runtime test today. | **FOCUSED:** parser/filename fidelity; no demonstrated wider design problem. | **NOT CLEARED:** no exact match in targeted searches; [#1573 review](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1573#discussion_r3495312963) reports a different CRLF problem, and #2586 changes a different parser. | **HOLD / lower priority.** Refresh test; do not inflate parser work into a flagship. |\n| AUD-005 — bundle truncates existing archive | **PASS:** current-upstream refusal changed a 25-byte existing output into a 22-byte empty ZIP. | **FOCUSED:** useful atomic-output/data-preservation work; not established as a senior flagship. | **NOT CLEARED:** no exact targeted match found; originating #1061 inline-review access returned connector 403. | **HOLD / focused fallback.** Not approved under all three gates. |\n| AUD-006 — idle MCP cancellation | **PASS:** current-upstream pipe test blocks after cancellation; real CLI answers ping, survives first SIGTERM with stdin open, exits on second. | **PASS, scoped judgment:** safe shutdown, input ownership, reader/goroutine lifetime and platform behavior; do not expand into an MCP rewrite. | **PASS in dated checks:** no exact report/fix found; introducing #1585 inline review (six comments) and discussion checked, plus targeted issue/all-state PR searches. Not a reservation. | **IMPLEMENTED LOCALLY after refreshed gates.** MCP tests/signal smoke pass; see validation limits and worktree log. Recheck ownership before publishing. |\n| AUD-007 — copy-truncated log follow | **PENDING:** source unchanged; no fresh runtime reproduction today. | **FOCUSED:** offset/rotation handling. | **NOT CLEARED:** no exact match found in targeted search; review coverage incomplete. | **HOLD / lower priority.** |\n| AUD-008 — insertion into empty file | **PENDING:** depends on supported server anchor contract. | **FOCUSED / UNCLEAR:** no broader apply-transaction failure demonstrated. | **NOT CLEARED:** adjacent #2984; no exact anchor fix identified. | **HOLD.** Contract and reproduction first. |\n| AUD-009 — SSE ID-only / empty ID reset | **PASS for parser behavior:** two current-upstream failures match standard SSE cursor cases. Entire server use of these frames is not verified. | **POSSIBLE:** protocol/reconnect correctness; confirm practical contract and impact first. | **NOT FULLY CLEARED:** no exact match found; relevant #1177/#1447/#1522/#1949/#2507 reviews checked. Earlier EOF findings are different. | **HOLD — rank 2 for validation**, not permission to implement. |\n| AUD-010 — SSE JSON precision | **PENDING:** decode/re-encode path unchanged; fresh runtime check not run. | **FOCUSED:** numeric passthrough fidelity. | **NOT CLEARED:** no exact targeted search match; inline-review coverage incomplete. | **HOLD / lower priority.** |\n| AUD-011 — api -F precision | **PENDING:** numeric fallback unchanged; accepted CLI value contract unverified. | **FOCUSED:** value coercion. | **NOT CLEARED:** no exact targeted search match; inline-review coverage incomplete. | **HOLD / lower priority.** |\n| AUD-012 — recursive token subtraction | **PENDING:** no demonstrated reachable exhaustion case; recursive data alone is insufficient. | **UNCLEAR:** a reachable accounting invariant could be substantial; a hypothetical depth cap is not enough. | **HOLD:** overlapping #2155/#2825/#2782; exact fix not established. | **HOLD.** Reachability, impact and coordination first. |\n| AUD-013 — stale semantic-search response | **PENDING:** generation gap remains; fresh out-of-order test needed. | **FOCUSED:** ordinary stale UI response guard unless wider request-lifecycle failure is shown. | **NOT CLEARED:** no exact targeted match; introducing-review coverage incomplete. | **HOLD / lower priority.** |\n| AUD-014 — pagination drops lower-bound metadata | **PENDING:** field propagation gap remains; no fresh runtime check. | **FOCUSED:** metadata propagation. | **NOT CLEARED:** [#2090 review](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2090#discussion_r3826175128) reports initial-view flags, not this pagination path. Do not call the two exact duplicates. | **HOLD / lower priority.** |\n| AUD-015 — resume second-parent history | **FAIL as confirmed bug:** code explicitly chooses first-parent history. | Potential design change, not established bug scope. | **NOT CLEARED:** #1727 is adjacent explain work. | **SKIP as bug; DESIGN ONLY.** |\n| AUD-016 — failed deletion loses recovery state | **PASS:** 6 November audit reproduces on `3c299b94f`; checkpoint survives while recovery links are cleared. | **PASS:** failure atomicity across state, refs, tombstones, partial success and concurrent writers. | **FAIL:** [exact prior inline report in merged #2696](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2696#discussion_r4212511866). User reports existing PR; separate fixing PR not verified. | **SKIP under strict novelty rule.** Reported is not the same as fixed. Preserve prior work and coordinate rather than duplicate. |\n| AUD-017 — unreadable Cursor workspace | **PASS:** fresh isolated permission test fails at current upstream; existing scope controls pass. Conditional case, not a universal leak. | **PASS as scoped judgment:** evidence uncertainty and conservative repository/privacy boundary. | **HOLD:** no exact resolver-specific fix found. [#2638 review](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2638#discussion_r4159197918) covers related failure-open collision scanning in another function. Open [#2615](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2615) removes this whole package; #2952 is adjacent. | **HOLD — conflicting active direction.** Do not claim a clean pickup or an exact duplicate without patch evidence. |\n| AUD-018 — Cursor session × workspace join | **PASS as measured enhancement:** baseline cost reproduced; no production-user frequency or optimization speedup established. | **PASS if needed:** bounded indexing with equivalent permission/duplicate semantics and scaling proof. | **HOLD:** no exact index implementation found, but open [#2615](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2615) proposes removing the affected package. | **HOLD — avoid optimizing a package proposed for removal.** Same component as AUD-017. |\n| AUD-019 — cleanup deletes a new turn’s staged copy | **PASS:** actual CondenseSessionByID interleaving loses newly published full.jsonl while newer pending state survives. | **PASS, scoped judgment:** generation-aware publication/cleanup and state persistence across concurrent hooks. | **PASS in scoped checks:** no exact issue/fix found; #2692 reviews and adjacent #2754/#2867 patches checked. Those do not close this window. | **READY — scheduled priority 1.** Recheck gates before implementation/publishing. |\n| AUD-020 — fallback substitutes a different session | **PASS:** real Git stores and an actually absent transcript blob yield metadata for ref-session but content for legacy-session at slot 1, with no error. | **PASS:** stable identity/provenance across partial-clone failures and backend coexistence. | **PASS in scoped checks:** #1630’s fallback requirement is a different case; no exact report/fix found. | **READY — scheduled priority 2.** Preserve genuine absent-checkpoint fallback. |\n| AUD-021 — identity-safe, linear session cleanup | **PASS:** both clear APIs delete valid chat.child when clearing chat; 2,000 stale sessions benchmark at 3.42–3.45 s and ~764–765 MB cumulative allocation. | **PASS for this combined scope:** session ownership, two clear paths, on-disk compatibility and quadratic sweep work share the directory-wide matching helper. | **PASS in scoped checks:** #1365 reports glob expansion, #2232 locking, not these dotted-ID and inventory-traversal cases. No exact implementation found. | **READY — scheduled priority 3.** One coherent cleanup PR, not two padded contributions. |\n| AUD-022 — task-ID collisions across parents | **PASS storage reproduction**, but current native producer frequency unverified. | Potential identity/schema problem; scope unagreed. | **HOLD:** active #2131 validates duplicate task IDs and changes merging. | **COORDINATE / SKIP as a clean pickup.** Do not duplicate that work. |\n| EXT-001 — config-based hooks | Supported feature request; no failure reproduced by us. | Potentially substantial migration/mixed-version work. | **FAIL strict novelty:** existing [#2580](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2580); adjacent #2388. | **EXISTING-ISSUE BACKLOG**, not new work approval. |\n| EXT-002 — pre-flight context metadata | **PENDING:** product contract, not demonstrated defect. | Potentially substantial schema work; direction unagreed. | **FAIL strict novelty:** existing [#763](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/763). | **DESIGN / EXISTING-ISSUE BACKLOG.** |\n| EXT-003 — checkpoint push blocks code push | **PENDING:** existing report; no independent reproduction by us. | Potentially substantial delivery/lifecycle design. | **FAIL strict novelty:** [#2794](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/2794), active #2715. | **COORDINATE**, not new work approval. |\n| EXT-004 — winget | **PENDING:** live catalog not verified. | Packaging scope; insufficient demonstrated systems-design work for this goal. | **FAIL strict novelty:** existing [#1304](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/1304). | **BACKLOG**, not new work approval. |\n| OWN-001 through OWN-020 | Historical reports; not all independently reproduced or freshly rechecked. | Not reassessed after failing ownership/novelty. | **FAIL / HOLD:** existing reports, claims, prototypes, PRs, superseded paths or non-CLI scope; individual links/reasons below. | **SKIP / COORDINATE** as individually recorded. None READY. |\n| TEAM-001 through TEAM-008 | Existing team/assigned umbrellas; no independent current reproduction by us. | Some substantial, but umbrella size alone is not a contribution scope. | **FAIL:** already filed/assigned or implementation exists; links below. | **SKIP wholesale pickup.** None READY. |\n| IDEA-001 — discovery scaling | **PENDING:** no precise remaining measured regression. | Potentially substantial if a real scaling invariant is shown. | **NOT CLEARED:** merged #1771/#1956 and related discovery work. | **PARKED.** |\n| IDEA-002 — overlap warnings | **FAIL:** no accepted problem; user rejected the product behavior. | Not evaluated further. | Not evaluated after user rejection. | **DROPPED BY USER.** |\n| IDEA-003 — durable handoff segments | **PENDING:** desired product/schema contract unconfirmed. | Potentially substantial; that does not establish need. | **NOT CLEARED:** no fresh novelty/ownership audit. | **DESIGN ONLY.** |\n| IDEA-004 — immutable review snapshot | **FAIL:** no accepted failure case; user rejected proposal. | Not evaluated further. | Not evaluated after user rejection. | **DROPPED BY USER.** |\n| IDEA-005 — native dispatch local | **PENDING:** disputed hypothesis, no supported reproduction. | Unknown. | **NOT CLEARED.** | **PARKED.** |\n| IDEA-006 — temporary checkpoint inspection | **PENDING:** may conflict with intentional state-only turn-end model. | Unknown until product contract is established. | **NOT CLEARED:** #1139 is a different migration problem. | **PARKED.** |\n| IDEA-007 — ref-write generation races | Existing publicly demonstrated work; not a new bug established here. | Substantial concurrency work, already undertaken. | **FAIL:** #2876/#2131/#2550. | **OTHER CONTRIBUTORS' WORK.** |\n\n### Verification scope for this gate pass\n\n- Fetched current upstream SHA, current #3015/#2696/#2638/#2952/#2615 metadata, all returned inline comments on #2696/#2638/#2952/#1572/#1573/#2090/#1177/#1522, and targeted all-state PR and issue searches for each concrete finding. Some broad searches exceeded one page or were noisy; those are **not cleared**, not proof of absence.\n- Compared affected candidate files from `711697ee5` to `3c299b94f`: the checked files are unchanged except help wording in `trail_watch_cmd.go`. Source equality preserves the old hypothesis, not a fresh runtime reproduction.\n- Re-ran AUD-017's isolated permission reproduction on an exported current-upstream tree. It failed on the two expected ownership assertions; the permission precondition was enforced, not skipped. Existing Cursor scope controls passed separately. Synthetic performance baseline was rerun once; this is not an end-to-end production workload.\n- Cursor's #2638 inline review report concerns collision-walk uncertainty in `cursor.go`; AUD-017 concerns session evidence in `cursor_chats.go`. They share a safety principle but are not claimed to be identical implementations. #2615's proposed package removal is the immediate reason to hold both Cursor candidates.\n- An exact old review report does **not** prove a current fixing PR exists or the bug is fixed. AUD-016 remains reproduced; it fails the user's strict novelty gate regardless. A separate exact fixing PR remains unidentified in this audit.\n- No new production implementation, issue, PR, commit or push was made. This tracker no longer recommends starting any historical candidate without clearing the missing gates.\n\n## Status and evidence rules\n\n- **OURS / PR OPEN**: we implemented it and have a public PR. This does not mean merged or accepted.\n- **REPRODUCED**: a focused failing safety-contract test exists at the recorded revision. Test-only work is not an implemented fix.\n- **BENCHMARKED**: current cost was measured; no optimized implementation or speedup is implied.\n- **SOURCE CHECKED**: affected source was inspected; no fresh runtime reproduction is claimed for that date.\n- **TAKEN**: an explicit claim, prototype or PR exists. An issue does not become available merely because GitHub shows no linked PR.\n- **COORDINATE**: related work or a reporter-led proposal exists; it is not proof someone fixed the exact defect.\n- **DESIGN / UNCONFIRMED**: a proposal or disputed hypothesis, not a confirmed bug.\n- **SKIP / DROPPED / OBSOLETE**: retain the reason; do not rediscover and recommend it as new.\n\n“No exact public match found” is limited to the searches documented in the evidence reports. It is not a reservation, assignment, maintainer approval or proof of no private work. Public GitHub association is not employment verification. Local IDs are stable tracker IDs, not GitHub issue numbers.\n\n## Scheduled contribution batch and commit policy\n\nUser authorized on 6 November 2026: create separate chats to complete and raise three vetted contributions, one at a time, and resume those chats after usage limits restore. Initial queue: **AUD-019 → AUD-020 → AUD-021**. Each must pass fresh legitimacy, substantial engineering scope and exact novelty/ownership checks before production implementation and again before filing. Skip an existing exact issue, PR, inline report or claimed prototype; never duplicate another contributor. If any queued item fails, record it and select the next truly eligible substantial item rather than force a third PR.\n\nWork through one active implementation chat at a time. Record each chat ID/host, branch/worktree, stage, next command, tests and issue/PR/trail links here. Continue the same chat after rate limits, rather than making duplicate chats for the same item. Do not resume work the user paused/cancelled or a chat waiting for required approval/input. The user authorizes continuation messages to the implementation chats created for this batch; unrelated project chats are outside this authorization.\n\n- **Batch execution permissions (user authorized 6 November):** start new contribution chats with Full Access and command approval `never` (`sandbox_mode = \"danger-full-access\"`, `approval_policy = \"never\"`). The trusted main Entire checkout has these project-local defaults in `.codex/config.toml`; global defaults and unrelated projects are unchanged. This is a tracked file with a local-only override: never stage/commit/push its permission lines in a contribution PR. Carry the local override to isolated checkouts if needed, separately from production changes. The scheduler/create-thread tools expose no permission arguments; inspect each worker's actual runtime permissions after launch/resume. Configuration and prompt text do not prove an existing chat changed modes. If app overrides or managed policy prevent Full Access, report the exact required user setting; never bypass enforcement or approve a blocked request automatically. Existing active worker was running without pending approval at this update; its launch permissions have not been changed or independently verified. Keep all gates, checks, serial scheduling and publishing limits in force.\n- **Pending approvals:** user requests that the batch not remain blocked indefinitely. Coordinator must surface a newly observed approval with the exact chat/action (or say action details are unavailable), record it and deduplicate unchanged alerts. On 6 November, AUD-019 chat `01a1ad2f-dc25-7103-ab06-dcf9f6c1ee1e` reported `waitingOnApproval`; supported thread output did not expose the pending command. The app tools have no approval operation, and Codex computer control is denied. User must select Full Access in the existing chat and handle its outstanding prompt; project defaults do not retroactively prove a change. Do not bypass enforcement, mutate internal approvals or execute a blocked action in another chat. Recheck status and resume the same authorized worker once clear.\n- **One coherent task scope per commit.** Keep the fix and its meaningful regression tests together; use separate small commits for independent hardening or documentation scopes. Do not collect unrelated tasks or an entire multi-issue batch into one large commit. Do not manufacture tiny commits or commit intentionally failing tests just to increase count.\n- **Before every commit:** run the repository-required `mise run check` on that tree. Before each push/remote code update: latest formatting, then `mise run lint`. Do not bypass failing checks or claim unrun suites passed. Document genuine baseline failures and resolve them before committing unless the user explicitly authorizes an exception.\n- Use a separate branch and isolated checkout per issue. Preserve the existing replay PR branch and all other chats’ uncommitted work. Do not merge our PRs, force-push, or run paid real-agent E2E tests. Deterministic canaries and normal Go tests are authorized.\n- Once the three gates pass and implementation is concrete/validated, the user authorizes opening the issue and matching PR and pushing the contribution branch to their fork. PR descriptions must show trigger, reproduction, root cause, solution, validation, limits and linked issue. Do the final duplicate check immediately before publishing.\n- After a push to an open PR, follow the repository rule to check its verified cli trail’s findings (not the PR number), fix/resolve real findings with explanations and recheck. Record completion only after the requested PR and required verification/review steps are complete, not merely because code compiles.\n- Save progress before stopping whenever possible: commit completed coherent scopes only after checks; record unfinished uncommitted work, current branch, validation state and precise next action. Usage exhaustion is not implementation completion.\n- Scheduled coordinator must use live `get_usage_limits` data. A missing reading is unknown, not a reset. Do not buy credits, redeem reset credits or switch billing/API authentication. Resume when ordinary allowance is available. Keep unchanged quota-wait runs quiet; notify on a completed PR, an actionable failure, or required user input.\n- Finite batch: stop scheduling new work after three qualifying PRs are raised and required findings/checks are handled. This does not authorize merging them or starting unlimited extra PRs.\n\n| Queue ID | Implementation chat / host | State | Next action |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| AUD-019 | `01a1ad2f-dc25-7103-ab06-dcf9f6c1ee1e` / `local` — Fix condensation cleanup generation safety | IMPLEMENTED LOCALLY; verification complete with two upstream integration failures; user exception required before commit | Await explicit baseline-test exception; no commit/push/issue/PR. After approval, refresh novelty, commit coherent seven-file scope, latest fmt+lint, fork push, issue/PR, verify trail findings. Preserve this chat/worktree; no second worker. |\n| AUD-020 | Not created | Queued | Wait for preceding item, then fresh gate check. |\n| AUD-021 | Not created | Queued | Wait for preceding item, then fresh gate check. |\n\n## Updating this tracker\n\n1. **Do not start a new implementation until every gate in the mandatory decision table passes.** Unknown/not checked/stale evidence is a hold. Check current code, intended contract, reproduction or benchmark, necessary senior engineering scope, issues, all-state PRs, comments, inline reviews, assignments and prototype claims. Record evidence dates. An exact existing report fails the strict novelty requirement even without a fixing PR; ask the user to change that requirement before an existing-issue pickup.\n2. Update the existing stable ID. Add new IDs only for distinct findings; do not relabel related subcases as independent flagship contributions.\n3. Keep discovery, reproduction, implementation, PR-open, merged and released separate. Record our work independently from the upstream reporter/owner. Preserve unknown links as unknown rather than inventing them.\n4. When starting implementation, record the chat/worktree, branch and stage in the cross-chat log. Add issue, PR and verified trail IDs when created. Mark intentional red tests clearly.\n5. Preserve rejected ideas, occupied work and superseded evidence. Add the reason and replacement link; do not delete history merely because an item is no longer recommended.\n6. A senior contribution is judged by the invariant, reproduction, design tradeoffs and validation, not patch size. Avoid widening a fix just to make it look substantial.\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":56500}},"started_at_ms":1794940386371,"completed_at_ms":1794940386374}}
