{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T18:33:07.253Z","ordinal":3269,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1eac8-bfb5-70a1-9b1e-6247b3f6b464","call_id":"call_0xvIJadKNVqNNc5ffA0wieDW","output":"Chunk ID: feaf28\nWall time: 0.0001 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 7223\nOutput:\nWarning: truncated output (original token count: 7223)\nTotal output lines: 128\n\n# Entire contribution tracker\n\nPersonal, shared project record for Puneet's Entire contributions. Created 6 November 2026 from the earlier audits and our decisions. **Assembly date is not verification date.** Public statuses below are dated snapshots; recheck before starting work.\n\nCanonical file: `/Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli/CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md`.\nAll project chats and worktrees should read and update this file rather than maintain separate copies. This is local coordination material, excluded from Git; it is not part of the upstream contribution.\n\n## Start here\n\n| Priority | Local ID | Decision | Next action |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Scheduled priority 1 | AUD-019 | **IMPLEMENTED LOCALLY; pending baseline-test exception.** See the existing worker's final 6 November record. | Continue the same owner after required input; do not create another implementation chat. |\n| Scheduled priority 2 | AUD-020 | Cross-backend fallback returns the wrong session. **READY in scoped checks.** | Start only after priority 1 completes or fails a gate. |\n| Scheduled priority 3 | AUD-021 | Exact session cleanup plus linear stale sweep. **READY in scoped checks.** | Start only after prior queued work completes or fails a gate. |\n| Alternate target, outside scheduled batch | AUD-006 | Idle MCP server ignores cancellation; real CLI SIGTERM case reproduced. **READY** after scoped three-gate check. | Local fix in MCP shutdown chat/worktree; see cross-chat log and validation limits. |\n| Second verification target | AUD-009 | SSE cursor-only/reset failures reproduced; server contract still unverified. | **HOLD.** Verify practical contract before implementing. |\n| Focused fallback | AUD-005 | Failed bundle overwrites existing output; freshly reproduced. | **HOLD.** Useful focused fix, not a cleared senior flagship; novelty review incomplete. |\n| Existing contribution — review only | AUD-001 | Our replay fix is implemented; PR #3015 is still open and unmerged, verified 13 November. | Continue the existing PR. Do not open another issue or PR for it. |\n| Enhancement published; outside scheduled bug-fix batch | ENH-001 | Brain workspace retrieval: measured serial scaling and ignored cancellation. **CONTINUE OUR PR — #644**, 14 November. | [Issue #643](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/issues/643), [PR #644](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/644). Six checked commits; final memory target PASS (83.42 MiB peak). Remote CI awaits maintainer approval; trail findings unavailable. Existing bug-fix batch unchanged. |\n| Stop new work / duplicate risk | AUD-016 | Real, substantial bug, but **already reported exactly** in #2696's review. User also reports an existing PR. | Fails the novelty gate. Retain the record of Puneet's work; do not start another implementation. A separate exact fixing PR has not been independently identified. |\n| Hold — feature withdrawal proposed | AUD-017 | Cursor permission bug freshly reproduced at current upstream on 6 November. | Open #2615 proposes removing the entire affected package. Do not start before ownership/direction is resolved. |\n| Hold — feature withdrawal proposed | AUD-018 | Cursor attribution cost measured; code still present. | Open #2615 proposes removing the package. Do not start an optimization that conflicts with that work. |\n| Excluded | AUD-002 | User confirmed another contributor already has a summary-target PR. | Add the exact PR link when identified; do not pick it up as ours. |\n\n## Mandatory decision table — three gates before starting\n\n**User rule, 6 November 2026: start a new implementation only after all three gates pass.** Unknown, conditional, stale, or not checked does not mean pass. Previous words such as “candidate” or “available” in historical evidence below are not permission to start.\n\n1. **Legitimate:** reproduce a current failure against the intended contract, or measure a meaningful performance problem. An intentional behavior, hypothetical concern, or missing field alone does not pass.\n2. **Substantial / senior scope:** identify the actual engineering judgment involved: failure atomicity, concurrency, identity, privacy boundaries, scaling or lifecycle ownership. Assess the necessary solution, not an artificially enlarged patch. A useful focused fix can still fail our present flagship-selection goal; that says nothing about its author's seniority.\n3. **New and clear to work on:** check issues, all-state PRs, bodies, comments, inline review findings, prototypes, claims and relevant changed files. An existing exact report fails the user's strict new-issue requirement even if unfixed. An issue-only pickup requires an explicit later decision from the user. Adjacent work is not automatically an exact duplicate, but unresolved overlap is a hold.\n\nOnly **READY** means all three passed with dated evidence. **CONTINUE OUR PR** applies to work already published by us; it is not a new-work approval. **HOLD** permits…18792 chars truncated…ead output did not expose the pending command. The app tools have no approval operation, and Codex computer control is denied. User must select Full Access in the existing chat and handle its outstanding prompt; project defaults do not retroactively prove a change. Do not bypass enforcement, mutate internal approvals or execute a blocked action in another chat. Recheck status and resume the same authorized worker once clear.\n- **One coherent task scope per commit.** Keep the fix and its meaningful regression tests together; use separate small commits for independent hardening or documentation scopes. Do not collect unrelated tasks or an entire multi-issue batch into one large commit. Do not manufacture tiny commits or commit intentionally failing tests just to increase count.\n- **Before every commit:** run the repository-required `mise run check` on that tree. Before each push/remote code update: latest formatting, then `mise run lint`. Do not bypass failing checks or claim unrun suites passed. Document genuine baseline failures and resolve them before committing unless the user explicitly authorizes an exception.\n- Use a separate branch and isolated checkout per issue. Preserve the existing replay PR branch and all other chats’ uncommitted work. Do not merge our PRs, force-push, or run paid real-agent E2E tests. Deterministic canaries and normal Go tests are authorized.\n- Once the three gates pass and implementation is concrete/validated, the user authorizes opening the issue and matching PR and pushing the contribution branch to their fork. PR descriptions must show trigger, reproduction, root cause, solution, validation, limits and linked issue. Do the final duplicate check immediately before publishing.\n- After a push to an open PR, follow the repository rule to check its verified cli trail’s findings (not the PR number), fix/resolve real findings with explanations and recheck. Record completion only after the requested PR and required verification/review steps are complete, not merely because code compiles.\n- Save progress before stopping whenever possible: commit completed coherent scopes only after checks; record unfinished uncommitted work, current branch, validation state and precise next action. Usage exhaustion is not implementation completion.\n- Scheduled coordinator must use live `get_usage_limits` data. A missing reading is unknown, not a reset. Do not buy credits, redeem reset credits or switch billing/API authentication. Resume when ordinary allowance is available. Keep unchanged quota-wait runs quiet; notify on a completed PR, an actionable failure, or required user input.\n- Finite batch: stop scheduling new work after three qualifying PRs are raised and required findings/checks are handled. This does not authorize merging them or starting unlimited extra PRs.\n\n| Queue ID | Implementation chat / host | State | Next action |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| AUD-019 | `01a1ad2f-dc25-7103-ab06-dcf9f6c1ee1e` / `local` — Fix condensation cleanup generation safety | IMPLEMENTED LOCALLY; verification complete with two upstream integration failures; user exception required before commit | Await explicit baseline-test exception; no commit/push/issue/PR. After approval, refresh novelty, commit coherent seven-file scope, latest fmt+lint, fork push, issue/PR, verify trail findings. Preserve this chat/worktree; no second worker. |\n| AUD-020 | Not created | Queued | Wait for preceding item, then fresh gate check. |\n| AUD-021 | Not created | Queued | Wait for preceding item, then fresh gate check. |\n\n## Updating this tracker\n\n1. **Do not start a new implementation until every gate in the mandatory decision table passes.** Unknown/not checked/stale evidence is a hold. Check current code, intended contract, reproduction or benchmark, necessary senior engineering scope, issues, all-state PRs, comments, inline reviews, assignments and prototype claims. Record evidence dates. An exact existing report fails the strict novelty requirement even without a fixing PR; ask the user to change that requirement before an existing-issue pickup.\n2. Update the existing stable ID. Add new IDs only for distinct findings; do not relabel related subcases as independent flagship contributions.\n3. Keep discovery, reproduction, implementation, PR-open, merged and released separate. Record our work independently from the upstream reporter/owner. Preserve unknown links as unknown rather than inventing them.\n4. When starting implementation, record the chat/worktree, branch and stage in the cross-chat log. Add issue, PR and verified trail IDs when created. Mark intentional red tests clearly.\n5. Preserve rejected ideas, occupied work and superseded evidence. Add the reason and replacement link; do not delete history merely because an item is no longer recommended.\n6. A senior contribution is judged by the invariant, reproduction, design tradeoffs and validation, not patch size. Avoid widening a fix just to make it look substantial.\n\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1eac6-41d3-7143-a221-cf44a37b6525","create_time":1794940387.253129}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":607,"sampled_through_sequence":604,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":3000}}
