*OURS — implementation complete; PR OPEN** at last check. Author: Puneet-Pal-Singh. | Reproduced cross-clone slot collision; user implemented session-ID merge/conflict handling and documentation. Main checkout is on `fix/preserve-concurrent-checkpoint-sessions`. | [Issue #30\n| AUD-002 | Generated summary saved on a newly attached, unrelated session | **TAKEN — user confirmed somebody else's PR**. Exact author/link not recorded. | Failing local reproduction and root-cause audit; no fix implemented by us. | Do not work as an unclaimed item. Add exact PR link when known; lack of a search result does not overri\n| AUD-003 | Runner tailoring overwrites intervening edits | **OBSOLETE — SKIP** | Earlier audit only. | Feature removed by merged [#2946](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2946); `runner_apply.go` removed. | 2026-11-03 |\n| AUD-004 | `experts --staged` corrupts quoted, literal or Unicode filenames | **SOURCE CHECKED — candidate; no exact public fix found** | Earlier parser audit; affected source unchanged at recheck. | `experts_cmd.go:588` in the recorded revision. Adjacent [#2586](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2586) fixes strategy hooks, not this\n| AUD-005 | Failed doctor bundle truncates an existing output archive | **REPRODUCED — focused fallback / HOLD under senior-selection gate.** | Fresh refusal test replaced existing 25-byte output with a 22-byte ZIP; baseline bundle tests pass. No production fix. | `doctor_bundle.go` truncates before collection. Useful atomic output fix;\n| AUD-006 | Idle MCP server ignores cancellation while blocked reading input | **IMPLEMENTED LOCALLY**, this MCP shutdown chat; no public issue/PR/commit/push. | Refreshed at `93045e384`; cancellation/cleanup fix, MCP race tests and real inherited-stdin SIGTERM/EOF smoke pass. | `/Users/puneetpalsingh/.codex/worktrees/mcp-shutdown/cli`, b\n| AUD-007 | Following a log misses bytes after copy-truncation | **SOURCE CHECKED — candidate; no exact public fix found** | Identified missing file-size/offset reset in `followFile`. | `doctor_logs.go:124`. Refresh focused truncation reproduction. Smaller operational fix. | 2026-11-03 |\n| AUD-008 | Suggested insertion into an existing empty file is rejected | **SOURCE CHECKED — contract agreement needed** | Identified empty-file anchor handling. | `trail_review_patch.go:292`. Related [#2984](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2984) changes rendering, not the anchor. Agree server anchor semantics before claiming a fix\n| AUD-009 | SSE cursor-only frames and empty cursor reset are mishandled | **REPRODUCED PARSER CASES — HOLD for server-contract validation.** | Current-upstream tests lose ID-only cursor and retain old cursor after explicit reset. Existing stream controls pass. No production fix. | Standard SSE examples reproduced; Entire server use/adv\n| AUD-010 | SSE JSON output loses large-integer precision | **SOURCE CHECKED — candidate; no exact public fix found** | Identified decode into `any` / float64 and re-encode. | `trail_watch_cmd.go:356`. Reproduce exact JSON passthrough loss. Smaller integrity fix. | 2026-11-03 |\n| AUD-011 | `entire api -F` rounds integer values outside int64 | **SOURCE CHECKED — candidate; no exact public fix found** | Identified ParseInt failure falling through to ParseFloat. | `api_cmd.go:297`. Define numeric input contract and reproduce. Smaller fix. | 2026-11-03 |\n| AUD-012 | Token …15992 chars truncated… |\n| ENH-022 | Git Sync: cancel-aware transfer bandwidth budgets | M | **HOLD — source-backed design.** Optional upload/download byte-rate budgets over relay and materialized paths, with progress distinguishing throttling from network wait. Keep defaults unchanged and cancellation prompt. Next: Need a real shared-runner/network constraint and show why existing injected HTTP client cannot sufficiently solve it. Lowest-confidence product-need candidate. |\n\n- Competitor evidence: Code.Storage direct file reads, ephemeral agent-state refs and parallel attempts; Origin CloneKit and changes-since-last-review tours. Inspiration is not proof of Entire feature absence or need. Hosted server capabilities are not assumed publicly contributable. ENH-017 requires real child-span timestamps/offsets before exporting a timeline; never invent timings by summing durations. ENH-019 extends persisted distributions; live histograms already exist. ENH-022 is lower-priority until a need beyond injected HTTP-client rate limiting is proven. ENH-014/021 may share one coherent baseline scope; do not split PRs to satisf\n- Exclusions retained: GitSync LFS is existing issue#59; Graph working-tree caching is existing issue#271; ForgeMark CI gates already have PR#6/#14; code-tour onboarding already has skills#9 and CLI learn#1146 (ENH-021 therefore remains adjacent/HOLD). CLI checkpoint filters already have issue#2718; not offered again. Unlimited ForgeMark finished-run retention and GitSync custom-ref mapping prefix failure were disproved in source. AUD-027 extends the character-validity question beyond source commit a81db6's existing blank/outside-refs report; strict novelty remains HOLD. No ENH-009 CI memory revival, no ENH-004 or ENH-012 duplication.\n- Validation PASS: nine focused observation test functions across actual review/GitSync/ForgeMark packages and the two verbatim-function probes; no full repository check, paid model, live forge load or production incident claimed. Brain cache reader and doctor followFile extracted unchanged with hashes; SSE uses a controlled blocking writer; moved-review case is a path identity fixture. Ordinary pinned Go toolchain/dependency downloads occurred through mise. No production edits, commits, pushes, public issues/PRs or outreach. Evidence/limits/commands/source URLs and ranked next work in `REPORT.txt`, `candidates.json`, `evidence-hashes.json`, \n\n\n- Disk recovered to2.5GiB and #3174 final check is in its remaining integration phase with earlier packages cached. Starting #3175's mandatory full check in its isolated worktree now, within this same chat (no worker/delegation). This supersedes the earlier choice to serialize all verification, with at most two bounded local builds and no performance claims from timings. Public\n\n- Additional patch-local compatibility issue found before publication: owned stderr assignment overwrote an existing BuildCmd stderr destination, unlike old StderrPipe validation. Preserved original rejection before pipe allocation; focused regression proves no replacement/no launch. New review race suitePASS. This same lifecycle/ownership scope remains one coherent refinement \n\n- Resource correction: overlapping full checks exhausted disk (compiler/linker and fixture `no space left on device`). `pr3174-check-complete.log` exit1/333.20s and `pr3175-check.log` exit1/589.90s are INVALID environment runs, not baseline-only verification or patch failures. Both commands finished; temporary Go build trees released, free space~2.4GiB. Restore strictly seriali\n\n- User replied to the scoped baseline-exception question: “fix only those two PRs please.” Continue only existing #3174/#3175, leaving the unrelated upstream failures out of these fixes and disclosing them in the PRs. This reply is treated in the context of the explicit conditional commit/update request: publication is limited to these two PRs and still requires all other c\n\n- Resource state changed materially: free disk now9.9GiB (previously~2GiB); current #3175 Go temporary build tree95MiB and integration phase already running. Starting #3174's final guarded-tree check with package parallelism1 while that phase completes; this supersedes strict serialization only with the measured~10GiB headroom. No third check/worker; no production changes outsi\n\n- Verification isolation: `pr3175-check-serial.log` exit1/524.56s after missing shared Go cache objects (including testify/testutil); this is not a code/baseline verdict. No repo command clearing that cache found; cause outside this tas