{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T18:34:57.728Z","ordinal":3323,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1eaca-6f3b-78f1-aa83-9c1d37cfca11","call_id":"call_dqYCCta96wBJ7sOKJLQ9JjhS","output":"Chunk ID: 545225\nWall time: 0.0000 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 2325\nOutput:\ncli {\"id\":2996,\"pr\":[\"open\",false,\"fix(review): persist findings when session matching fails\"],\"counts\":[3,0,1,6],\"relatedPaths\":[\"cmd/entire/cli/review/manifest.go\"],\"hits\":[],\"errors\":[]}\ncli {\"id\":1768,\"pr\":[\"closed\",true,\"feat(checkpoint): add checkpoint list --json (machine-readable listing; migrate off rewind --list)\"],\"counts\":[0,2,2,12],\"relatedPaths\":[\"cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint_group.go\"],\"hits\":[\"**Known minor follow-up:** the condensed `--json` truncation note suggests re-running with `--limit`, which `checkpoint list` does not yet expose (stderr-only, fires only past the default cap).\"],\"errors\":[]}\ncli {\"id\":2605,\"pr\":[\"open\",false,\"List remote-only imported checkpoints in fresh git-refs clones\"],\"counts\":[1,2,4,2],\"relatedPaths\":[],\"hits\":[\"- Imported prompts are read only for entries that survive `--limit`.\\r\"],\"errors\":[]}\ncli {\"id\":1589,\"pr\":[\"closed\",true,\"feat(transcript): externalize images (Claude Code, Codex) + capture Cursor sidecar images\"],\"counts\":[1,4,4,23],\"relatedPaths\":[\"cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/persistent.go\"],\"hits\":[\"- **Claude Code & Codex — transcript codec (lossless round trip).** Inline base64 images are lifted out of the transcript and replaced with a compact, path-bearing placeholder (`entire-asset:assets/img-<id>.<ext>`); on restore the exact bytes are re-injected in place. Contract: `ReinjectImages(Extra\",\"- **Real data:** Claude — a real 17MB session log round-trips byte-exact; Codex — 176 images across 12 real rollouts, valid magic on every asset, up to ~119 MB saved; Cursor — a real 48KB JPEG from an actual `store.db` extracted and verified.\",\"- **Timeout** — the `sqlite3` shell-out now runs under a 30s deadline so a locked/malformed `store.db` can't hang the commit/stop hook.\",\"cmd/entire/cli/transcript/imageextract/imageextract.go `newAssetID` ignores the `crypto/rand` read error. If `rand.Read` ever fails, this can silently generate an all-zero ID, causing asset filename collisions and incorrect placeholder→asset mapping (broken reinjection).\",\"cmd/entire/cli/transcript/imageextract/imageextract.go Fixed in f647e25. newAssetID now returns an error on rand.Read failure, propagated through uniqueImageName and ExtractImages; on failure the transcript is left inline rather than externalized with an all-zero id. A uniqueImageName guard also gua\",\"cmd/entire/cli/transcript/imageextract/imageextract.go The global value swap is intentional and does not break the round trip: it is a value-preserving, reversible substitution, so ReinjectImages restores every occurrence (image or text) to the identical bytes. A data-field-scoped swap was tried but\",\"- Wires extraction into manual-commit condensation **before** redaction and persists extracted assets into checkpoint trees; restores by reinjecting assets on read when placeholders exist.\",\"| cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go | Runs image externalization pre-redaction and plumbs extracted assets into checkpoint write options. |\\r\"],\"errors\":[]}\ncli {\"id\":1144,\"pr\":[\"closed\",true,\"feat: machine-readable export surface for sessions and checkpoints\"],\"counts\":[3,7,5,7],\"relatedPaths\":[\"cmd/entire/cli/explain_export.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/explain_export_test.go\"],\"hits\":[\"> `entire checkpoint explain` gains `--json` (metadata-only list or single-checkpoint envelope with `partial` + per-session `error` reporting), `--transcript` (stream v2 compact transcript), `--session-index` (select session in multi-session checkpoints), and `--limit` (cap JSON list output with tru\"],\"errors\":[]}\ncli {\"id\":2069,\"pr\":[\"open\",false,\"fix(checkpoint): externalize images in subagent transcripts before size cap\"],\"counts\":[1,4,3,12],\"relatedPaths\":[\"cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/persistent.go\"],\"hits\":[\"**Why / how it helps:** Subagent path only sanitized then size-checked/redacted, so image-heavy transcripts were dropped whole and Codex `input_image` base64 reached redaction intact (corruption risk).\",\"**How:** `prepareSubagentTranscript`: sanitize → optional `imageextract` → size-check externalized bytes; wire assets into persistent + ephemeral task writers.\",\"This PR updates the subagent-transcript storage pipeline in the checkpoint subsystem so that (when enabled) inline base64 images are externalized into checkpoint assets **before** enforcing the 50MB blob cap, aligning subagent handling with the main session transcript path and preventing image-heavy\",\"- Extend `prepareSubagentTranscript` to: sanitize → (opt-in) image externalize → size-check, returning extracted assets alongside the rewritten transcript.\",\"- Wire extracted task assets into both persistent (`treeWriter`) and ephemeral (shadow-branch) task checkpoint writers under `tasks/<id>/assets/`.\",\"| cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/subagent_transcript.go | Adds image externalization to the subagent transcript preparation pipeline and returns extracted assets. |\",\"| cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/persistent.go | Persists extracted task assets into the committed checkpoint tree under the task subtree. |\",\"| cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/ephemeral.go | Persists extracted task assets into the shadow-branch task subtree via tree-surgery changes. |\"],\"errors\":[]}\ncli {\"id\":3151,\"pr\":[\"open\",false,\"muskan/externalize-images-codex-generates\"],\"counts\":[0,0,1,9],\"relatedPaths\":[],\"hits\":[],\"errors\":[]}\ncli {\"id\":3057,\"pr\":[\"open\",false,\"fix(checkpoint): remove the partial pack a failed checkpoint fetch leaves\"],\"counts\":[3,2,4,3],\"relatedPaths\":[],\"hits\":[],\"errors\":[]}\ncli {\"id\":1166,\"pr\":[\"closed\",true,\"feat(review): warn user when review manifest is not persisted\"],\"counts\":[0,1,2,3],\"relatedPaths\":[],\"hits\":[\"**`cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go`** — Two-line debug log added to the `EnvSession`-not-set silent return. The other four branches in `adoptReviewEnv` already log at WARN (agent mismatch, SHA mismatch, malformed skills JSON) or DEBUG (success). This was the only branch with no breadcrumb, so a \\\"review \",\"> Prevents silent failures in `entire review` when local manifest persistence is skipped: `writePostReviewManifest` now prints a **user-visible note** (via new `warnManifestNotWritten`) when session state can’t be loaded, no matching review sessions are found, or manifest disk writes fail.\"],\"errors\":[]}\nentire-brain {\"id\":403,\"pr\":[\"closed\",true,\"Per-fact push + reachability-filtered pull (COR-2126)\"],\"counts\":[0,6,4,11],\"relatedPaths\":[\"internal/cli/hosted_feed_cache.go\",\"internal/cli/hosted_feed_cache_test.go\"],\"hits\":[\"- Feed-cache loader skips corrupt lines but a single >4 MiB line would wedge it (`bufio.Scanner` cap); no realistic fact approaches that size.\",\"When `state.json` loads but `records.ndjson` is absent, `loadHostedFeedCache` returns the stored cursor with an empty item map. Pull then resumes from that cursor and never refetches earlier pages. Facts not already in the branch store are skipped permanently until a server 400 forces a cursor reset\",\"internal/cli/hosted_feed_cache.go Fixed in ae76950a: a state.json without its records.ndjson now loads as an empty cache, cursor included, so the next pull refetches from the start instead of resuming past unseen pages. Pinned by TestHostedFeedCacheMissingRecordsResetsCursor.\"],\"errors\":[]}\nentire-brain {\"id\":452,\"pr\":[\"closed\",true,\"One memory-sync path: per-fact wire everywhere (COR-2233: COR-2234 + COR-2235 + COR-2236)\"],\"counts\":[0,4,3,64],\"relatedPaths\":[],\"hits\":[\"Both findings on d2a89cd are fixed in 0e353c1: the NO_EGRESS skip answers in JSON under `--json`, and a corrupt hosted binding fails the sync with a rebind remedy instead of warning and merging against the stale local head.\",\"internal/cli/facts_sync_cmd.go ### Corrupt binding syncs stale git-meta\",\"internal/cli/facts_sync_cmd.go Fixed in 0e353c1f: a corrupt binding now fails the sync with a rebind remedy instead of warning. The stale-gitmeta fallback it could reach is gone entirely — COR-2236 removed the local-gitmeta backend, so no code path merges against the stale local head anymore.\"],\"errors\":[]}\nentire-brain {\"id\":604,\"pr\":[\"closed\",true,\"Give foreground Brain writes priority over background work\"],\"counts\":[0,1,1,40],\"relatedPaths\":[\"internal/cli/facts_manifest.go\"],\"hits\":[],\"errors\":[]}\ngit-sync {\"id\":18,\"pr\":[\"closed\",true,\"Expand on integration tests\"],\"counts\":[0,2,3,6],\"relatedPaths\":[\"internal/validation/validation.go\"],\"hits\":[\"internal/validation/validation.go ### Same-repo check bypassed by trailing slash difference\",\"`ValidateEndpoints` compares URLs with plain string equality after trimming whitespace, but doesn't normalize trailing slashes. URLs like `https://example.com/r.git` and `https://example.com/r.git/` point to the same repository on virtually all Git hosting platforms, yet bypass this safety check. Th\"],\"errors\":[]}\ngit-sync {\"id\":108,\"pr\":[\"closed\",true,\"Bind explicit credentials to the host they were configured for\"],\"counts\":[1,6,6,7],\"relatedPaths\":[],\"hits\":[],\"errors\":[]}\ngit-sync {\"id\":122,\"pr\":[\"open\",false,\"fix: refuse POST redirects in guardRedirects unless FollowInfoRefsRedirect is set\"],\"counts\":[5,6,4,3],\"relatedPaths\":[],\"hits\":[],\"errors\":[]}\ngit-sync {\"id\":124,\"pr\":[\"closed\",true,\"fix: authenticate the GitHub repo-size preflight and log its outcome\"],\"counts\":[8,11,19,13],\"relatedPaths\":[],\"hits\":[],\"errors\":[]}\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1eac6-41d3-7143-a221-cf44a37b6525","create_time":1794940497.723874}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":631,"sampled_through_sequence":628,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":3000}}
