{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T18:35:47.254Z","ordinal":3344,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1eacb-30ab-7ee3-b63d-f3aa65b238ee","call_id":"call_0X9AC6IZW68PAwNFtlyeakPN","output":"Chunk ID: d16d7b\nWall time: 0.0000 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 2851\nOutput:\nWarning: truncated output (original token count: 2851)\nTotal output lines: 35\n\nincremental alternatives: [[2589,\"open\",\"feat(opencode): support OpenCode 2 with V1 fallback\"],[2635,\"open\",\"Secure Enclave-protected tokens\"],[2755,\"closed\",\"repo mirror detach: stop showing the access list\"],[2913,\"closed\",\"repo: add default-branch command\"],[2636,\"closed\",\"Support multiple agent homes across session workflows\"],[2616,\"closed\",\"repo refs: `.git` is never part of a repo name\"],[1511,\"closed\",\"trail: add resume command\"],[906,\"closed\",\"feat: Add daily dispatch notes workflow\"],[1729,\"closed\",\"fix(codex): write hook config to the location codex expects\"]]\nreview scope #1647: [\"open\",\"feat(review): exact scope and parallel skills for reviewer agents\",\"\\u003c!-- entire-trail-link-start --\\u003e\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/766\\n\\u003c!-- entire-trail-link-end --\\u003e\\n\\n## One-sentence summary\\n\\nWhen `entire review` launches a reviewer, it now hands that reviewer everything the CLI already knows — exactly which code to review, how long it may run, which tools it may use, and how to start its configured skill — instead of a vague instruction each reviewer had to interpret for itself.\\n\\n## Problems, as observed in real runs\\n\\n1. **Reviewers re-derived — and sometimes got wrong — what code to review.** The composed prompt only said *\\\"review the commits unique to this branch vs origin/HEAD.\\\"* Each reviewer then ran its own git commands to work out what that meant. In one live run, codex diffed in the wrong direction on a branch that was behind main and reported main's newer code as regressions the branch had introduced — 2 of the 4 high-severity findings in that run's final verdict were such phantoms, and the judge consolidated them without any way to notice.\\n2. **Reviewers' tool calls were silently denied.** Headless `claude -p` auto-denies any tool call that isn't pre-approved, and the review command passed no permission config. Reviewers bounced off denials for `git diff` / `git log`, then either worked around them slowly or skipped verifyin\"]\nreview scope discussion: **Relationship to #1312's task design** (for reviewers wondering whether the no-injected-task commits undo something intentional):\n\nThe default-task machinery (`profileTask`, `defaultGeneralTask`, the `Task:` prompt section + output-format protocol) all came from #1312. This PR preserves three of its four purposes and reverses exactly one, delibera\n**Update to the #1312-relationship table above**: after review discussion, the fourth row is now also **kept** — the branch no longer changes which workers receive the canonical task. Worker briefing is exactly main's behavior (every worker gets the user task or the built-in default; the A/B without the brief was ~35% faster but missed a real findi\nissue #2996 scope: ## Problem\n\nA local review can finish and print its verdict but leave `entire review --findings` empty. The manifest currently depends on matching a tagged lifecycle session for each reviewer. If no session matches the current worktree, the command drops the captured output; sessions from sibling worktrees can make the resulting diagnostic look like a worktree mismatch. The command also returns success when writing the manifest fails.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Save every reviewer's captured output and the judge's aggregate verdict in the local manifest even when session state is missing, cannot be read, or does not match. Attach a session ID only when the existing matcher finds a suitable session, so a sibling worktree's session is not attributed to the run.\n- Return a nonzero error if the manifest cannot be written, while printing the existing user-visible warning only once.\n- Use subsecond timestamps for manifest filenames and findings handles so reviews started in the same second can be saved and selected separately. Continue accepting existing second-resolution handles.\n- Remove the empty-manifest matcher diagnostics and their tests: an unmatched session no longer prevents saving a review. A saved run without a session ID does not currently explain why session matching failed.\n- Update the review architecture documentation and cover missing or partial session matches, command-level write failures for single and multi-reviewer runs, and reviews started in the same second.\n\n## Verific\nasset export matches: [[2844,\"open\",\"Link an agent's own commit in another repository\"],[2069,\"open\",\"fix(checkpoint): externalize images in subagent transcripts before size cap\"],[3045,\"open\",\"codex: offer to install hooks where Codex reads them in linked worktrees\"],[2891,\"closed\",\"Pi: externalize images and keep image-only user turns\"],[2892,\"closed\",\"Condense an IDLE session prepare-commit-msg linked by its live transcript\"],[2782,\"closed\",\"Count session and checkpoint tokens from each agent's running total\"],[2692,\"closed\",\"Remove shadow branches and line attribution\"],[2779,\"closed\",\"Count a turn's step and tokens once when its Stop repeats\"],[2897,\"closed\",\"transcript: one Codex item mapping for stored rollouts an…1398 chars truncated…\"Phase 2: pluggable checkpoint stores (registry + topology)\"],[2075,\"closed\",\"feat(agent): add Goose coding agent integration\"],[1381,\"closed\",\"feat(antigravity): populate checkpoint prompt field via condensation-time transcript decoding\"],[1995,\"closed\",\"fix(trail): send the pre-image anchor with --patch suggested changes\"]]\nBrain #403 exact line: - **Pull**: fetches the repo-wide delta feed (`GET /api/v1/repos/{id}/brain/facts`, keyset cursor persisted in a repo-level cache under the plugin cache tree), then rebuilds the branch store locally: keep a fact when its trail merged (`trailId`), any anchor commit is reachable from HEAD, it belongs to this member (token sub), or it has no session/commit anchors (repo pool) — plus this machine's own facts the feed has not seen. Removal pass stands down without member identity and spares records with local transcript anchors (proof they were distilled here).\n- Full suite + `-race` green; new coverage: wire client, feed cache, filter rules, cursor resume/reset, pull-only, retirement one-way, recycle decontamination, own-fact survival.\n- Live against aws-us-east-2 (`gh/entireio/entire-brain`): first sync pushed 958 facts; a fresh clone with an empty brain pulled all 958 with server-stamped authors, synced marker, and cursor; `recall` ranked the sentinel fact first; re-sync was idempotent (`unchanged=958`) and resumed from the cursor; a retraction in one checkout reached the clone as `retracted`, and the clone's stale active push did not revive it.\n- Feed-cache loader skips corrupt lines but a single >4 MiB line would wedge it (`bufio.Scanner` cap); no realistic fact approaches that size.\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n> **Push** sanitizes and identity-checks the branch store, chunks to `facts:upsert`, and skips HTTP when empty. **Pull** pages the feed into a repo-level cache (cursor + records under the plugin cache), filters the full cache with `keepHostedFact` (trail id, JWT `sub`, git reachability, repo pool), then rebuilds the branch store—dropping feed-known facts that fail the filter while keeping unsynced locals and transcript-anchored distillations. Invalid page tokens reset cache and cursor once; push failure still pulls but withholds the per-branch synced marker.\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 781685cfa63f4e8dadac90e87962e365e423db6d. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\ngit-sync source history: [[\"9273a9f4\",\"relay: cover shared history under the prefix; tighten the docs\"],[\"ffa894e7\",\"relay: leave unchanged independent-history tips out of the haves\"],[\"a81db6a5\",\"fix: reject inert and unmatchable scoped empty policies\"],[\"0f6a015e\",\"Validate ref names arriving from a remote\"],[\"720b519a\",\"Simplify after review: dedupe, trim comments, flatten conditionals\"],[\"6814963e\",\"Add RefScope.AllRefs to broaden mirroring beyond branches and tags\"],[\"5c60d930\",\"even more general url validation\"],[\"79e093e3\",\"Reject identical source and target endpoints\"],[\"f87ea426\",\"Move mapping validation into validation\"],[\"ebd2cf7f\",\"Clarify validation mapping ownership\"]]\n149 gitproto: close the remote helper's stdin only once: [\"internal/gitproto/helper.go\",\"internal/gitproto/helper_test.go\"]\n147 relay: request a thin pack when the target accepts one: [\"CHANGELOG.md\",\"docs/architecture.md\",\"docs/protocol.md\",\"docs/testing.md\",\"internal/gitproto/fetch.go\",\"internal/gitproto/fetch_test.go\",\"internal/gitproto/refs.go\",\"internal/planner/planner_test.go\",\"internal/planner/relay.go\",\"internal/syncer/git_http_backend_test.go\",\"internal/syncer/git_http_backend_thin_test.go\",\"internal/syncer/integration_test.go\",\"internal/syncer/syncer.go\",\"internal/syncer/thin_pack_test.go\"]\n145 relay: drop redundant haves with entire-maximal: [\"CHANGELOG.md\",\"client.go\",\"client_test.go\",\"cmd/git-sync/syncplan.go\",\"internal/gitproto/capability.go\",\"internal/gitproto/maximal.go\",\"internal/gitproto/maximal_test.go\",\"internal/syncer/integration_test.go\",\"internal/syncer/maximal.go\",\"internal/syncer/maximal_test.go\",\"internal/syncer/syncer.go\",\"types.go\",\"unstable/client.go\",\"unstable/client_test.go\"]\n142 gitproto: don't let NoErrAlreadyUpToDate mask cancellation: [\"internal/gitproto/fetch.go\",\"internal/gitproto/fetch_test.go\"]\n123 Preserve concurrent updates and recognize already-current refs: [\"CHANGELOG.md\",\"docs/usage.md\",\"internal/gitproto/convergence.go\",\"internal/gitproto/convergence_test.go\",\"internal/gitproto/helper_test.go\",\"internal/gitproto/push.go\",\"internal/gitproto/push_test.go\",\"internal/gitproto/readers_test.go\",\"internal/gitproto/smarthttp_test.go\",\"internal/strategy/bootstrap/bootstrap.go\",\"internal/syncer/integration_test.go\",\"internal/syncer/ref_snapshot_test.go\",\"internal/syncer/syncer.go\",\"internal/syncertest/http.go\"]\n122 fix: refuse POST redirects in guardRedirects unless FollowInfoRefsRedirect is set: [\"docs/protocol.md\",\"internal/gitproto/smarthttp.go\",\"internal/gitproto/smarthttp_test.go\"]\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1eac6-41d3-7143-a221-cf44a37b6525","create_time":1794940547.242377}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":641,"sampled_through_sequence":638,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":3000}}
