{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T18:37:14.586Z","ordinal":3374,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call","status":"completed","id":"fc_05a7fc4dc4b68e03016afc9ec2fb9887d0801175b7e4a67e31","name":"exec_command","arguments":"{\"cmd\":\"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\\n*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md\\n@@\\n All project chats and worktrees should read and update this file rather than maintain separate copies. This is local coordination material, excluded from Git; it is not part of the upstream contribution.\\n \\n+## Top five from the 20-candidate audit — 18 November 2026\\n+\\n+Ranked by evidence, reviewable scope and likely user value. This is a shortlist, not a change to the existing serial contribution schedule, claim, or authorization to bypass its checks. One candidate is READY in scoped public checks; four require validation. No implementation or publication started in this pass.\\n+\\n+| Rank | ID | Candidate | Decision and next proof |\\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n+| 1 | AUD-026 | Git Sync: compare HTTP repository identity without URL fragments | **READY, focused scope.** Git Sync main is still `67dd3a4e083e4faae4417c1849035c7c4638112c`, the revision of the public validator and loopback HTTP observations. `normalizeEndpointURL` still retains fragments. Refreshed all-state fragment/endpoint/same-repo/trailing-slash searches, six open PRs and changed files, 27 upstream head refs, validation history, and discussion/inline review/submissions for all six open PRs plus related #18/#108/#124. #18 documents a trailing-slash case, not the fragment case. No exact public report or claim found within this scope. Keep the patch to HTTP endpoint identity and regression cases. |\\n+| 2 | AUD-024 | CLI: keep healthy saved findings accessible when one manifest is malformed | **HOLD.** Main is still `76f1b5129b974afdf8e59e4ae3755083c10ff8ff`, same as the reader probe. Establish named- and list-view behavior, with visible damage reporting and no deletion or false claim of complete history. Open [#2996](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2996) changes persistence in the same file, not this reader failure in the reviewed scope; also checked #1166. |\\n+| 3 | ENH-015 | CLI: list assets and export one already stored checkpoint image | **HOLD.** Demonstrate the artifact recovery workflow on a real checkpoint fixture where the current export is insufficient; show byte-exact extraction, bounded reads, and explicit output-path behavior. Limit v1 to already-supported session assets. Compared [#1589](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1589), [#1144](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1144), [#2069](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2069), #3151 and #3057; no exact selective single-asset export identified in the inspected scope. |\\n+| 4 | AUD-025 | Brain: recover a locally damaged hosted feed cache without losing older facts | **HOLD, elevated overlap risk.** Main `984c8ed468f62586b081c9f143b3d35f7a96213c` still skips malformed feed rows. [#403](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/403) explicitly documents skipping corrupt lines and separately fixes a missing records file retaining the cursor. Require a complete synthetic delta pull showing the distinct malformed-row recovery failure and a fresh nonduplication check; do not refile either known behavior. Reviewed #452 and #604 as well. |\\n+| 5 | ENH-014 | CLI: opt-in incremental review from a saved, reproducible baseline | **HOLD.** Best larger bet. First prove repeated full review cost and test whether a delta scope preserves important findings. Start with committed, same-branch ancestry and fall back on an invalid baseline. Open [#1647](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1647) provides explicit review scope; its body, comments and inline reviews were checked, with no previous-review baseline found in that scope. Coordinate before choosing an interface; #2996 owns adjacent persistence changes. |\\n+\\n+- **AUD-032 superseded: already reported, novelty FAIL.** The [#1768](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1768) body explicitly calls out the exact `checkpoint list --json` truncation note recommending its nonexistent `--limit` option. Current `checkpoint_group.go` and `explain_export.go` still show the mismatch; the PR is merged but that known follow-up was not fixed there. #2089 concerns a different `checkpoint explain` false negative. Do not start AUD-032 as new work under the strict novelty rule.\\n+- Refreshed targeted issue and all-state PR searches, open title/body lists (CLI 288, Brain 24, Git Sync 6), current files and selected relevant PR bodies, changed files, comments, inline findings and review submissions. The HOLD candidates are not novel/ownership-cleared by this bounded check. Prior runtime probes are credited to their original dates; no new builds or runtime tests in this pass. Existing tracked PRs and worktrees remain with their owners.\\n+\\n ## Start here\\n*** End Patch\\nPATCH\\nrg -n 'Top five from|AUD-032 superseded' CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md; git --no-optional-locks status --short\",\"max_output_tokens\":1500}","call_id":"call_oV2DDOyYWIILYVwXFVU39MON","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1eac6-41d3-7143-a221-cf44a37b6525","create_time":1794940608.912792}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":655,"sampled_through_sequence":653,"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":104}}
