ed rows. [#403](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/403) explicitly documents skipping corrupt lines and separately fixes a missing records file retaining the cursor. Require a complete synthetic delta pull showing the distinct malformed-row recovery failure and a fresh nonduplication check; do not refile either known behavior. Reviewed #452 and #604 as well. |\n+| 5 | ENH-014 | CLI: opt-in incremental review from a saved, reproducible baseline | **HOLD.** Best larger bet. First prove repeated full review cost and test whether a delta scope preserves important findings. Start with committed, same-branch ancestry and fall back on an invalid baseline. Open [#1647](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1647) provides explicit review scope; its body, comments and inline reviews were checked, with no previous-review baseline found in that scope. Coordinate before choosing an interface; #2996 owns adjacent persistence changes. |\n+\n+- **AUD-032 superseded: already reported, novelty FAIL.** The [#1768](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1768) body explicitly calls out the exact `checkpoint list --json` truncation note recommending its nonexistent `--limit` option. Current `checkpoint_group.go` and `explain_export.go` still show the mismatch; the PR is merged but that known follow-up was not fixed there. #2089 concerns a different `checkpoint explain` false negative. Do not start AUD-032 as new work under the strict novelty rule.\n+- Refreshed targeted issue and all-state PR searches, open title/body lists (CLI 288, Brain 24, Git Sync 6), current files and selected relevant PR bodies, changed files, comments, inline findings and review submissions. The HOLD candidates are not novel/ownership-cleared by this bounded check. Prior runtime probes are credited to their original dates; no new builds or runtime tests in this pass. Existing tracked PRs and worktrees remain with their owners.\n+\n ## Start here\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\nrg -n 'Top five from|AUD-032 superseded' CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md; git --no-optional-locks status --short"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md\n8:## Top five from the 20-candidate audit — 18 November 2026\n20:- **AUD-032 superseded: already reported, novelty FAIL.** The [#1768](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1768) body explicitly calls out the exact `checkpoint list --json` truncation note recommending its nonexistent `--limit` option. Current `checkpoint_group.go` and `explain_export.go` still show the mismatch; the PR is merged but that known follow-up was not fixed there. #2089 concerns a different `checkpoint explain` false negative. Do not start AUD-032 as new work under the strict novelty rule.\n M .codex/config.toml\nM  cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_replay_test.go\nM  cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_replay_tree_test.go\nM  cmd/entire/cli/strategy/metadata_reconcile.go\nM  docs/architecture/ref-checkpoint-backend.md\nM  docs/development/checkpoint-implementation.md\n?? opencode_tracker.md\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":147130625}},"started_at_ms":1794940634928,"completed_at_ms":1794940635087}}
