s after local feed-cache corruption** | The reader can skip a damaged record and retain the cursor. If the next sync never recovers that fact, this is a meaningful data integrity fix. | **Hold for end-to-end proof.** Brain #403 already documents skipped corrupt rows and fixes the missing-file variant. Prove the distinct recovery failure before claiming it. ([github.com](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/blob/984c8ed468f62586b081c9f143b3d35f7a96213c/internal/cli/hosted_feed_cache.go)) |\n| 5 | **ENH-014 · CLI — review changes since a saved baseline** | The biggest feature here: reduce repeat review time and token cost when a branch gets another commit. | **Hold for a benchmark.** Compare full and incremental reviews on a representative branch, including whether the narrower review misses important findings. Coordinate with CLI #1647 on review scope. ([github.com](https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/main/docs/architecture/review-command.md)) |\n\nI dropped **AUD-032** from the queue: merged CLI **#1768** explicitly documents the exact `checkpoint list --json` warning that recommends a nonexistent `--limit` flag. The bug is still present, but it fails your strict novelty rule. I recorded that and the ranked shortlist in the [contribution tracker](/Users/puneetpalsingh/Documents/Code/OSSplayground/Entire/cli/CONTRIBUTION_TRACKER.md:8).\n\nThe best first three are **a small correctness fix, a recovery fix, and a user-facing feature**. Finish those in that order as they clear their gates; keep the last two as follow-ons rather than opening five speculative PRs.","started_at":1794940224,"completed_at":1794940688,"duration_ms":464062,"time_to_first_token_ms":125584}}
